me a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  v'),(22,'Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  Gimme a UHG!  v'),(23,'1 of 2**\r\n \r\n\r\nwe are quite insecure about who we are. we are constantly grasping at an essence that is not there. and day by day, that essence that we grasp at, changes. today i am feeling confident. someone told me i was beatiful, and so i grasp at my essence as being in my body. or today i am boring and mean. someone dismissed something i said and so i relate my \"self\" to my state of mind.\r\n\r\nbut none of these things are my \"self\". my \"self\" is a blank, completely empty of any inherent characteristic. and yet i grasp at it everyday and it causes me immense pain. \r\n\r\nme\r\ni chose this wallpaper. \r\n\r\nother person\r\nreally? it\'s ugly. \r\n\r\nme\r\nare you saying i have bad taste? \r\n\r\nand suddenly i\'m offended and the rest of my day is tainted with worry because i\'m fighting against the possibility that i am a person with bad taste. and i\'m angry at the antagonist1 because he accused me of having bad taste. and i want to fight with him or insult him, or more often, search out some salient fault in him to make my injured \"self\" feel better.\r\n\r\nbut every time i react with anger, an imprint is made in my mind. that imprint is karma. and then whenever i experience the circumstances of someone questioning my taste, that karma ripens, and i become angry, which creates another imprint to react with anger. and so i react with anger, which creates another imprint to react with anger, and the cycle goes on and on and on forever. this is samsara. this is the cycle of suffering.\r\n\r\nthe only way to stop the cycle is to understand the relationship of emptiness and karma. emptiness is the the inherent blankness of all things. karma is the energy that determines what we project onto that blankness. and we are helpless in the moment we perceive it, to change what we see. we are slaves to our karma. the only hope is to end the cycle. and the only way to do that is to react differently.\r\n\r\n'),(26,'<table width=\"70%\">\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<h3>what is swinney?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nthe word \'swinney\' can be used to refer to two different things:\r\n</p><p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li><a href=\"userpages.phtml?username=austin\">austin swinney</a>, the dashing young libra who created swinney.org\r\n</p><p>\r\nor\r\n</p><p>\r\n<li>swinney.org, the website where people (humans) write journal\r\nentries (usually text, with occasional images).\r\n</blockquote>\r\n</ol>\r\n</p>\r\n<h3>who writes on swinney.org?</h3>\r\n<p>\r\nanyone! <a href=\"submit_article.phtml\">including you</a>, if you want.\r\n</p><p>\r\nin the past, <a href=\"roll_call_all.phtml\">these people</a> have\r\nwritten on swinney.org. \r\n</p></blockquote>\r\n<h3>do i have to sign up or log in or something?</h3>\r\n<p>\r\nno, you don\'t have to sign up. just write a journal entry <a\r\nhref=\"submit_article.phtml\">here</a>. if you write more than\r\nonce, and use the same name every time, it\'ll be easier for people to\r\nfind what you\'ve written, but it\'s not a rule or anything.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>what should i write?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p> anything you want! entries have consisted of anything from bad\r\nhaiku to someone\'s irc chat logs to harrowing tales of near death.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p> carefully constructed texts and thoughtful rambles are always\r\nappreciated. you know, <i>writing</i>.  </p>\r\n\r\n<p> this isn\'t a BBS and this isn\'t a mailing list. posts that make us\r\nfeel like this is a BBS or a mailing list might not make it through\r\nour not-so-rigourous editorial process.  Cyantist has a good article\r\nabout this: <a\r\nhref=\"http://swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=935.txt\">who\r\ncensor\'s the censor?</a>\r\n\r\n<h3>who will read what i write?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p> no one can really say who reads what on this here\r\ninternet. all you can really bet is that some of the people who write\r\non swinney.org a lot also read swinney.org a lot, so they will\r\nprobably read what you write.  </p> <h3>ok i wrote something, howcome it isn\'t showing up?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p> swinney.org has a group of people who \"activate\" the things you\r\nwrite so everyone can see them.  </p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nsometimes the person activating decides what you wrote didn\'t\r\nhave enough content or was a mistaken submission. sometimes we are just lazy and\r\ndidn\'t go and activate the article yet. rarely, but sometimes,\r\nwhatever you wrote just gets veto\'d for nebulous editorial purposes.  .\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<h3>how come i commented on something and it was there, but then disappeared?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>swinney.org is not a place to come if you define yourself by the\r\nability to kick others down, or kick them when they are down.  also,\r\ndont come here to be annoying.  be thoughtful.  be challenging.  do\r\nnot be a prick.  this site is moderated by a hand full of fair people\r\nwho are not annoying or mean.  if your comment was removed and you feel\r\nit was done so unjustly, email <a\r\nhref=\"mailto:editors@swinney.org\">editors@swinney.org</a>.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>see <a href=\"article.phtml?id=1223.txt\">energy monsers, or how the F.O.L.K. wars have changed</a> by one of our resident moms, <a href=\"userpages.phtml?username=auntie\">auntie</a>.\r\n\r\n<h3>what are the \"access keys\" for swinney.org and why are they here?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Swinney.org is moving toward full compliance with <a\r\nhref=\"http://www.section508.gov/\">Federal Information Technology\r\nAccessibility Initiative</a>, Section 508 of the Rehabilitation Act\r\nAmendments of 1998.  the goal is to achieve the <a href=\"http://www.w3.org:80/\">Conformance Level \"A\"</a> as layed out by the <a href=\"http://w3.org\">World Wide Web Consortium</a>, (W3C).  there is a <a href=\"http://www.w3.org/TR/WAI-WEBCONTENT/full-checklist.html\">checklist of points</a> to this end.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>now more specifically about the \"access keys\" on swinney.org:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Windows Platform press the ALT key plus the access key/character\r\n(where character is the designated hot key). Then press \'Return\' on\r\nyour keyboard.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Macintosh Platform press the CMD key plus the character (where\r\ncharacter is the designated hot key). Then press \'Return\' on your\r\nkeyboard.</p>\r\n<pre>\r\nAccesskey = h		<b>h</b>ome index\r\nAccesskey = j		<b>j</b>ournal index\r\nAccesskey = c		<b>c</b>omments index\r\nAccesskey = s		<b>s</b>ubmit comment\r\nAccesskey = e		submit journal <b>e</b>ntry\r\nAccesskey = f		<b>f</b>aq index - answers\r\nAccesskey = a 		<b>a</b>dmin area\r\n</pre>\r\n<h3>for general assistance with this site, inqueries:</b></p>\r\n<p>austin swinney<br>\r\naustin@swinney.org<br>\r\nsanta cruz, CA, US</p>\r\n<p>Fri Jul 13, 2001 12:22 PM</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n'),(27,'Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar n