ar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  '),(30,'Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  '),(31,'Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  '),(32,'Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  '),(33,'Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  '),(34,NULL),(35,NULL),(36,NULL),(37,NULL),(38,'Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  Nar nar nar nar.  '),(39,'yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,yo momma,'),(40,'Trying out this new form before we get outta here and head over to House of Pies in the Feliz.  I\'m going to try a cream pie...'),(41,'<P>I called Somy today.  Her answering machine picked up with a computer voice.  I am never assured by a computer voice.  \r\n</P>\r\n<blockquote>\r\nâ€œBzzz Hello zzz to z leave zz a zz fax zzzzzz press zz one zzz to z leave z a z message zzzz press zz two zzzzzzz or zzzzz wait zzzz (BEEP)â€.  \r\n</blockquote>\r\n<P>\r\nThe answer seemed obvious to me.  I wanted to leave a message.  I couldnâ€™t get past the fax thing.  My message had to play off the fax thing.  Okay, so I will imitate the human fax voie, whatever that is.\r\n</P>\r\n<blockquote>\r\nâ€œBzzzzz incoming zzz fax zz for zzzzz Somy zzzzzzzz This zzz is zz Austin zzzz I zz am going z to zz a zz bar zz with zzzzz Arnoldâ€¦â€\r\n</blockquote>\r\n<P>\r\nNormally interrupts are fine.  I can deal, but not when I am leaving a message on a girls answering machine whom I barely know and have only been on one date with.  Arnold suggested I invite her to Ye Ole Rustic with zero notice.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI donâ€™t know any girls that would go on an impromptu second date with zero notice.  Having grown up with three sisters and two moms, I know that for the average woman, this is a great offence that insults as far as it suggests she can be ready at a momentâ€™s notice, as though perfection were a steady state and not hours of agonizing over what to wear and getting make up on just right.  I objected to Arnoldâ€™s proposal.  Arnold said he know plenty of women who would drop what they were doing to go on a second date.  That is what he implied when he said, â€œI know plenty.\"\r\n</P>\r\n<blockquote>To make a long story short, â€œzzzzzzzzâ€¦(Pickup) Hello?!  WHO is this?!â€</blockquote>\r\n</P><P>\r\nYes, it is I, Austin â€˜dip shitâ€™ Swinneyâ€ leaving a moronic message on your answering machine, not some crazed stalker with a phone message fetish.  I donâ€™t think Somy was impressed at all.  Not by the message, and not when I asked her out and she asked when and I said now.  Oh well.\r\n</P>'),(42,'<P>I called Somy again after work.  I got the machine voice again.  I resisted the urge to embellish and just stuck with the program.\r\n</P>\r\n\r\n<blockquote>â€œHi Somy, this is Austin.  Sorry I called you on such short notice.  That was kind of rude.  I hope you forgive me.  Anyway, I am going to get pie tonight at 8:30.  Would you join me?  Call me back 919-500-8393.â€</blockquote>\r\n\r\n<P>Then I went to DZAâ€™s house to eat dinner with him.  Fried chicken, lilâ€™ potatoes, corn.  It was a fabulous home cooked meal.  I think his mom was involved in some way.  It was funny how I got invited over.  I just called and started moaning about how tired I was and lazy.  I said I didnâ€™t have the energy to clean the one set of dished that I own.  They are still dirty from two days ago.  I honestly wasnâ€™t probing for an invitation.  Being tired, I didnâ€™t fee like leaving my bed.  I went through, and the meal was delicious.  I donâ€™t know what I would do here in LA if I couldnâ€™t get free meals from the Yeazza family.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nI called Somy and left another message about 7:50.  I volunteered to take a rain check on the pie and said weâ€™ll talk later.\r\n</P><P>\r\nThen DZA drove us over to Los Feliz to pick up Arnold and Chachi for pie.  Our timing was perfect.    Chachi and the Ballerina Girl were on their way out the door for a girlâ€™s night out.  Arnold was ready to go eat dinner, but didnâ€™t know where to get it.  We went to house of pies.  We talked to funny Stef on the way out the door.  I felt bad for not inviting her.  She looked like she was done with the idea, and her presence was such a hoot the previous pie night.  She is hella funny.  It was a reactionary boyâ€™s night though.  Girls out.\r\n</P><P>\r\nLorenzo showed up later after finding out our location from Funny Stef.  Lorenzo is effin funny too.  When those to get together, I crack ribs.  They insult each other back and forth until Funny Stef wins.  She always wins.  She is the undefeated champion of the caged California insult match.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nWe talked over pie about the movie Bullet with Steve McQueen. It is one of Arnoldâ€™s favorites.  We watched it later at Arnoldâ€™s place.  It has an amazing San Francisco car chase scene between a Charger and a Mustang fastback.  Arnold said they used 4 Mustangs in the filming of the chase because cars kept breaking down.  There was only one Charger required.  Arnold offered this as proof of the superiority of Mopar cars.\r\n</P><P>\r\nAfter pie, I talked us out of a rock show because I was tired from being woke up at 6 am by BMGâ€™s auto mechanic in Austin, TX.  Also because I drank the night before with Arnold and was mean all day.  I needed some detoxification time.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nI got home and Somy had left a message.  It was firm, â€œAustin, I just got home so I couldnâ€™t make the pie.  Hum, yea, weâ€™ll talk later.â€  \r\n</P><P>\r\nIt was funny how she said that last par, like it had been up in the air whether we would talk again and she only decided moments prior to leaving a message on my machine, but there was still a grain of uncertainty.  \r\n\r\nI was thinking, from a n easing-into-relationship P.O.V., I donâ€™t usually have anything in common with any one I date or know.  I just like to be with them.  Okay, one common thread is that I am best friends with people who are weird.  I have the Weirdo Clan.  My point though is that the field is kind of open, and what I like most about dating is knowing somewhere I can get a hug when I need it. Also, knowing someone I can give a hug.  Hugs are very intimate to me, not to be dealt out or received like a hippy giving away daisy pedals.  I know that with my past girlfriends, it took some significant hang out time before tension reached a plucky high note.  Then everything unfurls like love.  I need that.\r\n</P>'),(43,'<p>So, I started hanging out/sleeping with this girl that I\'m doing a show with.  And she\'s trying to move things along, like she\'ll say, \"I think I\'m at a point where I want to see a lot of you.\"  And it\'s just at this moment when I feel my world collapse, and for some reason, I get irritable, and my back starts to hurt, and I can\'t breathe.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I don\'t think this is normal.  I have a number of friends that seem to hold meaningful relationships with their partners, and I\'ve never seen them deal with the sort of symptoms I get.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>My feeling is that most of the stuff is in my head.  But, if I\'m feeling claustrophobic, what\'s wrong with stepping away?  I really enjoy time on my own.  I find that I become the most frenetic whenever I think I\'m giving up my independence, my ability to walk away whenever i want, my safety.  Ah, there\'s the rub...</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Should I go into this situation for precisely the reason that I fear it?  Is recognition of this fear a sign that there\'s something I need to face up to or grow from?  Or should I run like the wind?  I don\'t think I\'d get very far.  I\'ve slacked off on my jogging and I\'m smoking a pack a day again.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>well,  back to the elephants...</p>'),(44,'You are the most special pet.\r\n\r\nI love hearing things like that.\r\n\r\nYou make me soooooo happy. I think Iâ€™m going to cry.\r\n\r\nDo I get a trophy for that?\r\n\r\nDonâ€™t forget cute.\r\n\r\nYou gotta love me!\r\n\r\nI love compliments. Keep them coming.\r\n\r\nStop that. \r\n\r\nHave you ever looked in the mirror?\r\n\r\nIâ€™m like a fine wine.\r\n\r\nYouâ€™re making me hungry.\r\n\r\nI think youâ€™re just saying that. *blush*\r\n\r\nI know. People tell me that everyday.\r\n\r\nI get that all the time.\r\n\r\nNo news to me.\r\n\r\nHey, you wanna know something? Youâ€™re special, too!!!!\r\n\r\nI love you. Youâ€™re the best owner. I feel like a cup of tea.\r\n\r\nIâ€™m just as special as you are. \r\n\r\nYouâ€™re just saying that. \r\n\r\nYou really mean it?\r\n\r\n\r\nYou are the most special owner.\r\n\r\nAh, geee. What can I say? \r\n\r\nHey, you created me.\r\n\r\nI think that says a lot about you, too.\r\n\r\nHow come you never tell me that more often?\r\n\r\nSpecial is what special does.\r\n\r\nSome things never change.\r\n\r\nI think you are required to say that.\r\n\r\nDuh.\r\n\r\nItâ€™s about time you noticed.\r\n\r\nIâ€™m rubber and youâ€™re glue. Whatever you say to me sticks to you.\r\n\r\nI am like a fine wine.\r\n\r\nThatâ€™s not very original.\r\n\r\nDonâ€™t just tell me Iâ€™m special. Show me!\r\n\r\nI love being special.\r\n\r\nI guess you could say that.\r\n\r\nWant to see something special? Close your eyesâ€¦\r\n\r\nSPECIAL DELIVERY.\r\n\r\nI think Iâ€™m going to blush.\r\n\r\nThanks.\r\n\r\n*Yawn*\r\n\r\nAnd I am smart, too.\r\n\r\nYou never say anything about how cute I am.\r\n\r\nSpecial Smecial.\r\n\r\nYou should look in the mirror and tell yourself something nice.\r\n\r\nI donâ€™t deserve you.\r\n\r\nI want to hug you.\r\n\r\nWill you groom me more often? That makes me feel special.\r\n\r\nI always knew I was.\r\n\r\nIâ€™m not sure what youâ€™re talking about. Why donâ€™t you buy me something?\r\n\r\nYou are so beautiful. You really are!\r\n'),(45,'<P>I haven\'t even begun to listen to this live album off <a href=\"http://artandlies.com/zooberries/\" target=\'new\'>juan\'s site</a> and already I am depressed.  I guess I am not really depressed.  I am just hungry.  Blood sugar drops and so do my spirits.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I have been having a bad day.  Two days ago, the management of the company I work for realized they were not managing me.  My job was soOOo nice. Now all of the sudden I have to send daily status reports clear copied to seven people.  Fuck.  Leave me alone.  I feel like Eminem.  Just kidding.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I need a hug again.  I should stay home tonite though.  I haven\'t been home in a week, only for sleep.  The sleep hasn\'t even been too worth it.  At least I am able to go to bed at 12am.  I couldn\'t for a while there.  It was just too hot. I wasn\'t burning enough energy during the day.  Now I am lifting weights and it is much easier to fall asleep.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Apparently it is also much easier to blabber on about nothing.  I\'ll shut up know.</P>'),(46,'So i am \'ramping-up\' the submit(ted) splash page.  Hope it works and looks good.\r\n\r\n'),(47,'So i am \'ramping-up\' the submit(ted) splash page.  Hope it works and looks good.\r\n\r\n'),(48,'So i am \'ramping-up\' the submit(ted) splash page.  Hope it works and looks good.\r\n\r\n'),(49,'So i am \'ramping-up\' the submit(ted) splash page.  Hope it works and looks good.\r\n\r\n'),(50,'So i am \'ramping-up\' the submit(ted) splash page.  Hope it works and looks good.\r\n\r\n'),(51,'So i am \'ramping-up\' the submit(ted) splash page.  Hope it works and looks good.\r\n\r\n'),(52,'So i am \'ramping-up\' the submit(ted) splash page.  Hope it works and looks good.\r\n\r\n'),(53,'So i am \'ramping-up\' the submit(ted) splash page.  Hope it works and looks good.\r\n\r\n'),(54,'So i am \'ramping-up\' the submit(ted) splash page.  Hope it works and looks good.\r\n\r\n'),(55,'So i am \'ramping-up\' the submit(ted) splash page.  Hope it works and looks good.\r\n\r\n'),(56,'<P>Well, I don\'t think Somy will call me back.  You would not believe the stress.  I find it difficult to absorb the uncertainty of dating interest.  Does she like me or not?  Do I care either way?  Well, before women in Los Angeles approached me, I was fine single.  Isn\'t it amazing how someone can capture the imagination at the drop of a hat?  I think it is.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Anyway, party tonight in Venice.  Dza is driving over from South Pass because I am not feeling like going there.  Also, my place is on the way to Arnold\'s.  We are going to Arnold\'s.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>It is Friday, 5 pm.  Most people in L.A. are ready to go home.  I\'m not.  I\'ll be at work until I write this down at 8 p.m.  My home is not a very attractive place right now.  It is clean, but I don\'t feel like trailer trash lately.  A nap would be nice, but the chances of it becoming a reality even if I did go home are slim.  So I won\'t go home.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I\'m thinking about asking if the red haired Eatwell waitress would like to go on a date.  Fuck dates.  I want to know if she will hang out with me.  I am more interested in that then dates.  Dates make me nervous and tired and weird.  I wonder what her name is...?</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Her name is Sara.  I have already dated a Sara.  Sara\'s have attitude and so does she.  She likes post punk music aka \'indie rock\' and is looking very pretty today.  She smokes.  I had a smoke break with her.  Didn\'t catch the brand of cig.  She cusses alot.  She knew the definition of NarNar without a second of pause. She is quick.  She is a student at Occidental College.  Didn\'t catch the major.  She is tired and looks tired.  Her eyes have dark circles.  She is in a band, something that ends in a Z and is not the punk band Spaz.  She would like to go to indie rock shows, but not until November when she cuts back on her hours at work.  It is too hard, she said, working and going to school.  She thought she could do it.  She can\'t.  I know that feeling, I told her.  I told her to call me if she has the spontaneous urge to rock, or has insomnia.  She said sure and that I will definitely see here at the Eatwell. I like that.  I know a waitress at one of my favorite restaurants.  Even I don\'t date her--and I don\'t want to--I can still just be down on her turf.</P>\r\n\r\n<blockquote>\"Yoe Sara, sup?  I\'ll take a coffee.\"</blockquote>\r\n\r\n\r\n'),(57,'<P>wow. how cool is this? i can share my inner feelings in a journal with out my \"real\" peeps finding out about them!</P>\r\n\r\n<P>ok. i would like to talk about my dad. i can\'t do that in my real journal cuz he might find it. oh, wait. i have links to this site too. so he could find this. shit. oh well. :)</P>\r\n\r\n<P>so. um. i like candy. candy is good and sweet. sometimes it hurts my teeth, though. that sucks. i hate the dentist; however, not in a personal way. althought i would wack him in the head if i got a chance.</P>\r\n\r\n<p>thank you for letting me vent on your site, austin. i had a party the other night; jesse and senor lepard where there. wish you were too. bye.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>puppy</P>\r\n\r\n<P><em>aus: awe c\'mon, your dad is not going to read my site... =-)</P>'),(58,'<P> Ouch, I hurt.  My pain is a combo of aching muscles from bicycling yesterday to a similar feeling in my bones from sleeping on a pile of pillows in the Alexandria closet.  Sleeping on couches is an important lifestyle of having friends in L.A.  Sometimes you just can\'t make it home.  It is too far and the LAPD is too numerous.\r\n</P><P>\r\nYesterday I ate breakfast at a hipster joint and then I headed over to Arnold\'s for some concept analysis.  Afterward, we went on a grand tour of Los Angeles on bike.  The ride was from Arnold\'s on Alexandria and Franklin, up to the Observatory in the Hollywood Hills, down the fire trail and Arnold\'s semi-pro Hawaiian biking style left me in the dust, then across Los Feliz to the L.A. River, a long under the overpass, past the chamber of commerce macking in their territory, and out at a Philly sandwich shop.  Everything from the waist down is in pain, cramped.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI have to go to work now.  I should go home even though I don\'t want to.  Right now I\'m at the House of Pies.  I am battling morning rituals like brushing my teeth, shower, etc.  I\'m not right if I don\'t get that done.  I should probably wear something other than the same thing I have worn to work the past half month.  Same shoes, same jeans, same sweatshirt, same hat, variation is in the underwear and tee shirt.  I was thinking about getting a black North Face sweatshirt for twice as much as it should cost and wear it every day.  Maybe people wouldnâ€™t mind so much that my clothing never changes. I could live on because I represent rugged individually in the information age:  engineered urban cowboy crossing the ruff and tumble of everyday life in clothes with the capacity to become completely immersed in water without staying wet, instantly dry Austin. </P>\r\n\r\n<P>God, today is my birthday.  Please send me home from work early. </P>\r\n'),(59,'<P>There is a guy at work that I see all the time. Maybe it\'s because he wears the same clothes everyday. Maybe? I don\'t know. It could be his hat or his red shoes or the way he burps. It\'s kind of disgusting, but Hartman always says, \"God bless you.\" That\'s cute. \r\n</P>\r\n<P>\r\nI miss lookin at the back of their heads. It just doesn\'t seem right working their w/ H., B., and <a href=\"aim:goim?screenname=MissRockieH\">Rockie</a>. I miss <a href=\"aim:goim?screenname=grillamonk\">Grillamonk</a> and Swinney. Even though they hardly spoke a word to me, I feel sad because they were moved across the room. Did I say something wrong? Was I the problem? Why wasn\'t I consulted about the move? Why didn\'t they move me? I would have taken one for the team.\r\n</P>\r\n<P>\r\nI think it\'s okay that you wear the same clothes to work because it relieves the pressure on us, your co-workers, to \"dress up\" and looking \"hot.\" It also puts an end to the dating scene at work. I think the prospects are thin, though. So it really doesn\'t matter. \r\n</P>\r\n<P>\r\nHey, stop asking me to move my freakin\' desk J. If I have to move it or any other piece of freakin\' furniture again I\'m going to go all crazy in that office. I might even do a freakin\' kartwheel. Today I moved a plant to an office and filled the empty space w/ another plant. As I took the first plant away, it left a trail of dirty water. At first I felt kind of bad, but then, as I was hauling the plant to the office, I started to smile. My smile quickly faded because I realized that NarNar might be watching me. He cuts my pay check, you know. \r\n</P>\r\n<P>Christ, what happened to you? I\'m sick of moving my desk. It\'s been moved 73 yards. I don\'t even have a ruler. I just know. I\'m like that. </P>\r\n<P><em>aus: maybe some day you can come and visit us.</em></p>'),(60,'<pre>\r\nDate: Mon, 2 Oct 2000 22:09:27 -0500\r\nFrom: .~,/*Mom*\\`~. zz55p0@airmail.net\r\nTo: Austin Swinney austin@swinney.org\r\nSubject: HAPPY BIRTHDAY\r\n</pre>\r\n<P>We are all thinking of you and hoping that you\'re out having fun tonight.\r\nRemembering this day 24 years ago takes me back a long time.  Al and I had\r\ndecorated the most beautiful nursery you ever saw.  I don\'t suppose you have\r\nany memory of the colorful Noah\'s Ark wallpaper next to your crib, do you?\r\nWe had custom shutters made for all the windows, the kind with fabric\r\ninserts in them, to match the room.  We painted all the furniture white, and\r\nupholstered everything in green and white gingham checked fabric.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nYour Grandmother helped me sew a matching cover and bolster cushions for the day bed in your\r\nroom. She was amazing, in that she could do any kind of \"do-it-yourself\" project....She was a product of The Depression...she learned to do everything because she couldn\'t ever afford to have it done.  \r\n</P><P>The white rocking chair we bought to rock you in is still in our family room. You should have that someday.  (These days, people sit in it and watch the fish\r\nin the acquarium.) We even had beautiful green carpeting laid. \r\n</P><P>\r\nAs I said,\r\nAustin, you came home to a lovely room. It was a labor of love, and you were\r\na very, very,loved and beautiful baby. Happy Birthday twenty five years later!!  \r\n</P>\r\n<P>Love always, MOM</P>\r\n'),(61,'<P>I was geared to take a crap at work.  I got in there and dropped the kids off at the pool when, \"YEO, no towels!\"</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Damn, not my evening.  I had to use toilet seat covers.  If I were judging olympic shits and I saw someone execute a perfect .9666 on the porcelin throne, but then they had to use toilet seat covers to dry off, I\'d take away .2 for .7666.  Call me wack, but in order to preserve the art, we must play by the rules.  Gotta use toilet paper.</P>\r\n\r\n<P><a href=\"http://elly.org\">Elly</a> just pointed out that Camilla is starting to get fleshy on her cam.</P>\r\n\r\n<img src=\"http://wallflower.nu/cam/archive/sep00/shirt.jpg\">\r\n<P>and...</P>\r\n<img src=\"http://wallflower.nu/cam/archive/sep00/bra.jpg\">\r\n\r\n<P>Camilla is the cutest girl on the entire internet.  I don\'t know about this flesh thing.  It definately gets the pole up but is that what we are all out here for?  I am not.  I like the cute stuff.</P>\r\n\r\n<img src=\"http://wallflower.nu/cam/archive/sep00/23/boobies.jpg\">\r\n\r\n<P>I have been using Camilla\'s images on my desktops for a few months and don\'t plan on changing them to some other girl. </P>\r\n\r\n<P>But I have a sense of duty to not be a parasitic entity on this Net.  I have to contribute.  So my question is this: Do I have to start stripping now?  Camilla is essentially offering me a challenge. She does not know it. We don\'t know each other.  But we here at Swinney.org function on a honor system.</P>\r\n<img src=\"http://wallflower.nu/cam/archive/sep00/23/panties.jpg\">\r\n<P>And I have to say that Elly\'s brief recollection of the pervs that sent her email back when she used to supply the world with live nudie pics is suggests to me that I should consider stripping on the net as <i>wrong</i> where I will not do it.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Everything is about right and wrong, isn\'t it?  Black and white.  Life Noir.  Well, I hope for all our sakes that I find a peaceful resolution to this in my soul.  If I don\'t though, I suppose I am never too old to learn to be sexy for the camera <tt>=-)</tt></P>\r\n\r\n<img src=\"http://wallflower.nu/cam/archive/sep00/23/kissie.jpg\">\r\n'),(62,'<P>I was geared to take a crap at work.  I got in there and dropped the kids off at the pool when, \"YEO, no towels!\"</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Damn, not my evening.  I had to use toilet seat covers.  If I were judging olympic shits and I saw someone execute a perfect .9666 on the porcelin throne, but then they had to use toilet seat covers to dry off, I\'d take away .2 for .7666.  Call me wack, but in order to preserve the art, we must play by the rules.  Gotta use toilet paper.</P>\r\n\r\n<P><a href=\"http://elly.org\">Elly</a> just pointed out that Camilla is starting to get fleshy on her cam.</P>\r\n\r\n<img src=\"http://wallflower.nu/cam/archive/sep00/shirt.jpg\">\r\n<P>and...</P>\r\n<img src=\"http://wallflower.nu/cam/archive/sep00/bra.jpg\">\r\n\r\n<P>Camilla is the cutest girl on the entire internet.  I don\'t know about this flesh thing.  It definately gets the pole up but is that what we are all out here for?  I am not.  I like the cute stuff.</P>\r\n\r\n<img src=\"http://wallflower.nu/cam/archive/sep00/23/boobies.jpg\">\r\n\r\n<P>I have been using Camilla\'s images on my desktops for a few months and don\'t plan on changing them to some other girl. </P>\r\n\r\n<P>But I have a sense of duty to not be a parasitic entity on this Net.  I have to contribute.  So my question is this: Do I have to start stripping now?  Camilla is essentially offering me a challenge. She does not know it. We don\'t know each other.  But we here at Swinney.org function on a honor system.</P>\r\n<img src=\"http://wallflower.nu/cam/archive/sep00/23/panties.jpg\">\r\n<P>And I have to say that Elly\'s brief recollection of the pervs that sent her email back when she used to supply the world with live nudie pics is suggests to me that I should consider stripping on the net as <i>wrong</i> where I will not do it.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Everything is about right and wrong, isn\'t it?  Black and white.  Life Noir.  Well, I hope for all our sakes that I find a peaceful resolution to this in my soul.  If I don\'t though, I suppose I am never too old to learn to be sexy for the camera <tt>=-)</tt></P>\r\n\r\n<img src=\"http://wallflower.nu/cam/archive/sep00/23/kissie.jpg\">\r\n'),(63,'<P>I was geared to take a crap at work.  I got in there and dropped the kids off at the pool when, \"YEO, no towels!\"</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Damn, not my evening.  I had to use toilet seat covers.  If I were judging olympic shits and I saw someone execute a perfect .9666 on the porcelin throne, but then they had to use toilet seat covers to dry off, I\'d take away .2 for .7666.  Call me wack, but in order to preserve the art, we must play by the rules.  Gotta use toilet paper.</P>\r\n\r\n<P><a href=\"http://elly.org\">Elly</a> just pointed out that Camilla is starting to get fleshy on her cam.</P>\r\n\r\n<img src=\"http://wallflower.nu/cam/archive/sep00/shirt.jpg\">\r\n<P>and...</P>\r\n<img src=\"http://wallflower.nu/cam/archive/sep00/bra.jpg\">\r\n\r\n<P>Camilla is the cutest girl on the entire internet.  I don\'t know about this flesh thing.  It definately gets the pole up but is that what we are all out here for?  I am not.  I like the cute stuff.</P>\r\n\r\n<img src=\"http://wallflower.nu/cam/archive/sep00/23/boobies.jpg\">\r\n\r\n<P>I have been using Camilla\'s images on my desktops for a few months and don\'t plan on changing them to some other girl. </P>\r\n\r\n<P>But I have a sense of duty to not be a parasitic entity on this Net.  I have to contribute.  So my question is this: Do I have to start stripping now?  Camilla is essentially offering me a challenge. She does not know it. We don\'t know each other.  But we here at Swinney.org function on a honor system.</P>\r\n<img src=\"http://wallflower.nu/cam/archive/sep00/23/panties.jpg\">\r\n<P>And I have to say that Elly\'s brief recollection of the pervs that sent her email back when she used to supply the world with live nudie pics is suggests to me that I should consider stripping on the net as <i>wrong</i> where I will not do it.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Everything is about right and wrong, isn\'t it?  Black and white.  Life Noir.  Well, I hope for all our sakes that I find a peaceful resolution to this in my soul.  If I don\'t though, I suppose I am never too old to learn to be sexy for the camera <tt>=-)</tt></P>\r\n\r\n<img src=\"http://wallflower.nu/cam/archive/sep00/23/kissie.jpg\">\r\n'),(64,'<!-- Damn, not my evening.  I had to use paper toilet seat covers.  If I were judging olympic shits and I saw someone execute a perfect .9666 on the porcelin throne, but then they had to use toilet seat covers to dry off, I\'d take away .2 for .7666.  Call me wack, but in order to preserve the art, we must play by the rules.  Gotta use toilet paper.-->\r\n\r\n<P><a href=\"http://elly.org\">Elly</a> just pointed out that <a href=\"http://wallflower.nu\">Camilla</a> is starting to get fleshy on her cam.</P>\r\n\r\n<img src=\"http://wallflower.nu/cam/archive/sep00/shirt.jpg\">\r\n<P>and...</P>\r\n<img src=\"http://wallflower.nu/cam/archive/sep00/bra.jpg\">\r\n\r\n<P>Camilla is the cutest girl on the entire internet.  I don\'t know about this flesh thing.  It definately gets the pole up but is that what we are all out here for?  I am not.  I like the cute stuff.</P>\r\n\r\n<img src=\"http://wallflower.nu/cam/archive/sep00/23/boobies.jpg\">\r\n\r\n<P>I have been using Camilla\'s images on my desktops for a few months and don\'t plan on changing them to some other girl. </P>\r\n\r\n<P>But I have a sense of duty to not be a parasitic entity on this Net.  I have to contribute.  So my question is this:</P>\r\n <blockquote>Do I have to start stripping now?</blockquote>  \r\n<P>Camilla is essentially offering me a challenge. She does not know it. We don\'t know each other.  But we here at Swinney.org function on a honor system.</P>\r\n<img src=\"http://wallflower.nu/cam/archive/sep00/23/panties.jpg\">\r\n<P>And I have to say that Elly\'s brief recollection of the pervs that sent her email back when she used to supply the world with live nudie pics is suggests to me that I should consider stripping on the net as <i>wrong</i> where I will not do it.</P>\r\n<img src=\"http://wallflower.nu/cam/archive/sep00/23/kissie.jpg\">\r\n<P>Everything is about right and wrong, isn\'t it?  Black and white.  Life Noir.  Well, I hope for all our sakes that I find a peaceful resolution to this in my soul.  If I don\'t though, I suppose I am never too old to learn to be sexy for the camera <tt>=-)</tt></P>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n'),(65,'<img src=\'http://swinney.org/art/galleries/yellowpad/20000921cvs.gif\'>\r\n'),(66,'<P>I\'m worried. I still have your blankey.  I think I\'ll go down south at the end of the quarter to deliver it to you. I\'m sorry for the delay.  By the way, there is goin to be a wyclef & de la soul concert in novemeber on campus - if you\'d like to go then come up and you can retrieve your blankey too.</P>\r\n\r\n<p>By the way, you work with CVS? Im the project librarian for my group. I\'ll tell you all the sordid details later...</P>\r\n\r\n<P><i>aus:  dang, I should come up there and get it.  I\'ll email you.'),(67,'<P>Jobs are weird, and I\'m wondering, am I still an artist? Can a \"painter\" who has been known to wet himself in front of a <A HREF=\"http://www.ibiblio.org/wm/paint/auth/vermeer/vermeer.weighing-pearls.jpg\">Vermeer</A>, or cream his pants at even the thought of being in front of a Gerhardt Richter really be fulfilled, sitting in front of 1,310,720 flickering pixels, sculpting Disney-esque characters in three-dimensional CG space?</p>\r\n<CENTER>\r\n<P><IMG SRC=\"http://www.swinney.org/art/galleries/adam/Archer_wire_333x400.gif\"></P>\r\n</CENTER>\r\n<P>I guess it\'s cool to know that my dragon-slaying, maiden-saving, gold plundering little meshes will be manipulated by thousands of kids and college students around the world until their thumbs bleed and they throw their playstation out the window and go buy an XBox.  I\'m more of an artisan now, I guess - maker of marionettes for parents to buy for their kids at christmas time.  OK.  I feel a little better now.</P>\r\n<P>Plus, now I can buy that muscle car I\'ve always wanted.  Gyeeehaw!</P>\r\n\r\n<P><I>aus: and which muscle car would that be? Arnie and I saw a Dodge Charger Superbee the other day on Sunset.  Arnie had to stop and pray.  Me, I want a GTO with hyper suspension.</I></P>\r\n'),(68,'<P>Scribbling bullshit tonight.  My B-day was amazing.  I wish I know all who were there.  I wish I had a guest list:</P>\r\n\r\n<pre>\r\n+ Adam Yeager\r\n   L__> Chachi & Arnie -> Adam Lamas, Stephanie\r\n           |              Christian, Pat \r\n           L__> Moira, Becky, Quincy\r\n\r\n+ Neopets.com ->Adam & Donna\r\n</pre>\r\n\r\n<P>I guess seventeen people then.  DZA couldn\'t believe I managed such a great birthday party after living here in Los Angeles for only 2 months.  I know how.  Adam, Natchachi, Arnie.  Those three have introduced me to more people in the last couple months than I had met in the previous year.</P>\r\n\r\n<p>Natasha keeps introducing me to girls.  It is like being in high school again.  I have friends.  People who can take care of me being cool better than I can.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Bla bla bla, I better stop before I get all sloppy.  I wish I had pictures to show though.  I guess I have Arnie\'s Hawaiian babe card that he gave me.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I have a picture from my birthday last year of me and <a href=\"http://lepard.org\">the B.M.G.</a></P>\r\n<img src=\"http://swinney.org/art/austinchris_lrg.jpg\">\r\n\r\n\r\n'),(69,'<pre>\r\nFrom: Austin Swinney <aswinney@swinney.org>\r\nTo: dad \r\nSubject: Happy Birthday!!!!\r\nDate: Wed, 4 Oct 2000 15:09:07 +0000 (GMT)\r\n\r\nthanks for the persistant attempts to \r\ncontact me on my birthday.  now it is \r\nyour turn!  Happy Birthday!!!  Goldie \r\nand Rose say happy birthday too.  You \r\ncan\'t hear it, but they are thinking \r\nit.  Goldie is thinking it really hard.  \r\nIf she thinks about it any harder, God \r\nwill hear her over the groan of the \r\nUniverse.  I\'m thinking it pretty hard \r\ntoo.\r\n\r\nto another good year!\r\n                    austin@----------&\r\n\r\nFrom: Austin Swinney <aswinney@swinney.org>\r\nTo: dad alvisswinney@hotmail.com, \r\nSubject: Happy Birthday!!!!\r\nDate: Wed, 4 Oct 2000 15:09:07 +0000 (GMT)\r\n\r\nThanks for the Greeting!  I was born 56\r\nyears ago.  I was delivered by a country \r\nDoctor whose office was on the square in \r\nGoldswaite, Texas.  Family lore has it \r\nthat he took me out on the square to show \r\npeople how large I was.  A humble, yet \r\ntheatrical beginning to life.  \r\n\r\nLove Dad.\r\n</pre>\r\n\r\n<P><i>aus: I LOVE MY DAD!!!</i></P>\r\n'),(70,'<pre>\r\nTo      : arnie saiki <ohnie@earthlink.net>\r\nCc      : \r\nAttchmnt: \r\nSubject : Re: DeluxeClambake\r\n----- Message Text -----\r\nOn Thu, 5 Oct 2000, arnie saiki wrote:\r\n</pre>\r\n\r\n<BLOCKQUOTE>Last night\'s deluxe clambake was a real hoe down.  Another nowheresville jam session about the state of American affairs.</BLOCKQUOTE>\r\n\r\n<P>Yes indeed, I was slipping in and out of consciousness.  At one point it ceased to seem like you two were arguing.  I have to admit; I know nothing about American history.  I only know about the toes of American history as they dip into other places in Latin America.</P>\r\n\r\n<BLOCKQUOTE>I feel great.  It\'s 7:30, and it feels like the first day of school-- the quiet morning, the coffee brewing, Christian next door, packing her\r\nlunch.</BLOCKQUOTE>\r\n\r\n<p>I feel like lying in bed all day.  I felt that way yesterday too.  Round about 9 am I think I should get out of bed to be at work by 10.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I wake up, I shower, I drink orange juice, I dress, I leave the house.</p>\r\n                                                                                                  \r\n<p>I walk down Broadway and kick trash on the sidewalk.  I skirt the homeless and the shower less.  The farmer\'s market is open and I buy peaces from the beautiful farmer girls.  Checks get deposited at the Automated Teller\r\nService.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The day closes in on work.  I get to my nice little three-story office building and check my image in the four wall mirrors of the lobby.  Do Ilook good?  I look good enough.  All my punk clothes are dirty and I was stuck with what was left: Gap clothes.  Uhg.  Good thing the fashion army doesn\'t have an outpost at this location or I would be executed.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Elevators make me sick.  Up I go.</p>\r\n\r\n<BLOCKQUOTE>If the weather were any less gray, It wouldn\'t feel like such a productive day.</BLOCKQUOTE>\r\n\r\n<p>If the day were any more forlorn, Instant Messenger wouldn\'t be interrupting me with someone\'s problems trying to get into a server with a desktop shortcut.  As I write this with my AIM now turned off until I get coffee, people are talking about management procedures where by all the\r\nworkers send daily emails of what they have done and what they will do to each other, roughly down a bottle neck of power until it all reaches the bosses desk on the other end of the building in one neat statistics read-out.</p>\r\n                                                       <p>austin@----------&</p>\r\n'),(71,'<blockquote>What\'s up in LA?  How is the weather?</blockquote>\r\n\r\n<P>The weather is very nice.  Today is a kind of dont-get-out-of-bed\r\ndreary.  I like those days.  Too bad I had to get out of bed.  <tt>=-|</tt></P>\r\n\r\n<P>Work is okay.  The NarNars are seriously annoying.  It is like going to\r\nwork for a company that seems really cool and then finding out that it\r\ngets it\'s funding from the CIA.  Then you notice that all the people\r\nwearing suits have little black recievers pluged in their right ear.\r\n</P>\r\n<P>I am working on a new media startup dealing with new fiction and emmerging\r\nfilm makers with a friend of mine.  It is trying to tap into that\r\nHollywood money.  The odds are grossly against it working out, but if it\r\ndoes or even doesn\'t, it may help me get into a smaller working\r\nenvironment somewhere else.\r\n</P><P>\r\nThe people I work with are really great though.  I have no problem with\r\nthem.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI have fallen in with a click.  I am amazed how much LA is like\r\nhighschool.  You leave the house where you are secluded and sheltered and\r\nyou go into the world riding a school bus.  In this case the world is very\r\nmuch Los Angeles.  You quiver for a bit.  You shake.  Somebody sees you\r\nand thinks in the vaguest way that you might be cool.  Then they see that\r\nyou are cool and, like a gangster, you are made.  You have friends.  You\r\nhave enemies.  You have just enough money to live, buy lunch and an ice\r\ncream.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI am leaving after work to points unknown above Los Angels for a weekend\r\nof fishing.  That should be a trip. </P>'),(72,'<blockquote>What\'s up in LA?  How is the weather?</blockquote>\r\n\r\n<P>The weather is very nice.  Today is a kind of dont-get-out-of-bed\r\ndreary.  I like those days.  Too bad I had to get out of bed.  <tt>=-|</tt></P>\r\n\r\n<P>Work is okay.  The NarNars are seriously annoying.  It is like going to\r\nwork for a company that seems really cool and then finding out that it\r\ngets it\'s funding from the CIA.  Then you notice that all the people\r\nwearing suits have little black recievers pluged in their right ear.\r\n</P>\r\n<P>I am working on a new media startup dealing with new fiction and emmerging\r\nfilm makers with a friend of mine.  It is trying to tap into that\r\nHollywood money.  The odds are grossly against it working out, but if it\r\ndoes or even doesn\'t, it may help me get into a smaller working\r\nenvironment somewhere else.\r\n</P><P>\r\nThe people I work with are really great though.  I have no problem with\r\nthem.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI have fallen in with a click.  I am amazed how much LA is like\r\nhighschool.  You leave the house where you are secluded and sheltered and\r\nyou go into the world riding a school bus.  In this case the world is very\r\nmuch Los Angeles.  You quiver for a bit.  You shake.  Somebody sees you\r\nand thinks in the vaguest way that you might be cool.  Then they see that\r\nyou are cool and, like a gangster, you are made.  You have friends.  You\r\nhave enemies.  You have just enough money to live, buy lunch and an ice\r\ncream.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI am leaving after work to points unknown above Los Angels for a weekend\r\nof fishing.  That should be a trip. </P>'),(73,'<P>I turned the heater on today. My fingers are numb. I slept in sweat pants and a sweat shirt, socks too. Damn is it cold here! its not raining today, but it was yesterday. I would take a picture for you, Austin, but I cant get My act together to go buy a $600 digi camera that I <em>really</em> don\'t need. I have become such a house mouse lately, it makes me sick! My social activity for the weekend was going to see \"...And you\'ll know us by the trail of dead.\"</P>\r\n\r\n\r\n<P>I day dreamed about being a rockstar myself, while they were playing. I would of course, dye My hair black, and break a lot of shit on stage to amuse My goth fans.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I met Dusty Bottoms and one of his friends there. I bought whiskey, no coke (graduate). I was sleeping \r\nsoundly Saturday at \'bout 11, when I heard My awful doorbell buzz for about a minute straight. Matt n\' Mike waking me for a little bfast. We went to Night Hawk, \r\nFrisco dinner. You and I never went there, should have tho cause its a gamey dinner. </P>\r\n\r\n<P>So matt told me about a vespa rally going on, perked My interest. I could get any fools to go, jesse or juan. I really wanted to go take pictures of chicks on vespas cause it was raining, and all yucky.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I had dinner with Benwa at stars and talked some shop. I forgot about Matt and I drove down to LD\'s house, and \r\nAudra\'s, no one was there so I went on to Joe\'s Cafe, where the rally was at. </P>\r\n\r\n<P>They were packing up when I got there. I stood in the road taking mad pictures in the rain, as kids were putting vespa\'s in trucks. I turned, facing north on congress and caught a spectacular view of the capitol.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I rushed across the street to a hotel, that has received good reviews for its renovation. I walked into the bar, and was floored by a beautiful woman that I had seen the night previously at Atomic Cafe. She didn\'t have the same reaction as I did. I bought a glass of 5 dollar wine, and talked to her a bit. She was clueless as to why I was there. </P>\r\n\r\n<P>I had My camera, and a lil\' notebook to take notes about exposure settings and all that. She asked if I was staying there at the hotel, I think she thought I was posing as a journalist. I could have talked more to her, but I thought it best to leave the scene before I got silly. I drank My wine, crept out and drove home.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I have watched as many movies as a human can possibly watch on a long weekend.  My brain is mush... I am going to see My girlfriend\'s new movie tonight; \"Dancer in The Dark.\" </P>\r\n\r\n\r\n<P><I>aus: sounds cool and fun. I want to go to that night hawk place.  ...uhg, mondays suck.  Drank last night.</I></P>'),(74,'<P>I was living in a mountainous urban area where I know lots of girls.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nThen I had a bad day at some point and took it out on one girl.  I wrote on my website about her make up and was just generally mean.  An entire community of women in the mountainous urban area polarized against me.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI went to the produce market where she worked.  I was looking for her so that I could apologize, also looking to find out on what I had to apologize for. I insulted the ideals of womanhood in commenting on the many ways her makeup looked bad.  I made a mockery of an institution.  Billions of women all over the world wanted me to die.  Part of me thought it went beyond just makeup to the sins of man.  My position as a representative of mankind on the Internet left me wide open.\r\n</P><P>\r\nOutside the produce market and across the street, a skinny acrobat woman climbed a latter while her assistant, a stout man, held the ladder steady.  She walked a couple goose steps along the top of the building\'s edge.  She did a cartwheel.  She stepped off the edge to her death.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI apologized to the women of the produce market.  Sorry for all the times I did not know what to think.  Sorry for all the times I made judgements from premises that I made up.  Sorry for all the times I said I wanted to have sex and my girlfriend didn\'t.\r\n</P>'),(75,'<P>\r\nHolding hands and wishing well<br> \r\nTo our departing friend,<br>\r\nServed as a beacon for the subject.<br>\r\nLiving leave behind echoes of life<br>\r\nHaunting corners of the mind<br>\r\nYou see it in the darkeness<br>\r\nAgainst candle lit mirrors.<br>\r\nThe dancing of light defined by:<br>\r\nEncroaching nothingness, loneliness,<br>\r\nEnvironment for passing in the night.\r\n</P>'),(76,'<P>I saw this evening, three episodes of death.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>The first was a radio show on National Public Radio.  Every perspective in the Huntsville, Texas, execution process was interviewed: the Warden, the Chaplin, the reporters, the tie down crew.  They referred to the convicted as offenders.  None of them were comfortable with the idea of putting others to death.  They talked at lengh of the various ways that prisoners coped with thier comming execution.  They prayed, sang gospel songs, told lawyer jokes.  One prisoner began singing <i>Silent Night</i> when the Warden took his glasses off, a signal to begin injection.  Most thank the Warden, or appologise.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Later, I watched a cartoon on television adapting the three little pigs into a grotesque raucous of rhyming.  Two gross pigs hide from the Wolf at their botherâ€™s house, a pig that has his life together.  The together pig goes to the market and when he comes back, the wolf has already eaten his brothers.  Police arrive, a pack of wolves, and arrest the remaining pig for the murder of his brothers.  The motive: the gross pigs had drank all their brotherâ€™s beer so he killed them.  The pig is taken before a wolf of a judge and condemned by a jury of wolves, to death by frying pan.  </P>\r\n\r\n<P>Lastly, I saw a movie about a Czechoslovakian immigrant woman who is framed by her landlord for said landlordâ€™s own suicide at her hands.  Yes, he made her do it.  To get her to do it, he stole her money she had saved for her sonâ€™s eye operation that would prevent him from a blind adulthood that she herself suffered.  She killed her landlord to get the money back.  She was convicted in a trial by jury to death by hanging.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>On a normal day like today, I usually see nothing having to do with death or execution.  I do not know why today is different, but I will certainly consider what it means to put people to death when the horror lies in the death of the innocent.  Is it truly just as a society to terminate with uncertainty the lives of hundreds every year when the alternative is a dollar from my paycheck?  Is the responsibility of execution something that we as humans are capable of bearing?  There was a guard at the Huntsville prison where Texas executions take place, who had a nervous breakdown and after participating in over a hundred deaths.  He quit several years ago to continue his life as a carpenter.  He said he could see the eyes of those prisoners who died by lethal injection staring into his.  I would gladly pay a dollar not to ever see those eyes, and so that no one in any legal capacity would ever draw their paycheck from seeing those eyes.</P>'),(77,'<P>I invited one of my L.A. friends to a bar.  He showed up with his girl.  We drank.  Other friends were there.  Afterward, he told me to walk outside with him.  He had a surprise for me.  I knew he is a martial artist.  We work out at the gym together most workdays a week.  We ride the Stairmasters and watch women flexing on the machinery.  We walk outside the bar.  His girl follows us. He puts his arm over my shoulder.</P>\r\n\r\n<blockquote>â€œI said I had a surprise for you.  I didnâ€™t give you anything for your birthday.  This is your present.â€</blockquote>\r\n\r\n<P>He motions for his girl to walk up the alley adjacent the bar.  She walks up the alley under a streetlight.  The street is quiet.  No one is out.  \"Take it off, baby,â€ he says.  She coyly plays with her red leather overcoat.  It covers her to mid thigh.  â€œGo on, take it off,â€ he says.\r\n\r\n<P>I thought he was going to punch me in the stomach when he invited me out here telling me he had a surprise.  I thought maybe he was going to tell me I needed to go to his martial arts classes, like he always tells me.  I canâ€™t afford them.  I want to go though.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>She unbuttons her red coat.  The liner is black.  Her underwear is red: lace bra and thong.  I have never seen a woman dressed so beautifully.  </P>\r\n\r\n<blockquote>â€œYea baby, show him the back.  Turn around and show him the back!â€  </blockquote>\r\n\r\n<P>She drops the jacket into a fold and holds it to her belly and does a runway pivot.  Who am I to have such friends?  I just moved here.  This is fantastic. I believe this is happening.  She puts the coat back on.  I love Los Angeles.</P>\r\n\r\n<blockquote>â€œWhat did I say?  I had a surprise for you.  How did you like that?  Nice.â€</blockquote>\r\n\r\n<p>We say our good byes as much as we can.    I canâ€™t go back in the bar, not back to the boring conversation and idiotic antics.  I open the door.  The two skinny L.A. women are rubbing up against each other in a sexual manner to the sounds of a German bar keyboard playing tempo Rolling Stones songs.  Minutes later I excuse myself and go home.</p>\r\n'),(78,'<P>I invited one of my L.A. friends to a bar.  He showed up with his girl.  We drank.  Other friends were there.  Afterward, he told me to walk outside with him.  He had a surprise for me.  We walk outside the bar.  His girl follows us. He puts his arm over my shoulder.</P>\n<blockquote>\"I said I had a surprise for you.  I didn\'t give you anything for your birthday.  This is your present.</blockquote>\n\n<P>He motions for his girl to walk up the alley adjacent the bar.  She walks up the alley under a streetlight.  The street is quiet.  No one is out.  \"Take it off, baby,\" he says.  She coyly plays with her red leather overcoat.  It covers her to mid thigh.  \"Go on, take it off,\" he says.</P>\n\n<P>She unbuttons her red coat.  The liner is black.  Her underwear is red: lace bra and thong.  I have never seen a woman dressed so beautifully.  </P>\n\n<blockquote>\"Yea baby, show him the back.  Turn around and show him the back!\"  </blockquote>\n\n<P>She drops the jacket into a fold and holds it to her belly and does a runway pivot.  Who am I to have such friends?  I just moved here.  This is fantastic. I believe this is happening.  She puts the coat back on.  I love Los Angeles.</P>\n\n<blockquote>What did I say?  I had a surprise for you.  How did you like that?  Nice.</blockquote>\n\n'),(79,'<P>crap fucking shit.  time to go out drinking.  goddamnit.  off to los feliz.  i snorted some paxil and i\'m ready to have fun!</P>\r\n'),(80,'<P>I went to the famous titty bar that Courtney \r\nLove first shook her money maker at, Jumbo\'s.  It\r\nwas my first titty bar experience.  I can\'t call\r\nit relaxing at all.  I was on edge.  Something about\r\ndrinking in what my pastor would call a den of \r\ndepravity threw my groove off.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>The dancers were not that good, save one.  One \r\nwas really good.  My friend gave her lots of money.\r\nHe liked the large figure that she had.  He has never\r\ndated a girl with a real figure.  Said all he could\r\nget were skinny smoking bitches.  The evil girls.\r\nThe good dancer could ride the pole with amazing \r\nagility. I thought I recognised her from the \r\nOlympics this year.  I think she was on the U.S. \r\ngymnastics team.  Correct me if I am wrong.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I have dated one dancer and been roomates with\r\nanother. The girl I dated wasn\'t messed up at all.\r\nShe was really cool.  She used to put me in the \r\ntrunk of her Hundai and sneek me out to lunch.  \r\nThat was when I was a freshman in highschool, \r\nRockwall, Texas.  She would take me home after school\r\nsometimes too and fall asleep on my bed.  My stepmom\r\nwould come home and I\'d be watching some shitty \r\ntelevision show with my girlfriend asleep on the \r\nbed.  I know she must have been like, \"Oh lordy! He\r\nbrought his girlfriend home when no one was here...\"\r\nBut Yeo, she was just sleeping on the bed and I was\r\njust watching TV.  My parents were probably more \r\nworried that I wasn\'t macking then that there\r\nwere girls in the house without supervision.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>She even stayed the night at my mom\'s house.\r\nWe slept in the TV room.  In the morning, my mom \r\ntold me that it was okay if my <i>friends</i> stayed \r\nover but that we had to sleep in separate rooms.\r\nI remember thinking that girlfriend was so beautiful...\r\nShe had ton\'s of boys that she went out with though.\r\nThat really stood in the way of our relationship. \r\nI\'m not saying that we had a heavy one.  We didn\'t.  \r\nThat was why it was so cool.  She wanted to get\r\nmore serious on several occasions, but I couldn\'t jive,\r\nnot with the other dudes that she dated at the same time.  My\r\nfifteen year-old sense of pride found it hurtful, \r\nnot normal.  She was seventeen at the time.  A good\r\nthree formative years older than me.  What was I \r\nto do? Nothing.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Anyway, that is my review of Jumbo\'s titty bar. \r\nI hope you liked the segue.</P>\r\n'),(81,'<pre>\r\nyou might have said it works like this\r\nnothing but orion and gas colored stars\r\nand i was vanity fair\r\nlike a cashmere suit train\r\non another monday at 9am\r\nsaying\r\nwhere have you been?\r\nstanding left-handed on amsterdam \r\nsaying\r\nwhere have you been?\r\nand sleeping on my rain forest road mumbling\r\nwhere have you been? and what place is this?\r\n\r\npasting that jimmy dean postage stamp to my forehead\r\nand mailing me to acquiescent moons\r\nto winters past and future junes\r\nchocolate-chip minting me to the next lifetime\r\nand standing on star-lit shadows\r\nsquinting\r\ncause it\'s cold and rheumatic\r\nsaying\r\ni know this must be the street\r\nwalking blocks in rubber motion\r\nsaying\r\ni can see you from here\r\nclutching boiled peanut afternoons like candy\r\nsaying\r\ni must have the number wrong\r\nand slipping into Ecstasy\r\nForever\r\n\r\ndouble suns and twice-burnt potato thoughts\r\nshe\'s loves mes\r\nand he loves her...\r\nnot yets\r\nwaiting patiently for the over-eager crevice verses\r\nthe only curses\r\nthe only cures for my strange vampire addiction\r\nand cadillac church love\r\nsaying\r\ni was yours once\r\nin revolving door slide hammer\r\nsaying\r\nTHIS first and THAT next\r\nand now i\'m standing left-handed on amsterdam\r\nsaying\r\nplease god\r\nlet it be you\r\non certain thunderstorm tuesdays\r\nand goodbye ruby\r\n</pre>'),(82,'<P>Boring life this week...</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I am being to hard on myself.  After all, I did go to\r\na titty bar.  But today is Friday. I feel boring.  I am going \r\nout tonight with some friends to a party where I don\'t know\r\nanyone.  Maybe I\'ll take a camera and get some pretty pictures\r\nto look at and make me feel exciting.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I think I\'ll go hot tub jumping at Hollywood hotels.</P.\r\n\r\n<P>Bye.</P>\r\n<center>\r\n<a href = \'http://swinney.org/art/galleries/shitstick/index.htm\'>\r\n<img border=no src=\'http://swinney.org/art/galleries/shitstick/images/la_gloria.gif\'>\r\n</a>\r\n</center>'),(83,'i\'m just admiring your hotrod work here.  this isn\'t a real message.  have a good weekend and all though!'),(84,'<P>I like Leonard.  We passed cars in downtown glendale \r\ntoday and I gave him the finger.  He was ready.  He gave me \r\nthe finger back without delay. He also gave me a copy of his \r\n <a href=\'http://home.earthlink.net/~jfilan/\'>showerhead \r\npress</a> book, Shrimp!.  He is so cool.  I have number 44 of 200.\r\nI want to share a poem from it with the reading audience.</P>\r\n<blockquote>\r\n<h4>Lucubration #6</h4>\r\n\r\n<pre>\r\n\r\n\r\nAs for Hemingway,\r\n\r\nThe sun also rose along\r\n\r\nHis shotgun\'s barrel.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</pre>\r\n\r\n<P>Robert Roden<br>\r\n<a href=\"mailto:aphasiapress@hotmail.com\">aphasiapress@hotmail.com</a><br>\r\n<a href=\"http://www.csulb.edu/~rroden/rodent.html\">http://www.csulb.edu/~rroden/rodent.html</a><br>\r\nOrange, California</P>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n\r\n<P>I think I am going to put up more of these because sometimes\r\nI don\'t feel like sharing what kind of boring day I am having.\r\nMaybe I should start writing about the beauty of nature.</P>\r\n<P>heh, whatever.</P>\r\n'),(85,'<P>Oh, why bother.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I... I... I...</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I just don\'t know what to say about anything anymore.\r\n  It doesn\'t help that I am at S.\'s birthday party, \r\nand there are girls everywhere.  S. has a crush on me.\r\n  I have a mutual crush on the world.  And they are down \r\nstairs watching sex in the city.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Why don\'t I want to go back to my apartment in Glendale?\r\n  I don\'t know what is so bad about it.  Mabye it is all \r\nthe browns.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Enter A.L. asking me what I am doing?  Writing \r\nan email?  Is it all deep and important?  You look it.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Oh well, I guess I\'ll show him how this all works.  \r\nThe site, the submit and everything.</P>'),(86,'<P>I was walking in downtown Glendale today. \r\nOne, two, three passing the wedding dress \r\nshops.  I never wondered where wedding \r\ndresses came from.  I moved to Glendale and found out.\r\nI never \r\nsaw a store to suggest the various styles.  \r\nSometimes in downtown Glendale at night \r\nor early in the morning, when I am walking \r\nto or from work, I feel lonely.  The only \r\nsouls in sight are those of the mannequins\r\nfully dressed in wedding outfits, staring \r\nat cocked angles into oblivion.  I see them \r\nand I always want two things.  One, I want \r\nto be the wedding photographer.  I want \r\na wedding full of mannequins in their correct \r\npositions: perishers, brides maids, grooms \r\nwhatevers, bride, groom, pastor; in the big \r\nwood lined chapel with dark carpet and silk \r\nflowers everywhere.  People with their heads \r\ncocked and staring, frozen in a concentrated \r\nfocus upon the wedding.  Me taking pictures.  \r\nTwo, I want the hair on the groom to be mine.  \r\nI don\'t mean at the wedding.  I mean in real \r\nlife.  I want that stiff and over plump \r\ncoarse brown ken hair, blossoming brown \r\nbeautiful wig.</P>\r\n\r\n'),(87,'<P>I am kind of upset. I don\'t like saying that, but I am. And it\'s not because I just sat in traffic for 2 hours and I had to take a dump. No. It\'s because of the Elrons. They\'ve taken their masks off and I see their ugly faces.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Today it finally sunk in. They were my friends for a whole week and now they don\'t even look at me. For example, this evening I said, \"Hey Lou, how\'s it going?\" And Lou didn\'t even look at me. So you know what I did? I said it again. \"Hey Lou...what\'s going on?\" He looked at me. But guess what? He didn\'t even say \"hi\" or \"can I help you?\" or \"who the hell are you?\" He just looked at me and my jeans that I wear to work at least 3 days a week. So I said, \"Hey Lou, weird weather we\'re having, huh?\" I figured he might be shy and discussing the weather is the ultimate ice breaker. He said nothing. Whatever.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>So I get on the steps to go home and Lou opens the door for me. I go in, then hold the door for him. He doesn\'t even say thanks. Okay, I\'ll let that one go. We walk down the stairs and I try talking to him again. Nothing. I say, while pointing to a pile of trash by the stairs, \"Hey, it\'s my lunch.\" Lou lets out a nervous laugh. \"Going home?\" I ask. \"Yep,\" he said. Score. I got Lou to talk to me for the first time in 5 weeks. I was sure he forgot me. But how could he? We were best friends for the first week. He kept telling me that he has a son named Leonard. </P>\r\n\r\n<P>Well, we exited the building and he said good-bye but I wasn\'t ready to leave him. So I followed him. He got nervous and sped up. I walked faster. He turned around and said, \"I\'m parked in the structure.\" Shit. That did it. You know what I said? Nothing.  He didn\'t even make eye contact or shake my hand? Or hug? No. Or wink? Or kiss? Or nod? Nothing.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I used to have another best friend, too, but I\'m still waiting for her to come around and talk to me again. Maybe she\'ll wave to me tomorrow. Maybe. I just might forgive her. As for Lou, well, let\'s just say I\'m not babysitting his kid.</P>\r\n\r\n '),(88,'<P>\r\nThe keyword for this entry is nothing.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nNothing is very zen.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nDo nothing.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nWalk nowhere.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nSit.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nMeditation to do nothing.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nWorking for nothing.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nProducing no product.\r\n</P><P>\r\nThinking no conclusions.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nArgueing no point.\r\n  </P><P>\r\nHelping for no cause.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nTaking you shoes off where they used to be on so that when you stand you feel the blades of grass beneath your feet.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nProgramming without any goal.\r\n</P><P>\r\nWhen you rub your feet because they hurt, that is not meditation.\r\n</P><P>\r\nWhen you program too long to make yourself learn, that is not meditation.\r\n</P><P>\r\nWhen you sit crosslegged until your butt hurts, and say that you meditated for longer than ever before, that is not meditation.\r\n</P><P>\r\nMeditation is sitting and being aware of everything around you that you affect.\r\n</P><P>\r\nMeditation is watching the wakes that people cut through the gathering eternity.\r\n</P><P>\r\nMeditation is not pointless, even though I might want to say it is.\r\n</P><P>\r\nMeditation is stillness of mind to the joy of movement?\r\n</P><P><STRONG>\r\nI am going to drink in a non social environment, and it will be zen.\r\n</STRONG></P>'),(89,'<P>\r\nIn the office building where I work there is one urinal and one toilet in\r\nthe men\'s room.  Both have automatic flush sensors.  This is not an issue\r\nwith the urinal.  But if you pee in the toilet, and you didn\'t hunch to do\r\nit, the toilet won\'t flush.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nSo I had to pee really bad and somebody was manning the urinal when I got\r\nin there.  I decided to break the conventions of politeness and pee in the\r\ntoilet knowing full well that the next guy to drop the kids off at the\r\npool would be forced to do it on my territory.  Nothing is worse that\r\ncrapping on top of pee.  This goes doubly if the pee isn\'t yours.  Anyone\r\nwho has gone number two in an outhouse and got splashed knows what I am\r\ntalking about to the worst degree.  I\'ve had the worst happen to me\r\nbefore.  So, as part of an unspoken treaty with the world, I don\'t like to\r\nleave the toilet marked.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nLike I said though, with the sensors, there is no other option.  Okay, so\r\nyou could sit like a girl on the pot.  No way!  I am man.  I stand.  For\r\nevery time I have argued with my female house mates, or my mom, or my\r\nsisters about the right of man to leave the toilet seat up, I WILL NOT\r\nSIT AND PEE!  So I peed standing and the toilet didn\'t flush.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI then quickly exited the scene of the crime.  I didn\'t want to be caught\r\ncoming out of the stall having left my mark by the next man in line to do\r\nwhat the stall was intended fore;  finding a peepot would piss anyone\r\noff.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nI fled the scene of the crime and got off.  But two hours later, guess\r\nwhat?  I had to poo.  And, you know what?  my pee was still in the\r\npot.  I had to poo on my own cold pee water.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI got what I deserved:  a splash in the ass.</P>'),(90,'<p><strong>DJ Krush plays on my winamp</strong></p>\r\nan empty half pint of ben&jerry\'s sits on my desk<br>\r\nmy throat is parched from smoking winstons and drinking the beer from next door<br>\r\nmy inbox is empty<br>\r\nI have no desire to sleep<br>\r\n<pre>\r\n<strong>timestamp</strong>:0205:04;10262000\r\n</pre>\r\nSwinndog is going to host my Thanksgiving Holiday. He mentioned TJ<br>\r\nTuesday, I noticed that mushrooms are growing at my office<br>\r\nI have no personality<br>\r\nmy exgirlfriend pains me<br>\r\nmy housemate doesn\'t live here, but she cleans the kitchen anyway<br>\r\nI will be working in six hours<br>\r\nmy inbox will remain empty<br>\r\nI want a hug, i need a hug<br>\r\nI am negative<br>\r\nA friend belittled me yesterday, I am hurt by that<br>\r\nI couldn\'t get the scrowly mouse to work in linux, so installed windows, now i scroll<br>\r\nI think about girls, all day long<br>\r\nI have been to the store three times this week, still I forget to get the tortillas</p>\r\n<p><strong>DJ Krush plays on...</strong></p>\r\n<pre><a href=\"http://lepard.org\">B=>m<=G</a></pre>'),(91,'\"...and then he proceeded to reduce the number of cats to \r\nzero.\" -- overheard in the midst of a conversation about \r\nthis guy who was engaged in this little war with the \r\nneighbor lesbians.  see, he had this pit bull and the \r\ngirls had all these cats- maybe 10 or more; (all living, \r\nat this point)-- clearly the pit bull would kill one and \r\ndid.  so the girl owners freaked and yelled and then he \r\nyelled  and on and on until the girls upped the stakes \r\nand carved- \"EAT MY FUCK!\" with a nail into the paint \r\non the back of his car.  it was at that point that he \r\nloaded his 30 aught 6 and proceeded to reduce the number \r\nof cats to ZERO.    '),(92,'<P>I don\'t think I am going to do anything\r\nexciting this weekend.  I went to get sushi \r\nlast night with Leonard and although he paid \r\nfor it, I would exceeded my quota of indulgement \r\nfor the week if I did anything else.  I also saw\r\nDrunken Master 2 with Adamajah last night.  I would\r\nlike to just have a night of hacking on the \r\nswinnicle engine.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>When does Arnold get back?  I miss the hell out\r\nof him.  I think he gets back from Equador this \r\nweekend or something.  He doesn\'t have very many\r\ndays left in the month to arrive back.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>In other news, I haven\'t had a soundcard in my \r\ncomputer for a couple weeks now.  I am talking\r\nabout my work computer.  I used to have two computers\r\nat work and that made me special.  But then they\r\ntried to take my devserver, which is linux, and give\r\nit to a new employee and I didn\'t want them too.\r\nI let them have the dell.  The dell had a soundcard.\r\nThe devserver doesn\'t.  So i don\'t have a any music \r\nto listen to.  I used to listen to music all day\r\nlong at work.  I didn\'t really fret over the loss\r\nof that because I was happy to keep the devserver.\r\nOccasionally I can plug into Mr. SNAFU\'s speakers\r\nin the cube next to mine and listen to all the music I \r\nbacked up onto his porn partition.  That is what I \r\ndid today.  The experience is pleasant.  I listened\r\nto Modest Mouse, one of the many bands that I only\r\nhave on MP3.  I don\'t get to listen to them when\r\nI am at home.  Life was good in that respect.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I wonder if my kids are going to read this and\r\nlaugh that I used to listen to folkypunkyemo music?\r\nThey will probably be listening to the Fucking Cunt\r\nAll-Stars.  This will be years from now when pop music\r\ngoes through it\'s heavymetal/rap/punk fusion period\r\nand comes out with rhyming off beat loud and crappy,\r\nfuzzed up, cursing, hell music.\r\nThey will laugh that I was a hippy, not\r\nknowing that hippies were about 35 years before my time.\r\nKids...  they don\'t know anything.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>What the hell am I doing tonight?  Grilla wants me\r\nto go to kung-fu.  Should I pay the 80 bucks and go?\r\nAt least I would have something to do until 9 pm and then\r\nI could go and drink with him.</P>\r\n\r\n<H1>FUCK IT, Y<SUB>E</SUB><SUP>O</SUP>!  You only live once.  What is 80 Bucks\r\na month?</H1>\r\n\r\n<P>After all, I had much of fun the other night and they seem\r\nlike nice people.  I really want to do it too.</P>'),(93,'<FONT COLOR=\"#000000\"><FONT ABSZ=12 SIZE=3><BR><B><FONT FACE=\"Geneva\" FAMILY=SANSSERIF>You have just entered room Rboredasssaterdaymorning.SiamtheBMG has entered the room.</B><FONT COLOR=\"#0000FF\"><FONT ABSZ=10 SIZE=2><BR><B>iamtheBMG:</B><FONT COLOR=\"#000000\"><FONT ABSZ=12 SIZE=3>sup fewl<FONT COLOR=\"#FF0000\"><FONT ABSZ=10 SIZE=2><BR><B>robotec9:</B><FONT COLOR=\"#000000\"><FONT ABSZ=12 SIZE=3>fuck, we are a bunch of lameasses<FONT COLOR=\"#FF0000\"><FONT ABSZ=10 SIZE=2><BR><B>robotec9:</B><FONT COLOR=\"#000000\"><FONT ABSZ=12 SIZE=3>you are two hours ahead of me<FONT COLOR=\"#0000FF\"><FONT ABSZ=10 SIZE=2><BR><B>iamtheBMG:</B><FONT COLOR=\"#000000\"><FONT ABSZ=12 SIZE=3>yah - yah - no argue here<FONT COLOR=\"#FF0000\"><FONT ABSZ=10 SIZE=2><BR><B>robotec9:</B><FONT COLOR=\"#000000\"><FONT ABSZ=12 SIZE=3>i\'m looking for titty action on the webcams<FONT COLOR=\"#0000FF\"><FONT ABSZ=10 SIZE=2><BR><B>iamtheBMG:</B><FONT COLOR=\"#000000\"><FONT ABSZ=12 SIZE=3>i went to atmosphere with ryan tonigh<FONT COLOR=\"#0000FF\"><FONT ABSZ=10 SIZE=2><BR><B>iamtheBMG:</B><FONT COLOR=\"#000000\"><FONT ABSZ=12 SIZE=3>send link<FONT COLOR=\"#FF0000\"><FONT ABSZ=10 SIZE=2><BR><B>robotec9:</B><FONT COLOR=\"#000000\"><FONT ABSZ=12 SIZE=3>stile<FONT COLOR=\"#FF0000\"><FONT ABSZ=10 SIZE=2><BR><B>robotec9:</B><FONT COLOR=\"#000000\"><FONT ABSZ=12 SIZE=3>and listnenin