y<FONT COLOR=\"#FF0000\"><FONT ABSZ=10 SIZE=2><BR><B>robotec9:</B><FONT COLOR=\"#000000\"><FONT ABSZ=12 SIZE=3>no shit? me too<FONT COLOR=\"#0000FF\"><FONT ABSZ=10 SIZE=2><BR><B>iamtheBMG:</B><FONT COLOR=\"#000000\"><FONT ABSZ=12 SIZE=3>i am drunk and stone... and i been up alll day<FONT COLOR=\"#FF0000\"><FONT ABSZ=10 SIZE=2><BR><B>robotec9:</B><FONT COLOR=\"#000000\"><BR><B>iamtheBMG:</B><FONT COLOR=\"#000000\"><FONT ABSZ=12 SIZE=3>me too<FONT COLOR=\"#FF0000\"><FONT ABSZ=10 SIZE=2><BR><B>robotec9:</B><FONT COLOR=\"#000000\"><FONT ABSZ=12 SIZE=3>i should go home<FONT COLOR=\"#0000FF\"><FONT ABSZ=10 SIZE=2><BR><B>iamtheBMG:</B><FONT COLOR=\"#000000\"><FONT ABSZ=12 SIZE=3>rupa<FONT COLOR=\"#0000FF\"><FONT ABSZ=10 SIZE=2><BR><B>iamtheBMG:</B><FONT COLOR=\"#000000\"><FONT ABSZ=12 SIZE=3>the dr<FONT COLOR=\"#0000FF\"><FONT ABSZ=10 SIZE=2><BR><B>iamtheBMG:</B><FONT COLOR=\"#000000\"><FONT ABSZ=12 SIZE=3>get this<FONT COLOR=\"#FF0000\"><FONT ABSZ=10 SIZE=2><BR><B>robotec9:</B><FONT COLOR=\"#000000\"><FONT ABSZ=12 SIZE=3>is she sending me a effin wedding invitation<FONT ABSZ=10 SIZE=2><BR><B>iamtheBMG:</B><FONT COLOR=\"#000000\"><FONT ABSZ=12 SIZE=3>mrs iis crazy<FONT COLOR=\"#0000FF\"><FONT ABSZ=10 SIZE=2><BR><B>iamtheBMG:</B><FONT COLOR=\"#000000\"><FONT ABSZ=12 SIZE=3>MRS<FONT COLOR=\"#FF0000\"><FONT ABSZ=10 SIZE=2><BR><B>robotec9:</B><FONT COLOR=\"#000000\"><FONT ABSZ=12 SIZE=3>she got that, \"i\'m 24 and need to get married\" craze<FONT COLOR=\"#0000FF\"><FO2><BR><B>robotec9:</B><FONT COLOR=\"#000000\"><FONT ABSZ=12 SIZE=3>crazed parents in their twenties.<FONT COLO<FONT COLOR=\"#FF0000\"><FONT ABSZ=10 SIZE=2><BR><B>robotec9:</B><FONT COLOR=\"#000000\"><FONT ABSZ=12 SIZE=3>ok<FONT COLOR=\"#FF0000\"><FONT ABSZ=10 SIZE=2><BR><B>robotec9:</B><FONT COLOR=\"#000000\"><FONT ABSZ=12 SIZE=3>sleep it off<FONT COLOR=\"#FF0000\"><FONT ABSZ=10 SIZE=2><BR><B>robotec9:</B><FONT COLOR=\"#000000\"><FONT ABSZ=12 SIZE=3>later<FONT COLOR=\"#0000FF\"><FONT ABSZ=10 SIZE=2><BR><B>iamtheBMG:</B><FONT COLOR=\"#000000\"><FONT ABSZ=12 SIZE=3>uhhhuh<BR><B>iamtheBMG has left the room.</B>\n\n\n\n'),(94,'<P>i am perversely drawn into avoiding tourism by sitting in\r\nthis papaya.net cafe drinking espresso con leches and\r\nimbibing in your LA life.  Once again, I would be out\r\nexploring Quito if I had more disposable cameras and a\r\nwalkman.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>The internet is the worst thing to happen to the cafe/bar.\r\nI swear I used to meet people sitting at Les Amis, Orlin\r\nand Mogador, The Pink Pony and Max Fish.  Now I meet\r\nimaginary women flashing Austin in the late night, and\r\nevery now and then I find references of myself.  Where one\r\nmight find anxiety or distress in a mirror, I find comfort\r\nas in a chaise lounge:  i like plush furniture.  </P>'),(95,'<P>So I ran into this old friend of mine outside the Rumpus Room in Hollywood.  Well, not a friend really.  More like an annoying person I have known for a long time.  We all have them.  People that were never in the cool section of our address books: the first few pages that fall out first.  No, Just some guy that I went to school with a long time ago.  A long long time ago.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I see him and he looks the same.  Same thin frame.  Same faded blue jeans with holes in the knees.  Same white pony high tops with a generic red swish.  Same long hair, maybe a little thinner.  Same drawling blend of surf and Budweiser.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I think, jeezus, look what fell into the cracks of time.  It is Boedrick.  \"Boedrick, my man.  What is up, yeo?\"  \r\n\r\n<blockquote>\"Hey bra, what\'s up?  I haven\'t seen you in like--for ever, Man!</blockquote>\r\n\r\n<P>\"Yea, it has been a long time.\"</P>\r\n\r\n<blockquote>\"Maaaaaaaaahn,  So what\'s going down?!\"</blockquote>\r\n\r\n<P>\"Not your style, obviously.  So Boedrick, why do you have the same hair cut?\"</P>\r\n\r\n<P>And the answer was a simple one that I think we all understand:</P>\r\n\r\n<blockquote>\"It get\'s me laid, it gets me paid!\" </blockquote>\r\n\r\n<P>Enough said.</P>'),(96,'<P>sitting around.  adam is talking about the movies he will make.  darrell is talking about how to make them.  chris, donna, and athena are admiring the british keyboard.  chrissnafu is drunk.  athena is making spike comparisons.  austin is talking with british friend dave about WAP and XML.   nine inch nails. pulp.  radiohead.  yahoo\'s on computers at a party.  aiming, drinking, talking industry.  \"industry wave pushing you forward.\" </P>\r\n\r\n<P>darrel says to british dave:  art from head to hand.  you got an idea to do that and you created it.  it meets criteria.  in londo0n, salvadore dali, those colors you can\'t fit in a book.  look and that is art.  modern art in books you look past the colors.  in life, the intensity brings you in, you look at it on your own.  hang it on your wall and you have functions of alter peices and nooks in your house and you have what people meditate on.  it is what people really focused on apart from the cathedral.  the contemplative nature.  somebody like mark rothko, [][][] on top of each other.  blue.  art is like music, there is alway more band and more components, as much as you get into it there is always more.  something that cought my eye, backgrounds and backstyles at the elections, a glass clear table glowing modern art perfectly painted.  nobody fell out of bed and started crating these cubist works.  \r\n\r\n</P><P>\r\nthey lights go out and it doesn\'t glow.  chris has become incandescent with liqour.</P>\r\n\r\n<P> when you juxtapose the yeo and thye yeo bye bye bye </P>\r\n'),(97,'<p>ivy, oh ivy.</p>\r\n<p>i went to a costume party tonight, and I didn\'t dress up. This woman, Ivy, that i met a year ago next weekend - told me that she had a crush on me. Wow, what an angel that little Ivy is. She is also married. Damn, too late.</p>\r\n<p>A work friend hooked me up on a blind date. More news to come. The only thing I know is that I will be her birthday present. I am happy to know that I am worthy enough to be packaged up for someones birthday! Any other single ladies need a birthday present! It\'s been a while since I have been interested in anyone. We will see where this goes.</p>\r\n<p>I practice my recon skills tonight. You see, my former housemate (mr. swinney himself) moved out a few months ago, leaving behind a matress. So, i moved it out to the front porch, where it has stayed since he has left. That matress has been through it all, rainy days, hot days, and cold days. Soaking up every bit of grime it could absorb. Tonight I had had enough of that eye-sore. So, in my drunken stupor, I hoisted it up on top of my jetty (yah thats right, just like the comercial). I then drove to the nearest dumpster, (which for legal sakes i wont tell you where) and I tossed aside for someone else to take care of. Now I am feeling like shit for dumping my trash on someone else. I guess my karma will pay.</p>\r\n<br>\r\n<p>bad karma</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<P>aus: HAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHA!!!!!!!!</P>'),(98,'<h3>what eighty dollars buys.</h3>\r\n<P>$25 to leave the country\r\n<br>$16 for two nights in quito at the hostal vagabundo\r\n<br> $1 for every hour on the internet\r\n<br> $1 for breakfast at the hostal\r\n<br> $2 for breakfast anywhere else\r\n<br> $1 for several espresso con leches\r\n<br> $8 for my fly alpaca sweater I bought from a street vendor\r\n<br> $2 for the hat that I will wear every night from Nov-March\r\n<br> $33 dollars for a one way flight from loja to quito\r\n<br> $58 dollars if you4re stupid and book your flight too late\r\n<br> $4 for a cab from the airport to hostal vagabundo at night\r\n<br> $1 for a cab from hostal vagabundo to airport on sunday</P> \r\n<h3>morning</h3>\r\n<P> $.06 for an egg.\r\n<br> $.12 for bottled water.\r\n<br> $30 for a nice rug I almost bought Christian\r\n<br> $150 for the same rug I saw in a turisto shop\r\n<br> $12 for a sexy little italian luggage lock in Quito\r\n<br> $8 for the same lock Natasha will buy Arnie in Loja\r\n<br> $2 an hour it costs for me to live in LA (not including food)\r\n<br> $1 an hour if I split the rent & utilities with natasha\r\n<br> $.08 the cost of this list at the treehouse cafe</P>'),(99,'<P>The plane was delayed an hour.  We waited an hour and then they told us the passengers would not actually be exiting the terminal, but would be bussed over to an inspection area.  \"The inspection area is outside, to your right and the next building.\"  So there we went.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>We stayed there for another hour, in the next building. I stood wedged in the glass cylinders with revolving doors.  shook...shook...shook...shook... that\'s right, push the door. shook...shook...shook...  At some point I got a headache and decided to go look for Arnold outside.  I came back and Maxima was making a scene.  Yes, an approaching <a href=\"http://www.ronjeremy.com\" target=\"new\">movie star</a>.  This was my first movie star sighting, ever.  I would say it went well.  He looked tired from the flight from Honolulu.  I didn\'t shake his hand or ask for an autograph.  If he had looked happy, maybe....</P>\r\n\r\n<P>We found Arnold about an hour later in another building.  We walked back to the car while he told us about his stay in Ecuador.  I was feeling drained now, about 12:30am.  I wanted to go home.  My day had consisted of sitting in front of a computer chatting on aim and writing a script for a mailing list.  I drank a lot of coffee.  I did not at any point want to talk to anyone.  I wanted to be in my little computer coma and smile softly and talk not.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Leaving the airport, there was some confusion over the parking stub that ended in my *screaming* at Maxima.  That is right, I screamed at her.  SCREAMED.  Something like \'fuck off\'.  Arnold thought I was joking.  I wasn\'t.  Maxima decided to retaliate by with holding directions on how to get out of the airport.  Arnold talked more about Ecuador.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>We made it back to Los Angeles in a round about way without any help from the Navigator.  Once in downtown, we stopped at a late night Korean food stop.  The doors were locked.  You had to ring the doorbell.  The waitress would then verify that you are A) Korean or B) not a vagrant.  We were a bunch of B\'s.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>The food was all either hot or cold, or both.  Hot<>Cold/Spicy<>Cold.  It was all really good and served in stone bowls and metal cups.  Everything was really stylized.  There were 3-D renderings of humpty-dumpty eggs sitting on soup bowls.  You crack the egg in your soup which is served boiling. The egg cooks in the soup.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Arnold said it was a great place to take a girl on the first date.  I thought so at first because of the pace\'s style.  I\'d be proud to know that it exists.  But later I found out what that place really had in store.  My ass became the bowls of hell, a billow of fiery gas exploding at 5 minute intervals.  I thought this would truly be a fun place to take a girl on the first date.  I had a girl friend that farted after she ate once.  I thought it was funny.  She would play it off.  After eating at that place, there would be no hiding it.  You would drive home in the car blowing ass and believe me they would be stank.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I dropped Arnold and Maxima off at Alexandria-st and went home.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Note to self:  next time, wait for the passenger to call from the airport.</P>'),(100,'<PRE>\r\nthai food might as well\r\nbe called un-thai food\r\nbecause i\'m all loosened up\r\n\r\ni don\'t like it\r\n</PRE>'),(101,'<P>I woke up and the word \'Alone\'  was embedded in every strand of hair on me. I decided to live life like a movie, as Andy Warhol suggested. My mind and my body are still working on the budget.\r\n</P><P>Art as religion is the thesis I tried to live as a juvenile. I want to be caught in an epidemic of creativity. My body oozes text. It spells diskonektion. I demand to break Anxiety. Nothing left but to stop and direct my life away from Love and panic.\r\n</P>'),(102,'<P>\r\nToday is the office Halloween party.  I\'ve come dressed up as an electrical engineer, which means I wore my normal clothes but with socks that don\'t match.\r\n\r\nSwinney is supposed to dress up as an alien to poke fun at the NarNars.  He\'s been worried about that, but felt better when he found out that the cute email girl is supposed to dress up as an Alien Princess.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI wonder if I should call and let him know that he heard wrong -- that she\'s dressing up as an *Indian* Princess.\r\n</P><P>\r\nBut maybe it\'s best not to feed the paranoia.  Surely they aren\'t as vindictive as we fear.\r\n</P><P>\r\n*gulp*\r\n</P>'),(103,'<P>I was talking to Arnold after work.  We went out to Home Depot to get supplies so he could paint his ex-roomate off the walls.\r\n</P><P>\r\nWe talked.  While we were talking, I was listening to Nirvana, that album with all the fetuses on it, that song about wanting to be sad.  Also the one about appologies.\r\n</P><P>\r\nSo now I am at home listening to that song.  Why does my apartment smell so bad?  It smells like thirty years of odor.  I need to get incense that activates five minutes before I walk in the door.  That is the moment I notice the smell, when I walk in the door.  Shortly there after it goes away.  I think it is still here though,  \'looks both ways over the shoulder suspiciously, like someone is watching.\' sniff, sniff.  Nasty Glendale.  I wish I could paint the smell away.\r\n</P><P>\r\nIs this what I am coming to?  My next place will be a white walled insane asylum for middle class white collar workers.  \'Shhh,\' quiet the voices that say you are not working hard enough.\r\n</P><P>\r\nExit music.</P>'),(104,'<P>I woke up hella cold.  Somebody needs to turn on \r\nmy heater and that somebody is me.  The Ice Princess \r\nhas been sucking on my toes at night, tickling \r\nme.  It wakes me up and I can\'t go back to sleep.  \r\nSo, I run to the shower and get it all hot and \r\njump in.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Yawn. Now I have coffee and am okay.</P>'),(105,'<P>Robert moved to L. A.<br>			\r\nWeather was great.<br>	\r\nYes it was really good,<br>			\r\nSo was the Wood<br>				\r\nBefore you know\'d know it<br>		\r\nDevil may knew it,<br>\r\nhe\'s gay.</P>				\r\n\r\n<P>Hanging out in bars<br>\r\nIn Hollywood, like Mars,<br>\r\nRobbie found his first match.<br>\r\nOff like a light<br>\r\nWent sexual plight<br>\r\nRocks, socks, and stars.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Gaydom lead to drugs,<br>\r\nHush hush under the rugs,<br>\r\nThere he found his disease.<br>\r\nA spike, a bloke, a vile of coke...<br>\r\nNow he is down on the freeze.</P>'),(106,'<P>Oh, oh, oh, I\'m just tired and at work on a thursday that feels\r\nlike a monday.  It might as well be over.  Friday doesn\'t exist at\r\nthis point.  All of the days have run together.  I always am on the\r\ncomputer and I never go home for long unless to sleep.  It doesn\'t\r\nmatter if the day is tuesday or sunday.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Today is something new.  I am going to review the extraordinary email that I\r\nreceived this week.\r\n\r\n<P>I got an email from Fiona Maazel.  It seems I made it onto her\r\npolitical mail-out list and that she wants her acquaintances to vote for\r\nVice President Gore.  It was also a reminder to vote in general.  Yes,\r\nthe vote is next week.  I can believe it is next week, too.  This is\r\nAmerica, we have the opportunity to vote often.  Not on everything.\r\nWe do vote on people to vote on everything though.  And contrary to\r\nmedia involvement, have more than two choices for president.  I was\r\nlooking at the front of a copy of TIME magazine at Ralph\'s supermarket\r\nthe other night while on a beer run.  The cover says, \"The Choice,\"\r\nand there are pictures of Governor Bush on the left side and Vice\r\nPresident Gore on the right.  Well.  I am feeling less and less\r\ncompelled to vote for either one.  Yea, sure splitting with a third\r\nparty candidate is bad, BUT I think Nader has it going on in some\r\nways.  Hell, Gore does, and so does Bush.  Can we have a Cyborg for\r\npresident?  I\'ll vote for the one that funds artificial intelligence.\r\nI want it programmed with environmental consciousness, individual\r\nliberty protection where it does not hurt others, and corporate\r\nregulation.  MISTER PRESIDENT FOR 2004!</P>\r\n\r\n\r\n<P>Or better yet, I have mentioned lately that I plan on moving to\r\nSerbia when I am ready to retire.  They have something like three head\r\ngovernors don\'t they?  Now that is what I am talking about.  I have\r\nbeen to Serbia and it is beautiful.  Green, rugged, bombed.  I think\r\nI\'ll cut out of here when I am 40.  That is a good age for\r\nre-invention.  Hi, my name is AUXVIANEV.</P>  \r\n\r\n<P align=\'right\'>What else did I get?</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Well, I got an email from Elly.  Okay, I exchanged several.  There\r\nwas one that stood out because she said, <a\r\nhref=\'http://www.elly.org/passion/00/10/31/\'>\"haha. you are cool.\"</a>\r\nThat made me happy for about one and a half hours.  I put the email in\r\nmy fan mail folder where email goes when it is nice to me.  Those are\r\nmy emails for depressing days when I need people to tell me or I need\r\njustification that I am: cool.  Nice emails are a beautiful thing.  So\r\nunsolicited.  So permanent.  And coming from elly, is like getting\r\nemail from the cool person in high-school.  Also, I like helping people\r\nand I helped her A) use a my favorite editor Emacs and B) laugh.</P>\r\n\r\n<P align=\'right\'>What <i>else</i> did I get?</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I got an email from <a href=\'http://pamie.com\'>Pamie</a>.  It was\r\nkind of funny because I read in her journal that she left Austin for\r\nLos Angeles.  I thought I\'d send her a welcome to L.A. email that she\r\nwould get when she got to the City.  Assuming she would not check her\r\nemail on the road.  \r\n\r\n<pre>\r\nDate: Thu, 02 Nov 2000 14:03:34 -0600\r\nFrom: pamie, pamie@pamie.com\r\nTo: Austin Swinney, aswinney@swinney.org\r\nSubject: Re: WeLcOmE To LoS AnGeLeS!!!!\r\n\r\nHey you.\r\n\r\nthanks.\r\n\r\nwhen we doin\' lunch?\r\n\r\n-p\r\n\r\n\r\nAustin Swinney wrote:\r\n> \r\n> WeLcOmE To LoS AnGeLeS!!!!\r\n> WeLcOmE To LoS AnGeLeS!!!!\r\n> WeLcOmE To LoS AnGeLeS!!!!\r\n> WeLcOmE To LoS AnGeLeS!!!!\r\n> WeLcOmE To LoS AnGeLeS!!!!\r\n> WeLcOmE To LoS AnGeLeS!!!!\r\n</pre>\r\n\r\n<P>Doing lunch is the big joke here.  When I moved here <a\r\nhref=\'http://www.rosamundi.com\'>Viv</a> said the same thing to me.  We\r\nnever did lunch though.  I think it might actually happen with Pamie.\r\nI\'d like to know her.  I am kind of hoping there is one of those\r\njournal parties that happened in L.A. last year.  I\'d like to meet all\r\nthese people, <a href=\'http://shelleyness.com\'>Shelley</a> too.</P>\r\n\r\n<P align=\'right\'>What <i>else else</i> did I get?</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I got a wedding invitation from a friend that I used to work with\r\nat ibooks.com.  Well, we never actually worked together.  But I liked\r\nher.  And she tried to get me into quality assurance, which was her\r\nteam.  I am eternally grateful for her trying, twice.  It didn\'t happen\r\nthough and I quit ibooks and left Austin shortly there after.   I\r\nthink it was for the better.  I really like my job as a programmer and\r\nI like Los Angeles and all the new friends I have made.  Anyway, I\r\ntraded emails with her a while back and she didn\'t have any serious\r\nmen around she said, but look who is getting hitched!</P>\r\n\r\n<P align=\'center\'>Thanks for reading.</P>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n'),(107,'<P>i\'m drinking a cold, refreshing, coca cola. coke: america\'s favorite beverage, and the world\'s most recognized brand. whenever i hang out with my friend jim we talk about that.\r\n</P><P>\r\ni just put in a phone call to my friend joanna, because i decided randomly that olivia should see austin while she\'s visiting the USA in november.\r\n</P><P>\r\ni listen to a lot of indie rock. i can\'t think about anything but indie rock. i blame this on jeremy crown. i wish i was different than other people but i\'m not.\r\n</P><P>\r\nmy zits itch.\r\n</P><P>\r\nlife is fun.\r\n</P>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n'),(108,'its 4:30 on Friday and I\'m at work....aarrgh,the last half hour is always the worst.I\'m supposed to be in a day of the dead parade,its a Capoeira related thing.keep on keepin on dude!\r\n                             best,\r\n                             Mike'),(109,'<P align=\'center\'><font color=\'red\' size=7>it\'s Friday!</font></P>\r\n<P>...And I am having a dull sugar crash afternoon where everything I touch\r\nturns to chaos.  I just got back from the mall, that fountain of\r\nyouth.  It did not raise my spirits, although a found a national store\r\nchain responsible for popularizing the black clothed barbie look\r\nhaving a sale on silver puffy jackets.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I am all about silver, red, blue, black and military green.  Fuck-it,\r\nI like lots of colors, but there are some that I despise like teal,\r\naqua, anything pastel.  This silver jacket would go great with my\r\nsilver belt, silver satchel bag, red sneakers, red sweat shirt, and\r\nblack wranglers.  YEO!  <tt>=-)</tt>  I am talking about style here.  </P>\r\n\r\n<P>They also had a jean jacket, but I am not paying anyone more than five\r\ndollars for one of those and if I had my druthers, I\'d just pick one\r\nup off the bar floor when the crowds leave.  Drunk people start\r\nshedding you know.  Jean jackets are popular.  It is only a matter of\r\ntime before one gets left behind.  All my favorite clothes used to be\r\nsomebody else\'s favorite article.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>But back to the silver coat.  I would probably only get the vest.\r\nThere was a vest version.  It cost half as much and it is already\r\nNovember here in Los Angeles.  Bring a sweatshirt, but it really\r\ndoesn\'t get cold enough for a puffy jacket.  Not yet anyhow.  A vest\r\non the other hand is a good thing.  Especially if you are ruffing it\r\nat Arnold\'s house and the heat isn\'t blowing on a rainy sunday\r\nafternoon like last weekend.  Take it from me, there is a\r\nred vest in the closet.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>If I had a silver vest, I\'d just have to go out! because it would be\r\njust too <font color=\'red\'><tt>*hot*</tt></font> to be wearing inside.  \r\nYou know what though?  I don\'t need any silver vest.  I want a shake\r\nup in my life, a little something to get the stars going.  I\'m\r\nstarting to get bored enough to move out of my duplex-apartment, just\r\nfor the excitement.  That my friends is wack.  I don\'t want to move\r\nfrom one shitty apartment to another, or spend $75 dollars on a vest.\r\nI just want to sit back in a fluffy couch and smoke a joint.</P>\r\n\r\n<blockquote><i>Oh sorry, I can\'t say that on the air can I?  My parents\r\nmight hear.  Then I\'ll get grounded to my shitty apartment all over\r\nagain.</i></blockquote>\r\n\r\n<P>I think I am going to go home and eat polish sausage and sour kraut\r\nbecause I have been craving it for several weeks and just found sour\r\nkraut at Trader Joe\'s last week.  Look in the freezer case, not the\r\npickled items shelf.</P>\r\n\r\n<P align=\'center\'>Okay, thanks for reading.</P>'),(110,'<P>Listening to one of Arnold\'s John Fahey albums this morning. Bluesy,\r\ntrancey?  It is all about acoustic guitar.  No back up.  Just good old\r\nplucking and rattling strings.  I think a portion of it was recorded\r\nunder a highway overpass.  There is much urban noise in the\r\nbackground.  I like that.  It is like environmental folk music.\r\nSeeing his picture makes me want to wear sun glasses.\r\n</P><P>\r\nWe had a couple of memory lane drinks last night, Arnold & I.  By the time we were finished, I felt like I had kinda-sorta been a musician in New York City for several years around \'92 to \'95.  That is nice.  Arnold is a fun to listen to.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Then a friend came over and we three went driving.  We drove up Hollywood Hill to the\r\nnice neigborhood overlooking the City.  Arnold nodded off to sleep\r\nfairly quickly, in the front seat.  We drove around Los Angeles, China\r\nTown, and the place where all the food arrives into and leaves the\r\nCity of Love.\r\n</P><P>\r\nThe warehouses are interesting.  Some of them are painted beautiful\r\ncolors.  Some are bombed out with no windows.  There are beautiful ones with great names like Chung King Cross Roads and Hunan Exports and Rising Sea Gull Oceanic Product Express.  They have soft colors and\r\nklieg-like hallogen lights.  Part protective and part exibition.  With the lights, the concrete drive ways reflect a bleached white.\r\n</P><P>\r\nThe roads don\'t care who you are, Emperor or other.  Rough\r\nand under thirty year construction.  I think the construction people\r\ngave up and left when they arrived back to work one morning and\r\nsomebody had pinched the bulldozer during the night.  Pinched if it is\r\npossible to pinch something so large.  The bandits took everything\r\nexcept the orange traffic barrels.  Those are still very much\r\neverywhere.  I think maybe the construction workers left some time\r\nafter the area was invaded by indoeuropean armies of traders, the Huns.\r\n</P>\r\n<P>We also saw an old artist collective living arrangement warehouse that the some of Arnold\'s oldest friends used to live at.  Tonight is very much an tour.</P>\r\n<P>\r\nArnold missed all of this, his head bobbing to and fro.</P>'),(111,'<P>hey austin. you know i\'m going to have to do time in other weblogs now that i decided to be the kibo of blogger. i hope that\'s ok. honey, i can explain.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>well maybe it\'s not like kibo really. i guess the deal with kibo is that whenever anyone mentioned his name on usenet, he\'d appear. which isn\'t that big of a fucking deal, it\'s called grep. but for me it\'s more like i\'ll just appear whether you mention me or not. which i guess isn\'t like kibo in any way.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>it may or may not be that it\'s being done better elsewhere, it\'s the combination of it being done SO MUCH elsewhere and me being pretty thoroughly jaded with the whole scene, and me feeling like it\'s time to move onto some sort of greener pasture.</P>  \r\n\r\n<P>to tell you the truth last night i was really depressed and i have been for months. i know everyone thinks i\'m always depressed but i can tell you, that\'s not the truth. </P>\r\n\r\n<P>i\'d just like to challenge myself maybe. or maybe last night i wanted to kill myself or somehow fade from society entirely and that always makes me want to take my site down. </P>\r\n\r\n<P>even though i\'ve been having all these revelations lately that my purposes in life is to put my truth into words in the least vague way possible, well, maybe a web journal is the cheesiest way of doing that and the EASIEST way of doing that and since i spend so much time seeking validation maybe the print world could offer me some of that.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>don\'t get me wrong, i think the web is rad and i think it\'s cool that anyone can have a voice here. i just have this problem with feeling ordinary, it\'s probably really fucked up, a maladjustment, and it\'s probably the reason why i do things like get naked at parties.</P>\r\n\r\n<p>anyway.</P>'),(112,'<P>There are a great many things that I don\'t understand swirling around me today and yesterday.  I talk to my friends about them.  Why?  Why? Why?  Nothing major, just the nature of human pursuit.  Why do we push forward when pursuit of the unattainable holds us back?  Shrugs all around.  But I think it is more than a luxury. I think it is necessary.</P>  \r\n\r\n<P>I love this site.  There are many like it, but this one is mine.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>When I walk as a shadow through the valley of darkness every day, I have this web site.  It is my sense of accomplishment, pride, and better than a paper bound journal which no one ever reads, not even me.  In fact, it brings me closer to my friends who with every passing year, become farther and farther away.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Sure I write a lot of crap.  Most of it is not worth reading.  But on the occasion that I sit down and decide to just write, make something up, document something important, or anything of the sort, my skills are there.  If I never wrote, when the time came to write -- I don\'t think it would even occur to me.</P>'),(113,'<P>Last night was fun.  It was an A night.  I hung out with Adam Y., Adam L. Arnold.  That is four A\'s.  Adam L. actually cruised really early, leaving AAA.  At my birthday, there was a third Adam, Adam P.  AND there was fourth Adam, Adam M. That was an AAAAAA (6) night.  It kicked ass.  I love it when everyone is an \'A\'.  Makes me feel like I am in the proverbial \'A\' team that the Marketing department at my last two jobs has heralded.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>No where have so many A\'s been in congregation as here in Los *A*ngeles. It is all about the A\'s.  We are the L.A. A\'s.  Sorry if I am being confusing.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Maybe going to a party tonight.  Sunday night parties are the best.  The crazy fucks are tired or usually not present on suday nights.  Sunday night parties are for people who won\'t go out on fridays and saturdays because of the madness.  Maybe that is not true at all, but it is for me.  And I am an \'A\'.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Oh, Arnold says it is a Butoh performance by Oguri.  Hmmm, in Venice.  Cool.  Now I feel better about today.  I was kind of down on this sunday because I did not plan anything to look forward to.\r\n</P>\r\n'),(114,'<p>I like a woman. I like several women, actualy. No one woman inparticular. I have liked several women, I have loved only one. The one woman I loved, I still love only its just not healthy. So now I only like women, and try not to love them. I haven\'t been burned or abused, I have just forgoten how to love.</p>\r\n<p>There is another woman who loves me, but she loves another physicaly. We dont sleep together, but we argue like lovers. She asks me where I am, and she asks why I dont do things with her anymore. I am not her man, she has a man. I am her lover only through companionship. I don\'t think he loves her, and I, I only like her.</p> \r\n<p>So I am cought inbetween liking another woman, while being loved by another, while thinking about the one I love(d). Having one lover for sex, and another for companionship seems demented to me, but then again maybe its better. Seems as though I have gotten myself into a mess doesn\'t it? I dont love women anymore, I like them. I don\'t sleep with any of these women, and i don\'t plan on it becaues that would make it even harder.</p>\r\n<p> So then there is this one woman, a new woman, that I am attracted to, and I like her. I don\'t plan on telling her this, only because I would rather just like her from here. Daydream about loving her, or being loved by her. I think about how hard it would be to tell her about the other woman (the one I am just friends with).  I feel as though I need to go ahead and tell the other women to cool it with me, so that one day I can love a woman without just liking her. </p>\r\n<p>If the reader is having a hard time following this, imagine how the writer must feel - living it. Opportunity knocks softly, if you have to many women in your bedroom (bickering) it makes it harder to hear the knock. Same goes for everything I guess.</p>\r\n<p>A woman invited me to a fetish party, this is the woman that I like.</p> \r\n<p>I want|need to get laid. This is pathetic, I appologize.</p> \r\n<p>The B.M.G. will be in L.A. for thanksgiving. To see part of his family of course. Austin, Adam, all the other A\'s I don\'t know but have heard of, I will see you all soon. What are ya\'ll drinking? First bottle is on me.</p>\r\n<p>And yes, I did just watch a Hal Harltley movie. Fuck off.</p>\r\n<p>bmg</p>'),(115,'<p>I like a woman. I like several women, actualy. No one woman\r\ninparticular. I have liked several women, I have loved only one. The\r\none woman I loved, I still love only its just not healthy. So now I\r\nonly like women, and try not to love them. I haven\'t been burned or\r\nabused, I have just forgoten how to love.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>There is another woman who loves me, but she loves another\r\nphysically. We don\'t sleep together, but we argue like lovers. She asks\r\nme where I am, and she asks why I don\'t do things with her anymore. I\r\nam not her man, she has a man. I am her lover only through\r\ncompanionship. I don\'t think he loves her, and I, I only like her.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>So I am caught in between liking another woman, while being loved by\r\nanother, while thinking about the one I love(d). Having one lover for\r\nsex, and another for companionship seems demented to me, but then\r\nagain maybe its better. Seems as though I have gotten myself into a\r\nmess doesn\'t it? I don\'t love women anymore, I like them. I don\'t sleep\r\nwith any of these women, and i don\'t plan on it because that would\r\nmake it even harder.</p>\r\n\r\n<p> So then there is this one woman, a new woman, that I am attracted\r\nto, and I like her. I don\'t plan on telling her this, only because I\r\nwould rather just like her from here. Daydream about loving her, or\r\nbeing loved by her. I think about how hard it would be to tell her\r\nabout the other woman (the one I am just friends with).  I feel as\r\nthough I need to go ahead and tell the other women to cool it with me,\r\nso that one day I can love a woman without just liking her. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>If the reader is having a hard time following this, imagine how the\r\nwriter must feel - living it. Opportunity knocks softly, if you have\r\nto many women in your bedroom (bickering) it makes it harder to hear\r\nthe knock. Same goes for everything I guess.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>A woman invited me to a fetish party, this is the woman that I\r\nlike.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The B.M.G. will be in L.A. for thanksgiving. To see part of his\r\nfamily of course. Austin, Adam, all the other A\'s I don\'t know but\r\nhave heard of, I will see you all soon. What are ya\'ll drinking? First\r\nbottle is on me.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>And yes, I did just watch a Hal Harltley movie. Fuck off.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>bmg</p>'),(116,'<P>Most mornings out of the week, I arrive here and someone has made\r\ncoffee.  And that coffee sucks.  It is black as the ace of spades and\r\nworks on the toung like concentrated pine tar soap.  The stomach\r\nsame.  It is aweful.  How do they do it?  Well, upon inspection it\r\nwould seem that they fill the coffee filter to the top.  There is no\r\napparent ratio.  It is just fill the filter, put in eight cups of\r\nwater.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>This morning, I arrived in after the culprit, the offender, he of bad\r\ntaste, had just finished drafting his cup from the pot.  The first\r\ncup.  Now there were six cups of steaming shit water.  I took a\r\nquarter cup to taste the damage.  It was as bad or worse than I\r\nexpected.  I spit it out into the sink.    Already my appetite for\r\nmorning ritual was abused and withering.  There was still time\r\nthough.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I dug around for a bowl in the cupboard and filled the coffee maker\r\nhalf full again with water.  By the time it was done brewing, the\r\npot was full and the coffee was licking at the spout, about to over\r\nflow.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I siphoned off a cup with a straw because I was scared to touch the\r\npot, fearing it might spill all over the cup, my hand, and the\r\ncounter.  This kind of operation is just rude.  A rude way to start\r\nthe day.  My morning coffee is for all satisfying purposes ruined.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I will make directions to the effect of:</P>\r\n\r\n<P>THERE IS A RATIO IN MAKING COFFEE.  ONE NON-HEAPING TABLESPOON PER TWO\r\nCUPS.  IF THERE IS ANY CONFUSION OVER THIS, I BOUGHT THE COFFEE, DO WHAT\r\n I SAY, or BUY YOUR OWN STASH.</P>'),(117,NULL),(123,'<P>TEST How is it that thousands up on thousands connect to EFnet every day and I repeatedly get turned down for weeks on end?  I make a small gesture to BMG, I set him up an account to access IRC on my devserver and guess WTF?  Now I can\'t connect myself.  What the hell is that?  damn.</P>'),(124,'<P>TEST How is it that thousands up on thousands connect to EFnet every day and I repeatedly get turned down for weeks on end?  I make a small gesture to BMG, I set him up an account to access IRC on my devserver and guess WTF?  Now I can\'t connect myself.  What the hell is that?  damn.</P>'),(125,'<img src=\'http://swinney.org/art/steve_blur_med.jpg\' width=150 align=left>\r\n<P>Spleevin was one of my favorite roomates of all time.  I regret that I\r\ndidn\'t learn as much as I could have from him.  I think that much of\r\nwhat he knew just weirded me out.  No, not that.  I am just not a\r\nstructured spirituality person.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>We first met when I was trying to find people to move into my house in\r\nAustin at 31st and Speedway, fairly downtown.  The house was a dump.\r\nIt had a nice front porch though.  I am all about front porches.  The\r\nporch was defined and had a rail and an overhang.  You could really\r\nhang with your humans on that porch.</P>\r\n\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/art/galleries/nyc/images/2873_019.jpg\' width=150 align=right>\r\n<P>Steve just walked in the door and looked around the place really\r\nfast.  He was ready to take it.  I think it had been on the rentals\r\nsheet for a month.  Many people saw it, but just didn\'t dig the cheap\r\nrent, front porch, funk of the place.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I visited Spleevin in NYC recently.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>It was nice.</P>'),(126,'<P>I have to work at 11, so I got up at 6:40. Early for me. I sat in\r\ntraffic for an hour and fifteen minutes, driving north from Dallas to\r\nDenton.  I have just enough time to drive up there, vote, and drive\r\nback for work.  I am excited. </P>\r\n\r\n<P>I checked everything out and I am registered to vote.  I have to\r\n     go to that church by my old house where I have always voted. I\r\n     get there, and go in, and say hi, and they look me up and I am in\r\n     the big book of registered voters, of course.</P> \r\n<P>\"do you\r\n     still live at 1120 Fannin?\"</P> \r\n<P>\"no, I moved\"</P> \r\n<P>\"do you\r\n     still live in Denton County\"\r\n\r\n<P>oh. should I lie? yes or no?</P> \r\n<P>\"no\"</P> \r\n<P>\"then you can\'t\r\n     vote here\"</P> \r\n<P>Why did I not see this coming? I almost lost\r\n     it.</P> \r\n<P>\"where am I supposed to vote then?\"</P> \r\n\r\n<P>\"you can\'t\r\n     vote anywhere today\"</P> \r\n\r\n<P>He took my license and copied the\r\n     information onto a form entitled \"Disqualified Voters\".</P> \r\n\r\n<P>At this point we had all the element necessary for a public\r\n     shooting, except for the weapon and the loose nut. I wanted to\r\n     grab that hairy-faced stoner man-bitch and punch his fucking\r\n     jaw.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>He hands me a voter registration card and tells me about it, like I\r\n     wasn\'t already registered. I snatch it and storm out.  We\'ve seen\r\n     people storm out of places before.  You look like an idiot,\r\n     losing your temper. I was fucking pissed. Just pissed. </P>\r\n\r\n <P>In order to be registered in my county I would have had to go to\r\n Dallas an apply before I even lived there, to make the deadline.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>At that very moment I thought I would never live this down.  4\r\nyears until the next presidential election, and every time someone\r\nasks me if I voted I\'ll have to either tell this stupid story or just\r\nsay \"no\".  If they ask me who I voted for I\'ll have to just say that I\r\ndidn\'t vote.  I\'m already starting to live with it.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Sometimes it seems like it doesn\'t pay to tell the truth.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I drove back to Dallas.  I was listening to the yellow Bad Brains\r\ntape where the cover is a picture of the Whitehouse with a lightning\r\nbolt striking it. I felt the same way.</P>\r\n'),(127,'<P>so austin i popped in here cause you had a banner ad. and i thought you\'d be like auctioning yourself off for a date, and i could mess with the contestants or rig the online vote (election minded tonight :-). so what\'s the deal? and who got married? rumi? take care. ima come through santa barbara and los angeles sometime in december, maybe you have time to say hi.</P> <P>--sean</P>'),(128,'<P>Why do I suck?</P>\r\n<P>Last night I was lifeless. My movements were \r\nawkward. I felt like the year and a half I have \r\nspent playing Capoeira was wasted completely. \r\nI\'ve had days like this before but I never enjoy \r\nit. I couldn\'t pick up on the songs, even playing \r\nthe Berimbau felt weird.I hope I can make the \r\nadjustments I need to in my life to prevent this. \r\nTime will tell. Mestre Jurandir has told me that \r\nI have all the time in the world but its never \r\nenough training for me there are always new things \r\nto learn and old things to remember, sometimes the \r\nprospect is overwhelming.</P>\r\n'),(129,'<P>I was thinking on my walk to work this morning, up Broadway in\r\nGlendale, about the election and the Green party.  As it stands right\r\nnow, there is a 1200 vote difference between Bush and Gore in\r\nFlorida.  1200 votes between Gore and victory.  Congratulations Green\r\nparty, you won.  All the thousands of Green party voters won.\r\n</P><P>\r\nRepublicans: here is where you get what you asked for, well deserved tax breaks for\r\nthe wealthy 1%.</P>'),(130,'<P>12:15:32 J-Dawg: not bad; i heard from bmg this morning but had to dis him cause i was swamped with work\r\n</P><P>12:15:55 J-Dawg: get this: i\'m going to interview nsync tomorrow; should be pretty hilarious; do you have any burning questions?\r\n</P><P>12:16:10 robotec9: are you fucking with me?\r\n</P><P>12:16:51 robotec9: would you do me a favor?\r\n</P><P>12:16:51 J-Dawg: nope\r\n</P><P>12:16:56 J-Dawg: sure\r\n</P><P>12:17:09 robotec9: write about the experience in it\'s entirety on my website\r\n</P><P>12:17:55 robotec9: i don\'t give a shit what they say, but what your reaction is to the whole thing.\r\n</P><P>12:17:59 robotec9: PLEASE\r\n</P><P>12:18:12 robotec9: for an old friend whose favorite bike you stole!\r\n</P><P>12:18:29 robotec9: YOU OWE ME\r\n</P><P>12:18:36 J-Dawg: i might lose my job for something like that; can i promise you that i\'ll think about it \r\n</P><P>12:18:46 robotec9: totally anonymous\r\n</P><P>12:18:53 robotec9: no one will ever find out\r\n</P><P>12:19:06 J-Dawg: let me think about it; it would be great fun, i just need to make sure i cover my ass\r\n</P><P>12:19:09 robotec9: nobody visits my site anyway except for coolpeople.\r\n</P><P>12:19:22 robotec9: i swear to you total protection\r\n</P><P>12:20:35 J-Dawg: just let me think about it a little,\r\n</P><P>12:22:38 robotec9: and one more thing\r\n</P><P>12:22:49 J-Dawg: ?\r\n</P><P>12:22:52 robotec9: can you get an autographed picture to \"Homa\"?\r\n</P><P>12:23:14 J-Dawg: i\'ll see, i\'m not sure if it\'s going to be that sort of thing\r\n</P><P>12:23:23 robotec9: yea but....\r\n</P><P>12:23:39 robotec9: if anybody even moves in that direction, get one for homa\r\n</P><P>12:23:48 robotec9: it is my sister</P>\r\n\r\n<HR>\r\n<P>aus:homa is actually Aleonard\'s Girlfriend who likes NSYNC.</P>\r\n\r\n\r\n</P><P>22:10 Aleonard: homa\r\n</P><P>23:05 robotec9: what if they think he is making a sex joke?\r\n</P><P>23:55 Aleonard: it\'s okay. i\'d still get enough points to last me a life time. shit.\r\n</P><P>24:42 robotec9: he is going to try\r\n</P><P>25:41 Aleonard: HOT!\r\n</P><P>25:50 Aleonard: i owe him my life.\r\n</P><P>25:59 Aleonard: i just shiat in my pants.\r\n</P><P>26:01 Aleonard: thanks.\r\n</P><P>26:16 robotec9: coo\r\n</P><P>26:34 robotec9: i told him it was for my sister \"homa\"\r\n</P><P>26:39 Aleonard: cool</P>'),(131,'<P>I\'m launching in on the usual shit here.  Fuck.  What a two day period\r\nwe are having.  I am bleeding.  Bush is winning the presidency.  Can I\r\nsay how much I dislike liberal media, my liberal media, attacking\r\nconservative presidents?  It makes me sick at heart.  I got enough of\r\nit when Gingrich was the hip target.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I enjoy listening to the low end radio stations.  I like the news if\r\nit doesn\'t effect me.  I really don\'t feel like hearing about what the\r\nSupreme Court is going to overturn next month followed by a expose of\r\nreal life stories from people who know what it all means.  Damn.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I am going to the Republican headquarters to register as a supporter.\r\nI want Bush to be in office for me.  I don\'t want to be angry at him\r\nas a Democrat.  I want to make it personal.  When he does something\r\nevil, I want to feel betrayed by my leader.  I want to feel that he is\r\npersonally screwing me over. I am one of his constituents!</P>\r\n\r\n<P>If I were a Democrat and I voted for Gore and Gore won and then\r\nproceeded to do all the wrong things that I felt were against the\r\nnature of a predetermined pact that was initiated when I turned in my\r\nballot--you are right that I would send him letters.  I would call him\r\non the phone.  I would carry signs.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I\'d say things like, \"C\'mon man, don\'t appoint Justices that will\r\noverturn Roe V. Wade.  That is going to make many more people\r\nviolently unhappy than it will make people happy.\"  And, \"Don\'t cut\r\nthe funding for National Public Radio, what if the country became\r\nunstable and the economy collapsed:  How would you address the\r\nnation?\"</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Oh, maybe I am full of lies, and maybe I haven\'t done as many drugs as\r\nBush has.  And maybe my Grandfather wasn\'t involved in stealing\r\noil rights from Mexico or whatever, but I look forward to our new\r\nrelationship.  Maybe I\'ll look you up next time I am in D.C.</P>'),(132,'<P>It\'s pretty much over for me. I have threatened just about everyone here and I have a goddamn sheep\'s eye. </P>\r\n\r\n<P>Kadesh offered me a pretzel from her bag the other day. I took two. I am going down. I can feel it. I got too greedy. Why the hell did I take two? Man, if that didn\'t get me on some list...I am probably already on some list. Maybe two.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Harold has a cough today. Someone should give him a hug.</P>\r\n\r\n'),(133,'<P>i can\'t believe this. president clinton is on the tv and radio telling people that \"american\'s can\'t seriously say that their vote doesn\'t matter anymore.\"</P>\r\n\r\n<P>wha? doesn\'t he know how the president is elected? through the electoral college. the college is broken up by state. i live in texas. bush won texas by about 1.5 million votes. if me and 500,000 of my closest friends got together to protest the election and all voted twice and both times we voted for gore, we still wouldn\'t have changed anything.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>so, where exactly did my vote affect the outcome?</P>'),(134,'<img src=\'http://swinney.org/art/galleries/random/lux.jpg\'>'),(135,'<P>YES!  I am having the most awesome day.  I was hanging out on EFnet\r\nand this guy that I talked to like 5 months ago named RoboDoc showed\r\nup.  We are both named Robo* on EFnet and that was the first reason to\r\nbe friends.  Then when we got to talking, we found out that we are\r\nboth doing content management applications.  This was as I said, 5\r\nmonths ago when I was just getting started on the Swinnicle Manual\r\nOverride Super Charger engine.  I was on PHP looking for some help on\r\nit.  Turns out, he is working on a content manager too.  Fast forward\r\nmany months, and now I am working at ibiz2.com doing exactly what I\r\nwanted to do without a job, a content manager.  RoboDoc is working on\r\na security firm in Norway.  He said his content manager is file\r\noriented.  Like it does .mp3, .tar, gzip, etc.  It creates databases\r\nfrom spidering hard drives on a network.  I am thinking it would be awesome\r\nif we combined them.  RoboDoc is going to be in LA next year.  He\r\nwants to hang and I am totally down with that.  And he said if I am in\r\never in Norway...</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I have a cool new footer that is just unstoppable:</P>\r\n<PRE>\r\n._____LessThanNetZero Ghetto Internet Excess and Email______.\r\n|  Download Now           -->       http://www.swinney.org  |    \r\n|  Request a CDROM           -->        austin@swinney.org  |\r\n|___________________________________________________________|\r\n</PRE>\r\n\r\n<P>For those of you who don\'t get the joke, it is a take off on the\r\nNetZero Free Internet Access companies footer that they place on the\r\nbottom of all the email that gets sent out using their service.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I am going down to Web Volcano where all the ibiz2.com servers are\r\nto restart this dinky little server that has all my content stuff on\r\nit.  That is kinda fun.  I don\'t go down there very often.  Basically\r\nit means I get to leave work and be working.  That I find gratifying.\r\nI would be disappointed it there was something else I were to be\r\ndoing.  And sure there are things I am doing.  I haven\'t had a break\r\nfrom them in a long time though.  I might get a little card with my\r\nname on it and my face.  You know I have always wanted one of those!\r\nSo exciting!  So exciting!</P>\r\n\r\n<P>THEN! Oh yeas, the fun never stops with me some days, I am going to\r\nRoscoe\'s Chicken and Waffle with several of my favorite people.\r\nAleonard being one of them.  Maybe Pamie will go?  I don\'t know\r\nthough.  I just kind of sent her an email and figured WTF, everybody\r\nlikes chicken and waffles, right?  I hope so.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I figured I would include a quote from the PHP channel where\r\npresidential race insanity has thrown the topic off PHP into the\r\ndepths of politics:</P>\r\n\r\n\r\n<blockquote>\r\nxplode: good thing Clinton\'s name didn\'t start with a S cause if bush\r\nwon, we\'d have BSB for the last 3 presidents.....\r\n</blockquote>'),(136,'<p>I received an unsolicited email from a young Romanian woman wanting some help in a uncomfortable situation, needing a place to call home for a few weeks. My initial reaction was \"SCAM\" but I decided that I would cautiously follow up, part out of curiosity and part out of gut feeling that it was valid. I received another email from the day after, going into a few more details of her predicament, and expressing her intent. At first I was weary, and skeptic. Now I am thinking, what harm could be done? Much, I realize but isn\'t life risky anyway? Isn\'t this why we buy insurance, so we can live life careless?</p>\r\n<p>So I am addressing the nation, you my friends, what would you do? Would you let a stranger into your home? What questions would you ask? Would you just say no?</p> \r\n<p>I ask my neighbor, Gibby Haines, and he says \"its better to regret something you have done, rather something you haven\'t done.\" Of course, I could be asking for hell, as my brother states, heaven or hell. I think most people are more than willing to trust; only they have had too many people close to them break that trust. I think that is why more people in America aren\'t as willing to trust. Also, it is true that strangers can be bad. I am thinking that I could make a new friend. Thatâ€™s where I will leave it. I am going to allow this girl into my house, she is going to feel way more weird than I am, sure of that.</p>\r\n<p>Exciting stuff for me, got my mind off the damn elections. Elections, hmmm, brings me to another thought. I was driving a friend home from work today, when I realized I was driving down Congress Avenue. I could see the pink granite capitol of Texas in my rearview mirror, and I thought to myself: \r\n<blockquote>\"George, even if you end up winning this election, remember that over half of this country doesn\'t want you there. Furthermore, if you do move on up to Washington Ave and lay your head upon that Presidential pillow, picture your momma bitin it as yo daddy gave it to her!\" </blockquote>\r\n\r\n<p>I also want to remind him to look under the desk before he starts feeling around under there; I have reason to believe that billy left him a sticky present under there.</p>\r\n'),(137,'<P>Were everyone to applaud a performance only if others did it first, there would be no applause.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Your vote counted.</P>\r\n'),(138,'<P>remember bmg - remember - you must *invite* a vampire into your home for it to have any power over you.  course... on the other side..hot romanian vampire vixen dont sound so bad.   </P> '),(139,NULL),(140,'hi. i wanted everyone to know that i am famous on\r\nthe microsoft network. <a href=\"http://underwire.msn.com/underwire/social/inprofile/98profile.asp\" target=\"honkhonk\">see</a>?\r\n'),(143,'TEST	'),(144,'<P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P>\r\n\r\n<P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P>'),(145,'<P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Lu<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/145_1.jpg\' height=\'150\' align=\'left\'>v Cam Chicks! </P>\r\n\r\n<P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/145_4.jpg\' height=\'150\' align=\'right\'> Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P><P>I Luv Cam Chicks! </P>\r\n\r\n<P>END</P>'),(146,'<p>I am going to go downtown to play. It is Saturday, and all my usual playmates are either broke or at home asleep. Its only 10:00 pm. I think its the election stuff.</p>\r\n<p>BUT NOT ME!!!</p>\r\n<p>I have sixty some bucks in my pocket, wine in me belly, and I am in a good mood. My only option tonight is to go downtown to the Ritz and enjoy some music performed by the deucedeuce\'s very own, Derick the upstairs neighbor.</p>\r\n<p>Earlier I was invited by Derick to go see the Futants play. It sure beats checking my email three times every five minutes. Not to mention, I just DESTROYED a scanner. It was making weird noises. Being that I am not the hardware guru of my household, I decided I would let the floor take care of it. Guess what, hp doesn\'t make shatter-proof glass on their scanners. I am thinking about taking legal action.</p>\r\n<p>The girl I have been seduced by called me yesterday. I talked to her today. We talked for twenty minutes. I think its a deal, whata ya think? She is cool, and she wears all black.</p>\r\n<p>The Romanian girl is freaking me out, she emails me everyday. Each day she tells me of another problem. I am a helping person, but I refuse to be walked all over. I will find her a place to stay in a co-op. Maybe a meal or two. This isn\'t a charity house! Go see Ronal McDonald!</p>\r\n<p>aim--->iamtheBMG</p>'),(147,'<P>going through life without taking psychedelics is like going through life without having sex.</p>\r\n\r\n<P>-terrence mckenna</p>'),(148,'<P>i have walked all over the city three times.  \r\nthree laps.  up the hill, down, around, times three.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>hanging out with sean is really fun.  he takes\r\nmy picture allot.  i am like a supermodel.  i\'m learning\r\nto pose and stuff.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>tonight i\'m going to dinner with sean, kathy, elly,\r\nher boyfriend and the budist.  we are going to get\r\nthia food.  i haven\'t met elly, her boyfriend or the budist.</p>\r\n\r\n<P>sean is making coffee.  i\'m writing on his laptop\r\nand solififying my belief that laptops are cool.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i don\'t feel myself brimming with words right now.\r\ni am just having fun and not looking forward to \r\ndiving back to LA.  oh well...</P>\r\n'),(149,'<P>hi Austin, </P>\r\n<P>glad you got to sf after all.  sorry we were sleeping the other night so we didnt get to say good night and safe trip.  we miss you.</P>\r\n<P>cha chi and arnie</P>'),(150,'<P>it has been said that austin swinney is \'driven, as if by an engine.\'\r\nkid\'s, they were not telling a lie.  driving from LA to SF to LA, SX.\r\nmy stomach feels like a barf bag. my arse feels like a flotation\r\ndevice.  my ears feel popped.  my brain is quivering from the bends.\r\nmy mind is in the clouds.  my eyes hurt.  this is what happens when\r\nyou cross the mountain pass twice in one weekend.\r\n</P><P>\r\nvisiting SF was cool.  (what do you mean by ... cool?) i met internet\r\npeople that were very nice and made me wish that my friends were all\r\ninternet people too, not just some of them.\r\n</P><P>\r\nit also made me realize what awesome friends i have in LA and how\r\namazing that is, considering i have only been here a short time.  i\r\nguess because i thought, \'should i move here, sf?\' and the answer was\r\nno.  i asked myself why that is? and the answer was because i am not\r\nready to leave my friends in LA.  then i said, \'well you could fly\r\ndown to see them.\'  then i told myself to shut up.\r\n</P><P>\r\nuhg, i need some food.  and why is my computer beeping at me?  maybe\r\nit is trying to tell me i need to eat something and take better care\r\nof myself.  wouldn\'t that be nice.  a little reverse tamagachi.  is\r\nthat so hard to believe?  my computer taking care of me?  i don\'t\r\nthink so.\r\n</P><P>\r\ntime to go give girls chocolate from sf and visit with adam and arnie and\r\nchachi.  i hope they are still awake.\r\n</P><P>\r\ngood night, good bye.</P>'),(151,'<a href=\'http://durak.org/sean/pix/2000-11-12/index.php\'>http://durak.org/sean/pix/2000-11-12/index.php</a>\r\n<P>\r\n<ul type=square>\r\n<li>blond boys are <b>austin</b> (moi)\r\n<li>long brown hair boys are <b>sean</b> (see <a href=\'http://durak.org/sean\'>durak.org/sean</a>)\r\n<li>midnight hair with red tanktop and red blinds is <b>shelly</b> (see sine #rant@efnet)\r\n<li>smiley face with earrings next to shannon thinking japanese is\r\nsmiley name <b>jubal</b> (see pup #rant@efnet)\r\n<li>red haired botanist girls are <b>kathy</b> (see katfish <a href=\'http://durak.org/kathy\'>durak.org/kathy</a>)\r\n<li>big hat and round specs are <b>elly</b>(see <a href=\'http://elly.org\'>elly.org</a>)\r\n<li>skinny smiley with cigarette are <b>peter</b> (see <a href=\'http://hungry.com/~yeti\'>peter very nice</a>)\r\n<li><b>the buddist</b> is accepting a hug from me with surprise (use <a href=\'mailto:almaddo@ekno.com\'>al maddocks</a> living on a <a href=\'http://ekno.com\'>lonely planet</a>)\r\n</ul></P>'),(152,'<a href=\'http://cgi.ebay.com/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=498743429\'>gee, this is just great!</a>'),(153,'<blockquote><p>\"Starting a web business is the equivalent for my peer group of starting a garage band or starting a restaurant.\"</p>\r\n\r\n<p align=\"right\">from <a href=\"http://www.inu.org/scherzi/200011/entry10.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Scherzi & Sospiri</a></blockquote>\r\n\r\n<p>puppy\r\n'),(154,'<P>I got a strange phone call last night from this girl Amy.  Strange\r\nonly in that I haven\'t seen or heard from her in years.  We lived\r\ntogether at the infamous House of Commons in Austin, TX, some 6 or so\r\nyears ago.  We kinda off and on got along.  I don\'t think she hated me\r\nmost of the time.  She did often though.  I have that effect on\r\nwomen.  They love me.  They hate me.  Love. Hate. Love. Hate.  I think\r\nit has to do with my curious ability to be social and then anti\r\nsocial.  Social is interpreted as nice.  Antisocial is interpreted as\r\nmean.  I am nice.  I am mean.  Nice. Mean. Nice. Mean.\r\n</P>\r\n\r\n<P>\r\nAmy was one of the first girls to open my mind to this problem of\r\nmine.  \r\n</P>\r\n<!--\r\n<P>\r\nFirst, for my own conviction, I resent when girls that I am friends with love\r\nme.  Why is that?  I don\'t know.  That is a therapy session I am\r\nsaving for my mid-life crisis.  I don\'t think my mind is large enough\r\nto incorporate others within the relm of intimacy without feeling\r\nviolated and trespassed upon.\r\n</P>\r\n<P>\r\nI actually remember the moment I lost respect for her.  I have respect\r\nfor her now, but at the time, I was younger and more critical than I\r\nam now; and I\'ll say it: I was more of a dumbass than I am now.</P>\r\n-->\r\n<P>We were riding in her car, me, her, and trish, headed up\r\nhighway 35 from Austin to Dallas.  The car was an old Regan era\r\nchrystler security guard coupy thing. Amy and Trish were talking about\r\ntheir ideal future: small cottage in country, husband with no real job\r\nother than pulling raddishes and selling hay, children running around.\r\n19 year old me wanted to vomit on the floorboard of the car.  I\r\ncouldn\'t help but think they were following this train of conversation\r\nfor my sake.  What input did I have?  I think I said something classic\r\nand representative of a typical swinney foot in mouth statement,\r\n\"Who fed you that bullshit?! That is the stupidest thing I have ever\r\nheard.\"  What followed was the worst car ride possible.  Two hours of\r\nfuming girl thoughts comming from the front seat.  Me trying to wish\r\nmyself out of the back seat, and the car overheating 30 minutes\r\noutside Dallas.  If it couldn\'t have been worse, we had to pull over\r\nin a parking lot and sit under the quiet fo the night sky hating each\r\nother for half an hour while the engine cooled enough to start again.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>So Amy called last night while I was out at a bar drinking.  I got the\r\nmessage and she was asking if she could stay at my place.  How the\r\nHell did she get my number?  I have no clue.  She was flying through\r\nand was only in town the night.  Several years ago I stayed with Amy\r\nand Andra and a flop of their friends for one night in San Francisco.\r\nThis entitled her to stay at my place, she said.  My place was a\r\nwreck, is a wreck.  No one has ever been to my apartment for more than\r\nthirty seconds and ever gotten past the top stairs hall way.  My\r\napartment is forbidden.  Sometimes it doesn\'t even want me in it.\r\nThere is no place to sit, barely anyplace to stand.  It is filthy like\r\nan urban crack house.  There is no heat, and it is cold.  I couldn\'t\r\nhave her in my apartment at that moment.  I\'d have to hose it out or\r\nsomething.  Anyway, I called her cell phone number that she left and\r\nit was out of service.  So, I didn\'t have to worry about it.  My place\r\nis still wrecked.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I kind of wanted to see her though.  I think about her probably once\r\nevery year and a half.  I wish I had a picture of her.  She was pretty.</P>'),(155,'LOS ANGELES- Sociologists have noted an alarming raise in the number of closeted Medieval Barbarians in Los Angeles\'s Silverlake region. \"For years we\'ve observed social deviants such as Homosexuals, Bisexuals and Mulattos struggle for acceptance into the cocoon of our society,\" says Sociologist Holly Martins, head of University of Southern California\'s prestigious Gaywatch Program. \"But this is the first time we\'ve seen a form of social deviance \'rise from the dead\' \".\r\n\r\nAccording to Martins, the number of men and women in the Silverlake region, admitting their \'inner Barbarism\' is fast on the rise and is predicted to make-up at least 45% of the population in the greater Los Angeles area by the year 2003.\r\n\r\n\"I guess, I\'ve always known ever since I was child,\" says local Silverlake Barbarian, Hrothgar of the Umbar Steppe. \"I was never a very sanitary child.  Nor was I interested in playing with G.I. Joe, or Barbie for that matter. I tended to gravitate more towards Falconry and Metalurgy. Family trips to the beach were always a clear indicator of my closeted nature. There was always some \'incident\' involving my parents and the parents of some strange child who\'s sand castle I spontaneously destroyed.\" \r\n\r\nThe coming out experience can be so alienating and psychologically damaging that support groups have been formed by the new Barbarian community. \"I hurt inside...\" claims local Piano Teacher and Mongol Raider, Thulsa Ala Kahn. \"Coming out of the closet was one of the hardest things I\'ve ever done.\" When asked what provoked his outing he stated \"I\'m tired of feeling like there\'s something wrong with me. Thank Crom, these support groups are here. I\'m finally coming to terms with my biological urges to conquer Europe on horseback.\" \r\n\r\nThis social phenomenon is taking its toll on the local dear population. \"We gotta\' wear something,\" claims Silverlake postman Boromir Slayer of Wyrms Rosenberg. \"Chainmail is just too time consuming to weave. Hardened leather is a lot easier to make and might I add a hell of a lot more comfortable, especially on my route during those LA summers.\" \r\n\r\nThe birth of this phenomenon has spurned a negative reaction from  the already well established Homosexual population in the Los Angeles suburb. \"Just the other day some Homo hucked a brick at my head and called me a \'Visigoth\'.\" explains Ala Kahn. \"I was almost tempted to unsheath my scimitar and slice open his abdomen. But I knew if they Gay and Barbarian community was ever going to find peace, pillage and mass slaughter would probably deter the process\" \r\n\r\n\"We wish they would all just move to their own island.\" States Mark Todd Kinsley, local Gay poet and actor. \"There they can all die of Beubonic Plague or whatever those sword wielding, dark age dominating, long haired queers get.\"\r\n\r\nAccording to anthropologists the Barbarian community has rapidly come into its own as a culture. Cultural manifestations specific to the Barbarian population have been recorded and analyzed. \"They spend a lot of time trying to figure out something called \'the riddle of steel\'. I\'ll be damned if I know what that fuck that is.\" States Stuart Bick, head of the Anthropology division at the University of Chicago. \r\n\r\nNew studies have also revealed the birth of a few more yet far smaller forms of social deviance in the greater Los Angeles area. In Santa Monica, a growing number of closet 17th century Pirates have been reported. And with the birth of LA\'s new underground Metro system, a few instances of closeted Neo-Lithic Bison Painters have been recorded. \"Its the craziest thing,\" says transit cop Lee Van Smith, \"They\'re totally naked, and painting pictures of bison on the walls, in blood.\"      \r\n'),(156,'<P>LOS ANGELES- Sociologists have noted an alarming raise in the number of closeted Medieval Barbarians in Los Angeles\'s Silverlake region. \"For years we\'ve observed social deviants such as Homosexuals, Bisexuals and Mulattos struggle for acceptance into the cocoon of our society,\" says Sociologist Holly Martins, head of University of Southern California\'s prestigious Gaywatch Program. \"But this is the first time we\'ve seen a form of social deviance \'rise from the dead\' \".\r\n</P><P>\r\nAccording  to Martins, the number of men and women in the Silverlake region, admitting their \'inner Barbarism\' is fast on the rise and is predicted to make-up at least 45% of the population in the greater Los Angeles area by the year 2003.\r\n</P><P>\r\n\"I guess, I\'ve always known ever since I was child,\" says local Silverlake Barbarian, Hrothgar of the Umbar Steppe. \"I was never a very sanitary child.  Nor was I interested in playing with G.I. Joe, or Barbie for that matter. I tended to gravitate more towards Falconry and Metalurgy. Family trips to the beach were always a clear indicator of my closeted nature. There was always some \'incident\' involving my parents and the parents of some strange child who\'s sand castle I spontaneously destroyed.\" \r\n</P><P>\r\nThe coming out experience can be so alienating and psychologically damaging that support groups have been formed by the new Barbarian community. \"I hurt inside...\" claims local Piano Teacher and Mongol Raider, Thulsa Ala Kahn. \"Coming out of the closet was one of the hardest things I\'ve ever done.\" When asked what provoked his outing he stated \"I\'m tired of feeling like there\'s something wrong with me. Thank Crom, these support groups are here. I\'m finally coming to terms with my biological urges to conquer Europe on horseback.\" \r\n</P><P>\r\nThis social phenomenon is taking its toll on the local dear population. \"We gotta\' wear something,\" claims Silverlake postman Boromir Slayer of Wyrms Rosenberg. \"Chainmail is just too time consuming to weave. Hardened leather is a lot easier to make and might I add a hell of a lot more comfortable, especially on my route during those LA summers.\" \r\n</P><P>\r\nThe birth of this phenomenon has spurned a negative reaction from  the already well established Homosexual population in the Los Angeles suburb. \"Just the other day some Homo hucked a brick at my head and called me a \'Visigoth\'.\" explains Ala Kahn. \"I was almost tempted to unsheath my scimitar and slice open his abdomen. But I knew if they Gay and Barbarian community was ever going to find peace, pillage and mass slaughter would probably deter the process\" \r\n</P><P>\r\n\"We wish they would all just move to their own island.\" States Mark Todd Kinsley, local Gay poet and actor. \"There they can all die of Beubonic Plague or whatever those sword wielding, dark age dominating, long haired queers get.\"\r\n</P><P>\r\nAccording to anthropologists the Barbarian community has rapidly come into its own as a culture. Cultural manifestations specific to the Barbarian population have been recorded and analyzed. \"They spend a lot of time trying to figure out something called \'the riddle of steel\'. I\'ll be damned if I know what that fuck that is.\" States Stuart Bick, head of the Anthropology division at the University of Chicago. \r\n</P><P>\r\nNew studies have also revealed the birth of a few more yet far smaller forms of social deviance in the greater Los Angeles area. In Santa Monica, a growing number of closet 17th century Pirates have been reported. And with the birth of LA\'s new underground Metro system, a few instances of closeted Neo-Lithic Bison Painters have been recorded. \"Its the craziest thing,\" says transit cop Lee Van Smith, \"They\'re totally naked, and painting pictures of bison on the walls, in blood.\"      \r\n</P>'),(157,'<P>I myself voted for Randy \"Macho Man\" Savage. Now, I know what you\'re all thinking, where was he on the ballot? \r\n\r\nAll I have to say is crayons are a powerful thing. Suddenly the ballot was a lot more diverse with Randy Savage, Billy the Horse (who is an actual horse, except he ran for president), and Yucca (who\'s an actual potted Yucca plant representing the state of Wisconsin in the senate for the past 37 years). \r\n</P><P>\r\nGore did not receive my vote because I can\'t figure out whether or not his daughters are attractive. This is usually a tell tale sign of a displaced trans-dimensional entity. And sadly, I\'m a tad rustic in my sentiments towards the trans-dimensional. Lets put it this way, I would not drink from the same water fountain as a man from another dimension, therefore why would I want one for president? I\'m fully willing to accept the possibility that the ambiguity of the Gore sister\'s beauty might have something to do with the four inch cataract I have bulging out of my eye. However, I still feel that those from another dimension should either go back to their original dimension or get an island somewhere and start their own country.\r\n</P><P>\r\nBilly, being a horse, did not share my political views when it came to Abortion (I am pro) and Gay Rights (also pro), therefore he did not get my vote. Plus, I am a firm believer in the separation between church and state and we all know how religous zealots horses can be.\r\n</P><P>\r\nBush did not receive my vote because, well, he can barely write his name in the ground with a stick. \r\n</P><P>\r\nNow Buchanan was a tough one. And I nearly punched that hole until I realized I was filling out one of the dreaded \"Dung Locust\" ballots. As a result I put extra effort into distinguishing between Buchanan\'s hole and Billy the Horse\'s. But then I felt a change of heart. Although Buchanan never mentioned kicking trans-dimensional beings out of the country, he sure did seem angry at them Mexicans. I figured hey, close enough. Yet as my push pin approached Buchanan\'s hole (I know how that sounds) I suddenly remembered I was no longer a Nazi from the 1930\'s. I had given that up just before adopting my 18th Century Pirate personae, or what I like to call my \"Arrggh\" years.\r\n</P><P>\r\nNadar did not receive my vote because of his veiws. I found his views to be too perfect and beneficial for America and mankind as a whole. And I could never consciously vote for a man who could be SO right and yet look SO wrong. Judging by Nadar\'s posture, the glassy look in his eye and the brittle nature of his hair, its clear that he is dying of some sort of disease, most likely of an extra terrestrial origin. \r\n</P><P>\r\nYucca did not receive my vote because voting for a potted plant is simply absurd. \r\n</P><P>\r\nBrown, the Libertarian did not receive my vote simply because of the painfully fresh memories I have of the battle of Quinox and the outer rim. The Libertarians had allied themselves with the Killari and the Yull which left me and my team of Rangers to battle three different intergalactic races all of which were represented by members of my own platoon. Many of my best friends died in the vacuum of space during that battle, I myself only just barely made it out alive. Therefore I could never vote for a man who represented a race of beings whom at one time, ruthlessly tried to dominate the galaxy and deplete it of yogurt.\r\n</P><P>\r\nIn the end it was definitely Randy \"Macho Man\" Savage. No man epitomizes America more in my eyes, except for maybe Mario Van Peebles.\r\n</P>'),(158,'<P>First of all, no comments about my hair. It\'s a touchy subject. HOW DARE YOU SWINNEY?!?!?!?! Who do you think you are? This is my hair. I like it. I don\'t have any beef w/ yours. Or your fancy belt. You\'re probably the one who leaves all the goddamn pubes all over the American Standard. That\'s really neat how they are all stuck to the lip of the piss pot like that. How do you do that? Do they just fall out when you unzip? Or do you pluck them w/ tweezers. You know how I can tell that they are yours? They are modeling for me. Posing on the porcelain. Like some blonde kid in San Francisco. \r\n</P>\r\n<P>Secondly, Mr. Swinney, I\'d like to take this time to thank you, yes thank you, for asking me to dinner, telling me that you were going to pay and then you made me pay. THAT\'S UNAMERICAN, YOU COMMUNIST GORE LICKER! And you know what really sucks? Do you? You made me eat chicken and waffles. YOU VIOLATED MY STOMACH! I hurt for weeks.\r\n</P>\r\n<P>Swinney, I am tired of your empty promises, your pubes on the urinal, and your judgement on my hair-style. Swinney, goddamn you! This is your last warning. Don\'t look behind you. I swear...\r\n</P>\r\n<P>BANG!</P>'),(159,'<P>\r\nMOCA\r\n</P><P>\r\nPaul McCarthy show.\r\n</P><P>\r\nNatasha and I took my grandmother to the Japanese American Museum, where she let her membership expire.  Even after buying a brick for my cousin, she still had to pay for admission because the receptionist, Ken Nakamura was a cock sucking dicweed.\r\n</P><P>\r\nAs we left, I saw that Paul McCarthy was having a show so I dragged Natasha and my grandmother to it. As we walked in there was a father standing with his arm on his son as he proceeded to fuck the mechanical goat in the ass.\r\n</P><P>\r\nNatasha asked me if I wasn\'t embarrassed.  My grandmother laughed.  \"What does it mean?\", she asked. Well, uh... it\'s the American Family...\r\n</P><P>\r\nAfter more videos and butts and excrement, we came to a beautiful woodlands.  After walking through the woods, I saw a father fucking a tree, and a sun humpimg the pines...\r\n</P><P>\r\nThe american family should only be viewed by other members of your family.  Nate was blushing.\r\n</P>'),(160,'<P>I miss being able to openly scratch my\r\nchest hair at work.  I used to sit here at my\r\ncomputer and get the urg to reach in that \r\ntwo-missing-button gap in my shirt and scratch\r\nscratch  scratch.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Now i can\'t do that.  Oh it is so sad.</P>'),(161,'<P>Ever almost died by car?  I was riding my bike home from work in\r\nAustin a year ago when a old ford truck full of lawn mowers and\r\nspeeding, ran a stop sign, never slowed down at all, and missed me by\r\n1 <sup>1</sup>/<sub>2</sub> feet.  That was fucked up.  I vomited on the curb afterward.  I\r\nthought I might as well be dead.  I would not have lived.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>So yesterday I saw a car going too fast hit a car turning when it\r\nshouldn\'t have been.  This was on the street by my house that I cross\r\nto go to work.  Again, I thought that could have been  me getting\r\nhit.  I would have broken my legs and probably my pelvis.  Fly into\r\nthe windshield and peal some portion of my scalp or face off, then\r\nroll over the hood/roof, and land on the curb with a thud.  That guy\r\ndriving the little Honda that hit me would be stunned.  He would not\r\nbelieve that it just happened.  The old man in the barber shop would\r\nhave called the ambulance.  Fire trucks would come.  The man that hit\r\nme in with the old Honda would not have auto insurance.  My parents\r\nwould have to pay my bills in the hospital.  I might not walk again.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>My uncle died after a few years of operations to restore his spine\r\nand abdomen from the meat loaf that it was reduced to when\r\nhe fell out of a kit plane from fifty feet up and landed on the\r\nrunway.  His best friend was flying the plane.  His best friend was\r\nhis wife\'s brother.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>My dad took a few days before he believed that his brother was dead.\r\nIt was the same brother that accidently poked my dad\'s left eye out\r\nwith a stick when they were children.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>At the funeral, my dad didn\'t want to stay.  He doesn\'t like all the\r\npeople mourning.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I wonder, my dad can\'t mourn.  Would he be able to live if I were hit\r\nby a car and died after two years of operations?  What if I wanted to\r\ndie like my uncle did.  He wanted to die.  He was proud.  He didn\'t\r\nlike people helping him.  He didn\'t want to live.</P>'),(162,'<center>\r\n<P><font color=\'blue\'><strong><tt>california hairless</tt></strong></font></P>\r\n\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/162_1.jpg\'>\r\n<P><font color=\'blue\'><strong><tt>(natural habitat)</tt></strong></font></P>\r\n</center>'),(163,'<!-- i can\'t talk about it. -->\r\n\r\n<a href=\"http://www.nerve.com/Fiction/Cosper/storyProblem/main.asp\">something</a> that <a href=\"http://www.saturn5.com/~darwin\">darwin</A> sent a long time ago that still seems to be relevant.\r\n\r\n'),(164,'<p>I made myself oatmeal this morning for breakfast. As I was eating it, I realized that life (my life anyway) is much like oatmeal. Sometimes it is runny and loose. Like when I have not much going on, or when I am feeling rather bored. Other times, it is thick and full of content. Like when I am in school, learning much, having a romantic fling, and not worried about sleeping. Either way, as I see it right now, life is tasteless, neither runny nor thick; much like my oatmeal this morning. Yes there are times when it is full of spice, and full of excitement, but for the most part it is bland. No matter how much sugar, or honey I add it is still just oatmeal. This is not a complaint, merely an observation. A friend of mine told me that when life tastes like oatmeal, it is the time in which most people deside to get married. I agree with her, but for myself I would much rather have a lot of hot sex, be a rock star, and drive a GTO. Another friend of mine told me that she thinks that our generation goes through a mini-mid-life crisis every five years. I liked my Dad best when he was going through his mid-life crisis. I think that a mid-life crisis sounds life fun, especially after observing his.</p>'),(165,'chicken wings at the rustic make me hott'),(166,'<P>i am like a pheonix rising out of a crappy morning.  everyone was bite bite bite this morning.  there is resiliance in the alexandria house though.  we had a little therapy session on the back porch.\r\n</P>\r\n<P>i have spent all my weekend at this house.  i have squatter rights to arnold\'s G4 mac.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i was talking to xianfoy about journals.  she decided not to keep one online.  it made me think about what kind of person it takes to write online.  aside from the whole privacy issue, i think one must a) not care if they misspell a word to the entire world like i did twice this morning b) admit that one has ideas that are erronious, because it will happen c) stifle the fear of being a fool.  i think to be in the public eye is to be a fool.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>oh, and you have to like to do it more than most things.  me: i like it more than television, movies, girl friends, and getting messed up.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i love this website.  i guess that makes me narcissistic, and one who is in love with his work.  for me this is a religious experience.  i am in communion with the Internet.  the Internet lives inside me.  and the best thing is sitting on the porch talking to all my Internet friends.  visiting them at their convenience.  life online is good that way.</P>'),(167,'<P>Well Well Well, who do we have here?  Me.  I\'m sick.  suck.  My luck.\r\n(he says in between sucking sound of snot.) My life.\r\n</P><P>\r\nThis weekend was great.  I stayed at arnold and cha-chi\'s house like a\r\nfreeloading loser.  like a couch boy.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nSaturday I went home and did laundry and cleaned.  I think that is\r\nwhat really needed to happen.  I needed to clean.  When my place is\r\nclean it makes me want to read.  I didn\'t though, I went back to A/C\'s\r\nhouse.  I think I am going to stay home and read tonight though.  I\r\nfeel bad when I spend too much time over there.  I can\'t imagine that\r\nthey would be anything other than sick of me.  Maybe they aren\'t.  I\r\ndon\'t know.  I try to contribute.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI was talking to arnie about it.  how it is difficult for me to live\r\nalone.  i like hanging out so much that i prefer to live with others.\r\nhe and chachi think i am like their kid.  i think that is funny.  i\r\nthink they are like my girlfriend.  my time sponging interpersonal\r\nadventure that is more interactive than TV and less troublesome than\r\nsex.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI wrote an email out to all my friends and relatives (both biological\r\nand online) sunday morning.  I just felt like saying good morning to\r\nas many people as possible.  maybe for the karma.  my day didn\'t\r\nreally reflect it, but the long term could have been affected:\r\n</P>\r\n<font size=-1>\r\n<pre>\r\nPINE 4.21   MESSAGE TEXT                      \r\nDate: Sun, 19 Nov 2000 16:57:27 +0000 (GMT)\r\nFrom: Austin Swinney <aswinney@swinney.org>\r\nTo: my friends \r\nSubject: sometimes i bug in the morning\r\n\r\nIf I were a bug, I would want to live \r\nin a patch of mint.  I would eat mint and \r\nlive in candy land.\r\n\r\nIf I were a bug, I would live in a coffee \r\nbean bush and after a night\'s sleep, I would \r\ncollect my morning coffee from the dew on the leaves.\r\n\r\nIf I were a bug, I would live on a coca plant \r\nin colombia where the weather is nice to bugs.  \r\nAnd I would eat my plant and race around.\r\n\r\nIf I were a bug, I would live on a rose bush\r\nin los angeles.  Every night I would make love to\r\nthe lady bugs on a bed of rose pedals.  In the morning\r\nI would swim in rose water dew.\r\n\r\nIf I were a bug, I would live on a cactus because\r\nI want no one to touch me.\r\n\r\nIf I were a bug, I would live among the blades of\r\ngrass with all the other bugs.  And the ants would\r\nbite me.\r\n\r\nIf I were a bug, I would live in the flower in the pantry\r\nand a woman would look down at me and say, \"look there is\r\na bug in the flower.\" And I would say back, \"That is right,\r\nI have squatting rights to this land!\"\r\n\r\nIf I were a bug, I would live in austin\'s underwear \r\nand make him scratch scratch scratch.\r\n\r\n______LessThanNetZero Ghetto Internet Excess and Email_______\r\nDownload Now     http://www.swinney.org\r\nRequest a CDROM  austinzero@swinney.org\r\n_____________________________________________________________\r\n</pre>\r\n</font>\r\n\r\n<P><STRONG>le wears headphones</strong></P>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/167_2.jpg\'\r\nheight=\'150\' align=\'left\'>'),(168,'<p>My very good friend and co-worker, zooberries, noticed today that I had removed all of my personal belongings from my cube.\r\nHe was very curious as to why. I really didn\'t have a good answer for him, therefore I told him not to worry about it in a sly sorta way. This perked his interest, and led to many questions.</p>\r\n<p>Now this guy, Zoooberries, is know for his pranks that he plays on his close friends. He has gotten me countless times, and swindog as well. He is also very good at knowing when I am messing with him. Like the time I tried to ensure Zoob that Austin was an elron. Anyway, tonight I had given him just enough bait to lure him in to ask more, and well he took it... read what happened:</p>\r\n<font color=\"blue\">Zooberries</font>: TELL me where u are moving too damn it</br>\r\n<font color=\"red\">iamtheBMG</font>: ha..ha..</br>\r\n<font color=\"red\">iamtheBMG</font>: california</br>\r\n<font color=\"blue\">Zooberries</font>: u quit</br>\r\n<font color=\"red\">iamtheBMG</font>: yup</br>\r\n<font color=\"red\">iamtheBMG</font>: two weeks</br>\r\n<font color=\"red\">iamtheBMG</font>: i am going to find an apartment this weekend</br>\r\n<font color=\"red\">iamtheBMG</font>: ill be back on tuesday</br>\r\n<font color=\"blue\">Zooberries</font>: damn u could of told me u know. when were u gonna tell me? when u were in california!</br>\r\n<font color=\"blue\">Zooberries</font>: :-(</br>\r\n<font color=\"red\">iamtheBMG</font>: not until i give my two weeks</br>\r\n<font color=\"red\">iamtheBMG</font>: i am going to put in my two weeks when I get back</br>\r\n<font color=\"blue\">Zooberries</font>: ah i c. ok. i got it now. it all onthe qt</br>\r\n<font color=\"red\">iamtheBMG</font>: yup</br>\r\n<font color=\"red\">iamtheBMG</font>: its been a month since i decided. </br>\r\n<font color=\"blue\">Zooberries</font>: i c</br>\r\n<font color=\"blue\">Zooberries</font>: what instigated this</br>\r\n<font color=\"red\">iamtheBMG</font>: i cant stand to see *girl* with that another man</br>\r\n<font color=\"blue\">Zooberries</font>: WHAT!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!</br>\r\n<font color=\"blue\">Zooberries</font>: this is b/c of her? </br>\r\n<font color=\"red\">iamtheBMG</font>: partly</br>\r\n<font color=\"red\">iamtheBMG</font>: i just can\'t deal with it anymore</br>\r\n<font color=\"blue\">Zooberries</font>: hmm</br>\r\n<font color=\"blue\">Zooberries</font>: ok</br>\r\n<font color=\"red\">iamtheBMG</font>: i am surprised you are shocked</br>\r\n<font color=\"red\">iamtheBMG</font>: i thought you knew that it was my plan all along</br>\r\n<font color=\"red\">iamtheBMG</font>: i just gotsta get back to my element.</br>\r\n<font color=\"blue\">Zooberries</font>: no i didnt know</br>\r\n<font color=\"red\">iamtheBMG</font>: gotta move on...</br>\r\n<font color=\"blue\">Zooberries</font>: i see that</br>\r\n<font color=\"red\">iamtheBMG</font>: i\'ll miss you, and a few others -- but thats all i got...</br>\r\n<font color=\"blue\">Zooberries</font>: it sucks</br>\r\n<font color=\"red\">iamtheBMG</font>: guess what?</br>\r\n<font color=\"blue\">Zooberries</font>: ?</br>\r\n<font color=\"red\">iamtheBMG</font>: wanna here another secret?</br>\r\n<font color=\"red\">iamtheBMG</font>: promise me not to tell anyone, ok?</br>\r\n<font color=\"blue\">Zooberries</font>: ok</br>\r\n<font color=\"blue\">Zooberries</font>: im not telling anyone about u leaving its ok with moi</br>\r\n<font color=\"red\">iamtheBMG</font>:<font size=\"16\"><strong> GOTCHA SUCKA!!!</strong></font></br>\r\n<font color=\"blue\">Zooberries signed off at 10:29:05 PM. </font></br>\r\n<font color=\"blue\">Zooberries signed on at 10:50:15 PM.</font><br>\r\n<font color=\"red\">iamtheBMG</font>: hehe<br>\r\n<font color=\"red\">iamtheBMG</font>: you mad?<br>\r\n<font color=\"blue\">Zooberries signed off at 10:50:40 PM.</font> \r\n\r\n<p>I think zooberries is mad at me. I can\'t tell yet. You know I got nothing but love for you my man!</p>\r\n<p>I am in for it! I am scared what he will do to me =/</p>'),(169,'<P>can i just tell you how much netscape sucks ass? for example, on the splash page for this site: the car graphic overlaps on the editable text field AND the text below it... and this is not the only instance of this i have seen. it is really pathetic.\r\n</P><P>\r\ncss support sucks, layouts can\'t happen (both were better in previous versions and in general worse than IE...); it is slow to open....\r\n</P><P>\r\nit just sucks. if i could say one thing about this product i would have to say it sucks. for example, i would write to the bossman and i would say.\r\n</P>\r\n<PRE>\r\nmr. andersson:\r\n\r\ngive up. you suck.\r\n\r\nthank you for your time.\r\n\r\nregards,\r\n\r\npuppy\r\n</pre>'),(170,'<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/170_1.jpg\'\r\nheight=\'150\' align=\'left\'>\r\n<P>To transform the perception of the world and to change the structure of society is the same thing. By liberating oneself, one changed power relations and therefore transformed society. They therefore tried to construct situations which disrupt the ordinary and normal in order to jolt people out of their customary ways of thinking and acting. </P>\r\n\r\n'),(171,'16:26:43 robotec9: i\'m going to miss working with you, man\r\n<br>\r\n16:27:06 chrissnafu: ditto sir.  \r\n<br>\r\n16:27:25 chrissnafu: though you probably *won\'t* miss me screaming at the top of my lungs as if i\'m being burned by acid.  \r\n<br>\r\n16:27:28 chrissnafu: and misc. things like that.\r\n<br>\r\n16:27:35 robotec9: you will always be snafu to me.\r\n<br>\r\n16:27:44 chrissnafu: hhe\r\n<br>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/171_1.gif\' height=\'150\'><img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/171_2.gif\' height=\'150\'>'),(172,'<P>trained like a rat waiting for cheese.  It\'s dark, getting near 8 o\'clock which means Austin must be on his way.  A and I quite enjoy Austin\'s company.  Its rather strange but when it gets dark i start wondering where he might be..cruisin in the Honda civic, listening to some warrior rap...I dont know.  I dont know what Austin does when he\'s not here. he knows what were doing, the same thing we\'re doing when he arrives.  So i see how the trap has been set..destined like a rat to wait for the cheese.  cheese anxiety....is this normal? </P>'),(173,'<P>First you must light the gas water heater.  then \r\nyou must go under the deck and open the water valve.\r\n  Next you go into the house, through the kitchen to\r\n get the shampoo and soap.  then back outside, down \r\nthe path, through a little garden and wala! you have\r\n reached the shower.   if it is night you will be \r\nquick, wondering if the tarantulas are sleeping yet.\r\n  If you are like me and have to take your glasses \r\noff, you will hope they do not fall onto the earth \r\nwhere you can not find them.  are there snakes?  is \r\nthere a full moon?  do you hear the bats?  what \r\nabout the owls?  you look out across the way to the \r\nforest wondering if the spectacled bear is out \r\ntonight.  and where do those monkeys sleep and why \r\nare they so hard to see?  All the time you hear \r\nanimals... but you cann not see them.  Scent.. why \r\nis there not  a word for the loss of scent?  One can\r\n be deaf, dub or blind .. but loss of scent?  we do \r\nnot count our losses.  maybe if my sense of smell \r\nwere developed I could track the animals.  I would \r\nknow when they were close and could wait for them \r\nto show themselves. Once I had a dream that a parade \r\nof animals walked in front of me.  i was so happy \r\nwhen i woke up from that dream.  I felt that in some\r\n part of my consciousness i had been spoken to by a \r\nwhole other species.  somewhere i had slipped through \r\ninto a world other than that of humans.    i do \r\nbelieve animals communicate in ways that we can \r\nnot understand.  \r\n</P>\r\n<P>i feel really lucky to have been to a place on this planet that is so alive that i can not take a shower without being aware of that life.\r\n</P>\r\n<P>sometimes i miss the rain.</P>'),(174,'<P>\r\ni brought a piece of chocolate to work today and left it in the car\r\nthinking i\'d give it to xianflux tonight.  but i am bored now, so i may just\r\nwalk down to my car and eat it.  maybe not.  i\'m not sure.\r\n</P>\r\n<P>\r\nit is a dark chocolate piece like those i brought last time, only it\r\nis filled with dark chocolate in the center too.  the syrupie kind.\r\ndark chocolate on the outside, dark chocolate on the inside.  i had a\r\npiece last night.  it was the most chocolate experience ever.\r\nsomething about the richness of san francisco chocolate!  mmmmm.  \r\n</P>\r\n<P>\r\ncome to think of it, although xianflux and i are friends, i don\'t know if\r\nwe are such good friends she should have this piece of chocolate\r\ndownstairs in my car and not me.  she would definately appreciate this piece \r\nof chocolate sitting downstairs in the front passenger seat of my car\r\nmore than me.  but then my day is really been a continuation in direct\r\nlineage of with my hair brush falling into the toilet this morning\r\nwhilst i was readying for work.\r\n</P>\r\n<P>\r\ni deserve this piece of chocolate.\r\n</P>'),(175,'<P>\r\nI am sick and tired of this. I really am. I just got the estimate from the shop. $1300.02. I am not sure what the 2 cents is for but I am sure it is for something very important. I feel kind of sad and violated. I know it\'s just a car...but it was the very first thing I ever bought MYSELF and someone fucked it up for no reason. No reason at all.</P>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/175_1.jpg\' height=\'150\'> \r\n\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/175_2.jpg\' height=\'150\'> \r\n\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/175_3.jpg\' height=\'150\'>\r\n\r\n'),(176,'<P>happy thanksgiving all ya freaks!!\r\n</P><P>\r\ni give thanks<br>\r\nfor it <b>all</b> even though <br>\r\nsometimes i know not whether <br>\r\nthe life this flying vision <br>\r\nis sweet or sour but damn <br>\r\nit sure keeps on coming <br>\r\ndon\'t it?\r\n</P><P>\r\nwerd.  love to --\r\n</P>'),(177,'<P>Well, Thanksgiving is finally here, and we finally get to meet BMG. A long awaited day here at the alexandria house. Friends, food, and booze, my kinda day! I\'m actually looking forward to this holiday day, and thats unusual for me(I am not a holiday person). It\'s my first here in Los Angeles, and I actually have lots of things to be thankful for. I won\'t bore everyone with the details, I\'ll just say there are many.\r\nWell, it\'s time to get down to some serious cooking.....</P>'),(178,'<P>New Zealand doesn\'t celebrate Thanksgiving.  This is not because we have nothing to be thankful for, but I guess it might have something to do with the fact that our first settlers were drunken whalers.  Pilgrims are probably nicer people, but I bet the whalers would have been more fun. </P> \r\n\r\n<P>Anyways, next week, I\'ve decided to cook a Thanksgiving meal at my flat, so if you\'re in Auckland, come along and offer a genuine American perspective on it all.  Bring $5 for food costs and also, can you please bring some red plastic cups as seen in every American teen movie?  My flat is obsessed with red plastic cups.  Our friend who is working at Disneyworld over the summer has promised to bring some back for us, and then we\'re going to throw a Frat Party.  You can\'t buy them in New Zealand, but you can buy turkeys here.  Just no one really does.  </P>\r\n\r\n'),(179,'<P>I thought about my Grandma yesterday on Thanksgiving. I think about her more often than that sounded like. I want to tell her that I miss her, but she isn\'t here anymore. Happy Thanksgiving to you Grandma! I wish I could see you again.\r\n</P>\r\n<P>\r\nLove,\r\n</P>\r\n<P>\r\nScott\r\n</P>'),(180,'<P>i purchased a laptop from dell today.  i am now in a whole new league of internet professional.  i am \'mobile\'.  i can surf the net from the couch.  i can do photo shoots wearing all black.  i can be an internet barbie.</P>\r\n\r\n<P><STRONG>i owe my credit card a lot of money.</STRONG></P>\r\n\r\n<P>by the way, want to know what Internet Relay Chat is like on Eris Free NETwork?</P>\r\n<FONT SIZE=\'-2\'>\r\n<PRE>\r\nymy Closing Link: 64.210.3.222 (You are not authorized to use this server)\r\nymy Connection closed from irc.plur.net: Success\r\nymy Connecting to port 6667 of server irc.plur.net [refnum 12]\r\n[plur] Looking up your hostname...\r\n[plur] Checking Ident\r\n[plur] Your forward and reverse DNS do not match, ignoring hostname.\r\n[plur] No Ident response\r\n</pre>\r\n</FONT>\r\n<center>thanks for reading</center>'),(181,'<P>\r\nI havenâ€™t had anything to say in a while.  Makes me feel funny that people are on this site saying stuff.  I like it.\r\n</P><P>\r\nArnie wake me up at 230 am after I got back from a club downtown with cha chi, k3, bmg and mister lamas.\r\n</P><P>\r\nBeing woke up like that leaves a sick feeling in my stomach, like when I was a kid on road trips over night, driving in the car, and we would arrive at grandmaâ€™s house in boise city, Oklahoma, at 4 am.  Somebody would wake me up and transfer my little lifeless body to a sleeping bag on the floor in the living room of her home.  I would have the incredibly disturbed feeling in my gut that I have now.  It is a feeling of disturbed and unfinished dreams.  I think my mind is trapped between dimensions.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nArnold woke me up to see his latest video editing job that he worked on all day.  It is finished to a point.  While he played it for me, I had several dreams.  In and out of dream land in two minutes.  Weaved reality.\r\n</P><P>\r\nNow the edges of my eyes hurt around the corners.  I need water and I need the will to drift back into dream land.  Right now I am involuntarily fighting it.  But in a few moments, I will be sleeping again.\r\n</P>\r\n<P>I\'m glad I woke up.  I\'m glad I am going back to sleep now.</P>'),(182,'<P>El Paso ,The giant truck stop of Texas,which backs right up to the armpit of the world,Jaurez.Every time I go back I remember why I left,its brown ,its dirty the kind of dirty you can see from several hundred feet in the air before you land.The Smog billows up and over the border from Jaurez ,the color alone makes my eyes burn,I guess their a little behind in clean air controls.</P>\r\n <P>But this time I went down to El Paso to attend a hearing involving A child support suit that my mother has placed against my father in yet another chapter of this 26 year old fued.So lets sum up, shitty air ,dirty brown suburbs,Stressfull family shit and nowhere to get decent cup of coffee ,as you can tell I  didn\'t have any fun and it cost me 300 dollars due to  short notice and the friggin holiday.I\'d also like thank the Judge for asking both council for a brief so I can fly back in 30 days,just in time for Christmas.</P>\r\n<P>I wish I was a test tube baby.</P>'),(183,'<center><img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/183_1.jpg\'></center>\r\n<br>\r\n<center>dog with viberating ears, sean@<a href=\'http://durak.org\'>durak.org</a></center>'),(184,'<P>Good morning america.  I have work to do that will involve me\r\nthinking.  I don\'t feel like thinking right now, so I am not working.\r\nI\'m just floating around like the homeless junk boat people in Hong\r\nKong.  By the way, we are meeting in Hong Kong late july of 2003 if\r\nyou want to go.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I have a large thanksgiving plate of leftover stuff that I am not\r\nsupposed to talk about.  I should put it in a time release file to\r\nsurface one year from today after everyone that I know no longer\r\nremembers who I am or cares what I think.</P>\r\n\r\n<P><I>What are you referring to austin?</I></P>\r\n\r\n<ul type=box>\r\n<li>romance\r\n<li>people I don\'t like\r\n<li>life at work\r\n<li>things that I don\'t always get my way on\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<P>You know what I mean.  I just feel like cranking.  \r\nNormally I would say bitching, but now that I hang out with feminists\r\nagain, I can\'t say that. If I am cranky, and I say bitchy,\r\nbitchy=cranky and since it is understood that the slang \'bitch\'\r\nreferred to women asserting themselves long before before it referred\r\nto cranky men, it is like saying that I am acting like a woman.  By\r\nassociation, that woman would be cranky.  Extrapolate: all women that\r\nassert themselves are not disenfranchised human beings, but cranky\r\nbitches not accepting their roles.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Everything that is not polite in the world that we all deal with individually all the time but never talk about because if we did talk about it, people would hate us, is what I am feeling today.  Talking about it is blowing the cover, losing the confidence game.  It is the underlying truth behind superstition.  If you break an antique mirror lined with silver, the owner of that mirror is going to hate you for 7 years.  If you talk about people behind their back, those people will grow to dislike you after they no longer trust you.  It is not bad luck, it is bad policy.</P>\r\n\r\n<P><I>Deep breaths...</I></P>\r\n\r\n<P>If you want to know what I really think, email me and I\'ll tell you all the things that don\'t mean anything to you but would make a specific other person very angry.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Oh me oh my, is this what it has come to?  I hope not.  I want to talk about evil villains and beautiful women.  Maybe tomorrow.  Maybe I just need to go digging in the archive to find out what sorts of things I used to think were interesting.  Oh, I know, restaurant reviews and stuff like that.  Also name dropping.  Jesus, I am not having a nice warm fuzzy day today.  Ask me why? why?  I can\'t tell you.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>In the mean time, why not ask yourself why you never ask me any questions?  I shouldn\'t always be the one to write original things.  I\'d like to answer some questions every now and then.</P> \r\n\r\n<P>I know what it is.  It is these damn dress shoes I am wearing.  They are uncomfortable and are turning me into a marketing person.  I need some sneakers.  You are reading my mind rebelling against the unkown.</P>'),(185,'11-27-00<br><img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/185_1.jpg\'>'),(186,'<P>It is someone who chooses the opt out of a relationship?  Sometimes hearts get broken, so lovers leave.  It is the person who has no estimable reason for breaking up, just because.  Sometimes they have a reason. </P>\r\n\r\n<P>My personal favorite is the one where the I don\'t want to break up and it is my fault.  Funny that I am familiar with that one, even though that has never really happened to me.  I have always known they were over before they were over.  Attribute this to early warning signals.</P>\r\n\r\n<ul type=square>\r\n <li>Eyes not contacting.  \r\n <li>Conversations not flowing.  \r\n <li>Leaving the coat on inside the bedroom.  \r\n <li>The beady eyed and furrowed brow Neanderthal, \"get away,\" look.\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n'),(187,'<center>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/187_1.jpg\'>\r\n<p>these are for keeks.</P>\r\n</center>'),(188,'<P>Austin is a beautiful city.  I think I just needed a break from there.  I am not saying I\'ll go back, but I did need a break.  I don\'t think anything will be left of it by the time I might move back.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI was at dinner with the crew last night and somebody asked me if it was hard to find work in LA and I said compared to what?  Compared to Austin it is easy.  Why?  Because there are too many smart people there and a test tube economy that can\'t support it\'s baby food spoon.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI worked at an Internet startup there that employed college graduates to do monkey work.  I knew it was time to go when they started hiring high-school students.  I assume it was to pay less.  Fuck that.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI have friends who couldn\'t find jobs.  There are college graduates at the day labor pool trying to get jobs as lawn mower studs.\r\n</P><P>\r\nWhat is worse than this is that there is nothing left of what I loved about Austin.  No more Conan\'s Pizza.  The entire drag has been replaced with Urban Outfitters.  Christ, I can\'t even remember how many stores closed.  I just remember walking down the street and talking about what store closed because of rent increases that week.  No more hanging out with college friends because they have scattered themselves back to where they came from.  Fuck it, I never really gave a shit about Conan\'s Pizza.  It was the friends.  Once you have lived somewhere with all your greatest friends and then they leave, every last one of them, life becomes difficult.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI couldn\'t make friends like those again in Austin.  JJ, Apurv, K-Dogg, Spleevin, Delorenzi, all the co-op people that I liked.  Fuck, I don\'t know.  I lost a lot of friends.\r\n</P><P>\r\nNow I live in Los Angeles.  I have great friends here.  I don\'t want to go back to Texas.  I will never graduate from UT.  I don\'t like that place.  Ask me why?  Because they don\'t have Texas Studies!\r\n</P><P>\r\nOh well...  BMG just visited, and my brother scott will be here in January to see Shellac.</P>\r\n<P>And I miss Bender.</P>'),(189,'<P>I have the opportunity to move into a new-to-me house, out of my old-to-me shitty two story mobile home.  I wanted to.  I still want to.  The rent is kind of steep, though a good deal for me.  I\'d love to live there so I guess I\'ll do it.  It is a one bedroom cottage with a kitchen and living room, yard and drive way.  Pretty nice for a loser like me.  It would be nice because it doesn\'t smell like old people.  It smells like firewood.  Firewood is more acceptable.  Though still stinky.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Rent is 150 more than what I pay now.  I think I can do that.  I will need a raise sooner than later though because bills will be difficult to pay.  I should just sell my car and become a disciple of cha chi\'s dad, the eco-hermit.  that sounds more attractive than getting a raise.  funny that would be the case.  maybe i am not as America as i seem. <tt>=-P</tt></P>\r\n\r\n<P><a href=\'http://durak.org/sean/\'>Sean would be jealous</a> of my lawn even though he complains about Los Angeles\' smog when he lives in San Francisco.</P>\r\n\r\n'),(190,'<PRE>i\'m locked in here with the silver bitch\r\nshe\'s looking good\r\neyes going all off in separate directions\r\npull up your shirt and gleam\r\nilluminate the room \r\ntravesty\r\napostasy \r\npretty pink eye sockets</PRE>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/190_1.gif\'>'),(191,'<P> \r\nJ: Hi austin, how are you doing?\r\n</P><P>\r\nA:  I am depressed.  I want to move but it is pointless to move to another lonely one person apartment where no one will visit me.\r\n</P><P>\r\nJ: Like the one you have already?\r\n</P><P>\r\nA:  Yea, just like that one.\r\n</P><P>\r\nJ:  You know, you never even give the address out?  I\'m sure somebody would come visit you if you invited them over.\r\n</P><P>\r\nA:  Yea, probably.  But I hate the place.  There is no where to sit and I am boring by myself.  I can only work off other people.  I am a social parasite, feeding off groups.\r\n</P><P>\r\nJ:  Wow, you really think so?  That is kind of sick.  Maybe you should get some help with that.  I can give you advice, but I\'m hardly objective.\r\n</P><P>\r\nA: Tell me about it.  Talking to you is like talking to the mirror.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nA: I did get health insurance today from ibiz.com.  Whupty fucking shit.  I never go to the doctor.  The only thing health insurance is good for is popping pharmies for recreation.\r\n</P><P>\r\nJ: Back to my last statement...\r\n</P><P>\r\nA:  Yea yea yea, been there, not going back.  I think it would make a good suplementary income, slinging pharmies.\r\n</P><P>\r\nJ:  Save yourself the trouble.  <b>I</b> have done that, did some time, too.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nA:  Wow, what a dumb reason to get put away.\r\n</P><P>\r\nJ:  Okay, don\'t go there.\r\n</P><P>\r\nA:  As I was saying, I think I shouldn\'t move into this house because it will not solve anything for me.  I will still run from loneliness and hang out too much at alexandria house.\r\n</P><P>\r\nJ:  Didn\'t steph say you should just live in the alexandria house closet?\r\n</P><P>\r\nA:  Yea, I actually think the broken down minivan would be a cool crib.  I don\'t think they like me hanging around so much already.  As it is, they get a break from my ass taking up space when I go home to sleep.\r\n</P><P>\r\nJ:  ...and when you go to work.\r\n</P><P>\r\nA: Yea, then too.  You know, sometimes I think I should just move to Houston and live near my Dad.  Or live with my brother Scott in Dallas.  They would not get sick of me.\r\n</P><P>\r\nJ:  Whatever dude, I doubt it.  They would get sick of you.  AND you would be hella sick of those cities in under a month.  Not to mention it is cold in the winter and hot in the summer, unlike beautiful California.\r\n</P><P>\r\nA:  You are right.  I love the weather here.  It is like shorts and a tee shirt for six months and sweatshirts for six months.  If you play your cards right, you can go for eleven months without breaking a sweat.\r\n</P><P>\r\nJ:  I have to get back to work...\r\n</P><P>\r\nA:  uhg, work.\r\n</P><P>\r\nJ:  I know.  I can\'t wait to retire.\r\n</P><P>\r\nA:  me2,  peace.out\r\n</P><P>\r\nJ:  rite rite\r\n</P>'),(192,'<p>I had planned not to go to my Company Christmas party for the past 4 weeks. Now, the day before the party, I am being blackmailed into going. Its a blind date thing, and it is scary to me. I don\'t act well in these types of situations. I am either too silly or too serious.</p>\r\n<p>Now I have to go buy slacks cause the only slacks i have are for a 250lb gorrila. I am a 200lb gorilla, therefore the slacks don\'t fit. I will probably buy a tie too. I dont wanna buy either. I should have made an excuse. I am such a sucka! I will probably have a good time, I don\'t know why I am such a dork.</p>\r\n<p>On another subject, I had a great time in Los Angeles. I am so very honored to have spent the time with such beautiful people. Thanks for sharing yourselves. I hope to return the favor at some point. Best of luck to all of you!</p>\r\n<p>bmg</p>'),(193,'<P>im a flashback person. im in class, not listening to lecture, flashbacking. im at the cafeteria, eating and flashbacking. and since its december im flashbacking to last december. </P>\r\n\r\n<P>its like punching an old bruise over and over again, remembering how things went down that december. ever since january, i was bitter about everything - how we broke up, the lies, and just him. like why the fuck did i pick him? why the hell did i stay with him? why couldnt he be a man and leave me instead of cheating on me? \r\n</P><P>\r\nguess if i was a good person i wouldn\'t have told everyone what an asshole he was for doing the things he done, and if i was a better person i wouldnt be so bitter about that relationship.\r\n</P><P>\r\ncuz in the meantime i kept overlooking the fact that a friend of mine wanted to hook up, kept overlooking the fact that i should move on. \r\n</P><P>\r\nso now i have a new bf, part of me is still hurt, still scared as fuck that the same ol shit will happen again. im sure he\'s tired of me of the but\'s or maybe\'s.  maybe we wont work out, but i guess im willing to gamble.\r\n</P><P>\r\nmy ex is calling tomorrow...i want to ask him if he really did fuck that girl and why came running back to me...should i? i probably won\'t ... gotta remember the ex-ho and wannabe playa is the past not the future - unless I swing that way.</P>'),(194,'<P>Those of you that follow swinney org might have seen a posting by me saying that my flat was planning on holding a traditional American Style Thanksgiving Dinner this year - despite the fact that we live in New Zealand, are not American, it\'s summer here and no family were invited.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I think that\'s maybe why today was so good.  I did the turkey and the pumpkin pies and everything, but there were no family feuds.  We weren\'t trapped in the house by blizzards  - instead we lay out in the sun getting even drunker after stuffing ourselves full of the lunch.  However, as the whole idea was based on the Thanksgiving episode of Dawson\'s Creek, I made everyone stand around in a circle, hold hands and say what they were thankful for.  It was super super cheesy, but it did also seem kind of appropriate and sweet and nice and stuff.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Or maybe I\'m just really happy from drinking for 12 hours and still being elated that the first time I ever cooked a turkey (something even my mother never tried) it turned out perfectly!</P>'),(195,'<P>This last week, the date is not important, I go to bed with a mug of hot mint tea and the only pieces of historical literature I own.  Two bibles, one in English, the Oxford translation, the other in English also, but the Jewish publication translation. I root around in them for some of the old passages I studied once.  Mostly the Law and Kings.  I have never read anything in the New Testament. </P>\r\n\r\n<P>I listen to classical music.  It is a charming scene.  I sit, read, compare translations, listen to music, turn out the light, and fall asleep.  Sometimes I fall asleep and later turn out the light.  Then I can\'t go back to sleep for a few minutes.  But I fall back into sleep soon enough.  Some nights I leave the radio on.  When I do, it is because I am curious what my mind will do with the sound as I sleep.  Also because the music is beautiful.  In the past, I left it on the news station playing the BBC.  Now just the classical station.\r\n\r\n</P><P>\r\nWithout fail, I wake up in the late hours of morning before dawn stretches her rosy red fingers across the sky, and in the twilight of darkness will ring the sound of angels.  Their voices are accompanied by stringed instruments.  Then I turn the volume off annoyed, roll over, and fall back to sleep.\r\n</P><P>\r\nDave, are you listening?  You are probably in a monastery somewhere.  I stopped by a photo of us hanging in the hallway, on my way to bed tonight.  It is the picture of kdog, jebro, you and I.  I miss you Dave.  I always will.  I miss my books too.</P>\r\n'),(196,'<center>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/196_1.jpg\'>\r\n</center>'),(197,'<P>that last entry, with its little bit about the dawn and her rosy red fingers, made me smile because it reminded me of something from a billion years ago.  see, one of my (many) nicknames is \"rosy-fingered dawn\". it got tagged on me by my college pal tony, who\'d spent a lot of time reading \"the odyssey\" one semester.\r\n</P>\r\n<P>\r\nanyway... well-after this nickname stuck, i got invited to an ides of march costume party. word on the street was that if you wanted to attend, you had to dress up as a classical god or goddess. or at the very least wear a toga.  being the clever monkey i am, i dressed up in a mess of gauze curtains, slapped some red nail polish all over my fingertips, and headed for the party. \r\n</P>\r\n<P>\r\nwhen i got there, my friends looked me over and said, squinting, \"hey! who the hell are YOU supposed to be?!?\"  i stuck out my arms like a six-year-old, waggled my fingers, and yelled, \"i\'m rosy-fingered dawn!!!!!!\"\r\n</P>\r\n<P>\r\nthen i went to the keg and drank some beer.  a lot of beer.  i\'m still not sure how my sheets managed to stay on.\r\n</P>'),(198,'<P>To <i>complain</i>.  I began to complain in order to start working.  Nothing about the job was prepped to make it easier for me.  So I complain.  Nowadays, whenever I write the word complain, I think of Bartholomew Mule\'s character Rollie played by the perpetual (ex)boyfriend of Xianfoy.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Complain with a <i>\'t</i>.  I think how Xianfoy is strapped on a rollercoaster of complaint, and how her boyfriend is the main character of this short movie called \"Complain\",  a movie about a man who takes even the most severe form of complaint, suicide, lightly.  Also how Xianfoy screams at Arnold sometimes over a slight complaint.  How the entire culture of this house where everyone meets is permeated by argument.  At its core, the argument often seems just complaint.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>It has distorted and destroyed the word \'complain\' for me.  When I say \'complain\', I thank God that it isn\'t so bad.  And it isn\'t.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Complain with an <i>\'ing</i>. People hang around here complaining because they love each other.  They could stop complaining, but then the energy of complaint might not make it out in some other form. It might turn into a horrible cancer, or unhappiness as a form of listlessness.  Energy does bad things when not let out.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>There is always that hope in hearts that complaining can turn into kisses.  All that energy, and it is amazing at times, like the pillar of fiery God, might one day be put to beautiful use.  If you can\'t be happy, and you are not complaining about it; then were you happy, what use would you be to society?  Who needs a Buda that doesn\'t talk, that is like the hippy with a brain tumor.  I\'d rather have a Buda that screams at the top of her lungs.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I am holding out for people to run out the back of the house throwing flowers and chocolate, screaming, \"I love the world, and I love you!\"  That would be beauty.</P>\r\n'),(199,'<pre>\r\n<knox> If you have access to      #########       These hashes are supposed\r\n<knox> a set of female genitals    #######        to be pubic hair covering\r\n<knox> I\'d suggest that you         #####         the pudendum.\r\n<knox> compare them with this        ###\r\n<knox> schematic. Single females\r\n<knox> might like to use a mirror    /U\\          U is the clitoris\r\n<knox> (or two) to verify that     /\' . `\\        . is the urethra\r\n<knox> they\'re set up like this.  /\'  _  `\\       The rest of the characters\r\n<knox> I should probably say     { | / \\ | }      are supposed to be the outer\r\n<knox> that this is intended to  { ` \\ / \' }      lips (labia majora), the inner\r\n<knox> represent a view of the    \\ ` ~ \' /       lips (labia minora), and the\r\n<knox> genitals with legs spread,  \\ ` \' /        vagina (or is that vulva?)\r\n<knox> looking up through the torso  ~|~\r\n<knox> as if the woman were a         O           O is the anus\r\n<knox> telescope.\r\n</pre>'),(200,'<h3>Staring the swordplay of Kaz, Leonard, Robotec9, Adamaja.</h3>\r\n\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/200_1.gif\'>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/200_2.gif\'>\r\n\r\n<P><a href=\"http://neopets.com\">Neopets of course...</a></P>'),(201,'<PRE>\r\nÃ¹Ã­Ã¹ mode/#rant [+oooo halos knox robotec9 robotec9_] by QJ\r\nÃ¹Ã­Ã¹ mode/#rant [-o robotec9] by QJ\r\nÃ¹Ã­Ã¹ #rant  You can\'t do that thing, when you don\'t have \r\nthat swing (You\'re not channel operator)\r\nÃ¹Ã­Ã¹ mode/#rant [-o robotec9_] by QJ\r\nKatana: spread the love\r\nKatana: and take some away\r\nQJ: anyone know who robotec9 is?\r\nÃ¹Ã­Ã¹ mode/#rant [-o+b robotec9 *!*life@64.210.3.*] by QJ\r\n>>> You have been kicked off #rant by QJ (prole)\r\nÃ¹Ã­Ã¹ [#rant] Banned from channel\r\n</PRE>\r\n\r\n<P>Ahhh, democracy of the internet...  fucked off.</P>'),(202,'<P>ya know aus, i feel bad that i still have your blankey. i feel worse that i havent been able to get my pedestrian ass to the post office and send it out to you.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>last night i couldnt sleep, which pissed me off considering i had a 7 o\'clock final, and for some reason i kept having flashes of you and your blankey. how i had broken that bond. how you must hate me. how my children will end up to be the spawn of satan.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i quickly mapped out a plan to send your blankey in time for xmas so that you could have one of those hallmark-feel-oh-so-good christmas.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>but i still felt bad. no, i told myself, i must redeem myself of all my sins.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>so if you want your blankey, you will visit me and i will take you out. you like lap dances?</P>\r\n\r\n'),(203,'<P>i wanted pizza tonight at 11 pm and there was no place to get it.  all closed at 11 pm on mondays.  man, that is not why i moved here.  i was so angry i would have phoned the mayor, whoever it is, to vent.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>after digging around on losangeles.citysearch.com for the phone number of the pizza hut five blocks away.  Bubkiss.  aparently pizza hut did not pay off citysearch this month.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>when i finally did get the number for a pizza hut: closed at 11 o\'clock.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i spit. i cursed.  i wanted to slam and kick.  i went to check if my car was still blocked in.  it wasn\'t.  i left arnold asleep in the COMMAND CENTER and headed to Albertson\'s to buy some jones root beer and stoffer\'s pizza boats.  i cought all those lights that stop changing regularly at 11 pm.  long seven minute lights.  i sat and watched cars go by at intervals of 45 seconds to a minute.  i screamed. i got to the grocery store and was out inside of 4 minutes.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>on the way back, i was trapped behind a twenty mile per hour cadillac.  fuck me running.  i screamed.  i ranted.  i stopped at a seven minute light.  long intervals of silence in the world.  car passes.  on the radio, alan watts the esteemed zen master talked about the fabric of the universe in the chinese neo buddist term LI, traditionally meaning \'jade etchings\' or \'muscle fiber\'.  give me some green! i yelled.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>the rest of the drive home was a warp.  i don\'t remember it.  only pulling into the parking place.  the rest of the time i was preoccupied with alan watts being a christian therapist, listening to him attempt to make troubled christian followers more comfortable with being wrong about God.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>god the humanoid.  is a tree made of wood? no, a tree is wood.  is a mountain made of rock.  no, a mountain is rock.  is the universe made of god? no, the universe is god.  god the pattern.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>now i want to be like all my friends: jobless.  but i have to be off to bed and then off to work.  maybe my life will be changed for ever tomorrow.  i know i have to remain open to that sort of thing.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>hi le, how\'s your li?</P>'),(204,'<p>I promise much, deliver little. I know this; I am going to send Austin and Arnie toys. Christmas presents if you can call them that.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Arnold, I promise you this:</p>\r\n\r\n<li>One SCCSI hard drive for your akai recorder\r\n<li>Adobe Premiere 5.0 (I found the pc version!, no mac yet)\r\n<li>Something else, I canâ€™t remember right now (do you remember? <a href=\"mailto:bmg@lepard.org\">bmg@lepard.org</a>)\r\n\r\n<p>Austin, I promise you this:</p>\r\n\r\n<li>One lynksis router (oh you know how much I love it)\r\n<li>Hundred feet of CAT5 wire (you bye the connectors)\r\n<li>And something else, I think (do you remember?<a href=\"mailto:bmg@lepard.org\">bmg@lepard.org</a>)\r\n\r\n<p>I am thinking that the reason I canâ€™t get redhat 6.0 to install on my new server at work is because I made these promises and have not yet delivered. Bad karma to say youâ€™ll do something then to not do what you said you would do. I am trying my brothers, really truly I am! A little more time! </p>\r\n\r\n<p>I am at work, its 5 am. I have been here since about 3 am trying to get this damn box up. Problem is, it has a very old ISA video card, and it can barely render the install screen. I am going to ask for a new video card. I want to use the GUI damn it! Please! I want to feel cool, and to use the KDE 2. Please let me have at least that! Ok, you linux dorks, I am sure you are going to say, â€œwell, if you are configuring a server you donâ€™t need the gui, you can do it all command line.â€ NO MR. LINUX! I WANT THE GUI!!!! </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Ok, I am not that mad, but it sure would be nice to configure everything with KDE. As soon as I set it all up I wonâ€™t need to use the gui, I swear. </p>\r\n\r\n<hr>\r\n<p>I had weird dreams last night. I dreamt that my great grandmother was still alive, and that she was in the hospital. All my homies were there, and the damn phone kept ringing. When some one would answer the phone, no one would be there. Then my great grandmother, Laurina Pearl, noticed that she had the word evil tattooed on her chest. Sure enough right below her throat was the word â€œevil.â€ We thought that the surgeon on of the nurses did it. We all freaked out pretty heavily, including Laurina Pearl. Then dream started to speed up rapidly, phones ringing, Laurina Pearl speaking Spanish into the phone and then <strong> *poof*</strong> the bed is gone, and in its place is a tv with my great grandmother crying on the screen. I run franticly around the room, looking for the people that were there moments ago, no one is in the room besides me. Nothing is in the room. No windows, no pictures no tv, no chairs, or lights. I am freekin! I run down the hall, its not a hospital I realize. I run down some spiral stairs that are made of wood, and I end up in a room with a little boy in it. The little boy has just rolled a â€œdrumâ€ brand cigarette and I ask him how much it will cost me for a smoke. He replies that it will cost me a dollar. I think to myself that a dollar is a bit steep for the depression. I offer him a nickel, and I get a toke. He tells me that he knows where my purpose isâ€¦ I wake up. And this is why I am here at work...</p>\r\n<p>Whew, what a nightâ€¦</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n <p>For those interested, my blind date was greatâ€¦ read about it here on\r\n<a href=\"http://www.jessejoker.org/display_entrys1.php\"> jesseâ€™s site</a>. </p>\r\n<p>well its back to the boxâ€¦ Just felt like sharing what is going on in my head. No more coffee, chris.</p>\r\n'),(205,'TAKE ECSTASY WITH ME<br>\r\n(from \'holiday\' by the magnetic fields)\r\n</p><p>\r\nYou used to slide down the carpeted stairs or down the bannisteryou stuttered like a kaleidoscope \'cause you knew too many words \r\nyou used to make ginger bread houses we used to have taffy pulls\r\n</p><p>\r\nchorus: Take ecstasy with me baby take ecstasy with me.  \r\n</p><p>\r\nYou had a black snowmobile we drove out under the northern lights a vodka bottle gave you those raccoon eyes we got beat up just for holding\r\nhands \r\n</p><p>\r\nchorus: Take ecstasy with me baby take ecstasy with me.  \r\n</p><p>\r\n<a href=\"http://www.uffda.com/~le/mp3/Magnetic%20Fields%20-%20Take%20Ecstacy%20With%20Me.mp3\">howabout an mp3?</a>\r\n</p><p>\r\n<b>also:</b> everything\'s gonna be ok.'),(206,'<P>So...I was lonely and bored in LA.  Picked up shop and moved to Silicon Valley.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Now...I\'m lonely and bored in San Jose.  Damn.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>But at least my salary doubled.  Oh, and work gave me a laptop with bad RAM.  Whooo!</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Somebody come visit me.</P>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/206_1.gif\' width=400>'),(207,'<P>I have been falling asleep at strange times lately.  early like 11.  then i wake up now, like 2.  wee hours of the morning is a good time to be in irc and not much else.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i wish i were out patrolling the streets like batman or rorschach.  nah, i\'d get hurt.  i wish i were riding on the back of a garbage truck.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>hang on for dear life.</P>'),(208,'<a href=\"http://oof.diaryland.com/assoonas.html\">here it is</a>'),(209,'no'),(3276,'<br><br>Dear Sir/Ma\\\'am:<br><br>\r\nI greet you in the name of our Lord. My name is Poonlarp. I am a widow and a mother of two, all girls. I know you will see my letter to you as an embarrassment considering the fact that we do not know each other. I plead with you to be patient with me. I feel very pleased to contact you for\r\nsome assistance and business relationship. I live in Nigeria with my children. My late husband was a loving, caring and hardworking businessman who died unfortunately in a ghastly auto crash. Before the sudden death of my beloved husband, and father of my daughters, my late husband intended to establish a business in the united states of America with the sum of $30 million United States Dollars, but unfortunately he died before this proposed venture.<br><br>\r\nFollowing his death, his family members insisted that I am not entitled to his property (Assets and money) since I am a woman and my offspring\\\'s\r\nall girls as I do not have a male child for my husband. Well, according to some barbaric traditional laws here in Nigeria (Africa) which doesn\\\'t permit a woman to inherit a man\\\'s property, as they are expected by tradition to take over the management of his business and other properties including myself who automatically becomes a wife to one of his immediate brothers. Unfortunately to this wicked family members, the $30million United States Dollars which my late husband intended to use in establishing a business in the United States was deposited in a bank account unknown to his family. I and the lawyer is the only one aware of this money, so I have discussed this matter with a staff of the bank that I want this money personally so that I will be able to take care of my children\\\'s educational needs since my husband\\\'s family members vehemently opposed the furtherance of their education. According to the staff of the bank, the best way to secure this money is to transfer this money to a bank account outside Nigeria for safe-keeping, later it will be used for business establishment subject to\r\nthe advice of whosoever finally assists us. At this juncture, I therefore ask for your sincere assistance in providing us with your bank details and the enablement to facilitate the remittance of this fund into your nominated account. As soon as I get your positive response, I shall provide you with all the necessary detail for this transfer. However, I have decided to to give you 30% of the total money as a reward for your sincere assistance and the remaining 70% of the money will be for my investment as I will want to\r\nkeep aglow my late husbands dream of investing in real estate. <br><Br>\r\nTo be able to help me, kindly send through my email, your personal details including your\r\ncontact information for easy communication.<br><br>\r\nThanking you for your anticipated response,<br>\r\nPoonlarp<br>\r\n'),(210,'<P>I am at 65% geekness.  Yesterday I went into Fry\'s Electronics and\r\nasked the sales guy at the networking isle if he had a \"Linksys\r\nEtherfast 10/100 56K PC card.\"  I stopped in my tracks and my eyes\r\nleaped out of my skull, whipped around and stared at myself with\r\namazement.  Did I just say that?  Wierd.  Then I bought a Linksys\r\nEtherfast DSL modem.  To make my arguement stronger, I put Linux on my\r\nnew dell laptop without ever booting the preinstalled operating system\r\nfrom Redmond.  Wierd.  Anyone who has installed Linux in the last 2\r\nyears, and especially previous to that, has a horror experience trying\r\nto install it.  Well, I have anyway.  And I went to put it on this new\r\n1700 dollar machine.  Arnie wanted to know why I wasn\'t happy that I\r\nhad a new computer?  Because I was anticipating a hellish night trying\r\nto get X window manager to recognise my video card.  But Yeo, it went\r\non without a problem.  It was beautiful.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Then, this morning I set up the home office network at Alexandria\r\nHouse.  That too went smooth with some help from BMG and <a\r\nhref=\"http://benderbooks.com\">Happy Benway</A>, especially for Apple\r\nG4 help.  Mims hates apples and all their kin.  So anyway, the net is\r\nall functioning.  I have to go next door to Kiki\'s and swap out her\r\nGateway modem with one of my many NIC cards.  I have too damn many.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>After that I need to get my laptop online and customize it.  I hates\r\nthe defaults.  It needs sexy pics on the desktop.  I\'ll bust into my\r\ncollection of <a href=\'http://wallflower.nu\'>wallflowers</a> to that\r\nend.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>So whatever happens to me today, I thought after the network, I have\r\ndone my daily accomplishments for the day.  Turns out I wasn\'t done\r\nyet though.  I finished the Ibiz International Image Patent Manager\r\nfor ibiz.com.  Sweet.  I\'m having such a good day.</P>'),(211,'<CENTER>\r\n<h1><TT>I do not know why poundrant hates me so much.</TT></h1>\r\n<img src=\'http://www.chiamattt.com/o/weapon/robot.jpg\'>\r\n<h1><TT>I will not give up.</TT></h1>\r\n<img src=\'http://www.chiamattt.com/o/weapon/mgun.jpg\'>\r\n<h1><TT>I will never surrender.</TT></h1>\r\n<img src=\'http://www.chiamattt.com/o/weapon/chemical.jpg\'>\r\n</CENTER>'),(212,'<P>i\'ve said it ever since i got to college, but now i actually mean it. im leavin computer science for good. this is my last quarter as a computer science major.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>ya know what? im actually gonna miss it.  cuz when people asked me what i was majoring in they looked at me with that sort of admiration, that \"dude you must be smart\" look, well that and the \"ugh freak!\" look. the best part was that i surprisingly made a lot of unlikely friends. </P>\r\n\r\n<P>this quarter i was in a software engineering group with four other guys. they were hardcore. they loved this shit. they loved wires, memory, and plastic parts. they prolly could reinvent the term \"cyber sex\". and thats what finally made me leave. i admired they way they loved what they were doing...i want that too. well not the unnatural love for wires part.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>so this is for the guys and all the other hardcore peeps...keep it up guys</P>\r\n'),(213,' Austin shows up at the Alexandria house every evening and in the pockets of his jacket he keeps a piece of very fine chocolate for someone.   Sometimes i find the chocolate hiding on my desk.  Occasionally, he gives it to one of the other girls, and then i have to sit and watch them eat their chocolate.  He only brings one piece a day.  Some days, its your day.  Some days, its not.  I told him we\'re like sea lions at the aquarium, when the trainer comes by with a pocket of fish.  Not all the sea lions get a fish everytime.\r\n\r\n'),(214,' Austin shows up at the Alexandria house every evening and in the pockets of his jacket he keeps a piece of very fine chocolate for someone.   Sometimes i find the chocolate hiding on my desk.  Occasionally, he gives it to one of the other girls, and then i have to sit and watch them eat their chocolate.  He only brings one piece a day.  Some days, it\'s your day.  Some days, it\'s not.  I told him we\'re like sea lions at the aquarium when the trainer comes by with a pocket of fish.  Not all the sea lions get a fish everytime.\r\n\r\n'),(215,'<p>Austin shows up at the Alexandria house every evening and in the pockets of his jacket he keeps a piece of very fine chocolate for someone.   Sometimes i find the chocolate hiding on my desk.  Occasionally, he gives it to one of the other girls, and then i have to sit and watch them eat their chocolate.  He only brings one piece a day.  Some days, it\'s your day.  Some days, it\'s not.  I told him we\'re like sea lions at the aquarium when the trainer comes by with a pocket of fish.  Not all the sea lions get a fish everytime.</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/215_1.jpg\'>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n'),(216,'<P>Rainy weather has got me slipping and tripping in my loafers.  LOAFERS!  That\'s right, I wear loafers because I am a slacker.   Nobody slacks like me.  But let us get the definition of slacker out of the way.  By my definition, a slacker has to have something he or she is supposed to be doing.  You can\'t not have a job and be a slacker.  People that don\'t have jobs are in my conservative opinion not slackers but losers.  There, I said it.  Put the shit bags on my doorstep. BUT KNOW THIS:  i want to be a loser, it just doesn\'t make economic sense to me.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Slacking is really and economic philosophy.  Slackers should be deported from the great United States of America.  We don\'t play the game right.  We work twenty hour a week jobs in fifty hours.  We dress nicer when we are doing less.  We don\'t take showers necessarily or wash our clothes usually, but yet appear neat and clean.  It is a game of deception.  The slacker will be the last discovered.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>It is not about hawking modonna\'s pubic hairs to tourists like in the movie <i>Slacker</i>.  It is about feeling entitled to time.  Time is the slacker\'s.  Work is the spice of time.  Over spiced time is ruined.  Under spiced time is bland.  The culinary masterpiece is subtle yet provocative of beauty in flavor.  One does not over consume a masterpiece.  Moderation.  The slacker has several bites.  He is not a hog or a hunger artist.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Slacking is a respectable style necessitated by the time and place that the slacker lives in.  It is no wonder that it has a corresponding religion.  I don\'t know much about that religion.  Religion is too excessive for me.  I think like most pursuits, there are those that live the adventure, and those who research it: religion.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>It is time for me to get back to my fifteen minutes of work for the hour.  Thanks for taking your fifteen minutes on this web site, or more if the case may be.</P>\r\n'),(217,'<P>I\'ve given up on a girlfriend, school and ottawa, but I will never give up on my page and I will never give up trying to be a part of pound rant. Perhaps the most important reason I go into rant is because I like talking with le. She\'s cool and I respect her a lot. From le\'s page I noticed that a lot of the people in poundrant were cool and mysterious as well and ever since then i\'ve sort of had a hard on for the channel.</P>\r\n<P>I\'ve given in to all the rant rules I can figure out. I\'ve shut off and stopped using away/back messages and I try and talk as little as possible. Those seemed to be the biggest reasons for me getting banned and so I tried to fit in. Things seemed to be going ok. I idled and stayed in teh channel kick/ban free for about two weeks and then boom.</P>\r\n<P>Perhaps i\'m getting kicked for other reasons. Reasons involving my lack++ of computer knowledge--. As easy as it would be to just tell them all to fuck off and take the channel over with 4 botnets and some spray painted keyboards and monitors that project images into the faces of the user, I must admit that I think a lot of the people in pound rant are interesting and nice.</P>\r\n<P>I miss rant. </P>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/217_1.jpg\'>\r\n'),(218,'<IMG SRC=\"http://swinney.org/journals/images/218_1.jpg\" width=400>\r\n\r\n<P>I think there must be a sign on my forehead or there was an instructional meeting for people to learn how to ask me to do something w/out me saying no. I can\'t say no. I don\'t know why can\'t I? Why is that? Do you know? </P>\r\n\r\n<P>Most of the time it\'s not a big deal. Like the other day, Chuck and I were eating at Mario\'s and some Redskin fan asked me to hold her table down while she got up. By the way, she was a BIG Redskin fan...if you know what I mean. I had to press down w/ all of my weight to keep the table steady. That was no big deal. I could have said no but I was caught off guard. It\'s okay, though, she needed help up. But that was not the end of me not saying no. Next she wanted me to move the chairs out of her Redskin loving BIG ass. I did not say no. I wanted to but I didn\'t. I thought this was her last request and I was able to grant it...no big deal. But then she told me, not asked me, to open the doors for her, and bring a chair out for her to sit on so she could wait for the van to pick her ass up. I could have said no but that I was already in it too deep. Besides, she was already most comfortable bossing me, a complete stranger around. </P>\r\n\r\n<P>So my lunch was getting cold and Chuck was of no help--he continued to eat regardless of my absence (thanks Chuck). Okay, so anyway, outside of the deli, she put in my hand (opposite of kindly handing something to someone) a calling card and TOLD me to make a call for her. I almost did it. But I said no. And for a few minutes I felt like an asshole for not helping her out. You know, it was like I didn\'t follow through w/ the mission. I felt like I was going to hell for not helping her, I mean, Jesus would have called for her. Fuck, if he had a car he would have driven her home. Fuck, he would have given her his car. \r\n</P><P>\r\nI got her to the phone. I did every thing she told me to do up until I realized that I am such a fucking pussy and never stick up for myself. So I said no. No.\r\n</P><P>\r\nLike the other day at fruckin work. I had to play mover for the afternoon w/ a couple of other guys that can\'t say no either. Being around people that can\'t say no doesn\'t help me either. We start to feel bad for each other. We don\'t want to hurt each other\'s feelings. We just don\'t want to upset anyone. Are you happy reading this? Because I could start over if you want me to. You just have to tell me what to write.\r\n</P>\r\n<P>I am going to leave you all w/ one of Ted Berrigan\'s Sonnets:\r\n</P>\r\n<blockquote><P>LIII</P>\r\n<P>\r\nThe poem upon the page is as massive as<br>\r\nAnne\'s thighs    belly to hot belly we have laid<br>\r\nSerene beneath fervous folds, flashed cool<br>\r\nin our white heat   hungered   and tasted   and<br>\r\nGone to the movies   baffling combustions<br>\r\nare everywhere!  like Gertrude Stein at Radcliffe,<br>\r\nPatsy Padgett replete with teen-age belly!  every-<br>\r\none\'s suddebly pregnant and no one is glad!<br>\r\nO wet kisses, the poem upon the page<br>\r\nCan tell you about teeth you\'ve never dreamed<br>\r\nCould bite, nor be such reassurance! Babies are not<br>\r\nLike Word Origins and cribbage boards or dreams<br>\r\nof correspondence!  Fucking is so very lovely<br>\r\nWho can say no to it later?\r\n</P>'),(219,'<P>\r\ndeflowered on your bedroom floor<BR>\r\nbasking in the blue light coming from<BR>\r\nyour computer screen<BR>\r\nwhich is pretty appropriate<BR>\r\nall things considered</P>\r\n<P>\r\nyou\'d been fondling my breasts <BR>\r\nwhile I typed out messages to <BR>\r\na girl that disapproved of you and me<BR>\r\nand I don\'t know if there even is <BR>\r\na \'you and me\' to disapprove of</P>\r\n<P>\r\nbut I do know that you were my first<BR>\r\nand I felt bad for telling you it hurt too much<BR>\r\nand that we had to stop<BR>\r\nafter all that fuss <BR>\r\nbut I want to thank you anyway<BR>\r\nyou\'re so special to me </P>'),(220,'<P>I started a channel on IRC today called annoying, with chiamattt.  i didn\'t know that he was related to ratmice as his name is matt rice.  it doesn\'t get much more funny than that in the nomenclature department, except for maybe goatnutz and chewballs.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI sent Olivia an email today that I felt strange sending her.  It was a proclamation of how beautiful she is.  I was looking at some of her pictures in the image directory of oxy.gen.nz.  But what right does that give me to make a comment like that?  I don\'t think any really.  How far is it from harassment.  After all, I am in the channel on IRC that she is in, and elly, which by the way is purely coincidence.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI am in that channel because I like matsukaze very much and that is where he hangs out.  He also hangs out in SF-Raves, but yeo, I am A) not a rave kid and B) those people are not very friendly.  Sure it is one thing to say that #rant is unfriendly, but they are not snobs.  Not that I can tell.  They are an eighth grade lunch table that has been suspended for ever.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI I I I I am self possessed.\r\n</P><P>\r\nBTW, the sound card on my Inspiron 3800 didn\'t configure and I need to hack at it.\r\n</P>\r\n\r\n\r\n<P>\r\nI found a nice Tahoe blue image of camilla for my desktop.  camilla is a human representation for all computers with personality.  not to say she isn\'t very real and a very passionate human being.  i don\'t know.  i do know that she takes the most amazing images of her self from her webcam.  like IRC is nice to have running in the back ground of your day, camilla is nice to have on the background of your day.  when i see her face lurking, pensive, exploring vision back there, i sway with humanity.  type click type, edit edit, ahhh there is life camilla.  life!\r\n</P><P>\r\ngood night.</P>'),(221,'<P>I haven\'t done anything all day except leave to consume food.  Even then, one of the two times was to get money to pay the delivery driver.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI was walking out of someplace thinking the various reasons I don\'t care to go out anymore to bars and drink with friends.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI guess I don\'t see any point.  The odds of me \'meeting someone special\' are so infinitesimal that trying repulses me.\r\n</P><P>\r\nLamas knows what I am talking about.  Dates with women that find the outlook just as abysmal.  I guess that is the antithesis of real.  If you don\'t hope it to happen, then give up because the endeavor is pointless.\r\n</P><P>\r\nMany people are going through loneliness right now.  Hey, it is the holidays.  I spend most of my time not considering the future but reflecting on the past.  Part of me wants to call my last girlfriend in new york and offer to pay her plane ticket to visit because I love her through some abstract appreciation for people that make me feel passion.  The other part of me is ashamed for \'wasting my time thinking about it\' or so the words echo in my mind.\r\n</P><P>\r\nAnyway, I want. answers.\r\n</P>\r\n<pre>\r\nchiamattt> do you know the answer?\r\nchiamattt> what is greater then god\r\nchiamattt> more evil than the devil\r\nchiamattt> rich people need it\r\nchiamattt> poor people have it\r\nchiamattt> and if you eat it you die\r\n</pre>'),(222,'<P>Here I am again.  Sitting on the guest bed at arnie and nates.  The blankets smell like bar from when sad kristien stayed here the previous night.  Sad kristien is so very sad.  She thought life sucked the other day.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI don\'t have a phone, not one that I use anyway.  So today, this is going to be probably all the contact I will give my parents.  I like to contact them on Sundays.  It is a habit that I started in high school.  Sunday morning is call parents time.  Or Sunday night.  I usually managed to sneak it in at those times.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI wonder if they expect me to call?  I wonder if in the back of their head, they think all day, \'when is aus going to call?  has he called yet?\'  I think that is the way I would be with my kids.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nAustin waking up on Sunday: \'Today I get to talk to little A.  I hope he doesn\'t forget.  He won\'t forget because he loves me.\'  That is what I would think.  And then little A. would forget to call, and I would be a little disappointed.  Mrs. A says that when I don\'t call it is usually because I have a little girlfriend.  That is right enough.  When I have a little girlfriend, I am like Leonard, I don\'t go home.  But sometimes I don\'t have a girlfriend, I just am not home.  Now is one of those times.\r\n</P><P>\r\nBig A would give me a cell phone if it guaranteed that I would call him once a week.  My brother didn\'t have a phone for what seemed like years.  Big A wanted to buy my Brother a phone because he never called.  Mrs. A doesn\'t like spoiling the little ones, so she wouldn\'t go for it.  All money goes through Mrs. A, unless it is the cash in Big A\'s pocket.\r\n</P><P>\r\nOnce, Big A came to visit me while I was in college living off 75 dollars a month after rent.  I had a large (then but small by my standards now) credit card debt.  Big A gave me the money to pay it off in front of my friends.  It was a mortifying experience, but I needed the money badly.  Big A thought it was funny, giving Little A 400 dollars.  I thought it was a huge amount of money.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nKdog was there and she teased me about it later.  She always picks the things that I am most insecure about to hound dog me on.  I hate her that way.  I love her that way.  Kdog skinned fish in Alaska for money.  But then she drover her dad\'s hot rod Japanese car all through college.   I had jobs, just not all the time.  The nature of college jobs is that you must find one every effing semester.  I am so glad to be out of that.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI am going to visit Big A and Mrs A for Christmas in a couple weeks.  They live in Houston as of this month.  I think it is funny that I am going to visit them in their new house and new city.  I am leaving from my new house and new city.  We are in the same place, on opposite coasts.  Los Angeles to Houston.  Come in Houston.\r\n</P><P>\r\nOkay, Bye.\r\n</P>'),(223,'<P>I went up to SF to play with Carter and Randall this weekend.  After searching in vain for a classy strip club, we were strolling through the Market Street financial district at 3:00 AM, on the way back to Carter\'s apartment.\r\n</P><P>\r\nOur conversation on the nature of fiction writing was suddenly and rudely interrupted by several thugs jumping out of a \'88 Chevy Blazer.  They started pounding on a bunch of college jocks and their girlfriends walking down the sidewalk across from us.\r\n</P><P>\r\nThe girls were screaming, and the jocks were handling themselves pretty well considering they\'d been taken completely off guard.  It didn\'t take long for that to change, when another guy came out of the blazer swinging a length of heavy chain, and suddenly the first guys from the truck had knives in their hands.\r\n</P><P>\r\nMeanwhile Carter and I are hiding behind the columns of the Fidelity Mutual building, both of us dialing 911.  Carter got an operator first, so I hung up and concentrated on getting the tag number from the Blazer.  It didn\'t take long for the whole thing to wrap up once the fist throwing was replaced by slashing knives, so the thugs are starting to climb back into the Blazer by now.  One of the jocks is down, bleeding on the sidewalk, another is stupidly running after the Blazer that\'s speeding away down New Montgomery street.  The girls are still screaming.\r\n</P><P>\r\nWe hear the first sirens as we\'re running across the street, and the guy with the adrenaline high is back from chasing the Blazer, yelling at the girls to split.\r\n</P><P>\r\nMost of the guys were lucky enough to get away with just chain and fist marks, which is bad enough.  The one guy is still breathing and bleeding, but with stab wounds to his face and neck.  Not pretty.\r\n</P><P>\r\nPolice come, an ambulance makes its dramatic entrance and exit, we give our statements, and things are about calm again, when one of the officers says to Carter, \"don\'t I know you?\"\r\n</P><P>\r\nTurns out that about three of the cops were in the bunch that stormed Carter\'s house a couple of months ago, after he had pulled a gun on what he thought to be a burglar on his fire escape, but turned out to only be his half-naked neighbor spray painting some boards at 4:00 in the morning (???).\r\n</P><P>\r\n\"Your neighbor is a real asshole!  Sorry about waking you up that night.\"\r\n</P><P>\r\nAh, life in the city.</P>\r\n\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/223_1.gif\' width=\'400\'>'),(224,'<P>xmas is here again, and once again, the holidays have got me in a foul mood. i dont know why it happens. i don\'t recall any horrible event anywhere in my past that may have triggered these feelings of ickiness, but they are here, so i deal with them. </P>\r\n\r\n\r\n<P>this month marks the end of the first year in LA for me and i feel like i\'ve accomplished nothing. i\'ve worked some shitty jobs and had some crappy relationships with boys. basically i\'m just living life here like i lived it in florida. i have different surroundings and different friends. i should be having fun. life in LA was this big deal for me, i was gonna be someone and do something with my life. i\'m not doing any of that, and i feel damned useless.</P>\r\n\r\n\r\n<P>somehow, this town is sucking the life out of me, it\'s hard living here, and it hurts me to have this general malaise of bullshit hanging over my head all the time. i really wanted to make life here work, and it just doesn\'t. i miss my mom and my cat. i hated florida and wanted a change, but things arent any better here really.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i guess its just me. i want to find something that makes me happy. where do i need to go to do this? church? nah, <a href=\"http://laweekly.com/christ/\">J.C. is never the place to go when youre feeling lost</a>, i don\'t care what the christians say.  i feel like i\'m expending all my energy trying to have this great life. and i\'m exhausted. one of these days man, life is gonna be good. maybe when i get over my bullshit.</P>'),(225,'<P>Sometimes, (like this morning on the way to work)when I get cut off by some lane-weaving asshole driver, I summon up a nice loogie from deep within and, if I get the chance, send it sailing towards the offender\'s car.  Ooh, direct hit to the passenger window. I feel good.  I say aloud, \"Justice!\"  Then, I look in my rearview mirror and hope the guy didn\'t see me because he\'s a scary gangster and I\'m like the singer from The Verve, a beanpole.  \"Shit,\" traffic\'s heavy, and my wagon couldn\'t beat his benzo... he\'s turning. phew! coast is clear.  \"Justice.\"</P>\r\n'),(226,'<P>An Article About Magic Elfs(sic)</P>\r\n\r\n\r\n<P>For the longest time me and some guys at the office have been throwing around the idea of making a light-hearted comedy about the holocaust called \"Punch-out\".  It centers around a fun-loving Nazi who enjoys spreading gossip and punching little kids in the face.  Anyway, the script needs a lot of work and we\'re constantly throwing new things into the mix, but it\'s sort of been a labor of love for all of us. While we devote the bulk of the day to working on our latest piece of mass-market tripe, a serious drama about a monkey who wins the tour de france, our heads are elsewhere. Obviously we would love to be able to put the time and effort required of a movie like \"Punch-out\" into it, but it\'s an art flick and right now we really need the monkey. \r\n</P><P>\r\nDid I say monkey? Oh god, please kill me now.\r\n</P><P>\r\nSo anyway, I came to work ten minutes late the other day and I had an interesting conversation with our production coordinator, Sandoval.\r\n</P><P>\r\nMe: Sandoval, I had the wierdest dream last night.\r\n</P><P>\r\nSandoval: Oh yeah? Is that why you\'re late?\r\n</P><P>\r\nMe: Actually, yes. I was desperate to write down everything I could remember about it, because it would be the perfect seque between the first and second acts of \"Punch-out\".\r\n</P><P>\r\nSandoval: (INTERESTED) Oh really? Do tell!\r\n</P><P>\r\nMe: In my dream I was you! Well not you, exactly, but I was the production coordinator for a marginally-successful, hollywood-based independent feature film production company not unlike our own, only they weren\'t stuck with generic bottled water. They had the good stuff. Not Evian, mind you, but something like Poland Springs. \r\n</P><P>\r\nAnyway, so Matt comes in, and he\'s still him, just a lowly production assistant, and he looks like shit. And get this, he\'s ten minutes late! All disheveled and unshowered, and I think he may have been crying, so I\'m all \"Explain your tardiness, young man,\" and he\'s all \"I\'m sorry, we just found out my aunt has breast cancer\" and I\'m like \"\'Breast cancer\'? That sounds made up?\"  He\'s just kinda like \"Huh?\" and I\'m all \"You\'re fired.\"\r\n</P><P>\r\nThen I woke up.  But seriously, wouldn\'t that be awesome right after the part with the clowns and the fire trucks?\r\n</P><P>\r\nSandoval: Yeah, I\'m seeing it, definitely... but...\r\n</P><P>\r\nMe: (reading his mind) Well of course we switch the production office locale for an ice cream parlor!\r\n</P><P>\r\nSandoval: Bingo!\r\n</P><P>\r\n\r\nSo then me and Sandoval decided to blow off work and get some drinks at a strip club. Our boss, the executive producer, Lou, was pretty pissed off but we said we were in a meeting and we had left a message with Matt.  So then Matt ended up getting fired, which, all in all, seemed pretty ironic.</P>'),(227,'<P>Austin, I have dreams. I have dreams of your red hot Pumas of love. It takes a powerful individual with strong fashion sense to learn the rules and then break them, all in one pair of FUCKIN\' HOT SHOES! And they float around in my dreams, ripe with color, disembodied, and ethereal. Your smiling face appears behind them, orbited by gleaming red Pumaa, and suddenly I am awake! Oh, the bed, it is wet!</P>\r\n\r\n\r\n<a href=\"http://fonem.org\">\r\n<img src=\"http://fonem.org/img/pumas.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"click here for RED HOT SHOE AXXXION\"></a>\r\n\r\n\r\n'),(228,'<P>I decided to take it outside tonight after a failed attempt at seeing the new movie, \"Crap,\" by the same writer/director as suck greats as \"Lock Stock and Two Smoking Barrels.\"  But you know what?  It took me an hour to get there from Glendale and it was \"sold out but you can sit in the front if you want.\"  No thanks please, just punch my parking ticket please.  Now it is 976688029 seconds since the first Unix computer was turned on and I am sitting at the White Horse bar in the noland between Los Feliz and West Hollywood, sipping on Arnold\'s favorite spirit, one of the many arnisms I have picked up besides hanging around his house entirely too much.\r\n</P><P>\r\nThe bar is red.  Red like the classic type red bar.  Every major city has at least one.  Major < 300,000.  Los angeles, being three million has about 12.  I am in the second one that I learned of.  It is an Adam Lamas bar.  There are couches and pictures of all the patrons thumb tacked on two walls of a corner.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nThe bartender is the jerk.  He asks me if I have an acceptable form of internationally and federally respected form of personal identification that contains at minimum, my name, headshot, unique serial number, date of birth, and seal of authoritative certification.   Fuck you jerk off.  I hand him my drivers license issued to me in Boseman, Montana, four plus years ago.   It expired last October second, my birthday.  I am 25, born ninteen hundred and seventy five in Dallas, Texas, United States of America.  Austin Graves Swinney.  Steet address, General Delivery, West Yellowstone, Montana.  Good luck tracking me down with that.  Still, it is all good enough for a whiskey on a tuesday night.\r\n</P><P>\r\nThere are two people in the bar other than myself.  I don\'t think I can listen to this for long.  Poor guys stock that he had in his company is worthless.  It could have been worth a hundred thousand dollars, maybe \"I\'ll\" get something out of it, but ...  he trails off.  The phone rings.  Maybe he will forget what the subject was and go back to watching Regis Filman\'s Win My Million Sixty-Four Thousand.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nMan, I don\'t give...  I don\'t care what is going on with that television.  I don\'t want to know.  Which state\'s island does \"snow falling on cedars\" take place?  Washington.  Good thing he was right for Sixty Four Thousand Dollars.  \"Gettin\' up there into some serious money.\"  Take it and run you fool.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI should just stop right now.  This entry cost one five dollar whiskey, and a one dollar tip.  Lucky if I get out of here with thirty six dollars in my wallet.\r\n</P><P>\r\nbye, thanks for reading\r\n</P><P>\r\nOh, and the bartender just fucking asked me to leave. What a dick head.\r\n</P>\r\n										'),(229,'<P>I wouldn\'t say I\'m frought with anxiety, exactly, but there is definitely something in the air.  Something electric.  Barely muted hysteria?  Not quite, but a palpable feeling of anticipation abounds as the world waits for the event that will most likely change its course forever with just four little words.\r\n</P><P>\r\nDude, where\'s my car?\r\n</P><P>\r\nAs I look at the calender, I realize I haven\'t gotten a decent night\'s sleep in almost six weeks.  Ironically, one of my best nights was just yesterday.  Even though it\'s so close I can almost taste it, I\'ve reached the point where I\'ve made peace with my destiny.  It\'s going to happen.\r\n</P><P>\r\nFor the last week I had been plagued with horrible, recurring nightmares that prevented me from getting any more than a half hour or so of fitful slumber.  Often the nightmares would take the shape of mundane activities; buying soap, eating lunch or talking to my mom on the phone.  It wasn\'t what was happening that disturbed me so, it was what wasn\'t happening.  Though the me of my dreams went about his life completely oblivious, there was another me, the observer, who stood above, unseen and unheard, screaming in vain \"What are you doing?  Get off your ass and go see this movie!  Change your shirt first!\"\r\n</P><P>\r\nIt\'s now past midnight, officially the eve of the premiere and now I have nothing to do but wait.  I realize trying to take my mind off of it would be futile, so instead I have begun crafting collages about my feelings towards the movie.  They are quite good, especially considering the sheer number of them and my lack of readily available periodicals to construct them with.\r\n</P><P>\r\nSo anyway, dear friends, all I can offer in the form of advice is buy your tickets early and see it with someone you love.  Unless of course that someone is rude and tends to talk loudly while others in the theater are trying to watch the movie because if I happen to be in that theater I will not hesitate to shove my fist so far down your fucking throat that I will be picking your pubic hairs off my knuckles.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nJust kidding!  That was just a little holiday humor in the spirit of the season.  Happy Festivus everyone and I hope to see YOU at the movies!</P>'),(230,'Iâ€™VE JUST STUMBLED ON TO A CONSPIRACY WORTHY OF TABLOID INK!  Men in ties never wash their hands, after urinating into porcelain holes in the wall.  Iâ€™ve seen at least five hundred or so do this. And tubes donâ€™t lie. No matter how hard you tie them around your vein.  Men in ties, with germ stained hands are roaming offices around the globeâ€¦right now.  Shaking other tie wearing hands in a secret exchange of penis knowledge.  And you wonder where the power comes from?'),(231,'I\'VE JUST STUMBLED ON TO A CONSPIRACY WORTHY OF TABLOID INK!  Men in ties never wash their hands, after urinating into porcelain holes in the wall.  I\'ve seen at least five hundred or so do this. And tubes don\'t lie. No matter how hard you tie them around your vein.  Men in ties, with germ stained hands are roaming offices around the globe, right now.  Shaking other tie wearing hands in a secret exchange of penis knowledge.  And you wonder where the power comes from?\r\n\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/231_1.jpg\' width=\'400\'>\r\nTUBE: \"i created man and woman on the 13th day of my 88 month long orgasm\"'),(232,'<P>The first two days of my month long hawaiian vacation is spent looking for aloha.  Despite popular belief, aloha is not found hiding in the grass skirts of the local wahines, nor is it contained in the cranium of the coconut, rather, aloha is a sentiment of love and respect, caring, the feeling of belonging and acceptance-- much like the warmth bestowed upon all who get yelled at and insulted at the alexandria island in the middle of LA.\r\n</P><P>\r\nSadly, what is most apparent here is the vacuous shouting of strangers in a bump-bump club, congestion and traffic, discussions about the short tempers of drivers who, like cholestorol, clog the major arteries of the island with saturated fat.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nLooking for Aloha ought to be the sequal to waiting for godot, partly becasue my own solipsistic meanderings has not quite managed to get me out of my skin. In all probablitiy, I know that as soon as I wash the bleach from my hand (I am currently cleaning scum off the walkway at mumsies), I will jump into the sunshine and roll about the beach like a big fatso, inflated and decompressed.</P>'),(233,'<P>It is 7:30 and where are you?  I ought to be hearing you drive up Mikahala Dr-- the gravel under your wheels making that gravelly noise we all try to emulate when doing foley.  You walk in the door and hoot \\\"arnieee!\\\" and arrive in the living room that overlooks beautiful waikiki.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nWith barely glance of honolulu\\\'s city lights, you settle into the uncomfortable rattan upright and turn on the computer.  You curse that the monitor is the least ergonomic you have been on: The keyboard is a little too high, the terminal is buzzing near your right ear and the monitor is on the ledge at the top of a rolltop desk... roughly two feet too high and about 45 degrees off to the right.  You squint, you stand, you sit again, you curse, you stand... can\\\'t stand it.  \\\"damned that sticky mouse!\\\"  You go to the kitchen to pour yourself a ketel one or bushmills. instead you find smirnoff or JD.\r\n</P><P>\r\nNate comes home.  we exchange our daily stories. some of those stories fall onto the floor and get mopped out with the muddy footprints.  Others of them linger about and are referred to on following days. \\\"What do you MEEEEEEAAAAAAAAANNNNNNN!\\\" we squeal,\r\n</P><P>\r\nsleep arrives, and I leave you in the computer room, straining your neck, until you eventually fall asleep on the bed, near the desk.  You have dreams about geckos, they whisper in your ear at night,those transluscent, ghostly lizards.\r\n</P><P>\r\nSame scene, alternative backdrop.  I ask you... blaah blahh blahh, Getlit, blaha blah.\r\n</P>'),(234,'<P>narcoleptic narcs roam the schools of my dreams, trying to snuff out the the thoughts of sex with socks, and breasts with mouths that bite my tongue.......so soft.......i loved the way they ran, with their little feet bouncing on the floors, tip, tap, tip tap. tommy ran and fell on his ass, but didnt hurt himself cos the ground was covered with cell tissue, hundreds of cells to bounce on, i\'ll rent one for our next childs birthday party...........just dont forget to invite tommy, he\'s a wonderful bouncer </P>'),(235,'<P>Desert zoos filled with old Chinese women in cages, sitting there, contemplating how to put out the red light. Silver slitted retina heaven, brings joy to the tiny boys who come from far and wide. Their necks throb in the heat of the desert, but the ointment created from silverfish intestine cures all, and brings good times for one more day, out in the sun, at the Royal China Zoo.</P>'),(236,'<P>I was drinking with my best friend from high school tonight, and also my flatmate.  Around 2am we got bored, and so   we headed out into the street to commit acts of larrikanism.  The street signs, however, were too high up for us to steal, so instead we amused ourselves by taking Supermodel posing shots in the middle of the highway, or pole dancing shots around various flagpoles.  And then my friend Penny plonked herself down in the middle of the bush.  I said \"hey that looks like fun\" and did it too.\r\n</P><P>\r\nAnd now I am bleeding. \r\n</P><P>\r\nAnd of course my camera film ran out right when we got topless. Where\'s the justice in this world?\r\n</P>'),(237,'<P><TT><STRONG>\r\n<font color=\"red\">Ã¹</font>\r\n<font color=\"white\">Ã­</font>\r\n<font color=\"red\">Ã¹</font>\r\n</STRONG> \r\nOK, you\'re not /away anymore. Did you have fun? </TT></P>\r\n<P>Not really.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>mah, fu.  I\'m going to DC.  GashT is so cool.  He gave me <a href=\"../../music/soulcraft.mp3\">Bad Brains</a>.  My days are so much better now.  I can sit and listen to <a href=\"../../music/voyage_into_infinity.mp3\">Bad Brains</a> and I can\'t hear anything.  I can\'t hear the annoying people wanting my participation.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nHow bad can a day be when it starts with Quickness and Voyage to Infinity?  Not bad.  If Bad Brains are rasta, i want to be rasta too.  Grow me some dreds.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nI wonder if I can get out of work today?  Doubtful.  I am already at work.  But I would really like to be surfing in Hawaii right now, picking sand out of my thong.  I know what you are thinking, you and me both.  Let\'s go!  Arnold is already there.  Rat.  I bet he isn\'t having any fun either.  Then Nate is going to leave.  Then kiki is going to leave.  Then I am going to have the entire compound to myself. hrm.  sounds lonely.  maybe someone will come visit me.\r\n</P><P>\r\nThen it is austin to houston.  Is it the holidays?  Is it winter?  strange.  If there were not a mall next to my office, I wouldn\'t suspect something was up.  Oh, then there are the lights on the street.  But those could be for el dia de los muertos.  So who is to say?\r\n</P>\r\n<P>I guess I won\'t be home so much for the rest of the month.  After Houston is San Diego to meet up with Sean\'s grandma\'s apple pie.  Maybe a little mountain isolation and disconnection.  Maybe let the scar tissue in my finger tendons harden a little.</P>'),(238,'<P>It\'s been six whole months since I\'ve seen my bf.  House arrest is a bitch. But strangely I\'ve fallen for him more durin our time apart.  The little icq\'s that tell me he misses me melt my lil heart. I\'m so easy.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI see him next week - I\'m so terrified.  I envision him seeing me across the room and thinking, \"I waited 6 months for that?\"  What pisses me off is that every other video there is this huge breasted bitch with a slim waist, a gigantic muscular booty, and a a perfect face. Don\'t you girls eat? Shiiet.\r\n</P><P>\r\nIf he realizes that I\'ve been eatin a lot since I last saw him, fuck it. Rooooaaaar</P>'),(239,'<P>I like to play uno and eat pizza.  Sometimes I eat too much pizza and then I don\'t feel good.  Like right now.  That\'s the good thing about uno, you can play it alot without getting sick of it.  Unless you eat the cards.  Someone told me that humans can\'t digest wood but I think my tummy ache is actually coming from the laminate or the ink on the cards. </P>\r\n<P>\r\nI also drink alot of water.  I have a brita pitcher, I usually fill it up a few times a day.  I don\'t fill it until it\'s empty because I like to drink cold water.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nI have a picture of me and Curtis Armstrong.  He was \'Booger\' in \'Revenge of the Nerds\'.  He was also in the sequel but I don\'t know which part he played in that.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nThis picture is me about to jump off a cliff in Griffith Park.  At the time I was quite despondent over my failure to become a magician.  Now I don\'t even want to become a magician anymore.  It\'s crazy, I don\'t even like magic.  I certainly don\'t advocate suicide.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nI live near the Brady Bunch house.  They put up a fence and planted trees but you can still tell it\'s the place.  Me and my friend found a dead dog and we brought it to the Brady Bunch house and said \"Oh no, Tiger\'s dead!\".  They didn\'t think that was very funny.  It was probably because the dead dog was a german sheppard and the real Tiger was a collie or whatever the hell dog that was.  Anyway, the real Brady Bunch didn\'t look anything like they do on tv.  I know the camera adds ten pounds or whatever, but these seemed to be completely different people.  Ok, so none of that really happened.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nI like writing haikus.  Here is one I wrote just for this occasion:\r\n</P>\r\n<PRE>\r\nPlease go out with me\r\nDon\'t let me die a virgin\r\nThat was just a joke\r\n</PRE>\r\n<P>\r\nSo, in summation:  I live near the Brady Bunch house, I like haikus, water, pizza and uno, and I hate magicians.  I seem to have covered all the hot-button topics of dating in the 2000\'s, but if you have any other questions feel free to email me.  References available on request (not really). </P>\r\n\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/239_1.jpg\'>'),(240,'<P>There I was,headed for destiny a momment say, like now.  No. ....Now like W. Mr. Shatner,traveling at lightspeed.......................only faster?</P>\r\n  '),(241,'<P>Who would have thought that journal entries dating back to 1998 would take up 8mb of space?  Not me, that\'s for sure.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nSee, I\'ve only got 15mb of space on my domain, but I thought I had 50.  I also had no idea how much  space I was taking up.  But then the guy that hosts my site went and put in new software that blocks you from uploading more if you\'ve exceeded your space limit, and since I\'m on 22mb - and I didn\'t realise - I can\'t put anything new up on my site until I\'ve deleted like 7mb of stuff, or at least moved it elsewhere.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nSo what\'s a girl to do?  I can\'t put my dumbass ramblings up for my little fan club to read, so i\'m forced to take my whinings elsewhere.  More specifically, I\'m uploading here.  Which actually works out really well in the end.  The other night when i was drunk and had jumped in the bush, I thought I wrote about it in my journal or on my mailing list, but then when I sobered up in the morning, I couldn\'t find it anywhere.  Except it was here, on Swinney.org.  I don\'t remember posting it here, but that\'s okay, I\'ll accept it as one of life\'s little (drunken) mysteries.  And my scratches are healing now, thanks for asking.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nMy neck really really hurts.  Is anyone skilled at massage?  I\'ll trade you something for a neck rub.  \r\n</P>\r\n<img\r\nsrc=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/241_1.jpg\' height=\'150\'>'),(242,'<P>i had a unexpected beautiful night last night hanging out with an adam and a new friend.  new friend showed up about 4 out of the blue.  i was tearing the carpet and furniture out of my new room.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>we talked for a while, then adam showed up.  we talked some more.  she wanted to hike up the hill in griffith park to the foot of the world famous Rebel Without a Cause observatory.  so that is what we did, and i am sore.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>then we went to Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon, a fine film.  long, beautiful, stunning cable kung-fu action of amazing beauty.  very romantic.  sad.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>afterward i wrote some emails in bed and chatted on irc.  then i turned my laptop off.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>4:00 am, the neighbors leave.  it sounds like someone is breaking into the house.  i am awake and not going back to sleep.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i turn on my laptop, it boots up.  it skips the graphical log in screen and goes strait to the command line.  curious, i log in.  i attempt to start a graphical session:</P>\r\n<pre>\r\naustin@swinstar>:  startx\r\n</pre>\r\n\r\n<P>nothing happens.  i get a blank line.  i figure, fine, i just wanted to go online so i resolve to stay at the command line until some time in the afternoon when i feel like dealing with this whole graphic problem.  i type:</P>\r\n<pre>\r\naustin@swinstar>:  ping swinney.org\r\n</pre>\r\n\r\n<P>nothing.  fuck me running.  i hate it when this happens.  helplessness is not a feeling that i embrace.  it makes me angry.  i turn into the incredible hulk. and if that isn\'t bad enough, it does a half assed shut off after idling for less than 3 minutes.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i toss and turn in my new room, my new bed, for a few hours until 6:30 a.m.  then i get up and shower.  make coffee.  reinstall.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i know it is really rude to reinstall, but lets face it, i have had the laptop for a two weeks and there is nothing on it that i care about anyway.  everything is on the server or my computer at work.  my life\'s work happens over the Internet.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>reinstalls #1 and #2 happen with the same results as before.  i got to work and my irc connection is dissed.  trying to reconnect is not happening.  i cannnot get a server.  so now i want this morning to end.</P>\r\n\r\n<table border=3 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=3><tr><td bgcolor=\'black\'>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/242_1.jpg\' align=\'center\'>\r\n</td></tr>\r\n<tr><td bgcolor=\'black\'>\r\n<font color=\'CCCCCC\'><P>beautiful <a href=\'http://oxy.gen.nz/olivia\'>olivia</a> got her tee shirt that i sent her.  doesn\'t it look nice? i don\'t see why she wants a boob job.</P></font>\r\n</td></tr>\r\n</table>'),(243,'<P>so, im here in florida and i have an appointment with a temp service tomorrow. woo hoo!</P>\r\n<P>life with mom isnt bad, its just so damn boring. im watching even more tv than usual, which for those of you that know me, might find this impossible..but i assure you. its true. ive also been spending twice the amount of time on the internet. god, im constantly staring at a box. the phone just rang and it was someone wanting to meet me about a reception position. get this, in a gym!!! hahahaha. hilarious. me working at a gym. okay i finally stopped laughing. if they pay me enough, i might even work out. bwahahahaha. okay the laughing again has subsided.</P>\r\n<P>well, in conclusion, i miss you guys and i hope you are all doing well. have a good xmas and all that stuff, and call a cab or walk on new years.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>now that you all have my email..i expect lots of mail damnit. lots!</P>'),(244,'<P>\r\nLast night was the nicest night I have had in a while, away from the Internet.  DSL is down.  I used my roomate\'s evil aol analog account to get my mail.  Some of it was nice.  Then I was forced to do things like read a book and hang out with friends.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI would not have hung out with friends, but K3 came over.  She seems nice.  She is a heart breaker, I have heard.  Funny thing is that last time I went out with her and Mister Lamas (had dated), he asked me if I was interested in her and I explicitly said no.  He asked why and I said that I don\'t tend to cut women a gentlemen\'s amount of slack.  Everyone gets the same.  And he understood.  I thought K3 seemed like she would not do well with my distaste for gender roles.\r\n\r\n</P><P>\r\nUnfortunately I am perhaps a liar.  Maybe not though.  She is interesting and different.  Interesting?  Well, as a musician, she knows things about music that I don\'t know exist.  I\'m not a musician.  In fact, I would say she knows more about music than I know about anything.  I really don\'t have any dedication to anything (* except maybe the Internet) and I appreciate people that have dedication to a love that they try to make a profession.  Or not, but that do it regardless even.\r\n</P><P>\r\nCha Chi came over late last night, about 11 pm, just after K3 left because she is concerned about this romantic interest of K3 and I. She doesn\'t want K3 trashing me.  She feels K3 would be a lasting negetive emotional experience for me.   I think I let her know that I can take care of myself.  Maybe not. It is hard to tell.  I don\'t blame her for being concerned.  It is nice to have friends that watch your back.  Cha Chi is crazy good.  We talked about GF\'s and BF\'s and all that, then talked about radicalism in the States and abroad until 3:30 a.m.  Cha Chi and K3 have been friends since they were young children.\r\n</P><P>\r\nVery much a princess that K3, Cha Chi pointed out.  I don\'t have a problem with princesses.  Sometimes I detest the princess metaphor, especially when self declared, and when it is meant to make me feel inferior.  And it has been used against me before.  The accusation being that I am not a prince.  I\'m not. Just a normal strange person.  I guess that is why it hurt that time, \"I am a princess, you don\'t deserve me,\" way back when.\r\n</P><P>\r\nCha Chi says K3 is bad because she doesn\'t know what she wants and instead of driving to Santa Monica, picking up stray guys in Bars, following them home, fucking and running; she picks up guys among Cha Chi\'s friends.  Guys like me.  Guys like Mister Lamas.  Guys who are lonely or who don\'t know what they want, don\'t care to know.  Guys that like the idea of sleeping with a beautiful girl.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI am not looking for that special someone to spend the rest of my life with.  I have a few in mind already and they content me for daydreaming purposes.  Dreaming.  I don\'t mind not knowing what I am looking for.  Cha Chi said she thinks K3\'s form of finding what she wants is to sleep with available guys that are certified good by her friends.  Friends like Cha Chi.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI have dated girls like K3 before.  The ones that won\'t introduce you to their friends or family.  It was wierd the first time it happened to me.  But I enjoy getting to know my girlfriends, even if that means getting to know that they don\'t like to mix their friends.  (I am tripping, I don\'t like that.) It is a lack of respect.  I have friends that I wouldn\'t mix.  We find friends in strange places, through each other, through work, through roomates.  Tree branches don\'t grow into each other.  I have never picked a girl up in a bar and likely never will.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI don\'t feel like getting my heart broken again.  It is one of those things I can\'t help.  I have to pay for breaking so many hearts in the past.  I think it is a 1:1.25 ratio at this point.  If I get my heart broken two more times, I should be at 1:1.  Then I can start anew.\r\n</P><P>\r\n\r\nI\'ll match K3\'s interest.  If I find myself at some point in an elevator swooning from her scent and fantasizing, then so be it.  But as Cha Chi pointed out, if I find myself sitting on the edge of a bed discussing sexual history and rapidly indexing the time line of extremely personal experiences, hurrying up to make casual sex less strange, well you know.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nWe are all entitled to make our own mistakes. \r\n</P><P>\r\nSo, I guess I am going to get to know K3 better and see who she is.\r\n</P>\r\n'),(245,'<pre>\r\nevery child has a right to be loved\r\nno baby,no baby,is poor\r\nour god has given this\r\nthe youth of today\r\nthey pray\r\nthe youth of today prepare\r\nand the youth of today is the free child of tomorrow.........\r\nand these are the rights of a child...\r\nto be with god; heart, soul,and deeds.\r\nto have clean clothes and money...\r\nthe gift of life is priceless and every child is surely blessed...\r\nour god has given this...\r\n</pre>'),(246,'i\'m on the couch at 6am. awake. <a href=\"http://maz.org/~bcm\">brian just woke up</a>.\r\n</p><p>\r\ni was in the middle of writing some more <a href=\"http://standing.ontheoutside.com/le/coffee.html\">senryu with jo</a>. brian came out to the living room in his boxers. i said \"is \'fucked\' one syllable or two?\" and he said \"one, unless you\'re going with the elizabethan pronounciation.\"\r\n</p><p>\r\nmeh.</P>'),(247,'7:00 a.m., I watch the sun rise from my office at work.  I got here at 6:15.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nI am awake because I went to sleep exhausted last night.  Too many late nights and early mornings.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nMornings usually start with a terrible dream.  Babies shitting in my mouth followed by me vomiting.  That was yesterday.  Today it was me murdering a woman.  Trying to, with a long collapsed umbrella.  I don\'t know why.  I was very bad at it.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nAustin are you fucked up?  No.  I just had a fucked up conversation with Cha Chi the other night.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nAmong the topics was a girl that was murdered by her boyfriend in upstate New York on the steps of a church.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nI had a girlfriend years ago that told me the same story.  It happened in her home town.  It happened in Cha Chi\'s  college town.\r\n<br><br>\r\nSo, welcome to my dream world.  I incorporate things that come up in intense conversation into my dreams.  I don\'t own them.  I am not crazy.\r\n<br><br>\r\nNone the less, for the first time in my life, I feel like going to a confessional.  <a href=\"http://swinney.org/journals/images/247_1.jpg\">I want these awful things out of my mind</a>.\r\n<br><br>\r\nI feel like a medium.'),(248,'<P>I am against textual ambition. The secret themes of my devastation have \r\n      led me here, in boredom, without memory, plotting to start again. All of \r\n      my past is solidly behind me at last, yet I will always be a victim to a \r\n      sexy dress. I am waiting for the perpetual playback of my failure to cease. \r\n      The fury of captivated words amaze me. As amusing as living your life in \r\n      2D. Nothing frustrates me more than the twentieth century. Nothing frustrates \r\n      me more than a woman who will not let herself be adored. Like an undeveloped \r\n      dream, it is time for me to dial up a groove. </P>\r\n      <p>\"doko ni datte, hito wa tsunagatte iru\" // \"no matter \r\n        where, people are all connected\"</p>\r\n '),(249,'<p>\"computer desk\"<br>\r\n<p>a kitchen article requisitioned from the puppy merger, listening to pop music from the storage garage</p>\r\n\r\n<p><and the golf clubs that paid for college making splendid window props</p>\r\n\r\n<p>positing a non-cartesian existence like<br>\r\npositing a non-existence and<br>\r\nsleeping with nihilists while giving morning confession with substantialists</p>\r\n\r\n<p>a blustery day in joker\'s pooh corner </p>\r\n\r\n<p>i haven\'t gotten out of these pjs in days</p>\r\n\r\n<p>and i\'m in hiding<br>\r\na reclusive reflex<br>\r\nlike the need for nicotene</p>\r\n\r\n<p>bloody knuckles and broken fingers rage heedlessly against the stone wall karma</p>\r\n\r\n<p>when from out the 24th al coda a slight mood levitation and incorporeal mind wings with tumbling leaves to osprey perch </p>\r\n\r\n<p>the interstate highway<br>\r\nand the waffle house<br>\r\nand the pulse made subtle in freezing water<br>\r\nlike the first car to pass this way in six hours</p>\r\n\r\n<p>and i\'m in hiding<br>\r\na recursive reflex<br>\r\ncompiled from recursive cause</p>\r\n\r\n<p>a latent headache from the cambrian era ripening in this high-noon of cigarettes and regrets</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\"<em>What a day has arrived!  What a thick light of milk,<br>\r\ncompact, digital, indulges me!<br>\r\nI have heard its red horse neigh<br>\r\nnaked, shoeless and radiant.<br>\r\nI cross with it over the churches,<br>\r\nI gallop through barracks stripped of soldiers<br>\r\nand a foul army pursues me.<br>\r\nIts eucalyptus eyes steal the shadows,<br>\r\nits bell body gallops and strikes.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I need a lightningstroke of persistent splendor,<br>\r\na festive relative to take on my inheritence.</em>\"<br>\r\n-<em>Neruda </em>(Dream Horse)</p>'),(250,'<P>i cant wait till the races are over and i can shrinkwrap myself back up. i hate being exposed to the the naked air and germ babies floating everywhere. always trying to find homes and gardens in my lungs.  little legs with harm have no place in my heart. i wish they?d just get a clue already. somebody ...pass me the Tussin.</P>'),(251,'<pre>\r\nrobotec9> k*.com said to \'dress nice\' tomorrow evening.\r\n\r\nrobotec9> i dont\' think i have a \'dress nice\' look in my closet\r\n\r\nrobotec9> i dont\' think i have a closet!\r\n\r\nadamajah> your old interview clothes?\r\n\r\n robotec9 panics in the jeans he has been wearing every day for 3 mos\r\n\r\nchiamattt> i say dress the way people see you all the time.\r\n\r\nchiamattt> thats how i live life\r\n\r\nchiamattt> i aint about the cloths on my back.\r\n\r\nrobotec9> chia hasn\'t ever, EVER, had a GF\r\n\r\nchiamattt> robotec9: i havnt ever had one. but girls have asked me out.\r\n\r\nadamajah> haha\r\n\r\nrobotec9> weak\r\n\r\nrobotec9> =-P\r\n\r\nrobotec9> can i archive that statement?\r\n\r\nchiamattt> all im sayin is yer anxiety is a pure example of your\r\n            socialization.\r\n\r\nchiamattt> no\r\n\r\nrobotec9> haha\r\n\r\nchiamattt> id prefer it if you didnt.\r\n\r\nchiamattt> not every one is mature enough to need to know that kind of\r\n            information\r\n\r\nrobotec9> ROARHAHAHA\r\n\r\nchiamattt> most think im a pathetic loser\r\n\r\nrobotec9> M\'Kay\r\n\r\nrobotec9> hahaha\r\n\r\nrobotec9> <chiamattt> not every one is mature enough to need to know \r\n                       that kind of information\r\n\r\nrobotec9> M\'KAY!?\r\n\r\nrobotec9> haha\r\n\r\nadamajah> lol\r\n\r\n robotec9 starts crying\r\n\r\nadamajah> haha\r\n\r\nrobotec9> oh shit\r\n\r\nadamajah> damn  dude\r\n\r\nrobotec9> hahaha\r\n\r\nadamajah> people are starting to look at me funny\r\n\r\nchiamattt> whatever</pre>\r\n\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/251_1.jpg\'>'),(252,'<P>haiku is a 5-7-5 verse about nature.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>senryu is a haiku-like verse, not neccessarily about nature.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>ok.</P>\r\n\r\n'),(253,'<P>haiku is a 5-7-5 verse about nature.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>senryu is a haiku-like verse, not neccessarily about nature. </P>\r\n\r\n<P>ok.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>also, the marvelous <a href=\"http://www.chiamattt.com\">chiamattt</a> won\'t stop sending me email and i had a conversation with someone via two way pager. that someone was on my porch at the time. here is a gif of pine.</P>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/253_1.gif\'>'),(254,'<P>i am joining K3 at a restaurant with her co-workers tonight.  i have to dress nice.  this poses a problem for me.  i just moved.  i have no nice clothes that are not A) missing buttons B) wrinked in a laundry basket.  eff.\r\n</P><P>\r\non the brite side of things, i know what i am going to eat:  Spicy Lemongrass Bouillabaisse.  K3 will have to pronounce it for me.  i think she knows french, or german.  one of the two.  eitherway, i am unable to pronounce \'oui\' and \'aisse\'.  i can handle the rest though.  maybe i\'ll just say \'Spicy Lemongrass Lobster please.\'  i bet it is going to be $30 dollies.  \r\n</P><P>\r\ni\'m listening to Shellac.  they are comming on tour next month.  my brother scott and his girlfriend are flying in from dallas to see both shows.  i can\'t wait to see those two, and Shellac.  i must say it is the most anticipated concert of the year.  i play air guitar in my cubicle.</P>'),(255,'<P>Unfamiliar ceilings: they do not equal pleasure. I now hate this silent and incongruent feeling. I hate trying to recapture the moment of undress, the second the lights went off, the instant i felt her radar vision on me. You don\'t have the tactful ears and the attention to details it would take for me to confess. You don\'t care for me to present the mediocre details you desire. Do you know what it is like to be destroyed? Do you know what it is like to have x-ray vision and stare at breasts all day?</P>'),(256,'<P>get it here:  <a href=\"http://swinney.org/projects/joker.txt\">joker.txt</a>  and be sure to thank <a href=\"http://jessejoker.org\">jessejoker.org</a> because he worked hard on this script and i did not.</P>'),(257,'<P>Things that have stranged me out in the past couple\'o days:</P>\r\n\r\n<LI>Finding out that the woman I work with, a PR guru type was actually in the army for 15 years\r\n<LI>Finding out that the super boring receptionist is a lesbian - I don\'t know why this is so suprising, but I dunno, I just thought she was way too ordinary.  Not that lesbians are unordinary.  Okay, so this point\'s sounding really dumb, but it did seem valid when I started.\r\n<LI>Getting my first ever four digit pay cheque.  Wahoo!\r\n<LI>Calling up a senior citizen\'s centre to enquire about using their hall for a community meeting we\'re planning, and having the person on the other end answer \"Hellooooooooooooo you\'ve reached the land of Cukoo\" before a big long silence.  Confused, I thought it was an answering machine and hung up.  When I rang back, the lady answered \"Hellloo, you haven\'t reached the land of Cukoo\" .  Very odd.  \r\n<LI>Joining a cult yesterday.  Okay, so it wasn\'t actually a cult, it was the Stonecutter\'s Guild.  Well, technically it was the Freemasons.  And I guess if you wanna get specific, I didn\'t join them, just witnessed their secretest rituals in the Masonic Lodge.  Well, there was no one else there except for the guy that let me in.  Fine, I\'ll admit that it wasn\'t a ritual or anything, but I did truely get to go into the Temple in the Masonic Lodge.  It was absolutely crazy looking - all blue carpet and thrones and compasses and altars and a big ass gold \'G\' hanging from the ceiling.  I\'m probably the only woman in that place\'s history to ever get in there, and that makes me feel pretty darn special.\r\n\r\n<P>Maybe these are all a lot more strange in my head. </P> \r\n\r\n<P>Possibly the strangest thing is watching the guy next to me cleaning his desk.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nOooh, there\'s been a bad piece of press about a project I\'m involved in, this is exciting.  However, if it results in the project being scaled down or changed and I lose my job, that won\'t be very exciting.  Nevermind.\r\n</P><P>\r\nHappy Holidays!    </P>'),(258,'<p>\r\nI decided a couple of days ago that I am no longer going to date a girl I have been seeing for about 2-3 weeks. Not that I have had a bad time with her, actually I have had a great time with her. Just that I am not the type of guy that can just drop everything I am, and everything I usually do just to be a good boyfriend. I get in trouble with this every time I date someone new. Is it my failure, or lack commitment energy? I donno! \r\n</p>\r\n<p>Sounds like the Alexandria house is swarming with excitement with their new addition. I wonder how things are around there, I am sure it still carries the warmth that I felt over thanksgiving. More so, now that mr. Swindog himself is now a full time member!\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nMy house is much warmer now that my roommate (k2) has returned from her extended stay in New York. It was nice to have a conversation with her this morning. Nice to have someone ask, \"hey, you hungry? I am gonna make somethin to eat!\" Of course, it is also nice that she is around to make sure the toilet seat stays down.\r\n</p>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/258_1.jpg\' height=\'250\'>\r\n<p>\r\nI miss talking to my friends, its been a while since I have talked to my friends. Swindog aimed me and asked if I was depressed. No, not depressed. Consumed by a girl, consumed by work, consumed by Deltron 3030, thanks AGS.\r\n</p>\r\n'),(259,'<P>I once sucked on a telescope so long that I saw the sun burn out.  My mom told me that i\'d go blind, but I woke up the next morning seeing only faint images of jesus sitting on a toilet.  I was so sad my mom had me hospitalized for 4 months?then came the TV dinners?\r\n-Oh how left over TV dinner fat makes you most happy when you?re all alone on a Thursday night. Down in the bowling alley of 1986 Florida ringworm leather couch stations.  I remember watching The Flight of The Navigator, Disney always knew how to molest me with flying saucers and blue screens.</P>\r\n\r\n\r\n<PRE>-TUBE 2:6</pre>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/259_1.jpg\'>'),(260,'<P>\r\nWell it\'ll be a cold Christmas for the Chastain/Mayfield household visiting my mom in Des Moines this weekend.  Zero degree lows at night 9 not that I\'m likely to actually be out in it, but it makes me feel tougher just being near harsh elements (even if the nearness comprises the wall of a house and to comforters).\r\n\r\nMom\'s pretty jazzed about us coming.  Sister Sue is bringing her 2 teens and I\'m brinigng my 2 teens.  Hope mom hasn\'t forgotten that teenagers are basically sub-humans and appropriately lowers her expectations or the visit - short as is may prove too long.\r\n</P><P>\r\nOl\' Bernard is gonna stay with us at least another semester.  He\'s actually pretty fun to have around - even if we do fight some.  I know he appreciates getting away from the poverty of his Mom\'s place and sharing our household - and it makes me feel pretty good about sharing our blessings with him.   But Lonna is the real star.  She already had 2 boys and didn\'t want anymore - but she agreed to it anyway because she knew it was important to me.  Now she puts in as much time with B man as I do - and she\'s pretty good with him, too\r\n</P><P>\r\nWell I better go to bed, cuz I\'m beat - but I finally got a toy website going and I play with it every night till I pass out (Like now).  Any words of widom on building a site, and tools to use, etc would be appreciated.\r\n</P>\r\n\r\n   '),(261,'<PRE>\r\nTo      : <a href=\"http://www.kirstinashe.com\">K*.com</A>\r\n\r\n\r\n----- Message Text -----\r\nho ho hooO,O,O,oo man, office parties--\r\n\"i had that last time.\" \r\n\"what is that?\"\r\noh my ho, ho, ho, i\'m fat.\r\n\r\ni think it\'s the lobster:\r\nboullaboullaboullaboise!\r\nwhat? good lord,\r\ni can\'t hear for the noise.\r\n\r\nis that your specialty?\r\nit looks like an aquarium exploded.\r\noh dammit, i did it again.\r\nexcuse me, i\'m drunk. i\'m bloated.\r\n\r\ni don\'t know what to do,\r\nto act, they\'re all watching.\r\nwhen i was buying presents today,\r\ni got a ticket for parking.\r\n\r\nback to the house for some news,\r\nnude women, the show.\r\nthey look kind of like...\r\nwell, ya\' know.\r\n\r\nhave another drink,\r\ni made them all week,\r\nno, they are stong.\r\nmariah carry, that freak.\r\n\r\npresents go all around,\r\nbarbies, candy canes, sexy lariats.\r\ni wish k. got one,\r\ni\'d like to see her wear it.\r\n\r\noh my, lotion, i love it\r\nlet me just, SNORT!\r\nhere, have a napkin.\r\nhere, have a tart.\r\n\r\nIt\'s christmas time, swinging,\r\nsinging, nice little poem.\r\nnot read out loud, no one will know.\r\nwe didn\'t get snow, but it blows.\r\n</PRE>\r\n'),(262,'<P>It may be just me, but I really do feel about a hundred bucks more sexier with my hair chopped and colored and fucked with just so.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I dunno. Maybe its just me! A HUNDRED BUCKS! fuuuuck.</P>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/262_1.jpg\'>'),(263,'if post gets through then something has gone very very wrong.'),(264,'<PRE>\r\nDearest,\r\n\r\nRacing shadows against the clouds,\r\nDescending toward Dallas,\r\nThe site is breathtaking, heavenly.\r\nThe wonders of life and beauty\r\nCannot be sad for us.\r\nWhy the World? Why people?\r\nBut none come close to:\r\nWhy me so far from you?\r\n\r\nMy truest love,\r\n\r\nAustin  \r\n</PRE>'),(265,'<pre>\r\nWe have to stop meeting like this,\r\nMy heart only lives to see you,\r\nAnd without seeing you only dies\r\nWith a longing farther than miles.\r\nCurse the tether of nothing that\r\nHolds us apart, my love.\r\n</pre>'),(266,'<H1><TT>merry xmas</TT></h1>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/266_1.jpg\'><BR>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/266_2.jpg\'><BR>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/266_3.jpg\'><BR>\r\n<H1><TT>Note: Bruce Lee Patch</TT></H1>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/266_4.jpg\'><BR>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/266_5.jpg\'><BR>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/266_6.jpg\'><BR>\r\n\r\n'),(267,'<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/267_2.jpg\'>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/267_1.jpg\'> '),(268,'<P>\r\nAustin, his hair is a patch of gold filament all balled up in the bottom of a basket, like the kind the bunnies nest in at the pet store.  \r\n</P>\r\n<P>\r\nAustin, his heart is an ostrich egg, hard-shelled but larger than most breeds, and speckled.  \r\n</P>\r\n<P>\r\nAustin, his manner is as subtle as the 144 seperately named signature whites in the Ralph Lauren housepaint collection: Beach Find, Driftwood, Linen, Porcelain, Hampton, Salt Bluff, etc.  \r\n</P>\r\n<P>\r\nAustin, his wit sparkles like shiny things you find on the ground when you\'re walking with your head down not expecting to see anything; not just foil gum wrappers but other things like plastic jewels and beetles, and a particular smooth red seed from an exotic Indian tree.  \r\n</P>\r\n<P>\r\nAustin, he was named after a city that he also happened to live in.  \r\n</P>\r\n<P>\r\nAustin wears red winged shoes like Hermes, and is almost as fast. \r\n</P>\r\n\r\n<P>\r\nAustin is not as weird as Caravaggio\'s painting of St. Thomas inserting his finger up to the second knuckle into the gaping wound on Christ\'s side, nor is he as immodest as Ingres\' Odalisque showing her fanny, but like both Austin is the essence of composition and good lighting.</P>'),(269,'<P>I was running my fingers over my neck this morning, when I found a lump.  It\'s not insignificant in size, and it\'s kind of under my ear, and it hurts a little.  Apparently it\'s not in any place where there\'s glands, and none of the possible explanations my family have offered up seem very plausible or are very reassuring.  It\'s a bump.  Come over and feel it.  I\'m scared.  I\'m hoping that soon it\'s going to rear a little white head that I can squeeze and have pus run out of and just be a pimple, which is funny, cos it\'s not normal that you want pimples.  Mum says to keep an eye on it, and to go to a doctor if it grows.  I\'m hoping it doesn\'t grow.  </P>\r\n\r\n<P>The purpose in writing this down was to hopefully exorcize it.  That worked last time I had a \"health problem\" - I wrote the following poem and the next day what I was waiting for arrived. So yeah.    </P>\r\n\r\n<P><B>Ode to My Panties</B> </P>\r\n<P><I>You are so white <br>\r\nwashed and bleached in the sun <br>\r\nI keep looking down <br>\r\nyou sparkle back up at me <br> \r\npure and white and not so virginal<br> \r\nand I want you stained with red <br>\r\nyou should be stained with red <br>\r\nyou should have been stained with red a month ago</I></P>\r\n \r\n\r\n\r\n'),(270,'<P>The first time I met K-Dogg, she was on the porch at house of commons.  She gave me the worst \'drop dead, loser\' look I had recieved in a long time.  To my credit, she claims she gives that look to all strange guys approaching her.  I believe her.  That was back in 95?</P>\r\n\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/270_1.jpg\'>\r\n\r\n<P>Since then, we have been through quite a bit together.  Maybe not together in the sense that we were both present, or that we dated because we never have, but I did sleep on the floor of her apartment for weeks at one time.  We have many of the same friends, mainly because I am adopted by her friends.  But most importantly, we share our spiritual journeys on irregular occasions like this one where we went to lunch at a mexican food restaurant somewhere in the Woodlands.  And also, we can make each other cry.</P>\r\n\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/270_2.jpg\'>\r\n\r\n<P>We talked about boys and girls and how they get allong and do not.  I enjoy talking to K-dog about her boyfriends.  She gets them and holds on to them until they tear her apart.  I guess that is normal.  I don\'t go to the extremes that she does.  But she is an extreme person.  The kind of guys she goes for are those carabiner boys who exude rocky mountain experience.  When they hit the rocks, they hit hard.  Never harness yourself to a carabiner boy.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>This is K-dog for you, alias K2.  Also known as Kyrsten K., which is a phonetical derivative of Kirstin, not to be confused with K3, also known as K*.com, or the properly spelled: Kirstin.</P>\r\n'),(271,'no'),(272,'<P>Christmas 2000.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>after staying out all night, hanging with my uncle, I got alcohol poisoning. I was completely unpresent our sympathy christmas eve dinner.  I can\'t help but feel that the only reason we were invited was becasue my grandmother just passed away, and they knew that my mom, uncle and cousin were lost without the matriarchal leadership of ...</P>\r\n\r\n<P>oh shit  gotta go to dinner.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>anyway it was a good story</P>'),(273,'<P>I give up.  I thought it would be nice.  It would have been a sort of watermark in moving to Los Angeles.  Can you really say you lived somewhere until you have had sex there?  Sure you can.  But would you have a good reason to leave?  No you wouldn\'t.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I am going to have another one and a half years, at least, to get \'lucky\'.  It is not a luck issue at all.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Kiki said that living with girls (2) would get me laid.  Those were her exact words with the voice adjusted.  I knew she was wrong.  Living with girls is more accurately described by another of my friends as, \'living with two moms.\'</P>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/273_1.jpg\'>\r\n<P>The problem is:  do not date anyone that your friends know or that your roomates know.  At the top of the list this means EXes.  Next come friends of.  These are illegals.  Trouble is always to follow.  I have done both.  I am a proud man though. I do not like to make the same mistakes twice.  So, I am sorry darling, very sorry.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>You know, I hate being single all the time.  It is good for a while, but i am not a balanced person.  I am fairly level.  But I do have Ã°, and it does force me to spin off ever so slightly until one day it gets so bad that i do something stupid like have sex with a roomate\'s friend or a roomate\'s ex.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Sorry for any inconvenience upon the community that I love, even though maybe I shouldn\'t.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Please, don\'t make me eat my words.  I really hate writing stuff like this.  It tastes bad.  It always makes me wish there was nothing wrong in the world.</P>'),(274,'<PRE>\r\nShe is so fine!\r\nOlivia makes me blind.\r\nThere are others, but\r\nNone that so ravish intellect\r\nWith irrational thought.\r\n</PRE>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/274_1.jpg\'><BR>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/274_2.jpg\'><BR>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/274_3.jpg\'><BR>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/274_4.jpg\'><BR>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/274_5.jpg\'><BR>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/274_6.jpg\'><BR>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/274_7.jpg\'><BR>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/274_8.jpg\'><BR>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/274_9.jpg\'><BR>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/274_10.jpg\'>\r\n'),(275,'no'),(3277,'<P>\r\nA hundred men stood in a sloppy line, 3 to five abreast, as silent as the dead. They were dressed in black from head to toe, swaddled in ill-fitting coats, faces covered with ski masks. They swayed, not making a sound save for their breathing, which in the ten degree winter night formed clouds of steam around their heads. Not a star was visible in the sky; an orange glow of sodium-arc floodlights lit the scene as they waited for directions to be given.  A man in a black coat and a white sailorâ€™s cap walked out of the building, 125 pairs of eyes watching his every move. Without a word, he began walking down the snow-covered sidewalk, and, almost as an afterthought, waved for them to follow with a curt movement of his hand. The group of silent men followed jerkily behind him, colliding with each other as the moved down the street into the night, as black and silent as the face of Death itself. The date was January sixth, 1996, and this was my first day in the United States Navy. \r\n</p><p>	That morning I had woken in my motherâ€™s house, in the comfort of the bed I had slept in for most of my life. I had slept late, as usual. Today was the dayâ€”I was directed to arrive at five pm that afternoon at the recruiting center, to be driven to Columbia, an hour and a half away, to await a flight to Chicago, Illinoisâ€”to the Navyâ€™s Recruit Training Center, Great Lakes. \r\n</p><p>	The atmosphere in my motherâ€™s house that morning was a strange blend of nostalgia, celebration, and cold, deadly fear. I felt like a man sentenced to be executedâ€”there was no backing out of this now. No way. I had been \\\"pre-enlisted\\\" for about six months prior to my ship-out date, and I had clung to my imminent entrance into the Navy like a drowning sailor hanging on to a buoy. As my friends entered college, preparing to continue their education, I worked a couple of  jobs that I could have gotten easily, high school diploma or no high school diploma, and I made a bare pittance at them. I relied on my parents for any major expenses, including room and board. I gained weight, became somewhat depressed. But above it all, to excuse and explain the triviality my life had become, was the Navy. The beautiful, golden idea of the Navy. \r\nI would be a military man, like both of my grandfathers had been, and their fathers, and their grandfathers in the Civil War, and probably all the way back to eternity. Some were higher-ranked than others; there were officers and enlisted men, some probably saw action and others not, but all had served their country, and so I too was off to do the same. In my mind, however, the Navy would be serving me.  </p><p>\r\nAs I walked around the house I had spent my childhood in, amid the quiet trees and streets of Dillon, I was glad for the waiting to be over. I felt that I had accomplished something, had been accepted as an enlistee in the Navy, but not only thatâ€”I was guaranteed a special job, as an Operations Specialist, because I had done so well on the military aptitude test given to every student at Dillon High during our junior year. My grades, however, were very poor and I had been denied admission at three colleges, despite a good score on the SAT. I needed the Navy, and it was there for me when I realized that my choices for college were limited to the depressing facilities outside town, near airports, cheap hotels, and interstates. The word glowed before me like a neon sign: TECH. I wanted to be a doctor! I was supposed to be smart! Very smart! I couldnâ€™t go to tech. My pride wouldnâ€™t let me. My only honorable optionâ€”join the military. I would become a hero to my family, make the folks proud to have a son \\\"in the service,\\\" doing his duty, preserving the family name. The Navy sounded the least boring and dangerous, and offered me the best job, so I said \\\"yes\\\" and was pre-enlisted, just like that, and I spent the next several months, as I said, in dissolution. As I walked around the house that day, having the occasional cookie, trying to watch a little TV, I took a moment to congratulate myself a little. I was now an adult. I felt ready to go.</p><p>\r\n<i>to be continuted...</I>'),(276,'<a href=\"http://durak.org/sean/pix/2000-12-25/\"><img src=\"http://durak.org/sean/pix/2000-12-25/2000-12-23-los-angeles.jpg\" height=150 width=602 border=0></a>\r\n<br><b>2000/12/23 - glendale:</b> finally, i get to see austin in his post-<a\r\nhref=\"http://www.ibooks.com/\">ibooks</a> <a\r\nhref=\"http://www.swinney.org/resume/\">professional</a> habitat,\r\nworking his php voodoo on content management for the\r\nneopets. austin showed up on a holiday, showed off a very clever copyright tool he developed for <a href=\"http://www.neopets.com/\">neopets</a>\' visual assets, helped\r\nhimself to tshirts and a **CERTAIN** calendar, then took me out to lunch in an italian grocery, where the flagship deli sandwich is called `bebe jesus.\'  the wait is long, but that\'s cool, austin has <a href=\"http://www.kirstinashe.com/\">matters of consequence</a> to\r\ndiscuss, and there\'s nothing like spying on a throng of impatient hungry people in los angeles. despite the odor in my car, i completely\r\nforgot to hand back austin\'s ripe, dirty laundry from his <a\r\nhref=\"http://durak.org/sean/pix/2000-11-12/\">november excursion to san francisco</a>.\r\n'),(277,'<p>I am an evil boy. Without a conscious knowing of what I have been doing I have found myself in a predicament that is going to be hard to reconcile. I am speaking about relationships. Three relationships to be exact; all of which have good points, and bad. I think I have a big problem with these things. It is a mess, I tell you. \r\n</p><p>\r\nWeekend is coming up, there is much going on but I have found that I am going to be battling the inevitable, telling all three of them that I can\'t go on like this! Honestly, I don\'t want to date anyone right now. Then there is the sexual thing, and the friendship thing. Fortunately, I know what to do about it all, only it sucks to willingly break a heart or two, or three in my case. I am hoping that they too feel the same and that it is only my imagination that hearts will be broken. Could be that it will be my heart that gets broken. \r\n</p><p>\r\nIs it bad to be dating three people at once? Should you tell them about the others? \r\n</p><p>\r\nAll of my friends are women, and the ones that know what I have been up to are more than mad at me. I am that guy that never does these things, the guy that they have looked to as that stable type guy that commits and all that. I have let them down, and they have expressed it to me. One said, \"you are doing exactly what <U>insert ex boy-friends name</U> did, you are acting like a typical male.\" Oooh, that hit me in the soul, and it hurt. She is right though. I have done a bad deed. I repent! I am sure this will affect my karma for years to come, and I am worried about that, sincerely. I once went to a palm reader and she told me that I will have one love in my life, but it will be short lived. That\'s scary too. \r\n</p><p>\r\nWill I forgive myself? Yes, for I feel as though I am just exploring myself right now. I got into this mess because I felt alone, and then all of the sudden I hear soandso thinks I am cute, and then another soandso expresses interest, and then an old flame comes back into the picture. I want to be a part of all of them, I want to be there friend, but I also like kissing them too! Dirty, dirty little boy? I am ashamed of me. The attention is too much; I can\'t handle it. It is hard to plan my weeks; trying to remember which one I told I would do what with.\r\n</p><p>\r\nTake my advice boys, if you haven\'t learned already, keep it simple and stick to one, love her and treat that one well. \r\n</p>\r\n'),(278,'<p>I am an evil boy. Without a conscious knowing of what I have been doing I have found myself in a predicament that is going to be hard to reconcile. I am speaking about relationships. Three relationships to be exact? all of which have good points, and bad. I think I have a big problem with these things. It is a mess, I tell you. \r\n</p><p>\r\nWeekend is coming up, there is much going on but I have found that I am going to be battling the inevitable, telling all three of them that I can? t go on like this? honestly, I don?t want to date anyone right now. Then there is the sexual thing, and the friendship thing. Fortunately, I know what to do about it all ? only it sucks to willingly break a heart or two, or three in my case. I am hoping that they too feel the same and that it is only my imagination that hearts will be broken. Could be that it will be my heart that gets broken. \r\n</p><p>\r\nIs it bad to be dating three people at once? Should you tell them about the others? \r\n</p><p>\r\nAll of my friends are women, and the ones that know what I have been up to are more than mad at me. I am that guy that never does these things, the guy that they have looked to as that stable type guy that commits and all that. I have let them down, and they have expressed it to me. One said, ?you are doing exactly what >insert ex boy-friends name< did, you are acting like a typical male.? Oooh, that hit me in the soul, and it hurt. She is right though. I have done a bad deed. I repent! I am sure this will affect my karma for years to come, and I am worried about that, sincerely. I once went to a palm reader and she told me that I will have one love in my life, but it will be short lived. That?s scary too. \r\n</p><p>\r\nWill I forgive myself? Yes, for I feel as though I am just exploring myself right now. I got into this mess because I felt alone, and then all of the sudden I hear soandso thinks I am cute, and then another soandso expresses interest, and then an old flame comes back into the picture. I want to be a part of all of them, I want to be there friend, but I also like kissing them too! Dirty, dirty little boy? I am ashamed of me. The attention is too much; I can?t handle it. It is hard to plan my weeks; trying to remember which one I told I would do what with.\r\n</p><p>\r\nTake my advice boys, if you haven?t learned already, keep it simple and stick to one ? love her and treat that one well. \r\n</p>\r\n'),(279,'<p>Austin</p>\r\n<p>\r\nI\'m an old friend of bmg\'s and he told me to write you to ask what BMG stands for.  He said that you should tell me.  So--what does it stand for?</p>\r\n<p>\r\nCoonJT\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n'),(280,'BLA! Yes i think.'),(281,'<p>After seeing \"Crouching Tigger, Hidden Dragon\" I now have a huge \r\n  crush on <a href=\"http://www.esquire.com/women/gallery/001201_mww_ziyi_frame.html\">Zhang \r\n  Ziyi</a>. Tomorrow I have to go get a VCR after living without one for a year. \r\n  <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/wishlist/2RTC2JBER2E83/107-4700664-9436535\">Amazon \r\n  Wish</a> lists are Evil. I\'m going to get a second job at a sex shop working \r\n  nights so I can buy it all. end of transmission.</p>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/281_1.jpg\' width=400> '),(282,'<P>365 days in a year and i was in love for only one. 24 hours in a day and i was in love for only 15 minutes.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>If i can tell you i will try.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Soaked in paint, I was resting next to a radio. It was a Sunday afternoon, I was conducting a reassessment of every strand of every tissue in my heart.  </P>\r\n\r\n<P>I was in agony, her finger felt like tongues. There are no parallels. I?m forgetting words. Sun. Pink. Place. Red. Survival. Butterflies.  </P>\r\n\r\n<P>I cannot trust memory. Farewell to eternity.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>My mind dismantles illuminated images of her. The line and the limits of meaning are creeping around my corners. Everything is fragile. </P>\r\n\r\n<P>I discovered closure in the pavement. I have reached that low. </P>\r\n\r\n<P>This air is too thing for my accidental pulse. I am bound to ignore the expiration date on my soul. Suspend belief in cells and atoms. </P>\r\n\r\n<P>Actually I met her at a party.</P> '),(283,'<font size=6>\r\n<pre>\r\n\"Fluffy Coated Girl Sitting in Tree,\"\r\nYou are a tropical bird of paradise.\r\nI am an ornithologist with a Leica.\r\nSelling pictures of you on Ebay,\r\nNo one ever meets the reserve price.\r\n</pre>\r\n</font>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/283_1.jpg\'>'),(284,'<P>I miss the Garland Gang.  That\'s what we call our flat, and associated hangers on.  I\'m talking to one of my flatmates on a shitty ICQ webbased chat session, and trying to get him to run my webcam (he\'s in my room, I\'m at my parents\' house) so that I can see some Brad Pr0n, but it\'s just not the same.  \r\n</P>\r\n<P>\r\nI\'m also listening to \"The Sound of Garland Christmas Mix\" which is a mix tape of really cheesy pop that we gave all our associates for Xmas, and it makes me want to dance in our hallway.  It\'s two days until I see all my friends again.  We\'re doing the Garland Roadshow - moving our flat into a tent in the middle of the country for New Years Eve.  It\'ll be fantastic.  Brad and I will dance to Enrique Inglesias, staring each other straight in the eye.  Clayton and I will dance to everything else, and he\'ll accidently grope me and I will tell him off.  Simon and I will laugh lots together and try and corrupt our much sweeter other friends.  </P>\r\n\r\n<P>The boys won\'t be dressed as faeries this time, but I still like this picture:</P>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/284_1.jpg\'>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n'),(285,'<p style=\"font-family: verdana, arial, helvetica; font-size: 10pt; color: #990000\">i was looking at <a href=\"http://www.supersnail.com\">julian supersnail\'s site</a>, more specifically at the dyke parade 2000 shots.  i looked at every photo, and that was a lot.  i felt something weird stirring in my belly.</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-family: verdana, arial, helvetica; font-size: 10pt; color: #990000\">it was jealousy.</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-family: verdana, arial, helvetica; font-size: 10pt; color: #990000\">ok, so sine is meant to be my girlfriend, but it\'s NOT REAL.  it\'s PRETEND.  i want a real girlfriend.  i want to have a nice girl who will visit to give me kisses and will go walking around with me and dance with me at clubs and be a brat and make me cry.</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-family: verdana, arial, helvetica; font-size: 10pt; color: #990000\">i don\'t know if i was built to be single.  i like people.  i like to cuddle and snuggle and love and i really, really like regular sex.</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-family: verdana, arial, helvetica; font-size: 10pt; color: #990000\">hi.  i am couped up in a bumfuck hick country town with no one but my family and my brother\'s repellent friends.</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-family: verdana, arial, helvetica; font-size: 10pt; color: #990000\">sigh.</p>'),(286,'<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/286_1.gif\' height=\'150\' align=\'right\'>\r\n\r\n<p>k-dog, Jill and I went to the blackcat down on sixth st. to listen to the stingers play some movin ska sounds. I had decided earlier in the evening that I wouldn\'t go, but then after having a great conversation and meal with k-dog I decided that it would do me some good to get out and mix with the crowds. I had never seen the Stingers; therefore I didn\'t have to pay the $3 cover charge that k2 and Jill had to pay. We danced like crazy to nearly every song, till our big hearts gave out. I think we had the most fun out of everyone there. I am sure of it.</p>\r\n<p>When we got home, K2 and I made hash browns and eggs, for a late night snack. That hit the spot! I dreamt of furry, fluffy cute animals. '),(287,'<P>Well, here I sit, pondering the meaning of my every action. After a while I realize that almost everyone else is doing the same thing. The ones who aren\'t are dead, the ones who are being don\'t need to. I guess that leaves me somewhere in between.\r\n</P>\r\n<P>I always hoped I would be more....</P>'),(288,'<P>I miss having friends like BMG who will go to breakfast with me at 6:13 a.m.  I am awake because I fell asleep last night too early.  I started the spiral at 11.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>If BMG was in town, I\'d call him and wake him up.  He would rather be woke then miss an opportunity to not sleep.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>k*.com came over last night and we hiked Griffith Park and watched PI.</P>'),(289,'<p style=\"font-family: verdana, helvetica, arial; font-size: 10pt; color: #990000;\">hello, look at my body, it is red and crispy all over.  this is kinda nice looking, but god damn it hurts just a wee bit.</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-family: verdana, helvetica, arial; font-size: 10pt; color: #990000;\">today the sun came out again and i lay on the lilo (the plastic kind, not the boot OS switcher kind) in the pool until i kinda fell a little bit asleep and now, oh now, my skin is amber and beautiful but scritchy and probably ridden with cancer.</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-family: verdana, helvetica, arial; font-size: 10pt; color: #990000;\">why is it that it seems reasonable to brave cancer just to be a pretty colour?</p>\r\n<p><b>(IMAGE CENSORED DUE TO EXTREME UGLINESS.  BUT LET ME TELL YOU, BOY WAS I SUNBURNED! - olivia, 10/06/2001)\r\n<!--<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/289_1.jpg\'>-->'),(290,'<P>I suffer for my mother\'s happiness.  She owns cats.  They cause me great ill.  I lie in bed at night for hours unable to breath, wheezing, coughing.  I take several medications.  Four.  One to interfere with histimines at the point of entry: the nose.   One, an oral, to keep the histimines from multiplying and inflamming the respiratory system (too late).  One is an inhaler for the asthma, but doesn\'t really address the chest congestion, which has become the cause of my sleeplessness, sore lungs, and sore throat.  The last, is a decongestant which doesn\'t seem to work, but does seem to make all the other symptoms more pronounced.  I should be taking ibuprofen.  My new habit of grinding my teeth while trying to clear my throat has caused all my molars to ache.  I called the airlines today and couldn\'t get a flight back home.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nThe doctor says my asthma may deteriorate under these conditions.  The tissue develops scarring. My mother seems sorry.  She dotes a little to assuage her guilt, and of course has no intention of ditching her year-round cat habit for a child who appears only on the holidays.  I tell her next december I will go to India, that i will never return, I threaten to take the first flight out and she makes the saddest face, sad enough to touch a few chambers in an asthmatics irregularly beating stimulant-addled heart.  Sad emoticon here.\r\n</P><P>\r\nThe cats continue to charm the household with their coy antics.  I feel as if the lining of my lungs is peeling off.   I want to hate them and I fantasize that they will disappear.  But they love me just as much as the next person and their little faces belie none of the spite I would like to attribute to them.</P>'),(291,'<P>I was going to spend New Year\'s Eve with one of my capricious blonde lady friends who was going to import herself into town. It was not meant to be. So alone it is. I have no resolutions, it was Very Difficult year. With the precision of a nuclear bomb I shall enjoy the night.</P>'),(292,'<P>K*.com: \"You get attached and you don\'t want to let go even though it isn\'t right.\"</P>\r\n\r\n<P>\"There is a german guy I met that I am not over.\"</P>\r\n\r\n<P>She wants to go to music school in Germany.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I haven\'t got any love interests.  I just want to take a hot bath.[msg(sine)] i am fine\r\n[msg(sine)] i just had one of those times today where i have a bunch of fun\r\n            with a girl, but then i get really crabby and reclusive\r\n[msg(sine)] i believe it to be a reaction tied in with yin/yang\r\n[msg(sine)] i don\'t know how my normal daily life is different.  it may be\r\n            that i choose to do things and then change what i am doing really\r\n            fast\r\n[msg(sine)] so that i am not doing the same thing around the same people for\r\n            very long at one time\r\n[msg(sine)] and i don\'t get backlashes, i just do stuff that isn\'t very fun,\r\n            like work\r\n[msg(sine)] have fun/ work\r\n  I haven\'t got one though.  Only a luke warm one.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I should buy some running shoes and run in them.  Sometimes I want to be Forrest Gump at that time in life, running across the united states with a bunch of wierdos following me.</P>\r\n\r\n<Pre>\r\n[msg(sine)] i am fine\r\n[msg(sine)] i just had one of those times today where i have a bunch of fun\r\n            with a girl, but then i get really crabby and reclusive\r\n[msg(sine)] i believe it to be a reaction tied in with yin/yang\r\n[msg(sine)] i don\'t know how my normal daily life is different.  it may be\r\n            that i choose to do things and then change what i am doing really\r\n            fast\r\n[msg(sine)] so that i am not doing the same thing around the same people for\r\n            very long at one time\r\n[msg(sine)] and i don\'t get backlashes, i just do stuff that isn\'t very fun, like work\r\n[msg(sine)] have fun/ work\r\n[msg(sine)] that isn\'t completely correct though because what i am refering t\r\n            is very much tied to intense situations\r\n[msg(sine)] if someone gets too close to me for a moment or a little while, i\r\n            react with a backlash later on\r\n[msg(sine)] how much later on?\r\n[msg(sine)] well, about as much later as it took to get there in the first\r\n            place.\r\n[msg(sine)] so if i hang out with a friend for a 2 hours and then we have an\r\n            intense emotional episode\r\n[msg(sine)] then two hours later i experience a backlash\r\n[msg(sine)] and i get reclusive and spiteful\r\n[msg(sine)] i hate it\r\n[msg(sine)] i really just want to be nice to people all the time\r\n[msg(sine)] or nice with people\r\n[msg(sine)] i want to be close\r\n[msg(sine)] oh man, it is all fucked\r\n'),(293,'<p>yesterday i woke up sucking a lemon<br>\r\nsleep the new year schleppy dong<br>\r\nmaking carrotine scrunched faces<br>\r\nand when the cube drops<br>\r\nit\'s your ass</p>\r\n<p>so sleep the new year schleppy dong<br>\r\nand i\'ve had about enough of your attitude<br>\r\nmr. overgrown baby man<br>\r\nmr. beans and rice frying pan stan<br>\r\nit\'s a new year now<br>\r\nand that means i don\'t have to listen to your<br>\r\nfillabuster antics anymore<br>\r\nwelcome to the millenia of being ignored</p>\r\n<p>and sleep the new year schleppy dong<br>\r\nand dance close with the lover<br>\r\nto the lover\'s favorite song<br>\r\nand save a slice for me, mr. wong<br>\r\nit can\'t be long now<br>\r\nthen we\'ll concatenate the centuries gone<br>\r\nin a memory train<br>\r\nand some chilis baby back baby back baby back ribs</p>\r\n<p>happy new year, schleppy dong!</p>'),(294,'<P>New Year\'s Eve was a couple days ago.  Many people made resolutions to change their life in  12 months or less.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I don\'t really believe in that.  I am on a fiscal system.  Every 4 months I take my goals, evaluate my progress, and adjust my direction or make new goals.  Usually I have only one goal, maybe two.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>But for the spirit of New Year\'s Eve, I want to make one for the entire year.  I think I came up with one that is fairly simple:</P>\r\n<P><STRONG>This year I will finally push myself over the edge.</STRONG></P>\r\n\r\n<P>What is your new year\'s resolution?</P>'),(295,'<a href=\"http://durak.org/sean/pix/2000-12-25/\"><img\r\nsrc=\"http://durak.org/sean/pix/2000-12-25/2001-01-01-griffith-park-01.jpg\"\r\nheight=150 width=606 border=0></a> <b>griffith park</b> on the way\r\nback to san francisco, i got to check out the alexandria compound at\r\nhalf capacity - <a\r\nhref=\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/userpages.phtml?username=kiki\">xianfoy</a>,\r\n<a href=\"http://www.kirstinashe.com\">kirstin</a> and <a\r\nhref=\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/userpages.phtml?username=Austin\">austin</a>\r\n- they took me to marvel over los angeles food ($10 usd for a bagel,\r\nthanks :-) and then xianfoy led the sublime sunset tour of griffith\r\npark. despite living in la for two years i had only seen this place in\r\nthe <a\r\nhref=\"http://us.imdb.com/List?endings=on&&locations=Griffith+Park+Observatory,+Los+Angeles,+California,+USA&&heading=18;with+locations+including;Griffith+Park+Observatory,+Los+Angeles,+California,+USA\">movies</a>. nice\r\nway to end a vacation and kick off the new year.\r\n\r\n<br><a href=\"http://durak.org/sean/pix/2000-12-25/\"><img\r\nsrc=\"http://durak.org/sean/pix/2000-12-25/2001-01-01-griffith-park-02.jpg\"\r\nheight=150 width=606 border=0></a>\r\n\r\n<br><br>\r\n'),(296,'<P>Xerox the Intergalactic SuperBOOBIE is attacking planet Mezzotint. ?MEZZOTINT THIS!?  I shall cover the streets with cards displaying this crucial warning. It must be said. </P>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/296_1.jpg\'>                                  \r\n\r\n<P>engravers need to feed their children too. MEZZOTINT THIS!</P>\r\n'),(297,'<P>She entered my ministry of arts with an abused piano, like my carved shadow, following and digging a hole behind me.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>She situated me in the company of the extraordinary just to beat my amusement, and my congruent search for arms to collapse in.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>She was sleeping under pianos, drinking next to cellos, dressing in pale pink underwear, playing with me like a new toy with chew marks of her ownership.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I knew she longed for a dark room with two beds and an open window. I knew she injected rain, and deprived me of food so that I would learn her discipline.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Six storms after midnight and nine rooms down the hall,\r\na clumsy girl stumbled into my pile of magazines.\r\nNot much later, her room was my castle.\r\ndeath to her morals, death to her threads,\r\ndeath to her memories, death to her past\r\ndeath to her medication, death to her will,\r\ndeath to her diary,long live my cruelty.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Three sighs into one night and the bed was too small.</p>\r\n\r\n<P>Karma and alcohol made her aggressive.\r\nI made her demonstrate her talent, \r\nShe made me showcase my weakness,  \r\nI was waiting for an accidental meeting with purity in the next city. \r\nCrawling for talent, a spare change.\r\nMemorizing her eyes for repetition and confessions.</p>\r\n\r\n<P>I bow for status, holding hands and confronting a barricade of grief.\r\nTaking time to concentrate on our sparks and her voice.\r\nThe one condition was not owning an ounce of mercy\r\nAnd only surviving on passion or an imitation of it.</p> \r\n'),(298,'<PRE>\r\nGarlic,\r\nA beautiful meal is twisted around my lower chakra.\r\nTi voglio bene, like a good itallian meal.\r\nHow come a three dollar sauce tastes so good?\r\nAnd the last glass of a month old white...\r\nWhy was that wine the best i have had?\r\nMy thanks to you is a kiss for all this bliss.\r\n</PRE>'),(299,'<P>On my way into the parking lot of my apartments tonight, I realized consciously for the first time that the parking spaces are very thin, and very narrow. They are a bitch to park in correctly. Some people are good at parking.  Some people are very bad at it. Some don\'t seem to be trying at all, but who knows. I have been mediocre about it lately, but now that I\'ve realized how very thin and very narrow these parking spaces are I will change I will improve my performance, and drastically.  From now on I will consider it a game to ace the parking lot. I have to be deliberate about this because my vehicle takes much physical strength to steer, to say nothing for parking gracefully. </P>'),(300,'<P>For the moment, I am depressed.  A slight smile moves across the face because I haven\'t been depressed in several weeks.  I have that sad feeling that moves over my body in waves.  It is a sadness for who I am and everything that I do.  It is the saddness that I get when I am open with a friend and I talk about myself.  I do not know why sharing leaves my mind burdened but it does.  Maybe it is guilt.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI haven\'t worked genuinely in a month and that lack of accomplishment hurts.  I am only happy when my mind is free.  Right now, it is free to do a great many things, but there is a small part that wants to do what I am supposed to and work with people and be productive.\r\n</P><P>\r\nThen there is the part that wants isolation.  It is not loneliness.  It is quietude.  I want me.  I want all others that I have no love for to stay away.  Those that I love, I want around me.   Sometimes, not even them, this is only when I need to collect my thoughts.\r\n</P><P>\r\nTomorrow I am going to work.  I will still feel sick, a little.  I want to go to work though.  I want to get something new to work on and I want to finish it.  I still don\'t feel like talking to people about work, but I will try.  I don\'t know what is stopping me.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI need physical exercise to get this feeling out of me.\r\n</P>'),(301,'<p>My friend Rachel turned 20. So I called her and told her that at long last the mystique is gone, it has expired now that she\'s is not in her teens.</p>\r\n\r\n<P>I don\'t know how to react anymore to someone I can\'t be with and can\'t be without.</p>\r\n\r\n<P>What keeps me from Depression is knowing I will see U2 in concert this year. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>To cheer up the screen you are currently viewing, below is bjork.</p>\r\n\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/301_1.jpg\'>'),(302,'i miss my friend\r\nshe went to disney world with her mom\r\nshe asked what i wanted her to bring back for me\r\ni told her I wanted a plush tar baby from \"song of the south\". she said she would try. she is my best friend. \r\nsometimes my apartment is like a plastic hamster box but usually i like it.  \r\ni like the song called \"music\" by madonna and mirwais ahmadzai. the strippers sure seem to like it. i love musicians. i like that song \'lack of almost everything\' by eyehategod. the live one from austria. i think it was sweet of them to dedicate it to charles bukowski.\r\nmy favorite food is cheerios sometimes. with vitamin d milk.\r\nthis bitch x looks too complicated for me. it keeps writing all these words and i don\'t do anything. \r\nme and brad finished writing a good song today. i\'m looking forward to having it subverted tomorrow at band practice.\r\ni hope my friend is going to come home safe and bring me \'darby o\'gill and the little people\' action figures. that was the second movie i remember seeing that wasn\'t a cartoon.\r\n'),(303,'<P>i miss my friend</P>\r\n\r\n<P>she went to disney world with her mom</P>\r\n<P>she asked what i wanted her to bring back for me</P>\r\n<P>i told her I wanted a plush tar baby from \"song of the south\". she said she would try. she is my best friend. </P>\r\n<P>sometimes my apartment is like a plastic hamster box but usually i like it.</P>  \r\n<P>i like the song called \"music\" by madonna and mirwais ahmadzai. the strippers sure seem to like it. i love musicians. i like that song \'lack of almost everything\' by eyehategod. the live one from austria. i think it was sweet of them to dedicate it to charles bukowski.</P>\r\n<P>my favorite food is cheerios sometimes. with vitamin d milk.</P>\r\n<p>this bitch x looks too complicated for me. it keeps writing all these words and i don\'t do anything. </P>\r\n<P>me and brad finished writing a good song today. i\'m looking forward to having it subverted tomorrow at band practice.</P>\r\n<p>i hope my friend is going to come home safe and bring me \'darby o\'gill and the little people\' action figures. that was the second movie i remember seeing that wasn\'t a cartoon.</P>\r\n'),(304,'This goes out to a girl, who I hope will never read it:\r\n<p>\r\nYour smile is like a thousand candles\r\n<br>\r\nI would cross a desert to simply be witness to you\r\n<br>\r\nYou mean more to me than you will ever know\r\n</P>\r\nThat\'s it\r\n'),(305,'!!!\r\n</p><p>\r\nwhen i wake up, i immediately check my email if email is available to me. sometimes i pee or putter first but sometimes i have been dreaming about checking my email or the people who might write me or the work i should have been doing, so i roll out of bed and beeline for the machine.\r\n</p><p>\r\n\"checking my email\" actually means flipping through all my screen sessions and looking for anything of note that may have occured while i was asleep. scrolling back through <a href=\"http://www.efnet.org\">irc</a> buffers, checking to see what /m messages have arrived on <a href=\"http://www.icb.net\">icb</a> during my time of idleness, and looking at my my personal email. it\'s usually not till later in the day that i deal with workmail and mailing lists.\r\n</p><p>\r\nnow, the great thing about this, is that this morning, when i woke up, there were things that had happened since i went to bed that made me laugh and feel joy and love my friends. like this:\r\n</p><br><br>\r\n<tt>\r\n<*s5*> i\'m stoned<BR>\r\n<*<a href=\"http://www.steve.org\">s5</a>*> the simpsons is really funny\r\n</tt>\r\n<p>it might not be really funny to YOU that my diminuitive gayish friend steve was stoned, but i love steve and know him so well, and waking up to the thought of him stoned, drooling, and guffawing at the simpsons really sets my day off right. i mean, this morning, i started my day with this, affection and laughter, brought to me by the internet! it\'s so cool!\r\n</p><p>\r\nok thanks.'),(306,'<p>Starboard focus screaming and the lights beneath which castles<br>\r\n   blossom like extemporaneous thinking kites<br>\r\nFor you I have ground these kernels<br>\r\nFor you I have laid about the bed majestical with my<br>\r\n  purple xylephone soundings<br>\r\nFor you I will tear beneath the crumpling<br>\r\n  Beneath the vascillating<br>\r\nAnd the familiar, the too near montage instrument<br>\r\nPacify, calcify, for adonai<br>\r\n  and what other more noble reason we imply<br>\r\n  with the bluffing blanks<br>\r\nGive me more sanctity and I will calypso<br>\r\nGive me more logic and I will bevel<br>\r\nThis is all that I mean to say<br>\r\nThat for you the scrunching of brows<br>\r\nIs the symbol of joy<br>\r\n  And I am your pick-up truck<br>\r\n  And I am your harmony voice<br>\r\n  And I am the brilliance that spills down your face</p>\r\n<p>taken from <a href=\"http://www.jessejoker.org/poetryex.php?op=get&id=62\" target=\"blank\">this day</a></p>'),(307,'<P>And so I went to this party last Saturday night, didn\'t get laid, got in a fight. Uh huh. Now that you have that stuck in your head, may I direct your attention to <a href=\"http://community-2.webtv.net/BzzzyBee/Central\">this guy</a>. I\'m going to vegas this weekend for the first time, maybe we can hook up and \"jam\" so he can \"name drop\" me on his list of \"famous rock stars.\"</P>\r\n<P>I got a new necklace. I have never in my life bought a piece of jewelry for myself, until now. I wore it out last night and got literally at least 25 compliments. Very cool.</P>\r\n<P>I am working on a new interface/perl thinger for <a href=\"http://fonem.org\">fonem</a> so I am not updating it...until later. Sorry, soon okay?</P>\r\n<P>Saturday night, sonic\'s goodbye party. Many brilliant, unnerved, drunk, drug-addled, uncomfortable and at ease people I adore mostly and abstain from occasionally. I took my friend Laura B with me and she was amazed at the people who were there. Me too. Can we do it again sometime under not so sad circumstances?</P>\r\n<P>I\'m a vampire, I\'m a zombie, I\'m a vampire. I\'m alive. This week, I am kinda glad that I am.</P>'),(308,NULL),(309,'<P>it wasn\'t supposed to happen like this.  i was supposed to get the gift off ebay and give it to her and she would think i am the most on point person she knew because my present for her is so great and exactly what she wanted.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>now i have a mission in life:  to make up for this error.  i will find another and it will be hers.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>it will be done.</p>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/309_1.jpg\'>\r\n<font color=\"red\">\r\n<blockquote>\r\nDuke Ellington at the Piano - Songs and Piano Solos, published by Robbins Music Corporation, copyright 1943; 17 selections; 48 pages; fair condition; some staining and cover wear upper right front cover; book is complete.  Selections:<p>\r\n    <ol>\r\n        <li>I Got It Bad\r\n        <li>A Portrait of Bert Williams\r\n        <li>Bojangles   \r\n        <li>Five O\'Clock Drag\r\n        <li>Day-Dream\r\n        <li>In a Mellow Tone\r\n        <li>Dusk\r\n        <li>I Never Felt This Way Before\r\n        <li>All Too Soon\r\n        <li>Concerto for Cootie\r\n        <li>Bli-Blip\r\n        <li>The Brown-Skin Gal in the Calico Gown\r\n        <li>Morning Glory\r\n        <li>Blue Goose\r\n        <li>Oh! Miss Jaxson\r\n        <li>Serenade to Sweden\r\n        <li>Ko-Ko\r\n    </ol>\r\n<p> \r\nBuyer to pay fixed cost of $3.00 for shipping and handling<p>\r\nCheck out my other auctions for more piano music from the 1920s-1950s. Also popular, jazz and ragtime books.\r\n</P></font>'),(310,'<PRE>\r\nle> you guys\r\nle> i just had a childhood trauma lifted\r\nle> austin i\'m going to type this out, i want you to put it on your site on\r\n          my behalf\r\nle> i\'m too sleepy to do it\r\nle> so here\r\nle> i was walking down the street with peter and i mentioned that today i saw\r\n          a kelly green el camino\r\nle> and he didn\'t know what color kelly green is\r\nle> so i explained it to him\r\nrobotec9> ok\r\nle> and in explaining, i had a childhood memory of my mother making pep squad\r\n          costumes for the other girls in my third grade class\r\nle> because, they had to have kelly green underpants to wear with their\r\n          outfits, cuz it was a school color\r\nle> and that is how i learned what color kelly green is, because of these\r\n          cheerleader underpants. in lawton oklahoma in the early 80s.\r\nle> it was around this time that i developed my affinity for el caminos as\r\n          well.\r\nle> but, the childhood trauma that was lifted was not really related\r\nle> i called my mother to ask her to remind me about the pep squad uniforms\r\n          and during the phone call i remembered that during that year i was\r\n          in a school talent show\r\nle> i sang \"that\'s what friends are for\"\r\nle> and until today i carried with me the memory of being very bad in this\r\n          talent show\r\nle> because no one had let me practice singing into a microphone, so when i\r\n          went out on stage and my voice was amplified i tweaked out\r\nle> so, i have always felt upset about this talent show.\r\nle> but tonight, my mother informed me that i was not bad in the talent show\r\nle> she and i have not spoken of this talent show for at least 10 years.\r\n\r\nle> but she told me that i was actually GOOD in the talent show, despite what\r\n          i may think\r\nle> so i\'m feeling a lot better about everything now.\r\nle> also i ate dinner so i think that helps.\r\nle> the end.\r\n</pre>\r\n<!--\r\n<center>\r\n<table border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0 bordercolor=\'gray\'>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td align=\'center\' bgcolor=\'black\'>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/310_1.jpg\'>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td align=\'center\' bgcolor=\'black\'>\r\n<font color=\"gray\"><h2><TT>Bad Elly</TT></h2></font>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</table>\r\n</center>\r\n-->'),(311,'<P>I\'m at work right now, the job that I have previously loved, and felt that I was going really well at and was all excited about.\r\n</P><P>\r\nExcept for now.\r\n</P><P>\r\nRight now I want to curl up in a ball and bawl my eyes out.  I\'m trying to organise displays around the various shopping malls in the area, and they\'re all being mean to me, and wanting me to pay, and having height restrictions, and just bullying me. My boss is listening in on my phonecalls and telling me how to do things differently, and while her advice is good, it\'s making me feel woefully inadequate, and I  just feel like I am no good at this job, and I\'m over my head, and I\'m messing everything up and there\'s no chance I\'ll get my contract extended and everything will be a complete disaster. \r\n</P><P>\r\nI majored in Multimedia, not PR.  Anyone want to pay me to make them a cd-rom instead?</P>'),(312,'<font size=-1>\r\n<PRE>\r\nFrom aswinney@swinney.org Wed Jan 10 09:01:28 2001\r\nDate: Wed, 10 Jan 2001 08:58:40 +0000 (GMT)\r\nFrom: Austin Swinney <aswinney@swinney.org>\r\nTo: \r\nSubject: hi\r\n\r\n\r\ni just saw traffic.  it was a very downward pulling movie.  all the\r\ncharacters are dirtied by the drug big top.  people are out doing each\r\nother to get what they want.  they get high, they crash.  the doers do\r\nwell by not doing and the do nots do bad by not seeing.  the visionaries\r\ndo well to get what they are looking for.\r\n\r\nempathy and sad feelings go with the people who cannot see what they are\r\ndoing to themselves and those around them.  why doesn\'t the camera spin\r\naround and give them a view of their eyes\' sight?  that was me.\r\n\r\nwhy do we not know ourselves, all of us.  we live with ourselves our whole\r\nlives.  if only we could be together.  humans are a separated\r\nhurd.  separation brings intelligence.\r\n\r\ni will probably post this on my site because that is what i do.  really\r\nthough, i was writing it to you.  this is the way i get when i don\'t go to\r\nthe gym.  i am an endorphin addict.\r\n\r\naustin\r\n\r\n______LessThanNetZero Ghetto Internet Excess and Email_______\r\nDownload Now     http://www.swinney.org\r\nRequest a CDROM  austinzero@swinney.org\r\n_____________________________________________________________\r\n</pre></font>'),(313,'<p>\r\nbreakfast: grapes. coffee. cookies. coffee. grapes. cookies. coffee.\r\n</p><p>\r\ngo in the kitchen, look at the loaf of bread i bought yesterday. peer at the avocado sitting next to it. try to imagine how bread and avocado can work together to equal a nutritive (if that\'s not a word i don\'t care) breakfast.\r\n</p><p>\r\ni\'ve got a muscle spasm in my back. caused by a pinch nerve in my neck. caused by typing. caused by a need to feel connected. caused by... the human condition.\r\n</p>\r\n'),(314,'<pre>\r\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-N-E-W-S-=-B-U-L-L-E-T-I-N-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\r\nMatsukaze, aka Sean, is in the hospital recovering from\r\na collapsed lung.  his brother daniel says he is fine.\r\nsean will be in the hospital for another one to two\r\ndays.  his direct line there is 415-202-1695.  the \r\nhospital is 2425 Geary, near Divisadero.\r\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-E-N-D-=-B-U-L-L-E-T-I-N-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\r\n</pre>\r\n<TT>14:36:15 robotec9: sean is in the hospital with a collapsed lung.  i am leaving for san francisco via my house to pick up  some things.  i be back sunday.\r\n</TT>\r\n<BR><BR>\r\n<center>\r\n<a href=\"http://durak.org/sean/\">\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/314_1.jpg\'>\r\n</a>\r\n\r\n</center>'),(315,'<P>The long haul to recovering from an immensely satisfying one-month hiatus from one\'s life is to take some time to familiarize with old surroundings, and squeeze what we have become into the tiny space I sometimes call home.  I have grown in ways my kitchen hasn\'t; the living room did a double take, barely recognizing me; the stairwell remarked upon my new shaggy do; the bathroom, like an abandoned cat ignored me by withholding hot water; my bedroom attempts solace, and it is a good friend; the studio developed a stutter in my absence and I am going to have to send it to therapy; the garage too, needs a salve and some attention-- looking saggy and depressed, I walk through tears and snot; the backyard, once a social hub is an enraged child wanting attention; luckily, natasha the disciplinarian, is sweeping the place back into shape.</P>'),(316,'<P>It is Thursday night and I want don\'t want to study anymore.  I\'d rather talk on the telephone and go out dancing with my buddy who just got back from Hawaii.  I\'m not a jealous, petty person, but I must admit that when I saw that handsome tan on Arnie, I was swooning... and Natasha was radiant, too.\r\n</P>\r\n<p>\r\nFor dinner, I ate like a pig!  I had one bag of corn chips, some broccoli, and a hefty heap of doodads that arnie found in his dead grandmother\'s closet.</p>\r\n<p>\r\nmy new haiku to austin:</p>\r\n<p>\r\nwith or without cheer<BR>\r\naustin driving in the rain<BR>\r\npoof san francisco<BR>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n'),(317,'<P>Yesterday I took <a href=\'http://elly.org\'>Elly</a> to the airport.  We talked about <a href=\"http://chiamattt.com\">chia\'s</a> development as a jedi and that he is at the Luke Skywalker as young man stage.  This is exibited by his still lurking fascination for war and revolutionary violence--not to be confused with chia the pascifist and student of conflict resolution.  I dropped Le off at her flight.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I went directly to take <a href=\"http://durak.org\">Sean</A> some computer gear and razor.  He is doing well.  I wrote more on that, but it is on my laptop at his apartment, stranded without an internet connection.</P>\r\n\r\n\r\n<P>Right now, I am at <a href=\"http://www.hungry.com/~yeti/\">peter\'s</a> flat.  we met up for dinner last night and and and ate, drank beer, drank coffee.  We talked about a bunch of stuff.  Power companies.  We talked for a while about how to steal ATM machines.  Whether you should impale it with a fork of some kind and drive off with it, blow it up, use a harpoon, use a hay bail lifter, or what?</P>\r\n\r\n<P>We were in castro, the more gay then not part of town.  It was nice being hot as fuck for a change.  I don\'t mean temperature, it is kind of cold.  But just having the waiter put that extra spring in his step to get me my order.  This in contrast to earlier in the day over at the fisherman\'s warf where the sales staff at a shoe store fully ignored me holding a demo shoe in my hand wanting to try on a pair of shoes.  Also, we were seated before any one else.  Peter says this was because he was freezing his ass off for thirty minutes waiting for me.  I was really late.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I like to think we were seated because we were such a cute couple.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Anyway, we ate and it was good.  Then we went to a coffee house and drank coffee.  Then we came back to (here) his crib and played Tony Hawk\'s Pro Skater 2, and another game, for a while.</P>'),(318,'<P>I am a victim of 500 lonely nights. Thus I went looking for a saviour, but I outran him to the cross.\r\n\r\nWanted, wanted: The Girl That I Want\r\nProfession: none, or \"secret agent\"\r\n</P><P>\r\nWhat I want is Not Your Body, but the soul you contain, your architecture.\r\nYour naked incision,\r\nThe restrains of my savage admiration.\r\nThe contempt of your youth.\r\n</P><P>\r\nMy pride is limping, traveling in my extreme chaos.\r\n</P><P>\r\nTo stand at the foot of the bed and compose. This was my rebellion. Her lull body, just there in bed producing thoughts in various temperatures and surfaces. \r\n</P><P>\r\nI drain the words; reports of my demise are greatly exaggerated. My stimulating prosecutor suggests death to those who trace, delineate and memorize the bodies that held them last night.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nNobody does it as good as you. Someone might write words in my skin, but for her I become a etch-a-sketch and they fall right off. She\r\nasked me not to lie. To spill the precision. \r\n</P><P>\r\n\" I swim in your love, I drown in my loneliness \" L.C.\r\n</P>'),(319,'<p>I am trying to quite caffeine. I stopped yesterday, and have a headache today. Last night I had a headache, and so I bought a bottle of wine. That bottle of wine is now on my front lawn, along with a full serving of fussili pasta with veggies. I am also quitting drinking. I am also quitting smoking. I am also no longer smiling. This can be a good thing. </p><p> I am in love with a british girl named sally; I have never met sally. I have seen her at parties I go to. She knows me, and tells my friends that she thinks I am cute. She continues to ask about me... She has a british accent, and I am curious. Her name ends with a \"y.\" With a few exceptions, all of the women I have dated (or want to date) have a \"y\" or a \"y\" sound at the end of their name. This is not my choice; it is the choice of their parents.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I miss having Austin around; it is nice to have your bestfriend around. Can you people let Austin come see us here in Austin sometime, we won\'t let the republicans take him away? We all do miss his happy face.</p>'),(320,'<P>\r\nFor about four years straight, I wore 10 up black leather doctor martin boots.  Every day, in the rain, the sun, the snow.  I wore them to school, to parties, to a funeral, to concerts, raves and everywhere in between.  I was a grunge girl.  I had plaid shirts and scruffy clothes to match.  My docs would lead me into mosh pits or forests or wherever else I found myself.\r\n</P><P>\r\nAnd then one day, I just didn\'t like them anymore.  I wanted to look more stylish.  I  was dressing slightly more sophisticated.  And besides, my second identical pair of black leather 10 ups were almost completely worn through on the soul too.  I was digging pop music more and more, and just got sleepy and tired at concerts and raves. \r\n</P><P>\r\nI\'m having a bit of an identity crisis lately.  I wish I could still feel young.  I\'m sure Peter Pan wore docs.     \r\n</P>'),(321,'<P>I wish I had time to write in the ol\' journal more.  I never really was a big journal person; good at writing theses, but bad at just venting.  Usually, it\'s spurts of random poetry and 5-minute paintings instead.  I don\'t know.  Am I too stable, not creative enough?  My girlfriends usually get ensnared by the fact that I\'m an artist, and then leave because I\'m too stable.  I don\'t vent enough.  They feel confused.  \"You\'re so unique(weird), you\'re a painter, but you\'re always happy.\"  I don\'t do art because I\'m unhappy.  I do art because I\'m happy.  Mostly, anyways.  I\'ve known a few others like me.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Look! I\'m venting!</P>         '),(322,'<P>Tonight I am going out with Sine.  Sean said, \"Ah, going out on a rave scene photography expedition?  That is good.  I am glad your trip isn\'t completely wasted.\"</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I think this is funny.  Not funny ha ha, but funny hmmm.  This is what happens when you love your friend.  You drive for nearly four hundred miles to take them a computer and clean their apartment, take the trash out, fix things that were dropped and put them back together.\r\nAnd the friend think you must be bored and ready to go.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>What would I feel like if I were presented with this:</P>\r\n<UL>\r\n<li>get better\r\n<li>get operation\r\n<li>get infection\r\n</UL>\r\n<P>Deep breath.  I can\'t breath out of one lung.  That lung has one hole in it. little bubbles come out of it.  A tube enters my chest, an inch in diameter.  it puts in liquid and pulls out liquid.  the liquid it pulls out has air bubbles in it.  Bacteria from down the hall enter the tube.  Big trouble.\r\n</P><P>\r\nSean, I made you a sign to wear around your neck.  \"No bacteria allowed in this room.\"\r\n</P><P>\r\nI don\'t want an operation.  I need my lungs, all of both of them.  I can heal. I have faith in my body.  It does most of what I want it to, with the exception of that spinal thing.  I should not count that against it.  No, that is genetic.  Genetics are not fair.  In my case, genetics are a pain in the ass.  Anything that cannot be argued against is not fair.\r\n</P><P>\r\nMy dad has the molecules of DNA for the spinal thing.  He had an operation to enlarge the bone at the base of the spine that the spinal cord passes through.  That bone is normally just the right size, but in our case, deposits of some kind build up there requiring:\r\n</P><UL>\r\n<LI>a shot\r\n<LI>an operation to clear it out\r\n</UL><P>\r\nIn my Dad\'s case, the operation didn\'t work.  Now he is slowly losing his ability to:\r\n</P><UL>\r\n<LI>use his legs\r\n<LI>use his hands\r\n</UL><P>\r\nI set up a galileo remote control system in dad\'s house so he can control all things with a remote device on his wheel chair.  He is like this because the operation went wrong.  Now imagine how I feel sitting in a hospital bed with a 1\" tube entering my chest and a doctor telling me that I might just heal with time, in which case there is a fifty percent chance that this will happen again, or to put it another way, a fifty percent chance that this won\'t happen again.  And that if I choose to have the operation, there is a 100% chance this won\'t happen again.  I think she must have rounded up from 99.9999(+/-) wherein lurks the disasters like what happened to my father.\r\n</P><P>\r\nLet me reiterate:\r\n</P><UL>\r\n<LI>I sit here another week and my body heals itself, maybe I get infected, there is no percentage in on the chance of infection\r\n<LI>I get put under and cut open by two surgeons, no one has said what sort of things go wrong with something like that, maybe I loose a lung?\r\n<LI>I sit here for a few more days waiting to heal and thinking if I am willing to keep waiting to heal\r\n</UL>\r\n<P>I will be better.  I will be alright.</P>'),(323,'<PRE>\r\ni am trading my friends in.\r\ni am trading my stress in.\r\ni am braiding my loose ends.\r\ni am leading life.\r\n</PRE>'),(324,'<P>Knowing what you want is important. It allows you to distinguish between the dreck of life that can encroach on your personal space and those shining experiences which enrich your soul. Being able to communicate what you want and need to someone who will love you regardless is a rare thing indeed.</P>\r\n<P>The first true test, and I am glad it is over. I feel renewed to be able to see beauty from another point of view. To find in a person great insight and scope of view is why I live. I am not afraid to ask for what I want. And maybe even expect it to happen, if I want it hard enough.</P>\r\n\r\n'),(325,'<p>Concentration is so stong tonight. Unable to think of anything else but whatever it is that I focus on. Outside sounds no longer exist. My hands no longer exist. My body no longer exists. My senses nearly turn themselves off.</p>\r\n<p>I cannot sleep. I am wide awake and my stomach is in knots. I smoke too much. The cat seems to understand these things and gives me a respectful, if not loving amount of distant interaction.</p>\r\n<p>Everything blurs into two categories:</p>\r\n<p>Things I have noticed before, and things I have not.</p>\r\n<p>What do you suppose it the chemical composition of my brain right now, and how does it differ from a more \'normal\' state for me?</p>\r\n<p>My extremities are cold, the center of my body and my heat are hot. My cheeks are flushed. I do not understand how my body works, and I wonder at how many years people spend learning about those things.</p>\r\n<p>I wonder if they see themselves as more or less human and real than the people who know less about their bodies and minds as they do.</p>'),(326,'<P>I\'d had a really bad morning because one of my flatmates has told me he\'s moving out, and so I\'m really annoyed with him, but conversations with other friends has made me even more worried and frustrated with him, so at lunchtime, I went down to the beach and went wading, which mellowed me out, and then I went to this place called Burgerfuel.</P>\r\n<P>So, I was sitting at a table there, sifting through Arena magazine when this guy comes up to me and asks if I\'m waiting for someone or if he could sit with me.  I said sure, go ahead, but we didn\'t strike up conversation.  I figured he was just sitting there cos there were no other tables, although there was a whole empty counter.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Anyways, eventually the serving girl comes over and was like \"I accidently cooked an extra order of kumara chips (that\'s sweet potato fries to you) - would you two like to share them?\" and so of course we said yes.  And so then we started talking, and he had an English accent despite being south african, and he was scrawny and vunerable looking with really long eyelashes and soft brown eyes, all of which are excellent qualities. I don\'t remember his name - but he knows mine.  After babbling to him about my flatmate dilemas, I told him if he was looking for a flat, he should give me a call.  I asked if he was going to the Big Day Out tomorrow and he is - for Placebo and PJ Harvey only, just like me.  So there\'s me swooning on my stool, especially when he said he\'d hope to see me there, and was I taking my cellphone because he\'d call me, and if that didn\'t work he\'d get up on stage with PJ Harvey and page me.  </P>\r\n\r\n<P>I\'m all gooey now.  I don\'t think he\'ll call, but hey, he cheered me up - I think he was heaven-sent.  </P>\r\n\r\n<P>Excuse me while I go and giggle in a corner for ages and ages over this film cliche.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Tehehe!</P>'),(327,'<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/327_1.jpg\'>\r\n<P>i am bored.  this doesn\'t mean i \"need work to do.\"  i don\'t.  i have plenty of work to do without the help of anyone else.  i am just bored of trying to figure out what is wrong with my project.  i am bored of eating sandwiches at lunch.  i am bored of going to the gym.  i am bored of trying to understand and bored of trying to explain the meaning of friendly to myself.  le would say:</P>\r\n\r\n<PRE>le:> you need a vacation</pre>\r\n\r\n<P>but i just had one.  i think the more vacations i take, the more i need vacations.  vacations are just a transition from working most of the time to vacating most of the time.  you stop staying in one place and start leaving all the time.  leaving work.  leaving home.  leaving friends.  leaving that table that you used to eat lunch at and play dominos with your golden friends.  you leave computer chat programs.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>the path to tom hanks the fedex driver back from vacation in the bahamas standing at the crossroads of middle-of-nowhere texas.  when i saw that, i was envious.  i wanted to be in his shoes.  i was ready to deliver that package. <a  href=\"http://webopedia.internet.com/TERM/p/packet.html\">all i have are these packets.</a>'),(328,'<p>Fireplace, firelight<br>\r\nCasts ominous shadows on scarred skin<br>\r\nAnd a luminous face preceeds a luminous touch<br>\r\nWords that have been formed<br>\r\nStopped by immediacy and<br>\r\nYour heart in my throat<br>\r\nThe way cosmos condescends<br>\r\nTo our silence and the soundless \"yes\" and \"yes\" and \"yes\"<br>\r\nForming all argument<br>\r\nAnd your heart in my throat</p>\r\n<p>The closet demon consequence<br>\r\nAnd an apathetic answer to an anxious question<br>\r\nDivisive fear, once risen<br>\r\nUnchecked by necessity and<br>\r\nMy tongue in your hair<br>\r\nThe way that corn-flake terror crows<br>\r\nCareless and the stoic \"i can\'t\" and \"i won\'t\"<br>\r\nForming all argument<br>\r\nAnd my tongue in your hair</p>\r\n<p>You take me to the pinnacle<br>\r\nTo the apex of experience<br>\r\nYou show me all joy and wonder<br>\r\nYou unlock all mystery<br>\r\nYou say all of this<br>\r\nÂ Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â all of this<br>\r\nÂ Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â will be yours if you<br>\r\nÂ Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â bow down and worship me</p>\r\n<p>Hosanna</p>\r\n<p>taken from <a href=\"http://www.jessejoker.org/poetryex.php?op=get&id=53\">This Day</a>'),(329,'<p>Kinda bored and/or restless today, so, I wasted way too much time browsing through personals on Salon.com.  A portion of mine goes: </P>\r\n\r\n<P><B>In my bedroom, you\'ll find:</B>\r\n<BR>A black cat I call \'fat sausage\'.</P> \r\n\r\n<P><B>Why you should get to know me:</B> \r\n<BR>I\'m relaxing. I\'m like a jacuzzi on legs, with ears. I\'m a painter on hiatus because I somehow got sidetracked last year on the way to grad school and now find myself a 3d computer animator guy. I work on short movies and video games and stuff...I hear myself say things like, \'full-motion video sequence\', \'NURBS suck!\', and \'What\'s the poly-count on that model?\'...Hey, if it means I can afford to live in Santa Monica, it can\'t be that bad. </P>\r\n\r\n<P><B>More about who I\'m looking for:</B>\r\n<BR>That differs depending on what day it is. Right now I\'m happy and I\'m reluctant to give that up and get my heart broken again. Friends are cool. I think I want a dog. A pug! A pug that likes \'fat sausages\'!</P>\r\n\r\n<p>pucecom and axia_sidereal\'s profiles are really good.  Hey, I saw \'em first!</P>\r\n \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n'),(330,'<P>globopolis\'s investors pissed their pants and pulled out out of prague yesterday - 120 kids out of work and one texan  :0</P>\r\n\r\n<P>hungover and jobless...</P>\r\n\r\n<P>thoughts??</P>\r\n\r\n<P>fuck work.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>or rather fuck working for someone else.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>time to start up my own start up.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>for now i start with coffee and a smoke.</P>\r\n\r\n<P><FONT SIZE=7>jeb</FONT></P>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/330_1.jpg\'>'),(331,'<PRE>\r\nlove flies, butterfly wings\r\nwind howls as the bug sings\r\npatterned love, colored meaning\r\nbright flash as though to scream\r\nno touching, \r\ni love you like a bug\'s dream\r\nmindless,\r\nwith octagonal eyes for loving\r\nthree thousand sights of beauty\r\nare not enough for little me\r\n</PRE>'),(332,'<p>I\'ll never complete my web page.</p>\r\n<P>And thank god that does not judge youth and is of no importance. </p>\r\n<P>What I can accomplish and what I desire do no seem to Intersect.</p>\r\n<P>My creativity has a foul-mouthed agent.</p>\r\n<P>The Most important words to me at the moment are Discipline and Creativity. </p>\r\n<P>I used to be artistic. </p>\r\n'),(333,'<P>i went to an enormously fun party last night at the <B>Lyman Cooler</B>, a house on Lyman street named \'the Cooler\'.  i showed up with a couple of my girlfriends, one on each arm.  there was no where for the limo driver to park the strech so he left it out front and it got towed.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>there are a few things to note:</P>\r\n<UL>\r\n<li><P>i heard arnold play the blues on guitar.  not really blues i guess, but some kind of guitar style that reminded me of Austin.  that city has happy blues.  arnold was playing those.  many things remind me of Austin ever since b.m.g. said i should come back because my friends miss me.  juan too.  and then i was on <a href=\'http://lepard.org\'>b.m.g.\'s site</a> and he had a few pictures of my old neighbors, the b.m.g. his self and starseed\'s cafe.  the star\'s picture hit me the hardest.   it made me nostagic.</P>\r\n\r\n<li><P>the party goers were shooting off bottle rockets and the pit bull athena was trying to eat them before they took off.  one went into the parking garage across lyman street and exploded causing a reverberated sonic experience that was beautiful.</P>\r\n\r\n<li><P>one of the house residents drunk to the point of great creativity went across the street saying, \"mutherfuckers tag shit all around this city.  well this is *MAH* turf and i\'m going to tag it.  from this drive way to the wall across the street is Lyman mutherfucking Cooler!\"  and he walked across the street and wrote Lymon Cooler, then changed the \'O\' to an \'a\' when bystanders clued him in on the correct spelling of his own crib.  the \'N\' looked like a hieroglyphic.  i nearly lost consciousness from hysteric fits of laughter at the name \"Lyman Cooler.\"</P>\r\n\r\n<li><P>i made a robotic toy dance and danced it with kiki.  this morning she was dancing it in the kitchen to while making lunch.  very funny.</P>\r\n</UL>\r\n<P>thanks for reading.</P>'),(334,'<font size=\"2\">how about that &quot;<a href=\"http://news.cnet.com/news/0-1003-200-4539749.html?tag=st.ne.1430735..ni\" target=\"_blank\">stopping \r\n              light</a>&quot; thing? pretty crazy, eh? i am really excited about \r\n              the possibilities.... and, in other news, an interesting question \r\n              has come up: the english language capitalized the pronoun, &quot;I&quot; \r\n              while many other languages do not capitalize their equivilant. in \r\n              fact, the only pronoun in the english language that is capitalized \r\n              is the pronoun, &quot;I.&quot; doesn anyone know why?</font>\r\n\r\npuppy.'),(335,'<P><font size=\"2\">how about that \"<a href=\"http://news.cnet.com/news/0-1003-200-4539749.html?tag=st.ne.1430735..ni\" target=\"_blank\">stopping \r\n              light</a>\" thing? pretty crazy, eh? i am really excited about \r\n              the possibilities.... and, in other news, an interesting question \r\n              has come up: the english language capitalized the pronoun, \"I\" \r\n              while many other languages do not capitalize their equivilant. in \r\n              fact, the only pronoun in the english language that is capitalized \r\n              is the pronoun, \"I.\" doesn anyone know why?</font>\r\n\r\npuppy.</P>'),(336,'<P>So, since early December, I have been employed by a city council as part of a community consultation consulting the population on a specific initiative the council will (hopefully) be implementing.  My job has been to organise and run a road show of community meetings and public displays of information all around the area.  I have been working very hard along with the Communications officer from this division, and a seperate consultant.  The roadshow is due to start in one week\'s time.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Today, I come into work and find that actually, we might not be running the community consultation after all, because it\'s election year and the councillors don\'t want to draw attention to the problems.  So we have to wait.  </P>\r\n\r\n<P>Arrgh!  Politics is fascinating to watch, but as this is my first taste of actually being directly affected, it\'s also extremely frustrating.  </P>\r\n\r\n<P>Right now the communications officer and the consultant are out shopping. The chief engineer on the project is, I think, at the pub.  I just hope that my contract is water-tight so I get a big redundancy payout if my services are no longer required.  </P>'),(337,'<p style=\"color: #990000; font-family: verdana, arial, helvetica; font-size: 10pt;\">so i closed down my website and moved to melbourne.  i don\'t actually have that much to say, except that Thomas Bangalter of Daft Punk (with such hits as Da Funk, Around The World and Burnin\') emailed me to ask why i took down my website, cuz he liked it.</p><p style=\"color: #990000; font-family: verdana, arial, helvetica; font-size: 10pt;\">now, this may mean nothing to you.  but dude, he\'s a minor celebrity, and one that i dig too (i saw him dj while i was in london a few years back), so you can probably understand that i am a little bit stoked about it.</p>\r\n<p style=\"color: #990000; font-family: verdana, arial, helvetica; font-size: 10pt;\">not stoked enough to put back my journal though.  my plan is coming together and will involve webcams, audio, and a total invasion of any privacy i used to have.</p>\r\n<p style=\"color: #990000; font-family: verdana, arial, helvetica; font-size: 10pt;\">thanks for listening.</p>\r\n\r\n'),(338,'<P>Things are settling down. We just had a good 3 days in Vegas, eating piles of salmon and shellfish and salads made of cute tomatoes and figs and exotic cheeses, and of course, champagne. Nice insulation from the force-fed transition of power in Washington. I hung out with Social Distortion\'s accountant. Drunk boys asked me to be in their band, \"Fucked in the Head.\" I played blackjack and won, then the pit boss got rid of the dealer because he would toss in an extra chip here and there. I made machines spit out piles of filthy quarters, and I ended up washing my hands frequently. Dirty money.</P>\r\n<P>Free drinks rule. I smoked indoors, pretty much everywhere I went. I\'m not much of a smoker, but I have never been able to quit completely, and I took the opportunity to smoke pretty much wherever I was. It was weird. I felt like I was breaking the law, polluting the air and myself and all around me at leisure. Then I realized the air was never stale or smokey, because they constantly pipe oxygen into the casino to keep sullen gamblers awake. Pretty rad.</P>\r\n<P>I wore my vinyl snakeskin pants and my fuzzy kangol as much as possible. Kris was smiling a lot, except when we had to spend money of course. He got really nervous when I sat down at the blackjack table, but relaxed as my pile of chips grew. We\'ve reached a point in our relationship where we know this is the beginning, and we can start building shit. We drank a lot and had crazy monkey sex all over the hotel room. MMmmmm.</P>\r\n<P>The last day in Vegas was surreal and loopy from lack of sleep and pickled brain. Our friends got married the night before, we crammed 16 people into a 10 person limo and went downtown to the courthouse. Yep. Real Vegas spur-of-the-moment kind of shit. Then people started looking at me and kris and making lurid suggestions. I froze with fear, then kris took me in his arms and started slow dancing with me. Hee.</P>\r\n<P>So sunday I spent most of the day eating more shrimp and champagne and playing crazy taxi. I hate video games for the most part, but something about racing games makes me happy. I don\'t like shooting stuff. I do like driving really fast.</P>\r\n<P>Now I am back home, pissed off about <a href=\"http://fonem.org\">fonem</a>, not knowing what to do with it. I suppose I should just do something. I have a new desk, here, in a box. I am going to put it together so I can draw stuff again. I had dreams about drawing clouds last night. I think it\'s time to stop standing on the neck of the artist that I really am. Anyway.</P>'),(339,'<PRE>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nmorning oranges\r\nsucking sweet juices from pulp\r\ni am chewing you\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</PRE>\r\n<a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/B000003FKN/qid=980354004/sr=2-2/ref=sc_m_2/107-0407585-6937333\">\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/339_1.jpg\'></a>'),(340,'<p>\r\nthe street is wet and muddy and salty and slushy in places. In other places its steamy and frozen. I dont quite know what to make of the streets in this city. The lines are fresh, but the cracks are rampant. Ice plays tricks with the street. </P>'),(341,'Books, tuition, rent, food...I\'m broke.  You\'ll prolly see me on some commercial askin you to contribute 75cents a day so I can buy hald a burrito.\r\n\r\nAnd the thing is my weird expenses keep comin up. Like my bf thinks its funny to steal my underwear. If he only knew how much panties cost. Shiiet. And everyone\'s bday is comin up. \r\n\r\nSo I\'m headin over to the job board. My roomie jus got a job at the cafeteria cuz she\'s desperate for cash money.  Me too babe...me too'),(342,'<P>Books, tuition, rent, food...I\'m broke.  You\'ll prolly see me on some commercial askin you to contribute 75cents a day so I can buy hald a burrito.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>And the thing is my weird expenses keep comin up. Like my bf thinks its funny to steal my underwear. If he only knew how much panties cost. Shiet. And everyone\'s bday is comin up. </P>\r\n\r\n<P>So I\'m headin over to the job board. My roomie jus got a job at the cafeteria cuz she\'s desperate for cash money.  Me too babe...me too.</P>'),(343,'<P>A soft ray of the sun\'s light seeps in, falling onto the wall beside me, filling the rest of the room with a hollow glow, dully illuminated. i close my eyes..</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Listen to the articulate trickle of water through the drain pipes, along with the dripping of the taps. Listen to the lull of it\'s whispers, it\'s song, and feel the room dim with the passing of clouds by the sun.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Sink deeper into the water, let it flow across my body, ripple beneath my fingertips.  Deeper, deeper, until i\'m breathing the same breath back for quite some time, until the water stills.  Open my eyes, stare in awe at the blurred ceiling-sky, try to capture the veil of fractured space, to later pull it down over passing normalties, turning them into surreal pointillistic paintings.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Rise, sit up a little, breathe, then tilt my head back as the water trails off me in little dropplets.  Still myself, but for the constant dipping of my fingertips or hand into the water for some small effect entertained in amusement, childish wonderment, or simply consistency, of water on water, hand on water, hand in water, and other such things along similiar lines.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Whisper your name, tell you a story or some trivial little thing laced with words that would not come, were i to know that you were listening or that they were to be repeated.  Listen to my voice, go over whatever i may be telling you until i remember the words, until i remember which ones i happen to place emphasis on in my head, and how i do so with my voice, if only to have it sound right, be right, just once, regardless of whether or not there is something wrong in that you\'ll have no knowledge of it, of it\'s existence, even, having not been given the chance to listen.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Lay for hours, soaking, bathing, eyes closed or near closing, playing stories, poems, songs, events over and over in my head, mouthing words, whispering, questioning, even singing to myself, half-alseep, drifting away, to some other place, to some other world, alone, so alone, little girl lost.</P>'),(344,'<p>Thu Jan 25 02:14:32 PST 2001</p>\r\n<p>Reaching in the dark for the cat\'s food scoop. I close my eyes and go by feel. My ankle hurts from where I dropped a pan on it earlier in my day. I smell the stale cigarette smoke on my hands and in my jacket. I hear the neighbor\'s washing machine. Spin cycle.</p>\r\n<p>Visiting old friends tonight, not really knowing what to say. Not really knowing what to do. We talk about sex. About the Chinese New Year. About losing weight. Candles are lit. We remember other times. Other people.</p>\r\n<p>Asking the bus driver how the hell to get home.</p>\r\n<p>Taking the bus, which comes after an eternity, dropping me off far before my stop.</p>\r\n<p>Walking. Remembering. Cars and people pass me by.</p>\r\n<p>Not caring about them. Not caring about the bus anymore. I just want to walk. To be left in the peace and quiet and symbolism of my body and the road and the obstables I will meet. Of never really knowing what comes next.</p>\r\n<p>I stop in a coffee shop and ask for a drink from the quiet man with a thick accent.</p>\r\n<p>I clutch this cup, paper. It\'s warm. It feels like a weight in my hand. I feel like an automated holiday puppet with 5 simple, repetitive movements. I remember being a small child and staring at these figurines in a mixture of wonder and fear.</p>\r\n<p>I continue to my home. Pushing hard over a hill. I\'m not going to let things like gravity stop me. I must keep the same pace. The same rythm of travel so that I can think.</p>\r\n<p>I wonder who else is out there tonight walking to where they need to go. I wonder about the homeless men who I see. What they think about all day.</p>\r\n<p>And here I am. I\'m trying to figure out my head, and how it works. In the mean time, politics and business continue. I dont understand the world outside of me. I cant understand the things inside of me. I wonder how anyone makes sense of this world.</p>\r\n<p>I think I am learning that I need to come to peace with myself before I can address the issues I have with the world.</p>\r\n<p>I know that this is all cliche tripe. I know that every person who has ever kept a journal has written something like this. But there is something beautiful in it. It\'s still real to me! And to every person who has written something like this, or felt like this: Huzzah!</p>\r\n\r\n<p>-yeti</p>'),(345,'<p>i have this old velvet patchwork quilt which was originally my parents.  i may have even been conceived on it.  it was handed down to my brother, and then to me.  i hauled it between about 4 flats in auckland and then to sydney and now to here.</p>\r\n<p>whenever i get in bed and snuggle into this quilt, a sense of calm and peace decends over me and i suck my thumb and all is good in the world.</p>\r\n<p>my last lover was like this blanket for me.  i was wrapped up his love and his unconditional acceptance of who i am.  the way we were sewn together, like patchwork, bound by our common loves and hates, daily joys and despairs, the knowledge that it was just us.  against the world.  forever.  and that it wouldn\'t change.</p>\r\n<p>so now, after all the beds the velvet patchwork quilt has lain upon and been laid upon, after bearing witness to ectasy and paid, after around 20 years, the quilt is starting to fade and the seams are beginning to unravel.</p>\r\n<p>and my ex lover and i talk on the phone from other cities, and stop sharing our heartbreak and our good times.</p>\r\n<p>and life goes on.</p>'),(346,'<p><font color=\"#0000ff\">i too miss the kiss of treachery<br>\r\n<font size=\"+2\">mr. smith</font><br>\r\ni too fall through walls<br>\r\ni ache and press in furs<br>\r\nhiccup exhaustion<br>\r\nand expect everything<br>\r\nover and over and over<br>\r\n<font color=\"#ffffff\"><strong>resign<br>\r\nresignation<br>\r\nplease accept my resignation<br>\r\ni have resigned myself to this<br>\r\nresignation</strong></font><br>\r\nand the odd way the<br>\r\ncaterpillars move in my gums<br>\r\nhow this couldn\'t have ever<br>\r\nhow this was never quite<br>\r\nhow the only known thing<br>\r\nand the fuzz moves like<br>\r\nsteppe grasslands<br>\r\nin the wind<br>\r\non the roof of my mouth<br>\r\ni too miss the kiss of treachery<br>\r\n<font size=\"+2\">mr. smith</font><br>\r\ntwisted in a headstand<br>\r\nso the world appears right-side-up<br>\r\nand my <font face=\"courier\" color=\"#ff0000\">lipstick</font> is smudged<br>\r\ncarelessly across your face<br>\r\nas i am the organism inside you<br>\r\nthat purges<br>\r\nand i too am full of space</font></p>'),(347,'<PRE>\r\nrecognise this as your own nature\r\nabondon fear\r\nabandon the terror you project\r\nlet you mind rest beyond flesh and bone\r\nlook from a place of understanding\r\nyou mind is a conduit\r\nyour mind is as vast as the universe\r\nrest in this\r\nrest in the clear light of existance.\r\nthis light is divine\r\n\r\n--from Neurosis, Prayer (2000)\r\n<a href=\"http://neurosis.com\">http://neurosis.com</a>\r\n</PRE>\r\n\r\n<P>ambient guitar and drum and media.  the music is very heavy.  it is not your typical spiritual rock.  the sound is very dark and can take the mind to distant dark places.  chaos is not bad, but a state.  embracing chaos is liberating relief of the pressure to fit into conceptions.  embracing chaos as a form of happiness leads to easier found beauty in life.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>your mind is as vast as the universe.</P>'),(348,'</p><p>\r\ni have a lot of upheaval and things getting broken and relationships being inconsistent. but then i go read <a href=\"http://www.logy.org/~xep\">xep\'s site</a> and am reminded that i love xep a lot and she isn\'t going anywhere. and if i contact her she will always be xep, and i think she will always like me. once i said to her that she could say anything to me and it could never change my initial judgement of her, which was that i am tremendously fond of her.\r\n</p>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/348_1.jpg\'>\r\n<p>\r\nalso xep has a <a href=\"http://www.mildew.org\">qq</a>, who comes to my house and rescues me when i have not had coffee. sometimes we go to sushi and talk about many things, some of which are totally nonsensical and some of which are importantly truthful.\r\n</p>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/348_2.jpg\'>\r\n<p>\r\nand i go to their house sometimes and am allowed to lay between them in bed and be accepted and spoken to in quiet voices. and they fall asleep and i gather my socks in the dark and tiptoe out past the ferret cage in the hall. trip out onto hayes street with a feeling of unparalleled wellbeing because i know them and it\'s all ok.\r\n</p><p>\r\n '),(349,'<PRE>\r\nI thought I\'d free-style a little...\r\n\r\nOrange hatted\r\nin aloha house\r\nwhere time smoked\r\na joint\r\nand now she\'s too lazy\r\nto get up again.\r\n\r\nDidn\'t particularly notice\r\ntill you came naked-chested,\r\nand chula-pee rugged\r\nto make me coffee.\r\nThree cups\r\nhiking\r\nkung-fu fighting\r\npoetry writing\r\nand rodeo riding my recent rollar coasters\r\nhope I am worth\r\nthis handful of neurosis\r\nI have manufactured like pearls.\r\n\r\nToo much muscle in my head\r\nToo many wheels spinning\r\nyou set them on their side\r\ntill their whisper became\r\nsofter hushed\r\nquestioned their purpose\r\nthings could be much simpler\r\nI would like that\r\nlike you are simple\r\nand elegant\r\na mathematician\'s dream.\r\n\r\nAll that\r\nand an orange hat.\r\n</PRE>'),(350,'<PRE>\r\ni met this honey on the down stroke with no job and little money,\r\n\r\nshe is a little broke but much mo in the works than some holly rock bunny.\r\n\r\nshe has charm and style, matching nature hiking for miles\r\n\r\ni seen her in red -- beautiful looks stopped my heart\r\n                                        nearly made me dead\r\n\r\nher shirt had lil roses, beautiful smells filled my noses\r\nso hot -- send the lime green glendale firetrucks to put me out with hoses\r\n\r\nsometimes i get slumpy and my day gets a little bumpy\r\ni dont want to see nobody,  leave me all alone,  \"i don\'t want no honey!\"\r\n\r\nbut then she shows up and i rub my eyes\r\nlittle birds flit to my sholder\r\neverything is nice, and i\'m not no kid\r\n                        i am much older\r\n\r\nshe makes me happy like a crazy grandpappy\r\n                        doodlie dappie\r\nshe leaves and i head out on the block all slap happy jappie\r\n\r\nwondering: whose this girl that clocks masterpieces?\r\nsixteen track orchestral female jesus\r\nrunning off in crazy directions\r\nbut always comes back for my affections?\r\n\r\nthere is no end to this rhyme in sight\r\ni want to keep her, squeeze her, hold her tight.\r\n\r\nshe is my friend\r\n                to defend\r\n                        with all my might\r\n\r\ni\'ll keep her warm\r\n                in my dorm\r\n                        and give her love all night.\r\n\r\n\r\n</PRE>'),(351,'<p>I am trying to decide where would be the best place to live. I like boulder, but belize is beautiful too...</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I want to rent a gto and drive to the coast... I hope LinearB and Joker come with...</p>\r\n\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/351_1.jpg\'>'),(352,'do we write to set ourselves apart or bring others closer to us?\r\n\r\nponder.'),(353,NULL),(354,'<P>People shy away from you because you are a strong person. You don\'t have to show people what you do. People know who you are. So many people are wary of you, but I know that you have a good heart. You\'ve never done anything BAD. And we admire you so much, you\'re fucking beautiful. Thats why you have a support group in us. You don\'t have to say anything, people know who you are. You don\'t have to bring them over and pull out your photos and show them. Put them on the walls so that they can look at them. These people don\'t care what you\'ve done, they want to see what you are DOING. They don\'t want to hear about shit that happened in the past.</P>\r\n<P>I don\'t give a fuck what other people say. I\'m not in this to make friends, I am here to make art. This is what feeds my art. Thats why we are sitting here talking, because you see that in me and you recognize it. I think sometimes thats why I come on so strong, because it takes a strong person to be on the level. I just want to get my shit out there, to have people see through different eyes for a second, and see what a good time can be had.</P>\r\n <P>\"You must really love this.\"<BR>\r\n*points at camera*<BR>\r\n\"Yeah, well, of course. Why do you spin records?\"<BR>\r\n</P>\r\n<P>I feel sad. I just have this really strong voice, I am verbal as well as visual. A lot of people are put off by me. I think a lot of times people put me off more than they realize. \r\nRight now, I just want to draw and take photos and leave something fucking gorgeous behind, because people are quick to find fault before beauty. Especially me.</P>\r\n<P>I gotta think about this one.</P>'),(355,'<P>hi my name is Austin and i live on the second floor.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i am busy with my brother in town and trying to be my normal self at the same time.  people want me to do what i usually do and i just can\'t.  ever tried to chauffeur people around los angeles?  it is the worst.  i don\'t want to get in a car for a week.  yesterday i drove from here to santa monica (35 min) to orange county (1 hour) and back to santa monica and back home.  3 hours in the car.  i am out of patience for riding on my ass trying to think of nothing other than what exit is coming next and where do i turn and trying to to hit any cars.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>being save is not even on the agenda.  i just don\'t want to wreck.  please God, do not let them hit me.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>yesterday in orange county (shit hole) i had to deal with a rude mercedes benz suv driver flicking me off while i backed out of the krispy kreme parking lot.  he was in some huge hurry to go through the drive thru line.  partially because i had been watching amateur skate boarders for the previous 3 hours, partly because i was in a car full of people to watch, i got out of the car and hurled a doughnut at the SUV.  it sailed over the wind shield.  i hate that my aim throwing things is so awful.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>the driver got out and wanted to fight me.  i got in my  car and drove off.  the entire scene was hysterically funny.  i wish i had put the doughnut on his car antenna.  i think that would have been more brave, like the indian game of running up to your enemy and smacking him on the ass as a form of humiliation.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>yesterday went on forever.  i went to the shellac show.  shellac is my brothers favorite band ever.  well, his favorite musician: steve albini.  being with scott at that show was like accompanying a devout catholic from the baptist belt to personally meet the pope.  scott is from texas where steve albini, a native of various northern united states, will never tour.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>scott was in <B>rapture</B>.  he was deeply offended that the crowd did not appreciate the performance of such a great man as albini.  i was into the show as much as i could be without alienating my date.  but i did not come near to scott.  i don\'t think anyone in the entire house was on scott\'s level last night.  no one.  it is out of the question, really.  scott was moved to tears almost.</P>\r\n\r\n<P><B>i worry about him.</B></P>\r\n\r\n<P>can i be in a coma now?  it is sunday and i have been in my car since i got out of bed at 10:30.  when i get done typing this i am going to do elly\'s meditation that she sent me where light passes through the top of my head and down my spine and balls up in my hands, into my knees and out my feet into the ground and down toward the center of the earth.</P>\r\n\r\n<P><B>ever thought of light as being attracted into the center of the earth?</B></P>\r\n\r\n<P>i was taught that in physics things like light mostly go away from, not into.  this does not mean that we are not bombarded with light, but in the sense that large geological and astronomical bodies give off light and are bombarded by it, but light does not enter.  not the sense that energy flows through the universe into the top of my head.  after driving in los angeles for the last three days, i will gladly sit and try to get cosmic energy to pass through my head on it way into the center of the earth.  i will wonder where that energy comes from.  maybe from my friends.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i am here.  i am going to meditate.</P>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n'),(356,'<p>I havn\'t felt this way in what seems like a very long time. I dont feel depressed, i just feel a very strong sense of futility. I do nothing with my life. It does not upset me because I do nothing under the guise of being a university student. Come May, ill be guiseless and i\'m afraid the impact of me hitting the great unknown will be too much. I think about how simple a bullet looks when it enters the chamber. Its smooth. However, the nanosecond it leaves the barrel it warps, changes shape. I will be leaving the barrel soon, and perhaps the only thing im grateful of is that I do not move at over 400 feet per second. \r\n</p>'),(357,'<P>Motor is a cool club in Hamtramck Michigan.  Saturday we saw an awesome dj, Stacey pullen.  Lauren was so excited (she cant wait to tell her friends in NY that she heard Stacey pullen and the cover was only $12).  We danced, had a round of shots and some Kettle One.  (Of course there had to be something to remind me of Alexandria).</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Shawnee saw pictures of La and got homesick.  Lauren and I called the house drunk and talked to hUbbard and Arnie..the conversation went somethuing like</P>\r\n<PRE>\r\nhow do you spell your last name\r\n</PRE>\r\n<P>random.  very random.  Its been real , its been good. and its even been real good but now I gotta go back and nestle in the armpit of my ohnie.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Bye bye Detroit.  Till we  meet again...</P>\r\n'),(358,'<p>as day six dawns, i swish foul tasting saliva about in my mouth.  cigarette is the word when need is the verb.  and a glance at the day planner reveals...</p>\r\n<p align=\"center\">nothing to do again</p>\r\n<p>i\'m like winona ryder after she got fired from <u>good morning grant</u>, only i\'m male and not working on a documentary and i haven\'t called psychic hotline...yet.  i\'m not working on anything, except pieces of tail and writing fan mail and the holy grail and a way back into the pail.  and i spend a lot of time dreaming and a lot of time, not very serious at all, and a lot of time on my back, and a lot of time in vacancy (not to be confused with serenity) and a lot of time spent, generally, a lot of time spent.</p>\r\n<p>i met a boy named frank mills...</p>\r\n<p>yo thief.  where you at?</p>'),(359,'<p>This is great, being unemployed. Running around playing with your old work friends, going to movies in the afternoon.</p>\r\n<p>Actually, i get a sick feeling in my stomach evertime i check my balance. Survival mode has kicked in, racing around trying to find the next life maintainer. Some people tell me to stay where i am at, while others tell me stories of grandeur of places far west of here.</p>\r\n<p>What does your heart tell you, son. Thats what the good voice says while the other is telling me about all the cool bands playing this week. Well let me tell you something mr so an so, i got plans, i got dreams, hopes and dreams.</p>\r\n<p>I got busted people, i got busted good. I was being a childesh little coy boy. I re-engineered an entry about sex and girls after hearing that the girl had been reading. The authority is after me:</p>\r\n<pre>\r\n<font color=blue>robotec9:</font><font color=black>uh oh, do i have to take your passwd\r\naway for tampering with the evidence?</font></pre>\r\n\r\n\r\n'),(360,'<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/360_1.jpg\'>'),(361,'<PRE>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nuninspired, slightly slumped\r\nshe thinks about her life\r\nachieving great things\r\nis on her list to do\r\n\r\nthe vacuum makes noise\r\n\"rrrrreerrrrreerrrrree\"\r\nunder the furniture it whines, grinds\r\nthe music of an engine under strain\r\nit can be deafening but it cleans\r\n\r\nshe puts the vacuum in the closet\r\ncloses the door on that until next week\r\nmoves a lock of hair from her face\r\nchecks vacuuming off her list\r\n</PRE>'),(362,'<p>Hallucination, dream, or imagination?</p>\r\n<p>I dont know the answer, but I will tell the story about what ever the hell it is.</p>\r\n<p>There are a line of faces. They are expressionless, and numbered. I know that there are at least 4, and that one is labeled \"No. 11.\"</p>\r\n<p>The interesting thing about the faces is that they are in varied states of disease, and decomposure. Some of the faces are simply red and cracked. Others are missing cheeks, eyes, a nose, or just large patches of skin.</p>\r\n<p>The faces are being questioned. \"Who are you? Where were you last night? What is your name?\" The faces do not respond. They are expressionless. I wonder if someone is questioning dead, or severed heads. I cant tell if the faces are just stonewalling, or not.</p>\r\n<p>I reach out to touch the face labeled \"No. 11\" and it\'s skin is mealy, and yet slightly abrasive. Rubbing cornmeal on a flat, hard surface is similar, but does not possess the qualities of lifeless and clammy flesh at the same time.</p>\r\n<p>At this point, the No. 11 face starts to rot. It starts to turn green. It starts to fall apart. \r\n</p>\r\n<p>I\'m mortified about what I\'ve done. While the faces have not taken on a lifelike persona in my mind, and I feel like I\'ve destroyed a valuable dish belonging to my poor grandmother. Something like that.</p>\r\n<p>I tell the faces that I am sorry. That they have to be there. That people are asking them these questions. I tell them that I am sorry to have touched No. 11. For some reason, I tell them about the Indy 500.</p>\r\n<p>At this point, I leave the dream/hallucination/imagination/insanity around this time. The only other thing I recall is walking away from the faces, down a blurry and underlit tunnel, but I\'m not sure where the tunnel leads.</p>\r\n<p>Hope yall have a nice night.</p>\r\n<p>-yeti</p>'),(363,'<P>I spent over twelve hours in a Mall yesterday.  It was open from 9am - 9pm, and I was there, trying to encourage the public to take an interest in their City Council\'s efforts to clean up the beaches.  In ten minutes, I\'m heading out to that same mall, to spend eight and a half hours there.  This is not what I call fun.  However, I will be paid time and a half for seven hours of that time.  My back hurts from the dumb collapsible chair that I have to use.  My mind hurts from the lack of stimulation all day.  I\'m already bored of this job and it goes on for another month.  Help!  \r\n</P><P>\r\nI want to encourage you all to send me witty and brilliant text messages if you feel my pain - +64212127920 .  Thank you.  </P>'),(364,'<p>&lt;january&gt;<br>\r\n  &lt;e-mails&gt;<br>\r\n  &lt;sent&gt; 520 &lt;/sent&gt;<br>\r\n  &lt;deleted&gt;627&lt;/deleted&gt;<br>\r\n  &lt;/e-mails&gt;<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  &lt;acquisitions&gt;<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  &lt;hardware&gt; TDK VeloCD CDRW 12x/10x/32x drive&lt;/hardware&gt;<br>\r\n  &lt;software&gt; Office 2002&lt;/software&gt;<br>\r\n  &lt;software&gt; 3D Studio Max 4 &lt;/software&gt;<br>\r\n  &lt;dvd&gt;X-files: fight the future&lt;/dvd&gt;<br>\r\n  &lt;dvd&gt;My so called Life&lt;/dvd&gt;<br>\r\n  &lt;dvd&gt;Cowboy Bebop: session 6 &lt;/dvd&gt;<br>\r\n  &lt;book&gt;Visual guide for XML&lt;/book&gt;<br>\r\n  &lt;book&gt;Visual guide for Flash 5&lt;/book&gt;<br>\r\n  &lt;comics&gt;Amazing Spider-Man&lt;/comics&gt;<br>\r\n  &lt;comics&gt;Namor&lt;/comics&gt;<br>\r\n  &lt;comics&gt;Fantastic Four&lt;/comics&gt;<br>\r\n  &lt;comics&gt;Zero Girl&lt;/comics&gt;<br>\r\n  &lt;magazine&gt;Computer Arts #53&lt;/magazine&gt;<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  &lt;/acquisitions&gt;<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  &lt;soundtrack&gt;<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  &lt;song&gt; Tomorrow Comes Today&lt;/song&gt;<br>\r\n  &lt;artist&gt; Gorillaz<br>\r\n  &lt;song&gt; Lady With The Spinning Head<br>\r\n  &lt;artist&gt; U2<br>\r\n  &lt;song&gt; Summer - Overture<br>\r\n  &lt;artist&gt; Kronos Quartet <br>\r\n  &lt;song&gt; Sent You Up<br>\r\n  &lt;artist&gt; Knife In The Water<br>\r\n  &lt;song&gt; King Of Sorrow<br>\r\n  &lt;artist&gt; Sade<br>\r\n  &lt;song&gt; Falling Down<br>\r\n  &lt;artist&gt; Muse<br>\r\n  &lt;song&gt; Won\'t Last Long<br>\r\n  &lt;artist&gt; Tom Petty<br>\r\n  &lt;song&gt; Play My Game<br>\r\n  &lt;artist&gt; the Donnas<br>\r\n  &lt;song&gt; Leave Me Alone So I Can Rock Again<br>\r\n  &lt;artist&gt; JSBX<br>\r\n  &lt;song&gt; Good Dream<br>\r\n  &lt;artist&gt; P.J. Olsson<br>\r\n  &lt;song&gt; Bombs Over Baghdad <br>\r\n  &lt;artist&gt; Outkast<br>\r\n  &lt;song&gt; Garden <br>\r\n  &lt;artist&gt; Ani DiFranco<br>\r\n  &lt;song&gt; Things have changed <br>\r\n  &lt;artist&gt; Bob Dylan<br>\r\n  &lt;song&gt; Shit, Damn, Motherfucker<br>\r\n  &lt;artist&gt; D`Angelo<br>\r\n  &lt;song&gt; Lovely Head<br>\r\n  &lt;artist&gt; Goldfrapp<br>\r\n  &lt;song&gt; Walk Don\'t Walk<br>\r\n  &lt;artist&gt; Prince<br>\r\n  &lt;song&gt; Farewell<br>\r\n  &lt;artist&gt; TAN DUN<br>\r\n  &lt;song&gt; Ojos Asi<br>\r\n  &lt;artist&gt; Shakira<br>\r\n  &lt;recipient state= &quot;California&quot;&gt;Austin &lt;/recipient&gt;<br>\r\n  &lt;recipient state= &quot;New York&quot;&gt;Brooke &lt;/recipient&gt;<br>\r\n  &lt;recipient state= &quot;Texas&quot;&gt; Rochelle &lt;/recipient&gt;<br>\r\n  &lt;recipient state= &quot;New York&quot;&gt; Starla&lt;/recipient&gt;<br>\r\n  &lt;recipient state= &quot;New York&quot;&gt; Sam&lt;/recipient&gt;<br>\r\n  &lt;recipient state= &quot;Texas&quot;&gt; Sara May&lt;/recipient&gt;<br>\r\n  &lt;recipient state= &quot;Texas&quot;&gt; Lani &lt;/recipient&gt;<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  &lt;/soundtrack&gt;<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n \r\n  &lt;/january&gt;</p>'),(365,'<p>\r\nlet me tell you about my special friend the egg marmot. She likes to sit on your shoulder and stick her green snout in your ear and tell you what the other person in the room is thinking. indeed, this a telepathic egg marmot. \r\n</p><p>\r\ni don\'t know why she likes me best, but i think it\'s because i smell like popcorn. i work in a popcorn factory, i come from a long line of popcorn workers, and i know i was born to be one. she was born to be mine. and i sure am lucky, cause she kisses me with her little snout and i am the luckiest guy in the world. she sits on my feet when they\'re cold too.\r\n</p><p>\r\ntoday i bought us a whole bag of popcorn and ate it all, just for her. mmm mm mmm, that was really good popcorn. i must buy at least 5 gallons of unpopped popcorn kernels for us each week.\r\n</p><p>\r\ni sure do like her! she\'s my baby. the end.\r\n</p>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/365_1.gif\'>\r\n'),(366,'<p>I beleive in one world language, naturally evolving over time. i believe that humans will forget about the past, in so far as trying to re-live it. they will look to the future because the future IS natural. The past is man made, in regards to how people write about it. The history of the world has as many sides as it has cultures, borders, peoples.</p>'),(367,'<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/367_1.jpg\'>\r\n\r\n<P><TT>\r\ni feel depressed today. i woke up depressed.  illustrated by my clock saying 09:50 when i had to pull myself up and squint just to hear it speak to me with red LED bathed high morning light.  my brother plugged it in when he was here.  i will go home and unplug it.\r\n\r\n</P>\r\n\r\n<P>\r\n\r\nbut i am happy for my computer world of passing numbering.   i feel sad.  where did the stability leave itself today, tangled in my subconscious REM.\r\n\r\n</P>\r\n<P>\r\n\r\ni think i jinxed myself when i said i was happy last night.  i had everything so clearly in order.  nothing has changed.  i overlap with people.  i am never lonely.  i am never bored.  challenges are all before me.  i still have my PMA but i am comfortable.\r\n</P>\r\n\r\n<P>\r\nwhat is this all about then?  it is about never under estimating the balance, never admitting i am ahead.    never stopping to believe.  make it all seem easy in my mind.  do not think about the complexity.\r\n</P><P>\r\nmy mind teaches me a lesson about emotional hubris.\r\n\r\n</P></TT>'),(368,'<p>Good lord, good evening, good morrow.</p>\r\n<p>I write on Senor Swinney\'s site again.</p>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/368_1.jpg\'>\r\n<p>The thing I have been pondering this evening, well one of them anyway, is wide open spaces. In cities, in the woods, everywhere.</p>\r\n<p>So what is it about these places that draws me? It\'s the smell. The taste. The utter desolation, at the same time as the bone crushing fear and realization that you are free. Totally free.</p>\r\n<p>Today has been full of Richard Buckner. Some tears. A lot of weird thoughts.</p>\r\n<p>I was wondering earlier if people who see the things I write on the internet think I am totally fucking crazy.</p>\r\n<p>I spent a good portion of my afternoon wandering around in my backyard putting my eye 1cm or so from plants, and any other object I could get close to, and focusing in on that. It\'s fairly interesting the things you get from this:</p>\r\n<p>A headache</p>\r\n<p>A much more intimate view of common objects</p>\r\n<p>A few pokes in the eye that lead to itching and tearing</p>\r\n<p>I had this dream last night that I was a young boy, and that I was pulling off my toes and replacing them with pebbles. I recall that they were a beautiful agate color, and that I was excited.</p>\r\n<p>At some point the hair on my body became more interesting than my toes in my dream. I was outside and had found a preying mantis, who I asked: \"Do I know anything about life?\"</p>\r\n<p>The mantis did not reply, but in some telepathic way told me that it would assist me with hair removal.</p>\r\n<p>I allowed it to pluck hairs out of my forearms.</p>\r\n<p>Thinking about it now, and with my hazy recollection of entomology, I believe that the mantis was definately female. This was not important to my boy-self in the dream.</p>\r\n<p>At this time, the pain in my dream from hair removal caused the dream to become black and white. I could not see clearly out of one eye.</p>\r\n<p>I was touching trees. Feeling the bark on my fingers. It was slimy, almost sponge-like.</p>\r\n<p>I decided it was time to climb these trees. Reaching up for a large branch close enough to reach, on these great northern hardwood trees, I tried to clamber up the trunk. My toes fell off.</p>\r\n<p>I woke up.</p>\r\n<p>So yeah. Wide open spaces. Beauty in them. You see more things, and less things than you would ordinarily. They are eerily magical.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>-yeti: Angel or alien? Maybe a little of each.</p>'),(369,'<P>\r\nLast night around 3 thirty in the morning I cracked open the medicine cabinet in my florescently lit bathroom, in search of some Visine.  Instead, I found a strange package with a picture of a disembodied nose on it, full of furry little strips that looked like band-aids.  A little curious, I pulled one out and discovered that these strange, sticky bandaids were designed to be taped across your nose in order to help you breathe better.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nMy dad has passed on to me his hereditarily runny nose, which has led many people to ask me embarrassing questions about why I appear to be picking my nose (when I\'m really just itching it,) and was the second reason on my former boss\'s list of reasons for firing me.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nRemembering how my rebellious nose was partly responsible for my current state of, \"I\'m in a transition-phase, Thank You!\" I opened one of the funny band-aids and stuck it on my nose.\r\n</P><P>\r\nA whooosh of startlingly spring-cold air rushed inside my nose, and I had a clamourous sensation that my nasal cavities had expanded like noisy balloons.  The tape felt freeing and confining, the air was very cold flowing in and out of my nose. \r\n</P><P>\r\nI wondered, is this what it feels like to be normal and have a normal nose?  I\'m not sure if I like it.\r\n</P>'),(370,'<p>Most of the trees are without leaves. The air is clean and a bit crisp yet enjoyable under the sun. Having spent time with friends, watching movies, drinking too much last night and ending up having the foreign girl and the jill drive the bmg home in his own car, i have found peace the next day. The jill waking me up sometime after the sun rose, then coming over to the house to partake in good conversation while listening to some mice on mars making strange electronic noises. My best friend calls me on the phone, and i imediately recognize how nice a phone call can be when its somebody you long to talk to. Then going to get some afternoon breakfast with you friend the jill at the restaurant that the foreign girl works at, continuing good fun conversation. Returning the jill to her truck that was safely resting at the teachers parking lot where we had left it the night before. Daydreaming about what to do next, not wanting to plan next, wanting to just let the wind take me where i need to be taken to. Arriving at home, listening to electronic bach, sitting on the porch drinking a fine glass of water, wondering what the jill thinks of me, while i am exploring my own thoughts of her, anticipating more blissfull conversation with her later in the day. Wanting her to know, what i know about me thinking about her, writing in a protective web journal where i am neither judged nor poked fun of because i am amongst only friends that care to read what i am thinking. Am now wondering how i got into such a great mood, realizing that things are good in this light. Wanting to share with you what i am feeling this very moment. Returning soon.</p> '),(371,'<p>DON\'T TOUCH ME THERE<p>\r\n\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/371_1.jpg\' align=\'left\'>\r\n<p>No one held a gun to my head.  I VOLUNTARILY chose to see \"Dude Where\'s My Car\" on opening night on Hollywood Boulevard.  As I suspected, the movie was so unfunny it made me angry.<p>\r\n\r\n<p>Luckily, I decided to see the movie in the unruly teenager capital of the world so although the movie did not amuse me at all, I had my fellow moviegoers to amuse me.<p>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/371_2.jpg\' align=\'right\'>\r\n<p>A group of about six 11 year old girls sat directly behind me and talked throughout the entire movie.  \"What did he say?\"  \"Do you think he\'s gonna die?\"  \"What does his tattoo say?\"  I kept turning around to glare at them.  One of them said \"THAT LADY HAS A FUCKEENG PROBLEM..SHE KEEPS LOOKING AT ME, EH\"<p>\r\n\r\n<p>Two rows behind me and to my right a way, a couple made out and wrestled noisily throughout the whole film.  I kept hearing smacking noises and \"AYE!  DON\'T TOUCH ME THERE!\"<p>\r\n\r\n<p>I HAVE to use that line....<p>\r\n<CENTER>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/371_3.gif\'>\r\n</CENTER>'),(372,'<!--\r\n<P>\r\nI just found out what the salary for my new job will be, and it made me really really happy - until I stopped to figure out what I\'d get after tax. \r\n</P><P>\r\nIt turns out that although I will be getting a fairly significant rise from my job right now, I\'ll be jumping into another tax bracket, so I\'ll actually end up getting paid a fairly significant amount less.\r\n</P><P>\r\nThis is just wrong on so many levels!  \r\n</P>\r\n-->\r\n<P>I\'ve always been a fairly liberal person,and I would like to think that I had a fairly socialist nature.  But this just isn\'t fair.  Why did I study so hard to get a good job when I could just be say a receptionist and get paid the same amount?\r\n</P><P>\r\nGRRR! \r\n</P><P>\r\nAnd just while I\'m bitching, I\'m very very very tired of being abused by members of the public right now for my job.  If you want to have a say in the quality of your beach water, might I suggest that you fill in a form and/or attend a public meeting as opposed to just hurling filthy language and complaints at the Communications Assistant?  She\'s certainly not going to pass your concerns on if you can\'t make the effort of going through the proper channels.  \r\n</P>\r\n'),(373,'i am the girl behind the window<BR>\r\nthe girl that scoops out beans, rice, special sauce on your tortilla<BR>\r\n\r\ni make 6.25 an hour<BR>\r\n\r\ni get pissed with holier-than-thou bitches<BR>\r\n\r\ni sing snoop dogg songs in my head while waiting for customers<BR>\r\n\r\ni work at the the school cafeteria\r\n\r\n'),(374,'Hey Guys,\r\n\r\n<p>LinearB here. \r\n\r\n<p>Today I was on the 900 block of Lamar - topped at the intersection. \r\n\r\n<p>Kaboom.\r\n\r\n<p>I was rear-ended. The car hit me so hard that it knocked my car into the car in front of me - and that car into the one in front of it.\r\n\r\n<p>My beloved Chevy Wagon is totaled.\r\n\r\n<p>The real pisser is that, even though it ran like a dream, it was an old car. The guy\'s insurance company will probably only give me 1500ish for it - and I\'ll probably have to wait a month to get it. At the same time, it\'ll probably cost me 4000 to get a car of equal reliability.\r\nI\'ll probably have to sue the guy for the difference.\r\n\r\n<p>How will I get to mojo\'s now?'),(375,'<p>\r\nisn\'t it dorky for le to say that she\'s sad? how can that be, when she portrays herself as such a cute/nice/happy/fruit girl on swinney.org? let\'s look back at some of her submissions:\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><p>i am safe in my friends<br>because some of them are virgos</p>\r\n<li><p>life is nice<br>because of the internet and my friends</p>\r\n<li><p>this morning<br>i forgot to sleep</p>\r\n<li><p>something is good<br>and it\'s this thing that oof wrote</p>\r\n<li><p>the magnetic fields<br>i love this song</p>\r\n<li><p>i\'m famous<br>blurb</p>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\ndo these look like things that a sad person could write? i mean really, is there even a dollop of negativity there? so why is le acting grumpy and high maintenance on chat?\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nmaybe she is on the rag. i hear steak and toblerone are good rag foods. also if your s.o. punches you in the gut a few times you will feel less bloated. side effects may include nausea and vomiting.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<*dzengoff*> SUCK IT UP<br>\r\n<*dzengoff*> STRAP ON<br>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nmy thoughts exactly.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<small>note: above chat snippet taken out of context. any resemblance to living persons, past or present, is purely coincidental. overall, there is a smell of fried onions. goodonya mate</small>\r\n</p>'),(376,'<P>so sitting on market street drinking lychee\r\nflavored tea and a man pushing a cart walked\r\nby and stopped to say something very important\r\nto other tea drinkers.  he laughed a lot and\r\nwaved his arms around and was so excited. and\r\nduring the arm waving a plastic spoon fell from\r\nthe cart but he was too busy to notice so the\r\nspoon stayed on the sidewalk.</P>\r\n<p>\r\n10 minutes later a man in a suit who wasn\'t excited and had no cart and did not laugh stepped\r\non the spoon.  it made a scrapey noise and he\r\ndid not like it.\r\n</P>\r\n<p>\r\nthat is all.\r\n</P>\r\n\r\n'),(377,'<P>Have you ever heard that the best things in life are free?  I think that one may have to pay the price for \"be-living\" that.  It is only life that is free. I am liberal only to the liberal and dead only to the dead, strong to the weak and weak to the strong.  I long.  </P>'),(378,'<PRE>\r\nLook what we do fe\' dem.\r\nLook what thanks we get.\r\nThe one who clean the shit\r\nmust remember it\r\nToo much overload,\r\nwhole house a tumble down.\r\nSometimes we no drink tea,\r\njust to help our situation\r\nSometimes we no drink tea, \r\njust to clean up you\'re pollution. \r\nLook what we do fe\' dem.\r\nLook what thanks we get.\r\n</PRE>'),(379,'<PRE>\r\n<*le*> swinney.org is the new home of many of our friends<br>\r\n/m le oh i see!<br>\r\n/m le so you\'ve been hiding the cool place from me THIS WHOLE TIME<br>\r\n<*le*> well i didn\'t want you to show up and embarass me.\r\n</PRE>\r\n<H1><FONT COLOR=\"RED\">hi.</FONT></H1>'),(380,'<p>My last three fortune cookie fortunes:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>1) \"You will inherit a large sum of money\"\r\n<BR>\r\n2) \"Soon you will be sitting on top of the world\"\r\n<BR> \r\n3) \"Your love life will be happy and harmonious\" \r\n</P>\r\n\r\n<p><b>=</b></P>\r\n\r\n<P>1) Someone you love will die.\r\n<BR>\r\n2) You will have no friends and be very lonely.\r\n<BR>\r\n3) I don\'t want a girlfriend!\r\n</P>\r\n\r\n<P><I>And to think, I had these sitting on my desk for several days.</I><BR>\r\nI threw them away.</P>'),(381,'<P>\r\nfuckin a. that damn holiday is comin up. nuthin like fruity candy and stuffed bears with \'i love you\' emblazoned across their fluffy chests.\r\n</P><P>\r\nlast year i spent it alone under my comforter eating a box of chocolates (in a imaginary exchange with austin). this year i may suffer the same fate.\r\n</P><P>\r\ntho i have a bf, we do the long distance thing. any advice how to deal with it BESIDES masterbating a lot?</P>'),(382,'<p>i am a very lucky being</p>\r\n<p>the recent dissolution of ibooks.com, or more specifically, the firing of most of its staff, brought an end to one of the most amazing periods of my life.  i\'m not clinging.  i don\'t wish i was still employed there.  in fact, towards the end, it started to get ugly and feel forced.  yucko.</p>\r\n<p>this is purely rumination, by the way.  this is reminiscence at its grossest, so proceed with caution.</p>\r\n<p>while working there i became good friends with swinney, bmg, and dj1_luna.  i was hired during the brilliant flash of insanity that was the last months of the previous millenium.  these three were already employed there.  sometimes i feel like, no matter how old i get, i\'ll still be the near-sighted thirteen-year-old, gangling, and pimpley, and awkward.  i started work there, greener than green, with a twelve-gauge ego in my pocket to keep me safe.  i didn\'t know anything.  they pretended not to notice.  they\'re still pretending not to notice.  in fact, now, fifteen months later, swinney and bmg and dj1_luna are touchstones.  that is to say, they have become horizon references for me.  and they\'ve never been very critical of my monstrous afflictions.  and they\'ve drinken, and dranken, and drunked.  and they\'ve recommended, and referred, and gone about the business of being fucking bad-ass companions without too much whimpering (cept maybe luna from time to time...hee).</p>\r\n<p>so...i\'m not drunk.  i swear.  i\'m just indulging a moment of gratitude.  and noticing good fortune.  and tipping my hat.</p>'),(383,'<PRE>\r\ncool  air  washes  in  from  the  window\r\n\r\n       waves  that  make  no  sound  \r\n\r\n              they  crash  on  the  floor\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nlight winged bugs hermit crab around in the air\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nthe ceiling\'s night sky is \r\n\r\n                                 opaque\r\n\r\n\r\nthe stars are blocked out by a cloud of plaster\r\n\r\n\r\n      i would pay an extra $300 rent this month\r\n\r\nif i could live on the beach with sand in my hair \r\n\r\n</PRE>\r\n<blockquote>admit it tom hanks, you enjoyed yourself, and never liked the work. and there was alway uncertainty with her, she was going to leave you for leaving her anyway.\r\n</blockquote>'),(384,'<p>\r\n\r\nyo i master your software in seconds<BR>\r\nemailin\' you bug reports<BR>\r\nkeep your programmers guessin\'<BR>\r\nwritin\' scripts deeper than your OS<BR>\r\nmy code be lookin\' like a mess<BR>\r\ni confess<BR>\r\nbut my executables you will be blessin\'<BR>\r\ntrick, go to confession<BR>\r\nyou can\'t manage your math<BR>\r\nmy equations bring wrath<BR> \r\nmy bots laugh<BR>\r\nat all in their path<BR> \r\ndunk your hard drive in my bath<BR>\r\nlike a krispy kreme<BR>\r\ndunkin\' like i was on the dream team<BR>\r\ntrimp! your drive is steamed!</P>'),(385,'<p>\r\n\r\nyo i master your software in seconds<BR>\r\nemailin\' you bug reports<BR>\r\nkeep your programmers guessin\'<BR>\r\nwritin\' scripts deeper than your OS<BR>\r\nmy code be lookin\' like a mess<BR>\r\ni confess<BR>\r\nbut my executables you will be blessin\'<BR>\r\ntrick, go to confession<BR>\r\nyou can\'t manage your math<BR>\r\nmy equations bring wrath<BR> \r\nmy bots laugh<BR>\r\nat all in their path<BR> \r\ndunk your hard drive in my bath<BR>\r\nlike a krispy kreme<BR>\r\ndunkin\' like i was on the dream team<BR>\r\ntrimp! your drive is steamed!</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I think Vegetable Thins are the best crackers money can buy.</P>'),(386,'<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/386_1.jpg\' align=\'left\'>\r\n\r\n<P>do not duplicate copper keys that warn you of actions such as these.  wise men used to carve symbols in stone now they carve keys for the human beings who like to forget where they put their heads this morning.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>the morning is a good time to play with stucco.</P>\r\n\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/386_2.gif\' align=\'right\'>\r\n\r\n<P>i want to scrape stucco off a building at random. leaving only scratches and a few peeled moments. i want to paint small fig trees under each peel flap and leave two small words for those brave enough to discover new things: \"FIG TREE\"</P>\r\n\r\n-TUBE\r\n'),(387,'<P>I need someone to run my life for me, and handle the little things that I forget about or am too busy to do.  </P>\r\n\r\n<P>Your <B>duties</B> will include:</P>\r\n<LI>Paying bills\r\n<LI>Finding me a new house to live in\r\n<LI>Doing my laundry\r\n<LI>Organising social events with my ever drifting circle of friends\r\n<LI>Reminding me to drink lots of water with my alcohol and to take vitamins and do yoga\r\n<LI>Filling my car with petrol\r\n<LI>Doing the grocery shopping for basic foods not covered under the \"I\'m stoned at the supermarket\" trip\r\n\r\n<P>Your <B>perks and benefits</B> are really too numerous to list, but briefly:</P>\r\n<LI>All accomodation provided.  (You can even sleep curled up at my feet if you wish)\r\n<LI>Great food cooked for you as long as you\'ve been to the supermarket recently\r\n<LI>Fantastic company\r\n<LI>An easy going boss\r\n<LI>Time off for good behaviour\r\n<LI>Job satisfaction from knowing that you\'ve made my life run smoother.  \r\n\r\n<P>Apply in writing to <A HREF=\"mailto:joanna@hubris.co.nz\">joanna@hubris.co.nz</A></P>\r\n\r\n'),(388,'<p>\r\nit seems like nothing, thinking about it in passing, but when the times comes it is going to seem like so much longer. there are reasons and reasoning.\r\n</p>'),(389,'<P>ah, at last someone pays attention to the kind of web product presentation i like. yes, who really Cares about the product, learn to care about the audience. why give us a screenshot right away? why give us product specifications? nope, the way to catch my attention is to just save all that money you would normally spend on a \"graphic designer\", \"web artist\" stuck up snobish fresh faced under 30 motherfucker who doesn\'t know who Basquiat is, much less Linchestein and Picasso or Wahrhol for that case.\r\nThat\'s right, All you need is just a nice cute well formed girly girl on your homepage BOOM right off the bat! and then you give her her own e-mail address at the company so she can get her own fan mail and thus respond to my flirty advances. plain cutelicious. may this be the trend of the future\r\n<BR>\r\n<P><a href=\"http://www.aimster.com\">www.aimster.com</a></p>'),(390,'<P>panda farms.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>please, just copulate.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>lucky big fat happy</P>\r\n\r\n<P>better get sexy</P>\r\n\r\n<P>what is wrong?\r\n\r\n<P>you do not think she pretty?</P>\r\n\r\n<P>he is not handsome?</P>\r\n\r\n<P>if you do not sexy kids:</P>\r\n\r\n<P>cartoon candy wrap pictures</P>\r\n\r\n<P>little children think</P>\r\n\r\n<P>you are imaginary</P>\r\n\r\n<P>like Dodo candy</P>\r\n<!--\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/390_1.jpg\'>\r\n-->'),(391,'<p>\r\n\r\ni dream. i come up with a lot of boundaries. boundaries i think will make me happy. the whole \"i want...\r\n</P><PRE>\r\nbig windows.\r\nliving room you can live in.\r\nnice rug. \r\nnik-naks.\r\n</pre>\r\n<P>\r\nthe funny part about all of it is that i have it all and im not happy. yet i still think of just new nik-naks, and new rooms and new windows. I dont know where it all ends and im afraid of getting sucked in. I dont want to be rich, but i want to do well enough that i can settle down running a cafe or bar. old ex cool kids chillin to the chiamattt mp3 archive. \r\n</p>'),(392,'<P>I\'m talking on AIM with a friend I haven\'t seen in a year.  We\'re three timezones away, watching the same program on HBO about a 15 year old Scottish prostitute who gets another chance in life.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Thank you, Direct TV, for this moment of male bonding.</P>'),(393,'<P>i do things sometimes that are very wrong to my friends.  i know from my history that this is true.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>several weeks ago i posted a picture of a friend and it was rude.</P>\r\n \r\n<P>the action on my part caused conflict and hurt some peoples\' feelings.  no one likes to lose their temper.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i try to participate in this site for people to live and be creative and happy.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i apologize for my breach of that contract.</P>'),(394,'<Pre>\r\n\r\n{\r\nJumbled in numbers\r\n(sucked) into this &screen\r\nI need to be \r\ndebugged;\r\n\r\nWorking <mod%> longing \r\ninfinity compiles...\r\n\r\n== Austin,\r\n\r\nI need\r\na hug.\r\n\r\n}\r\n</Pre>'),(395,'so tonight the POURING RAIN decided to interfere with the signal from my direcTV dish. do you know that commercial on the cartoon network where they sell the cd full of children\'s songs? like \"eentsy weentsy spider something something spout\" or \"oh where oh where has my little dog gone\"?<br>\r\n<br>\r\nso the happy smiling faces of the excited children, stacking alphabet blocks, and their approving clucking mothers suddenly turned into multi-colored low-res blocks of distorted motion! choppy stop motion with trailers of broken green and blue cubes. i mean, out of nowhere.<br>\r\n<br>\r\ni\'m a cartoon network junkie. elly recently moved into my house and i\'m worried that she thinks i\'m a tv addict. i\'m not *that* bad honestly. i do other things! i have hobbies. sometimes i send out witty email covering some finer point of obscure music. once i thought about designing a portable shower made out of vacuum cleaner parts. i\'m really not boring!<br>\r\n<br>\r\nearlier this week, my dsl provider went out of business. mercury retrograde astrology etc.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nmy cat finally started using the robobox! i\'m very excited. the first time i showed her the clawing plastic arm of the self-cleaning as-seen-on-tv amazing-time-saver for the modern-living urban-young-lazy-irresponsible bachelor, she protested, and staged a hunger strike for 48 hours. but i was determined to never scrape a litterbox ever again.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nso i did that trick you do with cats where you slowly transfer items that smell like the old thing she\'s comfortable with into the new thing she fears. and tonight! she finally warmed up to the idea. dzzhhweeee! scrapey scrapey scrapey! plunk!<br>\r\n<br>\r\nthe litterbox lived in elly\'s new room for a while, but this is finally fixed. sand was everywhere, cats are so messy. sorry elly, but i had to vacuum your panties.<br>\r\n'),(396,'<p>My life has changed, since getting involved with swinney.org, for the better in many ways. I quit doing drugs, handled inabilities to communicate and now have a way to really help my friends and family with their life problems and unhappiness. </P>\r\n\r\n     <p>Prior to getting into swinney.org I can remember many days of personal depression, questions about life and who I was, why people were the way they were, etc. I have not only answered these questions, but have learned far more. I can also count the number of days on two hands that I have felt unhappy in these past 8 months since being involved with swinney.org. This is amazing to me!<p>\r\n\r\n'),(397,'<P>sunrise: 7:03am</P>\r\n<P>it will never stop raining. i have decided to accept this as truth. i have a new ritual during the rainy season, i call it \"pumping the roof\".\r\n</P><P>\r\nto pump the roof, i tie two plastic bags around both of my boots. i roll my pants up three times, put on a raincoat, and pop a ricola lozenge in my mouth. i dig out the orange extension cord from the closet and allow it to dangle near the door leading to the roof. then i walk out on the roof and slosh through the lake. in the middle of the lake is an electric pump, its power cord is usually drowned in the flooding. i dry off the prongs to the power cord with the soft fleecy part of my raincoat, to avoid electrocution. then i connect the power cord to the orange extension cord. next, i use a pair of plyers to straighten out the hose leading out from the pump. the hose typically bends in half against itself, blocking the flow of water out of the pump. the other end of the hose dangles over the side of the house, and would likely drench anyone approaching the front door unexpected. so let that be a lesson! CALL FIRST. \r\n</P><P>\r\nnext i wade through the lake, back to the door, and tear the plastic bags off my shoes before coming back into the house. then i plug the orange extension cord into the wall, using my right arm, taking care to not cross my arm over my chest. this is to avoid electric current passing through my heart on its way to the floor. at this point, the pump should be running. i walk downstairs to the living room, open the window, and verify that the water is indeed draining from the hose. it usually is. if it\'s not, then i wrap yet another layer of vinyl tape around where the hose meets the pump.  draining the lake is a multi-hour process.\r\n</P><P>the roof is still pumping and i\'m considering that i might like to watch the sunrise later.</P>'),(398,'<P>I return to these lines \r\nthe same way I came before,\r\nin a room where no one notices.\r\n<BR>\r\n<P>Wanted, Wanted: a trauma kitty.\r\nPerfect for\r\nIntoxicated blues.\r\nWith possible advancement\r\nTo be the emissary of my grief.\r\n<BR>\r\n<P>Having been resold my heartbreak\r\nAt wholesale and for profit.\r\nOver and over.  I took the time to stop\r\nsearching my infrastructure.\r\nI am blank now.\r\n<BR>\r\n<P>In an incomplete bedroom \r\nI attempt to capture\r\nthe art of discovering everything again.\r\n<BR>\r\n<P>The value of faith is declining into insulation.\r\nI dream of a deliberate wave,\r\nof subscribed dreams,\r\nof gentle mental oxidation.\r\n<BR>\r\n<P>Modernity ends.\r\nPleading that I encrypt\r\nmy technical prayers\r\nor filter whispers of hope.\r\nMy church is a satellite,\r\nAn infection without talent. \r\n<BR>\r\n<P>In my silent interlude I learned that\r\nI come from the last breath of an expired thought.\r\nFrom the calculating movements\r\nof light sources and the ignorance of darkness.\r\nFrom the last notes of a burning violin.\r\nFrom the unread last page of a book\r\nand a love letter that I never sent\r\n\r\n'),(399,'</p><p>\r\ns5 and i are going to install a confessional booth. i will go into the confessional and talk to the camera about how even though i have nothing against gay people, i wish s5 didn\'t have such a chip on his shoulder about being gay.\r\n</p><p>\r\nthen, s5 will go into the confessional and talk about how he wishes everyone would stop persecuting him for his sexual orientation. \r\n</p><p>\r\nthen, he\'ll walk around the house with plastic bags on his feet carrying a pair of pliers.\r\n</p><p>\r\nthe end.\r\n</p><p>\r\n\r\n'),(400,'</p><p>\r\ns5 and i are going to install a confessional booth. i will go into the confessional and talk to the camera about how even though i have nothing against gay people, i wish s5 didn\'t have such a chip on his shoulder about being gay.\r\n</p><p>\r\nthen, s5 will go into the confessional and talk about how he wishes everyone would stop persecuting him for his sexual orientation. \r\n</p><p>\r\nthen, he\'ll walk around the house with plastic bags on his feet carrying a pair of pliers.\r\n</p><p>\r\n<a href=\"http://128.174.172.76/chf/pub/surveyreports/sep-oct95/ducks.html\"><img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/400_1.gif\'></a>.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n'),(401,'</p>\r\n<p><tt>\r\n<*yeti*> If I am going to get filovirii, it better not be from fucking<br>\r\n<*yeti*> BOLIVIAN RATS<br>\r\n<*yeti*> er<br>\r\n<*yeti*> DISPLACED BOLIVIAN RATS<br>\r\n</tt>\r\n</p><p>\r\ni should be asleep.\r\n</p><p>\r\neven though i broke my vow of silence a long time ago, i\'m still feeling guilty for talking.'),(402,'<P>Don\'t <I>EVER</I> hit the \"Esc\" button when writing in the journal.  Especially if you\'ve just spent a considerable amount of time on an entry and you\'re just checking it over for typos.</P>\r\n\r\n<p>FUCK!</P>\r\n\r\n<P>...end transmission...</P>\r\n\r\n<P>What I was trying to say before my words \"Esc\"aped me, in a slightly more elegant and less hurried way, was that all this storming has put me in a reflective mood, and I was reflecting about how cool it is that the two best friends I made in Austin (NES and robotec9) are now in my town and doing well.  It\'s like some kind of foreign exchange program or something.  For four years I partook in Stubb\'s BBQ and slackdom, and now they are now partaking in Roscoes Chicken n\' Waffles and crackdom.  LA is my home.  It\'s nice to have visitors.</P>    '),(403,'<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/403_1.jpg\'>'),(404,'<p>\r\nbut seriously, does anyone have experience doing silkscreening? have they the equipment so i can try it once to see if it\'s worth buying the apparatus for?\r\n</p><p>\r\ni want to make little posters.\r\n</p><p>\r\ni will make you soup with quinoa if you do!\r\n</p>'),(405,'<P>When I\'m in the office and not out meeting the public, I often don\'t have a whole lot to do.  What I do instead of working is sit at my computer, and write on Swinney Org.  Or I try to do the <A HREF=\"http://nzherald.co.nz/crosswords\">daily crossword</A>.  The problem I have with the crosswords is that I\'m not very good at them, and I\'m not very patient, so I often just push the \"reveal\" button too on every single word I can\'t get within 30 seconds.  My grandmother would be turning over in her grave if she was dead.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>In other news, I\'m moving house, although we haven\'t found a new place yet, so I\'m trying to get rid of all my possesions.  However, I\'m a material girl, so I\'m not very good at this.  All I want is to dispose of things <!-- or people --> that I don\'t want or need any more.  House cleaning is good.  </P>'),(406,'<P>it is cold and rainy.  i am cold and lonely.  where is my Mei Xiang?  she is not here.  i am cold and lonely. </P>\r\n\r\n<P>i am wet and cold.  i am like a wet dog trying to stay out of the down pour by sitting under the stoop, only i am already wet.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>where is my Mei Xiang?  she is not here.  somewhere cold and wet she is sitting, not here.  i miss her.  i have no one to talk to.  where is my lady?</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i turned the heat on.  it is not working.  i am cold.  i am wet.  i am going to take a bath so then i will be hot and wet.  that will be better than this.  cold. wet.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>whither, wet, cold.</P>'),(407,'<P>  I\'m wondering...</P>\r\n\r\n<P>How many people have occaisonal - like once or twice a year, freak outs.</P>  \r\n\r\n<P>Freak-outs include momentary insanity, yelling, screaming, or hysterical sobbing, uncontrolled emotion bursting forth for some reason that is apparent but not necessarily understandable. </P>\r\n\r\n<P>What\'s the verdict?  Any takers?</P>'),(408,'To: robotec<br>\r\nFrom: LinearB<br>\r\nSubject: favorite C books\r\n\r\n<p>1. <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0133262243/\">Harbison and Steele. C: A reference manual</a>\r\n<p>2. <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0131774298/\">van der Linden. Expert C Programming: deep C secrets</a>\r\n<p>3. <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0131315099/\">Plauger. The Standard C Library</a>\r\n<p>4. <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0131103628/\">Kernighan and Ritchie. The C Programming Language</a>\r\n<p>5. <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0201183994/\">Kelley and Pohl. A Book on C</a>\r\n<p>6. <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0201563177/>Stevens. Advanced Programming in the Unix Environment</a> \r\n<p>7. <a Href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1565921399/>Oualline. Practical C Programming</a>\r\n'),(409,'<p>\r\nnow is the time to contemplate the tummy.\r\n</p><p>\r\nthe tummy of weeb, lo, it is round.\r\n</p><p>\r\ni savor the little spot that is right under my navel, it is a little rise. if it were land, i would camp there during flood warnings. it is smooth and obliquely shaped.\r\n</p><p>\r\ni can put my thumb in my bellybutton. i can hold my toes and count to three. \r\n</p><p>\r\ni can drink more water so it will slosh when i go to bed which is right nowNOW\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n'),(410,'<PRE>\r\nthe cat has my tonge\r\n        and\r\n  words like mice  \r\n are hard to catch\r\n</PRE>'),(411,'<P>how come everytime i flip thru the channels i see more of these fake court room shows? do we really need a jerry-springer-type scenario in the court? and some of these stories are retarded. whats next lap dances in the dmv? psh bitch please.</P>'),(412,'<p>So yesterday I wasn\'t feeling real well and I think it caused me to be quiet \r\n  and grumpy. I have been leading a rock \'n\' roll lifestyle for the past two weeks. \r\n  Going to shows, going out drinking, not sleeping and hanging out with the girl \r\n  that wears all black. To tell the truth she doesn\'t wear all black, \r\n  she is quite colorful actually. I am having such a great time with this girl! </p>\r\n<p>It was valentines yesterday. I was feeling ill; not up to par. She knew this. \r\n  She calls me, says she\'ll be right over. I am so excited, but I stink cause \r\n  I have been in bed all day so I jumped in the shower. The second I hit the shower, \r\n  she walks in saying my name softly so as not to scare me like she usually does. \r\n  I am startled at the speed in which she arrived. Turned out she called while \r\n  on the way to my house, just to make sure she isn\'t intruding. I get out of \r\n  the shower, try to dry off, try to look awake and with it, and because of my \r\n  current disposition I make things awkward. I don\'t know if it was cause I was \r\n  surprised or if it was my cough, but I think I scared her away... She leaves \r\n  unexpected and I am left to thinking that she is wanting to pull away, or tell \r\n  me that she needs her space.</p>\r\n<p>I go to my room, looking around I see a single rose and box of something. I \r\n  run outside after her as she is pulling away... </p>\r\n<p>Turns out that she thought I was pulling away, pushing her away er something \r\n  along those lines... Not the case. So she comes over later, bringing me all \r\n  sorts of get well treats. (soup, odwalla juice, rice dream chocolate ice cream, \r\n  mmmm.) We watched a movie, <a href=\"http://us.imdb.com/M/title-exact?+Book+of+Life,+The\" target=new>Book of Life</a>, and then fell asleep comfortable and \r\n  happy.</p>\r\n<p>This is what was in the box: </p>\r\n<p><img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/412_1.jpg\'></p>\r\n<p><a href=\"http://www.sexyfingerchamps.com\" target=new>The Sexy Finger Champs</a> play this weekend, you going???</p>\r\n'),(413,'<PRE>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nmy lower chakras are\r\nO U T OF C O N T R O L\r\nand i am depressed too\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</PRE>\r\n<CENTER>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/413_1.jpg\'>\r\n</CENTER>'),(414,'<p><p align=\"justify\">\r\nthere was an entire email thread recently about the mantra \"om mani padme hum.\" the best thing that happened was that i learned about a work of art that <a href=\"http://www.alexgrey.com\">alex grey</a> did, called \'prayer wheel.\' here is a description of it, and a picture. taken from <a href=\"http://www.alexgrey.com\">the alex grey site</a>.\r\n</p><blockquote><p align=\"justify\"><i>\r\n\"In Tibet, prayer wheels are used by monks and laity to increase the power of their meditation. Carved or printed on all prayer wheels is the mantra - Om Mani Padme Hum - literally meaning, Om, Hail the Jewel in the Lotus, Hum. With the correct understanding, the mere utterance or inspection of this mantra is believed to transport one directly to paradise. The mantric prayer is dedicated to the Buddhist deity of active compassion, Avalokitesvara. It is said that when Avalokitesvara saw the suffering of the world, He sprouted one thousand hands and arms to assist the world, each palm containing an eye of unobstructed vision. \r\n<br><br>\r\nIn the performance of \'Prayer Wheel\' my wife and I were bound together along with a skeleton, while holding a realistic baby doll and a knife. Our bodies were all painted gold. We were attached to the Prayer Wheel which turned as we walked around it chanting the mantra. After circumambulating for an hour and a half, I cut the rope attaching us to the Prayer Wheel and we walked out of the space. Sound was recorded at the Avalokitesvara Initiation given by Deshung Rinpoche in Cambridge, Massachusetts, January 1983.\"\r\n</i>\r\n</p><br>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/414_1.jpg\'>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n'),(415,'<p>\r\nthere are worse things in the world than being hungry and tired, but i can\'t think of them right now. why do i want to write in swinney right before bed? when my mental reserves (plums, peaches) are at their lowest?\r\n</p><p>\r\ntoday i sorta got offered a job at pearl paints, at the sterling rate of 7 dollars an hour. my god, how low have i sunk?!@ i alternate between \'oh that\'s not so bad, you only need something part-time\' to \'i couldn\'t live on cheezits for that amount of money in the city, come ON don\'t be a boob.\' sigh. on the other hand, i could prolly rack up at least 10 an hour through some five fingered employee discounts. but i\'d hate to stoop that low, i know it\'s dumb, but i would just rather not. from what i hear, everyone else does it. buh.\r\n</p><p>\r\ni\'m all excited about making my own silkscreen print screen apparatus. i dream of a soup and silkscreening tea party at my place, though eating and handling cadmium orange at the same time shouldn\'t be indulged. too much. at one time.\r\n</p><p>\r\njeff says that i say the following phrases very often:\r\n</p><p>\r\n\"i\'m sure it\'s very nice...\"<br>\r\n\"i see...\"<br>\r\n\"oh really...\"<br>\r\n</p><p>\r\ni\'m really not british, i swear on a pile of tories.\r\n</p><p>\r\nand i say he says the following a lot:\r\n</p><p>\r\n\"holy subterreanean hot dog cheese tunnel, batmn\"<br>\r\n\"poke me in the eye- again! ...harder!\" <br>\r\n\"that\'s... pleasant\" - reply to my comment that i sprinkled my snot in his water glass <br>\r\n</p><p>\r\nokay just kidding, he doesn\'t really say those things. well, okay, the last one. well. okay. \r\n</p><p>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/415_1.jpg\'>\r\n</p><p>\r\nlike, bed. like, totally, dude.\r\n</p><p>'),(416,'<p>and all i ever wanted</p>\r\n<p>this phrase is a signifier, like a crescendo notation or a mezzo forte.  it doesn\'t really mean, \"all that person really wanted ever\". or even if it does, that\'s not really the point.  it denotes that what comes next is rub-worthy, is glue and snot, is morter and stitches, is heartbeat of the universe, is clue to all that is, is the is, is is, is.</p>\r\n<p>and when he led me away from the artifice, he said, \"you know, all i ever wanted was the voice in my head to say REST.  it\'s all right.  you\'ve done enough.  rest.\"</p>'),(417,'<P>what does it mean to be like i am right now?  i am like austin lacking that crutial few points of enthusiasm that gets me off my ass and makes me shine.</P>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/417_1.jpg\' align=\'right\'>\r\n<P>it is not funny, but i thought about it walking down the stairs minutes ago.  i am like me, same every day movements.  and i am happy all day.  then i get home and i am tired and the same feeling that gets me to visit my friends becomes less an engine that drives me and more a feeling of loneliness.  and i think to myself, hey man you should just go over to adamajah\'s place and play video games and laugh.</P>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/417_2.jpg\' align=\'left\'>\r\n<P>i am tired.  so i do not go to santa monica.  i would have to come back.  not really.  i could crash on the couch and go running on the beach in the morning.  now there is an idea.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>next friday night i am sleeping at dza\'s place.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i hope this letter to kdog gets sent.  i think it will. i don\'t remember her address anymore.  funny thing is it used to be my address too.</P>'),(418,'<p>\r\neveryone has a poop story. what\'s yours?\r\n</p><p>\r\nthe inspiration for that thought was remembering that lovely saturday a couple of years ago when i went on a sunny promising saturday morning to do my laundry at the laundromat. it was so nice. it was so sunny. \r\n</p><p>\r\nwhile doing my laundry, i kept getting little whiffs of... something peculiar. i thought i might have stepped in something, so i go outside and do the cat litter shuffle on some grass, some visual inspections, and wander back inside to do my business. ten minutes later, as i sit on one of the little benches inside to read my newspaper, i realize something horrible.\r\n</p><p>\r\n<b>i am sitting very close to a big pile of shit.</b>\r\n</p>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/418_1.jpg\'>\r\n<p>\r\ni look down, (i didn\'t want to) and yes, someone had taken an enormous dump in the laundromat. from the bench i was sitting on. i had a little bit on me.\r\n</p><p>\r\nnow, those of you who know me, know that i\'m a little bit anal. i can\'t help it. i just am that way. so after you envision me going out of my mind for just the littlest tiniest infinity of a minute, you can envision the rest of that hour, my running gently back to my house, stripping, bleaching, and ultimately never wearing my favorite plaid shirt and loosey jeans again. they just weren\'t the same.\r\n</p><p>\r\nnow. your turn!</p>'),(419,'<PRE>\r\n\r\n\r\na thin woman got posted on\r\n                vermont st\r\n                cross walk\r\n\r\n  like a post out of place\r\n               she got hit\r\n               & she broke\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</PRE>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/419_1.gif\'>\r\n'),(420,'<p>so i\'ve been sitting at this damn computer for the vast majority of the weekend and now have that \"fuck, i\'ve wasted my weekend\" feeling that ends up lasting all week. meanwhile, i\'m promising myself that next weekend i\'ll do the things that i\'ve been meaning to do for months and realising that these thing will probably never get done.</p>\r\n<p>you know?</p>\r\n<p>truth is i have no desire to go out and play in the sunshine. i have no desire to go and eat, drink and fuck shit up with the posse. i have no desire to get out and make the world a better place.</p>\r\n<p>see, it\'s my best friends birthday today.</p>\r\n<p>i am in sydney, australia. she is in yogyakarta, indonesia. i won\'t be seeing her for another five months. i really miss her!</p>\r\n<p>i called and we spoke and we laughed and i finished the bottle of her favourite wine. then i realised that i\'m a pretty lucky girl.</p>\r\n<p>how many of you realised that (from australia) a call to indonesia costs the same as a call to uzbekistan?</p>\r\n<p>craziness.</p>'),(421,'</p><p>\r\nmorning. \r\n</p><p>\r\ni woke up at 5am today, because i went to sleep at 9pm, because i went to a rave the night before and i was tuckered out. dancing barefoot and breathing nag champa while surrounded by dreadlocked hippies in flouro gear really takes it out of you. that plus being up all night. eating breakfast with other cracked out ravers in a diner in ukiah california. mmm oatmeal. we crashed at a crappy hotel before driving home. the cuffs of my overalls were muddy from wandering around in a field of sheep outside the party. \r\n</p><p>\r\nbut anyway, i woke up at 5am. it had been raining all night. <a href=\"http://www.steve.org\">s5</a> went to bed as i was waking up. so, i became s5 while he slept. what did i do?\r\n</p><p>\r\nfor starters, i watched cartoons. scooby doo! scooby scooby doo, where are you. also i ate dry cereal out of the box and drank some juice. i read <a href=\"http://perceptions.diaryland.com\">perceptions.diaryland.com</a> which is pretty good. <a href=\"http://www.cyantology.com\">cyan</a> pointed it out.\r\n</p><p>\r\nthen, i began to agonize about the roof. the lake was larger than i had ever seen. obviously, the roof needed pumping. i stood looking out over the lake. i bit my lip. yes, it definitely needed pumping. but my intrepid capricorn homeowner friend was fast asleep.\r\n<p><p>\r\n7:30 am at this point. i meekly opened the sliding door onto the roof and carefully fingered the power cord to the pump. it was laying under the lake. i considered electrocution. i started to uncoil the extension cord but was unable to commit. i wandered back into my room. \r\n</p><p>\r\ni chatted. i posed for the cam. i mentioned the need for roof pumping to my friends on irc. no advice. i paged <a href=\"http://www.hungry.com/~yeti\">peter</a>: \"hi, i think i should pump the roof. s5 is sleeping. can you wake up and get on chat?\" no response. i was all alone and the lake was growing.\r\n</p><p>\r\n8:45 am at this point. i stood and considered the lake once more. it was time. i rolled up my pants, and waded barefoot out into the lake. i sloshed across the lake and grabbed an empty clay flower pot, and rested the power cord on top of it, thereby rescuing the power cord from the water. i moved the pump over to the deepest part of the lake and fiddled with the hose to remove kinks. at this point my bare feet were numb and aching from sloshing around in ice cold rainwater.\r\n</p><p>\r\nupon coming back into the house, i plugged in the extension cord (and, since <a href=\"http://swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=397.txt\">steve says it\'s a bad idea</a>, i was careful not to cross my arm over my heart while doing so). i was not electrocuted.\r\n</p><p>\r\ni walked downstairs and stuck my head out the door to ensure that water was coming out the hose and splashing all over the front steps. it was. the pump was working! i pumped the roof! i am clever and useful!\r\n</p><p>\r\nalso, i put the lake on ellycam.\r\n</p><p>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/421_1.jpg\' height=\"240\" width=\"320\" alt=\"pumping the roof\" border=\"1\">\r\n</p>'),(422,'<h1><STRONG><a href=\"http://elly.org\">elly</a> as performance artist</STRONG></h1>\r\n\r\n<P>1) talk on IRC about doing a thing<sup>1</sup></P>\r\n<P>2) partially do that thing<sup>2</sup></P>\r\n<P>3) point cam at thing<SUP>3</SUP></P>\r\n<P>4) <a href=\"http://swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=421.txt\">write journal entry about problems reconciling doing / finishing said thing</a><SUP>4</SUP></P>\r\n<P>5) finish</P>\r\n\r\n\r\n<TT>\r\n\r\n<h2><B>STEP <sup>1</sup></B></h2>\r\n\r\n<P>[08:23am]\r\n<BR>\r\nle> i\'m worried about the lake (<a href=\"ahttp://swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=397.txt\">a pool of water that collects on S5\'s roof</a>)\r\n</P>\r\n\r\n    <P>\r\n    <img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/422_1.jpg\'>\r\n    </P>\r\n\r\n\r\n<P>\r\n[08:23am]\r\n<BR>  \r\nchiamattt> le, what is wrong with the roof?\r\n</P><P>\r\n[08:23am]\r\n<BR>  \r\nchiamattt> like\r\n</P><P>\r\n[08:23am]\r\n<BR>  \r\nchiamattt> isnt it slanted?\r\n</P><P>\r\n[08:23am]\r\n<BR>   \r\nle> but <a href=\"http://www.steve.org\">s5 is sleeping</a> and i\'m sorta afraid to meddle with the pump\r\n</P><P>\r\n[08:23am]\r\n<BR>  \r\nle> flat\r\n</P><P>\r\n[08:23am]\r\n<BR>  \r\nchiamattt> FLAT ROOF = WRONG ROOF\r\n</P><P>\r\n\r\n<h2><B>STEP <SUP>2</SUP></B></h2>\r\n<P>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/422_2.jpg\'>\r\n</P>\r\n<P>\r\n[08:28am]\r\n<BR>  \r\nle> ok i think i\'ll go deal with the roof\r\n</P>\r\n<P>\r\n[08:33am]\r\n<BR>  le> ok.\r\n</P>\r\n\r\n<h2><B>STEP <SUP>3</SUP></B></h2>\r\n\r\n<P>\r\n[08:33am]\r\n<BR>\r\nle> i am about to do pumpingtheroof cam.\r\n</P><P>\r\n[08:33am]\r\n<BR>  \r\nle> hold\r\n</P>\r\n\r\n<P>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/422_3.jpg\'>\r\n</P>\r\n\r\n<P>\r\n[08:35am]\r\n<BR>  \r\nle> ok\r\n</P><P>\r\n[08:35am]\r\n<BR>  \r\nle> the cam is trained upon the lake.\r\n</P><P>\r\n\r\n[08:36am]\r\n<BR>\r\nle> and the pump.\r\n</P>\r\n\r\n\r\n<h2><B>STEP <SUP>4</SUP></B></h2>\r\n<P>\r\n[08:36am] \r\n<BR>\r\nle> <a href=\"http://swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=421.txt\">swinney.org entry forthcoming.</a>\r\n</P>\r\n</tt>\r\n<CENTER>\r\n<h2>fin.</h2>\r\n</CENTER>\r\n\r\n'),(423,'<p>i am jobless<br>\r\ni am not wanting to be burdened with job<br>\r\ni must have a job, nevertheless;<br>\r\ni sit<br>\r\ni read<br>\r\ni write<br>\r\ni take pictures<br>\r\ni listen to music<br>\r\ni talk to friends.<br>\r\nit cannot get any better than this<br>\r\nbut i can be better than this too<br></p>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/423_1.jpg\'>\r\n'),(424,'<p>i read auntie\'s site this morning, and had some thoughts.\r\n</p><p>\r\nit\'s true, all the things she describes about being in love. but being in love isn\'t enough. (nor are fat babies.) both people have to feel the same level of commitment to each other, and even then, sometimes it doesn\'t work out. there is no formula, there is no certainty. especially when setting the foundation for the rest of my life, which is what i was doing. i was in a relationship with a lovely, sweet man, and it didn\'t work out. and when i had to leave for my own sanity and sense of self, it was the hardest thing i had ever done. because everyone thought we were happy and perfect together. i thought so too, despite our differences. there were doubts. but it came down to the times when walking alone, when awake at night, when looking up at the stars, was i certain that this person would make me happy ten years from now? was he in my heart? did he bring out the best in me? \r\n</p><p> \r\nafter a while, i admitted to myself that the answer was no, and i got on with it. it was hard. but it made my life the happy thing it is right now. \r\n</p><p>\r\ni hope this entry will be seen as what it is, concern for everyone involved, not a criticism of auntie or anyone else who loves her. i don\'t want to stir up trouble, just wanted to share. shining chrysalis le. shining loving mom. hard decisions. life.</p>'),(425,'<p>\r\nterrible i am when i sit and think about who i am and where i live and to whom i look too and to home i look down. violent action visions of terror. to wield power like other great men is what cravings desire and to all who know me this might come as a suprise. i look down on culture and language and notions of not moving forward. there is living and there is living and there is moving and there is moving. development is bias and we all know this. restructuring is a rip off and embargo\'s dont do a thing. we all know this. we pass laws and we change laws. we get rights we lose right. the cycle of looking towards history for reasons and excuses goes on and to what end? '),(426,'<p style=\"color: #99000; font-family: verdana, arial, helvetica; font-size: 10px;\">happiness is marked for me by moments; either in memory of or the act of being in.  example:</p>\r\n<ul style=\"color: #99000; font-family: verdana, arial, helvetica; font-size: 10px;\">\r\n<li>the act of catching a beautiful sunset and watching it as the sun kisses and is swallowed by the horizon, breathless from running to the waters edge;</li>\r\n<li>a lover whispering accepting and sweet things into my ear while i am drifting off to sleep;</li>\r\n<li>being encompassed by a crecendo of moving music, goosebumps blooming on your skin;</li>\r\n<li>the split second of satisfaction while walking through a park with the sun warming your bare shoulders;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p style=\"color: #99000; font-family: verdana, arial, helvetica; font-size: 10px;\">if happiness can be measured in moments, can love?  is it possible to have true love with a person for one moment?  is love like happiness - not a constant satisfaction, but the act of rememberance and the tiny moments of happiness that we relate to our lovers?</p>'),(427,'<P>I have missed you</P>\r\n<P>In terrible ways</P>\r\n<P>It\'s been so long: </P>\r\n<P>I won\'t, say what, I won\'t say where.</P>\r\n<P>Thinking about sex when brushing your teeth </P>\r\n<P>Is not the perfect way to begin the day. </P>\r\n\r\n<P>\"It will rain soon, my roses will drown\" - J.B.</P>\r\n'),(428,'<p>You people must know that banjos are so awesome. I will now tell you a story.</p>\r\n<p>For me, there are few instruments that can rival the banjo for matching so many moods. There is some sort of banjo music for everything.</p>\r\n<p>But mostly, banjos bring me to that calm place. The place in you where things are okay. Where things are right between you and the world. It took a long time for me to find that out. Banjos are when you are walking somewhere alone and you feel free, and you feel ecstatic to be alive, and nothing could make you want to be in any place but where you are at that moment.</p>\r\n<p>Today, I was listening to banjos on BART (Tony Furtado and Dirk Powell) and I was thinking about how I would really like to learn to play the banjo, for myself, and also to attempt to share that with my friends.</p>\r\n<p>I walk in my front door, and there is an instrument case there. It looks remarkably like a banjo case to me. elly is sitting at the computer with a big big smile on her face.</p>\r\n<p>\"Is that a banjo?\"</p>\r\n<p>\"No. It\'s just the case.\"</p>\r\n<p>I open it, and inside is a banjo.</p>\r\n<p>Well fuck me. It\'s a banjo! elly got me a banjo! I\'m the happiest boy on the planet. I will have to learn to play this banjo now.</p>\r\n<p>One day, maybe I will play something on the banjo for some of you. It might not be the best thing banjo playing ever, but I will be happy, nervous, and the music will make me feel like God came in my brain.</p>\r\n<p>I must now go lay me down in my bed and sleep. Before I do, I will listen to some more banjo music and dream.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>-yeti</p>'),(429,'</p><p>\r\nchaya took antibiotics and now she is not sick anymore. this means she\'s fucking hyper:\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<pre>\r\n<*chaya*> SO SO HYPER\r\n/m chaya hi!\r\n/m chaya are you feeling better?\r\n</pre>\r\n<p>...</p>\r\n<pre>\r\n<*chaya*> coffee loves you\r\n<*chaya*> it loves you even when you have morning breath\r\n<*chaya*> it wants to give you a big wet coffee hug<br>\r\n<*chaya*> this would be one of those times that my mom would tell me to\r\n<*<a href=\"http://www.chaya.org\">chaya</a>*> go run around the block and work off some energy<br>\r\n\r\n</pre>\r\n\r\n\r\n'),(430,'<PRE>\r\n=>Date: Wed, 21 Feb 2001 23:00:19 +0000 (GMT)\r\n=>From: Austin Swinney <aswinney@swinney.org>\r\n=>To: xianflux <xianfoy@aol.com>\r\n=>Subject: italian white chocolate\r\n=>\r\n=>i hope you like it\r\n=>\r\n\r\nDate: Wed, 21 Feb 2001 20:08:00 EST\r\nFrom: Xianfoy@aol.com\r\nTo: aswinney@swinney.org\r\nSubject: Re: italian white chocolate\r\n\r\nDear Austin:\r\n\r\nyou think i\'m going to fall for that old dollar-bill\r\non a string trick again? you\'re just trying to be \r\nprovocative so that i rush home and make you \r\nMiso-Broccoli.  If i leave here and drive, drive, \r\ndrive for an hour with the one singular notion that \r\nwhen i get home there is going to be italian white \r\nchocolate there waiting for me, i\'m sure one of several \r\nthings will happen:\r\n\r\n1.  there will be swinney-rationed piece of white\r\nchocolate smaller than awar-time allotment in a \r\nthird-world country\r\n\r\n2.  there will be no white chocolate, only a stomach \r\nholding, laughing and rollicking swinney.\r\n\r\n3.  i am being subjected to a controlled variable \r\nlab test the results of which will be posted on \r\nswinney.org.  \"Situational Response to Chocolate \r\nStimula on the Y (confined or home-bound) Group\"\r\n\r\n\"Day two:  subject appeared on premises 2.3 hours \r\nfaster than the control group at the mention of \r\nwhite italian chocolate.  These findings indicate \r\ngreater measure of rapidity than with the effect \r\nof placebo substances such as little debbie snack \r\ncakes, napoleons or goobers on similarly confined \r\nsubjects.\"\r\n\r\n4.  There is in fact white italian chocolate waiting \r\nfor me at the house and when i arrive it will be \r\nprominently displayed and a beaming, proud swinney \r\nwill appear to receive thanks for his thoughtfulness.\r\n\r\nWe shall see.  I arrive by 9.  Kiks\r\n</PRE>'),(431,'</p><p>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/431_1.jpg\' height=\"240\" width=\"320\" alt=\"farg\" border=\"1\">\r\n</p><p>\r\ntonight i feel farg. i hate feeling farg. farg is not being able to find something when you really need to find it. standing in line for an hour in the wrong line up. getting hit in the ballsack with a paintball going two hundred and thirty feet per second. farg is all of this and more. farg is a word, an emotion, and genre of music. i came across farg for the first time one summer when i stepped on a nail. the second and probably more horrible farg came next when father poured iodine onto wound. farg. farg. farg. recent fargs include dropping frenching forgetting that french also counted as an option. farg. having to tell mom about french farg. fargÂ². Nevertheless i keep going. cant never let a farg get you down. well not all the way down. i have been told that fargz come and go, and that after a while you get used to fargs and they just become something to talk about with the boys.\r\n</p>'),(432,'<p><font face=\"Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif\">having a few bad days lately. \r\n  No not depressed, not really. scared, hell yah. i am always scared. scared about \r\n  everything. i am apocalyptic, i over-react about everything. thinking that the \r\n  president is out to kill me, and people like me. scared that i will continue \r\n  living my life the way i am living my life. </font> </p>\r\n<p> <font face=\"Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif\">i see the genetically \r\n  enhanced wonder people when i ride my bike down to the drag. at times they make \r\n  me furious. i have to remind myself that they have fears too. maybe more than \r\n  myself. sometimes i forget people are people, just some seem more extraordinary \r\n  than othersâ€¦ </font></p> \r\n<p><font face=\"Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif\">an enhanced sorority girl \r\n  walking by with her pumped frat boyfriend told me the other day, \"get a fucking \r\n  job.\" in my head iwas like, yah! i know, i be pathetic sometimes! instead i \r\n  replied, \"eat balls, die bitch.\" and then proceeded to flee the scene before \r\n  brutus added it all up. </font></p>\r\n<p><font face=\"Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif\">this situation, did a few \r\n  things to me.</font></p>\r\n<ol>\r\n  <li><font face=\"Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif\" size=\"2\">it made me furious</font></li>\r\n  <li><font face=\"Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif\" size=\"2\">made me laugh, briefly</font></li>\r\n  <li><font face=\"Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif\" size=\"2\" size=\"2\">made me sad that there \r\n    are people out there like that</font></li>\r\n  <li><font face=\"Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif\" size=\"2\">got upset with myself \r\n    for being just as bad as her</font></li>\r\n  <li><font face=\"Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif\" size=\"2\">made me think about \r\n    my appearances</font></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p><font face=\"Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif\">i think that if one spends \r\n  a little time with anyone, with facades gone, that they will find that you have \r\n  something in common with that other person. for example, President non-elect \r\n  George W. Bush\'s second favorite restaurant in Austin is <a href=http://austin360.com/auto_docs/dining/17159.html>Hoovers</a>, \r\n  first being <a href=\" http://austin360.com/auto_docs/dining/15874.html \">Jeffrey\'s</a>; \r\n  my first being a plethora of others not including <a href=\" http://austin360.com/auto_docs/dining/15874.html \">Jeffrey\'s</a>, \r\n  but still he likes <a href=http://austin360.com/auto_docs/dining/17159.html>hoovers</a> \r\n  and i like <a href=http://austin360.com/auto_docs/dining/17159.html>hoovers</a>.</font></p>\r\n<p><font face=\"Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif\">i wish i would have said \r\n  something nice, friendly, and polite to the sorority girl, so as to let her have this feeling instead of i. afterall i was minding my biz, having a daydream while sitting on the sidewalk, \r\n  picking my nose, listening to birds chirp. i wonder if she feels like shit for what she said? why should i feel bad about what \r\n  i said; she hit me first... still i feel bad.</font></p>\r\n\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/432_1.jpg\'>\r\n'),(433,'<p>\r\nthe sun plays tricks with the sun through the screen and into my room. night day day night midafternoon its nice to be out of school out of work out of money. the days end with sleep and begin with bowls pills and showers. iv applied. iv tried to merge with society. stuck on the gravel shoulder waiting for an opening. back in the home country they\'d have let me in. back in the old country we never locked our doors. things change. who changed and who accepted? those are the things i ask.\r\n</p>'),(434,'<P><TT>i have a place to start right in front of me, a cup of hot coco.\r\n<br><br>\r\ni was lying in the dark, drifing with monk on.  \r\n<br><br>\r\nmy dream was you, a visual representation \r\n<br><br>\r\ntalking through an hour glass\r\n<br><br>\r\nsqueezing through mass reduction is easier when reduced mass accelerates simultaneously.  then i land in your mind.  that is how i imagine it.\r\n<br><br>\r\nsip sip sip sip\r\n<br><br>\r\n(my girl has a ghetto booty =-) it is so sexy.) \r\n<br><br>\r\nsip sip sip</TT></P>'),(435,'<P><A HREF=\"http://hubris.co.nz\">I</A> was talking to <A HREF=\"http://oxy.gen.nz/olivia\">Olivia</A> on the telephone today, and she was fabulous.  She was talking about people, and so she asked me if I knew <A HREF=\"http://www.elly.org\">Elly</A>, so I said \"not really, but I do read Swinney dot org\".  But I said \"Swine-E\" because that\'s the way I\'ve always said it in my head, and she  laughed at me.  Apparently that\'s not how you say it at all.  She laughed and laughed and said that she didn\'t think that <A HREF=\"http://www.swinney.org\">Austin</A> would be too impressed.  I said maybe I should <A HREF=\"http://swinney.org/journals/submit_article.phtml\">write about it</A>, and she said maybe I should.  And so I did. I\'m sorry Austin - I have always said your name wrong.  If it makes you feel better, you can call me \"Joanne\" except that I really really hate that.   \r\n</p>'),(436,'<p>\r\nI said somethings i shouldnt have said to some people today and it sent me downhill. Im so god damn lonely. perhaps for my entire life i have been lonely and it has gotten to the point where i v started asking myself crazy questions regarding sexuality and myself. i drive myself crazy. so god damn shy about so god damn much i get through life never really so a lot to the same person for a long period of time. Iv never had a soul brother. Iv never connected with anyone close and everyday. Instead of talk to myself. spend more time with myself and have the same conversations over and over again that the extreme thoughts begin to look more and more natural...and less and less \"wrong\" or errrrrr \"not me\". to the point of not even wanting a life consisting of anything sexual. and for a period that was great. the same problems surfaced when \"unsexual\" things like cuddling and holding hands and basic standard stupid things came up into question. Its all just shit. My life, while filled with so many extremes and neat \"things\" has been missing the one thing anyone needs. it sucks. i hate it. and i cry.\r\n</P><p><img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/436_1.jpg\' alt=\"meat.\" width=\"520\" height=\"300\">\r\n'),(437,'</p><p align=\"justify\">\r\nmy first boyfriend took this with a polaroid camera that i got for christmas that year. i was naked. i\'ve lost the original. today i was emailing with a guy who first found my site in 1997, and back then he told me <a href=\"http://www.elly.org/mail/jeffrey@web-net.com/May-06-1997-01:13:53\">i look just like his ex girlfriend</a>. i scared him today because not only do i still have his email, i still have the <a href=\"http://superdeluxe.com/people/elly/images/random_web_peeps/metoo.jpg\">picture he sent me back then</a>. but he scared me right back because he still has this picture of me.\r\n</p><p align=\"center\">\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/437_1.gif\' border=\"1\">\r\n</p><p align=\"justify\">\r\nkinda makes a person want to <a href=\"http://swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=162.txt\">grow their hair out</a>. that, however, would not make me 14 again.\r\n</p>'),(438,'<p>i feel shocked, upset, and betrayed.\r\n</p><p>\r\ntonight i decided to wash my laundry. it\'s long overdue, i\'m even wearing my pair of emergency underpants (even the emergency socks are soiled and unusable). unless i finish the laundry tonight, the possibility of a fashionable nightclub romp is out of the question.\r\n</p><p>\r\nunfortunately, my housemate left a 3-day old damp comforter in the washing machine. no problem, i thought, i\'ll just transfer it to the dryer. but i could not! because the dryer is <b>full of towels</b>!\r\n</p><p>\r\nangrily, i flung the towels to the filthy laundry room floor, grumbling curses and vitriol in her name.\r\n</p><p>\r\ni\'m not planning to be home when she arrives, so i will leave her an angry post-it note on the bulletin board that we have reserved for intra-house communication.\r\n</p><p>\r\ni expect that she will respond to this issue in  a thorough and timely fashion.\r\n</p><p>\r\nthis could be the final straw in our relationship. to date, she has:\r\n</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>terrorized my cat<br>\r\n<li>openly spread rumors regarding my sexuality<br>\r\n<li>left piles of unwashed dishs in the sink<br>\r\n<li>moved my personal possessions to the basement<br>\r\n<li>used my computer to download illegally pirated music files<br>\r\n<li>used the shower without permission<br>\r\n<li>pumped the roof without me, robbing me of my only remaining joy<br>\r\n</ul>'),(439,'<p>my name is anonymous n.  I have a problem with sugar.  I\'ve always had this problem.   I came home last night and like an alcoholic fixes himself a double stiff drink at the end of the work week, i made some of my roommate\'s cocoa cause he\'s out of town and i put extra cocoa in it--and i was thinking \"I\'m gonna get fucking wasted. I\'m gonna knock myself out.\"  And then i drank it and i felt good all over--relaxed.  I kicked sugar once before.  It was hard.  I always had cravings.  You know when I was a child I quietly got up before everyone in the house so I could have my morning Oreos (tm)? I ate four, until I was older, when four just didn\'t have the same effect, so I had five. I kept a box of chocolate cakemix and a pink plastic spoon (from Baskin-Robbin (tm)) in the closet for the emergency moments when i couldn\'t find my dad\'s stash. (damn! always one step ahead!)  And barring chocolate cakemix, the last resort was yellow cakemix (actually quite tasty but a poor third.)  It was Betty Crocker Cakemix (tm). This was before \"pudding in the mix.\" Now that i\'m an adult i can afford the good stuff.\r\n</p><p>\r\nI can\'t reveal my name because i am well-respected in the natural foods community for my vegetable-promoting ways.  I pack pour or five different fruits in my lunchbox everyday, and steeamed greenbeans, and spinach tofu pockets, so no one really knows that i have a problem. sure, i will have a cookie in a social setting, but i keep the real stuff hidden--like, i sneak out of class to steal candy from the financial aid lady\'s desk. \r\n</p><p>\r\ni want to change.  i\'m going to try.  my roommate is an enabler.  thank you for listening.\r\n</p>'),(440,'no'),(441,'<P>ok here is the deal. I want to quit smoking and I have made april 1st my quit date. no joke. I need help though. Does anyone know of any cool toys I can play with or any neat methods for quitting? the patch wont work for me. Its more of a hand/oral thing i think. they should really make a nicotine nail polish for nail biters. </P>'),(442,'</p><p>Seeing BMG\'s awesome picture\'s with text made me look for these. of course i didn\'t take the pictures at all.\r\n</p><p align=\"center\">\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/442_1.jpg\' border=\"1\"><br><br><br>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/442_2.jpg\' border=\"1\">\r\n</p>'),(443,'<p>sometimes i am so sick of the wuh wuh wuh. i run from my monitor and curse the day i became an html slave.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>then i come to read the diaries of the children i have grown to love so much, but they aren\'t children anymore, they are growing up.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>and i am wondering if they realize i am not a grownup anymore, i am growing down.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>it is a wonderful circle, this growing down.  you get to enjoy life all over again knowing what you found out on the way to forty and avoid all the pitfalls as you travel the roads you took before without the curves and dead ends and stuff.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>i could not have done it without mark.  how lucky i am!</p>'),(444,'<pre>\r\ncars have souls.\r\nwhen they die, \r\nthey drive the sky\r\nat night as ghosts\r\nabove the city\r\nsometimes there are drivers\r\nbut most live\r\n</pre>'),(445,'<p>this is joanna but not hubris joanna (hi joanna!) but rather <a href=\"http://standing.ontheoutside.com\">standing.ontheoutside.com</a> joanna -- i should also say that i doubted my mom when naming me ever expected me to clarify my existence with a URL.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>so i\'ll stop lurking now, i guess, and start being jo and hi.</p>'),(446,'<p>s5\'s ass, circa 1999.\r\n</p>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/446_1.jpg\' width=\"320\" height=\"240\" alt=\"eeyore\" border=\"1\">'),(447,'<p>s5 is worried about clean drawers. he appears to be a victim of elly sprawl.</p>\r\n<p>artists can not be held responsible for taking care of mundane things like remembering to put the wet clothes in the dryer...</p>\r\n<p>elly is an artist.</p>\r\n<p>examples of art, poetry, and prose during childhood:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>once placed an entire box of 64 crayons on a hot radiator to see what would happen.\r\n<li>created snowscape across kitchen with large box of oatmeal while singing appropriate snow ditty.\r\n<li>published underground newspaper in high school resulting in near explulsion. \r\n<li>made a giant cigarette from rug tube that requires special packaging and is so wonderful it has been moved by professionals in special packaging across oceans and states.\r\n<li>when confronted by grandmother at age two about lack of desire to eschew diapers announced that she was NOT a baby, she was \"a woman who wet her pants and liked it.\"\r\n</ul><em>this last should be worth any unfortunate sexual preference remarks, if more ondits are needed for retribution, please ask.</em>\r\n'),(448,'<p>\r\naustin (from austin)\r\n</p><p>\r\nyou need to move here.\r\n</p><p>\r\nand be with us.\r\n</p><p>\r\nit\'ll be like The Firm, but better.\r\n</p>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/448_1.jpg\'>'),(449,'<P>\r\nendorphins #1:\r\n</P><P>\r\n<img src=\"http://daintycore.com/tattoo.jpg\" alt=\"ow\">\r\n</P><P>\r\nand well, this is just cool. i made a dress out of astroturf:\r\n</P><P>\r\n<img src=\"http://daintycore.com/dress.jpg\" alt=\"doormat\">\r\n</P>\r\n'),(450,'  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" >JesseJoker \r\n    has been renting shit at the video store. These are some suggestions:</p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" ><a href=\"http://www.spe.sony.com/classics/allaboutmymother/frames.html\" target=\"_blank\">All \r\n    About My Mother (Todo Sobre Mi Madre)</a></p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" ><a href=\"http://zone51.com/kingdom/index2.htm\" target=\"_blank\">The \r\n    Kingdom</a></p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" ><a href=\"http://www.best.com/%7Edrumz/Hartley/Films/tbol.html\" target=\"_blank\">The \r\n    Book of Life</a></p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" ><a href=\"http://store.yahoo.com/animenation/av-1290.html\" target=\"_blank\">Cowboy \r\n    Bebop </a></p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" ><a href=\"http://www.foreignfilms.com/films/2721.asp\">Insomnia</a></p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" ><a href=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/0790746999.01.LZZZZZZZ.gif\" target=\"_blank\">Key \r\n    Largo </a></p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" ><a href=\"http://weeklywire.com/filmvault/austin/g/graysanatomy1.html\" target=\"_blank\">Gray\'s \r\n    Anatomy </a></p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" ><a href=\"http://www.rottentomatoes.com/movie-1039801/about.php\" target=\"_blank\">Kafka</a> \r\n  </p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" ><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/6304239149/ref=ase_cmgworldwide/107-0925865-3098917\" target=\"_blank\">Giant</a></p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" ><a href=\"http://www.eusa.ed.ac.uk/societies/filmsoc/films/chungking_express.html\">Chunking \r\n    Express</a></p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" >\"I \r\n    know a gentleman who looks like you. In fact he looks more like you than you \r\n    do yourself.\" - kafka.</p>'),(451,'  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" >JesseJoker \r\n    has been renting shit at the video store. These are some suggestions:</p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" ><a href=\"http://www.spe.sony.com/classics/allaboutmymother/frames.html\" target=\"_blank\">All \r\n    About My Mother (Todo Sobre Mi Madre)</a></p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" ><a href=\"http://zone51.com/kingdom/index2.htm\" target=\"_blank\">The \r\n    Kingdom</a></p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" ><a href=\"http://www.best.com/%7Edrumz/Hartley/Films/tbol.html\" target=\"_blank\">The \r\n    Book of Life</a></p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" ><a href=\"http://store.yahoo.com/animenation/av-1290.html\" target=\"_blank\">Cowboy \r\n    Bebop </a></p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" ><a href=\"http://www.foreignfilms.com/films/2721.asp\">Insomnia</a></p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" ><a href=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/0790746999.01.LZZZZZZZ.gif\" target=\"_blank\">Key \r\n    Largo </a></p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" ><a href=\"http://weeklywire.com/filmvault/austin/g/graysanatomy1.html\" target=\"_blank\">Gray\'s \r\n    Anatomy </a></p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" ><a href=\"http://www.rottentomatoes.com/movie-1039801/about.php\" target=\"_blank\">Kafka</a> \r\n  </p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" ><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/6304239149/ref=ase_cmgworldwide/107-0925865-3098917\" target=\"_blank\">Giant</a></p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" ><a href=\"http://www.eusa.ed.ac.uk/societies/filmsoc/films/chungking_express.html\">Chunking \r\n    Express</a></p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" >\"I \r\n    know a gentleman who looks like you. In fact he looks more like you than you \r\n    do yourself.\" - kafka.</p>'),(452,'a list:<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<li>i will hope brian is happy, with his new life and new friends.<br>\r\n<li>i will miss elly\'s frenetic peace at home.<br>\r\n<li>i will wonder when we\'ll lose xep and eric to melbs.<br>\r\n<li>i will miss olivia because i always do.<br>\r\n<li>i will hope peter lets loose and underplans for italy.<br>\r\n<li>i will hope allison doesn\'t have to come home early from thailand.<br>\r\n<li>i will be psyched for chaya, and i will worry about scary things happening while she\'s far.<br>\r\n<li>i will run off to joshua tree, and dance under the full moon.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nwhen we all think of each other, we\'re never far away.<br>\r\n'),(453,'<pre>\r\nBeautiful\r\n  Where I wallow on spaces\r\n  Mixture\r\n     Crossiant and apple seed\r\n     Or tonic sans mead\r\n     For such stuff one bleeds\r\n     In asphyxiating tweed\r\n    The silk-knotted obligation noose\r\n  Hear me, children\r\n    Saith one\r\n  A black tuniced historian\r\n  Perilous perched on spires\r\n  Gonging and ticking and ceaseless\r\n    Like Stygian fire\r\n  Hear me, quoth he\r\n  Tick-tock, tick-tock\r\n  And wallets are all we require\r\n</pre>\r\n'),(454,'<font face=\"verdana\" size=2>\r\n<p>i used to think that i was the only one who <a href=\"http://sent.diaryland.com/012501.html\">hated february</a>. i mean, i hate february so much that i even made myself a <a href=\"http://standing.ontheoutside.com/tapes/february.txt\">CD</a> designed to fight the evils of the month.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>but i didn\'t know others felt the same way!<BR>\r\nwhat is up with february?</p></font>'),(455,'<P>it is 1 a.m. at the world headquarters of the international company. i was locked in.  the result of being here late and not saying anything.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i had to pee and i wanted a snickers bar.  it was necessary.  so it went off.  i peed and got a snickers.  the alarm went off. i called the security company and told them:</P>\r\n<P>\r\nA) not to come to the office building, false alarm\r\n</P><P>\r\nB) if they do come, to have the metal out because it is going to be blazing saddles\r\n</P>\r\n<P>i had french fries and a milk shake for lunch and have been bombing the area ever since.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>the beautiful <TT><A href=\"http://kirstinashe.com/\">K*</a></TT> sent me her latest piece of music done for composition class.  <a href=\"http://swinney.org/music/Kirstin.mp3\">it is an mp3</A>.  i think it is beautiful.  the song goes with an imaginary movie scene set in bosnia with some refugees.  she can say more about it, i don\'t know the specifics.</P>'),(456,'<p>i have to make a will in case they kill me in the hospital.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>i will upload it to my server in a protected word document and then, if i die, everyone can read it so there will be no confusion as to my last wishes.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>i have 13 days to figure out what my last wishes are.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>the only thing i am sure of is that i want to be buried in my red rabat shoes.</p>'),(457,'<font face=\"verdana\" size=2>\r\n<p>listen, all of you who\'re in austin need to go see the donnas and bratmobile tonight at emo\'s!</p>\r\n<p>they are such fantastic girls! they sing about being drunk and doing drugs and having lots and lots of sex and you just can\'t help loving them with reckless abandon.<BR>\r\nlyrics like, \"you\'ve got a crush on me/ and it\'s easy to see/ that you write about me/ in your diary.\"<BR>\r\nawww donnas.</p>\r\n<p>my friend jason and i will be there, so look for us if you decide to go! i look sorta like <a href=\"http://mr.unpopular.com/~joanna/\">this</a>!\r\n</font>'),(458,'<p>what am I suppose to write about?  me?  Oh I\'m stupid and boring.  Bleh.</p>'),(459,'<p>Is this my diary?  I don\'t know I\'m so confused.... How did I get here anyway?  Oh dear I\'m so scared.</P>\r\n\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/459_1.gif\'>'),(460,'<P>\r\nFour and half years ago or so, I was flat-ass broke and living with my elderly aunt and uncle for a few months.\r\nI had just come back from living in Japan for two and half years.\r\nThis was a strange and desperate place. A definite <TT>downer</TT> of a time.\r\n</P>\r\n<P>\r\nI spent my 28th birthday there getting loaded on vodka and percocets.\r\nThis was in the house while my Aunt and Uncle were visiting the east coast for a month. </P>\r\n<P>\r\nThis all started innocently and not unusually enough by being alone on my birthday and\r\ndeciding to call some people I hadn\'t talked to in a while.\r\nNext thing you know, suddenly the idea of a few drinks seemed the thing to do.\r\nOne long phone call and a huge OJ and vodka later, the percocets that I knew were in the\r\nmedicine cabinet were alluring me. Hmm.. let\'s start with 2, no 3, what the hell, 4.\r\nThen the calls to Japan. Local friends were few and far between, so I had to go\r\n\"international\" at this point.</P>\r\n<P>The calls continue I\'m feeling pretty good and I\'m not even *that* embarassed that\r\npeople can tell I\'m half-crocked as I\'m slurring my words babbling away.</P>\r\n<P>\r\nWell, you know, as it often is, too much is not quite enough. It\'s about midnight. Early,\r\nright? I\'ll just down two more percs with this drink. That\'ll do me good.</P>\r\n<BR>\r\n<P>I don\'t have very much in the way of a clear memory of that night, other than I called\r\npractically everyone I knew. Some were good calls. Some made me cringe, especially the\r\nlater ones that must have led people to believe that I was not quite allright back home.</P>\r\n<P>\r\nNext \"morning\" I woke up at about 5 very confused. \r\nI was still in my clothes on top of the covers in exactly the same position when I first\r\nlied down. Was it night still? Or dawn? Dusk. (Looking back and forth at the clock, hazy\r\nconfusion)</P>\r\n<P>I felt terrible not because of the hangover (not bad actually just *foggy*) but from\r\nthe embarassment and overall feeling of being a total loser. What level had I sunken to?</P>\r\n<P>Later that night, driving past a gas station I worked at for exactly four weeks once.\r\nI felt glad that I have progressed in some ways at least.</P>\r\n<i>Today</i> by the Smashing Pumpkins comes on the radio (yes, a shit sell-out\r\nband, but before shit <I>Siamese Dream</I> and <I>Pisces Iscariot</I> were two\r\ngood albums.) It is \"break-up\" music for me. The music you play at that time\r\nlater engrained in your brain and emotional background.</P><P>\r\nI feel sad, or is it happy? Happy to feel(?) Happy that life is strange and F\'ed up(?)<BR>\r\n<B>Or is it just the opiates?</B> Yes, definitely -- a long half-life no doubt.<BR>\r\nRegardless, I pulled over by the side of the road, crying. <BR>\r\nWaves of nostalgia, pain, confusion, bliss, endorphins...</P>\r\n<P>I remember that snapshot of my life and the strange peaceful confusion of those few minutes.</P>'),(461,'<P>\r\nFour and half years ago or so, I was flat-ass broke and living with my elderly aunt and uncle for a few months.\r\nI had just come back from living in Japan for two and half years.\r\nThis was a strange and desperate place. A definite <TT>downer</TT> of a time.\r\n</P>\r\n<P>\r\nI spent my 28th birthday there getting loaded on vodka and percocets.\r\nThis was in the house while my Aunt and Uncle were visiting the east coast for a month. </P>\r\n<P>\r\nThis all started innocently and not unusually enough by being alone on my birthday and\r\ndeciding to call some people I hadn\'t talked to in a while.\r\nNext thing you know, suddenly the idea of a few drinks seemed the thing to do.\r\nOne long phone call and a huge OJ and vodka later, the percocets that I knew were in the\r\nmedicine cabinet were alluring me. Hmm.. let\'s start with 2, no 3, what the hell, 4.\r\nThen the calls to Japan. Local friends were few and far between, so I had to go\r\n\"international\" at this point.</P>\r\n<P>The calls continue I\'m feeling pretty good and I\'m not even *that* embarassed that\r\npeople can tell I\'m half-crocked as I\'m slurring my words babbling away.</P>\r\n<P>\r\nWell, you know, as it often is, too much is not quite enough. It\'s about midnight. Early,\r\nright? I\'ll just down two more percs with this drink. That\'ll do me good.</P>\r\n<BR>\r\n<P>I don\'t have very much in the way of a clear memory of that night, other than I called\r\npractically everyone I knew. Some were good calls. Some made me cringe, especially the\r\nlater ones that must have led people to believe that I was not quite allright back home.</P>\r\n<P>\r\nNext \"morning\" I woke up at about 5 very confused. \r\nI was still in my clothes on top of the covers in exactly the same position when I first\r\nlied down. Was it night still? Or dawn? Dusk. (Looking back and forth at the clock, hazy\r\nconfusion)</P>\r\n<P>I felt terrible not because of the hangover (not bad actually just *foggy*) but from\r\nthe embarassment and overall feeling of being a total loser. What level had I sunken to?</P>\r\n<P>Later that night, driving past a gas station I worked at for exactly four weeks once.\r\nI felt glad that I have progressed in some ways at least.</P>\r\n<i>Today<i> by the Smashing Pumpkins comes on the radio (yes, a shit sell-out\r\nband, but before shit <I>Siamese Dream</I> and <I>Pisces Iscariot</I> were two\r\ngood albums.) It is \"break-up\" music for me. The music you play at that time\r\nlater engrained in your brain and emotional background.</P><P>\r\nI feel sad, or is it happy? Happy to feel(?) Happy that life is strange and F\'ed up(?)<BR>\r\n<B>Or is it just the opiates?</B> Yes, definitely -- a long half-life no doubt.<BR>\r\nRegardless, I pulled over by the side of the road, crying. <BR>\r\nWaves of nostalgia, pain, confusion, bliss, endorphins...</P>\r\n<P>I remember that snapshot of my life and the strange peaceful confusion of those few minutes.</P>'),(462,'<P>\r\nfunny thing, life -- determined by a collection of forces that\r\nare essentially not of your own choosing...</P>\r\n<P>\r\nAfter being broke for six months, back in the US I finally found a job. This was good.\r\nI smelt of cigar and perfume smell from the family members. It reminded me of my situation,\r\nbut now I was out, in my own apartment a month after the job.</P>\r\n<P>I was the teenager getting out of the house. Marijuana, a forbidden fruit in the land where I lived\r\nfor the last two and half years in Japan and last six months in various residences who would not\r\nappreciate it, was now an option.</P>\r\n<P>This was in december of 96, revelling in my freedom I would lay on the floor of my\r\nentirely unfurnished apartment, feeling the fuzz on the carpet.\r\nLooking upward at the ceiling I could imagine all of San Diego in it\'s mild winter\r\nweather near the ocean.</P>\r\n<P>One of my few possessions was a CD walkman, and after smoking some weed for the first time in several\r\nmonths I listened to <I>Tool</I>. Again, like my current life totally overplayed and trite. At that time\r\nthough very tripped out.</P>\r\n<P>During the day I would anxiously wander around my new job trying to get accustomed to my new life\r\nin America.</P><P><CENTER>----------</CENTER></P>\r\n<P>Fast forward to <B>now</B>. I\'m now at a crossroads again. A new job, possibly.</P>\r\n<P>This time though it\'s a lot different. I am not desperate. I don\'t smell like cigars and perfume.\r\nI don\'t smoke weed and listen to Tool. I am not flat-ass broke. There not any way that you could consider\r\nme <I>adolescent</I> at all, even though I think somewhere inside I don\'t ever made that change \r\nentirely.</P>\r\n<P>Yes, this time it\'s much more difficult. Now I\'m not reacting to the latest crises that I\'ve gotten\r\nmyself in.</P>\r\n<P>This is complacency. This is what happens when the place that you thought you would be working\r\nat for a year, two tops, becomes four and a half. <BR>\r\nNo more worries at work. Just the slow inevitable drain and numbness. Danger, excitement... vastly\r\noverrated at this point. Forget about it. Who needs it?</P>\r\n<P>But it\'s good. Forget about the schemes and dreams. Get used to what you do. Like it. Feel comfortable.\r\nSafety is good. Why rock the boat? Be satisfied with what you have since that\'s all you\'re\r\ngoing to get. Don\'t fool yourself. Don\'t throw away what you\'ve built up.\r\nIt\'s bullshit to think about how great things are going to be. Right here and right now they\'re not so\r\nbad are they?</P>\r\n<P>But anyway... the funny thing is after complaining about my job for the last few years, ever since I\r\ngot it I didn\'t realize that underneath it all I am really <B>used to it</B> and I\r\n<B>really do like it.</B>\r\nNo major problems, no politics, very comfortable, safe.</P>\r\n<P>That said... I know it, I think I gotta go. Time for a change.</P>\r\n<P>Trade the cushy position with office window, for a cubicle in a grungy internet startup I suppose.\r\nI still don\'t know.</P>\r\n<P>In this moment of indecision it\'s relief and agony.\r\nI can think about new challenges, new potential, just... <B>new</B> in general. <BR>\r\nBut \"new\" can really suck too. Bad environment, no understanding, high-pressure. Ahh.. but I can stay\r\nright where I am I don\'t have to change after all, nice same office, nice same slow, <B>gradualness</B>.\r\nBut then again, five years from now... same place. Goddamn you suck, how lame. You passed by so many\r\noppurtunities...</P><P>\r\nWell after all it\'s still just a \"job\". Having to show up somewhere to do some crap for someone you\r\ndon\'t really care about. Maybe I\'ve been doing the crap I\'ve been doing for so long that I don\'t even\r\nsee it that way anymore. Maybe it\'s not always \"crap\". In any case I shall sit and dwell\r\non it for awhile.</P>'),(463,'<a href=\"http://swinney.org/journals/images/436_1.jpg\"><img src=\"http://swinney.org/journals/images/436_1.jpg\" width=350 alt=\"click to enlarge\"></a>\r\n<p>\r\nok listen here. im serious. the pizza with gravy thing might not be the \"in thing\" in wherever you are in the world, but I talked to the owner of the place and he told me the gravy thing is 80% of his sales. (dont bother with the \"he must have no business\" crap cuz im being serious). The whole gravy and pizza thing is a crazy combo that isnt exactly politically correct among food people these days. We have the vegans who would absolutely vomit at the site of this delight, and thats fine. Im not asking vegans to eat it. Im not asking anyone who is allergic to any of the ingredients to eat it. Im not asking anyone who thinks it looks gross to eat it. I just think all you people should be a little more honest in their reaction. Less dramatic. \r\n</P><P>\r\nI think oysters are good. People say the same things. \"oh my god oysters makes me want to absolutely retch my guts out and die!!!!!!!\". By the end of their rant on oysters they get to the point. \"the texture is just so gross\". THERE WE GO!!!!. \r\n</P><P>\r\nOk, now ill admit that I do the ol exagerundy on a lot of things, but not when it comes to food. aight!?! so all you closed minded and ignorant people who would normally eat gravy on chicken or roast beef, and pizza when drunk and feelin the munchies, but not at the same time can GO TO HELL!!!! try it once and tell me you almost spewed, but dont just say that from looking at a picture. \r\n</P><P>\r\n<STRONG>GOD DAMN IT IM MAD!!!!!! </STRONG>\r\n</P><P>\r\ni dont even think ill eat the pizza again i had the shits so bad after, but holy fuck it was good, and holy shit it just pisses me off when people start dissin it. Sorta like people who thought black people were \"different\" and enslaved them. Yeah thats how all you closed minded food bastards are like.</P>'),(464,'<TT>\r\nheadphone cord<br>\r\nrubber light up worm<br>\r\nwashcloth (wet only)<br>\r\nthumb<br>\r\nfingers<br>\r\nother people\'s fingers<br>\r\nstrings from hoody<br>\r\nother people\'s hoodie strings<br>\r\ncuff of my sleeve<br>\r\n<a href=\"http://vagabondage.com/lf/koininboone/25/small\">cow</a>\'s ear<br>\r\ncow\'s tail<br>\r\nice<br>\r\nthose little strips of plastic from bottle lids<br>\r\nin fact, i carry one of those around with me at all times<br>\r\ncable ties<br>\r\ngarbage ties<br>\r\npeter\'s backpack straps (bad idea)<br>\r\n</TT>\r\n'),(465,'<p>\r\ni was going to type something but i chickened out.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nwhere is everyone these days?\r\n</p>'),(466,'<p>\r\nshe called she said she wanted to talk she said because of boy we could not joy and so the story ended and we became back friended which is negative in my world and while blah isnt blah its still blah to me. do you understand how frustrated i am with life? I have the material shit upto my ass. high tech wahzooz and top of the line do rags and all that live jazz. I think i cut the key but then the locks all change into new ideas and new mindedness and then i get the talk. the talk. in the serious  voice. the talk to mom voice at christmas best behaviour. trying the casually eat the peanut and honey roasted legs that look like the colour of the things in the jar the peanuts and then i just try to make the flame go down. if you into that. if you know what the talk or given the talk iv given the talk but not in so many words i think the talk was good but i did not give the talk i wanted to talk and i ran around the table and back into the woods no more tylers i know its sad and i know ill live but fuck it was just stupid in the first place justify thank say back to irc. </P>'),(467,'<p>\r\ndriving home through the central valley, it\'s 4:30am. the 3 cups of coffee i drank in los angeles have completely worn off.\r\n</p><p>\r\nthe steering wheel looks like a lovely pillow. and the road looks just straight enough to doze off for only a second.....\r\n</p><p>\r\nso i pull into the next truck stop. swallow 200mg of ephedrine and 8oz of nasty filth percolating at the bottom of the gas station carafe.\r\n</p><p>\r\ni pay for fuel (92 octane, i spoil my car). next to the register is a large display of cassette tapes, for all the bored truckers needing to break their 14 hour silence. everything you\'d expect from the trucker genre: allman brothers, dolly parton, lynyrd skynyrd.\r\n</p><p>\r\nbut LO! what\'s this! BLACK SABBATH!! buried deep in the stack of otherwise unassuming country-western ass rock favorites.\r\n</p><p>\r\ndriving home, in the middle of nowhere, tearing up farmlands at 100mph in my fully radar protected german machine of destruction, black sabbath playing as loud as humanly possible. the sun is rising.\r\n</p><p>\r\nand right at the moment i knew for sure that noone was looking, \"war pigs\" was the next song. i remembered every word, and belted them out as loud as i possibly could. i even sang along to the tony iommi overtracked guitar solos.\r\n</p><p>\r\nfuck. life could not get better than this.\r\n</p><p>\r\nin case you forgot the words, relive high school with me for a sec and sing along:\r\n</p>\r\n<blockquote>\r\n<pre><tt>\r\nGenerals gathered in their masses,\r\njust like witches at black masses.\r\nEvil minds that plot destruction,\r\nsorcerers of death\'s construction.\r\nIn the fields the bodies burning,\r\nas the war machine keeps turning.\r\nDeath and hatred to mankind,\r\npoisoning their brainwashed minds.\r\nOh lord, yeah!\r\n\r\nPoliticians hide themselves away.\r\nThey only started the war.\r\nWhy should they go out to fight?\r\nThey leave that role to the poor, yeah.\r\n\r\nTime will tell on their power minds,\r\nmaking war just for fun.\r\nTreating people just like pawns in chess,\r\nwait till their judgement day comes, yeah.\r\n\r\nNow in darkness world stops turning,\r\nashes where the bodies burning.\r\nNo more War Pigs have the power,\r\nHand of God has struck the hour.\r\nDay of judgement, God is calling,\r\non their knees the war pigs crawling.\r\nBegging mercies for their sins,\r\nSatan, laughing, spreads his wings.\r\nOh lord, yeah!\r\n               --Black Sabbath, War Pigs\r\n</tt></pre>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n\r\n(long guitar solo)'),(468,'<P>i know a yeti.  he is a beautiful creature.  i am at work now lamenting that i cannot go get coffee with him.  he is not from around these parts.  los angeles has few yeti.  if there are any, they live near my house in the hollywood hills, but i doubt it.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i thought about it and i think i never want to work in a cublicle environment with my yeti friend ever.  i would be terrified if i looked over the divider to the next row and saw the yeti sitting at a computer.  it would just be wrong.</P>\r\n\r\n\r\n<P>the yeti are solitary.  they work alone or in small groups.  the yeti cannot be caged.  they must have migration corridors within which to roam.  those corridors must be open and consisting of a narrow home in the rocks, a cave, or townhouse.  maybe a mound out in the wildes.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>there must be coffee houses in the migration corridor.  yeti drink coffee enough for three men.  there must be yeti friends near by.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>the yeti migrates in certain seasons.  sometimes he is to be seen.  othertimes, he is making marbled paper and you will not see him.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i look forward to migrating closer to yeti myself.  they are magical creatures to have in your midst.  love the yeti.  do not fear him.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>and alway be prepared to throw down with the yeti, because they are like that.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>and remember:  always fight to keep your yeti free range!</P>'),(469,'  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" >Look \r\n    Austin, <a href=\"http://www.achtungbaby.org/Links.html\" target=\"_blank\">My \r\n    Links</a> almost done, or as done as i will get them.</p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" >I\'m \r\n    Reading: <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1573228583/qid=983579092/sr=1-1/ref=sc_b_1/102-2475912-2958520\">Speaking \r\n    With the Angel</a></p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" >E-mails \r\n    sent last month: 834.</p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" >[ \r\n    February Soundtrack ] </p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" >Tank! \r\n    - Yoko Kanno</p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" >Big \r\n    Girls Are Best - U2</p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" >Latin \r\n    Simone - Gorillaz</p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" >I\'m \r\n    afraid of americans - David Bowie</p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" >Way \r\n    Below The Radio - Lisa Germano</p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" >The \r\n    Shinning - Badly Drawn Boy</p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" >Style \r\n    It Takes - John Cale</p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" >Butterfly \r\n    - Tori Amos</p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" >For \r\n    No One - the Beatles</p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" >You \r\n    Sort Of Humman Being - Emm Grynner</p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" >Die \r\n    Like Someone - Eve\'s Pulmb</p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" >Kiss \r\n    Movement 10 - John Cale</p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" >Would \r\n    You Like To Swing On A Star - Frank Sinatra</p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" >Memphis \r\n    - Polly Harvey</p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" >Pyramid \r\n    Song - Radiohead</p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" >[Aquisitions]</p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" >DVDs: \r\n    Bring It On, The Game, The Invisible Man, Insomnia, Toy Story Boxed Set, The \r\n    Thomas Crown Affair, The Sopranos 1st Season Box.</p>\r\n  <p style=\"FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: lucida sans unicode\" align=\"left\" >\" \r\n    a computer lets you make mistakes faster than any other human invention...\"</p>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/469_1.gif\' border=\'1\' alt=\'\'>'),(470,'<P>today i feel wack.  whenever that happens on a weekend, i end up at work.  it does not take much effort to figure out why that is.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>if i don\'t have anything i want to do, i go to work.  that is the way it always is.  i think becuase although i do not want to do whatever it is, i always have something to do at work.  so it makes a good fill in candidate for something to do.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i am going to go to the gym in an hour or so.  i missed going to the gym all week.  i don\'t usually slack like that.  but i had a bunch of work to catch up on after my last trip to san francisco.  and that work is exciting.  i am learning something new.  that is always fun and difficult.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>tonight i am going to an Indian music presentation at k*\'s yoga house.  i look forward to that.  she is going to give me a massage in preparation for starting back to work as a grappling therapist.  i am going to be grappled.  not to be confused with a sensuous massage, i guess.  getting grappled actually hurts.  it is painful.  i have never had a full grapple experience.  i think i am going to get that today.  she told me not to work out to hard because my muscles will be sore and the grappling will *hurt worse*.</P>\r\n\r\n<!-- kill here // they can\'t handle the truth...\r\n\r\n<P>k* and i are getting allong well.  we offend each other every now and then, usually i think because one of us is tired or hungry or stressed.  i am pretty good at blowing that stuff off when it is her on the prowl.  when it is me, i feel bad for a few yours or a day after.  i\'ll send her a poem or appology and she is usually very forgiving, unless we tangle over something portent, then she will hold her ground.  somtimes she gives it up to the extent that i can come up with a reasonable arguement.  other times i am wrong.  i usually let that stuff go.  i don\'t mind that we have differences of oppinion.  i like it?</P>\r\n\r\n<P>lately, the last few weeks, i have wanted to tell her i love her.  i get really strong feelings to that effect.  i love you, i feel.  sometimes it is very strong.  like when we get in a tangle, i feel very strong love for her.  it is my heart telling me that whatever we get angry about, it is not nearly as important as my feelings for her.  and i become extremely appologetic.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>this in contrast to how i deal with others that i tangle will with.  i am not so forgiving.  only when i love them will i fogive them.  i should get beyond this.\r\n</P>\r\n\r\n<P>san francisco is heavy on my mind. i want to move there.  i don\'t know if it is because i am running from people that i am angry at?  i guess i am.  i want away from the house i am in.  how did i end up in two negative places in a row?  that apartment in Glendale, and now this duplex in Los Feliz.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i like my friend kiki, but i really think that the neighbor arnie is bad.  he has some problems both outwardly obvious but also some that opperate on an almost imperceptible level.  he is mean to people subtly causing them great greif when they don\'t know what the did to deserve it.  maybe they did not do anything to deserve the level of negative energy he exudes.  maybe they do.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i used to think that kiki had just negative energy that she had in her she needed to get out, but that is not right to me anymore.  now i believe arnie throws it at her and she is giving it back.  very sad.  very very sad.  she is so nice.  i give her nice energy and she gives it back.  kiki is very giving in what she recieves.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>she says arnie must be forgiving because he is such a creative genius.  i never see it though.  i think he is abusive and that is all.  i really do not appreciate abusive genius.  i have seen it before and it sucks the life out of the real geniuses, those who have love.</P>\r\n\r\n\r\n-->'),(471,'<P>today i feel wack.  whenever that happens on a weekend, i end up at work.  it does not take much effort to figure out why that is.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>if i don\'t have anything i want to do, i go to work.  that is the way it always is.  i think becuase although i do not want to do whatever it is, i always have something to do at work.  so it makes a good fill in candidate for something to do.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i am going to go to the gym in an hour or so.  i missed going to the gym all week.  i don\'t usually slack like that.  but i had a bunch of work to catch up on after my last trip to san francisco.  and that work is exciting.  i am learning something new.  that is always fun and difficult.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>tonight i am going to an Indian music presentation at k*\'s yoga house.  i look forward to that.  she is going to give me a massage in preparation for starting back to work as a grappling therapist.  i am going to be grappled.  not to be confused with a sensuous massage, i guess.  getting grappled actually hurts.  it is painful.  i have never had a full grapple experience.  i think i am going to get that today.  she told me not to work out to hard because my muscles will be sore and the grappling will *hurt worse*.</P>\r\n\r\n<-- kill here -->\r\n\r\n<P>k* and i are getting allong well.  we offend each other every now and then, usually i think because one of us is tired or hungry or stressed.  i am pretty good at blowing that stuff off when it is her on the prowl.  when it is me, i feel bad for a few yours or a day after.  i\'ll send her a poem or appology and she is usually very forgiving, unless we tangle over something portent, then she will hold her ground.  somtimes she gives it up to the extent that i can come up with a reasonable arguement.  other times i am wrong.  i usually let that stuff go.  i don\'t mind that we have differences of oppinion.  i like it?</P>\r\n\r\n<P>lately, the last few weeks, i have wanted to tell her i love her.  i get really strong feelings to that effect.  i love you, i feel.  sometimes it is very strong.  like when we get in a tangle, i feel very strong love for her.  it is my heart telling me that whatever we get angry about, it is not nearly as important as my feelings for her.  and i become extremely appologetic.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>this in contrast to how i deal with others that i tangle will with.  i am not so forgiving.  only when i love them will i fogive them.  i should get beyond this.\r\n</P>\r\n\r\n<P>san francisco is heavy on my mind. i want to move there.  i don\'t know if it is because i am running from people that i am angry at?  i guess i am.  i want away from the house i am in.  how did i end up in two negative places in a row?  that apartment in Glendale, and now this duplex in Los Feliz.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i like my friend kiki, but i really think that the neighbor arnie is bad.  he has some problems both outwardly obvious but also some that opperate on an almost imperceptible level.  he is mean to people subtly causing them great greif when they don\'t know what the did to deserve it.  maybe they did not do anything to deserve the level of negative energy he exudes.  maybe they do.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i used to think that kiki had just negative energy that she had in her she needed to get out, but that is not right to me anymore.  now i believe arnie throws it at her and she is giving it back.  very sad.  very very sad.  she is so nice.  i give her nice energy and she gives it back.  kiki is very giving in what she recieves.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>she says arnie must be forgiving because he is such a creative genius.  i never see it though.  i think he is abusive and that is all.  i really do not appreciate abusive genius.  i have seen it before and it sucks the life out of the real geniuses, those who have love.</P>\r\n\r\n\r\n-->'),(472,'<PRE>\r\ni once knew a friend\r\nbut not always.\r\n</PRE>\r\n<font size=1><a href=\"http://home.earthlink.net/~jfilan/shrimp/shrimp.html\">shrimp</a></font>'),(473,'<P>sitting beneath the old commie radio jamming tower - wondering how to grapple with the time around me - moments now - seen for the taking - and moments ahead that hide just behind a probablity haze - i can see just not enough to have much influence of the path these bubbles of time take - and just who is seeing who? aaaaaaaaaaaa!!!!!! what\'s a man to do - multiply all this by love - and then the world gets tricky to compakt into these dull tools we call words.  </P>'),(474,'<p>there is this broad who tries to sue me twice a year, every spring and every fall.<br><br>\r\n\r\nit\'s that time of year again.<br><br>\r\n\r\ni hope she remembers that you reap what you sow because one of these days she is gonna catch me in a bad mood and i am gonna sue her ass right back so hard she\'ll think a fifty foot donkey has mounted her high on viagra.<br><br>\r\n\r\nmaybe today is the day, huh?<br></p>\r\n'),(475,'<font face=\"verdana\" size=2>\r\n<p>i\'ve decided that the way various friends of mine relate to my cat and vice versa is an interesting little study. for instance:</p>\r\n<ul><li><b>my roommate, john</b> mostly ignores the cat but sometimes taunts her and derives great pleasure from this. she seems ambivalent to him.</li>\r\n<li><b>sara</b> likes to play games with her. that often either dissolve into petting or result in many scratches on sara\'s arms and, once, face.</li>\r\n<li><b>elly:</b> \"jo, your cat\'s bowl is empty.\"<BR>\r\n\"oh that\'s okay. she already ate once a day. i feed her again tonight.\"<BR>\r\n\"wait so you only feed her twice? i just fill the bowl whenever it\'s empty. maybe that\'s why my cat is so fat.\"</li>\r\n<li><b>patrick</b> she mostly hides from. will occasionally come out and watch him and then hide again. he\'s tall and he paces.</li>\r\n<li><b>jason</b>, she loves. the minute he sits down, she\'s in his lap. i suspect she loves him more than she loves me.</li>\r\n<li><b><a href=\"http://mr.unpopular.com/~szajic\">stefan</a></b> causes strange behavior in my kitty. one night she would flop down a few feet from where he was sitting on the floor, and roll over, staring at him. he would extend his hand and she would jump up and run away. so he would stretch closer to her. she\'d get some distance from him, flop, and roll over. he\'d reach for her and she\'d jump up and run away.<BR>\r\nat night, she would hop in bed with us and nuzzle stefan\'s nose until he awoke. (she never does this with me.)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\ninteresting, to say the least.'),(476,'<P>In the last 7 days I have read 2 books entire.</P>\r\n\r\n<B>\"100 Years of Solitude\"</B> by Gabriel Garcia Marquez and <B>\"The Left Hand of Darkness\"</B> by Ursula K Le Guin. They were both very good, by which I mean that I assume they must be good because I got a little sad after reading them.\r\n\r\n-darwin\r\n'),(477,'<P>le thinks part of the house in aus is maybe haunted.<br><br>\r\n\r\ni believe that there are places with bad karma.  many years ago when we were in germany, we drove through this one stretch of woods near a place called walthershausen and we got totally freaked out at the oppressiveness and evil feeling of it all.<br><br>\r\n\r\ntwo k\'s up the road, the woods looked the same, but the evil feeling was gone.<br><br>\r\n\r\ni\'ve always thought that something terrible happened to some jews in those woods.  or maybe the evil was older than that.<br><br>\r\n\r\non the other hand, i really like this duplex we live in here in texas.  it has no redeeming qualities really, except that it feels good to be here.<br><br>\r\n\r\nthe place where it was built had been cattle range for as long as anyone had any history of the area.<br><br>\r\n\r\ni like to think that some time or the other some people who were in love camped where this duplex now sits.</P>'),(478,'<p><font face=\"verdana\" size=\"2\">\r\ni am not a young person.  this gives me some experience on which to draw.<br><br>\r\ni avoid litigation of all sorts whenever possible.<br><br>\r\ni have served on jury duty three times and never tried to get out of it.<br><br>\r\ni have been threatened with lawsuits by three different persons in my life.  in every instance the reason for the lawsuit had no basis in fact and when push came to shove, they offered to settle out of court.  in every instance i suggested that they go ahead and sue since i knew they had no case and even if they had won they were about to be unpleasantly surprised to learn i had no assets.<br><br>\r\n\r\ni have been the victim of medical malpractice a dozen times in my life.  negligence by the military medical system has given me:<br><br>\r\n<ol>\r\n	<li>a heart attack with attending heart damage\r\n	<li>liver disease\r\n	<li>put me into a semi-coma state for several days\r\n	<li>caused me to fall and break my face\r\n	<li>caused numerous miscarriages and other \"female problems\" for which i am about to have unwanted, but necessary surgery.\r\n</ol>\r\ni have a \"case\" in every one of these instances, complete with hard evidence, depositions, etc.<br><br>\r\ni have elected not to sue. my reasoning is that the time it would suck from my life, the necessity of sustaining the anger and feelings of injustice needed over a long period, and the indignities that would be suffered in pre-trial investigations, questioning by sharks working on contingency fees, etc. are just not worth any monetary gain.<br><br>\r\n<strong>BUT</strong><br><br>\r\nthere are times and circumstances when i would undertake lawsuits that lasted for years and never blink an eye.<br><br>\r\nif someone hurt my husband or one of my children because they were maliciously negligent, i would sue.<br><br>\r\nif someone was doing something that hurt innocent people and refused to stop, then i would try to find a way to help sue with other people.<br><br>\r\nyou don\'t have to sue for money.  you can sue for actions, you know.  or you can sue for so much money people faint when they count the zeros and then you can settle out of court for the thing you wanted them to do in the first place.<br><br>\r\nsuing people just because you think that they, or their insurance company, will pay you a bunch of money guarantees bad karma.<br><br>\r\nsuing people because they don\'t subscribe to your personal belief system or won\'t make special considerations for your belief system that their belief system doesn\'t accept, that will bring bad karma.<br><br>\r\nlying or cheating or harassing people in order to win a lawsuit will bring bad karma.<br><br>\r\nbut, if you think you are right about something, and someone else is really, really wrong, and their position is harming you or people you love and care for.... then i guess it\'s okay to sue, if you don\'t mind the crap you have to go through to do  it.<br>\r\n</font></p>'),(479,'kiks: funny you should mention cats who are kicked. my mother\'s cat was recently killed by blunt force trauma the vet thinks was caused by a kick. i wrote about the asthma i suffered as a result of this particular cat--i\'m quite sure i didn\'t want any harm to come to it, but not a month later his little limp body was found in a puddle in the back yard. it is a very painful subject for me. i want very much for the person who did this to know that they hurt this little thing so badly that he died and made my mother cry for three days. i\'m not sure how this works into your karmic scheme. Am i heavy and confessional today or what? '),(480,'<P>Things I did today : </P>\r\n\r\n<ol><li>Woke up around 3pm.\r\n<li>Traded mp3s. (:30)\r\n<li>Ate a bowl of oatmeal and some australian breakfast biscuits which I didn\'t like very much. Speculated with my roommate <a href=http://saturn5.com/ben>ben</a> about possible plans for a Colin Powell vice-presidency. Tried to simulate moving a boxspring downstairs with a mattress, alone. Started the dishwasher. (:45)\r\n<li>Submitted resumes for jobs I need but don\'t want. (:30)\r\n<li>Mixed techno records. (:40)\r\n<li>Picked up ex-roommate in the mission, brought him back to the house, moved a boxspring down a flight of curved stairs, smoked two hits off a bowl, played unreal tournament, gave ex-roommate a ride home as we discussed the mechanics of exchange and friendship. (2:20)\r\n<li>Cooked Pasta/Asparagus/Tempeh for dinner. Accidentally put too many red pepper flakes in because the top filter thing was missing. Ate dinner and watched <a href=http://saturn5.com/ben >ben</a> play Phantasy Star Online until the Simpsons came on. Watched the Simpsons episode \"Viva Ned Flanders\" and then went downstairs. (2:00)\r\n<li>Thought about <a href=http://www.cyantology.com>cyan</a> a lot. (:ongoing)\r\n<li>Took a bath and read <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0553562967/qid=983885013/sr=1-3/ref=sc_b_3/107-5764267-1077301\">Bellwether</a> by Connie Willis. Stretched while in the tub. (~240 pages, 3:15)\r\n<li>Quick yoga routine which I do from a book and therefore probably at least a little wrong but helps a lot anyway. (:50)\r\n<li>Writing this. (:20)\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p>Time unaccounted for : about ~3:00.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>-darwin</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n'),(481,'<P>Describe desire.</P>\r\n<P>\"How goes your obsession?\" she said.</P>\r\n<P>\"Which one?\" I answered.</P>\r\n<P>Dying is not original.</P>\r\n<P>Why do foreign films have so many silent moments?</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Undressing the pieces is more fun than the whole, </P>\r\n<P>among the tomato\'s sweat and the lettuce\'s freckles,</P>\r\n<P>I plead that you encrypt my wish. </P>\r\n\r\n<P>The saturnalia dream,</P>\r\n<P>Do I live inside of it</P>\r\n<P>soaked in Lo-Hum lines</P>\r\n<P>maybe a chasm for the capricious</P>\r\n<P>space of breathing in your</P>\r\n<P>delicate expectations of me.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Am I your subject</P>\r\n<P>or your object,</P>\r\n<P>I squint to tell the difference</P>\r\n<P>in the confinement of your</P>\r\n<P>mad hope or hate.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>This anticipation</P>\r\n<P>is a place for supreme delight.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>In the end I am not confined</P>\r\n<P>To the confinement of your angles</P>\r\n<P>And the stark solipsist exclamation point</P>\r\n<P>That I am.</P>\r\n\r\n'),(482,'<p>\r\nhi im wayne. im writing this chapter for a novel. and its about having a bad time at benihana. like the characters go there and get drunk and eat the crappy expensive food. i\'ve had this experience there twice. i remember the pictures of celebs. the freaky salad and this creamy sauce they put on everything\r\n</P>\r\n<p>\r\nim wondering if you have had an experience in benihana and maybe have any details that might jog my memory, so i don\'t have to go back for \"research.\" you can email. or.\r\n</P>\r\n<p>\r\nthank you kindly.\r\n</P>\r\n '),(483,'<p>\r\nhi im wayne. im writing this chapter for a novel. and its about having a bad time at benihana. like the characters go there and get drunk and eat the crappy expensive food. i\'ve had this experience there twice. i remember the pictures of celebs. the freaky salad and this creamy sauce they put on everything\r\n</P>\r\n<p>\r\nim wondering if you have had an experience in benihana and maybe have any details that might jog my memory, so i don\'t have to go back for \"research.\" you can email. or.\r\n</P>\r\n<p>\r\nthank you kindly.\r\n</P>\r\n '),(484,'<P>i take acrobatics with this <a href=\"http://www.sane-vigilante.com\">girl.</a></P>'),(485,'<P>\r\ni have been feeling lately that i do not contribute to this community.  the reason is simple, i have been feeling too strongly for telling the world.  you know how that is.\r\n</P><P>\r\nthat aside, i recognised a pattern a few minutes ago when i was standing in the kitchen waiting for the water to boil and feeling like a refugee from myself.\r\n</P><P>\r\ni am never together.  i travel in two parts.  one part is harmonious and focused, working towards a goal.  the other part is meandering and not knowing what is going on.\r\n</P><P>\r\nthe harmonious and focused part of me follows through with speed.  it is love.  it is beautiful.  it is amazing to be around.\r\n</P><P>\r\nthe meandering and lost part of me stumbles though whichever side of life it is occupying at the time.  it is hate.  it is sadness.\r\n</P><P>\r\nthese two halves exchange.  one will be at work.  one will be at home.  sometimes the same one is at work and at home and the cycle takes days or weeks or months to turn over.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nother times it is a daily exchange.  i am one way at home and a different way at work.  i am happy, productive.  i follow through.  i make others happy.  then i move into the other part of the day.  i frustrate people.  i am rude.  i am mean, and worst of all, i am hateful.  i see peoples weaknesses and they come out.\r\n</P><P>\r\nsometimes this is fine, for my bad side i become the recluse.  i disappear.\r\n</P><P>\r\nother times i have people close to me at home.  i have a girlfriend.  i have a bestfriend.  i have a roomate.  that is when i hurt myself and others.\r\n</P><P>\r\nand i hate it.  i hate myself.  i hate what i say.  i have no excuse other than time and prophecy.  and those are no excuse to the people i love.  they only help me try to outrun myself.\r\n</P>\r\n<P>\r\nthis is why people turn to religion.  they cannot trust themselves with themselves.  some people anyway.  people like i am almost.\r\n</P>'),(486,'<P>Today I worked up an appetite. You hear that phrase a lot but mostly it just means that people have been doing something else and therefore haven\'t been eating.</P>\r\n<P>I had my second <a href=http://www.omulu.org>capoeira</a> class in two days today, on account of scheduling problems with the regular tuesday/thursday classes. This means that I trained incredibly strenously two days in a row. Usually there\'s a day in between classes where I don\'t do anything with my muscles but feel them ache.</P>\r\n<P>It\'s hard for me to understand how I could stand not working out. There was a period of two or three years there where I took part in very little physical activity and smoked a lot of cigarettes. I guess that I thought it was going to work out for me or maybe I just didn\'t understand that I wasn\'t going to be little-kid-healthy anymore. When I was a little kid I used to ride my bike everywhere, and I skiied all winter and I played baseball.</P>\r\n<P>Anyway, when I got back home from capoeira I was incredibly thirsty and incredibly hungry. I had worked up an appetite. Using tired muscles for 2 hours straight and my blood sugar (or whatever) was probably really low. I made my patented lazy vegetarian exerciser meal, which is a can of corn, a can of beans and a can of soup together in a pot. MMM. </P>\r\n<P>The point I\'m trying to make is that building strength both fills and creates needs. Learning how to do things makes them easier, but also creates a type of pleasant pressure to see what other things you can learn. A person can maintain a given state approximately forever, but when viewed relatively it is surely decay.</P>\r\n<P>In <b>\"The Left Hand of Darkness\"</b> there are these heads of this weird interplanetary federation-body-type-tyhing and they are called \"Stabiles.\" A friend of mine released a record by Stewart S. Walker on his <a href=http://tekrecs.com>record label</a> called \"Stabiles.\" I searched for information on the internet about it and found only references to the record and a type of sculpture which apparently contrasts with a \"Mobile\", like you used to make in grade school. This is the sort of realization, (much like the sample of \"Aliens\" where one of the guys says \"those lights\" in DJ SS\'s \"Lighter\") that I tell people about and they have no idea what I\'m talking about. Or why I care.</P>\r\n<p>There\'s a million things to be do/know, why does it seem like most people I know aren\'t really doing or knowing any of them? How long can people keep feeding without doing anything that makes them hungry again?</P>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin'),(487,'<P>     Yoga floats thoughts into my mind from a strange peaceful plane.  Deadpan Subconscious one-liners.  Answers.  Always very simple.  I call them, *yoga moments.* ...\r\n</P><P>\r\n\r\n    Setting: a brain full of {Why haven\'t you put up a good web-site by now?  Why haven\'t you done your taxes?  What are you going to do in June when your current job ends?  Who\'s going to hire you?  Why don\'t you have another album yet?  Why haven\'t you why didn\'t you why shouldn\'t can\'t haven\'t ???!!!}\r\n</P><P>\r\n      Then came Shivasana, Badekinasana, Ardechandrasana, and a voice like a lotus laser beam... instantaneous transmission... blue chakra bandwidth... </P>\r\n<BLOCKQUOTE>\r\n<P>\r\n*Driving yourself into sleeplessness and stress and unhappiness is not productive, it\'s destructive.  It backfires.\r\n</P><P>\r\nThere is nothing you NEED to do.<BR>\r\n  Everything that must be done, gets done.\r\n</P><P>\r\n  Be in life like a yoga pose.  Not lazy, not aggressive, don\'t injure yourself.  Focus.  It\'s all about focus and RELAXED effort.  You put in the effort and throw away the outcome, having faith that the best outcome arises from good intentions, pure focus, and effort, not self-terrorizing.*\r\n</P>\r\n</BLOCKQUOTE>\r\n<P>\r\nPhew!  \"But how can I be RELAXED and working hard at the same time?\"...  asks my lost-in-fog consciousness.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nMy subconscious laughs omnisciently at me, *Trust yourself a little.*\r\n\r\n</P>\r\n\r\n\r\n'),(488,'i am depressed.<br><br>\r\nnot your every day down in the dumps depressed, but the kind where, if you worked as a cashier at walmart, you\'d take a look at the long line of people and then turn off your light and pull your drawer and turn in your locker keys and name tag.<br><br>\r\n\r\ni want to go home. but i don\'t know where that is anymore.<br><br>\r\n'),(489,'<P>i was driving home from work and feeling my brain all heavy in the front.  it feels like it weighs more than the rest of my brain.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>after reading that the frontal lobe controls emothions and personality, i decided that my diagnosis of a heavy frontal lobe must be correct.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>maybe my bone plate is too big.  perhaps i am just a bone head like my uncle would say.</P>\r\n<a href=\"http://www.neuroskills.com/index.html?main=tbi/bfrontal.shtml\"><img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/489_1.jpg\'></a>'),(490,'<P>A  while ago, someone wrote here on Swinney about how they went to see \"Dude, where\'s my car?\" voluntarily at the movies.  Well, it\'s just arrived here in this country, and I\'d been out Dancing in the Street with my ex flatmate, and then another ex flatmate and long term best friend wanted to go to the movies and see something really stupid, so what did we see?  Yep, that\'s right.  And it was really really really funny.  Perhaps I drink too much.  </P>\r\n\r\n<P>\r\n\r\nAnd this is where I get told  that I\'m sick and obsessed, or just wrong, but to everyone else who\'s seen it - didn\'t that good alien in the brown leather look kind of like Austin?  I mean, like if you\'d actually only seen a picture or two of him, and you were drunk, and you were sitting in a movie theatre thinking about past swinney entries anyways? </P>\r\n\r\n<P>  \r\n\r\nGosh I make myself sound tragic.  But someone\'s gotta do it.  \r\n\r\n</P>'),(491,'<P>A  while ago, someone wrote here on Swinney about how they went to see \"Dude, where\'s my car?\" voluntarily at the movies.  Well, it\'s just arrived here in this country, and I\'d been out Dancing in the Street with my ex flatmate, and then another ex flatmate and long term best friend wanted to go to the movies and see something really stupid, so what did we see?  Yep, that\'s right.  And it was really really really funny.  Perhaps I drink too much.  </P>\r\n\r\n<P>\r\n\r\nAnd this is where I get told  that I\'m sick and obsessed, or just wrong, but to everyone else who\'s seen it - didn\'t that good alien in the brown leather look kind of like Austin?  I mean, like if you\'d actually only seen a picture or two of him, and you were drunk, and you were sitting in a movie theatre thinking about past swinney entries anyways? </P>\r\n\r\n<P>  \r\n\r\nGosh I make myself sound tragic.  But someone\'s gotta do it.  \r\n\r\n</P>'),(492,'most americans appear to have a high respect for people\'s salaries, thus putting a teacher on a low rung of the social scale - but a functionally illiterate sports star or actor is placed on a pedestal.<br><br>\r\n\r\ni find it pretty fucking amazing that those who have talents that are showcased in public arenas such as stadiums and theaters are given this sort of positive attention.<br><br>\r\n\r\ni can\'t help but think of the roman coliseum when considering it.<br><br>\r\n\r\nand we all know what happened to the romans...<br><br>\r\n\r\nperhaps we need to seriously rethink the attention and accolades we give to the people who hold our children\'s minds in the palm of their hands for six hours a day.<br><br>\r\n\r\nperhaps we ought to pay them more money since that is what we appear to value as a worth-o-meter, and perhaps we need to get serious about getting rid of the ones who suck.<br><br>\r\n\r\nmany schools spend a great deal of their budgets on sports programs that are not geared to the actual physical education and health of children, and ignore the art,literature, history, and music programs because there\'s not much glory in turning out a kid who can recite shakespeare or read music, or know the location of the continents when handed a map, and there is a lot of glory in putting some ten year old in a leotard to perform gymnastics or a fifteen year old into shoulder pads to pound hell out of other fifteen year olds in a stadium.<br><br>\r\n\r\nwhen i was a kid we had to memorize great poetry and recite it in class.  we had to know where countries were located and something about the geography,politics, population, and customs of each one.<br><br>\r\n\r\nnowadays nobody cares if a kid takes world history and geography, but they care a lot if the kid takes black history. which is silly, because if u.s. and world history and geography are properly taught, they cover black history when they cover the rest.<br><br>\r\n\r\nand while i am complaining, it seems like it would be a good thing if there were some rules about teaching factual information instead of pop-culture media representations of history.<br><br>\r\n\r\nan inordinate amount of space in american history books deals with events that have been immortalized on film or blasted into our living rooms by news media, giving short shrift to all the rest.<br><br>\r\n\r\nit is only by understanding the whole of our history that we can teach our children to avoid making the same mistakes again in the future.<br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\n'),(493,'<P>i wish i could be somewhere else sometimes...</P>\r\n\r\n<P>Rain dew and tiger foot. A table of calculations from long ago day cycles. When they wore white drapes. A smooth pressed stone wall U could lose yourself to.  Lose all thoughts of this and that.  A blackened porcelain cylinder. An insect leg making its rounds. And bending with tiny insect leg hairs. A place.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i wish i could be somewhere.</P>\r\n\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/493_1.jpg\'>'),(494,'</p>INCLOSED. ONE (1) soul.</p>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/494_1.gif\'>\r\n<P>Beaten up fuct strangled. killed. smooth away lifes problems and become someone else. OH HHAHAHAHA very funny dear. mother FUCKERS try and break my crown. door shuts. NO GHOSTS NO SKELETONS. SLICE SLICE. so fuck it all cos i don\'t care. you\'re all whores and i\'m a fag and i\'ve got no mother and i\'ve got no dad. goodbye.</P>\r\n\r\n'),(495,'<P>it was uneventful.  \"austin, can i speak with you...  we are going to let you go.  things just aren\'t working out.\"</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i was liking my job too.  oh well.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>some investors were in today.  it was pretty transpart.  neospaz is getting some money and the marketing department didn\'t want me to have any because we didn\'t get along.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i knew it would happen.  so the question now becomes, what do i do?  where do i go?  i was planning on leaving LA june 1 for san francisco.  maybe i will just leave earlier.  it is not inconvenient.  i had planned in advance for a reason though.  kstar was going to come and she couldn\'t leave until june.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>well, i need a job.  that is about all i have to say.</P>\r\n'),(496,'there is a doll company that makes baby dolls that look and feel like real babies.<br><br>\r\n\r\nit is called the <a href=\"http://www.leemiddleton.com\">lee middleton</a> doll company.<br><br>\r\n\r\nin several places across the country they have these things called \"doll adoption centers.\"<br><br>\r\n\r\nthey are set up to look like nurseries in hospitals and the people who work there dress up as nurses.<br><br>\r\n\r\ndoll collectors go into these stores and adopt baby dolls.<br><br>\r\n\r\nthey pay large money for these dolls, which also have a very nice profit margin and sell in the neighborhood of $200 or so for most of them, but they also carry a line of dolls for kids to play with that are only $50 or so.<br><br><img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/496_1.jpg\' alt=\"scary dolls\"><br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\nit is a well known fact that in time of recession people spend more money on collectibles and crafts than they do in times of prosperity.<br><br>\r\n\r\nit wouldn\'t cost a lot to build out and stock one of these adoption centers, and the good thing is that there aren\'t any within several hundred miles of sf.  maybe 50k for the entire shebang - meaning permits to build out of storefront to inventory and nursey uniforms.<br><br>\r\n\r\nit would be a hoot, and very popular with the tourist trade.<br><br>\r\n\r\nit would be fun to play nursey/doctor in costume.<br><br>\r\n\r\nyou could use the profits to fund your vegan restaurant and yarn store whcih would take longer to set up.<br><br>\r\n\r\nif you open a vegan restaurant, you should have some food for non-vegans. you should ask gaby and mo\'s in austin if they will show you how they make their turkey sandwiches which i dream about sometimes.<br><br>\r\n\r\n'),(497,'<P>I want to go to Osento today. I live in Marin now but I miss sparkling sunny days in the Mission, when I would wake up alone and single in Noe Valley....so I am going back there today to sit naked in the sun and soak and try to destress.</P>\r\n<p>\r\nI feel bad sometimes for missing that time in my life. Guilt. It\'s sad. I miss the city more than I thought I would.\r\n</p>\r\n<P>Hi.</P>'),(498,'<P>  So, Austin got fired.  Hmm, I got fired myself back at the beginning of January, so I have had some time to think over what it means to be fired, and I decided that it is a spiritual event in one\'s life.</P>\r\n<P>Yes, that\'s right!  The Universe is doing you a favour by getting you fired.   The Universe said, \"Austin, you really want to move to SF, and you really want a new job.  Since you\'re not going to do it yourself, I\'m going to help you.  You may lose money and experience some stress, but getting fired will rocket you out of a situation where you were stagnant, unappreciated, and unfulfilled.  You got what you came for, now keep going.</P>\r\n<P>In the 2 weeks before you got fired, you were lost, confused about what you wanted, frustrated and bored by things.  All of a sudden, you\'ve got a twinkle in your eye again, and you look excited.    Back to the dangerous landscape of life!  Who needs Survivor?\r\n</P>'),(499,'<P>Y\'know, i\'m starting to think there\'s not much wrong with evangelizing. Most days, i feel like i\'m about two steps away from getting a placard and a megaphone and hittin the corner.</P>\r\n<P>They always said: Don\'t talk about your progress down the Path.  Don\'t BRAG about it.  And the implication always felt like: This stuff\'s just for us Cool Cats. Kind of like unconscious spiritual elitism. But more and more, i\'m feeling that openness about everything is kinda holy. so:</P>\r\n<P>It started about a month ago. In addition to the yoga and dietary choices, i gave up the pot and booze, the ol\' COPuLATION and the beating off.  And then discovered i probably had parasites, so got some herbs for they ass.  And OH, MAN.  i never knew it could be like this.</P>\r\n '),(500,'<P>Like this: fasting yesterday, a little loopy, went to the library, looked for a Carlos Castaneda book, something called \"Earth Medicine\" on the same shelf caught my eye. Perused the back - evidently a syncretization of astrology and Native American shamanism. (Maybe they were never divergent?) Opened it to a random page. And the page read, \"Falcon: 21 March - 19 April.\" My birthday\'s April 14th. And every word was true.</P>\r\n<P>It said I was an extrovert. Prone to starting new things. \"Like movements,\" my brain thought to itself . \"Or revolutions,\" my ego chimed in.  \"Yeah,\" Brain went, \"Like one T. Jefferson, another Falcon of note.\"</P><P>But my heart wants to start a religion. i just feel all this compassion for everything lately, where before there was just contempt or jealousy. i mean, i have an urge to transmit this to other people. What if the world were set free?</P><P> Maybe this is just an attachment thing, something else to let go of.</P><P>Or maybe i\'m losing my fucking mind. Who\'s to say?</P> '),(501,'<PRE>\r\n I can\'t believe Austin is leaving\r\n in just a few days,\r\n and I have no idea\r\n when he\'s coming back \r\n and how things are working out\r\n And I am stuck here\r\n for 3 months.\r\n\r\n :-(\r\n\r\n</PRE>'),(502,'<P>this phone of mine, it is very old.  i would say it is nearly obselete.  but we will see.  it is large, black, plastic.  it is a motorola.  it is called a \"Personal Communication Device\".  could be used for self defence.  looks like a prop.  a big plastic.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>it used to be adam\'s mom\'s phone.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i will use it in the process of securing employment and causing panic on the BART.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i am packed. i am packin.  i have a dangerous phone.  i have a will.  i will rock.  i will not collect fungi.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>goodbye and or see you soon</P>\r\n\r\n'),(503,'The daily I-Ching:<BR>\r\n<BLOCKQUOTE><TT>\r\nThis hexagram represents acting so as to proceed on the Path, warily practicing introspection; it follows on the previous hexagram <I>revolution</I>. <I>Revolution</I> involves gaining joy through illumination, refining metal by fire, removing old impurities. Removing old impurities does not mean forgetting things, forgetting the body, extinguishing the mind, and stopping thoughts; it is necesary to remove impurities in the midst of action in order to accomplish the task. <B>This is because the Tao is alive, in movement; it is neither material nor void. <i>We use wordly realities to practice the reality of the Tao, and use human affairs to cultivate celestial virtues;</I></B> both striving and nonstriving, comprehending essence and comprehending life, the endless work all must be done in the midst of activity. Thereofore there is a path of development in <I>thunder</I>.<BR>\r\n</TT></BLOCKQUOTE><BR><BR>\r\n\r\nChange can be good. In fact even though I sometimes dread it, it\'s our only hope, right?<BR>\r\nThe element of surprise, the unexpected, the nature of chaos and sudden action.<BR>\r\n'),(504,'<p>i have a spare bedroom now.  it may or may not empty tomorrow.</p>  \r\n\r\n<p>i have only lost my temper once with austin, and it inspired him to write sad things on this site about how he was mad at himself for being mean.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>now it\'s my turn. i was very mean to someone i love today. then i had to lie down and take a nap.  i lashed out because he hurt me. the result: feeling devastated that i could be so reactive and vicious to someone i miss. this particular interpersonal technique never seems to work out well for me.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>i\'m not worried about austin leaving. or shall i say i\'m not yet a believer.</p>'),(505,'<P>I have been doing a lot of catching up with the Swinstar, since I have been offline and in Florida for 17 days. I am writing in response to Darwin\'s post about Stabiles, and what I know about them.</P>\r\n<P>Alexander Calder (1898-1976), an American sculptor, used abstract organic forms and a sound knowledge of engineering techniques to reinvent sculpture so that it moved and \"lived\". Both the artist\'s father and grandfather were sculptors, but Alexander studied to be a mechanical engineer. Somewhere along the way, he followed in his family\'s footsteps and began creating sculpture.</P>\r\n<P>He had a lifelong obsession with motion and dynamics. As a young artist in Paris in the 1920\'s (think Dadaism), Calder invented a <a href=\"http://www.calder.org/SETS_SUB/work/work_98_30_html/work_frame_A00264.html\">circus</a> full of miniature performers that were activated by the artist into realistic analogues of the motion of their counterparts in life. Certainly he delighted in amusements in Paris similar to the \r\n<a href=\"http://www.sanfranciscomemories.com/musee/mechanique.html\">Musee Mechanique</a> at the Cliff House here in SF.</P>\r\n<P>Calder was inspired after a visit to Mondrian\'s studio in the early 1930\'s to take the warm rectangular shapes from the painter\'s works and set them in motion. Because of his whimsical, hand-cranked moving scupltures, Calder\'s works became popular with masters such as Marcel Duchamp, who named them \"<a href=\"http://www.calder.org/SETS/work/work.html\">Mobiles</a>\".</P>\r\n<P>As a result, Calder later made <a href=\"http://www.calder.org/SETS_SUB/work/work_53_76_html/work_frame_A00367.html\">static sculptures</a>, resulting in the label \"Stablies\". Any sculpture that doesn\'t move could be considered a \"stabile\", but I think it mostly refers to the specific works of Alexander Calder.</P>\r\n<P>I\'m inspired this week to try making a mobile. You guys should do it too! Maybe we can take photos and compare.</P>\r\n'),(506,NULL),(507,'<p>Hi there. I just wanted to share the incredibly experience I had at The\r\nFuture Primitive Soundsession party last night. It was, without a doubt,\r\none of the best parties I have _ever_ been lucky enough to attend and it\r\nwill immediately come to mind whenever I question why I love hiphop music.</p>\r\n\r\n<P><a href=http://www.cyantology.com>Cyan</a> and I arrived at the space (a 200-300 capacity loft in SOMA) around\r\n10:30pm. The party hadn\'t even started yet, so we chilled and then went in\r\nwhen the music started. The people throwing the party had a a full bar,\r\na nice little soundsystem (which had plenty of thump) and a solid setup\r\nall around. People started filtering in, and the DJ played the kind of\r\ndancehall that\'s a guy toasting over hiphop classic beays. Like, you know,\r\n\"bwatty bwoy blah blah\" over \"the bridge is over\" by BDP. I\'m ok with this\r\nkind of music for an hour or so, but he played for 3 or 4 hours and it was\r\na bit much.</p>\r\n<p>In any case, people kept coming in, drinking, dancing, having a good time.\r\nWide variety of people in the crowd.. hiphop kids, the odd raver, a\r\nsprinkling of nerds, provacatively dancing lesbians. The DJ kept saying\r\nZ-Trip was on his way, but around 2:20 we started getting antsy. It was\r\nhot as hell and the place was _packed_. We were considering leaving but I\r\ntold Cyan that I couldn\'t come to this party and spend all this time\r\nwaiting to see Z-trip and go home empty handed. Right about then, Z-trip\r\nwalked in with his record crates.</p>\r\n<p>Z-trip is a no-nonsense guy. He came in, checked out the equipment,\r\nreplaced the parts of it he didn\'t like (carts, headphones), set up his\r\nrecord crates in a row behind him and got down to business. He played a\r\nfew records and this big guy in the crowd started yelling \"I ain\'t\r\nimpressed! I ain\'t impressed! You might be a big deal in Arizona but I run\r\nthings in the Bay Area!\" He kept going on and on like this for a few\r\nminutes and kept saying \"I have my records, I\'ll go get them and let\'s\r\ngo!\" Finally, Z-trip motioned to him \"ok\" and he left to go get his\r\nrecords.</p>\r\n<p>The guy came back up with his posse and his record crates. He stepped up\r\nand he started doing scratch routines. He and Z-trip traded off every 4\r\nrecords or so. I should probably mention that Cyan and I were standing\r\nabout 2 feet to the back and side of the turntables, so this whole battle\r\nwas right there in front of us. The challenger had decent skills, but you\r\ncould tell that Z-trip was just toying with him. He scratched in little\r\ndiss-samples and pulled out some whitelabels with the sample \"I bet you\r\ndon\'t have this in your crate!\" =)..</p>\r\n<p>Every time the challenger was done with a routine, Z-trip brought it up\r\nanother notch. He mixed Christina Aguilera over \"sweet emotion\" by\r\nAerosmith.. he mixed in Ray Charles.. he scratched, cut, sliced, diced,\r\nblended and pureed. The crowd got progressively more and more hyped as the\r\nenergy built. Eventually the challenger conceded and was extremely chill\r\nabout it. He explained that his challenge was intended to push Z-trip to\r\n\"show us something\" and it certainly worked! This kind of battle is true\r\nhip-hop, and I think true humanity at its finest. Competition bringing out\r\nthe best in people..</P>\r\n<p>So, after this, the crowd totally hyped, Z-trip just laid down cut after\r\ncut of hiphopfunksoulgrooverockbluesjazzreggaepopnewage goodness. Backing\r\nup ultimate kaos\' \"casonova\" with hiphop drums, digable planets, de la\r\nsoul, transformer scratching..  unifying all sorts of bumpin\' music with\r\ntwo turntables and a mixer.</p>\r\n<p>The cops finally shut it down at around 4:20. I will never forget the\r\nenergy, all the smiling faces, all the dancing people and the _music_.\r\nThat party is what I have been looking for and have so seldom found since\r\nI moved to SF. Future Primitive Soundsystem and Bombshelter DJs impressed\r\nthe hell out of me, and, more importantly, made me smile like a\r\nmotherfucker. Inspired me. Gave me hope for humanity. Turned the party\r\nout.</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n'),(508,'<p>Hi there. I just wanted to share the incredible experience I had at The\r\nFuture Primitive Soundsession party last night. It was, without a doubt,\r\none of the best parties I have _ever_ been lucky enough to attend and it\r\nwill immediately come to mind whenever I question why I love hiphop music.</p>\r\n\r\n<P><a href=http://www.cyantology.com>Cyan</a> and I arrived at the space (a 200-300 capacity loft in SOMA) around\r\n10:30pm. The party hadn\'t even started yet, so we chilled and then went in\r\nwhen the music started. The people throwing the party had a a full bar,\r\na nice little soundsystem (which had plenty of thump) and a solid setup\r\nall around. People started filtering in, and the DJ played the kind of\r\ndancehall that\'s a guy toasting over hiphop classic beays. Like, you know,\r\n\"bwatty bwoy blah blah\" over \"the bridge is over\" by BDP. I\'m ok with this\r\nkind of music for an hour or so, but he played for 3 or 4 hours and it was\r\na bit much.</p>\r\n<p>In any case, people kept coming in, drinking, dancing, having a good time.\r\nWide variety of people in the crowd.. hiphop kids, the odd raver, a\r\nsprinkling of nerds, provacatively dancing lesbians. The DJ kept saying\r\nZ-Trip was on his way, but around 2:20 we started getting antsy. It was\r\nhot as hell and the place was _packed_. We were considering leaving but I\r\ntold Cyan that I couldn\'t come to this party and spend all this time\r\nwaiting to see Z-trip and go home empty handed. Right about then, Z-trip\r\nwalked in with his record crates.</p>\r\n<p>Z-trip is a no-nonsense guy. He came in, checked out the equipment,\r\nreplaced the parts of it he didn\'t like (carts, headphones), set up his\r\nrecord crates in a row behind him and got down to business. He played a\r\nfew records and this big guy in the crowd started yelling \"I ain\'t\r\nimpressed! I ain\'t impressed! You might be a big deal in Arizona but I run\r\nthings in the Bay Area!\" He kept going on and on like this for a few\r\nminutes and kept saying \"I have my records, I\'ll go get them and let\'s\r\ngo!\" Finally, Z-trip motioned to him \"ok\" and he left to go get his\r\nrecords.</p>\r\n<p>The guy came back up with his posse and his record crates. He stepped up\r\nand he started doing scratch routines. He and Z-trip traded off every 4\r\nrecords or so. I should probably mention that Cyan and I were standing\r\nabout 2 feet to the back and side of the turntables, so this whole battle\r\nwas right there in front of us. The challenger had decent skills, but you\r\ncould tell that Z-trip was just toying with him. He scratched in little\r\ndiss-samples and pulled out some whitelabels with the sample \"I bet you\r\ndon\'t have this in your crate!\" =)..</p>\r\n<p>Every time the challenger was done with a routine, Z-trip brought it up\r\nanother notch. He mixed Christina Aguilera over \"sweet emotion\" by\r\nAerosmith.. he mixed in Ray Charles.. he scratched, cut, sliced, diced,\r\nblended and pureed. The crowd got progressively more and more hyped as the\r\nenergy built. Eventually the challenger conceded and was extremely chill\r\nabout it. He explained that his challenge was intended to push Z-trip to\r\n\"show us something\" and it certainly worked! This kind of battle is true\r\nhip-hop, and I think true humanity at its finest. Competition bringing out\r\nthe best in people..</P>\r\n<p>So, after this, the crowd totally hyped, Z-trip just laid down cut after\r\ncut of hiphopfunksoulgrooverockbluesjazzreggaepopnewage goodness. Backing\r\nup ultimate kaos\' \"casonova\" with hiphop drums, digable planets, de la\r\nsoul, transformer scratching..  unifying all sorts of bumpin\' music with\r\ntwo turntables and a mixer.</p>\r\n<p>The cops finally shut it down at around 4:20. I will never forget the\r\nenergy, all the smiling faces, all the dancing people and the _music_.\r\nThat party is what I have been looking for and have so seldom found since\r\nI moved to SF. Future Primitive Soundsystem and Bombshelter DJs impressed\r\nthe hell out of me, and, more importantly, made me smile like a\r\nmotherfucker. Inspired me. Gave me hope for humanity. Turned the party\r\nout.</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n'),(509,'<p>dear austin,\r\n</p><p>\r\nhave a safe drive to SF.   i have a stomach ache from being sad, and one from all the ghiradelli chocolate you gave me right before you drove off--an extra portion for farewell\'s sake.\r\n</p><p>\r\ni only had two days to prepare for this, hence the no-austin angst. i was so excited for you i forgot how much this was going to suck for me.  \r\n</p><p>\r\nthere will always be a place in alexandria street garage for your boxes--that is akin to permanent resident status, a great honor.\r\n</p><p>\r\nlove, kiki\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n'),(510,'<p>When does it end?<br>\r\n  Never<br>\r\nHe lives this life<br>\r\n  He has his moments<br>\r\n  Sometimes it\'s so close<br>\r\n  So close<br>\r\nWhen does it end?<br>\r\n  Never</p>\r\n\r\n<p>An eternity of breaking<br>\r\nDown walls<br>\r\nBreaking sound barriers<br>\r\n  Of silence<br>\r\n  To find the one thing<br>\r\n  The something<br>\r\n  Worth saying</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I feel ridiculous<br>\r\n There\'s nothing else to say<br>\r\nI am in love with you<br>\r\n There\'s nothing else to say</p>\r\n'),(511,'here i go, off to the hospital.<br><br>\r\n\r\nelly wants to know what they will do with the bits they remove.<br><br>\r\n\r\ni told her that once they inspect them thoroughly, they will then do the obvious:<br><br>\r\n\r\nerect a golden dais and worship the holy auntie parts.<br><br>\r\n\r\nactually, i think they incinerate them...<br><br>\r\n\r\ni am not liking this, but in 7 minutes i must go get in the car and be driven to a place i don\'t want to go where they will do things to me i would rather not have done.<br><br>\r\n\r\n'),(512,'<table width=\"50%\" bgcolor=\"#990000\">\r\n<tr>\r\n<td align=\"top\">\r\n<font color=\"#cccccc\">\r\n<tt><pre>\r\nmy uterus\r\n carries the torch\r\nwhile my mother\'s rotting womb\r\nis in a plastic bag somewhere,\r\n orphaned \r\n(unlike me; child of a mother)\r\n\r\n   BIOHAZARD: medical waste\r\n\r\nmeanwhile, my loins are soggy\r\n not quite bursting forth with their monthly \r\nflood, but\r\n i feel my female organ, up there\r\n full of juice.\r\n\r\nripe.\r\n a crushed mango\r\n a soft peach\r\n  soon it will begin to drip and stink\r\n guts.\r\n \r\nit feels not unlike a plastic bag, \r\n heavy with viscous red ooze.\r\n\r\n but mine is alive.\r\n\r\n</pre>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</table> '),(513,'<table cellpadding=\"5\" cellspacing=\"2\" bgcolor=\"#990000\">\r\n<tr>\r\n<td align=\"top\" bgcolor=\"ff9933\">\r\n\r\n<pre>\r\n\r\nmy uterus\r\n carries the torch\r\nwhile my mother\'s rotting womb\r\nlies in a plastic bag somewhere,\r\n orphaned \r\n(unlike me; child of a mother)\r\n\r\n   BIOHAZARD: medical waste\r\n\r\nmeanwhile, my loins are soggy\r\n almost ready to burst forth with their monthly \r\nflood, but\r\n i feel my female organ, up there\r\n full of juice.\r\n\r\nripe.\r\n a crushed mango\r\n a soft peach\r\n  soon it will begin to drip and stink;\r\n guts.\r\n \r\nit feels not unlike a plastic bag \r\n heavy with viscous red ooze.\r\n\r\n\r\n</pre>\r\n<center>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/513_1.jpg\' height=\"240\" width=\"320\" alt=\"womb painting\" border=\"1\">\r\n</center>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</table> '),(514,'<P>yoko and me, we sit here.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>we don\'t go out much because we don\'t have money.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>yoko and me, we have the same friends.  yoko actually knows more people than i do.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>yoko and me, we sleep together.  i fall asleep and yoko sleeps on my legs.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>this morning i tripped on yoko in the hallway.  she didn\'t understand this and would not talk to me for an hour.  she went underneath peter\'s bed.  yoko was angry.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>yoko wants to surf the internet often.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>yoko and me drink coffee together.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>yoko and me do what we like.  we don\'t always hang out.  sometimes yoko just goes and sits in the hall way.</P>\r\n\r\n<P><B>yoko and me</b></P>'),(515,'<P>Austin met a celebrity this morning, and gave her some neopets stickers.</P>\r\n\r\n<CENTER><img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/515_1.gif\'></CENTER>'),(516,'<p>i must have some virgo in my chart...</p>\r\n<p>i love routine. i am reassured by the things that stay constant in my life. the drive to work. the daily morning trip to the breakroom for coffee and cereal. the fact that every day when i come home from work, i check the mail first, and if there\'s a postcard, i read it as i walk up the stairs to my apartment. yea, routine!</p>\r\n<p>i have noticed that my cat craves routine, also.<BR>\r\nevery night when i go to sleep, i\'ll shut my bedroom door almost all the way and then crawl in bed. within a few minutes, she nudges the door open and leaps into bed and meows, once. i snap my fingers and she comes and finds my hands and i pet her until i\'m too tired to do so anymore. then she circles my body a few times, finds the space in between my legs, and settles down.</p>\r\n<p>in the morning, the alarm goes off, i turn it off, and she begs for petting, meows for food. i stumble out of bed to brush my teeth, she circles her bowl until i feed her, which is always right after i connect to the internet and right before i take a shower.</p>\r\n<p>we\'re a good match.</p>'),(517,'<h1>Five Things I am Good At</h1>\r\n<p>\r\n<ol><li>DJing.\r\n<li>Cooking nutritious vegetarian food.\r\n<li>Riding my bicycle.\r\n<li>Writing.\r\n<li>Caring about people.\r\n</ol>\r\n<p>\r\nWhat are <b><u>you</u></b> good at?</p>\r\n<p>\r\nIn other news, just finished \"<a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0553562738/o/qid=984743049/sr=8-1/ref=aps_sr_b_1_1/102-0853127-9496139\">Doomsday Book</a> (1993, 578 pages) by <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/search-handle-url/index=books&field-author=Willis%2C%20Connie/102-0853127-9496139\">Connie Willis</a> and I reccomend it to all readers. Connie Willis sure does know how to write. Certainly better than than <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/search-handle-url/index=books&field-author=Stephenson%2C%20Neal/102-0853127-9496139\">Mr. Excessively Verbose</a> </p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n\r\n\r\n'),(518,'i came home from the hospital about an hour ago, mark has gone to the pharmacy to get medications, dashed (okay, it took ten minutes to go ten feet)in here to let everyone know i am fine as can be expected.<br><br>\r\n\r\ngory details when i am not watching the driveway for mark to catch me in front of machine.<br><br>\r\n\r\ni only managed to read ten pages of the trashy romance.  which is a good indication of my general condition.<br><br>\r\n\r\ni usually read three books a day....\r\n\r\n'),(519,'<P>ahh, what the heck..</P>'),(520,'<H1>Ooh SHIT!</H1>\r\n<P>so i\'m up in the a.m.<BR>\r\nyoko clawed the kicks<BR>\r\nbright and early<BR>\r\n7:16 am [le] if you hang your feet off the side, she will attack<br>\r\n</P>\r\n<P>today:</P>\r\n<UL>\r\n<LI>cell phone connect\r\n<LI>grocery store\r\n<LI>call k\r\n</UL>\r\n\r\n<P>i wondered around the castro area looking for things like cell phones and groceries.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i stopped at the hospital and called <B>k</B>.</P>\r\n<Blockquote>\r\n<P>\r\na: hi<BR>\r\nk: hi where are you<BR>\r\na: the hospital<br>\r\nk: OHMYGODWHATHAP...<br>\r\na: oh nothing, just needed to use the payphone<BR>\r\nk: shit, don\'t do that to me<br>\r\na: oops, hehe</P>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n<P>{interlude}yoko is the feline in charge over here~!{/interlude}</P>\r\nwalking down 18th, up that hill is <a href=\"http://steve.org\">s5\'s</a> house.  why not go visit him?</P>\r\n<blockquote>\r\n<P>\r\n5: lets go get some food?  you eat food still?<br>\r\na: *shrugs*<br>\r\n5: well, you can get some coffee\r\n</P>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n<P>look around, baby carrages.  i think they bring them in pregnant special for this neighborhood, noe valley.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>brbrbrbrb, hi, this is my cell phone.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>and we head back to the 5 house with girlscout cookies.  5 later is pukeness.  too many cookies by about 4.  i get tired and sleep to 5:30 then go to the park with steve.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>swings</P>\r\n[07:16pm] [adamajah] why am i still at work?<BR>\r\ngood questions abound<BR>\r\n<P>Bye</P>'),(521,'<p>tonight\'s notable moments, for your voyeuristic pleasure:</p>\r\n<p>[le] how come<br>\r\n[le] i keep doing shots of vodka<br>\r\n[le] but nothing happens</p>\r\n<p>[le] one time<br>\r\n[le] olivia said<br>\r\n[le] al a girl needs to be a lesbian is two rum and cokes</p>\r\n<p>[chaya] HELLO AUSTRALIANS<br>\r\n[chaya] i miss you<br>\r\n[zev] where are you?  you should be HERE</p>\r\n<p>[le] why afren\'y yhr vodka hsots working.</p>\r\n<p>[zev] iubfukke!</p>\r\n<p>[*le*] rememeber that time we kissed in your kitchen?<br>\r\n[*le*] we can SO do better than that</p>\r\n<p>[tripitaka] aw, PINK HAIR WIFEY GOODNESS</p>\r\n<p>[*zev*] everyone misses you!</p>\r\n<p>[tripitaka] dude i am so crazy-eyed ravaging random girls pixies fucked up dunk<br>\r\n[tripitaka] DEBASER!</p>\r\n<p>[tripitaka] there is tits<br>\r\n[zev] HI TITS</p>\r\n<p> </p>\r\n<p>hi.  i like things; stuff is neat.  also i would prefer it if the people were not on the other side of an ocean.</p>\r\n\r\n'),(522,'<p>hi there,<br><br>\r\n\r\ni like this place.  this is an interesting concept, i must say.  however i\'m a dumbass and i filled out the form wrong last time and my full name ended up on the authors list.  that\'s bad.  can we take that off?<br><br>\r\ni\'m reading this book right now called \"the quantity theory of insanity\"  its really great.  basically, it is a collection of short stories that depict insanity from several different angles.<br><br>\r\nthe first story reminds me of beetlejuice, because it is about where you go when you die.  apparently, you are become the \"living dead\" and you inhabit the part of your city that you hated the most in your living years.  so, if you don\'t like the tenderloin, that\'s where you\'ll end up.  the story actually takes place in england, which ads that english dry humor that i like so much.<br><br>\r\ni asked this question on my diary yesterday and i wanted to ask it here, because you can actually respond.<br><br>\r\nif you knew how many books you could read between now and the time that you died, would you choose your books more carefully?  how can you apply this to your life as a whole as well?<br><br>\r\n-cyan\r\n</p>'),(523,'<P>this entire predicament was foretold by my mom.  i told her i had a girlfriend and my mom said, \"oh damn.\"</P>\r\n\r\n<P>why mom?  what is wrong with that?</P>\r\n\r\n<P>mom: i thought maybe you would move back to texas.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i see.  now i am in sf and i have a girlfriend in LA.  and it means very much to me.  i don\'t like being the kind of person that leaves his girlfiends.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i think she wasn\'t important enough for me to stay.  that is what leaving means right?  or does it mean that i was very unhappy in los angeles and when i was fired from my job i considered it a release from a place that maybe i never should have settled in?</P>\r\n\r\n<P>that sounds about right.  i am rolling on.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>we are young right?</P>\r\n\r\n<P>give up the race.  it is a myth.  i don\'t know anything that i should do.  i don\'t want to be alone though.  i know so many alone people.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>kiki: who am i?</P>\r\n'),(524,'<pre>\r\nthis room.\r\ni move inside it like a womb.\r\n\r\nno outside invitations for entry.\r\nmy pink blanket covering all. slinking between sheets. my smell. my scent.\r\nfor me alone. to know.\r\n\r\n\r\ndream lovers....they move too slow to break through.\r\ngroove me. damn you.\r\n\r\n\r\nthey all just want to be dominated. they crave it like mongrel dogs licking\r\ntheir lips. angry freaks. no will to speak of. \r\n\r\ni\'ll whip you. \r\n\r\nright into the past\r\nand present\r\nbruised accent.\r\n\r\nthe ebb and flow\r\nmoving. my body slow. smack behind yours.\r\n\r\n\r\ne v i l    i n f i n i t e    e r o s    g l o w\r\n\r\n\r\nreversed attractions . . . ultimate satisfaction.\r\n\r\na comparison\r\nof have\r\nand have nots.\r\n\r\nremembering\r\npast lives come and go\r\nto loves love lost.\r\n\r\nconspiracy freaks\r\nweak\r\nfor this pink stuff.\r\n\r\nmidnight springtime solo rut.\r\n\r\n</pre>'),(525,'<P>\r\nSo there\'s all these layoffs and I am waiting until tomorrow to find out  my current round of finding out fate. I guess I will have some income still, or join my husband in unemployment. The funny thing is, what I fear most is missing the point of it all. If I get canned, we are both suddenly free to roam with several k\'s of dollars stashed. I love it here in the Bay Area, I really do, but what if this happens, we are both set free, what if we are supposed to go somewhere? Do something? We made a plan last night to revisit things in a year, when I have hopefully gotten some cooking classes in and worked free at some restaurants, when his IT skills are better. He is 37 and is depressed by not having computer classes in college. He knows his stuff, but he can\'t back it up with a degree, there weren\'t any when he was in school! In a year we see what we have learned, and maybe leave. I don\'t want to leave, but at the same time the excitement of change is like the blinking light on a smoke detector. Remember me, I am still here, are you thinking about me?\r\n</P><p>\r\nI don\'t want to miss the door that opens when one closes. Maybe it won\'t close and we can keep our goals of what to do in the coming year. \r\n</P><p>\r\nI wish he could find a job. It has been a month and his severence is run out. I have no control here, no way to help in this, other than offer suggestion.\r\n</P><p>\r\nOn the other hand, yesterday I went to a fire hydrant graveyard, and saw hundreds of old and new hydrants, all kinds. I learned how to know where they pull water from by what color their tops (bonnets) are. What it means if they are flat on top or have that ball shape. How to know where the water main is in the street by looking at the top of the hydrant. I saw brand new ones still with tags and clean silver chains. The world is wondrous even as it makes me worry.\r\n</P>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/525_1.jpg\'>'),(526,'<p><font face=\"Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">I was not expecting \r\n  to have a job in March. In fact I had planned a cable TV movie watching (TMC \r\n  channel) marathon this month. Got a booklet at barnes and nobles and highlighted \r\n  all the movies I wanted to watch. Also i got a Ton of DVD\'s. As luck ( or my mum\'s prayers) would have \r\n  it, my first interview this month made me and offer and I took it and I am working. \r\n  <br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  [day one ] I had not realized I was replacing someone. I reckon that she left \r\n  in November. During my interview she was briefly mentioned as someone who needed \r\n  lots of micromanagement. So during day one it is up to me to look through my \r\n  predecessors stuff. I don\'t like this so much, I am anxious to be done and have \r\n  my own system in place. Lucky me she has left behind a very detailed word document \r\n  with her duties and contacts. I have many job functions, her old job is only \r\n  one of them. In addition to her stuff I am also assisting a software engineer. \r\n  He\'s an old timer who has been a programmer since the early eighties and this \r\n  is highlighted by his mad DOS skills. I will work closely with him for time \r\n  being says my boss, it\'s cool because he curses in funny ways. He was showing \r\n  me the difference between a DOS editor and the windows counterpart I want to \r\n  use, so his macros work great in DOS but when he gets to the windows version \r\n  he is not as successful \"and this is where I say fuck you\", he said. \r\n  Once he ran into some notes from the guy who wrote this one program we are messing \r\n  about with and he says \" I should of cut his balls off\".Â Â I \r\n  giggle a lot on the inside when in his office. His next door office neighbor \r\n  is a hoot, and was instantly friendly to me, at the end of the week I find out \r\n  that they\'ve been working together for over twenty years, they have comedic \r\n  timing.I have an office mate, he was very friendly, his jobs demands a lot of \r\n  talking on the phone, he likes to rock and listen to this alt-rock station all \r\n  day, he is gone most of the day. My boss is cool, he knows his technology, I \r\n  love his office because there is gear and software all over the place. He works \r\n  late. These are facts. At first I have a junky computer. Filling-out HR paperwork \r\n  takes so much time. Ugh. Anyway a good first day. Former first day at work stories: \r\n  my trainer cuts my finger with a letter opener, I got food poisoning. </font></p>\r\n<p><font face=\"Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">[day two] I get \r\n  a better machine. An athlon thunderbird with win2k. That\'s more like it. 17\" \r\n  monitor though. I have modified my pc a bit but I will wait a month to change \r\n  the wallpaper to my girly girl montage wallpapers. I start buying breakfast \r\n  again, I had not eaten breakfast since I got laid off. I get fatigued in the \r\n  afternoon, which is a bit excepted after laying about in my flat for a month \r\n  and a half. I can\'t wait to get some posters and pictures in my office. I have \r\n  lots of room but I am afraid I will be getting a sharpie bulletin board. On \r\n  this day I get to work on stuff that will reach the final product the day after. \r\n  I bring headphones, mp3s, and I\'m back into my groove. Our T1 provider goes out \r\n  of business so I only have mail. Its sort of nice to be at a company that does \r\n  not go to a stand still when there isn\'t a Net connection. The net will be back \r\n  next week or so. I get my own in the box copy of Dreamweaver 4. yay. </font></p>\r\n<p><font face=\"Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">[day three] more \r\n  than a few new employees have arrived at this place so the usual pizza party \r\n  speech lunch occasion happens. I shake lots of hands and run into many funny \r\n  guys back in production. Lots of them are Hispanic but no one asks me where \r\n  I am from and if I speak Spanish. This has never happened. This is a plus b/c \r\n  I get very annoyed when such questions are posed.</font></p>\r\n<p><font face=\"Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">[day four] I get \r\n  a CD-writer. Part of my job is sending out software updates on a monthly basis, \r\n  I will be burning quite a lot of cd\'s during the middle of the month. I decide \r\n  to install it myself ( to be efficient) and it turns problematic and my boss \r\n  has to come in and try to fix it and I do nothing for about an hour an a half. \r\n  What a nightmare, I come off as half a twit for commencing this problem but \r\n  in the end it was a pc problem. </font></p>\r\n<p><font face=\"Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">[day five] The \r\n  company buys breakfast on friday\'s but I forgot about it and brought my own, \r\n  i am remided. Lunch with my boss, his wife and my trainer, they get into arguments, \r\n  its funny. I stay out of it. Nice New Job week ends.</font></p>'),(527,'<pre>\r\ni have a lump in my throat the size \r\nof this state that i live in.  i am \r\nenervated and melancholy and on the \r\nverge of tears.  and i am completely \r\ndrained of energy, did i mention that?  \r\nah yes, i suppose i did.  i hope\r\ntomorrow, will be less exhausting.  i \r\nhave taken to drinking again.  i am the \r\nhighway sign:\r\n               uneven pavement\r\n               next 400 miles\r\n</pre>'),(528,'<p>i am kat.\r\ndepending on where and when you meet me.</p>\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n<p>lately i\'ve been spending most of my days roaming california.\r\nsan francisco. santa cruz. south bay.\r\n. . . no matter how far i go it\'s always home.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>i like working for myself. \r\ni can wear my slippers\r\nand whatever else that suits my fancy.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>i write a lot.\r\nbut i don\'t worry too much about proper grammar.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>sometimes i make things.\r\n[pictures. stories. businesses. websites. seafood stew]</p>\r\n\r\n<p>i have a dog.\r\nmost people call her a spaz.\r\nshe is the epitome of unconditional love\r\n...and a fearless explorer.</p>\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n<p>when i grow up, i want to be just like her.</p>'),(529,'<p>Take a journey with me and eleven of my closest friends... (though I am sure \r\n  we can fit more in)</p><p>\r\n<a href=\"http://www.busforsale.com/bowman/bowman%20index.htm\" target=\"blank\"><img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/529_1.jpg\' height=\'150\'></p><p>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/529_2.gif\' height=\'150\'></p></a>\r\n<p><b>destination</b>: Anywhere!</p>\r\n<p><b>total price</b> : $55,000</p>\r\n<p><b>price each</b>: $4,583ea </p>\r\n<p><b>when</b>: once all money is received</p>\r\n<p>sign up now.</p>'),(530,'<p>\r\ni might as well stay home and listen to the sound of the phone as it doesn\'t ring. i might as well pretend to hear your voice as you tell me you\'ve moved on. and i\'m still here. barely breathing...definitely not moving on. and i can\'t help but wonder what you\'re doing right now. what you\'re thinking...and the past two months have been crazy for me. and i don\'t know what else to do but rationalize. and over analyze. and cry. and i don\'t know how to tell you that you were wrong. you shouldn\'t have been that way and then i think and i wonder if maybe you weren\'t so wrong after all. maybe i deserved to be strung along...and every little part of me wants to hate you for not liking me. and i want to congratulate myself because all my skepticism has paid off. somebody has proven me right. everyone fakes it. nobody cares. you shouldn\'t trust anyone. how silly do i sound? i can\'t say exactly what it is that i want to say...everything comes out wrong and forced and stupid.\r\n</p><p>\r\ni\'m disappointed because i thought you were a possibility. i told you my secret and just like everyone else...you backed away. and maybe i don\'t deserve to be close to someone. maybe i\'m too flawed for that. but i thought i at least deserved \"something\"\r\n</p><p>\r\nsomething so that i didn\'t have to rely on a friend to tell me you were seeing someone else...i was hoping you\'d be the one to save me from feeling like a complete idiot.\r\n</p><p>\r\nand i\'m so sick of being scared to trust people. so sick of being insecure. so sick of my relationships and mistakes repeating themselves over and over and over and i\'m so sick of my flaws beating against my eyelids when i try to sleep.\r\ni\'m just scared.\r\n</p><p>\r\nand this has nothing to do with you...\r\n</p><p>\r\nwhoever you are... \r\n</p>\r\n'),(531,'<STRONG>\r\n<P>my eyelids are swollen shut from falling asleep and waking up and falling asleep and waking up.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>we don\'t really fight.  we do argue.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>who are we to move through life with each other, intercepting communication patterns, trying to decode them.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>we have a war of love.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i love you so fierce i would do things that seem unconscionable.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i am so tired.  i will go to sleep tonight without brushing my teeth.  there, i said it.  now i will brush my teeth.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i love you.</P>\r\n</STRONG>'),(532,'<p>Today I started my new job at the Texas School for the Blind and Visualy Impared. I love it; it is more challenging than any computer program could ever be, to me.</p>\r\n<p>I was told at the end of my eight hour shift that today was a difficult day, and not to be scared off. I agree, it was difficult. I am not scared away, infact I am challenged in a new way. A thing in me that I have not seen before, something just grabbed ahold of me and said \"you need to be doing this.\" Okay, the fact I didn\'t have a job may have had some bearing on this; although I did turn down the higher paying jobs to do this... am I a hero, or am I just where I need to be? I am learning much from just one day. I am frightened; more than the kids maybe.</p>\r\n<p>Maybe I will sell all four or five of my computers, buy a bus, and go camp in the desert for a few years just to meditate on my place in this world? Maybe I will.</p>\r\n<p>I am not supposed to be like this? k-dogg says I have changed since the first time she met me. Have I? Have I really? Damn, I feel like the same little scared boy swinging on the swings in third grade and getting teased because I was chubby.</p><p><b>CHUBBY KIDS ARE COOL</b></p>'),(533,'<P align=\"justify\">So tomorrow, I put on my funny hat, and my funny robe, and my red black and white hood, and I join a couple hundred other people walking up the main street of the main city in Auckland.  A couple of hours later, I get to sit in a room full of people, and eventually they\'ll call out my name and I get a piece of paper. </P>\r\n<p>\r\n<img src=\"http://swinney.org/journals/images/533_1.jpg\" align=\"right\" alt=\"joanna in grad hat\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" border=\"1\" hspace=\"6\">\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<P align=\"justify\">\r\nI know that the above paragraph probably makes me sound all cynical and everything, but I\'m really excited.  This is the culmination of three years of work, and two  years of anticipation before that.  I\'ve made so many friends in the past three years, ones that I\'ll know for life, and ones that\'ll drift away in a few months, and I\'ve learnt the importance of being able to tell the difference.  I\'ve learnt all about the media.  I\'ve learnt a little sociology.  I\'ve learnt about me.  And I\'ve survived.  That\'s what I\'ll be celebrating tomorrow.  \r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<P align=\"justify\">Graduation is a token ceremony, but it\'s  important.  It\'s tangible.  It\'s where I get to be with the people that have  mattered the most the past three years and feel good about  having got so far.  And from tomorrow onwards, I will be Joanna McLeod, B.C.s .  </p>'),(534,'<P>listening to the rain again. listening to your silence. fucking to bush. crying because it\'s over. missing you before you leave. nothing feels right. tattooed on me forever. your part of me. and you can leave. wearing your jim morrison coat. untouchable face. you can leave with your pouty lips and your mexican skin. i\'ve packed your things. your free to go. build your walls. tell your lies. don\'t look at me. i\'m dying. loving you was too easy. hating you is hard. this is wrong. we\'re supposed to be forever. for now. suck it up. don\'t look back. walk away. before i crack...i still feel it.</P>\r\n<CENTER>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/534_1.jpg\'> \r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/534_2.jpg\'>\r\n<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/534_3.jpg\'>\r\n</CENTER>'),(535,'<pre>\r\n\r\nWhat happened?\r\n\r\nLife strikes\r\nand nothing\'s\r\nleft\r\nbut scorched rubble\r\nand the reaching hands of a body\r\nburied under bricks\r\ngasping\r\nto be\r\nsaved.\r\n\r\n</pre>\r\n'),(536,'<p>sometimes i forget how important secrets are. i think that sometimes i go out of my way to share secrets because they\'re one of the most sure fire ways to get people\'s attention. at the same time, i\'m always fascinated by and in awe of people who seem so mysterious and yes, \"secretive.\" i guess i\'m just scared that if i start withholding my secrets from people, they won\'t think i\'m mysterious; they\'ll just ignore me and move on.</p>'),(537,'<table border=1 bordercolor=\"#333333\" bgcolor=\"#cccccc\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td><table border=0 width=98%><tr><td><p>words words words<br>\r\ndo you think, in this case<br>\r\nit would be all right to lie a little?</p>\r\n<p>words <font size=\"+1\">words</font> <font size=\"+2\">words</font><br>\r\nsometimes i wish you had a cyber bar, swinney<br>\r\nso we could all come to swinney.org and it would be like <font color=\"#ff0000\">cheers</font></p>\r\n<p>words <font size=\"-1\">words</font> <font size=\"-2\">words</font><br>\r\nmmm, baby, i am so <b><i>hot</i></b> for you<br>\r\nyou make me so hard in my pants<br>\r\nthat i feel like i could grind against you (or softly stroke your hair) for the rest of my life, taking only short breaks for naps, meals, and bowel movements</p>\r\n<p>worms worms worms<br>\r\njesus, that slays me<br>\r\ni was afraid of worms, roxanne!!!</p>\r\n<p>words <font color=\"#333333\">words</font> <font color=\"#555555\">words</font><br>\r\nit deafens me, sometimes<br>\r\nthe raging voice of \"should\", shrieking \"warning\" and \"beware\"<br>\r\nbut tonight, i am afraid of nothing<br>\r\nand i hear all sounds clearly<br>\r\nand i act gracefully with a lucid mind<br>\r\nand every breath is courage<br>\r\nand each instant destroys<br>\r\na little bit more of the darkness</p>\r\n<p>words <strong>words</strong> words<br>\r\ni john 4:18 - <br>\r\n\"there is no fear in love, but perfect love casts out fear.\"</p>\r\n<p>words words words<br>\r\nand it is far less frightening to me to die<br>\r\nto lose this body<br>\r\nthan to live without conviction and evolution</p>\r\n<p><i>words words <b>words</b></i><br>\r\nit is impossible to receive without taking<br>\r\nit is impossible to hate without being hated<br>\r\nit is impossible to scorn without being scorned<br>\r\nit is impossible to resolve without dissolving<br>\r\nit is impossible to live without dying<br>\r\nbut it\'s possible to communicate without words</p>\r\n<p><font face=\"Verdana\">words words words</font><br>\r\nwhat is the matter?<br>\r\nslanders = bushy eyebrows * grey beards<font size=\"-2\"><sup><a href=\"http://huney.org/words.htm\">2</a></sup></font></p>\r\n</td></tr></table></td></tr></table>'),(538,'<p><font size=\"13\" color=\"red\"><B>\r\nMONKEYASS OVER DONKEY\r\n</b></font>\r\n</p><p>\r\n<tt>\r\n*s5* haha. i am laughing really hard about something weeb wrote\r\n<br>*s5* \"i am all monkeyass over donkey out of line here. \"\r\n</tt></p>\r\n<p>also, i always check the \"art\" box under \"which category best describes you?\"</p>'),(539,'<PRE>\r\n. go to the gym\r\n. set up an apache server with php and mysql\r\n. talk to the job fairy\r\n. have coffee with s5\r\n. make dinner and give some to peter\r\n. finish my poop story for weeb\r\n</PRE>'),(540,'<p>there are two pretty important astrological events that have been affecting many of us, and i thought i\'d share.\r\n</p><p>\r\nthe first event is venus retrograde, passing through the sign of aries. venus went into retrograde on march 9th, and will be moving direct again by april 20th.\r\n</p><p>\r\nplanets are said to be \"retrograde\" when their motion around the sun appears to be backwards, relative to the earth. to an astrologer, a planet in retrograde will have its energy reversed. either backwards or inward.\r\n</p><p>\r\nvenus is the planet that rules love and relationships. during this retrograde period, love relationships will feel stunted and broken. hidden pain and difficulties will bubble up to the surface. those who are normally shy might feel more expressive with a lover.\r\n</p><p>\r\nwith venus in aries, the expression of love will take on a quality of being brutually honest, selfish, aggressive.\r\n</p><p>\r\nthese two forces together can be unfavorable for relationships. normally loving couples will erupt in a frenzy of second thoughts, as everything that was once hidden in a cozy bliss, gets shoved out into the open.\r\n</p><p>\r\nhow to get through it? remember that retrograde periods are a good time to retreat, reflect, reconsider. and with venus in aries, it\'s a good time to clear the air with honesty. perhaps being alone and separating from your mate. whether just for one night in a hotel room, or permanently, or somewhere in between. but as long as you use the time productively, to understand what your relationships mean to you, to understand how they enrich you, and where they swallow you up.\r\n</p><p>\r\nthe second event is from chinese astrology (which i know very little about, but i do know a few things).\r\n</p><p>\r\n2001 is the year of the snake, and everyone has been touched by this in some way. the snake is a destructive influence. it seeks to destroy all false realities, and bring us back to the center of what\'s real. the snake is like shiva.\r\n</p><p>\r\nlast year was the year of the dragon, when we built and created and filled everything with wild hopes and impossible dreams. this year, the snake will deflate all of the nonsense, leaving us with the very core of what we created. at the end of all the destruction, we are left with a firm foundation to build from.\r\n</p><p>\r\nthe recession we\'re in right now is a good example of the snake\'s influence.\r\n</p><p>\r\nhow to survive the year? find comfort, look for any shred of reality that feels grounded. remember to be present, remember that scarcity encourages resourcefulness. remember to breathe.\r\n</p><p>\r\ngood luck everyone.\r\n</p>'),(541,'<p>perhaps something society adopts as a general rule is that tough decisions are the meaning of love. I found some letters of my moms when i was going through boxes after the fire. they were in a big box of pictures. so many of the pictures were of my mom, dad, and brother. pics of the old country, paris, noranda, toronto. vacation pics. laughing pics. pics with the dogs and cats. the relatives and birthday parties, christmas and easters. grandma and grandpa all so much younger and more energetic.</p>\r\n<p>the letters were written after the seperation, and contained so many riddles. she still loved(s) my father it said at one point. i read this and started crying. there was just so much of everyones life but mine. the pictures stopped when i was three. this box also represented a time when my mom was so much more happy. I grew up while my mom grew down. I think about this box of pictures and papers a lot. I realized that love isnt the most powerful thing on earth. my mom made a very hard decision leaving my father. she made the right decision. i just hope she thinks so too. </p>'),(542,'<img src=\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/542_1.jpg\'>'),(543,'<P>it\'s so much easier for me to sit here and write all this pretentious, melodramatic crap than it is for me to actually reach down inside and pull something out that really means something. because guess what? i don\'t care about you. i really don\'t. it\'s that \"un attainability\" crap that everyone talks about. it\'s the fact that i can\'t have you, that makes me want you. </P>\r\n<PRE>\r\n\"every song has a you\r\na you that the singer sings to\r\nand you\'re it this time.\r\nbaby, you\'re it this time.\"\r\n--ani difranco \r\n</PRE>\r\n'),(544,'<p>we\'re supposed to be friends now. i broke it off. we live down the street from each other. i still love him, i just can\'t be with him. and hey, we\'re still friends. but this feels even worse. i miss the fun, but hanging out now seems so hard. he keeps touching me the same way he used to, and saying no seems so silly. so yeah, maybe we shouldn\'t hang out. but don\'t friends hang out? this was a friendly ending. a \"maybe someday but we\'re not going to think about that now\" ending. and all this different behavior is just so goofy feeling. so fake. so staged. how do you say no to someone you used to say only yes to?</P>'),(545,'<p>Get up. No shower. Drink coffee with s5 and weeb and swinney. Talk about anarchism. Think that I should have showered. Sweaty buttcrack.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Head home. Think about shower. Opt for geeking instead. Listen to rock music.</p> \r\n\r\n<p>Leave house, play frisbee with swinney, and some kid who didnt like swinney. Think about shower.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Buy groceries. Think about shower. Get coffee again. Walk home. \r\nGet home. Think about unpacking groceries. Opt for geeking instead. Listen to rock music. Think about shower.</P>\r\n '),(546,'<pre>\r\n i need some lovin\'\r\n killa on the move\'n\r\n far from home\r\n always on the roam\r\n couch surfin\' nigga\r\n picked up bed bugs\r\n in my beard\r\n make me scratch my mugs\r\n livin\' dirty\r\n time for a smoke, it is honker thirty\r\n life sucks\r\n trying to make a bucks\r\n frisco can be tuff\r\n finding work is ruf\r\n finding the time to go to the gym\r\n and stay buff\r\n castro foolz\r\n pinching my ass,\r\n yo those guys really looze\r\n listing to punk rock at peters\r\n the volume is off the meters\r\n the neighbors are yellin\'\r\n \"YO your apt be smellin\'\r\n and it is true because we don\'t take out the trash\r\n hard to find time for that shit when you aint makin cash\r\n just sitting around listening to johny cash\r\n peter has all four thousand albumz\r\n even that one that cash played at the state penz\r\n where i am going to end up with the blues\r\n if i don\'t find some kind of good news\r\n i am despirate\r\n a pirate\r\n a whirlpool of killa moves\r\n unemployed and kiking the ryhmes in #unemployed\r\n i must say that i am really annoyed\r\n get president rosevelt up in the bitch\r\n before i find myself diggin a ditch\r\n for me myself and i\r\n pray to eye and eye\r\n jah better helpus\r\n !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\r\n</pre>'),(552,'<P>and we heartfully listened to everyone\'s beliefs about contract law without judgment?\r\n</P><P>\r\nRattles and drums in ojai. Three hours of Esalen and reiki--i got some serious work done.  stone tub and hawks overhead, tea with long bearded men in the dark.  work retreat. solar power everything. radiant, elder Lola wants to hear everyone sing:  wenda hey-yo.  buddha painted gold.  meditation yurt.  Pottery in the pottery yurt!  council!  big spiders in the dome and a view of misty striated rock cliffs. thich nhat hanh used to visit there.  i want to stay, but it is easy to have peace in a quiet place.  harder to have peace on the 5 South.\r\n</P><P>\r\nI tried to explain the \"law is an important tool for social change\" thing to people as i stood in a bamboo grove overlooking the valley. They looked at me as if they would let me continue to believe my own story.\r\n </P><P>\r\nOur eco-warrior houseguests from ecuador have 1500 acres and a great need for hands.  what else is there to do, and what could possibly be more worthwhile. \r\n</P>\r\n'),(553,'<p>my life is an endless series of unfinished projects, half-baked ideas, and broken promises.</p>\r\n<p><i>these boots were made for walkin</i></p>\r\n<p>some time ago, i hardwired it in my head that boots = strength.</p>\r\n<p><i>and that\'s just what they\'ll do</i></p>\r\n<p>i bought new boots today.  KISS boots.  asskickers.</p>\r\n<p><i>one of these days these boots are gonna walk all over you</i></p>\r\n<p>i have a Plan.  me and my boots are going to plow through it all.  we will leave no stone unturned.</p>\r\n<p><i>are you ready boots?  start walkin!</i></p>'),(554,'<PRE>she travels back up the world\r\n\r\nnorth\r\n\r\nfrom that smithy in aruba\r\n\r\nbeen gone since epiphany\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nat tampa international\r\n\r\nno hellos\r\n\r\nÂ³i think they ruin my bootsÂ²\r\n\r\nshe says\r\n\r\nÂ³they saw i went to venezuela\r\n\r\nand spray something on them.\r\n\r\nidiot.\r\n\r\nwhy would i wear these boots\r\n\r\nin venezuela?Â²\r\n\r\nÂ³donÂ¹t worryÂ²\r\n\r\ni say\r\n\r\nÂ³they make new boots every day.\r\n\r\ntheyÂ¹re killing cows every\r\n\r\nday\r\n\r\njust to make you more boots.\r\n\r\ndid you get a lot done?Â²\r\n\r\nÂ³yes.  what about you?Â²\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nlater:\r\n\r\nÂ³i saw that guy from maracaibo.Â²\r\n\r\nÂ³did he say what the hell happened\r\n\r\nto my money?Â²\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nbefore sunrise at the airside:\r\n\r\ncoffee jag, leaf-wet, bleary, goofy,\r\n\r\nnervous around each other\r\n\r\nhour ride home\r\n\r\nlisten to eno, another green world\r\n\r\ngarage to garage\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nmom and dad\r\n\r\nare at 