Â²\r\n\r\nÂ³i will.  i t grows back.\r\n\r\nthis is just for work.Â²\r\n\r\nÂ³no, you did it ?cause\r\n\r\nyou like it.\r\n\r\ni think you got some of the\r\n\r\nbitch in you.\r\n\r\nwork, my ass.Â²\r\n\r\nÂ³that may well be.\r\n\r\nwhoÂ¹s to say?Â²\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nroll over:\r\n\r\nÂ³i was gettinÂ¹ freakyÂ²\r\n\r\ni say\r\n\r\nÂ³wasnÂ¹t myself.\r\n\r\nnot grounded or something.Â²\r\n\r\nÂ³yeah.  i saw you at the airport.\r\n\r\nyou had the big eyes.\r\n\r\nyou need to watch that\r\n\r\nshit.\r\n\r\nyoga and candomble\r\n\r\ndonÂ¹t mix too good.Â²\r\n\r\nÂ³i think i just needed\r\n\r\nto get laid.Â²\r\n\r\nÂ³yeah.  and i just think\r\n\r\nyouÂ¹re a big flakejob.Â²\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nÂ²how is it\r\n\r\nyou know the word\r\n\r\n?flakejobÂ¹\r\n\r\nbut not ?mapleÂ¹\r\n\r\nor ?salmonÂ¹?Â²\r\n\r\nÂ³how much swedish\r\n\r\ndo YOU know,\r\n\r\nnumbnuts?\r\n\r\nor german?\r\n\r\nor french?\r\n\r\nor russian?\r\n\r\nor dutch?Â²\r\n\r\nÂ³i know some german.Â²\r\n\r\nÂ³you couldnÂ¹t even\r\n\r\nask for the menÂ¹s\r\n\r\nroom.Â²\r\n\r\nÂ³well, according to you,\r\n\r\ni could use either one.Â²\r\n\r\nÂ³you got that right.Â²\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nat port of tampa today:\r\n\r\nthey bring out the crates.\r\n\r\nin the big one\r\n\r\nclockworks on a\r\n\r\npedestal.\r\n\r\nangels riding red devils\r\n\r\nred devils riding angels\r\n\r\nday-glo mermaids playing\r\n\r\nsoprano saxes and\r\n\r\nclarinets.\r\n\r\nthe customs guy\r\n\r\ncrosses himself.\r\n\r\nÂ³what is that?Â²\r\n\r\nhe says\r\n\r\nÂ³aluminum?Â²\r\n\r\nÂ³the figures are pewter.\r\n\r\neverything else is steel.Â²\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nat her dealerÂ¹s in channelside:\r\n\r\nsitting around\r\n\r\ndrinking woo-woos\r\n\r\nwaiting for two thirty\r\n\r\nfor the thing to open.\r\n\r\nÂ³the planetsÂ² on the stereo.\r\n\r\nÂ³venus should come before\r\n\r\nmarsÂ²\r\n\r\nshe says\r\n\r\nÂ³it starts too heavyÂ²\r\n\r\nÂ³wellÂ²\r\n\r\ni say\r\n\r\nÂ³you just call up olÂ¹ gustav\r\n\r\nand let him know