place.<BR>bring your ass with me.\"<BR>we go out to his car<BR>and bring up<BR>a case of moet<BR>two bags of ice<BR>take-out chinese<BR>dixie cups<BR>a carton of camel deadheads.<BR><BR>fill the sink with ice<BR>and four bottles of champagne.<BR>he sits on one<BR>of the metal folding chairs<BR>and pulls some<BR>black tar<BR>out of his jacket.<BR>lays it on the desk<BR>along with a stem,<BR>picks up the manuscript<BR>and skims through it.<BR>sees me eyeing the tar.<BR>\"do this many pages tomorrow,<BR>and i\'ll see you with some more<BR>tomorrow night.\"<BR><BR>eat, drink,<BR>smoke.<BR>he tells me some secrets,<BR>whispers in my little ear<BR>about a scheme<BR>to make everyone the same.<BR>says there\'s a cybercash shitstorm,<BR>a fury of exponents<BR>held in a leyden jar<BR>in a server<BR>in a bank<BR>on guernsey.<BR>says they\'ll let it loose first in hong kong.<BR>then approach the imf under<BR>sovereign status.<BR>ask for a trillion to keep it hemmed in.<BR>right before i pass out,<BR>i say \"how do you know you aren\'t all fools?\"<BR><BR>dream there\'s a war.<BR>tampa\'s levelled.<BR>i walk through the ruins of the old theatre<BR>downtown.<BR>run into jean-michel basquiat<BR>and mackenzie king<BR>playing chess on the<BR>mezzanine.<BR>samo\'s got a maya symbol, a spiral,<BR>painted on his cheek.<BR>he tells me,<BR>\"ultimately, WE DO NOT EXIST.\"<BR><BR>i take a rowboat<BR>out to the casino boat.<BR>the retirees<BR>are still feeding tokens<BR>into the slots<BR>they never heard the news.<BR>\"don\'t tell me about<BR>no nuclear war, boy,<BR>this thing\'s about to pay off.\"<BR><BR>what will i miss most about anna?<BR>the way, after we\'d watch movies,<BR>that she\'d repeat her favorite lines<BR>for days on end.<BR>after we saw \"requiem for a dream,\"<BR>appropos of nothing, she\'d say,<BR>\"nice and easy - mashed potatoes.\"<BR>or \"ass to ass.\"<BR>after \"repo man,\"<BR>she\'d walk around saying<BR>\"fucka john wayne.\"<BR><BR>wake up with the feeling<BR>that nothing around me is real.<BR>this comes upon me unexpectedly<BR>lasts for days at a time.<BR>everything\'s so mundane.<BR>seen it all before.<BR>people with their heads, arms, legs,<BR>privates, breasts, ideas.<BR>no variation, one to the next.<BR>no surprises.<BR><BR><I>I said to myself: three days<BR>and you\'ll be seven years old.<BR>I was saying it to stop<BR>the sensation of falling off<BR>the round, turning world.<BR>into cold, blue-black space.<BR>But I felt: you are an I,<BR>you are an Elizabeth,<BR>you are one of them.<BR>Why should you be one, too?<BR>I scarcely dared to look<BR>to see what it was I was.<BR>I gave a sidelong glance<BR>--I couldn\'t look any higher--<BR>at shadowy gray knees,<BR>trousers and skirts and boots<BR>and different pairs of hands<BR>lying under the lamps.<BR>I knew that nothing stranger<BR>had ever happened, that nothing<BR>stranger could ever happen.</I><BR><BR>put the record back on,<BR>write some more.<BR>around dark,<BR>decide i need a vacation<BR>from this vacation,<BR>go over to the university of tampa library,<BR>read about the Method.<BR>there\'s a girl<BR>on the sofa next to mine.<BR>latino, blonde.<BR>sees me looking at her,<BR>looks me in the eye.<BR>i wink at her.<BR>she winks back.<BR>\"de donde es usted?\" i say.<BR>\"i don\'t speak spanish,\" she says.<BR>her name\'s natalie.<BR>from connecticut.<BR>scottish mom, dominican dad.<BR>i ask her,<BR>\"do you like to party?\"<BR><BR>she liked to party.<BR>and she had money.<BR>visited an atm,<BR>went by ray and fauna\'s<BR>for supplies.<BR>(five days later, they\'d be busted<BR>for prescription fraud.)<BR>dropped by the whitledge for some champagne.<BR>checked into the economy inn,<BR>two blocks down kennedy.<BR>third floor, up on top.<BR><BR>we do some lines:<BR>pink coke.<BR>drink the moet,<BR>smoke geeked joints,<BR>smoke a wet baby.<BR><BR>i start phasing in and out.<BR>next thing i know:<BR>she\'s sucking my balls and fucking me with an empty champagne bottle.<BR>got