ok her arm. She leaned in close and whispered in her ear as they walked.\r\n<p>\r\nThen she looked back at me and winked. The bitch.\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nA massive bouncer allowed us into a roped off area at the back of the club. There was a row of heavy black velvet curtains and Tsing pulled one back, inviting us in. Then she let the fabric slip closed into place and we were alone. The main stage was only a dozen yards away, AC/DC thundering from the speakers, but in our little compartment it was as muffled and private as a confessional. Tsing Tao had me sit on the little love seat at the end of the booth.\r\n<p>\r\nShe stood very close to the Destroyer and kept whispering in her ear. Her hips swayed in tiny movements in time with the distant music. She put the Destroyer\\\'s hands on her hips and slowly backed her towards me. When the back of her legs touched my knees Tsing Tao pushed her gently into my lap. My arms automatically went around her, my hands sliding under her shirt, and she twisted around to kiss me. She licked my teeth and bit my lips. I cupped her tiny breasts and pinched her nipples hard enough to make her gasp. \r\n<p>\r\nTsing Tao reached over to turn a knob that brought the music from the stage into our little lounge. Lynyrd Skynyrd broke over our heads in a thunderclap. She climbed on top on the Destroyer and started her act. Suddenly I was supporting the weight of two women and what had seemed a fabulous idea in the abstract was now crushingly concrete. I couldn\\\'t get a decent breath. My hands fell from the Destroyer and lay listlessly on the cushions. They had forgotten me. I was just a lumpier cushion.\r\n<p>\r\nTsing Tao was no longer dancing. She kissed and fondled the Destroyer, who responded in kind. Sing bit her neck and raked her throat with her teeth and then looked at me, the lobe of the Destroyer\\\'s ear caught in her teeth. The Destroyer\\\'s heavy breathing began to vocalize as moans, growing in volume as Sing pulled her shirt up and went to work on her breasts. I watched over the Destroyer\\\'s shoulder as Tsing Tao unbuckled the girl\\\'s belt and slid her pants out from under her ass. Then she slipped a hand between her legs and the Destroyer\\\'s moans began to reach porn star volume until Sing moved past her towards me and the Destroyer sucked on her breasts like an infant.\r\n<p> \r\nTsing kissed her ears and cooed to her. But she was talking to me as she said, \\\"<I>Ooooooh</I> baby is this what you want? Is this what you oh <I>honey</I> that feels good, do you like this? Is this what you want? Are you a little slut? Are you my little slut?\\\" The Destroyer gasped, \\\"Yeah, <I>yeah</I>.\\\" I felt my eyes fill with tears. Tsing Tao reached around behind the Destroyer, unzipped my pants and pulled my cock free. She started lapdancing again and then I slipped inside the Destroyer and she started <I>howling</I> \\\"Oh god awwwwwooowww <I>god</I> FUCK ME PLEASE FUCK ME.\\\" Tsing Tao grabbed Bad Batz Maru and shoved it in the Destroyer\\\'s mouth. I thought God <I>this is really fucking bad</I> but instead of stopping I grabbed the Destroyer\\\'s bony hips even tighter and tried to split her in half. She spit out the penguin and muffled herself in Tsing Tao\\\'s breasts. Sing rested her chin on the blonde girl\\\'s head and watched me. She offered encouraging moans of her own but her face was stony.\r\n<p>\r\nI should have stopped. I should have thrown them both off me and walked out. But I just wanted to be with Tsing Tao again, even if she would only get as close as this hate-fuck-by-proxy. I fucked the Destroyer as hard as I could and pretended she was the next girl down. When I came Tsing Tao bit her hard enough to leave mirrored crescents of angry red dents on her shoulder.\r\n<p>\r\nThe Destroyer collapsed back against me. She tilted her head back and nuzzled my throat. I stared at the floor. Tsing Tao got up and said, \\\"I\\\'ve got another show in five minutes.\\\"\r\n<p>\r\nI struggled to pull out my wallet. I handed her five twenties and she accepted them with a small triumphant grin. Then she slipped out through the heavy black curtain. I was suddenly aware our little love nest stank of cologne and old come. \r\n<p>\r\n\\\"Oh my god, that was <I>fun</I>,\\\" the Destroyer said. \\\"Can we do this again sometime?\\\"\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n'),(2964,'<p>\r\nWhen I was young, there existed a television commercial that advertised some kind of pastry.  The woman that presented the ad had a very strong Dutch accent and described the pastry as being \\\"layer, upon layer, upon layer!\\\"  Sometimes I think I could describe myself in this way - and with the accent - layer, upon layer, upon layer!\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nI have so many different opinions and conflicting thoughts, that I often confuse even myself.  See, typing this out I\\\'m not even sure what the hell I\\\'m talking about.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nEveryone has that thought in the back of their mind.  You know, the one that you know is there but that you usually ignore because it seems ridiculous?  Like an ex boyfriend once said to me:\r\n\\\"You know all those people who liked you, the ones who you knew liked you but you didn\\\'t particularly want to do anything about it?  The difference between you and me, is that I did.  I screwed them all.\\\"\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nAt first I thought he was just gross.  Then I realised, it\\\'s a mindset.  \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nDon\\\'t worry, I\\\'m not going to shag every boy I come across, but I\\\'m going to adapt some of what he said.  You see, I live a double life.  Is being a gemini sending me insane?  Probably.  I go to my job every day, organise the helpdesk, fix broken things and talk to a lot of angry people.  All day every day, I\\\'m dreaming about my music, hearing my songs in my head, seeing the bright lights.  And until recently, this was just a dream.  Now I\\\'m making it a reality.  I\\\'m sorting some of it out.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nThis has felt so good, so relieving that I\\\'m applying this rule to other areas of my life.  Why hold back when there are so many possibilities, so many chances to act on things I would normally hold back on?  I can tell people what I really think, I can move away from the city, I can see anyone I like, I can study if I want to.  I can fucking live.  I can do what I like instead of what is expected of me.  I can see through the clouds.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nThis may not seem like a new concept to a lot of you, but for a long time I have had two minds about almost everything.  The truth, and the dream.  I get so mixed up sometimes I don\\\'t know where I am or what I\\\'m doing, hence the place I live most of the time - Lala Land, the place in my head.  Layer, upon layer, upon layer.  At the moment though I feel like I know where those layers are.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nNow I\\\'m not sure I said what I wanted to say, but hey.  Sometimes I just don\\\'t know what the hell I\\\'m talking about.\r\n</P>'),(2965,'<img src=\\\"%%img4%%\\\"> <br>\r\n<p>\r\nlast wednesday nite, i went out with a group of friends to celebrate one of my friend\\\'s last nights in ottawa.  she was moving to toronto the next morning.  we ended up on the patio of this little irish pub, and proceeded to drink.  and drink.  and drink.  the patio was fairly empty, so we decided to spin up a couple joints for the walk home.  but as we were rolling them, we started discussing just smoking them right there.  we all agreed the appropriate thing to do would be to ask the bartender (who we also think was the owner of the pub) if he minded if we smoked there.  his answer was simple: \\\"If you got em, smoke em.  If i wasn\\\'t working, i would join you.\\\"  we tried to convince him to join in on them a few more times, but he always politley refused.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nas everyone was geting ready to leave, and settling up various tabs, a few of us stood out on the street in front of the pub, and started to admire one of the new mini\\\'s.  out of nowhere the bartender stepped outside, unlocked the doors with his remote, and told to hop in and take a look if we wanted.  so, of course, we did.  and i must say, i was quite impressed.  a nice layout, and it had a standard, 6-speed transmission.  sweet.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nanyways, everybody settled up and we started wandering home.  on the way, we passed this old theatre that had been converted into a church.  it still had the big theatre marquee out front, and the church put messages up on this.  on this nite, the sign read \\\"Annual Convention.....\\\" well, we immediately thought that with a couple quick switches, the sign could very easily read \\\"Anal Convention.....\\\"  the only problem was the height of the sign, which was up at at least a second story level.  after a quick debate about whether or not we were too drunk to try this, we decided we needed to be at least that drunk to attempt it.  so a couple of my friends put out their hands, and i stepped up.  they hoisted me up a ways, just enough for me to get a hand on the ledge, and then i climbed up the rest of the way.  after ducking out of the view of a few passing cars, i made the switch, and climbed back down.  mission complete.  we laughed the entire way home.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<img src=\\\"%%img6%%\\\"> <br>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nthen, last nite we went out drinking, and stumbled across the new issue of the ottawa x-press, a local weekly paper hilighting some of the musical and cultural events happening around the city.  to our shock, on page 3, right at the top, was a picture of the sign! we all cheered quite loudly.  the caption read \\\"Come all ye faithful: New members welcome at the cornerstone house of refugee apostle church on wellington street.\\\"  it is the first time my work has ever been published  =)\r\n</p>\r\n'),(2966,'when i decided to retire from the web design business last year, i thought that what i would do was write stuff for other people and then they would pay me money and i would be happy.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\ni got a couple contracts to do just that.\r\n<br><br>\r\ni reneged.\r\n<br><br>\r\ni don\\\'t want to write things for other people for money.\r\n<br><br>\r\ni want to write what i feel like writing when i feel like writing it, and i don\\\'t want anyone but me to edit it.\r\n<br><br>\r\ni think the wuh wuh wuh publishing freedom has made it impossible for me to write for money.\r\n<br><br>\r\nin fact, now that i am no longer beholden to any web publisher or advertiser for the content of my sites, i am having wild imaginings of publishing whatever the hell i feel like on sites that were once pretty tame and for women and collectors and get thousands and thousands of page views per day.\r\n<br><br>\r\nand i am probably going to do it, too.\r\n<br><br>\r\nin fact, i have already written a rant or two my fingers are dying to ftp up to the front of auntie.com\r\n\r\n'),(2967,'<P>The hum and smog of the city.\r\n</P><P>\r\nThe painted dishes in the glass credenza then began falling over and the glass door sprung open.  In a few minutes the shaking subsided.  Mrs. Beah knew she would not move an inch from her secure spot in the doorway.  She had too much common sense to go risking her life for a few precious plates.  Her feet were grounded.Before she had time to lose her composure, the plates and bowls began to slide down the polished oaken shelves and onto the floor.  One by one, and some, two at a time, they continued to dive, as though head first, onto the hardwood floor.\r\n</P><P>\r\nMrs. Beah watched in quiet solitude until the shaking stopped permanently.  That afternoon, Mrs. Beahâ€™s daughter came by to check on her mother and helped to get her house back in order.  Mrs. Beah rested her eyes on the pieces of her precious dishes, and turned away as her daughter swept them into a cardboard box.  Her daughter made a checklist of what needed to be replaced and left, promising to come back with some new things.\r\n</P><P>\r\nMrs. Beah decided not to go to mass earlier that day.  Her decision had nothing to do with the earthquake.  She spent the day thinking about her husband.  He was the sort of man who took her boots off for her whenever they came home during the winter months.\r\n</P><P>\r\nâ€œWhy did you take him away?â€ she asked as though there was someone else in the room.  And she covered her face with both hands.\r\n</P><P>\r\nWhen her daughter returned, Mrs. Beah had already resolved to do a few things.  She watched as her daughter opened a cardboard box out of which she resurrected a set of six plates and six bowls in plain white china, except for a little grey, almost, modern-looking stripe around the edges.  â€œThese are for you.  Theyâ€™re not as elaborate as your old ones, but theyâ€™ll do the job.â€  Mrs. Beah, stared in a blank absence at the grey stripes and said nothing.\r\n</P><P>\r\nThe Sunday following the earthquake, Mrs. Beahâ€™s daughter and son-in-law and their two boys ate roast beef and potatoes from plain white plates with grey stripes around the edges.  Mrs. Beah ate nothing at all.  This concerned her daughter and son-in-law, but they knew they could do nothing.  Mrs. Beah refused to eat from of a plain white plate; she refused it all week, and was already beginning to thin in the cheeks.  After all, there was no longer any incentive.</P>'),(2978,'<p><b>In my pocket is Â£2.55 and â‚¬0.66 (66 euro cents)</b></p>\r\n\r\n<p>I live in Northern Ireland (the British bit), close to the border with the Republic of Ireland (the Irish bit). We\\\'ve had this funny euro money for a while now but until today it hadn\\\'t struck me what it actually means.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Living here invariably means using both British Pounds and Euros on a daily basis. You get used to it. <i>One Euro = 60p</i>, ok got that. Well some people do. Some people just can\\\'t grasp it, but those people are the same people that can\\\'t tie their own shoelaces.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>You see each country that uses Euros mints their own coins. All Euro coins have the same face design. A naive 1970s Epcot Center style design plus the face value. On the other side, each country can print whatever the hell they like. Irish Euro\\\'s have, you guesed it, a harp. Euro notes are the same everywhere.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>But i digress</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Today, in my change, I noticed something new. A Spanish Euro. Some dude that looks like a hispanic William Shakespeare grinning at me from the back of my shiny 20c coin. That\\\'s when it struck me.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><b>Europe has a single currency.</b></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Which is slightly unsettling yet kinda cool at the same time.</p>\r\n\r\n'),(2968,'5 hours of being left alone with yourself and whatever wandering thoughts you might have. <br><br>\r\nA quick inventory of the situation - Ottawa to Toronto with 3 stops in small towns along the way. Still drenched in sweat and covered in dirt from all the long boarding, hands still raw and stinging from all the pavement smacking and grabbing at griptape, one grumbling stomach courtesy of its attempts to digest the cow I had for lunch (only thing I\\\'ve kept down the last 2 days), $5 to my name and on the way back to the city to my crap ass job marketing shitty government sponsored documentary film.<br><br>\r\nThe hangover on the second day of the trip was a hidden blessing, had to break off from the guys to nurse back my health and humanity at the sisters. With the sister comes the longboarding (cuz I can\\\'t afford one) and her psuedo roomate (lives across the hall) they both manage the local skate shop together. With the guys in dissarray all doing their own thing I hang with the roomie while the sister lady is working overnight @ the club.<br><br>\r\n<b>The Roomie:</b> 28, Beautiful, Skates, Snowboards, Motorbikes, Photographer, Handywomen, and just all around creative with an amazingly diverse skill set.<br><br>\r\nThe Roomie dates younger, cute, usually not so gifted boys. I\\\'m younger and she has said that I am cute on a few occasions as for the dumb thing I could fake if I don\\\'t qualify. This is definitely one of those situations where the label of <i>Little Brother</i> of the best friend isn\\\'t me help out.<br><br>\r\nTook in a bit of a local skate comp. with both the Sister & Roomie the last day. The main event that day though was the talk with the ex about going to law school @ Bond University in Surfer\\\'s Paradise, Australia. I\\\'ve never been but with a name like that... Glad to see the ex is doing well, she ran her first marathon this year. Memories of waking up in her one room apartment and rolling over on the futon to see her already up and on the eliptical trainer. If I can\\\'t get the coin together to go to Bond, I can at least be glad she will. We used to talk to each other about law school late at night as we laid in bed after getting off our shift at the bar.<br><br>\r\nIf I end up staying in Canada I think I\\\'ll have to move back to Ottawa.<br><br> '),(2969,'<P>As the no-longer-functional clock fell to the ground and broke into two pieces.  Then the fruit, which was too bruised to eat anyway, began tumbling down the side of the wooden table.  Mrs. Beah thought of her husband.\r\n</P><P>\r\nHe was the sort of man who would come home from work early and take her for long drives away from the hum and smog of the city.\r\n</P><P>\r\nThe painted dishes in the glass credenza then began falling over and the glass door sprung open.  In a few minutes the shaking subsided.  Mrs. Beah knew she would not move an inch from her secure spot in the doorway.  She had too much common sense to go risking her life for a few precious plates.  Her feet were grounded.\r\n</P><P>\r\nBefore she had time to lose her composure, the plates and bowls began to slide down the polished oaken shelves and onto the floor.  One by one, and some, two at a time, they continued to dive, as though head first, onto the hardwood floor.\r\n</P><P>\r\nMrs. Beah watched in quiet solitude until the shaking stopped permanently.  That afternoon, Mrs. Beahâ€™s daughter came by to check on her mother and helped to get her house back in order.  Mrs. Beah rested her eyes on the pieces of her precious dishes, and turned away as her daughter swept them into a cardboard box.  Her daughter made a checklist of what needed to be replaced and left, promising to come back with some new things.\r\n</P><P>\r\nMrs. Beah decided not to go to mass earlier that day.  Her decision had nothing to do with the earthquake.  She spent the day thinking about her husband.  He was the sort of man who took her boots off for her whenever they came home during the winter months.\r\n</P><P>\r\nâ€œWhy did you take him away?â€ she asked as though there was someone else in the room.  And she covered her face with both hands.\r\n</P><P>\r\nWhen her daughter returned, Mrs. Beah had already resolved to do a few things.  She watched as her daughter opened a cardboard box out of which she resurrected a set of six plates and six bowls in plain white china, except for a little grey, almost, modern-looking stripe around the edges.  â€œThese are for you.  Theyâ€™re not as elaborate as your old ones, but theyâ€™ll do the job.â€  Mrs. Beah, stared in a blank absence at the grey stripes and said nothing.\r\n</P><P>\r\nThe Sunday following the earthquake, Mrs. Beahâ€™s daughter and son-in-law and their two boys ate roast beef and potatoes from plain white plates with grey stripes around the edges.  Mrs. Beah ate nothing at all.  This concerned her daughter and son-in-law, but they knew they could do nothing.  Mrs. Beah refused to eat from of a plain white plate; she refused it all week, and was already beginning to thin in the cheeks.  After all, there was no longer any incentive.\r\n</P>'),(2970,'<IMG ALIGN=\\\"CENTER\\\" SRC=\\\"%%img1%%\\\"><BR>\r\n<p>\r\nOld man Mc Adoo. He sits watching his miniature automaton blacksmith. He say\\\'s it\\\'s steam powered and i believe him. Old man Mc Adoo never says a whole lot. He just sits\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nOld man Mc Adoo. His minature steam powered automanton blacksmith looks suspiciously like a GI Joe. The type with the small lever appearing from the rear of his velour crew cut. The small lever that moves his eyes side to side.</p>\r\n<p>\r\nBut to old man Mc Adoo, it\\\'s a blacksmith, and it\\\'s all he\\\'s got</p>'),(2971,'<P><B>lesson the first</B></P><P>it\\\'s summer, 1985.  my girlfriend michelle (17) and i (15) are at my cousin\\\'s wedding.  for the first time, i learn that weddings make women horny.</P><P>michelle is a cheerleader.  her blonde hair is cut in a pageboy.  she has relatively large breasts with silver dollar-sized areolas.  i fantasize about putting my thing between them someday.  she\\\'s third in her class and lives for prince.  she\\\'s the one who turned me on to prince.</P><P>at this time, i\\\'m a jock.  i play football in the fall, wrestle in the winter, and hold down second base in spring.  i like wrestling the best but don\\\'t figure out why until a few years later.  i work out five times a week and have a great body for my age.  girls like me not only because i\\\'m nice-looking, but moreso due to the respect and compassion with which i\\\'ve been taught to treat people.  i part my hair in the middle and kind of feather it back.  i\\\'m sure you\\\'ve seen the pictures.  throughout high school, i stay either first, second, or third in my class.</P><P>two weekends prior to the wedding, i lose my virginity to michelle in the back seat of her renault, deep in the state forest.  we\\\'re drunk on lowenbrau that her sister bought for us.  (whatever happened to lowenbrau?)  she keeps rewinding the tape, listening to \\\"little red corvette\\\".  i\\\'m finger-fucking her; she\\\'s stroking my dick.  she puts a condom on me and spreads her legs apart.  i make for the promised land.  \\\"wait, wait,\\\" she says, \\\"the song hasn\\\'t star