y from american idol after simon has said something nice. i want to punch him.<br><br>\r\n\r\nstop grinning like that you popstar cunt.<br><br>\r\n\r\ni toss the playstation controller at richard and abduct my noodles up to the bedroom before he can say anything. sustenance and a cat-nap. essential pre-rave preparation.<br><br>\r\n\r\nwell normally not, actually, but i don\\\'t want to talk to the thing on my couch right now.<br><br>\r\n\r\nsix hours and twenty-seven minutes passes...<br><br>\r\n\r\nrested and re-invigorated i lay out my clothes for the evening. i can hear chatter and people moving about downstairs. some of the others have arrived.<br><br>\r\n\r\nschweet. other people to talk to.<br><br>\r\n\r\ni carefully pull on my suit of rave-armour. my silver-grey psycho-cowboy jeans, white air jordans, white hugo boss sweatshirt and bolle shades. now i am complete.<br><br>\r\n\r\ni am jehannum, moksha, fleshharrower... raver.<br><br>\r\n\r\nheading downstairs i see alan, ivory, and james have arrived. wassup peeps. this also means that the pills have arrived and i can relax.<br><br>\r\n\r\n\\\"nice one bruvva\\\". great. richard saw human traffic once, and he is now part of the chemical generation. i turn to berate him but the words choke in my throat...<br><br>\r\n\r\nhe is wearing exactly the same clothes as i am.<br><br>\r\n\r\nyou\\\'re starting to scare me, you single-white-female cunt.<br><br>\r\n\r\nhe grins back at me. my head is clouded for a moment by the strange image of ruben studdard and randy jackson kicking the crap out of clay as simon holds up a card that says \\\"7 out of 10\\\", and the audience is cheering...<br><br>\r\n\r\ni blink and the dizzy spell stops. i look round at the others and try to focus on something.<br><br>\r\n\r\n\\\"chuppa chups!\\\" blurts out ivory. and i wonder if her rush has kicked in yet...<br><br>\r\n\r\nit\\\'s a small matter, but it gives me focus so we head for the star mart.<br><br>\r\n\r\neleven minutes passes...<br><br>\r\n\r\ni rummage through the half-empty wibbly plastic container on the counter. come on, please, there must be some milky ones left...<br><br>\r\n\r\nit is essential for a successful and sustained ecstasy high, that one does not ingest citric acid of any kind. therefore orange, lemon and other such chuppa chups are a foe, cunningly disguised as friend.<br><br>\r\n\r\n\\\"yeah we\\\'ve got green-j\\\'s, it\\\'s gonna be awesome!\\\"<br><br>\r\n\r\ni look up, terrified, and my worst fears are realised as i see richard talking at an unacceptably unsubtle volume about the lovely little pills that are currently stashed in my back pocket, safe from perspiration in a souvenir mint-tin i got from an actress.<br><br>\r\n\r\ncome on, let\\\'s get to phoenix you socially leprotic cunt.<br><br>\r\n\r\ntwo hours and six minutes passes...<br><br>\r\n\r\nchowie is in full flight on the main dance floor. i dropped a couple of minutes ago, and i\\\'m swaying gently back and forth on the top balcony, surveying the beautiful chaos below.<br><br>\r\n\r\nmy shirt and shoes glow a satisfying black-light purple-blue. the smell of sweat mixes with drakkar and fahrenheit, perfumes i could never name, the faint powdery odour of red bull...<br><br>\r\n\r\ni spy richard in a corner trying to chat up ivory. good luck you no-hoper cunt.<br><br>\r\n\r\nbut i don\\\'t really care. because i am home. nothing matters now.<br><br>\r\n\r\nthree hours and forty-one minutes passes...<br><br>\r\n\r\nk-90 holds court as we charge in place as one. the glorious bass rattles every part of me in a way that is not possible in any other environment on our beautiful planet.<br><br>\r\n\r\nthis is what it is all about. no hatred, no prejudice, no fear, no war. in here there is only love and dancing.<br><br>\r\n\r\nivory is kissing alan and it\\\'s beautiful, even though i\\\'d rather be with her myself. my whole life, amounting to nothing more than a few possessions in an overpriced yet shitty apartment, suffices now.<br><br>\r\n\r\nthere is nothing that we cannot do. no hurdle that we cannot overcome. let\\\'s get osama and george w in here and they will never fight again. fight? hell they\\\'d be hugging by dawn.<br><br>\r\n\r\nno-one who knows this feeling could ever hate.<br><br>\r\n\r\nand there\\\'s richard. amusing, keen richard who never gives up. he\\\'s coming over to me and smiling, like that guy clay who i hope gets a recording contract even though he didn\\\'t win.<br><br>\r\n\r\nwe hug and he hands me a drink. i chug back a couple of mouthfuls and it is divine. ice cold, with little chewy bits.<br><br>\r\n\r\n\\\"that\\\'s gorgeous man. you\\\'re the best. what is it?\\\"<br><br>\r\n\r\nand there\\\'s a strange sensation coming over me, something i can\\\'t quite place yet... no wait, oh god it couldn\\\'t be, could it...?<br><br>\r\n\r\n\\\"orange juice dude! good for ya!\\\" he grins back at me.<br><br>\r\n\r\nfour seconds passes...<br><br>\r\n\r\nyou absolute cunt.<br><br>\r\n\r\na matter of moments for me to come down. a matter of weeks for his face to completely heal. a matter of months until i am allowed back into the club.<br><br>\r\n\r\nwhy is there always one?<br><br>\r\n'),(3361,'<p>she came to pick me up at 4pm.</p>\r\n<p>she drove her white car to the front of my house, where i grow rocket and other nice things.</p>\r\n<p>we greeted one another, and i put my seatbelt on. we were gong to pick up my lover from her house, which is located just over the river.</p>\r\n<p>i could sense that my mother wasn\\\'t pleased with my decision to defer my studies for sixth months. i didn\\\'t know she hated being in public with me and my girlfriend.</p>\r\n<p>caitlin is turning 22. she is my younger sister. we were going out to share a meal, my sister and her partner, me and my partner, and my parents. it would be nice, i thought.</p>\r\n<p>seated, at the restaurant, between my mother and my lover, we talked for ten minutes until my mum started speaking in a loud voice\r\n<br>\r\n\\\"ALANA MAKE SUZI STOP TOUCHING YOU I AM FEELING EMBARRASSED AND UNCOMFORTABLE AND YOU MUST STOP BECAUSE LOOK AT YOU, PEOPLE ARE STARING AND LAUGHING AT YOU SO MAKE SUZI STOP HOLDING YOUR HAND\\\".\r\n<br>\r\n<p>my mum looks like she is going to hit me if i do not comply. i do want to be thumped in public by my homophobic mother in a public place because of holding my lover\\\'s hand.</p>\r\n<p>i cry, i do not mean to, i cannot help it and i cannot fight it she is hurting me through her hate.</p>\r\n<p>my mother leaves the table after more yelling at me. i am horrified. she leaves my sister\\\'s birthday dinner. she drives home, alone, before we have ordered our food, and leaving my lover and i without a way to return home.</p>\r\n<p>i leave the building for some air. i continue to cry. i smoke a cigarette and remember how fucked some families are.</p>\r\n<p>later, my father tells me that my mother will not wish to talk to me nor see me for a while. i know this.</p>\r\n<p>this morning, afterward, i feel pain. i feel exhaustion. this is all i wish to tell.</p>'),(3362,'GIF89aâ€™Ã¶Å¾:YJÂ¶MFvâ€ KO?Ã‰ÃŠpÂ¿â€¡Ã>bÃ’C?Â§P?Â­ÃÃ‡â‚¬TÃ£62xÂ°Ã Aâ€œ~â€”(Ã¢Â³Ã§2Â Ã£Ã â€“)ÃÃ™a_Å½Ã€â€™JÃ²0iPDÂ¥Ã‰\\Â±KÃ‚FÃ§1â€ºÂ´%?Ã£ÃFGWÃ‚;Å’Â«Å¾RÃ— hÃ—ÃÃ€Â»sÂ´[dËœ mË†?;AÂ®Ãƒ|?ÃŽ6PÃ Alâ€ºÃ¸J?Ã˜\nÃ•Â¼EÂ°kA(<â‚¬?%[Ã±ÃŠmÃ€ â‚¬Æ’Ã’I%.AÃ€Æ’Â¹Ã’Â¸â€ºÂ­=Â¯ÃƒÃ¤Â°y\'â€¢L*JHÂ¡TÃ¿ ÃžU$YJÃ™â€â€Æ’0NÃŒQÃ’4 Â¨â€ž=Å’â€™â€œiÂ³Â¹ÃƒÃŒ8Ã=Â²Ã”\"lÂ¼â€˜â€ Ã¼Â¡]lÅ¡â€ UÂ¨Ã€`Ã=2Ãœp;bÂ Ã›QÃˆIEk_=Ã€Ã£ÂºÃ˜Ã¡+Ã” L\ZÃ¡â‚¬?Â¶Â¥5Ã=1`Ã‡o;y+Ãƒ5`ABÃ”]IÃˆBÅ“\r Â¡Â³F$Â¦XÃ£&Bâ€œ!Ãž$@qxPX\Z8Â©Â¸Ã¡?â€˜Ã¸iâ‚¬dXÅ¡5AÃ…Å½+ÃžHs]8Ã€dZ=Ã…s/J%â€¹bâ‚¬5?Xâ€™Ã„Ã“Ã•CÃ½Å½@Â¥i9Ã¤P?IÂ²ÂªÂ¿AÅ“BG?Ã¨â‚¬JFEâ€žRÂ­Ã¼Ã `+ÃÅ Ã’Ã¤Â±ÃŸ;â€¢Ã€â€˜Ë†Ã’â€œ9MÃ¶Â¢â€”ÂµÃ¶CÂ½Ã¦Â¹,.ÃŒ	\ZÅ’Å s%Ãâ€¡Xâ€VLGÂ¨Ã—\'Âµ)yl%ÃœÃŒ9Â£Ã¿(QnÃ²â€”Ã©{)`Ã¡ÃŽYtÃªÃ˜â€”5Â­â€°ÂºÂ  \n2Ã›$Â¼}fs.â€”Ã²â€;Ãžâ€Â»ÂµaÅ½nÂ´Ã¿Ãq ÃˆÃ‰yN7y?Ã­k_SÃ‡Ã‰Ã¬ÃµÅ“sÂ®Ãƒ$@IdÃœÂ«