the commentator as\r\nit was originally intended,\r\nfor giving multiple P.O.V. on\r\nevents.<BR> <B>nice</B>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(333,303,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','oooh, angry detractor.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(334,310,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','le the entire reason I \r\nstarted playing the violin at \r\nage 8 was because I couldn\\\'t \r\nsing. I have always and \r\nforever wanted to be able to \r\nsing. the closest I could get \r\nwas playing the violin, which \r\nthen became my life for the \r\nnext 12 years. la \r\nlalalalalaaaa!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(335,307,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','hey le, I didn\\\'t get into a \r\nfight, I was singing an old \r\nLita Ford song. so don\\\'t \r\nworry. I didn\\\'t have time to \r\nget really drunk so I didn\\\'t \r\nget to brawl with \r\nsay....Jason W. Also, I was \r\nso compelled by Winston \r\nSmith, I didn\\\'t know who he \r\nwas but I demanded to know \r\nhis name. Caleb introduced us \r\nand we chatted for a moment. \r\nThen he walked away and Caleb \r\ntold me about the Dead \r\nKennedys stuff. I nearly \r\ncried on the spot, for real. \r\nLaura B had a blast, she \r\nloves geeks. She wants to \r\nsell clothes to geeks. So you \r\nshould come hang out with us \r\nsometime because she is super \r\nlaid back and nice.\r\n\r\nI wish I could have stayed \r\nthere longer.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(336,310,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sean','i work with kelly green, and\r\nnever appreciated her parents\\\'\r\nsense of humor until tonight.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(337,307,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','what is the dead kennedys\r\nthing that made you cry on the\r\nspot?',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(338,307,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.winstonsmith.\r\ncom/gallery/albums/big/dk_fran\r\nkenchrist.html\\\">THIS</a>, \r\nbeing one of my first \r\nmemories forever imprinted on \r\nmy brain. My sister \r\nthankfully hung out with \r\nskate punks when I was a wee \r\nlass, and she had a pile of \r\nDK vinyl that I would \r\nsecretly listen to when \r\nnobody was looking after me. \r\nWarped my mind forever, \r\nSaturday Night Holocaust and \r\nHoliday in Cambodia.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(339,307,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>As a child, the first album\r\nI ever saved up my meager\r\nallowance to purchase was the\r\nDead Kennedys album \\\"Give Me\r\nConvenience or Give Me\r\nDeath.\\\"  It was my\r\nintroduction to the world of\r\nblowing mad cash on music and\r\nalso of censorship.  My\r\nparents took it from me and\r\nsold it to one of those \\\"We\r\nBuy CD\\\'s\\\" places and didn\\\'t\r\neven give me the money.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>I asked them why.  They\r\nsaid because it had a song on\r\nit called too drunk to fuck. \r\nI think their motives were\r\nironic.  Conceivably, they\r\ndidn\\\'t want me to be\r\ninfluenced to go out and get\r\ntoo drunk to fuck.  Honestly,\r\nI don\\\'t think it was as bad as\r\nit sounded.  I don\\\'t have to\r\nbe very drunk to be unable to\r\nfuck.  Of course, I am beyond\r\nthe stage of desperate\r\nhorniness.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>My mom also stole my most\r\nprecious combat boots\r\nem-blazoned with the words\r\n\\\"Punks Not Dead\\\" on the sides\r\nlike a corporate sport shoe\r\nlogo.  Funny thing about that\r\nwas I wore them for well over\r\na year.  I think she was\r\nstaring at them on the floor\r\none day and must have just\r\ngotten sick of me leaving them\r\naround.  They used to hide\r\nthem whenever I left them out,\r\nmy mom and my step dad.  They\r\nwere such fuckers of\r\nroommates.  I will probably be\r\nas bad one day.</P>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(340,312,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'<b>joker</b>','sometimes i think that the \r\nwhole point of meditation, is \r\nexactly that.  that is to \r\nsay, to slow down your mind \r\njust enough, more than \r\nenough, to see who you are \r\n(and aren\\\'t).',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(341,312,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','coincidence?: \r\n<P>yesterday i missed going to\r\nthe gym.  i came home very\r\ntired and unable to sleep\r\nbecause (presumably) i drank a\r\ncup of coffee late in the\r\nafternoon.  i lay in bed tired\r\nlistening to the neighborhood\r\ndog bark very loud.</P>\r\n<P><TT>\r\nrobotec9:> every time i go to\r\nbed, the rottweiler starts\r\nbarking like the baskerville\r\nhound.\r\n</TT></P>\r\n\r\n<P>then i got up and\r\ncomplained about it some.  i\r\ndecided to meditate.  it is\r\ndeeply disturbing to have an\r\nunfulfilled urge to get bad\r\nenergy out.  i had not\r\nmeditated in a long time.  it\r\nwas nice.  i didn\\\'t have the\r\nproblem of noise distractions\r\nthat i used to have.  i was\r\nable to keep the noise out of\r\nmy mind.</P>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(342,209,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sawks','too late, she has been \r\nassimilated by melbourne\r\n\r\nw00p ass',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(343,313,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','<P>breakfast!</P>\r\n<P>coffee, bagel with warm \r\ngoat cheese and avocado \r\nslices. Giant cup of fresh \r\ngrapefruit juice with 2500mg \r\nof vitamin c tablets.</P>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(344,314,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','I\\\'ll clear them... Send \r\nlove...',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(345,314,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','I\\\'ll clear them... Send love \r\nfrom me...',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(346,313,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Joanna','I missed breakfast because I \r\ngot up late and had to run to \r\nwork.  However, later I was \r\ninvestigating Glenfield Mall \r\n(as part of my job, I swear - \r\nI work for the city council \r\nand we\\\'re going to be doing a \r\ntraveling roadshow of \r\ninformation about a \r\nbeachwater project we\\\'re \r\ninvolved in and I\\\'m going to \r\nbe putting the display in the \r\nmall) and I just about wet \r\nmyself in glee when i came \r\nacross a Dunk\\\'n Donuts.  \r\nThere is only one other \r\nDunk\\\'n Donuts Shop in all of \r\nNew Zealand, you see, and I \r\nhaven\\\'t had them in six years \r\nsince I left Japan.  So I was \r\nvery excited, and needless to \r\nsay that was my highly \r\nnutritious breakfast.  ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(347,313,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','\r\ni had a big slog of wet socks \r\nfor breakfast. honest! as \r\nsoon as i got up, i shuffled \r\ninto my kitchen, which had \r\nflooded overnight, and instead \r\nof a nice cup of iron woman \r\ntea for breakfast, i stepped \r\ninto cold, not so friendly, \r\nrainwater. in my socks, so it \r\nwas extra sneaky.\r\n\r\ni also had some hippy cereal \r\n(organic golden flax by health \r\nvalley, yum yum!) and some \r\nricemilk. \r\n\r\n*smooch*',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(348,314,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sic','if you read this before you \r\nhead down to LA...drop \r\nby...well wishes',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(349,312,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'uhuru','I love drinking alcohol.  I \r\nnever used to understand the \r\nconcept of alcoholism until I \r\ngot into the professional \r\nworld and began \\\"going out \r\nfor drinks\\\" on a fairly \r\nregular basis.  It\\\'s a \r\nrelease you have to work hard \r\nfor otherwise, i.e. ride your \r\nbike up some hills, write a \r\nsong and play it, meditate \r\nfor a long time, scream and \r\nyell and jump up and down, \r\njust put some effort into \r\nsomething.  Release.  Release \r\nthrough alcohol is very \r\npassive.  All you do is \r\naccept the substance into \r\nyour body and subtle things \r\nloosen in your consciousness, \r\nrelaxation automatically \r\nbegins to pervade your \r\nsenses, it\\\'s sickening \r\nreally.  I guess I\\\'m writing \r\nthis because I\\\'m a little \r\nhung over.  I drank a whole \r\nbottle of wine last night.  I \r\ndidn\\\'t think I was a whole \r\nbottle type of girl.  But I \r\nhold my booze pretty well, I \r\nguess. The thing that \r\ndisturbs me is not \r\nhungoverness, it\\\'s...well, I \r\nkind of like the feeling, the \r\nfuzzy slowness, deliberate \r\nmovements.  I don\\\'t feel \r\nbad.  I feel quiet.  I\\\'ve \r\nbeen getting a lot of work \r\ndone.  I feel like people \r\nlike me when I\\\'m in this post-\r\ndrunk phase, I\\\'m calm, \r\nmelancholy, ironic.  It makes \r\nme think of Hemingway and \r\nFitzgerald and how they just \r\ngot completely tanked every \r\nday, maybe after writing, \r\nmaybe before.  For Hemingway, \r\nprobably after.  For \r\nFitzgerald, I think it was \r\nbefore, during, and after.  \r\nTheir stories often revolve \r\naround people drinking.  And \r\nall the time I was growing up \r\nreading those books, I never \r\nunderstood the power of \r\ndrunkenness, the power of red \r\nwine to release something in \r\nme that\\\'s caught.  Now I \r\nunderstand.  Does that make \r\nme an alcoholic? I feel like \r\nI made love to that wine last \r\nnight, drank it down like \r\ncups of gold.  I sang and \r\nplayed and drank wine.  \r\nSomehow I feel that I\\\'m \r\nletting some part of myself \r\ndown, getting this involved \r\nwith alcohol.  But part of \r\nme--the budding alky, I \r\nguess--doesn\\\'t ever want to \r\ngive up that cheap ticket to \r\nrelease.  Since I\\\'m going to \r\nVegas this weekend, now isn\\\'t \r\nreally the time to get on the \r\nwagon.  ',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(350,316,'2003-02-28 09:38:46',464,'Kiki','Arnie!  This is an outrage!  \r\nI did not write this, I \r\ndislike doodads! (I do want \r\nto take credit for the haiku, \r\nhowever).  You are totally \r\nbusted, Arnold, this is \r\nAppropriation of Name and \r\nPublicity Placing Person in \r\nFalse Light and you are \r\nliable for damages according \r\nto the Restatement Second of \r\nTorts sections 652C and 652E. \r\nYou just wait until Austin \r\ncomes back. He\\\'ll restore \r\njustice by properly crediting \r\nyou for this work.  I did \r\nnotice your dashing tan, \r\nthough.  Austin, succor!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(351,316,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'arnie','excuse me, but methinks I have \r\nbeen falsely accused.  In fact-\r\n- I think it was you who wrote \r\nthe \\\"welcome home\\\" entry.  I \r\ncan tell by your well placed \r\nsemi-colon.\r\n',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(352,317,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'DZA','good game... ;)',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(353,317,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Adam\\\'s Uncle Tim','doesn\\\'t know what to say, but \r\nhe likes the article, and is \r\nquite familiar with The \r\nCastro... Remembering the \r\ntime I made Adam sit \r\nthrough \\\"Manufacturing \r\nConsent\\\" at the Castro \r\nTheater.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(354,316,'2003-02-28 09:38:46',464,'Kiki','J\\\'accuse,Arnie! You admitted \r\nin the driveway...you cannot \r\nretract now.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(355,315,'2003-02-28 09:38:46',464,'Kiki','Good use of semi-colon, \r\nArnie.  I couldn\\\'t have done \r\nit better myself.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(356,317,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'arnold','can you pick me up the new \r\nLetter E album at Aquarius \r\nRecords on Valencia and 22nd or \r\nsomewhere around there?\r\n\r\nSee you soon\r\n',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(357,317,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','austin can we be friends?',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(358,317,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','Mothers rest. has a new crew, \r\nand they are cute as ever. I \r\nsaw a friend of yours there.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(359,316,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','very funny <TT>=-)</TT>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(360,318,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'<b>joker</b>','if it were too much to ask, \r\nshe would have asked',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(361,319,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'dj1_luna','I agree. Austin i missed \r\nhere. I cheer you on yer no \r\nmo smoking decision.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(362,321,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'<b>joker</b>','wow! that\\\'s cool.  and you\\\'re \r\na real \\\"artist\\\".  that is to \r\nsay, you make \\\"art\\\" in \r\nthe \\\"arts and crafts\\\" sense \r\nof the word art.  you paint.  \r\nnow that you mention it, i \r\ndon\\\'t know too many unhappy \r\npainters.  even the trailers \r\nfor pollock that i\\\'ve seen \r\nsuggest that he painted \r\nbecause it made him happy.  \r\nooo.  maybe that\\\'s it.  do \r\nyou paint because it makes \r\nyou happy? or is happiness a \r\npre-condition of painting?',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(363,318,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Joanna','where do I apply?',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(364,321,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','it was my understanding that\r\ndza paints when he is not\r\nhappy.  he is happy now.  he\r\ndoesn\\\'t paint now.  girls are\r\nnot interested now.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(365,320,'2003-05-10 16:09:14',79,'yeti','\\\"I was hip once.\\\"\r\nThat about sums up how I feel \r\nsome days. ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(366,321,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'DZA','hmm.  I don\\\'t think i\\\'ve been \r\nsignificantly depressed for \r\nover a year.  And I haven\\\'t \r\npainted in a year.  I swear \r\nit\\\'s the job though.  And \r\nwomen, well, that\\\'s always a \r\nslow moving front because of \r\nmy contentness with \r\nsingledom, or my passiveness.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(367,321,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'<p><b>joker</b>','so, no, wait.  when exactly \r\ndo you paint?  swinney says \r\nit\\\'s when you\\\'re depressed \r\nand you said you haven\\\'t \r\npainted in a year.  so, if \r\nyou don\\\'t create (paint) when \r\nyou\\\'re \\\"stable\\\", doesn\\\'t that \r\nsuggest that you <b>only</b> \r\ncreate  when you\\\'re \r\n<b>unstable</b>???!!!<br>\r\ni have no further questions, \r\nyour honor. (<i>confident \r\nstroll back to the \r\nprosecutor\\\'s table and seat \r\nself with a flourish</i>).',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(368,318,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Author','apply for what ? ',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(369,317,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','who did you see there?',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(370,321,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'DZA','in art there are no answers, \r\nonly questions... ;)',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(371,321,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'DZA','<P>OK.  To clear this up (I\\\'m \r\nnot sure if i\\\'ll be writing \r\nin austin\\\'s journal again any \r\ntime soon):</P>\r\n<P>Fact: I am happy most of \r\nthe time.</P>\r\n<P>Fact: I paint whether I\\\'m \r\nhappy or depressed.</P>\r\n<P>Fact: Girls find me \r\nattractive because I \r\npaint.</P>\r\n<P>Fact: Girls find me \r\nunattractive because I am \r\nhappy/stable(=boring) most of \r\nthe time.</P>\r\n<P>Fact: Are we clear?!</P>\r\n   ',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(372,323,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','i am blowing my nose.\r\ni am scratching my eyes.\r\ni am dying of allergies.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(373,321,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'<p><b>joker</b>','yo dza.  chill and don\\\'t \r\nleave.  i was only being \r\nplayful.  you sounded so \r\nhappy, that i thought you \r\ncould easily take a little \r\nneedling.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(374,323,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'<p><b>joker</b>','i am passing gas.  i ate \r\nbeans at the olive garden.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(375,323,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'<TT>aus</TT>','<P>I drank shiner.\r\n<BR>I have a head ache.\r\n<BR>I feel like barf.\r\n</P>\r\n',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(376,321,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'DZA','Oh, that\\\'s cool.  At least I \r\nhave like 5 comments now...',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(377,323,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','<p>I sold my soul to the \r\ndevil.\r\nI pay him nearly a grand per \r\nmonth.\r\nI am a resident of the west \r\nside.</P>\r\n',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(378,323,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','<P>I am constantly saddened, \r\ngrateful, and amused.</P>\r\n<img \r\nsrc=\\\"http://fonem.org/invadeti\r\nny.jpg\\\">',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(379,323,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'robotec9','<CENTER><P><TT>i am\r\nconstantly<BR>\r\nfalling in love<BR>\r\nand falling out of<BR>\r\nlove</TT></P></CENTER>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(380,325,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','I started to eat carrots \r\ninstead of smoking. i am \r\nafraid my skin will turn \r\norange. These things \r\nhappen  you know. I don\\\'t \r\nknow why, but they do. ',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(381,325,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'robo','you forgot about matsukaze\\\'s\r\nthird category of things you\r\nhave not noticed you have not\r\nnoticed.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(382,324,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'<B>robotec9</B>','<CENTER><U><font\r\ncolor=\\\"CC3366\\\"><strong>\r\n<P>sine sine sine. \r\n</P><P>everyone loves you. \r\n</P><P>\r\nsine sine sine, all day long.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nsine is so cool.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nsine is so great.  \r\n</P><P>\r\ni love sine. \r\n</P><P>\r\nsine is a sexy bitch. \r\n</P><P>\r\n<a\r\nhref=\\\"http://fonem.org/cam/\\\">sine\r\nget naked</a>.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nit must be nice to be\r\nsine.</P>\r\n</strong></font></U></CENTER>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(383,279,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kittykat','well 1st of all, i haven\\\'t \r\nseen yer site in awhile...and \r\ni like it.  2nd of all, i HAD \r\nto tell you that the above is \r\nthe best description of BMG\\\'s \r\nname i have ever heard.  i \r\nlaughed my ass off.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(384,327,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'<TT>robotec9</TT>','<TT>Q:  having checked out a\r\ncvs module and finished, run\r\nupdate, and committed changes,\r\nis there a particular way of\r\nremoving the module from the\r\naccount that checked it out,\r\nor does one just remove\r\nit?</TT>',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(385,327,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'<TT>robotec10</TT>','<TT>A: Why yes, as a matter of\r\nfact.</TT>  \r\n<PRE>\r\n(cvs detach MODULE_NAME)\r\n</PRE>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(386,332,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<B>stateless?</B>\r\n<P>stop trying to be other\r\npeoples work.  stop following\r\nthose incessantly uncreative\r\ndesign sites.  they suck. \r\nones in thousands.  do\r\nsomething for yourself and\r\ndon\\\'t compare it to anyone\r\nelse.</P>\r\n<P>stop whining and start\r\ntalking loud.</P>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(387,332,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'dj1_luna','it has nothing to do with \r\nthose incestuous sites.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(388,332,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'dj1_luna','i was not whining. that\\\'s \r\nmisreading of what i wrote.',5,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(389,332,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','i have been hearing about this\r\nsite of yours since i met you,\r\ncoming up on two years.  just\r\nput the fucker up.  nobody\r\ncares what it looks like and\r\nyou will feel better after you\r\ncalm down and stop thinking\r\npeople are out to think you\r\nare not creative.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(390,332,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'LinearBenwa','\\\"stop whining and start \r\ntalking loud.\\\" Yeah, that\\\'s \r\ngonna be my slogan from \r\nnow on. Yeah.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(391,332,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','i really like you alot, \r\njuan.  i just want to see you \r\nhappy.  sometimes this drives \r\nme to give you advice.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(392,333,'2003-02-28 09:38:46',464,'kiki','it was a moment of \r\nliberation, considering we \r\nwere only there for an hour \r\nbefore swinney was asking to \r\ngo home, but an hour was \r\nenough, as it seems we all \r\nhad other late night agendas. \r\nLots of musicians there and \r\nthe music was excellent, as \r\nwas the robot dance.  I have \r\nto ask myself: why don\\\'t i go \r\nout more often?  The lyman \r\ncooler is the spice of life, \r\nand law school is big doughy \r\nballs of overboiled gnocchi.  \r\nThe lyman cooler is the \r\nincense and bong hit of life, \r\nand law school is the stale \r\nodor of dusty federal \r\nreporters and congressional \r\nquarterlys.  the lyman cooler \r\nis the squealing wail of \r\nfeedback and flailing of \r\ndrums, and law school is the \r\nlow hum of flourescent lights.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(393,333,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'LinearB','BMG forgot. I miss you too.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(394,333,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Joanna','It sounds like a very cool \r\nparty.  I think everything is \r\nclassier when it has a name \r\nattached to it, whether it be \r\nthe venue or the theme or \r\nwhatever.  And to spread the \r\nparty name around everywhere, \r\nnow that\\\'s just extra \r\nspecial.  ',5,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(395,333,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Beiemjei','Yes, Yes LinearB, so sorry. --\r\nStars has a few new faces \r\nworking the counters, I \r\nthinks there is a 17 year old \r\nboy working there... Still, \r\nstars is stars, young or \r\nold... I have found that El \r\nSol La Luna makes a great \r\nbreakfast but they aren\\\'t \r\nopen 24hrs; nor are they 5 \r\nblocks away...',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(396,335,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'GOD','about the light, <b>I</b> give\r\nup.',5,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(397,335,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Satan','MuaHaHaHaHahaaaaaaaaugh!',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(398,333,'2003-02-28 09:38:46',464,'kiki','historical note:  Pat, the \r\noriginal occupant and \r\nvisionary of Lyman Cooler, \r\ncame up with the nom.  Lyman, \r\nthe street, + (lime + lemon) +  \r\nrefreshment. And somehow it \r\nstuck.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(399,333,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'arnold','It was named after the other \r\nkristien\\\'s parents.  Jennifer \r\nand the now deceased Pat Lyman.\r\n',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(400,333,'2003-02-28 09:38:46',464,'kiki','not',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(401,333,'2004-07-27 05:14:09',63,'olivia sez',' houses with names are good.  \r\nparties with names are good.  \r\nmy new house in st kilda is \r\ncalled nirvana.  it is a \r\nhaunted mansion.  what more \r\ncan you ask for?',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(402,324,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','<P>It\\\'s nice to be sine when \r\nmy brain chemistry is in \r\nbalance. I just got back from \r\nVegas. It was fucking rad.</P>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(403,333,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'robotec9','well olivia, hmmm, what more\r\ncould you ask for?  let us\r\nthink for a second...  Me and\r\nSine handcuffed together to\r\nthe bed post?  i know you just\r\nwant sine, but i want you both\r\nand it was my idea.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(404,338,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'<B>robotec9</B>','<P><TT>\r\n<B>sine the gangstar</B><br>\r\nscopin\\\' lotto bill<i>z</i>\r\nfrom\r\nafar<br>\r\nwhat\\\'s that in your dek<br>\r\ni\\\'m going to give you heck<br>\r\nsteal your kizzash<br>\r\nand leave you with the\r\nsmell<br>\r\nof smoking hasheesh</tt></p>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(405,337,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Joanna','Ooohlivia, you have \r\nabsolutely no idea how 