5 01:46:04',17,'austin','i always wondered how you met\r\nme =-)',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(430,351,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','i am heading out of town \r\nsoon... i started packing up.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(431,351,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<STRONG>****BLOWS\r\nWHISTLE****</STRONG><BR>\r\n<H1>WHOOOOOOOOT!</H1>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(432,347,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'[arcanum]','Sometimes the brightness \r\neclipses all else.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(433,348,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','<P>okay so before I was \r\ntrying to think of how to \r\ndescribe xep and qq, and all \r\nI could think of was \r\nluminescence. and gems. they \r\nare gems of people. they glow \r\nwith curiosity, and twitter \r\nwith humor. being with them \r\nmakes you want to be like \r\nthem. everything is \r\ncomfortable, your intellect \r\nis sharpened and nudged \r\naround playfully. often times \r\nyou don\\\'t even have to say \r\nmuch. facial expression as \r\nlanguage is second nature. \r\nand sometimes, thinks are \r\njust plain snarky. many of \r\nthe words xep and qq and I \r\nuse to chat at each other are \r\nnonsense words, \r\nlike \\\"meepleemnurblx\\\" \r\nand \\\"fanfenfreep\\\".</P>\r\n<P>and just now, on icb:</P>\r\n<P><xep> elly just called and \r\nsaid she is at 8th and market \r\nwith no pants<BR>\r\n<xep> ok time to bring \r\npants<BR>\r\n[=Sign-off=] xep \r\n(xep@pvorus.logy.org) has \r\nsigned off.<BR>\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(434,348,'2004-07-27 05:14:09',63,'olivia sez','<p>we were talking about \r\ntravelling around australia \r\nand stupid german tourists \r\nbathing in crocodile infested \r\nwaters and riding motorbikes \r\nwhen eric said, \\\"i\\\'ll teach \r\nyou to ride a motorbike.  i\\\'ll \r\ncome by tomorrow\\\".  i said \r\nsure, knowing that he \r\nwouldn\\\'t, but still liking the \r\nidea and not being interested \r\nin giving up the pretense that \r\nit would happen.</p>\r\n<p>the next morning i was \r\nawakened by a helmeted \r\neric, suited up and ready \r\nto teach me to ride a real \r\nmotorbike.</p>\r\n<p>after i rode up and \r\ndown elly\\\'s street a few \r\ntimes, i got on the back \r\nand rode over to pick up \r\nxep, and then on an \r\nextended tour of san \r\nfrancisco, ending up at \r\nxep\\\'s circus school to \r\nwatch a performance, \r\nfollowed by sushi.</p>\r\n<p>eric and xep are a \r\nspecial breed of person.  \r\nthey made me feel at ease \r\nand they showed me \r\nincredible hospitality and \r\nthey\\\'re smart and they\\\'re \r\nbeautiful.</p>\r\n<p>that\\\'s all i have to \r\nsay.</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(435,355,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'<i>joker</i>','you\\\'re very accomodating, \r\naustin.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(436,355,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sic','my ex is from orange...see why \r\nwe didnt work out?',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(437,355,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','but! Shellac was awesome, \r\nright? ',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(438,355,'2004-07-27 05:14:09',63,'olivia sez','<p>i live upstairs from you.  \r\nyes, i think you\\\'ve seen me \r\nbefore.</p>',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(439,355,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'The Date','What do you mean \\\"without \r\nalienating...\\\"',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(440,355,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'the date','I was really tired and needed \r\nto go home.  Austin needed to \r\nstay and support his brother\\\'s \r\nband-worship.  I had no money \r\nleft, but he put me in a taxi \r\nand sent me back to my car, so \r\nI could sleep.  Isn\\\'t that \r\nnice?  No one has to feel \r\nguilty that wa',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(441,355,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','this is the most tired Monday\r\ni can remember.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(442,355,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'mike','Never underestimate a metaphor\r\n',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(443,357,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'the black chair','<P>i heard about that phone\r\ncall. arnie said a suburban\r\nfilled with screaming drunken\r\ngirls and he wanted to know\r\nwho was driving, \\\"just watch\r\nthe road, i told them.\\\"</P>\r\n\r\n<P>arnie had been recording\r\ncountry music all night.  he\r\nwas drunk but not screaming. \r\nhe had a wonderful smile of a\r\nman who had created something\r\nand it had gone much better\r\nthan planned.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i listened to the song.  i\r\nwanted more songs.  i wish\r\narnie recorded more.  i like\r\nhim when he is really happy\r\nand excited about something\r\nthat went well.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i like most people in that\r\nstate of well accomplishment. \r\nhubbard was in that state\r\ntoo.  the stranger with the\r\nvocals, i am not sure what\r\nstate he was in.  i am\r\nguessing he just thought he\r\nwanted to go home.  he didn\\\'t\r\nknow he was already home.  not\r\nyet anyway.  if he sticks\r\naround and records some more\r\nsongs, soon enough he will\r\nrealize where he is.</P>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(444,357,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kiks','i am shamed into coming over \r\nto hear the fruits of the \r\nmagic song harvest.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(445,357,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'arnold','oh my god where have I been?\r\n',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(446,357,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'arnold','oh my god where have I been?\r\n',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(447,355,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Scott','They were playing the quiet \r\nsong about how sad his \r\ngirlfriend was when his aunt \r\ndied, and how she might be \r\ndancing with his mother in \r\nheaven, and the crowd was \r\nyelling insults at the band \r\ntrying to get their \r\nattention. I would have found \r\nthat offensive no matter who \r\nthe band was.',5,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(448,355,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','i feel bad that i even wrote\r\nthis.  i had a really\r\nstressful weekend.  i should\r\nbe bound and gagged to stop me\r\nfrom speaking when that\r\nhappens.  stress equals a\r\nnegative lack of direction for\r\nme.  why can\\\'t i just be in\r\nsanta fe right now?  i want to\r\nhave breakfast in that wierd\r\nrestaurant with the half\r\nfloors and theme rooms.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(449,358,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'