to throw beer \r\nbottles at the apartment \r\ncomplex next door to my \r\nhouse.  just lob them over \r\nthe three story wall and into \r\nthe court yard.</P>\r\n<P>those bottles, i stole \r\nfrom seven eleven</P>\r\n<P>i used to <TT>*work*</TT> \r\nat seven eleven.</P>\r\n<P>i was violent often.</P>\r\n<P>i think it was the job.</P>\r\n<P>this comment is burn! burn!\r\n</P>',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(600,407,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','pretty often. why do you \r\nask?',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(601,406,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i didn\\\'t know panda bears \r\ntook showers.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(602,400,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jim','the key will be in the usual \r\nplace?',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(603,407,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','hi, i\\\'m elly. i freak out a \r\nlot. often i sob openly. s\\\'ok!',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(604,407,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'feltchBoy','I knew ashton. Not that well. \r\nI freaked a few months ago, \r\nfist in monitor, tears on \r\ncheek and chin. I tried \r\nbouncing a scanner off the \r\nhardwood floors.  A friend of \r\nmine adds scars to his arms, \r\nthis is not healthy; he is a \r\nrock-star so it goes with/ \r\nadds to the tude. I remember \r\nthrowing real tantrums when I \r\nwas younger, much much worse \r\nthen. I am glad I have evened \r\nthose out. I used to blow \r\nshit up. Then I found a job \r\nwhere I could blow shit up \r\nlegaly. I got out of that \r\nbiz, due to emotional cut \r\nbacks. I think that the best \r\nmethod that I have found for \r\ncontrol of these fits is long \r\nwarm/cold showers. That or \r\npunching a monitor; makes you \r\nrealize how stupid you are \r\nacting quite fast.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(605,407,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sic','every friday from 10-12',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(606,406,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sic','whats up with pandas? are they \r\nthe mascot of swinney.org?',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(607,407,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Joanna','1-2 times a year?  1-2 times \r\na month more like.  I cry, \r\nscream if I\\\'m by myself, and \r\nbreathe funny.  If I\\\'m really \r\nupset and angry, I get \r\nnauseous and retch for a long \r\ntime. ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(608,409,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Joanna','Why does Dunkndonuts sell \r\nbagels?  Does it have a \r\npolicy that it only sells \r\nfood with a hole in the \r\nmiddle? It just doesn\\\'t seem \r\nwhole.  ',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(609,412,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'<b>joker</b>','a-chooo!  a-chooo!<br>\r\nme too.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(610,412,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'LinearB','The Sexy Finger Champs are \r\nplaying? F-ck yeah, I\\\'m going.\r\n<p>So where are they playing?',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(611,411,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'<b>joker</b>','word.  i come from trailer \r\ntrash.  i grew up with it.  i \r\nwas raised in the trailer \r\ntrash capital of the world.  \r\nthis in no way softens the \r\nedge of the whiny, grating, \r\nignorant, garish sounds that \r\nnow have big important \r\ntelevision voices.  i blame \r\nyou, arsenio hall.',5,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(612,413,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'six syllables','om mani padme hum',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(613,412,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','they are playing at the \r\nredeyed fly, satty night... \r\nlate, headlining... go robot \r\ngo!!! We should talk austin \r\ninto puting up a small mp3 \r\ncollection...\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(614,410,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'who, who','speak your mind child.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(615,413,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sic','what the he-eeell is a chakras?\r\n',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(616,412,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'dj1luna','i am driving all the way back \r\nfrom fort worthless just to \r\nsee the finger champs!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(617,414,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'<b>jesse</b>','interesting commentary from \r\nHHDL: <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://tibet.com/Buddhis\r\nm/om-mantra.html\\\" \r\ntarget=\\\"_blank\\\">http://tibet.c\r\nom/Buddhism/om-mantra.html</a>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(618,413,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'mk','(he\\\'s got crabs, sic)',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(619,413,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>here is what happened.  i\r\nstarted stay up late studying\r\nfor my C class.  i began to\r\nlose sleep.  i neglected all\r\nthe tasks that think to do\r\nwhen i <b>just sit and\r\nthink</b> because i stopped\r\nhalting my day to looking for\r\nthings to do.  Hmmm, what\r\nshould i do?  i\\\'ll clean my\r\nroom.  no.  i would think, i\r\nshould be studying.  always. \r\nif i am not studying i should\r\nbe getting exercise or eating\r\nfood or with friends.  most\r\nnotably with friends.   </P>\r\n\r\n<P>the loss of sleep, the\r\nneglect of duties causing my\r\nhome to become cluttered and\r\ndirty, and constant feeling of\r\nobligation brought on by a\r\nprogramming class, all\r\ncontributed to my feeling\r\ndepressed.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i am doing better know. \r\nwhen i recongise it happening,\r\ni am already over the worst of\r\nit.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>also, i ate *way* too much\r\ngarlic in the last three\r\ndays.</P>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(620,413,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sic','1)how come you didnt tell me \r\nyou are goin to school again?\r\n2)what the he-eeel is a \r\nchakras? didnt answer my \r\nquestion homie',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(621,409,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','<p>that\\\'s sick and wrong. but,\r\nnot as wrong as popeye\\\'s\r\nselling something they call\r\n\\\"shrimp etouffe\\\" which, as far\r\nas i can tell, is a pile of\r\nrice with orange slime on top.\r\nits fraaanch, you know.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(622,414,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','i think this piece really\r\nspeaks to me. especially the\r\nstrapped to your lover and a\r\nskeleton with flaming ohms in\r\nthe background. how many times\r\nhave we all dreamed this? when\r\nwill it end?!',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(623,414,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sean dreilinger','since when is Om not good\r\nenough by itself? <a\r\nhref=\\\"http://elly.org/\\\">le</a> \r\nwhen is th field trip to check\r\nout the work of <a\r\nhref=\\\"http://swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=151.txt\\\">al\r\nmaddocks</a> in san\r\nfrancisco\\\'s buddhist\r\ntemple(s)? ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(624,413,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','</p><p>\r\ngarlic is good for colds. i \r\nhave a cold.</p><p>chakras \r\nare little sources of \r\nspinning energy in the body, \r\nbelieved to affect health and \r\nspirituality. the belief in \r\nthe chakra system in the \r\nhuman body is very ancient \r\nand spans more than one \r\nculture. <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.kheper.auz.co\r\nm/topics/chakras/chakras.htm\\\">\r\nhere\\\'s a site about \r\nchakras</a>.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(625,414,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','that field trip is NEXT\r\nweekend when i come visit.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(626,414,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','i wanna come visit too!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(627,415,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>i was listening to the\r\nradio last night and there was\r\na show interviewing the\r\ndirector of the institute of\r\nunlikely research (or\r\nsomething like that, it was on\r\nnpr).  the subject was a study\r\nof accidents done by doctors\r\nin an island community.  the\r\nradio show was examining an\r\nemergency room check in form\r\nwith a field entitled, \\\"Struck\r\nby falling coconut.\\\" \r\napparently the dangers of\r\nfalling coconut\\\'s are great in\r\ntropical areas.  a five pound\r\ncoconut with husk falling from\r\nthe likely height of 80 feet\r\nabove will gain speed to\r\napproximately 50 miles per\r\nhour.  in this senario, being\r\nhit on the head with a coconut\r\nis potentially crippling if\r\nnot deadly.</P>\r\n<P><B>watch the nutz.</B></P>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(628,415,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','when peter and i were staying \r\nin a strange bungalow on a \r\ntiny 13 acre island in the \r\ncountry of vanuatu, we were \r\nterrified by the loud \r\ncrashing and slamming noises \r\nwe sometimes heard - then we \r\nrealized they were falling \r\ncoconuts! also there were big \r\ncrabs that lived in holes in \r\nthe ground and slimy \r\ncreatures that live inside \r\nshells and are very \r\npoisonous. ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(629,415,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','<TEXT=\\\"RED\\\">\r\nI like crabs.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(630,416,'2002-04-12 05:27:03',57,'weebie','wow, this is the best swinney\r\nentry, ever. i shall keep\r\nwhisperin it to myself\r\ntonight, as i go to sleep.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(631,416,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','\\\"the best Swinney entry,\\\" are \r\nsome strong words.  i like it \r\nvery much.  but i do not like \r\ngrades.  can we just say it \r\nis \\\"all weeb ever wanted\\\"?',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(632,415,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','we spent a longtime throwing\r\nfallen coconuts at hanging\r\ncoconuts in an attempt to\r\ndislodge them from their\r\nperches.  after about an hour\r\nwe finally succeeded.  it then\r\ntook several more hours to get\r\nthe husk off because all we\r\nhad was a pocket knife and one\r\nof those crappy cheap camping\r\nshovels.  when it was finally\r\nopen we scraped the meaty bit\r\nout with our teeth, like\r\ngofers, and cooked rice in the\r\nwater that lives inside.  i\r\nthink you can tell it\\\'s going\r\nto be a good coconut when it\r\nsloshes around a lot.<p>\r\nthe eel missed the worm block\r\nentirely tonight and the\r\ngouramis ate it all.\r\n',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(633,415,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','!! the juice lady told us that\r\ncoconuts are mostly milk and\r\nno meat when they first fall\r\nfrom the tree, but the milk\r\nturns INTO the white pulp you\r\ncna eat after a while. we were\r\nin awe. the coconut you see\r\nabove was taken inside and\r\ninterrogated cruelly with a\r\nkitchen knife. or we tried to,\r\nactually. we only took sad\r\nlittle wedges out of one side\r\nbefore we collapsed from\r\nexhaustion.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(634,418,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'LinearBenway','So ein ScheissGeschichte. \r\nVielen dank fur den auskunft, \r\nnicht. ',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(635,417,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','The Deuce Deuce\r\n4016-a Maplewood\r\nAustin, TX 78722\r\n\r\nK-dog is on a journey, she\\\'ll \r\nbe back soon tho.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(636,416,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','is too.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(637,416,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','is too.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(638,418,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kirstin','Warum ist es, dass man bloss \r\nauf Deutsch redet wenn es um \r\nScheisse geh',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(639,418,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','Wo est der krappenplatz?',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(640,418,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Herr LinearB','kirstin: das moechte ich gern \r\nwissen.\r\n<p>Machen wir Herr weeb \r\nverantwortlich!',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(641,420,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>mo aussies.</P>\r\n<P>i have had lots of friends \r\nleave.  i have left lots of \r\nfriends.  why just the other \r\nday bmg was saying that i am \r\nstill one of his best friends \r\ndespite my moving to Los \r\nAngeles.  (he must be \r\nbuttering me up for \r\nsomething. <TT>;-)</TT>)</P>\r\n\r\n<P>adamajah once went to \r\ncosta rica for a very long \r\ntime.  he would send me poems \r\nthat he wrote with his \r\nfriends.  i wish i could find \r\nsome of them.  they are \r\nbacked up on my harddrive in \r\nunix format from when i \r\nexported my entire \r\nCCWF.CC.UTEXAS.EDU account a \r\ncouple years ago.  there was \r\none about \\\"Her hips swang in \r\nthe galaxial breeze\\\" that i \r\nliked very much.</P>\r\n<P>my friend kdog leaves \r\nwhere ever she is every few \r\nseasons, dejected and \r\nsearching.  i got used a long \r\ntime ago.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>my girlfriend my go to \r\ngermany for a year.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>matsukaze, i knew him for \r\na couple months before he \r\ndisappeared for months.  then \r\ni tracked him down on irc.  \r\nhe is a good friend now.  i \r\ntalk with him most day.  just \r\na sentence or too.  sometimes \r\ni go to SF and see him.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i have other friends that \r\ni see in SF occasionally.  I \r\nsee them online often.  some \r\ni don\\\'t even see \r\noccasionally.  but if i have \r\nmet them once, and i talk to \r\nthem nearly every day, that \r\nconstitutes a good \r\nfriendship.  certainly much \r\nbetter then most people i \r\nknow.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i like having my friends \r\nall over the place.  it helps \r\nme get out.  i can plan \r\nquality time with them.  like \r\nthe Zero Three Expidition to \r\nan unknown point in the south \r\nMediterranean, perhaps Turkey \r\nor Egypt.  someplace with \r\npyramids, cammels and sand.  \r\nor maybe Singapore.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>anyway, it becomes natural \r\nfeeling to have friends that \r\nare around you and friends \r\nthat are gone.  some of my \r\nbest and longest friends are \r\nnot within driving distance \r\nof my home.  but keeping them \r\nfriends makes the \r\nrelationship sweeter.  they \r\ncan age with time, and gain \r\nflavors that the new friends \r\ndon\\\'t have.</P>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(642,420,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'aus10','<B>NOTE: Singapore is not in \r\nthe south \r\nMediterranean.<BR><BR>M\\\'kay?\r\n</B>\r\n',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(643,420,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Joanna','Many of the people I love \r\nlive in Australia.  Well, at \r\nleast two or three anyways.  \r\nI\\\'m lucky because it\\\'s only a \r\nfour dollar phone call away, \r\nbut it\\\'s just a matter of \r\ncalling at the right time and \r\nnot being too drunkly \r\nincoherant when I do get \r\nthrough.  ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(644,418,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','wo ist Sie Poopenschtorie?@!',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(645,421,'2004-07-27 05:14:09',63,'olivia sez',' ahahahhah!  now here for me\r\nis swinney entry #1.  can you\r\nimagine our little heroine le\r\npumping a roof?',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(646,422,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i love you austin!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(647,270,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>a couple of red winter\r\ncrackers.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>this day has come to\r\nrepresent my friendship with\r\nkdog.  whenever i think of her\r\nnow, i think about our\r\nconversation this day.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>we talked about what it is\r\nlike to leave lovers behind\r\nand then want some kind of\r\nresolution.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>... want them to understand\r\nwhat happened to them and\r\nus.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>it also is representative\r\nof the classic, \\\"hi\\\",\r\n\\\"goodbye\\\", \\\"see you in a\r\ncouple months/years\\\", that is\r\nour friendship.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>kind of like checking\r\nin.</P>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(648,423,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'aus10','amen, my brother.<BR><BR>amen.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(649,421,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','le you are my roof lake pump \r\nbarefoot wet cold heroine.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(650,417,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'DZAstadamajah','theres a cool coffee shop \r\ndown the street too.  ',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(651,418,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'dza','jue\\\'puta!  Habla en mi \r\nlengua, pinche monos!',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(652,423,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','Now that is a nice effin\\\' \r\npicture.  Can I buy a print \r\noff you?',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(653,424,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','</p><p>\r\nyeah dude. my mom just wants \r\nme to be with peter because \r\nshe perceives peter to be \r\ndoting like my dad is to her -\r\n it\\\'s partially true, but i \r\nthink my father smothers my \r\nmom in a way that would drive \r\nme absolutely insane. i don\\\'t \r\nwant what my mom wanted. not \r\nentirely anyway. \r\n</p><p>\r\npeter and i are gently re-\r\nentering our relationship. \r\nit\\\'s lots and lots of hard \r\nwork... and unfortunately, it \r\nhasn\\\'t got much to do with my \r\nmother\\\'s dreamworld of true \r\nloves and fat babies, \r\nof \\\'meant to be together\\\' and \r\nall that. i\\\'m not sure i \r\nwas \\\'meant to be\\\' with \r\nanyone - being alone was \r\nnever as difficult as being \r\nin love, and isn\\\'t love \r\nsupposed to be easy?\r\n</p><p>\r\nwho knows, maybe mom is right \r\nand it all comes down to fate \r\nand everything else that we \r\nbuild around it is just zen \r\nperception bullshit to make \r\nthings seem like we planned \r\nthem. ego.\r\n</p><p>\r\nshrug! ',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(654,423,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','no need to buy brother... \r\nwhat format do you need? \r\ntiff? eps? do you want it on \r\npaper? its a digi pic... and \r\nit wasnt touched up... so it \r\nshould come out pretty nice \r\non paper... lemme know...',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(655,424,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','rad. you have such clarity. \r\n<p>i turn into a stuttering \r\nmoron when trying to talk to \r\nmy mother about my life \r\ndecisions, so as a result, i \r\nnever talk to her at all.hmm, \r\ncome to think of it, i\\\'m not \r\nall that good at verbal \r\ncommunication with people in \r\ngeneral! hah.</p><p>what \r\nstrange, wonderful eggs we \r\nall are.</p> ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(656,425,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'<b>joker</b>','i am highly suspicious of \r\nhistory.  it\\\'s subjective and \r\nderiving meanings from it \r\nseems no different to me than \r\nan oracle reading omens \r\n(<i>not to suggest that i \r\ndon\\\'t believe there is any \r\nvalue to oracles and omens, \r\nbut i notice folks tend to \r\ntreat divining differently \r\nthan history, when they share \r\nmany similar qualities</i>).  \r\nthere seems to be little \r\ndoubt that history is a by-\r\nproduct of time (hee).  other \r\nthan that, what can one say \r\nabout it, with certainty?',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(657,426,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','we\\\'ve been over this but i\\\'ll \r\nkeep on, because i like to \r\nthink about it too.\r\n</p><p>\r\nlately i have thought \r\nthat \\\'happiness\\\' is not the \r\nsame as \\\'contentedness.\\\' and \r\nbecause of that i have \r\nthought, happiness for me \r\ncomes in bursts of pure joy, \r\nmomentary, finite. like you \r\ndescribe. which makes me \r\nthink that contentedness is \r\nsomething to strive for, \r\nwhere as happiness is kind of \r\na crap shoot.\r\n</p><p>\r\n(do they have the \r\nphrase \\\'crap shoot\\\' in \r\naustralia? a gamble.)\r\n</p><p>\r\nalso, my friend <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.feh.com\\\">cale\r\nb</a> pointed out recently \r\nthat a lot of people think to \r\nbe HAPPY you must be having \r\n<i>fun</i>. allow me to \r\npostulate that though having \r\nfun may make you happy, fun \r\nis not required to achieve \r\nhappiness. sometimes, \r\nhappiness and contentedness \r\nare achieved via very unfun \r\npaths. or seemingly tedious \r\nand mundane tasks. \r\n</p><p>\r\nright. these are my two \r\nrecurring thoughts regarding \r\nhappiness lately.\r\n</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(658,426,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'puppy','<p>oooooo - happiness. i \r\nalways think about this. \r\n\r\n<p>for those who don\\\'t know, \r\ni was recently married and \r\ndid so in the catholic \r\nchurch. they have \r\nrequirements that the couple \r\nhave pre-marital counsuling \r\nand such... one of the topics \r\nwas about happiness and the \r\nexpectations of marriage. i \r\nwas not expecting to hear the \r\nhosts of such a talk say that \r\nyou can\\\'t be happy all the \r\ntime. but that\\\'s what they \r\nsaid. i mean, i know that, \r\nyet i wasn\\\'t expecting some \r\nbig, faceless organization to \r\ntell me something like that. \r\ni expected them to teach us \r\nwhat all of the sit-coms and \r\nall the other tv shows tell \r\nus: \\\"something is wrong with \r\nyou if you are not happy.\\\"\r\n\r\n<p>but that\\\'s not what they \r\nsaid. in fact, they were \r\nadament about the notion \r\nof \\\"un-happiness\\\" and that it \r\nis physically impossible to \r\nbe happy all the time. \r\nthe \\\"bad\\\" marriage is one \r\nthat strives to be happy all \r\nof the time; that marriage \r\nwill not meet that goal. the \r\nhosts taught that it was ok \r\nto strive to only \r\nbe \\\"content.\\\"\r\n\r\nanyway... that\\\'s my two \r\ncents. and, if i may \r\nadd, \\\"it\\\'s\\\" not about \r\nhappiness. it\\\'s about \r\ncommunication and growth.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(659,426,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sean','dz why are you measuring love?',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(660,426,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','lately i have been so sad all\r\nthe time that i have just come\r\nto accept it.  during\r\ntraining, however, anything\r\nemotional is gone.  it is a\r\nmeditation.  i had gotten used\r\nto the feeling of coming home\r\nand feeling blue that when\r\ntoday when it didn\\\'t happen,\r\nit took me by surprise.  there\r\nwas a tenuous grasp with a\r\nmomentary happiness.  i didn\\\'t\r\nwant to pounce on it too\r\neagerly because that might\r\nscare it away.  instead i\r\ngently tested the waters it\r\nwas offering and allowed\r\nmyself a small glow.  it is\r\nstill there now, several hours\r\nlater.  it is not an epic,\r\nstaggering happiness.  it is a\r\nsmall contentedness about\r\nnothing.  it is comfortable,\r\nfor now.  is that true\r\nhappiness?\r\n',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(661,426,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kiks','if you eat tons of fruits and \r\nvegetables and skip the \r\nprepared and packaged and \r\nanimal you will achieve \r\ncellular happiness.  it\\\'s \r\ntrue.   it helps if you have \r\ntime to groove with the \r\ncosmos and the trees and do a \r\nlittle dancing.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(662,425,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kiks','maybe it\\\'s time to revise \r\nyour resume.  You could put \r\nthe power thing in your \r\nmission statement.  \r\n',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(663,426,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jojo','i definitely agree with elly \r\nwhen she says you don\\\'t need \r\nto be having fun to be happy. \r\ni am at my happiest when i am \r\ncalm and snuggly and not \r\ndoing much at all.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(664,426,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'huney','<p>lately i\\\'ve come to \r\nunderstand happiness as the \r\nabsence of afflictive \r\nthoughts, ideas, etc.  these \r\ncould include depression, \r\nanger, worry, fear, et al.  a \r\nlot of people (including \r\nmyself) don\\\'t like to think \r\nabout things in terms of what \r\nthose things are not, but \r\nlately i have found this to \r\nbe the most helpful method of \r\nassessment.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(665,426,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'ashton','first of all, happiness for me\r\nis measured out in seconds\r\nuntil i get a different job\r\nthe fuck away from here.  a\r\njob where i can stay until\r\n10pm and then come in 7\r\nminutes late without having to\r\nlisten to the donut snatcher\r\nask me if i just got here.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(666,427,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'huney','&nbsp;&nbsp;what i wish for \r\nyou is what i wish for all \r\nand you are so deserving of \r\nevery happiness and you will \r\nhave them, every pleasure, \r\nevery happiness<br><br>and \r\nnever believe the sex-crazed \r\nlunatics that venerate \r\ncopulation like a deity<br>  \r\nit\\\'s a beautiful thing, \r\nsure<br>\r\n&nbsp; like taking a \r\nbeautiful shit',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(667,426,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','haha, donut snatcher. ',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(668,420,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<B>your website is\r\ndown.<BR>your email\r\nbounces.</B>\r\n<br>somebody did not pay their\r\nbills.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(669,428,'2003-07-24 15:44:23',165,'joker','&nbsp;&nbsp;i like bela fleck',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(670,428,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'ashton','<P>that is the most beautiful\r\nstory i have read in a long\r\ntime.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nloving gifts are more moving\r\nthan, than, well they just\r\nare.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ni was having kind of a crap\r\nday because of the donut\r\nsnatcher, but now i feel much\r\nbetter.</P>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(671,428,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','yetis are kin to bumkins.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(672,430,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','Miso-Broccoli',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(673,429,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','i have heard coffee enemas \r\nare good.  i have never had \r\nan enema though.  maybe i \r\nwould have a coffee one if i \r\nwere not too embarrassed to \r\nask.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(674,425,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>having studied history, i \r\nalways found myself drawn \r\nfurther and further back.  \r\nthe lure of what started it \r\nall pulled me.  all history \r\nhas links to a point, then \r\nthe links stop.  or they take \r\nanother form:  archaeology, \r\nscience, whatever.\r\n</P><P>\r\nin college, i ended up \r\nstudying ancient greece, \r\nrome, and the middle east.  \r\nbasically the mediterranean.  \r\nand i remember when we \r\nstudied oracles.  much of \r\nwhat was considered written \r\nrecord come from oracles.  \r\nthe oracle at delphi said \r\nsuch and such.  and it was \r\nwidely understood that \r\noracles, essentially think \r\ntanks to use a modern \r\nmetaphor, were politically \r\nmotivated.\r\n</P><P>\r\npeople would ask oracles when \r\nthey needed a meaningful \r\nanswer.  in much the same \r\nsense, i studied history \r\nbecause i needed a meaningful \r\nanswer based on other \r\npeople\\\'s experience.\r\n</P><P>\r\nnone the less, in my mind i \r\nalways wondered loudly what \r\nit all meant?  \\\"what does it \r\nmean?\\\" was a persistent \r\nquestion that would drive me \r\nsleepless.  all it meant was \r\nthat if i was going to say \r\nsomething on a topic, \r\nhistorically speaking, it had \r\nbetter be politically \r\nmotivated.  and if i didn\\\'t \r\nfeel politically motivated \r\nwhen portraying history, i \r\nhad better be happy with a \r\nC.</P>\r\n',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(675,429,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'chaya','it\\\'s true.  it might just be \r\nthat i am terribly excited not \r\nto be sick anymore, but also \r\npenicillin makes me hyper and \r\nrestless.  i decided in a fit \r\nof impulsive antibiotic frenzy \r\nthat i should get on a plane \r\nand go visit <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://christop.com\\\">sha\r\ndok</a>.  immediately.\r\n\r\ncan\\\'t. stop. bouncing off the \r\nwalls. send help. regards. ',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(676,429,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','</p><p>just yesterday my \r\ndoctor was telling me i \r\nshould have enemas and also \r\nhe told me about having his \r\nown coffee enemas. he said he \r\nfelt like he could walk on \r\nwater after having a coffee \r\nenema.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(677,430,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'</p>le','</p><p>was there chocolate or \r\nnot?',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(678,426,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','happiness is real. love is an \r\nidea.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(679,429,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','ok well iv had a small bowel \r\nseries and never again will i \r\nput anything but a finger up \r\nmy ass. that means coffee too!',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(680,429,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'</p>le','<p>really chia? what about a \r\nstrapon dildo? attached to a \r\nhot girl?\r\n</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(681,428,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','you kids, you cute cute kids!\r\n-i don\\\'t know how yeti lasted\r\nthis long without one,\r\nactually.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(682,430,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sean','5. xianfoy burns more calories\r\npondering possible outcomes\r\nthan any chocolate can\r\nprovide. housemates polish off\r\nsaid chocolate during\r\nxianfoy\\\'s analysis paralysis.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(683,431,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','sounds sorta like... <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://superdeluxe.com/p\r\neople/elly/schwag/\\\">schwag</a>\r\n!',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(684,431,'2003-05-10 16:09:14',79,'yeti','<p>I\\\'m a bastard. But I have \r\nto mention it. \r\nThe \\\"tournament standard\\\" for \r\nthe fps on a paintball is \r\n280, and 230 is just too slow \r\nto do much good. Also, above \r\n320 will cause a lot more \r\nball breakage.</p>\r\n<p>Sorry to hear of the \r\nfargliness that is occuring \r\nin your life, dude.</p>\r\n<p>-yeti</p>',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(685,431,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','libra rising.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(686,431,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','yes. 280 is the standard for \r\noutdoor paintball. However i \r\nworked in an indoor paintball \r\nfield where the standard was \r\n230. you arent a bastard, you \r\njust think speed is universal.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(687,429,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','hmmmmmmmmmmm. possible. ',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(688,432,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>hoover\\\'s my ass!  i never\r\nfucking saw him in there. \r\nthat is just courting the\r\nblack vote.  that is all that\r\nis.  he doesn\\\'t have the\r\nconstitution or the time to\r\nspend clutching his stomach\r\nafter a good meal, to go to\r\nhoover\\\'s.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i dream of chicken fried\r\nsteak.  one thing that\r\ncalifornia lacks is good food\r\nwith character other than the\r\nbazilion asian\r\nrestaurants.</P>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(689,432,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>oh and, fuck that bitch and\r\nher ass munch gorilla\r\nboyfriend.  i *still* have to\r\ndeal with that type of\r\nperson.  you know what?  they\r\nare dicks even after college. \r\nthink about it, every dick you\r\nhave worked with so far has\r\nbeen a type A frat boy, am i\r\nright?  these people never\r\ngive up.  they are trained ass\r\nholes.  learn to live with\r\nthem or you will never hold a\r\njob for long because they are\r\neverywhere.</P>\r\n<P>balls.</P>',5,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(690,432,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','balls and ass. ass and balls.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(691,432,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','my last boss was a type B \r\nfrat boy. i laughed and \r\nthought it was ironic, me \r\nbeing a frat boy-hater-fo-\r\nlife, but he turned out to be \r\na good guy.  i still can\\\'t \r\nstand type A\\\'s though. ',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(692,432,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i got an email from my friend \r\n<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.dominiwear.co\r\nm\\\">domini</a> recently. it \r\nwas a reply to an email i \r\nsent here wherein i stated \r\nthat i was unhappy, ugly, \r\ndepressed. she said: \\\"i\\\'m not \r\ngoing to try to pull you out \r\nof your depression, because \r\nyou can learn a lot about \r\nyourself when you\\\'re \r\ndepressed.\\\" so yeah,