e\r\nhad such the secret crush on\r\nyou.  hmm.  past tense?',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(718,438,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','um, steve?  i used your \r\nshower without permission \r\nas well.  hope you don\\\'t get \r\nto bent out of shape about \r\nit.  i\\\'m *really* sorry.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(719,310,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','you weren\\\'t just good, you \r\nwere amazingly wonderful.  i \r\nremember thinking that it had \r\nto be a miracle of god\\\'s \r\nsense of humour for you to be \r\nborn with perfect pitch from \r\nthe loins of two people who \r\ncouldn\\\'t sing a note between \r\nthem even if they were really \r\nstoned and practiced for \r\nyears.  some moms are not \r\ntruthful about this sort of \r\nthing.  you know that i am \r\nnot that kind of mom.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(720,407,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','it\\\'s okay, dear.  the key to \r\ncontrolling the frequency of \r\nfreaking out is to pay \r\nattention to what triggers \r\nthe incident.  i found out \r\nthat diabetes was triggering \r\nmy episodes of rage.  who \r\nwould have thought?  you \r\nmight be allergic to \r\nsomething.  if you actually \r\nhurt other people when you go \r\nnuts, that\\\'s something you \r\nneed to fix right away.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(721,441,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','i want to quit smoking, too.  \r\ni think we should try \r\ntogether.  i think i will \r\nbegin by attempting to not \r\nsmoke in front of the \r\ncomputer.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(722,441,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'chaya','oh hey, i want to quit smoking \r\ntoo.  before my birthday in \r\napril.  but see, i\\\'m going to \r\nparis in \r\n(tendaystendaystendays) and \r\nlord knows i can\\\'t NOT smoke \r\nin paris.  dilemma.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(723,441,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','tea tree oil toothpicks are \r\nawesome. they cause your \r\nmouth to tingle. the taste is \r\nstrong, therfore smoking \r\nafter chewing a stick tastes \r\nquite horrible...\r\n',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(724,443,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'pupilsdilate','You seem like a wonderful \r\nmother. I love to read what \r\nyou have to say.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(725,436,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','that is fucking disgusting.',5,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(726,441,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Joanna','<P>Toys and things to do? You \r\nneed <A \r\nHREF=\\\"http://www.mondotime.com\r\n\\\">Mondo</A>!  I don\\\'t know if \r\nthey sell them wherever you \r\nare, but I\\\'m tragically \r\naddicted.  It\\\'s a lollipop \r\nand a collectable figure, and \r\nthere\\\'s like 60 different \r\nones, and they try to teach \r\nyou history, and the more you \r\ncollect the further into the \r\nwebsite you can get, and once \r\nyou have nine, you can \r\ndownload the game.... </P>\r\n<P><I>I don\\\'t really work for \r\nthem</I></P> ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(727,429,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','okay dammit i avoided it for \r\na long time but hi.\r\n\r\ni needed to tell you that i \r\nheard living on a prayer at a \r\ncoffeehouse tonight and it \r\nused to be one of my favorite \r\nsongs when i was a kid and i \r\nbegan singing to \r\nmyself, \\\"working for the man, \r\nshe brings home the pay for \r\nlove. oooooooh for Luh-Uv. \r\nyou\\\'ve got to HOLD ON --\\\"',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(728,444,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','s5: thank you for letting us \r\nstay at your beautiful home.  \r\nit has been one of the \r\nfunnest, most free spirited \r\ntrips to anywhere i have \r\nhad.  your hospitality was \r\nperfect.  i would say this to \r\nyour face, elly\\\'s too, but you \r\nare getting bent back into \r\nshape as we speak.  i must \r\nmove on though.  the road \r\ncalls.  k*.com is falling \r\nasleep.  crankums will \r\nensue.\r\n<BR>\r\n<TT>=-)</TT><BR>peace',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(729,445,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','fuckin a. i was waiting for \r\nyou, jo. i feel calmer \r\nalready.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(730,445,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Hubris Joanna','<P>Hi Joanna!</P>\r\n<P>It gets worse when people