 they \r\nweren\\\'t totally drunk, \r\nstoned, or out of their ever \r\nlovin\\\' minds.  it hadda be an \r\naccident.  if it\\\'s a true \r\nfood then i am afraid.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(822,439,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','i am a diabetic, it\\\'s still \r\nnot a cure for the sugar \r\ncraving. perhaps you could do \r\nlike i do -- eat one bite and \r\nthen drink a glass of water, \r\nwait 15 minutes and eat \r\nanother bite.  it takes a \r\nlong time to eat a donut that \r\nway, but it makes you \r\nappreciate it so much more.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(823,466,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'pat','umm.. I need to read it a \r\nsecond time.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(824,440,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'pat','Thats special, the same thing \r\nwas not seen anywhere in \r\nAmerica today.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(825,464,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','-hoodie drawstrings\r\n-my fingers and thumbs\r\n-gum\r\n-my boyfriend\\\'s elbow, \r\nyesterday\r\n-collars of tshirts\r\n-my fingernails\r\n-my bottom lip',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(826,464,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','my nails (i have this gross \r\nhabit) and my fingers. i have \r\nbeen trying to kick this \r\nhabit since i was 9, but \r\nwhenever i get stressed or \r\ninvolved in something like \r\npainting or knitting, i bite \r\nmy lip or my fingers. it\\\'s \r\nreally not a good idea with \r\npainting... bitey bitey! \r\nchomp nip chew',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(827,464,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','-- the little circles of \r\nplastic on soda bottles are \r\nthe best. the best. i bend \r\nthem into shapes in my mouth \r\nwith my tongue and teeth.<BR>\r\n-- coffee stirrers, plastic \r\nand wooden. i love the wooden \r\nstirrers at spider house \r\nbecause after i suck on it \r\nprofusely, i can then PLAY \r\nwith it by tearing it into \r\nlittle shards.<BR>\r\nin fact, having said that, i \r\nshould add that i usually \r\npick things to put in my \r\nmouth that i can also take \r\nout and play with later.<BR>\r\n-- the bracelets elly bought \r\nme.<BR>\r\n-- my own thumb, fingers.<BR>\r\n-- woobie.<BR>\r\n-- my lower lip<BR>\r\n-- plastic spoons, the \r\nsmaller the better. the best \r\nare the ones from baskin-\r\nrobbins, the little pink ones?\r\n<BR>\r\n-- really almost anything \r\nthat is small and either 1) \r\nplastic or 2)circle-ish, i \r\nwill put in my mouth. i\\\'m \r\nlike a child.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(828,469,'2003-07-24 15:44:23',165,'joker','dj_1luna is The Game.<br>\r\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n&nbsp;no one can see the \r\nmatrix',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(829,470,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','i guess i am going to give my\r\nmassage to kiki because she\r\nhurt her back this morning\r\nreally bad.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(830,470,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>god, i feel shitty today. \r\nreally bad.  i woke up with it\r\nthis morning.  really i think\r\ni went to bed with it.\r\n</P>><P>i am not sick i just\r\nfeel irritated.  and it is\r\ntotally a feeling.  i have no\r\nailments or problems like my\r\nshoes being to small or\r\nsomething.</P><P>i need to go\r\nto the gym, i know it.  part\r\nof my funk is that i don\\\'t\r\nwant to.  which is usually a\r\ntell tale sign that something\r\nis wrong. \r\nfunny.</P><BLOCKQUOTE>but\r\ndoctor, i feel fine, i just am\r\nsick of\r\nyou.</BLOCKQUOTE><BLOCKQUOTE>nurse,\r\nthe patient is demented, put\r\nhim on the medication,\r\ndouble.</BLOCKQUOTE>\r\n<P>i need to get something\r\ndone in my life today. \r\nsomething. something.\r\nsomething.</P><P>ants in my\r\npants.</P>',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(831,470,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','i just pooped and now i feel\r\nmuch better.  i think it had\r\nbeen a while.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(832,470,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','when in doubt, don\\\'t panic, \r\nand have a nice bowel \r\nmovement. that\\\'s what my mom \r\nalways said.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(833,470,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kaz','yeah, whatever',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(834,470,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','purge.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(835,470,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','but kaz, tell us what you \r\n*really* think',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(836,467,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jp','hehe, Black Sabbath \r\nrocked.<BR>\r\n<I>War Pigs</I> is good, \r\n<I>Iron Man</I> too -- \r\nclassic.<BR>\r\nHere\\\'s my guilty pleasure, Ted \r\nNugent\\\'s <I>Overdrive</I>. Yes \r\ncheezy as hell, but dammit I \r\nam always so pumped when I \r\nhappen to hear that song on \r\nthe radio.<BR>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(837,467,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jp','correction on above it\\\'s Ted \r\nNugent <I>Stranglehold</I> I \r\nmeant.<BR>\r\nAnd come to think of it, why \r\nshould I deride my own taste \r\nas cheezy?<BR>\r\nI support the Ted Nugent\\\'s \r\n<i>Stranglehold</I> without \r\ncompromise -- so there.<BR>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(838,466,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jp','I\\\'m going to riff on your \r\nthing...<BR>\r\n<TT>\r\nA friend of mine once put tuna \r\nin ceramic bowl. He lit the \r\ntuna on fire... I\\\'ve lost \r\ntrack of him.<BR>\r\nBaking soda can make water \r\nfizzy and it can put out \r\ngrease fires. It can be used \r\nto freebase cocaine and in \r\nelementary school science \r\nprojects.<BR>\r\nBut whenever I feel the eyes \r\nof fate pressing in darkness, \r\nmy box of baking soda contains \r\nthe stench of a rotten \r\nlemon.<BR>\r\nVacuum -- lonely refuge from \r\nthe fires of hate and desire. \r\nAnd so I remain motionless in \r\na junkyard frig.<BR>\r\n</TT>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(839,473,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'pictures','<P>austin wants to see them \r\nof the commie radio jamming \r\ntower.  </P><P>hi jebro, i \r\nwas wondering how you are \r\ndoing?  bmg said you are \r\ntrying out for Blade 2.  \r\nwhich reminds me, somebody \r\nsaid recently that whenever \r\nthey see the actor wesley \r\nsnipes on the movie screen, \r\nthey think, \\\"hey look, its \r\nWesley Snipes!\\\"</P><P>i \r\nthought that was really \r\nfunny.  some actors just \r\ncan\\\'t get away from \r\nthemselves.</P><P>i guess the \r\ninternet industry is done in \r\nprague?  it is winding down \r\nhere too i think.</P><P>more \r\nand more i am thinking that i \r\nget to experience my first \r\neconomic depression.  i am \r\nnot scared of it.  i owe some \r\npeople money, but i am not \r\nthe only one.  i am sure the \r\nbanks will understand, \r\nwhether they like it or not, \r\nwhy i am not paying them when \r\nthe time comes that i am \r\njobless and out of money \r\ncompletely.</P><P>until \r\nthen...  stoli!</P>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(840,473,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'little birdie','I hear jebro shaved his head! \r\nFUCK N\\\' SHIT, MAN!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(860,474,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','to be fair, i have been \r\ntalking to securities \r\nlitigation and class action \r\nattorneys, many of whom \r\nare opportunistic sharks. i \r\nreally don\\\'t enjoy talking to \r\nthem, i feel that they\\\'re \r\nmotivated by getting a piece \r\nof the largest possible \r\nsettlement, and less \r\nconcerned with protecting \r\nmy rights. i ask about \r\nkarma because in this \r\ncase, i am initiating the \r\nlitagtion. i can\\\'t really \r\ndiscuss the specifics here, \r\nbut there\\\'s a part of all this \r\nthat makes me feel icky. \r\nfwiw, i have an enormous \r\namount respect for you and \r\nyour career goals. i can \r\nimagine that you have to put \r\nup with a lot of lawyer \r\nbashing.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(842,473,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','i do not believe you.  jeb \r\nwould never do that.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(843,474,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','what does she try to sue \r\nyou for? i\\\'m starting a \r\nlawsuit this year, and i\\\'m \r\nconcerned what effect it will \r\nhave on my karma. i already \r\nfeel icky from consorting \r\nwith lawyers. what should i \r\ndo? loofah and wheatgrass \r\naren\\\'t cleansing enough.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(844,474,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'chaya','perhaps a refreshing coffee \r\nenema would set you straight?',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(845,474,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','it\\\'s hard to explain -- \r\nusually she wants fifty grand \r\nbecause i won\\\'t link to her \r\nsite.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(846,473,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'lil birdie','i hear that someone has \r\npictures...',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(851,475,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>what would happen if my \r\nbowl got filled every time i \r\nemptied it?</P>\r\n<P><i>i think about stealing \r\nfist fulls of \\\"pops\\\" from the \r\nbox at <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://steve.org\\\">\r\ns5\\\'s</a> house.</i></P>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(852,467,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.gee.kz/pete\r\nr/for_s5.mp3\\\">this</a> is \r\nfrom yeti. i like him.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(853,475,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i feel the fact that i\r\noverfeed my cat has something\r\nto do with my recent\r\nrealization that i am all\r\nabout the svadisthana chakra,\r\nthe chakra of desire and want,\r\nof sexual energy too. i\r\nassociate this with decadence.\r\ni don\\\'t know if it really\r\nmakes any sense though.\r\n',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(854,476,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i spend a lot of time laying\r\nin various warm rooms of the\r\nhouse reading \\\'memoirs of a\r\ngeisha\\\' and it\\\'s so good i\r\njust get lost in it and read\r\ncertain paragraphs over and\r\nover. it makes me want to look\r\nat pictures of geisha and\r\nstudy their faces.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(855,476,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<tt>\r\n&lt;*s5*&gt; what book are you\r\nreading?<br>\r\n/m s5 \\\'memoirs of a\r\ngeisha\\\'<br>\r\n/m s5 it\\\'s so good!<br>\r\n&lt;*s5*&gt; what is it\r\nabout?<br>\r\n/m s5 hi silly. it\\\'s the\r\nmemoirs of a geisha.<br>\r\n&lt;*s5*&gt; well you know!\r\ndon\\\'t judge a book<br>\r\n/m s5 haha<br>\r\n</tt>',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(856,476,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>i want to read two books in\r\na week.  what is stopping me? \r\ni must sleep.</P>\r\n<P>is it okay if i just listen\r\nto two new albums in a\r\nweek?</P>\r\n<UL>\r\n<LI>asian dub foundation:\r\nRafi\\\'s revenge\r\n<LI>bjork: selma\\\'s songs\r\n</UL>\r\n<LI>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(857,474,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kiks','give me a break.  who do you \r\nthink monitors human rights?  \r\nlawyers. the fucked-up-the \r\nass/rape comment is \r\ncompletely uncool.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(858,474,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kiks','consorting with lawyers and \r\navailing yourself of the \r\nlegal system does not create \r\nbad karma, but comments like \r\nthe few above do.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(859,474,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','objection heard <BR> <BR>\r\nmotion to have the case thown\r\nout. <BR> <BR>\r\nlet us remember that we cannot\r\nmake blanket negative lawyer\r\ncomments where we have\r\nlawyers. <br> <br>\r\nbut i will note that the\r\nviagra donkey mounts the woman\r\nwho hired the lawyer, not the\r\nlawyer. <br><br>\r\nM\\\'Kay?',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(861,474,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kiks','it is true that there are \r\nabuses of the system.  but its \r\nnot like most attorneys \r\narene\\\'t aware of that and \r\naren\\\'t working to curb the \r\nexcesses of greed.  unlike \r\nmost professions, lawyers have \r\nprofessional codes of ethics \r\nthey are necessarily bound to \r\nadhere to at the risk of \r\nlosing their license to \r\npractice.  unfortunatly, you \r\ncannot be debarred merely for \r\nbeing an asshole.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(862,474,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','a sort of apology.<br><br>\r\nthe negative angry diatribe \r\nwas not a comment against \r\nlawyers in a general \r\nway.<br><br> it was a \r\nspecific comment aimed at a \r\nspecific sleazy \r\nperson...<br><br>\r\n...who not only \r\nmisrepresented herself as a \r\nperson with a whole other \r\nprofession, but has a history \r\nof behaviour that caused a \r\nnormally pleasant person (me) \r\nto make ugly \r\ndiatribes.<br><br>\r\n\r\nperhaps if you read my <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://auntie.diaryland\\\"\r\n>diaryland</a> entry you \r\nmight understand some \r\nbetter.<br><br>\r\nobjection sustained.<br>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(863,474,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','ahem: *<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://auntie.diaryland.\r\ncom/\\\">the correct \r\nurl</a>*<br><br>\r\nslinking away slapping fat \r\nfingers....<br>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(864,478,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'maya','&nbsp;it often seems that \r\nkarma is attributed the \r\nqualities deists give to a \r\nrewarding and punishing god, \r\nin our culture.  <br>\r\n\\\"if i act thusly, i will be \r\nrewarded with a good \r\nkarma.\\\"<br>\r\n\\\"if i act thusly, i will be \r\npunished with a bad \r\nkarma.\\\"<br>\r\ni believe this is a \r\nmispresentation.  karma is \r\nsimply and only, the law of \r\ncause and effect.  \r\nassignation of \\\"good\\\" \r\nor \\\"bad\\\" to the <b>effect</b> \r\nis a wholly subjective \r\nundertaking, to be made by \r\nthe consciousness perceiving \r\nsaid <b>effect</b>.<br>\r\na good example of this \r\nis \\\"kicking the cat\\\".  for \r\nthe kicker, a good karma is \r\nripening, inasmuch as the \r\nkicker\\\'s consciousness has \r\nattained a human body large \r\nenough to dominate and abuse \r\nthe cat, and inasmuch as the \r\nkicker finds this position, \r\npleasant.  for the cat, it is \r\nan unpleasant karma, inasmuch \r\nas the cat has attained a \r\nbirth in a body capable of \r\nbeing dominated and abused by \r\na human being, and inasmuch \r\nas the event of being kicked \r\nwas unpleasant (not all \r\nbeings find being kicked, \r\ndistasteful).<br>\r\nthe karma being collected in \r\nthis event, and the karma \r\nripening are two separate \r\nthings.  the kicker burns a \r\nkarma from a past action that \r\ncaused another pleasure, and \r\ncollects the karma to \r\nperceive itself being \r\nkicked.  the cat burns a \r\nkarma to perceive itself \r\nbeing kicked, and collects \r\nthe karma for whatever action \r\nit reacted with.  if it did \r\nnot react, then no new karma \r\nwas collected and an \r\nunpleasent karma was used up \r\n(again, assuming the cat \r\nfound this event \r\nunpleasant).<br>\r\nin terms of litigation and \r\nkarma, it might be helpful to \r\ncompare the potentially \r\npleasant event of winning a \r\nlawsuit, with the potentially \r\nunpleasant event of losing a \r\nlawsuit.  in this light, it \r\nalso might be helpful, like \r\nauntie said, to examine one\\\'s \r\nmotive, as this will be the \r\nmost powerful karma collected.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(865,478,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kiks','it is no less scandalous to a \r\nlawyer (or law student) that \r\nabuses happen in the system.  \r\nit is no consolation to know \r\nthat the same contingency \r\nsystem that brought us the \r\nshark makes it possible for \r\npeople who have been \r\nseriously wronged to have \r\ntheir day in court without \r\nworrying about how they will \r\npay for the case--contingency \r\nlawyers who sue corporations \r\nfor devastating injuries to \r\nconsumers, for instance.  i \r\nhave a professor who sued \r\nmilosovic on behalf of the \r\nbosnian women who were raped, \r\nand the ethiopian government \r\nfor the forced deportation of \r\neritreans, who lost their \r\nhomes and livlihoods.  law \r\nbrought us the civil rights \r\nmovement, and women\\\'s rights \r\nand the pursuit of those laws \r\nensures that we are \r\nprotected \\\"in fact\\\" and not \r\njust \\\"on paper.\\\"  i\\\'m sorry \r\nthat you\\\'ve had trouble with \r\nthe law.  meritless suits are \r\nlegalized extortion.  to be \r\nperfectly honest, i\\\'m looking \r\nforward to the day when i can \r\nthrow my weight around a \r\nlittle bit.  i\\\'d put that \r\nlady in her place for you--\r\npro bono too.  ',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(866,478,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kiks','funny you should mention cats \r\nwho are kicked.  my mother\\\'s \r\ncat was recently killed by \r\nblunt force trauma the vet \r\nthinks was caused by a kick.  \r\ni wrote about the <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/j\r\nournals/article.phtml?\r\nid=290.txt\\\">asthma</a> i \r\nsuffered as a result of this \r\nparticular cat--i\\\'m quite \r\nsure i didn\\\'t want any harm \r\nto come to it, but not a \r\nmonth later his little limp \r\nbody was found in a puddle in \r\nthe back yard.  it is a very \r\npainful subject for me.  i \r\nwant very much for the person \r\nwho did this to know that \r\nthey hurt this little thing \r\nso badly that he died and \r\nmade my mother cry for three \r\ndays.  i\\\'m not sure how this \r\nworks into your karmic scheme.\r\n\r\nAm i heavy and confessional \r\ntoday or what?',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(867,476,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'daphne','100 Years of Solitude has to \r\nbe one of the world\\\'s finest \r\npieces of literature. The \r\nlayers of meaning and imagry \r\ncouldn\\\'t possibly be uncovered \r\nand understood in such a short \r\ntime. Try reading it again and \r\nsavoring it like fine cognac. \r\nTry reading Marquez\\\' Love in \r\nthe Time of Colera, too.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(868,476,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Joanna','\\\"Love in the  Time of \r\nCholera\\\" was absolutely \r\nmagnificant and breath-taking \r\nand wonderful and made me \r\nbelieve in love again.  So \r\nmaybe it\\\'ll take me until I\\\'m \r\neighty before I\\\'ll  love and \r\nbe loved like that,  but \r\nthat\\\'s okay.    ',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(869,476,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','reading is <b>fun</b>damental.\r\n\r\nfreal do, I read \\\"100 years\\\" \r\nas I read books I like. I. \r\nRead. Every. Word. That\\\'s why \r\nit took me as long as it did, \r\nbecause there\\\'s a gigantic \r\nweb of people involved and \r\neach one of them is actually \r\npeople. I don\\\'t really know \r\nhow I could have read it more \r\nslowly, without reading it \r\nagain, which I may very well \r\ndo.\r\n\r\nwrt two new albums a week, I \r\nsuggest finding a friend with \r\nmp3 hookups, and then you can \r\nlisten to two new albums ever \r\n148 minutes..\r\n\r\nthis input is disorientingly \r\nsmall.\r\n',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(871,480,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>our lyric of the day today\r\ncomes from the well known rap\r\nartist, eminem.</P>\r\n<P>like most of the lyrics\r\nthat we get here on the\r\nswinney channel, it displays\r\nremarkable pathos and gives\r\nthe listener insight into the\r\nlife and struggle of a man on\r\nthe edge of natural\r\ninstict.<B>:</B></P>\r\n<PRE>\r\nTired of having to deal.\r\n\r\nTired of having to deal with\r\nthe bullshit \r\nwithout grabbing the steel.\r\n</PRE>',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(872,480,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','\\\"time unaccounted for\\\" == \r\nchat.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(873,480,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','ok, sorry for the quote of the\r\nday by eminim.  it just popped\r\ninto my head when i was in the\r\nshower. <BR><BR> i know people\r\nthink he sucks.  i didn\\\'t get\r\naround to listening to it\r\nuntil multiple years after\r\nit\\\'s release. <BR><BR> in\r\nfact, i am surprise it has had\r\nsuch a lasting effect on mtv. \r\n*again*, not because i watch\r\nmtv, i don\\\'t.  but, everytime\r\ni hear about eminim it is in\r\nrelation to some appearance he\r\nmade on mtv that makes the\r\nnewspaper.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(874,480,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>Eminem\\\'s latest album has \r\n1 or 2 good songs on it. The \r\nfirst full-length album is \r\nexcellent and displays how \r\ntalented the little nerd \r\nactually is. </p>\r\n<p>\r\nCompare \\\"guilty conscience\\\" \r\nto \\\"bitch please II\\\" and you \r\nwill see what I\\\'m talking \r\nabout.</p>\r\n<p>I still maintain that if \r\nEminem were black, he would \r\nnot be pop, instead he\\\'d be \r\none of the most respected and \r\ndick-rode underground MCs \r\n_ever_. Before he became \r\npopular, all of the \r\nunderground kids were all \r\nover him. Then, when he \r\nbecame popular, they decided \r\nto ignore his talent and \r\nskill and put him in the \r\nVanilla Ice bin. Wack.</p>\r\n',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(875,478,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jp','Navy doctors must really be \r\nincompetent because they \r\nmessed up my grandma too. They \r\ncut a nerve and she lost \r\nhearing in one ear in an \r\noperation.<BR>\r\nAs for as lawsuits, I go by \r\nthe same rule of avoiding any \r\nlegal action if possible.<BR>\r\nI\\\'ve considered suing once, \r\nbut the amount wasn\\\'t quite \r\nenough to make it worth \r\nit.<BR>\r\nOne thing I\\\'ve found is that \r\nsome people are like \r\n<i>poison</i>. It\\\'s best not \r\nto deal with them if you can \r\nbecause just making them a \r\ncenter role in your life fills \r\nit with negativity.<BR>\r\nYou can\\\'t always do that \r\nthough... oh well.<BR>\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(882,483,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sic','i ordered this vegetable thing \r\nand it was in a foil plastic \r\nthing...he kept it on the \r\ngrill till the plastic \r\nballooned like someone\\\'s \r\nhead...we thought vegetables \r\nwere gonna fly',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(877,483,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'reader','say what? those prices at \r\nthat place are nuts. i can \r\nimport my own personal \r\njapanese cook with what you \r\npay at that place.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(878,483,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','isn\\\'t benihana the place \r\nwhere they chop things really \r\nfast and then you get freaked \r\nout that they might cut their \r\nfingers off in front of you \r\nand when it\\\'s all over you \r\npay a huge amount of money \r\nfor the fear?',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(879,481,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'best friendly','describe \\\"hot girl.\\\"',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(880,483,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','when i went, our chef with the\r\nblades had two western style\r\n6-shooter holsters, one on\r\neach hip.  he kept his blades\r\nin them and liked to practice\r\ndrawing them to the cutting\r\nboard.<BR><BR>note: this was\r\nin dallas.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(881,483,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','oh, and he spun the knives\r\nlike a wild bill in his\r\ntravelling circus.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ni wonder what his sex\r\nfantasies were like?',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(883,481,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','it\\\'s a reference to a tori \r\namos song. \\\"past the mission, \r\ni once knew a hot girl.\\\"',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(884,484,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','what kind of personality?',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(885,484,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','king of the world.  won\\\'t take\r\nyour shit.  knows her stuff. \r\nknows you know she knows her\r\nstuff.  knows the world is\r\nwatching her.  fun.  laughs a\r\nlot.  tells good stories. \r\ncatty. has an ass kicking\r\nhandstand.  kicks cop cars if\r\nthey cut her  off on her\r\nmountain bike.  \r\n<p>\r\ni\\\'ve been trying to tell her\r\nstories that gross her out for\r\nthe last year and so far have\r\nonly been successful once.  it\r\nwas the rock hard ball of puss\r\nin the tongue story.  then she\r\nsaid the same thing happened\r\nto her.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(886,485,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'pat','Yeah! the roomate part, yeah.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(887,430,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'pat','bulk bin carob{{^^',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(888,485,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','everyone is two people, at \r\nleast, sometimes \r\nthree.<br><br>\r\ni\\\'m a great believer in a \r\nprayer my grandmother had on \r\nher bedroom wall:<br>\r\ngod grant me the serenity to \r\naccept the things i cannot \r\nchange.<br><br>\r\nthe courage to change the \r\nthings i can.<br>\r\nand the wisdom to know the \r\ndifference.<br><br.\r\nit sounds simplistic, but it \r\nworks. saying you are sorry \r\nis necessary when you screw \r\nup.<br><br>\r\nwhen you screw up on the same \r\nstuff over and over, people \r\nare less likely to forgive \r\nyou.<br><br>\r\nthe trick is to identify \r\nwhich infractions you can \r\ntruly promise to change, and \r\nwhich you are pretty sure you \r\nwill keep repeating.<br><br>\r\nonce identified, you can only \r\npromise to <em>try</em> to \r\nchange them.<br><br>\r\nthose who love you will \r\nappreciate your honesty and \r\nyou will be able to stop \r\nbeating yourself up over \r\nthem, which, in turn, will \r\nactually give you the courage \r\nto move from <em>trying to \r\nchange</em> right into \r\n<em>new you.</em><br><br>\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(889,481,'2003-07-24 15:44:23',165,'joker','what foreign film were you \r\nwatching?',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(890,485,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','i\\\'m right with auntie on this \r\none.<BR>\r\nyo there\\\'s even a billy joel \r\nsong about it -- \\\"the \r\nstranger.\\\"<BR>\r\n(mmmm. billy joel.)<BR>\r\npoint being, we all have \r\nthese just awful sides to \r\nourselves that are petty and \r\nsilly and angry and \r\njudgmental. i personally use \r\nwriting to exorcise those \r\ndemons. i\\\'ll be in the middle \r\nof a train of thought and \r\ni\\\'ll use some vile phrase and \r\nimmediately my inside editor \r\nshouts, \\\"oh my GOD cross that \r\nout, that\\\'s just evil.\\\"<BR>\r\nso i leave it in.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(891,486,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','in leonard cohen\\\'s <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.amazon.com/ex\r\nec/obidos/ASIN/0679748253/\\\">be\r\nautiful losers</a>, he talks \r\nabout various saints and holy \r\npeople who stopped eating for \r\nwhatever reason and then \r\nnever had to eat again. never \r\ncraved food. this reminded of \r\nthat and i need to research \r\nthis. might be good info for \r\n<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.divinities.or\r\ng/\\\">divinities</a>, ells, in \r\nfact i think you should read \r\nthat book because it\\\'s a fast \r\nread and the narrator is \r\npartially concerned with the \r\nsainthood of <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.catholicism.o\r\nrg/pages/kateri.htm\\\">catherine\r\n tekakwitha</a> and has \r\nbeautiful folk tales of her \r\nlife.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(892,486,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.public.iastat\r\ne.edu/~roymeo/Cohen/beautifull\r\nosers.html\\\">first page of the \r\nfirst chapter of beautiful \r\nlosers</a>.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(893,484,'2002-03-05 20:17:36',17,'austin to xep','<P>....  <nods head over to\r\nthe side> . . .  the puss in\r\nthe tongue story?  out with\r\nit! <TT>=-)</TT></P>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(894,486,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','the man named mike is very\r\nmuch a capoeira artist.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(895,487,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'meep','warning ** warning : spiritual\r\ninterference.  \r\n<PRE>\r\n--- kirstinashe.com ping\r\nstatistics ---\r\n3 packets transmitted, 3\r\npackets received, 0% packet\r\nloss\r\nround-trip min/avg/max =\r\n2.9/3.2/4.0 ms\r\n</PRE>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(896,487,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'k2','If kirstin\\\'s words spoke to \r\nyou, repeat after me (with a \r\nmischievous and knowing glint \r\nin your \r\neyes): \\\"Mmmmmmmm...yoga.\\\"',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(897,488,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>ME TOO!  Yea Depression!  \r\n<FONT SIZE=3\r\nCOLOR=\\\"red\\\">Ra!</FONT> \r\n<FONT SIZE=4\r\nCOLOR=\\\"red\\\">Ra!</FONT> \r\n<FONT SIZE=5\r\nCOLOR=\\\"RED\\\">Ra!</FONT> \r\n</P> <P>Go Team Go!</P>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(898,487,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'pat','What would R2-D2 say?',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(899,486,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i have a copy of \\\'beautiful \r\nlosers\\\' and keep meaning to \r\nread it. i read another book \r\nabout crazy men and saints \r\ncalled \\\'virgins and martyrs\\\' \r\nby simon maginn, it also \r\nfeatured some starvation. also \r\nthere is a track on the cd \r\n\\\'dead again\\\' by the golden \r\npalominos about a starving \r\nmartyr',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(900,484,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','she does this perfect \r\nhandstand, where she only \r\nindents at her muscledly, \r\ntiny, usually spandexed \r\nwaist. <br>\r\nand yet the only time i\\\'ve \r\nmanaged to talk to her, she\\\'s \r\ngrinned at me with her cat \r\nlike mouth, and i lost my \r\ntrain of thought. weeb try to \r\nturn on the charm. weeb fail \r\nmiserably as she laughs at me \r\ngaping at her implanted \r\nfangs. they are so cute! ',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(901,489,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','or maybe the barometer is \r\nrising.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(902,484,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','fangs?  wicked',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(903,485,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','i recognize when i am knocked \r\noff my usual equilibrium \r\nof \\\'being nice\\\' but i rather \r\nenjoy it. it makes me daring, \r\ni push at boundaries of \r\nacting socially acceptable, \r\nusually if i can\\\'t find \r\nanother way to say it without \r\nbeing dishonest. it\\\'s my only \r\nexcuse. i think sometimes, \r\nbeing sloppy with your \r\nemotions, is not a bad thing. \r\nif i feel weird, strange, and \r\nintroverted, i roll with it. \r\ni embrace my inner doof. \r\nusually people tolerate the \r\ntroll i become, and i am \r\nimmensely grateful for it. as \r\nsome sort of poor recompense, \r\ni shower them with my usually \r\nabundant, unreserved aries \r\nlove glitter.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(904,489,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i don\\\'t like thinking about my \r\nguts',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(905,486,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','ells, it\\\'s \\\"dead inside,\\\" not \r\ndead again. you keep throwing \r\nme all off when you say that \r\nbecause dead again is that \r\nyummy scary kenneth branagh \r\nmovie with the scissors.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(906,488,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','yes!<BR>\r\nmy friend pierre called \r\ntonight and said, \\\"do you \r\njust feel horribly sad \r\nlately?\\\" and i said, \\\"YES!\\\" \r\nand he said, \\\"it\\\'s the \r\ncouples. it\\\'s all the fucking \r\ncouples. it\\\'s that season and \r\ni\\\'m not in a fucking couple. \r\ni hate them.\\\"<BR>\r\n(i love pierre.)',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(907,488,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'pat','It sounds more like auntie \r\nwalked away from the journal \r\nentry.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(908,492,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'swinney','ok, it is now time to move to\r\na server with htdig search\r\nengine. <BR><BR> i know there\r\nis an article somewhere on\r\nhere about history. <BR><BR> i\r\ncannot remember where it is or\r\nwho wrote it.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(909,489,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','i think my ribcage is \r\nasymmetrical. but i feel like \r\nmy doctor would laugh at me \r\nif i told him this.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(910,493,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'knives out','dirty your face with desire \r\nand grace god given. i\\\'m \r\ngoing to go spill my guts \r\nnow. night falls quickly. \r\nwe\\\'re lost in the woods. \r\nstumbling fuct out of the \r\nwoods chased by bears. when \r\nwill i see her again? only \r\nthe other side of friends. ',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(911,493,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'TUBE','i want to spill my guts in a \r\ncrowded restaurant and blame \r\nit on the waiter.  or \r\nwaitress. i am not biased \r\nwith gender. only hair.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(912,493,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'knives out','oh god i was so nice to you \r\nthe other day it was almost \r\nlike a nightmare. (insert \r\nhere) a fact: love is blind, \r\ngod is love. fact: ray \r\ncharles is blind. therefore: \r\nray charles is god.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(913,493,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'TUBE','ray charles is not blind. he \r\njust thinks sunglasses look \r\ncool on black men. he told me \r\nso in a dream. promise.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(914,493,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'ad nauseum','post hoc ergo propter hoc',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(915,495,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','well, austin, I would say \r\nthat a congratulations is in \r\norder. No big deal, fuck it.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(916,495,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i\\\'m really worried about all\r\nthe people out of work.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(917,495,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','with all of our cumulative \r\nexperience, we should start a \r\ncoffee house.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(918,495,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i\\\'ve been saying for a while\r\nthat what we need to do is\r\nstart a 24 hour vegan eaterie\r\nand record store. because\r\nthere\\\'s no good food in sf for\r\nvegans in the middle of the\r\nnight. and because we all\r\nsecretely want to work for a\r\nrecord store. ',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(919,486,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','heh you\\\'re right.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(920,494,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Pearly','do tell us more about who you \r\nare oh person with a \r\nradiohead song as a name.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(921,495,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Monkey Man','Dude. What the FUCK!!!!!!!!! \r\nI was so blown away. I was \r\ngoing back & forth as to \r\nwhether I should say \r\nsomething, came very very \r\nclose, then tried to just \r\nchill. The chill \r\nwon, ....this time\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(922,492,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','i voted for more money for \r\nschools to use for arts/music \r\nprograms in a recent local \r\nelection. maybe if we write \r\nour senators and make use of \r\nour local legislature, things \r\nwill change. it\\\'s good to \r\ncomplain, but i tend to get \r\nmore upset than i need to be \r\nif i don\\\'t have an idea of \r\nhow to act constructively.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(923,494,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','and who quotes billy corgan',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(924,495,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','that would be a good front \r\nfor your friendly local pot \r\nconnection. and it could be a \r\nyarn store. SF needs a good \r\nyarn store.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(925,495,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sic','dude im sorry...visit if you \r\nneed a place to crash and some \r\ndrinks',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(926,489,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sic','for awhile i thought i had a \r\nbrain tumor...rose thought i \r\nwas crazy...and i said that \r\nwould explain everything',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(927,494,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'knives out','cute. stealing from \r\nmr.corgan? oh i see, the \r\nsiamese dream lyric \\\"mother \r\nfuckers try and break your \r\ncrown\\\", hmm...nice. ;)\r\n\r\noil oil.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(928,494,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'knives out','p.s. pearly = radiohead bside.\r\nthanks bye.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(929,494,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','no, i was meaning the line \r\n\\\"you\\\'re all whores and i\\\'m a \r\nfag and i\\\'ve got no mother \r\nand i\\\'ve got no dad\\\" from \r\nmellon collie.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(930,495,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','what le said.<br><br>\r\nwhen i was in sf this \r\njanuary, i was struck by the \r\nimpossibility of obtaining \r\nfood in the middle of the \r\nnight in a town where nobody \r\nsleeps until the sun comes \r\nup.<br><br>\r\nrents are down now, since \r\neveryone is unemployed, but \r\neven the unemployed must eat \r\nfood.<br><br>\r\nmany years ago a lot of \r\nbusinesses sprung up in the \r\nhaight to fill the needs of \r\nthe population.  dad was \r\nthere and he saw it \r\nall.<br><br>\r\nsf needs a vegan coffee \r\nhouse/restaurant/yarn \r\nstore/but there is another \r\nopportunity i know about if \r\nyou want to hear it, one that \r\nmight get you more cash for \r\nfewer dollars in a hurry. i \r\nwill write about it.<br><br>\r\npack your bags young man and \r\ngo north.<br><br>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(931,496,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','mom.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(932,496,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','you must not \\\"mom\\\" me when i \r\ncome up with these great \r\nideas.  even if you are \r\nembarrassed.  because that is \r\nwhat moms are for.  our \r\ngreatest goal in life is to \r\ncause our children to shake \r\ntheir heads and wonder how \r\nthe hell they were spawned \r\nfrom such crazed \r\nloins.<br><br>\r\ni love you very much, you \r\nshould be glad i don\\\'t shave \r\nmy head and get nekkid on \r\nwebcams.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(933,496,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','diana, the ex, used to own a\r\ndoll shop in san francisco. \r\nit was quite popular and had a\r\nloyal following.  i hid in my\r\nroom when the people came over\r\nto do their doll things.  they\r\nwould all sit around a big\r\ntable doing various things to\r\ntheir hollow eyeless doll\r\nheads depending on the state\r\nof completion.  sometimes they\r\nwould be sanding the seam out\r\nof the head.  sometimes they\r\nwould be painting eyelashes on\r\nwith a brush that only had one\r\nor two hairs.  sometimes they\r\nwould purchase some eyes,\r\nwhich lived in a drawer.  i\r\nliked to open the drawer and\r\nlook at all the eyes.  so many\r\neyes.  at the end of the day\r\nthey would set their heads on\r\na shelf near the kiln to be\r\nfired.  the shelf looked like \r\n<a\r\nhref=\\\"http://logy.org/~xep/dollheads1.jpg\\\">this</a>.  ',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(934,495,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'rosie k.','i\\\'m sorry.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(935,494,'2003-07-24 15:44:23',165,'joker','galaxies full of nobodies, \r\ngiving us the farewell run \r\naround, i took my virgin mary \r\nax to his sweet baby jane, \r\nlost my innocence to a no \r\ngood girl, scratch my face \r\nwith anvil hands, coil my \r\ntongue round a bumblebee \r\nmouth...',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(936,497,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','hi, xep likes vroom vroom...',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(937,497,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','there was a reason that tony \r\nbennett\\\'s song was so well \r\nliked.  it is because it\\\'s \r\ntrue.<br><br>\r\ni\\\'ve been lots of places, and \r\nsf is still the best city in \r\nthe world, better than paris \r\nor rome or munich or anywhere \r\ni can think of.  the only \r\nplace i can think of almost \r\nas good is savannah, which \r\nalso caters to people who \r\nlike to use their feet.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(938,494,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Pearly','p.s. like, i know what my \r\nname is.\r\n -Man O War',5,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(939,498,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','yes. pray to god, but keep \r\nrowing for the shore.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(940,498,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','ohm',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(941,494,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'knives out','drift all ya like from ocean \r\nto ocean.',5,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(942,498,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kstar','I know it sounds like I\\\'m \r\nevangelizing, but I\\\'m actually \r\nserious, in a kidding sort of \r\nway.  You know what I me',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(943,497,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i dunno. melbourne is pretty\r\ngreat. hi lunesse :)',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(944,494,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Pearly','and if i sign \\\"lift\\\" will you \r\nquote it as well? who are \r\nyou?- big ideas. ',5,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(945,493,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Pearly','\\\" i wish that something would \r\nhappen \\\" \\\"where do i go from \r\nhere?\\\"',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(946,501,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'pat','Not exactly!',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(947,500,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Pat','I voted for you!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(948,502,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','k.y.e.o. my brother. talk to \r\nyou soon... good luck.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(949,502,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'dj1_luna','you\\\'ll be missed here, there \r\nand everywhere',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(950,499,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sultana','in my experience it\\\'s \r\npossible to distract from the \r\nPath the very people you want \r\nso much to help by \r\nproselytizing.  in my \r\nexcitement and enthusiasm i \r\nmay misspeak (or something) \r\nand confuse, confound or \r\nunnerve the victim of my Good \r\nIntentions.  Not always, mind \r\nyou, sometimes when someone \r\nis open to and interested in \r\nthe same things it can be \r\nfantastic!  A meeting of the \r\nminds!  A fellow Traveler!  \r\nSo rather than seeing it as \r\nelitism, i see this \\\"code\\\" as \r\nan acknowledgement that there \r\nare master teachers, people \r\nwho are well practiced, or \r\ntrained even in speaking \r\nabout the Unspeakable.  and \r\nwe, you, or me -- anyone can \r\nbecome just such a teacher.  \r\nwith patience, diligence, \r\ncompassion, devotion, love, \r\njoy, equanimity, and all that \r\ngood stuff we can turn all \r\nliving beings on to \r\nliberation and enlightenment -\r\n- the best game around.  \r\n\r\nthat thought makes me really \r\nhappy;-))  ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(951,495,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','in other words, sf needs a \r\nmagnolia.<BR>\r\nthis was a problem for me \r\ngrowing up in houston. \r\nsometimes you just \r\n<b>really</b> don\\\'t want \r\nhouse of pies food, again. \r\nyou want a deep eddy burrito.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(952,495,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','i *love* magnolia\\\'s love \r\nmigas.  lets contact them \r\nregarding franchise \r\nopportunities.  i want to eat \r\nthere in the mornings at 3 \r\na.m.  i want garlic on my \r\nmigas.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(953,496,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kiks','auntie sounds uncannily like \r\nmy mom and my auntie.  I have \r\na secret thing for collectors \r\nbarbies.  Like <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.barbiecollect\r\niblesstore.com/html/collection\r\ns.html\\\">Goddess of Love \r\nBarbie,</a> who\\\'s wearing a \r\ntoga and has grecian ringlets \r\nlike Aphrodite.  Or Goddess \r\nof Wisdom Barbie.  ',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(954,483,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','I waitressed at a pseudo-\r\nbenihana in florida way back \r\nwhen. I have stories, if you \r\nare interested. The place was \r\nexactly the same, teppan-yaki \r\nexpensive faux japanese, but \r\nmore central-florida redneck \r\nand seedy. ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(955,504,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','s5',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(956,504,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<font size=7>KIKI YOU \r\nMANIPULATOR!</FONT>',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(957,504,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'quote','<BR>\r\naus: (gets off fone with k*)\r\n<BR>\r\nkiki: so are you going to \r\nstay then???\r\n<BR>\r\naus: no, she wants me to go\r\n<BR>\r\nkiki:  WHIPPED!\r\n<BR>\r\naus: YOU MANIPULATOR!',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(958,498,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i leave you guys for 3 days \r\nin the desert, and now look \r\nat all this.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(959,504,'2003-02-28 09:38:46',464,'kiki','Welcome to my world!  Vicious \r\nand manipulative!  ',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(960,504,'2003-02-28 09: