\r\nhope you are back on swinney \r\nsoon.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(998,511,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'<b>surgery update</b>','email from sister today. mom\r\nis sittin up, sans uterus,\r\nreading romance novels. -le',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(999,505,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','I remember being very little \r\nand seeing mobiles in our \r\nhouse. My father used to make \r\nthem.\r\n\r\nI wonder if this artist you \r\nspeak of was at all \r\ninfluenced by the Italian \r\nFuturists, whom I love a \r\ngreat deal, and who toured \r\nParis some time just before \r\nthe 20\\\'s. They too were \r\nobsessed with movement and \r\nenergy in all their works, \r\nincluding sculpture. But I am \r\nprobably quite biased; I \r\ndelight in their fascism and \r\nmilitarism, so totally \r\nagainst the grain and in-the-\r\nface of most artistic ideals.\r\n\r\nArt, fart, enough for now.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1000,509,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'mika','chirp! sqweek!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1001,505,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','this is my favorite example \r\nof Italian Futurism. No doubt \r\nCalder was inspired by people \r\nsuch as Boccioni.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1002,505,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://192.41.13.240/art\r\nchive/f/futurist/unique.jpg\\\">t\r\nhis</a>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1003,511,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','beautiful. get well, auntie.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1004,505,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','hopefully i don\\\'t ever dump\r\nanybody because they haven\\\'t\r\nheard of some obscure metal\r\nband i dig.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1005,505,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','ZENI GEVA',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1006,513,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'cyan','hrm.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1007,513,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','it is a good poem.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1008,371,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'aDamage-ah','I challenge YOU to a GAME OF \r\nHORSE SHOES',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1009,514,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'K*','Got a new girlfriend already, \r\nhuh',0,0,0,0,N