n on their \r\nfaces.  i know that sounds \r\nweird.  but, what do you \r\nsuppose collagen comes from?  \r\nthey say that they mostly use \r\nunborn cows and the like, but \r\nit isn\\\'t always true.  more or \r\nless, your poem disturbed me. \r\n ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1041,517,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'huney','<ol>\r\n<li>acting</li>\r\n<li>thinking</li>\r\n<li>listening</li>\r\n<li>writing</li>\r\n<li>playing</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<b>things i\\\'m not good at</b>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>long-term planning</li>\r\n<li>saving money</li>\r\n<li>cooking</li>\r\n<li>lying to other people</li>\r\n<li>bridge pose</li>\r\n</ol>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1042,517,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i would really really like to \r\nlearn how to cook.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1043,517,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'<B>austin</B>','<OL>\r\n<LI>funniness\r\n<LI>being loud\r\n<LI>being quiet\r\n<LI>not giving up\r\n<LI>being there\r\n</OL>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1044,519,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','i got this picture from the \r\nbmg.  i think he has finally \r\nfound his look.\r\n<BR>\r\n<img \r\nsrc=\\\"http://swinney.org/art/ga\r\nlleries/bmg/20.jpg\\\">',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1045,519,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','hi cyan. we\\\'re watching the\r\ntransformers movie.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1046,513,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','yeah i talked to peter last\r\nnight (on the phone - he\\\'s in\r\nitaly) and he said \\\"it was\r\nkind of disturbing, sweetie\\\"\r\nheh.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1047,519,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','le wants me to get the\r\nsoundtrack.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1048,513,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i liked the poem. especially \r\nthe images of fruit.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1049,519,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'chaya','wants you to get the \r\nsoundtrack \r\ntoo.<br><br>...MORE THAN \r\nMEETS THE EYE.<br><br>curses, \r\ni will be singing that for \r\ndays now.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1050,520,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','three days in sf and he\\\'s \nalready found the swings. \nnot bad.\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1051,519,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sawks','<br>\r\nyou have the transformers \r\nmovie and you didn\\\'t invite \r\nme round to watch \r\nit!!!!!<br><br><br>\r\n*sob*\r\n',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1052,517,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','1: not being able to think of \r\nanything i\\\'m good at.<BR>\r\n2: finding good presents for \r\npeople.<BR>\r\n3: worrying <BR>\r\n4: cuddling <BR>\r\n5: being clumsy\r\n',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1053,521,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Joanna','\\\"every girl\\\'s a lesbian after \r\ntwo rum and cokes\\\", if you \r\nwanna be pedantic, which I \r\ndo, after drinking  Guiness \r\nand kissing  German traveling \r\nboys.  ',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1054,521,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'chaya','[le] on further \r\nconsideration<br>\r\n[le] i think the vodka \r\nshots<br>\r\n[le] had an effect',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1055,521,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','um... hi.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1056,521,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','happy st patrick\\\'s day!',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1057,521,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','HI TITS! we miss you, come \r\nhome now now now.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1058,521,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','is le in austin? if she is \r\nshe should call me, 796.6131. \r\nor anyone else that is in \r\ntown for sxsw. a little \r\nswinney.org luncheon on \r\nsunday perhaps? Oh, and I can \r\ngive her austin\\\'s mail =)',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1059,521,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','no austin! only australia. \r\naustin sometime soon though.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1060,521,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','<p>um. i\\\'m in austin. all the \r\ntime. i live here.</p>\r\n<p>SONG: OHIA TOTALLY KICKED \r\nMY ASS LAST NIGHT.</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1061,521,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','or SONGS: OHIA.<BR>\r\nfound out the pronunciation \r\nis oh-HEE-a. which is \r\ninteresting.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1062,519,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'cyan','that picture kicks ass!  that \r\nso rocks.  ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1063,519,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'cyan','btw, how is that movie?  \r\ndarwin burned a copy for me \r\nand i lost it! :(',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1064,513,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','hmmm.... le prefers to write \r\ndisturbing poetry rather than \r\nboring poetry.<br><br>\r\nshe learned a long time ago \r\nthat i would rather she be \r\nbrutally honest than \r\ncarefully concealing.<br><br>\r\none interesting note.  when i \r\nwas pregnant with her, she \r\nwoke up every night at 10pm \r\nand kicked in definite rythym \r\ntoward my left side until \r\ndawn.<br><br>\r\nis it any wonder she like to \r\ndance all night?<br><br>\r\ni think they took the auntie \r\nbits and burned them up in \r\nthe hospital incinerator.  i \r\nforgot to ask.<br><br>\r\ni am now exhausted from \r\ntyping this much.<br><br>\r\nback to bed. i love you \r\nlittle child, and i liked \r\nyour disturbing poem.  now \r\nwrite one about decadence and \r\nbuying new shoes and eating \r\ndelicious stuff and the sun \r\nshining and the breeze \r\nblowing over the bay and all \r\nthe pretty boys posing in the \r\npark trying to attract a one \r\nminute stand...',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1065,522,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'cyan','wow, check out all those \r\ngrammar errors.. whoo hoo!  i \r\nshould have a contest, \\\"if you \r\nfind them all, you win a cup \r\nof coffee!\\\" .. or something \r\nlike that. \r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1066,522,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','i think i have chosen my \r\nbooks wisely on something \r\nlike that pretense.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ni won\\\'t read something that i \r\ndo not want to read.  i have \r\ntaken a few risks, some of \r\nwhich did not pan out.  i \r\nhave read some things that \r\ndidn\\\'t need reading.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ni would have to say that the \r\ncreme of greek classics were \r\nthe best bang for the buck.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ngreek classics are more \r\napplicable to daily life for \r\nme than \\\"TCP/IP NETWORK \r\nAdministration\\\" is.  it is \r\nnot so much that good books \r\ngive me instruction as they \r\ngive me peace of mind that i \r\nam not alone.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ni think',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1067,523,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'K*','I like being a \\\"squeezy\\\".\r\nGood you are writing again.\r\ncathartic',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1068,522,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p>when it\\\'s time to give up \r\non a book, i\\\'ll spend hours \r\nscanning and rescanning \r\nthe same page, but making \r\nno progress. in the past i \r\nwould berate myself into \r\nsticking to it, eventually \r\nfinishing the chapter, but \r\nlater giving up. now i will \r\nrecognize this pattern right \r\naway. this is my head\\\'s way \r\nof telling me, you are \r\nreading something you do \r\nnot enjoy. please stop.</p>\r\n<p>i submit this as an \r\nanswer because the \r\nnumber of books and the \r\nrange of experience i can \r\nabsorb in my lifetime *is* \r\nlimited. and optimizing the \r\nbest use of my time means \r\nrecognizing where i get \r\nstuck, and be ready to put it \r\naside and move on from \r\nthere.</p>\r\n<p>it doesn\\\'t always work. i \r\nhaven\\\'t showered yet \r\ntoday.</p>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1069,522,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i forgot to ask, would \r\nknowing the integer value of \r\nmaximum books you could \r\nread in your lifetime feel \r\nmore or less limiting than \r\nunderstanding your habits \r\nand resources? both are \r\nlimits, but the latter is just \r\nmore mutable. do \r\nresources feel infinite, \r\nunless they are concretely \r\ndefined in advance?',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1070,522,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','<p>the only book i\\\'ve ever \r\ngiven up on in my life was \r\nauden\\\'s women in love. i\\\'ve \r\ntried to read this literally \r\ndozens of times. to no avail. \r\ni always give up. considering \r\nmy voracious reading \r\nappetite, that\\\'s pretty \r\nastounding.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1071,523,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','i\\\'ve been alone for a really \r\nlong time and i like it. it\\\'s \r\ndone me well. which is not to \r\nsay that i don\\\'t crush, don\\\'t \r\nfall in love, don\\\'t get \r\nlonely, don\\\'t sometimes wish \r\ni had someone. just never \r\nenough to actively do \r\nsomething about it.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1072,523,'2003-02-28 09:38:46',464,'kiki',' who are you?',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1073,523,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','i asked you first.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1074,523,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','modest mouse says\r\n<pre><tt>\r\nand i\\\'m lonesome when \r\nyou\\\'re around\r\nand i\\\'m never lonesome \r\nwhen i\\\'m by myself\r\n</pre></tt>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1075,520,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','</p>\r\n<tt>\r\nburritos<br>\r\ncat<br>\r\ncoffee from martha\\\'s<br>\r\n<a\r\nhref=\\\"http://hungry.com/~yeti\\\">his</a>\r\nwarm skin<br>\r\nthe littermaid<br>\r\neating popsicles with s5<br>\r\n</p>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1076,520,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'cyan','were they made from real girl \r\nscouts?  you know they are \r\ngood when they taste just \r\nlike the girl on the box.\r\n\r\n*smirk*',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1077,520,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','now now. more talk like that \r\nand they won\\\'t allow me \r\nback in the playground.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1078,522,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'cyan','yes steve, i think we feel \r\nthat the resource is infinite. \r\n you can apply this question \r\nto much of anything.  \r\nsometimes, i think about this \r\nwhenever i have to do \r\nsomething unpleasant or i \r\nrealize that i\\\'m at a job that \r\nis driving me crazy. (this \r\nquestion helped me to get out \r\nof my last job)  i just told \r\nmyself, \\\"is this really worth \r\nit?\\\"  mostly, because i did \r\nthe equation of my life and it \r\nwasn\\\'t fitting in with the \r\npart that had to do with \r\nhappiness.<br>\r\nsometimes, i worry that i\\\'m \r\nwasting my time with something \r\nwhen the payoff in the end \r\nisn\\\'t something i\\\'m going to \r\ncarry with me for the rest of \r\nmy life.  then i question the \r\nimportance of that question \r\nand wonder why i thought it \r\nimportant to begin with.  as \r\nyou can see, i spend most of \r\nmy time questioning everything \r\nand at times it can drive me \r\nnuts.  anyhow, if i knew how \r\nmany books i could read \r\nbetween now and the time i \r\ndied, i think that it would \r\nslow me down some, because i \r\nwould choose everything with a \r\nnew understanding.  perhaps i \r\nwould read less?  i dunno.  \r\nmaybe i would sit down and \r\nmake a list of what i wanted \r\nto read?  see, that is a \r\nproblem too, because your \r\ninterests change over the \r\nyears..<br>\r\nits 4am.  i\\\'m not going \r\nanywhere.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1079,525,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','i was passing a bakery the \r\nother day.  i think i might \r\nbe a baker again.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1080,517,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Lunesse','1. Cooking<p>\r\n2. Bellydancing<p>\r\n3. Writing<p>\r\n4. Adapting<p>\r\n5. Creating environments<p>\r\n<p>\r\nOne thing I am very bad at:<p>\r\nNOT WORRYING SO MUCH\r\n',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1081,525,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','<p>i\\\'ve been trying to figure \r\nout what i could do that \r\nwould make me really happy. \r\nhow to simplify.<BR>\r\nthe ideal job, i decided, \r\nwould let me work with \r\ninteresting people and listen \r\nto good music all day. it \r\nwould be challenging but low-\r\nstress. rewarding but not \r\nnecessarily high-pay.</p>\r\n<p>i think that i want to \r\njust. work in a record store. \r\nwrite reviews. go to shows. \r\nmaybe (hopefully) become a DJ \r\nsomeday. <b>this</b> is what \r\ni love, music is my passion, \r\nwhy am i not doing it all the \r\ntime?<BR>\r\n(at least i\\\'m lucky enough to \r\nbe in a good town for this.)\r\n</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1082,526,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','cool, i am envious you have a \r\njob.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1083,517,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','I\\\'m good at:\r\n\r\n1. Sitting on furniture.\r\n2. Touching myself.\r\n3. Evoking a feeling of \r\nemptiness and dejection from \r\nthe people around me.\r\n4. Crawling into small, warm \r\nspaces.\r\n5. Cooking. \r\n',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1084,526,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','awesome. Does this mean \r\nthat you will be having a \r\nparty soon?',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1085,521,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','that\\\'s odd, cos when we saw\r\nthem in seattle, the dude said\r\n\\\"oh-high-uh\\\"',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1086,525,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','<p>\r\ni\\\'m also considering going\r\nback to school for an IT\r\ndegree. because i don\\\'t have\r\none now, i have to be\r\n\\\"assessed positively\\\" by the\r\naustralian computer society in\r\norder to get a visa. i plan to\r\nlive in many other countries\r\nas well, and i don\\\'t want to\r\nsuffer this headache again.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\non the other hand, i started a\r\nfilmmaking class last week.\r\nmaybe i\\\'ll become an important\r\nartist and they will all beg\r\nfor me.\r\n</p>',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1087,523,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'yes','<pre>\r\nbut i can\\\'t help the \r\nfeeling...\r\ni could blow through the \r\nceiling...\r\nif i just turn and run...\r\nand it wears me out...\r\n</pre>\r\n',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1088,527,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','word, i have to drive to Los \r\nAngeles in a few minutes.  i \r\ndo not love driving for \r\nmillions of miles.  i have \r\npeter\\\'s cd collection to perk \r\nmy spirits though.  and, i \r\nhave had way too much coffee \r\ntoday.  my brain is in the \r\nvice grip of caffine excess.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1089,527,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Jeru Tha Damajah','i am the kwong jong lim of \r\nhip hop.',5,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1090,521,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','so, <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://home.webworks2000\r\n.net/osiris80/songsfaq.htm\\\">ix\r\n</a> is right. apparently \r\njason molina just pronounced \r\nit \\\"o-hee-uh\\\" twice to fuck \r\nwith us. damn him and his \r\nsexy sexy ways!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1091,517,'2002-09-