t \r\nbeautiful machine. i know a \r\ngood banjo player.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1101,529,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','no coming back! just drive \r\nand drive, stop where it \r\nlooks cool. odd jobs here and \r\nthere. South America, \r\nCentral, you name it. We will \r\ngo there.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1102,529,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','how would one find the privacy\r\nfor a wank?',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1103,529,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','we would all be very good \r\nfriends, of course.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1104,529,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','wow it\\\'s amazing how that \r\ncost is exactly a year\\\'s \r\nworth of rent for me. hmmm.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1105,529,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','fuck yeah.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1106,529,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','wait, does the 55 grand\r\ninclude a driver and gas?',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1107,529,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','if the driver is ME!  byo gas.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1108,529,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','we will have to talk about \r\nthat when we get the \r\nmoney...=)',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1109,529,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jeb','yo - when do we go? :]',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1110,529,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'dza','Hey that\\\'s pretty much the \r\nlayout of the Green Tortoise \r\nbus that I took from OR to \r\nLA.  Wanking: I had to sleep \r\nnext to this canadian guy and \r\nthis french girl who fucked \r\neachother all night.  They \r\nhad just met.  I\\\'m \r\npermanently scarred.  But, \r\nForward Ho! on the Maroon \r\nMoon Bus!',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1111,529,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','ok. when do we leave?? ',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1112,529,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.greentortoise\r\n.com\\\">green tortoise</a>++',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1113,530,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','*hug* stranger',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1114,530,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','it\\\'s like you are stuck in an \r\ninfinite loop. the key is to \r\nbecome non-linear.\r\n\r\nthis helps me:\r\nSutta Nipata - \r\nOvercome your uncertainties \r\nand free yourself from \r\ndwelling on sorrow. If you \r\ndelight in existence, you \r\nwill become a guide to those \r\nwho need you, revealing the \r\npath to many. \r\n\r\n',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1115,533,'2003-07-24 15:44:23',165,'joker','congratulations!',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1116,532,'2003-07-24 15:44:23',165,'joker','that\\\'s fantastic, man.  i had \r\na feeling that you would do \r\nreally well at that.  and i\\\'m \r\nsure you have changed, though \r\nwhat i know of you is \r\nconstant: even-tempered, \r\nindefatigably kind, generous, \r\nwide-eyed, and yes, a little \r\nchubby.  ;-)',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1117,532,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','<b><i>indefatigably<i><b>: \r\nincapable of being fatigued. \r\ni had too look it up.  ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1118,530,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','\r\n<p>I like that quote much, I \r\nam going to put it on my \r\nfridge next to these: </p> \r\n<p>If you take good care of \r\nyourself, you help \r\neveryone.<br>\r\n  You stop being a source of \r\nsuffering to the world,<br>\r\n  and you become a reservoir \r\nof joy and freshness.\r\n<p align=\\\"left\\\"><i>Thich Nhat \r\nHanh<br>\r\n  Teachings on Love</i>\r\n<p align=\\\"left\\\">Our deepest \r\nfear is not that we are \r\ninadequate. Our deepest fear \r\n  is that we are powerful \r\nbeyond our measure. It is our \r\nlight, not our darkness, \r\n  that frightens us. We ask \r\nourselves, who am I to be \r\nbrilliant, gorgeous, talented \r\n  and fabulous? Actually who \r\nare you not to be? You are a \r\nchild of God. Your playing \r\n  small doesn\\\'t serve the \r\nworld. There\\\'s nothing \r\nenlightened about shrinking \r\nso \r\n  that other people won\\\'t \r\nfeel insecure around you. We \r\nare born to manifest the \r\n  glory of God within us. \r\nIt\\\'s in everyone. And as we \r\nlet our light shine, we \r\n  unconsciously give other \r\npeople permission to do the \r\nsame. As we are liberated \r\n  from our own fear, our \r\npresence automatically \r\nliberates\\\' others.\r\n<p align=\\\"left\\\"><i>Nelson \r\nMandela</i>\r\n<p \r\nalign=\\\"left\\\">ENJOY!!!!!!!!!!!!\r\n! (we have little time here \r\non this spinning \r\n  rock)<br>\r\n  <i>jeb</i>\r\n<p align=\\\"left\\\">Dry your \r\neyes, dear. Go out and live \r\nlife!<br>\r\n  <i>bmg</i>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1119,533,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','aWeSoMe! I can\\\'t wait for \r\n<i>me</i> to do the same!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1120,530,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','sometimes it\\\'s just good to \r\nhave someone say \\\"poor \r\nbaby.\\\"<br><br>\r\npoor baby!  you just know \r\nthat you deserve better than \r\nsomeone who makes you cry.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1121,530,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'rational one','i miss being a drama queen. \r\nindulge for me',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1122,533,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','i went to kerrville folk \r\nfestival instead of my \r\ngraduation. i have wondered \r\nif i would have more closure \r\non that chunk of my life if \r\ni\\\'d sweltered in the texas \r\nsun in a long black robe like \r\neveryone else.\r\n<p>\r\ncongrats, joanna!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1123,533,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','I drove to LA with my mom in \r\na Uhaul full of my paintings \r\ninstead of sitting in the \r\nsweltering texas heat.  They \r\nmailed my diploma.  It\\\'s been \r\n2 years and I don\\\'t regret it \r\nso far.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1124,531,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','*theme song from Love Boat*\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1125,531,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','oops, that doesn\\\'t really seem\r\nappropriate, considering how\r\nearnest the prose was, but\r\nthere it is. i am all\r\nmonkeyass over donkey out of\r\nline here.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1126,531,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'cyan','awe, that is enough to make \r\nany girl melt.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1127,531,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','uhg.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1128,533,'2003-07-24 15:44:23'