le to carry things \r\nfor you.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1288,582,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kat','<p>ooh yea, n cheetos [when \r\nlife gets all liquored up, \r\nthey\\\'re the best]</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1289,580,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','oh. that\\\'s nice. ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1290,580,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','i just realized how snotty \r\nthat sounded. quiet \r\nappreciation is hard to \r\nconvey over text.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1291,167,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','wow, i thought i was the only \r\none who had the urge to read \r\nafter cleaning their rooms. \r\nnothing like sitting in your \r\nchair, reading with your feet \r\nup on a clean, made bed. \r\n*orgasms*',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1292,582,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>\r\nmy girl\\\'s love<br>\r\nher arms around me<br>\r\nfresh pops from the box on\r\ns5\\\'s counter<br>\r\nindie rock<br>\r\na dip in the hot tub until i\r\nam dizzy<br>\r\ndew on my life<br>\r\nsupport<br>\r\na job</P>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1293,582,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kat','<p>ooohhhhh<br>\r\ngetting nekkid hottub \r\ndizzzy<br>\r\nthen eating ice cream<br>\r\nwith shared spoons<br>\r\nand your fellow nekkid \r\nfriends</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1294,580,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'s5 appreciates jo','can i quote you on that?',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1295,564,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Paul','So who says doers don\\\'t \r\nthink?  Doers are the folks \r\nwho get stuff done - not just \r\nthink about it or delegate or \r\nget someone else to do it.  \r\nSeems to me I\\\'d just as soon \r\nbe recognized as someone who \r\nactually DOES something - \r\nthere\\\'s too many \r\nthinkers/talkers/posers/wannab\r\nes - to be able to DO \r\nsomething and be recognized \r\nfor it is a positive not a \r\nnegative - I wish I could do \r\nmore - but it\\\'s easier to \r\ntalk and dream about it than \r\nto actually do it.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1296,583,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','it\\\'s funny how hard it is to \r\nlook in the mirror at \r\nourselves when we look around \r\nus and see all these people \r\nwho appear, on the surface, \r\nto be better than we \r\nare...<br><br>\r\nthe truth is, you can\\\'t be a \r\nbutterfly.  you don\\\'t know \r\nwhat that woman saw when she \r\nlooked in her own mirror, or \r\nwhat demons she faced when \r\nshe did her own report \r\ncard...<br><br>\r\nthe first step to change is \r\nrecognizing that a change is \r\nneeded, and the best way to \r\ndo it is a baby step at a \r\ntime.<br><br>\r\na lot of people find it \r\ndifficult to change \r\nthemselves in any way, \r\nphysically or emotionally, \r\nbecause they don\\\'t think they \r\nhave the strength to do \r\nit.<br><br>\r\nthat\\\'s because they count \r\nchange as radical differences \r\nfrom the way things are \r\nnow.<br><br>\r\nnobody said change had to be \r\nradical.  for example, if you \r\nfeel like you are ignoring \r\nyour family for the computer, \r\ndon\\\'t swear off the machine \r\nfor the day or days or even \r\nhours -- just start by \r\nsomething small -- plan on \r\ngetting up and sitting at the \r\ntable for a family meal \r\ninstead of noshing at the \r\nkeyboard.  turn off the \r\nteevee and talk to each other \r\nfor 30 minutes, then turn the \r\nmachines back on. sounds \r\nsmall and insignificant, but \r\nit makes a difference, and \r\nit\\\'s a change.<br><br>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1297,583,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','man, it is easy to be nice to\r\nsomebody elses kids.  in fact,\r\nthey are not yours.  big\r\ndifference.  besides, your\r\nkids are *way* more a pain in\r\nthe ass than most.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nalso, at funereals, everything\r\ngets candy coated.  i promise\r\nto say only good things at\r\nyours.  like that you played\r\nfrisbee with me and took me to\r\nboyscout camp.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ni love you because you took me\r\nto boy scout camp.  several\r\ntimes.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\n(paul is my step dad)',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1298,559,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kat','mmmm. been there. done that \r\njob. bit off more than i \r\ncould chew. had to spit it \r\nout. at some point [better \r\nsooner than later] you need \r\nto be totally upfront about \r\nyour feelings/thoughts, \r\notherwise bitterness insues \r\n[on both sides]. im \r\nhopelessly hopeful and think \r\nthere is always a chance to \r\ngo new places...but you have \r\nto realize it gonna be a new \r\nplace, things never stay the \r\nsame.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1299,584,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','i\\\'m a water sign so i\\\'m used \r\nto, not only making plans \r\nthat i have no intention of \r\ncarrying out, but frequently \r\ngetting other people more \r\nexcited about these plans \r\nthan i am. and i like to \r\nthink that if i get them \r\nReally excited, they\\\'ll start \r\nthe project with me and then \r\nwhen i get bored and start \r\nwandering away, they\\\'ll \r\ncontinue with it and make \r\nsomething really great. i \r\nhope.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1300,583,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','you bought austin and i \r\nbagels at wheatsville coop, \r\nchicken fried steak at \r\ntrudy\\\'s, and went on an great \r\nbike ride with us... much \r\nlove for you here, Paul.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1301,584,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','maybe it\\\'s a metaphor for\r\nrising out of the ashes of\r\nyour past, like a flaming\r\norange-red phoenix. like a\r\ngriffin, like a tree.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1302,584,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','cardinal sign! ugggh why am i \r\nstill awake at 6:30am?',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1303,584,'2004-07-27 05:13:57',63,'olivia','i hate that you\\\'re leaving.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1304,584,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p>travel is much like \r\ndeath, xep. and you\\\'ve built \r\nso much history and context \r\nin melbourne, that coming \r\nhome will be like \\\"killing\\\" \r\nthat other person, and \r\ngiving life again to who you \r\nare here in san francisco. \r\n</p><p>\r\nthink of death as a symbol \r\nfor crossing between \r\ndifferent lives you\\\'ve created \r\nfor yourself. i know that \r\nyou\\\'ll be safe. i miss you, \r\ncan\\\'t wait til you\\\'re back.</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1305,571,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'right brain','Take no books (or prisoners)\r\n\r\nWrite five instead.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1306,586,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','i support daydream #1. \r\nespecially the visiting me \r\npart.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1307,586,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','what language do they speak \r\nin australia? O\\\'well, who \r\ncares I will go there...',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1308,584,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kat','oooh ooh ooh, what jo said. \r\nwait...is that something we \r\nwater signs do? this would \r\nexplain a lot of me. where \r\ncan i find more hardcopy info \r\non this to show to my mother \r\nso she wont be so \r\ndissappointed that i never do \r\nwhat i say im gonna do?!',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1309,586,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','i day dream of having a kitty-\r\ncat named Fat Sausage Jr.  \r\nWhen I come home she runs up \r\nfor some foot-squashing and \r\nrabbit-feet fun.  (foot-\r\nsquashing: when you squash a \r\nkitty with your foot and \r\nhe/she rolls over and \r\nstretches out like a banana.  \r\nrabbit feet: when you tickle \r\na fat kitty\\\'s belly and make \r\nhis/her two back paws \r\nconvulse and scratch.) ',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1310,584,'2002-03-05 20:17:36',17,'austin to s5','i very much wanted to kill my\r\nl.a. self at first.  now i\r\nfeel more comfortable, more\r\nlike i have a san francisco\r\nself.  i think it is okay to\r\ngo back and visit for a few\r\ndays.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1311,587,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','despite the beauty of this\r\npicture, i am repulsed.  o.,\r\nyou are gross.  put me in the\r\ncategory with s5.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1312,587,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','actually i found the story to \r\nbe pretty erotic.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1313,584,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','i understand totally the \r\nconcept of putting in words \r\nthe fear of dying in order to \r\nnegate the possibility of it \r\nactually happening.<br><br>\r\ni don\\\'t much like flying, not \r\nbecause i am afraid of \r\ncrashing, but because i am \r\nafraid of terrorists.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1314,586,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','i knew the minute i met you \r\nat jo\\\'s house that you would \r\nmove to usa someday sooner \r\nrather than later.<br><br>\r\nwhen you come visit jo you \r\nshould be sure to plan a day \r\nor two with dad and i, \r\nbecause he likes to cook for \r\npeople and buy them presents, \r\nand i love all of the people \r\nwho love elly.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1315,587,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','when i was 11 i had dandruff \r\nlike that and i don\\\'t know \r\nwhy, but i also enjoyed \r\nscratching my head to the \r\nrawness and i got a big ol\\\' \r\nugly place on it and the \r\nstupid school shrinks decided \r\ni was disturbed.  i was \r\nunable to put the scratching \r\nsatisfaction into words so \r\nthey entered the \\\"fact\\\" of my \r\npsychological problems into \r\nmy school records and to this \r\nday i cannot explain the \r\ntruth to my mother.  she has \r\nher own sense of reality and \r\nfamily history.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1316,584,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','<p>\r\nauntie, hopefully nobody\\\'s\r\ngoing to hijack the flights\r\nfrom florida to texas.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\ni\\\'m a water sign too (i think\r\n- if aquarius isn\\\'t a water\r\nsign then astrology really is\r\nstupid). i behave exactly as\r\ndescribed above. maybe\r\nastrology isn\\\'t stupid.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\ni like my melbourne self, with\r\nall its bumps and bruises, so\r\nmuch more than my sf self.\r\nit\\\'s much more creative and\r\nenergetic and motivated to\r\nenjoy life. it helps a lot\r\nthat my melbourne self doesn\\\'t\r\nhave to work a day job.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nxep, i\\\'m sorry i didn\\\'t hug\r\nyou goodbye.\r\n</p>',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1317,584,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'madame s5','<p>aquarius is the water \r\nbearer, an air sign. \r\naquarius is about, among \r\nother things, bringing new \r\nideas to other people. ix, \r\nyou have your moon in \r\ncancer (i have this too), \r\nthough, which is about as \r\nwatery as it gets: sensitive, \r\nnurturing, intuitive, though \r\nnot necessary appearing so  \r\non the surface.</p>\r\n<p>the trait you guys are \r\ntalking about is cardinality. \r\ncancer is a cardinal sign, \r\nas are aries, libra, and \r\ncapricorn. cardinal signs \r\nare all about \r\nbeginnings.</p>\r\n<p>everyone\\\'s chart \r\ncontains all planets and all \r\nsigns, expressed in \r\ndifferent ways in relation to \r\neach other. so knowing \r\nwhat your sun sign is \r\ndoesn\\\'t tell you very much, \r\nuntil you start to examine \r\nwhat all the other \r\narchetypes are doing in \r\neach arena of life.</p>\r\n<p>astrology is a useful \r\ntool for understanding \r\nyourself and others, though \r\nit can also be used as a \r\ntool to make excuses for \r\nyour less noble \r\nqualities.</p>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1318,587,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','if i didn\\\'t know you, that \r\nstory\\\'d be quite gross. but \r\nseeing as i know you, it just \r\nmakes me giggle.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1319,584,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','oh. i read that it was a \r\nwater sign trait to make \r\nplans you never carry out. \r\n<BR>\r\nand. hey! i wasn\\\'t making \r\nexcuses.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1320,587,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','yes! auntie and olivia, your \r\nstories reminded me of a \r\nfriend of mine whose entire \r\nfamily has different hair-\r\nrelated compulsions. her mom \r\nendlessly searches her own \r\nhair for split ends and then \r\nvery slowly splits the entire \r\nhair. her sister chews her \r\nhair compulsively, so much so \r\nthat there is always a damp \r\nsection of her hair. and she \r\nherself endlessly wraps the \r\nsame section of hair around \r\nher right index finger. \r\nalbeit the most attractive of \r\nthe compulsions, BUT. there \r\nis actually a psychological \r\nterm for having compulsive \r\nbehaviors regarding your own \r\nhead/hair! and now i can\\\'t \r\nremember it.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1321,587,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i think anything involving the\r\nharvesting of one\\\'s own bodily\r\ncreations (fluid, skin, poo,\r\netc) is really satisfying: zit\r\npopping, booger picking,\r\nscraping dead skin off with\r\nyour nails, peeing...\r\n</p><p>\r\ni like olivia because she pops\r\nmy zits without asking and it\r\nis understood that this\r\ndoesn\\\'t lower the my opinion\r\nof her (or hers of me) even a\r\ntiny bit.\r\n',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1322,588,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','hi! uhhh. hi!',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1323,584,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','*nod*. just a general \r\nstatement! i even clicked \r\n\\\"best friendly\\\".',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1324,587,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','you know, if you think the \r\ndandruff chunks are \r\nsatisfying, you should start \r\nbleaching too. for about a \r\nweek after i\\\'m freshly \r\nbleached, it\\\'s HUNTING \r\nSEASON for scabs. woo \r\nchemical burns!',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1325,584,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'chaya','aries sun, cancer rising, \r\nlibra moon.  SO MUCH CARDINAL \r\nSIGN.  elly once wrote me a \r\nthing about why i am <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://chaya.org/beginni\r\nngs.html\\\">beginnings.</a>  \r\nsometimes i wish i wasn\\\'t, \r\nnot so much.  maybe i\\\'d get \r\nmore things done.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1326,586,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'chaya','oh fine.  i see how it is.  ',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1327,586,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','*megaphone*',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1328,586,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'chaya','oh my god so much megaphone.  \r\nSO MUCH MEGAPHONE.  i will \r\nnow click \\\"burn!  =burn!\\\" in \r\nanticipation of the megaphone.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1329,586,'2004-07-27 05:14:09',63,'olivia sez',' oh, chaya, bathing in your\r\npresence is just a given,\r\neveryone knows that you would\r\nbe my primary motivation for\r\nmoving.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nhi chaya!  i like you!<br>\r\n<br>\r\n*clicks best friendly*',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1330,586,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'chaya','aww!  *smoosh*  i miss you \r\nliv, please come back to us.  \r\nalso, need megaphone badly.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1331,588,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','<p>she sure is a nice \r\ngirl.</p>\r\n<p>i think about this so \r\nmuch. so much. not just with \r\nelly, with so many people. i \r\nthink about the <b>tiny</b> --\r\n and i really minute \r\ndecisions -- that i made that \r\nhave led to incredibly \r\nfulfilling friendships and. \r\nit makes it hard to not \r\nbelieve that there\\\'s some. \r\nbigger. cosmic things going \r\non.</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1332,588,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','<p>also. i think about this a \r\nlot with music. music is such \r\na good way to prove how the \r\ntiniest moments can change \r\nyour life.<BR>\r\nlike i put a magnetic fields \r\nsong on a <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://standing.ontheout\r\nside.com/tapes/elly.txt\\\">cd i \r\nmade for elly</a> but it \r\nwasn\\\'t until she and olivia \r\nwere here and we were driving \r\ndowntown to see a movie, \r\ncramped in the cab of my \r\ntruck, and listening to \r\nvolume one of 69 love songs, \r\nthat (i think) elly really \r\nliked magnetic fields.<BR>\r\n(it\\\'s a small example. but \r\nit\\\'s interesting. music is so \r\ngreat!)</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1333,587,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'slm','the word is trichotillomania. \r\n (my mom and my aunt both have \r\nthis and it drives me up the \r\nwall.  the image of my mom \r\npulling at her hair -- not \r\npulling it out, just \r\nseparating out one strand and \r\npulling it -- is burned into \r\nmy mind\\\'s eye.  makes it very \r\nhard to sleep on long car \r\nrides when one is sitting in \r\nthe back seat.)',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1334,588,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','it\\\'s true about jo being why \r\n<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/j\r\nournals/article.phtml?\r\nid=205.txt\\\"> i like the \r\nmagnetic fields</a>. also, i \r\nsubsequently influenced at \r\nleast two <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://oof.diaryland.com\r\n\\\">other</a> <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://maz.org/bcm\\\">peop\r\nle</a> to really like the \r\nmagnetic fields. so that \r\nmeans, by transitive \r\nproperties, jo has foisted \r\nthe magnetic fields on at \r\nleast three people that i \r\nknow of. oh, four. there\\\'s \r\nalso olivia. there\\\'s nothing \r\nso great as showing people \r\ngood music you like.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1335,588,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','<p>stefan is the reason that \r\ni like the magnetic \r\nfields.</p>\r\n<p>people i have since turned \r\nonto the band: jesse, \r\nmelissa, harley, michael, \r\nels.</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1336,588,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','le is my darling child who i \r\nlove very much and she is \r\ntruly amazingly wonderful and \r\ni am glad other people \r\nrealize that, too.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1337,591,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Joanna','I never ever ever ever did it \r\nwhen I was a kid, I was like \r\n18 when  I started it, and I  \r\nblame Oh completley, but I \r\nsuck my thumb when I\\\'m \r\nfeeling insecure.  I spelt \r\nincompletly wrong, sorry.  \r\nTwice even.  Double sorry. I \r\ndo have immaculate \r\npunctuation though, I think.  ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1338,586,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','hey chaya do you have a \r\nmegaphone too? you should get \r\none.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1339,584,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','this is comment #14.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1340,580,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'delayed jo response','oh yes. of course.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1341,591,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i rub my first toe and big toe \r\nagainst each other. \r\nsometimes i twirl my hair, \r\neven though it\\\'s short. ',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1342,592,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','swinney is the bestest. are \r\nthey going to alcatraz?',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1343,584,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','curses! foiled again.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1344,592,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'snafu','erm...where is the image?',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1345,592,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'snafu','...and unfortunately we \r\ndidn\\\'t have the foresight to \r\nbuy Alcatraz tickets 392847 \r\ndays in advance.  :\\\\',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1346,593,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','My mom got some of that tuna \r\nin the pouch. She said it \r\nwould be convenient. I ate \r\nsome of it. I didn\\\'t mix it \r\nwith anything and I ate too \r\nmuch of it. It was a bad \r\nexperience, yet conveniently \r\nso. I applaud the pouch.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1347,591,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','For comfort I move my jaw \r\naround. When I stretch it in \r\na certain way it makes \r\ntearing and popping sounds. \r\nIt is like cracking the \r\nknuckles.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1348,588,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','le is nice. I don\\\'t know what \r\nher or your world is like, \r\nbut it seems nice and kind of \r\nwonderful sometimes. I don\\\'t \r\nhave any friends. I have some \r\ncolleagues and we discuss \r\nthings. One of them broke up \r\nwith his girlfriend on the \r\ngrounds that \\\"anyone who is \r\nnot my colleague is my \r\nenemy\\\". And I guess that sums \r\nup what goes on here.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1349,587,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','This is good to hear. I have \r\nvery long hair and some nasty \r\ndandruff myself, and use all \r\nkinds of stupid shampoos for \r\nmy scalp. It really is \r\nterrible, the shampoos kill \r\nmy hair. It is comforting to \r\nsee someone out there who can \r\nlive -- nay, <i>thrive</i> -- \r\nwith it.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1357,588,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Jason','Also, I think the Magnetic \r\nFields ae a part of the \r\nreason that Jo and I are \r\nfriends.  That and \r\nGeography.  and Salon.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1351,594,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','you should talk to (www.)\r\nchiamattt(.com).  he puffs \r\ntreez all day.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1352,591,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','mine aren\\\'t so cute, so i \r\ndon\\\'t know if they qualify: \r\n<br>\r\n1) crack my wrists by \r\nspasmodically flinging them \r\nin circles. only seen in full \r\nfledge stress situations.<br>\r\n2) (a little cuter than the \r\nprevious) shuffle my feets \r\nover each other like crickets \r\nsinging- shuf-shuf-shuf. jeff \r\ntells me that i do this right \r\nbefore i fall asleep. and \r\nwhen i\\\'m content, like when \r\ni\\\'m reading a good book.<br>\r\n3) tugging at my earlobes \r\nabsentmindedly.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1353,590,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','sublime',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1354,596,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','austin. i will introduce you to \r\nbusvan. good quality \r\ninexpensive furntiure that \r\nyou can get delivered in a \r\nday or two. i\\\'ll even go \r\nwander around the \r\nshowroom with you, if you \r\nwant.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1355,591,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','the earlobe thing is painfully \r\ncute.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1356,596,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'dza','s5 wants to marry austin! s5 \r\nwants to marry austin! nah \r\nnah nananah!',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1358,584,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','i\\\'m voting for this entry as \r\nthe one with the most \r\ncomments ever. ever times a \r\nmillion.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1359,593,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kat','<p>i love the pouch. \r\n*anything* in a pouch is \r\nworthy of attention. costco \r\nhas an awesome chinese \r\nchicken salad meal with all \r\nthe meat precooked and in an \r\noh-so-easy to reheat pouch. \r\nand stouffer\\\'s made some good \r\ntortellini in a pouch. you \r\ncould just pop it into \r\nboiling water and it came out \r\nperfect...but i dont think \r\nthey make it anymore. the \r\npouch is almost as cool as \r\nvelcro.</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1360,593,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','mmm mom\\\'s tuna salad. xep \r\nmakes vegan tuna salad that \r\ntastes creepily like real \r\ntuna.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1361,588,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','*excite* hi jason!!!',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1362,596,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i can help you make an altar. \r\nit is what i do. and if you \r\nhave one, i will leave \r\nobjects on it.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1363,596,'2002-03-05 20:17:36',17,'austin to elly','<P>i will take you up on\r\nthat.  i wonder what will go\r\nthere?\r\n</P>\r\n',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1364,584,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','hi.  the plane didn\\\'t crash.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1365,600,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','so where are the pictures?',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1366,601,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'gage','d00d.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1367,601,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','That is a very nice red wall.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1368,602,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','what is your astrological\r\nsign? i guess: earth sign. ',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1369,602,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'paul','Pisces',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1370,602,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','oh. i am bad at guesses.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1371,602,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','i dont have one of those lists\r\nfor today.  maybe i will find\r\none somewhere.  but i can tell\r\nyou this:  jennifer capriati,\r\ni have a huge hibernating bear\r\ncrush on her.  ever since i\r\nread a people magazine article\r\nabout how she went on a sex\r\ncrazed drug binge.  i read\r\nthat and i was in love.  i may\r\nhave had a crush on her before\r\nthat,in truth, i know i did.\r\nwhat a fiery star of humanity\r\nshe is.  i love her.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1372,598,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','hm.<br><br>\r\ni lived two hundred miles from\r\nmy family for years and never\r\nsaw them very often, maybe i\r\nwould see <a\r\nhref=\\\"http://swinney.org/journals/userpages.phtml?username=paul\\\">paul</a>\r\nbut that is it for the most\r\npart.  i guess that is why i\r\ndo not mind moving around so\r\nmuch lately.  i realized how\r\nmuch i have to live with\r\nmyself and how little i rely\r\non others.  \r\n<br><br>\r\nthe hardest person to leave is\r\nalways my roomate.  i always\r\nmiss my roomate too.  roomates\r\nare as close as it comes for\r\nme to being married.  i live\r\nwith them and see them every\r\nnight and all weekend, we get\r\nin fights, we forgive each\r\nother. so on and so forth.\r\n',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1373,598,'2002-03-05 20:17:36',17,'austin to austin','yes, but you do in fact rely\r\non others heavily and you know\r\nit.  i admit, saying you do\r\nnot does help your arguement\r\nthough.  ',5,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1374,603,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','you are definitely the spawn \r\nof my loins.<br><br>\r\ni\\\'m really sorry about the \r\nparanoia genes, darling \r\nchild.<br><br>\r\nbut, don\\\'t you really like \r\nthe ones that get you excited \r\nabout new stuff and the ones \r\nthat make you really \r\ninterested in other people?\r\n<br><br>\r\n',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1375,602,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','mmm. tennis skirts.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1376,599,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Brenda','I liked your writing today.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1377,593,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'nikki','my mama makes me tuna noodle \r\ncasserole (same thing) with \r\npeas and peanut butter \r\nsandwitches... mmm... \r\nsometimes I eat so much I get \r\nsick!  ',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1378,601,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','i am a small asian bush today.\r\n',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1379,593,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','there are a lot of things in\r\naustralia with pouches.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1380,602,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','Paul, you are the coolest. ',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1381,591,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','during tetrasomia there was a\r\nlot of fire.  back stage xiao\r\nhong, who was supposed to be\r\non \\\"make sure the curtains\r\ndon\\\'t catch on fire\\\" duty\r\nspent most of his time setting\r\nhis fingers on fire\r\nintentionally.  he would set\r\nthem on fire, then shake them\r\nso it would go out, then pinch\r\nhis ear lobes.  i asked him\r\nwhy he pinched his ear lobes\r\nand he said there\\\'s an\r\nacupressure point there that\r\nmakes the fingers stop\r\nburning.  i think he just\r\nliked to pinch his ear lobes\r\nthough.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1382,601,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'cyantist','wow!  your hair looks awesome!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1383,576,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'cyantist','that sent diaryland page \r\nrocks!  ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1384,605,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','think oedipus rex.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1385,605,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'cyantist','s/frisbe/frisbee/g',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1386,605,'2003-05-10 16:09:14',79,'yeti','exit 0',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1387,598,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kat','<p.the cakes r baked and only \r\nthe passed out people are \r\nleft. im one of them. the \r\nparty was good...but im still \r\nfeeling sorry for myself.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>and yea the hardest part \r\nit leaving my roommate.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>austin you saved my \r\nass.... stupid frijole [me]. \r\ni was so upset i couldnt see \r\nstraight enough to add a \r\ntitle.</p>',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1388,598,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kat','6:00  am  ...woohoo',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1389,601,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','what now, brown cow?<br> \nweeb.com/curly/ \n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1390,588,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<B>i have le\\\'s cat on my\r\nbutt.</B>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1391,606,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>where are you getting this\r\ncash from juan?\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ni don\\\'t understand the dvd\r\naddiction.  i guess it is like\r\ncollecting books.  probably\r\nexactly alike.  i usually\r\nalways buy books.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nbut then i saw the SF library\r\nnear my house at 24th between\r\nValencia and Mission and it\r\nhad a sign out front that\r\nsaid, \\\"Thank you for visiting\r\n<u>this</u> branch of the San\r\nFrancisco Library System.\\\"  I\r\nthought, what i nice\r\ninvitation.  I am going to go\r\nthere.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nso i think i will go there\r\nmonday and check out a copy of\r\n\\\"Duane\\\'s Depressed\\\" by Larry\r\nMcMurtry.  I have wanted to\r\nread that book for a while.  I\r\ndo not care that it is the\r\nlast in a trilogy.  i am going\r\nto read it and if i like it i\r\nwill read the others.</P>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1392,607,'2004-07-27 05:14:09',63,'olivia sez',' i bet le will having\r\nsomething intelligent to say\r\nabout this, but as far as i\\\'m\r\nconcerned, didn\\\'t everyone\r\ncover this topic to death\r\nabout a year ago?',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1393,603,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','ahaha. and then i got the \r\nemail today in my inbox when \r\ni got home and thought, \\\"oh \r\nboy. i should reply to this \r\nright away. i bet she\\\'s been \r\nwaiting for this answer since \r\nfriday afternoon.\\\"<BR>\r\nbut instead i ate some ice \r\ncream.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1394,608,'2003-05-10 16:09:14',79,'yeti','Fabulous Furry Freak Brothers\r\nToo Much Coffee Man\r\nSwamp Thing\r\nSome more I cant think of.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1395,608,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','i like you, liv. please come \r\nsnuggle. love, jo.<BR>\r\n(oh i should be constructive, \r\ntoo. the only comics i ever \r\nread were sandman. and i sure \r\ndid love them.)',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1396,588,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','jason! you\\\'re totally right! \r\ni never would have responded \r\nto your salon personal if you \r\nhadn\\\'t written about the \r\nmagnetic fields! oh huzzah!\r\n<BR>\r\n(this is jason. he\\\'s one of \r\nmy bestest friends. i love \r\nhim very much. please pet \r\nhim.)',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1397,608,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'pdo','I highly recommend \r\nTransmetropolitan.  Also, \r\nreprints of Sandman never \r\nhurt :)',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1398,607,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','fitzgerald had interesting\r\nstories to tell about other\r\npeople as well as himself.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1399,608,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','<p>\r\ni\\\'m going to put my comic\r\ndatabase back together today\r\nor tomorrow. it will live <a\r\nhref=\\\"http://www.maz.org/bcm/comics\\\">here</a>.\r\nof course this depends on s5\r\nfinishing his mysql\r\ninstallation.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nonce it\\\'s online, i will hire\r\nsome monkeys to scan all the\r\ncovers.\r\n</p>',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1400,609,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kdawg','come back! come back! come \r\nback!  Ummm...if you want to, \r\nthat is.  ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1401,609,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','sometimes i think this website\r\nis all about luring people\r\nbetween san francisco, austin\r\nand melbs.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1402,608,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p>i second yeti\\\'s freak \r\nbrothers recommendation. \r\na lot of the comics are \r\nabout san francisco in the \r\n60s and 70s, which is \r\nsuper cool.</p>\r\n<p>\r\nothers:\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\n<li>eightball, or anything by \r\ndaniel clowes for that \r\nmatter, is psychologically \r\nsurreal.\r\n<li>anything by adrian \r\ntomine (optic nerve is pretty \r\ngood)\r\n<li>anything by robert \r\ncrumb (of <b>course</b>)\r\n<li>anything by jhonen \r\nvasquez, especially for \r\nrecovering goths (hi.). \r\n\\\"squee\\\" is so funny that \r\nyou\\\'ll wet yourself.\r\n<li>and pick up random \r\ncomics published on \r\nfantagraphic.\r\n</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1403,607,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','some people do both (i.e. post \r\nfiction on the internet and \r\nwork on art in the real \r\nworld). i use postings as a \r\ntool to keep the specious crap \r\nout of the rest of the stuff \r\ni\\\'m engaged in.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1404,608,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'dj1_luna','<p>&quot;Kill your \r\nboyfriend&quot; by <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.popimage.com/\r\nprofile/morrison/012501morriso\r\nn_guide.shtml\\\">grant \r\n  morrison</a></p>\r\n<p><a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.preachersdivi\r\nnity.com/\\\">&quot;Preacher&quot\r\n;</a> by Garth \r\n  Ennis and Steve Dillon<br>\r\n  <br>\r\n  <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.darkhorse.com\r\n/products/pg_profile/sku_92256\r\n/sec_search/index.html\\\">Sin \r\n  City</a> by Frank Miller</p>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1405,610,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p>i\\\'ve been here 5 years, \r\nand i\\\'m still just as in love \r\nwith san francisco as the \r\nday i moved here.</p>\r\n<p>i feel like the city is alive.  \r\neven through all the chaos \r\nand struggles that the <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.sfbg.com/\\\"\r\n>bay guardian</a> harps \r\non, the dynamic nature of \r\neverything adds an intensity \r\nto life here that can be both \r\naddictive and \r\noverwhelming.</p>\r\n<p>i think the same thing \r\nthat drives people away is \r\nwhat keeps me in san \r\nfrancisco. it\\\'s not for \r\neveryone. glad to see that \r\npeople are still coming, \r\ngood luck with your new \r\nlife.</p>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1406,609,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','i just talked to kdog on the\r\nphone. she said the jobless\r\nand layed off austinites are\r\nmeeting monday mornings for\r\nbreakfast.  i know that\r\ntraditionally that sort of\r\nmeeting is supposed to be a\r\nmotivational event where\r\npeople cheer each other on to\r\nfind work.  somehow i think it\r\nmust be more like an\r\ninquisition on the economy led\r\nby disgruntleds.  maybe i will\r\ndrive down there and say hi\r\nsome time.  i feel like\r\nexhausted here.  i am like a\r\nfailed california venture.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1407,612,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<PRE>. go to sine\\\'s party!\r\n</pre>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1408,608,'2004-07-27 05:14:09',63,'olivia sez',' ok i forgot about too much \r\ncoffee man and squee.  i have \r\nread and enjoyed already.  \r\ngood to see that two of my \r\nfavourite sf boys are on my \r\nwavelength.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1409,615,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'cyantist','dirty and hungry.<br>\r\ndesperate and lonely..<br>\r\nbroken.. <br>with a story to \r\ntell..<br>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\nnot free from himself.<br><br>\r\n\r\nalthough this is lovely \r\nsteve.. most homeless people \r\nhave nothing for you to envy. \r\n \r\nit is easy to be like him. \r\npack your bag right now and \r\nwalk out the door. it wouldn\\\'t \r\nbe long until you figured out \r\nthat your life can be more \r\nfree than you could have ever \r\npossibly imagined without \r\nhaving to take that walk in \r\nhis shoes.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\nhomelessness is not a romantic \r\nnotion. <br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n  ',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1410,614,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'cyantist','\\\"Sometimes there\\\'s so much \r\nbeauty in the world I feel \r\nlike I can\\\'t take it, like my \r\nheart\\\'s going to cave \r\nin.\\\"<br><br>\r\n\\\"                             \r\n            i guess i could be \r\npretty pissed off about what \r\nhappened to me but it\\\'s hard \r\nto stay mad\r\n                              \r\n           when there\\\'s so \r\nmuch beauty in the world \r\nsometimes i feel like i\\\'m \r\nseeing it all at once and\r\n                              \r\n           it\\\'s too much may \r\nheart fills up like a balloon \r\nthat\\\'s about to burst and then \r\ni remember to\r\n                              \r\n           relax and stop \r\ntrying to hold on to it and \r\nthen if flows through me like \r\nrain and i can\\\'t feel\r\n                              \r\n           anything but \r\ngratitude for every single \r\nmoment of my stupid little \r\nlife you have no idea what\r\n                              \r\n           i\\\'m talking about, \r\ni\\\'m sure but don\\\'t worry you \r\nwill someday\\\"<br><br>\r\namerican beauty.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1411,605,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'cyantist','i still don\\\'t get it!!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1412,613,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'cyantist','nice people rule.  some people \r\nappear to be nice, but really \r\naren\\\'t. <br>\r\nfor example... wet girl... in \r\ntight jeans... and he wanted \r\nto take you home? :)',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1413,605,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','isn\\\'t oedeipus rex a movie \r\nwith whoopie goldberg in it?',5,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1414,613,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','i wouldn\\\'t wear tight jeans!\r\nno way, honey :)\r\nyech.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1415,446,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'cyantist','mmmm... callipygian',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1416,615,'2004-07-27 05:14:09',63,'olivia sez',' is it just me or is cyan\r\ndetermined to take the romance\r\nout of everything?  how\\\'s your\r\nsex life, honey?',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1417,615,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','some context:<br>\r\n<br>\r\nthe man in the story is a \r\nwanderer. his possessions \r\nwere kept in a hiking pack, \r\nnot a shopping cart. i was \r\nthinking along the lines of \r\n<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.amazon.co\r\nm/exec/obidos/ASIN/01400\r\n42520/o/qid=986206541/sr\r\n=8-1/ref=aps_sr_b_1_1/10\r\n3-5569293-2999038\\\">dhar\r\nma bums</a>.<br>\r\n<br>\r\ni wrote this because earlier \r\nthat day i was out to lunch \r\nwith <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.athayoga.c\r\nom\\\">kristie</a>. among \r\nother things, we talked \r\nabout the nature of being \r\nand attachment, the \r\nsignificance of \r\npossessions and status, \r\nand how it all relates to \r\none\\\'s personal journey. the \r\ntitle itself was meant to be \r\nironic, as envy is just \r\nanother form of \r\nattachment.<br>\r\n<br>\r\ndon\\\'t fuck with me, cyan. \r\nwhile i understand there\\\'s \r\nstill some element of <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.boondocks\r\nnet.com/kipling/kipling.html\\\"\r\n>white man\\\'s burden</a> \r\npresent in our thinking, \r\naccusing me of \r\nromanticizing the homeless \r\nis completely out of \r\nline.<br>\r\n<br>\r\ni know it\\\'s fashionable to \r\npretend that we all \r\nsympathize with the \r\nhomeless. but the fact of \r\nthe matter is, very few \r\npeople are willing to break \r\nout of their middle class \r\nsuburban consumer \r\nobsession long enough to \r\ngive much more than \r\nguilt-ridden lip service.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nwhich brings me to your \r\nill-conceived comment \r\nposted above. i feel that it \r\nspeaks for itself.<br>\r\n<br>\r\ni am shocked that someone \r\ni once respected would \r\nstoop to jumping down my \r\nthroat on this otherwise \r\npeaceful and civil online \r\ncommunity.<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<font \r\ncolor=\\\"#FF0000\\\"><h1>BUR\r\nN! BURN!</h1></font>\r\n',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1418,605,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','oedipus rex is from greek \r\nmythology. and later was \r\nadopted by freud as the \r\narchetype explaining the \r\nmale motivation: to find a \r\nwoman identical to his \r\nmother, sublimating the \r\nunconscious desire to have \r\nsex with her.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nmartha stuart is supposedly \r\nthe ideal homemaker, so \r\nthere you have it. fetish \r\nexplained by oedipal \r\ndesires.<br>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1419,614,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i liked this post, please \r\nwrite more often. and next \r\ntime the wind is this \r\nblustery: kite flying!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1420,613,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sawks','<br>\r\nwhen jo gets wet she \r\nsmells like compost :P',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1421,601,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.saturn5.co\r\nm/steve/photos/index.cgi/w\r\neeb\\\">contrast</a>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1422,615,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','okay, children, here\\\'s what \r\nmom says:<br><br>\r\ncyan appears to have had a \r\ngut reaction to the horrors \r\nof homelessness without \r\nstopping to consider the \r\njournalist.<br><br>\r\nsteve has hurt feelings \r\nbecause he can\\\'t believe that \r\ncyan would think so lowly of \r\nhim.<br><br>\r\ni don\\\'t think cyan really \r\nbelieves steve to be callous, \r\nand now it\\\'s time to say \r\nsorry.<br><br>\r\nnow my 2 cents:<br><br>\r\nnot everyone who is homeless \r\nis that way because of some \r\ntragic reason.<br><br>\r\neveryone with lots of \r\nresponsibilities may be \r\ntempted to chuck them all and \r\nrun away at one time or \r\nanother. i believe that the \r\nwords were about that \r\nwish...<br><br>\r\nthose words made me feel a \r\nlittle envious, too, and \r\nhaving been homeless myself a \r\nfew times in my life, i think \r\ni have a unique \r\nperspective.<br><br>\r\nsay sorry now and make \r\nup.<br><br>\r\nlove and kisses,<br><br>\r\nauntie\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1423,614,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','how lovely!<br><br>\r\nknowing a yeti is indeed a \r\nwondrous thing!<br><br>\r\ntell us more, dear \r\nboy.<br><br>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1424,610,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','if i didn\\\'t have another life \r\ni had to live, i would be in \r\nsf, too.<br><br>\r\nbe sure to spend some time \r\nsitting in the sun at that \r\ncafe in the castro with \r\nchairs outside.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1425,611,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','i like to watch the \r\nteevee.<br><br>\r\none of the most fun shows to \r\nwatch is imus in the morning. \r\nthat man is the grouchiest \r\nperson i ever saw and i am \r\nmesmerized by the mean things \r\nhe says and how nuts he is \r\nand i wonder how the hell he \r\nmanaged to turn that into a \r\ncareer and i wish i could be \r\ngrouchy and get paid for it, \r\ntoo.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1426,612,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','flying into austin last \r\nnight, the steward said that \r\nwe have arried in dallas... i \r\nnearly shat myself... then he \r\nsaid, april fools...',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1427,614,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i came from far away, to \r\npress myself against the \r\nyeti and breathe',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1428,612,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','my father named me april.  i \r\nhave always hated april fools \r\nday.<br><br>\r\nit\\\'s more fun to do that \r\nstuff on days that are not \r\napril 1st.  it confuses the \r\nhell out of people.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1429,607,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','</p><p>i don\\\'t know. i think \r\nthe ease of internet \r\npublishing does shorten \r\nour attention span. it\\\'s kind \r\nof like video games or mtv \r\nfor writing. i worry a lot \r\nabout the fact that i can\\\'t \r\nseem to motivate to write \r\nsomething longer or less \r\nself referential. \r\n</p><p>\r\non the other hand, i think it\\\'s \r\nreally important that the \r\nformality has been removed \r\nfrom self expression. i can\\\'t \r\ncall it \\\"good\\\" or \\\"bad\\\" that \r\nanyone can say anything on \r\nvery short notice, i can only \r\nsay that it\\\'s different. it\\\'s \r\nmaking us relate to each \r\nother differently. and that\\\'s \r\nimportant.</p>\r\n',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1456,622,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','maria i\\\'m so sorry that your \r\nexperience in austin was \r\ntainted by this. you should \r\nhave just emailed me ahead of \r\ntime and you could have \r\nstayed with me. or dakota.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1431,607,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','i worry a lot that linking \r\nthings and then commenting on \r\nthem passes as writing.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1432,615,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','okay, i will write it, but \r\nyou know i\\\'ve never even told \r\nmy kids or husband the \r\ndetails, so it will be hard \r\nto write.<br><br>\r\ni will do it if elly doesn\\\'t \r\nmind.  she hates hearing sad \r\nstories of my childhood.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1433,565,'2002-04-12 05:27:03',57,'weeb the unholy','i just wanted to say: BOMBASS\r\nRestaurant. so there.\r\n',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1434,616,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'mike','left out whole words..my ,my!',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1435,613,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','i do not!\r\nsawks when are you coming \r\nhome to play? i miss you.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1436,615,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'cyantist','how erudite of you \r\nsteve.<br><br>\r\nleave it to you to pull out \r\nthe Jack Kerouac reference.  \r\nwhat next.. \\\"on the road?\\\"  \r\n<br><br>\r\nyour poem was well written and \r\ni admire you for that, however \r\nbuddy... all is fair in love \r\nand war.  prepare for flame.  \r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\ni\\\'m probably one of the \r\nstrongest advocates of leaving \r\neverything behind you and \r\nhitting the road with nothing \r\nbut a blankie, a knapsack, and \r\nsome sort of vague plan.  \r\nhowever, most homeless people \r\nhave nothing like this in \r\nmind.  your poem didn\\\'t \r\ndescribe what you intended and \r\nthat was merely my statement \r\nabove.  yes.. not all homeless \r\npeople are down and out and \r\nhard on their luck.<br><br>\r\nmy exboyfriend and i were \r\nhomeless for nearly four to \r\nfive months and we travelled \r\nall over the place without a \r\ncare in the world.  this was \r\none of the best experiences in \r\nmy life and i never was truly \r\nhomeless.  everywhere i went \r\nbecame my home.  everything i \r\nsaw and did was part of my big \r\nadventure, until one day.. i \r\nrealized that i might not be \r\nable to pull out of it.  i \r\ncould have ended up a person \r\nthat you might disregard on \r\nthe street begging you for a \r\nspare anything.  lucky for me, \r\ni figured out early in life \r\nthat this wasn\\\'t the path that \r\ni wanted to take.  pulling \r\nmyself up by the bootstraps \r\nwas hard indeed..<br><br>\r\nyes auntie, i too have a \r\nunique perspective on what \r\nlife is like being homeless \r\nand being a wanderer for that \r\nmatter.  there\\\'s a difference \r\nbetween the chosen word of \r\n\\\"homeless\\\" and \\\"wanderer\\\".  \r\nnot everyone can be Jack \r\nKerouac.<br><br>\r\npeople that are homeless, \r\nbreak my heart on a daily \r\nbasis.  when i see them, i \r\ndon\\\'t see anyone that is truly \r\nfree.  i see a person \r\nstruggling with themselves and \r\nthey are confined in their own \r\nprisons.  their mind being \r\ntheir own jail cell.  even \r\nwanderers have this problem.  \r\ni didn\\\'t want responsibilty \r\nand i had to lay low under the \r\nlaw so as not to be caught \r\ngalavanting across the united \r\nstates as a minor with my \r\nboyfriend who was of \r\nage.<br><br>i find that most \r\n\\\"wanderers\\\" romanticize this \r\nnotion of freedom and \r\neventually end up lying to \r\npeople about why they are \r\nreally out there to begin \r\nwith.  very few people you \r\nmeet will actually tell you \r\nthat they did this on their \r\nown accord.  it is far too \r\nfashionable to say that \r\n\\\"society made me do this\\\" or \r\n\\\"i had no choice\\\".<br><br>\r\nsee, you poke your finger at \r\nme as if i \\\"fashionably\\\" \r\nsympathize with people that \r\nare without a home.  actually, \r\nit is quite the opposite.  i \r\nunfashionably try to teach \r\nthem how to fish rather than \r\ngive them a fish.  i\\\'m \r\nunfashionably calloused to \r\nhomelessness.<br><br>if \r\nsomeone wants to be out there, \r\nthey need to be reminded that \r\nit was their *choice*, and \r\nthey are not a victim of \r\ncircumstance.  there\\\'s no \r\nreason for anyone to live that \r\nlife unless they want to.  if \r\nyou want to.. i\\\'m behind you \r\n100%.  i don\\\'t see you as the \r\nkind of person who would lie \r\nto people and tell them that \r\nyou have no money, food to \r\neat, or a place to call home. \r\n as long as you have friends \r\n.. which you have many, you \r\nwill never be \r\nhomeless.<br><br>\r\nhow long have you gone without \r\na meal or a shower \r\nsteve?<br><br> next time you \r\nsee a person like the man you \r\nsaw the other day, you should \r\ngo up to him and ask him how \r\nhe got there.  ask him why.  \r\ntry to have a better \r\nunderstanding of something \r\nbefore you glorify it.  if \r\nhe\\\'s a jack, then so be it.  \r\ni\\\'ll stand here wrong in my \r\nmismatched socks.<br><br>\r\nyou have financial freedom, \r\nand i think you should use \r\nthat to your advantage to \r\ntruly hit the road.. but to \r\nnever be homeless.  that was \r\nmy only point.  a journy like \r\nthat *is* romantic.  living \r\nlife without a plan, isn\\\'t.\r\n',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1437,618,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'cyantist','i love scottsdale.  i wish i \r\npicked up on the fact that you \r\nwere going there, and i could \r\nhave given you some advice on \r\nfun!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1438,619,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'chaya','flying home from paris, as \r\nsoon as we flew over \r\ncalifornia i could not stop \r\nsinging \\\'california uber \r\nalles\\\' and i am afraid it is \r\nstuck in my head for good.  \r\ni\\\'m glad you\\\'re home.  a lot.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1439,620,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','thank you for sharing this. \r\nit is a vivid story.  my\r\nparents were orphans.  they\r\nhave never told me anything\r\nregarding that time period.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1440,618,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','really! damn, i would have \r\nloved that... i did pick up \r\nsome fresh lemons from my \r\ndad\\\'s back yard, that was \r\ncool too. i just couldnt get \r\npast all of the $$$.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1441,615,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','poetic musings shouldn\\\'t be\r\ntaken literally, and the\r\nwriter attacked. this seems\r\nwrong to me.\r\n',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1442,615,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'cyantist','no offense weeb, but that is \r\nlike telling me that i \r\nshouldn\\\'t think.  if we \r\nshouldn\\\'t take poetry \r\nseriously, then what is the \r\npoint of taking anything \r\nseriously?  this is *life*. \r\nsometimes people don\\\'t get \r\nalong.  sometimes, it is \r\nimportant to challenge one \r\nanother.  not everything in \r\nlife is as simple as \\\"kiss and \r\nmake up\\\".  not everything is \r\nwarm and fuzzy.  his poem \r\nisn\\\'t being taken \\\"literally\\\", \r\nit is being interpreted \r\nsubjectively.. which i am more \r\nthan allowed to do.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1443,620,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'cyantist','thank you very much auntie.  \r\ni\\\'m happy that you shared your \r\nexperiences as a child.  most \r\npeople are too uncomfortable \r\nto be honest about what it is \r\nto be human.  i\\\'m really happy \r\nthat you made it .. alive and \r\nwell and happy with beautiful \r\nchildren and a wonderful \r\nhusband.  you are truly a \r\ngift!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1444,612,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'cyantist','i think that april fools \r\nshould be a paid holiday.  \r\npeople should get the day off \r\nto play pranks all day long.  ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1445,605,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'cyantist','ahh!  i see the motivation.  \r\ndo women have martha fetishes?',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1446,618,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'cyantist','did you get a chance to go to \r\ntempe?',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1447,615,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<P>It never ceases to amaze \r\nme what y\\\'all San Franciscans \r\nconsider \\\"attacking\\\".. I \r\nwonder sometimes what would \r\nhappen if someone \r\n<u>actually</u> attacked \r\nyou.</p>\r\n<p>If someone disagrees with \r\nthe viewpoint of a piece of \r\nart (as they understand it) \r\nwhat should they do? I\\\'m \r\nboggled as to how having your \r\nart questioned is so \r\npersonally insulting..</P>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n\r\n',5,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1448,615,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','cyan is spot-on. poetry is \r\nabout unraveling metaphor. \r\nand with any art, there is \r\nboth intent and perception. \r\nthe creator and the viewer\r\nare each allowed to take \r\nwhatever they want from a \r\nsymbol. often when i\\\'m at \r\nthe <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.sfmoma.or\r\ng\\\"/>moma</a>, i want to rip\r\ndown those little signs they \r\nput up next to the more \r\nabstract pieces.<br>\r\n<br>\r\ni wrestled with using \r\n\\\"homeless\\\" instead of \r\n\\\"wanderer\\\" because i knew\r\nit was such a loaded word. i \r\nfeel that i am already on a \r\njourney, simply by being \r\nmindful of the choices i \r\nmake. and thinking about \r\nwhat it would be like to \r\nchoose homelessness is \r\nuseful for me: by examining\r\nthe two extremes (wealth vs \r\nnothing), it allows me to \r\nunderstand why i live how i \r\ndo.<br>\r\n<br>\r\noriginally cyan challenged \r\nme in chat. and after i \r\nexplained the context, she \r\ncould understand where i \r\nwas coming from. i really\r\nappreciated the challenge; \r\nit helped me question my \r\nown intent and look deeper \r\ninto my motives for posting \r\nthose words.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nbut just for fun, we decided \r\nto play out the drama, to \r\nsee how it would go. \r\nperhaps it was april fool\\\'s \r\ntomfoolery? maybe it was\r\nperformance art? or the \r\nramblings of a couple \r\nbored geeks who just \r\nwanted to get punchy? who \r\nknows. but beyond the \r\nstaged ad hominem, i really \r\nenjoyed reading cyan and \r\nauntie\\\'s stories that\r\ncame out of this.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nlife for me is all about \r\nfinding pleasure in the \r\nchallenges, and this\r\none has kept me \r\nentertained all \r\nmorning.<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<font \r\ncolor=\\\"#0000FF\\\"><b>best \r\nfriendly!</b></font>\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1449,615,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kaz','\\\"Still and all,\\\" said Colton \r\nTrainu, as he folded his hat \r\nand wrapped it with five \r\npounds of string, \\\"it sure \r\nbeats bathroom duty at \r\nCrandell\\\'s Bitchhouse.\\\" ',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1450,615,'2003-05-10 16:09:14',79,'yeti','<img \r\nsrc=\\\"http://www.gee.kz/peter/y\r\nc.jpg\\\">\r\n',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1451,615,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','my only point was that i \r\nshouldn\\\'t be told how to \r\ninterpret a piece, no matter \r\nhow \\\"right\\\" people think they \r\nare.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1452,615,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p>dave eggers on art \r\ncritics:</p>\r\n<br><br>\r\n<i>\r\n\\\"I think criticism, more \r\noften than not, completely \r\nmisses the point.\\\"\r\n</i>\r\n</p><p>\r\n(from a really great <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.harvardadvoca\r\nte.com/summer00/eggers_article\r\n.phtml\\\">interview with \r\neggers</a> in the harvard \r\nadvocate. \r\n</p><p>\r\n',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1454,605,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','to some extent. but usually \r\nthey want to \\\"be\\\" martha, \r\nwhich is more adoration \r\nthan a fetish. i don\\\'t think \r\nyou\\\'ll find too many women \r\nmasturbating to martha \r\nstewart celebrity look-alike \r\nporn.<br>\r\ni think that martha and \r\nbarbie are the two ends of \r\nthe spectrum.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nfwiw i\\\'m typing this wearing \r\nlatex gloves, on my way to \r\nclean the cat litter area. \r\nthere\\\'s a bit of martha in all \r\nof us!<br>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1455,621,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','hi. you should publish this.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1457,622,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jorge','what that little shit needs is \r\nto die. well, not die in the \r\nwestern way of speaking, but \r\ndie in that vaguely existential \r\n\\\"walk around miserable\\\" way, \r\nand i dont know if thats \r\nexistential cos im not \r\nexistential or 65 or drink at \r\nthe starbucks on 50th and \r\n9th... well, i do, but i dont \r\nwatch the x-files anymore. \r\nyeah, he\\\'s a dick. *snaps*\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1458,619,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','le you fuck me up in such a \r\ngood way. keep on truckin.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1459,621,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'secret girl','you are a tree. you are so \r\nstrong.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1460,613,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','look, it\\\'s a sawks!',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1461,614,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','dude, you smell like a yeti',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1462,605,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','he came in my room, snapping \r\nthe gloves onto his hands. he \r\nnodded at me and said \\\"now, \r\nthis won\\\'t hurt a bit.\\\"',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1463,615,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','i\\\'m amused when boyfriends (or \r\ngirlfriends) come out of \r\nnowhere with a witty retort in \r\ndefense of their s.o.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1464,608,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','Try web comics.  Some of them\r\nhave art and plots to rival\r\nany on paper.  Some are just\r\nfunny.\r\n\r\nHere\\\'s a partial list:\r\n<ul><li>www.sluggy.com</li>\r\n<li>www.clanofthecats.com</li>\r\n<li>www.schlockmercenary.com</li>\r\n<li>www.sinfest.net</li>\r\n<li>www.megatokyo.com</li>\r\n<li>www.exploitationnow.com</li></ul>\r\n\r\nman, wish there was a way to\r\npreview comments. :)  always\r\nparanoid I bothced a tag\r\nsomewhere...  (I\\\'m too lazy\r\nfor hyperlinks so you get to\r\ncut and paste.)',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1465,621,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','i did -- right here. :)',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1466,608,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','Oh, and of course\r\nwww.pvponline.com for the\r\ngamers in the audience.  ;-)\r\n\r\n(partial list I follow I\r\nmeant, there are bajillions\r\nmore out there of course)',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1467,615,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P> it is a tight knit of art\r\nand criticism here.  i do\r\nthink there is a separation\r\nbetween the artist and the\r\ncritic.</p>\r\n<P>  i do not think that the\r\nartist is obligated to act in\r\ngood critical discourse form.  \r\n</P><P>\r\nthe artist\\\'s role is to be his\r\nor her self.  if that means\r\ntaking critics comments\r\npersonal, well, the artist is\r\nallowed to be closed to\r\ninterpretation or criticism in\r\nhis own mind. \r\n</P><P>\r\n i just hope he continues to\r\ncreate his art.</P>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1468,626,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>to sum it up:</P>\r\n<PRE>\r\nRENT IN THREE CITIES FOR TWO BEDROOM MULTI FAMILY\r\nALL SAME (hardwoods, no washing machine, etc.)\r\nALL LOCATED IN OR NEAR DOWN TOWN (not suburban)\r\n\r\nAUSTIN . . . . . . 680 \r\nLOS ANGELES  . . . 780 \r\nSAN FRANCISCO  . .2000\r\n</PRE>\r\n<P>there you have it.  what of melbs?  i think it is like\r\naustin.  i haven\\\'t been there though.</P>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1469,626,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>oh, and hi dude. <TT>=-)</TT></P>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1470,625,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>i had a squeezy.  i do not know that i do anymore.  it is\r\nkind of sad.  i miss her.  me and her only work if we can\r\nsqueeze each other.</P>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1471,245,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','afs;lkdja;sldjk  <A href=\\\\\\\"http://fc.com\\\\\\\">fc.com</a>',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1472,625,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'chaya','i miss my squeezy too.  when i miss my squeezy a lot, i \r\nmake a big mess in my house that turns into art or clothing \r\nor cookies.  and then i eat the cookies and it is not so \r\nbad.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1473,617,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'eoj','moving <strong>is</strong> hard, whether it be down the \r\nstreet or across the country.  having familiar routines is \r\nso very much part of \\\'home\\\'.  when that all breaks down, \r\nand you have to readjust it to a new place, it is confusing \r\nand it doesn\\\'t make sense and you can feel lost and \r\nirrational (even if you aren\\\'t a female at the wrong time \r\nof your cycle).  you can get stuck on the strangest things \r\nwhen settling in to a new place, and have insane \r\nfrustrations over the smallest little this-or-that.   but \r\nall of this is really that important-- after all, you have \r\nto live in your house some portion of nearly every day, so \r\noptimizing for comfort and sanity is a really good idea.  \r\nsometimes all the little things seem so big that comfort \r\nand sanity escape you for a bit.  that\\\'s okay.  it\\\'s part \r\nof moving and changing and growing.  but you must know \r\nthis, so i shall say no more.\r\n',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1589,633,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','yes, it is very bright, isn\\\'t it?  i am loving it very \r\nmuch. my <a href=\\\"http://www.saturn5.com/auntie\\\">saturn5 \r\nsite</a> is purple, which also pleases me.<br><br>\r\n\r\ni am going to make more bright things because i like it.  \r\none time elly made a site that was brilliantly green and \r\norange and she had a picture of her that sto drew and it \r\nwas my most favorite of all her sites.<br><br>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1475,618,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','yah, I have been to tempe, and I liked tempe better than \r\nscottsdale... ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1476,623,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','are you angry?',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1477,626,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','<p>okay this is making me crazy. HI! i\\\\\\\'m an austinite. and \r\na nice girl. i don\\\\\\\'t know a single other austinite on this \r\nboard -- i take that back. i know jesse. hi, jesse! -- and \r\ni think it\\\\\\\'s about damn time that i did. thank you.</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1478,609,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Paul','Hey Austin - while you\\\\\\\'re between jobs as it were and \r\nyou\\\\\\\'re still relatively unencumbered - by kids, mortgages \r\nand the like, check out Twin Oaks - I\\\\\\\'m sure you\\\\\\\'ve heard \r\nme mention it before - That\\\\\\\'s one of the places I\\\\\\\'ve \r\nalways \r\nwished I\\\\\\\'d hooked up with before I got married.  I think \r\nyou\\\\\\\'d really enjoy it - for a while anyway - maybe a long \r\nwhile.  Commune/Co-op that started up in 1976 I think - \r\nWhole bunch of land in Va. about 80 folks.  My dad and I \r\nwent to visit in 1982 - I thought it was very intriguing \r\nand quite attractive with a good balance of creative, \r\nartistic, wholistic, and pragmatic values that have enabled \r\nthe community to remain solid even after 25 years.\r\n\r\n<P>But I\\\\\\\'ve never visited with anyone who\\\\\\\'s been there \r\n(except that 1 afternoon with my Dad)- so you never know, \r\nbut anyway - here\\\\\\\'s the link if yer innerested.</P><P>\r\nhttp://www.twinoaks.org/ </P>',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1479,617,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','aw eoj, i actually kinda forgot to be reasonable, so this\r\nwas exactly what i subconsciously needed to hear. thanks for\r\nsaying it so well, it made me feel a lot better.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1480,615,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','that eggers interview fucking rocked and i am still thinking\r\nabout it. i liked his book too. the end.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1481,626,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','<p>i too am an austinite... i also know linearB, i know of \r\njo. And i am sleeping with jessejoker. ok not really , but \r\ni wish i was.</p><p>move to the mountains or sf,  \r\nalthough if you were to move to melbourne you would \r\nbe the first person i know to have moved there from \r\naustin... then i could live through your experiences, and \r\nmaybe i would end up there one day too...</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1482,625,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','yuck',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(16782,2769,'2002-05-22 17:41:56',81,'felicity','Thanks, everyone.  It\\\'s nice to know that laundry lovin\\\' is a universal experience.  Suddenly I feel all warm and cuddly. (sort of like a well worn sweatshirt fresh out of the dryer)',1,188,0,0,'216.42.123.44','en'),(16783,2766,'2002-05-22 18:19:42',123,'dcc','I\\\'m not too sure about obesity being the next big strain on the healthcare systems in the world. Geriatric care will be going through the roof over the next couple of decades as more and more babyboomers retire, get old, and have to be taken care of.',3,253,124,0,'66.207.199.132','en'),(1483,626,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'dj1_luna','i live in autin, but i don\\\\\\\'t think i\\\\\\\'m an austinite, \r\ni\\\\\\\'ve \r\nstill got the stench of fort worth with fumes of dallas \r\nuptightness',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1484,626,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p>melbs: huge house on beach with fireplaces and two \r\nstories: $1000/mo.\r\n</p><p>\r\ni too wish i was sleeping with jesse.\r\n</p>\r\n',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1485,626,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','swinney.org austinites need to throw a party together.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1487,626,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'psywillow','i am an austinite. i know bmg, dj1_luna and jesse. I AM \r\nsleeping with jesse.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1488,626,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'psywillow','sleeping with dj1_luna too',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1489,626,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','<p>i <i>was</i> an austinite,  but my home called.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1490,624,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','i want to see the pictures ',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1491,626,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','swinney.org party! Sounds great to me, but can we get the \r\nman himself to come? ARE YOU COMING OUT HERE AUSTIN G. \r\nSWINNEY????',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1492,626,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','<p>seriously. we should start an email list of cool austin \r\npeople.</p>\r\n<p>i will look into this.</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1493,627,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>that makes me very angry.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i heard those countries are like that.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>maybe you didn\\\'t give him enough money?</P>',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1494,627,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','<p>jeff, i am sorry man.</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1495,628,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','hella yA! I dislike those fuckers at compusa too. \r\nSometimes, i ask them questions just to hear them say \r\nabsurd things like there is no difference between ata/60 \r\nand ata/100, 5400rpm and 7200rpm. I then say, oh really! \r\nAnd i walk off laughing to myself, thinking i am the \r\nsmartest man in the world... and then i talk to someone and \r\nthey do the same to me. I walk away, humbled and \r\nembarassed... but no, really compusa sucks hairy ass. \r\nPrices suck, and then they want you to buy a return policy!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1496,628,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'timepilot84','You could save yourself a lot of trouble by moving into\r\nPortland, your travel times would be cut in half. :)',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1497,627,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','ugh. that sucks.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1498,626,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','austinpals@maz.org',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1499,615,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','yeah. that eggers interview has really colored my thoughts \r\nsince i read it, and effectively changed or strengthened \r\nsome of my opinions. he has a really great way of putting \r\nthings into words.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1500,628,'2003-05-10 16:09:14',79,'yeti','<p>Dude. Why you would be embarassed? The speed \r\ndifferences between ATA/66 and ATA/100 are \r\nnoticeable. That\\\'d be like saying that SCSI-1 is the \r\nsame speed as UW2-SCSI. Oh well. CompUSA is like \r\nFrys. Argh, those fuckers.</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1501,628,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','i hate comusa.  hate.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1502,628,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','fry\\\'s is much much worse than compusa. fry\\\'s is like a \r\nmedieval bazaar, except less mud.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1503,608,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','things i love:\r\n<p>\r\nking cat comics - john porcellino<br>\r\nanything by brian ralph (cave-in, most recently)<br>\r\nthe poems of david lasky, who is just an uncategorizable\r\ngenius<br>\r\nmost of highwater comics\\\' artists, like brian chippendale,\r\nwho i think did this minicomic that i will have buried with\r\nme when i go: \\\"crab claws\\\"<br>\r\nc.ware, of jimmy corrigan fame<br>\r\nchester brown, who did this amazing series based on the real\r\nlife of Louis Riel, a native canadian who led resistance\r\nagainst french colonizers in the 1800\\\'s i think.<br>\r\nit\\\'s usually not my thing, but this comic called \\\'castle\r\nwaiting\\\' is just so well done, i had to like it a lot.<br>\r\n</p><p>\r\nhmm, this isn\\\'t helping my productivity any...</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1504,626,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','or: [airportcode]@swinney.org',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1505,626,'2004-07-27 05:14:09',63,'olivia sez','rent in melbourne for our huge house: $480.00 per week, in\r\nau$.  life is cheap and really good here.  i love it.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1506,628,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>I can\\\'t wait for Fry\\\'s to build there location in\r\nAustin.  :-)  Mainly because I want to see if it\\\'s as bad as\r\nI\\\'ve heard it is.</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1507,629,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'iiieee','your vivid words are painful and beautiful. <p>Having a good \r\nlife with supportive, loving, wonderful parents (like you \r\nwere, I imagine. You remind me of my own mother.) and a \r\nmiddle class family income supporting you is great for a \r\ngrowing up child, yet unfortunately numbing--intelligent \r\npeople can always acknowledge the bad stuff, but it\\\'s \r\nimmensely hard to actually understand and feel and \r\n<i>see</i>. Thank you.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1508,630,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','wow, auntie. Thank you for being here to share these \r\nreal life stories. You are one of those people that I want \r\nto be like. --- as far as the lack of comments, well I can \r\nsay that I was overwhelmed by it, a loss for words... \r\nmaybe because i dont relate, or maybe because i relate \r\ntoo much with my own real life past. Anyway, i would \r\njust like to say thank you again for sharing... hugs and \r\nkisses...',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1509,630,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>i moved around as a kid.  i resent it some.   i\r\nunderstand why it happened.  it wasn\\\'t because we were\r\nforced to.  it was ambition driven job chasing.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i do not want to be an ambition driven job chaser.  i\r\nalready am though.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i always want a job that is better and more interesting. \r\ni always want to keep my friends.  that is why this site\r\nexists.  where ever i go i want to keep my friends in touch.\r\n</P>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1510,628,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','fry\\\'s is like adding compusa and bestbuy... but with stuff \r\nthat you can get at altex to. altex is cool, but they are \r\nway expensive... much better than radio hack... i hate all \r\nof them... computers should be free.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1511,429,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','you guys make me want to have hot wasabi jalapeno dry ice\r\nsuper dildo enemas. give it to me, UH UH\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1512,631,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','the best cure for depression is a combination of chocolate \r\nand doing something nice for someone else and cleaning \r\nsomething really good.<br><br>\r\n\r\ni think bathrooms and kitchens are the best to clean when \r\nreally depressed.  for slight depression, floors and \r\ndusting are good and washing clothing items.<br><br>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1513,632,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>you can\\\'t just post that like that.  step up to the mic\r\nplease.  i want to know what you think first.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>and most of all, i want to know why doggy style is\r\npercieved as being disrespectful?</P>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1514,632,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','don\\\'t you know that everyone is dying to know what old \r\npeople like?  i am not voting yet, i want to see pros and \r\ncons.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1515,632,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','mom.',5,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1516,632,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i\\\'m not going to take the bait.<br>\r\n<br>\r\n\\\"you\\\'ll just have to find out for yourself.\\\"<br>',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1517,632,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','steve. please don\\\'t fuck my mom.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1518,632,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<b>destabilizing</b>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1519,632,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','&lt;-- ?',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1520,633,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','blue background. ie5. macintosh. red-blooded \r\namerican male.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1521,632,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','doggy',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1522,632,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','yes please.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1523,632,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','missionary is a good gateway position.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ndoggy style is sometimes the obvious choice.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1524,632,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i like to see my lover\\\'s face.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1525,632,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p>whether or not doggie is considered disrespectful \r\nvaries widely, as preferences often do. but the \r\ndominant / submissive power relationship is made \r\nmore obvious in doggie than with missionary.\r\n</p><p>\r\nthe \\\"top\\\" and \\\"bottom\\\" roles are more clearly defined, \r\nand the fact that the two partners don\\\'t (can\