lating my liver \r\nand reduced to channel surfing infomercials.<br><br>\r\n\r\ndo you paint bright colored things?  red underpants is \r\nalways a good subject if you get stumped for one.\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1657,653,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'maria','how about swinney \\\"authors\\\" who wished they lived in \r\naustin? ',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1658,623,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'maria','jorge is the pillsbury doughboy with an attitude. he is \r\nalso the coolest boy the world has ever seen. trust me; i \r\nknow him rather well. ',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1659,649,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'timepilot84','Now, there\\\'s a difference between Professors and teachers. A\r\nlot of prof\\\'s I\\\'ve met could care less about the art of\r\nteaching, they\\\'re more interested in publishing and being\r\nadmired by their peers. \r\n\r\nIn my experience, public school teachers are definately\r\nbetter \\\"teachers\\\" than college teachers (except Community\r\nCollege teachers, who are in a lot of ways public school\r\nteachers). Teaching in the lower grades isn\\\'t going to make\r\nyou famous or rich and it\\\'s a difficult job that has very\r\nlittle reward other than the satisfaction of a job well\r\ndone. \r\n\r\nYou\\\'d really have to want to be a grade or high school\r\nteacher to put up with all the draconian BS that public\r\nschool teachers are put through these days for that little\r\npay. \r\n\r\nNot to say, of course, that there are <i>no</i> College\r\nProfessor\\\'s who are good teachers, it\\\'s just not a\r\npre-requisite for the job.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1660,645,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','can you do math in my ear while we rut against each \r\nother? (also, one american dollar scores you about two \r\naustralian dollars).',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1661,645,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','unless you are xep in the airport heading back to sf \r\nfrom .au, then you get like .25 on the dollar.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1662,649,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'insomniac','http://www.usatoday.com/life/health/general/sleep/lhgsl011.h\r\ntm',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1663,598,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'insomniac','html O.K.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1664,598,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'insomniac strikes again','<p><font face=\\\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\\\" size=\\\"2\\\" \r\ncolor=\\\"#660066\\\"><a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.usatoday.com/life/health/general/sleep/lhgs\r\nl011.htm\\\">sporadic fatal insomnia</a></font></p>',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1665,647,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kat','oh cool...i will be in san antonio around the 18th. i\\\'ll \r\npost when i get there!!!',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1666,650,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','emacs?  philistine.  ;^)',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1667,649,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i think i\\\'ve beaten insomnia. it\\\'s nice to feel rested.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1668,649,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'chaya','i think i caught your insomnia, steve.  i hate it.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1669,638,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','peter owns a pair of red underwear',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1670,652,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'iggeeboo','<font face=\\\"arial\\\">I\\\'m hoping for you =)  Take Care!</font>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1671,639,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','tuggy, long ago you explained the term reacharound to me.  \r\nnow i think i need to know what bukake is.  i am very \r\ninterested, but i sure hope it is not anything like this \r\none dreadful thing i found when i surfed the porn sites a \r\nwhile ago....',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1672,652,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'dj1_luna','i\\\'ve asked for author bios as well.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1673,652,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<a href=\\\"http://steve.org\\\">do your research.</a>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1674,650,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P> bluesky reminds me of wheatsville.  i always saw that\r\nstuff in the cooled beverage case.  i usually get the abita\r\nroot beer or reed\\\'s raspberry ginger beer.\r\n</P><P>\r\nme and adamajah used to go there and chill out front often. \r\nwe would eat pints of ben and jerry\\\'s, the entire pint, and\r\nrevel in the extreme fattness of it all.</P>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1675,650,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','i\\\'ve become an old man, austin.  it now takes me a few \r\nsittings to finish a ben&jerrys, instead of one.  it was \r\nhell-a-hot in TX though...',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1676,654,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kdawg','Please! be cautious and well instructed in Shoulderstand.  \r\nIt\\\'s a fantastic asana (my favorite) but bruises should not \r\nhappen.  Inform your teacher about what happened.  You \r\nshould be on your shoulders, not your vertebrae.  Make sure \r\nyou\\\'re getting the full benefit of the pose. Yoga, yoga, \r\nyoga -- yeah! ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1677,652,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Peaseblossom','http://www.astro.com',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1678,652,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','astro.com is the diary of things that haven\\\'t happened \r\nyet.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1679,654,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','yeah i told her. i have never had shoulderstand bruise me \r\nbefore, it was weird. maybe i was off the mat? ',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1680,655,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','yesterday i saw a man pushing a shopping cart down the\r\nmiddle of page street.  he stopped, dropped trou, and peed\r\nright there in the middle of the street.  i said \\\"you\\\'re a\r\nfunny man!\\\" but he did not hear me.  i have a quiet voice.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1681,654,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','hi. my soft squooshy center nuzzles your soft squooshy \r\ncenter. i like you an awful lot, kid.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1682,655,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','(chaya. you\\\'re neat.)',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1683,654,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','perhaps you should try eating one of those potato thingies \r\nyou gave me for the plane trip home.  this should help your \r\nappetite.<br><br>\r\n\r\nmaybe you need to come home and visit mom for a little \r\nshort while.  i will hug you a lot and we can sing songs \r\nand dad will make some vegan chili for you and we will put \r\nit over slices of polenta.<br><br>\r\n\r\nor paint a picture.  paint something that makes you laugh.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1684,650,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kat','i love my dog...she makes warm spots for my feet in the \r\nbed. and she nibbles on me when we wrastle. and she grunts \r\nat me if i talk to her while she\\\'s trying to sleep. i love \r\nsticking my nose in her fur and smelling her doggy smell.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1685,627,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','if you didn\\\'t get that space it means a better one is out \r\nthere, you need to go find it.  be sure to wear red \r\nunderpants while you search.  this is important.  i will \r\nexplain about the red underpants sometime in the future.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1686,656,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','mom.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1687,652,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','use some of your leftover bucks to buy some red underpants \r\nfor the interview.  i would have taken the maid in a \r\nheartbeat.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1688,656,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','are you momming me?  hah!  you think i am kidding.  ask \r\nelly, she will tell you that i have ALWAYS believed in red \r\nunderpants.  get some.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1689,656,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','my friend janine bought me an excellent pair of red \r\nunderpants as a going away present the first time i moved \r\nout of home.\r\n\r\ni believe that they did make me feel exta-special whenever \r\ni wore them. the orange stitching on them also helped.\r\n',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1690,656,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>I think that any sort of special underpants work well.  I\r\nhave a pair of silk boxers I wear to job interviews, that\r\nhave the most outrageous fish printed all over them.  Makes\r\nme giggle, which keeps me from getting all uptight.</p>\r\n<p>I also have a pair of black cotton boxers covered in red\r\nanarchy symbols.  These are still undergoing testing, but I\r\nthink their area of efficacy is test scores.  At least I did\r\nbetter on my last quantum exam when I was wearing them.</p>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1691,656,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>\r\nI have a pair of maroon drawers. Do those count?<P>\r\nI have never felt special while wearing them..<p>\r\n\r\n-darwin\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1692,656,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>Also, auntie, there are some forms of hepatitis which \r\nare extremely contagious. It is, unfortunately, one of the \r\nthings you can get from poor sanitation, or in prepared \r\nfood at a restaurant, or etc. Low-probability chance, but \r\ncertainly possible.<p>\r\nI know someone who has hepatitis.. she got it from a blood \r\ntransfusion in the early 80s before they screened for it. \r\nHer liver is extremely fucked up and she has no money to \r\npay for medical care. However, she has kept her head up and \r\nshe is an inspiration. Perhaps you\\\'d like to speak with her \r\nin email about liver disease and the challenges she\\\'s faced?\r\n<p>If so, let me know and I will get you in contact with \r\nher..<p>\r\n(thinking happy thoughts in auntie\\\'s direction)\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1693,655,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','the other day, austin and i saw this guy protesting into his\r\ncellphone: \\\"i\\\'m going to a _meeting_\\\" while cruising down\r\nthe street in office clothes on his skateboard. he was\r\nindeed, on his way to a meeting. so surreal.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1694,656,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<BR>\r\ni have many many pairs of red underwear, and as many pairs\r\nof other colors and prints.\r\n\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nand look at me :)',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1695,658,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','what\\\'s your address?? :)\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1696,656,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Danielle','when I wear red underpants, I always feel compelled to tell \r\npeople. \\\"Good morning, I\\\'m wearing red panties today!\\\" Maybe \r\nthat puts me in high spirits because it always get a \r\nchuckle. =)',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1697,657,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kat','beating myself up (in more ways than one). picking my scabs \r\n(in more ways than one). running myself ragged (in more \r\nways than one). tripping over my own feet (in more ways \r\nthan one). losing myself in other people (one way seems to \r\nbe enough).',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1698,657,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','kat is also good at metaphors. :)',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1699,654,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','nothing is better than staying home alone. staying home from\r\nschool. rainy day. making icky sandwiches for yourself.\r\neating all the junk food you want. dropping crumbs all over\r\nthe couch. yeah.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1700,659,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','that first sentence made me laugh.  now i will read the\r\nrest.<BR><BR>\r\nshe should probably get a second opinion on the lithium.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1701,659,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>i feel the same way about using drugs to eliminate\r\nunproductive emotions.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>the emotional cubicle.  if you are going to work here, we\r\ndemand a high level of productivity.</P>\r\n\r\n<PRE>hands the health insurance packet</PRE>\r\n\r\n<P>see if you can get that day dreaming and floundering\r\nproblem of yours taken care of.  it is great that you think\r\nabout these things so intently, but the time has come to DO\r\nthem.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>just think of it as putting your blinders on:</P>\r\n\r\n<PRE>motions hands to the temples blocking peripheral\r\nvision</PRE>\r\n\r\n<P>you are like a horse now,  you are thinking strait ahead.\r\nkeep your wagon on the road.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>now go to the doctor.  i am sure he can get you what you\r\nneed in a pill form.  did i mention that we only allow pill\r\nform at this company?  yes you can drink, but other than\r\nthat, let us just stick to the pills.</P>',5,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1702,659,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','<p>i love you because you ARE a madwoman.</p>\r\n<p>i would also like to add that Zb\\\'s kittykat doctor wants \r\nto put Zb\\\'s kitty on kitty-paxil-prozac-\r\nriddlin...</p><p>Zb\\\'s kat is almost as crazy as Zb; and I \r\nlove them both (not equally).</p>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1703,659,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','<p>at the risk of getting all <u><a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1573225126/stan\r\ndingontheout\\\">prozac nation</a></u> here, or \\\"<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://us.imdb.com/Title?0116768\\\">brain candy</a>\\\" \r\nfor that matter, obviously there are some people for whom \r\nthese drugs are absolutely necessary and, thus, god-\r\nsends.</p>\r\n<p>i get sketchy when doctors recommend drugs rather than, \r\nsay, therapists. or life modification. no, don\\\'t change \r\nyour diet or try to stop overextending yourself, don\\\'t \r\nleave abusive relationships, don\\\'t try exercise or yoga, \r\njust take this pretty blue pill and see what happens.<BR>\r\ngrr!</p>\r\n<p>i, too, revel in my craziness. it makes me a better \r\nartist. and a more empathetic friend, for that matter!<BR>\r\nbut there was a time in my life where i\\\'m certain, in \r\nretrospect, that i was dangerously bi-polar. if i\\\'d started \r\nmedicating then (which would probably have been good for \r\nme), i might <b>still</b> be taking it now, six years \r\nlater, when i don\\\'t need it whatsoever. and would that same \r\ndoctor be around to advise me to stop?</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1704,657,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'cyantist','1. being naive <br>\r\n2. inspiration to others<br>\r\n3. strong when times are tough<br>\r\n4. gardening!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1705,656,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kat','i have some super satiny gold upderpants that just make me \r\nfeel like sliding off the world when i wear them. oh, and \r\nthat\\\'s a good thing.  :p',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1706,645,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Orisha','html O.K. standard algebraic retort whenver mathematics are \r\nmentioned..a kneejerk reaction which can be approximated by \r\na loud female  voice shouting LET X=X.  Listen for the \r\nechoes coming back from canyon walls and all I hear is sex, \r\nsex, sex...Cripes! How did ice cream get on my Freudian \r\nSlip? Cancel them damn rhumba lessons, god dog, and live \r\nevil!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1707,654,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Orisha','html O.K.I favor Contemlative Dwelling in My Bed..ites best \r\ndone on a rainy day when other workers are busy in  the \r\nhive so you can be somewhat smug.  Surround yourself with \r\np0illows and if not allergic, at least one cat.  I \r\npersonally prefer two.  Mine are healers and perform a \r\nkitty-accupressure just where I need it. Have a stack of \r\npleasure reading handy. Perhaps a little light oscillator \r\nfan action.Nag champa incense in the next room. Keep a \r\njournal handy to doodle in, brainstorm, make lists which \r\nturn into poems or the other way round.Wonder why you \r\nalways turn your bedrooms into Voodoo lounges and ambient \r\nliterary opium dens.  Fuck ambition, I come from Venus.  I \r\ndont want a career, just want to careen. Just be me. Have a \r\nlazy day life. Use all the colors in my box and go beynd \r\nthe lines, cause that\\\'s where the good stuff is. And she \r\nsaid that all in one breath! Now exhaling a cool stream of \r\nopium between parted lips. Staring at you, with indolence \r\nand defiance. You don\\\'t  like it> Turn the page',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1708,658,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Joanna','I haven\\\'t got a post office box, so I\\\'d rather not put my \r\naddress directly onto a web page (although I\\\'m waaaay too \r\neasy to stalk).  But if you email me, joanna@hubris.co.nz , \r\nI will tell you.  Because it\\\'s always best to have direct \r\ncontact with maybe-crazys.  ',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1709,343,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'orisha','html O.K. its really sort of a situation that can be best \r\nviewed through a magritte painting..imagine an ocean full \r\nof such dreamers, each one thinking that they are the only \r\nones there...and further imagine that this image all takes \r\nplace in the head of a greater dreamer, who is in turn a \r\ndream in the head if a still greater dreamer..ad infinitum.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1710,656,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','i rarely ever wear underpants, some may think this is \r\nfor voyer reasons... i do wear the underpants on special   \r\nthings such as going to the doctor, spending the night \r\nat relatives houses and friends houses... i wear them \r\non dates, just cause you never know. I wear them on \r\ninterviews... i also hate doing laundry, and austin can \r\ntell you that when I do I fold everything 6\\\"x6\\\", yes it is \r\ntrue. I had a conversation with austin about drawers a \r\nfew months ago, and he had told me about male \r\nthongs sold at macy\\\'s. I am trying to locate a pair \r\ncurrently, and my birthday is may 10. ;-)',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1711,654,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','i enjoy Self Copulation In My Bed',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1712,657,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','darwin, your crusade makes me smile',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1713,663,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p><a href=\\\"http://sinfest.net/d/20000420.html\\\">Bachelor\r\nCooking Show</a> strip from the always-funny <a\r\nhref=\\\"www.sinfest.net\\\">Sinfest</a>.</p>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1714,663,'2004-07-27 05:14:09',63,'olivia sez',' i am in love with both of you.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1715,659,'2003-05-10 16:09:14',79,'yeti','<p>My experiences with someone who has battled Bipolar \r\nDisorder are quite\r\ndifferent. I guess I would like to start off where I best \r\nknow how.</p>\r\n<p>I do not believe that severe bipolar disorder is healthy \r\nfor the person\r\nwho has it, and I do not believe that it is \\\'who they are.\\\' \r\nI do not think\r\nit is a construct of society. I do not think it is a label \r\nwhich is applied\r\nto people who are not the same as everyone else.</p>\r\n<p>I dated and lived with a woman who has severe bipolar \r\ndisorder. For\r\nMelissa, the \\\'crazy thoughts\\\' were not half the fun of \r\nliving. They were\r\ndebilitating, and served ultimately to do her far more harm \r\nthan any good\r\nshe got from them.</p>\r\n<p>Melissa took a lot of different medications. From \r\nlithium to\r\nantiepileptics. She took them so that she would be able to \r\nhold a job, so\r\nthat she could go to school. So that she could keep her \r\nfriends. She took\r\nthem so that she could support herself at all.</p>\r\n<p>Melissa used to leave the house late at night sometimes. \r\nI would find her\r\noutside crying. She told me that she didnt want to be \r\ncrazy. She told me she\r\njust wanted to live a normal life and not have her blood \r\ndrawn 3 times a\r\nweek, see a psychologist twice a week, take 18 pills a day, \r\nor have to find\r\nsome excuse to explain why she didnt get to work or \r\nclass.</p>\r\n<p>I think that for people who must take medications for \r\nBipolar disorder,\r\nthe choice is a really hard one. The medications cause a \r\nmultitude of their\r\nown problems. Things like blurred vision, vertigo, \r\nexcessive body hair\r\ngrowth, weight gain, depression, migrane headaches, muscle \r\ntwitches, lowered\r\nplatelet counts, heart palpitations, and on and on. You \r\nhave a trade off of\r\ntaking medication so that you can live normally, but you \r\ndont get to feel\r\nnormal either way. You get to feel fucked up. This was hard \r\nfor Melissa.</p>\r\n<p>Was it easy for me to date Melissa? No, not really. When \r\nshe would start\r\nto cycle, it would often mean me not sleeping for 3 days \r\nbecause I needed to\r\nbe there to help her, support her, or keep her from hurting \r\nherself. She\r\nused to throw things at me. Cut herself with razors, or \r\ndestroy all of the\r\npictures of the family she loved so much. I dont think I \r\nhave ever heard\r\nmore hateful, angry, mean, painful comments from anyone in \r\nmy life than from\r\nMelissa when she started to cycle.</p>\r\n<p>The hard part was, she didnt remember any of it when she \r\nstabilized\r\nagain. There wasnt a way I could address the \\\'problems\\\' \r\nthat I had or the hurt\r\nfeelings I harbored with her.</p>\r\n<p>When she wasnt cycling, she was a wonderful person to be \r\naround.</p>\r\n<p>The methods that I know of that are in common practice \r\nto treat bipolar\r\ndisorder are primitive at best. They cause pain, suffering, \r\nand loss of self\r\nesteem in many of the people who take them. I really hope \r\nthat some day,\r\nsomeone will understand enough about the disorder to treat \r\nit well. The\r\nalternative to current treatments for it is no treatment at \r\nall, and that is\r\nwholly unacceptable for some people.</p>\r\n<p>The alternative to taking medication to try to reach \r\nsome semblance of\r\nnormal for Melissa was never dating someone. Never keeping \r\nyour friends for\r\nlong. Never having a steady job. Never having the *choice* \r\nto decide if she\r\nwanted to live have a normal life. Strike the spouse, \r\nstrike the divorce,\r\nstrike the kids, strike the 9 to 5 job, strike the affair, \r\nstrike weddings,\r\nthe nursing home. Those werent options for her unmedicated. \r\nShe did not wake\r\nup every day (if she slept the night before) loving every \r\nminute of it. It\r\njust wasnt part of being crazy for her, I guess.</p>\r\n<p>As much as Melissa wanted to be happy and lead a good \r\nlife, that was not\r\npossible for her without medication of some sort. It did \r\nhelp her a lot to\r\ntake it, even with the harm it did.</p>\r\n<p>I often wonder what happened to Melissa. After we broke \r\nup, she moved\r\naround a lot. She wasnt able to hold jobs. She wasnt able \r\nto keep an\r\napartment. Our cats ran off because she wasnt able to take \r\ncare of them and\r\nherself, I guess. I hope that they found good homes. Those \r\ncats kept her\r\nsane sometimes.</p>\r\n<p>The last time I talked with her, she was taking \r\nmedication again,\r\ngoing for a degree in Zoology, and holding a steady job. \r\nAfter that, her\r\nphone was disconnected the next time I attempted to reach \r\nher. I hope and\r\npray that she has found a good life somewhere, and that she \r\nhas managed to\r\nfind a way to live with her disorder. I think I will always \r\nbe wondering,\r\nthough.</p>\r\n<p>I just wanted to share that with people to give the \r\nother side of drugs\r\nlike these, to disorders like these. There are people who \r\nthey really do\r\nhelp.</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1716,663,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','ok, maybe weeb said something about coconuts.\r\n\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nokay weeb?!  are you happy now?!\r\n\r\n<BR><BR>\r\n=-P',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1717,663,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','*looks innocent*<br>\r\nall i know is, perhaps the boys forgot to dilute the \r\ncoconut milk with water...',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1718,659,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','that was balls out, peter',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1719,659,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'zb playing devil\\\'s advocate','i am sorry. i am not the be all end all seer of anything. \r\nperhaps it is me, me not wanting it for myself. me sad and \r\nsitting here at 6am unable to sleep. me confused and lost \r\nand hoping that lithium isn\\\'t the only answer for souls \r\nlike mine. me feeling alone. my other friend commented the \r\nsame as well: \\\"i read it, i am just not sure i agree with \r\nyour assesment of the illness.....just because you can\\\'t \r\nsee it yourself, doesn\\\'t mean that she doesn\\\'t need help \r\nfor it, she went to a doctor because she felt she did, i \r\nguess i would respect her for that.  if the dr feels \r\nlithium is the best route, let her try it, she can always \r\ncome off it.  some of what you described about her is \r\nTYPICAL of the disease and it is harder for her to deal \r\nwith than anyone else, is all i am thinking.\\\" \r\nyeti, your courage and melissa\\\'s are inspring. thank you. i \r\nhope she is well also.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1720,657,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i am really bad at remembering things and quoting \r\nthem. however i am good at keeping secrets. i\\\'m also \r\nreally good at taking care of my cat, helping people \r\nfigure what to do with their lives, hosting web sites, and \r\neating. i think that\\\'s 5 things. i am terrible at origami.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1721,663,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'chia says','you all shouldstop yer nattering.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1722,666,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','steve. you never cease to puzzle me.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1723,663,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sean','google? no wonder. you should try your cooking searches <a\r\nhref=\\\"http://www.search.com/search?channel=19&cat=33\\\">here</a>,\r\ne.g. search for recipes including <a\r\nhref=\\\"http://www.search.com/search?channel=19&cat=33&q=coconut+milk\\\">coconut\r\nmilk</a>.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1724,666,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>you just made me laugh out loud.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1725,667,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>do tell, in which co-op do your loyalties lie?</P>\r\n\r\n<P>flow the porn.</P>\r\n',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1726,666,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'da','dude!\r\n\r\n*makes devil sign*\r\n\r\ni first listened to this song in a walkman on the way to a \r\nchurch retreat.  one of the bad kids let me borrow the tape.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1727,663,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'da','i have a really serious curry algorithm that i\\\'ve been \r\nthreatening to foist on people recently.  it might happen \r\nsoon.  beware.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1728,521,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'da','i\\\'ve heard the same sentiment expressed thusly: \\\"every girl \r\nin san francisco is two glasses of wine away from a lesbian \r\nexperience.\\\"  or maybe: \\\"lesbians equal ratings\\\" -howard \r\nstern in <i>private parts</i>.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1729,657,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'da','<s5> i am a write-only gossip device',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1730,657,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'da','<p>blah, this needs an edit.  that was supposed to \r\nread...</p>\r\n<p>\r\n&lt;s5&gt; i am a write only gossip device</p>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1731,656,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'da','i have no special underpants, and i\\\'m flailing.  i\\\'ve been \r\nconsidering making a sock purchase, but i was thinking \r\nthat\\\'d be my reward for getting a job, not for having to \r\ncontinue to look for one.<br><br>\r\ni hate being poor.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1732,654,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'da','elly, you mentioned this last night and i forgot to mention \r\nthat the same thing happened to me once.  it took me a \r\nwhile to figure out what was going on; i kept thinking \\\"how \r\nthe hell did i bruise the center of the top of my \r\nback?\\\"<br><br>\r\nanyway, yeah, whoever said this already was right: it\\\'s \r\nfrom not sitting on your shoulders when you do it.  i\\\'ve \r\nnoticed now that it feels real different when you\\\'re doing \r\nit right than when you aren\\\'t...you can kind of feel your \r\ntop vertebrae lift safely on the ground when your shoulders \r\ntake the load.\r\n<br><br>\r\nalso, i\\\'m thinking this week i\\\'ll finally make it to yoga, \r\nand it\\\'s not just because i had a stray partially ambiguous \r\nsexual fantasy about kristie last night.  hm!\r\n',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1733,538,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'da','in my first post, i checked \\\"Girlfriend\\\", then hesitated, \r\nthen unchecked it.  my post was lame though, and should by \r\nall means get its ass moderated.<br><br>\r\nwhich, according to austin on chat just now, it was.\r\n',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1734,667,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'maria','my loyalties lie in the co-op i am a member of. we are \r\nsmall, fun, the house is cozy, and our cooks are fucking \r\namazing. \r\n\r\n',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1735,668,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','you\\\'re the pilot. radio the tower.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1736,596,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'da','room altars are good.  i never quite got the altar in this \r\nplace to click...i\\\'m going to put a little more effort into \r\nmaking it go the next time i move.<br><br>(i never quite \r\ngot anything in this place to click)',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1737,666,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'chaya','neat, now i\\\'ll be singing this all day instead of PUMP UP \r\nTHE JAM.  thanks!',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1738,670,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','um. this is pretty much the only way i make popcorn. i \r\ndidn\\\'t know it was a lost art.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1739,666,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','let him who hath understanding reckon the number of the\r\nbeast, for it is a human number...',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1740,670,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'da','well i\\\'m slower than most of the other kids.  ask anyone.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1741,668,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','for god\\\'s sake man, get a hold of yourself. suck it up and\r\nstrap on a sack.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1742,670,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','there\\\'s this thing called microwave popcorn. it\\\'s very\r\npopular with the kids.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1743,668,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kat','he wanted to KNOW who was this person and where did she \r\ncome from??? he said you are a goddess...you leave me on \r\nfire...you are my muse...leaving me unbuttoned from the \r\ninside. the temptation was irresistable. the emotions \r\noverwhelming. i was swirled, and tumbled, and left blazing. \r\ntouched. i said i love you. and he said...sorry i dont care \r\nfor you like that.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1744,670,'2003-07-24 15:44:23',165,'joker','one of my fondest memories of the divorce years with my \r\nsiblings and mother was old fashioned popcorn.  microwave \r\nis ok, but nothing compares to real butter!!',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1745,670,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'you know who this is:','Even better: Yaya\\\'s Popcorn. Comes in the weeb approved \r\nflavors of plain, and herb. The closest to God I\\\'ll ever \r\nget.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1746,670,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','yaya is greek for grandmother. except the stress is on \r\nthe second syllable.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1747,497,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'da','melbourne sounds pretty fabulous.  sydney, too.<br><br>\r\nsf is awful nice and i\\\'ve had plenty of time to contemplate \r\nthat after moving to berkeley.  i\\\'m hoping i\\\'ll figure out \r\nsome way to move back soon.<br><br>\r\nbut i did have one experience with a city that made me \r\nthink sf might not be the sine qua non of urban \r\nexperiences.  a year and a half ago i went to a conference \r\nin montreal and i was completely blown away: tons of \r\naffordable, appropriately dense and diverse housing, great \r\nstreet life and energy, awesome public transportation, \r\nbonus french accents, tons of totally sweet, lush little \r\ncafes.\r\n<br><br>and: i met a complete stranger in a pub the second \r\nnight i was there, and the night before i left we stayed up \r\nall night hanging out in heavenly nookie land.  she pushed \r\nme out the door at 7am, i cabbed back to my hotel to grab \r\nmy stuff, and my next memory is standing outside the \r\nterminal smoking a du marier thinking \\\"merde!  that rocked.\\\"\r\n<br><br>so since that evening pretty much reformatted my \r\nbrain, who knows what montreal is actually like.  i\\\'m sure \r\nthe weather stinks in the winter.  but i did get the idea \r\nit was pretty cool city.  of course, sf\\\'s feeling of \r\nimprovability is certainly part of its charm.\r\n',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1748,608,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'da','i have yet to really dig into comic books.  but: i dig the \r\nbondage fairies a lot.  cute pixie chicks getting the bone \r\nfrom various animals when they aren\\\'t busy doing each \r\nother. *shrug*',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1749,636,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'da','i took a girl home to thanksgiving last year for the first \r\ntime in what seemed like forever.  she got along fabulously \r\nwith everyone and the whole thing just made me incredibly \r\nhappy.<br><br>\r\nthey even had lunch with her two weeks ago while they were \r\nin new york.  this didn\\\'t make me as happy because it \r\nreminded me how much i miss the lot of \\\'em and how damn far \r\naway they all are.<br><br>\r\nideally, i would like to be a train ride away from my \r\nparents.  not sure when or if that\\\'s ever going to work \r\nout.  and of course i\\\'d desperately like to be local to a \r\nworking romantic relationship, somehow.\r\n<br><br>\r\nbtw auntie\\\'s original post here almost made me cry.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1750,636,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'da','oh also, speaking of jealousy: <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.compersion.org/\\\">www.compersion.org</a>.  \r\ni\\\'ve started to very gradually and (i hope) nonthreatingly \r\ntell my family about this in the hopes that it\\\'s going to \r\nhead off confusion down the road.<br><br>\r\nthey seem to be adjusting alright to the idea that i\\\'m \r\nreally serious about equanimity in my romantic \r\nrelationships; i think there was a while where they were \r\nsure that even my feeble, highly localized and halting \r\nattempts at discerning and rejecting the patriarchal model \r\nwere going to cost me somehow.  since traditional roles \r\nbasically worked out alright for them, it\\\'s difficult for \r\nthem to see why i\\\'m challenging them (and admitedly, it \r\ntook me a while to accept that those roles really do work \r\nfor them).',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1751,517,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'da','the difficulty of this question is exactly proportional to \r\nmy overall general level of self esteem.  right now it \r\nseems damn near impossible.  i try anyway, this is a nice \r\nexercise:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>1. i\\\'m good at kissing and making out and stuff too.\r\n<li>2. i\\\'m good at cooking up harebrained web interface \r\nschemes.\r\n<li>3. i\\\'m ok at at least attempting to build such things.\r\n<li>4. i\\\'m a good listener.  mostly anyway.\r\n<li>5. i\\\'m good at making weird connections, like when i \r\nonce explained to someone how s&m and christianity both \r\noffer completely compatible frameworks for understanding \r\nthe nature of power in relationships.\r\n</ul>\r\neh these are lame, but i tried.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1752,140,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'da','oo, and so is <a href=\\\"http://www.girlwonder.com\\\">molly \r\nwright steenson</a>. *drool*',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1753,664,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'(','</p><p>\r\nthis is good to read and see. i want to hug you. also i \r\nwant you to not worry in your almostasleep times. those are \r\nthe best times, cuddled up with the blankets, rubbing one \r\nfoot against the other, going through the bodily motions of \r\ngetting down to sleep. meditative moments like that are not \r\nfor worries, worries are for when you can do something \r\nabout them, sometime during business hours.\r\n</p><p>\r\ni get so worried at night sometimes, so full of things to \r\ndo and take care of that i can\\\'t sleep until i wake up and \r\nwrite a list.</p>',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1754,564,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'da the ambivalent','i try to be nice to recruiters, even when they\\\'re obviously \r\nworking hard just to rub a half-dozen or so neurons \r\ntogether.  note that these efforts seem to have brought in \r\nroughly diddlysquat karmawise in my current job/funding \r\nsearch.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1755,668,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sawks','<br>\r\nya\\\'ll needs a new hobby, like breakdancing, or \r\nmicrobiology\r\n<br><br>\r\nkeep ya head up',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1756,670,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','this reminds me of a story my brother-in-law told me. he \r\nworks in a juvenile detention center and was complaining to \r\nsome of his charges that he had a lot of 45s, but the belt \r\ndrive on his record player was broken. after he explained to \r\nthem what a 45 was, they asked him why he didn\\\'t just put \r\nthem in this CD player.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1757,670,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','i am glad to see da here writing things again.  da is one \r\nof my boys who fell into a hole a while back and he may not \r\nknow that i have been praying for him very much that he \r\nwill find himself on the path to a future that will make \r\nhim happy.<br><br>\r\n\r\nhomemade popcorn is a nice beginning.  another nice thing \r\nis cinnamon toast.  and chocolate milk.  the vegans can use \r\nmargarin and soy milk, but there\\\'s nothing like real butter \r\nfor cinnamon toast and if i were not a diabetic these days \r\nand trying to lose some weight to help my liver, i would go \r\nmake myself about six slices of cinnamon toast and a half \r\ngallon of chocolate mile right now.<br><br>\r\n\r\ni am very fond of the 3 flavor popcorn you buy in huge tins \r\nand i eat a bunch of it, except mark eats the caramel corn \r\npart on account of the diabetes business.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1758,671,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>i want a job that *requires* i have a four wheel \r\noptional vehicle.  dang.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>NoFX</P>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1759,672,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','found the answer here:\r\n\r\nwww.chariot.net.au/~gmarts/easter.htm\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1760,655,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','some friends of mine just told me a story about recording \r\nfreeway sounds under the freeway by 2nd and bryant and a \r\npantsless woman wandered out of a little shed thing inside \r\nthe parking lot and proceeded to stare right at them and piss \r\non the side of the shed and then wander back in.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1761,674,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','hey simon, you know about <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.cyantology.com\\\">cyan</a> don\\\'t you?',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1762,674,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','no! haha! i just sorta thought of it randomly.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1763,261,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','you are a funnyfunny man, aus10.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1764,675,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','*swoon*',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1765,675,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>even though i can only see a small portion of this el \r\ncamino, i know what the rest of it looks like.  even the \r\ncolor scheme.</P>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1766,675,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'chaya','it is a really great el camino.  let me tell you.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1767,676,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','i love you each and every one. :)<br><br>\r\n\r\nmom',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1768,676,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','<p>*envy*; but i had a great weekend. Went to houston and \r\nlistended to dutz-dutz. </p><p>i am leaving for west texas \r\nin the morning, my grandmother is in intensive care due to \r\nanother heart attack. send some good vibes my family\\\'s way, \r\nplease, we are needing it.</p>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1769,676,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sigh','  that\\\'s all.  something about melbourne.  defeated.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1770,676,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','</p>\r\n<p>austin: dude, i\\\'m pretty sure we could make vegan haggis \r\nwith what i pulled out of the garbage disposal</p>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1771,676,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Joanna','you guys have such a sexy kitchen ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1772,671,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','we\\\'re all thinking happy safe dad millican thoughts, auntie.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1773,667,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','TRIBAL DRUM JAM!\r\n\r\n-H.O.C.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1774,668,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','(o) nice supportive',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1775,676,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>late last night, i got this /message from s5:</P>\r\n\r\n<PRE>\r\n<*s5*> i think i just saw a ufo\r\n</PRE>\r\n\r\n<P>was it real?  or was just the brown noodle proton\r\nwater?</P>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1776,675,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','chaya, remember driving around listening to sweet emotion at \r\ntop volume windows down, arms out, banging on the doors to \r\nthe beat?\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1777,676,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','damn.  all you unemployeds are having so much fun up there.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1778,664,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','everyone has those moments when they secretly wish they had \r\nthe nerve to make the ultimate runaway from \r\nproblems...<br><br>\r\n\r\nit usually happens at three in the morning.  my best advice \r\nis to go to bed and wait for tomorrow.<br><br>\r\n\r\neach of us has a part to play.  which is why i think i need \r\nto write about steveline sostilio, and i will now.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1779,678,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','note: pronounced \\\"stevalean\\\"',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1780,677,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p>\r\n<table width=\\\"200\\\" height=\\\"200\\\" bgcolor=\\\"669933\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" \r\ncellpadding=\\\"0\\\" cellspacing=\\\"1\\\">\r\n<tr>\r\n<td width=\\\"10\\\" height=\\\"10\\\" bgcolor=\\\"#ccff99\\\"></td>\r\n<td width=\\\"10\\\" height=\\\"10\\\" bgcolor=\\\"#ccff99\\\"></td>\r\n<td width=\\\"10\\\" height=\\\"10\\\" bgcolor=\\\"#ccff99\\\"></td>\r\n<td width=\\\"10\\\" height=\\\"10\\\" bgcolor=\\\"#ccff99\\\"></td>\r\n<td width=\\\"10\\\" height=\\\"10\\\" bgcolor=\\\"#ccff99\\\"></td>\r\n<td width=\\\"10\\\" height=\\\"10\\\" bgcolor=\\\"#ccff99\\\"></td>\r\n<td width=\\\"10\\\" height=\\\"10\\\" bgcolor=\\\"#ccff99\\\"></td>\r\n<td width=\\\"10\\\" height=\\\"10\\\" bgcolor=\\\"#ccff99\\\"></td>\r\n<td width=\\\"10\\\" height=\\\"10\\\" bgcolor=\\\"#ccff99\\\"></td>\r\n<td width=\\\"10\\\" height=\\\"10\\\" bgcolor=\\\"#ccff99\\\"></td>\r\n<td width=\\\"10\\\" height=\\\"10\\\" bgcolor=\\\"#ccff99\\\"></td>\r\n<td width=\\\"10\\\" height=\\\"10\\\" bgcolor=\\\"#ccff99\\\"></td>\r\n<td width=\\\"10\\\" height=\\\"10\\\" bgcolor=\\\"#ccff99\\\"></td>\r\n<td width=\\\"10\\\" height=\\\"10\\\" bgcolor=\\\"#ccff99\\\"></td>\r\n<td width=\\\"10\\\" height=\\\"10\\\" bgcolor=\\\"#ccff99\\\"></td>\r\n<td width=\\\"10\\\