=\\\"10\\\" height=\\\"10\\\" bgcolor=\\\"#ccff99\\\"></td>\r\n<td width=\\\"10\\\" height=\\\"10\\\" bgcolor=\\\"#ccff99\\\"></td>\r\n<td width=\\\"10\\\" height=\\\"10\\\" bgcolor=\\\"#ccff99\\\"></td>\r\n<td width=\\\"10\\\" height=\\\"10\\\" bgcolor=\\\"#ccff99\\\"></td>\r\n<td width=\\\"10\\\" height=\\\"10\\\" bgcolor=\\\"#ccff99\\\"></td>\r\n<td width=\\\"10\\\" height=\\\"10\\\" bgcolor=\\\"#ccff99\\\"></td>\r\n<td width=\\\"10\\\" height=\\\"10\\\" bgcolor=\\\"#ccff99\\\"></td>\r\n<td width=\\\"10\\\" height=\\\"10\\\" bgcolor=\\\"#ccff99\\\"></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</table>\r\n</p>\r\n',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1781,666,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'cyantist','*smile*',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1782,677,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','i too like graph paper. my favorite journals for writing \r\nare the leather bound graph paper kind. mmmm.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1783,677,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>Graph paper and mechanical pencils are an especially\r\ndeadly combination for me.  :-)  If I have both of those in\r\nfront of me it\\\'s hard to resist doodling on something.</p>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1784,675,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'chaya','YES.  can we do that again?  that ruled.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1785,677,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','<a href=\\\"http://www.chiamattt.com\\\">chiamattt</a> used to \r\nhave a grid motif thing going on.  now the beauty is gone :(',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1786,679,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>welcome erin,</P>\r\n<P>my friend steveronimous sent me an email from \r\nnyc three days ago chronicling the waves of desire that \r\nwash over him seeing the first bare female arms of \r\nspring on the university of brooklyn campus.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>\\\"best friendly\\\"</P>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1787,677,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','whenever they gave us graph paper in elementary school\r\nart class i would always draw a robot.  i couldn\\\'t help it.\r\nsometimes i\\\'d try to draw something else but it\\\'d always\r\nend up being the same old robot.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1788,677,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','my secret to neat organic chem notes: graph paper. \r\n<br>diagrams, formulas, equations, math, and written \r\nnotes<br> coexisted peacefully side by side.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1789,352,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','i\\\'m definitely glad that i write to bring other people \r\ncloser to me.i used to be a lame teenager and did the \r\nopposite, though. hm.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1790,667,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Heinessen','A serving of potent laxatives in the enemy co-op\\\'s carrot \r\njuice or whatever fruity-voodoo-hippie drink they enjoy \r\nought to do nicely.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1791,677,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Heinessen','Graph paper is sexy.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1792,676,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','or maybe it was a helicopter.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1793,680,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','how very interesting.  i read a journal from the old west \r\none time about how women would chew pemmican until it was \r\nsoft and mushy and then feed it to the old folks and small \r\nchildren, i found it alarming.<br><br>\r\n\r\ni suspect the vegans are cringing at your choices, but \r\ndon\\\'t worry, they are lovely at accepting different \r\nopinions.<br><br>\r\n\r\ni personally would prefer a diet of excellent food prepared \r\nby world class chefs and delivered to me in covered \r\nsterling dishes.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1794,677,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p>such a beautiful post, brought me back in time to \r\nmy undergrad engineering years.</p>\r\n<p>theorem: all good ideas are conceived late at night, \r\nin diners, on the backs of napkins.</p>\r\n<p>corollary: all difficult problems are solved in \r\nbathrooms, during a shower or otherwise, and \r\nimmediately transferred to magazine subscription \r\ncards.</p>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1795,679,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','hello erin!  in texas the bluebonnets and black-eyed susans \r\nare blooming everywhere and we are wearing shorts and \r\nsandals.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1796,671,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','mark is safely in white sands now and he said they had dust \r\nstorms and the desert was very beautiful in a desert sort \r\nof way, although he prefers trees.  he is being careful. i \r\nmiss him very much.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1797,680,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sawks','<br>\r\ndudes! (and duderinas)<br><br>\r\n\r\nits all about the<br><br>\r\n\r\n<font size=\\\"7\\\"><b>YEAR O\\\'CURRY</b></font><br><br>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1798,672,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','i like it that you can now get different versions of peeps \r\nat halloween and easter.  i think they should make them for \r\nmothers day, too, only from something that doesn\\\'t have \r\nsugar so i could eat a whole package instead of just \r\none.<br><br>\r\n\r\ni\\\'ve always found it interesting how different people in \r\ndifferent places celebrate the same holidays.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1799,661,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','food for thought:  why is it that sometimes certain words that\r\nyou never think of suddenly start appearing everywhere as soon as you notice\r\nthem while you read.  i never use the word hubris.  it\\\'s not one of my\r\nwords.  in the last three days two people have used it in a conversation\r\nwith me on the telephone and i have found it in two of the books i read\r\nyesterday.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1801,667,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'maria','haha. no, we don\\\'t drink carrot juice, we drink insane \r\namounts of apple cider, soy/rice milk, and regular milk. \r\nany other kind is rare. ',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1803,676,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','\\\"land salt.\\\" i like that. i\\\'ve never heard it called that \r\nbefore.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1800,679,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','summer just ended in san francisco. two weeks of \r\nwarmth, now rain wind wind wind wind. i am looking \r\nforward to my journey to new mexico.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1804,678,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','<p> I knew a very nice boy, he had blue hair and seemed \r\ninteresting, he was very funny. I told him we should become \r\nfriends, and we did, sort of, slowly -- no rush, right?</p>\r\n<p> Well, he hung himself pretty soon after that.</p>\r\n<p> I know someone like him, someone who is still alive -- \r\nand sometimes I think he will follow a similar path.</p>\r\n<p> In High School I had an English teacher who said \r\nsomething about those who take their own lives, he said \r\nthey\'re the people the world needs the most. He said it in \r\na strange way, totally lacking in judgement, it was one of \r\nthose odd moments when someone distant from you suddenly \r\nbecomes totally human.</p>\r\n<p> Anyway, I don\'t know what I\'d do if I\'d known my friend \r\nwas going to end it. Probably nothing. I\'ve seen my friends \r\nmake decisions I think are really terrible, but I can\'t \r\nstop them and don\'t try to. Anyone who doesn\'t respect my \r\nabsolute authority over my own life is not my friend, and I \r\nextend the same respect to those I consider mine.</p>\r\n<p> Maybe it\'s a different form of morality. Or maybe just \r\na glorified version of powerlessness. Praise the fallen, in \r\nany case.</p>',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1805,683,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sawks','<br>\r\nhey! have you found the \\\'comment below\\\' thingy? :)<br>\r\njust checking',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1806,683,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sawks','<br>\r\nfuck i\'m anal! sorry',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1807,678,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','<p>um. we\\\'re not talking about watching your friend date \r\nthe wrong person. we\\\'re talking about suicide. any \r\npsychology class you take will teach you that suicidal \r\npeople do everything they can to alert the people around \r\nthem that they\\\'ve made this choice because they very \r\ndesperately want to be prevented from doing it. speaking as \r\nsomeone who was suicidal, please please please do not \r\nperpetuate the myth that suicides are \\\"lost causes\\\" and you \r\ncan\\\'t do anything to change their mind. it\\\'s really the \r\nopposite. no one craves positive attention and affection \r\nmore than someone who is severely depressed.</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1808,683,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','clap clap clap clap anais nin',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1809,680,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>you are going to be an american indian in n.y.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>as i recall from boyscouts, pemican can be pretty nasty\r\nfor all the reasons you mention above.  go for it though. \r\nmaybe you can send me a brick if you make the stuff.  i\\\'ll\r\ntry it.</P>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1810,681,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>oh darn! i was just telling yeti i think you are a\r\nfreak.  if you made all that up, i guess you are normal so\r\nfar as we all wish we could be power brokers in art and\r\nmedia and emotion, or just one or two of those.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>* sat on computer all day.</P>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1811,681,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','i really don\\\'t understand your apparent hostility.  what \r\ndoes it matter if i made this up or if it\\\'s god\\\'s honest \r\ntruth? i assumed this was an open forum and posted this to \r\nshare it with other people.  it continually amazes me that \r\nmost of those i encounter who claim to be open-minded don\\\'t \r\nrealize how conservative and doctrinaire they really are. i \r\nhave attempted in every way i know how to take part in this \r\nonline community, but it appears to be closed to outsiders. \r\ni\\\'ve never met anyone i thought was a freak.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1812,681,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>wow, i had this rather long reply to your offense and then i\r\nresized the browser window and it was erased on the\r\nrefresh.  i guess no-cache meta tags are not the answer for\r\nthat problem problem of duplicate posts, or maybe netscape sucks.\r\n<br><br>\r\ndamn.\r\n<br><br>\r\nanyway, the jist of it was for you to take a chill pill, i didn\'t mean anything bad.   i throw the word freak around to much, generally i just use it to describe something that is out of the ordinary.</P>\r\n<P>i hate it when technology causes loss of information.</P>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1813,681,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','i\'m sorry i misunderstood your intentions, then. i put that \r\ndisclaimer on there, well, i really don\'t know why i put it \r\non there except to make sure nobody thinks i\'m admitting to \r\nsmuggling hashish into the country. i think there\'s \r\nsomething that exists outside what we know as \"truth\" \r\nor \"imagination\" or \"deceit\" or \"art\", and it\'s something \r\nwe all have in common and is more real than real. that\'s \r\nwhat i strive for in my fiction or wistful ramblings or \r\nlies or straight reportage or whatever it might be. it\'s \r\nkind of liberating to not have to pin it down. some truth \r\ncan be better expressed through fiction than through \r\njournalism. suspension of disbelief and all that. there\'s a \r\nnigerian probverb: \"all stories are true.\" i like that \r\napproach. i think you folks are all great. you give me \r\nhope. much love.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1814,683,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','hey, i\\\'m anal too!  nice to meet you.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1815,681,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'dj1_luna','\\\"Every artist is a cannibal, every poet is a thief\r\nAll kill their inspiration and sing about their grief\\\"\r\n',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1816,674,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'cyantist','wow.. that is cool.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1817,676,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','i gave in to my revisionist tendencies and added a line to \r\nthis otherwise exquisite text. forgive me.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1818,676,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','i look scarily like my mom in the frame where i\\\'m opening a \r\nbeer. genetics is inevitable.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1819,678,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','i had a dream about this last night.  a friend had lost the\r\nwill to live and this showed itself by her become ill with a\r\nfatal disease.  she was in my care at the moment of her\r\ndeath and i just held her and let her slip away.  i wasn\\\'t\r\nsad, though, because it seemed like what she wanted.  when\r\nother people showed up they asked me how i could have let\r\nthat happen.  i was flustered and didn\\\'t know what to do at\r\nall and not until they had said something did it occur to me\r\nthat i should have tried to help.  then my friend turned\r\ninto the spirit of san francisco and mean people from the\r\nmarina moved into jim and kristie\\\'s old apartment.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1820,682,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'qq','I always have a knee-jerk cringing reaction when I see\r\nrational/analytical vs. artistic/creative presented as a\r\ndichotomy. Aside from the fact that most of us are all\r\nway too conditioned to see everything as a dichotomy, I\r\nthink this is a particularly harmful one. This is\r\nbecause it contributes to people seeing scientific, \r\ntechnical, or mathematically oriented people as uncreative\r\nand uninspired, and it contributes to people seeing\r\nartists as flaky, flighty, or unable to understand how \r\nthings \\\"really\\\" are. It may also make those very people\r\nlimit themselves unwittingly: \\\"I\\\'m a painter! There\\\'s no\r\nway I could learn abstract mathematics, and why would I\r\nwant to anyway?\\\" or \\\"I\\\'m a programmer/hacker/statistician.\r\nI\\\'d never be any good at drawing or photography.\\\" \r\nI like all kinds of things. What\\\'s wrong with a painter who\r\ngets off on the aesthetic beauty of calculus or a programmer\r\nwho makes big ugly sculptures out of clay? What\\\'s wrong\r\nwith us for finding either of those surprising?',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1823,686,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p>geekaustin: this isn\\\'t california, dammit!</p>\r\n<p>hm. huh?</p>\r\n\r\n',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1824,681,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','<a href=\\\"http://www.beatthief.com/\\\"\r\ntarget=\\\"_new\\\">http://www.beatthief.com/</a>',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1825,686,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','sounds to me like austin (the town) has an inferiority\r\ncomplex.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1826,686,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>i have never really understood that tag line.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nthe entire time i lived in austin, i had never been to\r\ncalifornia.  no that i am in california, i still don\'t\r\nunderstand it.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nmaybe it should change to \"news for austin\'s geeks\" since it\r\nis like slashdot kinda.  i suppose that is implicit in the\r\ndomain name though. \r\n<BR><BR>\r\nor maybe it is a curse, like, \"austin doesn\'t have\r\ncalifornia\'s labor laws, damnit.\"  i could see that.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nor \"austin doesn\'t have lots of rich people like california\r\nhas to support the tech sector, damnit.\"\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nor \"intel just stopped construction on the new headquarters\r\ndowntown, damnit.\"\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nor \"Bush is not from austin, damnit.\"\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nor \"mojo\'s is too crowded, damnit.\"\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nor \"spider house\'s coffee tastes like it was sun brewed with\r\nwater from the LA river using the lipton ice tea method, damnit.\"\r\n</P>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1822,686,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'LinearB','recruiter koans.\r\n\r\n<p>\\\"Are you looking for a Kernel Hacker?\\\"<p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\\"What aspect of Kernel Hacking? Memory management? \r\nSocket Programming? Writing Device Drivers? Interprocess \r\nComunications?\\\"\r\n\r\n<p>\\\"Do you think that Kernel Hacking is a logical \r\nprogression from shell programming? If so, at what point \r\ndoes shell programming become Kernel Hacking?\\\"\r\n\r\n<p>\\\"Who\\\'s Colonel Hacker? Will he be interviewing me as \r\nwell?\\\"\r\n\r\n<p>Greetings from LinearB and <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.geekaustin.org\\\">GeekAustin</a>\r\n\r\n<p>p.s. Swinney. How about a preview button for the comment \r\nfield?\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1827,686,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'LinearBenway','Well, I\\\'m not too fond of the Austin!=California tagline. I \r\ndon\\\'t know what I was thinking when I selected - probably \r\nlegions of trailerpark-guntotin-linuxusin-postalworkers.\r\n\r\n<p>So I changed the tagline. \r\n\r\n<p>And then came a barrage of emails saying: \\\"What are you \r\ndoing, selling out?\\\", \\\"Is Austin becoming \r\nCalifornia?\\\", \\\"Why don\\\'t you move to SiliconValley, you \r\ndotcom e-hole!\\\"\r\n\r\n<p>So I changed it back.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1828,686,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>ok, i didnt get that job.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>fuck</P>\r\n\r\n<P>FUCK</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i am feeling totally screwed.  not that i usually get the\r\nfirst job that i interview for anymore.  nowadays it is\r\nabout the fourth that i get an offer for.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i feel like going back to texas.  at least i can afford\r\nto live on 8 dollars an hour there.  i could go work for\r\nstarseeds or something.</P>\r\n\r\n<P> i can not believe i have all this knowlege about\r\ntechnology and it\\\'s use in my head now and there is nothing\r\nto do with it.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>dumb dumb situation i am in.  i am ready to go back to\r\ntexas and back to anonymity of the \\\'career\\\'.  no one asks\r\nwhat you do because they are too embarassed about what they\r\ndo.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i want to be a mechanic in south austin when i grow\r\nup.</P>\r\n\r\n<P><i>do not give up yet.</i></P>',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1829,681,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','hi matt. can we get your astrological sign? ',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1830,686,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'olivia sez:',' don\\\'t do it austin.  cuz then you\\\'d have to say \\\"hi, i\\\'m \r\naustin from austin\\\".  and that would be confusing.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1831,681,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','aries. 4/14/70 12:38 am. one month past when i was due \r\n(don\\\'t know if that makes a diff or not).\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1832,681,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','place of birth = brooksville, f-l-a\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1833,678,'2002-03-05 20:17:36',17,'austin to xep.','<P>\r\nthat is really a nice story.\r\n<BR>\r\n<BR>\r\ni have never known anyone to die.  no one close to me has \r\never died.  it is one of my greatest fears that someone \r\nnear me will die.  \r\n<BR>\r\n<BR>\r\nfear\r\n</P>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1834,686,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','<p>austin goes by \\\"bubba\\\" when in austin. so its more \r\nlike, \\\"i am bubba, bubba from austin.\\\" </p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1836,686,'2002-03-05 20:17:36',17,'austin to elly','see, i told you.  bmg.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1837,686,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>tech sector certainly isn\\\'t doing any better here.  I\\\'m\r\nin the same boat, how can all this knowledge I have in my\r\nhead apparently matter not a whit?  Is the web going to fade\r\ninto irrelevance after less than a decade?  I\\\'ve probably\r\napplied to 50 jobs in the past month, and have gotten\r\nexactly zero interviews.  Fuck, fuck, fuck.  I really don\\\'t\r\nwant to have to go back to working at Taco Bell or washing\r\ndishes in the Chemistry Dept.  The irony is that in many\r\ncases over the past two years I\\\'ve prioritized computer\r\nknowledge over chemistry knowledge, what I\\\'m theoretically\r\nmajoring in.  Did I screw up my chem grades for naught? Very\r\ndepressing.</p>\r\n<p>I\\\'ve actually been thinking about moving out to Silicon\r\nValley, because there are 5-10x more jobs in my field there\r\nthan there are here.  Anyone in SF or wherever be willing to\r\nhave an itenerant (sp?) perl/unix developer temp roomie for\r\na few months if I landed a summer contract?  I\\\'m polite and\r\ngenerally smell nice and I would probably look cute sleeping\r\nunder the coffee table...</p>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1838,686,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','haha. we already have a few of those. don\\\'t come here. not \r\nnow.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1839,678,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kini','yeah\r\n<br>last year i went from having no-one close to me ever \r\ndie, to losing three people within six months of each other.\r\n<p>it kinda sucks.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1840,686,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sawks','<br>\r\ndont be afraid to broaden your horizons - \\\'computer \r\nprogramming\\\' is for nerds! and the world could always use \r\nanother fluffer\r\n<br>\r\n',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1841,686,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','what does this mean, austin:<br>\r\n\\\"austin to elly: see, i told you. bmg.\\\"',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1842,690,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','<p>oh my god i love goth clubs.<BR>\r\ni used to make quite a hot goth. but now even when i <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://standing.ontheoutside.com/cam/halloweeny/cam104\r\n3.jpg\\\">i try</a>, it doesn\\\'t quite work like it used to.</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1843,690,'2004-07-27 05:13:57',63,'olivia','wow.  well it seems to work pretty well.  if you can top\r\nthat, crikey, you\\\'d have all the sad boys lying at your\r\nfeet!  what i mean is, you look nice :)',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1844,690,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','one thing i like about goth clubs more than raves is that\r\nyou don\\\'t have to pretend to want to hug people.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1845,690,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','oh sad boys. picture me wearing my floorlength cleavage \r\nrevealing black velvet dress, all gothed up and bored, \r\nwatching friends dance to remixed nin songs in a smoky club \r\nin downtown dallas while a boy who\\\'s wearing a shirt made \r\nof electrical tape towers above and stares at my breasts \r\nand tells me about how much he hates himself. <BR>\r\nwhat i need to do is go to goth clubs with <b>you</b>, liv.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1846,690,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'LinearB','<p>Once I was going into a 7-11, and I had this floorlength \r\nIssey Miyake black rubber trenchcoat on, and my face was \r\nall covered with shiseido. I had been doing this so much \r\nthat I actually forget how I must look. This guy comes up \r\nto me and sez \\\"Show me your teeth\\\". What? \\\"Show me your \r\nfangs. You\\\'re a vampire, aren\\\'t you?\\\" \r\n\r\n<p>ausgoths just don\\\'t get dolled up to go out anymore. \r\n\r\n<p>I\\\'m looking forward to<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.jwz.org\\\">JamieZ<a/> re-opening the <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.dnalounge.com\\\">DNA Lounge</a>. A bunch of \r\nthe crazies who I went with to the <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.inmove.de/doomsday/frame-set.html\\\">Skinny \r\nPuppy Reunion Concert</a> all want to meet in SF for the \r\nDNA\\\'s opening. Imagine, a roomful of people who dress you \r\nwith their eyes, then undress you, then dress you again...\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1847,693,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'chaya','i will be continuing the celebration of chayafest through \r\nthe weekend.  tonight, there will be fire and engine \r\nstarter and blowtorches and tequila in a flask.  friday and \r\nsaturday, some hippies, some oontz oontz, probably some \r\nmore drinking.  and i will celebrate zombie jesus day with \r\na REALLY HUGE HANGOVER.  just as god intended. ',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1848,693,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'maria','i don\\\'t really know what is happening on friday night. \r\nthere may be several house parties that i *could* go to, or \r\ni could go see crouching tiger, hidden dragon at the second-\r\nrun movie theater (yeah rural ohio!), or or or or. i don\\\'t \r\nknow. i might just stay home and sleep. \r\n\r\nsaturday is the day of excitement -- hopefully off to get \r\nsome sort of visual aids, and drag ball, my college\\\'s \r\nversion of the prom. lots of new people will be in town \r\nvisiting, everyone will be dressed up, and i will hopefully \r\nbe intoxicated. wish me luck. \r\n\r\nzombie jesus day will be spent working the hangover shift \r\n(noon to three pm), doing homework, and attending the house \r\nmeeting for the co-op i will be residing in next year. \r\nwoowoo. \r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1849,693,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kini','<p>hiking! camping! pancakes! woo!',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1850,693,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'annette','I will be:\r\n<br><br>Seeing my best friend who inconsiderately moved \r\naway but is now back for a little while. Buying some books \r\nat my favourite bookstore. Going to see Princess Mononoke. \r\nKnitting my scarf. Cooking and eating delicious noodles. \r\nSnuggling, relaxing and petting Elvis.\r\n<br><br>I also wanted to go on a picnic but we have a \r\ncyclone right now so I don\\\'t think that will happen.\r\n<br><br>... OK, I just looked out the window and it is \r\nbright blue and sunny. Where did the cyclone go? Perhaps a \r\npicnic after all!',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1851,691,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'juan','<P>technology is so boring.</P>\r\n <P>\r\nI had a really \\\"i\\\'m gonna throw this motherfucking computer\\\"\r\naway night 2 weeks ago.\r\n</P> \r\n<P>I was going to be an English teacher who decied on a\r\nGraphic Design major\r\nwho decided the designs look better in my head. ( and of\r\ncoursre there are tons of other major factors that concluded\r\nmy college\r\ncarrer)</P>\r\n\r\n<P> it has been nice not using dreamweaver at all work\r\nb/c the web site is not that important at the moment.\r\nhow refreshing.\r\n</P>\r\n<P>just rambles. after reading your post. we all knew this\r\nnew new new world order would come about. we\\\'ll be joking\r\nabout 1999 in\r\nthe future.</P>\r\n<PRE>\r\nand i don\\\'t know if u will remember\r\nbut when i got my car\r\nand it was brand new\r\nand we all went to lunch for the first time\r\nin my brand new car, we stoped for Ice snow balls\r\non lamar and there was a young Cute girl operating the place\r\nand i drive by yesterday\r\nand there she is, a year later.\r\nit made me think oh happy guys hanging out in this damn heat\r\ndays.\r\n</PRE>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1852,693,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>i like to run around like a spastic screeching:</P>\r\n<H1>kini ... kini ... keeeeeeeeeneeeeeeeeeee</h1>\r\n\r\n<P>what does it mean?</P>\r\n\r\n<P>what does it meeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeean?!</P>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1853,690,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>I like goth clubs.  But I think I\\\'m probably too boring a\r\ndresser to really fit in.  I wear interesting colors inside\r\nmy head, not on my outside.  At least I think they\\\'re\r\ninteresting.  I\\\'m sure accountants find double-entry\r\nbookkeeping to be interesting.  I don\\\'t know what the point\r\nof this post is.  Oh well, at least knives aren\\\'t dancing in\r\nthe kitchen.</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1854,695,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','that was nice.<BR>\r\n(best friendly.)',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1855,691,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','so did you get all these things done today?? i bet you did. \r\ni bet you\\\'re the king of the mountain, you rascally wabbit, \r\nyou.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1856,693,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Joanna','\\\'Kini\\\' means: Most  wonderful person in the world.  \r\n<BR><BR>\r\n\r\nHey Swinney Readers, April 22nd is the 3rd Annual \r\nInternational Give Stuff to Joanna and  Kini Day. Give \r\nstuff to us.  ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1857,696,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','blessed one.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1858,697,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','first of all, that is the greatest opening line of anything\r\ni have read on this site (in recent memory).  nice.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nsecond, i dont have the guts to say anything else about\r\nthis, much less talk about the wierd sex dreams that i have\r\nhad.  yes, WIERD.  maybe some day when i am senial.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1859,698,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'neo','nice matrix.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1860,697,'2004-07-27 05:13:57',63,'olivia',' i want to have that dream.  i also would like to be fucked \r\nby a girl with a cock.  hi.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1861,698,'2004-07-27 05:14:09',63,'olivia sez',' what is bragg\\\'s?  also, isn\\\'t it distubring how many \r\ncommonly used items we refer to by brand name?',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1862,698,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'oh','yeah it\\\'s fucked up. but braggs is this liquid aminos stuff \r\nand that was too big to fit in the matrix.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1863,697,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i would suck it. i mean, why not?',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1864,698,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>Ah! It\\\'s a sparse diagonalized matrix[1]!  Noooooooo!</p>\r\n<p>Sorry, linear algrbra flashback. ;-)</p>\r\n<p>[1] making it easy to invert, producing the carnivore\r\nversion I guess (V^-1 == C).</p>\r\n<p>Nerdliness aside, that looks yummy.  I\\\'ll have to try\r\ncooking some combinations of that soon (loooove olive oil). \r\nThanks for sharing your cooking skillz!</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1865,697,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>Have any of the swinney guys dreamed of being female?  I\r\nnever have that I recall, I\\\'m just curious if the\r\ngender-change dream is common (yeah, I know that in this\r\ncase it was just genitalia, but that\\\'s a pretty big part of\r\ngender, at least on a biological level.  on a psychological\r\nlevel who the heck knows what gender is...)</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1866,697,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','but steve, you are not gay.  but sine, you are not male.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\n<PRE>\r\nWARNING * * * * WARNING  * * * *\r\nGENDER OVERLOAD IN PROGRESS\r\nSHUT DOWN REACTORS .........\r\n</PRE>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1867,693,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sawks','<br>\r\ni am posting this from mac os x where i just built \r\napache+php+mysql, that was my mission for friday\r\n<br><br>\r\nweekend = ummm grooverider+bike rides+design+\r\nsleep+tidy flat',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1868,698,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','<P>Bragg\'s Liquid Aminos! Yay Weeb! The magical combination \r\nof <a \r\nhref=\"http://www.bragg.com/aminosproduct.html\">Bragg\'s</a> \r\n+ nutri yeast was introduced to me in 1992 when my raw \r\nfoodie pal dragged me out to a Rainbow Gathering. Ever \r\nsince, they have been an integral part of my diet.</P>\r\n<P>Favorite things to eat:<BR>\r\n<BR>\r\n-Avocado half with the hole filled with liquid aminos, \r\nnutri yeast, olive oil, eaten witha spoon.<BR>\r\n-Bowlsfull of sprouted seeds, raw corn, tomato, carrot, \r\nsunflower seeds, raw beet slices, radish, raw snapped peas \r\nor beans, avocado, red onion, dark greens, nutri yeast, \r\nliquid aminos, olive oil.<BR>\r\n-Organic bananas.<BR>\r\n-The water from the front of my fridge.<BR>\r\n</P>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1869,697,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','yes, but I am a fair shade of gay.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1870,697,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<pre><tt>\r\nN - O -V - E - L - T - Y\r\n</tt></pre>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1871,700,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','Hurrah! A DAMAJAH!!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1872,702,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','you better go look at this so sine will stop posting it all\r\nover the place!',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1873,702,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','right, that\\\'s <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.gorillaz.com\\\">www.gorillaz.com</a>.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1874,702,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','what\\\'s that url again?',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1875,702,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','you know, <a href=\\\"http://www.gorillaz.com/\\\">this \r\none</a>.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1876,702,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>What was it again? ;-)</p>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1877,702,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','<a href=\\\"http://fans.gorillaz.com\\\">fans.gorillaz.com</a>\r\n\r\ner, wait...',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1878,702,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>&lt;rant&gt;Question:  Bozoids at Macromedia make Flash 5\r\nfor linux.  This is probably pretty close to a straight\r\nrecompile I\\\'m guessing, because the Netscape plugin API is\r\nthe same AFAIK across the spectra of things Netscape runs\r\non.  The why can\\\'t they come out with Shockwave for unix? \r\nIs Shockwave really that different from Flash?  Argh!  HULK\r\nSMASH PUNY CODERS!!!&lt;/rant&gt;</p>\r\n<p>The stories and comments could really use a preview\r\nfeature.  I\\\'d submit a patch if I could get a tarball o\\\'\r\nsource (and figure out an elegant fix).</p>',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1879,692,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>I\\\'m with you dude, searching for tech work here in Austin\r\nis a bitch right now.  At least  you\\\'re getting calls.  :-) \r\n(If anyone needs a perl/java/php/unix/web/sql/networking\r\nnerd in Austin, <a\r\nhref=\\\"mailto:orion@ccwf.cc.utexas.edu\\\">drop me a line!</a>\r\n(hey you never know who might read this))</p>\r\n<p>(btw I\\\'m the same orion as the geekaustin author/frequent\r\nposter.  don\\\'t feel bad we didn\\\'t post you\\\'re last story, I\r\nasked Linear about it (I leave the story approval to him)\r\nand he said by the time he noticed it in the submissions\r\nqueue it (the event) was already past...)</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1880,692,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>s/you\\\'re/your/g</p>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1881,692,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>Maybe all us dispossed Austin techies could band together\r\nto form a sort of mega-startup.  The only problem is what\r\nidea do we band together around?  I know I have the skills\r\nto run the mundane computer architecture of a startup (lan\r\nthrough wan and external services like mail and web and\r\nwhatnot).  I just can\\\'t think of anything particularly\r\ncompelling to do, further in this fiscal climate who would\r\nbankroll a just-over-the-threshold-of-23-years coder whose\r\nprimary degree a) isn\\\'t done (5 hours remain) and b) isn\\\'t\r\nin CS or EE (it\\\'s chemistry, and if anyone makes smart\r\nremarks about how hard CS is I\\\'d like them to sign up for CH\r\n354L here at UT, Quantum Mechanics and Statisitical\r\nThermodynamics (with a side order of Rate Kinetics and\r\nSpectroscopic Applications) with Dr. Ivan \\\"I Vill Kick Your\r\nPansy American Asses\\\" Bersuker)...</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1882,697,'2004-07-27 05:13:57',63,'olivia',' steve, when will you admit that you just want to suck a\r\ndick?',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1883,686,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>Heh, well my horizons are already too damn broad.  I\\\'m\r\nalmost done with a BSc. chem degree, focusing organic.  Oh\r\nwait, I also have a quasi-minor in business.  And a\r\nquasi-minor in computer science.  These minors are quasi\r\nbecuase when you\\\'re a BS student you don\\\'t have a major or\r\nminor only the Degree Program.  (I\\\'ll have about 170 hours\r\nwhen I graduate.)  So I could go be a chemist lab rat\r\nsomewhere.  But I don\\\'t love chemistry, not really, not\r\nanymore.  It\\\'s computer science/IT that I love, either\r\nprogramming or the simpler joy of <em>making stuff work</em>\r\nas a sys or net admin.  Yeah, life sucks dick sometimes and\r\nyou just have to do whatever you can find to get by, but\r\ndamnit, I really want to do something I care about.</p>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1884,693,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','i\\\'m playing d&d at <a\r\nhref=\\\"http://www.conquest.asn.au/2001/\\\">conquest</a>.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1885,702,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','that\\\'s a whole lot of hacker jargon in one sentence.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1886,702,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sawks','<br>\r\nbecause shockwave doesn\\\'t hook into the browser \r\narchitecture (like flash does) for graphics and audio, it \r\nhas its own engine, including hardware calls\r\n<br><br>\r\nthats why its so much faster than flash, and why the \r\nshockwave plugin is a lot bigger, and also why it can do \r\nproper 3d and video editing and other fun stuff\r\n<br><br>\r\nto make shockwave for linux they\\\'d have to coerce apple \r\ninto writing quicktime for linux as well as building a \r\nshockwave player from the ground up to support x \r\nwindows, so yeah... its a different story...\r\n<br><br>\r\nmac os x suffers from this as well - but at least there \r\nyou can run mac os 9.1 apps (including shockwave) in \r\nclassic mode (which isn\\\'t an emulator, so it takes full \r\nadvantage of the hardware)\r\n<br><br>\r\nsorry for all the tech :)',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1887,699,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Joanna','Hollywood Squares taught me that male fireflies shine their \r\nlittle lights in order to attract mates',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1888,699,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>all the cables and ports and stuff does seem sort of\r\npornographic in a hentai-tentacle-sex sort of way...</p>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1889,702,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','&lt;cartman&gt;Ah, son of a bitch!&lt;/cartman&gt;',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1890,702,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sawks','<br>btw,<br>\r\njamie hewlett is the shit, but gorillaz beats are kinda \r\nwack :)',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1891,699,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sawks','<br>\r\ntent-baseT? r0wr<br>\r\n<br>\r\nblinking lights == the closest we get to seeing the soul \r\nof the machine\r\n<br><br>\r\nwhen i\\\'m humping a few gigs across the network and \r\nthe orange collision light on the hub goes nuts i always \r\nfeel a little guilty...',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1892,702,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','i second the submission from orion to do a preview feature \r\nfor the comment area.\r\n',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1893,693,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sawks','<br>\r\nix is well into larp, he plays a dainty maiden with a heart \r\nof pus',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1894,699,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'orisha','html O.K.I think it may be genetic, orion.  I recall as a \r\nchild at night staring for hours at a red blinking light \r\nover a factory near my home...i believed it was sending \r\nmessages and f I could just get the ssequence right I could \r\ndecode it..I also like, when traveling at night, so see the \r\ntoweres blinking...and of course, there is the thing with \r\nthe lights at Christmas.  Probably no one here is old \r\nenough to remember when TV sets and radios had vacuum tubes \r\nthat glowed orange in the backs of the TVs...you could look \r\nin there and squint your eyes and pretend you were viewing \r\na vista of rockets, ready to go to Mars..or..the outer \r\nlimits...I still like to study the filaments of lights and \r\nlike to think of that analogy as being an artist and poet.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1895,692,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'puppy','hey, orion. have you ever considered going into chip \r\narchitecture? with a degree in chem, i am sure there is \r\nsome demand for your knowledge... and with all the chip \r\nmakers here in austin, i am sure something could pan out...',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1896,682,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'orisha','html O.K. I think that I meant not to speak in terms of \r\nabsolute dichotomies--but in actuality it is more like \r\ndegrees across a spectrum.  Looking back, I think alot of \r\nthis kind of dichotomy thinking got started with the \r\nleft/right brain theories and that just hasn\\\'t been borne \r\nout by how the brain actually functions. I dont think any \r\none is a pure type...probably kind of like the bell curve \r\ndistribution...but I know that I myself lean to the \r\nintuitive, oceanic side of the spectrum...for one thing, I \r\nthink in images, not words or numbers..if you were to look \r\ninto my mind, it would be a continually evolving montage of \r\nimagery, sound, speech and the occaisional postit note of \r\npracticality tossing in the breeze.\r\nI would someday like to be able to appreciate the beauty \r\ninherent (supposedly) in mathematics..well, I do..like the \r\nFibonacci ratios, the fascinating geometric structures of \r\nradiolarian life...it\\\'s just algebraic equations that bore \r\nme.  I did like geometry as a kid because I could go off on \r\nwild tangents.......',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1897,661,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'orisha','html O.K.Hubris has never been lurking in my vocabulary \r\neither...i think sometimes these things are almost \r\nomens..or mirrors of something going on in your life...or \r\nin the life of someone you know..or sometimes an even \r\nbroader application...for some odd reason I have never \r\nliked that word, as I also dislike etiquette.  Hubris to me \r\nis like being up to your ass in smashed tomatoes with a \r\nsoundtrack of yowling cats...all in a room of trick mirrors.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1898,698,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','<p>i was once asked how i survived when i first moved to \r\naustin and was living alone on $320/week.</p>\r\n<p>mostly <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://standing.ontheoutside.com/recipes/ramenstirfy.t\r\nxt\\\">ramen stir fry</a>, <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://standing.ontheoutside.com/recipes/veggiechili.t\r\nxt\\\">veggie chili</a>, and lots of boil-in-the-bag brown \r\nrice.<BR>\r\nmexican food is also a big savior. you can make burritos \r\nwith beans, rice, and cheese for 50 cents a pop.</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1899,693,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','<BR>\r\nweekend=lazing, playing with kitten that izzy is \r\nbabysitting, thomas and i being thrashed at scrabble by \r\nizzy, reading book, watching videos, concord dawn vinyl \r\nrelease thingy at the box.<BR>\r\n<BR>\r\nwho plays scrabble, anyway?\r\n',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1900,690,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','I saw a Thomas Beagle and a Kim in those photos! What are \r\nthey doing in Melbourne?\r\nI used to live in their flat. Lalala.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1901,699,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','dude! Orion, i am with you on the blinkin light thing! i \r\nhave a cable modem (make fun of me if you wish, but dsl \r\nisnt in my area) and i love to see those lights go! \r\nattatched to the cable modem i have a router and an 8 port \r\nhub pushing out to all the other computers in my house and \r\neven my neighbors... (sshhh don\\\'t tell). anyway the point \r\nis, that at night my room is bombarted by some 30+ led\\\'s, \r\nall green with the a few reds and oranges here and there... \r\ni get excited when i see the network utilization meter on \r\nthe hub hit 80%, no really it excites me...',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1902,697,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','i\\\'ve had dreams in which some of my hot male friends had \r\nvaginas.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1903,693,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'annette','scrabble!!!!!!!',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1904,697,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','i had this dream once where there was this person who i \r\nwas just insanely attracted to and i couldn\\\'t figure out\r\nwhy. all i wanted to do was get on them.  i can\\\'t remember\r\nif i thought they were a girl or a boy but when we started\r\ndoing the nasty it turned out they were either an FTM\r\ntranssexual or a hermaphrodite.  as soon as that was\r\ndiscovered everything made sense.  i\\\'ve always been drawn to\r\ngender inspecific people.\r\n<p>\r\nhi\r\n</p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1905,702,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>So who do I bug for a tarball? :-)</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1906,698,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','enter cynic: i have a feeling that braggs is really just soy\r\nsauce.  the aminos it speaks of are also present there.  the\r\nnutritional information is almost identical.  it does have a\r\nslightly different taste which is nice though.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1907,692,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>It seems interesting, but where would I even start?  It\r\nseems like a pretty orthagonal skill set, even to hacking\r\ncode.  (There is some fascinating ochem that goes into\r\nmaking the photoresists used in chip making.  The quest for\r\never smaller unit linkages and resists that decompose into\r\nnon-toxic subunits continues.  This field and advances in\r\nthe laser/maser/whatever-radiating-thingies are what lead to\r\nsmaller chip features and thus smaller or more powerful\r\nchips (I mean, they are the necessary prerequisites for the\r\ndesigners being able to build at that level).)</p>\r\n<p>Hmm.  Is there a book somewhere called \\\"Design EE for\r\nIdiot Chemists\\\"?  :-)</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1908,692,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','I know what you mean about the clothing thing btw.  My last\r\ninterview (last august, before school started), I wore a\r\n$500ish suit (pretty spiff for a college student anyway,\r\ntotally derived from the generosity of my fiancee\\\'s\r\nparents).  And because my feet had grown since I got dress\r\nshoes last or something, my doc martens.  The ones with the\r\nred anarchy laces.  Oh well, I didn\\\'t get the job, but I\r\nthink it was because they wanted an Oracle expert (which a)\r\nI\\\'m not, and b) they didn\\\'t list in the ad).',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1909,681,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'zb','aries unite. twelve days late.\r\nhappy birthday matt.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1910,702,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','let me check it into cvs.  the domain is moving servers as\r\nwe  speak, so give me a couple days.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1911,697,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','i day dream about having a vagina... does that count?',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1912,700,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','who is this adamajah? and how did he come by this name?\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1913,700,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<TT><a href=\\\"http://yeager.tv\\\">* A * D * A * M *</A></TT>\r\n<PRE>\r\nAndriod Designed for Assassination and Mathematics\r\n</PRE>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1914,702,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','saturn5 productions: the internet presence provider that \r\nworks *for you*!',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1915,700,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','entry pending',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1916,698,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'s5 queries xep','are you talking about the US RDA \\\"nutrition facts\\\"? they \r\nare only allowed to list nutrients that cover the bare \r\nminimum of government mandated health information.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1917,704,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','reminds of \\\"travels with charlie in search of america\\\" by \r\njohn steinbeck. steinbeck is so the shit. \\\"cannery row\\\" is \r\nsuch a beautiful lyric novel.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1918,692,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'puppy','well, my wife has a biochem degree and works in the failure \r\nanalysis lab at amd... she might be someone to talk to if \r\nyou are seriously interested in jumping into that foray... \r\ne-mail me and we can hook-up',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1919,698,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','cynic O.K: yeah, i thought the same thing when i looked at\r\nthe bottle. it sounded like it was just soy sauce? times\r\nlike these make me realize i need a good liquid chromograph.\r\nhmmph.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1920,705,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','I have to go out and take photos of strangers to put in a \r\nmagazine. Sometimes it gets me into places for free, which \r\nis why I started doing it in the first place. The only \r\ncatch: I have to go to places I normally wouldn\\\'t go on my \r\nown. It\\\'s kinda cool. I dunno where I will end up going \r\ntonight but it would be really rad to shoot pics of you \r\nguys and get them in the magazine. And drink come beer. etc.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1921,703,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','fuckin\\\' transformers rock.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1922,705,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','sweet.  i\\\'m down.  and so is my mop-top.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1923,705,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','cum beer?',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1924,705,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','bukkake?',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1925,698,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>well, I am taking instrumental analysis this term.  :-)\r\nPick your poison: HPLC, LCMS, GCMS, NMR, FTIR, blah blah. \r\nOf course I\\\'d need a few six-packs to bribe the operators\r\nwith (\\\"Dude, sixer of dos equies if you can give me a spec\r\nof this...\\\") ;-)  Actually I doubt they\\\'d let me.  They\\\'re\r\nnervous enough with me running olive oil through the HPLC.</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1926,707,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>\r\nthere is no official #swinney, there is however #annoying on\r\nefnet which will most often require identd, and is plagued\r\nby some of the most annoying personalities on the Internet.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nlog on at your own risk.\r\n</P>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1927,705,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','gross',5,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1928,704,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'mika','<BR><BR>\r\n<pre>*squeek*</pre>\r\n<BR>\r\n(destabilizing)',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1929,698,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','ok, upon not very much research, i think the main difference\r\nis that soy sauce is fermented soy beans and braggs is just\r\npressed or raw?  maybe?  in that case, it\\\'s possible there\\\'s\r\nsome nutritional value present in braggs that isn\\\'t in soy\r\nsauce because it gets lots in the fermentation or heating\r\nprocess.  i do not think it\\\'s very significant though.  this\r\nis all speculation.  it still tastes good.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1930,708,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>i am posed the question, do i believe you speak the truth\r\nabout yourself or fiction?\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nis it really your birthday and are you really 31?\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nare you really at your parents?\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nis it really hot?\r\n</P>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1931,705,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','hahhaa mrs. johnson\'s donuts.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1932,707,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i logged off irc. ',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1933,707,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','you can only chat with us if you promise not to talk about\r\ngeek shit all the time.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1934,707,'2003-05-10 16:09:14',79,'yeti','<p>Try something like this: (adapted to your NAT setup)<br>\r\naccess-list 111 permit tcp any host 1.2.3.4  eq 113</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1935,707,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','penalty:  offsides.  yeti: 5 yards.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1936,708,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','<P>Yes.</P><P>Really.</P>\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1937,707,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'eoj','orion: think outside the IRC\r\n',5,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1938,697,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'eoj','one time i had a dream that two of my male friends were gay \r\nlovers, even though they\\\'re both