erous envy.  i know \r\nthat for 98% of the time they\\\'re nothing but a source of \r\nmany variegated miseries, but...i at least go through \r\nphases where being pregnant sounds like the most amazing \r\nthing in the world.  and i feel like with the whole 28 day \r\ncycle thing, womenfolk have an intimate and obvious \r\nreminder of their connection with the great wheeling cycles \r\nof the universe.  boys are just as connected on some level, \r\nit\\\'s just easier for them to forget.\r\n<br><br>\r\nyeesh, could i sound like more of a hippy?',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1946,709,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i can\\\'t say this enough: dancing is the drug.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1947,693,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','having a larger collection of words does not equal \r\n\\\"smarter\\\".',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1948,705,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','ewwww. gross.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1949,712,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','i take it you two know each other?',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1950,712,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'anon','I love Princess.  She is my therapist.  When I am rich, I \r\nwill pay for her to just sit around waiting for me to come \r\nand lie on her leather couch.  She keeps me sane.  Thank \r\nyou for everything Princess.  \r\n<BR><BR>\r\n(\\\"You are not allowed to be a no-one on Swinney\\\")',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1951,717,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','i wasn\\\'t going to post this, but austin made me.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1952,717,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','all my favorite kids\\\' stories involve exploding animals. \r\nhurrah.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1953,716,'2003-07-24 15:44:23',165,'joker','the thing about eggs though is that\\\'s where it all starts.  \r\nyou know what i mean.  i mean, you got this egg, right?  \r\nand it\\\'s got charcoal powder on it or maybe it\\\'s angel dust \r\nor camel shit.  who gives a fuck?!  you know?!  but inside \r\nof this little egg is like this little piece of energy.  \r\nand it\\\'s holding the shell together and slowly destroying \r\nit at the same time.  so that finally the energy that made \r\nthe shell in the first place is the energy that hatches \r\nit.  and then the energy that comes out of the shell comes \r\nout in the form of a NEW shell?  and then that starts and \r\nthe energy that holds together the egg of the chicken and \r\nfetus is the energy that will eventually destroy it...you \r\nknow?<br>\r\n...i like to break the yokes...',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1954,709,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kat','set the floor on fire. grooving body desire.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1955,717,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','hi.  i made a cake today.  it is a very concerned cake. \r\nit\\\'s not sure it wants to be eaten.  here is the <a\r\nhref=\\\"http://www.logy.org/~xep/days/2001/041501/bunnycake.jpg\\\">cake.</a>\r\n',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1956,717,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','i had a dream last night mainly about stripey scarves',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1957,713,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'g.f.k.','<p>Examining early net usage by adolescents is interesting. \r\nI\\\'m curious as to what can be learned about people by \r\ncommunity choices made during their early days on the \r\nInternet, in particular those that became involved in\r\ndeviant communities. warez, hacking/cracking, etc.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Do people decide to join communities or do communities \r\ndecide to include people? I believe the answer is in the \r\nmiddle, but I\\\'d like to know what you think \r\n<i>specifically</i>.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>How are people affected based on their participation in \r\nthese communities? Does Darwin exhibit personality \r\ntendencies that can be understood via his (zero)days as a \r\npirate? Did those tendencies exist prior to his \r\nparticipation within the community, or were they fostered by\r\nit?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>made up examples for (and apologies to) Darwin the \r\npirate:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Darwin is unhappy and/or lonely.</li>\r\n<ul><li>seeks pleasure and/or acceptance within \r\ncommunity</li></ul>\r\n<li>Darwin is a snobbish materialist.</li>\r\n<ul><li>spends times in pursuit of differentiating himself \r\nfrom others by having material objects they do not</li></ul>\r\n<li>Darwin lacks respect for law and/or capitalism \r\n(same).</li>\r\n<ul><li>trades in stolen objects</li></ul>\r\n<li>Darwin is uncomfortable with his identity.</li>\r\n<ul><li>seeks anonymity via alternate monikers</ul></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>A question: are the list items after the first even \r\nrelevant let alone true? Do people join a community during \r\ntheir adolescence because they feel drawn to its ideology \r\nor because the community is willing to accept us?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If \\\'positive\\\' communities are available to accept a \r\nyouth, would participation in them have contributed to \r\ntheir development in a vastly different way, or are all \r\ncommunity experiences roughly the same?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Do people become deviant due to personality tendencies, \r\nor because deviant communities accept them more \r\nreadily/easily than others? </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Can all deviants--excepting the psychotic/psychopathic--\r\nbe explained as \\\"individuals that lack self-esteem and tend \r\ntowards seeking negative reenforcement/attention\\\", or does \r\nthat explain only a subset of the deviant community, or \r\nnone of it at all?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I\\\'m aware of a field of study called \\\"Psychology\\\" which \r\nmay have addressed these questions, but I\\\'m interested in \r\nyour human intuitions rather than scholarly textbookery.</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1958,718,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','hi steve. how the fuck are you? ',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1959,717,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','xep, that\\\'s the saddest most worried-est cake i\\\'ve ever \r\nseen.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1960,717,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i am fond of the cake.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1961,715,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'eoj','<P>to quote they might be giants:</P>\r\n\r\nno one in the world ever gets what they want and that is \r\nbeautiful<BR>\r\neverybody dies frustrated and sad and that is beautiful\r\nand they want what they\\\'re not<BR>\r\nand i wish they would stop<BR>\r\n\r\n<P>[strategic truncation for emphasis]</P>\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1962,715,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'eoj','<P>bah, there really needs to be a preview feature :)</P>\r\n\r\nno one in the world ever gets what they want/and that is \r\nbeautiful/everybody dies frustrated and sad/and that is \r\nbeautiful/and they want what they\\\'re not/and i wish they \r\nwould stop\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1963,719,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'tuesday','<Pre>\r\ni was walking along the way to the park \r\nwhen i saw a pigeon shitting on a park bench.\r\na cloud moved across the sky\r\nbetween me and the light\r\nshadow moved in like clouds\r\nmy hand moved instinctively\r\nto the revolover in my pocket\r\nthunder in the background cracked.\r\nthe pigeon died on the ground\r\nwhere it belonged.\r\n</Pre>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1964,719,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','<P><img src=\"http://imagehost.auctionwatch.com/bin/imageserver.x/00000000/madcaps/LowRider3.jpg\" width=\'400\'>>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1965,719,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','d\\\'oh.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1966,715,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'orisha','html O.K.<there are said to be two tragedies in life: one \r\nis to get your heart\\\'s desire and the other is not to get \r\nit.  I also like this one: that the world to the thinking \r\nman is a comedy, but for the man who feels, it is a tragedy.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1967,718,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','scary.  i dont know if i could play that.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1968,715,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','html is just O.K. LaTeX better.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1969,699,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'orisha','html O.K.<i also think all the glittering lights are in a \r\nway reminiscent of the opulent splendor of the night sky..a \r\nblinking light is also a pulse of sorts, hynotic...h