unlinked<br>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1995,722,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'olivia sez:','<p>i am all about collages.</p>\r\n<img src=\\\"http://oxy.gen.nz/images/misc/gimp_bus.jpg\\\"\r\nalt=\\\"mmmmmmmm?\\\" width=\\\"497\\\" height=\\\"396\\\" border=\\\"0\\\"><br>\r\n<p>it was elly\\\'s idea.</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1996,723,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','that movie is the best thing to be viewed on this screen \r\nsince i downloaded honeymoon heat. ',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1997,719,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','lowrider bike chicks are dope it seems too!',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1998,724,'2003-07-24 15:44:23',165,'joker','in the words of my general semantics instructor (and he was \r\nprobably using someone else\\\'s words)<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n\\\"words don\\\'t mean.  people mean.\\\"<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\ni find the idea of creating a new language absolutely \r\ndelightful to imagine.  instead of calling the cop \r\na \\\"fucking pig\\\", i could refer to him/her as a \\\"snarker \r\ncinckle froother\\\" and those \\\"in the know\\\" could all have a \r\ngood time without anyone getting hurt.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nthe problem with this, of course is that eventually, when \r\nthe numbers of those \\\"in the know\\\" reaches a critical mass, \r\nthis deviant language would become the new pop standard.  \r\non the one hand, it\\\'s a natural linguistic evolution, the \r\nnatural selection being to develop a language of constant \r\nfreedom.  and on the other, it\\\'s destined to fail because \r\nit\\\'s predicated on exclusiveness, which is quite \r\nirresistable.</p>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(1999,724,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','so you know the first thing i thought of was clockwork \r\norange.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2000,724,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'mike','How about Esperanto?',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2001,722,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','hey! can i get some <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://standing.ontheoutside.com/cam/blue_hair/\\\">blue \r\nhair</a> love, please?<BR>\r\ngreen elitists.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2002,722,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','<img src=\\\"http://www.fonem.org/misc/howdy.jpg\\\">sure.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2003,724,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','wasn\\\'t esperanto designed for the exact opposite reasons\r\nthough?  a unifying language... a combination of many of the\r\nmost commonly spoken western languages?',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2004,722,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','here is some more.  because this page is all about vanity,\r\nright?<p>\r\n<img src=\\\"http://logy.org/~xep/splix/xepshairsmall.jpg\\\">\r\n</p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2005,725,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jack','sean sent your resume....\r\ninterested in contract work?\r\nnothing right now but usually\r\nplenty...',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2009,726,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','having a website usually helps.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nmost of us do this for ourselves.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\npersonally i am a doer.  <-- yeti made me say that.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nexcept for reading long posts.  i am no good at that.  i\r\nhave the attention span of a gnat.  i learned late in my education to stop trying.  i just glance over\r\nstuff.  if the person is someone it think is sexy or\r\nmysterious then i will probably read what they write.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ni wear off with the mystery or the sexiness.  i think the\r\nmystery came crashing down when you admitted to creating a\r\nfiction.  it was poor form, i believe.  had you just left\r\nthe post without any explanation, i would have wanted even\r\nmore to know who you are.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nas things stand, i am annoyed that you want acceptance so\r\nmuch.  i am not interested in your background.  i want to\r\nknow who you are online.  where is your website?  those are the\r\ncredentials that i look for.  even if it sucks ass, it is\r\nstill something that says to me, \"this person is down.\"\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nlet me know who the fake matt is.  the aka.  the alias.  the\r\nmachine between you and the world.  mundane boring life is\r\nwhat i am here to escape.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2010,724,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p>this is excellent, gfk, though i\\\'d like to clarify the \r\nintended nature of the question.</p>\r\n<p>while it\\\'s difficult to disagree with the assertion that \r\nno one should be assaulted with noise, i am asking \r\nabout the reverse situation. i used a sound system as \r\nan analogy, and while that may not have been the best \r\nchoice, it was what stimulated my original thought.</p>\r\n<p>how does a community incubate and spread ideas \r\nthat are considered dangerous by an existing power \r\nstructure? how do people (activists, thinkers, artists) \r\nthrive as revolutionaries within a system that continually \r\nstrives to further persecute communication? (you \r\nmentioned our waning civil liberties. assume the US \r\nconstitution does not apply.) turn around the arrow of \r\nassault to face the opposite direction.</p>\r\n<p>i find it interesting that you finger a \\\"terrorist group \r\nthat organized over the internet\\\" as your example, \r\nbecause this is precisely how the WTO protests were \r\norganized, and how they were later (and incorrectly) \r\nperceived by the general population: as terrorists. the \r\nbig media corporations (who stand to profit from world \r\ntrade) were highly effective at quelling the message of \r\nthe peaceful protesters, choosing instead to point \r\ncameras at the lunatics smashing windows. spin \r\ncontrol and \\\"poisoning the well\\\" are yet another form of \r\nidea censorship.</p>\r\n<p>what if internet grassroots organizing were \r\nuniversally equated with terrorism? could another \r\nsimilar protest successfully organize, without \r\ninterference or persecution by a government or ruling \r\nbody?</p>\r\n<p>i am asking not specifically about the WTO, but it\\\'s a \r\nrecent example of what i\\\'m talking about. i would even \r\ndraw a parallel between the organizers\\\' use of the \r\ninternet and the adoption of a new language.</p>\r\n<p>furthermore, i would argue that the mainstream \r\ncommunity is orders of magnitude more guilty than the \r\ndeviant community of crossing the line between \r\nevangelizing and imposing a belief system. examples: \r\ncorporate promotion of narcissism and obsessive \r\nconsumerism, government promotion of misleading \r\nscare tactics regarding drug use. counter example: \r\npunk rock activists yelling in your face about the \r\nenvironment.</p>\r\n<p>which method employs subtlety? which method is \r\nmaginalized? which message is sponsored by the \r\npower structure, and which is suppressed by the power \r\nstructure?</p>\r\n<p>how could a message with noble intent, but no \r\noutlet or support, promote itself within a system \r\nthreatened by change?</p>\r\n\r\n',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2007,724,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'g.f.k.','\r\n\r\n<p>I think the idea of attempting to create another \r\nlanguage specifically for \"deviants, gypsies, artists, and \r\nrevolutionary thinkers\" is counterproductive if you have \r\nany interest in the ideas of that community being heard and \r\npotentially adopted by others. What is the point of \r\npreaching to the choir? Certainly there is value in sharing \r\nideas within this community, but why does it need to be \r\ndone in a broadcast manner, and why via subterfuge?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Deviants can share their experiences and information on \r\na grassroots level, between individuals, and the language \r\ndoesnt need to obscure itself in those environments.  This \r\nprevents censorship in that it is difficult to censor \r\npersonal conversations without stepping all over the few \r\ncivil liberties US courts are still willing to defend, and \r\nit allows for information dissemination to be personal.</p> \r\n\r\n<p>Broadcasting should be about giving people what they \r\nwant, otherwise you\'re imposing upon them. The line between \r\ndeliberate (even malicious) imposition and evangelizing a \r\nbelief system is not blurry at all, but seems to be crossed \r\nby the deviant community quite often. Seeking to insult or \r\nassault those that do not share your beliefs only serves to \r\ncreate greater barriers between you. It\'s difficult for me \r\nto think of positive examples of information that benefits \r\nfrom being obscured and can only be effectively transmitted \r\nin a broadcast manner. On the other hand, a recent negative \r\nexample can be found in the media reports of terrorist \r\ngroups using steganography and the Internet to coordinate \r\nacts of terror.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I\'m not suggesting that deviants shouldnt be allowed to \r\ntake pleasure in each other and celebrate together once in \r\nawhile, but doing so in a manner that is likely to be \r\ninsulting to the public at large is disrespectful, and \r\nseems to me a deliberate attempt to further seperate from \r\nsociety. Preventing outsiders from hearing your message is \r\nelitist, and if done so in an obvious way (in public), it\'s \r\nsimply rude.</p> \r\n\r\n<p>Public expression should be public for a reason. The \r\npoint is to spread your ideas to a wide audience. Limiting \r\nyour audience with barriers to entry, especially one as \r\nextreme as language, is against the point. If you\'re \r\nlooking for a way to engage in a public circlejerk, it \r\nmight work, but it\'s no less insulting or assaultive to the \r\nnon-believers. Moreover, instead of assaulting them with \r\ninformation, you\'re assaulting them with *noise*. If you \r\nwant to marginalize the value of your expression, codifying \r\nit into a secret language is a great way to do it. Your \r\nideas would not need to be eliminated by the power-complex \r\nof goverment or society to be suppressed. They would die of \r\nself-immolation.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I would say efforts would be better spent working to \r\nexpand the audience for your message. Broadcast in every \r\nlanguage, with no bias.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Besides, this hypothetical language already exists. It\'s \r\ncalled subtlety, and it\'s a beautiful thing.</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2008,725,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','you could work in gay porn.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2011,725,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','yeti and austin and i are going to start a furniture \r\nmoving company: gaynakedmovers.com',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2012,726,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>did i just type that?  fuck.  i dont mean any of it. \r\nexcept that last part about the machine.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>hi.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>ps: are you done with the movie yet?  do you have footage online?</P>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2013,726,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sic','hey you get love from me *wee*',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2014,726,'2003-05-10 16:09:14',79,'yeti','<p>Matt,</p>\r\n<p>Take it from someone who is a \\\"senior.\\\"</p>\r\n<p>Never, ever, <b>EVER</b>, listen to people who \r\nare \\\"doers.\\\" Austin is a doer. Believe me, I know.</p>',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2015,726,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'noonespecial','i am with you matt; but for the most part this space is for \r\npeople that like to hear themselves talk. not that anything \r\nis wrong with that.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2016,725,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','<p>hey austin</p><p>i tried emailing you earlier, only it \r\ncame back to me??? Anyway, just thought i would tell you \r\nabout the duval house that has two rooms for rent at the \r\nend of june. $220 a month + plus all the fun you can \r\neat.</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2017,726,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','show me something on the internet that is not about that.\r\nshow me something in modern pop culture that is not about\r\nself promotion.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2018,726,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i know i, personally, am jealous. also i am a smart ass.\r\n',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2019,725,'2002-03-05 20:17:36',17,'austin to bmg','that is definately good to know.  if i dont find something\r\nby the end of this month, i will learn to spell assess.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nand i think my email works now.  some of it does anyway.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2020,726,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','ok a serious response. i think you have to be patient to \r\nwork your way into a community. just participate, get to \r\nknow people one on one, and wait. if you are so good and \r\nnice like you say, we\\\'ll know soon. ',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2021,726,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'s5 nods to xep','the process of journaling is about hearing yourself talk, \r\nreading your own writing. while the comment feature \r\ncan feel like a chat or a message board, this site is still \r\na journal.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nswinney.org is doubly-voyeuristic because i get to read your \r\nthoughts and you get to read what i think about \r\nthem.<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<h2><font color=\"#FF0000\">*smooch*</font></h2>',5,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2022,727,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','for the record, <b>i did NOT post this</b>.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2023,726,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','hey swinney did you think i was sexy and mysterious?',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2024,726,'2002-03-05 20:17:36',17,'austin to le','number of ellycam images in my dirs: 426',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2025,726,'2002-03-08 04:52:47',65,'le to swinney','you should meet <a href=\\\"http://christop.com\\\">shadok</a>. ',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2026,727,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p>a straight boy recently told me that he would put a cock \r\nin his mouth, because \\\"it\\\'s no different than having \r\nanything else in your mouth.\\\"\r\n</p><p>\r\nsort of related:\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\na well known san francisco dj once told me the only way to \r\ntruly know a boy is to touch his anus. \r\n</p><p>\r\ni like that boys can be penetrated too. it makes me feel \r\nbetter.\r\n</p>\r\n',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2027,727,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','it makes the boys feel better too.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2028,727,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'UnÃ¡ldur','hmmm, not that it matters, but how do i post pictures along \r\nwith my post?',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2029,726,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'swinney','does all this mean we have a fringe elite forming?  \r\n<BR><BR>\r\nwhere is darwin in all this?\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nfinally we can see some real heart felt use of the comment\r\ncategories.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2030,727,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>you post them when you submit an article.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i think the key word there is <b>submit</b>.  you should\r\nhave seen that button.  instead of following the continue\r\nlink, you click browse, then find the image in the deep dark\r\nrecesses of your hard drive\\\'s gay porn collection and post\r\nhim up.</P>\r\n\r\n',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2031,726,'2004-07-27 05:13:57',63,'olivia',' personally, i have no interest in anyone i don\\\'t already\r\nknow, unless they\\\'re a hot chick.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nhello, did i die?<br>\r\n<br>\r\nwhere are MY cam photos in swinneys dir, and le do you know\r\nhow many camshots of you I have?<br>\r\n<br>\r\nhm?<br>\r\n<br>\r\nit\\\'s all about me, isn\\\'t it.<br>',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2032,726,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','<p>i find it interesting and telling that matt doesn\'t mention\r\nthe possibility that he hasn\'t said anything well-crafted or\r\ninteresting enough to warrant a response up there. hmm.\r\n</p><p>\r\nit\'s also disturbing to meet someone who thinks that they\r\nare owed acceptance and respect. that\'s not the way things\r\nwork, online or in the real world. sorry!\r\n</p><p>\r\nfollow that old adage, \"show, don\'t tell.\" it works better than whining.\r\n</p>\r\n',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2033,727,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','hm. UI.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2034,727,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','Uranus Interface?',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2035,727,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','swinney. fucking go to bed.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2036,726,'2003-05-10 16:09:14',79,'yeti','<h1>HA HA HA HA!</h1>\r\n<h1><b>YOU = CHUMP!</b></h1>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2037,726,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','jeez weeb. harsh.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2038,727,'2004-07-27 05:14:09',63,'olivia sez',' god bless you steve, i love you.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nwhy do people freak out that they might like to do\r\nsomething.  i\\\'d like to stick my toes in a vat of warm jam. \r\nOMG!  I\\\'m a deviant!   Do what feels good.  That\\\'s all.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2039,726,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p>why can\'t we all just get along?</p>\r\n<p><img \r\nsrc=\"http://www.saturn5.com/steve/images/nice.jpg\"></p>',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2040,726,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','why was my response more harsh than anyone else\\\'s? do you\r\ndisagree with what i\\\'m saying or how i\\\'m saying it? should\r\nwe avoid being harsh to each other in order to provide a\r\nprotected area to be open with each other? i might agree\r\nwith that. but not always. this is one of those times.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2041,726,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'ULTRA VIOLENCE','KITTY EAT BUNNY',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2042,724,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>My view on this is that the mechanism of Control is \r\nsignificantly more effective at co-opting and absorbing the \r\npower of individuals than the individuals are at combatting \r\nControl. As the resources and knowledge are concentrated in \r\nthe arms of Control, the ability for individuals or small \r\ngroups to have an effective say in the decisionmaking \r\nprocess (<b><u>or even an informed say in the framing of \r\nthe decisionmaking process</b></u>) approaches zero. This \r\nis to say that Control holds all of the cards because they \r\nbrought the deck to the game.</p>\r\n<p>I read a really good book about this about four or five \r\nmonths ago. It\\\'s a historical survey of the way a corporate \r\npower exercised power in a localized area, consistently \r\ncontrolling and manipulating people against their interests \r\nand against an awareness of their actual interests.</p>\r\n<p>It seems to me that Control has always had the upper \r\nhand, but the barriers to overthrow of Control have been \r\nsmaller in pre-industrial society. For example, if you want \r\nto lead a slave revolt against a bunch of people holding \r\nyou hostage with spears and swords, it\\\'s much easier than \r\nif they have machine guns, incapacitating gas and cameras \r\neverywhere. Also, manipulation of perception is \r\nsignificantly more developed now, so you have the \r\n<u>illusion</u> of the consent of the subjugated. You \r\nconfuse people into fighting for something that doesn\\\'t \r\ndiminish Control in any way, meanwhile Control solidifies \r\ntheir hold in other ways.</p>\r\n<p>Control has no job other than being Control. Those \r\nfighting Control have other priorities as well (living, \r\nloving, eating) and therefore I think they are inevitably \r\nbound to lose.</p>\r\n<p>Not sure if this directly answers your question, but I\\\'m \r\ncurious what reading you\\\'ve done of case studies of \r\nsubjugated classes attempting to effect change, and the \r\nmechanisms of Control.</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2043,723,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sapphire','<p>I was gonna check out this posting but I got caught up \r\ncounting the hairs on my cat (it was important!)<p>',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2044,727,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>Dude, relax, it\\\'s just sex.  As long as you\\\'re a \r\nreasonable person about being safe and caring about your \r\npartner, it\\\'ll work out.</p>\r\n<p>Maybe you\\\'re bisexual?</p>\r\n<p>I\\\'m not a sex therapist, and I\\\'m pretty plain-jane \r\nhetero, so I can\\\'t say that I have the experience to \r\nperfectly understand your perspective.  So if you don\\\'t \r\nagree with what I\\\'ve said just chalk me up as a know-\r\nnothin\\\' honkey.  :-)</p>\r\n<p>(Why is it that when I feel like a worthless piece of \r\ncrap I feel better when I\\\'m trying to soothe someone else \r\nor lend them a hand?  I thought us atheist/objectivist \r\ntypes were supposed to be brave Stalinist marble people \r\ncrashing into the future without regard for difficulty or \r\nsomething....)</p>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2045,726,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>It\\\'s not really about what we have to say to YOU, it\\\'s \r\nwhat you have to say to US (or better, to YOURSELF).</p>\r\n<p>I read swinney because I like to hear the funny or \r\nwhimsical things that happen to other people much like me \r\n(sometimes angsty 20-30somethings).  I like to WRITE to \r\nswinney becuase maybe sometimes I can help somebody out \r\nwith a few words, or share something people might like out \r\nof my fucked up life, or to work something out of my head \r\nby writing it down.</p>\r\n<p>So don\\\'t get hung up.</p>\r\n<p>(I am sometimes curious how the swinney.org community \r\nwould take to me in person.  Don\\\'t know.  I\\\'ve been a \r\nfucking wreck emotionally for about two months now, so I \r\nimagine I wouldn\\\'t be the best company.  Just stress++++.  \r\nI think that austin, bmg, s5, et al. and I would get along \r\nwell knocking back a beer at the Dog and Duck or Crown and \r\nAnchor here in town, and I get the feeling some of the \r\nrabid vegans would throw things at me (I eat meat and wear \r\nleather).  And le seemed to be entirely too interested in \r\nme talking about math.  ;-) Such is life.)</p>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2046,725,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>Dude if you come back to austin and I\\\'m still here \r\n(might take a job in Houston), I\\\'ll buy you a beer at the \r\npub of your choice.  Just for being cool.</p>\r\n<p>(If you needed to move swinney.org I\\\'m sure Lynn would \r\ntry to lend a hand.  I have a p166 that is probably going \r\nto get turned into a server in the next couple of months, \r\ndon\\\'t know if that\\\'s too wimpy for this site.)</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2047,727,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'seven','<font face=tahoma>labels are just about useless - except \r\nfor abbreviating explanation - and very little even needs \r\nto be explained. <br>act . <br>do . <br>enjoy . \r\n<br><br>resist classification. <br><br> it makes us \r\nsmaller.  and we can be BIG.</font>',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2048,726,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','come visit sf!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2049,722,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>OK, here\\\'s an image of me in case anyone was curious.  \r\nIt\\\'s about two years old, but I don\\\'t look that different \r\n(OK, about an inch taller and ~80 pounds heavier (I was \r\nAuschwitz boy then, my kidneys were dead, and well, you \r\ndon\\\'t eat much when you\\\'re in that place), the main \r\nconsequence of which is out of consideration for the \r\neyesight of my fellow man I would wear a regualr tshirt \r\nunder my leather jacket instead of a mesh one)).   Oh and I \r\nhave a buzz now.  My hair sort of oscillates between \r\nshoulder length and buzzed.</p>\r\n<img src=\\\"http://ccwf.cc.utexas.edu/~orion/images/mike.jpg\\\">\r\n<p>Or see what happens when I get bored with the <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.gimp.org\\\">GIMP</a>: <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://ccwf.cc.utexas.edu/~orion/mike_closeup.html\\\">13\r\n2Kb Html Table version of closeup picture</a></p>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2050,727,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sawks','<br>\r\nso you should like, maybe try a little snowballing or \r\nsomething, see if you get into it?<br><br>\r\n',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2051,727,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','or... possibly... BUKAKKE\r\n',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2052,726,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>I\\\'d love too but I have no money.  And since the job \r\nsituation there sounds very tight, I probably wouldn\\\'t have \r\nany money there either.  And since the place is expensive \r\nto live in and I have large fixed financial obligations to \r\ndeal with anyway (like immunosuppressants; kideny \r\ntransplant receipient I am), I don\\\'t think I\\\'ll be anywhere \r\nbut here for a reasonably fixed value of here for the next \r\nyear or so.</p>\r\n<p>But I want to someday.  It\\\'s on the List.  You know the \r\none of which I speak:  \\\"when I have money/ free time/ \r\nfreedom I\\\'m going to do X, Y ... omega\\\".  :-)</p>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2053,725,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sawks','<br>\r\ni think you should devote some time to learning quark \r\nand publishing an issue of cocksmoker magazine\r\n<br>\r\ni would buy a copy',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2054,722,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','whew, for a second there i thought you had no shirt on \r\nunder that leather jacket!',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2055,726,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sawks','<br>\r\nummm yeah, its not like swinney is some sort of \r\nrampant love fest or anything - these people just live \r\nand grow together and thats how it works<br><br>\r\nyou are here, and you are saying your bit - thats \r\nplenty<br><br>\r\n',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2056,726,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i want to know more about the kidney transplant. did \r\nyou get any weird memories from the donor?',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2057,726,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','see matt? look how nice we are. we are contributing to \r\nyour post!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2058,727,'2004-07-27 05:13:57',63,'olivia','<span style=\\\"color: #006600; font-size: 20px; font-face: \r\nverdana, arial, helvetica;\\\">BAGPIPING</span>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2059,725,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Joanna','Sawks, what do you do in your spare time?  I say stop \r\npretending you\\\'re  ever going to do Isotope, and start up a \r\nCocksmoker site instead. \r\n(best friendly)\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2060,727,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','maybe you should try ... <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.mrcranky.com/movies/legendofbagger\r\nvance/12/4.html\\\">teabagging</a>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2061,727,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Joanna','What is bagpiping?  Or would it corrupt me to hear?',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2062,713,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>It seems you have three questions, and I\\\'ll attempt to \r\naddress them as best I can. Hopefully you\\\'ll revisit this \r\ntopic, otherwise this will be a lot of typing for a post \r\nnobody will read. =)</p>\r\n<ol><li>Do people join communities or do communities decide \r\nto include people?</li>\r\n<li>How are people affected by their participation in these \r\ncommunities?</li>\r\n<li>Are deviant communities significantly worse for people \r\nthan positive/mainstream ones / are they more likely to \r\naccept?</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p>\r\n<b>First</b>, I feel (as you do) that communities and \r\npeople meet each other in the middle. There are barriers to \r\nentry to any social group. The piracy scene I think is an \r\nexcellent example because the exchange is on its surface. \r\nIn the case of the mp3 scene, for example, there are four \r\nmajor classes of people. They vary in their access to the \r\nconcrete resource of the scene, which is access to sites \r\nwhich have mp3s, ISOs, DiVX and VCD movies and the credits \r\nto be used to download them.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The lowest is the leech. The leech has no resources to \r\ncontribute and therefore only drains resources. The \r\nresources consumed in this case are time and bandwidth. The \r\nleeches are the largest population of people in the mp3 \r\nscene, but they achieve the least benefit for the time and \r\neffort they expend.</p>\r\n<p>Above the leeches are the grunts of the scene. These \r\npeople are rippers (those who contribute music for \r\ndistribution) and those who run limited-resource \r\ndistribution points. The leeches leech directly from these \r\npeople, but the number of leeches are so great and the \r\nresource pool is comparatively small. These people achieve \r\na greater result, but they have to have resources to \r\ncontribute and they have to be smart enough to find entry \r\npoints which point upward in the heirarchy.</P>\r\n\r\n<p>The penultimate level in the mp3 scene are the couriers \r\nand group staff. These people have access to sites which \r\nhave a variety of things, and an economy of scarcity. For \r\nexample, a courier for a given mp3 group has access to the \r\nreleases of that group before anyone else, and also to the \r\nsites affiliated with that group. These sites get the \r\nreleases before any other sites, allowing the people who \r\nare fortunate enough to be on them the ability to send them \r\nto other places before anyone else. Because there is a \r\ncurrency (1:3 byte ratio - ie upload 1 meg and you can \r\ndownload 3), these are coveted and limited positions. The \r\nlimiting factor in this case is the amount of users the \r\nsite can accommodate. Consequently, the amount of \r\ncommitment and \\\"work\\\" on the part of these people is great, \r\nbut the rewards are immense. The primary contribution of \r\nthese people is <u>time</u>.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The highest level in the community are the siteops and \r\ngroup leadership. These people have access to specialized \r\nresources and generate immense value. For siteops, the \r\nprimary contributions are physical : bandwidth, system \r\nstability, hardware for the sites to run on. The group \r\nleadership are also frequently the people with the software \r\nand organizational know-how to run both individual groups \r\nand sites.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The reason I\\\'ve given you this breakdown is that you can \r\nsee how easily this maps to other communities. Each person \r\nhas a contribution to make, and the economy (scarcity of \r\nresources (knowledge, time, bandwidth)) shapes their role \r\nfor them. I believe that the individual decides to join the \r\ncommunity based on needs they define (in this case, \r\na \\\"need\\\" for free music and/or a need for validation), and \r\nthe community utilizes them based on the resources they are \r\nable to contribute. This explains how some people stay on \r\nthe lowest tier (outsiders in a social scene) and how \r\nothers become part of the \\\"in\\\" crowd. In this specific \r\ncommunity, much of this striation is explicitly based on \r\nconcrete contibutions.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><b>Second</b>, I think that people join deviant \r\ncommunities for about the same reason they join other \r\ncommunities. They \\\"<i>Get In Where They Fit In</i>.\\\" For \r\nme, the pirate community has appealed in two major ways. \r\nFirst, I get access to things that I want. A good example \r\nis that I can hear KRS-ONE\\\'s new album two months before it \r\ncomes out in stores, or I can watch \\\"The Sopranos\\\" on my \r\ncomputer without having to have HBO. Second, I can place \r\nmyself as a player according to defined rules of the game \r\nbeing played. If I, for example, am the #3 top uploader on \r\na given site, I know what that means in reference to my \r\npeers. This is a type of certainty that is uncommon in \r\nother circles. I believe that these are the two primary \r\nmotivating factors for most pirates. The Candy Man of THG \r\n(a pioneering PC piracy group) puts it this way :\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>\\\"Being a computer pirate is a totally insignificant, \r\nunimportant, useless thing to be, but we were the best, and \r\nbeing the best is always a rush. No matter what it is you \r\nare the best at.\\\"</b></p>\r\n\r\n<p>I don\\\'t think that the concept of deviancy is a \r\nsignificant part of the awareness of most pirates. The vast \r\nmajority of piracy is personal-use, and many pirates either \r\nhave no resources to purchase the things they \\\"steal\\\" \r\n(young teens with limited cash) or buy other things in the \r\nsame category, as a result of the trial afforded by the \r\nfree version. For example, I regularly buy music and have \r\nrepeatedly bought music that I first heard as MP3s. \r\nPirates, I think, view their social group as just another \r\nsocial group, albiet one with extraordinary benefits. Of \r\ncourse it has an effect on their perception of, for \r\nexample, the MPAA, RIAA, SPA, BSA or other industry groups. \r\nThey have an understanding of the ratio of quality product \r\nto garbage which is much greater than many other people, \r\nbecause they have greater access than most people. Most \r\nentertainment industries are built on a foundation of crap \r\nthat people wouldn\\\'t buy if they could try it first, and \r\ndigital piracy short-circuit this trap.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>This brings us to the question of whether deviant \r\ncommunities are worse for people than mainstream \r\ncommunities. I\\\'d argue that there really isn\\\'t much \r\ndifference. The barriers to entry and rules of the game are \r\ndifferent, but they still involve barriers and rules and \r\npeople. I <u>do</u> believe, however, that the specific \r\nfocus of the community has an effect on the person who \r\njoins it. For example, a depressed person who joins a \r\ncommunity of goths or junkies will have a different \r\nexperience than the same person with hippies or ravers or \r\ncapoeiristas.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The final thing that I have to say about this is that \r\nI\\\'m not sure that I understand where the lines for your \r\ncharacterization of \\\"deviant\\\" are drawn. This has lead to \r\nproblems differentiating \\\"deviant\\\" from \\\"mainstream\\\" \r\ncommunities in my analysis.. please clarify!</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2063,727,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','okay, I have dreams that I am an incompetent stripper, that \r\nI have a cock, and I desire to fuck about 10 people I know \r\npersonally, hopefully all at once.\r\n\r\nokay I said it. I feel better now!\r\n\r\nDo you guys think I am gay? Does that mean I can have sex \r\nwith Olivia and Xep and Le? Or should I get dreads first? I \r\nam CONFUSED.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2064,727,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sawks','<br>\r\nas far as i can tell, the dreads come afterwards \r\n:P<br><br>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2065,725,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sawks','<br>\r\ni have to do something cool with \r\neverybodywangchungtonight.com first\r\n<br>\r\nbut, well, ok maybe!',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2066,727,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sawks','<br><br>\r\nhands up who wants to volunteer for some pioneering \r\nexperiments in \\\'tea-piping\\\'?<br><br><br>\r\nalso \\\'bag-bagging\\\', but this is recommended for \r\nexperts only',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2067,727,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','I think porn is bad; and smoking is bad, but not the \r\nsame. why is porn bad? I think it lends children and \r\nignorant adults the wrong idea about men and women, especially gay men and women. From my experience, sex is not like a porn - much \r\nmore is going on. so yes, i think porn has corrupted \r\nyou, now go to church you heathin.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2068,726,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'seven','thoughts re: journaling/self-promotion - to say this site \r\nis a journal or a this or a that is kind of bullshit.  \r\nmaybe for you- it is changing all the time and people are \r\nusing it for various purposes. i personally find the \r\nentries that are not self-fixated/promoting to be much more \r\nfull and interesting - but i guess that is true of people \r\nas well.  there are minimal limits here on swinney - we can \r\ncontribute whatever we want - simply the fakt that bubba \r\ninstructs \\\"write in the journal\\\" doesnt make the site a \r\njournal. also i happen to know that in the very first \r\nswinney.org (which was made of balsa wood)he actually \r\noriginally wrote \\\"write on my gerbil\\\". so it\\\'s really hard \r\nto say what the hell this is. j\r\n',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2069,726,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','What kind of marker would you use to write on a gerbil?  :-)',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2070,726,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','dog and duck! crown and anchor! two of my favorite local \r\nbars!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2071,725,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','I think that the webization of science and engineering\r\njournals (by extenstion includes medical) will be a Big Deal\r\nover the next few years.  Right now full text online\r\ndatabases typically only extend about back to 1995 or so. \r\nSome of these journals have been around for almost 200\r\nyears...  All that information is still \\\"trapped\\\" in paper\r\nform.  Several journals and publishing companies have said\r\nthat in the next five years they want to get _everything_\r\nonline.\r\n\r\nAs for money in the field, consider that one subscription to\r\nElsevier\\\'s \\\"Tetrahedron Letters\\\" is about 67,000USD/year if\r\nI recall correctly.  That\\\'s for a site sub.  A personal sub\r\nis still on the order of 1000+USD/year.  Multiply that by\r\nprobably 5000 to 50000 subscribers and that\\\'s the revenue in\r\none year from one magazine where the publisher doesn\\\'t even\r\npay for the articles.\r\n\r\nSo this means lots and lots of putting things into databases\r\nand designing good query interfaces to those databases and\r\nstuff like that.  Not glamorous perhaps but it would pay the\r\nbills.  More likely I suspect would be mass-conversion to\r\nPDF (which holds diagram or equation laden papers much\r\nbetter than plain VARCHAR or TEXT fields ;-) ), followed by\r\nsummarising the papers into a search database (probably\r\nautomatically; I know you can search into a PDF but a\r\ncache\\\'d search set in a database would probably be waaaaaay\r\nfaster).',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2072,726,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','I think the dog and duck has better food but I think the\r\ncrown has better (==more selection) beer.  But I change my\r\nmind frequently.  :-)  Makes sense, I think the crown is\r\nmore of a beer bar whereas the Dog&Duck is more of a \\\"I\\\'m\r\nhungry for lunch and happen to want a Guiness too\\\" bar.\r\n\r\nMaybe we should have one of those places be the place for a\r\nswinney.org-in-austin get-together?',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2073,726,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','also? that bunny kitty picture is heartbreakingly cute.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2074,726,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>s5:  I\\\'ll post a story about it soon if you\\\'d like. \r\nNothing odd like the memories thing happened.  :-)  I\\\'m just\r\nyour average 20something renal patient.</p>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2075,727,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','HOLY SHIT! sawks! i had a dream last night that i met a \r\nwoman here that told me that she was engaged to you.<BR>\r\nand i was like. the sawks in australia? liv\\\'s friend?<BR>\r\nit was weird. i only just remembered when i saw your name.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2076,724,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<blockquote>how do people (activists, thinkers, artists)\r\n                                                    thrive\r\nas revolutionaries within a system that continually\r\n                                                    strives\r\nto further persecute communication?</blockquote>\r\n<p>Well, from the look of the grubby socialist-and-anarchist\r\nPunk \\\'zines scattered all over here, I\\\'d say cheap\r\nphotocopiers... :-)</p>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2077,727,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<blockquote>the image in the deep dark\r\n                                                    recesses\r\nof your hard drive\\\'s gay porn collection and post\r\n                                                    him\r\nup.</blockquote>\r\n<P>oh god, now the goatse.cx guy will show up here... ;-) \r\n(this is a slashdot.org in joke, and if you willingly view\r\nthat site, well, ya gots problems (I\\\'m not hyperlinking to\r\nit for a reason, if you go there you have to cut and\r\npaste))</p>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2078,728,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>What\\\'s a \\\"cama\\\"?</p>\r\n<p>Obviosuly it emits steam, but maybe it\\\'s some\r\nsteam-emitting thing I\\\'ve never heard of?</p>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2079,722,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>Nope, mesh.  And I have blue eyes, not black-hole-daemon\r\neyes (the digicam that took that shot really sucked as I\r\nrecall, contrast was all assmonkeyed).</p>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2080,729,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>I think you\\\'ll get a good job.  Soon.  What \\\"good\\\" 