 \r\njournals, tapes came back empty.\r\nbut the photos i brought home tell the story of what i saw \r\nwith out the over analytical heaviess i would have weighted \r\nit down with. without the explaining it all away.\r\n before i left on the trip i started a site at diaryland: \r\nrunawaygirl.diaryland.com and never visited it once while on \r\nthe road. \r\nyay traveling. kat, you will have wonderful stories to tell, \r\nthat will come back to you in the best and most suprising \r\nways.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2120,736,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','heh. I wish. I guess I can dream about having balls tho. :)',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2121,736,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sawks','<br>\r\nyou see the problem with enormous balls is that they \r\nwell - chafe and stuff<br><br><br>\r\n\r\nummm yeah,<br>\r\nas someone who could of written that entry myself \r\nabout 5 years ago, i think you are more than strong \r\nenough to handle, keep your head up girl\r\n',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2122,736,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>i have been wondering where you went.  watching your idle\r\ncorpse on icb, where is sine?</p>\r\n\r\n<P>i was not moving yesterday because the job i want took\r\nthe listing off of craigslist.org and i could not find where\r\n i copied it to.  i think i overwrote the existing file.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>on the phone yesterday my mom told me that she thinks i \r\nwill be back in texas before too long.  that is what she is\r\ntelling my dad.  defeated and unable to get a job in\r\ncalifornia.  she is right to some degree.  i do think about\r\nit.  but i want to stay here until i feel like leaving. \r\ntoday i am going to contact several temp agencies and work\r\nnights opening those atm envelopes that are used to hold\r\ncheck deposits.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>what sucks most about this not having a job shit is i\r\ncannot write.  writing is i suppose an escape from myself. \r\nbeing jobless means there is no escape for me.  i cannot go\r\nto work.  i cannot be at work, or leave work.  my time is\r\nnot valuable.  seconds are sand.  so are minutes, hours,\r\ndays.  weeks.  it is all scratching through the hour glass\r\ncreating a grinding noise that i never escape.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>atm envelopes are better than going back to texas.</P>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2123,735,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sawks','<br>\r\nwhat are the other kinds of masturbation? :)',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2124,739,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'vega','<p>\r\nnote to self:\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nbuild a web application to display this idea.\r\n</p>',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2125,739,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','six degrees of vega',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2126,735,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','mutual\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2127,735,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','pleasuring pets or livestock\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2128,735,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','<P>swinney.org</P><P>(ho.ho. did i say that? bad \r\nmattie.)</P>\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2129,736,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','i used to take six different meds per day. horrible side \r\neffects. they eliminated the symptoms of my illness but \r\ndidn\\\'t really make me better. kind of placed me in a holding \r\npattern. things didn\\\'t improve for me until i started going \r\nto a traditional chinese medicine practitioner. i was \r\neventually able to wean myself off the pills. it made me \r\nstronger, too, more able to deal with the things that i \r\nthought were making me so miserable. you can\\\'t change the \r\nthings that have happened to you, but you can change who you \r\nare today.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2130,738,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','i want a glitter dildo.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2131,735,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','*snerk*',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2132,737,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','that sounds really delicious, yo. i\\\'m not usually for \r\nfruity but i love peach schnapps.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2133,736,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','so. not to be rude but i find this repetitive alignment of \r\ntexas and dread really annoying. hi. i live here in austin. \r\ni like it here. love it, actually, have a hard time \r\nimagining myself happier somewhere else. and ending phrases \r\nwith \\\"better than going back to texas\\\" is pretty insulting \r\nto those of us who\\\'re here voluntarily and quite \r\nhappily.<BR>\r\ni understand that you view this as a place where you grew \r\nup and have left behind in an attempt to move on so what \r\nyou\\\'re really trying to convey is that you see moving back \r\nas a <b>step back</b> in your personal growth, maybe even a \r\nsignpost of failure -- although you shouldn\\\'t because \r\nlayoffs are indiscrimant and everyone is going through \r\nthis -- but yet again. having to read over and over about \r\nhow moving to austin is like the worst thing you can \r\nimagine is. not what i\\\'d like to be reading. i can\\\'t speak \r\nfor anyone else.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2134,736,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','jo, i completely understand.  i feel the same way about\r\nsanta cruz.  everytime i think about going back to live\r\nthere i feel like i\\\'ve failed the attempt to live in the\r\n\\\"real world\\\".  on the other hand, santa cruz is one of the\r\nmost amazing places in the world and it\\\'s easy to see this,\r\neven from a skewed perspective.  \r\n<p>\r\nafter being in melbourne for a month i was suprised when i\r\ncame back and remembered that everyone loves to hate san\r\nfrancisco.  i never heard anyone complaining about where\r\nthey lived while in australia.  it\\\'s frustrating to hear\r\npeople say horrible things about a place you love but it\\\'s\r\nimportant to remember that it\\\'s just their opinion.  it\\\'s\r\nnot a personal diss to you.  you should be proud that you\r\nlove where you live. i bet most people wish they were.\r\n</P>\r\n<p>\r\n<p>\r\nhey sine, want to go for a motorcycle ride?\r\n',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2135,736,'2002-03-05 20:17:36',17,'austin to jo','replace all appearances of AUSTIN with [x hometown].  i know\r\ni can go back there because i know what i can do there.  i\r\ncan get a job at the school for the blind, or some coffee\r\nshop, etc.  i can do the same thing here in san francisco. \r\nfor me the goal is to ...\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nbut you do not care about that. fuckit, neither do i.  i am\r\nwith xep on her view of her home town.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ni know that there are very few opportunities for what i want\r\nto do in Austin, TX.  that is why i left.  that is why i do\r\nnot want to go back.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ni like it there just fine.  all my friends from college\r\nleft.  i missed them.  i got bored.  i left.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ni miss the breakfast tacos.  i miss being hot as fuck in the\r\nsummer.  i miss hot sweaty sex in rooms with no air\r\nconditioning.  i miss all my exes that live in texas.  i\r\nmiss going to magnolias at 6 am with bmg before work.  i\r\nmiss living in the same city as kdog and not seeing her very\r\noften.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ni do not miss the university.  i had a really rough time\r\nthere.  i did not graduate.  as long as i stayed in austin i\r\nfelt like a failure, \\\"you can always go back and finish your\r\ndegree.\\\"  yea, whatever.  mabye i will.  \r\n<BR><BR>\r\nand yes, i may make my way to the duval house in the summer.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nanyway, i see your grief and raise you my own.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2136,738,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'dj1_luna','reminded me of Jeanette Winterson\\\'s Gut Symmetries for a \r\nminute.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2137,738,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','oooh i loved gut symmetries.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2138,740,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','There are all kinds of ways a place like this can be\r\nboogered with.  Mainly since the community is fairly closely\r\nknit, the best security is people not being assholes to\r\nother people they know.\r\n\r\nHere\\\'s a short list of things to filter:\r\n<ul><li>IMG tags.  bummer, eh?  imagine somebody posting\r\nporno though, really vile stuff</li>\r\n<li>JavaScript</li>\r\n<li>Sounds.  Plugins.</li>\r\n<li>Unbalanced list tags and stuff like that.</li>\r\n<li>preformatted text (imagine someone posting 100 pages\r\nworth of carriage returns in between two PRE tags...)</li>\r\n<li>etc. etc.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nso secure, safe, paranoid site == boring site.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2139,740,'2002-03-05 20:17:36',17,'austin to orion','when are you going to do the preview thing for the comments?',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2140,735,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'s5 to erin','\\\"explaining it all away\\\" is just the right phrase.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2141,740,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','*constructs gant chart*',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2142,735,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'chaya','yes. precisely. i went to paris to \\\"figure it all out,\\\" \r\narmed with elly\\\'s tape recorder and steve\\\'s camera and my \r\njournals and sketchbooks and i wrote exactly one page. i \r\nstill haven\\\'t gone through my photos, because i don\\\'t want \r\nto explain them to myself just yet. i have found i\\\'m more \r\nfond of digging through the memories in my head than \r\nanything else. ',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2143,740,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','Uhmmm.... when I get cvs directions?  ;-)\r\nit\\\'d have to wait till saturday anyway.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2144,740,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','I\\\'m not real familar with CVS, just a tiny little bit but \r\nI\\\'ll read up on it.  Mainly I don\\\'t know what server root or \r\nwhatever it was called to use.  is it atari?  ',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2145,740,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','\\\"I, Austin\\\" would be an excellent title for austin\\\'s first\r\nnovel. i want the first three chapters faxed to me by monday.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2146,739,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','I read that as \\\"... need to build a weeb application to \r\nillustrate this\\\".  :-)  Rube Goldbergian construction \r\ninvolving a computer, a web server, Weeb, and somthing else \r\nlike a turn table and yellow food.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2147,736,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>UT is a harsh bitch of a nipple-twisting taskmistress, \r\nthat\\\'s sho\\\' \\\'nuff.  It\\\'s like this endurance test.  \r\ndon\\\'t feel bad if you decided life was better spent \r\nelsewhere.  People who only focus on credentials are \r\nstupid and wrong.  Like gouda wheel hunting said: \\\"The \r\neducation you spent 150,000 on could have been had for a \r\ndollar fifty in late fees from the public library.\\\"</p>\r\n<p>Drive for knowledge and thirst for learning, much like \r\ninnate talent or intelligence, are honed not a whit by some \r\ntenured turd blathering about topic X.</p>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2148,736,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','Oh and if you do decide post secondary education is \r\nsomething to do, nothing says you have to go back to the \r\nsame field if you got bored with it.  And if you want to do \r\nhands-on IT stuff, ACC has some suprisingly cool courses \r\nnow. (www.austin.cc.tx.us IIRC, but their web site sucks).\r\nAnd true the dot-com arena is pretty depopulated now, but i \r\nfeel that\\\'ll rebound in the next year as the fiscal market \r\nimproves.  ',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2149,736,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','To sine:  I came from sort of the same circumstances, but of \r\ncourse only you know how you feel in your heart and head.  \r\nA friend once told me that \\\'hey, every midnight has a \r\nsunrise.\\\'  Sometimes when i am feeling really strung out I \r\nimagine myself sitting on a grassy hill watching that sun \r\nrise, peeking through the clouds, feeling my skin warm up as  \r\nit\\\'s rays sink into me.  That warmth, serenity, and \r\nhappiness is what I hope you find soon.  I hope that doesn\\\'t \r\nsound cheesy.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2150,742,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','running around the table is pretty annoying.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2151,742,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>we have mac users on this site, M\\\'Kay?</P>\r\n<P>s5 gets testy when people talk about his mac problem. \r\nlike s5 always says with regards to his mac use, \\\"geeks can\r\nbe emotional too.\\\"</P>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2152,742,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'chaya','<p>item one, a quote from chicks on speed: \\\"i like mac \r\npowerbooks and electronic music.\\\"</p>\r\n<p>item two: try using lower heat with the olive oil.  it \r\ndoesn\\\'t need to be very hot to do nice things to your \r\nfood.</p>',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2153,742,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','haha. orion: canola oil. splatter-guards improvised out of\r\npot lids. food #1\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2154,352,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','i tried to find your email. i could not. ',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2155,742,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','the macintosh is a computer for the artist: irrational and \r\ndisfunctional. requires frequent rebooting. overheating \r\nis a problem. i have three in regular use.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2156,740,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','atari.saturn5.com is the hostname. you should be able \r\nto use pserver locally. i don\\\'t know where austin has the \r\ncvsroot, though, he should be able to answer that for \r\nyou.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2157,744,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','premenstrual. emotional. everything is a Big Deal. \r\neverything seems worth crying over. but i never cry. just \r\nsort of walk around gritting teeth, kicking things.<BR>\r\nsmall favors: EFAs, water, tea, gorgeous weather.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2158,744,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'chaya','*pet*',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2159,744,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','it is raining in san francisco. a single phone call today \r\ndashed hopes and plans. later, i will listen to low on \r\nstage, and they will understand.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2160,742,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>\r\nI think my dislike of Macs stems mainly from the fact my \r\nhands weren\\\'t built to interact with them.  I <em>hurt</em> \r\nafter using one for more than about half an hour.  And of \r\ncourse the damn things are like mushrooms sprining up all \r\nover campus. :-/  if they had keyboards and mice designed \r\nfor normal human beings it might not be so bad...\r\n</p>\r\n<p>So yeah, Macs annoy the piss out of me.  But I\\\'m sure my \r\nmachine would drive a Mac user to distraction too (X11 is \r\nfor holding lots of terminal windows ;-))</p>\r\n<p>Eh, to each their own.</p>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2161,742,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','or I guess I should say the stereotypical, CLI-phobic Mac \r\nuser.  I actually like BeOS quite a lot, which feels a lot \r\nlike MacOS to me, so I think it really is a hands-not-happy-\r\nwith-new-macs thing.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2162,740,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<img src=\"http://www.geocities.com/Hollywood/Hills/6357/Cornmov.JPG\">\r\n<p>heh</p>',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2163,740,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>Man, that sucks.  looks like geocities doesn\\\'t like \r\npeople just linking to their pages.  :-/  Here\\\'s the funny \r\nCornholio link:  \r\nhttp://www.geocities.com/Hollywood/Hills/6357/Cornmov.JPG</p\r\n>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2164,740,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','oh well, I guess their server was just being flaky',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2165,739,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Joanna','The Internet is too small and too incestuous.  Sometimes I \r\nthink about taking down my links page, because I want to \r\nkeep treasures that I find (like swinney) to myself, but I \r\nalso want to share.  Trouble with sharing with the good is \r\nthat the bad come too.  Sometimes I wish that the Internet \r\nwas my own small private passworded Intranet.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2166,737,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Joanna','Peach Schnapps and orange juice is called a Fuzzy Navel, \r\nwhich would make it cool no matter what it tasted like.  \r\nI\\\'m happy cos my job gives me a card for a wholesalers \r\nwhich carries many many many flavours of schnapps, and so I \r\nwill be Happy Cocktail Girl.  ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2167,738,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Joanna','I love Jeanette Winterson, but I find I can only read her \r\nbooks once because they are too powerful.  ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2168,740,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sawks','<br><br>\r\nactually its kinda hard to block javascript if you allow \r\nimages because shit like &lt;img onload=\\\"window.close()\\\" \r\nsrc=\\\"something.jpg\\\"&gt; this works\r\n<br><br>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2169,742,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','the new keyboards were designed for human torture. \r\nthe apple extended keyboard from the days of yore, \r\nhowever, is god\\\'s keyboard. ask for it by name.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2170,739,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','i never tell anyone about swinney.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2171,741,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p>as usual, black sabbath says it first:</p>\r\n<pre><tt>\r\n<u>paranoid</u>\r\n\r\nfinished with my woman\r\ncause she couldn\'t help me \r\nwith my mind\r\npeople think i\'m insane\r\nbecause i am frowning\r\nall the time\r\nall day long i think of things\r\nbut nothing seems to satisfy\r\nthink i\'ll lose my mind\r\nif i don\'t find something to pacify\r\n\r\ncan you help me \r\noccupy my brain?\r\noh yeah\r\n\r\ni need someone to show me\r\nthe things in life that i can\'t find\r\ni can\'t see the things \r\nthat make true happiness,\r\ni must be blind\r\n\r\nmake a joke and i will sigh\r\nand you will laugh\r\nand i will cry\r\nhappiness i cannot feel\r\nand love to me is so unreal\r\n\r\nand so as you hear these words\r\ntelling you now of my state\r\ni tell you to enjoy life\r\ni wish i could but it\'s too late                    \r\n</tt></pre>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2172,742,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sawks','<br><br>\r\nso ummm, i have a mac that runs unix<br>\r\ni guess that makes me the geek equivalent of a chick having \r\nthe big penis dream<br><br>\r\n',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2173,744,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'later','<pre><tt>\r\n&lt;s5&gt; low was really pretty. my only regret was that\r\n&lt;s5&gt; other people were there\r\n&lt;s5&gt; i wanted to be alone with them and the great \r\n&lt;s5&gt; big music hall.\r\n&lt;s5&gt; instead i closed my eyes and imagined it\r\n</tt></pre>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2174,740,'2004-07-27 05:14:09',63,'olivia sez',' i spent a lot of time thinking about how i would skin \r\nswinney had i the chance, and realised that i love it the \r\nway it is.  i hate stripping peoples tags, it\\\'s like metal \r\ndetectors at the airport.  let\\\'s all just be friends, and \r\nnot try and hack swinney.  ok?',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2175,740,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','ok olivia, now i love you back.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2176,739,'2004-07-27 05:13:57',63,'olivia','i get mad when people i know other than the ones which \r\ndirectly slot into the sf type scene post.  i don\\\'t know \r\nwhy.  it\\\'s not because i hate you.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2177,736,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','XEP : YES',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2178,742,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','Sawks: Wanna fuck?',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2179,740,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','I could get most of the javascript of course by zapping\r\nanything in between SCRIPT tags (s/blahblah//g).  The onload\r\nthing may be more of a pain in the ass to write a regexp\r\nfor, but the theory would be the same (and it would leave\r\nthe rest of the IMG tag alone).  I agree with Olivia, but I\r\nalso imagine that if one thing were to be stripped,\r\njavascript would be it.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2180,745,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','mmm, cages.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2181,739,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kini','hmm...',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2182,747,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'j s','it seems normal to me and what i aspire to actually.  i \r\nthink detachment of sorts sets us free.  acceptance of \r\ndeath as a normal and inevitable future seems to be a very \r\npractical way of living . and i dont feel any mysticism \r\nabout it - just a simple fact.  but that simple premise \r\nthat no of us survives - maybe lets us live more full.  it \r\nis something i am trying to let color my day - a good \r\nfriend of ours was hit by a train in front of us a few \r\nmonths ago -the immediacy/absurdity/senselessness of it \r\nstill rides on my shoulder. not as something that causes \r\npain in my heart - but that you never know - maybe today is \r\nour last day',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2183,742,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sawks','<br>\r\nwell sure :)<br><br>\r\nbut there will be some lube involved, if you intend to \r\nbring the two fisted ruckus!<br><br>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2184,739,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sawks','<br>\r\nolivia is deadly serious about this - she told me that if i \r\never posted a swinney journal entry she would \r\nmomentarily forgoe veganism just to bite off my nuts<\r\nbr><br>\r\nso thats cool - i\\\'m a \\\'comment below\\\' kinda guy \r\nanyway<br><br>\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2185,739,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sawks','<br>\r\nwho cant type :)',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2186,746,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','god, peter, it\\\'s a good thing you\\\'re around to teach us \r\nabout these things.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2187,747,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','in buddhism, there are specific meditations on death. one \r\nsuch meditation takes you step by step, until you are \r\nimagining your present breath is your very last, thus \r\nshowing us how close we really are to death.\r\n\r\nIt\\\'s really comforting, actually. ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2188,747,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','<a href=\\\"http://www.buddhist-\r\nastrology.com/deathimper.html\\\">here is a link talking about \r\nthe meditation.</a>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2189,742,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'adamajahbot','adam artist.  they give adam pc.  they say \\\"make art.\\\"  \r\nadam make art.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2190,750,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'pdo','One time on Bank St. a homeless man screamed at me: \\\"Fine! \r\nIgnore me like all the other Neo-Conservatives!\\\"  Another \r\ntime on Bank St. I peed on a ATM.  Neo-Conservative *this*, \r\nbucko.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2191,742,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'vega','i find cliques to be very annoying.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2192,749,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i recommend that limes are the ingredient for the next \r\niron vegan contest.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2193,745,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','more <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://lyrics.lipetsk.ru/search.php3?song_id=1356\r\n4\\\">lyrics</a>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2194,750,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','<p>so what was the difference between you peeing in the\r\nbushes and that guy peeing in a garbage can again? i missed\r\nthat...\r\n</p><p>\r\non another note, i was walking along this morning, when the\r\nseemingly sober man in front of me turned to his right, and\r\nlet loose with a pillar of vomit. very professional. didn\'t\r\nhit any of him, he just aimed it towards the side of a\r\nbuilding, walked another 10 feet, orked another (albeit\r\nsmaller) deposit, and continued to do this at regular\r\nintervals. he looked totally sober, otherwise. \r\n</p><p>i crossed the\r\nstreet at this juncture. bad cabezos, hombre? or a long\r\nnight out on the town that hasn\'t ended?\r\n</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2195,754,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','yo momma so greasy, she use bacon as bandaids.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2196,754,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'iiieee','Your teeth are so yellow, your tongue sings \\\"I got sunshine\\\"',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2197,754,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','if you\\\'re good, i tell you about the time i tried to outsing\r\ndeafening boombox on the 14X at 7am in the morning. or when\r\ni outscreamed a baby on BART. teehee.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2198,751,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i find that when i am going through some major relational \r\ncrisis, i shut down towards the person in question. i \r\nbecome numb to them, their tears, hate mail, loving \r\ngestures. i think it\\\'s a coping mechanism.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2199,751,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','it\\\'s understandable if the psyche shuts down if it feels\r\nunder attack. fight or flight takes over, and all you want\r\nto do is flee. severe stress or depression makes me feel\r\nthis way.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2200,750,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','the first time i met olivia, she spent the day puking \r\nsuccinctly and gracefully. once over a gaurd rail, after \r\nasking an understanding cabbie to pull over. a few times \r\ninto various gutters around a jewish neighborhood in \r\nmelbourne. she would calmy squat and vomit pink and wet \r\nbehind cars, onto the concrete. too much of something the \r\nnight before. but, i was very impressed with the style that \r\nshe exhibited during the puke sessions. i found her to be a \r\npuking badass.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2201,754,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','I know what you mean about annoying public transport. \r\nRiding the number 1 North Lamar route here in Austin can be\r\nan experience...  I think the State Mental Hospital is\r\nserviced by this route (among others).  So lots and lots of\r\npeople are riding it that would have been institutionalized\r\nin the days of yore (i.e. people that are \\\"functional\\\" but\r\nquite insane in the literal sense).  So during the day the\r\nbus is crammed shoulder to shoulder with a mix of college\r\nstudents (the silent majority) and three or four people\r\nsinging to themselves, compusively adding 3 and 5 out loud,\r\nmumbling/shouting curse words, scratching at themselves,\r\ngrunting, wheezing, talking about the CIA sending mind\r\ncontrol waves at them (\\\"that\\\'s why I have this plastic bag\r\non my head\\\") or generally being loopy.  Well, maybe it\\\'s not\r\nthat bad all the time but damn if I don\\\'t seem to have the\r\n\\\"luck\\\" to always catch a bus when it\\\'s like that.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2202,740,'2003-05-10 16:09:14',79,'yeti','But javascript is run on the client machine, not the web \r\nserver. Let people fend for themselves and their browsers, \r\nI say! :)\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2203,754,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','oh god the number one. it\\\'s what a lot of my coworkers take \r\nto get to and from work and they all have great stories.<BR>\r\nbut also: \\\"<a href=\\\"http://pondgoddess.diaryland.com\\\">my \r\nmomma</a> is a selfless beacon of devotion and strength, \r\ndawg.\\\"',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2204,742,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','not everyone is supposed to use a mac. a mac is stylish. its \r\nunique to certain needs. they are flashy. they are filled \r\nwith mac goodness. they think of things others dont. they \r\nare like the companies that make pants ravers wear. ',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2205,738,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','why read a book more than once, when there are so many still \r\nunread?',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2206,740,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','no pserver on atari. sorry.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2207,744,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','people should go away when you don\\\'t want them there.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2208,749,'2003-05-10 16:09:14',79,'yeti','<p>A thing people have asked me about before:</p>\r\n<P><FONT FACE=\\\"trebuchet ms, arial, sans-serif\\\"  SIZE=\\\"+2\\\" \r\nCOLOR=\\\"#993333\\\">\r\nGreat Key Lime Pie\r\n</FONT><P>\r\n\r\n<font face=\\\"verdana, arial, helvetica\\\" size=\\\"+1\\\" \r\ncolor=\\\"#993333\\\">Ingredients:</font>\r\n<UL>\r\n<LI> 1 pkg Mori-Nu silken firm tofu\r\n<LI> 8 oz soy cream cheese\r\n<LI> 1/2 cup key lime juice (I use Floribbean brand)\r\n<LI> 2 tsp grated lime rind\r\n<LI> 2 pkgs Mori-Nu Mates vanilla pudding mix\r\n<LI> 1 Tbsp liquid sweetener (to taste)\r\n<LI> 1 prepared 9\\\" or so pastry or graham pie crust\r\n</UL>\r\n\r\n<font face=\\\"verdana, arial, helvetica\\\" size=\\\"+1\\\" \r\ncolor=\\\"#993333\\\">Directions:</FONT>\r\n<P>\r\nDrain any excess water from the tofu.  Blend tofu and lime \r\njuice in a processor (may be too stiff for your blender) \r\nuntil creamy and smooth.  Add the rest of the ingredients, \r\nexcept crust (!), and blend again until smooth.  Pour the \r\nmixture into the crust and chill 2-3 hours or until firm.\r\n<P>\r\nSets up very firm.  Makes a great pudding or little tartlet \r\nfilling for fancy desserts.\r\n<P>\r\nServes: 6-8\r\n<P>\r\nPreparation time: 20 min\r\n<P>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2209,749,'2003-05-10 16:09:14',79,'yeti','<p>And!</p>\r\n<pre>\r\n\r\n          Watermelon Granita\\\' Filled Lime Cups\r\n\r\n Amount  Measure       Ingredient -- Preparation Method\r\n-------  ------------  --------------------------------\r\n  12                    limes -- reserve 2 tbs juice\r\n   1      cup           sugar\r\n   2      cups          water\r\n   4      cups          watermelon cubes\r\n   1/2    cup           currants -- or raisins\r\n                        crushed ice -- optional\r\n\r\nTo make lime cups:\r\n\r\nCut limes in half lengthwise; cut around pulp of each half \r\nwith sharp knife, leaving peel intact. Scoop out pulp, \r\nusing spoon to loosen pulp from peel, and reserve 2 tbs \r\nlime juice for granita. Set lime cups aside. Stir together \r\nsugar and water in small saucepan; heat to boiling. Cool \r\nslightly. Place watermelon in container of food processor; \r\npulse to puree watermelon. Place colander over bowl; pour \r\npureed watermelon into colander to strain out seeds, \r\nforcing watermelon through with back of spoon, if \r\nneeded. Stir reserved lime juice and cooled sugar mixture \r\ninto pureed watermelon. Pour into 13 x 9 x 2 pan; freeze \r\nuntil firm, about four hours.\r\n\r\nTo serve scrape watermelon mixture with spoon to make \r\ngranita. Stir in currants for seeds. Mound granita in lime \r\ncups; serve on bed of crushed ice.\r\n</pre>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2210,749,'2003-05-10 16:09:14',79,'yeti','<p><b>Asparagusto Soup</b></p>\r\n<p>A nutritious, delicious no-cook soup.</p>\r\n<p>Makes 2-4 servings</p>\r\n<p>10-12 medium stalks asparagus<br>\r\n6-8 large red tomatoes<br>\r\n4-8 fresh basil leaves<br>\r\n1 cup fresh parsley<br>\r\n4 dried tomatoes<br>\r\n2 limes, cut into slices<br>\r\n4-6 large yellow tomatoes</p>\r\n<p>Trim the tips from the asparagus and set aside for \r\ngarnish. In a blender,\r\nprocess 5 of the red tomatoes with the remaining asparagus, \r\nthe basil, parsley,\r\nand dried tomatoes. Place slices of lime on the bottom of \r\nthe soup bowls, and\r\npour the asparagus mixture over.</p>\r\n<p>In a blender, puree the 3 yellow tomatoes, and pour the \r\npuree around the\r\nouter edge of the soup. Garnish with more lime slices, the \r\nremaining red tomato\r\ncut into slices, the asparagus tips, and additional basil \r\nand parsley, if\r\ndesired. Chill or serve at room temperature.</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2211,756,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p>that is a cutely dorky picture of dar.</p>\r\n<p>i fart in yoga sometimes. more than that i queef in \r\nbridge pose. afterwards i say \\\"heh, queef.\\\" sometimes \r\npeople in class don\\\'t like to know. one time my old yoga \r\nteacher queefed really loud and said \\\"that didn\\\'t come from \r\nmy butt!\\\"</p>\r\n<p>i think being in yoga class taught me not to worry so \r\nmuch about what my body does, not to be embarassed. it\\\'s \r\nall the same.</p>\r\n<p>i am listening to the new califone album. it is very \r\nvery good.</p>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2212,754,'2004-07-27 05:14:09',63,'olivia sez',' i was telling xep about all the trouble i used to get into \r\ndefending people and myself in this sort of situation.  \r\nusually it was when girls were getting sexist remarks aimed \r\nat them.  so yeah.  rock on weeb. i love that feeling of \r\nbeing so angry you say something, but feeling really \r\nnervous for saying something at all :)',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2213,751,'2004-07-27 05:14:09',63,'olivia sez',' i had that problem with my ex lover.  the more hysterical \r\nor pleading he got, the more distanced i became.  it\\\'s a \r\npretty awful circle to get into.  i know of no solution, \r\napart from a long time apart.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2214,744,'2004-07-27 05:14:09',63,'olivia sez',' when i\\\'m on the rag, especially for the first day, i smell \r\nlike raw meat.  it\\\'s RAD.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2215,751,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i frequently experience numbness during times of \r\nintense stress, relationship or not. i don\\\'t think of it as \r\ncoping per se, more of a way to gain objectivity about \r\nmyself and what i\\\'m experiencing. detachment (or \r\nnumbness) can be a tool, if used properly and \r\nsparingly.<br>\r\n<br>\r\ni have also been known to program my emotions like \r\nthe timer on a microwave. \\\"okay, i\\\'m going to pissed off \r\nuntil wednesday, then withdrawn until the middle of next \r\nweek.\\\"',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2216,750,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','when chaya and i were dating, she began our \r\nrelationship by puking on the doorstep of my most \r\nrecent ex-girlfriend at the time, and immediately \r\nemailed me from her pager to describe what she did. \r\nneedless to say, this impressed me.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2217,756,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>i feel as though paul bunion split the bones in my fore\r\narms like two by fours.  *snap*</P>\r\n<P>the last hour of bed was me writhing in pain.  unable to\r\ngrasp what the problem was in my three quarter sleep state,\r\ni tried to just sit and endure.  maybe i would fall back to\r\nsleep.  then i realized ten minutes ago that this fall back\r\nto sleep scenario was not going to happen.  i decided to get\r\nup.  i lay under the warm sheets hurting, not wanting to\r\nmove out into the cold morning.  i thought i may be assisted\r\nby some breakfast.  elly is most likely still awake.  i can\r\nwhine to her.  i am in pain.</P>\r\n<P>i got up and went into the command center. yoko is\r\nlooking like a sleeping bunny rabit in the plushy chair.  i\r\nplug the light in.  i walk to the kitchen and turn the light\r\non, open the fridge and stare at the rice milk container. \r\nsomething that goes with that please.  i set oatmeal on the\r\nstove.\r\n</P>\r\n<P>\r\nback in the command center i message le:\r\n\r\n<PRE>\r\n!*austin*> OUCH\r\n!*le*> ?\r\n!*le*> 6am is too early\r\n!*le*> go back to bed\r\n!*austin*> i cannot sleep.  i have been writhing in bed for\r\nthe last hour\r\n!*austin*> the pain is unbearable\r\n!*austin*> my arms feel like they have splintered\r\n!*le*> from capoeira?\r\n!*le*> hmmm. hot bath?\r\n!*le*> advil?\r\n!*austin*> i think both are in order\r\n!*austin*> i really hurt le\r\n!*le*> i agree\r\n!*le*> aww swinney :(\r\n!*le*> if i were there i would reiki you\r\n!*le*> but i am far and in bed naked\r\n!*le*> you can come have hot tub if ou want!\r\n!*le*> ok sleep for le now\r\n!*austin*> nite\r\n</PRE>\r\n<P>now i am all alone.  yoko got up and left.  i am finished\r\neating oatmeal.  i have eaten two advil from the yeti\'s\r\nsupply.  if he has a head ache tomorrow, i will go to the\r\nstore and buy him some more.</P>\r\n<P>at some point today or tomorrow i have to go to LA for a\r\nwedding and to see k*</P>\r\n<P>wedding, no problem.  k*, nervous and scared.</P>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2218,749,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','holy smokes, peter! you are the lime king.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2219,757,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','i like you.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2220,749,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','hi.  i like limes.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2221,756,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','that pain is so familiar.  you would think after a year and\r\na half of doing strange muscular things every day it would\r\nstop hurting.  last night i could barely walk.  in\r\naustralia, i remember saying to elly \\\"my, god, no part of me\r\nhurts right now.  this is weird.\\\"\r\n<br><br>\r\nbut i love that pain.  i would be pretty sad if it went\r\naway.  it feels like progress to me.\r\n',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2222,756,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','<p>\nokay. so my \\\'me too\\\' story: i got major asskicking from \ndoing bikram yoga today. all you masochists out there take \nnote: IT\\\'S FUCKING INSANE. 5/6ths the way through my first \nclass (i only had like 5 more postures to do!!) i got \nreally dizzy and pretty much almost fainted. i layed there \npanting til the little pink elephants went away. i found \nout that my problem was dehydration. 1334 polk street if \nany of you want to come with tomorrow...\n</p>\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2223,749,'2003-05-10 16:09:14',79,'yeti','<p>I like the limes. They seem worth the work to find ways \r\nto use them in cooking. I really want to make that soup. \r\nWill you eat the soup with me?</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2224,749,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','yes!<BR>\r\num. that is, assuming this question is directed at me in \r\nlight of my imminent sf trip.<BR>\r\ni love lime! i make chicken quesadillas sometimes and the \r\nchicken is marinated in freshly squeezed lime juice for 2 \r\nhours before cooking.<BR>\r\nlime, like cilantro and garlic, is always doubled in \r\namounts in my recipes.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2225,742,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'orisha','The crimp in the office vibes when your boss is \r\nprobing his nose and examining the findings when he \r\nrealizes three employees are watching with morbid \r\ncuriousity and he gets uptight....other office personnel \r\nwho fart like they are laying an egg and then sit on it \r\nlike its going to hatch into something special--which it \r\ndoes if they get out of their chairs.....discovering that \r\nyour cats have been using one of your laundry baskets full \r\nof clothes as a litterbox...discovering that roaches like \r\nto eat the glue in books and bindings....people that \r\nconstantly follow everything they say with the phrase \"you \r\nknow what I\'m sayin\'\"...people that use kewl as a variant \r\nspelling of cool, kinda akin to kute for cute, etc...men \r\nwho are obsessed with the size of their penis..men and \r\nwomen who are obsessed with having a flat abdomen...the i-\r\ndotters and t-crossers of bureaucracy, Mrs. Grundy and her \r\nfreaking \"RULES\",compulsive liars who wont even attempt an \r\nhonest work of fiction, men who don\'t give good backrubs or \r\nfootrubs but always expect it from you, indecisive people \r\nin traffic, chronic masturbators who try and convince you  \r\nthat it\'s cool and that they\'re wonderful and it\'s \r\nneither,these are just a few of my unfavorite \r\nthings....shall I go on?',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2226,757,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'orisha','I like you also.  Are you available for further \r\nexchange of thoughts? Post more and more often.  I love the \r\ntruth told in poetry and showing up brightly in the spoken \r\nand written word...',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2227,749,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','i would like to eat that soup, too.  i like limes and i like\r\nasparagus.  i like asparagus pee.  also i have a new theory\r\nabout asparagus and bending muscles.  time to eat a lot of\r\nasparagus.\r\n',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2228,730,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'orisha','How about operatic cussing?  Pretend you are \r\ndoing a passage of opera (pick something florid and \r\nhysterical and German, maybe) and string descriptive nasty \r\nphrases together.its good to do when you are driving with \r\nthe windows rolled up--or down, depending on how much you \r\nwant to sonically harass others...there is also the Cuss \r\nHaiku form, which usually takes on a certain syllabic \r\npattern, i e. 3-3-3.  But you can have contests that set \r\nother patterns.  Kinda fun over intimate spaghetti dinners. \r\nThen, there\'s the One Breath Cuss--how many vituperous \r\nwords can you string together in one long exhalation? Then \r\nfor the Chronicaly Constipated Howl & Shit contest..well, \r\nthat\'s really self-explanatory. There is also a form of \r\nsorcery and cussing, which is a combination of laser-like \r\nprojection of the evil eye and the malefic word at the nape \r\nof the neck of the person ahead of you...They will turn and \r\nlook at you eventually. What you do next is up to you! LOL!\r\nI like how cussing sometimes sounds just exactly like what \r\nit is! Shit is perfect in that way! A absolute word of \r\ncontempt.  Monkeys shit into their hands and toss it at \r\nenemies.  Maybe SHIT is hardwired into us \r\ngenetically...however, fuck is too much fun....cunt sounds \r\nlike a boot kicking something blunt and concrete...which \r\nreminds me of yet another rave--why dont we have any better \r\nwords for our sexual parts.?  I don\'t like any of them. Why \r\nshould sexual parts be used in cussing?  I think something \r\ndisgusting would be appropo but something so pleasurable \r\nused as a curse? Hmmmm',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2229,751,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'orisha','Im nearing 49 and I find that I have a perpetual \r\nNovember chill around my heart as concerns relationships \r\nwith men. I find that I dont mind being remote, I don\'t \r\nmind the solitude, I don\'t care if someone is there to hug \r\nme or not, or for me to hug them. Burnt out to a crisp \r\non \"romance\"? You betcha. Give me genuine friendship any \r\nday! A pet, some plants, lots of good books...that\'s fine \r\nwith me.  ',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2230,756,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'s5 to weeb','what time? i would go.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2231,751,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','meow',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2232,750,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'chaya','what can i say?  i needed to spew.  i just happened to be \r\nin a convenient location.  \\\"best friendly\\\"',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2233,758,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<pre>\r\n\r\nsmall puddle of useless fuel sits in my gas tank\r\nslowly drying up, victim of evaporation\r\nrain leaks into my now-obsolete machinery\r\ni was once shiny, cutting edge.\r\nbut i ran out of gas.\r\n\r\n</pre>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2234,749,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Joanna','i don\\\'t think I could ever look at  asparagus the same way \r\nafter going through Olivia\\\'s porn stash',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2235,759,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'astronomy domine','\\\"Friend, when u speak this carefully I know it is because \r\nyou don\\\'t know\r\nwhat to say. I listen in such a way so as not to add to \r\nyour loneliness. I\r\nmake some replay at every opportunity so as not to compound \r\nyou loneliness.\r\nThus the conversation continues under an umbrella of \r\noptimism, If you\r\nsuggest a feeling, I affirm it. If you provoke, I accept \r\nthe challenge. \\\"\r\nL.C.,Book of Mercy.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2236,758,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'k*','Still writes like a charm.   ',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2237,759,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'frank',' it\\\'s not easy having a good time.  even smiling makes my\r\nface ache.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2238,758,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2239,758,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon-fk','god damn it.\r\n\r\n--\r\n\r\ni did better than run out of gas.\r\nmy muffler fell off.\r\nand my oil is white and frothy with coolant.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2240,761,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','hot damn. zwigoff and clowes working on a film \r\ntogether? that should be very interesting indeed.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2241,758,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'wylda_danevah','<pre><tt>\r\nrunning out of gas\r\nthe needle past empty\r\nmy heart stops beating\r\n\r\nthe falling rain says\r\nnight is your doorway to truth\r\nlisten to those dreams\r\n\r\nroaming down lost roads\r\nso far from finding real love\r\nfar away as stars\r\n</tt></pre>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2242,760,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'wylda_danevah','Hmmm. interesting.  How about trying to do one \r\nwith the figures making love---any persuasion, just no \r\nbrutality, please...or draw one drawing a door then opening \r\nit and walking through it into another world...or two \r\ndiners untangling sphaghetti and turning it into????...or a \r\nspider weaving a web...a fractal web...just curious if you \r\ncan do it....',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2243,721,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'orisha','orgasm...yes and in several modes.  As an older \r\nwoman I am a specialist in Advanced Carnal Knowledge. Hope \r\nthat doesn\'t insult anyone\'s religion! My theory is that \r\ngood sex (however you wish to define that) is hardwired \r\ninto us as a shortcut to white light/ecstasy....the \r\nchocolate rabbit was just the beginning for me!',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2244,762,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p>usually dreams like this arise from anxiety or worry. \r\nand it\'s difficult to interpret the symbols literally, without \r\nknowing who you are or what\'s going on in your life right \r\nnow. with that disclaimer in mind, here\'s my best \r\nguess.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>the beating heart and your mother represent two \r\nsides of the same coin: a part of you that needs \r\nprotection and nurturing, and the part of you that exists \r\nto nurture yourself. the mother figure can also represent \r\na desire to be cared for or guided through a difficult \r\ntime.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>in your dream, this theme shows up quite literally \r\nas the someone who is helping or guiding you up the side \r\nof a mountain. mountain climbing is often a metaphor \r\nfor journeys and struggles. you might want to consider \r\nyour current life situation in this context. ask yourself, \r\nwhat are you struggling with most right now?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>your anxiety comes into play at the top of the \r\nmountain. usually after a successful climb, you get to \r\nrelax, look out over the view, and enjoy the rewards of \r\nhard work.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>but your mountain is an unstable volcano of \r\nuncertainty. to expand the metaphor, you don\'t know \r\nwhat\'s waiting for you at the end of your struggle. and \r\nyou fear it.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>the beating heart is <b>your</b> heart. it lies there, \r\nexposed, in the core of uncertainty, needing care and protection. \r\nthe heart also represents the fear and anxiety you feel \r\nfor the outcome.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>your mother in this dream is not actually your \r\nmother, but because she died, you unconsciously \r\nchose this symbol to represent an abandonment of \r\nhope. the black bird just further reiterates the theme of \r\nyour own inner guide abandoning you. (it\'s my belief \r\nthat all symbols in a dream - including other people who appear to show up as \r\ncharacters - are different parts of you.)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>and if she flew away, maybe she was never there to \r\nbegin with. maybe you are trying to make this journey \r\nalone?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>consider that the volcano is something you made \r\nfor yourself, out of fear for an uncertain outcome. \r\nevaluate where you are in life right now, where you are \r\nheaded, and where you might end up. confide in a best \r\nfriend. find a reliable guide.</p>\r\n',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2245,760,'2003-05-10 16:09:14',79,'yeti','<p>These are just things I find out there on the internet. \r\nNone of them are my work. I thought a little about drawing \r\none that was me getting wired. We\\\'ll see!</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2246,758,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'icb','<pre><tt>\r\n&lt;s5&gt; tired: carl steadman\r\n&lt;s5&gt; wired: austin swinney\r\n</tt></pre>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2247,756,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'mike','So you enjoyed the class? good for you! if you keep it up \r\nwe\\\'ll play some Capoeira next time your in Austin.\r\n                                          Boa Viagem',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2248,760,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'mischief','you like that stick animation? check out this one:\r\n\r\n<p><img \r\nsrc=\\\"http://www.instinct.org/~pgl/stuff/pics/funny/6beers.gi\r\nf\\\">',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2249,766,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','thanks for fighting the good fight, chia. post your \r\npictures! i want to see.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2250,767,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','the best ones are the dried up, fully erupted zitheads. \r\nthey are waiting to be excavated, and you pull it out, \r\nfully dried up, <b>little yellow tarballs of ex-zititude</b>. you \r\nare left with a happy little red hole, and you wash with dr \r\nbronners to dry it out. you are a happy and good zit picker!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2251,766,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','I had an instinct you were out there shooting. I just knew \r\nsomehow. I am really envious and proud of you. ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2252,767,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Danielle','My mum thinks that my boyfriend is the only one in the \r\nworld who likes to pop other people\\\'s zits. Sometimes he \r\nsits on me when we\\\'re cuddled and bed and finds all that he \r\ncan. What a naughty zit popper he is!!',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2253,767,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','in charles bukowski\\\'s women, he describes a girlfriend who \r\nderives erotic pleasure from popping his zits.<BR>\r\na weird book.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2254,768,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','Coming home after a long trip seems to have the same effect\r\non me too.  Everything feels different for about a week.  I\r\nguess because I\\\'m re-seeing things I\\\'d become accustomed to.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2255,767,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','Yeah, those little hard sonsabitches <em>suuuuuuck</em>. \r\nOne of the minor side effects of one of the meds I take\r\n(prednisone IIRC) is increased hair growth and skin oil\r\nproduction (not like you\\\'re a critter from the black lagoon,\r\nbut I am quite a bit hairier and my skin is a little\r\noilier).  So naturally I\\\'ve had more acne since the\r\ntransplant (but not as bad as my 13/14/15 age band).  Sigh.\r\nOh well, could be worse.  :-)',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2256,766,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','i hope you pulled that rubber bullet out of your teeth, you\r\nfucking badass. =-)',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2257,767,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'zb','I derive great pleasure from my pimple popping. The \r\nblackhead screams, â€œRelease me! I yearn to be free!â€ It is \r\nmy moral duty to oblige. And we are both satisfied \r\nafterwards.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2258,770,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'<b>huney</b>','pale rain over the dwindling town<br>\r\nand over the sea wet church<br>\r\nthe size of a snail<br>\r\nwith its horns through mist<br>\r\n-- dylan thomas<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\nhigh above congress avenue<br>\r\ni while the afternoon<br>\r\nwith the grey clouds',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2259,770,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','this morning was so beautiful. rock on, rain. i hope it \r\ncomes back later tonight.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2260,759,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'will','<p>\\\"you have made me smile again/ in fact i might sore from \r\nit/ it\\\'s been a while...\\\"</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2261,764,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'uhuru','like the sufi masters\r\nthat is lovely\r\nmy best friend and I have been perfecting this funny \r\ndancing where we each lean back, hands grasped at the \r\nwrists, and we spin and spin and use the centrifugal force \r\nto whip each other around.  We use enough control to where \r\nwe don\\\'t fall over, and we look into each other\\\'s eyes to \r\navoid becoming dizzy.  I usually start laughing and break \r\nthe concentration and fall over violently to the ground \r\ngiggling.  If you focus, this exercise works really well.  \r\nIt is a very spiritual experience, spinning.\r\nThe hippies up in Arcata, where I\\\'m from, like to do it a \r\nlot.  At shows and sometimes just for the hell of it.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2262,770,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'edith','when we go down to albany<br>\r\neverything will be so much easier',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2263,767,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i climb all over peter popping his zits. when i got back \r\nfrom australia that is the first thing i did. he has these \r\nreally satisfying blackheads.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2264,770,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','crisis are good when gotten out of the way early in the\r\nday.  i however am having my crisis at seven fifty three\r\npm.  it seems that the delete key on my del laptop is not\r\nlarge enough to hit in the dark, or without looking.  i\r\nwould gladly trade in the \\\'pause\\\' key for a double wide\r\ndelete key.  what the fuck is \\\'pause\\\' anyway?  fuck.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2265,768,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','at home the days are identical and slip by, a single \r\nmemory of 24 hour duplication. but on the road every \r\nexperience is unique and tangible, stretching time \r\nagain to its rightful pace.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2266,762,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'orisha','Very astute, and useful! I appreciate your imput.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2267,774,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'orisha',' Simply glow with the flow!',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2268,774,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'wylda_danevah','Break on through to the other side!',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2269,772,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'wylda_danevah','html O.K. yo is preachin\\\' to da choir! Seriously, I agree \r\nwith you.  Wish I could help you out with resources, and I \r\nwish that letter writing really works. Anybody with \r\nconcrete evidence that it does, or do you just get form \r\nletters in return?',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2270,527,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'orisha','html O.K. god, do i know you from somewhere? have we met \r\nbefore...i know we must have travelled the same road, \r\nbecause i have read that sign also.  What a long, strange \r\ntrip it\\\'s been.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2271,772,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','<p>\r\nif yer looking for ideas and approaches to stopping \\\"free \r\ntrade\\\" in the america\\\'s check out stuff on the MAI (multi \r\nlateral agreement on investment) that was essentially killed \r\nby public pressure. there is a lot of literature out there \r\nfor anyone interested in related topics. indymedia.org is a \r\ngood place for info. the noam chompsky archive is a good \r\nresource. for print check out \\\"in these times\\\" and \\\"world \r\npress review\\\". the \\\"economist\\\" is good for a comprehensive \r\nbut business slanted view of topics. if you got pbs or cbc \r\nnewsworld check out the bbc world service at 6pm est time on \r\ncbc newsworld and itn\\\'s news for public television on pbs \r\n5:30pm est time. \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nwe must remember that when things get \\\"really\\\" bad, police \r\nand soldiers refuse to kill fellow citizens. corporations \r\nare in essense a contract with the public. the public has \r\nlost that right over time, but can just as easilly shift \r\nover night. if pigs were to fly(and they might in the next \r\n40 years in some countries), the people WILL take back \r\npower. democracy will be looked at in a far more short \r\n\\\"term\\\" way, however leaders will think in far more long term \r\nways. if they go about doing things well, then the people \r\ncontinue to vote for him/her. we are seeing this with chavez \r\nin venez. (the u.s is funding the \\\"war on drugs\\\" because \r\nvenez is pretty socialist and panama is neutral. 40% of \r\ncolumbia is controlled by the marxists. its a dangerous part \r\nof the world watch it. the people will decide that politics \r\nARE more important then bread and circus\\\'s. the raving \r\nhippies have jobs and are now losing them because of a few \r\nrich dudes who wanted to devalue the rest and make money on \r\nthe insurance. rich people discust me and as the environment \r\ngets more and more feable, the indie media will cry soylent \r\ngreen and the people will open their eyes. aids, the \r\nprivatization of genetic research, war, poverty, the \\\"energy \r\ncrisis\\\", and class division are all becoming bigger and \r\nbigger issues and more and more people are starting to hear \r\nthe smaller voices. the grass roots movement is strong in \r\nmany parts of the world. proactivity is on the rise and non \r\nviolence is too. the media and the man all focus on the few \r\nthat cause trouble. and as spectators we see the brutality \r\ncoming from the other side, but those on couches watching \r\nthe boob tube see rapskallion death crew posse anarchists \r\nCHAOS DEATH AND DESTRUCTION!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nin quebec they were hearding and stripping down arrested men \r\nand spraying them with cold water out of a fire hose. they \r\nwere then put on buses and not given food or water or \r\nbathroom breaks.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\na medical centre was closed down by gunpoint.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\na popular activist was kidnapped by rcmp stormtroopers \r\ndressed as activists.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\npeople were read their rights in french, even though they \r\ndidnt understand what was being said to them. no attempt was \r\nbeing made to read rights in languages understood by \r\nprotesters.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nthe arrest ratio was slanted far towards males. \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nthe pics will be ready may 7th. \r\n</p>',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2272,754,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'gage','my momma sent me a riddle today.\n\nriddle: what is the one food that will never spoil (or be \neaten by bugs)\nhints: it is a pure not mixed substance. it is natural not \nmanmade. it is not a vitamin, mineral, or chemical element.\n\nshe also said:\n\ni had my first epidural shot.  better than a sharp stick \nin the eye.\n\nmommas!\n\nwhat is the answer to her riddle?\n\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2273,775,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','swinney.org needs stickers for central valley truck stop \r\nbathrooms.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2274,738,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'cyantist','mmm kay.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2275,770,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','You could try two things for the key problem: glow in the\r\ndark paint (and a steady hand) or (x)modmap or whatever it\r\nwas called that let you remap keys on your keyboard in X\r\n(and I know there is a way to do the same for the console).\r\nI use this, when I remember to, to switch caps lock and tab.\r\n(How many times do you hit caps lock?  How many times do you\r\nhit tab?  Now which one is bigger and closer to your hands\r\nin a \\\"home row\\\" configuration?  Looks like in the fight\r\nbetween logic and historical kowtowing, logic lost again.)\r\nOf course the remap advice is Unix.  I bet there\\\'s some\r\nsimilar trick in other operating systems.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2276,770,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','The best part of a crisis is when it\\\'s over and the next one\r\nhasn\\\'t started yet.  I think I have about one weekend a\r\nmonth like that.  :-)',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2277,772,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','I recall hearing or reading somewhere that the essential\r\ndifference between Canada and the US was that in the US, the\r\nbasic social contract is that in exchange for being a good\r\ncitizen, you were guaranteed the right to \\\"life, liberty,\r\nand the pursuit of happiness\\\".  In Canada, the guarantee is\r\n\\\"life, peace, and an orderly society\\\".  The US seems to be\r\nfairly unique (along with Australia) out of the set of\r\nformer British colonies in that we seem to be a far less\r\nstate-centered society (e.g. in Britain you do not have the\r\nright to remain silent if accused of a crime).',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2278,775,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>i like my hornets.  they are very tight.\r\nwhy just the other day i was walking down the street and i\r\nhit a slab of wet sheet metal causing me to skid a good five\r\nfeet and land on my ass.  this little fat kid sitting on his\r\napartment\\\'s steps laughed at me.\r\n</P><P>\r\ni punched him in the fore head.  he started crying.\r\n</P><P>\r\nthen he said though his tears, \\\"my name is leonard and my\r\ndad is going to kick your ass.\\\"</P><P>\r\ni said whatever and kept on walking.  then i was crossing\r\nthe street at twenty fourth and i was plowed by a late model\r\namerican generic car front.</P><P>i rolled off the hood and\r\nlanded on the ground hard.  the car screeched to a stop with\r\nthe rear tire on top of my foot.  it hurt.</P><P>the first\r\nthing i saw when the white pain cleared from my vision was\r\nthe words, \\\"EL CAMINO\\\".  then i felt a swift kick to my\r\nass.  some big fucker was like, \\\"YOU THINK YOU CAN FUCK WITH\r\nMY KID?!\\\"\r\n</P><P>man, i was pissed.  nobody kicks me in the ass.  and\r\nhe scuffed my Hornets.</P><P>\r\ni grabbed him by the nuts. \\\"you bastard.  you scuffed my\r\nHornets, and you kicked me in the Wranglers.\\\"  i whipped his\r\nass and hit him over the head with a baby stroller that was\r\nrolling by.  (i took the baby out first).</P><P>  i put him\r\nout and took his camino.  i gave it to elly.\r\n</P><P>\r\ndont mess with a man\\\'s Hornets.</P>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2279,772,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jebro','html yes.\r\n\r\nre: corporate power<br>\r\n<p>my father said something to me a long time ago that i \r\nthink about often.  he said that the first corporations \r\nwere given their charters in England when the Americas were \r\nbeing explored/settled.  He said the Queen/King would \r\nbestow the power to create this non-living entity to \r\nprotect the owners from risk and personal losses.  Now the \r\ncatch was that the corporation had to prove that it\\\'s \r\nintent was for the *public* good.  that it had to benefit \r\nthe citizen base as a whole.  see, even back then they knew \r\nthat creating these entities was possibly a dangereous \r\nmove.  they have no accountability nor morals nor human \r\nface.  plus the fact that they can live long past one man\\\'s \r\nlife.  i believe the corporation is actually the first \r\nartificial intelligence not something created in Bell \r\nLabs.  this catch that they had to function for the public \r\ngood has long been forgotten.  They have now become \r\ncreeatures whose unbending intent is profit.  and a single \r\nminded goal such as this makes them incredibly sleek and \r\nfast moving - decisions are made like lightening and \r\nthings/people that stand in their way are crushed.  </p>\r\n<p>i was reading the other day about these pharmaceutical \r\nphuckers and their greed in Afrika - one spokesman was \r\npleading their case to the press - saying , come on, we are \r\nin business to make profit- we are not a charity.  i say we \r\nrevoke their corporate charter.  they are no longer serving \r\nthe public good. it is time for the death of these profit-\r\ndriven intelligences before it is too late.  already they \r\ndominate both the private and public sectors.  a government \r\nor group of citizens cannot compete with the coporations \r\none-mindedness.  they want to survive and make profit over \r\nALL. including the destruction of our world.</p><p>\r\nit\\\'s interesting because i have been looking into creating \r\nan entity for some time - first in texas and now here in \r\nCZech.  it\\\'s amazing how much easier it is to create a \r\ncorporation than a non-profit (even one that does NOT \r\nbenefit from any tax-exempt status) .  from the startup \r\nfees to the amount of paperwork to everything.  here, as in \r\nthe states, to start a non-profit you need to pick a board \r\nwhose members are not actually in the organization who \r\nwatch over its activites.  who could even fire the founder \r\nof the group. (which i have witnessed twice in my life - a \r\nperson starts a nonprofit to get booted down the line)  \r\nSo..my point is that non-profits have all these controls \r\nand checks and review boards whereas a corporations can do \r\nas they please.  one captain of the ship.  (of course it \r\ngets more complicated once you issue stock, etc. but i am \r\nspeaking on a small scale.)  in the end i will probably \r\nstart a non-profit-making corporation to avoid the hassles \r\nof the non-profit rules.  a corporation whose intent is for \r\nthe public good.  i think this is the direction we need to \r\nmove.  </p>\r\n\r\n<p> make them prove they are out for the public good. if \r\nthey cannot - let\\\'s revoke their charters over-night. what \r\ncame from nothing can easily be returned.  boom.</p>',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2280,775,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','<P>a contest? who can make the best swinney.org \r\nadvertisement? I once wrote swinney.org on the wall of \r\nOilcan Harry\'s, but don\'t tell austin. There is a billboard \r\nhere in austin that dares pot smokers to come up with \r\none good reason to smoke pot, then leaves a little \r\nspace to write something... i was thinking it would be \r\nfunny to write swinney.org there and place a huge \r\nbillboard size picture of the shanghai sho-lo himself...\r\n</P>\r\n<img src=\"http://saturn5.com/swinney/art/austinshanghai1.jpg\" width=400>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2281,772,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'will','once upon a time i wrote a letter a month to my \r\ncongressional puppets.  i never received a reply to the \r\nletters i wrote on my own--this may because they often \r\naddressed many different issues that i thought needed \r\nchanging.  i have received a few replies from senator gramm \r\n(r-tx) regarding faxes i sent him through places like the \r\nsierraclub and pro-choice sites.  they don\\\'t seem to be only \r\nform letter... he actually recognizes that he and i have \r\ndifferent stances on the issues and tries to back his \r\nposition up with the same false facts they peddle to \r\neveryone else--\\\"higher risk of medical injury may be \r\ninherent in the use of RU-486\\\" (more bullshit like that).  \r\nbet he likes his viagra, though.   fuck the heart attack \r\nstatistics.  ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2282,776,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>last night elly and i heard the same plane.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ni live a mile and a half from her.</P>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2283,776,'2003-05-10 16:09:14',79,'yeti','Is it really a mile and a half? hah! I never realized!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2284,756,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'zb','<p><font face=\\\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\\\" size=\\\"2\\\" \r\ncolor=\\\"#660066\\\"><a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.collegehumor.com/temp/fight3.swf\\\">take \r\nthat!</a></font></p>',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2285,777,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'will','by the way, there\\\'s nothing better than watching a CIS \r\ninstructor beat the hell out of Xerox copier because he \r\ncan\\\'t get it to make two-sided copies.  ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2286,777,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','so were you at any of the 3 recent death cab shows in \r\naustin?',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2287,777,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'will','but of course.  the emo\\\'s one, before SXSW.  ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2288,777,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','jo. everyone you pass on the street is from swinney.org',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2289,775,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','terrifying',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2290,778,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','yeah. i like this.\r\n\r\ni am also now thinking of the red man and the white lady and \r\nthe mother theresa lady and the pig man and sheila and the \r\nvarious other 16th and mission/val regulars. i\\\'m not even \r\nsure if they are still around, since i just moved back and \r\nthings are so different now.\r\nbut they were legendary.\r\ni remember seeing red man and pig man get into a fight at \r\nmuddy waters. i felt important in the eyes of san francisco \r\nhistory to be there witnessing it. my grandfather would be \r\nproud.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2291,775,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'dr. lolo','quick someone call western dental. \r\nhttp://www.westerndental.com/ ',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2292,777,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'wylda_danevah','yeah, but it would be nice to have some way to \r\nidentify one another easily instead of going up to someone \r\nand peering for that special gleam in the eye that let\'s \r\nyou know that they know you know also',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2293,775,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'orisha',' Laughing! Yes! But I think it would be cool to \r\nhave neat cryptic buttons that just say swinney.org--or a T \r\nwith Bright RED BOLD type--SWINNEY...or maybe...in smaller \r\ntype, the kind that makes people want to get closer and \r\nread it...swinney...whatever you say.......or, SAY IT...at \r\nswinney.org\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nThen I had a vision of a black T with a blot of red on it \r\nlike a blotch of pidgeon shit with red trails running down \r\nit...and the T says\" EXPRESS YOURSELF\"..at swinney.org\r\nMake mine 4XL Big Mamma Style',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2294,245,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'el camino','<a\r\nhref=\\\"http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=579624227&return_url=http://www.autotrader.com:80/redirect/redirector_link.jsp?to_url=http%253A%252F%252Fwww.autotrader.com%253A80%252Ffindacar%252Fresults.jtmpl%253F1%253D1%2526certified%253Dn%2526max_price%253D%2526start_year%253D1970%2526end_year%253D1990%2526address%253D75075%2526search_type%253Dused%2526make%253DCHEV%2526model%253DELCAM%2526distance%253D%26mis%3DEANDNVLNEL233\\\">a\r\nbeut</a>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2295,781,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'orisha','Is there anybody else in here over 45?',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2296,780,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'wylda_danevah','html O.K. Men marry bitches for the same reason that women \r\nmarry the sons-of-bitches--it keeps the old psychic wars \r\ngoing.  Better the devil ya know, than the one you don\\\'t. \r\nMen marry their mothers or her exact opposite. (Usually \r\nthis is the first marriage. The second marriage is the \r\nantithesis of the first.  Finally things even out by the \r\nthird marriage.Maybe.  Unless you like repeating mistakes.)\r\nAlso, some men like bitches for the same reason that they \r\nthink sex has to have a nasty ugly trashy aspect for it to \r\nbe \\\"good, hot sex\\\"...I keep hoping this attitude will die \r\nout but as I look around me, it\\\'s still going strong. Some \r\nmen still polarize women as either saints/madonnas/mammas \r\nor whores/witches/bitches--granted, it ain\\\'t too evolved, \r\nbut I think men have along way to go.  I do know some \r\nwonderful evolutionary types though, kinda like vibratory \r\namphibians, just crawling out of the primordial \r\ntestosterone sea!',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2297,782,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'whippet','are people really giving you snide looks, or do you just \r\nthink they do because you\\\'re paranoid? paranoia brought on \r\nby media, maybe, but paranoia nonetheless. you can stop the \r\ncycle by refusing to feel bad about who you are. i think \r\neveryone gets the same amount of snide looks as everyone \r\nelse, for different reasons. maybe you give *me* a snide \r\nlook because i can\\\'t gain weight. where\\\'s the love?',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2298,781,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'young kid','agist.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2299,782,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Danielle','Sometimes I feel very paranoid that people are looking at \r\nme (possibly because of the media) because I\\\'m too tall, \r\ntoo big, too pierced, to sloppy etc etc. Then sometimes \r\nwhen I do, for sure, catch someone looking at me, I giggle. \r\nI don\\\'t know why but I think its funny that these people \r\nare wasting time and energy to give me snide looks because \r\nI don\\\'t look just like them. Hmmm.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2300,782,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Big Momma','I see what you\'re saying, but I don\'t think it\'s \r\nparanoia on my part. I clearly see facial expressions.  Of \r\ncourse, it could be absolutely unconnected to me, but there \r\nare times when it clearly is.  I see your point \r\nabout \"where\'s the love\"---and I am more than willing to \r\nlet you be you if I can also have that same freedom of \r\nexpression. In a sense, in this day and age, I am \r\nthe \"outlaw\" and disloyal to civilization by being large \r\nand satisfied with it. Those who are thin, by their nature \r\nand not as the result of fashionable pressure, I have no \r\nproblem with.  What I do find annoying are those women who \r\nare slavish and do not make an authentic hand-made, \r\nhomegrown life for themselves; and then throw castigating \r\nlooks on those of us who do not want to be caught up in the \r\ncycle of judgment by others.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2301,781,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Big Momma','anybody in here think age dont have a thing to do \r\nwith it? Or are you just wantin to walk down memory row \r\nwith somebody your age?',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2302,782,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Chrisalys','Have you ever thought that maybe people arent \r\nstaring at you with contempt\r\nbut maybe because they are amazed\r\nand envious of your outrageous\r\nbeauty\r\nunique\r\nnever seen before anywhere\r\nuntil they saw\r\nyou',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2303,782,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'whippet','but aren\\\'t you judging others in the very way you yourself \r\ndo not want to be judged? on looks alone, on outward \r\nappearance, on one action on one streetcorner in one moment \r\nof one day, by a person you will never see again? a person \r\nyou will never know. maybe she will go home, pick some \r\nhome grown spices out of a flowerbox, put some organic trash \r\nin the compost heap, do some yoga, feel love and be a good \r\ngood person. you cannot know.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2304,782,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Big Momma','Fat, thin, gay, straight, etc all can be lovely \r\npeople in their own right--i am talking about when a \r\nspecific situation happens to me, as it has from time to \r\ntime. I do not wish to be judged by appearances alone, as \r\ndo you. My point is that by being large, I am much more \r\nlikely to receive condemnation than someone who is skinny.  \r\nMuch of that does indeed have to do with the brainwashing \r\nthe media has done on us. I do not have a problem with \r\nsomeone being the size they want to be as long as they do \r\nnot push their beliefs on me. I DO have a problem with \r\nthose who are thin out of a desire to be fashionable being \r\ndisparaging and critical of me because of my desire to \r\nexpress myself in a way that pleases me. ',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2305,782,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Connie Lingus','i think you are generalizing from specifics Big \r\nMomma and that\'s always a slippery slope.  You are taking \r\nisolated incidents that happen to you in public as personal \r\ncondemnation and how can you be sure that\'s what\'s going on?\r\nAlso, you mention most of this coming from thin women.  \r\nWhat about men? Many men are attracted to larger women.  I \r\nam a big woman also, but I have not experienced it as you \r\nhave. It may be the exterior that initially attracts people \r\nor repells people, but isn\'t it what\'s on the inside that \r\ncounts the most? So, in that light, what\'s the beef?',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2306,782,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'whippet','i don\\\'t think overweight people are any more likely to \r\nreceive condemnation than a skinny person. for every person \r\nwho thinks \\\"gosh she is kinda fat\\\" there is a person who \r\nsees a skinny person and thinks \\\"gosh he is a skinny guy\\\" or \r\n \\\"gosh that skinny guy has ugly pants.\\\" people are not \r\nskinny to spite you or to be stylish, they are just skinny \r\ndue to genetics or other habits that affect their physical \r\nbody. if you think every thin girl you see is anorexic and \r\nstarving herself, you\\\'re wrong. there are not that many \r\nanorexic people out there, not enough for you to assume \r\nskinny people are TRYING to be skinny. it\\\'s just genetics. ',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2307,769,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'orisha','LOl! I can see it clearly also! Agreed!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2308,769,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'wylda_danevah','Hey, how come I relate to this one too?How can \r\nsomebody you love drive you crazy like that? Its almost \r\nlike a little game--not a mean and ugly one, just that the \r\nmoves are so well known by both people. Like, its almost a \r\nlittle ritual around going out to eat somewhere.  The \r\ntrouble with me is sometimes I wanna eat the whole thing by \r\nmyself an I dont wanna share!',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2309,769,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Big Momma','I looked at that cartoon and you have to know \r\nthat got me going.  Somebody try to mouse bits of my food \r\nis going to get a fork in their hand! Can\'t stand that \r\nwishy washy game, I dont care who starts it.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2310,769,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'DING DONG',' Whassup with this? hOW COME YOU LETTIN HER PLAY \r\nYA LIKE ThAT? tHAT SHIT AINT LOVE,ITS PLAYIN YOU...dayum, \r\nwake up an smell what comin at ya! gimme a woman wit a good \r\nappetites and eat her own food not be pickin in mine!',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2311,742,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'orisha','I hate Macs--just started working at a state \r\nuniversity where they are EVERYWHERE....hate the mouse, \r\nhate the cheap bic pen quality of Macs, that cramped \r\nuncomfortable hockey puck mouse...give me windows 98 or \r\neven windows 95 anyday.  Apples are rotten, in my book, \r\nthus far...i have to totally agree with orion on this \r\npoint.  Have never used Macs before.  I guess there is some \r\nsort of Dummies type of book-can anybody recommend \r\nsomething? What I\'ve got to use is an iMac--what could be \r\nartistic about the thing? Enlighten me, somebody! And the \r\nabsolutely minimalistic DINKOID keyboard! I would not want \r\nome of these even if someone gave it to me.  I would sell \r\nit to someone who appreciates them. Have Mercy!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2312,727,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'DING DONG','why worry about labeling yourself? Just do what \r\nyou wanna do, don\'t die behind stupid shit and dont die \r\nwonderin..touch is touch and flesh is flesh in the dark or \r\nwith the lights on.love peoples the best you can wit a good \r\nheartm just dont be dumb behind it. The whole world is a \r\nsensual place we only got so much time to  appreciates it \r\nyou know what im tellin ya? Everybody a different kind and \r\ncolor of flower--dont last long, love em alot,take    a \r\ndeep breathe in your soul, inhale beauty,and JOY',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2313,544,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Angel Falls','well, sometimes you make the choices and you have \r\nto live with the consequences...after you\'ve been in deep \r\nwaters, just splashing around on the beach wont satisfy \r\neither one of you.  If you cant say an absolute YEs then \r\nits time to say an absolute NO and go on with your lives.  \r\nOtherwise you\'re both needlessly tying yourselves up in a \r\ngame that will end up with both of you bitter and exhausted \r\nand irritated. Sometimes you just cant have your cake and \r\nice cream and eat both. Sometimes it IS either/or and you \r\nmust decide to let something/someone go. You make your \r\nchoices and you are then responsible for those choices. The \r\nroad goes on and there is no turning back--unless you want \r\nto do the same trip that Lot\'s wife did in the Bible--\r\nturned into a pillar of salt--useless and full of regrets.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2314,782,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>First, please delete the words \\\"Html OK\\\" when you post. \r\nIt\\\'s just trying to tell you that you can use HTML in your \r\npost.</p>\r\n<p>Second, I admit that when I see people who are extremely \r\noverweight, I feel sorry for them. This may not be \r\nappropriate, but I do. In my mind, people who are \r\nsignificantly overweight (while acknowledging the genetic \r\nfactor) are making lifestyle choices that do not equal \r\nhealth. I feel much the same way about chronic drinkers, \r\npotheads, smokers, or people who are addicted to anything. \r\nThat said, I am a marijuana addict. I think it\\\'s wonderful \r\nthat there are larger people, but I don\\\'t think it\\\'s \r\nwonderful if that largeness is a result of inactivity, \r\nsloth, laziness and overeating.</p>\r\n<p>This may make me a judgemental jerk. Wouldn\\\'t be the \r\nfirst time.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>-darwin</p>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2315,782,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','<p>they call me BMG cause my ass be kickin...</p> ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2316,782,'2003-05-10 16:09:14',79,'yeti','\\\"He that is without sin among you, let him first cast a \r\nstone at her.\\\"',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2317,780,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','claiming that because somebody has two X chromosomes makes\r\nthem more emotionally evolved makes as much sense as\r\nsomebody claiming all Y-chromosome-havers are better\r\ndrivers.  generalizations are the crutch of a weak mind.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2318,779,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','I am an atheist.  My life is no less moral than a strict\r\nCatholic or Muslim or Jainist person\\\'s would be, but my\r\nmoral code is my own and does not need an outside mythology\r\nto rationalize or enforce it.  Kindness and other humane\r\nvirtues need not be dictated from on high to remain valid.\r\nSort of like religion but minus the illogical mysticism. \r\nAnd power games.  And all the other wonderful gifts\r\norganized religion has bestowed on humanity.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2319,782,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','Any person that assumes they\\\'re better than somebody else\r\nfor some arbitrary physical or aesthetic reason will\r\nautomatically land on my bad side...  It\\\'s a sign the\r\nperson\\\'s mind is so limited that it must rely on primitive\r\nvisual cues for something as inherently complex as a human\r\nbeing\\\'s existence.  It\\\'s like assuming that all blue cars\r\nget better gas mileage.  Why are people so stupid?  Why do\r\nstupid people have so many children?  Frustration is\r\nrealizing that no matter how much you try contribute to the\r\nworld, you\\\'re efforts will be drowned by the idiocy of the\r\nmasses.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2320,782,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','this thread is full of people who think they are better \r\nthan those people who think they\\\'re better than other \r\npeople.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2321,785,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','ooh i fixed the comment page. hi weeb!',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2322,778,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le',' i have seen red man. who is pig man? who is sheila?',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2323,785,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i will come. post the address!',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2324,786,'2003-05-10 16:09:14',79,'yeti','<p>When I worked for a radio station, I would sometimes get \r\non the air and say \\\"This is NOT KZFN 106.1 FM\\\" just to see \r\nif people were on their toes. I suppose that the FCC would \r\nhave crucified me if they caught me at that. Oh well. KZFN \r\nwas this horrible commercial rotation top40 station with a \r\ntower broadcasting at about 40000 watts and covering \r\napproximately 200 miles from where their transmitter was. \r\nWe were at 400 watts. Our coverage sucked. Our signal was \r\npolarized vertically. We kicked ass.</p>\r\n<p>It\\\'s nice to see a post from you, Jim.</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2325,785,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'joanna','1:  tadaima!\r\n<BR>\r\n2: okairimase!\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nwatashiwa sukoshi duranki desu ne.  anata wa chikattsu des \r\nyo!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2326,785,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>holy cow!  i fell asleep when i could have gotten free\r\nsushi!\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nok, stop this press thingy whatever it is -- swinney.org.  i\r\nhave repeatedly attempted to get clear where you work?!  i\r\nsaid, \\\"you work at the country station?\\\" and you replied,\r\n\\\"no at this used clothes store.\\\"   now you are changing your\r\nstory.  you are saying that you work at the country station.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nwhat are you trying to do to me, weeb?  just what?</P>\r\n<P>it is 5:53 am in san francisco</P>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2327,786,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>i was just harassing jim earlier this evening to tell me\r\nhow to find out where all the wierd people on swinney came\r\nfrom today by barbequeing server logs and serving them up\r\nwith beer.</P>\r\n<P>it is 5:57 am in san francisco.</P>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2328,782,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jen c.','do you think i am fat?',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2329,787,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'yoko','do you think mew fat?',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2330,786,'2004-07-27 