s to sum it up for me.  Big Momma,I think you \r\nlike to stir up a hornet\\\'s nest just to see what would \r\nhappen, just like that sex question awhile back.  Some good \r\nresponses though.  Liked orion\\\'s also. But all of you seem \r\nto be at your best with a provocative question.  I also \r\nlike how some people write poetry, or just free \r\nassociation.Great site. I think I could get addicted to \r\nswinney.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2362,744,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'alanna','try depo.  it makes mentrual things very strange.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2363,792,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'johnny','<b>a rush and push and this land is ours.</b> <br><br> on a \r\nside note--there is a stinky old man that can\\\'t play the \r\nflute for shit and sits on a cement bench in grendale, ca, \r\njust like the old man, playing the flute above in your \r\nlovely picture.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2364,352,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','weeb at weeb.com<br>\r\nrinse, repeat, enjoy.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2365,782,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','not to stir up trouble or anything, but i guess i\'m the only\r\none that can see big momma\'s point. people DO give fat\r\npeople snide and superior looks. i have seen it. or to anyone that\r\ndoesn\'t look like they \'belong\' in a neighborhood. i\'ve been guilty\r\nof this in the past and i have definitely seen it happen. so\r\nyeah, if i were a larger sized person, (and i happen to\r\nthink that it is mostly genetic and not a product of \"bad\r\nlife decisions\") i\'d prolly be pissed off too. just a thought.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2366,786,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jim','HTML OK',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2367,797,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','I guarantee you about 75 percent of people out there who \r\nare in school get help from A)the government B)the school \r\nitself or C)loans. Don\\\'t be fooled. It cost me around 100k \r\nto get through school after all was said and done and my \r\nparents\\\' contribution was negligible.\r\n\r\nMaybe some of them are well taken care of but many of their \r\nfriends may not be, so they downplay their wellbeing rather \r\nthan flaunting it.\r\n\r\nJust my opinion.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2368,770,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'deb-b','albany AND boston, hmm?  i went to north jersey tuesday \r\nmorning at an obscene hour and i think newark airport is \r\nabout 2 hours away... drivers up there are n u t s',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2369,793,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sawks','<br>\r\nso umm, you first',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2370,793,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'evil s5','i\\\'m from happyland!! where everything is HAPPY!!!!!',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2371,793,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','<BR>\r\nAuckland, New Zealand. Originally from Wellington, New \r\nZealand.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2372,793,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','<BR>\r\nAuckland, New Zealand. Originally from Wellington, New \r\nZealand.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2373,795,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'not_loco','listen you pink floyd listening jive turkey! who the hell \r\nare you telling us what to do and what not to do in the \r\ncomments section ?',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2374,786,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','monkeys and padlocks jim?',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2375,786,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','i do so like the soft nice jim! *pet* *pet*\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2376,792,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'romano','I am that stinky old man. Says you about my flute playing.  \r\nWatch yer mouth, son.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2377,793,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'romano','I\\\'m just floating here in the web.  I\\\'m the ghost in the \r\nmachine.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2378,793,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'romano','I\\\'m just floating here in the web.  I\\\'m the ghost in the \r\nmachine.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2379,793,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','<p><b>\\\\/\\\\/EST SIDE</b></p>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2380,793,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'frustin','is there in echo in here? ',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2381,797,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','<p>\r\nrelatively speaking, if you\'re living in the US, you\'re \r\nalready \"rich.\" i\'m not \r\nconvinced that all that\'s wrong with the world is a nice set of\r\nglasses.\r\n</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2382,795,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','i think this belongs in the comments section too.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2383,793,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','The place where deer and antelope roam.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2384,793,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Mike','I only exist in your mind\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2385,793,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jill','Mike ~ did you get my message?',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2386,798,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'uhuru','Do I ever know the feeling!  I just moved out (at my \r\npartner\\\'s indirect request), and I tried to be optimistic, \r\nor rather, to see the true value of alone time.  As it \r\nturns out I\\\'ve been alone rarely.  It is FUN to have space, \r\nand you will find that paintings NEED it if they are going \r\nto be birthed.  They can\\\'t do it in a hectic, social \r\nenvironment.  Ditto poems, novels, and songs.  Hence the \r\nloner artist type, I suppose, although I do derive \r\nexquisite pleasure from collaborating.  It\\\'s good to \r\nchannel abundant sexual energy into music.  Or painting, \r\nI\\\'m sure, if that\\\'s your thing. Something about singing and \r\nplaying guitar just really gets my rocks off.  So, I want \r\nto say to you, congratulations on your newfound vistas.\r\nuhu',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2387,797,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'maria','there is a college owned by disney? that is frightening, \r\nbut considering what i\\\'ve been discovering about my \r\nschool\\\'s money practices, i wouldn\\\'t say we are so far \r\nbehind. my school costs 35K. just about. ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2388,797,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','how much money does it cost to brush your hair?',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2389,797,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'xep again','or... what is wrong with not presenting yourself as wealthy?\r\nwhy is that a bad thing?  should people with money just\r\nspend it on items that affect how they look so everyone will\r\nknow they have money?  i see no purpose in that.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2390,797,'2002-03-05 20:17:36',17,'austin checks xep\\\'s dreads','<P>hm.</P>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2391,797,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','you are sitting in the computer lab at cal arts, yes?\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2392,798,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','hu r yu, uhuru? ;)',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2393,798,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sphs','maybe you could even make a puppet.\r\nthe garage is always open to you my friend.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2394,798,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'adam','thanks nate',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2395,795,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'orisha','What comment section DOES it belong to?  The Red Queen \r\nbecause of the Mad Hatters Tea Party? Smells like Pink \r\nFloyd hybridized with old ravings from the Fire Sign \r\nTheatre mixed with? As far as absurdity, I think it holds \r\nits own with most of the rants I\\\'ve read on this site.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2396,797,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','what are you saying, austin?\r\n',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2397,797,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'alanna (looking around)','Not anymore, I\\\'m not.\r\n\r\nYes, Disney owns a college - or \\\"started it and pays all \r\nthe bills\\\".  Few obviously know about it, but it\\\'s one of \r\nthe most popular places to go if you\\\'re interested in \r\nanimation or filmmaking.\r\n\r\nPeople here are funny: they\\\'re very shifty about personal \r\nconversations, which is odd, and they really don\\\'t want to \r\ntalk about where they\\\'ve been.  Whether they\\\'re embarrassed \r\nbecause they\\\'re from a rich family or they\\\'re not remains \r\nto be seen.  \r\n\r\nBut I do notice things...like the hippie with the \r\nMercedes.  Those are the things that come close to annoying \r\nme (and really do annoy me sometimes).  I think in terms of \r\nacting, of course, and it does look like some are playing a \r\npart...',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2398,802,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','people with less than ten posts don\\\'t appear on the left. \r\nthis is a trial run. DO NOT BE ALARMED',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2399,802,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'astronomy domine','so these are like, the usual suspects lines up or something',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2400,802,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'orisha','but I have only 7 posts to my name, therefore<10.  So, why \r\nam I still here? Moaning and abject prostrations! Perhaps I \r\nam not WORTHY! ',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2401,793,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'orisha','i live in a strange little old house deeeep behind the Pine \r\nCone Curtain in East Texas--just me and my dreams.  Well, \r\nwhat\\\'s left of them, anyway.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2402,797,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'rich kid','<p>rich kids need hugs to.</p>  <p>what is rich? you \r\nmean wealthy? what is wealthy?  are you less a person \r\nif you are rich? are you not as \\\"en\\\"riched as those who \r\nare not?</p>',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2403,798,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','you could make paintings of pick up trucks. i dont know \r\nwhy i say that, but for some reason today I was walking \r\nalong the street counting pick\\\'a\\\'ma\\\'trucks... and i \r\nthought to myself, hmm i could take lots of pictures of \r\ntrucks and make some sort of collage out of them... \r\nchevy trucks that is... and there are plenty of them here \r\nwhere i am at... i personaly like the pre 1988 chevy pick \r\nups, they look beefy and they are loud...',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2404,795,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'orisha','besides which, not loco, I dont think the Saucerful was \r\ntelling what one could or could not do in the comments \r\nsection! Looks like a segue from the Red Queen meander.One \r\npost could instigate a new perspective or a digression--\r\nwhich may or may not fit into a comment.  New category? \r\nDigressions, anyone? Tea and trumpets? Sound and fury? \r\nSturm and Draino? Drawn and quartered?  Have we but two \r\nchoices, then? Either Bang or Whimper? Neither Twixt nor \r\nTween? In my opinion, we haven\\\'t lightened up enough yet.\r\n',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2405,802,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sultana','Nice \\\'n streamlined!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2406,797,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'maria','as a pretty low income student at a very expensive college, \r\ni can certainly relate to alanna\\\'s comments. but it\\\'s not \r\nhow they present themselves (though we do have quite our \r\nshare of dreadlocked rich hippies, let me tell you), it\\\'s \r\nmore their mentality and how completely out of touch with \r\nreality a lot of these kids are. i\\\'m not saying all upper \r\nclass kids are like this, and it is not a crime to come \r\nfrom an affluent background. it is of course, not your own \r\nfault what you are born to, and people shouldn\\\'t be \r\npenalized for things that really are out of their hands. i \r\njust don\\\'t like the stupid ones that their heads up their \r\nasses and better yet, the ones that pretend like they know \r\nwhat it is like to not have any money because they \r\nobviously don\\\'t. ',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2407,802,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'orisha','lets hope to celebrate a happy union between content and \r\nfunction..i appreciate streamlining as a design concept and \r\nI also like that many-layered visionary flourish, lush \r\npsychedelic terrain, rambling reports from those who have \r\ntaken a walkabout in the Beyond Within. Postcards from the \r\nEdge.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2408,802,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','because it is those with five or more... i am getting angry.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2409,770,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jorge','karma karma.... cha cha cha\r\n\r\nso, um, whats gone around has come around.\r\nand youve been left at balthasar\\\'s holding\r\nthe check for two. lobsters, i believe.\r\n\r\nthere\\\'s a cyanide sale on aisle 8, bottoms up,\r\ncockblaster.\r\n\r\njorge\r\n',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2410,802,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'orisha','angry at what? or who? me?',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2411,807,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>this entry / picture really wants me to hang out with you\r\nchia.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i feel *exactly* the same way.</P>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2412,797,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>Love makes the world go \\\'round, but it gets a lot of help\r\nfrom money and angular intrinsic momentum.</p>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2413,809,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>did you get a job in H-Town? </P>\r\n<P>if so, are you not with your girlfriend anymore?</P>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2414,807,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','fucking hell, that photo rules.\r\n<BR>\r\nImperialst fallout is the perfect fodder for great art.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2415,798,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','fucking awesome. I think swinney could become a creative \r\ncollective on the web. we can share our projects and \r\ninspire each other.<BR>\r\nseems to be happening on its own. :)',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2416,809,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>I have the job and the girl.  :-)</p>\r\n<p>Houston isn\\\'t too far from here (especially on 71, I\r\nswear that road was built to speed on).  We\\\'re going to\r\ntrade off driving to the other\\\'s cities each weekend (i.e.\r\none weekend I come to austin and see her and my other austin\r\nfriends, the next she comes to see me).</p>\r\n<p>We\\\'ve had some problems with our relationship these past\r\nfew months.  That whole venus-in-retrograde thing.  But I\r\nthink that it\\\'s healing and will be even stronger than\r\nbefore.</p>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2417,809,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>And I think the FCC relaxed their emissions limit or\r\nsomething.  Driving down to Houston the other day I got KLBJ\r\nalmost 2/3rds of the way there on 71.  And this was during\r\nthe day so it couldn\\\'t have been an ionosphere bounce.</p>\r\n<p>This is nice because the tape player in my Pimp Wagon is\r\nall fuqt. ;-) (does a \\\'90 mitsubishi count as a pimp\r\nwagon?)</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2418,802,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i just saw swinney punch the mirror all apocolypse now and \r\nshit. i think he is losing it.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2419,809,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>that is cool.  i did the leave girl/town thing.  i dont \r\nrecommend it unless you want to leave the girl and the \r\ntown.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>somehow i think you guys will be okay though.  \r\nsomething about your status as a man who has had an \r\norgan replaced.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i think you are kind of my idol.</P>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2420,782,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>If it\\\'s \\\"mostly genetics\\\", why are Americans so much \r\nfatter than everyone else?</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2421,808,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'astronomy domine','\\\"ocean spray\\\" is a very good song by the Manic Street \r\nPreachers. fact.',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2422,800,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>hi kat</P>\r\n\r\n<P>missions are nice.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i have this delimma.  i could continue to pay for my\r\nmeals in couch change, and stay here or i could fulfill my\r\nrole as the nomadic worker and head to the next town for the\r\npromise of a wage.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i have already moved residences 4 times this year. \r\ncities 4 times, states twice.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>or i could stay here in sf.  i could sell my car and buy\r\na motorbike like qq\\\'s.  then i would be unable to leave\r\nbecause i would have nothing to leave in except a\r\nmotorbike.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>or i could sell my car and buy my truck back from my\r\nbrother.  he is getting a new car.  this would require me\r\nreturning to texas, moving again.  moving moving moving.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i read once that moving removes years from the life\r\nspan.  i think about that.  my conclusion is that it is all\r\nin the mind.  if you view moving as a chore, or being forced\r\nto move, uprooted from friends and family, then you will\r\nlose life when you move.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>but then i think, no you will lose life however you view\r\nit, however you think.</P>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2423,802,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'but..','what if someone has only one thing to say...but it\\\'s really \r\ngood?',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2424,802,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'remember','austin that this is fun. and that mirrors hit back.  :)',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2425,807,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','<b>my</b> initial response to this was, \\\"wow. chia looks \r\nreally hot in that picture.\\\"<BR>\r\nthat\\\'s sort of like hanging out. but with more kissing.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2426,813,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','Ladies and gentlemen, SUB!!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2427,813,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','maybe YOU\\\'RE boring.  we\\\'re all wondrous and magic people.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2428,813,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','<p>\r\nhmm. it\\\'s funny, the other day i realized that the\r\njournaling aspect of writing on the web is really a\r\nfascinating new thing. have you noticed how it has\r\ninfluenced major printed writing sources? and also the way\r\npeople design for print? print design has started emulating\r\nweb design, which i think is hilarious.\r\n</p><p>i like peeling back the layers of a person\\\'s writing\r\nvoice, and comparing the layers with each other and with\r\nwhat i know about a person. i think we\\\'ll look back and\r\nrealize that journaling was just as important as the\r\nproliferation of the independant press.\r\n</p><p>\r\nboob cam shots aren\\\'t as exciting to me. but to each their own.\r\n</p>.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2429,811,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'you are','DESPERATE!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2430,811,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'if there\\\'s grass','on the field, play ball!',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2431,813,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','mememememe, yes me. If it were not for this site, i \r\nprobably wouldn\\\'t communicate with dear friends of \r\nmine, just so happens i get to learn about new people \r\ntoo. Its kinda like having a conersation in the kitchen of \r\nyour favorite home, with your friends/family... i am not so \r\nsure if this could be considered Vain... friendly\\\'s come \r\nhere usually. I have never really done much writing, this \r\nhere is a space where i feel comfortable writing... and \r\nthings i want kept secret, i keep secret. ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2432,813,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jem','dear sub,\r\nlet\\\'s get married.\r\nyour pal, jem\r\n',5,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2433,813,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','Dear Jem:<br>\r\nLet\\\'s both jump Sub.<BR>\r\nYour pal,<BR>\r\nSine.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2434,811,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'dj1luna','\\\"you are\\\" - u don\\\'t make sense',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2435,807,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','you look like jack kerouac in this picture.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2436,814,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>word.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>what the fuck am i going to do today?  i have been\r\nwearing the same wranglers, blue hanes teeshirt and burgandy\r\nsweater for OVER A WEEK.  it was smelling pretty bad the\r\nother day when temperatures got into the high eighties and\r\nit was hot and sweaty under the sun.  then the smell went\r\naway, kind of.  maybe i just got used to it.</P>\r\n<P>i was at yoga the other day and i smelled worse then\r\nelly.  and i was proud.</P>\r\n<P>i really need to do laundry.  i have a plan to do it to. \r\ni am just going to do a change of clothes to wear for the\r\nnext two weeks.  one load containing my other pair of jeans,\r\na teeshirt, and my hoodie.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i do not want to go overboard with laudry though.  spare\r\nme having to find a clean shirt every morning.  feeling\r\nguilty when i realize there are no clean underwear and i\r\nhave to reverse some of go freeballing.  free me from trying\r\nto find socks that are not stiff or a sweatshirt that is\r\nnot  covered in cat hair.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>let me be free.</P>\r\n\r\n<P align=center>~BORN--TO--SMELL~</P>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2437,814,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','<PRE>\r\n[adam> yo yo yo yo\r\n[adam> please excuse me while i roc the mic\r\n[adam> someone stole my car\r\n[adam> but thats alright\r\n[adam> because i get real far on my trike\r\n[adam> i\\\'m bustin keystyle at high speeds\r\n[adam> i\\\'m like mca but i\\\'m wearin tweed\r\n[adam> and if you wanna catch me you best wear skids\r\n[adam> yo i\\\'m on a sugar high cause trix are for kids\r\n[adam> your style is baldin\\\'\r\n[adam> you\\\'re wearin\\\' a wig\r\n[adam> foot and mouth disease\r\n[adam> because you\\\'re a pig\r\n[adam> but enough of the silly\r\n[adam> cuz i\\\'m rhymin with reason\r\n[adam> to all you sucka emcees\r\n[adam> it\\\'s huntin season\r\n[adam> see i\\\'m built like honda\r\n[adam> but i look like a pontiac\r\n[adam> movin with stealth\r\n[adam> always cover my tracks\r\n[adam> rockin sticky treads\r\n[adam> takin turns at ninety\r\n[adam> hold on to your threads\r\n[adam> cuz my road is windy\r\n[adam> and when i\\\'m not on the mic\r\n[adam> i bust on some canvas\r\n[adam> stormin your gallery\r\n[adam> clear out all the wack shit\r\n[adam> most artists are hipocrits\r\n[adam> sellin out for cheese\r\n[adam> i taunt you like a howler\r\n[adam> swingin from trees\r\n[adam> hoooo hoooo\r\n[adam> bitch, you in my jungle\r\n[adam> i\\\'m tossin the mic\r\n[adam> but you always fumble\r\n[adam> i\\\'m like vesuvius\r\n[adam> hear me rumble\r\n[adam> ///////\r\n[adam> peace\r\n</PRE>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2438,800,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Kat','<p>you know i seem to have times when it feels like i am \r\nalways moving. and it is stressful but ive gotten to the \r\npoint where i realize it happens in phases. i may be in one \r\nplace for what i think is a long time and then im ready to \r\nmove on....and thats when the phase hits. its really just \r\nabout exploring...transition doesnt happen immeadiately, it \r\ntakes time. so you go through several moves all in a short \r\nperiod because youre trying things on for size...finding \r\nwhat works best.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>i think thats a good thing. dont box yourself into one \r\nthing just because you think you need to \\\'make\\\' it work. or \r\nbecause it seems like thats what you need to do because \r\neveryone else is doing it. [says the girl who struggles \r\nwith this constantly]</p>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2439,813,'2004-07-27 05:14:09',63,'olivia sez',' puh-lease.  dissing personal writing on the web is SO last\r\nyear.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2440,816,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','when is eyore\\\'s birthday?',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2441,816,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','tomorrow.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2442,813,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','being boring is okay. perhaps you don\\\'t realize that we \r\nWANT to read about the trivialities of your life, because \r\nthis makes our own trivial existences seem less isolated, \r\nmore exciting, and then we touch each other through the \r\ncybers and you may not know me, but i am willing to know \r\nyou and i want to do so.<br><br>\r\n\r\nlife is so big, capsulizing it in tiny bits on swinney \r\nbrings it all into perspective.<br><br>\r\n\r\nplease do brain dump now.<br><br>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2443,814,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','please don\\\'t bird dubya, i love him very much.',5,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2444,800,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'auntie','i have moved 29 times in 29 years.  i am a little broken, \r\nbut i\\\'m not dying anytime soon.  moving is good. it brings \r\nnew friends and new places and new ideas.<br><br>\r\n\r\ntexas is nice, i will be going to florida for 6 weeks \r\ntomorrow and then i am coming back to texas and then in \r\nseptember i am going back to florida for 4 months and then \r\nback to texas again for a while.<br><br>\r\n\r\nin between all that i think i will come back to sf and \r\ncheck on le, spawn of my loins, just so she stays on her \r\ntoes and maybe tuggy will be home when i come and we can \r\nplay archie mcphee with kristie and jim and xep and eric \r\nand yeti and swinney, too and they will let me have that \r\nfrigging easter egg hunt at last and did you boys like the \r\nchicken that laid the eggs?<br><br>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2445,813,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p align=\"justify\">to address the idea of the <a \r\nhref=\"http://benbrown.com\">ego as design</a> phenom, <a \r\nhref=\"http://www.undesign.org/undesigners/bremser.html\">wayne</a> said this, and i agree:\r\n</p>\r\n<blockquote><p>\r\n\"Doing good design involves a sacrifice, an offering, no \r\nmatter how much you are getting paid. Part of the sacrifice \r\nis agreeing to become anonymous. Your fingerprints will \r\nstill be on the thing, but it\'s not your face, it\'s not \r\nyour name, it\'s not your whimsy.\r\n</p><p>\r\nIt means giving up this \"brand called me\" shit.\r\n</p><p>\r\nFind something you want to share with the world and, for a \r\nlittle while, try being a nobody.\"</blockquote>\r\n</p><p>\r\n...\r\n</p><p align=\"justify\">\r\nbut that addresses a different (and ultimately, i think, much more damaging) niche than that \r\nof the personal writer on the www. recently, all my friends \r\nhave gotten journals. just when i thought we\'d all stop \r\nwriting on the www, when i thought journaling had been \r\nsaturated, MORE people i knew started in. <a \r\nhref=\"http://cyantology.com\">cyan</a> started, <a \r\nhref=\"http://oof.diaryland.com\">oof</a>, <a \r\nhref=\"http://saturn5.diaryland.com\">steve5</a>, and  <a href=\"http://weeb.diaryland.com\">weeb</a> started. <a \r\nhref=\"http://pondgoddess.diaryland.com\">our</a> <a \r\nhref=\"http://auntie.diaryland.com\">moms</a> started. even \r\nthe perpetually close-mouthed xep began writing online. \r\n</p><p align=\"justify\">\r\ni\'m at a loss to understand this new flood of verbosity, \r\nbut i will tell you that it makes me happy. people are \r\nstruggling to document themselves, and better, to explain \r\nhow it was. i think nothing is more educational than trying \r\nto explain how it was. because it\'s in those moments of \r\ntrying to explain that you realize how it REALLY was, how \r\nintricate, how hard to explain life really is. how precious \r\nsomething so complicated must be. how insane you are to try \r\nand document the spindly delicate threads of syncronicity \r\nthat pull you through the days.\r\n</p><p align=\"justify\">\r\nis it vain? self absorbed? me me me. it is, but we are young. \r\nwe will have our fill of me me me, or, we will solve our \r\nbiggest issues inside our writing and build out to other \r\ngoals upon that. i think most of us have lots of non-me \r\ngoals and dreams, and we work on those. we make art (<a \r\nhref=\"http://weeb.com\">paint</a>, <a \r\nhref=\"http://chiamattt.com\">take pictures</a>). we <a \r\nhref=\"http://divinities.org\">concoct schemes to change how \r\npeople think about religion</a>, we want to be <a \r\nhref=\"http://standing.ontheoutside.com\">massage artists</a> \r\nor <a href=\"http://steve.org\">activists</a>. all this \r\npersonal blah blahing does is make us know ourselves (and \r\nLIKE ourselves even in our honesty!) in a place where we \r\ncan support each other, where we are, the www. and the \r\nbetter we know ourselves the more good we can do out there. \r\n</p><p>\r\nok.\r\n</p>\r\n',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2446,816,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','plastic cups of beer<br> \r\nribs<br> \r\nhacky sack<br> \r\ncostumes<br>\r\nkids<br>\r\nstoners<br>\r\nfrisby golf<br>\r\nturkey drumsticks<br>\r\ntrees<br>\r\ndirt<br>\r\ndogs<br>\r\nsunglasses<br>\r\nhippies<br>\r\nyuppies<br>\r\nhot sun<br>\r\nbelly dancers<br>\r\njugglers<br>\r\nco-opers<br>\r\nfratboys<br>\r\nwater balloons<br>\r\nbikes<br>\r\ndrum circles<br> \r\neyores<br>\r\n<br>\r\ndid i leave anything out?    ',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2447,810,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p>things i like about jo:\r\n</p><p>\r\n<li> she is always open to suggestion\r\n<li> she builds forts in her house\r\n<li> i can call her and tell her that i just called to \r\nshare with her how comfy my bed is and how i\\\'m about to \r\ntake a nap and she is not phased\r\n<li> she doesn\\\'t scold me for being a bad vegan when she \r\ncatches me with my hand in the cheetos\r\n</p><p>\r\ni dunno about me. need to drink coffee before i can make \r\nthat list.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2448,814,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','did you smell me in yoga austin? i did not smell you. but i \r\ndid hear you crack your toes and it made me crack a smile. \r\nthen i remembered i was supposed to be relaxing so i tried \r\nto act like i didn\\\'t notice.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2449,815,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'-','insanity: repeating the same set of actions over and over, \r\nbut expecting a different response.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2450,807,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','chia is totally hot. (taurus)',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2451,816,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','swinney you think if we start driving now we could make it? \r\ni wanna be there.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2452,814,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','sorry auntie, but I am going to do it again as he leaves.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2453,744,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Kat','depo is evil. it makes your whole body strange. and who \r\nwants to be a stranger to their body?',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2454,817,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p>you look like you might really enjoy eating fruit maybe, \r\nin some kind of perverse way.\r\n</p><p>\r\nmaybe i\\\'m projecting.\r\n</p>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2455,817,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Kat','eating fruit has always made me think of sex. juicy \r\ngoodness. ripe skin. swelling. it makes me want sex. with \r\nhumans that is...not fruit.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2456,817,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>please excuse the le.  she is feeling poetic and saying\r\nwhatever she wants today.  (her words)</P>\r\n\r\n<P>so where are you at in the southern united states, and\r\nwhere is the picture of your dog?</P>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2457,817,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p>i knew it.\r\n</p><p>\r\nmy astrological guesses about kat: scorpio, taurus, \r\nsagittarius.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2458,807,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','photo is by hool. his site is down. it will be back tho. \r\nwww.inconduit.com',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2459,818,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','why is today so LUSTY. i bet mercury is in scorpio! where \r\nis s5!',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2460,813,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','<p>\r\npeople who used to write their lives down and publish them \r\nas thought and not as life were called great thinkers. they \r\nmerely put a religious or social slant on things. what most \r\npeople fail to realize(through class socialization) is that \r\nevery mind is capable of great thinking. it just needs \r\nsupport.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nthrown down the chains my friends. money hasnt made \r\nanything. it buys things. people make things.\r\n</p> ',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2461,816,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','eeyore\\\'s is cool.  too bad I have to go to Houston.  :-/\r\neeyore\\\'s, half price books, a shady courtyard on campus, \r\nthe alamo drafthouse, dog & duck pub, crown & anchor, \r\nthat\\\'s austin to me.  not that glass-and-money-money-money \r\nexpanse that is dotcomland up through mopac (yeah I\\\'m a \r\ngeek dot-com programmer nerd, but I have the heart of a \r\nhippie)',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2462,816,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','oh and of course zilker park in the summer time.  and emma \r\nlong city park (good god that water is cold though!).',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2463,815,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','don\'t know much about boston, but craig\'s list has a local \r\nsite for it:  <a \r\nhref=\"http://boston.craigslist.org/\">boston.craigslist.org</a>.  good luck!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2464,814,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>Every time I hear the phrase \\\"freeballing\\\" I have to \r\ngiggle because it reminds me of that Tom Petty (sp?) \r\nsong \\\"Free Fallin\\\'\\\".  Just replace \\\"free faaaaaaaallin\\\'\\\" in \r\nthe song with \\\"free baaaaaaaaallin\\\'\\\"...</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2465,811,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','The restart thing reminds me of fooling with my apache \r\nserver at home.  :-)  cool picture, what artist did that?',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2466,816,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sean','when is swinney\\\'s birthday?',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2467,810,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','cheetos aren\\\'t vegan?  I thought they were made out of, \r\nlike, air and artificial coloring/flavoring.  :-)  If it \r\ndoesn\\\'t come from a plant OR animal...  Maybe it\\\'s only \r\nquasi-sinful, since it just tastes like cheese...  a demi-\r\nsin.  The Diet Coke of Sin.  \\\"I didn\\\'t go to Evil Medical \r\nSchool for 8 years to be called Mr. Evil!\\\"  wooo I\\\'m being \r\nsilly.  loopy_aquarius_mode=on',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2468,810,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','*sense of humor<BR>*willpower: i hem and haw around, but \r\nonce i\\\'ve made my mind up to do something or abstain from \r\nsomething, i can stick to it.<BR>*imagination<BR>*ability to \r\nsee the positive in the negative<BR>*big heart full of love\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2469,810,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','<BR>also:<BR><BR>my scary good HTML skillz\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2470,810,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','(thanks ells. that made happy tears come to my eyes.)',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2471,812,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','I know how much it sucks to be sick for a long time and \r\nthen try to rebuild afterwards.  Good luck.  Have you \r\nthought about short-term contract gigs?  That way you get \r\ncash and you don\\\'t have must-always-ne-at-work-today-at-9am \r\nworries in addition to getting well.  Like elance.com or \r\nsomething (I mention them becuase now it seems that with \r\ntheir partnership w/ eBay, you can get <em>anything</em> on \r\neBay, including a job to pay for your eBay habit).  Here\\\'s \r\nsome other linkage: dice.com (nice metro-restricted \r\nsearch), and computerjobs.com (e.g. \r\ntexas.computerjobs.com).  I\\\'m sure you\\\'ve heard of \r\nmonster.com.  Anyway, good luck again.  :-)',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2472,813,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Joanna','Ever since I can remember, maybe from when I was 8 onwards, \r\nI have wanted to write and publish an autobiography.  \r\nHowever, the reality is, unless I sleep with someone famous \r\nor kill a whole bunch of people, the chances of a publisher \r\naccepting my autobio are very very small.  I can publish \r\nmyself on the Internet though, and so I do.  Having an \r\naudience makes me perform better, it\\\'s that simple.  ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2473,817,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','<p>You have nice eyebrows and look like you have the \r\ncapacity to kick some ass.</p> ',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2474,819,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Suyujen','<p>Agreed. Let us destroy these things and hide in the sand \r\nand wait for the beachpeople to replace them. When they get \r\nclose enough, we emerge and the unrighteous are slain. A \r\nshrine is made of their bones and God will shine down upon \r\nus.</p>\r\n<p>Tuesday good?????????????????????????</p>',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2475,818,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','I am made uncomfortable by this boisterous conduct!',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2476,817,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','you have a nice ass and look like you have the capacity to\r\nkick some eyebrows.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2477,819,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'alanna','you mean...the beach ever was safe?',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2478,811,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','uhhh how does that shirt stay on?',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2479,821,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','i apparently really like to use the world \\\'couple\\\'.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2480,821,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','reminds me of that nick cave song where every line is about\r\nthe girl\\\'s black hair.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2481,821,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sawx','<br>\r\nchaya likes vb! she has been \\\'integrated\\\'<br><br>\r\nph33r melbourne<br><br>\r\n',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2482,819,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>If ABC cleans up the beach, is the advertisment worth \r\nhaving a clean beach?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>-darwin\r\n',5,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2483,815,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>I don\\\'t like Boston.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If you want to know why, I will tell you. However, \r\nswinney.org\\\'s UI will probably preclude you reading this \r\npost again.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>-darwin',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2484,818,'2004-07-27 05:14:09',63,'olivia sez',' i really like this swinney piece.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2485,821,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'chaya','melbourne #1.  for reals. ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2486,818,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','lots',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2487,815,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','if you don\'t like the UI, you can:\r\n<br><br>\r\n1. live with it\r\n<br><br>\r\n2. mock up a new UI and maybe we\'ll do it that way instead\r\n<br><br>\r\n3. make your own website\r\n ',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2488,819,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','It offends me to be bombarded with advertizing everywhere I \r\nlook. Lately it has been getting to me even more, because \r\nso many adverts insult my intelligence, such as the one on \r\nthis barrel. I feel resentful that many of these \r\ncorporations assume that I am a couch ridden, taco-mcKFC-\r\nbell-burgerking eating, stock market obsessed, old navy \r\nclone. I don\\\'t want to see people trying to make a buck by \r\nspoiling the scenery. Arrgh! It fucking kills me. Like the \r\nIBM Linux campaign spray painted on sidewalks. You have no \r\nchoice but to look at it. And now that the entire western \r\nhemisphere (aside from Cuba) will be swapping spit with big \r\nAmerican corporations, I expect not to be able to go \r\nanywhere without having the fucking Taco Bell chihuahua \r\nsnapping at my ankles.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2489,816,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','spider house, showdown, austin java company, book people, \r\npease park, driving 50 down lamar between 15th and 26th. \r\nkids on the drag, the SMELL in the air in the mornings right \r\nabout now, fresh plus, happy friendly strangers striking up \r\nconversations. <BR>\r\ni, too, will miss eeyore\\\'s. i\\\'m at my parents\\\' house.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2490,807,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','oh. fucking. taureans. helpless with taureans.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2491,815,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','can we have a link to \\\'others\\\' within the list of authors, \r\nthen it can take you to another page with a listing of all \r\nthe other authors? ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2492,820,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','DAMN! I look like a 15 yr old boy! Why didnt yall tell me \r\nthat! When was this taken? HAHAH, Austin looks high, was it \r\nhis birthday party?',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2493,821,'2004-07-27 05:13:57',63,'olivia',' you know, that should read: each one of us collapsed into\r\nour bed<b>s</b>.  3, to be exact.  but yeah, it was a good\r\nnight.  i like dancing.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2494,819,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','if the KKK cleans up the highway, is it worth having a KKK\r\nadvertisement?',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2495,797,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','i wish chiamatt would comment on this post.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2496,811,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Lunesse','that\\\'s exactly what my thought was, le.\r\n',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2497,820,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'p.blossom','\\\"stop [yer] whoring!\\\"',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2498,815,'2002-03-05 20:17:36',17,'austin to le','<P>too bad he will probably not be back to read this post...\r\nbecause of the UI.</P>\r\n\r\n<PRE>\r\nDate: Wed, 18 Apr 2001 06:05:01 -0700 (PDT)\r\nFrom: darwin@saturn5.com\r\nTo: austin@swinney.org\r\nSubject: UI thing that swinney.org needs\r\n\r\n\r\nswinney.org needs a thing similar to the \"last 5 entries\" which is \"last 5\r\nentries with new comments\" which helps reference older entries that people\r\nmay still be commenting on. Otherwise, once something is out of the last 5\r\nor 25 it becomes irrelevant except historically. Also, without something\r\nto draw the eye, people need to keep checking a particular entry to see if\r\nsomeone has said something they want to read.\r\n\r\n-darwin\r\n</PRE>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2499,823,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'ComCon','<p>This is Command-Control -- return to base.</p>',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2500,807,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','yeah me and taurus have a problem too.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2501,819,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','<P>haha. holy shit. My search on cnn.com reveals eyebrow-\r\nlifting irony! Hilarity ensues.</P><BR><P><a \r\nhref=\\\"http://cnn.looksmart.com/r_search?\r\nlook=&isp=zcb&key=kkk+adopt%2da%2dhighway&search=0\\\"><img \r\nsrc=\\\"http://www.fonem.org/img/gaygaygay.jpg\\\" \r\nborder=\\\"0\\\"></a><BR></P><P>And the irony continues with <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://archive.showmenews.com/archive/2000/May/2000052\r\n3News10.htm\\\">this</a> story that ran on May 23, 2000. Side-\r\nsplittingly funny! But wait, HANG ON! Mel Carnahan! Yeah, \r\nhe\\\'s the governor of Missouri who basically gave a big FUCK \r\nYOU to the KKK, as any mentally abled person would, and was \r\npreparing to run for a seat in the senate. Why leave \r\nMissouri? For the soul purpose of defending the nation \r\nagainst Sen. John Ashcroft, a failed presidential hopeful \r\nand snarly white guy.You may remember sexy Frau Ashcroft \r\nfrom such hits as \\\"The Confederacy Was Not A Perverted \r\nAgenda\\\", and \\\"I\\\'ll Block the Nomination of Black Missouri \r\nSupreme Court Justice Ronnie White and Piss Off All the \r\nBlack People In Missouri So Much They Will Vote My Sorry \r\nAss Out Of The Senate.\\\"</P><P>\r\nFrom salon.com:<BR>\r\n\\\"Ashcroft is widely known for opposing St. Louis\\\' plans for \r\nschool desegregation, blocking the nomination of Bill Lann \r\nLee to head up civil rights enforcement at Janet Reno\\\'s \r\nDepartment of Justice, as well as Clinton\\\'s choice of Dr. \r\nDavid Satcher, the black nominee for surgeon general. But \r\nit was the senator\\\'s opposition to White that galvanized \r\nthe black community. \\\'We sent a very clear message that \r\nthat kind of demagoguery would not be tolerated,\\\' says \r\nRice. (He concedes that having voted Ashcroft out of office \r\nonly to see him nominated for attorney general simply adds \r\nto blacks\\\' frustration.)\\\" </P>\r\n<P>So our hero, Mel Carnahan, runs opposite incumbent Frau \r\nAshcroft in a blazing senatorial race! But just as Mel is \r\nabout to cross the finish line, he burns up with his son in \r\nan even more blazing plane crash! Hmm, and the \\\"accident\\\"\r\noccurred on the eve of the third presidential debate, which \r\nhappened to be held in...*GASP*...ST. LOUIS! And just where \r\ndo you think his plane crashed? You guessed it. St. \r\nLouis.</P>\r\n<P>See none of dat mattered to tha bruthas and tha sistas \r\nof Missouri, cuz they voted Ashcroft\\\'s cracka ass cracka \r\nass out of the Senate anyway, and replaced him with a dead \r\nguy. They would rather see a dead guy go to the senate than \r\nhave to live with 6 more years of watching their senator \r\ndis their people and rub elbows with the KKK. They also \r\nwrote American History(tm) by making goodly Mel the first \r\ndeceased person to ever be voted into office. Whoo! So then \r\nlovely Mrs. Mel agreed to take her late husband\\\'s senate \r\nseat. THE END!</P><P>\r\nTat\\\'s what you would think, since Gore was probably going \r\nto win the election in 3 weeks. It was fairly safe to \r\nassume Missouri would be rid of Ashcroft. If only the poor \r\nsaps knew what was in store for not only Missouri, but the \r\nentire nation. Now, we see the beginnings of a step back in \r\ntime, a leap back into pre-civil rights days. Fuck, I think \r\nwe are headed back to pre-civial war days.</P>\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2502,819,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','i suggest taking that to the abc offices and throwing it\r\nthrew a window.  you might want to use a sledge hammer on\r\nthe window though because it is probably break resistant.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2503,819,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'thetwoFFs','i have a vision. TELEvision. don\\\'t like it. don\\\'t watch it. \r\nno need to whine about it.',5,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2504,821,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kini','o, will you adopt me?',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2505,815,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','yeah, i\\\'d like to know why you don\\\'t like boston. i always \r\ncheck back on my own posts, self-obsessed little monkey \r\nthat i am.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2506,821,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','thanks for the grammar lesson.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2507,825,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','<BR>\r\nhelp me! i ache so.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2508,825,'2004-07-27 05:14:09',63,'olivia sez',' fuck yeah girl.  take what you\\\'ve got and run with it.  so\r\nmany gifts.  so vivacious.  you are a GIVER.  you will\r\nalways be loved.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2509,824,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','anyone with mars in sagittarius lives for the road. i\\\'ll \r\ngive you a reading when i get home next week.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2510,828,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','the s5 nebula.\r\n\r\n<PRE>    \r\n  *  * ^   %  %^\r\n     *% $  #&  % $ @#    ( &\r\n    (  & ^     \\\\ \r\n         $   ^  % #  (%)     ( *&^$        \r\n</PRE>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2511,815,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<h1>Why I Don\\\'t Like Boston</h1>\r\n<p>I don\\\'t like Boston because I\\\'m from Providence, Rhode \r\nIsland. This means that Boston is my closest <b>BigCity</b> \r\nand that shapes my viewpoint.</p>\r\n<p>Boston is something like five times as big as Providence \r\nand has twice as much going on. The people are East-Coasty, \r\nwhich is good and bad. They\\\'re less likely to be cheery or \r\nhappy but they\\\'re also less likely to be really fake. The \r\nelectronic/rave music scene is very small and there aren\\\'t \r\nmany parties or any good weekend parties. For a city the \r\nsize of Boston, this is embarassing and disappointing.</p>\r\n<p>My generalized experience of Boston is that the scenes \r\nfor Hiphop, live rock and getting drunk in smoky bars are \r\ngood. Anything else (more complex/intellectual/etc) is \r\ndrowned in a sea of beer, freezing cold winters, frowning \r\nfaces, clueless students and conservatism.</p>\r\n<p>On the other hand, Boston is a very pretty city. \r\nAlthough it\\\'s pretty expensive to live there, the public \r\ntransportation is pretty darn good. There\\\'s lots and lots \r\nof nice parks and tons of trees. The waterways aren\\\'t as \r\nincredibly polluted as they used to be. There\\\'s lots of \r\nbirds. It\\\'s close to New Hampshire\\\'s mountains and woods, \r\nMaine\\\'s beauty, Rhode Island and Cape Cod\\\'s Beaches.</p>\r\n<p>It doesn\\\'t sit right with me, which is why I didn\\\'t move \r\nthere. Something about it makes me feel trapped like \r\nProvidence, just in a bigger box.</p>\r\n<p>I could probably go on for a while.</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2512,819,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>Freedom of speech extends to unpleasant or hateful \r\nspeech.</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n',5,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2513,829,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'sawx','<br>\r\ncute bong!<br>\r\nvery german rubberman :)',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2514,830,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','you can chew on my leg anytime, now that i know we are \r\nfriends. i have not done it yet but someday i will try to \r\ngnaw your foot off at the ankle. we will go through this \r\nmany times and later we will look up and say we have been \r\nfriends a long time. that we are, as the kids say, homies.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2515,829,'2002-03-08 04:52:47',65,'le to dave','dave i like you. i know you\\\'re frustrated with me. what i\\\'d \r\nreally like is for you to call me and tell me what your \r\nthoughts on secular humanism are. i have been thinking \r\nabout it lately. i want to exercise my brain.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2516,825,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','universal life energy',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2517,829,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','this picture depicts what you wrote very well. ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2518,829,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'c to the h to c h i a','i know',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2519,821,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'da','sounds like a fun night, and yay, i like visual basic too!  \r\ni don\\\'t think i\\\'m so integrated, though.  (destabilizing.  \r\ni\\\'m feeling a bit feisty this morning, i suppose.)',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2520,829,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','<p>\r\nle, i dont really know what to say about secular humanism. \r\nlike ok for instance they say that ideologies, religion; \r\npolitical or social, must be examined by the individual and \r\nand just because. i agree with this, but thats a pretty \r\nanarchist, liberal, far left view. I mean individualism has \r\nbeen around for a long time. i think to create yet another \r\ndogma(secular humanism) is a bit weird. they argue science \r\nover myth. who doesnt these days? haha.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nthey argue for a \\\"better understanding of ourselves, our \r\nhistory, our intellectual and artistic achievements, and the \r\noutlooks of those who differ from us\\\", and all sorts of self \r\nliberating \\\'things\\\'. they discuss how our history and the \r\nway we perceive it is imperfect and possibly the only reason \r\nthey dont call themselves leftists is because the left has \r\nanswers to the problems of today. I get the feeling that \r\nsecular humanists are lazy. i get this feeling because they \r\nhide behind the shroud of being a philisophical organization \r\nof free thinkers. perhaps im being too critical. id like a \r\nreply. i dont know what your views are. \r\n</p>\r\n',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2521,830,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Sunset gun','\\\"You got to know when to hold em ,know when to fold em \r\n,know when to walk away , know when to run\\\"..I love that!',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2522,832,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>i laughted out loud three times reading this.</P>\r\n<OL>\r\n<LI> the unsually unremarkable daily existance\r\n<LI> semi lodged lenghtwise across the median\r\n<LI> federally regulated iced coffee\r\n</OL>\r\n\r\n<P>i hope you get the job, though it would mean moving, you\r\ncould take your sailboat with you because it is not\r\nuniversity of arizona that you interviewed at.</P>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2523,830,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','once upon a time i met a guy named eric and i thought he\r\nwas really cool.  we started hanging out and i thought he\r\nshould read the book snow crash so i found a copy at\r\naardvark\\\'s on church and and gave it to him.  then we moved\r\nin together so we had two copies of it.  later on, in the\r\nsame life time, weeb mentioned she was about to go buy a\r\ncopy of snow crash.  i said, hey, wait, i have two copies so\r\nyou can have one.  i brought it to work and it sat on my\r\ndesk for about 6 months and i forgot to give it to her even\r\nthough we ate lunch together a lot and she worked just one\r\nfloor above.  by the time i remembered she had already\r\nbought a copy.  oops.\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2524,815,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','thanks. i\\\'ve never lived in a a real BigCity before, just \r\ntampa and orlando (those are mostly just little business \r\ndistrict downtowns with hugs suburbs around them). i\\\'m kind \r\nof looking forward to it in a way. i guess i\\\'ll judge it \r\nwhen i get there. the housing does seem pretty expensive, \r\nthough.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2525,830,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','what\\\'s a \\\"water dog\\\"?\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2526,830,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','jeff gave me a copy of snow crash for my/our birthdays so \r\ni didn\'t have to buy one. then i moved in with him and now \r\nwe have two copies between us. we have snow crash excess. \r\ni think that this copy of snow crash should now go to \r\naustin-bean-growly-ankle-chompy-boy. you know, i just had \r\na thought- if you feel growly, you should growl. i won\'t mind, promise. if i weren\'t vegancranking myself, \r\nthat is. <p>\r\ngnwlwprrruff!</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2527,829,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p>well i don\\\'t understand, are you lumping individualism \r\nand objectivism in together? i am not familiar \r\nwith \\\"individualism\\\" but i will say that i think \r\nobjectivism and humanism is kind of unrealistic. because \r\nthose belief systems put too much trust in each human being \r\nto live up to their full potential. in the same way \r\nlibertarianism assumes that everyone will just \\\"take care \r\nof themselves.\r\n</p><p>\r\nalso, i am a big ball of emotion, often ruled by feelings \r\nand impulsive or intuitive behavior rather than \\\'reason\\\' \r\nalone, which makes me worry about the \\\"science as god\\\" \r\nideas of humanism.\r\n</p>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2528,828,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','<BR>\r\nLaban (punch, float, wring, dab, press, flick, slash, \r\nglide). ',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2529,819,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'andre the giant','<b>OBEY</B>',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2530,829,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','i would like to read a defense of objectivism outside of \r\nthe context of capitalism. in other words, i want an \r\nobjectivist to explain to me how one goes about leading \r\na \\\"productive, entirely independent\\\" life -- neither a \r\nborrower nor a lender be yadda yadda -- in a culture where \r\naltruism isn\\\'t just imposed through religious traditions \r\nbut is part of the way of life. objectivism is all about \r\nself-sufficiency but how successful could an objectivist be \r\nin, say, india or tibet? ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2531,830,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','haha, water dog~ water doggie...  its a male thing, \r\nusually occurs first thing in the morning, sometimes \r\nrefered to as \\\"morning wood.\\\" Nuf said?',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2532,830,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>wait am minute.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>there is morning wood, which is a hard on induced by\r\nerotic dreams and it says hi to you in the morning...</P>\r\n\r\n<P>then there is a water dog, which is a hard on in the\r\nmorning, much like morning wood, except it is not going to\r\nbe satisfied until you have pissed.</p>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2533,736,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','<p>\nremember this: your capacity for sadness is also your \ncapacity for joy.\n</p>\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2534,736,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','<p>\nremember this: your capacity for sadness is also your \ncapacity for joy.\n</p>\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2535,833,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>good thing we dont have anyone here from oklahoma city. \r\ni believe we ran into problems with this kind of topic (me\r\nand austin, tx; xep and santa cruz, ca).</P>\r\n\r\n<P>also, it is good to have anonymity on topics like this. \r\nsometimes i wish elly wasnt so good at sniffing out who\r\nwrote what based on a form of hand writing analysis applied\r\nto text on a computer screen that she has pioneered.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i dont understand that part of your entry about the guy\r\nthat makes you laugh and cry on the inside.  does the crying\r\npart have anything to do with the laughing, or is it an\r\nunrelated side effect of knowing this person?</P>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2536,825,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','do you ever find that giving somebody a massage relaxes you\r\nas much as it did them?  happens to me all the time.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2537,819,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','but free speech shouldn\\\'t be bought.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2538,834,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>long articles are a good way of keeping the dillitants\r\naway.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ni am tired.  we (peter, elly, and i) drove forty miles to\r\nobtain some krispy kreme donuts last night.  it was fun. \r\nthe donuts were not as good as mrs. johnson\\\'s though.  not\r\neven by a long shot.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\n  i am fat.  i will take your advice smile lots and run and\r\nstuff.  i dont want to commit to cleaning right now.  i feel\r\nmore like going back to sleep.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nas far as the spring fling goes, i dont think i will be\r\nhaving one this may.  i dont want one at the moment.  i\r\nwould like to just take a rain check for some time in\r\ndecember when i get back from egypt.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nuhg, i feel like a rolley pollie.  so fat.  so fat.</P>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2539,834,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'dj1_luna','::blush::',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2540,834,'2002-03-05 20:17:36',17,'austin to weeb','<P>a poem of two sets of two matching lines, ahem:</P>\r\n\r\n<PRE>\r\ni am coming over         \r\ni want that book\r\nand i am going to run\r\nbecause my ass is fat\r\n</PRE>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2541,830,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','ok. gotcha.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2542,834,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','i thought egypt was in 2003',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2543,834,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','I thought 2003 was hong kong? When is Tokoyo? I am \r\ngoing to take you guys/gals to Pataya, Thailand in 2005. \r\nBetter start working on that ass austin. ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2544,834,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','<p>I want pictures, DAMN IT! Now get to work.</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2545,835,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','<p>and what are those people doing now? I think they \r\nare living life, seeking a new experience... looking for \r\nsomething new to freak on. Maybe this is all happening \r\njust in time for <a \r\nhref=\'http://www.austinchronicle.com/issues/dispatch/2\r\n001-04-27/big_cover.jpg\' target=new> the second coming</a>.</p>',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2546,835,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','\ni\\\'ve been too lazy to look for a job. does that count as a \nrecession?\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2547,828,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<pre>\r\nin dmv form\r\nwaiting, wainting, wait\r\nlife is line\r\n</pre>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2548,835,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','Damnit, too late. Those hip young kids. I can never catch \r\nup.',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2549,834,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','yes, yes, 2003.  i am just getting kind of antsy.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nbmg: what do you want pictures of?',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2550,834,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','i want pictures of all the authors... all that can supply \r\nthem... for a project of mine...\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2551,836,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<H1>I USED TO LOVE YOUR SHOW!</h1>\r\n\r\n<P>email me and i will get you a shell.</P>\r\n<P>austin@swinney.org</P>',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2552,834,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','I can\\\'t wait until it\\\'s warm enough to go swimming on a\r\nregular basis.  :-)  Figure, what, another few weeks at\r\nmost?\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2553,834,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','austin swinney at weeb\'s:\r\n<p>\r\n\"ooaargh i\'m scratching my fat! i\'m scratching my fat cause it ee-itches!@!\" (mad scrabbling sounds)\r\n</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2554,819,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>Free speech will be influenced by the forces of \r\ncapitalism (or as I like to call it : \\\"people having to \r\neat\\\"). This doesn\\\'t neccesarily preclude your own speech, \r\nbut you have to realize that resources effect your ability \r\nto promote your viewpoint. Speaking beyond your personal \r\nvoice (stickers, posters, advertising, skywriting) costs \r\nmoney. This means that it is not \\\"free\\\" as in \\\"no cost\\\", \r\nbut only \\\"free\\\" as in \\\"you are allowed to say it.\\\"</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2555,835,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'yawn','\\\"it\\\'s cryin\\\' time again..\\\"\r\n',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2556,834,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','austin. road trip to texas. come on.\r\n<br><br>\r\nbmg i will goto goodwill and get a fucked up prom dress and \r\nwear it for your birthday.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2557,834,'2002-03-05 20:17:36',17,'austin, hm','drive to texas.<BR><BR>\r\nthat is a long road trip, as road trips go.<BR><BR>\r\nyou will have to drive the whole way because i cannot be\r\ntrusted to stay within the speed limit.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2558,834,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','<p>to aus: did you ever pay your tickets from the \r\n<em>wyoming</em> trip?</p><p>bmg to le: If you wear \r\na prom dress, so will I. *all giggles*</p><p>austin \r\ndoesn\\\'t want to drive cuz his ass still hurts from when \r\nhe mooved out there...</p>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2559,834,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo to le','elly. you big jerk. i\\\'ll be in sf during bmg\\\'s birthday. \r\nyou can\\\'t go to austin.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2560,834,'2002-03-05 20:17:36',17,'austin to jo','elly wasn\\\'t going to really. see you in sf :)',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2561,835,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'a kid','who wonders why all these laid-off kids are acting like they \r\nare auto industry factory workers who have dedicated their \r\nentire lives to the company only to be swept out the door a \r\nfew years before retirement.\r\nget off your ass and find something else to do. you\\\'re young, \r\nand influential. you certainly managed to do a number on my \r\ntown while i was away.\r\n',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2562,835,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','there is really little i can say about migrant tech workers\r\ndriving up market values and suckling their paychecks until\r\nthe fat spills all over the land except that i like being an\r\nauto worker and i really want to continue to be an auto\r\nworker.  it beats the hell out of making shopping carts.  \r\n<BR><BR>\r\nas for your town, well, if the city had not lured in\r\ncorporations with tax abatement, and dreams of becoming a\r\ntechnopolis in the new millinium, you would not have ever\r\nseen the higher prices of rent because of demand and greedy\r\nland lords.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ndo not try to blame anyone that you live in a beautiful\r\ncity.  start a revolution, grab all the land and do it your\r\nway.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nin the mean time, shun the Internet and go back to watching\r\ntelevision and reading books, or sit tight and wait because\r\nwe will all find jobs again and be back at blowing mad cash\r\nin your local bars and coffee places which should all have\r\nwireless internet by then.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\n<I>cheers!</I>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2563,835,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','i actually can\\\'t think of any of the laid of people i know\r\ncomplaining about it.  the media is excited by it.  it\\\'s fun\r\nto laugh at the kid who fell in the mud.  but what if the\r\nkid really likes mud?  is it still fun to laugh?\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2564,836,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'LinearB','Robo..\r\n\r\nCan I get a shell...\r\n\r\nI made my firewall too mean.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2565,839,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'LinearBenway','So When\\\'s the Swinney.Austin Party?',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2566,837,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Linear','My mother fell down last Friday. She\\\'s 78.\r\n\r\n<p>Apparently she fell face down, broke her\r\nglasses; one of her eyes was swollen shut,\r\nand I guess her arms and ribs are bruised\r\ntoo.\r\n\r\n<p>The scary thing was that she doesn\\\'t\r\nremember how she fell down.  ',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2567,839,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','<p>... what\\\'s up man? how are you doing? lets catch up \r\nsoon?</p>',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2568,839,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','that other guy hitting on linearb\\\'s ex girlfriend...  i\r\nslept with his ex girlfriend.  he got very mad.  made me\r\nwish i had not.  it was not worth it.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2569,837,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','my god, auntie. this is horrible. i\\\'m not a prayer but i \noffered one up anyway just now. i hope she recovers \nquickly.\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2570,837,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','twice my mom has fallen.  once she broke her elbow and\r\nknocked a tooth out and another time she broke her arm. \r\nis it so scary because we invision our moms as being the\r\nones who take care of us?  is it scary to think we are the\r\nones who take care of them now?  i don\\\'t think i could ever\r\ndo as good a job.\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2571,839,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'LinearBenway','You mean you slept with this ex? You never told me. Her \r\ndefinition of \\\"sex\\\" must have been quite a surprise. \r\n<BR><BR><img \r\nsrc=\\\"http://www.desertbooks.com/gallery/itsquietnow.jpg\\\">',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2573,833,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'kat','well im not really in OKC...just nowhere, Oklahoma. or you \r\ncould say...somewhere South of Kansas City. ha. laughing \r\nand crying. youve never loved and lost the comedian type i \r\ncan see. the ones who arent ever serious about anything. \r\nthe ones who make you feel like any hurt you might have is \r\njust \\\'oh so petty\\\' ...im the overreactor, the radioactive \r\nemotional rollercoster. love me he says. then boy watch \r\nout...your job is fair game for dicing and slicing. so are \r\nyour friends. dont forget your family. and of course we \r\njust have to through in a good gut rolling belly laugh or \r\ntwo about the way you look.  of course...its just all in \r\ngood fun. cause i love you.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2574,839,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','no no no, i slept wit the ex of the guy sitting indian style\r\non the chair.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2578,837,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'xepmom','To Xep: Don\\\'t you worry about your momma, sweet child. I fall \r\ndown because I don\\\'t pay attention and crash around too fast. \r\nTo auntie: post-op advice for your mother: Ensure that she \r\ndoes her deep breathing regularly to prevent complications \r\nand don\\\'t let her get constipated (a side effect of pain \r\nmeds). Pooping in the hospital is difficult enough.\r\n',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2576,839,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'LinearBenwa','You shoulda slept with my ex instead. I wouldn\\\'t have \r\nminded.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2577,839,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'LuckyLinear','Besides, who is he to make a big deal. He was at <B>my</B> \r\nstore, hitting on <B>my</B> ex-girlfriend. He was probably \r\ndrinking <B>my</B> liquor as well.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2579,834,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo to austin','oh i know. i just really enjoy calling elly a big jerk. :)',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2580,837,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','um i would <b>freak out</b> if anything happened to my \r\nmonster mama. and i mean <b>FREAK. OUT.</b>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2581,839,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','Austin wanted me to flip his SUV over on its side... i \r\nsaw that fucker not to long ago... kembro the \r\nassmuncher... ',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2582,839,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','to Linear: is that a picture of your x-girl?!!!',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2583,839,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','you slept with kimbro\\\'s ex?',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2584,836,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','Linear: firewall barking again?  barkbarkbarkbarkbark  :-)\r\nI\\\'ll have a static ip at the new place so you should be able \r\nto let me ssh in to ga if need be.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2585,833,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','so he\\\'s an ass, in other words.  I\\\'m a joker, always have \r\nbeen, but the critical distinction is to laugh with people \r\ninstead of at them.  I think you should put a bag of flaming \r\ncrap on his doorstep.  But maybe I\\\'m an extremist.  ;-)\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2586,839,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','TTTTTTOOOOOOOOOOOOOGGGGGGGGGGGGGAAAAAAAAAAA!!!!!!!!<br>\r\nOK, I just felt like saying that.  I feel the urge to cover \r\nmyself in mustard and run seminaked through the streets \r\ncarrying a keg of beer in one hand and a bevy of nubile young \r\nwomen in the other. But maybe I\\\'m getting out of hand.  \r\nMaybe.  You never know what might be an appropriate response \r\nto life.<br>\r\nSeriously though, how does this weekend sound for a \r\nswinney.org@austin party?  If no parties @ people\\\'s places, \r\nthen maybe a meet at a pub?\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2587,839,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>jesus people, you all know each other from everywhere. \r\njust go get a beer tonight.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>it is not like you have to work tomorrow or something\r\n=-)</P>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2588,839,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','notice the tall boy phenomena of trying to shrink down his \nvolume so as to seem less gigantuan. cute.\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2589,837,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','<P>Sweet gramma auntie, heal quickly and rest. I offer up \r\nsome happy mama news for the ones who may not be so \r\nhappy.</P>\r\n<P>Yesterday was my mother\\\'s 5-year survival mark in her \r\nfight with breast cancer. Her cancer had metasticized when \r\nthey found it in 1996, and took her left breast and most of \r\nthe lymph nodes on that side. She was diagnosed with stage \r\n4 cancer, pretty much the most serious stage of the \r\ndisease. Nobody knew what would happen.</P>\r\n<P>Now that is has been 5 years, she has an %85 -%90 chance \r\nof living her full life span without a relapse. It is just \r\namazing to me what she has accomplished, she is an angel. \r\nIf she makes it to 10 years, she has almost no chance of a \r\nrelapse. I can\\\'t wait for that anniversary.</P>',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2590,835,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','I wonder if #a came first or #19.  I think the numeric\r\nchannels were first.  As I recall the first time I got on\r\nIRC was like early \\\'94, or something.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2591,839,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','I miss desert.  cool place.  what ever happened to that\r\ncrazy chair statue?',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2592,839,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Linear to Orion','The treebase was completely rotted. The <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.matthewjfeiner.com\\\">artist</a> didn\\\'t dry \r\nand cure the wood properly. Who knows where the chair went. \r\nI had no room for anything when I closed. I could use some \r\nof that furniture now.\r\n\r\nOrion call me, cause you never answer your phone.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2593,840,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'EasyLinear','I remember your motorcycle. You kept it parked at ibomb \r\nmost of the time. BruBru said to me: \\\"Nothing good is going \r\nto come out of that motorcycle.\\\"\r\n\r\n<p>I wonder if randy\\\'s motorcycle is still parked at that \r\nbuilding.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2594,840,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','what the hell does that mean?<BR><BR>\r\nrandy\'s motorbike was nice and roboteckie.  i should have bought it off hm for peanuts.',4,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2595,840,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Danielle','Whats wrong with Honda Civics?',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2596,840,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','they are too perfect.  my car doesnt need me and it makes\r\nthe relationship seem too one sided.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ni have to feel wanted.  the car just goes and goes.  never a\r\nhitch.  never needs to be oiled in the joints, never needs\r\nnew shocks, never needs a tune up.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ni am bored with it.\r\n',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2597,840,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Punky Brewster','\r\n    I drive a forklift :/',6,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2598,839,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'jo','i\\\'m definitely pro - doing something before this weekend as \r\ni will be out of town this friday to may 15.',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2599,840,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'Henry','Yes, Punky. Remember I bought that forklift for you so you \r\ncould take Brandon to the vet. I took a lot of baby photos \r\nto pay for that lift. I hope you are happy.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\nLove,\r\n<br>\r\nHenry P. Warnimont',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2600,840,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','austin\\\'s bike was so nice! i rode it once, but i almost \r\nwrecked. adamajah saw that. i still think that a scooter \r\nwould be nice... jitka has a scooter, i wanna buy it from \r\nher.',0,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2601,841,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'bmg','can i see it? the old site? is it another address?',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2602,841,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>bender, you know at least one of everybody.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>this all strikes me as really sad.  sad to have the sum\r\ntotal of all that work on a crappy box in your living room. \r\nsad that it is ...  sad.  i think your association is of the\r\nbox and Cinnamon is beautiful.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i hope they pay your dsl bill, but i understand if you\r\nare willing to take the bill for the rest of ibooks\\\' time on\r\nthis Internet.  maybe the box will get cracked and the\r\ncontent dispersed out on the Net to live forever.</P>',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2603,842,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','stand on your head.\r\ncut your hair with nail clippers.\r\nmake up a song and go to safeway and sing it loudly as you \r\nwalk really slowly down each aisle. maybe without even \r\nlifting your feet off the ground, just sliding.\r\nstick your finger in your ear and see how long you can hold \r\nit there without laughing.\r\nor my favorite is to take the names of people you know and \r\nswitch the first letters of their names, i.e. sue and carl = \r\ncue and sarl. sarah and barb = barah and sarb.\r\ngood luck.\r\n',1,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2604,842,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','grab darwin and come make pad thai with me and matsukaze,\r\n6:45.',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2605,842,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>It\\\'s tuesday. Tues/Thurs dinner no workie. Mon/Wed/Fri ? \r\nMe like Thai Food.</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwONG',3,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2606,842,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>Oh, and simon. I like that game too. The only people I \r\nreally play it with are Mulder and Scully. I think they\\\'d \r\nbe much funnier if they were Sculder and Mully.</P>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin',2,0,0,0,NULL,'en'),(2607,840,'2001-05-04 19:41:22',0,'<b>le</b>','<img src=\\\"http://elly.org/img/camino/camino6.gif\\\" \r\nborder=\\\"1\\\" alt=\\\"\