i\\\'m afraid of.  cuz i never have \r\nanything to say to them, or any useful questions to ask them \r\nso i can just listen.  awkward. </P>\r\n\r\n<P>anyway jem seems ubercool and i am actually jealous that \r\nyou are meeting her.  though i will meet her someday, there \r\nis no hurry.  so, enjoy.</P>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'64.3.15.93','en'),(2693,854,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p> too bad he already changed his dj name \r\nto \\\"noahphex\\\"..</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n<p> people know people I know from vrave\r\n',2,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(2694,855,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>this is part of a syndrome called \\\"night terrors.\\\" my \r\nmother suffer(ed/s) from them and they are extremely \r\ndisturbing to her. She occassionally will have a nightmare \r\nwhich she wakes up from and is confused from for a few \r\nminutes. Very scary to hear if you don\\\'t know that\\\'s what \r\nit is..</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<a \r\nhref=http://www.nightterrors.org/>http://www.nightterrors.or\r\ng/</a>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n',1,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(2695,859,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<PRE>\r\n(sara|jem|simon)++\r\n</PRE>\r\n<P>simon is not scarey, unless you are recovering from being\r\nbadass--trying to kick the habit.</P>\r\n',2,0,0,0,'64.51.232.105','en'),(2696,859,'2001-05-05 17:17:35',0,'chaya','dude.  simon is the bestest drinking pal around.  period.  \r\ni am looking forward to running around being a badass with \r\nher tomorrow.',6,0,0,0,'158.252.211.146','en'),(2697,859,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','\r\ni slept in, i am the grandmamma. all hail!\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(2698,859,'2001-05-05 19:50:51',0,'pecker','<b>FULL OF GRACE!!!</b>',2,0,0,0,'209.178.128.18','en'),(2699,859,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','<b>yawn</b><p>\r\n+-stretch-+<p>\r\ngood morning, pals.<br>\r\ni feel a little fuzzy.<br>\r\nthanks for coming out last night, austin.<br>\r\na slow evening but we got to see a little fire, right.<br>\r\nas soon as the el is back running, i promise we\\\'ll go \r\ndrinking in that.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(2700,859,'2001-05-05 20:50:37',0,'bmg','<p>I wanna go drinking with Austin! You are lucky Simon; \r\nAustin is fun to drink Maker\\\'s Mark with... The best \r\ndrinking experience that I had with austin was his funeral \r\nwake at Club Deville... what a hoot. I went drinking with \r\nMsCreant, Dj_luna, SarahMay, and ZB last night... Ended the \r\nnight at Oilcan\\\'s, Luna danced. Tonight is Sonic Youth, \r\noutside in the rain at Stubbs. </p>',1,0,0,0,'64.123.9.81','en'),(2701,862,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>it is good to see you putting your sad time to <BR>good use. \r\ncooking dinner for the crew the other night was also <BR>good. \r\nthat food filled a brief hole in my life.  i look forward<BR> to\r\nmore dining experiences.  i can cook some things too.</P>',2,0,0,0,'64.51.232.105','en'),(2702,861,'2001-05-06 03:59:52',0,'alanna','<P>\r\nerm, no one talking?\r\n</P>\r\n<P>\r\nanyhow.&nbsp; i\\\'ve never had one myself, but i heard from a \r\nfriend who does that the smaller ring you get the less \r\nchance it\\\'ll mess up your teethies.&nbsp; her ringlet is so \r\nsuper tiny, you can only tell it\\\'s there when it catches \r\nthe light.&nbsp; which i always thought was a neat effect.\r\n</P>',1,0,0,0,'156.3.140.245','en'),(2703,861,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','i used to dip coppenhagen and it fucked up my teath and\r\ngums. does that count?\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ncyan, i hung out with your man tonight.  we watched\r\nhillbilly tap dancing movies.  i kind of expected to see you\r\nthere but nope.',2,0,0,0,'64.51.232.105','en'),(2704,861,'2001-05-06 06:10:18',0,'Danielle','How long have you had it? I don\\\'t have my labret but I do \r\nhave my lip done and it took awhile for everything to \r\nsettle down. If you think the jewellary is wrong, then it \r\nprobably is. Check out something with a flat backing, like \r\nthis http://tonguestud.com/labrets.html but dont go too \r\nshort because of swelling and such. I dont know what \r\nexactly a fishtail is so maybe this is what you have \r\nalready... Also I\\\'ve found with piercings that if they just \r\nwont heal right (after quite awhile) then I\\\'ll switch the \r\njewellary. Sometimes your body just doesn\\\'t like the \r\nmaterial or the shape etc and new jewellary can work \r\nwonders. GOOD LUCK!! =)',1,0,0,0,'24.68.193.134','en'),(2705,861,'2001-05-06 06:11:26',0,'Danielle','Oh you did say flatback. Duh?! Is it close enough to your \r\nlip to put a ring in it? That might helping healing.. \r\nanyways.. enough from me ;)',1,0,0,0,'24.68.193.134','en'),(2706,863,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','<BR>\r\nI had to be a dead body in a student film once, after I was \r\npoisoned by a jealous ex or something like that.\r\nI was all pale and bluishpurple. It was kind of scary \r\nlooking in the mirror and seeing myself as what I\\\'d look \r\nlike left dead for a while. My best friend was not happy \r\nwhen she saw me all made up for this part.',0,0,0,0,'203.96.111.202','en'),(2707,861,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','the labret definitely fucked with my gums. i played with it \r\na lot though. as far as redness, try soaking the corner of \r\na washcloth in hot seasalt water, and applying that to it. \r\nit will help it keep from getting infected, and that should \r\nhelp redness go away. :)\r\n<br><br>\r\nas far as jewelry, i have a really nice flat jewel in mine \r\nthat i got from body manipulations on 16th. it was really \r\nexpensive tho! i bet you could get a nice one online \r\nsomewhere for cheaper.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(2708,861,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','also! you could get a \\\"fishtail\\\" which i hear destroys \r\nteeth less. i have never tried it tho. there are some \r\npictures of a fishtail here: <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.bodycircle.com/labret_jewelry.htm\\\">http://w\r\nww.bodycircle.com/labret_jewelry.htm</a>. ',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(2709,861,'2001-05-06 09:15:08',0,'jeb(ro)','(based on observation, education, and experimentation:)\r\n\r\n+ the redness *should* go away quickly - a couple days - if \r\nthere are no allergic reactions or infections.  if it \r\npersists - go back to your piercer and get some aftercare --\r\n> (definitely part of the job)\r\n\r\n+ a large flatback is the preferred piece of jewelry to \r\nstart with.  it helps the inner mouth heal more rapidly.  \r\nthe teeth damage issue is more of a long term, repetitive \r\nclicking problem.  i would advise keeping the piece you \r\nhave until the initial healing is completed. If you change \r\nthe piece now - you will essentially be repiercing in the \r\nsame spot which could result in scar tissue trapped inside \r\nthe healing flesh.  And regarding rings: they are \r\ndefinitely trickier to heal because of their more mobile \r\nnature.   Now...after saying all this - comfort is \r\nimportant so if it\\\'s really bothering you - i would say \r\nagain to return to your piercer and talk it over with \r\nhim/her.',0,0,0,0,'195.122.213.82','en'),(2710,861,'2001-05-06 12:29:01',0,'cyantist','right on!  so helpful!  i *heart* swinney :) thank you',1,0,0,0,'64.172.164.74','en'),(2711,862,'2001-05-06 12:38:02',0,'cyantist','i\\\'m sorry you are sad love.  however, discovering this about \r\nyourself is quite a gift.. don\\\'t you think?',1,0,0,0,'64.172.164.74','en'),(2712,864,'2001-05-06 13:19:30',0,'cait','What are your feelings on pipes, clove cigarettes, cigars, \r\nand other fancysmancy light-and-smoke contraptions? \r\nNon-nicotine? et cetera?<p>Just out of \r\ncuriousity/encouraging discussion? ',0,0,0,0,'63.77.235.17','en'),(2713,865,'2001-05-06 15:08:55',0,'bmg','offering plate will go round.',1,0,0,0,'64.123.8.178','en'),(2714,864,'2001-05-06 18:15:13',0,'mojo23','My thoughts (to cait) on the other, fancier smoking devices,\nis that there is no beneficial difference, except in\ncool-factor .  They still allow you to take nicotine into\nyour body, and in fact they seem more *evil* because they\nundermine the negative aspects.  They make smoking seem more\nfun, even though the tobacco you put into your fancy pipe is\njust as harmful as the stuff they put into tailor-mades.\n\nIf you smoke, and cannot stop, try to grow and cure your\nown, or get your hands on some really good natural tobacco.\n(American spirits are ok,but they are owned by one of the\nbig-ass toxic nic companies, philip morris or rjr, etc.)\nYou won\\\'t avoid the nicotine (just the extra they pump, or\nbreed, into the leading national brands,) but you will avoid\nthe other nasties they stuff ciggies full of.\n\nClove cigarettes are usually not filtered, and are fuckin\\\'\nstrong, therefore not any better for you, perhaps worse.\n\nTry sucking on candy, penises, fingers, pens, anything to\nstop sucking on toxic cigarettes. I stopped smoking\ncigarettes a number of years ago by smoking a lot more hash.\n',3,0,0,0,'158.252.216.217','en'),(2715,864,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','<p>I think part of the key to quitting is honestly wanting \r\nto and getting over the idea that \\\"life is simply better \r\nwith tobacco\\\". I\\\'ve been able to quit for days/weeks at a \r\ntime, but it\\\'s more of just a challenge -- I don\\\'t \r\ngenuinely <i>want</i> to quit, so I go back to it.</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(2716,866,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','you better pay that ticket.',3,0,0,0,'64.51.232.105','en'),(2717,864,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','yeah, smoke more hash;-)\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.78.199','en'),(2718,866,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','i got a parking ticket in boston too. ',6,0,0,0,'64.229.138.140','en'),(2719,866,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','you have two sacks?\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.78.199','en'),(2720,835,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','the media frenzy now is that non-existant energy crisis we \r\nare all talking about. how about getting SUV\\\'S off the road. \r\nand while we are at it. how about decomissioning the M1-A1. \r\na gallon a mile is wicked. ',6,0,0,0,'64.229.138.140','en'),(2721,866,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>I miss dunkin donuts. Fucking California.\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin',5,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(2722,867,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','love is the finest weapon there is.  when all us little \r\npeople in all the nations are finally able to talk to each \r\nother, we\\\'ll make everyone see that the majority of us are \r\nso tired of all this arms race, missile defense, nation \r\nagainst nation, no regard for nature, pissing contest \r\nbullshit.  then the world will finally become what it \r\ndesires to be.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.78.199','en'),(2723,867,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>\\\"Music is the weapon of the future / believe it or not.. \r\nthe future is now\\\"</p>\r\n<p>-- AWOL One\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(2724,866,'2001-05-06 20:29:10',0,'chaya','there\\\'s dunkin donuts in both oregon and washington.  maybe \r\nyou ought to drive up and make a pilgrimage?',6,0,0,0,'158.252.215.166','en'),(2725,866,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>normally i keep a pretty low profile around here,\r\nespecially when it comes to confrontation, but i stop\r\nhere.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>dunkin\' donuts sucks ass.  why anyone (DARWIN) would\r\ncurse an entire state for not having dunkin\' donuts is not\r\nunderstandable.  i\'m sure i could arrange for a seven-eleven\r\nin texas to fedex overnight one of their \'fresh\' dunkin\'\r\ndonuts to you without any loss of quality!</p>\r\n\r\n<P>if you are attached to dunkin\' donuts, then maybe you\r\nshould come with me to texas to have a Mrs. Johnson\'s\r\ndonut.  my .50 cents stops there.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>and you didnt eat any of the donuts that i purchased and\r\nbrought to your house, even after you exlaimed, \"to cheap to\r\nspring for a dozen!\"  thus you must forfiet your statement\r\nthat you have an oppinion about donuts.  one cannot have an\r\noppinion about donuts, and pass up the opportunity to eat\r\none, especially when they are free.  especially when one has\r\njelly in it, just like you asked.</P> \r\n\r\n<P>p.s. dunkin\' donuts never handed me a free piping\r\nhot donut just for stopping by.  that is the hallmark\r\nof a true quality donut establishment.</P>',3,0,0,0,'64.51.232.105','en'),(2726,865,'2001-05-06 21:37:17',0,'sean','which costs more, RT airfare from SFO&lt;-&gt;Austin or\r\ngasoline?',1,0,0,0,'204.162.86.241','en'),(2727,866,'2001-05-06 22:45:39',0,'jo','clap clap clap!<BR>\r\nlemon-filled are my favorite. oh my god, lemon-filled from \r\nken\\\'s. oh good lord that\\\'s good shit.',1,0,0,0,'172.133.231.71','en'),(2728,866,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','in kaybek i stayed in a dunkin donuts motel (sortie 55).',6,0,0,0,'64.229.138.140','en'),(2729,866,'2001-05-07 00:09:23',0,'USA TODAY','Survey shows that 67% of americans LOVE THEIR JOBS!',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(2730,864,'2001-05-07 02:26:31',0,'cait','<p>well, what I meant when I wrote that was \\\'how do you feel \r\nabout smoking ANYTHING,\\\' hash included, which is why I \r\nincluded my comment about no nicotine. but in particular, I \r\nwas curious about Cyan\\\'s response. %)',0,0,0,0,'63.77.235.247','en'),(2731,864,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','i think it is romanic looking, and smells like ass.\r\n',4,0,0,0,'64.51.232.105','en'),(2732,864,'2001-05-07 03:58:58',0,'rusty','you go, girl...',1,0,0,0,'64.163.194.78','en'),(2733,862,'2001-05-07 04:01:48',0,'rusty','the psychological definition of depression is \\\"Repression \r\nof Emotion\\\".\r\n\r\nDepression is not an emotion in an of it self.  It is very \r\nblatantly trying to avoid emotion.\r\n\r\nA good thing to realize.',2,0,0,0,'64.163.194.78','en'),(2734,869,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p>what about getting him <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://elly.org/img/forsteve/muffin.jpg\\\">a pony like \r\nmuffin</a>? muffin is a very friendly pony.\r\n</p><p>\r