e it really feels like the worst is \r\nover.  at least this little bit is anyway.',2,0,0,0,'64.81.64.182','en'),(2754,873,'2001-05-07 19:20:38',0,'going down south','you cannot enjoy a sunset if you can\\\'t leave your bed',0,0,0,0,'209.86.4.120','en'),(2755,866,'2001-05-07 19:26:54',0,'da','darwin, i\\\'m tempted to just say that you\\\'re a little shit \r\nand that if you hate it so much here because all the people \r\nsuck and even the donuts are unsatisfactory, you should \r\nleave.  but no!  instead, i will suggest that you acquaint \r\nyourself with any of the fine locally owned donut \r\nestablisments of the area.  i\\\'ve sampled the output of a \r\nnumber of these outfits, both in the east bay and the city, \r\nand have rarely been disappointed.  they make a fine donut, \r\nand as an added bonus you\\\'re not adding to the bottom line \r\nof some giant corporate backed baked confection production \r\nand distrubtion juggernaut.',3,0,0,0,'64.81.64.182','en'),(2756,872,'2001-05-07 19:35:59',0,'erin','makers mark and coke. mmmm sweet! goes down tooo easy, yo.\r\n',2,0,0,0,'129.105.107.184','en'),(2757,868,'2001-05-07 19:47:58',0,'kat','<p>there is no good in being one\r\n\r\nyou are not.\r\n\r\n <br>\r\n\r\ndo you want me to jump through hoops?\r\nwalk water?\r\n\r\ni would give you the world if i could\r\n\r\n <br>\r\n\r\nall i have to spare \r\nall that i am.\r\n\r\n <br>\r\n\r\nbut there will be no walking on fiery coals \r\nwith bare skin \r\nburned raw\r\n\r\nthere is no worth in that\r\n\r\njust to see \r\nsomeone smile.\r\n<br>\r\nit only leaves me empty</p>\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'32.100.137.31','en'),(2758,874,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','i think about this problem you mention often and for years.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ni have been considering how to write archival software.  are\r\nyou a programmer?',3,0,0,0,'64.51.232.105','en'),(2759,872,'2001-05-07 20:44:34',0,'t.m.','mushroom tea, of course.  mmmmmm...to see...',0,0,0,0,'212.20.98.106','en'),(2760,874,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','but then i think that there are already sites all over the\r\nplace that cache the internet.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ni guess what i think it comes down to is just what you said,\r\nmid twenty something identity crises where people decide\r\nthey are tired of feeling responsible or attached to their\r\nwebsites so they delete them.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nlike elly\\\'s webcam which i think still has \\\"oh okay\\\" in the\r\ntitle bar from the last time she took her whole website down\r\nand then put it back up.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ni have a couple websites that i am just sick of seeing in my\r\ndirectories.  they are just annoying.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nmy head aches really bad right now and there is no advil\r\nwhatever left.',4,0,0,0,'64.51.232.105','en'),(2761,874,'2001-05-07 21:32:55',0,'blurker','Programmer is not what I am most frequently paid to be.  In \r\nfact, I\\\'m confident that if you interrogated me at any \r\nlength, you would not be afterwards likely to refer to me \r\nas a programmer.  But I had been tinkering with the \r\nlogistics of a model wherein web publishers could \r\neffortlessly \\\"self-archive\\\" to a database.  I would gladly \r\ncede the reigns to a more capable coder with a more clever \r\nconcept.  I ph3r that I am more technically suited to the \r\nmanual leg work of tracking down old self-archived content \r\nthat is no longer online.  I bet a lot of those old sites \r\nare on coffee-stained floppy disks somewhere and should \r\nreally be moved to an accessible central archive.  Remind \r\nme to wish I\\\'d done this after it\\\'s already too late; that \r\nlist is getting pretty long.  I can\\\'t help hoping that \r\nsomeone has already followed this train of thought further \r\nthan you or certainly I.',1,0,0,0,'12.75.78.254','en'),(2762,872,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','i will take this moment to say (in gus\\\'s absence)<br>\r\n<br>\r\nBUDWEISER 40z. duh!\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(2763,872,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>I don\\\'t like drinking a whole lot, but I like Vodka \r\nGimlets. Good Vodka + Roses Lime juice, salt the glass.\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin',2,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(2764,874,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','history is problematic. ',6,0,0,0,'64.229.140.30','en'),(2765,870,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>I never said that Snow Crash \\\"sucks dick.\\\" I said that I \r\nthink it\\\'s an action adventure novel with one really good \r\nidea in 500 pages. I think 500 pages is excessive for one \r\ngood idea. I am spoiled by <a \r\nhref=http://www.philipkdick.com>Philip K Dick</a>.</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n',3,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(2766,874,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p><a \r\nhref=http://www.textfiles.com>www.textfiles.com</a><br>\r\n<a href=http://hoe.nu>hoe.nu</a><br>\r\n<a href=http://defacto2.net/scene-\r\narchive>defacto2.net/scene-archive</a><p>\r\n<p>\r\nSome starting points..\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin',2,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(2767,870,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>\r\nis 500 pages excessive  for entertainment value?\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ni get a bit tired of the ancient religion corn and\r\nspeculation. but if it were not there, the book would be\r\nkind of pointless.  i suppose that is what you meant though,\r\nthat the book is kind of pointless.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nsometimes i forget that i read books because the\r\npointlessness of spending hours going over them compliments\r\nmy life so well these days.  i dont forget that very often,\r\njust when i am trying to find a good arguement to read them.\r\n</P>',4,0,0,0,'64.51.232.105','en'),(2768,868,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','that was a good entry chiamattt.  i actually read every \r\nword.  congrats on a weedless week :)',2,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(2769,875,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','sweeping was always my favorite chore.  it\\\'s tai chi.  \r\nsometimes i did the Turbo and started pop-locking on the \r\nceiling.',2,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(2770,872,'2001-05-07 22:53:31',0,'chaya','<p>ALLISON.  *sob*</p><p>i drink whiskey sours like they\\\'re \r\ngoing out of style.  and amaretto sours taste like candy.  \r\nsweet sweet boozey flavored candy.</p>',6,0,0,0,'158.252.241.115','en'),(2771,866,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i suggest that darwin acquaints himself with the locally \r\noperated \\\"donuts and chinese food\\\": a san francisco \r\ninstitution. 1 fry-a-lator, 2 cuisines!',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(2772,873,'2001-05-07 22:57:14',0,'kat','are you ready for the wake up call...when it comes will you \r\nknow what it is...will you flip the switch or make friends \r\nwith the dark...will you say goodnight to it all...will you \r\nfight it like a tiger or lick your wounds and \r\nwhimper...when the fear takes over do you let go...do you \r\nlust for it\r\n\r\n',4,0,0,0,'129.37.232.13','en'),(2773,854,'2001-05-07 23:13:09',0,'joyrider','<p><b>S5:</b>&nbsp;&nbsp;that\\\'s kind of what i\\\'d \r\nfigured.  bit late now.  i thought it was funny that they \r\ndemanded he turn over his websites in addition to the \r\n\\\"cease-and-desist\\\" - maybe they should\\\'ve asked for \r\nhis unsold mixtapes too...</p>\r\n\r\n<p><b>darwin:</b>&nbsp;&nbsp;vrave/spacebar \r\ncross-pollenization cuts the degrees of seperation way \r\ndown all over the place.  maybe we talked on vrave.  \r\nwho knows.</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'64.42.57.53','en'),(2774,608,'2001-05-07 23:29:36',0,'joyrider','<p>try these:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>chyna clugston-major\\\'s <b>blue monday</b><br>\r\nmod + new romantic + 2nd wave ska + hormones.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>evan dorkin\\\'s <b>fun with milk and cheese</b><br>\r\nviolent dairy products take on the mall.</p>\r\n',2,0,0,0,'64.42.57.53','en'),(2775,874,'2001-05-07 23:31:59',0,'pdo','Also, check http://www.archive.org/',2,0,0,0,'24.112.186.179','en'),(2776,875,'2001-05-08 00:16:50',0,'bmg','<p>haha. I still don\\\'t remember doing that! I am sure that \r\nI do it often.</p>\r\n<p>I am sitting here at work, Texas School for the Blind, \r\nand swinney.org looks amazing using lynx. There are a few \r\nproblems with reading it -- such as the list of authors \r\ncomes up first, then the article... so it seems as though \r\nnothing is there. but for the most part - it works. Also, \r\nwhen viewing it using the school\\\'s computers there is no \r\ncolor - it is all b&w... which is interesting, the front \r\npage is white instead of black... kinda funny...</p><p>ok I \r\nam done.</p>\r\n<pre>\r\n\\\"From the Halls of Montezuma\r\nTo the Shores of Tripoli;\r\nWe fight our country\\\'s battles\r\nOn the land as on the sea;\r\nFirst to fight for right and freedom\r\nAnd to keep our honor clean;\r\nWe are proud to claim the title\r\nof United States Marine.\r\n\r\n\\\"Our flag\\\'s unfurled to every breeze\r\nFrom dawn to setting sun;\r\nWe have fought in ev\\\'ry clime and place\r\nWhere we could take a gun;\r\nIn the snow of far-off Northern lands\r\nAnd in sunny tropic scenes;\r\nYou will find us always on the job--\r\nThe United States Marines.\r\n\r\n\\\"Here\\\'s health to you and to our Corps\r\nWhich we are proud to serve\r\nIn many a strife we\\\'ve fought for life\r\nAnd never lost our nerve;\r\n\r\nIf the Army and the Navy\r\nEver look on Heaven\\\'s scenes;\r\nThey will find the streets are guarded\r\nBy United States Marines.\\\"\r\n</pre>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'65.65.110.189','en'),(2777,874,'2001-05-08 00:28:48',0,'blurk','Packets of gratitude to Swinney.  Archive dot org is a \r\nfascinating (to me) project.  I\\\'ve just written for more \r\ninfo.  Thanks to all.',1,0,0,0,'12.75.57.187','en'),(2778,869,'2001-05-08 02:38:17',0,'mojo23','Muffin has a great butt.\nThanks S5, and I did give him a big smooch for you...\nDwarves are a good idea, any ideas where I might rent one\nfor a few weeks, just to see if i like them?',4,0,0,0,'158.252.212.159','en'),(2779,873,'2001-05-08 02:48:41',0,'mojo23','i liked paxil until it sapped my sex drive.  Then it soon\nbecame \\\'beer and pot and nothing else.\\\'\nHard to get off of, but now I often feel drawn to it again.\n It worked for a few months, then i just started noticing\nweirdness...sleep problems, sex problems.\nlame all around.\nbut, as mentioned above, you can\\\'t go look at the skyline,\nor even find your bong, if you can\\\'t get your head out from\nunder the covers.',3,0,0,0,'158.252.212.159','en'),(2780,866,'2001-05-08 05:10:47',0,'sic','duh. crispy creme donuts...people request that shit from \r\neast.',0,0,0,0,'4.16.224.142','en'),(2781,872,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','Black Devils and Fog Cutters on the house.',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(2782,874,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','I spent three days archiving the contents of neoism.org \r\nwhen it looked like it might go under.',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(2783,873,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','From the people I know, it seems like the best purpose for \r\nantidepressants is a temporary one to make the hard (and \r\nnecessary) work of figuring yourself out and breaking \r\ndifferent patterns of behavior and thinking a little easier.',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(2784,873,'2001-05-08 07:03:27',0,'rusty','kat - Yes!  ;)\r\n<p>\r\nMad Moll - I think that\\\'s probably true...  The one time I \r\nused them, I think they did help me effect my situation...  \r\nSince then I\\\'ve wondered if that was a good thing...  But \r\nthen I realized there was no point wondering...  it was \r\njust a thing...  Life has changing points, shit happens, \r\nenjoy it...  I\\\'ve spent so much time regretting, and being \r\nunhappy...  I feel empowered when I can get over it \r\nmyself...  I tell you what, I loved X... but if it does \r\npermanently lower seratonin, I\\\'m not gonna try it again...  \r\nI already had enough mood problems before my period of \r\ndoing X a lot...  I\\\'ve been tempted to take anti-\r\ndepressants a few times since the one time I did (about 7 \r\nyears ago)... but my main reason for avoiding them, was \r\nseeing the effect on people that were close to me who have \r\non them...  I\\\'ve known multiple people over the years who \r\nhave taken various versions, and although they were always \r\ngenerally happier, they did not at all seem like \r\nthemselves... or seem really alive... about six months ago, \r\nI would\\\'ve seriously benefited from them...  But I\\\'m glad I \r\nwas able to come through it myself...  I feel much fuller \r\nthan I did the time I did use them to escape the cycle I \r\nwas in then...  blah blah...  ;)',6,0,0,0,'64.163.194.78','en'),(2785,873,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i am tired of this topic of conversation.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(2786,872,'2001-05-08 07:33:59',0,'rusty','I have a sweet tooth...\r\n<p>\r\nmix some nice irish cream, coffee liquer, and vodka...  \r\nblended it\\\'s a mudslide, normal, it\\\'s a rattle-snake... \r\nprobably other names... super tastey... yum...',2,0,0,0,'64.163.194.78','en'),(2787,875,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','that is a beautiful song.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ni wonder what kdog does without knowing it?',3,0,0,0,'64.51.232.105','en'),(2788,872,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','cocaine',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(2789,873,'2001-05-08 09:57:29',0,'rusty','<p>\r\nelly\\\'s the boss...  I forbid anymore comments!  ;)',6,0,0,0,'64.163.194.78','en'),(2790,877,'2001-05-08 11:31:08',0,'designer vagina','yes. women now think their vagina\\\'s aren\\\'t good enough. \r\nthey can go to their favorite plastic surgeon and get nice, \r\npuffy labias to satsify the men in their lives.\r\n\r\nhttp://www.jendajournal.com/jenda/vol1.1/Dvagina.html',2,0,0,0,'66.68.34.51','en'),(2791,872,'2001-05-08 11:39:05',0,'Joanna','Thank you all.  Invitations are of course, in the mail. \r\nExcept for the person that suggested the armpit thing.  \r\nHaving my armpits once was good fodder for the weekly \r\nlaughing  lunch with my friends, but little more.   ',1,0,0,0,'203.167.158.181','en'),(2792,872,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','assmowers and beaver shots',0,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(2793,877,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','LOL',0,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(2794,879,'2001-05-08 16:36:24',0,'bmg','',1,0,0,0,'66.68.78.158','en'),(2795,879,'2001-05-08 16:41:19',0,'zb','i am truly sorry',0,0,0,0,'216.171.37.54','en'),(2796,879,'2001-05-08 16:46:40',0,'texticle','<TABLE width=250><TR><TD>\r\n     <p><font size=\"4\" face=\"Georgia, Times New Roman,\r\nTimes, serif\" color=\"#CC6633\">Head \r\n          Shrinking Made Easy</font></p>\r\n        <p><font size=\"3\" face=\"Georgia, Times New Roman,\r\nTimes, serif\" color=\"#003366\">Just \r\n          a little sun and sand.</font></p>\r\n        <p><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial, Helvetica,\r\nsans-serif\" color=\"#333333\"><b>Arts \r\n          & Crafts<br>\r\n          </b></font>. . . . . . .<br>\r\n          <font color=\"#666666\" face=\"Arial, Helvetica,\r\nsans-serif\" size=\"1\">by \r\n          Dusty Bottoms</font><br>\r\n          \r\n        <p><br>\r\n          <font face=\"Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"\r\nsize=\"2\">March 23, \r\n          2000</font> | <font face=\"Times New Roman, Times,\r\nserif\" size=\"4\"><b>A</b></font><font face=\"Times New Roman,\r\nTimes, serif\" size=\"3\">lright, \r\n          I\'m going to tell everyone how to make a shrunken\r\nhead, and as far as \r\n          i know, it works. </font></p>\r\n        <p><font face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\"\r\nsize=\"3\">The first (and \r\n          most obvious) step of this uplifting experience is\r\nto obtain the noggin \r\n          of what used to be a living breathing human being.\r\nDepending how important \r\n          aesthetics are to you, taking your time and really\r\nlooking around for \r\n          a nice specimen might be something to consider.\r\nI\'ve never done looked \r\n          very hard, nor will I ever. I grab the already\r\ndead and relatively fresh \r\n          one I find. Once you have procured the head you\r\nare ready to begin. \r\n          </font> </p>\r\n        <p><font face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\"\r\nsize=\"3\"> At this point, \r\n          you\'re going to need a hammer or something of the\r\nsort: blunt, easy \r\n          to swing, etc. Gently (ha!) crack the entirety of\r\nthe skull except the \r\n          facial area. It needs to get to the point of being\r\nmushy, as if it were \r\n          a big spongey ball. </font>\r\n        <p><font face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\"\r\nsize=\"3\">Now, remove all \r\n          of the brain tissue..make sure to take out every\r\nbit you can, as to \r\n          not retard the curing process. After all brain\r\nmatter is removed, promptly \r\n          fill the melon up with hot sand and place on a\r\nflat surface. Be certain \r\n          the dead head will be exposed to any and all\r\nsunlight throughout the \r\n          entire day. This curing process of filling with\r\nhot sand and drying \r\n          out will cause the head to shrink slowly and needs\r\nto be done over a \r\n          period of days. Obviously, the more you repeat,\r\nthe smaller it gets. \r\n          When your creation has reached the desired size,\r\nempty out the remaining \r\n          sand and you\'ve got yerself a shrunken head! Have\r\nfun! </font></p>\r\n      \r\n</TD></TR></TABLE>',4,0,0,0,'64.51.232.105','en'),(2797,878,'2003-07-24 15:44:23',165,'joker','and there are those that say hope is the greatest machiavel \r\nof all, compelling us to endure untold suffering, beyond \r\nreason and good sense all for the sake of maintaining \r\nthis \\\"feeling\\\", this high-level abstraction, the nebulous \r\nintention that it might work out.  hope for some is the \r\ngreat mitigator, blunting the native hue of resolution with \r\nthe sicklied and pale cast of...',3,0,0,0,'207.8.25.110','en'),(2798,879,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','thinking about it  makes ambition seem absurd.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nsee you on the flip side, dawg.',4,0,0,0,'64.51.232.105','en'),(2799,866,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','no reflection on the donuts places out here, but for pure\r\nnostalgia points, nothing beats the stratospheric sketch\r\nfactor of a dunkins doznutz at 2am in the morning. and their\r\npowdered donuts with their EXCELLENT COFFEE. just fucking\r\nbrilliant. \r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(2800,860,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','yay for eoj. i like the oej. what is this \\\"swinney.org black\r\nsubmit form\\\" that you mention?\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(2801,880,'2001-05-08 17:49:11',0,'astronomy','maybe i\\\'m the afterglow. i\\\'m in  a band you know. way down. \r\nway down.',6,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(2802,879,'2001-05-08 17:49:49',0,'robotec9','<PRE>\r\nyo dawg,\r\n\r\ni just herd,\r\nyou got a bend in your brain\r\nkilled you on the spot,\r\ni hope it didn\\\'t hurt.\r\n\r\nthanks for showing me how to play tony hawk 360,\r\ndrinking beer and wearing Depends when you pissy\r\nthat shit was funny, i still tell the story\r\n\r\nyou could drink like a fish\r\nthere was never no stoppin\\\'\r\nkeg parties at the crib\r\neffin\\\' everyone\\\'s hoppin\r\n\r\nyour scope of underground hip hop\r\nwas cleaner than the trim of your crop\r\nsorry we never got to do that album\r\nor grab the mic and let drop\r\n\r\ni know you would have rocked\r\npeople would have stopped and stared\r\nwho is that honkey who raps with no fear?\r\nthat was my homey dusty bottoms,\r\npour out your beer.\r\n\r\n</PRE>',5,0,0,0,'64.51.232.105','en'),(2803,880,'2003-07-24 15:44:23',165,'joker','hey there mr zeera<br>\r\ncan i have your sweater<br>\r\ncause it\\\'s cold cold cold...',3,0,0,0,'207.8.25.110','en'),(2804,879,'2001-05-08 18:16:52',0,'bmg','<p>Dusty Bottoms</p>\r\n<p>A year ago this week you and my friends threw a\r\nsurprise party for me; a celebration of my arival into this \r\nworld. This year I was hoping you would be there again \r\nto celebrate the story of me. This year for my birthday I \r\nwill be celebrating the memory of you and your \r\nlife.</p><p> A christian man could blame God for your \r\ndeath. Had it been a death from a bullet we could \r\nblame the Government for lack of gun control. If it were \r\ndrugs that took the life from you, we could blame the \r\nDrug war. But no, there is no one to blame, there is \r\nnothing to blame. Taken in your sleep, your longest \r\ndream; I cry that you have good dreams my friend. </p>',1,0,0,0,'66.68.78.158','en'),(2805,880,'2001-05-08 18:18:46',0,'jo','and this little masochist is lifting up her dress.',1,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(2806,880,'2001-05-08 18:18:48',0,'jo','and this little masochist is lifting up her dress.',1,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(2807,880,'2001-05-08 18:21:20',0,'bmg','<p>call me joker. come hang out with me, joker. let us \r\ngo do what persons do, joker. we can babble about \r\nscat cats, email birds, go in circles for a while.</p> ',1,0,0,0,'66.68.78.158','en'),(2808,864,'2001-05-08 18:35:41',0,'cyantist','<p><br>\r\ncait..<br>\r\ni think that smoking a substance like marijuana or *perhaps* \r\nhash would be ok.  personally, i don\\\'t feel that i could \r\never become mentally or physically addicted to either.  i do \r\nfeel that smoking pot drastically helps with calming your \r\nnerves as you try to quit smoking.  however, i prefer \r\nsmoking nothing.  it depends on the person .. really.  if \r\nsomeone honestly knows in their heart that they would abuse \r\nany drug.. they should stop and never use it again or use it \r\nin absolute moderation.  does that answer your question?\r\n<br>',1,0,0,0,'205.142.76.11','en'),(2809,881,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<OL>\r\n<LI>work and hang out with friends\r\n<LI>get fired / quit\r\n<LI>code like hell on your project and hang out with friends\r\n<LI>get a job, work and hang out with your friends.\r\n<LI>also, there is working and coding your project, while\r\nsick of friends\r\n<LI>do nothing sometimes\r\n</OL>\r\n<P>that is just me.</P>',3,0,0,0,'64.51.232.105','en'),(2810,879,'2001-05-08 19:51:40',0,'erin for bmg and all:','Hopi Indian Prayer\r\n\r\nDo not stand at my grave and weep.\r\nI am not there, I do not sleep.\r\nI am a thousand winds that blow.\r\nI am the diamond glint on snow.\r\nI am the sunlight on the ripened grain.\r\nI am the gentle Autumn\\\'s rain. \r\n\r\nWhen you awaken in the morning hush,\r\nI am the swift uplifting rush\r\nof quiet birds in circled flight,\r\nI am the soft stars that shine at night. \r\n\r\nDo not stand at my grave and cry:\r\n I am not there, I did not die.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'129.105.107.184','en'),(2811,881,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i just sleep less.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(2812,881,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i just sacrifice the friends.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(2813,879,'2001-05-08 20:29:19',0,'bmg','i am smiling, thanks.',1,0,0,0,'66.68.78.158','en'),(2814,880,'2003-07-24 15:44:23',165,'joker','all the cops in the doughnut shop say<br>\r\nway<br>\r\no<br>\r\nway<br>\r\no o<br>\r\nway<br>\r\no<br>\r\nway<br>\r\no<br>\r\n<br>\r\nwalk like an egyptian',1,0,0,0,'207.8.25.110','en'),(2815,881,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','volcanos?',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(2816,862,'2001-05-08 21:15:23',0,'AIDS','Rob, I think you need to play King\\\'s Quest IV again. It has similar color schemes to the above, plus it involves literally the most irritating sequence in the history of adventure gaming: i.e., the peril of rosella trying to climb up a big tongue to tickle that hangy gross thing that I can\\\'t remember the name of. It\\\'s odd how that\\\'s the only decent King\\\'s Quest game. I\\\'ve been replaying Quest For Glory series recently. They are considerably better. Yet they don\\\'t have playful pan. Did I ever show you highway61 revisted, my AGI game? The Pimp from Leisure SUit Larry 1 tries to put out Rosella. And your avatar is the Vampire from King\\\'s Quest 3. Much hijinks ensue. ',1,0,0,0,'216.165.3.211','en'),(2817,881,'2001-05-08 21:24:58',0,'cyantist','<p>i\\\'m going to be in asia for two months, so i guess i \r\ncan really put some effort into geeking out while i am there \r\nas well.  during the week, i won\\\'t be doing much around town \r\nuntil the weekend. has anyone here been to hong kong?</p>',1,0,0,0,'205.142.76.11','en'),(2818,881,'2001-05-08 21:40:44',0,'Mike','I wish I was in Hong Kong ,working or not.',1,0,0,0,'206.224.71.188','en'),(2819,881,'2001-05-08 21:41:08',0,'rusty','Tracy will know all the hot spots by now...  he\\\'s a social \r\nbutterfly...  Randy will probably know some cool places, \r\ntoo...  See the night life, checkout the New Territories if \r\nyou get a chance...  Take a boat out into the bay...  I \r\nnever did hit Kowloon when I was there...  There is this \r\ntiny ancient temple, which doesn\\\'t fit in at all with the \r\nskyscrapers all over the place, which is cool, but you\\\'ll \r\nfind more interesting temples in TaiPei (I assume you\\\'ll \r\nhit there sometime during the 2 months)',1,0,0,0,'205.142.76.11','en'),(2820,880,'2001-05-08 21:47:14',0,'bmg','tonight is a deville night, if anyone is game... ',1,0,0,0,'66.68.78.158','en'),(2821,880,'2001-05-08 22:30:47',0,'augie','<p>longing;<br>\r\nthings i long for;<br>\r\npeaceful nights and strangers at the door<br>\r\noh come in -<br>\r\ncome through the door;<br>\r\nyou\\\'ve been here before.</p>\r\n',3,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(2822,882,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','i want that dude\\\'s shoes',2,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(2823,881,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','<b>Hong Kong</b>:  make sure you go to Junk Bay, and Bird \r\nAlley.  and don\\\'t litter. :)',2,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(2824,881,'2001-05-08 23:51:28',0,'nancy lee smothered','eat vomit covered chicken and be happy.',3,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(2825,878,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>\r\nThe state motto of Rhode Island is \\\"Hope\\\".\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin',2,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(2826,881,'