t means more frequent visits to santa cruz. xep, \r\ninform saturn cafe.',3,0,0,0,'63.14.67.235','en'),(3389,1001,'2001-05-30 08:15:32',0,'jp','not only is he an asshole he can\\\'t even rhyme.<BR>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'24.0.133.128','en'),(3390,1004,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<i>missouri</i> is the \"show me\" state. jim should lay off \r\nthe pipe. also \"dead horse point\" is a beatiful name.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3391,1004,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<tt>&lt;jim&gt; every state is the show me state.</tt>\r\n',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3392,1003,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','addendum: i just subscribed to a crane fly mailing list \r\nhosted at washington state university. i\\\'m really excited! \r\ni hope it\\\'s VERY HIGH TRAFFIC',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3393,1003,'2001-05-30 13:17:40',0,'auntie','squoosh it!  it\\\'s evil!  he will get in your dreads and lay \r\ncranefly eggs that will burrow through to your brain and \r\nthen you will have thousands of them crawling around in \r\nthere....',4,0,0,0,'24.162.119.106','en'),(3394,1004,'2001-05-30 13:20:11',0,'auntie','show me what?  that is what i want to know.  i have never \r\nunderstood that motto. it\\\'s not like there is a whole \r\nhelluvalot to be shown in missouri.',1,0,0,0,'24.162.119.106','en'),(3395,1002,'2001-05-30 13:24:34',0,'auntie','sometimes you just need to go home.  it\\\'s okay.  you\\\'ll \r\nrenew yourself with people who love you unconditionally, \r\nhave some good ranting arguments with people who love you \r\nunconditionally and only want what\\\'s best for you, eat some \r\nstuff that makes you feel young and innocent again, and \r\nprobably find a job that surprises you.<br><br>\r\nhugs and kisses from auntie.',2,0,0,0,'24.162.119.106','en'),(3396,985,'2001-05-30 13:41:55',0,'auntie','i am an enfp.  the test says i am a two.  maybe i am.  \r\nmaybe not.<br><br>\r\n\r\nperhaps now would be the time to mention that the \r\nmissionary or doggy style discussion was very informative. \r\ndid anyone ever realize that doggy style won?<br><br>\r\n\r\ni find it interesting that there are so many enfps in this \r\ngroup.  the infps aren\\\'t posting much, they are too \r\nintroverted to bare their souls to the web.',3,0,0,0,'24.162.119.106','en'),(3397,1004,'2001-05-30 13:44:56',0,'erin to auntie:','its like illinois (land of lincoln) in that the good and the \r\nbeautiful and the memorable things about the state ain\\\'t as \r\nobvious...you need to be \\\'shown\\\'. i think. \r\n',0,0,0,0,'129.105.107.184','en'),(3398,1000,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','<p>\r\nthe saturn cafe, be still my heart.<br>\r\nplease reserve me a seat at the popular table.\r\n</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(3399,1004,'2001-05-30 16:58:11',0,'dj1luna','Kansas City ,missouri: The Best Zoo I\\\'ve ever been to. Best \r\nIMAX theatre. Best amphithetre (starlight theatre).',1,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(3400,1000,'2001-05-30 17:24:12',0,'adam','congratulations austin :)',1,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(3401,1003,'2001-05-30 17:25:04',0,'jo','\\\"VERY HIGH TRAFFIC\\\" caused me to giggle explosively, here \r\nat work.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(3402,1004,'2001-05-30 17:28:41',0,'jo','the best is new hampshire.<BR>\r\n\\\"LIVE FREE OR DIE!\\\"<BR>\r\ni aim to one day drive back and forth across new hampshire, \r\ngetting out of the car periodically, standing ON TOP of the \r\ncar, thrusting PUNK ROCK hands into the sky, and shouting \r\nat the top of my lungs, \\\"LIVE FREE OR DIE!!!\\\" over and over \r\nand over again.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(3403,1001,'2001-05-30 18:02:42',0,'MightyBLuJ','I know.   I have to work with the sonofabitch!   Have you \r\never noticed that the ones who have the least to say, are \r\nthe ones who never actually shut up?',4,0,0,0,'204.64.42.46','en'),(3404,1004,'2001-05-30 18:12:24',0,'erin to jo:','YES! they will especially like the punk rock salute in \r\nnewmarket, nh. growllll!\r\n',2,0,0,0,'129.105.107.184','en'),(3405,1000,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','is the saturn cafe the place we went after joan jett?<p>\r\ni put the neoprint on my computer at work. <p>\r\nso that people think i have friends.',1,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(3406,1000,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','<p>\r\nyes, it is.<br>\r\nand i put the neoprint on my i.d. with the others.<br>\r\nso the bouncer with know i have friends.<br>\r\nyay us.<br>\r\n</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(3407,1003,'2001-05-30 19:23:48',0,'chaya','wsu.  GO COUGS.',6,0,0,0,'158.252.240.81','en'),(3408,1004,'2001-05-30 19:25:26',0,'chaya','oh oh jo.  please take me with you.',6,0,0,0,'158.252.240.81','en'),(3409,1003,'2001-05-30 19:26:03',0,'Lunesse','I love really out there mailing lists. I\\\'m on one where all \r\npeople talk about is fire hydrants.\r\n\r\n',3,0,0,0,'209.213.209.50','en'),(3410,1004,'2001-05-30 20:14:36',0,'jo to chaya','well duh. you are clearly the first person i would think of \r\nto take with me.<BR>\r\nplease bring pixi stix, glitter, and caramels to throw out \r\nthe windows. we will listen to girl punk throughout our \r\nmini road trip. we will be wearing tutus and studded \r\nchokers. and we\\\'ll take my truck, so at rest stops, we can \r\nspread out a picnic lunch in the bed of the truck and throw \r\nlittle tea parties for ourselves.<BR>\r\nLIVE FREE OR DIE!!!',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(3411,991,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','on the way to bart in the morning jay and I have to walk \r\nthrough what he calls the \\\"pidgeon tunnel\\\", an overpass under \r\nwhich these relatively healthy but unappetizing birds shoot \r\nthe shit- I mean, bird shit, not conversation. every time he \r\nsays, \\\"NEVER AGAIN will we walk through pidgeon shit.\\\" but \r\nevery day, we go through it. we are used to walking on that \r\nside of the road.\r\n<p>\r\nthe moral of this story is, we must take some kind of joy in \r\nthe unpleasant company of the birds. the familiarity of \r\ntorture. or else why would we walk on that side every GODDAMN \r\nday?\r\n<p>\r\nand did you know that birds are the closest descendants of \r\ndinosaurs? \r\n',1,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(3412,991,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','oh, i said \\\"every day\\\" or something, but jay got laid off so \r\nnow its just me, and I never actually minded the bird shit.\r\n<p>\r\nhave i mentioned today that \\\"quotidien\\\" is a great word? \r\nsomeone used it at wayne/justin bbq. I think it was jo.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(3413,991,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','<p>\r\njulian told me recently that one night he came home super \r\ndrunk and threw up out his window. and the next morning \r\nnoticed that he had thrown up on the pigeons in their little \r\nnest area on the ledge below.<br>\r\new. ew. ew.\r\n</p>\r\n',4,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(3414,998,'2001-05-30 21:37:40',0,'incitor to le','yes i carry weapons.  following the laws of my state and city.  just because your life hasn\\\'t shown you why a person might need a weapon doesn\\\'t mean there is no reason.  my mother, step-father, two older step-brothers, my roomates and most of my friends all carry weapons.  i also carry handcuffs, duct tape, a multi-tool, and a first aid kit.  i\\\'m sorry you feel there is something dreadfully wrong with me for wishing to protect myself and those around me from what is so obviously a dangerous world.',4,0,0,0,'207.205.220.5','en'),(3415,1003,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','i really dont have a problem with bugs. I think they should \r\nbe allowed to live. Unless they are biting you, and \r\ncompromising your comfort. by disabling your ability to \r\nconsume products and services in any way.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(3416,1003,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Veer Moll','<p>I like ants. They are pure. A model for humanity.</p>\r\n',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(3417,1004,'2001-05-30 22:06:51',0,'chaya','*swoon* jo, will you marry me?',6,0,0,0,'158.252.240.81','en'),(3418,1005,'2001-05-30 22:49:45',0,'bmg','funny... you and i have probably been in the same place \r\nat the same time, yet I have never met you. ',0,0,0,0,'66.68.78.158','en'),(3419,1003,'2003-05-10 16:09:14',79,'yeti','yeti to chaya: Down with the cougs, go vandals!',6,0,0,0,'63.109.213.59','en'),(3420,1004,'2003-05-10 16:09:14',79,'yeti','<p>Auntie, I\\\'ve often wondered the same thing. I asked the\r\ninternet. It said:</p>\r\n<p>\r\n\\\"Show Me State\\\" A name attributed to Representative Willard\r\nVan Diver. It conotates a certain self-deprecating\r\nstubbornness and devotion to simple common sense.</p>\r\n<p>I\\\'m disappointed.</p>',1,0,0,0,'63.109.213.59','en'),(3421,1004,'2001-05-31 00:40:29',0,'jo','yes. ',1,0,0,0,'64.12.105.137','en'),(3422,1005,'2001-05-31 00:43:01',0,'jo','this seems to be a recurring problem, yes. i should throw a \r\nparty soon.',1,0,0,0,'64.12.105.137','en'),(3423,1007,'2001-05-31 01:37:26',0,'dj1luna','U2 Songs Sound Good All The Time. ',1,0,0,0,'24.93.61.58','en'),(3424,1007,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','\r\ni herniated while reading this. thanks, egg you irreverant \r\nlittle wascally wabbit.',1,0,0,0,'209.86.30.16','en'),(3425,1007,'2001-05-31 03:59:45',0,'kat','g love is good shit to listen too...especially when you\\\'re \r\nalone luving yourself.',0,0,0,0,'32.100.70.29','en'),(3426,1004,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','there are a lot of caves in missouri',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(3427,1005,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','it would be cool if bmg turned out to be one of the people \r\nyou list.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3428,1005,'2001-05-31 06:07:55',0,'kdog','mmmm...no, he\\\'s got character but i don\\\'t think he\\\'s any of \r\nthose characters.',3,0,0,0,'66.68.78.158','en'),(3429,1005,'2001-05-31 06:18:55',0,'kdog','\\\"yeah, and if this city is getting so big how come i keep \r\nrunning into the same 50 people?\\\"  \r\n\r\nsomething else to note:  how easy it is to get to know CARS \r\nin this town.  not the driver, just their car.  \r\n\r\n\\\"Oh hey there Jeep Cherokee (sitting in front of \r\nWheatsville) that I saw driving east on Ben White this \r\nmorning\\\" ???\r\n',2,0,0,0,'66.68.78.158','en'),(3430,998,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i dunno incitor, this goes back to you expecting people to \r\nbe bad. if you expect violence and prepare for it, that is \r\nthe message you send to the world and that\\\'s what you will \r\nget. i walk through sketchy neighborhoods at all hours, but \r\ni don\\\'t spend my time waiting for doom to happen. i \r\nunderstand \\\"be prepared\\\" but i also understand that \r\nnegativity begets negativity. ',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3431,1000,'2001-05-31 06:56:22',0,'sean','austin congratulations. glad you are destined for santa cruz &amp; goodbye to the urban cacophony and wall-to-wall people of SF. hope you\\\'ll let me come visit!',1,0,0,0,'158.252.208.188','en'),(3432,1008,'2002-04-20 20:49:51',273,'Quinn','I hope you be a jokester with this.  Sister, sixteen?  \\\"She \r\ndoes what she wants to do.\\\"  Marry a 30 yr old letch?  \r\nYuck.  She\\\'s sixteen and mom&stepdad should just \r\nstep in and say NO! sorry, you\\\'re 16 and dumb as a \r\npiece of toast still.  We all were dumb at 16.  Imagine \r\nchoices you made then affecting your life now.  Most of \r\nus would be fucked.  Fucked to the gills.  And yes I \r\nchoose my words inentionally.  Because anybody 30 \r\nwho would marry a 16 has buy one big F-word on his \r\natrophied little mind.  Geez, man.  What are ya out there \r\nin the world - slouching toward Jerry Springer show ?-  \r\nMaybe you\\\'re doing some kind of experimental writing, \r\nthat I just am to unhip to get, an in-joke extrodinaire for \r\nwhich my sincere little rant will be deconstructed and \r\nmocked - i dunno - just stumbled across this \r\ninteresting little site, linking and linking.  Ah...I\\\'ll take you \r\nas sincere and sincerely hope you kick this pervert in \r\nhis unholy, teen-marrying ass.  Terrible thought that \r\nsomeone has so little concern for a family mbr., that \r\nyou could \\\"want to like this guy\\\"...eh...fuggit....you have \r\nvery little love and misplaced trust.  Just buy the rubber \r\nstamp marked -DIVORCED- right now, so you can \r\nstamp it across the happy faces of this twisted couple \r\nnext year.  Sigh.',4,0,0,1,'198.185.18.207','en'),(3433,1008,'2001-05-31 14:07:08',0,'dj1luna','\\\"when you are 16 you think you can take on the world, and \r\nsometimes you are right\\\" - p. hewson',1,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(3434,1005,'2001-05-31 14:07:17',0,'jo','YES! yes i know what you mean. the \\\"just because no one \r\nunderstands you does NOT make you an artist\\\" bumpersticker \r\nsedan was in front of me while i drove today. and i was \r\nlike, \\\"oh yes. we meet again.\\\"',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(3435,1008,'2001-05-31 14:09:58',0,'jo','juan, i had that quote underlined in my u2 biography.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(3436,1000,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>i hope i can find a place with guest \r\naccomodations.</P>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3437,1008,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','I really don\\\'t think you\\\'re being overprotective here.  \r\nShe\\\'s too young to really understand love and the \r\nimplications of marriage I think.  How old is old enough?  \r\nI don\\\'t know.  Judging by some of the people I know, never.\r\nTell her to at least spend a year at college before she \r\nmakes decisions like this, not that school has much \r\ndirectly to do with it, but it does bring a bit more \r\nperspective and maturity.  And if they are destined to be \r\ntogether, they\\\'re both going to live for (barring accidents \r\nor sickness) 4 to 7 decades more, so one year either way is \r\nnot a big deal (i.e. love lasts through time and all \r\ndistance).\r\n\r\nSo, yeah, could work out.  But as a scientist might say, \r\nthe probability of that outcome is minimal.  :-)  Just my \r\n0.02USD.\r\n\r\nI have to say I respect you a lot for even giving the guy a \r\nchance.\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'24.162.55.146','en'),(3438,1008,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','(plus cmu is a good school, I have a friend who \r\nworks/studies there (math and cs), he says it rocks and I \r\ntrust him)',1,0,0,0,'24.162.55.146','en'),(3439,1008,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','(i went to college at 16 too, and trust me, it grows you up \r\n<em>real quick</em>, or else you just fail out; so as a \r\nkick in the maturity pants it does pretty nicely; just a \r\nside note)',1,0,0,0,'24.162.55.146','en'),(3440,1008,'2002-04-20 20:49:51',273,'Quinn','This little piece bugs me, so here I am back again..an\\\' \r\nthe more I think about it, the more it <i>pisses me \r\noff</i>.  \\\"Incitor\\\"...one who incites, seems like a big \r\nfreakin\\\' liar to me.  ',6,0,0,1,'198.185.18.207','en'),(3441,1008,'2001-05-31 21:01:55',0,'jo','i\\\'m really glad that i didn\\\'t marry anyone i was dating at \r\n16. or 18. or 20. which is why i\\\'m glad that i\\\'m still \r\nsingle.<BR>\r\n(at 16, there was a brief stint with a 28-y-o. which is \r\nweird because i\\\'m much less likely to date at 28-y-o now, \r\nat 23.)',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(3442,1000,'2001-05-31 21:37:03',0,'sic','congrats. go to the boardwalk and ride the big dipper 5 \r\ntimes in a row.',0,0,0,0,'129.65.91.41','en'),(3443,1008,'2001-05-31 21:39:52',0,'sic','show her a picture of an old dude and tell her thtaas what \r\nhe\\\'ll look like when she\\\'s 25.',0,0,0,0,'129.65.91.41','en'),(3444,998,'2001-05-31 21:59:12',0,'incitor to le','what i write here on swinney i write for me.  i don\\\'t do it for the audience, the replies i recieve are just a bonus.  i like hearing what people think.  however, don\\\'t believe that you are viewing my life in total.  what you are getting a is a tiny window pasted over with text.  when i go out, i try to keep a smile on my face.  i\\\'m friendly with store clerks and coffee slingers.  i don\\\'t get mad when there\\\'s a line, or someone screws up and has to ring my order in again.  i bullshit with waitresses and leave 30-40% tips.  i tip my cap to old folks, say hi to people i don\\\'t know, and in general try to be pleasant.  it tends to work.  i feel better for it, and people smile back.  i prepare for the worst because there was a time when i didn\\\'t, and i almost lost the chance to correct the problem.  i value those innocent souls who believe that if they don\\\'t worry about trouble, then trouble will rarely come to them.  but in my experience, this is not the case.  i\\\'m glad there are people who try not to think about it.  i find myself most attracted to women who are mostly gentle, and think not of violence.  but i must live my life based on what i have seen.  le, i like you as best i can like pixels, and i want for you and everyone to understand that i am not a violent or dangerous person.  i simply maintain that capability in case it\\\'s needed.  as i was telling darwin not too long ago, i\\\'m good in emergencies of all kinds.  i\\\'ve provided first aid countless times to people i didn\\\'t know.  overall i am happy with who i am, and how i\\\'ve changed since the darker days when i was younger.',3,0,0,0,'207.205.218.153','en'),(3445,1008,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','<p>\r\nwell i met the guy and while he looked about 20, his military ID clearly stated he was 30.  he seemed nice, but i just can\\\'t help wondering what a 30 year old is doing picking up 16 year olds on the internet.  they met on a MUD!!  good grief.  anyway, my mum and i grilled him for a couple of hours and learned alot about him.  not that we\\\'ve verified anything yet.  my final opinion was that he was very immature and he was certainly hiding alot of stuff.  all questions about his relationship with his parents were quickly derailed.  in the end however, nothing has come of this meeting.  we cannot control my sister barring the use of force.  at this point i\\\'m just pushing for her to not give up on college.  \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nas for the good Quinn\\\'s belief that i am a liar.  i was tempted not even to reply.  instead i ask all to consider that everyone has a life their own.  in some ways i live in a different world than many of you.  i see what is said here and think it\\\'s nice, a new, if incomplete world to explore.  my lifestyle isn\\\'t really a good one for most people, but do try to understand it\\\'s very real and for me most taxing.  i share it to clarify in my own mind what\\\'s going on, and in some small way show some other neet people a little of my world.  \r\n</p>',3,0,0,0,'207.205.218.153','en'),(3446,1005,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','\\\"The party scene is cool, but then again it\\\'s all the \r\nsame /<br>\r\nYou see the same faces, but at different places / <br>\r\nWhen you\\\'re up and ridin\\\' high everything is palsy-\r\npalsy /<br>\r\nGet a million pounds and all the skins give you hugs /<p>\\\"\r\n\r\n--Sadat X, \\\"Show Business\\\"<p>\r\n',5,0,0,0,'24.221.170.233','en'),(3448,1008,'2002-04-20 20:49:51',273,'Quinn','<p>Okay, then, apologies to Incitor.\r\n\r\n<p>Not that I mean to dig at yr soul or anything, but \r\nc\\\'mon, it seems a little impossible and talk-showy - the \r\n<i>truth is stranger than fiction</i> syndrome.  You \r\nshould really change yr handle tho, Incitor...it has \r\nprovocation inherent in it\\\'s nominal depths... And, \r\nbecause the story you relate is as much outlandish as \r\nit is sad, it seems to me that you\\\'re trying to provoke \r\nsome kind of faux-response (which you will later make \r\nfun of).\r\n\r\n<p>Like I said in my first note - skeptical because I \r\ndon\\\'t know you; besides, your name belies my trust.  \r\nCall yourself honestly or truth or beauty...call yourself \r\nReggie Jackson and I\\\'d sooner believe you.  \r\n\r\n<p>I guess I doubted because you seem so \r\nnonplussed by the whole affair...\\\"oh, I\\\'m being \r\noverprotective\\\"...if anything <you\\\'re being \r\nunderprotective!!!!</i> \r\n\r\n<p>Your sister is damned to a terrible life if she \r\nmarries this guy  He\\\'s obviously a pathetic freak if he \r\nneeds to lure some sixteen year old into the nuptuial \r\nfold.  \r\n\r\n<p>Do a search for him on Google, post his name in \r\nthis venue and see if anybody knows him.  He has not \r\nthe right to a shred of privacy.   Fer giddy\\\'s sake, Incitor, \r\nhe\\\'s marrying a MINOR (a LITTLE GIRL!!).  Has he had \r\nsex with her already?  IFSO....CALL THE COPS, HAVE \r\nHIM ARRESTED!!!! ',2,0,0,1,'198.185.18.207','en'),(3449,637,'2002-04-20 20:49:51',273,'quinn','uh...how old are you? 13?',0,0,0,1,'198.185.18.207','en'),(3450,1011,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','LE. CHAYA. LADIES, GIRLS, WOMEN. <p>\r\nwhere is our sexy little albino astrologer<p>\r\nit must have been in the stars, because i was up all FUCKING \r\nNIGHT drinking myself into grade C drunken corner ho mode, to \r\navoid smoking. have you ever heard chet baker\\\'s version of \\\"I \r\nget along without you very well\\\"? Quitting smoking turned me \r\ninto a jilted lover 1950s style, chrome and greasy hair.<p>\r\nand i spent all morning on the BART trying to figure out why \r\nI have to be so excited about everything. <p>\r\nand then I remembered dean moriarty, who people probably \r\nthought was kind of an asswipe retard, and I realized that \r\nwomen dont usually get so much credit for being freaked out \r\ndebaucherous ecstatic nutcake yowlers, that a loud, drunk \r\nwoman is perceived more as a grade C drunken corner ho and a \r\nloud, drunk man is a virile individualist, a misunderstood \r\npoet, a Whitmanesque bard. <p>\r\nI propose that on the full moon next week we make some sort \r\nof dykey horse-girl Cult of Diana movie with s5\\\'s video \r\ncamera in le\\\'s backyard.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(3451,1011,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','i feel so tame and homely.  when i think about being rowdy\r\nall i can ever think about is how much it will suck the next\r\nday.  ',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(3452,1011,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','xep you are neither tame nor homely. many can vouch for \r\nthis. also, it doesn\\\'t suck today because we just kept \r\ndrinking into today! :D :D :D :D *barf*',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3453,1011,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','i bet front handsprings would be hard with a hangover\r\nthough.',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(3454,1008,'2001-06-01 18:57:10',0,'hedwig','<p>You\\\'re right, Incitor, your sister is going to do what \r\nshe wants to do barring the use of physical force to hold \r\nher back.  I remember exactly how I felt at 16, even though \r\nI\\\'m 28 now.  I didn\\\'t want a soul telling me how to live my \r\nlife, but I also was a realist in some respects.  I knew I \r\ndidn\\\'t want a life of misery, and avoided most trails that \r\nwould lead to down that path.  I\\\'ve stumbled into the \r\ninternet romances, and they all ended horribly.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>On that note, I\\\'m wondering if you\\\'ve talked to your \r\nsister alone to see what it is she\\\'s thinking?  Internet \r\nromances are quick, pulsating and beat to a feverish drum.  \r\nThey\\\'re easy to spark and die quickly.  How long has she \r\nknown him?  I\\\'m guessing 3-6 months at most.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I feel so badly for your sister.  I\\\'m sure she\\\'s happy \r\nat the moment, but I see a terrible demise coming on.  \r\nShe\\\'s so close to the romance, she can\\\'t see the bigger \r\npicture.</p>\r\n',2,0,0,0,'198.92.137.130','en'),(3455,1009,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>hellow slight.<BR>\r\nanother austinite.</P>',2,0,0,0,'64.51.232.105','en'),(3456,1008,'2001-06-01 18:59:44',0,'hedwig','<p>erf... i\\\'m 27... i just aged myself in the previous \r\npost... </p>',2,0,0,0,'198.92.137.130','en'),(3457,1011,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','tsk.',4,0,0,0,'63.20.94.230','en'),(3458,1011,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','xep: you dont have to drink to be a crazed pagan maniac!<p>\r\nI think you do have to experiment with sleep deprivation just \r\na little though.<p>\r\nI dont think drugs are necessary to revel. i think music and \r\nwater and love. and even on a weekend night where you can \r\nsleep in the next day.<p>\r\n-People Against Goodness And Normalcy.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(3459,1008,'2002-04-20 20:49:51',273,'Quinn','maybe I\\\'m just too OLD SKOOL, but I really don\\\'t \r\nunderstand you people.  The LAW is on your side.  You \r\ncan cart this guy off to JAIL on statutory RAPE \r\nCHARGES.  <p>An\\\' sorry, but what kinda fucked up \r\nfamily even allowed her to DATE a 30yr old???  \r\nSheesh.  <p>It\\\'s sad to see stupidity carved into young \r\nflesh.  <p><i>blah, blah, blah, she\\\'s a headstrong teen \r\nand what am I going to do...i\\\'m helpless and she \r\ncontrols me...i can\\\'t act to SAVE HER LIFE because she \r\nhas the right to FUCK HERSELF UP FOREVER...that\\\'s \r\nher right....what can I do about it, I\\\'m just a helpless \r\nboob...a moron too...i was headstrong at her age and I \r\nknow how it is..</i><p>FUCK you guys!!!!  So USE \r\nFORCE....she\\\'s sixteen...stick her in a room and LOCK \r\nTHE DOOR...SIXTEEN YEARS OLD IS A FREAKIN \r\nBABY...this 30yr old is TWICE HER AGE.<p>SHE\\\'S A \r\nMINOR and you HAVE A RESPONSIBILITY TO LOOK \r\nOUT FOR HER....MOM  IS SUPPOSED TO MAKE HER \r\nDECISIONS....What kind of pansy is this mother anyway \r\nto be pushed around by a kid?<p>If some sixteen yr old \r\nstarted pushing me around on the street, I\\\'d lay into \r\nhim...If I saw some sixteen yr old mugging and old \r\nman, I\\\'d step in...if some sixteen yr old (my \r\ndaughter/mys sister, don\\\'t matter really) was gonna get \r\nmarried to ANYBODY....I\\\'d stop her and say YOU HAVE \r\nTO AT LEAST WAIT TWO YRS.  WHEN YOU CAN VOTE \r\nYOU CAN CHOOSE A HUSBAND. <p>Honestly, buster \r\nbrown, you better watch it, lest your sister end up....I \r\ndon\\\'t even want to say it....',6,0,0,1,'198.185.18.207','en'),(3460,1012,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<i>full of grace</i>',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3461,1008,'2002-03-05 20:17:36',17,'austin to QUINN','<P>over emphasis using caps detracts from your arguement.</P>',2,0,0,1,'64.51.232.105','en'),(3462,1008,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon to quinn','<p>\r\nlisten pal, as a kid who ran off at 15 to live my own life \r\nand make my own decisions and managed to do an alright job of \r\nmaking it to 22, why don\\\'t you fucking chill. yeah, ok, she\\\'s \r\n16, he\\\'s 30. it\\\'s creepy. it\\\'s probably bad news. but go \r\nlocking kids up in their rooms and roughing them up to \r\nprevent them from doing what their going to do anyway, what \r\nthe hell is wrong with you?\r\n</p>\r\n',3,0,0,1,'63.195.92.218','en'),(3463,1008,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','<p>\r\nokay.  first off, Quinn, your apology is not necessary.  i understand your viewpoint.  as for the handle incitor itself, i\\\'ve used it since my BBS days.  one night, hanging out on the river front in my home town, some friends and i were talking about...well...everything, aha, like free-range conversation.  and i kept challenging certain preconceptions my friends were expressing.  this one kid troy looks over at me and says, \\\"dude, there\\\'s something about the way you talk, it incites people.  makes us think about things in new ways.\\\"  i took it as a compliments and, with a minor alteration, as my handle.  i\\\'ve had other handles in the past, but i\\\'ve stuck with incitor for many many years, and am happy with it.  if people inherently mistrust words coming from someone calling himself incitor, well, i accept that.  it\\\'s no different from being branded a nazi or a racist since i\\\'m a skinhead.  i\\\'m willing to accept a certain amount of stigma, helps weed out close minded people sometimes.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nas for my sister.  using phsysical force to control a teenager can be a terrible thing.  my father tried, and we ended up fighting.  i was bigger than him.  i hurt him severely many times to my eternal shame.  my mother is a gentle person and would never countenance striking my sister at this point.  my offer of a pair of handcuffs was refused.  since they met on the internet (the other night was the first time they\\\'ve met in person) it is safe to assume they\\\'ve yet to have sex.  in my state, 16 is the age of consent, except in certain rareified circumstances.  the police can offer no help here.  they are engaged, but have not, and can not apply for a marriage license.  my mother and i made it clear to this guy that he will not be allowed to see my sister except under controlled situations.  thus, i\\\'m going to be spending a fair amount of time with this guy in the future.  i don\\\'t like him much.  but i love my sister very much and if i can\\\'t control everything she does, i can at least try to limit the damage she does to her life.  \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nin the end i think this guy is destined to be disappointed.  the age difference is important, but think of the maturity difference.  my sister wants things from life that this guy doesn\\\'t.  they have almost nothing in common.  she doesn\\\'t like sports, and hates fishing; two things he adores.  he is satisfied bumming about, not trying to pursue a real career, while she wants to do more with her life.  i was engaged once to a girl two and a half years my junior.  oh we were in love, and wanted to be together.  but in the end, she wanted to still be a teenager, out drinking and getting high with her friends.  i, on the other hand, had seen too much and done too much early on.  i wanted to sink my roots into the world and become a contributing member of the community.  she left me.  and i was nearly destroyed because i did not then understand how two people can be in love, yet not be on parallel paths.  we shared many interest; role playing, the militia, double whoppers with cheese, punk rock, etc.  and still it could not last.  my sister and this guy are going to end up the same way i think.  and i\\\'ve said as much to both of them.  they\\\'ve \\\'known\\\' each other for six months.  i\\\'ll be suprised if they are speaking in another six months.  in the meantime i can only offer my sister my hard won wisdom as it relates to this affair.  i try not to tell her how to live, instead pointing out my many errors and how she can avoid them.  every time i speak with her, i first ask about what she\\\'s been learning.  i ask if she\\\'s written anything new.  i try to avoid lecturing her.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nanyone who thinks i\\\'m not taking this seriously is missing a key piece of the puzzle.  i now have photos of this guy.  i have his name, his addy, and his fathers contact info.  i\\\'ve gotten some friends on the police force to run his background.  my step father (a retired naval officer) has checked his naval records.  of note, we\\\'ve discovered that he did not recieve an honorable discharge, only a good discharge.  which isn\\\'t so \\\'good\\\' in reality.  when we met him, i frisked him before allowing him into our vehicle.  my mother carried her pistol.  i carried my assorted weaponry.  in my ideal world, i\\\'d be able to beat him senseless as a warning.  but i can\\\'t.  i have to play it straight and hope my sister shows her intelligence at some point.  i refuse to date anyone more than three years younger than myself, so i think this guy is either dangerous or a moron.  which is also dangerous.  we\\\'ll see in time.\r\n</p>',3,0,0,0,'207.205.218.184','en'),(3464,1008,'2001-06-02 00:20:43',0,'tomato','you frisked him before you let him in your car?  \r\n\r\nyo, like a fucked up movie or something.',6,0,0,0,'165.247.205.123','en'),(3465,1012,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','\r\nok. name the time and place for an eighties party and i\\\'m \r\nthere with my stirrup pants and white lace socks with high \r\nheels. and more, much much more.',1,0,0,0,'138.110.236.51','en'),(3466,981,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>irc could be the problem.  xep has stopped chatting.  i\r\nthink the results are favorable.  initially, there was the\r\npossibility that she would not have anymore friends.  but\r\nlook, she still has friends, but not so many idle chat\r\nfriends, maybe.  i am going back to work soon and i will\r\nexit the chat world.  no chatting at work.  i wont be\r\nchatting at home either as i wont have an access to the net\r\nfor months at the least.  unless i figure out how to do\r\ndialup on my laptop, which i do not ever feel motivated to\r\ndo. (isnt that wierd, not wanting to figure out analog on\r\nthis thing?  maybe i just think of it as a good excuse to\r\nnot be online.)</P>',2,0,0,0,'64.51.232.105','en'),(3467,499,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>my path is on a motorcycle.  i really want one.  really\r\nbad.  bad enough to sell my car.  bad enough to desert my\r\nbelongings all over the western united states.  as i see it,\r\nif i get a motorbike, i will never make it back to LA to\r\npick up my stereo and various computer gear.  i dont really\r\ncar though.  if i cared, i never would have left the stuff\r\nat people\\\'s houses.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i am bored.  leaving messages in the archives.  randomly\r\nentering in id numbers in the url.  pot luck.  drinking\r\ncoffee.  life.</P>',4,0,0,0,'64.51.232.105','en'),(3468,1011,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','see, now you going to be assed out for like two days and s5\r\nis gone out of town, and egg is having an energy crisis. \r\nwhat am i supposed to do with myself?  who will hang out\r\nwith me?  qq.  that is it.  doesnt anyone sit aroound and\r\nplay video games?  darwin?  i need to enter the vast\r\nmindscape of time and emmerge the 18th to start my new job. \r\nhelp me.',4,0,0,0,'64.51.232.105','en'),(3469,1011,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','I\\\'ll hang out with you austin, if you still like me.',1,0,0,0,'64.81.65.205','en'),(3470,1012,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','I am going to have an 80\\\'s party and we will watch \\\"Valley \r\nGirl\\\" and \\\"Desperately Seeking Susan\\\" and drink wine \r\ncoolers and feather our hair.\r\n\r\nseriously.',1,0,0,0,'64.81.65.205','en'),(3471,1010,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','<pre>\r\nwhere o where are you tonight?\r\nwhy did you leave me here all alone?\r\ni searched the world over and thought i found true love\r\nyou met another and PFFT! you were gone\r\n</pre>',0,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(3472,1009,'2001-06-02 04:39:04',0,'auntie','every time someone takes advantage of someone weaker than \r\nthem, no matter how old you are, it scars you for life.  \r\nthe trick is to fade the scar.  talking about it begins the \r\nprocess.',1,0,0,0,'24.162.119.106','en'),(3473,1011,'2001-06-02 04:42:05',0,'auntie','i knew you were up to something.  i could feel it.  i wish \r\ni was up to something, too, but all the things i used to do \r\nwhen the moonbeams caught me are no longer possible or \r\nallowed. so i spent the day singing very loudly and \r\nthinking about the women in my life, too.  i love them all, \r\nespecially the ones that are the biggest pain in the \r\nass.<br><br>\r\n\r\nwomen rule the world. we are fucking invincible.',1,0,0,0,'24.162.119.106','en'),(3474,1013,'2001-06-02 04:46:20',0,'auntie','everyone feels left out sometimes. it\\\'s the way things \r\nare.  you gotta pick up your party feet and go to where the \r\npeeps are who you want to be with. no more waiting for \r\nsomene else to make the first move.  knock on the door, \r\nsend the page, message the party of the first part. close \r\nup the putty and do face time.  sing. dance. listen. don\\\'t \r\nworry about everything you say, just say everything with \r\nyour heart.  people love you very much, they know you \r\nbetter than you think and they will know what you mean. ',1,0,0,0,'24.162.119.106','en'),(3475,1012,'2001-06-02 04:51:01',0,'auntie','make le wear her barbie doll clothes. all in pink.  and \r\ngrammy jewels.  and blue eyeshadow. and take lots of \r\npictures so i can see.<br><br>\r\n\r\nif i had a waist i would wear a belted sweater dress.  \r\nperhaps i will wear one any-fucking-way.  i always put my \r\nmoney in my bra and i thought EVERYONE got too sleepy and \r\nslept in theirs so when they wake up in the morning they \r\nhave those sore places at the tops of their shoulders...',1,0,0,0,'24.162.119.106','en'),(3476,1013,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','thanks sweet auntie. in fact, I am picking up and going out \r\nto see pals tonight. ',1,0,0,0,'64.81.65.205','en'),(3477,1012,'2001-06-02 05:40:12',0,'sic','80s children unite',0,0,0,0,'63.93.74.43','en'),(3478,1013,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','oh sine oh sine oh sine\r\n',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(3479,1011,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','must be a day to raise cain or be mischevious.  i named a\r\nvariable \\\"$bitch_slap_chickens\\\" thursday afternoon, just\r\n\\\'cuz it made laugh; wanted to go eat sushi and get piss\r\ndrunk on sake but was too po\\\'... :-) pardon spelling, very\r\ntired...',1,0,0,0,'209.163.146.25','en'),(3480,1011,'2001-06-02 10:41:50',0,'rusty','cigarettes and whiskey and wild wild women...',6,0,0,0,'206.170.6.215','en'),(3481,1014,'2001-06-02 17:41:41',0,'jp','Hmmm, just found a random link,\r\n<A HREF=\"http://www.sonlight.net/\">The Enzyme Depot</A>.<BR>\r\nThere are three different kinds of enzymes. Do you know what\r\nthey are? Metabolic, digestive and food.<BR>\r\nMy dad started taking some for digestion and says they work\r\ngreat. If you\'re not having digestive problems then the kind\r\nyou have must be metabolic I guess.<BR>\r\nI think overall it helps with energy and detoxing you\'re\r\nbody, supposedly. If you just quit smoking maybe the doctor\r\ngave that to you to help get the garbage out of your\r\nsystem.<BR>\r\nI went to a chiropractor and he gave me all kinds of\r\nsupplements. One was a \"detox\" powder (it didn\'t taste like\r\nthe stuff you described though). Also another interesting\r\none was \"EPA-DHA\" which is an omega oil fatty acid\r\nsupplement. It has the \"good\" fat you get from fish,\r\navocadoes, etc. Lack of it supposedly make kids more prone\r\nto be hyperactive, so taking it is supposed to make you more\r\ncalm and focused, and feel better overall.<BR>\r\nI took it and noticed it actually made me kind of depressed.\r\nFor some reason I actually kind of liked the feeling of\r\ndepression because it was a *different* kind of depression\r\nthan usual. It wasn\'t really even depression, just an odd\r\nkind of moodiness.<BR>\r\nYeah, and the dream thing. I stopped drinking (just over a\r\nyear now) but I\'ve had a few dreams where I\'m at a party or\r\nsomething and just start drinking. In the dream I have this\r\nfear or guilt when I remember that I stopped already. The\r\nguilt even lasts for a minute or two until I\'m fully wake\r\nup.<BR>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'24.0.133.128','en'),(3482,1014,'2001-06-02 17:43:39',0,'jp','whoops... damn, totally screwed up that up trying to use a\r\nlink in there. Too bad you can\\\'t edit after post.',0,0,0,0,'24.0.133.128','en'),(3483,1014,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<ol>\r\n<li> peter\\\'s cd stash is not paltry.\r\n<li> josh is cool. he says \\\"aye\\\" instead of yes, but he \r\nsays it really slow. but he\\\'s not a surfer. ok.\r\n</ol>',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3484,1014,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','(i fixed it, jp)',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3485,1014,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','efa\\\'s are good shit.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3486,1011,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','update: 10:51am, saturday morning. fuck. we stayed up all \r\nday friday. i slept for 16 hours. life is really good. no \r\nill effects. ',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3487,1017,'2001-06-02 17:49:54',0,'jo','ironic that i\\\'m reading this while at work, on a weekend, \r\nworking on the new <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://barnesandnobleuniversity.com\\\">b&n \r\nuniversity</a> site.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(3488,1009,'2001-06-02 17:51:31',0,'bmg','hi slight.',0,0,0,0,'66.68.78.158','en'),(3489,1014,'2001-06-02 17:52:44',0,'jp','Thanks le :). You\\\'re fast.<BR>\r\nHow does your head feel today?<BR>\r\nHere\\\'s a good hangover cure:<BR>\r\n - wake up first thing and drink a lot of water<BR>\r\n - take at least 1500-3000mg of vitamin C and a few\r\nB-complex.<BR>\r\n - Eat some starchy food, frozen french fries are good.<BR>\r\n - go back to sleep until ready to face the world.<BR>\r\n - have a nice cup of strong coffee when you finally get\r\nup.<BR>\r\nYou\\\'re probably recovered by now. Watch out for that morning\r\ndrinking. It leads straight to alkie-ville.<BR>',0,0,0,0,'24.0.133.128','en'),(3490,1008,'2001-06-02 18:27:06',0,'bmg','<p>I find it ironic that Quinn accuses incitor of being \r\nnegative, when ALL of Quin\\\'s posts are neither \r\nconstructive, friendly nor supportive to the poing where I \r\nthought  Quinn was going to<em> Incite</em> a riot... \r\nand Mr. Incitor himself was not once thrown off by this... \r\nkudo\\\'s to incitor... a peaceful incitor.',1,0,0,0,'66.68.78.158','en'),(3491,1017,'2001-06-02 19:04:50',0,'ben','b&n univerity? Did not know such a thing existed - wow, now \r\nI\\\'m intrested. ',5,0,0,0,'208.143.2.208','en'),(3492,1017,'2001-06-02 19:25:49',0,'jo','i\\\'m such a pawn.<BR>\r\nbut i genuinely mean it when i say that i\\\'ve read most of \r\nthese classes (because i work with them all day long) and \r\nmany of them are really very good.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(3493,1018,'2001-06-02 20:41:09',0,'jo','i was sympathetic with the neighbor up until the part about \r\nthe neighbor not even living there. then it becomes an \r\nissue of his asking you to shoulder the intrusion of his \r\nfriend but he himself doesn\\\'t have to deal it. that\\\'s \r\nasking too much, in my humble opinion. i\\\'m assuming that \r\nwhen you rented, you were renting not just your living \r\nspace but the backyard, too. what if you wanted to have a \r\nparty or barbecue or something out there this summer? that \r\ncan\\\'t happen now.<BR>\r\nif i were in your position, i would tell set a reasonable \r\ndate by which he needs to leave and express it to both the \r\nneighbor and the man. then i would have a discussion with \r\nthe man where i explained nicely that i liked my privacy \r\nand felt uncomfortable with his continued intrusions.<BR>\r\ni mean, if it were me, this would seriously affect my \r\nhappiness at home, and if you\\\'re not happy at home, that \r\ncarries over to all aspects of your life. you need and \r\ndeserve a peaceful sanctuary.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(3494,1018,'2001-06-02 21:03:05',0,'jo','i should maybe mention that i\\\'m a cancer and a homebody and \r\nanyone fucking with my little corner of the world is just \r\nabout the worst and most grievious offense i can imagine. ',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(3495,1018,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','i\\\'m old fashioned and believe that my home is my \\\'castle\\\'.  invasion of any form is upsetting and potentially dangerous.  i don\\\'t really think compassion comes into play here.  it\\\'s possible to be compassionate and still make it clear to someone that you want little or nothing to do with them.  learning to say \\\'no\\\' is important.  i had a roomate once who didn\\\'t have a job.  we took him in to help him out, but there were limits.  he always tried to bum beer or cigs from me.  and i just told him \\\"no, go get a job, i\\\'ve helped you search the paper and the neighborhood.  now it\\\'s time you did your part.  when you make some money and prove you\\\'re trying to get on your feet, i\\\'ll lend you anything at all.  not until.\\\"  caring for someone does not imply that you must accept any behavior they care to display.  that logic leads to women who accept beatings every night.  likewise it\\\'s possible to help a homeless person out without letting them upset your whole life.',2,0,0,0,'207.205.218.186','en'),(3496,1008,'2002-04-20 20:49:51',273,'Quinn','All right incitor, it sounds like you\\\'ve got a good head on \r\nyour shoulders.  I respect your decent and intelligent \r\nresponses to my livid posts.  I hope things work out for \r\nall concerned. Much luck to you and yours. \r\n\r\nTo the rest of you who reacted so stupidly to what is \r\nobvious provocation: <i>get a grip</i>.  Sometimes you have \r\nto push people to get them to react.  Boy, oh boy. \r\nSometimes emotions have to be raw and violent and \r\nnegative.  I\\\'m not going to san francisco around and \r\npretend like I don\\\'t have opinions.  I have opinions.  \r\nSometimes they\\\'re loud and obnoxious. AND SOMETIMES THEY\\\'RE \r\nIN CAPS. ',1,0,0,1,'38.32.90.105','en'),(3497,1018,'2001-06-02 23:49:09',0,'auntie','you feel uneasy for several reasons.<br><br>\r\n\r\n1 - if the neighbor is not even in residence, why isn\\\'t the \r\nbrother living INSIDE his apartment?<br>\r\n<ul><i>probably because he is uneasy himself about allowing \r\nhis brother into his space.</i></ul><br><br>\r\n\r\n2 - your gut tells you the tent guy is more than just off-\r\nkilter - he\\\'s got serious problems that may cause him at \r\nsome point to threaten more than your privacy.<br><br>\r\n\r\nmy advice is, like all advice, potentially \r\nproblematic.<br><br>\r\n\r\ncontact the neighbor, tell him to put his brother indoors, \r\nand if he is not willing to do so, tell him that he has 30 \r\ndays to make other arrangements, because if his brother \r\nisn\\\'t sane enough to live inside his house, then he\\\'s not \r\nsane enough to live in your back yard.<br><br>\r\n\r\nthe neighbor may dump responsibility for asking his brother \r\nto leave on his asshole neighbor (you) and, if the guy is \r\nas uneven emotionally as you sense, he may decide to take \r\nretribution.  consider this before you act.<br><br>\r\n\r\nyou could just wait it out a little while longer.  chances \r\nare tent guy will soon grow weary of being in your back \r\nyard.<br><br>\r\n\r\ndon\\\'t invite him in.  but, if you think he is hungry or \r\nthirsty, wait until he is not in residence and leave food \r\nand water.  <br><br>\r\n\r\ntry to remind yourself of the only rule that matters in any \r\nreligion or culture -- \\\"do unto others as you would have \r\nthem do unto you.\\\" <br><br>\r\n\r\nthis does NOT mean you should drop wariness.  mentally ill \r\npeople are just that, mentally ill.  he is not responsible \r\nfor his actions if he doesn\\\'t live inside reality.<br><br>\r\n\r\n',2,0,0,0,'24.162.119.106','en'),(3498,1018,'2001-06-03 00:10:51',0,'bark','<p>get a big slobbery outdoor dog.',3,0,0,0,'12.110.65.83','en'),(3499,1020,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','\\\"slipped on my black ann taylor pumps\\\"\r\n<br><br>\r\n:(',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3500,1019,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Philo Moll','I can not concieve of life on the Outside. ',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(3501,1011,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Queer Moll','<p>I like to drink tea and pet cats????????   :(</p>',1,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(3502,1020,'2001-06-03 06:28:43',0,'auntie','but did somebody love him?  will they miss him? <br><br>\r\n\r\nfunerals suck.  nobody ever knows the right thing to say to \r\nmake anyone feel better, so everyone stands around looking \r\nsomber and wondering when they can decently leave.<br><br>\r\n\r\nand le, the black ann taylor pumps are standard wardrobe \r\nitems, even if they aren\\\'t ann taylor, you gotta have black \r\nshoes for important events that you don\\\'t want to attend \r\nbut you know you must.<br><br>\r\n\r\ni am sorry to say that the only black shoes i own now are \r\ncanvas and very comfortable and i have worn them to \r\nimportant events with the other standard summer wardrobe \r\nitem, the black linen dress.<br><br>',2,0,0,0,'24.162.119.106','en'),(3503,1019,'2001-06-03 06:30:39',0,'auntie','you don\\\'t have to be an academic hero for your parents.  \r\nwhat you have to do is go to the career center and get \r\nheadhunted by important companies so they will feel like \r\nyour education is actually going to get you a job someday.',1,0,0,0,'24.162.119.106','en'),(3504,967,'2001-06-03 09:04:38',0,'lulu','this sucks my tweeter, egg. what kind of a name is egg \r\nanyway. ooooohhhh, hi my name is EGG, i\\\'m hip with it, i\\\'m \r\nsoooo cooooll, read my article, i\\\'m sooooo awesome cause i \r\nwrote about lucky charms and a guy named sam, oooooohhh, \r\ntouch me i\\\'m golden.',2,0,0,0,'63.255.26.180','en'),(3505,1017,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','heh! just signed up for the jazz and classical music courses\r\nand the lord of the rings course (cos i want to read it\r\nagain before the first film anyway).\r\n\r\nthe angle sure worked on me, i just ordered $250 worth of\r\ncourse materials :)',0,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(3506,1011,'2001-06-03 10:38:37',0,'eoj','it\\\'s all about sleep depravation.  there are many routes.  \r\nthey all lead to the same place.',1,0,0,0,'64.3.15.93','en'),(3507,1008,'2001-06-03 10:51:43',0,'eoj','frisking people before they get in the car, well, it seems \r\nexcessive, even if this guy is the super-creepo-deluxe-with-\r\ncheese.\r\n\r\ni know if i met a girl\\\'s brother for the first time, and he \r\nfrisked me, i would be a little freaked out.  and there\\\'s \r\nthis interesting thing about life called the self-\r\nfulfilling prophecy.\r\n\r\nbut, little sisters are great.  i love mine dearly.  i can \r\nonly hope that rachel never gets into this kind of \r\nsituation.  she will be 16 soon.   luckily i think my \r\nmother\\\'s eagerness for my sister to have a boyfriend has \r\ncaused her to be less than eager to have one.  well \r\nluckily, and not so luckily.  \r\n',3,0,0,0,'64.3.15.93','en'),(3508,1013,'2001-06-03 11:07:34',0,'eoj','i\\\'d just like to say it was nice meeting you tonight. :)\r\n<P>\r\nin the department of disclaimers (since your post is a big \r\ndisclaimer), i do apologize if i did not seem excessively \r\nchatty.  music-filled clubs are for dancing, not chatting.  \r\n(hard to hear, and all that.)  but, catch me outside of a \r\ndance club: if i get started talking about something, it \r\ncould be frightening when i don\\\'t stop.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'64.3.15.93','en'),(3509,1019,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>Let me put it this way. You think college sucks. You\\\'re \r\nprobably right, as most colleges seem to suck. However, \r\nwhen you are in college there is vacation on the horizon, \r\nand you don\\\'t have to get up at 8am every day all year.</p>\r\n<p>Once you leave college, you enter a world where you need \r\nto work in order to eat. This means you have to do things \r\nthat you don\\\'t even enjoy, in order to achieve the \r\nfinancial flexibility required to prepare to do the things \r\nyou <u>do</u> enjoy.</p>\r\n<p>In school, you have clearly defined goals. In life, you \r\nfulfill whatever role you can fall into. For some people, \r\nthis means working at Burger King.</p>\r\n<p>But hey, I <u>like</u> the fact that I was born despite \r\nmy biological intention to strangle myself to death in the \r\nprocess. I <u>like</u> the fact that I can see with glasses \r\nas an aid. Does it matter that the economics forces \r\nrequired for such benefits also require tight integration \r\nwith my physical reality? Is it worth the 20-60 hours a \r\nweek that we spend taking care of our base needs and wants?\r\n</p>\r\n<p>On the inside of \\\"enter the 36 chambers\\\", there\\\'s a \r\nquote from each member of the wu-tang clan. The one for \r\nRaekwon (\\\"The Chef\\\") is :<p>\r\n<p>\\\"Niggaz gotta eat.\\\"</p>\r\n<p>College places an abstractive layer between the fact \r\nthat you need to eat and the rest of the things that you \r\ndo. Once you leave college, that\\\'s what it\\\'s all about.</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin<br>\r\nniggaz gotta eat.\r\n\r\n',4,0,0,0,'24.221.170.233','en'),(3510,1018,'2001-06-03 16:42:24',0,'cait','I may just be mean and selfish, but I would call the police.',0,0,0,0,'63.77.235.159','en'),(3511,1017,'2001-06-03 16:50:08',0,'cait','I think your dream indicates you have an asian fetish.',0,0,0,0,'63.77.235.159','en'),(3512,1017,'2001-06-03 17:06:50',0,'jo','dude, the lord of the rings course was a bitch because of \r\nall the character entities. those had to be manually \r\nentered, yuck.<BR>\r\nbut yo. those are 3 really good classes.<BR>\r\ni can\\\'t believe i\\\'m talking about this.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(3513,1019,'2001-06-03 20:02:29',0,'sic to darwin','tho i understand the whole rat race for some dollas...i dont \r\nsee much relief in college. i\\\'ve not had a long vacation \r\nsince i started cuz i go to summer school and im jus wiped \r\nout. i will think bout what ya\\\'ll wrote thanks',0,0,0,0,'129.65.91.56','en'),(3514,1022,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','<p>I can only exist in diads. I can not hang out with more \r\nthan 1 other person at the same time. It\\\'s just not fun for \r\nme. I shut down.</p>\r\n<p>I have very few friends, there is little planning to our \r\ninteraction. Usually just a single word on the telephone. \r\nIt was funny. While I was reading your message and thinking \r\nabout this, it happens:</p>\r\n<p>[ring ring]</p>\r\n<p>Me: Hello?</p>\r\n<p>Him: Cannol.</p>\r\n<p>Me: Okay.</p>\r\n<p>[hanging up]</p>\r\n<p>It\\\'s now clear that my friend will be here in 15 minutes \r\nand we\\\'re going to go out for cannolis and espresso. And on \r\nthis note, I should get dressed.</p>',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(3515,1024,'2001-06-03 23:44:36',0,'bmg','<p>dubai! why dubai? I did a little time outside of \r\ndubai... but  i wasn\\\'t there to visit. what is you attraction \r\nto dubai?</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.78.158','en'),(3516,1025,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<OL>\r\n<LI>vacuum car\r\n<LI>wash car\r\n<LI>wax car (not)\r\n<LI>place ad in sfchronicle/craigslist/exite/yahoo: \\\"2000 \r\nhonda civic, ghetto gold, boomin\\\' system, 26k mi., take it \r\naway: 13.5k\\\"\r\n<LI>wait\r\n<LI>take envelope of cash money to triumph dealer\r\n<LI>vroom!\r\n</OL>',3,0,0,0,'216.103.209.68','en'),(3517,1014,'2001-06-04 01:30:19',0,'chaya','i\\\'d like to note here that both elly and i woke up \r\nyesterday sans hangover.  not only that, we both woke up \r\nfeeling KICKASS.  i highly highly recommend staying up \r\nuntil you are hungover and then sleeping off the whole damn \r\nthing.  also.  vitamin c kicks ass.',6,0,0,0,'158.252.208.171','en'),(3518,1008,'2001-06-04 01:44:36',0,'chaya','\\\"i\\\'m not going to san francisco \r\naround.\\\"<br><br>cute.<br><br>(burn! burn!)',6,0,0,0,'158.252.208.171','en'),(3519,1011,'2001-06-04 02:21:25',0,'keuch2','if you try too hard to be different, you become normal. it \r\nbackfires.',1,0,0,0,'129.130.87.11','en'),(3520,1012,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','i cant get into decade-theme parties.  but why dont we \r\nchoose some place to go out and all get dressed up \r\nlike that.\r\n<p>\r\ni have been thinking of getting a feather-haircut. but its \r\ntrue that i got the idea about the belted sweater dress \r\nfrom a betsey johnson fall collection video. ',0,0,0,0,'216.175.103.38','en'),(3521,1012,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','to append the above: that means, yeah i know its in \r\nfashion currently, and boy is that funny.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.103.38','en'),(3522,1014,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','someone should send me some emergen-c.  le got me addicted \r\nwhen she was here.  that\\\'s her cure for everything - \r\nemergen-c.  and salt.',2,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(3523,1026,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>this is my spiral:</P>\r\n<PRE>\r\n           motorcycle\r\n   sell car             get a job\r\n           food?\r\n</PRE>',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3524,1029,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>the house fills with hoots and transports of gay joy \r\nas this piece is recited aloud and with pride!</P>',2,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3525,1029,'2001-06-04 07:19:09',0,'Mr. Garrison','<P>Jay, would you like to get up and share a poem with \r\nthe class?\r\n<BR><BR>\r\n...\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nwell, i liked it, how about you Mr. Hand?\r\n</P>',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3526,1031,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i was just doing yoga in the entryway. i like the \r\ncombination of extremes between shoulder stand and \r\nits counterpose, fish (there are others but i like fish). i \r\nlike how for about 20 seconds after i have finished with \r\nshoulderstand and fish, my back sends me these \r\nmessages like \\\"what is this destruction\\\" and then it \r\ncalms down, it says \\\"thank you.\\\"\r\n<br><br>\r\na long time ago i got stoned in your house and you are \r\none of the few who i can be happy stoned around, not \r\nnervous, no big deal, it\\\'s proper. a flashback of your \r\ndorm room at mills, a flashback of you leaning and \r\ngesturing with a bottle of whiskey during one of my lost \r\nmimosa weekends with you, and a flashback of \r\npouring water over shoulders at osento. \r\n<br><br>\r\ni don\\\'t know what i\\\'m doing, the past three days have \r\njust been stupid with this soaring emotion, just wanting \r\nto eat the planet alive, to cry, like, on the verge of \r\nscreaming at all times, but crazy screaming, not angry. \r\ni\\\'ve wanted you around a lot because i have needed \r\nsome egg. maybe i have needed to paint or be in \r\nbathtub pictures or i don\\\'t know. \r\n<br><br>\r\ni don\\\'t know',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3527,1031,'2001-06-04 09:22:31',0,'anon','<PRE>\r\n\\\'le,\\\' whispers the tree outside the window\r\nwatching her sleep and dreaming of sharing her bed\r\nseasons pass and the tree\\\'s want grows\r\nbranches out as though seeking sunlight in a dark clime\r\ntoward her bed\r\nand with the right wind\r\nit is rap rap rapping on the window with desire\r\n</PRE>',1,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3528,1031,'2001-06-04 10:58:22',0,'jp','Hello egg and le.<BR>\r\nYou conjure:<BR>\r\nplacid moonlight, earthy hippies, translucent windows,\r\nhidden daydreams...<BR>\r\nstoney chattering, urgent abandon, friendly discovery...<BR>\r\nstreet life,  fruits and vegetables, spoons.<BR>\r\n<BR>\r\nMoss with gold glitter. Languid blankets -- macrame, late at\r\nnight.<BR><BR>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'24.0.133.128','en'),(3529,1031,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i don\\\'t want the tree to eat me :(',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3530,1034,'2001-06-04 16:52:03',0,'jo','he\\\'s nice!<BR>\r\ntwo of his roommates (current <b>and</b> former) read this. \r\ni\\\'m sure they could give you all the ins and outs.<BR>\r\nmuahahaha.<BR>\r\n(my roommate, on the other hand, would just say, \\\"she \r\ncrushes a lot. a lot. and she makes tea for me. and likes \r\nvh1.\\\")',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(3531,1031,'2001-06-04 16:53:14',0,'gomez','Macrame????\r\n',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(3532,1035,'2001-06-04 17:20:44',0,'MightyBluJ','   I\\\'ve often said that \\\"a world with a sober Matt is like a \r\nworld without migas.\\\"   It\\\'s frighteningly true.',1,0,0,0,'204.64.42.245','en'),(3533,1033,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','\nyum. this makes me heart glow gladly, having just rescued \nmyself from the cesspool of suburbia. plug: Lucky Creation \n(854 washington) in sf chinatown. perhaps i shall go \nmyself today.\n\n',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(3534,1035,'2001-06-04 18:06:08',0,'szajic','\r\nI think computers can shake you, change you.  But only if you \r\nlet them.  Vonnegut was probably never shaken by a computer \r\nbecause he didn\\\'t want to be - probably many people here have \r\nhad words on a computer screen evoke a physical reaction.\r\n\r\nLast night put forth the idea that there\\\'s a generation of \r\npeople approaching 30 right now who never really let \r\ncomputers into their lives.  This silly generalization based \r\non older brothers and sisters of friends and conversations \r\nwith grad students.  I\\\'d like to hear thoughts, counter-\r\nexamples.  But the idea is that these people were too young \r\nto think to buy a computer (like, say, my parents did) but \r\ntoo old to use computers much during their formative years.\r\n',3,0,0,0,'130.91.196.77','en'),(3535,1035,'2001-06-04 18:37:03',0,'stellaloo','<P>I am one the generation of \\\'rapidly approaching 30\\\'. I \r\nhave let the computer into my life, however it took until I \r\nwas 25 to allow it to happen. \r\n</P> <P>\r\nI actively rejected anything to do with computers for the \r\nmajority of my life. My father, who has been the technology \r\nindustry since the 60\\\'s, attempted to lure me into his world \r\nof Macintosh, run and brun commands, etc and so on from the \r\ntime I was 10. I *hated* it. But then, things were different \r\nthen. The scope of entertainment for me was linited to \r\ncomplicated word games that I was inexperienced to \r\nunderstand and pacman with no colors! Arcade games were MUCH \r\nmore exciting. (Atari!). Into my teens, I was a rebellious \r\npunk rock girl who had much better things to do than geek \r\nout with Dad. \r\n</P><P>\r\nThen I moved to Arcada California and I had no money. The \r\nonly thing that I did have was my roommates college ID card \r\nthat resembled me enough to gain me access to the computer \r\nlabs at school, where I was introduced to the lovely world \r\nof the Moo. I was addicted. \r\n</P><P>\r\nI don\\\'t think that it\\\'s necessarily the computer that hooks \r\npeople and changes thier lives. I think it\\\'s the internet. \r\nComputers by themselves are rather boring. But when you add \r\nthe online experience, where just a button-click away is a \r\nwhole world of people to meet, ideas to share, information \r\nto research, it makes the experience so much more exciting \r\nand magical. Had the internet been around when I was in my \r\nearly teens (at least, had it been as commonplace as it is \r\nnow) I think that most in my generation would have been much \r\nmore attracted to it. \r\n</P>',0,0,0,0,'168.100.203.247','en'),(3536,1035,'2001-06-04 18:38:53',0,'stellaloo','er, make that ArcaTa, California.',0,0,0,0,'168.100.203.247','en'),(3537,1035,'2001-06-04 18:44:43',0,'LinearB','SORRY I MISSED YOU GUYS SATURDAY.\r\n\r\n<P>I woke up around 9:30pm and tried to call BMG to see \r\nwhere everyone was going, but I couldn\\\'t reach him.\r\n\r\n<P>..and I didn\\\'t have a number for you.\r\n\r\n<P>Oh well. till next time.',1,0,0,0,'207.8.3.193','en'),(3538,1035,'2001-06-04 19:00:52',0,'jo','there will be more opportunities. you can never have too \r\nmany drinking buddies.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(3539,1035,'2001-06-04 19:02:13',0,'jo','oh also. HI STEFAN! HI STEFAN STEFAN I HEART STEFAN HI HI \r\nHIHIHI!',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(3540,1035,'2001-06-04 19:36:48',0,'Strontiumdog','I think that a world without Miga\\\'s might just be \r\nalright.at least it would be better for my cholesterol.',1,0,0,0,'206.224.71.188','en'),(3541,1035,'2001-06-04 20:24:23',0,'MightyBluJ to Strontiumdog','BLASPHEMER!!!!!',3,0,0,0,'204.64.42.245','en'),(3542,1034,'2001-06-04 20:40:25',0,'kat','<p>i think last years roommate would probably say that im \r\nmostly mysterious. i tend to go thru long periods of quiet \r\nmusings secretly doing \\\'things\\\' in my room...broken by \r\nshort bursts of high energy bounciness demanding that \r\neveryone i know must go do things with me, eat with me, \r\nsleep with me, dance with me. in between all that i read a \r\nlot and hug on my dog, cook the occasional killer meal, and \r\nhave been known to partake in bizarre drinking/photography \r\nexperimentations. oh...and if you bring chocolate home that \r\nyou plan on eating, you better hide it. </p>',4,0,0,0,'12.64.48.233','en'),(3543,1038,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','dear allen ginsburg, why cant our lives be more like yours? \r\nits a joke, chet, its just a joke. \r\n<p>\r\ndear jay, i think you should read at the starry plough or \r\njustice league poetry slam.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(3544,1035,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','people probably asked the same thing when phones were coming \r\nout and microwaves. ',6,0,0,0,'64.229.135.28','en'),(3545,1031,'2001-06-04 20:58:06',0,'non2:','I think I\\\'m in love with le.  Is that possible?',1,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(3546,1035,'2001-06-04 21:21:36',0,'bmg to jo','<p>And, it was sooo much fun! We will have to do more of \r\nthat; turbo dog is good beer. Maybe soon, one day, our \r\nbeloved president & CEO Austin Graves Swinney will join us \r\nfor a swinneydotAustin lo-tech happy hour.</p>\r\n',2,0,0,0,'66.68.78.158','en'),(3547,1035,'2001-06-04 21:23:05',0,'bmg','oh yah, and sunday I watched another crispin glover \r\nmovie...\\\"At Close Range.\\\" River\\\'s edge was better.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'66.68.78.158','en'),(3548,1031,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','why don\\\'t you send me email with your, er, measurments and \r\ni\\\'ll let you know',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3549,1037,'2001-06-04 22:51:18',0,'sic','almost expected a tribute to the britney spears...happy to \r\nfind out not',0,0,0,0,'129.65.91.42','en'),(3550,1039,'2001-06-04 23:08:07',0,'cody','...and if you have 5 seconds to spare, I\\\'ll tell you the \r\nstory of my life...and do you have a vacancy? for a back \r\nscrubber',0,0,0,0,'63.239.171.226','en'),(3551,1027,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','media doesn\\\'t have a causal relationship with violence, rather it is part of a dynamic.  first consider the predisposition of the actor, which is based (at least in part) on Media Desensitization, Violent Role Models, Conditioning via video games and the like, povery, exposure to criminal or violent acts, and drug/alcohol use/abuse.\r\n<br>\r\nthat\\\'s not all however.  there are the demands of authority, in this case not normally the government but perhaps a gang leader, close friend, parent, coach, whomever.  to determine the weight of the demands of authority consider: proximity of authority and respect for authority.\r\n<br>\r\ngroup absolution (mob mentality): identification with group, intensity of group support for violence.  ever wonder why so many \\\'peaceful\\\' protests turn violent?  don\\\'t just blame law enforcement...\r\n<br>\r\nAttractiveness of victim.  is it safe and desirable to cause harm to another?  remember it is literally true that bullies are cowards.  a bully will give you every chance to prove you might be a danger to him or her, only when you do not respond in a way he or she reconizes will he or she attack.  consider: available strategies (weapons, friends, etc.), relevance of victim (enemy gang, wrong color skin, different class, etc.), payoff (status gain, possession of money or status symbols).  \r\n<br>\r\nin the case of not just violence, but killing, we need to consider the psychological distance involved.  consider:  physical distance (use of a firearm, baseball bat, bomb, flying a freaking airplane five miles up and dropping 2000lb. bombs, etc.)  emotional distance (social norms, racism, povery, anti gay feelings, anti social class, etc.)\r\n<br>\r\nin WWII our military learned just how hard it can be to enable violent behavior in soldiers.  infantry on the front had a firing rate of 15-20%.  out of those who fired, only around 40% were willing to fire at the enemy, the rest preffering to fire over the enemies head.  after realizing this, the military spent millions to condition our soldiers to be killers.  result?  in Vietnam the reported firing rate was 95%, with almost all of those being shots at the enemy directly.  \r\n<br>\r\nviolence is ugly.  rarely it is required.  if we as a society, and as a species, are going to gain control of violence we are going to have to stop marginalizing it.  simple causal relationships will never touch on the dynamics of conflict.  and we are, after all, animals, and nature not just sees animals hunt each other, but sometimes even go to war.  chimps for instance, have been known to kill each other in exceedingly violent ways even when population/food pressure is not a problem.  the victors of these wars then kill every baby in sight, eat the flesh of the defeated, and mate with the females.  \r\n<br> \r\nsince this subject is something i study and teach, i could go on forever boring you.  i suggest reading The Lucifer Principle by Howard Bloom, and On Killing by Lt. Col. Dave Grossman if you are truly interested in understanding violence in humans.  Or email me with any questions.',3,0,0,0,'207.205.220.210','en'),(3552,1039,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','i was looking for a job and now ive found a job, and heaven \r\nknows im miserable now. \r\n',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(3553,1035,'2001-06-04 23:23:45',0,'jo to bmg','how could river\\\'s edge be better than anything?',1,0,0,0,'172.138.156.94','en'),(3554,1027,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','just remembered this, check out the <a href=\\\"http://www.killology.com/\\\">killology </a> website.',3,0,0,0,'207.205.220.210','en'),(3555,1038,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>i read this jay, and i am bored sitting here.  what a\r\nboring day.  my head hurts and i dont know why.  i drank\r\nwater.  i ate food.  and i have annoying energy that is\r\npestering me.  but i like reading you poems. especially\r\nbecause i slummed around your floor all weekend getting in\r\nyour way and making you buy extra bagels.\r\n</P><P>\r\nthanks for the poems and thanks for the dinner the other\r\nnight, and the bagels the other morning.</P>',1,0,0,0,'64.51.232.105','en'),(3556,1035,'2001-06-05 00:29:15',0,'bmg','Watch at close range. =)\r\n',0,0,0,0,'66.68.78.158','en'),(3557,1035,'2001-06-05 00:31:38',0,'mscreant','\\\"you don\\\'t understand a goddamn thing, do you?\\\"\r\n\r\n',2,0,0,0,'66.68.190.232','en'),(3558,1033,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>I have eaten at this restaurant.</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n',2,0,0,0,'24.221.170.233','en'),(3559,1027,'2001-06-05 01:09:42',0,'cyantist','<br>\r\n<br>\r\ni\\\'m just curious as to why every country i\\\'ve ever been to \r\nbesides america, makes me feel safer and ostensibly has less \r\nviolence.  hong kong hasn\\\'t had a shooting in who knows how \r\nlong and the most violent thing that happens here is \r\npedestrians getting run over by taxis.  \r\n<br>\r\nyeah, i agree with you on the standpoint of the media.  i \r\nblame a huge portion of violence on it, as well as nurture \r\nin the home. \\\"if daddy or mommy says it is ok, then it must \r\nbe ok\\\".\r\n<br>\r\nthey have pc gaming rooms here with games like quake and the \r\nlot.  there\\\'s plenty of killing going on there.  no denying \r\nthat.  however, most everything here is based on cuteness.  \r\nit isn\\\'t often that hello kitty runs off to murder in a \r\nfirst person shooting game.\r\n<br>\r\ni worry about the affect our culture is having on other \r\ncountries.  hong kong is the most commercial place i\\\'ve ever \r\nbeen in my life.  this city revolves around spending money \r\nand shopping.  it is the passtime here.  people here shop \r\nlike no american i\\\'ve ever seen.  they have it down to a \r\nscience.  i suppose shopping is better than drinking until \r\nit clouds your judgement.   i dunno.   i\\\'m just confused as \r\nto why the american system is so broken.',1,0,0,0,'202.77.253.245','en'),(3560,1039,'2001-06-05 01:18:10',0,'good friend','hey you have good and strong stamna of writing, why don\\\'t \r\nyou try something revolutionry, which could amazed the world \r\nand make you remember forever and ever, i believe that you \r\nhave a good heart but you live in the dreams life, comeout \r\nman \\\" otherwise no body gone come to bring you out. ',1,0,0,0,'134.117.82.56','en'),(3561,1038,'2001-06-05 01:35:20',0,'lulu','what is this? poetry is overrated and irritating. go get a \r\nmexi-mullet, jay.  ooooohhh look at me, i\\\'m jay, i\\\'m a poet, \r\ni\\\'m sooooooo intellectual, touch me...oh...nope...you can\\\'t \r\ntouch me cause i\\\'m sooooo sizzling hot. my vocabulary is the \r\nsize of greenland...oooohhh i know where greenland is, cause \r\ni\\\'m jay, and i\\\'m sooooooo smart and awesome, i know \r\neverything you don\\\'t know....oh hey now, don\\\'t get too close, \r\ni\\\'m hot as satan\\\'s asshole.   \r\n\r\ngo get a mexi-mullet, jay.\r\n',2,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(3562,1038,'2001-06-05 01:36:20',0,'lulu','thanks for sending me my mail.\r\n',6,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(3563,1039,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','you all make me sad. email me at chiam@gee.kz<br>\r\nyou know. peters server. the guy who cares for me. the guy \r\nwho makes le smile. the guy who is busy. the guy who we all \r\nlook upto in some sort of waay or another. im so sick of \r\ntyping. im so sick of drinking.let me go home. im spinning.',6,0,0,0,'64.229.135.28','en'),(3564,1027,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','our system is only slightly more broken than everyone else\\\'s.  while you might feel safer in these other countries, the fact is you probably aren\\\'t.  crime rate stats notwithstanding (they are notoriously poorly compiled), violence is a problem almost everywhere.  look at what happened in nepal today.  part of the problem is that we are a society of victims.  too many people refuse to take a hand in their own protection.  woman refuse to stop wearing flimsy outfits into dark alleys while drunk.  mind you, even if they did stop, rape would still happen almost as often, and i don\\\'t mean to marginalize it.  people try to wish violence away.  like all hard things in life, we must, together, face the problem and find a solution.  and no perfect solution will ever come about.  but violence doesn\\\'t have to be as endemic as it is.  taking actual responsibility for ourselves is key here.  if you let the government protect you, you will not know safety.  protect yourself.  be aware.  plan ahead.  speak against violence, but recognize that sometimes it really is an option.  we need to stop worshipping the violent.  i could be classified as violent, and some, women in particular, behave as if i am the best thing ever.  this is a warning sign to me.  if a person likes that i am capable of violent action, if that is what attracts them to me.  they are no friend of mine and never will be.  violence is my last resort.  and while i\\\'m proud i can protect myself and others, i am never proud to have done so through the application of force.  i think we need to understand violence better.  if you\\\'ve never been truly attacked, life or death situation here, then it\\\'s awful hard to understand my views.  but if there were more people with my view on violence, it truly would be the last resort.  it won\\\'t go away unless we face it for what it is.',2,0,0,0,'207.205.220.210','en'),(3565,1040,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','hey sawks, can you get in contact with me regarding the \r\nproject at work i\\\'m on.  it\\\'s really urgent.  thanks.',1,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(3566,1040,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','brilliant o, just brilliant.',2,0,0,0,'64.51.232.105','en'),(3567,1040,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','hey austin tell that guy who runs this site to go play in \r\ntraffic. ',6,0,0,0,'64.229.135.28','en'),(3568,1043,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','people confuse the fuck out of me. really they do. im so \r\nfucking hurt and let down and depressed. ugh. ',6,0,0,0,'64.229.135.28','en'),(3569,1039,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','i write too much on this site. too much time on my hands. i \r\nneed a job. 66 posts. ugh. ',6,0,0,0,'64.229.135.28','en'),(3570,1027,'2001-06-05 06:07:23',0,'cyantist','<br>an old squatter friend of mine once had a shirt that\r\nsaid, \\\"there will be no peace until man no longer walks the\r\nface of the earth\\\".  upon first seeing this shirt, i was\r\nextremely sad.  however.. i\\\'ve come to the conclusion that\r\nperhaps it is right.  that as long as we continue to be what\r\nwe are, there will never be peace.  i just need to find it\r\non a smaller scale.  \r\n<br><br>\r\ni once lived in a commune near santa fe, when i was homeless\r\nand i have vivid memories of how peaceful everything was\r\nthere.  never once did a dispute break out amongst the\r\ndwellers that couldn\\\'t be solved with good old fashioned\r\nconversation.  why do we have to result in physical violence\r\nin order to preserve our ideals and morals?  why do we feel\r\nthe serious need to defend ourselves by inflicting pain? \r\nwhat does that prove?  how does that make one right?  (i\\\'m\r\nnot saying \\\"we\\\" in the reader sense, but as a population) \r\n<br><br>\r\nthe statistics for  hong kong and england speak for\r\nthemselves.  very little crime happens here in comparison. \r\ni feel safer walking around at night, because everything is\r\nvisible.  you are out in the open no matter where you go. \r\nthe only way i would feel in danger, is if everyone on the\r\nstreet turned on me.  granted, i don\\\'t walk in dark alleys\r\nalone.. but i just don\\\'t do that anyplace.  they scare me.\r\nwhat do you suppose we do about this?  how do we change?',1,0,0,0,'202.77.253.245','en'),(3571,1040,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','hi.',4,0,0,0,'209.178.136.30','en'),(3572,1043,'2001-06-05 08:45:56',0,'keuch2','beck\\\'s are great. fucking tops.',1,0,0,0,'129.130.231.113','en'),(3573,1046,'2001-06-05 17:29:36',0,'bmg','<p>O shit.</p><p>Bring it on Bubba!</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'66.68.79.197','en'),(3574,1046,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','oh my gawd. werent you the one who thought \\\"yanni is good\\\" \r\nyesterday. i saw you. i know who you are.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(3575,1045,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','i saw a czech woman play the ukelele on tv once. it has left \r\nan indelible mark on my soul. she had a microphone. she just \r\nscreamed and screamed into the microphone. i cant help \r\nmyself, when someone screams the right way i just wont forget \r\nit. actually, to tell the absolute truth i aodre the ukelele, \r\nand the wya you spell it. have you seen \\\"some like it hot\\\"?\r\n<p>\r\nor is this bullshit and im a sucker.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(3576,1040,'2001-06-05 18:12:41',0,'auntie','being off topic on swinney is impossible.  EVERYTHING is on \r\ntopic.  this is not a mailing list, it\\\'s swinney.',3,0,0,0,'24.162.119.106','en'),(3577,1044,'2001-06-05 18:18:24',0,'Lunesse','Tahiti. It\\\'s a nice place, but a lot more fun if you speak \r\nFrench.<p>\r\nMorocco. I am planning a France/Morocco trip for the spring \r\nof 2002, hopefully, or the year after that. I have been to \r\nFrance, but my husband has not, and I have been wanting to \r\ngo to Morocco for a couple years now.<p>\r\nThe island of Kauai, in Hawa\\\'ii. It is so laid back there, \r\nso non-GO GO GO when I returned to San Francisco, I \r\ncherished the first days of driving to work I had when \r\ngoing along at 40 or 50 felt just fine and dandy, before \r\nthe faster pace of the mainland robbed me of my brief \r\nexperience of relaxation, slowness, and \\\"I\\\'ll get there \r\nwhen I get there\\\" mentality.\r\n<p>\r\nThe Baja.\r\nSucking back a margarita and clams so fresh that if you \r\nsqueeze lemon on them and they don\\\'t move, they are not \r\nworth eating. Under a restaurant with no walls and a \r\nceiling of palm fronds, the beach for a floor and a \r\ntiny,weathered pier reaching out into the Sea of Cortez \r\njust a handful of steps away.',1,0,0,0,'209.213.209.50','en'),(3578,1044,'2001-06-05 18:22:33',0,'bmg','<li>austin, tx</li>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'66.68.79.197','en'),(3579,1041,'2001-06-05 18:44:57',0,'auntie','short of restoring the american family and small town \r\nvalues, i don\\\'t see any good answer to this problem any \r\ntime soon.<br><br>\r\n\r\nit\\\'s all a trade-off.  before divorce was respectable, \r\npeople stayed together in the same extended families \r\nforever.<br><br>\r\n\r\nthe old and sick were cared for because society demanded we \r\ntake care of our own.<br><br>\r\n\r\npeople had larger families, which meant there were more \r\npeople to share the caregiver load. and the financial \r\nload.<br><br>\r\n\r\nnow there are more people electing to live single, less \r\nthan zero population growth among most americans, divorce \r\ncauses financial and emotional complicationss.<br><br>\r\n\r\nsmall towns have digorged their offspring across the world. \r\nnobody lives near each other anymore.<br><br>\r\n\r\nmost families require two incomes to support mom, dad, and \r\none or two kids, there isn\\\'t any extra to support grandma, \r\nuncle joe, and freddie with schizophrenia.<br><br>\r\n\r\nthe only viable solution is to stop dumping the mentally \r\nill out of the mental hospitals onto the streets, make the \r\nVA hospitals take care of the vets.  <br><br>\r\nrebuild the welfare systems we have in place to take care \r\nof those who are truly in need, even if it means lifetime \r\nwelfare.  <br><br>\r\n\r\nAND, we have to teach the offspring of the mentally ill and \r\nunemployable how to take care of themselves, in spite of \r\ngrowing up in horribly dysfunctional situations. <br><br>\r\n\r\nand that means we need to do something about the education \r\nsystem, which is the root of many problems we see on the \r\nstreets today.  there is no short term solution.<br><br>',0,0,0,0,'24.162.119.106','en'),(3580,1044,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','prague is a nice place. tagged to all hell by the yootz tho. ',6,0,0,0,'64.229.135.28','en'),(3581,1045,'2001-06-05 19:43:12',0,'Grayson','I\\\'ve seen \\\"Some Like it Hot\\\" seventeen times.  I can play \r\nalong with M. Monroe.  I learned how to play the ukulele \r\nusing a copy of Radio and Television Mirror, dated June \r\n1951.  Arthur Godfrey is on the cover.  It showed the \r\nfinger positions for three chords. That\\\'s all you need.  I \r\nfound it in an antique store when I bought a a plaster \r\nbust of Danny Kaye.  This morning I bought a cheap \r\ncigar and smoked it on the corner of Boylston Street \r\nand Massachusetts Avenue.  I saw Robert DeNiro drive \r\nby in a SUV.  He was wearing a NY Yankees baseball \r\ncap.  ',1,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(3582,1041,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','30% of homeless people have a full time job. \r\n<p>\r\nhomelessness is a problem more and more now because less and \r\nless is being spent on mentally ill people who need \r\nroom,food, and attention. because most dont look at them as \r\na poductive segment of the economy, they are expected to \r\ncheck in and pick up their meds.\r\n<p>\r\nthe world bank and imf do this to other countries all the \r\ntime. they force them to spend less on social welfare and \r\nmore on \\\"development\\\". \r\n<p>\r\nreading and writing is development.<br>\r\nfull stomachs is development.<br>\r\nmedical attention is development.<br>\r\n<p>\r\nit just isnt profitable in a world where profit is number \r\none. \r\n<p>\r\nan easy solution to this mess is higher taxes, a tax on \r\ntransfers of money over borders and a more sympathetic \r\nmedia/government/voter. ',6,0,0,0,'64.229.135.28','en'),(3583,1044,'2001-06-05 20:28:51',0,'jo','well i mean, since he already said it...<BR>\r\nyes! come play with us!',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(3584,1044,'2001-06-05 20:39:39',0,'jp','I\\\'ve travelled around Asia before. A good place to go if \r\nyou want it to be *different*. Haven\\\'t seen any of Europe \r\nexcept for 3 weeks in London.<BR>\r\nThe ultimate grungy \\\"travelling\\\" destination is India. This \r\nis if you want to \\\"travel\\\" with backpack and $1 a night \r\nguest rooms and roughing it. I spent 6 weeks there and it \r\nwas quite an experience. Not a good place for a \\\"vacation\\\" \r\nthough. I came into Calcutta after living in Japan for 2 \r\n1/2 years. It was going from one foreign extreme to \r\nanother. The taxi ride from airport (where all the beggars \r\nand lepers congregate when international flights comes in) \r\nleft my lower jaw dropped the whole time. The whole way \r\nsaying \\\"Whoa!\\\" at all the cows, chickens, men pulling \r\nrickshaws, women with basket on their heads. It was like \r\nwalking into a National Geographic -- total chaos. India \r\nwill blow your mind.<BR>\r\nThailand is a cool place. Bangkok was a good place to \r\nrecover from India. Still somewhat grungy compared to Japan \r\nbut 100 time better than India. Best of all is to get out \r\nof the city to the mountains or islands were it\\\'s cleaner \r\nand the people are really mellow and smiley people.<BR>\r\nI\\\'ve heard it\\\'s obnoxious in China and Vietnam where there \r\ncommunist and give you grief or hassle for money.<BR>\r\nNext I\\\'d like to go somewhere in the south-pacific for fun \r\nand relaxation, and do the Europe thing eventually.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.172.123.3','en'),(3585,1044,'2001-06-05 20:41:56',0,'erin','telluride, Co. great fun. good camping not far. big ass \r\nmountain. mmmmmm...\r\n',0,0,0,0,'129.105.107.184','en'),(3586,1046,'2002-04-20 20:49:51',273,'Quinn','Lulu, you\\\'re boring, witless and you can\\\'t write for shit.',6,0,0,1,'198.185.18.207','en'),(3587,1046,'2001-06-05 21:28:06',0,'lulu','ooooohhhh hi, my name is quinn, i\\\'m soooo awesome, i\\\'m an \r\noriginal hemingway, i know a verb from a noun, i\\\'m soooooo \r\nswell. look at me! i can type soooooo fast, i\\\'m a wri-ter.',1,0,0,0,'63.255.35.205','en'),(3588,1046,'2001-06-05 21:44:13',0,'jo','hi, have we slipped into 7th grade and i didn\\\'t notice it? \r\nwhat the fuck?',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(3589,1046,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','lulu, I think you are sweet.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(3590,1044,'2001-06-05 22:01:46',0,'MightyBluJ','Zimbabwe!   Very nice.  pretty cheap, and one of the most \r\nbeautiful spots in Africa.  I hear it\\\'s a little unstable \r\nthough now...\r\n\r\nChina (Guilen, Xian, etc)could