imon\\\'s a photographer! well well well, aren\\\'t \r\nyou special.  oh you live in san francisco, you\\\'re soooooo \r\nhip...hip with it.  you\\\'re soooo coooool cause you live in \r\nthe bay area, are you a punk rock star, too?  ooooohhh i bet \r\nyou are, cause you\\\'re tooooo awesome.  take my picture.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(3609,1049,'2001-06-06 05:28:12',0,'jo','wow you must stop that before i hit you. burn burn.',6,0,0,0,'172.157.27.243','en'),(3610,1049,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','hey simon, how come you never came over to use the\r\ndarkroom?  where\\\'s the love?\r\n',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(3611,1049,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>oooooo, my name is lulu!  oh, i am such hot shit.  i \r\nlive in la la land.  i am golden.  dont touch me i \r\nwill burn you!  i am a creative genius.  hold my calls, \r\nlets do lunch.  who is on the phone?  the academy awards?  \r\noh please i cant be bothered.  i am LULU.</P>\r\n\r\n<P><B>i am soooooooooo los angeles.</b></P>',2,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3612,1050,'2001-06-06 07:05:55',0,'cyantist','what color did you paint your bathroom?  do you have\r\npictures?  did seeing your room painted white make you sad?',1,0,0,0,'202.77.253.245','en'),(3613,1050,'2001-06-06 07:06:45',0,'cyantist','i just saw the title after i asked the question.  pumpkin\r\norange and schoolbus yellow.  wow!  i bet that is really\r\nbeautiful. can we see pictures?',1,0,0,0,'202.77.253.245','en'),(3614,1050,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','digital cameras never do color justice, especially with a\r\nflash... but here <a\r\nhref=\\\"http://www.logy.org/~xep/days/2001/060501/bathroom.jpg\\\">it\r\nis</a>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\nno, i wasn\\\'t sad.  that time in my life had past.  i had a\r\nnew home, in iowa, and was busily making it my living\r\nmuseum.',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(3615,1050,'2001-06-06 08:08:10',0,'rusty','yes... that old room was amazing...  I have many a memory of\r\nit...  you remember that if and/or when the purge comes, I\r\nget to pick through the expulsed items...',1,0,0,0,'64.163.194.75','en'),(3616,1027,'2001-06-06 08:15:04',0,'rusty','At Great America there is a ride called Top Gun...  Walking\r\nup to the ride there is a all this military propaganda \r\nbeing spouted out...  There is a military sign-up form at\r\nthe entrance...  There are what could be \r\ncalled \\\'subliminal\\\' messages over the speaker system \r\nwalking up to the ride... It goes off about how our fighter \r\npilots were the best, and we took out 10 to 1 planes in \r\nKorea, and\r\nwe relied too much on technology in Vietnam, and our \r\nsoldiers lost their edge, so we have to keep sharp...  \r\nthere were all sort of military looking guys standing \r\naround...  It was quite a trip...  Tracy is a smart guy...  \r\nI can understand why he became more anti-american after \r\nbeing in the military...',1,0,0,0,'64.163.194.75','en'),(3617,1041,'2001-06-06 08:25:59',0,'rusty','If China was a true Communism, such things shouldn\\\'t \r\nexist...  But then again, Hong Kong is nothing like China, \r\nso I\\\'m sure there are some differences...  In a true \r\nCommunist state everyone should be cared for by the system \r\nand the society, and something like the divorce and broken \r\nfamily problems we see in the US wouldn\\\'t be a problem...  \r\nI have the feeling China itself probably still maintains \r\nthe extended family better than we do...\r\n<p>\r\nI hate that our generations cannot respect marriage \r\nanymore...\r\n<p>\r\nI put this quote on my website recently...  It is a quote \r\nfrom a sociology paper someone else wrote...  I don\\\'t think \r\n30 years ago that anyone would\\\'ve written such a thing in a \r\nsociology paper, but the fact that someone would these \r\ndays, shows that it is true now, because it is what much of \r\nsociety believes these days...\r\n<p>\r\n\\\"Marriage. An institute for the deprived and insecure. \r\nPerfect for the human race. However, due to human behavior \r\nour attempts to create such a structured and perfect union \r\nfail miserably.\\\"',1,0,0,0,'64.163.194.75','en'),(3618,1050,'2001-06-06 08:37:56',0,'cyantist','that is so awesome xep!  makes me wish i could paint stuff \r\nin my house.  what other alterations have you done to your \r\nplace?  ',1,0,0,0,'202.77.253.245','en'),(3619,1044,'2001-06-06 11:24:01',0,'Joanna','The next places I am going are Seeeedney, to see Kini, and \r\nMelbourne, to see O, so no travel hair dryer nessecary \r\nthanks girls.  \r\n\r\n<BR><BR>\r\n\r\nBut! I was watching The Alamo today, and thinking, my god \r\nwhat an awful movie, and what a waste to create such a crap \r\nstate (i\\\'m sorry, but Bush is my reference point here), but \r\nthen I realised that hey, actually all those Swinney people \r\nare from Austin, and they all seem to like it, so maybe \r\nit\\\'s not all bad.  So yes, I think if I ever make it to the \r\nUS, I might have to go to Austin.  ',1,0,0,0,'203.97.2.243','en'),(3620,1049,'2001-06-06 13:02:30',0,'hh','dear lu lu on the bridge, Please jump.',4,0,0,0,'24.93.61.58','en'),(3621,1050,'2001-06-06 14:44:03',0,'jo','oh that red looks exactly like the whorehouse red wall in \r\nmy living room.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(3622,1046,'2002-04-20 20:49:51',273,'Quinn','Direct antagoism is like a hollow statue.  I can poke my \r\nfinger through it. ',6,0,0,1,'198.185.18.207','en'),(3623,1050,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','cyantist: why can\\\'t you?  i have just painted various\r\nother walls.  our house is weird... it\\\'s the first floor\r\nand the basement.  the first floor is victorian, the\r\nbasement is very modern.  they don\\\'t meld well.  everything\r\nin the modern basement was stark white.  it was unpleasant\r\nto be there.  i didn\\\'t ask permission to paint, i just did\r\nit.  i feel it\\\'s worth possibly losing the deposit to make a\r\nhome i am happy with.  on the other hand, the person who\r\nlived here before painted the bedroom wasabi green and the\r\nlandlord didn\\\'t seem to care.  we\\\'ll see.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\nthese household decorating moments brought you to by\r\nheloise.',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(3624,1051,'2001-06-06 17:59:34',0,'bmg','word.',1,0,0,0,'66.68.79.197','en'),(3625,1051,'2001-06-06 18:01:13',0,'kat','he said he was happy with the way things we were. but then \r\nhe slept with other people. he said i made it all sound so \r\nhorrible. that he was horrible. but all i wanted was to be \r\nhappy. and for him to be happy. i was turning into somebody \r\ni didnt want to be. not because of him. but to be with him. \r\nnow he says i only used him. that i like to torture myself. \r\nand everyone around me. he doesnt make sense. sometimes \r\nlife doesnt make sense. but i know that i have to reach for \r\nwhat i crave. or silently suffocate. it still doesnt make \r\nsense. but yea...its going to be okay. ',1,0,0,0,'12.64.21.200','en'),(3626,1044,'2001-06-06 18:43:49',0,'MightyBluJ To Joanna','If you do come some day, don\\\'t voice your displeasure with \r\nTexas by  relieving yourself on the Alamo.  People can make \r\na rather big deal about that.  Texas is probably more like \r\nAustralia than many of us would care to admit though... ( & \r\nvice versa)\r\n\r\n\r\n-I was rather disappointed that Ozzy did not take up the \r\noffer to urinate on the Alamo drafthouse. missed \r\nopportunity I say.',1,0,0,0,'204.64.42.245','en'),(3627,1050,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','<p>\nyou would think that it would be bad for the digestion or \nsomething, but i think there is something very cuddly and \ncomforting about blood red walls. perhaps it was all that \ntime i spent as a kid being eaten by a whale. \n</p><p>\ni adore the xep. yes yes yesss. \n</p>\n',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(3628,1049,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','<p>\r\nlulu is special. we gotta be nice to her cuz she\\\'s not like \r\nthe other kids.\r\n</p>\r\n',3,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(3629,1049,'20