3728,1062,'2001-06-08 03:46:13',0,'jo','after the html for dummies book, you should pick up one on \r\npoetry. random line breaks do not haiku/senryu form make. 5-\r\n7-5 or it\\\'s just a short poem.',1,0,0,0,'172.159.186.180','en'),(3729,1062,'2001-06-08 03:55:13',0,'quoted','<pre><tt>\r\noooohh i know what you\\\'re thinking. you\\\'re thinking i\\\'m \r\njust a poor pathetic, ignorant, jerk off with nothing better \r\nto do than to write crap on some website that glorifies \r\nshit for poetry.\r\n</tt></pre>',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3730,1058,'2001-06-08 04:41:45',0,'bmg','<p>i just had bacon and eggs... (*burp*)</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.79.197','en'),(3731,1062,'2001-06-08 04:52:21',0,'lulu','ah jojo, c\\\'mon pal, lighten up buddy, i was just practicing \r\nmy<br>\r\nbreaks.  it wasn\\\'t really a haiku. are you a haiku?\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(3732,1062,'2001-06-08 05:02:19',0,'lulu','wait a second......<br>\r\noooooooh i\\\'m jo, i\\\'m a champion poet, i know how to write the \r\nperfect haiku cause i studied it in college all four years, \r\ni\\\'m soooooo awesome, oooooh i wear black clothes and recite \r\npoetry on sunday mornings while sipping lattes by the \r\nwindow....ooooooohhh i\\\'m sooooooo special.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(3733,1062,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p>Expect to be waxed to the max if you visit a salon for \r\na Brazilian treatment. A paper thong might be provided, \r\nbut most likely, you\\\'ll be in the buff. First the hair is \r\nsnipped with scissors so the wax can reach the \r\nfollicles. Then, using a wooden stick, a technician \r\nplaces warm wax on the area a little bit at a time. As \r\nwith a regular bikini wax, cloth strips are placed over the \r\nhot wax and, after it hardens, pulled away from the skin. \r\nA traditional Brazilian includes the labia and the area \r\nthat reaches into the buttocks. If there are stray hairs \r\nafter waxing, the technician may also tweeze the area. \r\nThe key to allowing wax to penetrate into the follicles \r\n(and provide the closest possible wax) is to relax. And \r\nmany women claim the treatment is not nearly as \r\npainful as it sounds.</p>',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3734,1062,'2001-06-08 05:56:15',0,'darwin to lulu','<p>You\\\'re really boring.</p>\r\n<p>-darwin</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(3735,1050,'2001-06-08 06:47:34',0,'xepmom','That room. I remember the night you held me while I cried \r\ngreat gulping sobs after Bob died. I cannot remember ever \r\nhaving seen you cry. (But, then, there\\\'s a lot I don\\\'t \r\nremember.) I liked the way your room looked, but the odor was \r\nof something stale, old, perhaps dead. Those were strange \r\ntimes. Rusty, I\\\'m glad you survived. Without Bob, we were \r\nwithout ballast or compass. Amazing how well we\\\'ve done since \r\nthat hard time. So many house mates since then -- each \r\ndecorating in his own style.  Marcella with her Native \r\nAmerican artifacts, Simon with his surfboards and posters of \r\nHawaaian kings, Caroline with her botanical and zoological \r\nprints. Caitlyn, whose drawings are still in the bathroom and \r\ngarage. Raina, the kitchen goddess who didn\\\'t care for \r\ncleaning up but was a great cook. The short-termers who just \r\nstayed long enough to get themselves together and find \r\npermanent housing. Oh, how could I forget Phil, who came for \r\na week and stayed for 8 months. Rusty, I remember seeing your \r\nroom once. It was as chaotic as xep\\\'s but lacked any color. \r\nDo you have colors now?  You are all dear people who have \r\nbrought color into my life. When you leave, the walls are \r\nonce again white and blank. When I move to Oregon, I will try \r\nto paint boldly. \r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.174.155.161','en'),(3736,1062,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to s5','steve youve had your bush ripped off?',0,0,0,0,'216.175.93.152','en'),(3737,1062,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p><a \r\nhref=http://www.lyricsengine.com/cgi-bin/main.pl/artistid.16\r\n1/an.AC_DC/albumid.0/songid.1438/sn.Big_Balls_/lyrics.html>I\r\nf you don\\\'t know, get to know, seen?</a>\r\n</p><p>\r\n-darwin',4,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(3738,1062,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p><a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.lyricsengine.com/cgi-bin/main.pl/artistid.1\r\n61/an.AC_DC/albumid.0/songid.1438/sn.Big_Balls_/lyrics.html\\\"\r\n>Here\\\'s that link that actually works!</>\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n',1,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(3739,1053,'2001-06-08 07:18:07',0,'cyantist','this entry brought me to tears after i read it.  how old \r\nwere you?  is this recent?',1,0,0,0,'202.77.253.245','en'),(3740,1061,'2001-06-08 07:22:28',0,'cyantist','chuckle.',1,0,0,0,'202.77.253.245','en'),(3741,1062,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p><a \r\nhref=\\\"http://saturn5.com/darwin/mp3/AC_DC-Big%20Balls.mp3\\\">I\r\nn all its audio glory.</a>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin',4,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(3742,1050,'2001-06-08 07:38:20',0,'rusty','*hug hug* xeppymommy\r\n<p>\r\nYes, I am glad I survived, too...\r\n<p>\r\nI never painted the room I had in Aptos... My parents \r\nrented, and wouldn\\\'t let me...  But after I got back from \r\nthe hospital I had lots of drawings I put up all over...  \r\nWhen we lived in Nash-Vegas, they bought a house, and let \r\nme paint the walls...  I loved that room...  I got more \r\ninto painting and drawing then...  Didn\\\'t do any sculpting \r\nafter Cabrillo, tho...  I did not paint it solid colors...  \r\nIt was all drawings, and grafitti style...  But the walls \r\nwere all covered...  When I ran back to Cali at 18, they \r\nscraped the paint off the walls...  I actually didn\\\'t even \r\npaint on canvas or anything for a long time after I left \r\nNash-Vile...  I have recently been re-creating my last \r\npainting I did back then...  And hopefully, I will keep up \r\nthe hobby...  It feels good...\r\n<p>\r\n:)',1,0,0,0,'64.163.194.75','en'),(3743,1061,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<P align=\"justify\">\r\nWHO THE HELL ACTIVATED THIS BULLSHIT! WHAT THE FUCK! DON\'T \r\nWE HAVE ANY GODDAMN STANDARDS AROUND HERE! THIS WHOLE \r\nCOMMUNITY IS FALLING TO SHIT!\r\n<br><br>\r\n<font size=\"+4\" color=\"Red\">BURN! BURN!</FONT>\r\n</P>',6,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3744,1062,'2001-06-08 08:08:03',0,'s5 to egg','bring me lulu.',1,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3745,1063,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','this is all getting very randy. it must be in the stars.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.93.152','en'),(3746,1063,'2001-06-08 08:35:56',0,'lulu','le, suck on this poetry girl.  oooooh le, you\\\'re sooooo cool \r\nwith your two letter handle, oooooooh i\\\'m soooo touched by \r\nyour lov-ing poem, ah, i\\\'m gonna go cry over there and \r\nshit....le, look what i learned today (page break)<br>\r\nyou\\\'re sweet.......don\\\'t let it get to your head tho.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(3747,1063,'2001-06-08 08:35:57',0,'lulu','le, suck on this poetry girl.  oooooh le, you\\\'re sooooo cool \r\nwith your two letter handle, oooooooh i\\\'m soooo touched by \r\nyour lov-ing poem, ah, i\\\'m gonna go cry over there and \r\nshit....le, look what i learned today (page break)<br>\r\nyou\\\'re sweet.......don\\\'t let it get to your head tho.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(3748,1021,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','police brutality fucking sucks ass.',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3749,1062,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','s5, when i\\\'m there next, let\\\'s get brazillian waxes\r\ntogether.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nyou may not have labia, but i do, and surely you have other\r\ngenital areas that could be lovingly harvested.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nwhy do i like the idea of brazillian waxing so much?',3,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(3750,1062,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','because you want to pay someone to attend, carefully, \r\nwith precise detail, to your genitals.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3751,1062,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','<BR>\r\nall i can say is... ouuuuuuch.<BR>\r\nbeing a slightly-hairy hippy suits me just fine.',0,0,0,0,'203.96.111.202','en'),(3752,1021,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','brutality fucking sucks ass.',6,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3753,1063,'2001-06-08 11:56:20',0,'rusty','I just read lulu\\\'s posts...  the wonderful antagonism there \r\nwithing has inspired me to say this to le\r\n<p>\r\n\\\'I am tired of this topic!\\\'\r\n<p>\r\n:)\r\n<p>\r\nI always back down, especially if I know someone, so my \r\nreaction to le dis\\\'ing one of my posts was too mellow...  I \r\nshall now make fun of her...\r\n<p>\r\n:)',4,0,0,0,'64.163.194.75','en'),(3754,1063,'2002-04-20 20:49:51',273,'Quinn:','<p><b>Deconstructing Lulu</b></p>\r\n\r\n<p>I  think it\\\'s fun to encourage Lulu.  \r\n\r\n<p>Y\\\'see-- it all comes down to the fact that we know \r\nshe\\\'s trying to get a rise out of us.  Her insistent \r\nprovocation is really ironic, because no matter how \r\nmuch she makes fun there\\\'s a double meaning.  \r\nThere\\\'s love behind her posts.  She really loves \r\nswinney.org, and all it\\\'s members.  Lulu mocks it \r\nbecause it\\\'s fun for her to get us to react.\r\n\r\n<p>It\\\'s like when you were in grade school and you \r\nliked someone, so you kicked \\\'em in the shins.\r\n\r\n<p>I get a kick out of her antagonism because, frankly, \r\nthe world isn\\\'t very interesting when its all love and \r\npudding.  Look back at my first posts a couple days ago \r\nwhen I reacted to incitor\\\'s comments about his little \r\nsister...some of that was sincere response and some \r\nof that was provocation.  I wanted people to react to me \r\nwith something other than platitudes.  It worked.  \r\n\r\n<p>When I was younger I took Lulu\\\'s tact of \r\n<i>in-your-face-isms</i>.  I even went so far as to \r\nsubmit literally shit-stained poems to a journal, hoping \r\nto get a dramatic reaction.  The poems weren\\\'t very \r\ngood, as my idiom lacked intelligence and decorum.  I \r\nguess I\\\'ve grown up.\r\n\r\n<p>I dunno.  Like I said in another post...you can poke \r\nholes through Lulu\\\'s act and see right through to the \r\nother side.  It\\\'s all bravado, a game, a show, <i>a \r\nschtick</i>.  Isn\\\'t it Lulu?  Isn\\\'t it?\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,1,'198.185.18.207','en'),(3755,1061,'2002-04-20 20:49:51',273,'Quinn:','It\\\'s actualy kinda funny.  Person should have called \r\nthemself \\\"Narcy Schism\\\" or somesuch.\r\n\r\nBut to back up le, standards are nice...however, some \r\nstandards stray into censorship.  Y\\\'gotta be real careful.',4,0,0,1,'198.185.18.207','en'),(3756,1061,'2001-06-08 12:56:59',0,'rusty','Oh come on...  Sure, we can see some amusement in it, \r\nbecause we all know web journals, and personal web pages \r\nare total mental masturbation, so this is kind of funny, \r\nbut the quality of this post is certainly less than say the \r\npost discussed in Cyan\\\'s rant about censorship:\r\n<p>\r\n<a href=http://swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?\r\nid=935.txt>\r\nhttp://swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=935.txt\r\n</a>',6,0,0,0,'64.163.194.75','en'),(3757,1061,'2001-06-08 12:58:58',0,'rusty','try that again:\r\n<p>\r\n<a href=\\\"http://swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?\r\nid=935.txt\\\">\r\nhttp://swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=935.txt \r\n</a>\r\n',6,0,0,0,'64.163.194.75','en'),(3758,1063,'2001-06-08 13:02:13',0,'rusty','So does that mean that when le wasn\\\'t atagonistic to my \r\npost, but just wanted it to go away, rather than create \r\namusing argumentative banter, or just ignoring it, that I \r\nshould\\\'ve been truely offended, because it wasn\\\'t even \r\nfunny like lulu\\\'s antagonism?!?!  ;)\r\n<p>\r\nhehe',4,0,0,0,'64.163.194.75','en'),(3759,1063,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','rusty, it wasn\\\'t a personal attack when i said i was sick \r\nof the topic. you wrote a post about antidepressants, \r\nand that topic of discussion (antidepressants: good or \r\nbad?) has come up on swinney before, as well as over \r\nand over again on chat, in personal conversations, and \r\nmore than one of my mailing lists. i\\\'ve stated my \r\nopinion on it so many times and seeing another thing \r\nabout it just made me feel tired. that\\\'s all. ',5,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3760,1062,'2001-06-08 13:31:21',0,'rusty','Large props to Darwin for the wonderful old AC/DC\r\n<p>\r\nOne of the finest, most truely meaningful songs ever created\r\n<p>\r\nIt brings a tear of joy to my eye...',1,0,0,0,'64.163.194.75','en'),(3761,1063,'2001-06-08 13:36:03',0,'rusty','<p>\r\nHuzzah!\r\n<p>\r\nSo don\\\'t read it...  ;)\r\n<p>\r\nI really didn\\\'t care, but it was time for me to do a little\r\ndelayed-reaction razzing...  ;)',1,0,0,0,'64.163.194.75','en'),(3762,1063,'2002-04-20 20:49:51',273,'Quinn:','<p>I dunno, Rusty.  I guess I just don\\\'t share your \r\nsense of humor.  I usually like humor that is smart, but \r\nLulu\\\'s posts are not really very smart...they\\\'re just quick, \r\nun-thoughtful posts.  \r\n\r\n<p>Sigh.  \r\n\r\n<p>I dunno.  I recently stumbled across this site by \r\nlinking from a poetry site that was linked to \r\nanother...and I thougt it was pretty cool.  But already I\\\'m \r\ngetting a little bored with it.  The intelligence that I \r\nthought was there, just seems to be more of the same \r\nboring shit that happens between human beings \r\neverywhere.\r\n\r\n<p>Some of the folks here are interesting, but 8 out of \r\n10 posts and comments (mine included) are too hasty \r\nto be much more than self-aggrandizement  and \r\nreactionary bullshit.\r\n\r\n<p>You missed my point entirely, Rusty.   \r\n\r\n<p>You Asshole.\r\n',1,0,0,1,'198.185.18.207','en'),(3763,1063,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','how can you people even care?',3,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(3764,1063,'2001-06-08 14:28:46',0,'rusty','<p>\r\nI got your point, Quinn...  So what?  Why are you concerned\r\nif I got it or not?  I\\\'m just not interested.  I find your\r\nresponses dull...  Too many words for simple concepts...  I \r\nthink you want to think your brain is bigger than it is.  ;)\r\n<p>\r\no - if I seemed like I cared in those posts, I must have \r\ndone a bad job of writing them...  I was having fun...',4,0,0,0,'64.163.194.75','en'),(3765,1063,'2002-04-20 20:49:51',273,'Quinn:','i am much too sensitive for this venue',4,0,0,1,'198.185.18.207','en'),(3766,1063,'2001-06-08 14:33:33',0,'rusty','Oh, Quinn...  In case it went over your head on what I was \r\nrazzing elly about, she made a comment on this post of mine:\r\n<p>\r\n<a href=\\\"http://swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?\r\nid=873.txt\\\">\r\nhttp://swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=873.txt\r\n</a>\r\n<p>\r\nAnd I reacted to her dis nicely then...  I decided to poke \r\nsome fun now...  However, since I am not lulu, people can\\\'t \r\nseem to just giggle and move on...  They have to write long \r\nprose of dullness, and call me names to make themselves \r\nfeel like they have a big dick...  :)\r\n<p>\r\n\\\'Have a nice day!\\\'',4,0,0,0,'64.163.194.75','en'),(3767,1063,'2001-06-08 14:38:21',0,'rusty','oh, Quinn... don\\\'t be that way... you were praising the \r\nsarcasm, and now you\\\'re getting sad because I didn\\\'t like \r\nbeing called an asshole, and reacted...  I\\\'m sorry...  \r\nsigh...',3,0,0,0,'64.163.194.75','en'),(3768,1063,'2002-04-20 20:49:51',273,'quinn','<small>i\\\'m sadder than you can possibly \r\nimagine</small>',4,0,0,1,'198.185.18.207','en'),(3769,1063,'2001-06-08 14:46:36',0,'rusty',':(',2,0,0,0,'64.163.194.75','en'),(3770,1063,'2001-06-25 16:08:32',0,'<small>quinn</small>','<p><small>i just didn\\\'t know that i was, oh so boring. \r\n&nbsp &nbsp ....that, <i>*sniff*</i>, i could take time to \r\nwrite something and have it declared, <i>*sniff*</i>, \r\ndull.\r\n\r\n<p>i\\\'m sorry i called you an asshole, rusty, i was just, \r\n<i>*snarfle*</i>, lashing out.\r\n\r\n<p>i do that from time to time.  <i>*sob*</i></small>',0,0,0,1,'198.185.18.207','en'),(3771,1063,'2001-06-08 15:11:03',0,'rusty','lol',6,0,0,0,'64.163.194.75','en'),(3772,1064,'2001-06-08 16:28:53',0,'LinearB','Last week, when I was at HEB (our megagrocer), I heard \r\nUltravox\\\'s Vienna. Last night at whole foods, I heard a \r\nMuzak version of VanHalen\\\'s \\\"Jump.\\\"\r\n\r\nI\\\'m no longer surprised at anything I hear. In fact, the \r\nlast time I was surprised was back in 1989, when I heard \r\nTangerine Dream playing at the Neiman Marcus headquarters.',0,0,0,0,'207.8.3.193','en'),(3773,1058,'2002-04-20 20:49:51',273,'Quinn:','It seems my precious has found another.',1,0,0,1,'198.185.18.207','en'),(3774,1064,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','that van halen\\\'s jump muzak mix (heh) has been invading \r\ngrocery stores for a long time. i remember sliding around the \r\ncastro safeway to it in my socks. wee!\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(3775,1063,'2001-06-08 18:38:35',0,'not_loco','I smell a love affair between these two. Maybe Lulu can \r\nmake it a 3some.',4,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(3776,1066,'2001-06-08 18:41:55',0,'dj1_luna','<P>\r\n<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.esquire.com/features/articles/001323_mfr_me\r\nmento_1.html\\\">Memento: \r\nThe original Short Story </a>',1,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(3777,1066,'2001-06-08 18:48:12',0,'zb','you remind me of me.  thanks dj. \r\n',0,0,0,0,'216.171.37.54','en'),(3778,1062,'2001-06-08 19:43:08',0,'bmg','<p>i look like a warewolf... just the idea of waxing \r\nmyself scares the shit out of me...</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.79.197','en'),(3779,1063,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i am tired of this topic.',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3780,1063,'2001-06-08 20:41:45',0,'lulu','everybody now.....',0,0,0,0,'63.255.48.82','en'),(3781,1067,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','<p>\r\nsniff! this really means a lot to me. it echoes my own \r\nfeelings so much! sniffle! sob! sigh!\r\n</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(3782,1067,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','lulu:  url, please ;)',3,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(3783,1065,'2001-06-08 22:13:21',0,'jo','i really dug this.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(3784,1067,'2001-06-08 22:30:50',0,'bmg','<p>owe... please don\\\'t go... you don\\\'t have to \r\nchange!</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'66.68.79.197','en'),(3785,1053,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','lemme see, around six years.  i was nineteen?  or rather, it began when i was 18 and lasted until i was six days past twenty.  i wasn\\\'t as young as i should have been being of those years.  ',1,0,0,0,'207.205.219.144','en'),(3786,1021,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','what can i say?  i both agree with you and think of you as being naive.  they did what was required by their duty.  life often requires that we understand:  you don\\\'t have to like, but you have to do it.',3,0,0,0,'207.205.219.144','en'),(3787,1064,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','fuuuuck. i just read through their website. i really want \r\nto work there.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3788,1066,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i didn\\\'t think memento was that great - it was kind of a \r\nshitty movie with an interesting gimmick, you know?',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3789,1064,'2001-06-09 00:22:37',0,'eoj','i\\\'m sorry, i just don\\\'t buy it.  muzak, as well as all of \r\nyou, surely must be on crack.  that\\\'s the only explanation.',6,0,0,0,'64.3.15.93','en'),(3790,1066,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>It seems like people are split 50/50 on this. There\\\'s \r\nthe people who feel that the story had to be as simple as \r\nit was in order to make any sense at all and communicate \r\nLeonard\\\'s perspective. Then there\\\'s the people who say \\\"if \r\nyou remove the way the story is told, it\\\'s just simple and \r\nwide open and boring!\\\"</p>\r\n<p>I like Memento because I actually connect to the main \r\ncharacter, and it drew me in to try to figure out what in \r\nthe world was going on. In the end, yes, it leaves a lot of \r\nthings wide open, but I prefer that to the typical happy \r\nending tacked on to every other film.</p>\r\n<p>Compare this to, say, \\\"Requiem for a Dream\\\", which uses \r\n3x as many gimmicks and is chock full of cartoonish \r\ncharacters.</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin',1,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(3791,1066,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','similar things could be said about the matrix or fight \r\nclub.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3792,1064,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','berklee college of music (not the same as UC \r\nberkeley) has coursework about writing and producing \r\njingles. it sounds fun. video game music would also be \r\nfun to write.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3793,1067,'2001-06-09 07:53:47',0,'rusty','aww... lulu, you kick ass, and you know it...  quinn was \r\nfucking with you cause you were amusing...  and he\\\'s not \r\neven posted on here yet, as far as I know, other that to \r\ncomment, so who cares?!?!\r\n<p>\r\nYou inspired me to stand up for myself on here... and I \r\nthank you for that...  I think I got brain... maybe even as \r\nmuch as Owl or Rabbit...  So, I think I deserve to be \r\nlistened to, even if some a-hole b-heads think they are old-\r\nskool Internet God/Goddesses...  I was here years before \r\nyou, even if it wasn\\\'t on Swinney, and maybe I was quiet \r\nthen, but I ain\\\'t gonna be now, just because you think \r\nyou\\\'re so cool...  I have naked pictures of you, so suck \r\nme...  Go home, and leave me the fuck alone, stick to your \r\nown corner of the world, and let me exist, you fucks...\r\n<p>\r\nLove ya, LuLu...  Even tho I never had a cow named that....',1,0,0,0,'209.245.5.171','en'),(3794,1066,'2001-06-09 07:55:24',0,'rusty','Unfortunately... none of you could see any of what I was \r\ngetting at...  I don\\\'t give a fuck if you do or not... this \r\npost was not truely about the movie itself... it was \r\ninspired by the movie, and if you cannot see the \r\ninspiration, or what is going on, fuck off...   thank you \r\nvery much....   The only person \r\ni hope responds to this anymore, is \r\nIncitor...  and maybe he will read and think a little \r\nfurther, since I can tell \r\nDarwin did, and that implies to me that incitor might \r\nalso...\r\n<p>\r\nfuck the rest of you, especially le...\r\n<p>\r\nI don\\\'t give a fuck that I know you, or that maybe you are \r\nas close to some people that \r\ni am close to...  I wanted to know you once...  Now rot in \r\nhell, you fucking non-understanding, self-centered shit-\r\nhole.....\r\n<p>\r\nhave a nice day!!!  :)\r\n<p>\r\nwow... am I moody this weekend,or what????',1,0,0,0,'209.245.5.171','en'),(3795,1066,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p>\r\n\\\"you fucking non-understanding, self-centered shit- \r\nhole\\\"\r\n</p>\r\n',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3796,1066,'2001-06-09 09:33:28',0,'rusty','you go, steve... point out what a shit-head I am, because I \r\nfeel like one...  I\\\'ve had a really bad weekend...\r\n<p>\r\nsorry le...  your responses to things I write really piss \r\nme off, and lately, I\\\'m really on edge...  I like you as a \r\nperson tho...\r\n',4,0,0,0,'64.156.37.135','en'),(3797,1069,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','yes.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3798,1069,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p>\\\"<i>the sun washes over everyone at some time in \r\ntheir life. the blue of the sky will move everyone to tears, \r\ngiven the right mood. i don\\\'t matter. my views don\\\'t \r\nmatter. my experiences don\\\'t matter. they only matter to \r\nme.\r\n\r\nuntil the insulation of the single human can be \r\ndemolished, communication is futile.</i>\\\"</p>\r\n<p>i can\\\'t accept this. it may be true but i can\\\'t accept it. \r\nall i do is communicate, it\\\'s all i live for. i won\\\'t ever stop \r\n<a href=\\\"http://www.elly.org/passion/01/06/09/\\\">trying to \r\ntell you what it\\\'s like</a>, because if i did i would \r\nprobably just lay down and die. i\\\'d have no purpose. i \r\njust want someone to know what i mean enough to \r\nmake me feel safe.\r\n</p> \r\n',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3799,1069,'2001-06-09 10:10:44',0,'rusty','<p>\r\nbeautiful...  exactly how I felt when I was young...  \r\nunfortunately, not even trying to communicate it is even \r\nworse...  I figured that out the hard way...',4,0,0,0,'64.156.37.135','en'),(3800,1069,'2001-06-09 10:14:49',0,'rusty','elly, I can soooo relate to what you write... it makes me \r\neven more sad about the pitiful responses you choose to my \r\nposts...  but that\\\'s okay...  blah...',4,0,0,0,'64.156.37.135','en'),(3801,1069,'2001-06-09 10:41:33',0,'rusty','<p>\r\none of my personal rambles that includes past thoughts on \r\nthis subject...\r\n<p>\r\n<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://tender.lumplings.com/crap/ramblings/060601.html\r\n\\\">\r\nhttp://tender.lumplings.com/crap/ramblings/060601.html\r\n</a>',4,0,0,0,'64.156.37.135','en'),(3802,1069,'2001-06-09 12:44:45',0,'Joanna','I love talking to you, Olivia, and reading your writings.  \r\nYou express things wonderfully.  I have always wished that \r\nI was as brave and as bold as you in saying things.  Please \r\nkeep talking, please keep telling stories.  You\\\'ve always \r\nhad a captive audience.  ',1,0,0,0,'203.97.2.243','en'),(3803,1069,'2001-06-09 13:31:26',0,'jp','Does this ever happen?<BR>\r\n<I><B>Phone rings...</B><BR>\r\n\"Oh, hi. Oh there\'s something reallly important and personal\r\nI want to tell you. First though let me hook the phone to a\r\nPA system so everyone in town can listen...\"<BR>\r\n</I>or<BR>\r\n<I>Okay... time to write in my secret diary... Once I\'m done\r\nI\'ll have to make copies so I can pass out flyers for\r\ntoday\'s entry...<BR></I>\r\nExpression overrated? Is it that expression is overrated or\r\nreally that certains <I>contexts</I> of expression are\r\noverrated? <BR>\r\nBeing able to express whatever you\'re thinking or feeling is\r\nnot overrated. Being eloquent or articulate is a good thing,\r\npretty much universally. The questions are what should you\r\nbe expressing, why, and to whom?<BR>\r\nIn general I don\'t like to use email than anything for work\r\nor very matter of fact things. It\'s totally lacking in the\r\n\"realness\" of actually being in that person\'s presence. When\r\nI write to people I haven\'t contacted in a long time I\r\nprefer writing a real letter or talking on the phone over\r\nemail. Any sort of deep personal communication or connection\r\nrequires real contact. <BR>\r\nThe problem with web sites, IRC, etc. is that it creates a\r\nphantom world. Expression via the internet *is* overrated.\r\nThe internet allows anyone to anonymously communicate with\r\nlarge groups of people -- this is why it\'s great and this is\r\nwhy it sucks.<BR>\r\nIt\'s that feeling I have when read something in a journal\r\nhere or somewhere else -- I feel like I\'ve entered into\r\nsomeone\'s little private world and I\'m peeping in through\r\nthe distorted glass of their fishtank. And it\'s great\r\nbecause I have this connection and I feel like I\'m in their\r\nworld... but I don\'t, I\'m not. That\'s why it sucks. That\r\nempty, disconnected feeling of interacting with\r\nrepresentations of people who are actually more imaginary\r\nthan real.<BR>\r\nYet I\'m doing it right now... investing large amounts of\r\ntime \"express\"ing some crap I feel compelled to \"express\".\r\nI expect nothing from it though and I\'ll admit I\'m an idiot\r\nfor trying. Noone I really know is going to read this\r\nanyway. If I had something I really wanted to say to\r\nsomeone... I\'d say it, in person. Why would I need to let\r\neveryone on the internet in on it? The internet is an\r\nextremely poor substitute for real conversation. IRC, and\r\nmessage boards and all that <B>suck ass</B> in my opinion.\r\nThey make you compulsive, they distort and reduce, and they\r\nmake you sit on your ass for long periods of time when you\r\nshould be out getting laid or walking in the sunshine or\r\nsomething good like that. <BR>\r\nMyself, I spend way more time than I would like attached to\r\nthis thing... but my livelyhood depends on it.\r\nI spent three years without using a computer after college\r\nand did not miss it... at all. I was too busy living in a\r\nforeign country doing my thing. <BR>\r\nSo anyway, this is not meant to be disparaging to anyone or\r\nanything. Bottom line I\'d say is that life truly lived means\r\ngetting away from the one-eyed demon that you\'re staring at\r\nright now. That applies to myself more than anything... but\r\nI\'m saying it to all.<BR></i></b>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,'24.0.133.128','en'),(3804,1069,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','i wasn\\\'t talking about expression over the internet.  purely\r\nin spoken conversations with people.',3,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(3805,919,'2001-06-09 15:13:33',0,'o to ert:','i know the nina simone version.  great song.  ert, i didn\\\'t\r\nknow you read swinney.  hi.',3,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(3806,426,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','i wonder if the sean who commented above is matsukaze.  he\r\nonce asked me \\\"how come you never talk about your\r\nparents?\\\".  he has penetrating eyes.  hm.',3,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(3807,345,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','when le and xep were here they found me some velvet\r\npatchwork pants not unlike this quilt.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nwell today, i went to the same shop and found patchwork\r\nvelvet pants which are EXACTLY MY QUILT.  they\\\'re made out\r\nof my quilt.  this shouldn\\\'t be strange, but the quilt is as\r\nold as i am.  it was given to my by my parents.  so WHERE\r\ndid they get this material from?<br>\r\n<br>\r\nanyway i put the pants on layby.  i\\\'ll have them on the\r\n15th.  i\\\'m in love.<br>',3,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(3808,289,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','this is the ugliest pic ever of me.  i demand it is taken\r\ndown.',3,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(3809,209,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','remember when it was ok to write meaningless crap on\r\nswinney.org?  this post is a perfect example.',3,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(3810,140,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','and so is mad mol:<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<i>Get lusty: Late at night when all the sane people are\r\nasleep I write steamy e-mails to my boy. When it?s dark and\r\nthe night noises take over, I become bolder, I grow sharp\r\nteeth and am not afraid to say what I want. Under the cover\r\nof darkness I allow myself to revel in my wants and needs.\r\nLusting after my boy, eight time zones away. - Mad\r\nMol</i><br>\r\n<br>\r\ndoesn\\\'t seem like the same mad moll as we have here. ',3,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(3811,209,'2001-06-09 15:54:48',0,'jo','cheers to going back and reading old stuff and commenting \r\non it, liv. good idea.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(3812,603,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','how is it possible to worry about people not responding to\r\nyou when you are the queen of leaving chat without a\r\nword?<br>\r\n<br>\r\nrelationship dynamics, the mind is a strange place.',3,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(3813,744,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','depo provera is evil.  it took me a whole year to get my\r\nperiod back after i went off it, and i was completely psycho\r\nthe whole time i was on it.  just say no to depo provera.  i\r\nwonder what it will be like if i have to go back on birth\r\ncontrol should i get a steady male sex partner at some\r\nstage.  ew.  i don\\\'t want to.',3,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(3814,1069,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','i\\\'m glad there are few moments in my life that are worth\r\nsharing with others. it really takes the pressure off.',0,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(3815,1066,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','a long time ago, when i was in college, i wrote a story about a retired foreign legionaire, who\\\'d lost everything he wanted in life to his own foolishness.  he\\\'d retired to Sidi bel Abbes after leaving the legion and spent half his time just wandering about, trying to fill the void in his life by consuming the people around him.  taking them into his life and then spitting them forth again.  my psych professor read it and wrote: \\\"Dave, first, i like it.  Second, I didn\\\'t like it at first.  Your main character doesn\\\'t care about anyone at all, even himself.  I found myself wondering why i should care about him, of course that was the very moment i began to identify with him.\\\"  \r\n<p>\r\nrusty, i too once burned or otherwise destroyed mementos of former relationships.  today i keep them, usually as a reminder of what happens when i lower my standards or forget to pay attention to the usual cues.  i like who am, but not my external life.  i don\\\'t like what i do for a living, but i like what i could do in time.  i don\\\'t like violence, but enjoy teaching and learning about it.  i am not an amalgamtion of things i own or do, i am a core surrounded by crust and glitter - these things i own and do.  it\\\'s easy to write people like me off, bitter and twisted, full of violent thought, and terrible past deeds.  but while it\\\'s acceptable to judge us for your own purposes, who can pass total judgement on another human being?  i don\\\'t need to be told when i\\\'m right, i know it.  because my being right applies only to me.  \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nwhat is a goal?  i can\\\'t define my goals when it comes down to it.  there are many things i want from life.  it is doubtful i will get them, or have the chance to pursue them.  last night, i needed to forget some things.  i wanted to go out a drink until i went blind, no longer able to look inside myself.  i snagged three good friends, and said \\\"i\\\'m going to drink until i can\\\'t drink anymore.  wanna come watch?\\\"  (most people have never seen me drunk, my friend are often curious what i\\\'m like.)  so off we go, and i drink two Guinness and then switch to water.  i\\\'ve put myself in the position where i cannot let go of myself without alot of...help.  we ended up spending the evening analyzing the dynamic of agression at the bar, and later, verbally bashing the socialists who sat down with us.  good fun.  i didn\\\'t forget what i so wanted to forget, but i found a good place to store it for a few hours. \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\n\\\"I\\\'m prepared for all emergencies but totally unprepared for everyday life.\\\"  How true this is of me.  I can deal with high stress emergency enviroments so well, but low and medium grade stress sends me quickly to insanity.  i think it has to do with the fact that i\\\'ve gotten myself stuck between two lifestyles.  the \\\'underground\\\' where skinheads, punks, drug dealers, etc. live and work.  and the place i love best, where friends do fun things together without a care.  where no one calls me \\\'nigger-jew\\\' at work, and asbestos actually is a reason to shut down a job site.  where threat of violence is something i don\\\'t need to think about.  rusty, you do not offend me in any way.  i take it as a compliment that you thought of me.  i\\\'m not used to people thinking of me as anything but a threat or as a disgusting person.  i\\\'m glad to my very heart that you, unlike so many today, are willing and even desirous of seeing the world through the eyes of others.  seeing what i see, certainly isn\\\'t going to subsume your beliefs, so any fear of my view is based on ignorance and mistrust.  this applies to any and all.  i love seeing what others see, it\\\'s so often prettier than what i see, and can help me refine my views.  \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\ni\\\'m getting tired of seeing filtered views however.  people who show me idealized parts of their lives.  i offer the good the bad and the ugly; i wish for the same in return.  this is why i\\\'ve written off so many friends.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nwow, i dunno where i meant to take this when i started.  i should drink some coffee before i write here.  oh well.  i think being angry, bitter, sad, and like should not be so reviled as it is today.  too many honest people are turned away by others who make the claim to open minds, but cannot follow through.  too many non-conformists demand non-conformity.  feminists insult women like my mother who actually enjoy raising a family as their primary and only duty.  anti-racists further the violence of thought and deed.  socialists make demands of fellow humans, claiming they know what is right.  the art of compromise has been relegated to a criminal act.  to be an activist means you are often an army of one.  to be who you are, totally, without reservation, is often to be rejected by all.  and i grow weary of it.\r\n</p>\r',1,0,0,0,'207.205.219.162','en'),(3816,1066,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','hell, don\\\'t even ask what i was replying to, it\\\'s forver going to be a mystery to me.  i don\\\'t think i made any sense at all...ugh',2,0,0,0,'207.205.219.162','en'),(3817,1069,'2001-06-09 18:33:00',0,'romano','BORing\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.78.238','en'),(3818,1069,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','\ni think it\\\'s lame that rusty is taking le\\\'s comment so \npersonally. reread it. it\\\'s not personal. hi.\n\n',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(3819,1069,'2001-06-09 19:26:35',0,'cyantist','wow, swinney is getting heated up lately.  i like your \r\njournal entry le, but i wish you would stop generalizing \r\ntaurus people.  i don\\\'t like bing marginalized.  i am cyan \r\nand i can\\\'t be described in astrological terms.  i\\\'m sorry.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\nbecause i\\\'m human, i know what it feels like to be \r\noverwhelmed.  this isn\\\'t a scorpio thing, it is a human \r\nthing.  \r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\ni know this is what you believe in and i appreciate it.  \r\nhowever, i know what and who that is all aimed at and i find \r\nit unfair to generalize people in that fashion.  to be \r\nhonest, i think that astrology can be fun and interesting, \r\nbut using it as an excuse for why people act as they do \r\nbecause it falls into a vague pattern is saying that we have \r\nno will of our own and that we do things because the stars \r\nhave alligned in a certain pattern and we have no choice.  i \r\ncan\\\'t believe that is true.  \r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\nyou of all people, seem to believe in individuality, however \r\nyour writing doesn\\\'t always express that.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\nrusty, i don\\\'t think she meant anything personal by her post \r\neither.  \r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\ni find that most of the posts on swinney in response to \r\nother peoples posts are generally ways of figuring out how \r\nthe post relates to them in some way no matter how \r\nsignificant.  \\\"i know how you feel, because i\\\'ve been \r\nthere\\\".  which is ok from time to time, but i wish that \r\npeople would delve into the topic at hand more and get to \r\nthe root of the post.  share a little of yourself and then \r\nask more about the poster.  i just wish there was a balance. \r\n however, i\\\'m happy that swinney exists.  i feel a sort of \r\nanxiety springing up here and i\\\'m wondering why.  \r\n',1,0,0,0,'203.184.249.130','en'),(3820,1069,'2001-06-09 19:37:54',0,'jo','</b></b></b>\\\"because i\\\'m human, i know what it feels like \r\nto be overwhelmed. this isn\\\'t a scorpio thing, it is a \r\nhuman thing.\\\"<BR>\r\nyeah, i agree.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(3821,603,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','when did i ever leave chat without a word?',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3822,1069,'2001-06-09 22:23:48',0,'jp','I\\\'m not exactly sure where my cranky diatribe above came\r\nfrom. I\\\'m just sorry that it ended up being in <B><I>bold\r\nitalic.</I></B> Argh.<BR>\r\nTwo ideas I went to cap this off with before I call it\r\nquits: glamour and honesty. These are basically\r\ncontradictory things to go after. Glamour, coolness,\r\nhipness, whatever always requires some level of\r\npretentiousness and attitude. It\\\'s image, not reality. It\r\npresumes that you\\\'re different, you\\\'re special, you\\\'re\r\nbetter, whatever. It\\\'s impressing others through force of\r\nwill, force of attitude. I see \\\"being cool\\\", \\\"being hip\\\" as\r\na really adolescent thing. It involves competition with\r\nothers to put down anyone who doesn\\\'t fit in. It\\\'s a\r\nconstant implied struggle. You have groups that split off\r\nfrom the \\\"mainstream\\\" since they feel different. But then\r\nonce in their own group a new standard arises for that group\r\nas to who is really \\\"in\\\" and who is  not. It\\\'s human nature\r\nto constantly look for the star and the outcast. I won\\\'t\r\nreduce all group dynamics to that but what keeps groups of\r\npeople *really* together is true friendship, trust, bond of\r\nexperience.<BR>\r\nThe whole term \\\"poseur\\\" as a put-down among adolescents is\r\nreally laughable since *anyone* striving to identify\r\nthemselves by the image they present is posing.\r\nWhen they say, \\\"you\\\'re a poseur\\\", what it really means is,\r\n\\\"you\\\'re not doing as good a job of posing as we are.\\\"<BR>\r\nSo anyway, back to honesty. The kind of honesty I\\\'m talking\r\nabout is one with lack of agenda in trying to impress some\r\nimage to others -- lack of pretense and not presuming your\r\nown wonderful uniqueness that others may not necessarilly\r\nfeel is so great.<BR>\r\nSo anyway there is a point to all of this. The point being\r\nthat the kind of expression I think was originally\r\nmentioned, the kind based on glamour, *is* empty -- to me at\r\nleast, or kind of annoying in any case. The kind of\r\nexpression of just plainly describing what you\\\'re thinking\r\nor feeling isn\\\'t pointless or empty. People that essentially\r\ntalk by thinking out loud all the time are honest. Probably\r\nalso not very tactful or appropriate but honest at least.\r\nWhen people that are presuming upon some sort of image they\r\nwant to project they are not being honest. It\\\'s largely an\r\nunconscious kind of deception.<BR>\r\nSo, in my case at least, I can take people being truly\r\nhonest. It doesn\\\'t bother me if they\\\'re consistently rude,\r\nobnoxious, blunt if they\\\'re just being themselves. That kind\r\nof expression is totally fine and necessary. Just as long as\r\nthe honesty extends to themselves, warts and all. Expression\r\nthat has the agenda of making an impression or presenting a\r\ncreated image is another thing.',0,0,0,0,'24.0.133.128','en'),(3823,1066,'2001-06-09 22:35:54',0,'jp','I thought this was a good movie. I love well made movies\r\nwhen they\\\'re actually unpredictable and make you think\r\nafterwards.<BR>\r\nrusty: if you\\\'re getting down on le purely from her comment\r\nhere you may be overreacting a little.<BR>\r\nincitor: don\\\'t worry about the \\\"rambling\\\" post. I got a lot\r\nout of it, probably more than if you tried to censor or\r\nstructure it.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'24.0.133.128','en'),(3824,1070,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','actually, \"if i bought you a plastic parrot with a light \r\ninside it\" came from the austin swinney excel \r\nspreadsheet. but it would be something i would like.\r\n',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3825,1070,'2001-06-09 22:50:20',0,'auntie','the plastic parrot only reminded me of how hard it is to \r\nexplain total joy.<br><br>\r\n\r\nlooking into the face of you child does the same thing, \r\nevery time you do it, and the FIRST time, well, that\\\'s \r\nsomething nobody has words for...<br>',1,0,0,0,'24.162.119.106','en'),(3826,1066,'2001-06-10 01:37:48',0,'rusty','I\\\'m in agreement...  I loved your comment, incitor...  I \r\nlike rambling...  \r\n<p>\r\nI also agree, my reactions to le were incredibly annoying to \r\nmyself, as much as they probably were to other people...\r\n<p>\r\nI have been moody about a few things lately, and my reaction \r\nto le had some emotion behind it that was inspired by other \r\nthings, that shouldn\\\'t have been pointed in her direction...\r\n<p>\r\nthe few times elly has commented on anything I post, it has \r\nonly been to say something very brief, that isn\\\'t amusing, \r\nor thought provoking, or supportive, but just dismissive, \r\nand I know that shouldn\\\'t matter...  It\\\'s just another \r\nthing...  I guess I just expected more of her if she was \r\ngoing to bother to comment...  It\\\'s my own problem that \r\nit bugged me...  and it was definately lame to act so angry \r\nabout it...  hey I\\\'m damn imperfect...  I prove it over and \r\nover...  heh...',3,0,0,0,'64.156.39.161','en'),(3827,1069,'2001-06-10 02:10:18',0,'jay','Certainly i\\\'ve felt this, but i think it\\\'s a mark of adulthood \r\nthat you take what you\\\'re given (a mind, a mouth, a \r\nbody), and you do something with it.  Communication is \r\nabout all we have, whether it\\\'s in art or words or touch, \r\nbesides like commerce and nose-picking, so work with \r\nit somehow.  It falls short, but what else are you gonna \r\ndo, self-medicate? Mope?\r\n\r\n',3,0,0,0,'209.86.7.182','en'),(3828,1066,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','expectations!',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3829,1069,'2001-06-10 03:59:09',0,'cyantist','jp, have you ever tried writing a journal?<br><br>\r\neither personal or published to the masses, i find it to be \r\nvery rewarding to yourself and others to do so.  i believe \r\nthat olivia\\\'s post is honest because she\\\'s discovering \r\naspects of herself and sharing them.  yes, she\\\'s projecting \r\nan image because we all seem to do that in one way or \r\nanother when trying to explain how everything affects us.  \r\n<br><br>\r\ni can\\\'t tell you why anyone besides me writes a journal, but \r\ni can tell you why i write mine.  i\\\'ve looked at hundreds of \r\njournals on the web as well as talked to many journalists.  \r\nthey do it for all sorts of reasons.  some are considered \r\nhealthy and some aren\\\'t.  some are ways of living through \r\nexhibitionism.  i\\\'ve seen people using it as a tool of \r\nmanipulation.  i\\\'ve seen people use it as a form of art.  \r\ni\\\'ve seen people use it as a way of communicating something \r\nthat they can\\\'t in person.  also, i\\\'ve seen people doing it \r\njust to be witty and funny.<br><br>\r\nthere are many more reasons why people do it and i\\\'m not \r\neven coming close to all of them.  about six months ago, i \r\nwas inspired to put my private journal online by a girl that \r\nposts on here.  le.  i was inspired by her own journal.  \r\nhowever, my journal is for me alone.  people sometimes ask, \r\n\\\"if the journal is for you, why do you put it online?\\\"  i \r\nenjoy reader feedback.  i find that most of my responses to \r\nmy post are cerebral and i\\\'ve never had an email that says, \r\n\\\"show me your tits!\\\"  i don\\\'t think that i attract that sort \r\nof crowd.  people write to me about how my post affects them \r\nor they question further.  this is fascinating to me.  also, \r\n by writing someting in a public forum, i\\\'m forced to face \r\nthe truth of my post.  i\\\'m forced to remember when something \r\nhappened and how it made me feel.  i also use it to \r\ncommunicate to my father, my sister, and people i \r\nlove.<br><br>\r\ni understand that olivia has a hard time expressing what she \r\nthinks in words.  not because she thinks that they are \r\nbetter than most thoughts, but because sometimes it is hard \r\nto find words to describe them.  she\\\'s also appearing to \r\nfeel that no matter what she shares with people that it \r\nwon\\\'t matter in the end because it is just important to her. \r\n this is a realization that many people come to in their \r\nlife and it is important.  yes, most of what you say ends up \r\nonly being important to you.  however, your words can \r\ninspire millions olivia.  you can do good with them by \r\nsharing your own experiences and i\\\'m sad that you gave up on \r\nyour own journal.  your writing was beautiful and i like how \r\nyou expressed your internal turmoil on a day to day basis.  \r\n<br><br>\r\njp, just because you don\\\'t understand it, doesn\\\'t really \r\nmake it wrong.  this is a lesson that i\\\'ve had to learn the \r\nhard way.  i don\\\'t understand many things and i place hard \r\njudgements on them.  then guess what?  i try it and find it \r\nalltogether really rewarding.  why don\\\'t you try?\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'203.184.249.130','en'),(3830,1069,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<P><b><font size=\"+3\" color=\"red\">\r\nM E R C U R Y</font></b> <font size=\"-2\">\r\n( i n   g e m i n i )</font><font size=\"+3\" color=\"red\">\r\n <BR>R E T R O G R A D E</font>\r\n<br><br>\r\n<b><font size=\"+3\" color=\"red\">\r\nM E R C U R Y</font></b> <font size=\"-2\">\r\n( i n   g e m i n i )</font><font size=\"+3\" color=\"red\">\r\n <BR>R E T R O G R A D E</font>\r\n<br><br>\r\n<b><font size=\"+3\" color=\"red\">\r\nM E R C U R Y</font></b> <font size=\"-2\">\r\n( i n   g e m i n i )</font><font size=\"+3\" color=\"red\">\r\n <BR>R E T R O G R A D E</font>\r\n<br><br>',6,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3831,1069,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','album cover!',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3832,1069,'2001-06-10 04:16:36',0,'cyantist','<br><br>\r\nand just what is that supposed to mean to us \r\nnon-astrological people le?',1,0,0,0,'203.184.249.130','en'),(3833,1069,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','it means shit is <b>fucked</b>.',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3834,1069,'2001-06-10 04:29:36',0,'cyantist','<br><br>\r\nand can you elaborate on that?  maybe that is my point on \r\nastrological references.  the rest of us don\\\'t get what you \r\nmean.  why is shit fucked?  could shit be fucked, simply \r\nbecause it is?  ',1,0,0,0,'203.184.249.130','en'),(3835,1069,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p>like all references (literary, biblical, movies, the \r\nsimpsons), some people get them, others don\\\'t. some \r\npeople are curious and will look them up on their own \r\n(google returns pages of information about mercury \r\nretrograde, btw), others don\\\'t care.</p>\r\n<p>references and metaphor serve as shorthand for \r\nconcepts. rather than type lengthy paragraphs (which \r\nhas been the habit here lately), i would rather explain \r\nmyself briefly, using pointers to ideas.</p>\r\n<p>starting with a base assumption that the reader \r\nunderstands nothing is useful only for technical or \r\ntextbook writing. i enjoy writing that challenges me to \r\nresearch and decode. you may not.  we\\\'re all wired \r\ndifferently, and stuff.</p>',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3836,1071,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>there is a track on the jungle sky compilation (4 or 5 \r\ni think) that has the sample, \\\"a circle, a circle, a circ, a \r\ncirc, a circle.  chaos e explosion -- moment of \r\nconception.\\\" and i guess it has to do with the big bang, \r\nlike a circle exploding outward and becoming less \r\ndense, larger and more complex or less complex?</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i like that song.  it has accompanying rap.  i dont \r\nhave it in front of me.</P>',3,0,0,0,'216.175.91.138','en'),(3837,1069,'2001-06-10 07:39:21',0,'jp','Mercury retrograde in Gemini - I think that means that\r\npeople are more likely to be chatty and cranky possibly.\r\nThat\\\'s my excuse anyway.<BR>\r\nMercurial -- changeable, volatile, fickle, erratic. Mercury\r\nrules communication and the signs associated with it are\r\nGemini (and Virgo). Not sure exactly what retrogade\r\nsignifies except it makes things all wacked I guess.<BR>\r\ncyan: you may get the wrong impression from my recent\r\ncomments. There\\\'s plenty positive about online journals I\r\njust happened to be more focused on the harsher, more\r\nnegative side of things.<BR>\r\nI have written journals at certain times in my life, not\r\nonline though. I wouldn\\\'t just say that online journals are\r\n\\\"wrong\\\" or \\\"bad\\\" (bad journal... bad, bad). In fact I\\\'ve\r\nspent a fair amount of time reading le\\\'s site and other\\\'s\r\nalso -- and I think they\\\'re good.<BR>\r\nHmm... to be concise though, the point I was trying to make\r\nis: false intimacy, self-indulgent narcissism, disconnected\r\neyestrain, blah, blah, blah. Yeah, that\\\'s good. Nice and\r\nharsh and judgemental. Kind of whiney too. Perfect.<BR>\r\nBTW, I have mars,jupiter,pluto in virgo and sun,mercury in\r\nlibra which is probably significant if mercury is retrograde\r\nin gemini, right s5?<BR>\r\n\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,'24.0.133.128','en'),(3838,1066,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','rusty, i don\\\'t really think your snapping at le was the worst thing i\\\'ve read in my life you know?  unusual i think, but perhaps i feel that swinney is so far from my life actual.  sometimes the way in which a friend reacts to our words drives us nearly mad, frustrations spill across them, acrid and razor edged.  it is the price we pay for love sometimes, causing pain or upset.  i don\\\'t know many here, but i\\\'ve got my tenuous judgements, and le is one of those who both brings short spikes of joy to me while often driving me to try pulling hair from my scalp...good thing i shave my head!  we are not perfect, neh?  but maybe we all are sharing something very special, and should appreciate it the same way little children appreciate good people; no strings attached.  truth be told, in well over a decade of online communication, i have never found a place quite like this.  even at work, where i am always miserable, knowing that upon coming home i can spend a few minutes reading the words of everyone here brings a bit of happiness.',1,0,0,0,'207.205.219.176','en'),(3839,1069,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','i think i\\\'m missing something in all of this, but what the hell.  complaints or lamentations about the failures of communication are pointless to me, being as isolated from human contact as i often am, communication in any form is usually appreciated.  when we fail to get something across that is important to us, do we not feel driven to try harder next time?\r\n<br>\r\ni like the taughtness to cyan\\\'s words here, and i agree with her, do not try to reduce people to a formula.  do not play the axiom game.  someone always uses different axioms than you.',3,0,0,0,'207.205.219.176','en'),(3840,1069,'2001-06-10 16:10:41',0,'cyantist','<br>\r\n<br>\r\ni wanted to know what you guys meant by it, not what google \r\nhad to say about it.    ',1,0,0,0,'203.184.249.130','en'),(3841,1067,'2002-04-20 20:49:51',273,'Quinn:','<p>Is two badd Lulu is goeing.  I wyl mis her grately.  I \r\nliked the playing arownd and nowe if she is gon I will hav \r\nverrie little fun on this syte.  Disapointing cuz I thought \r\nwe were too of a kind with different idiyoms.  \r\n\r\n<p>Sie.\r\n\r\n<p>Maybee I will even go away now.',1,0,0,1,'168.191.54.169','en'),(3842,1069,'2001-06-10 17:03:55',0,'astronomy domine','are we in a cave, staring at shadows, trying to \r\ncommunicate. maybe this site is a wall.',0,0,0,0,'24.93.61.58','en'),(3843,1069,'2001-06-10 17:17:46',0,'cyantist.','slide.',1,0,0,0,'203.184.249.130','en'),(3844,1069,'2001-06-10 17:53:57',0,'jo to s5','<p>except that when someone references pop culture, even if \r\nsome of the other people in the conversation don\\\'t catch \r\nthe reference, the conversation usually continues. it\\\'s a \r\nbrief tangent but not a conversation stopper.</p>\r\n<p>something that i have noticed about astrology \r\nenthusiasts and that i myself am guilty of is using \r\nastrology in a very dismissive, catch-all way. like when \r\nsomeone tries to explain to you for five minutes the \r\nproblems with their relationship and the only thing you say \r\nis, \\\"aries,\\\" in response, that person has a justifiably \r\ngood reason to be annoyed with you. that\\\'s true of \r\nanything. if a psych major responded, \\\"he has mother \r\nissues,\\\" you\\\'d be just as annoyed.</p>\r\n<p>it\\\'s been my experience that simply mumbling \r\nastrological terms is the least effective way of \r\nintroducing the concepts to someone.</p>\r\n<p>were you to say, \\\"listen, from what i know about \r\nastrology, this is sort of a fucked up time of the year for \r\nthese reasons...\\\" even if it\\\'s brief and you never go into \r\ndetail, people are much more inclined to further research \r\nit on their own. because you\\\'ve made it interesting to them \r\nby explaining why it\\\'s interesting to you.</p>',3,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(3845,1069,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Queer Moll','<p>I MOSTLY AGREE</p>\r\n<p>Certain experiments taken to either formulate a new \r\nmethod of expression or to simply stop making sense \r\naltogether...</p>\r\n<p>MOSTLY I AM THINKING that people talk far too much and \r\nthat things should be focused mostly on action. In person I \r\nam almost a mute.</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(3846,1069,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p>(to jo)</p>\r\n<p>this assumes that i want to use each conversation \r\nas a teaching opportunity for astrology. the thread that \r\nolivia started was about expression and understanding, \r\nand i wanted to hear about that, rather than hijack the \r\ndiscussion.</p>',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3847,1069,'2001-06-10 22:30:58',0,'jo','the only thing better than staying up all night talking to \r\nsomeone, becoming dizzy with transcendent conversations and \r\nnearly breathless because you can\\\'t talk fast enough to \r\nexpress all the things running through your mind --<BR>\r\nis spending a whole lazy weekend afternoon with someone and \r\nnever saying a word to one another. just sharing space and \r\nwordless peaceful silence.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(3848,1069,'2001-06-10 22:35:36',0,'jo','i felt that you were directly commenting on cyan\\\'s desire \r\nto know why elly brought up mercury in retrograde.<BR>\r\nso what i was trying to say is that cyan\\\'s questions about \r\nelly\\\'s comments didn\\\'t reflect a lack of desire on cyan\\\'s \r\npart to research, but her questioning why elly brought it \r\nup in the first place.<BR>\r\n',3,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(3849,1069,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p>because this doesn\\\'t always have to be about \r\nlinearly flowing conversation. sometimes we scribble \r\nand tag the words we want to see up next to the other \r\nwords, even if they make sense to no one else.\r\n</p><p>\r\ncommunication isn\\\'t always about the effective transfer \r\nof information. the design and placement of messages, \r\neven when obscured, is art.\r\n</p><p>\r\nto illustrate what i mean, i invite you to replace your \r\n\\\"FUCK WORK\\\" stickers with post-it notes, explaining \r\nhow you feel about working for salary, despite loss of \r\ncreative freedom in your daily life. loses impact, no?\r\n</p><p>\r\nit\\\'s so easy to explain it all away.\r\n</p>',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3850,1069,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','hi.',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3851,1072,'2001-06-11 00:27:54',0,'thom','\\\"no alarms, and no surprises please\\\"',1,0,0,0,'24.93.61.58','en'),(3852,1069,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','ok so a problem is that people expect you to tell them what \r\nis going on if they see you\\\'re in some kind of inner \r\nemotional turmoil or joy or whatever. sometimes it\\\'s not \r\npossible and you have to run away.  most times!<br>\r\n<br>\r\nmaybe i should hole up, become a recluse and communicate \r\nexclusively through art.<br>',3,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(3853,1069,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','describing the moment during the moment takes away \r\nfrom the moment. heisenberg, once again.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3854,1069,'2001-06-11 06:27:09',0,'jo','i\\\'ve found that i need a 6 month - 4 year buffer period \r\nbefore i can accurately capture emotional/tumultuous events \r\nin my life. when i\\\'m in them, i\\\'m just flailing and \r\nwondering when it will become normal again, while secretly \r\nhoping that it never does.',1,0,0,0,'172.164.37.27','en'),(3855,1069,'2001-06-11 07:13:46',0,'cyantist','<br><br>\r\nyes yes, olivia!  make art!  the world needs more artists \r\nthat produce tangible works of art.  there\\\'s nothing better \r\nin the world than a medium in which you can control and \r\ncontort to express anything you want.  it is still left to \r\ninterpretation, and the communication may still never get \r\nthrough.  however, it is a valiant effort none the less.\r\n<br><br>\r\nspeaking of heisenberg;<br><br>\r\na man gets pulled over in his car and the police officer \r\nasks the man if he knows how fast he is going and the man \r\nreplies, \\\"no, but i know where i am\\\"\r\n<br><br>\r\ndrum tap\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'202.77.253.245','en'),(3856,1074,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','dude.\r\n<p>\r\nyour booty shakes the most.\r\n</p>',0,0,0,0,'216.175.102.11','en'),(3857,1074,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<ol>\r\n<li> jay has cute undies\r\n<li> all those who can write good rhyming poetry \r\ndeserve worship\r\n</ol>',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3858,1074,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','dude.\r\n<p>\r\nyour booty shakes the most.\r\n</p>',0,0,0,0,'216.175.102.11','en'),(3859,1074,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','dude.\r\n<p>\r\nyour booty shakes the most.\r\n</p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3860,1069,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>i wanna be more like the ocean<br>no talkin man, \r\nall actions!</p>-juanas addiction.<p>jay is always \r\nsaying, \\\" i want to be a writer, but i have nothing to \r\nsay.\\\"</p><p> im feeling now that if you can effectively \r\ntalk to yourself (ie holing yourself up and expression \r\nthrough art) some of the pain of  miscommunication is \r\nalleviated. sometimes when you cant make a \r\nconnection with other people, it\\\'s because youve \r\nneglected your own language. </P> ',0,0,0,0,'216.175.102.11','en'),(3861,1064,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','You gotta love (be wistful for?) Muzak... at least for me, \r\nit was more or less the soundtrack of my childhood, until I \r\ndiscovered the radio...',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(3862,1069,'2001-06-11 13:21:36',0,'jo','hooray for discussions about the inability to express \r\nyourself which ironically produce more discussion and self-\r\nexpression than, say, anal sex.',1,0,0,0,'172.129.65.45','en'),(3863,1073,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','I was riding with a friend who crashed his jeep into a \r\ncabin, once.  It was quite moving, especially for the cabin.',2,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(3864,927,'2002-04-20 20:49:51',273,'Quinn:','<p>I too love Mark Helprin, one amazing fucking writer, \r\nSOLDIER OF THE GREAT WAR can break your heart. \r\nBut he was Bob Dole\\\'s speechwriter not Clinton\\\'s.  \r\n\r\n<p>Rick Moody is marvelous, quirky, funny and \r\nhalf-destroyed.  His books seem to devour themselves \r\nfrom the inside.  Good Stuff.\r\n\r\n<p>George Saudners does some good stories with \r\nhumor and panache.  Most are darkly funny.\r\n\r\n<p>Paul Auster is one of my favorites, though his last \r\ntwo were lacking.  Don\\\'t judge him by the movies \r\nbecause if you thought SMOKE was good, his novels \r\nare much, much better.\r\n\r\n<p>Haruki Murakami is absolutely brilliant and the \r\nstories just get stranger.  Check out his new one, \r\nSPUTNIK SWEETHEART.\r\n\r\n<p>Eggers rocks.  Keep buying McSweeney\\\'s too.\r\n\r\n<p>DFW gets to pedantic for my tastes.\r\n\r\n<p>Try THE HOUSE OF LEAVES by Danielewski.\r\n\r\n<p> You should NEVER EVER forget Raymond Carver.\r\n\r\n<p>Lorrie Moore will amaze and enchant you.  Then her \r\nstories will bite your ass when you turn your back.\r\n\r\n<p>I have to stick a plug in for Charles Bukowski who \r\nchanged the way I look at poetry and prose.\r\n\r\n<p>J.D. Salinger\r\n\r\n<p>An annonymous book called THE WAY OF THE \r\nPILGRIM inspiration for Salinger\\\'s Franny and Zooey.  \r\n\r\n<p>Douglas Coupland wrote one or two good books \r\nGENERATION X and MICROSERFS the rest suck eggs.\r\n\r\n<p>Stephen Millhauser; his book Martin Dressler won \r\nthe Pulitzer a couple of years ago and his work \r\nshimmers as if it were encased in ice.\r\n\r\n<p>Hemingway can do some amazing things.  His is \r\nthe grandfather of all the above.\r\n\r\n<p>You can\\\'t go wrong with Edith Wharton, especially \r\nETHAN FROMME.\r\n\r\n<p>THE SCARLETT LETTER is more than just an 8th \r\ngrade reading assignment.\r\n\r\n<p>I dislike most of Henry James, but DAISY MILLER \r\npleases me.\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,1,'198.185.18.207','en'),(3865,1074,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Phung Moll','<p>That\\\'s some tight shit, yo.</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(3866,1079,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','since we\\\'re on this subject, I would like to tell you all. \r\n\\\"Nietsche\\\" is pronounced \\\"Nee-CHA\\\". dont fuckin forget it!!!\r\n',1,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(3867,1079,'2001-06-11 19:20:03',0,'jo','bmg, you told it backwards. you mean that you sometimes \r\npronounce it \\\"aw-ree,\\\" and people say, \\\"oh you \r\nmean, \\\'awry.\\\'\\\"<BR>\r\nor at least. well that\\\'s the way you told it to us the \r\nother night and that\\\'s the way it makes sense.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(3868,1075,'2001-06-11 19:33:32',0,'jay','i love everything you have to say... and we should \r\nremember this thing about labor and pleasure. it\\\'s \r\nsomething i\\\'ve too easily forgotten.  There is incredible \r\npleasure in work, when the work is yours.  The work \r\njust hasn\\\'t been ours in a couple of years.  We\\\'ve been \r\ndoing dumbass internet work, putting pages online for \r\nbaby boomers and middle american housewives to \r\nread and dream over, because they are bored and just \r\ngot a computer from their son-in-law.<p>\r\nHave you ever read \\\"Arcadia\\\" by Tom Stoppard, or read \r\nessays about the aesthetic of 18th century English \r\ngardens?  The wealthy had acres upon acres to play \r\nwith, and for many years they did very classical things \r\nwith them, like the romans, plotting out spaces in grids, \r\nwith fountains and square surfaces of grass, with \r\nborders of trimmed shrubs and roses, etc.  But then in \r\nthe 18th century, there came the literature of the \r\nsublime, and then the gothic.  People were fascinated \r\nby that which was out of their control... the native \r\ncultures they were colonizing, the wild lands where you \r\ncould be mauled by lions and tigers and bears.  This \r\nbecame the dominant aesthetic for gardens too, the \r\nideal of natural beauty: the wild.  English gardens \r\nbecame these intricately planned \\\"wild\\\" spaces, with \r\nrolling hills that lead into dark forests and grand, \r\nunkempt shrubbery that could conceal whole armies of \r\nhiding children.  Eden became something less \r\nmathematical, and more threatening, chaotic, but they \r\nloved it for this very reason.  They\\\'d gotten bored with \r\nthe orderliness of their culture.  In the end though, it \r\nwent out of fashion, because what were these gardens \r\nbut simply another form of order, another template to \r\nuse in designing your lawns.',2,0,0,0,'216.175.103.64','en'),(3869,1079,'2001-06-11 19:46:00',0,'jay','don\\\'t forget the \\\"z\\\"<p>\r\nit\\\'s Nietzsche',3,0,0,0,'216.175.103.64','en'),(3870,1075,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>\r\nthats what i freakin hate about media labor. its empty labor, \r\npushing pixels that make images that sell products. its so \r\npainfully apart from the body. killed my sex drive for \r\nawhile. \r\n</p>\r\n<p>BUT at the same time, i dont believe that \\\"owning\\\" labor \r\nis the key to pleasure. that because i, egg, beat this cookie \r\ndough, it has meaning for me. I was really more just talking \r\nabout the convergence of leisure and labor in any possible \r\nprocess....that one couldnt negate the other, no matter. what \r\nam I? a zen post-marxist fruitcake batty insomniac prude.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>and I havent read that, you tried to make me read that \r\nback in the day and i think i fell asleep and drooled on it \r\nand had sex dreams.</p> \r\n',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(3871,1079,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>\r\nevery day i ask myself, why is jay not a spelling bee \r\nchampion? where is lulu when you need her.</p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(3872,1079,'2001-06-11 19:58:23',0,'bmg','<p>my point exactly, jo! I can\\\'t even tell my stories \r\nright! =0</p> Yes, jo is correct, I am wrong... I say aw-\r\nree, instead of a-rye. Through extensive government \r\ntraining, I am now fixed from saying aw-ree, i can\\\'t even \r\ntype it correctly.</p><p>.......fuck, I\\\'m a dork. if lulu \r\nwere here, she would make fun of me.</p>',1,0,0,0,'66.68.79.200','en'),(3873,1079,'2001-06-11 19:59:59',0,'bmg','I am getting ready to unload some 100+ computer books at \r\nhalf-price books. because I can\'t read...',1,0,0,0,'66.68.79.200','en'),(3874,1079,'2001-06-11 20:01:24',0,'bmg','I am getting rid of all my Nutzche books too.',1,0,0,0,'66.68.79.200','en'),(3875,1079,'2002-04-20 20:49:51',273,'Quinn:','flaccid is pronounced FLAK-sid\r\n',1,0,0,1,'198.185.18.207','en'),(3876,1079,'2001-06-11 20:25:28',0,'bmg','<b>flacÂ·cid</b><br>\r\nPronunciation:<pre> Ã·\'fla-s&d also \'flak-s&d\r\n</pre>',1,0,0,0,'66.68.79.200','en'),(3877,1079,'2001-06-11 20:29:07',0,'jo','i\\\'m about to get rid of 2 garbage bags worth of clothes. we \r\nshould have a garage sale, bmg. i mean, not for this stuff, \r\njust for the delight of having a garage sale. ',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(3878,1079,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg TO JO','we have this thing here called \\\"clothes swap\\\" where people \r\nbring the shit they dont want and try each other\\\'s outfits on \r\nand go away with it. it is SUPER FUN. elephant sale- styley. \r\nand at the end you pile the leftovers into a car together and \r\ngo to salvation army.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(3879,1079,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Snob Moll','<p>Actually, it\\\'s Neetz-che, where the last \\\"e\\\" should be \r\nsort of like \\\"eh\\\".</p>\r\n<p>The other day I learned how to properly \r\npronounce \\\'Artaud\\\'. With the French it\\\'s a little \r\ndifferent, though. It\\\'s not that we can\\\'t pronounce their \r\nwords. They just don\\\'t know how to spell.</p>\r\n<p>Nietzsche gets me horny, yo. The mustache is <i>so \r\nvery</i>, I want to rub against it, I want to feel that \r\ndrooping walrushair all over my body. Oh God. Oh God. He \r\nused to climb mountains. A very potent man. I have to take \r\na shower now :< </p>\r\n',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(3880,1080,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','steel pan. steel pan. steel pan.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3881,1078,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','i dreamt about xep before i met her, too.  more than once.',3,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(3882,1078,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','last night i had a dream about my wide angle lens.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(3883,1078,'2001-06-11 22:40:11',0,'Danielle','I think it might mean I need to meet Xep... hmmmm',1,0,0,0,'207.34.94.238','en'),(3884,1078,'2001-06-11 22:41:41',0,'rusty','I dreampt about xep before I met her...  I met her through \r\na combination of seeing her on the bus to santa cruz a few \r\ntimes, and then finding out she new some of the people I \r\nknew in the xbbs and ucscb scenes...\r\n<p>\r\nI remember the purple mohawk she had very well...  and she\r\nhad it when I dreampt about her...\r\n<p>\r\nbut, maybe I had seen her around cabrillo, or somewhere \r\nelse before I dreampt about her, and it was only after I \r\ndreampt about her that when I saw her I was so intrigued...\r\n<p>\r\nis it that dreams can have a large effect on our psyche and \r\nlives, or is it that dreams are premonitions?  No one can \r\ngive a definate answer to that, and if they think they can, \r\nI will be even less likely to believe any aspect of what \r\nthey say...  lol...',1,0,0,0,'205.142.76.11','en'),(3885,1078,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','last night while sitting in a bar surrounded by people i\r\nadore and want to be near always, i told xan of the dream i\r\nhad about her.  she was so excited that she was in my dream\r\neven though the content of it didn\\\'t please her.  she said \r\nsomething, in a drunken stumble, about our dreams being\r\nportals to the 4th dimension and she wondered how her 4th\r\ndimensional self had met up with mine.\r\n\r\nso i dunno, danielle.  i dunno how our 4th dimensional\r\nselves hooked up.  maybe we were both getting burritos at\r\nbalazzo and it was something in the beans.\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(3886,1080,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','i read a book recently in which there was an old cannon from\r\nthe revolutionary war on the grounds of a boy\\\'s school.  the\r\nbase of the cannon was a popular site for the boys to sneak\r\naway with a girl and get it on.  the cannon\\\'s hollow barrel\r\nwas filled with used condoms these escapades.  it was the\r\ncondom graveyard.',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(3887,783,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','old messages...\r\n<br><br>\r\ndamn, i love that sort of pain.\r\n<br>\r\nkung fu?\r\n',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(3888,895,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','so what happened?',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(3889,1080,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','if only i were a boy so i could jism into a stainless steel \r\npan and watch the little guys under a microscope dying,  \r\ntrying to impregnate the unyielding, frigid, steel. pan. ',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(3890,1081,'2001-06-11 23:21:43',0,'cyantist','yes.',1,0,0,0,'203.184.249.130','en'),(3891,1079,'2001-06-11 23:25:51',0,'jo','yes, this needs to happen. if just for an excuse to play \r\ndress-up.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(3892,1080,'2001-06-11 23:27:55',0,'jp','The book with the condom cannon -- \\\"The World According to \r\nGarp\\\". A lot of other interesting things in it also. That \r\nwas the first \\\"long\\\" book I read when I was 13 or so. It \r\nleft a lot of impressions.<BR>\r\nHappened to see Garp (Robin Williams) on Actor\\\'s Studio \r\nthis weekend.',0,0,0,0,'63.172.123.3','en'),(3893,1080,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','i didn\\\'t mention the title because i thought maybe austin\r\nand elly were tired of me talking about it.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\nsuch a good book.',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(3894,1081,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>\r\ngasp.\r\n</p>',1,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(3895,1080,'2001-06-12 00:00:29',0,'ben','all of irving is good, or for the most part, if you ask me, \r\nbut twisted, also. Try a widow for one year, next, if \r\nyou\\\'re looking for more.',0,0,0,0,'208.143.2.244','en'),(3896,1080,'2001-06-12 00:26:02',0,'jo','dude. hotel new hampshire.<BR>\r\ni\\\'ve read all of his except for piggy sneed and hotel new \r\nhampshire wins, hands down.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(3897,1079,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','haha.  lao tzu up there says, \\\"life is sweet.\\\"\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.79.36','en'),(3898,1084,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','<p>\r\nthe KGB bar. oh lordy me.<br>\r\n-slight twitch-<br>\r\nboy do i have some stories from that place.<br>\r\nthat block of 4th is my old block.</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(3899,1084,'2001-06-12 01:34:21',0,'panda','ROAR!',6,0,0,0,'64.51.232.105','en'),(3900,1083,'2001-06-12 02:41:25',0,'<TT>METH -n- DEATH</TT>','<PRE>\r\nfallen angel of\r\ndeath.  dripping blood. sinners die.\r\nburning neurosis.\r\n\r\nburn! burn!\r\n</PRE>',6,0,0,0,'64.51.232.102','en'),(3901,1083,'2001-06-12 04:06:14',0,'cyantist','i like that steve.  nice.',1,0,0,0,'202.77.253.245','en'),(3902,1085,'2001-06-12 04:16:49',0,'cyantist','<br>\r\n<br>\r\nyour last few entries have been so honest and forthcoming.  \r\nwhen i\\\'m done reading them, i find myself without words.  i \r\nfeel something in my belly that hurts with you.  perhaps it \r\nis my maternal instinct or my ultra violent punk rock past \r\nthat connects with your stories as if i were there or they \r\nwere my own.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\nalthough you hate moving, do you find that you can perhaps \r\nlook at this as a way to move past the old and into the new? \r\n i know it is bad to forget where you came from and what \r\nmade you who you are, but does moving perhaps allow you the \r\nfreedom of starting out fresh and creating newer memories \r\nthat might perhaps be better?  \r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\ni would never trade my past for anything else, because i \r\nknow it made me a strong person.  i think you identify with \r\nthat. \r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\neverything bad is good in a way.. if you take everything as \r\na learning experience.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\ni dunno, i\\\'m at a loss of words again.  i\\\'m sorry ',1,0,0,0,'202.77.253.245','en'),(3903,1084,'2001-06-12 04:21:00',0,'cyantist','<br>\r\ni\\\'m happy your father is ok!  wow, that is good timing that \r\nyou caught the car smoking before it blew up.  people \r\nshouldn\\\'t smoke in cars for that reason.',1,0,0,0,'202.77.253.245','en'),(3904,1081,'2001-06-12 07:02:08',0,'kat','<p>sweetness\r\nof le<br>\r\nhoneydew melon\r\nthe scent of green\r\neverlasting\r\namorphous\r\nlanguid \r\nchangeling</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'12.64.90.20','en'),(3905,1085,'2001-06-12 07:11:41',0,'kat','craziness. shuffling through. ten years past. an era. \r\nending tonight. finding those pictures. your arms curled \r\naround me. whispers of future things. always dreamt. the \r\ntwo and the four. but it didnt add up. so here i am. \r\nshuffling. shuffling. empty boxes. filled but still empty. \r\nthe end of a lifetime. can i breath again? not then. not \r\nthen. i found my own way. time to say goodbye. fire. \r\nphoenix. rising again.',4,0,0,0,'12.64.90.20','en'),(3906,1085,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','beach burn. bring the boxes, i\\\'ll bring the wood and \r\nflames.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3907,1083,'2001-06-12 07:30:22',0,'gracie','oh stevie, you\\\'re so poetic.  did you go to school for that?\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(3908,1075,'2001-06-12 07:34:26',0,'gracie','you sound like delightful people, may i drool with the both of you?\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(3909,1083,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i went to late night tv correspondence school.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3910,1083,'2001-06-12 08:07:25',0,'gracie','mmm hmmm.  i\\\'m listening.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(3911,1083,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','let\\\'s name the twins beatrice and gladys.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3912,1081,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','hey it\\\'s kat! *nuzzle* kat. *nuzzle* mojo the pooch. ',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3913,1081,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Thoon Moll','<p>hn\\\'te hah</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(3914,1083,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','<p>Heh.</p>\r\n<p>Dood. This is the coolest post ever. I can\\\'t get over \r\nit. I don\\\'t know what that red thing is. I don\\\'t want to \r\nknow. It is just too cool.</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(3915,1083,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'BlasÃ© Moll','<p>Seriously now.</p>\r\n<p>I just really can\\\'t stop looking/thinkingabout/talking \r\nabout this post. I want it to last forever. jesus.</p>\r\n<p>Sorry.</p>',1,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(3916,1083,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i am so unloved. :( :( :( :(',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3917,1083,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','should i make it longer? i can make it longer.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3918,1073,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','once when i was a kid, someone drank too much and \r\nflipped their car over onto the lawn of our house, nearly \r\ncrashing through the living room. this was my first \r\nexposure to \\\"the jaws of life\\\". the car was still flipped \r\nover on its roof, the door wide open (but the person still \r\nwedged inside), the radio projecting the 700 club at very \r\nloud volume, beer cans everywhere. the end.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3919,1085,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','on my way to work.  had to check an ebay bid o\\\' mine.  stopped here and saw.  cyantist:  the new seems always like the past.  i move there and find the same people in new bodies.  maybe i don\\\'t need to give up the past, or burn all this shite.  maybe i need to burn.  i feel tired and used up.  reviled.  uglier than yesterday and closer to the knife.  but then, i\\\'m leaving in a minute for a place where my name isn\\\'t dave but \\\'nigger-jew\\\'.',1,0,0,0,'207.205.219.242','en'),(3920,1087,'2001-06-12 10:55:15',0,'Joanna','My scar is fading now, and while I know that\\\'s a good \r\nthing, maybe I\\\'m going to miss it, the constant reminder of \r\nwhat it stood for, the fact that it stood for life and not \r\nsomething else.  The plus side is that it means that no one \r\nelse will ever find it and go \\\"what the fuck is that?\\\" and \r\nneed explanations.  Because no one\\\'s going to ever be able \r\nto look inside me and see, so it\\\'s only what shows on the \r\noutside that people will know.  I don\\\'t know if scars are \r\nuseful, or helpful, but I guess they\\\'re part of everyone.  ',1,0,0,0,'203.97.2.243','en'),(3921,1081,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','every time you\\\'re not in the mood to listen to someone\\\'s\r\nshit, why don\\\'t you say \\\"look, i\\\'m not in the mood to deal\r\nwith you being like this.  i will only be sarcastic and\r\nsnappy.  i\\\'m sorry, try me again another day.\\\"<br>\r\n<br>\r\nis honesty coupled with kindness really so hard?<br>\r\n<br>\r\nor am i just asking to be coddled?<br>\r\n<!-- this post is to no one in particular -->',3,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(3922,1087,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','<br>did you ever know just how hard i tried to bring you\r\nsunshine? but all i gave to you was moonlight.<br>',1,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(3923,1081,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<br><br>there needs to be a special safe word or hanky \r\ncode, exactly for this purpose. the signal would mean \"i \r\nlove you but i\'m going to stop talking to you/being \r\naround you now.\"',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3924,1087,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','moonlight',3,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(3925,1087,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','nothing but moonlight',6,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(3926,1087,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','<a href=\\\"http://www.artoffighting.com\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">art\r\nof fighting</a>',4,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(3927,0,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>wow, weird stuff happens when you hit that \\\"cancel\\\" \r\nbutton.</p>\r\n<p>YOU TAKE THE RED PILL</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin',6,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(3928,1086,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>Wow, weird stuff happens when you click that button.</p>\r\n',5,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(3929,1088,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>A lot of the content on this site is dead. For example, \r\nreference my huge <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?\r\nid=713.txt\\\">response</a> to a question someone asked me in \r\nresponse to a post. It took me too long to respond and it \r\nwasn\\\'t on the top 5 anymore and the person never saw it. I \r\noccasionally browse the things that people wrote back in \r\nthe day, but more often it\\\'s like reading a mailing list. I \r\nwonder what people sent in today?</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin',1,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(3930,1081,'2001-06-12 13:06:20',0,'auntie','5 is right.  a special word.  we should think of one.',1,0,0,0,'24.162.119.106','en'),(3931,1088,'2001-06-12 13:43:55',0,'sawx','<br>\r\nisn\\\'t that the point of the new \\\'view all the comments\\\' \r\nthingo?<br><br>\r\nanyways, i prefer to think of websites and humming and \r\nbubbling, but i think thats just a me thing....\r\n',2,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(3932,1087,'2001-06-12 13:45:36',0,'sawks','<br>\r\nmaybe if instead you had like, lil horns on your head \r\nthat grew?<br><br>\r\nthat would be cute, and you could poke ppl with em...',2,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(3933,1081,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to s5 & auntie','my GAWD joanne and I were fighting this weekend and \r\ntrying to work out this system. instead of drinking, we \r\nwent to Target.\r\n<p>we were pretending to browse after they didnt have \r\nunderoos and came across these goofy teen tank tops \r\nthat say in sparkly letters, \\\"I have issues.\\\"</p>\r\n<p>so we bought them. </p>\r\n<p>and agreed that next time we have a moment in \r\nwhich we love each other but cant solve anything, the \r\ncode phrase is \\\"I have issues.\\\"</p>\r\n<p>I\\\'ll let you know if it works out.</p>',0,0,0,0,'216.175.100.187','en'),(3934,1084,'2001-06-12 15:41:58',0,'bmg','<p>we are born alone, and yes we will probably die alone... \r\nbut I think that is why it is important to have friends, \r\nmake friends, do things with friends... because that \r\ncreates memories, a history... </p>',1,0,0,0,'198.214.191.101','en'),(3935,1083,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','oh 5! it\\\'s perfect the way it is, a nugget of \r\ninscrutability in a universe of causal relationships. let \r\nus gaze at it together. it looks like it would taste like \r\ncherry if i lick it. perfect.',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(3936,1088,'2001-06-12 16:24:42',0,'cyantist','<br><br>\r\nmy one swinney wish is that there be a section where you can \r\nsee the most recently commented on post.  that way you can \r\nkeep up with everyone\\\'s older threads that you find \r\ninteresting.',1,0,0,0,'203.184.249.130','en'),(3937,1085,'2001-06-12 16:33:29',0,'cyantist','<br><br>\r\ndave.. dave.. dave..<br><br>\r\nplease do not lose hope like that.  we should talk on the \r\nphone when i get back to the states.   i suck at email and i \r\nrarely respond.  when i do, it is because i\\\'ve mulled it \r\nover for days on end.  i want to hear why life has brought \r\nyou this much pain and maybe we can learn a few things from \r\neach other.<br><br>\r\nlike you, i was involved in an ultra violent scene that \r\nallowed me to take part of it, because i was an outcast of a \r\nbroken home.  i found my identity in the punk scene and \r\namongst working class skinheads.  my family turned into \r\ncommunists, punks, skins, and crusty street kids.  i saw the \r\nworst possible things happen to people.  some of these \r\nthings happened to me.<br><br>\r\ni\\\'m not the happiest person in the world, but i\\\'m doing \r\npretty well considering.  there are many times that i lost \r\nall hope and didn\\\'t want to go on with life any longer, but \r\ni found some shred of happiness buried deep within to hold \r\non to.<br><br>\r\nwhat is the last happy moment you had that you remember?  \r\nthink about it and cherish it.  you need a vacation from \r\nyour pain.  come to san francisco for a week or so.  can you \r\ndo that?',1,0,0,0,'203.184.249.130','en'),(3938,1081,'2001-06-12 16:34:37',0,'kat.passing.note.to.le','canceriousness: a peculiar heterogeneous divine affliction \r\nknown to cause infinite reverbertions of passionate \r\ndiscord. [ie: this receiver has no filter.]',1,0,0,0,'12.64.90.65','en'),(3939,1027,'2001-06-12 16:35:46',0,'decius','\\\"Hong Kong is an intellectual city.\\\" \r\n\r\nThe cab driver had been taking English lessons and fished \r\nfor a complement. He talked about the difficulties \r\nassociated with learning English. English vs. American \r\nspellings. The difference between Treat, Treaty, and \r\nTreatment... I had to strain and play very close attention \r\nto follow his ramblings... \r\n\r\nEventually he asked me what I thought of the people here. \r\nPeople in Hong Kong are reserved but friendly. They are \r\neasy to get along with. They are smart and they value \r\nintelligence. The Engineers here test you, test your \r\nintellect. If they find strength they respect you. If they \r\nfind weakness they ignore you. Its all very subtle...\r\n\r\nPeople in Hong Kong are too obsessed with phoney trappings \r\nof status. Titles. The brand awareness of the company you \r\nwork for. They want to be a high ranking employee at a big \r\ncompany that is well known. \r\n\r\nThere seems to be some disconnect between what they feel \r\nwill bring them respect from their friends and what they \r\nrespect in others... \r\n\r\nI couldn\\\'t put it into words for the cabbie... He offered \r\nthe above observation. \r\n\r\nTried to tip him... He refused, and explained... \r\nDignity. He was very serious about it. He also mentioned \r\nhonesty, sincerity, compassion... What he respects in a \r\nperson. He respects racial equality. Dignity was the most \r\nimportant thing. He is a professional. He provides a \r\nservice and he wants to do it well. He was very proud of \r\nwhat he was doing and he wanted to do it in the most \r\nhonorable manner possible. \r\n\r\nI wanted to extend my hand to shake his as I left the cab \r\nand he beat me to the punch. \r\n\r\nViolence.... Violence in America is directly related to its \r\nyouth. 200 years is not a long time culturally. A handful \r\nof generations. The span of two or three lifetimes. Imagine \r\nonly 200 years ago most of North America was uncharted \r\nwilderness. Imagine that. We know more about the moon then \r\nEurope knew about Utah in 1801. Guns... Guns... Guns... and \r\nThe Bible... Carved this nation... out of the wilderness. \r\nMost places with an extremely high rate of gun ownership \r\nand violent crime are places that HISTORICALLY were \r\nviolent. Seems strange to think that the media\\\'s gangstahs \r\nrolling through the hood with their AKs got that way \r\nbecause of what a bunch of white people were doing in that \r\nsame place 150 years beforehand, but there is a direct \r\ncorrelation. History doesn\\\'t provide the emotional context \r\nfor violent crime, but it provides the cultural context. \r\n\r\nPeople own guns. Guns are used to resolve disputes. Thats \r\nthe way things work. You better get a gun to protect \r\nyourself from all these other idiots with guns. Guns...\r\n\r\nBut I\\\'ll stop short of being an anti-gun person. If I want \r\nto own a damn submachine gun, then I\\\'ll own a damn \r\nsubmachine gun and I\\\'ll shoot it whenever I damn well \r\nplease. Of course I don\\\'t. Never owned a gun. Will never \r\nown a gun. But the minute you tell me the choice is not \r\nmine I will own a gun just to show you that it really is. \r\n\r\nI don\\\'t trust you to choose for me. You don\\\'t have my best \r\ninterests in mind often enough that I\\\'ve learned to second \r\nguess everything you tell me even if it is for my own good. \r\nDISCLAIMER: Personal anti-authority issue, not a \r\nrecommended social policy. Has to do with dealing with \r\nadults as a small child. Part of me. Not part of everything.\r\n\r\nAlthough in a way America has a problem with authority, and \r\nits one of the most unique things about it\\\'s culture. \r\nSomething about being born in violent overthrow of a \r\nforgien government. If the third world ever stabalizes \r\nthey\\\'ll carry such scars too, and I\\\'m digressing all over \r\nthe place now. Getting too tired to stick to a topic here. \r\n\r\nThe tie in is that the thing that needs to change is the \r\nculture, not the rules, and the culture will not change \r\novernight. Anti-gun people play a valuable cultural role, \r\nbut they would be more effective if they concentrated on \r\nmaking things a matter of personal choice. American\\\'s \r\naren\\\'t going to put down guns because their government said \r\nthey were bad. American\\\'s will put them down if they begin \r\nto decide that guns really aren\\\'t that interesting. \r\n\r\nBack to the media... I hate the idea of controlling that \r\nabout 100,000 times more then I hate the idea of \r\ncontrolling guns... Rule by cultural concensus is far more \r\ndifficult then rule by force, but its also heathier...\r\n\r\nAnd now we\\\'re on the internet having this conversation and \r\ntrying to figure out together what that concensus should \r\nbe.... \r\n',3,0,0,0,'203.184.249.130','en'),(3940,1027,'2001-06-12 16:42:06',0,'cyantist','thank you.  if i weren\\\'t so tired, i\\\'d have a better \r\nresponse.. however i think that you pegged just about \r\neverything decius.  your experience with the cab driver \r\nshould go on my cab site if i ever get it up.  that\\\'s great.',1,0,0,0,'203.184.249.130','en'),(3941,1087,'2001-06-12 16:54:37',0,'<p>kat</p>','<p>my first thought: be careful what you wish for.</p>\r\n<p>my best friend. my soul sister...she has the scars you \r\ndream of. on her face. on her hands. on most of her body. \r\nsince she was two and caught in a house fire. she and i \r\nhave often compared notes. her physical wounds. my \r\nemotional ones. they both cut deep. scars are heavier than \r\nyou think. they are not armour. they are a cross you carry. \r\nweight on your shoulders. i do all that i can to range free \r\nof it. to let go. i wouldnt want to have to look at the \r\ncrap ive been through...every day...in the mirror when i \r\nwake up. i feel it all a little too much. craving laughter. \r\nthen B walks in the door wearing a red tshirt. it has big \r\nbold letters that say \\\"FIRE\\\" and now i know why i love her \r\nso much.</p>',2,0,0,0,'12.64.90.65','en'),(3942,1075,'2001-06-12 17:20:53',0,'jay to egg','yeah, who are you?  All i was saying was that when \r\nyou\\\'re an artist, and you can work at your own creative \r\nlabor, the act of creation is pleasurable, and satisfying, \r\ncan produce an intoxication, even, akin to alcohol, but \r\nbetter.  That is a pleasure we should strive for. Why you \r\ngotta bring Marx into it and shit. <p>\r\nAnd who\\\'s gracie?  Is she mocking us? Because we \r\nmost certainly deserve to be mocked right now.\r\n',3,0,0,0,'216.175.100.187','en'),(3943,1088,'2002-03-15 00:17:55',129,'moebius','<p>darwin: speaking as a brandnew contributor to this site--\r\nby your invitation, natch--you ought to know that yr \r\nbiglong post and response was one of the first things I \r\nread. It gave me a lot of insight into who you were as a \r\nperson. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>I think the site would need to be seriously redesigned \r\nif we want to have lots of living, dynamic conversations. \r\nbut on the other hand all conversations die eventually, no \r\nmatter what you do. in my experience the ones that thrive \r\nare often unworthy of the extended attention--just like a \r\nlot of bad tv shows.</p>\r\n\r\n',2,0,0,0,'63.38.73.60','en'),(3944,1088,'2001-06-12 18:14:39',0,'bmg','word to cyantist... it is a good idea.\r\n',3,0,0,0,'66.68.79.200','en'),(3945,1075,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','LULU???!! is that you!!',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(3946,1086,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','dude.\r\n<p>\r\nwe\\\'re getting the band back together.</p>\r\nmang.',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(3947,1080,'2001-06-12 19:06:35',0,'Stella','I *must* disagree. The best John Irving book EVER is \\\"A \r\nPrayer for Owen Meany\\\". If you like Irving, esp. World \r\nAccording to Garp, you need to read about Owen. \r\n',0,0,0,0,'168.100.203.247','en'),(3948,1091,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>this reminds me of the desert.  there is little to \r\nwonder at but there is a biosphere and lots of little \r\ncreatures running around at night</P>',3,0,0,0,'64.51.232.102','en'),(3949,1092,'2001-06-12 20:08:00',0,'kat','rough skin sweat dripping\r\nhammer in hand breathing hard\r\nbuilding worlds from flesh\r\n',1,0,0,0,'12.64.13.29','en'),(3950,1092,'2001-06-12 20:09:03',0,'kat','<p> oh damn...that was supposed to be:</p>\r\n<p>rough skin sweat dripping<br>\r\nhammer in hand breathing hard<br>\r\nbuilding worlds from flesh</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'12.64.13.29','en'),(3951,1087,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','dunno about this.  my whole body is scarred.  from knives, knuckles, acid, explosives, razors, concrete, fire, hitting my dumb ass with a hammer at work, falling off of ladders.  sometimes i am proud of my scars, like a map of where i\\\'ve been.  but too often they\\\'re also a map of where i\\\'m going.  and i don\\\'t like what that implies for my future.  i remember when the scar across my carotid was first healing, and i was walking to lunch with some college friends, i saw a pretty girl, smiled and said \\\"hi.\\\"  now, i\\\'m not much of a looker to begin with, but she actually blanched when she saw my scar, my friend Brian said \\\"dave, i think she thought you were going to attack her.\\\"  it took a long time for me to get used to people, mostly women, looking at me, and then looking away for good.  the scars in your heart are every bit as real as any scar on my body, and to someone with a decent heart, every bit as visible.  just a thought.',2,0,0,0,'207.205.216.1','en'),(3952,1088,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','i agree with darwin\\\'s comment, and think cyan is on to something good.',2,0,0,0,'207.205.216.1','en'),(3953,1092,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','we\\\'re not all like that.  i\\\'m thinking about setting up a website for all of us err....not quite normal but not racist, sexist, and all that.  aha.  \\\"i\\\'m not a creep\\\" contruction workers support site.  \r\n<br>\r\ni heard the word \\\'nigger\\\' used with hostile intent exactly 34 times today, my boss really likes that word; i probably should not bother to count however.  this doesn\\\'t include the fact that i\\\'m called \\\'nigger-jew\\\' by almost everyone there.  blah.',2,0,0,0,'207.205.216.1','en'),(3954,1092,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','when i worked on construction sites most people wouldn\\\'t\r\neven make eye contact with me.  hrm.',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(3955,1027,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','decius...\\\"Violence.... Violence in America is directly related to its \r\nyouth. 200 years is not a long time culturally. A handful \r\nof generations. The span of two or three lifetimes. Imagine \r\nonly 200 years ago most of North America was uncharted \r\nwilderness. Imagine that. We know more about the moon then \r\nEurope knew about Utah in 1801. Guns... Guns... Guns... and \r\nThe Bible... Carved this nation... out of the wilderness. \r\nMost places with an extremely high rate of gun ownership \r\nand violent crime are places that HISTORICALLY were \r\nviolent.\\\"\r\n<p>\r\nthis bit here is a fallacy.  relating violence to the youth of our culture ignores historical evidence in other cultures.  the \\\'barbarians\\\' who conquered China every few hundred years had been around for quite a while.  tribal warfare in Africa isn\\\'t new, although the intensity of it has increased since western powers imposed artificial borders, thus thowing tribes together where they used to try and avoid each other.  Rome?!  Ireland?  Germany?  Please, what you seem to be doing is trying to boil violence down to something simple.  here in America we\\\'ve been trying that for years, and the violence gets worse.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\n\\\"Most places with an extremely high rate of gun ownership \r\nand violent crime are places that HISTORICALLY were \r\nviolent.\\\"  I\\\'ve seen many ATTEMPTED proofs of this kind of theory.  they are all wishful thinking at its worst.  In America high gun ownership is directly correlated to a drop in certain violent crimes.  The facts are available to anyone who wishes to look them up, rather than being spoon fed information by HCI.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\ncultural consensus?  sounds good in theory, but the fact is if the consesus was taken from only the people i know, it would be mere hours before i took up arms and fought.  i don\\\'t want everyone to be happy, to have a television and car; i don\\\'t care if everyone has and internet connection.  i don\\\'t like the unions and socialism is abhorrent to me.  i don\\\'t believe in \\\'human rights\\\', even if they sound good in theory.  cultural consesus is about as workable as anarchy.  and if you think anarchy is doable, consider that me and mine are better armed, better trained, and perfectly willing to take by force if need be.  as long as i am a member of a society which doesn\\\'t completely violate my beliefs, i\\\'m peaceful, force unacceptable lifestyles on me, and i will turn violent.  wishful thinking and pleasant theory will never be enough to fix the problems of humankind.  find something better.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n',4,0,0,0,'207.205.216.1','en'),(3956,1083,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Vileness Moll','<p>S5! Don\\\'t touch it! Perfection! Perfection!</p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(3957,1083,'2001-06-12 22:24:51',0,'critic','uh\r\n',4,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(3958,1081,'2002-03-08 04:52:47',65,'le to olivia','it seems like when i say \\\"sorry, i can\\\'t deal with you at \r\nthe moment\\\" to people, everyone gets pissed off. sometimes \r\nthe people who get pissed off aren\\\'t even the people i \r\nasked to lay off. i don\\\'t know. humans are difficult.',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3959,1085,'2001-06-12 23:55:28',0,'dawn','davey. you are one of the most beautiful people i know. \r\nanyone that thinks otherwise should be shamed. not only are \r\nyou honest and caring and giving and wonderful, you\\\'re so \r\ndamned cute, too, especially when you smile.\r\n<p>\r\nplease, go to san fran and visit. i\\\'ll pay for you to go if \r\nthat will help. \r\n<p>\r\ni love you.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'206.97.109.64','en'),(3960,1027,'2001-06-13 00:03:27',0,'rusty','fat chance...  but good luck in trying to find something \r\nthat would work...',6,0,0,0,'64.163.194.75','en'),(3961,1085,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','good grief',1,0,0,0,'207.205.216.1','en'),(3962,1085,'2001-06-13 02:36:59',0,'cyantist','<br><br>\r\nso what do you say?  yes?  no?  i\\\'ll be back in july and \r\nwould love it if you came out to stay with rob for a few \r\ndays or a week.  i\\\'m sure he\\\'d love that too!',1,0,0,0,'202.77.253.245','en'),(3963,1091,'2001-06-13 03:03:49',0,'cyantist',' - beautiful',1,0,0,0,'202.77.253.245','en'),(3964,1085,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','well, i\\\'d like to come out, but i\\\'m in the process of moving, with all the expenses that implies.  i\\\'m cash poor, with no savings.  maybe i can swing something.  \\\'course my business parter will want to kill me but he can suck it.  ',1,0,0,0,'207.205.216.1','en'),(3965,1093,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p align=\"justify\">i have done some freelance work helping nonprofits \r\nget online. in that context, most of the nonprofits i\'ve \r\ndealt with are not on the ball technologically (that is, if \r\nthey\'re not a technology-related nonprofit, like <a \r\nhref=\"http://eff.org\">eff</a> for instance), because of the \r\nlack of $$ and lack of focus on such things.\r\n<br><br>\r\nthat said, i think it\'s really fun to help make the lives \r\neasier for people who work at nonprofits by adminning their \r\nmachines, making their website better, etc. the difference \r\nis that smaller nonprofits NEED the help and are grateful \r\nfor it, as opposed to huge corporations who just have \r\narbitrary headcounts to fill, etc. i think people who work \r\nfor nonprofits tend to feel more appreciated.\r\n<br><br>\r\nas far as politics, i think there are politics in every \r\norganization. there are just different reasons for it.\r\n<br><br>\r\nyou should talk to swinney, the job he just got in scruz is \r\nfor a nonprofit. i bet s5 will have lots of insight too. \r\n<br><br>\r\ni think working for a .org is the BEST way a person with \r\ntech skills can contribute them to society. you might even \r\nvolunteer yourself to nonprofits that don\'t even know they \r\nneed you yet. :)\r\n</p>',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3966,1085,'2001-06-13 03:13:33',0,'cyantist','<br><br>\r\nyeah, i understand completely.  where did you move to?  ',1,0,0,0,'202.77.253.245','en'),(3967,1093,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','check out the <a \r\nhref=\"http://www.nomoreprisons.org/front.htm\">prison \r\nmoritorium project</a>. good folks; i met them at the \r\nDPF <a \r\nhref=\"http://www.drugpolicy.org/conference/\">conference</a> a couple weeks ago. they\'ve also worked the \r\nevils of globalization into the prison \r\ndiscussion.<br><br>\r\nas far as having to play politics in the workplace: in my \r\nexperience, power games are everywhere. consider \r\nthat in the non-profit world, it\'s all about amassing \r\npolitical power, to make your voice the loudest. i have \r\nstories about this but i\'d rather not post them \r\npublically.<br><br>\r\ni encourage you to jump in, but do it because you care. \r\npolitics run thick in every sector.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3968,1093,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','it also depends on what kind of position you\'re after. \r\nmany of the not-as-established groups might not have \r\nfunding for geek jobs, relying on volunteers or one-time \r\npayments to consultants. it\'s possible to make your \r\nliving as a hired gun for non-profits, but then again, \r\nyou\'re not out there, reaching people, lobbying, talking to \r\nfreaked out parents, writing press releases, \r\netc.<br><br>what kind of work are you interested in? in \r\naddition to the issues you care about, you should \r\nconsider your skillset, and what skills you\'d like to \r\ndevelop.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3969,1093,'2001-06-13 03:39:20',0,'tomato','just remember you have to pay the SF RENT.',1,0,0,0,'209.86.4.61','en'),(3970,1093,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','sf rent is getting better. and moving away is always an \r\noption.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3971,1087,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','<p>this post was kind of an experiment for me.  it was \r\nbasically inspired by the song \\\"A Design For Life\\\" by the \r\nManic Street Preachers - it was a tangent I had while \r\nlistening to the song. The tangent kind of meshed with a \r\ndream i had which involved a girl who had scars all up her \r\narms like zebra stripes - her blood was like aloe vera sap \r\nand it healed people it came into contact with.</p>\r\n<p>i clicked \\\"art\\\".</p>',3,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(3972,1093,'2001-06-13 03:48:32',0,'cyantist','<br><br>\r\nugh. sf rent.  see, i can\\\'t volunteer at this point, because \r\ni have no desire to be homeless.   i\\\'m mostly interested in \r\ngay and lesbian rights, human rights, how technology \r\neffects the non-profit model, or many of the other groups i \r\nsupport and agree with.\r\n<br><br>\r\nmy skill set is strong, because i\\\'ve had close to 9 years of \r\nworking experience thus far.  i\\\'ve worked for many \r\nnon-profits to varrying degrees and have held many hats \r\nalong that time line.  i have a BIG heart and i am super \r\nmotivated with a fire in my belly that is so strong that i \r\ncan light anyone\\\'s fire.  i\\\'m a great motivator.  my \r\ntechnical skills are pretty well defined and if i don\\\'t know \r\nhow something works, i have the tools at hand to figure \r\nanything out.\r\n<br><br>\r\nwith all that said, this type of work suits me.  it didn\\\'t \r\nreally make sense to me until late the other night when i \r\nwanted to cry reading stories of people losing all their \r\ndignity in prison for petty crimes.  it made me so ill.  i \r\nwanted to do something.  anything.  sure, i can donate \r\nmoney, but i want to get involved.  steve, you are so right. \r\n i want to do this, simply because i care.  i care enough to \r\nnot get paid well and to put my heart into it.  i want to \r\nhelp make a difference.  my only problem is not really \r\nknowing where to start.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'202.77.253.245','en'),(3973,1093,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','more thoughts:<br>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>go to conferences! this is where you\'ll meet the \r\nmost people and learn about organizations doing work \r\nthat you might not have known about otherwise. you\'re \r\nmuch more likely to find your dream .org job this way, \r\nthan from digging through craig\'s list.<br>\r\n<li>get involved in media projects. learn skills related to \r\nthe media (like writing press releases). consider that \r\nthe government and the american corporate power \r\nstructure have a multi-billion dollar propaganda media \r\nempire at their disposal. groups like <a \r\nhref=\"http://www.alternet.org/\">alternet</a>, <a \r\nhref=\"http://www.mapinc.org/\">the media awareness \r\nproject</a>, and <a href=\"http://www.indymedia.org/\">the \r\nindependent media center</a> are working the other \r\nside of the PR angle. shifting public opinion through the \r\nmedia is how things change, for the better or \r\nworse.<br>\r\n<li>explore connections you wouldn\'t have considered. \r\nfor example, the anti-prison movement and the drug \r\npolicy reform movement work closely in coalition. find \r\ngroups that may have ideals in common with your \r\nsocial concerns, and find out how you can get \r\ninvolved.<br>\r\n</ul>\r\n',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3974,1093,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','you\\\'ll be able to pay the rent. employed activists live in \r\nsf, too. just don\\\'t expect to live large, unless you don\\\'t \r\nmind picking up a few moonlighting sysadmin or web \r\ncontracts here and there. you\\\'re in a good position \r\nbecause you have other skills. (personally, i\\\'m planning \r\nto do <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.thevoicefactory.com/\\\">voiceover</a> \r\non the side for commercials, because it pays well.)',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3975,1093,'2001-06-13 03:59:53',0,'cyantist','<br><br>i can\\\'t just walk out of my current place and i have \r\nfinancial obligations.  such is life.  however, i know that \r\nthe salary they can afford me will pay the bills.  i just \r\ncan\\\'t indulge in the lifestyle that working for .com and \r\n.net companies afforded me.  we\\\'re spoiled, you know?  i was \r\ntalking to a friend about this the other day and we \r\nconcluded that we\\\'ve all been living pretty absurdly \r\ndecandent lifestyles.  (all of us who could, that is)  \r\nsome of us have been selfish and negligent.  there\\\'s more to \r\nthis world than the snowglobes we trap ourselves in.  i\\\'ve \r\nbeen stupid myself financially and now i pay the price for \r\nit.<br><br>\r\nthus is life, no use sitting around feeling like shit about \r\na mistake.\r\n<br><br>\r\nit is easy to say, \\\"just move!\\\"  it isn\\\'t that easy, when \r\nyou have people in your life that you value and don\\\'t want \r\nto move away from.  when i moved here, i gave most of that \r\nup and i suffered greatly as a result.. but came out \r\nstronger with even more close friends and loved ones.  \r\nmoving here has eventually become fantastic.  yes, i may be \r\ndriven out of sf by the cost of living and that is the price \r\nyou have to pay for trying to live in such a glittery city \r\nas san francisco.<br><br>\r\nsigh.  for now, i\\\'m in asia and i should try to enjoy it \r\nwhile i can. ',1,0,0,0,'202.77.253.245','en'),(3976,1088,'2001-06-13 04:47:17',0,'s5 to darwin','i bet the person read your response but chose not to \r\nreply. regarding deviant cyber-communities, btw, my \r\nfriend is writing her phd dissertation on this same topic. \r\nthanks for reminding me of that discussion, i\\\'ll pass the \r\nlink along.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3977,1088,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','if you know php, you can do whatever you want to \r\nswinney.org. it\\\'s in the cvs tree on atari, which many of \r\nyou folks have accounts on. \r\n',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3978,1092,'2001-06-13 05:12:06',0,'Danielle','I didn\\\'t mean my poems to be derogatory. I have a lot of \r\nrespect for people who can do such hard manual labour. The \r\nthings I wrote about are things that happen at the \r\nconstruction site across the street from where I \r\nwork.<p>Some guys actually built a box about the height of \r\na mailbox, but twice the width, out of scrap wood, and they \r\nsit in it and hotbox themselves. Anyways, that is all. \r\nPeace.',1,0,0,0,'24.68.193.134','en'),(3979,1088,'2001-06-13 06:47:56',0,'cyantist','-- LE -- werd!',1,0,0,0,'202.77.253.245','en'),(3980,1027,'2001-06-13 07:04:11',0,'cyantist','<br><br>\r\nok, i\\\'m confused.  we can\\\'t live by everyone\\\'s utopia, can \r\nwe?  if we are \\\"forced\\\" to live by your lifestyle, what \r\ngood does that do us if we don\\\'t agree?  or are you saying, \r\nthat everyone gets a choice in the matter and we can all \r\nlive how we please?  that won\\\'t work either.  maybe on a \r\nsmall scale, but not a large one.  \r\n<br><br>\r\ni\\\'m not certain what really makes america so violent.  yes, \r\nhistory has taught us that it is in certain human\\\'s natures \r\nto be violent.  we fight because we believe that something \r\nis so true, that we will die by it.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\\\"are you prepared to die for your beliefs, or just to dye \r\nyour hair?\\\" - subhumans\r\n<br><br>\r\nwars have been faught for women, religion, land, oil, \r\ndrugs, this right and that right, and whatever else fancies \r\nthe person who can pull clout and speak louder than the \r\nrest.  whoever has the most propaganda seems to win.  \r\n<br><br>\r\n\\\"this is what a jew looks like, this is how you spot a jew\\\"\r\n\\\"this is what a drug dealer looks like, this is how you \r\nspot a drug dealer\\\"\r\n<br><br>\r\nbeware of people! people are power hungry and \r\nselfish.  \\\"fuck you, i got mine!\\\".  that\\\'s what leads to \r\nthis sort of behavior.  no one knows how to be selfless \r\nwhen needed.  if every person gave up a little selfishness, \r\nwe\\\'d all be in a better boat.  \r\n<br><br>\r\ni think that decius\\\' views are valid.  they are all good \r\nobservations.  i can\\\'t conclude the truth from either of \r\nyou, because without an argument based upon concrete fact, \r\nthere\\\'s really no telling what the key element is to a \r\nsolution if we can\\\'t really pinpoint a problem.\r\n<br><br>\r\ni feel at a loss most of the time in situaions like this, \r\nbecause i feel powerless to change anything.  i can only \r\nhelp make my world a peaceful place and anyone in close \r\nproximity, by treating others well and giving respect and \r\nhoping for the same in return.  what can i do?  what can we \r\nall do?  where do you start?  can you?  \r\n',1,0,0,0,'202.77.253.245','en'),(3981,1075,'2001-06-13 07:25:23',0,'gracie','oh goodness no, i\\\'m not mocking you splendid people one bit.  \r\ni really think you and this egg person are just so eloquent \r\nand witty.  even your grand comments make me chuckle, *oh \r\nhoho hee hee* so, really, keep up the good work, you guys, \r\neven tho i really don\\\'t have a clue what you all are talking \r\nabout.  it all just sounds so delightful!\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(3982,1088,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://saturn5.com/swinney/dev/swinney.org\\\"><fo\r\nnt size=\\\"+1\\\"><B>oh mommy mommy, can i have \r\none?!</FONT></B></a>',2,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3983,1095,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Moon Moll','<p>I wish my home looked like that.</p>',1,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(3984,1027,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','one person\\\'s utopia is another\\\'s hell.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3985,1027,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','<p>\r\nAmerica is meant to be a Constitutional Republic.  if you don\\\'t like that system you can leave.  if you try to alter it, and succeed enough, i will fight you.  i do not have a problem using force, if you do, you will lose.  that is the attitude many of us have.  Utopia?  no.  i am not a utopian, i don\\\'t believe the concept is realistic.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nwars are fought over population pressure, sometimes you have to dig deep to understand that, but it\\\'s always there.  all the other crap is just motivation for the little people or kill-enabling.  i\\\'d like to say decius\\\' observations are good, but they are not.  i see little in those words which squares with what i\\\'ve seen, or any of the research i\\\'ve done over the years.  no soldier i know would agree, no general i\\\'ve met, no mercenary would even agree.  fanciful ideas, no matter how nice to contemplate, will not describe whence comes violence.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\ni have some ideas for you.  maybe i will even share them someday.\r\n</p>',1,0,0,0,'207.205.216.10','en'),(3986,1090,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','mom. all my friends think you are a porn fiend now. stop \r\nembarassing me in front of my friends!',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3987,1091,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i lived in savannah georgia. a city where the air is so \r\nthick with unseen weirdness that you feel like you could \r\nreach out and grab it. it is like a movie set.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3988,1027,'2001-06-13 11:01:57',0,'tomato','dude, what\\\'s yer email?<p>\r\n\r\nwas irag about population?  waws yugoslavia (1993 we \r\nbomed them first) about population?',5,0,0,0,'209.86.0.164','en'),(3989,1027,'2001-06-13 11:03:02',0,'tomatox2','dude, what\\\'s yer email?<p>\r\n\r\nwas irag about population?  was yugoslavia (1993 we \r\nbombed them first) about population?',6,0,0,0,'209.86.0.164','en'),(3990,1091,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','I lived down South, also, and I agree- there was so much \r\nuniqueness/strangeness in the air that it was almost \r\ntangible.  In alot of ways, living there can\\\'t compare to \r\nmy newer, urban home... but in alot of ways, it far \r\nsurpasses it, at least as far as imagery and memory go.',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(3991,1092,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','My better half works\r\non dirty construction site\r\ncat calls?  looks? never. ',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(3992,1090,'2001-06-13 12:26:26',0,'auntie','i am not a porn fiend.  i just like to make nekkid sims.  \r\nit is hard to make nekkid sims if you don\\\'t have the right \r\npictures to work with.  i certainly wouldn\\\'t want to make a \r\nnekkid sim that looked like ME.<br><br>\r\n\r\nif it makes you feel better, i spent an equal amount of \r\ntime at gapkids.com getting pictures of clothes to make for \r\nmy sim kids.<br><br>\r\n\r\n<img \r\nsrc=\\\"http://www.auntie.com/simstuff/B009fcchdmed_auntieblueg\r\napdress.bmp\\\"><br><br>\r\n\r\nPretty good, huh?',1,0,0,0,'24.162.119.106','en'),(3993,1081,'2001-06-13 12:37:39',0,'s5 to egg','i have <a \r\nhref=\"http://saturn5.diaryland.com/010522_27.html\">issues</a> with the word \"issues\".',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(3994,1092,'2001-06-13 13:13:06',0,'zb','<p>\r\n<font face=\\\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\\\">\r\nRedneck Haiku:<br>\r\nNaked in repose<br>\r\nSilvery silhouette girls<br>\r\nAdorn my mudflaps<br>\r\n<p>',0,0,0,0,'64.123.8.136','en'),(3995,1096,'2001-06-13 13:17:21',0,'jo to peter','here\\\'s what i think:<BR>\r\n<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.rhodamine.org/postcards.htm\\\">http://www.rho\r\ndamine.org/postcards.htm</a><BR>\r\n<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://standing.ontheoutside.com/postcards/\\\">http://st\r\nanding.ontheoutside.com/postcards</a><BR>\r\nwe should exchange postcards.',1,0,0,0,'172.148.153.244','en'),(3996,1090,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Veer Moll','<p>I really liked the porno thing.</p>\r\n<p>I am all: wait. She\\\'s a mom. Moms? Porno? Moms and \r\nporno? Is that...? Can that...?</p>\r\n<p>I suppose, statistically, it is a possibility, but...</p>\r\n<p>I have a mom, does...? What do moms do for fun?</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(3997,1096,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'peter to jo:','Definitely; will do.  lately i\\\'ve become somewhat of a \r\nphilatellic junkie for some reason. I guess it all started \r\nwhen I found a postcard from Thailand (meant for my \r\napartment\\\'s former tennant) in my mailbox and thought the \r\nstamps were pretty; it also had a pretty generic good-luck \r\nmessage that was endearing.  its also this tactile urge to \r\nput pen to card, lick a stamp, etc.  So, keep an eye out in \r\nthe mail.',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(3998,1081,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to s5','<p>irony, my friend.</p>\r\n<p>do I take myself seriously in a teeny bopper tank \r\ntop?</p>',0,0,0,0,'216.175.99.139','en'),(3999,1093,'2001-06-13 14:43:06',0,'stella','Cyantist - <P>One year ago, I lived in Berkeley, worked for \r\na technology, played the game. I had a fairly extravagent \r\nlifestyle. Luckily for me, they laid me off. Before that \r\nhappened, I had been thinking seriously of making some \r\nchanges, to make my life work something that I gave a damn \r\nabout. When I was canned, I left the industry. Now, I\\\'m back \r\nin school studying to be a teacher. I live in NY and am \r\ngoing to be teaching in inner city schools (if I get the \r\nFellowship.. PLEASE let me get the fellowship!) as of \r\n(hopefully) next January. I am flat busted, as compared to \r\nwhere I was last year, but my life is so much more FULL that \r\nit was then. I will have the opportunity to try and \r\nsee if I can make a difference in an area that I feel \r\nincredibly passionate about: Education. </P> <P>\r\nMoney, while a very nice thing to have, isn\\\'t stablity. It \r\ncan only help make life more comfortable.  Humans can adjust \r\nto any level of discomfort and any situation given the \r\ndesire and the courage. Think about it. </P> <P>\r\ns5 - I think you and I are long lost twins. </P>',0,0,0,0,'168.100.203.247','en'),(4000,1090,'2001-06-13 15:00:53',0,'jo','<a href=\\\"http://pondgoddess.diaryland.com\\\">mine</a> throws \r\nrocks.<BR>\r\nno, really. there are literally thousands of rocks in this \r\nlittle field next to their ranch house and my mom really \r\nlikes the field and wants grass and flowers to grow there \r\nagain. so earlier in the spring, she made the goal to throw \r\na hundred rocks a day down the cliffside and start clearing \r\nout the field.<BR>\r\nmy mom is my hero.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(4001,1090,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>Moms (at least hopefully) like sex, else they wouldn\\\'t be\r\nmoms.  Nothing so divinely wonderful as the obscene whisper\r\nof a lusty sex drive.</p>\r\n<p>I\\\'m at home today instead of being at work because I ate\r\nat Taco Cabana last night.  \\\'Nuff said.</p>',1,0,0,0,'209.163.146.106','en'),(4002,1085,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','you should make the indigo into an espresso machine: <a\r\nhref=\\\"http://www.nk-exa.co.jp/houdini/out/sgi_cafe.jpg\\\">like\r\nthis</a>',1,0,0,0,'209.163.146.106','en'),(4003,1083,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','cubist squahes bug<br>\r\nred and squishy on his sole<br>\r\nin scraping is art<br>\r\n<p>;-)</p>',1,0,0,0,'209.163.146.106','en'),(4004,1079,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','Do the garage sale!  You meet all kinds of cool people.  But\r\nthen ours was behind 1/2 price so maybe our sample set was\r\nskewed.',1,0,0,0,'209.163.146.106','en'),(4005,1087,'2001-06-13 16:00:13',0,'kat','<p>blood that heals.</p>\r\n<p>now that would be something. at one point in my life i \r\nstarted cutting myself to escape from the pain. the \r\nphysical was the only tangible thing left i could grasp. a \r\nway to overcome the mental anguish. a sad attempt to cry \r\nfor help. a frightening way too challenge oneself. how deep \r\ncould i go. and still hang on. fourteen on the outside. \r\nancient turmoil on the inside. if only the blood could have \r\nhealed me.</p>',1,0,0,0,'12.64.92.62','en'),(4006,1085,'2001-06-13 17:37:13',0,'cyantist','-- oh my that is so core.  that fucking rocks.',1,0,0,0,'203.184.249.130','en'),(4007,1092,'2001-06-13 18:37:00',0,'Danielle','Multimedia Student Haiku\r\n\r\nGo Pick Some Pantones\r\nStretch that vector all the way\r\nAnimate that Gif\r\n',1,0,0,0,'207.34.94.238','en'),(4008,1092,'2001-06-13 18:37:42',0,'Danielle','Or even:<P>\r\n\r\nMultimedia Student Haiku<P>\r\n\r\nGo Pick Some Pantones<P>\r\nStretch that vector all the way<P>\r\nAnimate that Gif<P>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'207.34.94.238','en'),(4009,1098,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>yes it is true. I have bought tortillas there and sat\r\ndipping in them in hot sauce, knowing that any further\r\nventures on the menu are disasterous.  the food there is\r\nrotten.  i have barfed at least twice.  i never ate there\r\nagain after the second time save tortillas.</P>',4,0,0,0,'64.51.232.105','en'),(4010,1100,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>we used to have \\\"kitty tv\\\" at my old house that i \r\nshared with three girls and 2 cats.</p>\r\n<p>it\\\'s birds and fish and stuff. the cats watch it! they \r\njump at it! i\\\'d love to read a paper on kitty tv perception. \r\nanyone?</p>',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(4011,1095,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to kat','<p>have you ever seen francesca woodman\\\'s \\\"on \r\nbeing an angel\\\" series?</p>\r\n<p>dude im so into this picture.</p>',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(4012,1098,'2001-06-13 20:30:33',0,'jo','they\\\'re open late-ish in houston. decent drunk food.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(4013,1099,'2001-06-13 20:34:09',0,'jo','i <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://standing.ontheoutside.com/nothere/3/\\\">built a \r\nfort</a> this winter. friends came over, we ate junk food \r\nand watched movies, we stayed up all night talking.<BR>\r\n<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://standing.ontheoutside.com/pictures/2001/fort_we\r\nekend/\\\">elly was there</a>; she and mandy and puppy passing \r\nthrough at the end of a long roadtrip, florida to texas.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(4014,1092,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','actually, i read your haikus to the guys at work.  the BEST response i got was: \\\"is that some kinda nigger shit?\\\"  mostly i don\\\'t think anyone understood the concept of a haiku, even when i explained it.  but i had fun trying.  i think i did.',2,0,0,0,'207.205.216.28','en'),(4015,1085,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','cyan:  8 blocks down from where i live now.  but the goddamn deposite and all...mebbe i should rob and bank.',1,0,0,0,'207.205.216.28','en'),(4016,1090,'2001-06-13 21:12:19',0,'auntie','moms are people who happen to have had children.  that\\\'s \r\nall.  when i think of myself as an age, i start at 23 and \r\nthen realize with a start that i am actually almost 48. or \r\nmaybe i am 49, i can\\\'t remember anymore, i was born on \r\noctober 24, 1953 at 8:35 am in Tampa, Fl. maybe an \r\nastrology expert could tell me if that means i will win the \r\nlottery any time soon...<br><br>\r