. is it \r\nmeant to be a list of things bad americans think?',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4032,1103,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','the last line is \\\"i guess this makes me a bad american\\\".',3,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(4033,1099,'2001-06-14 05:59:28',0,'jo','i would love a tshirt that had a flagpole on it and a flag \r\nmade of pants and written on the pants: \\\"all pants all the \r\ntime.\\\"',1,0,0,0,'172.136.187.135','en'),(4034,1103,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','yeah. but i don\\\'t understand. maybe my mental faculties are \r\nfailing. i don\\\'t understand anything about this post. i \r\ndon\\\'t understand anything!',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4035,1103,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','you don\\\'t understand my post?<br>\r\n<br>oh, i\\\'m sorry.',4,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(4036,1098,'2001-06-14 06:23:36',0,'kd.o.g.','i like the black bean tacos.  changos rules in the \r\nfreshness category.  Crazy Maria\\\'s Taco Express is \r\nexcellent too.  but both of these lose in the 24 hour \r\navailability column.  star(seeds) bridges the gap between \r\nlate hours and tasty, fulfilling drunk food nicely.  ',2,0,0,0,'66.68.78.183','en'),(4037,1103,'2001-06-14 06:25:08',0,'jp','This looks like it\\\'s some kind of thing put together by a\r\nright-winger type to get all his Rush Limbaugh listening\r\nbuddies all excited and riled up over \\\"liberals\\\" and\r\n\\\"political correctness\\\". I\\\'ve dealt with that kind in other\r\nareas. Obnoxious.<BR>\r\nAny few valid points it kind of makes is negated by the\r\nobviously ignorant redneck attitude where it comes from.<BR>\r\nThe buddhist ideal would be to not hate anyone, since by\r\ndoing that you\\\'ve already brought suffering to yourself and\r\nmore likely to bring suffering to others. One way of looking\r\nat is to see anger or hatred itself as the enemy, not any\r\nperson or group. You can still deal with whatever needs to\r\nbe dealt with, but without losing your peace of mind.',0,0,0,0,'24.0.133.128','en'),(4038,1103,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','no seriously, i just can\\\'t get what point badamerican.txt \r\nis trying to make! as a consequence i don\\\'t know what \r\nyou\\\'re reacting to and can\\\'t understand anything. seriously \r\ni just have no clue what\\\'s going on here at all. \r\nsuggestions welcome',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4039,1103,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i think i just need more context',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4040,1103,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','elly, don\\\'t get so excited!  i have no more context than \r\nyou.  my post is about my reaction to the statements \r\ncontained in the document.  that is all.<br>',3,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(4041,1103,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<br><br>badamerican is a summary of the \\\"every man \r\nfor himself\\\" belief system. note the recurring theme of \r\n\\\"i\\\'m doing X my own way, by myself, and damn you for \r\nsuggesting otherwise.\\\" you\\\'ll hear these people \r\nscreaming loudly for the next couple decades, as they \r\nare slowly obsoleted.<br><br>\r\nunfortunately, many people associate a return to \r\ntribalism with an abandonment or disrespect of their \r\nright to autonomy. time will show that the two are not \r\nmutually exclusive (in fact, they must coexist). in the \r\nmeantime, the badamerican diatribe is a reaction to \r\nthis notion.<br><br>\r\nthe name badamerican was chosen to be ironic, as the \r\nauthor believes his viewpoint to be \\\"more american\\\", \r\nthan the emerging trend of social awareness in this \r\ncountry.<br>',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4042,1103,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i\\\'m overexcited!',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4043,1103,'2001-06-14 06:54:55',0,'jp','le: it\\\'s all about politics. Some right-wing dude. Nothing\r\nmore I believe.<BR>\r\nThe \\\"bad american\\\" thing probably comes from\r\nself-consciousness over feeling like an ignorant\r\nconservative -- the uncultured, uneducated \\\"ugly american\\\".\r\nPlus conservatives in the south and midwest tend to view\r\nEurope (and California) as being \\\"liberal\\\", \\\"socialist\\\",\r\n\\\"wacko\\\", etc.<BR>\r\nYou hear the \\\"Enforce laws that already exist\\\" line from the\r\npro-gun people arguing against any new gun laws. Same with\r\nthe not seeing the constitution as being open to\r\ninterpretation, i.e. the 2nd ammendment for right to bear\r\narms.\r\n<I>\\\"I will not conform or compromise just to keep from\r\nhurting somebody\\\'s feelings.\\\", \\\"I think that being a student\r\ndoesn\\\'t give you any more enlightenment than working at\r\nBlockbuster or Jack-in-the-Box.\\\"</I><BR>\r\nI guess that makes him a flaming ignorant A-hole then... but\r\nproud of it though. Notice the slavery line too? Real\r\nnice.<BR>\r\nThe whole thing is some guy going, \\\"Yup, I am ahmerican. I\r\neat beef and have *real* sex with my wife that I keep\r\nbarefoot in the kitchen. She\\\'s not one of those femi-nazis.\r\nAhmericuh -- number one, don\\\'t forget it. Them blacks\r\nweren\\\'t all slaves, jus complainin that\\\'s all. If you don\\\'t\r\nlike americuh get out, and speak english if you can sneak in\r\nanyway..\\\" It\\\'s a list of things that some people can agree\r\nwith somewhat though.<BR>\r\nThat\\\'s my take anyway. What do you make of it?<BR>',0,0,0,0,'24.0.133.128','en'),(4044,1103,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i think i figured out it\'s a conservative libertarian. i \r\nwas just having a literal moment, i couldn\'t see the forest \r\nfor the trees. <!-- my north node is in libra, that\'s why i do \r\nthat. i\'d explain what that means but i hate all tauruses \r\nso i\'m trying to keep them in the dark. heh! -->',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4045,1101,'2001-06-14 07:15:34',0,'rusty','yummy, la rondalla...',4,0,0,0,'206.170.6.39','en'),(4046,1104,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i hear that moulin rouge was full of dancing dwarves.',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4047,1103,'2001-06-14 07:25:06',0,'jp','Could that moment be attributed to Merc... No, I won\\\'t say\r\nit.<BR>\r\nBTW, I looked up my chart and realized that it has Merc R.\r\nDoes that mean I\\\'m totally screwed or something? S5 do you\r\nknow about that?',0,0,0,0,'24.0.133.128','en'),(4048,1099,'2001-06-14 07:25:55',0,'rusty','I would guess darwin was referring to:\r\n<p>\r\n\\\"there comes a time when one has digested boys. when one \r\nhas learned each boy\\\'s two wishes in life, or each boy\\\'s 10 \r\nbig ideas, and learned the subtle way those simplified \r\nconstructions of identity play themselves predictably out \r\nin every slight gesture or system of behavoir, and learns \r\nthat she will be bored with men until she dies.\\\"\r\n<p>\r\nWhich could be offensive, if it wasn\\\'t so true...\r\n<p>\r\nBut the same could be said of girls...\r\n<p>\r\nAnd of course a boy or a girl who gets in this mind frame, \r\nalways gets back out of it, and then back into it...  We\\\'re \r\nall too simple, and yet too complex, and we love to roam \r\naround in little circles...\r\n<p>\r\nAnd then there are those beings who don\\\'t even have 2 \r\nwishes or 10 ideas that ever stay the same... or make any \r\nsense... lost in seas of confusion...  And then there are \r\nthose who just shout their\\\'s loud enough that people think \r\nthey must be brilliant...  but back to the basics:\r\n<p>\r\n\\\"Art is either plagiarism or revolution.\\\"<br>\r\n-- Paul Gauguin\r\n<p>\r\nI think that can go for most ideas, actions, thoughts, and \r\nso on...  I haven\\\'t seen a revolution in a while, but \r\nthere\\\'s enough variety out there to avoid boredom when you \r\nwant to...',4,0,0,0,'206.170.6.39','en'),(4049,1103,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','it\\\'s not a bad thing. email me your info and i\\\'ll give you \r\nmy take.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4050,1102,'2001-06-14 07:32:14',0,'rusty','good luck, and remember to pave the path with breadcrumbs, \r\nbecause eventually you\\\'ll run somewhere where all that \r\nstuff 