13.</p>',0,0,0,0,'209.86.7.95','en'),(4057,1104,'2001-06-14 08:18:44',0,'kat','yea. drunk dancing dwarves with lisps even.',2,0,0,0,'12.64.24.247','en'),(4058,1090,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','pornography is <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.lectlaw.com/files/sex03.htm\\\">illegal in \r\nthe state of utah</a>.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4059,1103,'2001-06-14 08:26:04',0,'jp','Hmmm...<BR>\r\nThe \\\"badamerican.txt\\\" is slightly different than the Carlin \r\none.\r\nLooks like they right-wing\\\'ed it up. Especially the slave \r\nline.\r\nI saw Carlin\\\'s act a couple of years ago and it was kind of \r\nfunny but he is very bitter for some reason.  Much better \r\nwhen he was the bad-word guy.<BR>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'24.0.133.128','en'),(4060,1103,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','the inevitable progression of the aging hippy: \\\"fuck free \r\nlove, i\\\'m busy clipping coupons\\\"',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4061,1102,'2001-06-14 09:07:18',0,'cyantist','-- interesting.  ',1,0,0,0,'202.77.253.245','en'),(4062,1102,'2001-06-14 09:10:23',0,'cyantist','<br><br>no kidding oof, where does such a place exist?  you \r\ncould sell this secret you know.  when you run away, you are \r\nlike the pied piper singing a tune so sweet that your \r\nproblems follow you in one way or another.  good luck, or \r\nperhaps this isn\\\'t about you and you are making an \r\nobservation.  like i said, intersting.',1,0,0,0,'202.77.253.245','en'),(4063,1099,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Thoon Moll','<p>It is all too foolish. I don\\\'t believe in boys. Or \r\ngirls.</p>\r\n<p>Mythology. I like forts and tunnels.</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(4064,1102,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<br><br>4 out of 5 dentists agree: transcendence fights 50% \r\n<b>more</b> cavities than escapism.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4065,1103,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Red Moll','<p>Laws are foolish!</p>',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(4066,1102,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','this peaceful place you seek is within yourself. within the \r\nstamen of a lilly. seek it, smell it, let it be as it is.',1,0,0,0,'64.81.65.205','en'),(4067,1099,'2001-06-14 10:05:42',0,'darwin to le','<p>Yes, because as we all know, it is words that have \r\npower, not the context in which they are used. The context \r\nof the word \\\"nigger-jew\\\", in this case, being a derogatory \r\nterm <u>directed at the person using it</u>. He should be \r\nashamed.</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n',4,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(4068,1099,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p>darwin, you smart ass.\r\n<br><br>\r\ndon\'t you think the connotation and history of a word can \r\nbe upsetting regardless of its intent? i think that it\'s \r\nsilly to use words that could upset or be misunderstood, \r\nwhen there are so many other words out there. \r\n<br><br>\r\n\"nigger\" is a good example of a word that causes people\'s \r\neyebrows to raise and stomachs to churn on sight. i\'m not \r\ntelling anyone what to say or think, but it seems like if \r\nyou don\'t gotta use it, you may as well not, and avoid the \r\npossibility of upset.\r\n<br><br>\r\ndave (hi dave) has used the word \"nigger\" and the \r\nphrase \"nigger jew\" an inordinant amount of times recently. \r\nit freaks me out. the connotation and history \r\nreally bothers me. i\'m a sensitive person, i guess? ...but \r\ni see those words and i feel sick in the same ways that i \r\nfelt sick during the school field trips to concentration camps \r\nthat i had to go on over and over during my childhood in \r\ngermany. it just gets me in the gut.  \r\n<br><br>\r\nsorry to bring up hitler and everything.\r\n</p>',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4069,1102,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>\r\nfear:regret:denial:self-\r\ndoubt:dishonesty:insincerity:anxiety:distrust:inconsistency:\r\nselfishness:impotence:the \r\ncold:expectation:uncertainty:depression:the \r\nquestions:calculation:rejection: \r\npessimism:negativity:distraction: \r\ninsensitivity:bitterness:tension: \r\nloneliness:frustration:discontent:self-\r\nobsession:impatience:faithlessness:immorality:dissatisfactio\r\nn:impatience:embarrassment:hopelessness:dejection:cruelty:de\r\nvastation:hurt:emptiness:anger\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\n<pre>\r\n#!/usr/bin/perl\r\n\r\nwhile(<>){ \r\n@array=split(/:/,$_);\r\n\r\n# the foreach even makes it pseudo-random!\r\nforeach $thing (@array){\r\nprint(\"i\'m going to run away from $thing. \" );\r\n }\r\n}\r\n</pre>\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nAs the Pharcyde <a \r\nhref=\"http://www.ohhla.com/anonymous/pharcyde/labcabin/runni\r\nn.phr.txt\">wrote</a>: <a \r\nhref=\"http://saturn5.com/darwin/mp3/Pharcyde-\r\nRunning_Away.mp3\">You can\'t keep running away.</a></p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n\r\n',4,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(4070,1099,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<br><br>penalty points for playing the hitler card.<br>\r\n<h1>OFFSIDES</h1>',6,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4071,1104,'2001-06-14 12:56:09',0,'bmg','<p>I did manage to hold onto the entire autechre and aphex \r\ntwin collection. Here is what I <a href=\'http://www.lepard.org/mp3s/\' target=new>lost</a></p>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.78.183','en'),(4072,1104,'2001-06-14 13:27:16',0,'zb','  <p><font face=\\\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\\\">\r\nOuch.<br>Did you really lose all of that?!<br>\r\n    Sucks...</font><br></p>',0,0,0,0,'64.123.8.22','en'),(4073,1104,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>bmg, send me an email (click on my email in my posts) \r\nand perhaps I can help you.</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin',1,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(4074,1104,'2001-06-14 13:52:58',0,'puppy','hey bmg: maybe you should find chris d. from ibooks to see\nif he still has the old mp3 files... that list you have\nlooked mighty familiar :) damn! i miss that place sometimes.\ncall me. disc golf this weekend?',1,0,0,0,'192.35.232.99','en'),(4075,1103,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','s5, marry me',1,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(4076,1099,'2001-06-14 14:36:58',0,'chaya','so um.  not to detract from the hitler or anything, but.  \r\negg.  i 