 we might \r\nfeel about restraint and its relationship to sex drive/sexual \r\npleasure. </p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(4098,1101,'2001-06-14 19:03:00',0,'jo to zb','my friend sara has this joke that she uses to test if \r\npeople are cool. this first is: <BR>\r\nwhat\\\'s black and white and has a dirty word in its name?<BR>\r\nsister mary fuckface.<BR>\r\nbut her second joke, if they pass the first test, is the \r\npirate movie one.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(4099,1108,'2001-06-14 19:25:28',0,'pkf','<p>some girls use a towel rather than a few kleenex...</p>',0,0,0,0,'216.171.37.54','en'),(4100,1108,'2001-06-14 19:41:30',0,'kat','i dont think even if the glow exists for men that it would \r\nbe the same for women. we just dont operate on the same \r\nwavelength. masturbating only increases my desire. like \r\nstoring power in a battery. it leaves me feeling magnetic. \r\nits almost as if i gain the ability to see things more \r\nclearly...everything else glows. i have x-ray vision. sex \r\nis different. ive only had one partner that left me feeling \r\nthat way. usually i just feel quietly drained and content \r\nafterwards. i think too much, or try to hard i guess. i \r\nwonder if what made the difference with my one lover is \r\nthat we spent months having cyber oriented sex sessions \r\nbefore we actually met. spending hours and hours exploring \r\nyour own body and then trying to describe every nuance of \r\nit lead me to a pretty amazing mental state.',1,0,0,0,'12.64.62.206','en'),(4101,1108,'2001-06-14 19:43:48',0,'SIC','<p>that section shuold read:<br>\r\n&lt;egg&gt;girls dont lose chi masturbating like boys do\r\n&lt;pie&gt;they don\\\'t use so many kleenex, either\r\n',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(4102,1098,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','oh gawd. taco cabana. i remember filling up on burritos \r\nthere before going to a co-op party (French House, i think) \r\nand then i remember the puke and the flying shits, and \r\nthat\\\'s all.  stay away from taco cabana.',3,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(4103,1105,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','i enjoyed that entry a lot K^2',1,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(4104,1108,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','so, what kind of glow do you have when you\\\'re not getting \r\nany dip, but you\\\'re jacking off every other day? isn\\\'t that \r\na kind of celibacy?',3,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(4105,1099,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','to le:  you are easy to freak out.  the word has connotations that are disturbing, my roomate matt and i are both vehemently opposed to racism have to deal with racists every day at work.  We hear the word \\\'nigger\\\' over and over.   some of the people at work are Klan members.  every day i have to hear how my people, the Jews, are the cause of everything bad in the world.  how, in league with the blacks, we seek to destroy the white race.  if you think it\\\'s horrible to see that word here, then imagine how it is for us.  i mention it alot because that word burns in my mind every day when i come home from work.  and if you think visiting a concentration camp\\\'s ruins are terrible, try being raised on stories of the camps.  my family numbers three survivors and i don\\\'t even know how many dead at Dachau.  i will never be able to forget the stories.  ',4,0,0,0,'207.205.216.56','en'),(4106,1102,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','hmmm...you want to borrow my pistol?',2,0,0,0,'207.205.216.56','en'),(4107,1103,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','i know i should probably have stayed out of this one, but...i think i agree totally with many of those statements, i agree partially with many more, and completely disagree with the rest.  it sounds alot like this asshole on the radio out here, Jim Quinn.  as usual i find myself wondering, if i\\\'m not a centrist, but certainly not a proper rightist, and leftism makes me vomit; what do i get to be?',3,0,0,0,'207.205.216.56','en'),(4108,1108,'2001-06-14 21:06:33',0,'cait','<p>Personally, I think it\\\'s ridiculous to assume that female \r\nand male sexuality is even remotely similar. I know that I \r\nam tired of living in a place where everyone views female \r\nsexuality through this weird historic patriarchal lens.',0,0,0,0,'63.77.235.136','en'),(4109,1106,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','people often identify with their wounds because they \r\nhave no other way to define themselves. same goes for \r\nthe guy in the lexus - it\\\'s just a different kind of wound.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4110,1108,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to adamajah','<p>well, the whole idea is that instead of blowing your wad \r\nand expelling your body of that energy, that you contain it \r\nin your body and regenerate it into some other activity/\r\nexpulsion/purpose. and that if you can contain it, rather \r\nthan expel it, you will have this overall projection of power \r\nand well-being. the french call the orgasm a \\\"petit mort\\\" or \r\n\\\"little death\\\", signifying that when you come, you expend so \r\nmuch energy that you die just a little.</p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(4111,1092,'2001-06-14 21:51:55',0,'kat','truck driver haiku</p>\r\n<p>eighteen wheels singing\r\nlonely road keeps moving by<br>\r\ntruckstop lights shine bright</p>',4,0,0,0,'12.64.61.42','en'),(4112,1092,'2001-06-14 21:52:48',0,'kat','<p>truck driver haiku</p>\r\n<p>eighteen wheels singing<br>\r\nlonely road keeps moving by<br>\r\ntruckstop lights shine bright</p>',4,0,0,0,'12.64.61.42','en'),(4113,1092,'2001-06-14 21:53:28',0,'kat','*duh*',6,0,0,0,'12.64.61.42','en'),(4114,1108,'2001-06-14 21:58:35',0,'a link','to <a href=\\\"http://saturn5.diaryland.com/010614_33.html\\\">s5\\\'s \r\nrecollection of our conversation.</a>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(4115,1108,'2001-06-14 22:05:16',0,'kat','what of wet dreams? sometimes that cant be avoided. my \r\nfriend has them when he goes without masturbating/sex. its \r\nthe body\\\'s own way of release [no ejaculation can lead to \r\nserious prostate problems]. ive even had a few myself. \r\nwaking up in mid-o is a bit disorienting. ',4,0,0,0,'12.64.61.42','en'),(4116,1108,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to cait','<p>[IF THIS ISNT LULU] is it really that different? the \r\nargument is a double-edged sword. one one hand, we dont want \r\nmale authorship trumping our understanding of our own \r\nexperience, but on the other hand, we dont want female orgasm \r\nobscured to mystique. There are pop psychologists like Dr \r\nRuth who have argued that female orgasm is purely \r\npsychological/emotional, which if youve ever had an orgasm \r\nyou know is DEEPLY untrue.</p>\r\n<p>speaking from a purely anatomical position, the penis and \r\nthe clitoris are made of the same tissue, its just that the \r\nclit has twice the amount of nerve endings.oooooweeee. but \r\nagain, we dont drop a load. which might make a difference.</\r\np>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(4117,1108,'2001-06-14 23:01:37',0,'bmg','<p>the dropping of the load isnt the fun part... i mean \r\nsure, any release has it pleasure - even taking the kids to \r\nthe pool for some diving lessons has its pleasure...</p>',1,0,0,0,'66.68.78.183','en'),(4118,1099,'2001-06-14 23:14:27',0,'jp','incitor: It really sucks that you have to work with people \r\nlike that. Have you considered a different field of work, \r\nor at least a different workplace? That\\\'s flat-out abusive \r\nwhat you have to deal with. I couldn\\\'t tolerate it. I \r\nwouldn\\\'t want to at least. I sometimes complain about \r\nfellow co-workers but it\\\'s totally trivial compared to what \r\nyou\\\'re talking about.<BR>\r\nAs far as the \\\"N word\\\", used with a certain intent it\\\'s \r\nprobably the most compactly vile word in the english \r\nlanguage symbolizing centuries of ignorance, evil and \r\ninjustice. Just saying or using the word itself isn\\\'t \r\nnecessarily \\\"bad\\\", but, considering the \\\"buttons\\\" that it \r\ncan press, you\\\'re really playing with fire if you don\\\'t \r\nmake clear the context or intent. Context and intent \r\ndetermines everything. In this case, I think anyone here \r\nwould understand what you mean -- you deal with racism and \r\nyou\\\'re just describing what you\\\'re hearing.',0,0,0,0,'63.172.123.3','en'),(4119,1108,'2001-06-14 23:22:57',0,'polly','hi there egg, in regards to your celibate glow \r\ncomment....i\\\'ve gotta say, women do obtain a celibate glow \r\nof some kind. i\\\'ve seen it happen.  they begin to turn a \r\nlight shade of purple as a slight glow of gold light \r\npulsates around their forehead. and as the \\\"glow\\\" continues \r\nto grow, their veins in the neck and forehead begin to \r\nprotrude and pulsate as well.  it is a magnificent sight if \r\ni do say so myself.  i must confess, dear friend, i have \r\nhad the celibate glow for about ten years now and just \r\ncan\\\'t seem to control the mad rush of boys falling over me \r\nand wanting to roll around with me in the haystacks over by \r\nmy auntie ruby\\\'s barn.  pure joy shimmys down my spine \r\nwhenever i see a boy sprinting across the wheat field after \r\nme with a big woody in his underroos.<br>\r\nmy dear dear girl, women have the glow...i have the glow, \r\nand boy oh boy DO i Love it!  i\\\'ve got control.  that\\\'s \r\nwhat the glow is my friend, besides it being a very big \r\nthrobbing headache, and a ridiculous shine on your \r\nforehead, it\\\'s a matter of control...I HAVE THE \r\nPOWER...HAHAHAHAHAHA.  all the girls now, laugh out loud \r\nwith me...HAHAHAHAHAHAHA!<br>\r\n<p>beef jerky time</P> ',0,0,0,0,'216.244.30.37','en'),(4120,1108,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','i think the thing about seth\\\'s friend is that he can orgasm, \r\nbut he doesnt drop the load. which means he retains the load-\r\nenergy but gets to have all the fun, and still be the most \r\ndesirable creature ever.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(4121,1108,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mastur Moll','<p>I\\\'ve had a lot of people tell me different variations of \r\nthis, about how holding back can give you extra energy, or \r\nimprove your \\\'chi\\\' and whatnot.</p>\r\n<p>I think it sort of makes sense -- I mean, it\\\'s \r\n<i>repression</i>. Wanking is normal. It\\\'s a drive (or part \r\nof a drive). If you shut that out, it will try to make its \r\nway to the surface in different ways and will probably be \r\nsublimated into something (hopefully) more constructive.</p>\r\n<p>Personally, I like to avoid repression of any kind, even \r\nif it\\\'s self-imposed. But I don\\\'t know. I\\\'ve heard so many \r\ngood things about this...</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(4122,1099,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','jp:  i appreciate your comment.  yes, i\\\'m trying like hell to get away from this job.  currently my business partner and i are attempting to finance our business, while waiting we are begining to teach an anti-rape course at the local crisis center.  as for the *sigh* \\\'n-word\\\', to be honest, i am accused of being racist everywhere but AT work.  i\\\'m a skinhead, people who know little of skinheads naturally assume i am a nazi.  this amuses me.  it has also led to some wonderful friendships, as i\\\'ve found that those who are willing to listen to me, and thus change their opinion of me are usually my type of people.  i don\\\'t care if people misuderstand me, i\\\'m used to it by now.  and i\\\'m not in this life to be popular or well liked.  getting offended by words is a waste of energy, sniveling about them is a sure way to get me to ignore someone.  i\\\'ve had trouble with nazis in the past, i don\\\'t care what they say to me, it\\\'s when they take action that i make a move.  once, around 4 years ago, i was dating and living with a woman of asian extract.  two nazi skinheads came to my table, as we ate together, and said: \\\"you fucking race traitor!\\\"  i smiled and replied: \\\"i\\\'m a jew dude, a member of ZOG, call me when you\\\'re ready to submit.\\\"  they left.  i laughed.  my girl freaked out.  she hollered at me for a few minutes.  my reply to her was this: \\\"Nicky, if i beat them to the floor, i\\\'d be feeding their hate.  they didn\\\'t have the balls to do anything.\\\"\r\n<br>\r\nlater that night however, as we walked home, we saw them again.  they had friends with them now.  as they confronted me, one of them grabbed Nicky.  i snapped out my baton and let it be known i\\\'d use it.  they left.  as an old time fighter, i can\\\'t let words get to me too much, else i\\\'d never have stopped fighting.  someone calls me a kike, i laugh.  it IS funny.  to me.  i know it\\\'s not funny to everyone, and i try to avoid causing a scene.  but when something i need to say, requires the use of offensive words, i never have, nor will i ever, shy from using them.',3,0,0,0,'207.205.216.56','en'),(4123,1108,'2002-03-08 04:52:47',65,'le to bmg','prostate.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4124,1106,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','<p>I\\\'m guessing all humans just about everywhere and during \r\nevery era have developed some way of communicating their \r\nstatus (or lackthereof) in public. I don\\\'t find the present \r\nvariation the most compelling...</p>\r\n ',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(4125,1099,'2001-06-15 00:23:57',0,'darwin to egg','<p>I\\\'m glad that you can at least admit that your stance is \r\ninconsistent.</p>\r\n<p>I\\\'m not sure what your statement about the world \r\ndiscriminating against women is supposed to indicate. Is \r\nthis a justification for the inconsistency of your stance? \r\nDo subjugated classes get a \\\"be an asshole free\\\" card?</p>\r\n<p>Oh, and \\\"I used to love her, but I had to kill her\\\" is a \r\nsong about Axl Rose\\\'s dog. Violence against female dogs!</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n',5,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(4126,1099,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','darwin:  reading the Shadow University will answer that.  there is a concerted effort by so-called intellectuals to create lopsided free speach.  but then, think of it, has anything really changed.  if a person thinks gays are an affront to his god, he is silenced at colleges across the us.  not so for the gays themselves.  equality is not what they are seeking.  they wish to overturn old inequities, replacing them with new ones.',3,0,0,0,'207.205.216.56','en'),(4127,1108,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','women read books, to learn how to ejaculate. men \r\nread books, to learn how to <b>not</b> ejaculate. what \r\nthe fuck is that all about.',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4128,1099,'2001-06-15 00:44:00',0,'rusty','I personally see nothing wrong with irrationally hating \r\nsomething or someone, as long as you keep it to yourself, \r\nand don\\\'t put it on them, or someone else that doesn\\\'t \r\ndeserve it...  We all should deal with our own irrational \r\nemotions...\r\n<p>\r\nI think silencing people who are causing problems with \r\ntheir hate is fair...  I can see someone having issues with \r\ngays if they had been hurt by one in the past, or had \r\nrepressed gay issues going on in themselves, and I can see \r\nthem possibly wanting to vent, but they shouldn\\\'t take it \r\nout ON someone...  It\\\'s their own issue...  Just because \r\nyou create a group that all shares the same personal issue \r\ndoesn\\\'t mean you now have the right to take it out on \r\nothers, just because you have backing...\r\n<p>\r\nI don\\\'t think I\\\'m arguing with anyone here...  It\\\'s a \r\nsimple concept, many would agree with... nothing intriguing \r\nabout this statement, I suppose...  except it does use the \r\nnasty word \\\'issues\\\'... heh...\r\n<p>\r\nSo, I basically am saying, I think it\\\'s perfectly \r\nreasonable to \\\'hate\\\'/silence hate groups...  But, it \r\ncertainly isn\\\'t going to fix things...  It just makes the \r\nhate groups have more hate, but it has seemed to lessen the \r\npower and size of those groups slowly over time...  so \r\nmaybe it\\\'s effective...  it\\\'s only a recent thing in the \r\nscheme of things, so why not let it happen, and see if it \r\ncan have a positive effect?\r\n<p>\r\nbut as for being mad at the opposite sex...  that happens \r\nto everyone at sometime in their life, or even multiple \r\ntimes...  shit, I\\\'ve hated men and women in general...  but \r\nsuch generalizations just make it more obvious how much the \r\nhuman race in general is pretty fucked up, and your \r\nproblems are not related to any group...  So what if I\\\'ve \r\nhad a lot of girls fuck my heart up?  It\\\'s not women in \r\ngeneral\\\'s problem...  So what if a lot of dominating \r\ncompetitive men have fucked with my life in the past?  It\\\'s \r\nnot men in general\\\'s fault...\r\n<p>\r\nI hate the whole human race equally!  :-D',6,0,0,0,'205.142.76.11','en'),(4129,1108,'2001-06-15 00:58:24',0,'liver to mastur moll','actually, i don\'t think it has anything to do with \r\nrepression.  i\'m in the middle of _The Multi-Orgasmic Man : \r\nSexual Secrets Every Man Should Know_ right now.  it\'s a \r\npretty interesting read.  basically, the point is that \r\nwhile most men associate orgasm with ejaculation, they\'re \r\nactually two distinct events.  usually orgasm immediately \r\nprecedes ejaculation, you have your six second ride and off \r\nyou go to stand in line again.  woohoo!\r\n<br><br>\r\nit\'s actually possible thought to separate the two and \r\nexperience fuller (and multiple) orgasms if you don\'t blow \r\nyour load at the top of the first hill.  \r\n<br><br>\r\ni\'ve been playing around some with the techniques outlined \r\nin the book (so to speak) and it seems pretty right on.  i \r\nkinda like ejaculating though, so usually i do it at some \r\npoint.  no celibate glow for me right now, but maybe i\'ll \r\ntry that at some point.\r\n<br><br>\r\naccording to the author you get more than just a celibate \r\nglow from not ejaculating.  you\'ll have more energy, live \r\nlonger, etc. if you do have orgasms but don\'t ejaculate.  \r\neven if you don\'t buy into all of that, it\'s an interesting \r\ntechnique to learn and the ejaculation control exercises \r\nare pretty useful too.  it never dawned on me before, for \r\nexample, that breathing is a useful control technique.  \r\nbetter, possibly, than thinking about programming.\r\n<br><br>\r\nhello.\r\n\r\n\r\n',3,0,0,0,'63.202.215.130','en'),(4130,1099,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to darwin, darling','<p>are you trying to tell me there is no subtextual wink from \r\nthe Guns N Roses song?</p>\r\n<p>you could try to tell me that.</p>\r\n<p>perhaps my intention was not clear in this piece, but I \r\nwas trying to illustrate the many ways that I might fluctuate \r\nin my discrimination against boys. like, \\\"boys suck today.\\\" \r\n\\\"oh wait, no they dont.\\\" so it was meant as a commentary on \r\ndiscrimination. perhaps it was too subtle, or imaginary on my \r\npart.</p>\r\n<p>and I dont think being a girl gives me an asshole license, \r\nbut in personal writing people tend to objectify other \r\ncharacters in their lives, and it just so happens - for \r\nreasons we can go into over beers ALL NIGHT LONG sometime - \r\nthat the greater majority of published writing available to \r\nus is written by men, and often about women, and often \r\nsimplifying women down to a quantifiable group. alls I was \r\nsayin in my comment was that while my voice is not \r\nnecessarily morally superior, it fills in a gap of authorship \r\nthat lives in written discourse as a cultural document.</p>\r\n<p>and I did assume it was lighthearted enough not to be \r\nconsidered political propoganda. file under \\\"personal essay\\\". \r\nthere you go.</p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(4131,1108,'2001-06-15 01:05:45',0,'liver','ok.\r\n<p>\r\nso next time i\'ll try inserting html tags.\r\n</p><p><i>fixed! --editor</i></p>',2,0,0,0,'63.202.215.130','en'),(4132,1099,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','rusty:  i cannot accept the silencing of anyone for any reason beyond the scope of the tests defined by the Supreme Court.  i\\\'ve noticed that much of what i have to say here is unpopular.  being silenced here on swinney would bother me, because i feel i have something to contribute and would like to continue to share with everyone, recieving their ideas in return.  try to silence me out in the real world and you cross the line where i prepare to get violent.  silence some of the hate groups i\\\'ve had run inswith and you can bet there will be violence.  you don\\\'t have to like a person\\\'s speech, you don\\\'t even have to respect it.  but you\\\'d damn well better learn to deal with it without the use of force.  and to silence someone in america requires quite a bit of force or threat thereof.  no, i would rather kill than allow people to be silenced.  i would die for that belief.  i would die to protect even the Klan and their hate for my people.  fight bad ideas with good ones.  else you are no better than a tyrant.',3,0,0,0,'207.205.216.56','en'),(4133,1099,'2001-06-15 01:20:13',0,'kathleen hanna','<p>you wrote the script now<br>\r\nyou made the rules<br>\r\ndont blame me<br>\r\nwhen you fuckin lose!\r\n',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(4134,1103,'2002-03-15 00:17:55',129,'moebius','My interpretation of the badamerican document--it\\\'s not \r\nwritten by a conservative or a libertarian--it\\\'s written by \r\nsomeone from outside of the States, trying to point out the \r\nattitudes they feel more or less define the average \r\nAmerican. It\\\'s a dark, mean-spririted parody, with a bit of \r\ntruth at the core. <br><br>\r\n\r\nOver the years I\\\'ve met several Canadians who will tell you \r\nthat 95% of Americans think this way. As well as \r\nAustralians, New Zealanders, and many europeans. And it\\\'s a \r\ntotally ridiculous generalization but then again it\\\'s easy \r\nto understand where that attitude comes from. All you have \r\nto do is listen to conservative talk radio for awhile to \r\nrealize the badamerican attitude is out there, and when it \r\ntravels, it pisses folks off.<br><br>\r\n\r\nAnd now we have an administration in power that would \r\ngladly work a lot of it into public and foreign policy if \r\nthey could.<br><br>\r\n\r\ns5: While it\\\'s true that the \\\"every man for himself\\\" \r\nattitude is a prevalent aspect of the overall American \r\npsyche, I doubt it\\\'s being slowly obsoleted. I think in \r\nfact we\\\'re busy importing it to the rest of the world along \r\nwith the rest of our cultural hegemony. I also don\\\'t think \r\ntribalism is exactly the answer--unless you define it \r\ndifferently than I do. But that\\\'s another conversation for \r\nanother day.<br><br>\r\n\r\n--Moe<br>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n',3,0,0,0,'63.38.73.118','en'),(4135,1103,'2002-03-15 00:17:55',129,'moebius','Whoops--failed to read the Carlin link before writing that. \r\nSigh. But still--you wouldn\\\'t believe how much of that I\\\'ve \r\nheard from my out-of-US friends, and they weren\\\'t \r\nreferencing Carlin.<br><br>\r\n\r\n--Moe<br>',1,0,0,0,'63.38.73.118','en'),(4136,1099,'2001-06-15 01:47:48',0,'s5 to our eggie','<p>this site is an ongoing battle between people who take \r\nthings too literally/seriously, and people who are just \r\nwriting about stuff. i forget which category i\'m in. though \r\nsometimes i use the word \"i\" to mean \"someone other \r\nthan me\".\r\n</p>',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4137,1108,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','<B>everyone</B> loses chi not only from masturbation but \r\nalso as a result of arousal.  it moves from your belly, \r\nwhere it usually lives, to your sex area and is dissipated \r\nfrom there.  consult your local qijong master fomoinfo.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.9.173','en'),(4138,1108,'2001-06-15 02:47:31',0,'kat','losing chi. do we really lose it? or is it just a matter of \r\nunderstanding that its not gone, but somewhere else. easily \r\naccessible, as long as you know how. i constantly battle \r\nwith my grasping for \\\'wants\\\' and the craving of my soul to \r\njust be. this is the flow. ',3,0,0,0,'12.64.66.16','en'),(4139,1108,'2001-06-15 03:31:57',0,'Danielle','I\\\'m trying to find my chi.<P> I\\\'ve never had an orgasm. \r\nEjaculatory or not. Hmmm.',1,0,0,0,'24.68.193.134','en'),(4140,1108,'2001-06-15 04:29:45',0,'twinkus to lulu','<P>it was thought as late as the early 17th century in \r\nFrance that if women did not get enough semen in \r\nthem, they might go insane.</P>\r\n<P>this was thought to be the problem with one of the \r\nprincesses of France in the Seventeenth century.  sorry, \r\ni dont remember which it was.</P>\r\n<P>although many see the idea of semen deficiency as \r\na cause for insanity in women as a silly superstition, i \r\nthink it explains quite a bit for some of the women today.</P>\r\n<P>hi lulu.</P>',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4141,1108,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','danielle. you should not be afraid to touch yourself! ',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4142,1103,'2001-06-15 04:59:54',0,'s5 to moebius','i\\\'ll define what i mean more clearly in another essay.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4143,1099,'2001-06-15 05:19:25',0,'rusty','<p>\r\ns5 - I think a large part of when those battles occur, is \r\nbecause with text it\\\'s hard to see the context around what \r\nthe people are saying, so it\\\'s hard to say \\\'well this is \r\nvery seriously stated\\\', or \\\'this has been presented to show \r\nthe irony of this situation\\\', or \\\'this is an outright joke \r\nbased on how obviously ridiculous what I\\\'m saying is\\\'...\r\n<p>\r\nincitor - I would never silence you, especially because I \r\nhaven\\\'t had a problem with anything you\\\'ve ever said \r\n(including this)...  And I totally understand what you\\\'re \r\nsaying about people fighting to keep themselves from being \r\nsilenced...  I think they definately have a right to...  \r\nlet me say this a little differently:\r\n<p>\r\n\\\"there is a concerted effort by so-called intellectuals to \r\ncreate lopsided free speach.  but then, think of it, has \r\nanything really changed. if a person thinks gays are an \r\naffront to his god, he is silenced at colleges across the \r\nus. not so for the gays themselves. equality is not what \r\nthey are seeking. they wish to overturn old inequities, \r\nreplacing them with new ones. \\\"\r\n<p>\r\nOkay, I would say this effort has been out there as long as \r\nthere has been any hate, or non-acceptance...  From back \r\nwhen the Jews were fight the Romans, the Muslims were \r\nfighting the Jews, up to freeing the slaves, women\\\'s rights \r\nto vote, anything that was revolutionary about fighting \r\nhate...  These have generally been battles against hating \r\nthat particular group that was involved, and getting \r\nequality for that group...\r\n<p>\r\nSo what you are worried about is this becoming a \r\nrevolutionary thing, like most such battles have been in \r\nthe past, where say the repressed Jews ended up having \r\ntheir philosophy win out completely over the Roman\\\'s...\r\n<p>\r\nSo you are worried about these things not really creating \r\nthe equality that should exist, but continuing to create \r\nnew inequalities...\r\n<p>\r\nThe \\\"concerted effort by so-called intellectuals\\\" that you \r\nare referring to I think has been around for a while, and \r\nit\\\'s existed in a lot o parts of society, which is why you \r\nwill actually see gay relations on TV now, and why the Klan \r\nis no longer a major major political power, and has many \r\nless followers...  I don\\\'t think the Klan has been \r\nseriously beaten down, or been prevented to express \r\nthemselves at all, but certainly, I think many parts of \r\nsociety have been trying to have a long term effect of \r\ngetting rid of and fighting the hate mentality that creates \r\nsuch a group...\r\n<p>\r\nI don\\\'t think that is necessarily a bad thing...  Seems \r\nlike a better method than say complete annihilation of a \r\ngroup so that another group can survive, or separatism, or \r\nconverting...  hehe... that\\\'d be funny if the Klan and Gay \r\nrights were religions...  Imagine Gay Rights activists \r\nconverting the Klan to all become Gay overtime, the way the \r\nJews converted the Romans?  lol...  anyhow...\r\n<p>\r\nI deinately agree, your viewpoint of everyone having an \r\nequal voice, and everyone being allowed to their beliefs, \r\nis DEFINATELY the most logical, fair thing...  But have you \r\never seen life be logical or fair?  No, you of all people \r\nhave not...  Someone will tip the boat if things are \r\nlogical and fair, to the point where it isn\\\'t anymore...\r\n<p>\r\nSo I think, if something is always going to not be \r\naccepted, I think it\\\'s best to not accept anything that \r\nisn\\\'t accepting of others...\r\n<p>\r\nThis of course is replacing one inequity with another... \r\nthe world will always have inequity...  But I think it \r\nmakes more sense to say it is okay to hate any group that \r\nis trying to put down another group...\r\n<p>\r\nThe only problem with that whole thing, is that it would \r\nonly work on groups that outreach preach non-acceptance...  \r\nLike Nazi\\\'s, the Klan, lots of Religions...  But it \r\nwouldn\\\'t prevent groups from having a hidden strategy to \r\nrepress other groups by claiming the other group hates \r\nthem, and should be put down...\r\n<p>\r\nBut then again, you can\\\'t ever know ahead of time about an \r\nIlluminati-style group...  Paranoia is a beautiful thing...\r\n<p>\r\nAnyhow, all this would ultimately push for everyone being \r\ntruely equal, and truely accepting one another, whatever \r\ntheir beliefs, without saying \\\'you\\\'re going to \r\nhell\\\', \\\'you\\\'re not allowed to marry this person because \r\nthey\\\'re this\\\', \\\'you can\\\'t do this or that to yourself\\\', and \r\nso on...  which could be considered a bit pinko-commie, and \r\na bit too froofy idealistic...  because the world will \r\nalways have inequality...  But seems better to have groups \r\nthat are based on not being accepting to begin with be the \r\nones that feel the weight of what that inequality does... \r\nbecause people are always gonna have to have someone to \r\nhate...  I choose to only hate groups that preach hate \r\nagainst some other group...\r\n<p>\r\nThe world has already been going that way slowly...  Which \r\nis why you\\\'re seeing what you are commenting on...  And \r\nit\\\'s been happening since the 60s...  I\\\'d like to see i it \r\nends up working...  because, yes more inequities will be \r\ncreated, but I\\\'d prefer it to the old inequities, since \r\nhuman nature would not work with true equality across the \r\nboard...\r\n<p>\r\nChoosing Gays as an example seems a bad idea...  There is \r\nnot a quota of Gays that some companies have to fill, there \r\nis not massive financial support for Gays to go to \r\ncollege...  Gays aren\\\'t allowed to get married, and there \r\nare laws specifically outlawing their preferred lifestyle...\r\n<p>\r\nI\\\'d say out of all the groups that have fought for equality \r\nin the last few decades, Gay people have the least \r\nacceptance, and certainly have no \\\'special treatment\\\' \r\ncompared to minority groups...  So I don\\\'t see them coming \r\nanywhere near repressing other groups...\r\n<p>\r\nAnd the argument of \\\'you chose to be that way, you weren\\\'t \r\nborn that way, so you\\\'re not like a minority\\\' seems like \r\none of the most ridiculous to me...\r\n<p>\r\nThis one might be more disagreed with by you or other \r\npeople, and that I fully expect...  I think people should \r\nhave a right to choose anything or them damn selves...  I \r\nyou \\\'chose\\\' to be gay, that\\\'s your goddamn right...  \r\nalthough many people have approached it as that they were \r\nborn different...  I say that doesn\\\'t matter...  I say it\\\'s \r\nyour life, and your body, and you should be allowed to do \r\nwhatever the fuck you want with it...  Drugs should be \r\nlegal, so should suicide, so should any kind of sex, as \r\nlong as you\\\'re not forcing someone else to do it, or \r\nhurting someone else while you\\\'re doing it...  All we ever \r\ntruely own in this life is our own mind, and our own body, \r\nand laws that prevent us from being able to do whatever we \r\nwant with them are complete bullshit...  Sure, \\\'God\\\' \r\ndoesn\\\'t like it...  Well, if you accept that version of \r\nGod, that\\\'s your problem...  God is another personal \r\nconcept, just because you choose to believe a pre-defined \r\nversion of God, doesn\\\'t mean that someone else can\\\'t choose \r\nfor themselves to let their mind believe in a different \r\nversion of God...\r\n<p>\r\nWhy do you call yourself a skinhead?  Just because your \r\nhead is shaved, because you are a s.h.a.r.p, or because you \r\nare trying to get that word to not be associated with neo-\r\nnazis?\r\n<p>\r\nAnyhow...  I once laughed at a neo-nazi skinhead that was \r\nhanging around my gutter punk scene in Santa Cruz (well, \r\nI\\\'ve actually done it more than once, to different \r\npeople)...  I didn\\\'t tell him he couldn\\\'t speak his mind, \r\nbut I certainly felt it was quite fine for me to speak \r\nmine, and be amused...  But boy he didn\\\'t like it, and \r\nwanted to kick my ass...  Because his beliefs truely are \r\nall based on rage...  which means there is no reasoning \r\npossible...  People only stop becoming skins after they get \r\nover that core of rage, and learn more about life, and see \r\nmore...  young kids that become neo-nazis more often than \r\nnot get back out of it...  I never got in a physical fight \r\nduring these confrontations...  Usually I would stand \r\nthere, or sit there, and wait to see if he would do \r\nsomething, and if he was going to, the other punks around \r\nwould grab him, and keep him away from me...  I\\\'ve avoided \r\nfights so easily since I was 11, for some reason, even \r\nthough my whole lie before that was really really \r\nviolent...  I\\\'ve sometimes wondered if fights stopped \r\noccuring because:\r\n<p>\r\n1: I stopped deeply hating, and wouldn\\\'t be aggravated \r\nenough to ever hit first anymore<br>\r\n2: I was no longer scared of death...  In fact I look \r\nforward to it...  I am not looking to die now...  Life is a \r\ntruely amazing experience...  I did want to die at one \r\npoint, and that\\\'s what started the mentality...  I did die \r\nbriefly, and now I\\\'m just not scared of it...  It was \r\npretty damn good, so when it comes again, I\\\'ll enjoy it...  \r\nTherefore, if I got in a fight where it got really hot, and \r\nit came down to him or me, I wouldn\\\'t feel the need to back \r\ndown...  If someone senses that, and they are afraid of \r\ndeath, and they\\\'re used to bullying people into backing \r\ndown, I think they\\\'ll tend to avoid you, or find a way to \r\nbackdown without it look like they are backing down, so \r\nthey can save face...\r\n<p>\r\nBut then again, maybe I\\\'ve just been really lucky since I \r\nwas 11...\r\n<p>\r\nheh... my turn to be too rambly... gonna shut my ass up...  \r\nneed some food...',4,0,0,0,'64.163.194.75','en'),(4144,1109,'2001-06-15 05:27:59',0,'jo','he even talked up some city girls.<BR>\r\nis talked up the equivalent of \\\"macked on\\\" or \\\"threw game \r\nat?\\\"',1,0,0,0,'64.12.106.66','en'),(4145,1109,'2001-06-15 05:32:42',0,'tomato','he just talked to them, he\\\'s kind of like me in that \r\nregard.  he likes talking to people and finding things \r\nout, different opinions, etc.  he did the talking in a very \r\nfriendly matter however.',1,0,0,0,'165.247.216.247','en'),(4146,1108,'2001-06-15 06:57:11',0,'lulu to twinkus','Henriette d\\\'Angleterre\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(4147,1109,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','sometimes i wonder if people are self aware of their self\r\nawareness.  it is interesting to see you say these things\r\nbecause you are one of the people i wondered that about.  is\r\nreed, the friend from college, aware also?\r\n',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(4148,1111,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p>i dream of horses constantly:\r\n<br><br>\r\nlaying in a large field at night. stampede of horses \r\ngallops over me. i\\\'m unscathed.\r\n<br><br>\r\nriding a horse, almost falling off, recovering at the last \r\nminute.\r\n<br><br>\r\nvisiting an island inhabited by small furry horses who come \r\nwhen i call, like dogs.\r\n<br><br>\r\negg calls me a horse dyke. i have an ongoing obsession with \r\nthe concept of a horse fetus. i imagine myself as a strong \r\nhorse when things are fucked. i took riding lessons for a \r\nwhile but got sick of being terrified of falling. xep says \r\nit\\\'s time for me to start riding again.\r\n</p>',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4149,1109,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i like that you are a watcher. ',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4150,1100,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','sprinkle a little catnip on his foodies. will help. also, \r\nhe may like just drinking fresh pure water until he can \r\nwork up to eating. we have a very nervous kitty, it took \r\nher a while to come out from under the futon.',1,0,0,0,'64.81.65.205','en'),(4151,1099,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i completely disagree with everything.',6,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4152,1109,'2001-06-15 10:31:43',0,'tomato','xep:  you wondered that about me?<p> (i met you once \r\nin person, i wonder if that is what you are talking about \r\n-- with olivia)?',1,0,0,0,'165.247.216.247','en'),(4153,1099,'2001-06-15 10:47:47',0,'rusty','heheh...  you go, steve...',6,0,0,0,'64.163.194.75','en'),(4154,1111,'2001-06-15 10:55:26',0,'tomato','have you ever gone to wyoming in the winter?  there are \r\nhorses there with bob marly locks (in the snow).<p>\r\nbut everyone carries guns in their car in case they run \r\nover a deer, usually it screams off into the underbrush \r\nand you need to put it (he/she) down.  such is life.  \r\nwyoming.',1,0,0,0,'165.247.216.247','en'),(4155,850,'2001-06-15 12:50:11',0,'Ojigi','I find that i get really down and mopey, when i\\\'m not being \r\nchallenged or productive.. I have to be doing something \r\nworthwhile to feel good about myself.  Creativity, making \r\nstuff, learning things, building things. cleaning, doing \r\nwashing. whatever! as long as it\\\'s productive then it makes \r\nme SO much happier.\r\n\r\nOjigi, \r\n\r\n\\\"the cheesecakes are on me!\\\"',2,0,0,0,'194.154.190.2','en'),(4156,850,'2001-06-15 12:55:28',0,'Ojigi','Mmmmm....Pistachio Cheesecake:\r\n\r\n<a href=\\\"http://www.mischaiscool.com\\\"  target=\\\"_blank\\\"><img \r\nsrc=\\\"http://www.mischaiscool.com/images/cheesecake.gif\\\"></a>\r\n\r\nMmmmm..\r\n',2,0,0,0,'194.154.190.2','en'),(4157,1111,'2001-06-15 13:14:06',0,'kat','when i paint i have a hard time painting anything but \r\nhorses. their images creep up out of nowhere. i use to \r\nthink it was because i was creatively inept. why do i keep \r\npainting the same thing over and over? symbols. part of my \r\ninner dialouge. they speak to me.',3,0,0,0,'12.64.12.168','en'),(4158,1109,'2003-07-24 15:44:23',165,'joker','<p>perhaps an interesting experiment if you\\\'ll have a lot \r\nof solitude time is trying to notice what\\\'s observing what \r\n(that is to say, \\\"the body is smelling pine sap, but what\\\'s \r\ntaking note of the body smelling pine sap?\\\").  generally \r\nspeaking, this requires a lot of quiet and a lot of \r\nstillness.  it can lead to some stentorian and emancipating \r\nrealizations, however, which makes it well worth the \r\neffort.</p>',1,0,0,0,'66.68.187.34','en'),(4159,1108,'2001-06-15 16:04:39',0,'not_loco','http://www.geocities.com/SunsetStrip/Towers/9676/divinyls.ht\r\nml#touch',1,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(4160,1108,'2001-06-15 16:54:52',0,'Danielle','Le: I\\\'m not, but it doesn\\\'t do anything. Neither does his \r\ntouch... :o/',1,0,0,0,'24.68.193.134','en'),(4161,1112,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','\r\n<p>today, you are Leopold Bloom.</p>\r\n<p>\r\nBloomsday is tomorrow.\r\n</p>\r\n<p> I really appreciate your entries, thanks.</p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(4162,1113,'2001-06-15 18:28:40',0,'kat','>>>its all gotta burn....wheres the matches?<<<',4,0,0,0,'12.64.30.39','en'),(4163,1109,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','yes, about you.  stories have been told about you for a long\r\ntime.  we are all storytellers.  ',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(4164,1113,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>the Lord hath chosen me for his sacrificial Ass. hog tie \r\nme at dusk with his mighty chains and drop me in the \r\ncauldron.</p>\r\n<p>wearing only a spandex unitard.</p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(4165,1113,'2001-06-15 18:54:29',0,'neck','Overanalyzing Iron Maiden is not recommended. ',4,0,0,0,'209.85.237.56','en'),(4166,1113,'2001-06-15 20:52:57',0,'rusty','There\\\'s plenty of room or analysis inside Iron Maiden...\r\n<p>\r\nAre you trying to say DeBarge, or Michael Jackson had more \r\nmeaningful stuff to say in the 80s?  ;)\r\n<p>\r\nIron Maiden doesn\\\'t wear spandex anymore...\r\n<p>\r\nThey inspired me to learn more about some things in history \r\nwhen I was young...  Not often that a band writes songs \r\nabout Alexander the Great, Ancient Egypt, Icarus, old Bible \r\nstories, and past wars, the Cold War, the end of the Cold \r\nWar...\r\n<p>\r\nAnd then the literature they wrote songs about, Samuel \r\nTaylor Coleridge, Robert Heinlein, Edgar Allen Poe, CS \r\nLewis, Aldous Huxley...\r\n<p>\r\nClassic movie, Quest for Fire...\r\n<p>\r\nAnd that\\\'s just some of the songs that are obvious where \r\nthey were inspired from...\r\n<p>\r\nThey were a good band for inspiring youth to think...  But \r\nif you think a band like the GoGos had more substance, \r\nalrighty then...\r\n<p>\r\nSongs about love, flirtation, dancing, being a girl...  \r\nCertainly not unworthy subjects, but they\\\'ve been done a \r\nmillion times, I think Iron Maiden found an impressive \r\nvariety of topics to discuss, even if they also weren\\\'t \r\nreally new topics...\r\n<p>\r\nI\\\'m glad I grew up on listening to Iron Maiden, and other \r\nnon-mainstream music of the time...  I think it gave me a \r\nmore open mind...\r\n',4,0,0,0,'64.163.194.75','en'),(4167,1108,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i bet there\'s a <a href=\"http://www.goodvibes.com/afterhours.html\">workshop</a> at goodvibes that can help.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4168,1108,'2001-06-15 21:31:58',0,'rusty','<p>\r\nDanielle - It\\\'s more likely something mental than \r\nphysical...  If it feels good, but you just never have an \r\norgasm...  The brain is the main real erogenous zone...',3,0,0,0,'64.163.194.75','en'),(4169,1113,'2001-06-15 21:57:57',0,'s5 to aus10','allow me to introduce you to rush.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4170,1099,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','<p>\r\nrusty:  i wasn\\\'t expressing concern over being silenced myself.  i was simply using myself as an example.  there have been, in the past, attempts to silence me.  in college there was an effort by certain professors...i handled it poorly and cornered a certain instrucor of mine who had been trying mightily to force my voice down...i forced her in to a corner and explained the workings of a car bomb in detail.  the chemicals needed, the electronics, the connections, the breaking of certain chemical bonds, the efficiency of the explosion, and the results for certain snotty people who might be in said car.  then i walked away feeling chuffed with myself.  thankfully a day later she cornered ME and we talked under a calmer climate.  i felt terrible and apologized, she likewise.  we became rather close, and in the end all efforts to shut me up ended.  i handled it so poorly that in truth, i deserved to be arrested.  but it shows how averse i am to enforced silence.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\ni am aware of the history of efforts to realign free speech, not just here in america, but everywhere.  i find it abhorrent.  and of course no one said life is fair; however, the same people i find most likely to complain that something is unfair, are the ones most likely to be working towards a new and profoundly unfair concept of free speech.  when i say people will fight, am i speaking of revolution?  no.  unless you consider the Oklahoma City bombing a revolution.  and i sure as hell don\\\'t.  i, to a limited extent, sympathize the frustrations of the persons involved.  but could never agree with their methods of seeking redress.  but i assure you, it will happen again and again; for as long as there are these government intrusions into our freedoms.  freedoms, i remind you, which are not GRANTED by the government; but affirmed by the PEOPLE.  The Bill of Rights is non negotiable; it is a written explanation of the rights inherent in mankind, American citizens in particular.  no portion of the Bill of Rights may be repealed, these rights may not be traded or stolen.  and i know that i\\\'d kill and die to see that respected.  there are others who would commit acts which even i would find disgusting to prevent their liberties from being taken away.  freedom of speech is a cornerstone of our society, at its worst it makes MY life interesting.  at its best it frees slaves, prevents wars, forces vital changes in institutions, and converts hateful people.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nseperatism is a likely event at this point.  we are splintering ourselves, and i know i\\\'d rather join a secession than live under the government most Left leaning persons hope for, and almost got under Clinton.  unless we can reopen the lines of reasonable communication, and learn once again to COMPROMISE, the Union is doomed.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nyou might find it interesting that years ago i had run ins with a group of gays that enjoyed \\\'straight-bashing\\\'.  thankfully they were small and un noticed for the most part, think of the backlash against all gays if the media had caught that one!\r\n</P>\r\n<p>\r\nconsider that every time you legislate someone\\\'s liberty away, sooner of later you in turn will feel a bite on your ass.  for clarity i will now state that \\\'i\\\' refers to myself, and \\\'you\\\' refers to no one in particular.  all it takes is a change in administration, i expect that with Bush in the White House, many laws Clinton signed to protect the \\\'downtrodden\\\' will be used to smash the hell out of the downtrodden.  let that be a lesson.  the best way for Americans to help one another is to just get the fuck up and do so.  legislation is not needed to help each other, unless you are too lazy to do it and hope for \\\'someone else\\\' to take care of the problem.  freedom requires responsiblity, and that is why most men dread it.  stop fearing freedom, we need to, all of us, get up and use it!\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nas for acceptance...who cares?!  fuck acceptance.  everywhere i go i am not accepted.  the rich think i am shady.  the ravers hate me because i despise drugs.  note: i think all drugs should be legal.  the punks hate me becuase i tell them to grow up.  the skinheads hate me because i am one, but refuse to play by their sick ass rules.  the middle class don\\\'t like me because i challenge their beliefs.  republicans don\\\'t like me because i don\\\'t like their party\\\'s core beliefs.  democrats don\\\'t like me because i\\\'m not a socialist and i refuse to feel guilt unless i\\\'ve done wrong.  greenpeacers and the like don\\\'t like me because i think they are trying to force a system that will never work.  note:  i am indeed concerned about the enviroment, and last time i gave a speech i delved in to my belief that enviorment friendly industry is ultimately more profitable than \\\'regular\\\' industry.  libertarians shun me because i think their party isn\\\'t doing anything.  the NRA folks don\\\'t like me because i say they are wimping out.  Jews tend to fear me or dislike me because i am a skinhead.  note: i was bar mitzvah\\\'d when i was 13.  singing hebrew when your voice is cracking is miserable!  anyway.  i think you get the picture.  i am not a popular guy, i relate fully to no groups and therefore those groups reject me.  but i have a fair sized group of excellent friends from a wide section of these groups.  we don\\\'t agree on everything, or even much.  but we have an abiding love and respect for each other.  i\\\'m proud of the friends i have, for their loyalty and respect.  for their intelligence and bizarre interests.  i\\\'m proud of them.  as a whole however, we need to cooperate, not get along wonderfully.  i know cops who hate gays, but would never ever allow that to enter into their duties.  i\\\'ve seen a nazi skinhead hanging out with a jew (me), a black girl from england (my friend renita), and a member of ARA (my roomate).  and that\\\'s not all i\\\'ve seen.  *grin*\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nall forms of sex should be legal i guess, excepting those involving children or unwilling partners.  you know:  trees, dogs, dolphins, my computer....\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\ni call myself a skinhead because that is, in part, an accurate if simple label for me.  my head isn\\\'t even shaved at this moment (been too lazy).  but i\\\'ve run with the skins since i was...i think around 14-15.  before that it was punks and such.  anyway.  i\\\'m a traditional skinhead...ska and all of that crap.  mind, i don\\\'t hang out with skinheads anymore \\\'cause racist or not they are all assholes in my experience.  my idea of a good night being a good american is not drinking heavily and then picking fights with innocent people.  but i still relate to skinheads because I managed to get something good out of my time as an active skin.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nnot fearing death will never help you get out of fights.  look deeper.  consider what camus had to say on suicides:  (i\\\'ve got to paraphrase here, sorry) A man ready to kill himself, who does not harm any others, still retains certain morals, for what hold can there be over a man ready to die?\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nwow.  i wish we could have this conversation over coffe or beer.  face to face.  it\\\'s worthy of that.\r\n</P>\r\n',2,0,0,0,'207.205.216.89','en'),(4171,1113,'2001-06-15 22:26:56',0,'MightyBluJ to Rusty','Ditto!\r\n  plus their bass player (Steve Harris) wrote a lot of the \r\nsongs.  which is very cool in my book.  He had more cool in \r\nhis earlobes than  nikki sixx could ever hope to attain.',1,0,0,0,'204.64.42.245','en'),(4172,1108,'2001-06-15 22:40:25',0,'Danielle','s5: Thanks, unfortunately I don\\\'t live in San Francisco \r\nbut thanks for the thought.<P>I don\\\'t really know what to \r\ndo about this. Maybe I\\\'m a-sexual.',1,0,0,0,'207.34.94.238','en'),(4173,1108,'2001-06-15 22:43:53',0,'mojo23','There\\\'s a great book on the subject:\nMantak Chai and Douglas Abrams\\\', \\\"The Multi Orgasmic Couple\\\"\nChia states that women do indeed lose chi when they orgasm,\nso he would argue that you could get that same celibate\nglow.  But they lose less chi, and he therefore doesn\\\'t\nencourage surpassing (denying) women\\\'s orgasm as often as he\nencourages it for men.\n\n\\\"After ejaculating, a man is tired, his ears buzz, his eyes\nare heavy and he longs for sleep.  He is thirsty and his\nlimbs feel weak and stiff.  In ejaculating he enjoys a brief\nmoment of sensation then suffers long hours of exhaustion.\\\"\n--Peng-Tze, a sex advisor to the famed Yellow Emperor\n\nOther interesting points he covers in this book include:\nTaoist Penis Massage\nTongue Kung-Fu\nMorning Prayer Sex',3,0,0,0,'158.252.220.26','en'),(4174,1112,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Athal Moll','<p>I have always been frightened of the 3 train and \r\nwhatever other ones are red and strangelooking like that, \r\nthey make me feel like I\\\'m in a Jeunet & Caro film.</p>\r\n<p>I remember riding them late at night with ladyfriend and \r\nwe would dance in the empty cars and go on the ferry till \r\ndawn without paying.</p>\r\n<p>Bad places, good times.</p>\r\n\r\n',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(4175,1113,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p>\r\nmy first love was an iron maiden fan. he had long black \r\nhair and wore a black jean jacket with an iron maiden patch \r\non it. he had combat boots and a incredibly big smile. it \r\nis because of him that i know lyrics to slayer songs.\r\n<br><br>\r\nit\\\'s really hard for me to think about him now, because it \r\nwas so long ago, but i have some really distinct memories \r\nof looking at him while he slept and feeling some new thing \r\nin the pit of my stomach about him. \\\"oh.. love?\\\" \r\n</p>',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4176,1108,'2001-06-15 23:28:56',0,'s5 to danielle','<p>there are also sex counselors you can seek out in \r\nyour area. (something tells me mojo23 might have \r\nmore information.) in absence of that, goodvibes sells \r\nbooks and videos (note: not porn, but instructional) \r\nabout technique and exploration - i recommend \r\nbrowsing their catalogue.</p>\r\n<p>everyone deserves to open up their sexuality. and \r\nthere are plenty of resources out there, should you \r\ndecide this is enough of a priority in your life.</p>\r\n<p>anyway, diatribe over. i\\\'m just responding to what i \r\nread into your comments. best of luck.</p>',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4177,1099,'2001-06-15 23:34:03',0,'rusty','Yeah...  you\\\'re cool...  ;)\r\n<p>\r\nIf you come into town, I\\\'ll hang with ya...',6,0,0,0,'64.163.194.75','en'),(4178,1112,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','egg: on a good day, i try ot pack the ambition of Dedalus \r\nchanneled into the carnality of Bloom, heh.\r\n\r\nMoll: yep, the creepy old red-bird trains freak me out some, \r\ntoo, especially at night.  I used to ride it into bklyn late \r\nat night and blink in the rythm of the lights flickering on \r\nand off in the empty car- if you did it right, you could \r\nmake the car seem pitch-dark.  I finally moved from bklyn, \r\nand find myself now living at yet another 3 train stop in \r\nthe city.  irony, irony. bad places good times, indeed, and \r\nthey\\\'re always an express stop away from each other.\r\n\r\n\r\n',3,0,0,0,'63.210.216.198','en'),(4179,1114,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Pong Moll','<p>Kind of like the A-team?????????????????????????????????\r\n</p>',1,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(4180,484,'2001-06-16 05:06:41',0,'eoj','i recently learned of some interesting chemical compounds:\r\ncadaverine and putrescine.  they are 6 and 5 carbon chains\r\nwith amine groups on the end.<P>\r\n \r\nthey are responsible, among other things, for the odor of\r\nrotting flesh, and the odor of bad breath.   the compounds\r\nare also present in semen.<P>',0,0,0,0,'64.3.15.93','en'),(4181,449,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','i\\\'ll be glad to write down some chinese for you to tattoo \r\non your arm. make sure it\\\'s really noticable, okay? ',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(4182,850,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','<BR>\r\ni miss you, mischa.\r\nyou are cool.',0,0,0,0,'203.96.111.201','en'),(4183,1114,'2001-06-16 06:22:42',0,'the punctuation fairy','. . . . . , . . ,. ,., ,.  . . ,,  ,, . . , ,, . . ,, ., , , ,.,., . , ,,. ,. ; ;, ., ; ,;, ., .,;, \r\n..',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4184,1113,'2001-06-16 06:32:42',0,'mojo23','<p>\r\nI was and am an Iron Maiden maiden.  \r\n</p><p>\r\nThey rocked my high school years, and they entertain \r\nme everytime I hear them...there was a video store I \r\nused to frequent that was always playing a Maiden \r\nalbum when I came in, and my face glowed, my mouth \r\nvoiced the lrics I could remember, and my head \r\nbanged.  Hair flew into the air.\r\n</p><p>\r\nI saw them in concert, the PowerSlave tour, circa 1985.  \r\nThey kicked ass.\r\n</p><p>\r\nAnd Rusty\'s right:  they did use their lyrics to inform their \r\nlisteners about various topics.  I made my mom listen \r\nto the Rhyme of the Ancient Mariner to prove that \r\nMaiden was the most intelligent metal band in the \r\nworld.  For real.\r\n</p><p>\r\nBut I heard there\'s been a reunion.  That\'s really \r\nunfortunate.  Bruce Dickenson had a bizarre solo \r\ncareer for a few years, and I guess it didn\'t work out as \r\nwell as planned.\r\n</p><p>\r\nAnd S5:  NEVER EVER introduce anyone to Rush.  It\'s 7 \r\nyears bad luck crossing the border into Canada.\r\n</p>',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4185,1116,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i can\\\'t believe you linked my homework.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4186,1116,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<tt><*s5*> i am misunderstood.</tt>',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4187,1116,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p><img \r\nsrc=\"http://steve.org/images/elly_blackmail.jpg\"></p>',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4188,1116,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','\\\'sup.',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4189,1115,'2001-06-16 14:12:02',0,'jo','no, not romantic. but sexy. there is no better fruit for \r\nwhich \\\"fleshy\\\" is the best possible adjective by which to \r\ndescribe it.',1,0,0,0,'64.12.103.66','en'),(4190,1115,'2001-06-16 14:12:50',0,'jo','er. i meant, not <b>poetic</b>, <b>yes</b> sexy.',1,0,0,0,'64.12.103.66','en'),(4191,1116,'2001-06-16 14:15:23',0,'jo','elly, although i recognize little punked out steve right \r\naway, i think you\\\'ve passed up a chance to photoshop up \r\nthis picture with big red circles and arrows that will \r\ndelineate freak from geek.',1,0,0,0,'64.12.103.66','en'),(4192,1112,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','<p>\r\nto think something through, on a bad day/confused day while \r\nstill living in new york, i rode the F train (the Fucker, \r\nthe slow boat to brooklyn) over and over. from 2nd ave to \r\nconey island and back. staring out the window. pacing back \r\nand forth. switching seats. switching cars. smoking with the \r\ndoor open and blowing it out in between the trains.\r\n</p>',1,0,0,0,'206.15.0.222','en'),(4193,1114,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','clever but predictable.  didn\\\'t really intend to NOT punctuate is so much as when i finished, i noticed i had not and didn\\\'t wanna fix it.  and what, no sexy semicolons?!',3,0,0,0,'207.205.216.105','en'),(4194,1114,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','oh!  ahaha.  i thought that was dirt on my CRT!  love those semicolons...\r\n',3,0,0,0,'207.205.216.105','en'),(4195,1116,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','this made my day. i must confess, i\\\'ve always said elly \r\nlooked really cute pre-vegan. i\\\'ll say it again. *drool* ',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(4196,1115,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','mangos are damn sexy. there\\\'s no other fruit i\\\'ve eaten \r\nlately that made me think i was giving head to a huge mango \r\nflavored hairy pussy. *picks teeth daintily* i know i sound \r\nlike a perv. i know i is ones.',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(4197,1099,'2001-06-16 18:01:31',0,'cyantist','world wide pants.  incitor, that\\\'s two invites!',1,0,0,0,'203.184.249.130','en'),(4198,1114,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<H1>I am a woman warrior!</H2>',0,0,0,0,'216.175.94.102','en'),(4199,1117,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','start the sf no-billboards initiative.  i\\\'ll sign.  i would \r\neven try to get others to sign.',2,0,0,0,'216.175.94.102','en'),(4200,1118,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p>\r\ni was with an academic once. i was naked in a bathtub and \r\nshe was crouched over the tub with her polaroid, her olive \r\nskin a constant distraction for me despite the barrage of \r\nbarked instructions: <i>now hold still, ok, now move your \r\nhead, JUST YOUR HEAD, really fast, keep moving it, keep \r\nmoving it, ok stop!</i> ...and a bright clip-light with a \r\nblue gel shining in my eyes on my belly too. she had said: \r\n<i>do you want to come over and let me take pictures of you \r\nin the tub?</i> and i had agreed, how could i not agree, \r\nwhat would i be to say no? i came on friday night and \r\nstayed until sunday, drinking whiskey at one point, \r\ndrinking a mimosa at one point, eating mushrooms at another \r\npoint. my hair was dirty and i borrowed her shirts and her \r\nsilk pants and life was really perfect then, kind of like it is now.\r\n</p>',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4201,1117,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','</p><p>you should read the book <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0312271921/\\\">no\r\n logo</a>:\r\n</p><p>\r\n<i>\\\"In No Logo, Klein patiently demonstrates, step by step, \r\nhow brands have become ubiquitous, not just in media and on \r\nthe street but increasingly in the schools as well.\\\"</i>\r\n</p>',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4202,1113,'2001-06-16 23:48:04',0,'szajic','responding to rusty:<p>\r\n\r\nI don\\\'t know anything about Iron Maiden.  But the GoGos \r\naren\\\'t as vapid as they seem.  If \\\"vacation, all I ever \r\nwanted, vacation, gotta get away\\\" doesn\\\'t express some kind \r\nof eighties existential longing to escape an absurd life, I \r\ndon\\\'t know what does.  Cf. <em>The Rules of \r\nAttraction</em>, by Bret Easton Ellis.  Holiday from what?\r\n<p>\r\n\r\nAnyway.  Probably not the best idea to analyze the GoGos, \r\neither (but but, see also the B-52s, \\\"roam if you want to, \r\nroam around the world, without wings (jet-set) without \r\nwheels (car culture)\\\"; sure they\\\'re coming from a different \r\nplace but aren\\\'t they getting at the same thing?) but I\\\'m \r\nin Boston with nothing to do until it\\\'s time to eat and \r\ndrink, and it\\\'s hot hot sweaty; afternoons that make me \r\nsleepy (but not tired enough to sleep, no).',3,0,0,0,'38.32.9.230','en'),(4203,1117,'2001-06-16 23:49:22',0,'dj1luna','radiohead were influenced by No Log to perform in a tent. \r\nfact.',1,0,0,0,'63.25.2.54','en'),(4204,1117,'2001-06-16 23:49:28',0,'dj1luna','radiohead were influenced by No Logo to perform in a tent. \r\nfact.',1,0,0,0,'63.25.2.54','en'),(4205,1113,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','look. it\\\'s stefan zajic.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4206,1118,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.eggthings.com/blueface.jpg\\\">hi</a>.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.94.102','en'),(4207,1116,'2001-06-17 00:14:16',0,'ROLLINS','rock on elly. i used to read The Pinion every day. where \r\ndo i get back issues?',1,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4208,1118,'2001-06-17 00:26:25',0,'kat','ha. i thought academics only \\\'talked\\\' about doing stuff and \r\nnever really did anything. im good at that. [really really \r\ngood at that] . . . look right here on the desk is my fancy \r\n35mm nikon. and look. . . right here is my notebook filled \r\nwith ideas of projects never realized. but i certainoly \r\ndidnt consider myself an academic. im more just an obsessed \r\nilliterate. i take lots of pictures with my cheap little \r\ndigicam. i really dig it. i dont think much about the pics \r\ni take....i just go with whatever inspires me. sometimes i \r\ndont even look in the viewfinder. shooting in a general \r\ndirection of the thing that caught my eye. they\\\'re much \r\nbetter than the ones i took when i was in art school and \r\nhad photography class and worried about making things \r\nperfect. i do lazy art now. it seems to suit me.',4,0,0,0,'12.64.84.116','en'),(4209,1118,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>whoever she is shes wack cause it aint true that \r\nacademics dont adopt new technology. its just that the \r\nnewest technology isnt always useful.</p>\r\n<p>it\\\'s never been something i bothered with though, \r\nso far.<p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'216.175.94.102','en'),(4210,1120,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','*waves* hello!',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4211,1120,'2002-03-15 00:17:55',129,'moebius','<br>the title should finish \\\"equivalent to hello.\\\" just in \r\ncase y\\\'all were confused.',1,0,0,0,'64.174.240.74','en'),(4212,1099,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','i\\\'m coming soon!  and call me dave cyan.',1,0,0,0,'207.205.216.105','en'),(4213,1120,'2001-06-17 02:31:07',0,'\\\"when harry met sally\\\"','... and that\'s how darwin and i met ... way back in \'01 ... \r\njust as handsome today as always ...',6,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4214,1118,'2001-06-17 03:41:57',0,'cyantist','-- austin, i\\\'m bummed.  i wanted to see.',1,0,0,0,'203.184.249.130','en'),(4215,1116,'2001-06-17 03:53:30',0,'mattie','i like to stalk myself.  nothin\\\' \\\'bout me on them internets, \r\nthough.  just some matt mccord who\\\'s a drummer in a sf band \r\ncalled \\\"tinfed.\\\"  maybe i\\\'m him when i\\\'m asleep.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.5.206','en'),(4216,1118,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','kat\\\'s right, it is not an \\\"academic\\\" who chooses one \r\nmedium over another, or embraces one habit of \r\nmaking things over another. it\\\'s actually a creative \r\nchoice to use old cameras whose product cant be \r\ncontrolled as easily as with a digital camera. the \r\nprocess is changed by the medium. now i sound like \r\nNPR. kill me. ',0,0,0,0,'216.175.94.102','en'),(4217,1117,'2001-06-17 04:06:41',0,'cyantist',' -- austin, how do i do that?  that would be great.  i \r\nreally love how you drive across the golden gate bridge and \r\nnarry a billboard is there to be seen.  it is awesome!  you \r\ncan actually really enjoy the hills next to mill valley.\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'203.184.249.130','en'),(4218,1119,'2001-06-17 04:30:01',0,'mojo23','fingers without nails can go places nails should never go.',3,0,0,0,'158.252.211.111','en'),(4219,1113,'2001-06-17 04:44:23',0,'jo','tonight stefan zajic called and we talked for an hour and i \r\nwas left with that feeling that you have whenever you\\\'re \r\ndone talking with someone who knows you that well -- that \r\nout of body, laughing is holy, conversation is \r\ntranscendent, type of feeling. <BR>\r\nhi stefan zajic. you are <b>large</b> in my mythology.',1,0,0,0,'209.163.198.48','en'),(4220,1113,'2001-06-17 04:49:07',0,'i heart pavement','what about the voice of geddy lee? how does it get so high? \r\ni wonder if he speaks like an ordinary guy.<BR>\r\n(i know him, and he does.)<BR>\r\nthen you\\\'re my fact-checkin cuz.',2,0,0,0,'209.163.198.48','en'),(4221,1117,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>here is an organization that supports municipal\r\ninitiatives in sf.  call them and they will either blow you\r\noff or send you reading materials:  <a\r\nhref=\"http://www.sff.org/\">San Francisco Foundation, sff.org</a></P>\r\n\r\n\r\n<P>here is the source for state initiative information.  i\r\nhave no idea if the processes are the same at the state and\r\nmunicipal levels, but: <a\r\nhref=\"http://www.cainitiative.org/\">Speaker\'s Commission on\r\nthe California Initiative Process</a>   ',3,0,0,0,'64.51.232.105','en'),(4223,1118,'2001-06-17 05:08:08',0,'kat','<p>lol. ive found it isnt at all easy to control the \r\noutcome with digital cameras. they have their own unique \r\nway of processing light. and there\\\'s no standard...so \r\nmoving from one camera to another means having to learn a \r\nwhole new set of quirks. and of course digital still isnt \r\nat all the same as film. not that one is better than the \r\nother. just different.</p>\r\n<p>course that could be said for many mediums. as well as \r\nother crap too. like people.</p>',4,0,0,0,'12.64.0.251','en'),(4224,1118,'2001-06-17 05:11:28',0,'kat','and of course my ramblings have nothing at all to do with \r\naustin wearing a sequined bra. lets do dinner sometime \r\nswinney. you bring the bra, ill bring some lederhosen.',1,0,0,0,'12.64.0.251','en'),(4225,1119,'2001-06-17 05:20:19',0,'kat','a chance to learn what other weapons you might have at your \r\ndisposal. and what does he have to give up?',2,0,0,0,'12.64.0.251','en'),(4226,1119,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<br><br>the five rules of fisting:<br><br>\r\nlube, lube, lube, lube, cut your nails.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4227,1113,'2001-06-17 07:52:33',0,'rusty to stef','<p>\r\nAs I said previously...  the GoGos were not totally \r\nmeaningless, but they had even less unique stuff to say \r\nthan Iron Maiden...  I liked the GoGos...  I like a huge \r\nvariety of music...  Your mentioning the B52s shows an \r\nexample of how many times the need to get away, and roam, \r\nand so on has been expressed in songs, in the 80s, and \r\nbefore, and since...  It is a common feeling, and we can \r\nall relate to such music...  But Iron Maiden sang about a \r\nlot of things people a lot of people never really bother to \r\nthink about, let alone write popular music about...  That \r\nwas my point...  Therefore, I would say, out of a lot of \r\nbands that you could use to inspire topics of conversation, \r\nIron Maiden is a great one to choose...  Perhaps I will \r\nstart some entries analyzing some of their songs on here... \r\nheh...',6,0,0,0,'63.229.86.150','en'),(4228,1113,'2001-06-17 07:54:06',0,'rusty','<p>\r\nI could include links to some mp3s, so people could follow \r\nalong...  I like that idea...  maybe I\\\'ll test it out in a \r\nfew days...',6,0,0,0,'63.229.86.150','en'),(4229,1120,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','i wonder how many of the same parties we were at.  the\r\ninstitute, the armory... late nights in the CC.',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(4230,1121,'2001-06-17 08:25:14',0,'jp','I have a few different types of recurring dreams, mostly \r\nbad unfortunately.<BR>The one that goes back the furthest \r\nis when I was a kid. I\\\'m at the beach at night. There\\\'s a \r\ncliff next to the shore. The recurring feature is the \r\nadvancing of the waves and tide coming in. Waves getting \r\nbigger and bigger, and I\\\'m scrambling to get up the cliff \r\nor find some way out. Even until fairly recently I\\\'d get \r\nsome kind of variation on that one. The constant theme \r\nbeing the kind of power the ocean has to make you feel \r\ntotally small and helpless. I\\\'ve had dreams where I was on \r\nshore or in a lighthouse, where enormous waves are looming \r\ncloser and closer. One where I was in a house on a cliff \r\nwhere I could see enormous churning waves and wierd whale \r\ntype creatures.<BR>\r\nI just had a bad dream like that last week. In it I was at \r\nmy parents house and the entire back yard was flooded with \r\nwater and there was some bizzare walrus/shark like creature \r\nsloshing around trying to get up the steps.<BR>\r\nAnother one is the \\\"where\\\'s my class?\\\" dream. In this one I \r\nhave this sudden realization that there\\\'s been a class that \r\nI should have been going to but had forgotten about. \r\nSometimes it will be I end up in a classroom for the first \r\ntime and I don\\\'t recognize anybody or know what they\\\'re \r\ntalking about but there\\\'s a test I\\\'m supposed to take.<BR>\r\nThe most recent recurring theme is the \\\"losing my ex-\r\ngirlfriend dream. It\\\'s either I\\\'m with her and she just \r\nends up getting lost somehow mysteriously and I go all over \r\nthe place to find her. Or a variation is I do find her but \r\nshe\\\'s to busy to talk to me. Kind of related to that one is \r\nthe \\\"being lost in strange city\\\" dream or it\\\'s more literal \r\nand I dream about Japan (where my ex is and I lived for a \r\nwhile). I\\\'m in a very large city with many twisting and \r\nturning alleys, underground subway areas, strange looking \r\nenormous structures.  I tend to have no idea why I\\\'m there \r\nand I have no money and generally just confused.<BR>\r\nYou know these recurring dreams aren\\\'t all bad though. One \r\nI\\\'ve had occasionaly is something of a lucid dream where \r\nI\\\'m flying around. I don\\\'t have total control but enough to \r\nknow that flying around would be cool. Normally it\\\'s some \r\ntype of enormous underwater city where I\\\'m zipping around \r\nlike it\\\'s an giant fishtank miles and miles across. These \r\nkind of good dreams if they\\\'re vivid tend to be in shades \r\nof green. ',0,0,0,0,'24.0.133.128','en'),(4231,1122,'2001-06-17 08:51:55',0,'jp','Hmmm... \\\"<B>If</B> there was a drug like \r\nthat?\\\" \\\"<B>Would</B> I take it?\\\"<BR>\r\nNo conditional needed, and yes I already did.<BR>\r\nI wouldn\\\'t say it\\\'s enough to \\\"know God\\\", or at least the \r\ntype of experience I imagine some people would have of \r\nthat.<BR>\r\nBut then why does getting to know God have to be so \r\ndramatic, and... conclusive? Why can\\\'t it be the whispering \r\nof the coincidences of the day, the transformations and \r\nconnections that finally happen, the everyday kind of \r\nlife.<BR>\r\nI consider drugs, psychedelic actually, to be something \r\nlike a panaromic view at the end of a road that\\\'s not going \r\nanywhere anymore. There are some really insightful and \r\namazing experiences you can have but it\\\'s *always* going to \r\nbe transitory, and eventually self-destructive. I\\\'ve \r\nalready given it all up for a while now, alcohol included. \r\nMy current day to day reality isn\\\'t nearly exciting/chaotic \r\nas it used to be and that\\\'s fine. It\\\'s much more \r\nstable/boring.<BR>\r\nThat\\\'s my new method of transcendance -- boredom. Not \r\nboring to me though, just for anyone looking in from the \r\noutside.<BR>\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,'24.0.133.128','en'),(4232,1122,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','a lesson learned is not transitory, jp. ',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4233,1120,'2001-06-17 09:30:26',0,'jp','And I just posted something mentioning coincidences, \r\n*before* I read this.<BR>\r\nYup, I have to say I am another person drawn in from le\\\'s \r\nsite. I was at work one day searching for something UNIX \r\nrelated and happened to come across the \\\"Hungry \r\nProgrammers\\\" site. \\\"Whoa, what\\\'s this?\\\" I thought. There \r\nwere a bunch of thumbnail photos for links and I \r\nthought, \\\"Let\\\'s see who this chick is\\\" being one of the few \r\ngirls among male programmers stood out. I was pretty \r\nimpressed because I hadn\\\'t seen any other journal/web-cam \r\nsites before. I spent a while tripping out on it all taking \r\nit in. I even sent some bad poetry I felt inspired to write \r\nthe first time. That was was around 98/99 so it\\\'s been a \r\nwhile. The strange thing is seeing through a web page le\\\'s \r\nlife progress over the course of a few years, through a lot \r\nof changes, in the background of a web browser. This last \r\nyear I\\\'ve only checked in every couple of months or so. And \r\nI started posting here when I got a new job a couple of \r\nmonths ago.<BR>\r\nBy the way, moebius, good idea to introduce yourself. I\\\'ve \r\nnever done that. I just started writing long obnoxious \r\nposts and the sporadic cryptic bad poetry out of the blue. \r\nI have bad manners. ',0,0,0,0,'24.0.133.128','en'),(4234,1122,'2001-06-17 10:06:24',0,'jp','Hi le. Yes a lesson learned is not transitory, but once \r\nlearned why keep it up anymore?<BR>\r\nI\\\'m not \\\"anti-drug\\\", I just prefer not to do them anymore. \r\nSome are mildly destructive and some are totally fucked, \r\nnone are worth my time anymore.<BR>\r\nI\\\'m going to avoid going off in any number of tangents on \r\ndrug/alcohol use since it could go on to long and easily be \r\nmisinterpreted.',0,0,0,0,'24.0.133.128','en'),(4235,1113,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','i love that pavement song with all my heart.  i loved it \r\nbefore i knew who pavement were.',0,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(4236,1116,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','is this because i stalked s5 on friday?  wouldn\\\'t you \r\ngoogle your future husband?',3,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(4237,1027,'2001-06-17 10:42:04',0,'decius','\\\"this bit here is a fallacy. relating violence to the youth \r\nof our culture ignores historical evidence in other \r\ncultures\\\"\r\n<P>\r\nIt sounds like you read me as saying that \\\"violence comes \r\nfrom America.\\\" I definately didn\\\'t say that. Violence is a \r\npart of every culture. What I said was that the NATURE of \r\nviolence in America. The way in which it manifests. The way \r\nthat it is used. Thats cultural, and as such is a function \r\nof our past. Violence does not work the same way \r\neverywhere, and some cultures are more violent then others. \r\nNoone who has travelled far from the United States and \r\nreally paid attention to the way violence works in other \r\nplaces would dispute that. <P>\r\n\r\nYou seem to be tying violence back into war. You provided a \r\nfairly good explanation of the reasons for war, which I\\\'ll \r\naddress shortly. Whats important to understand is that war \r\nis a subset of violence and one I was not referring to.<P> \r\n\r\nViolence can happen between societies and it can also \r\nhappen between individuals. I wasn\\\'t concerning myself with \r\nthe former. Furthermore, violence often happens for \r\neconomic reasons. It can also happen for other reasons. \r\nPeople do not abuse their children for economic/population \r\nreasons. Again, in my original missive I was not concerning \r\nmyself with the former kind of violence. I will in this \r\npost. <P>\r\n\r\nTaking that example futher, child abuse is not an instict \r\nand incidences of child abuse are not homogenius across \r\ncultures. Where does someone LEARN to abuse their children? \r\nIts a lesson that is passed down through generations, and \r\nonly fought through critical thought. The sort of child \r\nabuse that exists in the United States is most certainly \r\ncultural and historical. This is one example. There are \r\nmany many many more. <P>\r\nFurthermore, it is worth noting that the majority of \r\nviolent crime in the US occurs between people who know \r\neachother. The sort of random assailant crime that the \r\nmedia gets worked up about is actually far less common. <P>\r\n\r\nFact is that this should be backed with academic data that \r\nI don\\\'t have readily available. However, I think its so \r\npainfully obvious that I don\\\'t understand why its an issue \r\nof contention. <P> \r\n\r\n\\\"Most places with an extremely high rate of gun ownership \r\nand violent crime are places that HISTORICALLY were \r\nviolent.\\\" I\\\'ve seen many ATTEMPTED proofs of this kind of \r\ntheory. they are all wishful thinking at its worst. In \r\nAmerica high gun ownership is directly correlated to a drop \r\nin certain violent crimes. The facts are available to \r\nanyone who wishes to look them up, rather than being spoon \r\nfed information by HCI. \\\" <P>\r\n\r\nYou are totally misfiring here. I didn\\\'t say that places \r\nwith a high rate of gun ownership are places with a high \r\nrate of violent crime. Thats just not what I said. You \r\ncontinue to make a number of statements below that I agree \r\nwith although it seems like you think I don\\\'t... <P>\r\n\r\n\\\"i don\\\'t like the unions and socialism is abhorrent to me. \\\"\r\n<P>\r\nI don\\\'t like the unions either, although possibly for \r\ndifferent reasons then you do. I think that socialism is \r\ninefficient and therefore contributes to the problem of \r\nscarcity. I\\\'d rather have less scarcity then a more \r\nequitable distribution of resources. Scarcity is the \r\nfundamental problem that economy\\\'s grapple with. More on \r\nthat in a minute. <P>\r\n\r\n\\\"as long as i am a member of a society which doesn\\\'t \r\ncompletely violate my beliefs, i\\\'m peaceful, force \r\nunacceptable lifestyles on me, and i will turn violent.\\\"<P>\r\n\r\nOK, mind you I did make a specific arguement in my original \r\npost against the idea of forcing unacceptable lifestyles on \r\npeople... <P>\r\n\r\n\\\"i don\\\'t believe in \\\'human rights\\\', even if they sound good \r\nin theory.\\\"<P>\r\n\r\nActually I think you do, just not in an altruistic fashion. \r\nI think YOU think you should be able to think what you want \r\nto think, you think you should be able to have food on the \r\ntable, you think you should be given equitable treatment \r\nwhen faced with a criminal accusation. You sound like you \r\nwould be willing to die to defend those rights. Well, \r\nyou\\\'re not alone. Everyone has similar attitudes about such \r\nthings, and over several hundred years we\\\'ve figured out \r\nthat people in power who do not respect said interests in \r\nothers usually end up dead. So we\\\'ve abstracted the whole \r\nconcept and made it a matter of philisophical truth. What \r\ngroups like \\\"Amnesty International\\\" do is attempt to teach \r\nthese lessons the easy way instead of the hard way. <P>\r\n\r\n\\\"cultural consesus is about as workable as anarchy. and if \r\nyou think anarchy is doable, consider that me and mine are \r\nbetter armed, better trained, and perfectly willing to take \r\nby force if need be.\\\"\r\n<P>\r\n\r\nFreedom IS responsibility. What you are in effect saying \r\nhere is that you wouldn\\\'t have enough self control to \r\nhandle the responsibility of having to make decisions about \r\nwhat is right and wrong if you didn\\\'t have a government \r\nstanding over your shoulder answering these questions for \r\nyou. You\\\'re not alone. <P>\r\n\r\nI\\\'m not implying that anarchy is a possiblity on any \r\nresonable scale in any reasonable amount of time. What I am \r\nimplying is that its worth while knowing what the right \r\ndirection is so that one does not waste time walking the \r\nwrong way. <P>\r\n\r\n\r\n\\\"wishful thinking and pleasant theory will never be enough \r\nto fix the problems of humankind.\\\" <P>\r\n\r\nYou seem to be a fan of constitutional republics. Ever \r\nheard of John Locke? Adam Smith?<P>\r\n\r\n\\\"wars are fought over population pressure\\\"\r\n\r\nGreat point... Wars are usually fought because of scarcity \r\nof resources, which in effect means overpopulation, and a \r\nwar reduces the number of people in contention for \r\nresources, thus alleviating the problem regardless of who \r\nwins. \r\n\r\nThis, too, is changing...\r\n\r\nWar is not the only tool that humans have for alleviating \r\nscarcity. Humans also have science/engineering. They can \r\nfind ways to harness resources in a more effecient manner, \r\nsuch that they can server a greater number of people. \r\n\r\nHere-in lies my problem with socialism. Rewarding on effort \r\nrather than output incents inefficiencies that contribute \r\nto the fundamental problem. Eliminating scarcity is more \r\nimportant than equitable distribution. \r\n\r\nI have a problem with capitalism too. That problem is that \r\na system which places the greatest value on resources that \r\nare scarce also incents inefficiencies. Intellectual \r\nproperty is the most tangible example right now. Laws \r\nrequire competition over access to resources that need not \r\nbe competed over, because its the only way we know how to \r\nbuild an economy. \r\n\r\nAs our technology improves, our ability to operate outside \r\nof the hand of scarcity improves, and therefore we will \r\nneed to rely on war less and less to solve resource \r\nproblems. You can A. Go to war with Iraq or B. find a more \r\nreasonable power source. We\\\'re sitting on the fence. If \r\noption B was not available we would have taken Iraq over. \r\nThe fact that we haven\\\'t is fairly solid evidence that \r\nthings have changed in the last 100 years. They\\\'ve changed \r\nmore then they did in the preceeding 900. We don\\\'t need \r\nempires anymore. Think about it. Think about why...  \r\n\r\n',4,0,0,0,'203.184.249.130','en'),(4238,1122,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<br><br>\r\ni was at the same talk mark pesce gave; here\'s more \r\nbackground:<br><br>\r\nthe \"god gene\" is a reference to the emerging science \r\nof neurotheology (a hot topic lately; newsweek even \r\nran a cover story: \"religion and the brain\"). this is not about tripping.<br><br>\r\nmark pesce talks about two possibilities: either a world \r\nof humans who have achieved enlightenment, pushing \r\nagainst the boundaries of spirit and the unknown. or, a \r\nworld of humans consuming a hypothetical manufactured drug that \r\nstimulates the \"god center\" of the brain.<br><br>\r\nthe thought exercise is to imagine each possible world \r\nas an advancement towards transcending ordinary \r\nconsciousness. the value judgement is: which is \r\n\"better\", the drug or the spiritual process? are the \r\nresults the same? do we become a race of happy \r\npeaceful drones, enslaved by brain chemistry? do we \r\nbecome a race of super-humans, capable of infinite \r\npower or destruction?<br><br>\r\nis the brain a filter for the spirit, or is the brain the \r\nsource of spirit? this raises tangential questions about \r\nthe use of drugs (from zoloft to DMT) vs spiritual \r\npractice; questions about whether the spirit lies in the \r\nreductionist / material world, or as something \r\nundefinable; and questions about where we\'re headed.  \r\nthe topic of neurotheology has forced these questions \r\ninto center stage.<br><br>\r\nanyway i didn\'t intend to follow-up to this post (already \r\ndiscussed this topic a whole bunch after <a href=\"http://www.erowid.org/mindstates/\">mindstates</a> :) \r\nbut there\'s more context for all y\'all.\r\n',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4239,1121,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<br><br>recurring dreams go away if you release them; \r\neven just talking about them is often enough. \r\notherwise, the dream haunts you, as a constant \r\nreminder of an attachment to confront. face the demon, \r\nand the dream dissolves forever.<br><br>\r\ni wrote about my recurring dreams <a \r\nhref=\"http://saturn5.diaryland.com/010210_64.html\">elsewhere</a>. i love to know what people dream about. \r\nit says more about who you are than anything else.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4240,1117,'2001-06-17 13:12:05',0,'cyantist','-- let me find a new job first, and then we should talk when \r\ni get back to the states.  thanks austin.',1,0,0,0,'203.184.249.130','en'),(4241,1121,'2001-06-17 14:02:14',0,'cyantist','steve, did i ever tell you that you look like a cherub?\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<i>\\\"If you\\\'re frightened of dying and you\\\'re holding on, \r\nyou\\\'ll see devils tearing\r\n                                           your life away. \r\nIf you\\\'ve made your piece then the devils are really angels,\r\n                                           freeing you.\\\"</i>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n-- jacob\\\'s ladder',1,0,0,0,'203.184.249.130','en'),(4242,1121,'2001-06-17 14:03:10',0,'cyantist',' -- only problem with that paste is the word piece should be \r\npeace.  i should have read it before pasting.  :)',1,0,0,0,'203.184.249.130','en'),(4243,1123,'2001-06-17 14:13:58',0,'cyantist','-- sometimes fantasies should be lived out so that you \r\nrealize that you either wanted it to happen, or you get it \r\nout of your system.  everything other than the pregnancy is \r\ndoable :)  that\\\'s the one choice that should be made wisely. \r\n but, you know that.',1,0,0,0,'203.184.249.130','en'),(4244,1122,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','taking a drug is chaotic: you might experience the unknown, \r\nbut you\\\'re just getting wet, bobbing around, wading in, \r\nmaybe even <B>drowning</B> in the same waters you swim \r\nthrough, navigate, when you have a spiritual \r\npractice.<BR>why be a dabbler when you could do something \r\nreally meaningful for yourself and everything else?\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.5.253','en'),(4245,1113,'2001-06-17 16:17:53',0,'jo to o','it\\\'s my favorite pavement song, too. but my first pavement \r\nsong was \\\"unseen power of the picket fence,\\\" which was on \r\nthe \\\"no alternative\\\" compilation released in the mid-90s, \r\nand which i probably bought because it featured nirvana and \r\nsoul asylum. i\\\'d never heard of pavement.',1,0,0,0,'63.145.124.46','en'),(4246,1119,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','blatent dreams.  sometimes it\\\'s frustrating to see exactly\r\nwhere each dream comes from.\r\n<br><br>\r\nexample: last night\\\'s dream.\r\n<br><br>\r\na bunch of us were over at s5\\\'s house.  we were watching\r\ninstructional videos on how to be a good citizen.  my mom\r\nwas laughing at them a lot.  one of the videos came on and\r\ntold us it was time to fist mika.  steve said mika didn\\\'t\r\nreally like being fisted and would bite/scratch whomever\r\ntried.  myself, elly, and olivia all tried but we decided\r\nour hands were too big.  we decided it was cyan\\\'s job to do\r\nthe duty but elly said she (cyan) was very senstive about\r\nher very small hands (i have no idea what size hands cyan\r\nhas in rl).  i said that didn\\\'t matter, honor was at stake\r\nhere -- mika needed to be fisted.  cyan said she couldn\\\'t do\r\nit, it was just too weird.  we sat in a circle and had a\r\ndiscussion about how the prospect of fisting mika made us\r\nall feel.  no one was very happy about it.  \r\n<br><br>\r\nhuh.  destabilizing.\r\n\r\n\r\n',4,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(4247,1118,'2001-06-17 17:13:40',0,'qq','i use old cameras because I can control them better than\r\nmodern ones. A lot of times, even though I don\\\'t think it\r\nhas to be so, the price of increased convenience is reduced\r\nflexibility. I don\\\'t drag 45 pounds of camera gear around\r\nto make some sort of statement, I do it because it\\\'s the\r\nonly way I can get the results and qualities I want. If I\r\ncould make prints that looked like 8x10\\\" contact prints with\r\nsomething that fit in my pocket you can bet I\\\'d get rid of\r\nthe old monstrosity in a minute. :)  \r\n\r\nPeople get taken in by convenience and come to not even \r\nnotice what they\\\'re giving up. this goes for a lot of\r\nthings. I bet the art of conversation took a big nose dive\r\nwhen TV came on the scene. \r\n\r\nThis is not to say that I don\\\'t like digital cameras. \r\n',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(4248,1027,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','decius:  i didn\\\'t read you as claiming violence come from America.  i perfectly understood that you claimed violence in the US manifests primarily in our youth.  i would challenge any who claimed a) violence is due to the youth of our culture.  b) the violence is endemic only in our young.  it\\\'s just not true.  \r\n<p>\r\nas for tying violence into war, i think i did slip a bit there and concentrate on war a bit too much.  however, much of what i had to say is fully relavent to violence on a more personal level.  \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nthere is significant evidence showing that child abuse has become more and more prevalent as humans have moved from communal living, where it would take the acceptance of many for a behavior to continue, to private living.  of course what constitutes child abuse has been subject to quite a bit of interpretation.  by the standards of many places today in America, my mother was criminal when she reprimanded my younger siblings.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\n\\\"Furthermore, it is worth noting that the majority of \r\nviolent crime in the US occurs between people who know \r\neachother. The sort of random assailant crime that the \r\nmedia gets worked up about is actually far less common.\\\"\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\ni cannot argue with this statement because you and i are in full agreement.  i\\\'ve seen the stats and it\\\'s a simple truth .  random violence is most noticed because it is so shocking and dramatic.\r\n</P>\r\n<p>\r\n\\\"Actually I think you do, just not in an altruistic fashion. \r\nI think YOU think you should be able to think what you want \r\nto think, you think you should be able to have food on the \r\ntable, you think you should be given equitable treatment when faced with a criminal accusation. You sound like you \r\nwould be willing to die to defend those rights. Well, \r\nyou\\\'re not alone. Everyone has similar attitudes about such \r\nthings, and over several hundred years we\\\'ve figured out that people in power who do not respect said interests in \r\nothers usually end up dead. So we\\\'ve abstracted the whole \r\nconcept and made it a matter of philisophical truth. What \r\ngroups like \\\"Amnesty International\\\" do is attempt to teach \r\nthese lessons the easy way instead of the hard way.\\\"\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\ni agree with most of the above.  however let it be known that i do not see humans as having the inherent rights of:  food, water, happiness, pleasant surroundings, freedom from fear...etc.  freedom to try as best you and yours can.  that is what i believe in.  i would not really die to defend a \\\'right\\\', only a liberty.  rights are granted by the government.  liberties are reserved by those who establish the government.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\n\\\"Freedom IS responsibility. What you are in effect saying \r\nhere is that you wouldn\\\'t have enough self control to \r\nhandle the responsibility of having to make decisions about \r\nwhat is right and wrong if you didn\\\'t have a government standing over your shoulder answering these questions for \r\nyou. You\\\'re not alone.\\\"\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nyou are incorrect.  and firstly, you need to refrain from explaining to me what i mean.  i am well aware. and it is rather insulting.  i have more self control than you can imagine.  without being a member of a society that i value.  i will create one.  i will revert to a state of nature.  i will take from those who do not fit in my \\\'tribe\\\', i will build a new one.  that is not a lack of self control.  that is attempting to obtain a society i DO enjoy being a member of.  the government doesn\\\'t decide for me what is right or wrong, and i don\\\'t think i\\\'ll go into it on swinney, but if i\\\'m ever lucky enough to meet you, i\\\'d be willing to discuss it.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nplease...I\\\'ve stated in at least one post on here that i am a constitutional activist, or at least i think i did.  i\\\'m well accquainted with the beliefs and writings of the founders, as well as the writings of those whom they studied.  over the years i\\\'ve invested several thousand dollars in order to study the principles of our founders.  i read and analyze their writings constantly.  and i speak publicly on the subject, albeit not professionaly.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nas for your final paragraph i find that i am in TOTAL agreement with you.  i prefer capitalism to any other <i>economic</i> system, but feel that is should be tempered with human wisdom (aha!  there i go with wishful thinking) and compassion.  i have never been able to find a method by which we can retain our liberty and at the same time promote a healthier form of capitalism.  at least not without resorting to wishfully thinking that others will think as i do in relation to business practices.  most often i find myself in contention with fellow constitutionalist over this very paradox.  i find the behavior of business in America in particular, but across the world, unpleasant at best.  a longer range view will conserve our resources, find employees being treated better, protect the enviroment, develop newer and safer methods, and ultimately increase profits.  how do we force a long range perspective?  the activism of the citizens en masse would do it.  but i would find that solution acceptable only if it did not result in further laws restricting the liberties of those citizens.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\ni must admit decius, i hope someday we can meet.  i like what you have to say, even if i don\\\'t agree with it all.\r\n<p>',3,0,0,0,'207.205.216.129','en'),(4249,1123,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','i concur',3,0,0,0,'216.175.102.4','en'),(4250,1108,'2001-06-17 19:53:20',0,'sarah','<p>there are online masturbation and orgasm classes at <a \r\nhref=\"http://www.houseochicks.com/vulvauniversity/vu.html\">Vulva University</a> for anybody in remote areas or who is \r\nshy.\r\n\r\n<p>Also, I think one of the physiological reasons that boys \r\nget more worn out by orgasms than ladies is that male \r\nejaculation releases a whack of oxytocin, which i believe \r\nis an endorphin with a sedative effect. femmes have \r\nsomething different but i can\'t remember what it is.',3,0,0,0,'207.107.254.248','en'),(4251,1118,'2002-03-05 20:17:36',17,'austin to qq','what does a contact print look like?\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ni really completely understand.  egg\'s pictures look unique\r\nto me because if their manipulation and style.  i have a perfect\r\nexample, but i need a scanner to show it here.',2,0,0,0,'64.51.232.105','en'),(4252,1120,'2001-06-17 23:38:37',0,'moebius to xep','The institute and armory don\\\'t ring bells for me, but UCSC \r\nwas almost another life ago it seems, and for all I know I \r\nvisited them...but I remember well CC late nights and early \r\nmornings. that whole scene was a godsend for me. unix geeks \r\nhad the *best* parties.',1,0,0,0,'64.24.216.135','en'),(4253,1119,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','please don\\\'t fist my cat. :(',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4254,1122,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Red Moll','<p>I think drugs and sleep deprivation are useful, to a \r\npoint, when coupled with exposure to new information and \r\nnew experiences. Neural plasticity is useful.</p>\r\n<p>Useful for what? \\\"Enlightenment\\\"? Maybe. What \r\nis \\\"enlightenment\\\"? Finding truth? What is truth? If you \r\ndon\\\'t know what truth is to begin with, how the <i>hell</i> \r\nare you supposed to recognize it when you find it? \r\nBy \\\"feeling\\\" it? If all you need to do is \\\"feel\\\" truth, why \r\nbother reading or thinking or considering or discussing \r\nanything at all, don\\\'t all methods become arbitrary and \r\npersonal in this case? Or is it empirical, must it \r\ncorrespond to reality -- that isn\\\'t <i>enlightenment</i>, \r\nthat\\\'s science. Isn\\\'t enightenment supposed to be \r\ntranscendental? And what if we mix the empirical with the \r\ninuitive, what does that give us? Is that enlightenment? Or \r\njust two different types of <i>jack shit</i>? Beats me; all \r\nI know is that it\\\'s enough to deter me from using the word \r\nvery often.</p>\r\n',4,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(4255,1122,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p>a long time ago i registered metaprogram.com and \r\nmetaprogramming.com. i found a beautiful quote from \r\nterrence mckenna, and put it on the index page for the \r\ndomains (which don\\\'t have any content - just links to sites \r\nabout consciousness expansion). here is the quote:\r\n</p><p>\r\n<i>\r\n\\\"culture replaces authentic feeling with words. as an \r\nexample of this, imagine an infant lying in its cradle, and \r\nthe window is open, and into the room comes something, \r\nmarvelous, mysterious, glittering, shedding light of many \r\ncolors, movement, sound, a tranformative hierophany of \r\nintegrated perception and the child is enthralled and then \r\nthe mother comes into the room and she says to the \r\nchild, \\\'that\\\'s a bird, baby, that\\\'s a bird,\\\' instantly the \r\ncomplex wave of the angel peacock irridescent \r\ntransformative mystery is collapsed, into the word. all \r\nmystery is gone, the child learns this is a bird, this is a \r\nbird, and by the time we\\\'re five or six years old all the \r\nmystery of reality has been carefully tiled over with \r\nwords. this is a bird, this is a house, this is the sky, \r\nand we seal ourselves in within a linguistic shell of \r\ndisempowered perception, and what the psychedelics do is \r\nthey burst apart this cultural envelope of confinement and \r\nreturn us really to the legacy and birthright of the \r\norganism.\\\" \r\n</i></p> \r\n\r\n',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4256,1120,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','the armory is actually still around.  john dubois (spcecdt),\r\nzenomt, zap, bela lubkin, irene lubkin (pax), crisper...\r\nmany ucscb folks lived there.  the institute died in the\r\nlate 90s.  dvb (umlaut) and qarin (queue) both lived there. \r\nthere were numerous other geek hauses whose names i can\\\'t\r\nremember.  fwiw, i was the token underage punk kid.  \r\nsometimes seen with rusty, the even younger punk kid.  the\r\nCC was a happy place.  several times i spent the night under\r\nthe tables there when i missed the last bus home.  someone\r\nrecently gave me a blue adm3a that used to lived in the\r\nporter stat lab.  rad.\r\n',0,0,0,1,'209.228.7.6','en'),(4257,1122,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','yeah, chemicals are just about the only entre most people \r\nhave to something other than consensus reality.  they are \r\nuseful for opening the door, but the challenge is to learn \r\nto experience the same wonder without them. in practice, \r\nthey become just another attachment, something to let go \r\nof.<BR><I><B>sidis</I></B>(paranormal occurences assoicated \r\nwith transcendental practices; \\\"sidi\\\" is the term used in \r\nthe hindu tradition) are often very subtle, nothing like the \r\nflashbang chaotic disneyland ride of most psychedelic \r\nexperience. of course, they can be as intense as tripping \r\never gets, but more often then not, you don\\\'t notice them. \r\none day, you look around and think, \\\"hey, my life\\\'s not so \r\nfucked up anymore. i\\\'m not so moody; i\\\'m a whole person; i \r\nfeel <B>happy</B> every day. imagine that! it\\\'s like i\\\'m \r\nseeing my world through a different kind of filter; i look \r\ngood; i feel healthy and strong; and i\\\'m effortlessly \r\nradiating this joy to everyone i encounter.\\\"<BR>and then, \r\nthe sidis become only another attachment.:)       \r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.10.143','en'),(4258,655,'2001-06-18 02:22:41',0,'me','wow, you have the same name as my sister. this is a big \r\ndeal, considering not too many people your age have that \r\nname.',2,0,0,0,'24.202.17.130','en'),(4259,1123,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<PRE>\r\nmoving to another city\r\nbeing bored and reading books\r\nwondering who will be nice\r\nthere is this cool girl\r\ngoodbye\r\nmoving to another city\r\nbeing happy and playing all day\r\nwondering who will be nice\r\nthere is this cool girl\r\nmoebius strip\r\ngoodbye\r\nbeing bored and reading books\r\nchatting\r\nwanting to be in the hot tub\r\nhanging out with rowen\r\n</PRE>',4,0,0,0,'64.51.232.105','en'),(4260,655,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','there is a 12 year old chaya at school.  she does good front\r\nhand springs.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(4261,1119,'2001-06-18 03:07:42',0,'hh','and this nail centric boy would be... ? ',1,0,0,0,'24.93.61.58','en'),(4262,1118,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>a contact print is a print made by directly placing the \r\nnegative on the photo paper. thus there is no loss in \r\ndetail because you are not blowing up the negative at \r\nall.</p>\r\n<p>qq has a camera that takes an 8\\\"x10\\\" negative (v. \r\nthe usual 35mm). those crispy landscapes ansel \r\nadams took of like yosemite etcera are taken with 8x10 \r\nor 11x14 view cameras. nobody does it better, baby \r\nyoure the best.</p>\r\n<p>and im heeding what both kat and qq said about \r\ndigital photography. my question about technology is \r\nusually, is it capricious? and if so, where do I get \r\nsome?</p>',0,0,0,0,'216.175.91.214','en'),(4263,850,'2001-06-18 07:57:51',0,'ojigi','I\\\'m not cool! clever or funny, i think you have me mistaken \r\nfor a guy called mischa.. he\\\'s pretty cool.\r\n\r\n8)\r\n\r\n<a href=\\\"www.mischaiscool.com\\\" \r\ntarget=\\\"_blank\\\">www.ojigiiscool.com</a>',1,0,0,0,'194.154.190.2','en'),(4264,1119,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to hh','oh  hh, dont you savor suspense and mystery?',0,0,0,0,'216.175.91.214','en'),(4265,1123,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>chores, consumption of products/services, or \r\n\\\"dont\\\"s.<br>\r\nsew bed curtain<br>\r\nterry cloth flintstone dresses<br>\r\nget bangs<br>\r\nphone bill<br>\r\nclean up inbox<br>\r\nlearn unix better<br>\r\ndon\\\'t talk to strangers<br>\r\nfrosty highlights for the summer<br>\r\nflirtatious bob with bangs<br>\r\nquit smoking<br>\r\nquit drinking<br>\r\nno sex with exes<br>\r\noral hygeine<br>\r\ndisk space<br>\r\nphone bill<br>\r\navoid falling in love<br>\r\nlaundry<br>\r\nquit flaking<br>\r\nquit sniffing glue<br>\r\nno long distance luv<br>\r\nphone bill?<br>\r\nflinstone dresses<br>\r\nflirtatious bob, like a lulu bob, like silent movies<br>\r\ncancel land line and get celly?<br>\r\nget bangs.<br>\r\n</p>\r\n<p> i think its much better to be fantasizing about things \r\nyou aint done than trying to quit or avoid just about \r\neveryhting possible in this life.</p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'216.175.91.214','en'),(4266,1123,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<br><br>\r\ni can never avoid the sunrise, no matter how hard i try.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4267,1123,'2004-02-07 03:45:28',534,'griece','what are you even doing driving?  trade in the suv for a \r\nbike you earth raper.',6,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4268,1123,'2001-06-25 16:08:26',0,'griece:','er, <i>rapist.</i>\r\n\r\n<p>and i apologize for coming on so strong.  but I can\\\'t \r\nhelp myself.</p>\r\n<p> i just wonder how can anybody drive a vehicle and \r\nfeel good about themselves?</p>\r\n<p>the whole planet kinda sickens me</p>\r\n<p>your obsessions are self-absorbed and \r\nhedonistic</p>\r\n<p>go volunteer at a homeless shelter you young, \r\nignorant, snobby, self-important rich kid.</p>\r\n<p>go read a book and try not to tell anybody about it \r\nlike it\\\'s a special accomplishment</p>\r\n<p>this goes out to all of you little writerly \r\ntrance-dancing automotons<p>\r\n',0,0,0,1,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4269,1123,'2001-06-18 13:20:09',0,'chapulin','dear gracie, who the hell are you and why should we listen \r\nto you? should we feel graced by your self important \r\npresence?',4,0,0,0,'24.93.61.58','en'),(4270,1123,'2001-06-25 16:08:26',0,'griece:','<p>chaplin:\r\n\r\n<p>fuck yes, you should feel BLESSED by the fact I \r\ngrace this site with my wit and words.\r\n\r\n<p>people that feel that the are untouchable should be \r\nTOUCHED, messed with, <i>screwed</i> with.  \r\n\r\n<p>you are not untouchable in your little digital world. \r\nyou are sensitive and foolhardy.  you are quick to \r\ndefend because you feel that you are vulnerable.  you \r\nneed to be attacked and taught and torn assunder.\r\n\r\n<p>go cry, champagne.  go cry.',6,0,0,1,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4271,1120,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','hey!  I\\\'m new here too, but just jumped on in unannounced.  \r\ni admire your autobiographical post, though... i couldn\\\'t \r\ncollect my thoughts enough to pull one off. ',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(4272,1123,'2001-06-18 15:54:00',0,'chapulin','\\\"little digital world\\\"  hmm...get off the high horse. \r\nyou\\\'re nobody.',1,0,0,0,'24.93.61.58','en'),(4273,1123,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i think anyone typing on a computer made of plastic and other\r\ntoxic petroleum products - in a foreign country probably by slave labor, no less - needs to be pretty careful about who they call an\r\n\"earth raper.\" glass houses, etc. also, i don\'t want to have \r\nthe SUV discussion, can\'t one of the instances of the \r\nprozac discussion take the place of the SUV discussion?',0,0,0,0,'64.51.232.102','en'),(4274,1123,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','also:<br>\r\n<img src=\"http://www.gee.kz/peter/yc.jpg\">',0,0,0,0,'64.51.232.102','en'),(4275,1123,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to griece','<p>I love you. not the idea of you but YOU.</p>\r\n',0,0,0,1,'4.18.197.3','en'),(4276,1118,'2001-06-18 17:15:35',0,'20x24 polaroid','i am SEXY\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(4277,1118,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','does everyone who reads this know what \\\"elron\\\" is? that is \r\nimportant.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(4278,1118,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i once knew a jungle dj named juan. his dj name was \\\"el \r\njuan hubbard\\\"',4,0,0,0,'64.51.232.102','en'),(4279,1134,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p>hi. i changed your name to oof-boy because we have an <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://swinney.org/journals/userpages.phtml?\r\nusername=oof\\\">oof</a> here already. love, ed.\r\n</p><p>\r\nall the vegan restaurants in sf are closing. but you can \r\nget tofu mole burritos on haight. and there\\\'s lots of thai \r\nfood, vegan sushi at hanabi, vegan skewers at askew, vegan \r\nburritos at pancho villa (the rice is not chicken flavored \r\nand the beans are vegetable oiled, not lard, believe me, \r\nwe\\\'ve asked SO MANY TIMES). go to harvest market (market at \r\n16th) for vegan buffet, vegan cupcakes, surly dyke \r\ncashiers, vegan soup. rainbow is definitely the superior \r\nhealth food store. though there are small ones scattered \r\nall over the city. warning: the curly fries at sparky\\\'s \r\nhave beef fat in them. the other oof told me that.\r\n</p>',0,0,0,0,'64.51.232.102','en'),(4280,1134,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p>dude! the miso at hanabi is fish free!\r\n</p><p>\r\n<font size=\\\"+3\\\">SANS FISH</font>\r\n</p>',0,0,0,0,'64.51.232.102','en'),(4281,1123,'2001-06-25 16:08:26',0,'griece:','<p>A thoughtless and accusatory bunch, y\\\'are. All of \r\nyou.  \r\n\r\n<p>When its all peaceful agreement you slide down a \r\neasy slide, don\\\'t you  Enter dissent into the mix and \r\neverybody reacts, \\\'hey ho, -FUCK- somebody doesn\\\'t \r\nagree with our little utopian ideal where <i>it\\\'s all good, \r\nall the time</i> where <i>everything is true, and \r\nwonderful and valid and please pass the maple syrup \r\nplease because I like it on my pancakes and I just \r\nthought it was important to let you know.  oh, and I also \r\ndrive an SUV and want to fuck total strangers in this era \r\nof AIDS and yes maple syrup sure is good on \r\nbuckwheat pancakes. </i>.\\\'\r\n\r\n<p>Yeesh!\r\n\r\n<p>Community isn\\\'t onesided it\\\'s based on \r\ndisagreement and pontification and exchange and \r\nanger and love and fear and hate and loathing \r\nand...well you get the picture.  Don\\\'t you.\r\n\r\n<p>I use a computer because it\\\'s my livelihood.  If you \r\nchoose to drive a car, it\\\'s a choice.  You pay to do it.  \r\n\r\n  \r\n',5,0,0,1,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4282,1123,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','heeeheeeheeeheeheehahahahooohoohahaha\r\n',6,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(4283,1134,'2002-04-12 05:27:03',57,'weeb\\\'s belly says','<p>also! please note the following perfect pieces of food: the \r\ntofu-shiso roll at country station. mmm the tofu steak and \r\nfish-free miso soup at Take Sushi at 149 Noe st. *drool* \r\nthe bernal roll at Moki\'s in bernal heights. the tofu salad \r\nat hanabi\'s in the height. i think what i\'m trying to say \r\nis that I like tofu. yeah.</p>',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(4284,1134,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>go to oakland, eat fried chicken at the lake merritt diner \r\nand then have a drink at Baggy\\\'s By the Lake.</p>\r\n<p>something will happen to you.</p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(4285,1134,'2002-04-12 05:27:03',57,'weeb rectum says:','<p>for me, that \'something\' would be the hershey squirts. \r\nnothing speeds crispy fried animal product through the \r\nsystem quite like alkyholics. but! i do enjoy and appreciate the \r\nromanticism of fried bird and drinks by the \r\nlake.</p>',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(4286,1134,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','thanks weeb, im eating right now.*belch*\r\n',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(4287,1123,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to \\\"griece\\\"','<p>but griece, isnt your livelihood a choice like any other? \r\nyou could choose to scoop up jism at the XXX theaters on \r\nMarket, robotexan says you can make 40Gs doing that.</p>\r\n',0,0,0,1,'4.18.197.3','en'),(4288,1135,'2001-06-18 20:03:49',0,'auntie','coffee?  the answer is frigging coffee?  i am dying from \r\nliver failure and all i had to do was drink coffee?????  \r\nwell, i will try anything to keep off the transplant list, \r\nso here we go, coffee wired mom...',4,0,0,0,'24.162.119.106','en'),(4289,1123,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to griece','also, i am very impressed with your newly acquired html \r\nskills. go italics!\r\n',0,0,0,1,'4.18.197.3','en'),(4290,1128,'2001-06-18 20:16:27',0,'hedwig','<p>but I want to know what you haul back and forth for no \r\nreason.... *pout*</p>',1,0,0,0,'198.92.137.130','en'),(4291,1123,'2001-06-18 20:28:30',0,'kat','<p>wow. i didnt realize my mother was on here. hi mom! look \r\nat me. i can wave at you, chew gum, AND drive my suv all at \r\nthe same time. aint life grand?</p>\r\n\r\n<p\\\\>[you\\\'ve been around my whole life mom...and you still \r\ndont know me]</p>',4,0,0,0,'12.64.18.197','en'),(4292,1123,'2001-06-25 16:08:26',0,'griece:','<p>i don\\\'t live in SF, you sad little trendoids.  how can I \r\nhang out on Market?\r\n\r\n<p>the world is bigger than northern california.\r\n\r\n<p>SF is for over-educated and unemployed flakes in \r\ntheir early-twenties who think they are liberals because \r\nthey eat tofu\r\n\r\n<p>there\\\'s nothing important or interesting about eating \r\ntofu.  half the world eats tofu.  \r\n\r\n<p>why would you drive a car, let alone a SUV, in SF \r\nanyway?  take the fuckin\\\' BART you predictable, lazy, \r\nbourgeois freak.\r\n\r\n<p>yeah, i thought so kitty-kat.  you\\\'re just rebelling \r\nagainst your mom.  when you grow up you\\\'ll realize that \r\nshe was right.\r\n\r\n<p>why do you say that the SUV is evil and then try and \r\ndefend yourself?  you admit you made a mistake and \r\nthen defend youself because someone is more \r\nvehement.  \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n',6,0,0,1,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4293,1123,'2001-06-18 20:33:59',0,'kat','<p>\\\"go volunteer at a homeless shelter you young, ignorant, \r\nsnobby, self-important rich kid.\\\"</p>\r\n\r\n<p>heeeheeeheeeheeheehahahahooohoohahaha</p>',4,0,0,0,'12.64.18.197','en'),(4294,1135,'2002-03-15 00:17:55',129,'moebius','<br>I have recently gone on a 0 fat diet (or as close to as \r\npossible--around 35g a day is my target) because of the \r\nfact my body doesn\'t process triglycerides as well as it \r\nshould (that\'s supposed to be the worst kind of fat).<br>\r\n\r\n<br>But I was <i>overjoyed</i> to learn that I didn\'t have \r\nto give up coffee along with all the pastries, ice cream, \r\nand cheesy pizza! <br>',1,0,0,0,'63.38.74.52','en'),(4295,1135,'2001-06-25 16:08:26',0,'griece::::','<p>that\\\'s a stoopid diet, moebius.\r\n\r\n<p>the human body requires certain kinds of fats.\r\n\r\n<p>eat some nice grilled salmon at get those healthy, \r\nhealthy Omega 3s.',1,0,0,1,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4296,1123,'2001-06-18 20:44:11',0,'kat','if you cant laugh at yourself...well them damn. whats the \r\npoint?',1,0,0,0,'12.64.18.197','en'),(4297,1123,'2001-06-18 21:34:23',0,'kat:','I admit it griece.  I was wrong to post.  I am going away \r\nand never posting again.\r\n\r\nHEHEHEHEHEHEHEEHEHEHEH',6,0,0,1,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4298,1123,'2001-06-18 21:06:52',0,'kat','so mature of you to use my tag and pretend to me be. ',3,0,0,0,'12.64.18.197','en'),(4299,1135,'2001-06-25 16:08:26',0,'darwin to griece','<p>A surefire way to get people to listen to you is to call \r\nthem \\\"stoopid.\\\"</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n',5,0,0,1,'24.221.170.233','en'),(4300,1123,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','the \\\"YOU = CHUMP\\\" graphic should be the official \r\nswinney.org <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=1081.t\r\nxt#3923\\\">safeword</a> for \\\"this conversation needs to \r\nend.\\\"',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4301,1128,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','in my backpack:<BR>-black book (looks like a bible) with \r\nblank pages that i write on<BR>-\\\"glue\\\" by irvine welsh - \r\nreally good<BR>-\\\"jafsie and john henry\\\" - essays by david \r\nmamet<BR>-big folded piece of butcher\\\'s paper i\\\'m mapping \r\nout plot of new screenplay on<BR>-bundle of index cards<BR>-\r\nCD player with \\\"reveal\\\" in it<BR>-\\\"dots and loops\\\" in \\\"a \r\nlove supreme\\\" case<BR>-cheap trick, \\\"in color\\\"<BR>-\\\"the \r\nvery best of elvis costello\\\"<BR>-travis, \\\"the invisible \r\nband\\\" in \\\"the planets\\\" case<BR>-two pens<BR>-loose pages of \r\nanonymous dialogue and plot points<BR>-empty water \r\nbottle<BR>-a pair of scissors to work on collages whenevery \r\ni\\\'m bored.  i just got paranoid today as i was walking \r\nuptown - thought maybe they could be construed as a \r\nconcealed weapon(s?) do you think they could be?  knowing \r\nflorida law, probably. i\\\'m really thinking about moving.',1,0,0,0,'209.4.238.10','en'),(4302,1128,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','<BR>\r\nI had to read \\\'The Things They Carried\\\' for 20th Century \r\nLiterature... I wrote an essay about Mary Anne from the \r\nSweetheart of Song Tra Bong in my exam.... <BR>\r\nI just hope I pass, that\\\'s all.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'203.96.111.201','en'),(4303,1134,'2001-06-18 21:58:36',0,'sic','i love tofu...it is the answer to many questions',0,0,0,0,'207.62.162.110','en'),(4304,1134,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p>how could you forget axum on haight and pierce! \r\ndinner for N, please. prepare to get messy.</p>',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4305,1134,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','good tea comes from the castro st cheesery next to the\r\ncastro theater.  avoid the cheese though.',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(4306,1134,'2001-06-19 00:13:39',0,'oof-boy','WOW!  You people are really awesome.  I\\\'m going to be here \r\nfor a little while longer and it will be great to have \r\nsomething yummy to eat while i am here!  THANK YOU!',1,0,0,0,'216.34.244.18','en'),(4307,1134,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p>\r\noh also - there is some conjecture floating around \r\nabout the nature of thai food.\r\n</p>',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4308,1134,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','oh oh oh!  can\\\'t forget the cult resturants.  ananda fuara\r\non market at 8th/larkin and goldern era on o\\\'farrell at\r\njones.  the latter has really weird fake meat products. \r\nalso, vegan flan and vegan thai iced tea (with soy milk). \r\nshangri-la on irving or judah or something in the sunset has\r\nvegan hot and sour soup... also dishes that say things like\r\n\\\"this will cleanse your spleen\\\" in the description. \r\neverything there is vege and most is vegan.  mmm.\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(4309,1134,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p>\r\npricey:<br>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>joubert\\\'s - south african cuisine; family owned. \r\namazing.<br>\r\n<li>millennium - really foofy but really tasty. all vegan, \r\nbring your parents here.<br>\r\n<li>green\\\'s - world famous. also foofy but tasty. i\\\'ve had \r\nbusiness dinner meetings here (when the client pays).\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4310,1128,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','reading this reminds me of salinger, digging through \r\nhis characters\\\' medicine cabinets.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4311,1134,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p>\r\n... and i was about to type \"oh and breakfast at \r\norganicity!!\" ... but then i paused - for a moment of \r\nsilence ...\r\n</p>',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4312,1128,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','reminds me of castaneda: don juan advising carlitos to go \r\nahead and take that inventory, then throw it out \\\'cause it \r\nmeans fuck all.<BR>why does everything have to have so many \r\nmetaphysical resonances for me? it\\\'s like thinking you\\\'re a \r\ntalk show guest during every conversation. always on \r\nstage...\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.10.138','en'),(4313,1134,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','greens is the most un-vegan-friendly vegetarian resturant\r\ni\\\'ve ever been to.  they cook their rice in butter, have no\r\nvegan baked goods, put cheese on most of their salads, and\r\nthe vegan sandwiches they have suck.  grr grr!  burn! burn!',6,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(4314,1134,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','steve, thai food conjecture?  the fish sauce thing? ',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(4315,1134,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','yeah, what\'s the scuttlebutt?  too spicy to be \r\nsattvic?<BR><BR><B>ALSO:</B> what\'s a cult restaurant?  run \r\nby moonies? pls explain.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.10.15','en'),(4316,1134,'2001-06-19 01:37:05',0,'s5 to xep','butter in the rice?? i am shocked.',6,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4317,1134,'2001-06-19 01:38:40',0,'s5 about conjecture','yeah, the fish sauce thing. i hear it\'s only in coconut \r\ncurries, i hear some places don\'t use it at all, i hear it\'s \r\nin everything everywhere. i hear lots of things.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4318,1116,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>I have you all beat:  (<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.google.com/search?q=michael+jackson\\\">this \r\nsearch</a>) \\\"Search results 1-10 of about 1,800,000</p>\r\n<p>;-) And I didn\\\'t even expose myself to a webcam.</p>\r\n<p>And yes, that\\\'s really my name.  Ask LinearB or austin \r\nif you don\\\'t beleive me.</p>',1,0,0,0,'24.167.21.10','en'),(4319,1134,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>about thai food. most thai food has pork in it. i \r\nswear.  they sort of chop up pork and add it to \r\neverything the way mexicans add cheese to everything. \r\nand a thai restaurant in san francisco may not. most \r\ncurries are made not only with fish sauce, but with \r\nshrimp paste as part of the curry paste.  vegan thai food \r\nis a hilarious concept. but i bet it exists in san \r\nfrancisco.</p>',0,0,0,0,'216.175.105.120','en'),(4320,1134,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','we will send the vegan committee to do research.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4321,1127,'2001-06-19 04:49:28',0,'kat','i once came home to an extremely large cockroach laying \r\neggs on my pillow. i could only sleep on the couch after \r\nthat. of course that was until i woke up one day with a \r\nroach on my arm. thus went my life in Oklahoma.',1,0,0,0,'32.102.192.145','en'),(4322,1123,'2001-06-19 04:50:55',0,'kat','yea. im sorry y\\\'all...\\\'ive got issues\\\'',4,0,0,0,'32.102.192.145','en'),(4323,655,'2001-06-19 04:52:29',0,'me again','my sister\\\'s 20. most Chaya\\\'s are about age 12 because they \r\nare named after the late Rebbetzin Chaya Mushkah \r\nSchneerson, wife of the late Lubavitcher leader Rabbi \r\nMenachem Mendel Schneerson; consequently, they are almost \r\nall Chassidic Lubavitchers. As Chaya herself probably \r\nknows, the name means life or animal depending on how you \r\ntranslate it - (Chai-the root word- means life; Chaya means \r\nanimal). Anyway, i found it interesting - another older \r\nChaya exists who is also not a Lubavitcher.',1,0,0,0,'24.202.17.130','en'),(4324,1136,'2001-06-19 04:57:21',0,'kat','<p>*sigh*</p>',1,0,0,0,'32.102.192.145','en'),(4325,1139,'2001-06-19 05:48:08',0,'lulu','wait a second, why wasn\\\'t i asked about this???  dare i say, this is a splendid idea! you should squeeze as \r\nmuch as possible out of tits, and perhaps, just maybe allow a peek of that gruesome labia of yours....you \r\nknow, the one with teeth.  wait a second, can i participate in this peep show with you?!  hey we could even \r\nsell lulu and egg dolls there!  one could say \\\"oooooooh i\\\'m soooo awesome, look at me, i\\\'m golden!\\\" and \r\nthe other can say \\\"i slept in my bra again?!\\\"  and then her labia can snarl and bite.  \r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(4326,1139,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>you bitch. you break my home then you want in on \r\nthe moneymaking scheme. </p>',0,0,0,0,'216.175.105.120','en'),(4327,1139,'2001-06-19 06:15:05',0,'auntie','i knew a girl who worked in a peep show one time.  what you \r\nwould need is a window shade that would go up.  you \r\nwouldn\\\'t even have to let anyone in the house.  you just do \r\nit right out the front window.  you would need a second \r\nwindow like with one of those money pass through slots, you \r\nmake them give you five bucks and you pull up the window \r\nshade and give them a look, then quick, roll it down again. \r\neveryone will stand on the street and \\\"egg\\\" each other on \r\nto put more bucks in because the peeps are so short.  and \r\nif you let them pet your boobies, not only will they get \r\ndirty, but they will get sore.  if you make the peeps last \r\n30 seconds, you could make like $300 an hour if you are \r\nquick enough.  that ought to cover your fines for starting \r\na boobie riot on your street.',3,0,0,0,'24.162.119.106','en'),(4328,1135,'2002-03-15 00:17:55',129,'moebius','<br>I suppose I should add that my diet wasn\\\'t made up out \r\nof thin air; it\\\'s a mixture of advice from a lipidology \r\nclinic physician, a nutritionist working for same clinic, \r\nand my own commmon sense. Plus my girlfriend, who knows a \r\nthing or two about medicine.<br>\r\n\r\n<br>I\\\'m making sure to get a balanced diet, including \r\nprotein. \\\'Tis possible. Mainly I\\\'m avoiding saturated \r\nfats.<br>\r\n\r\n<br>I\\\'m just thanking my lucky stars they didn\\\'t cut out \r\nthe coffee too. \\\'nuff said.<br>',3,0,0,0,'63.38.73.190','en'),(4329,1138,'2001-06-19 06:21:40',0,'auntie','divorce sucks.  everyone should live happily ever after.',1,0,0,0,'24.162.119.106','en'),(4330,1139,'2001-06-19 06:30:48',0,'lulu','i\\\'d come back home to you if i could have in on the scheme, honey pie.  c\\\'mon honey nubby, lemme show \r\nem what i\\\'ve got....lemme show em my big hooters and rug to lay on! c\\\'mon, you know i\\\'m good for it. you \r\nknow i\\\'ll rake in the dough, and hey let\\\'s bring the thug in on the show, too.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(4331,1127,'2001-06-19 06:51:12',0,'s5 to kat','i wish i never read this. i\\\'m itching over.',6,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4332,1139,'2001-06-19 09:44:38',0,'sawks','this all sounds so agricultural!<br><br>\r\ndid you forget we were living in the age of immeadiate \r\naccess to hardcore digital pornography?<br><br>\r\njust go on chat, and tell guys you will play w/ your \r\nboobies if they paypal you some money<br><br>\r\nthen do it all webcam style...<br><br>\r\nadded bonus: if you are feeling prudish/sore you could \r\nfake it using a collection of someone else\\\'s pics, or just \r\nreuse a sequence of your own everytime<br><br>\r\n',3,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(4333,1141,'2001-06-19 09:47:29',0,'sawx','<br>\r\nsorry for spoiling the mood (kawaii!) but are you running \r\nos 9 or X le? - just curious :)<br><br>',3,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(4334,1138,'2001-06-19 09:49:23',0,'sawx','<br>\r\nummm, i reckon divorce is pretty neat if you\\\'re a kid w/ a  \r\nfuckhead dad who used to beat you up and then you \r\ndon\\\'t have to live with him anymore...<br><br>\r\nbut yeah',2,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(4335,1141,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','both. but i haven\\\'t booted into osx yet. i don\\\'t care.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4336,1138,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','hi.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4337,1140,'2001-06-19 11:10:48',0,'Joanna','When I started high school, we had this Big Brother/ Big \r\nSister mentory programme going on.  I\\\'d filled my form out \r\nstating I didn\\\'t want either, and so I was adopted by a \r\ngirl named Brittany, who\\\'d accidently signed up to be a big \r\nsister.  This was in 1994, and Brittany was from Seattle.  \r\nShe made me a mix tape named Jerry with genuine authentic \r\ngrunge and Alice Donut and her singing, and it introduced \r\nme to Liz Phair and PJ Harvey, and soundbites between \r\nfrom \\\'Sphere\\\' about aliens named Jerry and nutbars. It was \r\n150 minutes long and it was brilliant. My sister dubbed it \r\noff me, and my friends as well, creating the cult of \r\nJerry.  When my original died, luckily I got a copy off my \r\nsister, but by that stage, it was dub of a dub of a dub of \r\na dub of a dub off a live radio version in some cases, so \r\nthe sound quality is shite.  But it is still wonderful, and \r\nhas set the standard for all mix tapes to come. \r\n\r\n<BR><BR>\r\n\r\nInncidently,  if anyone knows a Brittany Tobiason who \r\nstarted at Evergreen University in  1995, I would love her \r\ncontact details please (or if that sounds too stalky, if \r\nshe could email me - joanna@hubris.co.nz , that would also \r\nbe grand.)  Thank you.    ',1,0,0,0,'203.97.2.243','en'),(4338,1128,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','...and, I actually threw out most all of that stuff after \r\nputting it in inventory here.  Why do I have this need to \r\nhave stuff live on?  Better here than in my wallet, though- \r\ndid I mention how liberating it is to have a 1/4\\\" thick \r\nwallet?  Heh.  I\\\'d do the bag contents, but it would be \r\nlong and weird- I\\\'ll do that on a rainy day someday.\r\n  ',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(4339,1135,'2004-02-07 03:45:28',534,'griece','<p>darwin, you\\\'re a dumbass.\r\n\r\n<p>I didn\\\'t call mr. moby \\\'stoopid.\\\'  i said a fatless diet \r\nwas \\\'stooopid.\\\'\r\n\r\n<p>and i like my choice of spelling too.\r\n\r\n<p>evolve, darwin.  evolve out of your petty semantic \r\ncriticism.  and read more carefully.',6,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4340,1139,'2004-02-07 03:45:28',534,'griece','<p>too bad \r\n<br>so sad\r\n<br>i\\\'m glad\r\n<br>i\\\'m not \r\n<br>your dad\r\n<p>XXX\r\n<p>if you go for it give drop me a line.  somebody told \r\nme I could pull down 40Gs mopping up all the sperm.\r\n\r\n',6,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4341,1136,'2004-02-07 03:45:28',534,'griece','car accidents.  not the small fender benders, but big \r\npile ups with twisted metal and red and orange flames, \r\nbroken glass and shredded rubber tires.  it doesn\\\'t \r\nmatter if anybody dies or not.  dot.coms going out of \r\nbusiness.  not just one dot.com, but lots of them, \r\nfolding like houses of cards and laying off lots of people \r\nwho then attend pink-slip parties with vacant looks in \r\ntheir eyes and suck down the booze and chat like \r\ntomorrow might be a little better.  brush fires and \r\nearthquakes that damage million dollar houses.  there \r\nwas one I remember where it rained and rained until \r\nthe house mud-slid down the hill.  then it caught fire \r\nand burned to ash.  surfers who die in the waves.  i\\\'ve \r\nalways hated surfers. the birds that protect their nest by \r\ndivebombing human beings, driving their \r\nbacteria-laden beaks under the skin.  boating \r\ndisasters.  high-prices for gasoline; i think they are way \r\nto cheap right now, try $3.00 a gallon.  a komodo \r\ndragon that bites an editor\\\'s toe off; now that\\\'s funny.  \r\npeople who fall of cliffs when trying to climb a mountain; \r\nwhose parachutes don\\\'t open; who strike their heads \r\nagainst overhaning shelves and knock themselves out.  \r\nbut mostly pink-slip parties.  dot.com layoffs.  i have to \r\nsay those crack me up the most.  cell phones that don\\\'t \r\nwork and people have to yell in them on the street with \r\nfrustration and anger in their voices.  people who walk \r\ninto poles because they\\\'re talking on their phone and \r\ndidn\\\'t see it coming.  i saw a woman crack her skull \r\nopen doing this--funny.  drunk teenagers who vomit on \r\ntheir own shoes.  scars.  the moment when you open \r\nthe doughnut box and somebody has already taken the \r\nlast doughnut and you think about all the cholesterol \r\nthat must be coursing through their veins right now and \r\nthey\\\'ve surely taken time off their lifespan.  smokers \r\nwho have wicked coughs and pretend like their \r\ncigarettes aren\\\'t killing them.  alcoholics with gin \r\nblossom noses who don\\\'t like to talk about their liver.  i \r\nlike these things.  slipping meat into a vegan\\\'s tofurky \r\ndinner and not telling them until the meal is over. haha, \r\nit is to laugh.  acting contrary just for the hell of it, to get \r\na rise out of people.  to jar them out of their provincial \r\nlittle minds.  funny.  gas attacks on a japanese subway \r\nand hoping it happens here.  in san francisco.  in new \r\nyork.  strange and futile cults that spring up and take \r\npeople to death, scaring most of mainstream america.  \r\ntrailer parks destroyed by tornados.  staplers and tape \r\ndispensers.  office jobs; i\\\'ve always thought the man \r\ndigging the ditch has it better than the CIO.  when you \r\nthink about it, he does.  ancient trees that fall \r\nsoundlessly in the forrest.  floods that ruin houses and \r\nbasements and render automobiles unusable.  car \r\ntheft.  nature encroaching on civilization and destroying \r\nit.  coyotes that kill the family dog.  history proving us \r\nwrong.  science proving us wrong.  writers that have the \r\nability to singularly mock a segment of society, that \r\nhave key insight, but the ability to remain detatched \r\nenough to criticize.  the deteriorization of the ozone.  but \r\nagain.  dot.com layoffs.  impossible dreams crushed by \r\nsociety.  hope for the flowers trampled by combat boots.  \r\nsweat-stained men with guns standing amidst the \r\npansies and periwinkles, breaking down the doors and \r\nstanding by silk-draped beds, breaking mirrors and \r\ntalking in loud voices.  yes.  these things make \r\n<i>me</i> smile.',6,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4342,1139,'2001-06-25 16:08:26',0,'lulu to griece','who are you? wonder woman?\r\n',0,0,0,1,'216.244.31.234','en'),(4343,1137,'2001-06-19 16:22:39',0,'auntie','you should print very carefully on the bottom of the \r\npicture:<br><br>\r\n\r\nYES',1,0,0,0,'24.162.119.106','en'),(4344,1139,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to sawks','<p>hi, youre right. how could I expect to make any dough \r\nmerely flashing a glimpse of the swedish twins when all those \r\nnet hos are out there doing it for free! cmon ladies, start \r\nthinkin. </p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(4345,1139,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','free the oakland two, egg, free the oakland two!\r\n',2,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(4346,1141,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','because it\\\'s necessary:\r\n<br>\r\n<img src=\\\"http://logy.org/~xep/splix/mutt.gif\\\">',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(4347,1141,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p> roommate tenderness is what its all about. this morning i \r\ncut up my dino jr sweatshirt into a muscle tee and jay \r\nshrieked, \\\"THATS what you are wearing to work today, miss?!\\\" \r\nbut then he put on the j mascis album and we sang along \r\ntogether, \\\"there never really is a good time...\\\"</p>\r\n<p>egg: what would i do without you? [sleepily looking on as \r\nhe wipes counter, makes coffee, warms pizza, washes dishes.]<\r\nbr>\r\njay: there would be no soap and the britta filter would not \r\nbe changed for 8 months. youd be washing your body with \r\nshampoo, or dr bronners.</p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(4348,1145,'2001-06-19 18:11:20',0,'bmg','<p>i was mugged about a year ago. During the course of this \r\nmugging my knuckles contacted this fellows teeth. Reminents \r\nof his teeth were in my knuckles, and i can still hear the \r\nsound of the smack. funny how that moment in my life seems \r\nto resinate in my mind as one of the bad and horrible \r\nthings that i have done, being that i was the one being \r\nattacked. I can\\\'t imagine punching my friend austin in the \r\nteeth and being able to repair the damage that it would \r\ncause our relationship. Hopefully he can\\\'t either. I am \r\nsure that I would quite possibly never look at austin the \r\nsame if he busted my fangse. I guess what I am saying is \r\nthat it sucks that you would allow yourself to harm your \r\nfriend, especially if you don\\\'t remember why you did it. I \r\nhope that it doesn\\\'t happen to you again.</p',1,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(4349,1135,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','i\\\'ve failed. this was supposed to be about love \\\'n stuff.  \r\nnot saturated fat in your diet, but saturated fat in your \r\nrelationship, caffeine in your love life, a bleached sugar \r\ninjection straight to the heart! woo! feel it!',6,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(4350,1135,'2001-06-19 18:18:40',0,'bmg','<p>i got it,  adam... but who has got you?</p> ',1,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(4351,1148,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p>actually, it\\\'s through insurmountable struggle that \r\nmany of us have found happiness. in some ways, this \r\nsite is a celebration of that. since your words look like \r\nthey\\\'re designed to rile everyone up, i suggest you avoid \r\nmaking any assumptions about who these people are, \r\nwhat they\\\'ve lived through, and how old they are. without \r\nrehashing everyone\\\'s sob stories here, i\\\'ll say this: \r\nyours are not unique, nor are they the worst i\\\'ve \r\nknown.</p>\r\n<p>in any case, welcome!</p>',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4352,1148,'2001-06-19 19:34:28',0,'Danielle','The Moon is pretty damn big in Canada.<P>Thats all.',3,0,0,0,'207.34.94.238','en'),(4353,1148,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','<p>pleez. i\'ve been poor. i\'ve been in manual \r\njobs, blue collar jobs. i know how it is to survive on 200 \r\ndollars a month. it beats you down. it makes you hate. you \r\nstart to resemble those homeless dogs with the half smiles \r\nof dementia, alternately whining and growling for your \r\nfood, feeling like the world owes you better. yeah, i felt \r\nlike my circle of friends were more interesting, more \r\nloyal. there was a more iron clad code of ethics. you had \r\nnothing except the next bad joke and big story for the next \r\nparty. you crashed and trashed because there was nothing \r\nelse to do. people would lend you money til payday. it just \r\noccured to me, that it doesn\'t feel like i have those \r\nqualities in friends anymore, even though we all make more \r\nmoney. \r\n</p><p>\r\nbut listen. i realized being poor wasn\'t the answer. \r\neveryone i knew then, was scheming and planning to get out \r\nof thier situations even while they were proud of being \r\nshitass poor. that\'s stupid. and dumb. most of those people \r\ngrew up and got out of their below minimum wage jobs. i can \r\nstill have close friends and make money. i don\'t need to be \r\nblue collar to be a human. it\'s easy to fall into lazy self-\r\nrighteousness, not realizing that other people do \r\ncontribute to community, do stand for something besides \r\ntheir economic strata. who are you? what do you stand for? \r\nwhat do your assumptions about other people say about you? hard questions. it looks like you have made \r\nmany a judgement of all of us without any facts. this is a \r\nsite for mental wanderings and dreamings. perhaps we do \r\nthis to escape our everyday, much like you.</p>',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(4354,1136,'2001-06-25 16:08:26',0,'darwin to griece','<p>Being a Satanist is as boring (and effectively the same) \r\nas being a Christian. Defining yourself in opposition to \r\nsomething else makes me sleepy. Ok, so you\\\'re \\\"different.\\\" \r\nSo what?</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n',5,0,0,1,'24.221.170.233','en'),(4355,1135,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>dude, i get it. when i got it, i get it bad. i get it in \r\nthe entire nervous system. i cant sleep/eat/focus, all the \r\ncliches...and my liver gets it too, cause i drink trying not \r\nto think. and then theres the bladder. i think im going to go \r\npee in my pants now.</p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(4356,1148,'2001-06-19 20:07:57',0,'jo','nicely said, steve and weeb.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(4357,1144,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','<p>peter, i love your photographs. i love your new \r\nyorkyness. you make me miss the city. i sound like a dork, \r\nbut do you sell prints?</p>',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(4358,1140,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>If you haven\\\'t already, I suggest reading \\\'High \r\nFidelity\\\' by Nick Hornby. He talks quite a bit about the \r\nart of the mix tape.</p>\r\n<p>As for me, I have regularly made mix tapes for people, \r\nprimarily people I was sweet on at the time. The first one \r\nthat I can remember was made for Dawn, at a time in my life \r\nwhere I was pretty intensely crazy. It contains a mix \r\nof \\\"Suck you Dry\\\" by Mudhoney followed by \\\"Drain You\\\" by \r\nNirvana. This was a romantic mix for Valentine\\\'s day, mind \r\nyou.</p>\r\n<p>I think the mix-cd is infinitely superior. Especially \r\nusing software like Sonic Foundry CD architect, you can \r\nmake extremely complicated mixes, including crossfading \r\ntracks into each other. You can arrange lots of little \r\nsnippets inbetween tracks and etc. I used to do this stuff \r\non tapes, but CHRIST was it a pain in the ass. I still call \r\nmix-cd\\\'s \\\"mixtapes\\\" even though they\\\'re not tapes \r\nanymore.</p>\r\n<p>The thing I like about mixtapes is that if you want to, \r\nyou can send very specific messages to the listener. For \r\nexample, a mixtape I recently made contains (among other \r\nthings) a chronology of my relationship with the mixtape-e. \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin',2,0,0,0,'24.221.170.233','en'),(4359,1136,'2001-06-25 16:08:26',0,'bmg to griece:','<p>haha, so funny. until it happens to you, then YOU\\\'RE AS \r\nPISSED as the rest of us that it happened... not so funny \r\nwhen the storm takes your own flesh and blood, when the \r\nguns take away your own mobility, when you are laid-off, \r\nwhen it happens in your town, when it takes away the people \r\nyou love, when someone laughs at the things that have \r\nhappened to you, or people you know... now is that so \r\nfunny... anything else you can laugh at? I am sure you got \r\nmore in there, you are doing good - get it all out big guy. \r\n</p> ',1,0,0,1,'66.68.76.248','en'),(4360,1148,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>i once lit my screen door on fire just to see what would \r\nhappen.  it burst into flames rapidly.  then i had to fix \r\nit.  it was annoying but now i know how to fix screen \r\ndoors.  come to think of it, most of the outcomes that i \r\nhave caused and regretted have stemmed from just wanting to \r\nsee what would happen.  i have never been curious about \r\npain.  i find out all that i need to know about that in the \r\ncourse of life.  like when i broke my finger on a \r\nbasketball.  or when my bed cought on fire.  or when i get \r\nin fights with my friends and family and stop talking to \r\nthem.  or when i betray someone.  i learn most things from \r\njust seeing what would happen if ...</P>\r\n\r\n<P>when i was 4 i lived in cleveland.  at the forth of july \r\nparade in our neighborhood, some kid took my bike and was \r\nriding it around in the cul-de-sac.  i have pictures of him \r\non my bike, vivid ones.  my bike was really beautiful.  it \r\nwas red white grips and training wheels.  there were red \r\nwhite and blue cray paper strips threaded in the spokes, \r\nand red white and blue streemers at the ends of the handle \r\nbars.  i dont remember how i got the bike back from him.  i \r\nconsider that i would not know what my bike looked like \r\ntoday had it not been taken by that boy.  to see him riding \r\nit around like that, filling my little mind with emotion \r\ncaused me to remember that moment vividly.  emotion is \r\nquite an elixir for memory.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>O cleveland of \\\'78, land of hot dogs and potato salad, \r\nfourth of july parades and houses with more than one \r\nlevel.  then the \\\'80s happened.</P>',3,0,0,0,'205.179.19.80','en'),(4361,1148,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>While many people in this \\\"community\\\" <u>are</u>, in \r\nfact, overly optimistic or idealistic, this doesn\\\'t mean \r\nthat they haven\\\'t faced the kind of challenges that you \r\nhave. They\\\'ve just had a different reaction to their \r\nchallenges.</P>\r\n<p>I understand that you\\\'re revolted by the relentless \r\npositivity, and I assure you you\\\'re not the only one. \r\nHowever, glorification of the kind of hopelessness involved \r\nin drunkenly breaking your friends teeth, or breaking your \r\nown finger.. I can\\\'t understand that. Relentless negativity \r\nis just as boring and naueseating as relentless \r\npositivity.</P>\r\n<p>It sounds like you have a drinking problem. Worse, it \r\nsounds like you\\\'re <u>proud</u> of it. Why?\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n',5,0,0,0,'24.221.170.233','en'),(4362,1136,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','to darwin and bmg:  perhaps this was just his rather weak way in telling me that my article was no good.  more to the point however, consider that sooner or later he\'ll meet someone like me.  and then he\'ll learn the hard way.  i\'ve had alot of problems with so-called satanists...sometimes they remind me of prey.',0,0,0,0,'207.205.220.143','en'),(4363,1135,'2001-06-25 16:08:26',0,'darwin to griece','<p>So let me get this straight. You\\\'re contradicting \r\nmy \\\"petty semantic criticism\\\" with.. a semantic criticism?\r\n</p>\r\n<p>If someone decides to do something, and you call that \r\nthing \\\"stoo[o]pid\\\", can you grasp the implication that that \r\n<u>person</u> is \\\"stoo[o]pid\\\"?</p>\r\n<p>I will say it again. Calling someone (or their \r\nactions) \\\"stoo[o]pid\\\" is a surefire way to get them to \r\ncompletely tune you out.</p>\r\n<p>But you knew that already.</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n\r\n',6,0,0,1,'24.221.170.233','en'),(4364,1136,'2004-02-07 03:45:28',534,'griece','<p>too my little bmg,\r\n\r\n<p>Smoke curling into a blue sky, something is \r\nburning but what?  What?  A woman forcing a laugh in \r\nan apartment three flights up.  All you hear is her voice.  \r\nDead plants in a window box.  Rubber tires, socks and \r\ncondoms in the gutter.  Porno book stores.   The feeling \r\nof loss you get when you pick up the phone and no one \r\nis there.  Empty diners.  Cracked coffee cups.  \r\nRoller-bladers, skateboarders and mountain bikers \r\nwith compound fractures.  Mining disasters.  And \r\ndotcom layoffs.  Those crack me up.  Computer \r\nsystems that crash at crucial moments.  Shoelaces that \r\nbreak right before your job interview.  People who don\\\'t \r\nknow saracasm when they see it.  Bungee cords that \r\nbreak and your luggage is spewed out over the \r\ninterstate.  Going down to the basement to find the \r\nfamily cat toying with a dead rat.  Windstorms that blow \r\nover trees.  The child playing with a box of melted \r\ncrayons.  Paper cuts.  Drinking enough whiskey  so that \r\nwhen your head hits the pillow you fall into a dreamless \r\nsleep.  Spilling hot coffee and getting blistered.  Cracks \r\nin the wall, crumbling stone.  A flashlight with dead \r\nbatteries during a blackout.  Public telephones that \r\ncannot receive phone calls.  Paper clips and rubber \r\ncement.  Squatters who live in empty buildings.   The \r\nbusiness man who tips over a fire hydrant, tears his \r\nslacks and pops his kneecap out of joint.  These \r\nthings, these things too, warm my heart.',6,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4365,1141,'2001-06-19 20:56:39',0,'kat','<p>i miss my old roommate. i worked at home...she in an \r\noffice. we\\\'d page each other in between sending obnoxious \r\nemails about plans for dinner. [more fun than when we were \r\nin gradeschool together. ha] she\\\'d bring home ice cream for \r\nme and even sometimes bake cookies. we once went to the \r\nanimal shelter and picked out a kitty. my dog loves that \r\ncat. i love that cat. my roommate loves that cat. ....we \r\nwere one big happy girl family.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>then i decided i just had to live in my truck for months \r\non end...just to see what it was like.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>what the hell was i thinking???</p>',1,0,0,0,'32.102.196.58','en'),(4366,1148,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','wow, even more arrogant than i am.  nice.  i know what you\\\'re talking about.  i\\\'ve seen the moon from several cities in Ohio, including Cleveland.  i didn\\\'t think much of it, i didn\\\'t like Ohio, i met alot of people like you there.  right hard cases, or so they thought.  unable to step back from themselves long enough to regain their humanity for even one moment.  i\\\'ve been out of work, been homeless.  i know about fighting your friends and moving past it.  i know about hard places and hard times.  so what?  some of the people here have suffered too, not the same way as you, or the same way as i have; but their lives are every bit as tangible as yours.  don\\\'t pull up a fucking chair, lean back, and tell everyone how it is.  it\\\'s never that simple.  maybe you should shut the fuck up, sit the fuck down, and learn something from the people here.  i think they know some important things you don\\\'t.  as i know from my life, being a tough guy is easy; being more than that takes hard work and alot of introspection.  are you anything more than a thug?  i\\\'d like to see.',6,0,0,0,'207.205.220.143','en'),(4367,1136,'2004-02-07 03:45:28',534,'griece','<p>incitor, i never said i was a satanist.  that was \r\ndarwin who made a comparison between how you \r\nlisted good things and I listed supposedly bad things.  \r\nhe thought that perhaps I was just being contrary to \r\nyour opinion and not just making a list of my own.  \r\n<p>i was not really judging you, or making a comment, \r\njust adding another voice to the conversation.  \r\n<p>more to the point, it seems that you are doing more \r\nof the judging, relating me to \\\"prey\\\" is just a little more \r\nthan a veiled threat.  do you live near cleveland?  you \r\ndon\\\'t seem to have the california voice that the majority \r\nof the other writers on this site seem to have.  i would \r\nguess that you\\\'re probably from the east coast.  am I \r\nright?\r\n<p>anyhow.  i would be hypocritical if I said that I didn\\\'t \r\njudge people.  i do.  my opinions are swift and \r\nsometimes severe, but believe me when I say I wasn\\\'t \r\njudging you.  I especially like the bit about \\\'cleaning the \r\nguns while watching the simpsons\\\' so perfectly white \r\ntrash, i laughed out loud.',6,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4368,1148,'2001-06-25 16:08:26',0,'griece:','<p>darwin, \r\n\r\n<p>I would guess from your comment that you don\\\'t \r\ndrink <i>enough</i>\r\n\r\n<p>incitor,\r\n\r\n<p>more later, buddy, it sounds like we may be two of a \r\nkind.',1,0,0,1,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4369,1148,'2001-06-19 21:10:45',0,'kat','if you dig a bit youd be surprised at what you find. \r\ndifferent from what you first expected. any place is as \r\ngood or as bad as another. hell exists in suburbia. \r\nparadise in the ghetto. if you want to look at it that way. \r\nwe all have our own cross to carry. what i see in the moon \r\nis what i leave myself open too.',2,0,0,0,'32.102.196.58','en'),(4370,1145,'2001-06-19 21:19:38',0,'chapulin','jaysus. you evil Frigid bitch.<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.geocities.com/ch_colorado/\\\">el chapulin \r\n</a> ',6,0,0,0,'24.93.61.58','en'),(4371,1136,'2001-06-19 21:21:52',0,'bmg','<p>oh come on now, we aren\\\'t here to compare dick sizes are \r\nwe? Fuck man, griece, you have got life all wrong, friend. \r\nYou talk really tough behind networks and servers. What was \r\nit that made you so strong? What makes you talk so tuff? I \r\nsee that you come here, invoking all sorts of rants, but \r\nfor what cause? your cause, if so, what is your cause? do \r\nwish we all act like you? your words dont scare me, nor \r\nothers, they just make me sad... sad for you. i cry for \r\nyou, i really, really do.</p><p>diversity has its prices, \r\nI\\\'m not giving in nonetheless. your words don\\\'t move me, \r\nthey are what i have learned to expect out of you... how \r\nlong have you lived like this? Is it working for you? Do \r\npeople like you, do they flock to you? Do people look up to \r\nyou in your hood? You have done good, i am for certain, \r\nonly i am not sure you would admit it.</p>',1,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(4372,1148,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>De La Soul has this to say about ghettos everywhere :<p>\r\n<pre>\r\n\\\"If ghetto thang can have its way in ghetto rage\r\nThen there must be some ghetto love and ghetto change\\\"\r\n</pre>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'24.221.170.233','en'),(4373,1136,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','yeah.  i live near cleveland.  pittsburgh.  been out there for a show now and again, or to visit friends.  threat.  no.  what\\\'s the point of threats over the internet, eh?  your kind are prey, mine too.  there\\\'s always someone tougher.  always. \r\n<p>\r\ni don\\\'t care if you judge me.  like you i make hard judgements, often quickly.  and yeah, i\\\'m from the east, but don\\\'t play it off like you have special skills pal.  a little reading could have shown you where i\\\'m from.  \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nyou sound like the skinheads around here.  so full of the working class hero bullshit.  i fell into that trap and have spent the last five years of my life trying to get the fuck out.  verbally bashing people is no better than randomly picking fights outside of bars.  the only people impressed are scum and yourself.  are you scum?  i\\\'m reserving judgement.  like you said, we could be two of a kind.  i know what it\\\'s like to be the hard man, the one who\\\'s stuck outside.  but i stopped letting that be my excuse for being a prick long ago.  have you?  you think cleaning a gun while watching the simpsons is white trash do you?  funny.  i think it\\\'s relaxing.  drinking myself into oblivion all the time, trying to hide my weaknesses in a bender.  letting the high become my excuse and my salvation at the same time.  that is white trash in my world.  \r\n</p>',3,0,0,0,'207.205.220.143','en'),(4374,1148,'2004-02-07 03:45:28',534,'griece','<p>darwin...\r\n<p>forgive me, what is a \\\"thang?\\\"\r\n',6,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4375,1148,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','don\\\'t be a tosser.  if you don\\\'t already know, you can figure it out.  ',4,0,0,0,'207.205.220.143','en'),(4376,1148,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>on the off chance that you\\\'re serious, the song is \r\ncalled \\\"ghetto thang\\\" which is of course slang for \\\"ghetto \r\nthing\\\" by which they are referring to the phrase \\\"it\\\'s a \r\nghetto thing\\\" as in \\\"it\\\'s a ghetto thing, you wouldn\\\'t \r\nunderstand\\\".</p>\r\n<p>They\\\'re trying to explain that people identify rage and \r\nhate and violence as \\\"ghetto things\\\", but that love and \r\nchange and peace are also \\\"ghetto things\\\"..</p>\r\n<p>Clear enough?</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n',1,0,0,0,'24.221.170.233','en'),(4377,1136,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','<p>\r\n\\\"the california voice\\\"\r\n<br>\r\nwhat is this exactly?<br>\r\n',4,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(4378,1141,'2002-03-15 00:17:55',129,'moebius','<br>this was a fine piece. those unknown noises in the \r\nnight and the security of good roommates. I was reminded of \r\nthe mockingbird that tortured us last year: they\\\'re \r\nnondescript little grey-brown critters by day, but at the \r\nwitching hour they morph into insomniac night-terrors.</br>\r\n\r\n<br>imagine one of those car alarms that changes tones and \r\nfrequency every two or three seconds when it\\\'s set off. now \r\nimagine that alarm going on for five hours, beginning at \r\nroughly 12:30 am. add to that the fact that the alarm has a \r\nseemingly infinite number of tones that are rarely \r\nrepeated. now put it in a tree in your next door neighbor\\\'s \r\nyard and set your work alarm for 6am. repeat nightly for \r\nabout six weeks. we got through it by investing in a tall \r\njar of earplugs.</br>\r\n\r\n<br>i also loved the \\\"rectangle of possibility\\\" line...i \r\nrecently purchased my first laptop (after working on \r\nlaptops provided by various jobs for years) and i loves it \r\nso. but it\\\'s a dell inspiron.</br>',1,0,0,0,'64.174.240.74','en'),(4379,1148,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','my parents were always pretty well off.  i never went \r\nhungry, except when i refused to eat my brussel sprouts.  \r\nas a teenager i ran away, slept in clothing bins, drank \r\nheavily, had sex with lots of people.  i worked ever since \r\nit was legal - 13, slogging away at the supermarket deli, \r\nhungover all the time, and grossed out by slicing ox tongue \r\nfor little old ladies to eat on their sandwiches.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nbecause i\\\'ve ALWAYS worked for money (i was mowing lawns, \r\ncooking dinners, shining shoes for pocket money) i\\\'ve never \r\nhad to be homeless or hungry by my own choice.  of course, \r\nnow i\\\'m 23 and have been working full time for 7 years.<br>\r\n<br>\r\ni dunno.  i lived in someone\\\'s lounge room when i made $16k \r\na year.  i ate a lot of pasta.  that\\\'s as close to hardship \r\nas i have got, so far.<br>\r\n<br>\r\ndoes that make me a bad person?  or just resourceful?<br>\r\n<br>',3,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(4380,1141,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','xi is the best room mate.  i can yell \\\"COCKSUCKER!!\\\" at him \r\nand he just gives me a shit eating grin, i can slam my \r\nentire body weight into him trying to knock him down and he \r\njust laughs, when i am poor at the end of the month he has \r\na well stocked change drawer which he insists i use.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nalso, he is taking the VEGAN CHALLENGE 2001 with me.  more \r\nabout that later.',3,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(4381,1148,'2001-06-20 01:49:47',0,'lulu','<p>griece, pft....nice name you self indulgent lice of a \r\nbabboon.  what is unemployment?  tell me, griece, or shall i \r\ncall you....QUINN?  tell me what you know about being \r\nunemployed, please, i want to know, being a kid who\\\'s never \r\nlifted a finger to work for shit.  tell me!  i\\\'m just gonna \r\nsit here in my cozy lazy boy and eat bon bons and drink my \r\nmartini as a tall skinny white boy fans me with a giant pink \r\nostrich feather.  go on...i\\\'m listening.  educate me. really. \r\n<br>\r\n*sip*<br>\r\n*fart*<br>\r\nwhat is a \\\"hard time\\\"?  is it like when you can\\\'t find the \r\nkeys to your beemer to go to whole foods to buy salmon steak \r\nfor your dinner with your lover?  or is it like when you just \r\ncan\\\'t wake up in the afternoon for the life of you because \r\nthe night before you snorted coke and drank champagne till \r\nyou passed out.</p>\r\n<p>lemme tell you something there buddy, i\\\'ve had some hard \r\ntimes.  like this one time when i went to the super market \r\nand i didn\\\'t have enough money to buy my caviar and don \r\nperignon, boy oh boy, was that a rough moment in my life.</p>\r\n<p>ooooooohhh QUINN, poooooooorrrr quinn, you\\\'re such a \r\nroughneck...a hard worker...a manly man....you\\\'ve gone \r\nthrough such tough times. you poor lil fella, you wanna come \r\nover and have some champagne with me?  cleveland sounds \r\ndarling, but california is wicked, dollface, just wicked. \r\ncome here and you\\\'ll become and instant celebrity. trust me, \r\nbunny, leave all your hardships behind in that lil ol city, \r\nyou won\\\'t have to work here in california, especially in l.a.   \r\nnobody works in this city we just drive around in fancy cars \r\nand talk on our cellies. c\\\'mon sugar muffin, i\\\'ll show you \r\nthe way to an easy life.<br>\r\ncall me!</p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(4382,1147,'2001-06-20 03:40:44',0,'cait','it beats the alternative.',0,0,0,0,'216.150.228.113','en'),(4383,1145,'2001-06-20 03:55:14',0,'lulu','i\\\'ll change your world, buddy. give me some bushmills and paps and i\\\'ll light fireworks in your world. c\\\'mon, \r\npal...show me what you\\\'re made of.   c\\\'mon, pal, sock it to me.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(4384,1147,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','i lived through my kidneys dying so i know how you feel\r\n(special diet, too many needles, etc), take pleasure in the\r\nsmall things like a sunrise or sunset, cool breze, a warm\r\ncandle lit bath, and try to remember that the disease\r\ndoesn\\\'t define who you are unless you let it. Stay on top of\r\nit, yes, but try to make it such that your whole life is\r\n{nasty illness}.  there is a cookbook, called \\\"just what the\r\ndoctor ordered\\\" (can\\\'t recall author, big tan book; if you\r\ndrop me an email @ p3rlm0nk@yahoo.com i\\\'ll ask the person\r\nwho has it now what the isbn is and who the 