ome over and look at the actual prints\r\nyay.',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.10','en'),(4400,1140,'2001-06-20 17:23:28',0,'moebeus to darwin:','<br>thanx for those comments. yeah, I\\\'m quite aware of the \r\n<i>High Fidelity</i> discussion of mix taping, and so is \r\nVowel--in fact in her essay she quotes from that book and \r\ninterviews Hornby. She has a kind of brutal take on the \r\nmain characters of the book (just keep in mind that she\\\'s a \r\nrock critic and is more-or-less enamored with the mix \r\ntaping thing herself):</br>\r\n\r\n<i>\\\"Clerks Barry and Dick are emotional criples stuck in \r\nthe mostly male pop culture of hell in which having seen a \r\nfilm (the right kind) or owning a record (ditto) acts as a \r\nsubstitute for being able to express what these things mean \r\nfor them. Since they are incapable of really talking about \r\nhuman feelings, they get by on standing next to each other \r\nat rock shows and making each other complicated tapes of \r\nobscure songs.\\\"</i>\r\n\r\n<br>sigh. and I recognize myself in that statement, to a \r\ndegree. which goes far to explain why I liked <i>High \r\nFidelity</i> so much.</br>\r\n\r\n<br>thanx also for the software tip, by the way. I\\\'ve been \r\nwanting to try something like that with the mix CDs but \r\nhave had a hard time figuring out which app would do the \r\njob best.</br>\r\n\r\n',3,0,0,0,'63.38.73.88','en'),(4401,1151,'2001-06-20 17:35:35',0,'counter-conscience','well, there is the writting...',3,0,0,0,'192.35.232.99','en'),(4402,1149,'2001-06-20 17:55:30',0,'xepmom','Come clean my house.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.174.155.3','en'),(4403,1136,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','bukowski lived in san pedro, california for over ten \r\nyears.  and before that, he lived in LA for like, 60. here\'s a <a href=\"http://www.smartpages.com/v/foghorn/beaches/southern/lacounty/sanpedro.jhtml\">reference</a>. ',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4404,1136,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','\r\n',0,0,0,0,'142.214.129.50','en'),(4405,1151,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<pre>\r\ndon\\\'t even know where i was last night\r\ndrinking cheap [BRAND NAME] scotch\r\nedge of chaos\r\nquick to anger\r\npours their drinks strong\r\ni saw him slash a guy\r\nhe had scotch, good stuff: [BRAND NAME, BRAND \r\nNAME]\r\nhe poured the whiskey\r\na bastard when he\\\'s drunk\r\nfucked up mug\r\ni lit up a cigarette\r\n</pre>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4406,1136,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','comparison is what starts war. comparison is what gets people \r\nlaid off and its what makes people think they are better then \r\nother. all we do is compare. it doesnt matter if you are \r\ncomparing good and bad, god and satan, dick and size, it all \r\nleads up to one person being put down and the other rising \r\nup. \r\n',6,0,0,0,'142.214.129.50','en'),(4407,1136,'2001-06-20 19:06:06',0,'kat','oh lordy.',4,0,0,0,'32.101.251.51','en'),(4408,1118,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to qq','<p>I can only imagine how beautiful these are in the flesh.</\r\np>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(4409,1150,'2003-07-24 15:44:23',165,'joker','i very much enjoy your writing, peter.  thank you.  and \r\nthough i know it should come as small consolation, i often \r\nwish that my life were boxed in brooklyn.',1,0,0,0,'66.68.187.34','en'),(4410,1150,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>when i lived in brooklyn I used to take the longer route \r\nhome on the \\\"B\\\" train so that I could peek out at the bridge \r\nand the magic hour on the way home or out. the way to live in \r\nNY is to keep your head outside as much as possible; the \r\ntendency is to draw inwards. keep your feelers open.</p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(4411,1136,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','i hate bukowski. he can\\\'t write worth shit. ',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(4412,1151,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','not bad...very familiar to the life i left behind.  is there more?',2,0,0,0,'207.205.216.195','en'),(4413,1151,'2001-06-20 22:03:27',0,'jay','this is good stuff for just off-the-cuff writing, if that\\\'s \r\nwhat it is.  Could be even better if add and edit... read \r\nsome Denis Johnson, if you haven\\\'t already.<p>\r\nI like what you got to say, my friend.',2,0,0,0,'63.203.225.62','en'),(4414,1150,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>\r\n\r\njoker: thanks, really. my motivation to post here has been \r\nthe great outlet it gives me, to turn my inward boiling into \r\nwords.  its given me a substantial feeling of joy to see \r\nthat my words are appreciated, and by such a varied, \r\nempathetic, intelligent crowd. i get the impression that \r\nno words on swinney.org are ever wasted words.<br>\r\n<br>\r\negg: thats so uncanny- I did the <i>exact</i> same thing.  \r\nmany are the nights that i rode the B to meet my love that \r\nlived at the other end of the line- the destination was the \r\ngoal, but the process was never dull- I think the Manhattan \r\nbridge gives one of the greatest vantage points in nyc... i \r\nsaw movies shot from it, police action on it, graf artists \r\non the go; all sorts of life blurring by in the twilight \r\nhours.  Feelers out, head in the open- good advice to remind \r\nmyself- thanks to you also.\r\n\r\n',3,0,0,0,'209.246.67.229','en'),(4415,1136,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','i don\\\'t agree.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(4416,1151,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','i agree, jay. especially jesus\\\' son.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(4417,1152,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>this reminds me, i have to get my red leather jacket back \r\nfrom patty. </p>\r\n<p> and. I LOVE YOU. </p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(4418,1148,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Innocent  Moll','<p>I never knew how easy I had it in life until I read this \r\npost. It\\\'s only now that I can truly appreciate my pampered \r\nschooling on the quiet, docile streets of NEWARK NEW \r\nJERSEY.</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(4419,1152,'2001-06-20 23:18:11',0,'