b on cleveland, and put all of \r\nthose bastards out of business..\r\n\r\nit took me three days, stopping here and there, to get \r\naway. it will be marked down as the best fucking thing i \r\never did for myself. \r\n\r\ncould have been a great city.. i know.. turned out to be a \r\nshithole.. i\\\'m sorry it took me so long to figure that out..\r\n',1,0,0,0,'64.81.71.97','en'),(4443,1045,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i spent two years working in boston. my only memories \r\nare of the freeway.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4444,1148,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','<P>when I was 19 I used to drink a lot of tequila and get \r\ninto fistfights with girls bigger and uglier than me. I \r\nsurvived. I lived out in the woods in Ocala, Florida for \r\nabout 4 months, growing my own food before I hitchiked to \r\nAtlanta where I had to survive by eating out of dumpsters. \r\nI squatted in a warehouse on Decatur Avenue across from the \r\nrailroad tracks. The bottom floor was covered in skateboard \r\nramps, grafitti, broken glass, and used condoms and \r\nneedles. There was a secret upstairs part that was \r\nrelatively closed off from the rest of the building where \r\nme and a few other people squatted. This was after being \r\nturned away from the homeless shelter at the MLK center for \r\nbeing female. I slept with my only pair of shoes tied to my \r\nwrist and with my violin case as a pillow so nobody would \r\nsteal them in my sleep. I managed to scrape up some money \r\nplaying my violin and did some drawings. I managed to get a \r\nshower at a kind strangers house and went into the Atlanta \r\nCollege of Art and got a scholarship for my artwork. A few \r\nyears later, I left with my degree and eventually ended up \r\nin SF. Does that make me a spoiled little kiddie? The \r\nsaddest part about your life seems to be that even tho you \r\nare several years older than we may or may not be, you act \r\nas if you are some angry drunken teenage snot out to \r\ndestroy himself and why not take someone\\\'s teeth out while \r\nyou\\\'re at it. Oooh what a big man you are. Grow the fuck \r\nup, pastyboy.',6,0,0,0,'64.81.65.205','en'),(4445,1157,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','actually elly looks really hot in that picture, I think.',1,0,0,0,'64.81.65.205','en'),(4446,1158,'2001-06-21 10:34:15',0,'kat','<p>those coop people know nothing about computers. i asked. \r\nthe butch girl is very cute. 360 would do me right but i \r\nworry too much about the dog that sleeps at the foot of my \r\nbed. the one that grunts at me when im restless. the one \r\nthat wakes me up at 4am wanting to go O U T. she needs a \r\ndrink i think. hell. i need a drink.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>le i think you forgot to add \\\'drinking buddy\\\' to that \r\nlist of myths.</p>',4,0,0,0,'12.64.18.35','en'),(4447,1158,'2001-06-21 10:40:23',0,'kat','<p>ps: i concur. Bronson is hot. if i ever get a cat im \r\ngoing to name it Mr. Majestyk. tho i think Billy Jack may \r\nbe somewhat more of a man then Bronson. more and hotter. \r\nthere is nothing finer than a guy who protects children and \r\nother living things.</p>',4,0,0,0,'12.64.18.35','en'),(4448,1128,'2001-06-21 10:46:31',0,'kat','i dont even have a wallet. cash, license and plastic in \r\npocket. we are good to go. i hate carrying shit around. the \r\nlast time i owned something resembling a wallet i lost it. \r\nand the 700 bucks i had in it. jinxed i tell you. they\\\'re \r\nall jinxed.',4,0,0,0,'12.64.18.35','en'),(4449,1153,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>\r\ns5: there are no two tangible things in this world that i \r\nadore more than my lomo and my 303.  both are old and worn, \r\nlook dead, but have amazing output.  good call!',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(4450,1161,'2001-06-21 12:13:16',0,'AMERICA','<p>\r\n<i>Written by: Neil Diamond</i>\r\n</p>\r\n<p><tt>\r\nFar<br>\r\nWe\\\'ve been traveling far<br>\r\nWithout a home<br>\r\nBut not without a star<br>\r\n<br>\r\nFree<br>\r\nOnly want to be free<br