at\\\'s up with the scrolling. it makes me shake my \r\nlaptop off to the side like an etch-a-sketch and then i get \r\ndizzy.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4495,1166,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','scrolling is the new &lt;BLINK&gt;',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4496,1166,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','<blink>LETS GET PISHED!!!</blink>',3,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(4497,1168,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','<A \r\nHREF=\"http://www.clas.ufl.edu/users/gthursby/mys/deikman.htm\">my \r\nfirst href:) hope it works...</A>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.9.247','en'),(4498,1168,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','well, shit no, it didn\'t. the url \r\nwuz:<BR><BR>www.clas.ufl.edu/users/gthursby/mys/deikman.htm<BR><BR>it\'s an article on mystic experiences from a kind of \r\nhumanistic psychology perspective - really \r\ngood.<BR><BR>also, anybody know where i can get sidney \r\nbechet\'s autobiography (\"treat it gentle\") by any chance. \r\namazon never heard of it. he was a mystic jazzman from \r\nn\'awlins. i wanna check him out.\r\n<p>\r\n<tt><i>fixed -- next time, include the http:// before the hostname. love, editor</i></tt></p>',1,0,0,0,'209.208.9.247','en'),(4499,1168,'2001-06-22 09:15:22',0,'tomato','to matt: you should check out powell\\\'s in portland, \r\noregon -- a very good bookstore, better in person, but \r\nthey have it.  it\\\'s out of print and in hardcover so it\\\'s 40 \r\nclams, but here you go:<p>\r\n<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.powells.com/cgi-bin/biblio?inkey=16-1\r\n112405437-0\\\">http://www.powells.com/cgi-bin/biblio?i\r\nnkey=16-1112405437-0</a>',1,0,0,0,'165.247.204.140','en'),(4500,1166,'2001-06-22 09:19:16',0,'tomato','necknape, where the hair meets the neck.  that\\\'s the \r\nbest part.  or just nice sunburns.',1,0,0,0,'165.247.204.140','en'),(4501,1166,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','<P><B>SWIMMEY.ORG</B></P>',1,0,0,0,'64.81.65.205','en'),(4502,1166,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','i like flaps',0,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(4503,1169,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i remember a day in oklahoma when the wind was \r\nblowing around the big green leafy plants in our front \r\nyard. i was in third grade there. i had two best friends: \r\nandrea meyer and a skinny blonde girl named mariah. \r\nandrea and mariah didn\\\'t like each other. my sister and \r\ni played barbies all day in the summer. we had a cat \r\nand a wading pool and a tornado shelter in the \r\nbackyard. the people who lived across the street had a \r\nbaby blue el camino. in the summer we stayed out late, \r\nbarefoot in the warm street in the dark. ',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4504,1136,'2004-02-07 03:45:28',534,'griece','<p>to weeb...\r\n\r\n<p>If you think Bukowski is bad, why do you think that?  \r\nIf you think he is a bad writer, have you read enough to \r\nactually judge that, or did you read half a novel and \r\nproclaim it shit?  Did you ever read \\\"The Night they Took \r\nWhitey\\\"  or  \\\"The Most Beautiful Woman in Town\\\"?  \r\nThey\\\'ll break your heart, my dear, they\\\'ll break your \r\ngodforsaken little heart.',6,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4505,1166,'2004-02-07 03:45:28',534,'griece','All hail the Some Like it Hot ref:  \\\"like jello on springs\\\" \r\nwords uttered by Jack Lemmon about M. Monroe.',1,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4506,1165,'2001-06-22 13:35:48',0,'darwin to auntie','<p>Auntie, similarly frustrating are the dreams where you \r\nare trying to get it on with a dream-lover but there\\\'s \r\nnowhere to do it or something stupid.</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n',1,0,0,0,'24.221.170.119','en'),(4507,1158,'2004-02-07 03:45:28',534,'griece','<pre>\r\nSteve McQueen \r\nClint Eastwood\r\nJames Cagney\r\n<b>Robert Mitchum</b>\r\n</pre>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4508,1166,'2001-06-22 15:14:51',0,'Jojo','I hail.  I prevail.  I entail.  I look for Wilder\\\'s film on \r\nsale.  Against the tyranny of tits I rail.  In this, as in \r\nall endeavour, I shall fail.',1,0,0,0,'209.242.148.3','en'),(4509,1166,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','some like it hot is one of my favorite movies. ',0,0,0,0,'216.175.99.176','en'),(4510,1170,'2001-06-22 17:50:41',0,'nobody!','so what happened to the Turkey and to Desmond?',2,0,0,0,'149.225.60.200','en'),(4511,1170,'2001-06-22 18:14:53',0,'kritik','seriously. don\\\'t leave us with a cliffhanger, it\\\'s a cliche!',5,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(4512,1136,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','hmm, i will have to check those out. i\\\'d like to read \nsomething of his i like. i read \\\'women\\\' and i \nthought it was sloppy and a really good description of the \nlife of a beatnik drunkard. but how interesting is that? \nyeah. drink. piss. wake up with some woman sucking your \ncock. hmm. *yawn* but i think it will just come down to \ntaste- some people can look at that and think \\\'what \ngenius!\\\' and i could look at it and think \\\'what a \nmisogynistic asshole!\\\'. eh.\n\n',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(4513,1166,'2001-06-22 19:42:32',0,'Jojo','Mee toe!\r\nI live in San Diego and go to the Hotel del Coronado all \r\nthe time (where Some Like It Hot was filmed)(mostly)(well, \r\nsome of it).  There one can bask and touch oneself as one \r\nimagines Marilyn basking and touching me, I mean, her.\r\n\r\nthat said:\r\n<blink>blink</blink>',0,0,0,0,'209.242.148.3','en'),(4514,1136,'2001-06-25 16:08:26',0,'griece:','<p>\\\"most beautiful woman\\\" is in the collection of the \r\nshort stories by the same name.  you can read it \r\nstanding in the bookstore\r\n\r\n<p>\\\"the night they took whitey\\\" is a poem in \\\"The \r\nRoominghouse Madrigals.\\\"\r\n\r\n<p>\\\"WOMEN\\\" is definitely the WRONG place to begin.  \r\nTry \\\"HAM ON RYE\\\" or \\\"POST OFFICE.\\\"',1,0,0,1,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4515,1136,'2001-06-22 20:46:31',0,'jo','or hollywood. hollywood = older bukowski going through the \r\nprocess of writing a screenplay adaptation of one of his \r\nbooks. some thoroughly hilarious commentary on show \r\nbusiness, writers, drinking.<BR>\r\nham on rye = lots of stories from his childhood and \r\nadolescence. i was blown away by the raw honesty of this \r\nprose.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(4516,1170,'2004-02-07 03:45:28',534,'griece','<p>why doesn\\\'t sombody else finish it?\r\n\r\n<p><i>are you afraid?</i>',6,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4517,1136,'2004-02-07 03:45:28',534,'griece','<p>you know it baby-jo\r\n\r\n<p>why don\\\'t you come up and see me sometime?',6,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4518,1156,'2001-06-22 21:57:28',0,'Pandora','Thank you.',4,0,0,0,'205.188.193.51','en'),(4519,1170,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i enjoyed this. i like stories without endings.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4520,1172,'2001-06-22 23:17:09',0,'Jojo','Christ Jesus, is it hot here in Hell.  My leggings are \r\nsmoking, the hair beneath are curlicueing into wee fleur-de-\r\nlis.  What to do, what to say?  I imagine you an icecube I \r\nrun along the length of my body, demarcating trade routes \r\nfrom my China to your Italianate peninsula, some frozen \r\nMarco Polo, dimunitive and bearing rumours of my spices to \r\nEuropeans weaned on stupid salt.\r\n\r\nOh but is it hot, and oh you are not here to divest me of \r\nmy heat.  I fan myself with my clothes like a loser; I need \r\nto be surrounded by eunuchs appended by palm fronds, I need \r\nto live in that long-ago era when giant ferns ruled the \r\nEarth, dinosaur ferns, sinuous and oh so Zen.',4,0,0,0,'209.242.148.3','en'),(4521,1172,'2001-06-22 23:20:22',0,'Jojo','<i>Rien Ã  faire, rien Ã  dire.</i><br><br><br><H2><i>Mal vu, \r\nmal dit.</i></h2>',2,0,0,0,'209.242.148.3','en'),(4522,1170,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','<p>Desmond, losing sight of his short term objective (as \r\ndo most of us) ran out from behind the shrubbery. The \r\ngrass was warm under his bare feet as he streaked through \r\nthe sunlight. Amanda looked up, and started to smile. The \r\nsmile started to waver as she caught the look on his face. \r\nSmiling, yet slowing to a stop, he slipped the still \r\nwarm turkey, orifice first, over the top of his head. It \r\nslid into place, a little jaunty, a little surprised, but \r\nresigned. It was heavy, and he steadied it with one arm. His\r\ncollar bone  and neck glistened from the juices as he stilled and stood there, staring into \r\nher almond eyes. Holding her hand, he paused, looked shyly at her \r\nearlobes then her eyes, as he whispered, \"Will you marry me?\"\r\n</p><p>\r\nThe sun sank a little deeper and the tips of her ears \r\nshadowed as she whispered her answer to him.</p>',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(4523,1170,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','hmm, it\\\'s really hard to finish someone else\\\'s story. and \ndoubly hard to escape the cheesy setup... apologies for \nthe bad fiction! eep\n',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(4524,1165,'2001-06-22 23:54:03',0,'auntie','i never had that one, darwin.  for years i had a recurring \r\ndream of doing it with a bearded scottish guy. i don\\\'t like \r\nmen with beards, and never thought scottish guys were very \r\ninteresting, so i can\\\'t figure that one out.<br><br>\r\n\r\nfor the past couple of weeks i have been dreaming that le \r\nis calling to me, she needs me right now, and i can\\\'t get \r\nto her.  i wake up in a panic and phone her, but she is \r\nalways surprised.  i may have to fly out there and see for \r\nmyself pretty quick, my eyes are bloodshot and my brain is \r\nfogged from lack of sleep.',0,0,0,0,'24.162.119.106','en'),(4525,1172,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','who you is, foo?\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.5.159','en'),(4526,1172,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','\\\'cause you sound like thomas pynchon. cool.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.5.159','en'),(4527,1171,'2002-03-15 00:17:55',129,'moebius','<br>griece, I hate to break this to you but <i>Barfly</i> \r\nis just a <i>movie</i>, you know? not your life story for \r\nchrissake.</br>\r\n\r\n<br>now impress us with a story/poem about how your white-\r\ncollar \\\"behind a computer\\\" job fits into this drinkin\\\' and \r\nbrawlin\\\' lifestyle. \\\'cause I\\\'m getting curious about \r\nthat.</br>\r\n\r\n<br>and keep in mind, <i>Fight Club</i> was just a movie, \r\ntoo.)</br>\r\n\r\n<br>peace, love, and hairgrease, Moe</br>\r\n',3,0,0,0,'64.165.96.58','en'),(4528,1153,'2001-06-23 03:17:47',0,'moebius to matt','<br>about Gravity\\\'s Rainbow: several friends of mine have \r\nsaid that that book will drive you insane. one other \r\nactually didn\\\'t get around to reading it until he was \r\ninstitutionalized for a couple of weeks. this apparently \r\nholds true even if you\\\'re a Pynchon fan.</br>\r\n\r\n<br>then again, my dad read the book in a week, under no \r\nspecial circumstances, with no ill effects (that I could \r\nsee). so perhaps that\\\'s all bunk. good luck. </br>',1,0,0,0,'64.165.96.58','en'),(4529,1153,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','when one has lost one\\\'s mind, then undergone transcendent \r\nphenomena which further blew out what was regained of that \r\nmind, one begins to believe that reality is just some kind \r\nof construct. i believe humans are capable of holding many \r\ncontradictory existential gestalts simultaneously. when you \r\nthink that, on the one hand, like the taoists, none of us \r\nexist, and on the other, that we exist in several parallel \r\nuniverses; when you know all about your shiva nature and \r\nyour legba nature and all your animal totems; when you feel \r\nthat you have a purpose, a calling to liberate all living \r\nthings from suffering, from existing if necessary, nothing \r\nmuch scares you.<BR><BR>\r\nbut none of that is anything special, ya know?:)\r\n \r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.9.236','en'),(4530,1161,'2001-06-23 03:55:44',0,'kat','<p>5th grade was in 1987???<br>\r\nneil diamond was in 1987???</p>\r\n\r\n<p>i think im losing it here people</p>',4,0,0,0,'12.64.18.240','en'),(4531,1172,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','what happened?',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4532,1172,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','it cut off the less than/greater than thingy at the end of \r\nthe tag when it compiled it or wherever the fuck it does, so \r\neverything after that was in the same font, \r\netc.<BR><BR>either that, or jojo put some bad juju on the \r\ncomment thingy. anybody know french, or whatever that is?\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.78.251','en'),(4533,1172,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','might be creole, now that i think about it.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.78.251','en'),(4534,1172,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i completely disagree with everything.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4535,1162,'2001-06-23 07:09:29',0,'eoj','little boxes on the hillside, little boxes made of ticky \r\ntacky, little boxes, little boxes...',4,0,0,0,'64.3.15.93','en'),(4536,1173,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<P>charles schulz is a genius:\r\n<br><br>\r\n<B>DOGS ARE ALLOWED TO KICK PEOPLE</B>',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4537,1173,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>\r\n<img src=\\\"http://deity.loa.com/~darwin/gfx/kick.jpg\\\"></p>\r\n<p>Rest in Peace, Charles..</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n',1,0,0,0,'24.221.170.119','en'),(4538,1168,'2001-06-23 11:47:52',0,'rusty','hah!',6,0,0,0,'63.229.85.142','en'),(4539,1169,'2001-06-23 16:45:35',0,'kat','yea. warm pavement under my bare feet. wading kneehigh \r\nthrough raging waters. a river. what use to be the street \r\nin front of our house. neighbor kids splashing. adults \r\ntaking stock. broken branches....wet leaves plastered on \r\njust about everything. you worried over the tomato plants \r\nwhile i collected hail stones like spring flowers. storm \r\nwarning. a hot shot of natures best. tornado season is here \r\nagain.',1,0,0,0,'32.101.251.223','en'),(4540,1171,'2004-02-07 03:45:28',534,'griece','<p>yeah, sometimes we are drawn to things because \r\nthey are like mirrors, because the truth in them is also \r\napplicable to OUR lives.  \r\n\r\n<p>good fiction is like a mirror held up to life, or \r\nsomesuch.  who said?\r\n\r\n<p>sometimes you go out and do, so that you can \r\nexperience and move past.\r\n\r\n<p>yes.',1,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4541,1170,'2004-02-07 03:45:28',534,'griece','what?  no cheddar here!!!!',6,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4542,1175,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','everybody got that?\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.9.79','en'),(4543,1175,'2001-06-23 23:04:40',0,'icecreamassasin','*yawn* re-run.',6,0,0,0,'24.93.61.58','en'),(4544,1175,'2001-06-24 00:34:31',0,'gary\\\'s spleen','how do you know you\\\'re smarter than the other barflies?  how\r\ndo you know that they\\\'re not writers, too?  how do you know\r\nthey\\\'re not playing you the fool?  why are your reasons any\r\nbetter than theirs?',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(4545,1175,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i think sometimes you just know.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4546,1175,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Pong Moll','<p>t00 mu(H fYt3 (lubzzz 4 uuuuuuuuu!!!!!!!</p>',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(4547,1158,'2001-06-24 03:21:47',0,'kat','<p>oh shit. and how could we forget Mr. Paul Newman in Cool \r\nHand Luke????</p>',1,0,0,0,'32.102.191.196','en'),(4548,1174,'2001-06-24 03:29:05',0,'kat','<p>middle ear imbalance = motion sickness<p>',4,0,0,0,'32.102.191.196','en'),(4549,1174,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i learned when i was a kid that reading in the car was a \r\none-way ticket to motion sickness. once i puked on an \r\numbrella in the backseat. now i don\'t sit in the \r\nbackseat anymore. in fact i almost always drive. this \r\nsomehow seems to be the cure.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4550,1176,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','gotta learn to crawl, etc.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.79.59','en'),(4551,1165,'2001-06-24 12:26:25',0,'rusty','<p>\r\nfuck dreams...\r\n<p>\r\nor maybe not...\r\n<p>\r\nI don\\\'t fucking know, and I don\\\'t fucking care...  They come \r\nevery night, and maybe it\\\'s best when you can forget them \r\nthe next day...  huzzah!',6,0,0,0,'63.229.87.190','en'),(4552,1173,'2001-06-24 12:28:59',0,'rusty','feh',6,0,0,0,'63.229.87.190','en'),(4553,1177,'2001-06-24 14:35:03',0,'de la soul','<pre>\\\"Anybody in the audience ever get hit by a car?</pre>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'24.221.170.119','en'),(4554,1177,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','maybe the driver was drunk too and didnt want to deal \r\nwith the cops.',4,0,0,0,'216.175.94.185','en'),(4555,1174,'2001-06-24 21:52:09',0,'maria','i listen to music really loudly, stare out the window, \r\nthink about sex, and make up stories for the people around \r\nme. since i don\\\'t drive, i\\\'m <b>always</b> on public \r\ntransportation. you get used to it. \r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'205.188.200.213','en'),(4556,1178,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','... and where\\\'s my cafepress swinney.org coffee mug?',5,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4557,1177,'2001-06-24 22:09:52',0,'i','worried about you!',0,0,0,0,'203.96.111.201','en'),(4558,1175,'2001-06-25 02:51:25',0,'heba hobba','<p> this sucks, dude.</p>',0,0,0,0,'216.175.89.171','en'),(4559,1178,'2001-06-25 03:12:18',0,'test','testicles',1,0,0,0,'64.51.232.105','en'),(4560,1178,'2001-06-25 03:13:10',0,'test','testicular cancer ward.',3,0,0,0,'64.51.232.105','en'),(4561,1178,'2001-06-25 03:14:09',0,'test','testroniks',4,0,0,0,'64.51.232.105','en'),(4562,1175,'2001-06-25 03:20:26',0,'heba hobba','said no such thing.',0,0,0,0,'64.165.201.108','en'),(4563,1185,'2001-06-25 03:25:14',0,'little girls','we love swinney.',3,0,0,0,'64.51.232.105','en'),(4564,1186,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<font color=\\\"#FF0000\\\"><H2>FUCK THIS EVERYTHING \r\nSUCKS I HATE CHANGE</H2></font>',6,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4565,164,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','oatmeal made with a big pinch of cardamom. oh hell yeah. \r\nand then followed with lots of raisins and granola. *dances \r\naround*',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(4566,1186,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','well, i don\\\'t HATE it, but there\\\'s nothing to say what it \r\nactually is on the front page anymore - it\\\'s rather \r\nconfusing - 5 new *what*?  what are thoughts?  where can i \r\norder my swinney.org cd?<br>\r\n<br>\r\ni guess at some stage i\\\'ll just have to suck it up and make \r\nan o.swinney.org or a swinney.oxy.gen.nz or something.  \r\nbah.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nreally and truly, i don\\\'t see what people were kicking up a \r\nfuss over.  swinney was perfect in it\\\'s original form.  a \r\nthing of beauty.',3,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(4567,1186,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','also it doesn\\\'t always display 5 new entries.  sometimes it \r\nonly displays 3.  hi.',3,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(4568,1186,'2001-06-25 05:58:39',0,'sawks<br>','wouldn\\\'t the easiest route to skinnability be to use \r\nstandards compliant html and let everyone set their own \r\nstylesheets? no extra backend chunking around \r\nrequired<br><br>\r\ngood example over at <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.waferbaby.com/prefs/\\\">http://www.waferbaby.\r\ncom/prefs/</a>\r\n\r\n',3,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(4569,1186,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','a lot of swinney\\\'ers don\\\'t have the choice of using \r\na \\\"standards compliant\\\" browser.',3,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(4570,1186,'2001-06-25 06:41:36',0,'sawks','<br>\r\nmozilla 0.9.1 0wns :P',3,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(4571,1186,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<br><br>\r\ntruth be told, i am not a tinkerer, so the backend \r\nchanges don\\\'t affect me that much. that said:\r\n<br><br>\r\no has good points. i like the original front page, with its \r\nmandate to read the journal or write in it, but don\\\'t do \r\nnothing. i miss the table borders; the new layout has a \r\ngeneral feel of floating text. even yahoo, with all its sexy \r\nminimalism, has little boxes enclosing different things.\r\n<br><br>\r\non the plus side, i really groove on the 5 random posts. \r\nand i like the changes in the page foward/page back \r\narrows at the top of the journal page. much needed.\r\n<br><br>\r\nconstructive!',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4572,1186,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','a thought: the \\\"5 old\\\" list is like swinney roulette.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4573,1186,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','yeah except NO ARTICLES BY ME EVER COME UP.',3,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(4574,1186,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','(and of course it\\\'s all about me)',3,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(4575,1178,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Avant Moll','My face hurts :~(',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(4576,1186,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Techno Moll','<p>Welp. I don\\\'t know shit about shit.</p>',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(4577,1186,'2001-06-25 11:16:31',0,'bmg','I liked the original front color scheme, with the orange \r\nthoughts... and i need boxes around my menu\\\'s. that is all. ',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(4578,1175,'2004-02-07 03:45:28',534,'griece','<p>hey, somone (i forget who) asked for an \r\nexplanation.   so, here I am, explaining \\\'bout stuff.  you \r\nwill see no more of this.  pay no attention to the man \r\nbehind the curtain.  \r\n<p>fuck you,',6,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4579,1186,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','\ni like the new functionality, perhaps we can put the old \nand the new in one column? the new over the old? it would \nbe a little more readable, methinks. you need a usability \nexpert! but, i like. change is good.\n',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(4580,1186,'2001-06-25 14:29:14',0,'sic','maybe you should leave the main page but with the old \r\nentries too...',0,0,0,0,'207.62.162.110','en'),(4581,670,'2004-02-07 03:45:28',534,'griece','<p>I think it\\\'s pretty pathetic that you didn\\\'t always make \r\nit this way.  There also used to be these things called \r\n\\\"records.\\\"  They were large plastic disks with grooves \r\nand they sounded infinitely better than CDs or MP3s.  \r\nPlus they were romantic and warm, similar to drinking \r\ngood scotch.  Hell, similar to drinking any kind of \r\nscotch.\r\n\r\n<p>Fuck you.',6,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4582,1172,'2001-06-25 15:45:57',0,'Jojo','I completely agree.  Everything is disagreeable.<br>\r\nGoddamnit I hate Mondays.  Ex-boyfriend wants me to pay him \r\nback.  His bank no longer accepts blow jobs.<br>\r\nHow curious to think that I was 5500% happier yesterday.  \r\nAnd just think how fucking miserable I was yesterday.',4,0,0,0,'209.242.148.3','en'),(4583,1189,'2001-06-25 16:34:03',0,'jo','yes.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(4584,1189,'2001-06-25 16:51:26',0,'kat','<p>a good description of my mood right now would \r\nbe \\\'rabid\\\'</p>\r\n\r\n',4,0,0,0,'12.64.78.117','en'),(4585,1186,'2004-02-07 03:45:28',534,'griece','where are my articles?  who took them?  how dare \r\nyou!!!!!!   ',6,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4586,1188,'2001-06-25 17:17:23',0,'zb','beautiful.',0,0,0,0,'216.171.37.54','en'),(4587,1189,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>let\\\'s get some bottle rockets.<br>\r\nand also, let\\\'s have a bonfire.<br>i will show you a good \r\ntime. is there anyone on swinney who can shoot a bottle \r\nrocket out his/her ass?</p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(4588,1186,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>where is the complete list of contributors?</p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(4589,1189,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','only after some thai. with the fish sauce',1,0,0,0,'64.132.148.219','en'),(4590,1193,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','\\\"the tao of pooh\\\" and \\\"the te of piglet\\\" are good books to \r\nread.',1,0,0,0,'64.132.148.219','en'),(4591,1158,'2004-02-07 03:45:28',534,'griece','you see, i contributed a note here.  a valid and good \r\none.  it has been erased.  i was mentioned in this post \r\nand now I cannot access my articles.  why is that?  how \r\ncan you erase me?  what have i done to you!?',6,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4620,1197,'2001-06-26 15:49:56',0,'bmg','<p>perl on NT, solution<br><a href=\'http://www.perl.com/pub/qa/Is_there_a_Windows_version_of_Perl?\'>www.perl.com/pub/qa/Is_there_a_Windows_version_of_Perl?</a></p>',1,0,0,0,'206.77.155.158','en'),(4592,1193,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Vongh Moll','<p>Uh, \\\"the higher they are the harder they fall\\\", or\r\nsomething, or is it \\\"the bigger they...\\\", I don\\\'t know, not\r\nmuch of a <i>falling</i> anyway -- I mean, you said yourself\r\n-- it\\\'s more like a deflation, so I guess it doesn\\\'t really\r\napply, but. Look. Just forget about it. Forget I said\r\nanything.</p>',1,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(4593,1189,'2001-06-25 22:55:28',0,'liver','<br>\r\ni\\\'d be up for a bonfire.  i work in the land of pallets, \r\nmalt liquor and bad taquerias, so i can bring pallets and \r\ncolt 45.  i cannot shoot bottle rocket out of my ass though.\r\n<p>\r\nweeb, i will kick your ass in 59 years and 364 days \r\nthough.  a race around the old folks home (twice) followed \r\nby competitive toe touching.  8am sharp.  winner take all.  \r\nyou\\\'d better not forget!\r\n',2,0,0,0,'63.202.215.130','en'),(4594,1172,'2001-06-25 23:59:42',0,'Jojo','I bid them adieux.  They did not reply; they did not seem \r\nto have heard me.  Their ruffled parasols fluttered briefly \r\nwith some unfelt breeze, and so I suppose I took my \r\nfarewells from that, and turned from them, their white \r\ndresses and black hair, their unseen eyes.  I had fashioned \r\nmy goodbyes in a series of musics and gestures, and perhaps \r\nthey heard and felt them, I told myself it didn\\\'t matter, I \r\nlived only for expression, not for praise, I lived to act, \r\nnot to provoke reaction.  Excoriation or alienation seemed \r\ntoo dramatic.  Let it suffice that I told them farewell, \r\nand turned away from them, that I renounced the possibility \r\nof their grace, and turned to some undiscovered fulfilment \r\nhere in the eternally turning away.',0,0,0,0,'209.242.148.3','en'),(4595,1137,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','perhaps im being sulky but as of late i feel as though im at \r\na difficult crossroads in my life. what to do? what to do? \r\nyeah i ask myself this question all the time. im currently \r\nemployed temporarily as an assistant logistics coordinator \r\nwith the humber school for writers. i help out with the \r\nhumber screen writers workshop, the writing workshop, and \r\nthe humber comedy school. i get to meet a lot of big names \r\nand while i dont get paid as much as the people who\\\'ve made \r\nit big, i hear a lot about that wealth and see what it can \r\ndo to people. i crave it. i crave it in a way shape and form \r\nthat makes me feel defeatist at the end of the day. my pant \r\nlegs are getting narrow instead of phatter and my shirts \r\nhave more buttons. in all i want to be where my brother is \r\nand while i think that is possible, i dont think im capable \r\nof the kind of work he does. i dont know what im capable of \r\nand thats what worries me. i read the job pages and i have \r\nnone of the skills employers are looking for. my job with \r\nhumber is a patrionage job and while its fun and i get paid \r\nbetter then what i was paid at the grocery store, i do not \r\ndo any of the things a logistics coordinator does. I simply \r\ndo the things a logistics coordinator does not want to do. \r\ni need to network. i need to speak with these famous and \r\nconnected people and make things work. i need to inform them \r\nof my skills and ask if there is anything out there for me. \r\ni need to become modivated and seek things out. perhaps i am \r\nsort of waiting for something to jump out and bite me in the \r\nass and maybe now im realizing that this just isnt going to \r\nhappen. van morrison said it best when he sang \\\"do you \r\nremember when we sang sha la la la la la\\\" ',6,0,0,0,'24.43.182.49','en'),(4596,1137,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','yeah, a song about singing. so nice.<BR><BR>you should do \r\nwhatever gives you joy in your life, and the money will take \r\ncare of itself.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.28.130','en'),(4597,39,'2001-06-26 02:16:40',0,'mama','said knock you out.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.28.130','en'),(4598,979,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','somebody done activated it.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.28.130','en'),(4599,1186,'2001-06-26 02:28:36',0,'Joanna','You know, as far as I\\\'m concerned, Swinney could have been \r\ndesigned in Microsoft Publisher and use clip art (and look \r\nlike <A  \r\nHREF=\\\"http://www.geocities.com/southbeach/docks/1233/\\\" \r\ntitle=\\\"my first website\\\">this</A>) and it would still be \r\nwonderful, as long as all you wonderful people keep writing \r\non it.  ',1,0,0,0,'203.97.2.243','en'),(4600,1186,'2001-06-26 03:01:42',0,'bmg','what about having the CHAOS section maintaining the same \r\nfive old articles for a day, but randomly picking them each \r\nday...? Joanna has got some mad html skills by the way...\r\n',1,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(4601,1189,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','<p>i\'m so there. i\'ll be the one who can still touch my \r\nnose \r\nto my knees and cunnilingiate myself. i\'m gonna be the \r\nwell-adjusted grandma, i tell you.\r\n</p><p>\r\nhai! this improvement in mood was  \r\nbrought to you today by: a trip to japantown, p-funk, \r\ndrinking \r\nnigori whilst doing housework, and this \r\n<a  href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0714840831/qid=993528424/103-7565094-5582223\">little \r\nshiny happy pink joy of a book.</a>  \r\n</p>',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(4602,1197,'2001-06-26 04:13:16',0,'dawn','At my job we often argue about charing for changes we insist \r\nthe customer make. \r\n<p>\r\nWe never come up with a blanket answer, generally deciding \r\ndepending on the cost and time involved. I guess here it \r\nwould depend on if you told them to make all the names the \r\nsame or not.\r\n<p>\r\nRegardless, I\\\'d probably write a script to rename the files \r\nand charge them for half the time. But, that\\\'s just me.\r\n',2,0,0,0,'208.161.7.250','en'),(4603,1197,'2001-06-26 04:15:29',0,'dawn','That would be \\\'charging\\\' not \\\'charing\\\'. I always see my \r\ntypos right after I hit the submit/send/\\\'I said it\\\' button.',2,0,0,0,'208.161.7.250','en'),(4604,1197,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>yeah, auntie, this sounds like a job for perl. if you \r\nwant, you can catch me on icb and describe the issue and I \r\ncan probably write a quick piece of perl to do it for \r\nyou..</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin',1,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(4605,1197,'2002-03-08 04:52:47',65,'le to dar','i have suggested perl to her before, but her site is \r\nhosted on an NT server where perl is not installed. \r\nwe\\\'ve been through it.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4606,1203,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i love tangelos so much.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4607,1197,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>still, depending on how the data is databased : how it \r\ngoes in and how it\\\'s modified, it\\\'s still possible that you \r\ncould modify the data before it goes into the database on a \r\nsystem that does have perl on it.</p>\r\n<p>in any case, just thought I\\\'d offer my unemployed perl-\r\nwriting services.</p>\r\n<p>\r\nI like perl!</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n',3,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(4608,1177,'2002-03-15 00:17:55',129,'moebius','<br>interesting coincidence:</br>\r\n\r\n<br>last night i got home from viewing the SF Pride Parade \r\nwith friends, booted up the machine, and started reviewing \r\nthe weekend\\\'s swinney.org action while I waited for my pal \r\nK to show up. we had a plan to go out to see dinner & a \r\nmovie. something to do in the absence of my dear mbear, who \r\nwas out of state, at a family function.</br>\r\n\r\n<br>i was reading your post, and was at the sentence \\\"Then \r\nI fully realised what had happened, so I called my friends \r\nand they took me to the hospital\\\" when the cellphone rang \r\nfrom somewhere in my leather satchel. probably K calling to \r\nsay he\\\'d be a bit late, but damn, the phone was buried \r\nsomewhere in there and now i had to dig it out before he \r\nwas sent to voicemail. that phone\\\'s a pain in the ass \r\nsometimes.</br>\r\n\r\n<br>so i reached over my table, unzipped the top pocket, \r\nplunged my hand in and FUCK FUCK FUCK something goddamn BIT \r\nme! i screamed, knocked the cat off my lap, lurched out of \r\nmy chair, looked in, and there\\\'s that brandnew x-acto \r\nblade, the cap having fallen off at some point. like a fool \r\ni was carrying it around in there for some proposed collage \r\nproject i might work on someday.</br>\r\n\r\n<br>so fuck fuck fuck, spraying blood everywhere, it\\\'s a \r\npretty deep cut, and all the time i\\\'m trying to stop the \r\nflow of blood i\\\'m thinking of that last line, of car \r\naccidents and emergency rooms and i don\\\'t want to go to the \r\nhospital. K shows up, i disenfect & bandage & mostly stop \r\nthe blood, he wipes the blood off the floor. and it looks \r\nlike i\\\'ve performed an animal sacrifice in the bathroom \r\nsink, so we clean that up too. </br>\r\n\r\n<br>somehow i decide to go with K to the dinner and movie \r\n(\\\"The Aniversary Party\\\": <i>very</i> good) and all is \r\nmostly well. but after getting back home i talk to some \r\nonline friends who convince me that hey, maybe the \r\nemergency room isn\\\'t so bad after all, they might not have \r\nto suture--my secret fear. so i walk over to the Kaiser \r\nhospital (lucky me, our apt is only four blocks away) and \r\nit turns out my friends are right. god bless america and \r\nsteri-strip technology.</br>\r\n\r\n<br>now all is well mostly and i\\\'ve learned i can type ok \r\nwith the bandage on. and i know bleeding finger does not \r\nequal hit-and-run injured foot and arm, but just so you \r\nknow, i was thinking of your story while i waited in the \r\nemergency room, watching mexican soap operas on the \r\noverhead set at 1:20 am. best, moe.</br>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.38.74.58','en'),(4609,1201,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','surrender through acceptance. don\\\'t blame yourself. let \r\nyourself feel, but allot yourself a time period. \\\"i feel like \r\nwallowing, like hating, like crying\\\" but only for two \r\nweeks. after two weeks i will move on. until then i will \r\nfeel as hard as i want, even it keeps me from moving, \r\nfrom feeding myself, from leaving the house. if despair \r\nis beyond your control, seek help. if it goes on and on \r\nand on. but if it\\\'s because of a situation or a time, let it \r\nbe. ',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4610,1202,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','come here.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4611,1202,'2001-06-26 07:06:49',0,'kat','<p>i spent sveral years of my adolescence living in an rv. \r\nat one point it was even parked in the middle of a \r\ncommercial district. no smokestacks tho...but i did work at \r\na gas station, so the petrol smell was rampant.</p>',2,0,0,0,'12.64.18.126','en'),(4612,1202,'2001-06-26 07:10:49',0,'kat','<p>ps: this was not the 70\\\'s, nor England. i spent the 70\\\'s \r\nin culturally dead San Jose enjoying a variety of crummy \r\nlower class apartments. a worse life than some, better than \r\nothers.</p>',1,0,0,0,'12.64.18.126','en'),(4613,9,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>this is the first post with actual content.</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin',2,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(4614,1201,'2001-06-26 07:46:19',0,'kv','hi. i don\\\'t know if you were being sincere or if it was a \r\nrhetorical question, or an expressive question, but anyway. \r\nyou know how anorexia (the eating disorder) is a symptom of \r\nother problem(s), like helplessness, lack of control, \r\ninsecurity, neglect, etc? i believe depression is, \r\nsimilarly, a manifestation, psycho-somatic, symptomatic. \r\nbeing sad and/or disliking yourself is your way of dealing \r\nwith issues that you don\\\'t even know you have. yet. \r\n\r\n<p>so, without knowing you or knowing your history or \r\nanything, all i can suggest is: attempt to voice your \r\nunvoiced concerns. think about anything that\\\'s bothering \r\nyou, and then re-think how much it really is bothering \r\nyou... and so on. \r\n\r\n<p>sorry if it wasn\\\'t a sincere question. -kv',0,0,0,0,'203.173.175.31','en'),(4615,1201,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Veer Moll','<p>I don\\\'t know what to say. I don\\\'t really get the \r\ndespair.</p>\r\n<p>I\\\'m a Moll. I\\\'m a temporary boy. I take naps and look at \r\nthings. I have no friends. I throw sticks into the water \r\nand stare at clouds. Someday soon I\\\'ll be kaput.</p>\r\n<p>Maybe the key is keeping it isolated from a reality \r\nwhich it may or may not have anything to do with, keeping \r\nit in perspective.</p>\r\n<p>But that\\\'s bullshit. I don\\\'t know what I\\\'m talking \r\nabout. I never have to deal with these things. I\\\'m \r\ndisposable. Here today, gone tomorrow, hope you find a \r\nway.</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(4616,587,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','just wanted to say, it clears up, eventually.  having dreads\r\nand not having to wash my hair is one of the best things\r\nabout being alive right now.  except i think people think\r\ni\\\'m skody.  maybe it\\\'s why nobody wants to have sex with me.',3,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(4617,1177,'2001-06-26 11:53:14',0,'Joanna','Me being the drama queen that I am, while I was in A&E, in \r\nbetween apologising to Maree and James for being such a \r\nmess, I was thinking about how I would tell other people \r\nabout it, and how I would write about it, and probably \r\nwhether or not it would make a good swinney post.\r\n\r\n<BR><BR>\r\n\r\nI\\\'ve been accused (by myself) of doing things purely for \r\nthe entertainment value to other people, but I didn\\\'t step \r\nin front of the car deliberately, I swear.  ',1,0,0,0,'203.97.2.243','en'),(4618,1197,'2001-06-26 13:42:13',0,'auntie','tuggy and le and i discussed how i should learn perl years \r\nago.  i have reasons for not leaving my nt host.  he has \r\nreasons for never asking me to go.  i like the way i do \r\nthings now, all in control of every piece of code, every \r\npage, myself.<br><br>\r\n\r\nle and i will make perl things someday together. just like \r\nwe used to make fudge.',1,0,0,0,'24.162.119.106','en'),(4619,1201,'2003-07-24 15:44:23',165,'joker',' i tend to agree with le\\\'s assessment regarding a \r\nprescribed wallowing time.  this can also be dangerous, \r\nhowever, as when the end of the wallowing time comes and \r\ngoes and the despair hasn\\\'t budged.<br><br>\r\nconcentrating on no \\\"i\\\" is very difficult, and because of \r\nthe way we all interact in this ordinary world (<i>that is \r\nto say, <u>conceptually</u></i>) one should understand that \r\nit\\\'s IMPOSSIBLE to, \\\"just kind of imagine\\\" a world without \r\nthe \\\"i\\\".<br><br>\r\nthis is why meditation.  meditation is all about letting \r\nthe so-called IMPORTANT things in this ordinary life go \r\nby.  it is IMPOSSIBLE to keep them from arising in your \r\nmind.  the key is, not to give them energy, not to chase \r\nthem or give them emotion.  meditate on stillness, meditate \r\non breathing, meditate on love and/or impermanence, but \r\nleave the worries of this life outside of the \r\nmeditation.<br><br>\r\nmy own meditative practice leaves much to be desired.  \r\nperhaps, if we\\\'re lucky, one of the many badass \r\npractitioners that frequent this site will say some words.',1,0,0,0,'66.68.48.125','en'),(4621,1207,'2001-06-26 16:18:22',0,'darkbloom',':scratches head:\r\nsay what?',5,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(4622,1207,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>\r\n<tt>I really like cicadas.  They used to be my \r\nfavorite \\\'animals\\\' i think.  I even learned to make origami \r\ncicadas out of paper; pretty gilded cicadas out of joss, \r\nfunky pop-op-art-ish cicadas out of left over Escher \r\nwrapping paper, thick cicadas out of index cards - all \r\nlooked much prettier than cicadas actually do.  oh \r\nwell.</tt>\r\n<br>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(4623,1201,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>\r\n<tt>everything is rarely fire for me, also.  when other \r\nroutes fail, i find myself grateful for my lover, whom also \r\nshares a periodic heavy coat of despair - we end up trading \r\ntidbits of our lot, and more often than not, we find that \r\nthe fresh perspective relieves some of the weight.  As in- \r\nshe explains her down-ness to me; i vicariously take it \r\non.  I explain some things that are getting me down, vice \r\nversa.  The idea that someone who understands can share \r\npure empathy with me is <i>very</i> relieving.  As you \r\nmentioned, its only a momentary solution (surrender) but \r\nits a very sweet one.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nof course, it makes us somewhat co-dependant.  i guess you \r\ntake the bad with the good, though? there\\\'s no easy answer- \r\ndo be sure to let me know if you find one!</tt>\r\n',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(4624,1197,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>\r\n<tt>ooooh, i <b>seethe</b> with sympathy for you... my job \r\nis peppered with random, repetative tasks that could be \r\ndone in seconds if the powers that be weren\\\'t windows-NT-o-\r\nphiles.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(4625,1197,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>\r\n<tt><b>bmg:</b> just noticed your comment... don\\\'t know if \r\nit helped her, but it helped me - thanks!</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(4626,1202,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>\r\n<tt>last year i lived between a gas station and a \r\nartificial-flavor manufacturer.  i do not kid you when i \r\nsay that the air in my neighborhood smelled like strawberry \r\ngasoline... it was ethereal.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(4627,1203,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<IMG \r\nSRC=\\\"http://www.juiceking.com/images/seasons/tangelos.jpg\\\" \r\nALIGN=\\\"left\\\" WIDTH=\\\"95\\\" HEIGHT=\\\"70\\\" BORDER=\\\"0\\\" \r\nALT=\\\"Pointer\\\"><tt>Not navels, not temples, not valencias, \r\nnot pink, red, or white grapefruit... no other has the \r\ncachet of the honeybell tangelo</tt><p>\r\n\r\n',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(4628,1197,'2001-06-26 17:51:49',0,'bmg','<em>Peter:</em><p>no, prob. I have used <a \r\nhref=\'http://aspn.activestate.com/ASPN/Downloads/ActivePerl/\r\nindex/\' target=new>ActiveState Perl</a> for sometime... infact, i \r\nlearned perl using NT... it works, and it works quite \r\nwell.</p>',1,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(4629,1201,'2001-06-26 17:51:59',0,'uhuru','few things:<br>\r\n*depression inevitably adds depth to your personality.  it \r\nadds beauty to your face and deeper, more lumninous essence \r\nto your soul.  remember this. <br>\r\n*the prophet has lovely words to say about grief and \r\nsadness: \\\"Your joy is your sorrow unmasked. And the \r\nselfsame well from which your laughter rises was oftentimes \r\nfilled with your tears. And how else can it be? <b>The \r\ndeeper that sorrow carves into your being, the more joy you \r\ncan contain.</b> When you are joyous, look deep into your \r\nheart and you shall find it is only that which has given \r\nyou sorrow that is giving you joy. When you are sorrowful \r\nlook again in your heart, and you shall see that in truth \r\nyou are weeping for that which has been your delight.\\\" <br>\r\nAnd this: \\\"Your pain is the breaking of the shell that \r\nencloses your understanding. Even as the stone of the fruit \r\nmust break, that its heart may stand in the sun, so must \r\nyou know pain.<br>\r\nAnd could you keep your heart in wonder at the daily \r\nmiracles of your life, your pain would not seem less \r\nwondrous than your joy;\r\nAnd you would accept the seasons of your heart, even as you \r\nhave always accepted the seasons that pass over your fields.\r\nAnd you would watch with serenity through the winters of \r\nyour grief.\\\"<br>\r\nI have also been in deep depression lately, and these \r\nthings help me to remember that it\\\'s a necessary part of \r\nliving a full life.\r\n\r\n\r\n',2,0,0,0,'216.185.7.75','en'),(4630,1203,'2001-06-26 18:00:17',0,'sic','that pic makes my mouth water <drools excessively>',0,0,0,0,'207.62.162.110','en'),(4631,1207,'2001-06-26 18:07:43',0,'xepmom','to Peter: Being a nurse, I misread Escher as eschar (the \r\nblack crusty slough produced by gangrene -- common in \r\nbedsores). This boy is a gnarley artist. \r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.174.154.239','en'),(4632,1202,'2001-06-26 19:46:29',0,'Danielle','I\\\'ve always lived in a house. My mum grew up in \r\nworking class England (although in the 50s, not the \r\n70s) and she has \\\"class\\\". She might not wear Gucci or \r\nPrada but she has respect for her parents and for \r\npeople in general and she has good character.  I don\\\'t \r\nknow why Im mentioning this but not every British \r\nperson gerw up in lower middle class with their parents \r\nworking at the mill etc. Its changed a lot since my mum \r\nlived there - I think its regressing.',3,0,0,0,'207.34.94.238','en'),(4633,1201,'2001-06-26 19:49:25',0,'Danielle','Whenever I feel real despair, I take a pill. I know this is \r\nwrong but I just can\\\'t deal with it. I went through many \r\nyears of agony, of wanting to die and not wanting to \r\nmove. I don\\\'t want to deal with that ever again, so every \r\nmorning I take a little blue pill and when I get too sad to \r\ncare about anything, I take more.',2,0,0,0,'207.34.94.238','en'),(4634,1209,'2001-06-26 21:22:45',0,'chi chi','i don\\\'t think astrology explains who you are, per se; but \r\nit is more of a guiding wind. one that you may follow or \r\nignore, as you choose. and that choice, of course, is a \r\nmanifestation of what the stars might be trying to say.',0,0,0,0,'64.165.201.108','en'),(4635,1209,'2001-06-26 21:25:51',0,'jay','this is beautiful, it is.<br><br>\r\nmaybe you should be an academic, write about semiotics... \r\nwonky shit like that.<br><br>\r\nor maybe, standing in a gallery of your work someday, hand \r\nsideways on hip, you\\\'ll say something about a mythical \r\ninfrastructure, and your rapt listeners will immediately \r\nthink you must have studied this shit for a long \r\ntime.<br><br>\r\nthe world is full of promise<br>\r\nand meaning<br>\r\nand books<br>\r\nand perfect coincidences that sometimes strike me as far \r\ntoo perfect to be mere chance, to be reduced to the level \r\nof accident. and, like astrology, i\\\'m hard-pressed to \r\ndiscount things that are so endlessly compelling, and so \r\neasily explained away by skeptics with the will to explain \r\naway wonder.',1,0,0,0,'63.203.225.62','en'),(4636,1209,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','a map of california doesn\\\'t decide where you\\\'ll go in \r\ncalifornia; nor can it predict whether you\\\'ll run out of gas \r\nbetween cities.<br><br>(i reuse that metaphor a lot. :)',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4637,1201,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','two things.<br><br>\r\ninterdependence is not the same as \r\ncodepedence.<br><br>\r\nthis quote: \\\"The deeper that sorrow carves into your \r\nbeing, the more joy you can contain,\\\" repasted again for \r\nemphasis.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4638,1209,'2001-06-26 22:19:33',0,'lulu','<p>the world is full of promises, and if you look at star \r\n594.0918zxfqi, it\\\'ll tell you that it IS full of promises.  \r\nwe\\\'re all destined for doom and deceit...just look at \r\njupiter when it\\\'s in the fifth house of mars when saturn \r\nretrogrades to the 7th house of remus.  perhaps \r\ncalifornians should find a new hobby....like...cow \r\nbranding.<br>\r\negg, would you like to go on a cattle drive with me?<br>\r\ni\\\'ll wait while you go ask the stars</p> ',0,0,0,0,'209.178.149.7','en'),(4639,539,'2001-06-26 22:20:53',0,'lulu','you go to the gym?',0,0,0,0,'209.178.149.7','en'),(4640,1209,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Nostalgia Moll','<p>In the homecountry, there is no astrology because people \r\ncan usually not see the stars. It\\\'s very cloudy most of the \r\ntime. It is also for this reason that we have only years; \r\nno months.</p>\r\n',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(4641,467,'2001-06-26 22:24:15',0,'Mayflower','War Pigs. Sounds like something you\\\'d play in a \r\ngarage band....\r\n\r\nTerrible singer...\r\n\r\nTrying oh-so-hard guitarist....\r\n\r\nKeyboardist who wouldn\\\'t practice.....\r\n\r\nDrummer who taped the whole thing. ',4,0,0,0,'24.23.7.191','en'),(4642,1206,'2001-06-26 22:52:37',0,'<P align=\\\"center\\\">two words','   cult status</P>',2,0,0,0,'205.179.19.80','en'),(4643,1201,'2001-06-27 00:05:29',0,'Jojo','It\\\'s thirteen hundred o\\\'clock.  The method I used to bury \r\nmy depression was self-medication.  Self-analgesia, self-\r\namnesia, whatever; it\\\'s a sublimation of my want for \r\nannihilation, that thing my doctor calls \\\"<i>suicidal \r\nideation</i>\\\" and that I call wanting to fall asleep.  So \r\nfor thirteen hundred hours, or what seemed like thirteen \r\nhundred hours, I spun and floated away from my bloated \r\ncorpse, and waited for death to extinguish me.  It has not \r\nextinguished me, which (vainly, vainly) I knew it would not \r\n(stupidly, stupidly: how recklessly we live our lives, \r\nimpatient for the thrill of becoming, achieving what \r\nsummits of extacy for a delayed payment of what despairs \r\nlater).  Is this making sense?  Ask me to make sense when I \r\nam depressed.<br><br>There is a book out called <i>The \r\nNoonday Demon: An Atlas of Depression</i> by Andrew Solomon \r\nwhich speaks to me now.  I haven\\\'t read it, perhaps I will \r\nbuy or shoplift it when I rouse myself out of bed \r\n(hangover, hangover: better that than actually hanging \r\nmyself).  One chapter describes how Mr. Solomon actively \r\ntried to infect himself with HIV with lots of unsafe sex.  \r\nI thought <i>I</i> had come up with that idea.  His \r\nrationale was not to die malingeringly from AIDS but to \r\nkill himself using HIV as an excuse.  I think this meme has \r\nlost out in popularity these days to \\\"suicide-by-cop\\\" --- \r\nsomething you people in the Bay Area must be overfamiliar \r\nwith, especially whilst watching \\\"Swordfish\\\" and its \r\nken.<br><br>When my brother was god, everything was \r\ndifferent then.',2,0,0,0,'209.242.148.3','en'),(4644,1203,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','are tangelos the oranges with the big buttlump?',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(4645,1201,'2002-03-15 00:17:55',129,'moebius','<br>for those unsure of what the reference to \\\"Swordfish\\\" \r\nis all about, look <a href=\\\"http://www.sfgate.com/cgi-\r\nbin/article.cgi?\r\nfile=/chronicle/archive/2001/06/15/MN193600.DTL\\\">here</a>. \r\nI was there that night with my parents and girlfriend. We \r\nwere watching another film, but we were evacuated along \r\nwith everyone else.</br>\r\n\r\n<br>JoJo, it sounds like you made it through the \r\ncosmodemonic wastelands yet again. I\\\'ve been worried for \r\nyou. love, moe.</br>',1,0,0,0,'63.38.73.212','en'),(4646,1208,'2001-06-27 01:39:19',0,'sultana','ahhhhh.  quenched.',2,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(4647,1201,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>\\\"At least three officers fired as many as 20 shots, \r\nhitting Stelley several times, Pera said.\\\"</p>\r\n<p>This indicates extreme police incompetence. One man with \r\na knife on a piece of chain is in no way justification for \r\napplication of deadly force. At <u>most</u> one shot, \r\nproperly directed at the <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.cnn.com/2001/ALLPOLITICS/stories/02/07/whit\r\nehouse.lockdown/\\\">legs of the victim</a> would have caused \r\nhim to drop the chain he was swinging the knife around on. \r\nFor almost anyone (except, perhaps, those on PCP or the \r\nextremely drunk) being shot once anywhere on your body is \r\nenough to make you fall over in shock. I\\\'m certainly not an \r\nexpert in the application of force, but it seems like if \r\nthe Secret Service can handle a <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.cnn.com/2001/ALLPOLITICS/stories/02/07/whit\r\nehouse.lockdown/\\\">guy with a gun on the white house \r\nlawn</a> without killing him, the SF police should be able \r\nto handle a guy with a <u>knife</u>.</p>\r\n<p>Suicide by cop only works when the cops are stupid \r\nenough to kill the person. Sigh.</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n\r\n\r\n',3,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(4648,1209,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to jay','<p>i am insulted by this suggestion to be an academic. \r\nwhat, egg and joseph campbell, egg and saussure, \r\negg and lyotard? gross. me and the frenchmen. why \r\ndont i just get a beret? i do have a lot of air in my chart \r\nthough...</p>\r\n<p>i have also been dry heaving for the past 5 hours. \r\nthere is a toothed alien trying to bust his little slimy \r\nhead through the fibers of my stomach. there is noone \r\nhere to look after me. i guess i will smoke pot. where is \r\nmommy.</p>',0,0,0,0,'216.175.102.223','en'),(4649,1206,'2001-06-27 02:10:17',0,'sally','<p>austin did anyone ever tell you that you look like the \r\nbad guy from \\\"raiders of the lost ark\\\"?</p>',0,0,0,0,'216.175.102.223','en'),(4650,1203,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','Come And Live In Florida. we all about tangelos here.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.28.175','en'),(4651,1196,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','talismans from friends. they are a little piece of \r\ninvincibility i carry around with me, melding their \r\nessences with mine. the grubbier the scrap, the more potent \r\nthe magic.',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(4652,1201,'2001-06-27 04:06:20',0,'moebeus to darwin','even though at the time it was a frightening moment (we had \r\nno idea what was going on: hostage situation? random \r\nkilling of moviegoers? mass hysteria at the awfulness \r\nof \\\"Swordfish?\\\") i agree that this killing was a gross \r\noverreaction on the part of the SF Police. (weren\\\'t tasers \r\nan option?) apparently a few others do too: there\\\'s already \r\nbeen a <a href=\\\"http://www.sfgate.com/cgi-bin/article.cgi?\r\nfile=/chronicle/archive/2001/06/20/MN128898.DTL\\\">protest</a>\r\n against the killing at city hall where the victim\\\'s mother \r\nand girlfriend spoke out. i hope they manage to take the \r\ncase to court.</br>\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.38.74.82','en'),(4653,1192,'2001-06-27 05:21:43',0,'kat','bookies, boozers, running away, leaving your woman....this \r\nis what makes someone a better person???',4,0,0,0,'32.101.251.110','en'),(4654,1194,'2001-06-27 05:24:15',0,'kat','\\\'jillin myself\\\' ha. i can\\\'t get those words out of my head. \r\nthey\\\'ve been there for days now.',4,0,0,0,'32.101.251.110','en'),(4655,1209,'2001-06-27 05:57:31',0,'mommy','mommy\\\'s in hell lil girl.  would you like me to bring you home some ice cream?\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(4656,1209,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to mommy','<p>mommy i just want you to wear my frilly pink dress \r\nand hold me. that is all.</p>',0,0,0,0,'216.175.102.223','en'),(4657,1212,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>i dont like rush, but can we have a band? i can wail \r\nand also, I can stay in key.</p>',0,0,0,0,'216.175.102.223','en'),(4658,1212,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p>\r\nyes please. as long as we call ourselves \\\'the \r\ncraneflies\\\'. or whatever, i just wanna play.\r\n</p>',1,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4659,366,'2001-06-27 09:44:14',0,'future','is history',0,0,0,0,'64.168.23.97','en'),(4660,1212,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','oh steve. you don\\\'t have to wait for me to leave the house to play \r\nrush. i like rush, because of tuggy.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4661,1201,'2001-06-27 12:22:36',0,'Jojo','I preach to you from National Public Radio, specifically \r\nAll Things Considered, which if it does not consider \r\n<i>all</i> things, <i>selbstverstandlich</i>, considers a \r\nheckova lot of more things than I do.  Monday afternoon\\\'s \r\nedition of the PBS FM NPR/ATC, at least here in St. Dead \r\nEgo, had a report on the number of mosquitoes that alight \r\non the skin in 30 seconds in Houston, TX (answer: a \r\nfuckload) and then a discussion with a police chief (or \r\nchef) in Kentucky (or Kosovo) where they had had \r\nfive \\\"suicide-by-cops\\\" in the last month (or month) alone.  \r\nOur cerebral, never-touched-a-gun Noel Whatsisname, you \r\nknow who I mean, the host guy who sounds like a reliable \r\nfuck if not the most pyrotechnic (his voice intimates that \r\nhe will cover all the important details of your fuck \r\nthoroughly and wittily, whereas Linda Ellerbee resonates \r\nstridently impatient vibes in her voice, whose journalistic \r\nstyle in contradistinction to Noel Steadyboy can only be \r\ndescribed as pulsing with a nervous urgency; oh, whilst you \r\nspread your petals bewilderedly on the public radio couch, \r\nquivering and trying to anticipate where Linda will next \r\nthrust her strapped-on dildo (arse or Madagascar?), Linda \r\nis already striding towards her next headline: \r\ncoincidentally, her path of sources leads through you.  It \r\nis patently irresponsible and irrelevant to imagine the \r\nfuck-prowess of the one\\\'s daily newsreaders, especially if \r\nyou make a point to pledge a healthy 15% of your annual \r\npaycheck to them; such thoughts remove the religious tinct \r\nof tithing and impugn calumny.  Anyway.  I like Noel.), \r\nwhatever, Noel and the police chief had a broadcast \r\nconversation which remotely resembled the following \r\nreportage:<br><br>\r\n\r\n<i>Big Noel</i>: Dude, why didn\\\'t you like tell your homies \r\nto like, you know, fuckin\\\' chill, you know what I\\\'m \r\nsaying?  Like \\\'stead of zeroin\\\' dat gat straight up a \r\nbrother\\\'s viscera and splattin\\\' his li\\\'l chilluns all up \r\nhis chinos, why not fuckin\\\' fire a warnin\\\' shot or sumpin?  \r\nWord.<br><\r\n<i>Police Chief</i>: What?<br>\r\n<br><br>The end result of the report was that the use of \r\ndeadly force was <i>much more</i> prevalent than one would \r\nordinarily assume [that is, in a country of civilised \r\ncitizens].  The police chief\\\'s response to Noel\\\'s question \r\nabout \\\"a warning shot\\\" was an incredulous snort: \\\"That\\\'s in \r\nthe <i>movies</i>,\\\" he said, \\\"shooting to disarm, shooting \r\nonly to wound -- that\\\'s pure Hollywood.  The truth is, if \r\nsomeone is coming close to you wielding <i>a sharp \r\nedge</i>\\\" [italics mine: to add emphasis to what seems a \r\nrationale for police use of deadly force: <i>possession of \r\na sharp edge</i>] \\\"--- you\\\'re not going to think.  You\\\'re \r\ngoing to have to protect yourself and the innocents around \r\nyou.  You\\\'re going to have to take care of the \r\nsituation.\\\"<br>\r\nThis is not a defence nor dismissal of the pathetic soul \r\nwho decided to complete his life by dying in a hail of \r\npolice fire in the world-famous Metreon.  (Nor shall I \r\ncomment on the quality of a life lived with a girlfriend \r\nwho believed watching \\\"Swordfish\\\" would cheer someone up, \r\nand who apparently believed \\\"I will die tonight\\\" is proof \r\nthat that cheering-up had been achieved.)[I should be \r\ntaking such events, such real tragesies, blah blah blah, \r\nless lightly.  Ah but in this as in all things in life, \r\nSimpson\\\'s Law of Tragic Parsimony prevails: \\\'It\\\'s \r\nfunny \\\'cuz I don\\\'t know them.\\\']  All I wanted to say (and \r\nmaybe I will say it) is that I predice suicide-by-cop will \r\nbecome more prevalent in the future, for any number of \r\ncultural theory rationales (for those, I refer you to Herr \r\nMoebius) and also because of these two mathmatic \r\ncertainties that almost amount to a theorom (hanc \r\nmarginalis) --- because cops, apparently, will kill at the \r\nflash of an incisor (don\\\'t smile at them) --- and because \r\nas you and I live on and on, everyone else will want to die \r\nthat much sooner.<br><br><br><br><FONT SIZE=2>It\\\'s now 20 \r\nminutes to 1 million o\\\'clock.  By this rate I should be \r\ndead by Thursday.',4,0,0,0,'206.170.125.94','en'),(4662,1214,'2001-06-27 14:10:10',0,'jo','dude, yawn.<BR>\r\ntruth is stranger than fiction and much more interesting.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(4663,1214,'2001-06-27 14:44:07',0,'darkbloom','*yawn* *yawn* speaking in 2nd person? 3rd person?',6,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(4664,1212,'2001-06-27 14:49:05',0,'danielle','getty lee makes my ears hurt. i dont like rush either. im \r\ncanadian, should i like this canadian icon? no. icky.',3,0,0,0,'131.232.18.99','en'),(4665,1214,'2001-06-27 14:56:46',0,'puh-leez','<br>\r\neven if we dont all like griece, do we have to be so \r\ncritical?',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(4666,1214,'2004-02-07 03:45:28',534,'griece','<p>hey, you create a persona, you deal with the \r\nconsequences.\r\n\r\n<p>I expect some degree of flak as I move on.\r\n\r\n<p>jo\\\'s comment that \\\'truth is stranger than fiction\\\' is \r\naccurate to a point.  but you have to deal with the \r\nfundemental construct of <i>writing things down</i>.  \r\nit\\\'s not natural to write, it creates an inherent fiction, \r\ntalking you three or four steps from reality to \r\npresentation.  when you write things down, post them \r\nand let others read you are, in a sense, performing.\r\n\r\n<p>even if i said, this morning I had a cup of coffee and \r\na seseme bagel, your are dealing with a true \r\nstatement, but the words are just shadows on the wall \r\nof a cave in comparison, there is a degree of truth AND \r\na degree of fiction to it.\r\n\r\n<p>griece as a fiction is really no different than le, egg, \r\nincitor, jo or austin, et al.  maybe they are writing things \r\ncloser to reality than I have been, but it\\\'s still an \r\nunnatural conetext.  \r\n\r\n<p>it\\\'s been said that human beings do maybe two \r\nthings that set them apart from the animals:  we smoke \r\nand we write.  I think that statement is fundementally \r\nuntrue, but it illustrates what I\\\'m saying.  it is not natural \r\nto light some weeds on fire and breathe in the \r\nsmoke...in fact, it\\\'s deadly.  It is also not natural to sit \r\ndown and transcribe ideas and stories into symbols.   \r\nThe act of writing is the act of reconstructing reality, a \r\nreconfigured reality is NEVER true.  \r\n\r\n<p>\\\"BUT THAT\\\'S THE WAY IT HAPPENED.\\\"\r\n\r\n<p>No, not really.  You can\\\'t ever write the truth because \r\nwords are too slippery and mostly unpractical to \r\ndescribe situations.  Words approach meaning, but \r\nmeaning is layered UNDERNEATH them.  The best \r\nthings in life reside outside of language as concepts \r\nand emotions.  It\\\'s what poets have been trying to \r\ncapture for years.  Love.  Beauty.  Truth.  The \r\nimpossibility of pinning these things down is the best \r\nproof there is a God.\r\n\r\n<p>I dunno if I\\\'m making myself clear.  This is half-rant \r\nand half philosophy.\r\n\r\n<p>Today I went to the store.  I ate a doughnut.  My bike \r\ngot a flat when I was twenty miles from home.  Terry \r\nbought a meat sandwhich from the store, but the meat \r\nhad gone bad.  \r\n\r\n<p>Sentences are only sentences.  Words are only \r\nwords.  They stand in for experience, but only approach \r\nit.  Nothing is true when it is written down.  Not even \r\nthis.',0,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4667,1214,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p><tt>\r\nSun Opposition Saturn \r\n</tt></p><p><tt>\r\nSun opposition Saturn in the composite chart presents real \r\nproblems: temperaments so different as to cause difficulties, a \r\ntendency to work against rather than with each other, a tendency \r\nfor one of you to inhibit and limit the other unnecessarily, and \r\nexcessive criticism of each other. \r\n</tt></p><p><tt>\r\nIt is possible for a relationship with this configuration to survive, \r\nbut several conditions must be met. First, criticism must be limited \r\nto really important problems. Second, the relationship should be \r\nopen enough so that you can get away from each other in your \r\ndaily lives and lessen the tension between you. Third, the two of \r\nyou must broaden your viewpoints and become more tolerant of \r\nwhat you reject in each other. And fourth, you must have feelings \r\nof genuine love or friendship for each other. \r\n</tt>\r\n</p>',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4668,1212,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','not to spoil the fun or anything, but it\\\'s geddy.\r\n\r\nps: check out the black eyed susans',0,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(4669,1214,'2004-02-07 03:45:28',534,'griece','<p>i\\\'m trying to be nice here and present ideas rather \r\nthan conflict.  did this not come across?',1,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4670,1212,'2001-06-27 16:07:37',0,'danielle','to amend my statement, i do like rush. yay for math rock. i \r\njust dont like geDDy lee so i turn them off as soon as the \r\nsinging starts. :o',2,0,0,0,'131.232.18.99','en'),(4671,1212,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Geddy Moll','<p>When I wear my sunglasses, people tell me I look like\r\nGeddy Lee. It makes me kind of sad.</p>',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(4672,1214,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','<p>He wasn\\\'t very realistic anyway.</p>',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(4673,1211,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Brazil Moll','<p>SUSPICION BREEDS CONFIDENCE</p>\r\n',3,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(4674,1214,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','<p>\r\nso, you\'re confessing that you wrote under a pseudoname to \r\nraise certain unpopular view points. i can dig that. but \r\nyour writing voice lacks... substance? direction? \r\ncharisma? editing? perhaps all these things. but then you \r\ngo on to defend yourself by saying that writing doesn\'t \r\nwork, no one can Show The Truth. sounds more like you\'re \r\ntrying to say that because people don\'t \"get\" you, \r\nyou try to fling the cloak of \"oh, but none of it Really \r\nMeans Anything\" over all of us. uh. we\'re not that dumb.\r\n</p><p>\r\ni don\'t buy it. good writing _does_ have power. and \r\nsome people use it so well i can feel what they\'re trying \r\nto say when they write. this is the point. this is why i \r\nsit down and type the little words together. \r\n</p><p>\r\nwhat\'s YOUR point, besides the little nebulous potshots? \r\nthe wise fool can exist in collaboration with this group \r\n(see www.ilovelulu.com) and so can differing viewpoints. \r\nbut when someone is being noisy for the sake of being \r\nnoisy, they run the risk of being exposed for the man \r\nbehind the curtain that they are.</p><p>\r\nalso, i guess i wished griece\'s persona was more believable. when it was obvious that he didn\'t fool anyone,  it became tiresome. nothing irks more than an author that doesn\'t believe in your intelligence. i think that\'s why i didn\'t like this experiment. if you\'re going to lie to me, at least be good at it.</p>',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(4675,1203,'2001-06-27 17:03:55',0,'Jojo','I shall now graduate this poem out of triple-A play and let \r\nit run about in one major league outing.  OK, this is a \r\ndumb reaction to reading above about \\\"a poem saved out of \r\nretirement,\\\" as if a 9-5 gainfully employed poem was \r\nsomehow more fitting to be seen in society.  I do not know \r\nwhy the work ethic of the otherwise dour Puritans* has \r\ngrabbed such a hold of the language in which we Americanos \r\ndiscourse of our desires, our poems, our reveries, our \r\ntangelos.  The metaphor of poetry as a craft, or the life\\\'s \r\nexpression of an artist as his \\\"work\\\" --- either these \r\nreveal the essentially mercantile and telos-oriented \r\ncomplicity of America\\\'s artistic endeavour, or this reveals \r\nmy utter incompetence in working for a living at \r\nall.<br><br>If I should anthropomorphise poems at all (and \r\nthere is absolutely no need why I should), I should like to \r\nregard poems as either effete pale youths too beautiful for \r\nthis world and for work at Burger King, or as shambling \r\nbums mouthing alternate Old Testaments with beards \r\nindistinguishable from the umber tangled thickness of \r\npeat.  What would you picture?  Something different, I am \r\nsure.  <br><br>\r\nYou know, I seem to complicate things far too much for \r\nanyone\\\'s good.  Oh well.<br><br><br><br>\r\n\r\n* or, for the less generically minded, Calvinists, \r\nHobbesians, Melanchthonites: only pedants would think of \r\nthis; and you pedants, I love you! give me your phone \r\nnumbers!',4,0,0,0,'209.242.148.3','en'),(4676,1211,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','In my case, suspcion breeds anxiety and then anxiety breeds\r\nself-consciousness and self-doubt.  It\\\'s a bitter cycle, I know.',2,0,0,0,'206.47.244.62','en'),(4677,1212,'2001-06-27 17:20:14',0,'danielle','once when i was wearing the hood up on a hoodie and dark \r\nglasses, this drunk guy told me i looked like the Unabomber. \r\nI was kinda unimpressed.',1,0,0,0,'131.232.18.99','en'),(4678,1203,'2001-06-27 17:28:10',0,'Jojo','and, umm, to keep with the citrus-minded poetry theme that \r\nI had forgotten in my previous post:\r\n\r\nI\\\'ve never had a tangelo, nor heard of one.<br>\r\nI thought of Beverley D\\\'Angelo, famous of \\\"National<br>\r\nLampoon\\\'s Vacation,\\\" I thought of fellatio,<br><br>\r\n\r\nof \\\"Rigoletto,\\\" of tic-tac-dough: but a tangelo<br>\r\nnever before has introduced itself into my impoverished<br>\r\n(I realise it now) existence.  Pity your poor Jojo,<br><br>\r\n\r\nverse-slack and insular, clouted by forced rhyme-a-go-\r\ngo,<br>\r\nsuddenly undone by rumours of big balled fruit.  Oh woe<br>\r\nis, well, me.  I should let this rhyme scheme go.<br><br>\r\n\r\nSuddenly a blank, distinctly oranger than orange<br>\r\nand spherical, has come apart in me, a space<br>\r\naches within me, born from rumour of some lovely fruit:<br>\r\n<br>\r\nwherever there is lack, there is desire: and I desire<br>\r\nto taste the taste of others, untantalus<br>\r\nthe myth of tangelos (tangeloes?) you\\\'ve cunningly \r\nwired<br><br>\r\n\r\ninto your poem.  Unblank me, teach me tangelo,<br>\r\nclose up the unfruit hollow taking shape within me,<br>\r\nfulfil this lack, this desire.  Fill my mouth not with \r\nwords.<br>',2,0,0,0,'209.242.148.3','en'),(4679,1213,'2001-06-27 17:35:34',0,'danielle','blended fruit juices dribbling down my chin',2,0,0,0,'131.232.18.99','en'),(4680,1201,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Pong Moll','<p>You are on fire, girl. You really are. Make more.</p>',1,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(4681,1214,'2004-02-07 03:45:28',534,'griece','<pre>\r\nWeeb, you\\\'re misunderstanding what I said.  I suppose \r\nthat part of my problem is that I just write this stuff \r\nsomewhat off the cuff.  Anyway, I didn\\\'t say that writing \r\ndoesn\\\'t have power.  I\\\'ve read so many books that have \r\naffected me deeply, that have toppled my sense of \r\nreality and forced me to rexamine myself.  I\\\'ve had a few \r\nstories published here-and-there in nondescript \r\ncollege journals so I must be doing something right \r\nwith that.  But this off-the-cuff shit is just like an \r\nexercise, a way to explore what people react to and how \r\nthey react to it.  It\\\'s not really a venue for art, because art \r\nis more considered and planned.  It\\\'s better.  \r\n\r\nWhat I was trying to say (I\\\'ll slow down and consider my \r\nwords here), is that writing is a construction, not a \r\nreality.  That\\\'s important, so I\\\'ll say it again:  WRITING IS \r\nA CONSTRUCTION, NOT A REALITY.  \r\n\r\nNow let me restate what I meant.  When a person sits \r\ndown to record their innermost thoughts and emotions,  \r\nthey may well-believe that they are putting down the \r\ngods-honest truth, and so they are.  However, words \r\nare slippery things that don\\\'t quite pin the bug to the \r\nboard.  You can write about jealousy and anger, fools \r\nand relationships, you can reconstruct your life on the \r\npage, but no matter how powerful and talented the \r\nwriter, they are trying to evoke something by using \r\nabstract tools.  That\\\'s what I\\\'m trying to say WORDS \r\nARE ABSTRACTS.\r\n\r\nLike a mathamatical abstract that uses formulae to \r\ndepict a concept, sentences depict concepts, they are \r\nrepresentatons of the real things, not the things \r\nthemselves.  Words, sentences and phrases are not \r\nthe end.  These abstracts can re-translate in our minds \r\nas actual emotion, but that\\\'s probably because they link \r\nto something familiar in our own lives.  Words can \r\nactivate sympathy but are not inherently sympathetic.\r\n\r\nWhy is this? \r\n\r\nLets bring up Plato again, more clearly this time.  You \r\nknow the shadows-on-the-cave story?  Well, words are \r\nthese shadows that are depicting the form of the real \r\nthings outside.  Words connect us to reality that is \r\ndeeper than ourselves.  There is something out there, \r\nbeyond us.  For lack of a better word, let\\\'s call it THE \r\nDIVINE.  What\\\'s bound up in THE DIVINE?  Love, truth, \r\nbeauty, etc., all those unknowables.  What words to is \r\nbring the divine to us.  They penetrate the barrier of \r\nlanguage and help us to understand.\r\n\r\nBut because words can only illustrate rather than BE \r\nTHE DIVINE, we are forever approaching, dancing \r\naround.  Words are our only link to the divine, but it is \r\nnot enough to truly bring it to us.\r\n\r\nThis is why the poets write, why the novelists keep \r\nchurning out books.  My argument here isn\\\'t a \r\njustification for the past stuff I wrote, it\\\'s an attempt to \r\nbroaden the conversation.  I could care less if I fooled \r\nyou with griece\\\'s barroom antics, that\\\'s not important.  \r\n\r\nAll I\\\'m saying here is that words are ineffective, but \r\nbeautiful.  They\\\'re all we really have to know GOD.  \r\nEverything else is just a futile dance.',1,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4682,1214,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','</pre>what i am, is calling you on your categorization that this place is the place for off the cuff stuff. \"it\'s not art\" doesn\'t cut it.people care and live here, so it IS art. and i do think that if you\'re going to write, it should be something you\'re going to put time into. i am not disagreeing with your abstract blah blah blah, so let\'s stop beating that poor dead horse.',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(4683,1216,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','petting of the le.\n',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(4684,1214,'2001-06-27 18:50:42',0,'Jojo','This is odd.  Apparently some of you operate on some \r\ntheory, or mathmatic, or religion, or scout\\\'s oath, or \r\nsomething, that personality and the myth of the individual \r\nis contingent in some fashion (transcendant? radial? \r\nelliptical? octal?) on a measure of <i>authenticity</i>.  \r\nThis is nice if one can take comfort in it.  I don\\\'t see \r\nhow one would, however, seeing just how many advantages one \r\nis afforded and how many disagreements are avoided when one \r\ntakes the perspective that we are all liars, frauds, \r\nbraggarts, ego snipers, inveterate fictioneers: and that ---\r\n most especially in this forum (which is my context, after \r\nall: if I\\\'ve bum-rushed some kind of private squabble made \r\npublic then this is all irrelevant, but I shall speak \r\nirrelevantly at anyroad [in the <i>reductio ad \r\ninfinitum</i>, everything is made irrelevant except the \r\nsound of distant laughter and the number ten] and then shut \r\nup) --- we make ourselves known to each other by our \r\nvarious <i>personnae</i>, delimned for those in the know by \r\napposite jeugonyms; what does it matter if one imaginary \r\nfigment is shown to have been in disguised?  greice, \r\nwhatever hir/hes intentions were, made poking gestures at \r\nunpeeling the onion of identity* by crawling beneath the \r\ntime-varnished wooden shell of this old chestnut**: \r\n<i>Everything is fiction.</i>****<br><br>\r\nWell, I\\\'ve just shot my wad trying to catch up to all my \r\nfootnotes here, so I\\\'ll shut up now.<br><br><br>\r\n------------<br>\r\n* and don\\\'t you just love to what lengths I go to make a \r\nvivid metaphor?  It\\\'s all for you, pedants of the world.  \r\nPedants of the world! I await your arrival at my door!\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\n** and look, I did it again!  I <i>love</i>***, simply \r\n<i>love</i> the baroque tics and arabesques I***** subject \r\na simple word to.  <br><br>\r\n\r\n*** \\\"Love\\\" is too strong a word, even for describing the \r\nrazorblade-embedded hailstorm of daily travails and joys \r\nthat passes for love in our anagapemanic culture.  I \r\npropose use of the expression \\\"#REF!\\\" in all future \r\nconversation instead of the vanished souvenier \r\nof \\\"love.\\\"<br><br>\r\n\r\n**** Actually, I have no idea if Griece said that, since \r\n(a) I don\\\'t have the wherewithal to refer to his posting in \r\nmy own posting [both because of the limitations of posting \r\nand because I am a lazyass logorrhite and graphomaniac who \r\ncannot be bothered to open another browser window], and (b) \r\nwhen I <i>do</i> read posts, I get to a certain point and \r\nthen my eyes glaze over and I just scan for some remark as \r\nan excuse to respond crankily.  Actually, I don\\\'t do this; \r\nI***** do this.<br><br>\r\n\r\n***** It may be useful to someone, probably not you, to \r\nrecall de Saussere\\\'s distinction between \\\"the enunciating \r\nsubject\\\" [\\\"l\\\'enonce\\\"] and \\\"the subject of enunciation\\\" [\\\"le \r\nsujet d\\\'enonce\\\"] wherein begins the semiotic and \r\nstructuralist study of identity.  De Saussere noted that, \r\nfor example, in the sentence \\\"I told you that I would never \r\nlet him touch my tits again,\\\" the \\\"I\\\" that is \\\"telling\\\" is \r\ndistinct from the \\\"I\\\" that is being told about.  If one \r\nwere to get all Lacanian on one\\\'s bidness, that one could \r\nsay that we all discourse in the realm of the Imaginary, \r\nwhere meaning is elided in a metonymy of referential \r\nsignifications: a mask or a trope, so to say, which \r\nsignifies only another mask or trope.  All this boils down \r\nto simply to the fiction of a unified, individual \\\"I\\\": \r\nlanguage, telling, fora posting, all expression is \r\npredicated on a schizoid faultline: it does not matter, in \r\nan \\\"only honesty counts\\\" way, whether \\\"greice\\\" or \\\"ur-\r\ngriece\\\" or \\\"ancient griece\\\" said this and that: it is all a \r\ncunning mobile of persuasive lies, told by a self-conscious \r\nliar.',4,0,0,0,'209.242.148.3','en'),(4685,1216,'2001-06-27 18:57:49',0,'danielle','*cuddles up to le*',1,0,0,0,'207.34.94.238','en'),(4686,1214,'2004-02-07 03:45:28',534,'griece','<p>Wow, JoJo, that was <i>really cool</i>.  \r\n\r\n<p>Only i\\\'m not nearly smart enough to understand half \r\nof what you said.  should i be insulted?  Were you \r\ndisagreeing?  Please help me out.  \r\n\r\n<p>However,  I smell some DFW in that, but i couldn\\\'t \r\npenetrate Infinite Jest, let alone Saussere, Derrida & \r\nCo.  I tend more toward Lorrie Moore, Haruki Murakami, \r\nRick Moody & Paul Auster as my personal icons of \r\ncontemporary fiction.  I did, however, read and enjoy \r\n<i>A Supposedly Fun Thing...</i>\r\n\r\n<p>I generally stay away from the philosphers.  In fact, \r\nI\\\'m a little m-bare-assed, what with my half-baked \r\nideas of the divine, \\\'n such, which I\\\'m sure look pretty \r\nthought-impoverished to you.  I don\\\'t know, I read some \r\nJulian Jaynes once and came up with this layman\\\'s \r\nphilosphy fusing the bicameral mind & language & \r\nconsciousness, qua qua qua.  But I haven\\\'t thought \r\nabout it too much lately, there\\\'s been beer to drink and \r\na job or two that I had to work, oh and I got married.\r\n\r\n<p>But reading your coment again, and again, and yet \r\nagain.  I\\\'m pretty sure that you agree with me, though I \r\nknow there was some sarcasm in there somewhere.  \r\n\r\n<p>Frankly, I\\\'m bitterly jealous of your brain.  \r\n\r\n<p> &nbsp P.S.  I bought a painting I really liked last \r\nweek.  I put it up on my wall and it pulled the nail out of \r\nthe plaster.  It fell to the ground and the corner of the \r\npainting dented.  It\\\'s now kind of lopsided, but still \r\nbeautiful in that way that paintings are beautiful.\r\n\r\n',6,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4687,1216,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>dude. lets smoke pot and listen to cat power.</p>',0,0,0,0,'216.175.106.219','en'),(4688,1213,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>i thought he was wearing tighty red-ies.</p>',0,0,0,0,'216.175.106.219','en'),(4689,1214,'2001-06-27 19:26:21',0,'chris','<p>hi, my name is chris. for the past year or so, I have \r\nbeen writing under the alias \\\'<a \r\nhref=\\\'http://www.swinney.org/journals/userpages.phtml?\r\nusername=BMG\\\'>bmg</a>\\\'. i have a deep conviction to tell \r\nyou all that in all honesty no part of my name actualy has \r\nthe letters B, M, or G, save my middle name, Mark. i would \r\nalso like to point out that in I am in contrast to the \r\ndefinition of the <a \r\nhref=\\\'http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?\r\nid=279.txt\\\'>Bass Master General</a>. i read self-help books \r\nabout love and relationships. I am sorry if you ladies, or \r\nmen, are disapointed.</p>',1,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(4690,1216,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','add whiskey. ok.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4691,1216,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i wish i smoked so i could smoke and pace. puff, pace.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4692,1212,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','geddy. thanks ix. it was 4am.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4693,1214,'2004-02-07 03:45:28',534,'griece','<p>\\\"people care and live here, so it IS art\\\"\r\n\r\n<p>people care and live in my apartment building, but \r\nthat doesn\\\'t make it art.\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4694,1215,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','check out <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.theice.org/\\\">theice.org</a>. it\\\'s all \r\nabout this guy\\\'s experience living in antarctica, repairing \r\nweather stations for a living. i fell in love with antarctica \r\njust from the overhead photos. there\\\'s *nothing* there.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4695,1214,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','your definition of art seems limited.',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(4696,1214,'2001-06-27 20:26:18',0,'puppy','so, just out of curiosity, what makes this different from\nthe <a\nhref=\\\"http://chatting.about.com/internet/chatting/library/blkaycee.htm\\\">Kaycee\nNicole hoax</a>?',3,0,0,0,'192.35.232.99','en'),(4697,1214,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','this is going to be an unpopular opinion, but i enjoyed \r\ngriece. i didn\\\'t find the charatcer to be particularly \r\nthreatening. though i think you could have gone deeper. \r\nyou were starting to write stories about the ordinary \r\npeople griece would come across in bars. i liked that.\r\n',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4698,1213,'2001-06-27 20:34:28',0,'chi chi','\r\nno, they were white. i remember a momentary \r\nblindness, as if i was looking into the sun. maybe it \r\nwas just his white arse.',0,0,0,0,'64.168.23.97','en'),(4699,1215,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>youre going to announce that you have a copy of \r\nVespertine and not rip it for us?</p>\r\n<p>you bastard.</p>',0,0,0,0,'216.175.106.219','en'),(4700,1216,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg is a wordy ho','<p>you wanna know something though? love doesnt \r\nreally do anything for  you, but you do realize that you \r\nare going to be jumping back on the love train again \r\nand doing the same shit over and over. you realize that, \r\nright? and in three years when some other love falls \r\napart youll be listening to cat power and going, \\\"dude, \r\nlove doesnt do shit.\\\"</p><p> that must sound like shit. \r\nanother prescription: bjork\\\'s homogenic. the last time I \r\nwas sad and broken up I put on that song that goes \r\n\\\"how could i be so immature to think he could fill the \r\nmissing elements in me? how extremely lazy of me!\\\" \r\nand sat in different configurations in my living room. \r\n</p>',0,0,0,0,'216.175.106.219','en'),(4701,1214,'2004-02-07 03:45:28',534,'griece','<p>s5,\r\n\r\n<p>I have a few more of those \\\"people I met in bars\\\" \r\nstories.  They\\\'re true.  They will still be written.\r\n\r\n<p>weeb,\r\n\r\n<p>My definition of art is not \\\"limited.\\\"  it is \r\n<i>rigorous.</i>',1,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(4702,1215,'2001-06-27 20:55:22',0,'homer simpsons','<p>\\\"mmm.. recirculated air..\\\"</p>',1,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(4703,1216,'2001-06-27 21:00:52',0,'dahlia','oh le. i am sorry you are sad, chickadee but this is so \r\nbeautiful it made me cry. \r\n\r\n*weeps into ceasar salad*',1,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(4704,1215,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','I\\\'ve had the Vepstertine promo for nearly two months now. \r\nIt\\\'s just a promo, though.  Some of the titles for the\r\nactual release are different and it\\\'s not the same tracks as\r\nwhat is going to be available in August, however, it is\r\namazing.  It is her best album yet and close to the point of\r\nbeing mind-numbingly perfect.  If you want it, e-mail me: <a\r\nhref=\\\"mailto:fuzzy@hax0rs.com\\\">fuzzy@hax0rs.com</a>.',1,0,0,0,'206.47.244.62','en'),(4705,1214,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>I think griece\\\'s (whoever that is) writing was/is pretty \r\ngood, but the persona was just plain implausible. There are \r\nquite a number of people who are alcoholic, etc., etc., but \r\nsomething about him never quite rang true. Sounded like a \r\nBukowski knock-off, really.</p>\r\n<p>If I have something to say about the whole other art \r\ndiscussion, I\\\'ll do it when I have more time or when I care \r\nmore.</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n',3,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(4706,1214,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','keep at it. the other night, i was working in my music \r\nstudio, trying to perfect a technique. to do this, i had to \r\nloop the same 4 measures over and over \r\nagain for about an hour. (i purposely chose 4 \r\nmeasures that i hated anyway - no sense in getting sick \r\nof something i might want to use for a song). the loop \r\ndroned and carried on, until i no longer heard music; \r\ninstead i heard the technique, floating over the notes, \r\nand at last i could manipulate the technique directly, \r\nshaping it into what i wanted. and such is the creative \r\nprocess. perfecting your voice is loud screeching pain \r\nto those who are witness.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4707,1214,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','ps. i thought griece should have been a woman.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4708,1214,'2001-06-27 21:38:57',0,'erin','interesting the \\\'implausability\\\' and \\\'unrealistic\\\' \r\ncomments..Griece reminded me OFTEN of my friend Jim to the \r\npoint i often wondered if it was him. aside from the \r\ncleveland bit. so maybe not implauable or unrealistic - just \r\nsomeone you\\\'ve never known.  \r\n',0,0,0,0,'129.105.107.184','en'),(4709,1214,'2001-06-27 21:57:25',0,'Jojo','Hello.  Hey, I\\\'d written what I thought was a scabrous \r\ncomedy about all this, starting off with a parody of \r\nacademia Ã¡ la whoever writes academic parody; and then I \r\nleft off because, well, I was distracted by something \r\nshiny.  I will post it, because it will puzzle and bore the \r\n<i>hoi polloi</i> and move the <i>roy phalloi</i> among you \r\nto auto-immolation, defenestrations and acts of <i>salÃ²-da-\r\nfÃ©</i>--- all things we need more of in \r\nCalifornia.<br><br><br> However, it\\\'s more sarcastic, \r\nbrittle, pompous, cold and cruel than most joke columns \r\nare; and I use the arguments discussed in this thread in an \r\nabsolutely cavalier manner.  There is an apology, or \r\ndisclaimer, embedded in my hahamento, but since it is \r\nsurrounded and permeated by a mustard-gas aura of scholarly \r\nupmanship reminiscent of the welcome reception gala at \r\nDachau (I mean the 1933 one, not the failed 1931 party, boy \r\nwas <i>that</i> a gas), I felt I should disclaim my \r\ndisclaimer prefaratorily-like, like in, um, this preface.  \r\nSo.  Following is how I spent Wednesday June 27 2001, \r\nbetween the hours of 5.00 pm and <i>aleph-null</i> o\\\'clock, \r\nwhen I could have prospered by staying home and playing \r\nwith myself (but I, I was feeling sinister).',4,0,0,0,'209.242.148.3','en'),(4710,1214,'2001-06-27 21:59:45',0,'Jojo the obstreporous','Read previous apology please, if you\\\'d read this following \r\nantilogia.\r\n\r\n\r\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\r\nI spent all morning writing my exegesis, in between bouts \r\nof smoking and bouts of coughing, only to find the argument \r\nhas moved on apace while I was writing.  Oh well.  And the \r\ninfamous griece has posted something quite remarkable, so \r\nremarkable in fact I would like to take this opportunity to \r\ndo a close reading of it and comment to some of the points \r\nraised.<br><br>\r\n(I was going to post again anyway because I had \r\nmisspelled \\\"juegonyms\\\" in my post; but since that\\\'s a \r\nneologism, it doesn\\\'t really matter anyway [and since the \r\nwhole point of my point was that nothing really matters \r\nanyway, it really doesn\\\'t really matter really \r\nanyway]).<br><br>\r\nOh, and a disclaimer: in my following reading, I raise \r\ncertain disagreements and critique what I find to be \r\nphilosophical and revealing psychological flaws of the \r\nfocalising intelligence that informs \\\"griece\\\"\\\'s piece.  \r\nThis should not be read as an attack on \\\"griece\\\": it \r\n<i>is</i> an attack, but not a personal one, since it is \r\nthe contention (as I understand it, anyway) that \\\"griece\\\" \r\nis a fictional contrivance employed by some cabal or \r\ncaballist to disavow any authorial responsibility, \r\naesthetic or intelligence.  Since this furthers the \r\npurposes of Dada, Surrealism and the New World Order, I \r\nlaud the invention of \\\"griece\\\".<br><br>\r\nThe original text is presented in underline, with comments \r\npresented in invisible-ink line.  Begin \r\nanalysis:<br><br><br>\r\n<U>Weeb, you\\\'re misunderstanding what I said.  I suppose \r\nthat part of my problem is that I just write this stuff \r\nsomewhat off the cuff.  Anyway, I didn\\\'t say that writing \r\ndoesn\\\'t have power.  I\\\'ve read so many books that have \r\naffected me deeply, that have toppled my sense of \r\nreality and forced me to rexamine myself.</U><br><br>\r\nThis introduces the narrator\\\'s strategy of authorial \r\nirresponsibility.  A distinction is made, hinted at here \r\nand elaborated bombastically later on, between \\\"books\\\" \r\nand \\\"reality,\\\" \\\"off the cuff\\\" and \\\"art\\\", \\\"understanding\\\" \r\nand \\\"saying,\\\" \\\"Weeb\\\" and \\\"I\\\"; narratologically, \\\"griece\\\" \r\nopposes binary pairs in a kind of Manichean dualism and \r\nleaves them there, without following the dialectic of his \r\nargument nor examining the value-ordinations implied by his \r\nargument -- a flawed logic, a useless galimitias, until one \r\nconsiders that the narrator (\\\"griece,\\\" and not \\\"griece\\\'s\\\" \r\nmeta-Author) is in fact a cunningly defensive, \r\nirresponsible, professedly artless intelligence, and that \r\nwhat passes for \\\"argument\\\" in his prose poem is in fact a \r\nslippery barrage of hollow profundities, Rimbaud-like \r\nmooning, Rambo-esque posturing, econo-sized and supermarket-\r\npriced insight, conmingled with a narrative consciousness \r\nthat both demands to be taken seriously and furtively \r\nsquirms out of being taken seriously.  Consider:<br><br>\r\n<u>  I\\\'ve had a few \r\nstories published here-and-there in nondescript \r\ncollege journals so I must be doing something right \r\nwith that.  But this off-the-cuff shit is just like an \r\nexercise, a way to explore what people react to and how \r\nthey react to it.  It\\\'s not really a venue for art, because \r\nart is more considered and planned.  It\\\'s better.  \r\n</u><br><br>\r\n\r\nThe carefully thrownaway line about magazine \r\npublication, \\\"in nondescript journals,\\\" brilliantly \r\nportrays \\\"griece\\\" as both charmingly modest and yet \r\nauthoritative (\\\"so I must be doing something right\\\": \r\npublication automatically validates his \\\"rightness\\\").  \r\nUnfortunately, this also allows the narrator to use \r\nthe \\\"appeal to authority\\\" argument, which, while sounding \r\nimpressive with all its grandiose talk and peeks of hard-\r\nwon knowledge, does not actually impress.<br><br>\r\n\r\n<u>\r\nWhat I was trying to say (I\\\'ll slow down and consider my \r\nwords here), is that writing is a construction, not a \r\nreality.  That\\\'s important, so I\\\'ll say it again:  WRITING \r\nIS A CONSTRUCTION, NOT A REALITY.  </u><br><br>\r\n\r\nThe tone is supercilious, condescending, as if it \r\nis \\\"obvious\\\" that \\\"WRITING IS A CONSTRUCTION, NOT A \r\nREALITY.\\\"  The narrator does not address the obvious \r\nquestion he raises, however, which is: What is reality, \r\nthen?  A more cogent quizzing would be, If writing is a \r\nconstruction, and writing is not reality, then is reality \r\n<i>not</i> a construction?  \\\"Griece\\\"\\\'s insistence on a \r\ntranscendant, transpersonal, anepistemological \\\"reality\\\" \r\ndiffers from the Lacanian use of the \\\"Real\\\" in \r\nthat \\\"Griece\\\" explicitly disdains the symbolic register \r\nwhich allows participants to <i>understand</i> their \r\nexperience of reality in the first place.  \\\"Griece\\\" faults \r\nthe construction of experience as fundamentally flawed \r\n(apparently in favour of some Creation-minded God-figure \r\nthat magically wills \\\"Reality\\\" as \\\"Griece\\\" will have it) \r\nand insinuates that any communicatication, based on such a \r\nflaw, would thus also be flawed, and therefore useless of \r\nconsideration.  (He recapitulates, in a Canadian kind of \r\nway, the whole of Gnostic Christianity.)<br>\r\n\\\"Griece\\\" problematizes his screed of failed communication \r\nby his use of that exact failure in his apoploxegy, and at \r\nonce luminously conveys a superior grasp of this knowledge \r\nand our stupidity for not recognising it.  Basically, he \r\nsays, \\\"YOU ARE STUPID.\\\"  He tells us twice.\r\n<br><br>\r\n<u>\r\nNow let me restate what I meant.  When a person sits \r\ndown to record their innermost thoughts and emotions,  \r\nthey may well-believe that they are putting down the \r\ngods-honest truth, and so they are.  However, words \r\nare slippery things that don\\\'t quite pin the bug to the \r\nboard.  You can write about jealousy and anger, fools \r\nand relationships, you can reconstruct your life on the \r\npage, but no matter how powerful and talented the \r\nwriter, they are trying to evoke something by using \r\nabstract tools.  That\\\'s what I\\\'m trying to say WORDS \r\nARE ABSTRACTS.</u><br><br>\r\nAnother brilliant use of abstraction to point out that \r\nabstraction is abstract, surrounded with examples so homey \r\nand easily intuitive that the fact they prove nothing is \r\nobscured by the warm glow of flawed understanding of \r\nnothing at all.<br><br><br>\r\n',4,0,0,0,'209.242.148.3','en'),(4711,1214,'2001-06-27 22:04:44',0,'Jojo','<br>Oh, I forgot the last line: \\\"look, something \r\nshiny.\\\"<br><br>And fuckadoodledoo, I forgot what I was \r\ngoing to say right now.<br><br>Trust me, it was real \r\nfunny.  Like Mrs. Lincoln in Ford\\\'s Theatre funny.',4,0,0,0,'209.242.148.3','en'),(4712,1216,'2001-06-27 22:27:06',0,'bmg','<p>days like this, I listen to Tracey Thorn blast out her \r\nvocal talents ... \\\"protection\\\" from massive attack is one \r\nsuch song i like to cry to... peace be with you sister.</p>',2,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(4713,1215,'2002-03-15 00:17:55',129,'moebius','<br>oh oh <b>Vespertine.</b> so there\\\'s something i\\\'ve been \r\ndesiring to hear for some time now. i gather the \r\ncolaboration with bay area laptop electronica wizards <a \r\nhref= \\\"http://www.brainwashed.com/matmos/\\\">Matmos</a> went \r\nwell?<br>',0,0,0,0,'64.165.96.58','en'),(4714,1218,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','<BR>\r\nthis is great :). i kinda understand.\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,'203.96.111.202','en'),(4715,1214,'2001-06-27 23:36:37',0,'????','??????????!',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4716,1218,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','god i wish i lived in sf so i could come on to women and \r\nnot be afraid of some kind of lynching for my troubles.  \r\nyou know, i probably would be too shy to hit on women in \r\nwhatever city i am living in.  i certainly can\\\'t even hit \r\non boys, and they\\\'re meant to like girls, right?<br>\r\n<br>\r\nsex and dating sucks ass.  i just want someone to love.',3,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(4717,1216,'2001-06-28 00:04:20',0,'Jojo the ovocephalic','<br><br>Thank you, O above posterhead, for mentioning \r\nTracey Thorne: I had just formulated the beginnings of a \r\nhatching of an ideation that perhaps I wanted to write down \r\nthe medley of the 4,000 radio stations simulcasting in my \r\nhead [and ask, peripherally, whether this was common or \r\nhave I died and been cryogenically stored inside a portable \r\ncorpsicle mp3 PDA box {I think 3M sells these}{och, I \r\nrealise I\\\'m stealing this from Philip K. Dick\\\'s \r\n<i>UBIK</i>; ach, so}] but no, not until you mentioned that \r\ncrushedmoonpie-faced chanteuse did I think of Tracey \r\nThorne\\\'s <i>A Distant Shore</i>:<br><br>\r\nHow can you bear to go on this way?<br>\r\nWhen each time we meet you turn the other way<br>\r\nEverything has now been said<br>\r\nNow the fire is cold and dead<br>\r\nLeave behind your tears unshed<br>\r\nNew opened eyes must look ahead<br>\r\n       - <i>New Opened Eyes</i>, duh<br><br><br>\r\nAnyway; le, I had wanted to write a poem to you, for no \r\ngood reason than you\\\'re sad, and the shellshocked quality \r\nof your writing invites every human reading it to comfort \r\nyou; your friends invite you to smoke and listen to cat \r\npower (they sound like good friends); and I\\\'ve no idea what \r\nwe other strangers can offer you, so I looked about in the \r\nfucked-up WKRP of my head to see if I could piece a poem \r\nand send it to you, one stranger to another (though (though \r\nthis means nothing) I would be writing too from the \r\nbattlefield of broken relationship: here, in the interval \r\nbetween heartbreak and hello, the pause separating the \r\nothers significant and in that will ruin our lives and \r\nsteal our cats\\\' affections, I could write you a poem that \r\nmay distract you from the the recognitions and reflections \r\nof the life that\\\'s disappeared, I could write you a poem, \r\noh I am being selfish, I would write you a poem simply out \r\nof my anxiety of never saying anything poetic again: for \r\nthe poetry had gone out of my life like an extinguished egg \r\ncandle: and I would write you a poem, isolate to \r\nsupplicant, in the hopes of discovering in the invocation \r\nand loss into the poem a metre, a sense of rhyme, a music \r\nthat has been stupidly gone since I fell out of \r\nrelationship and into remaining.  Auden said, Poetry is \r\nuseless; and you know, he\\\'s right, poetry, like love, will \r\nnot overcome depression, nor the triumph of death, nor the \r\npain of mourning, nor a whole litany of enormous, gigantic \r\nthings.  You know that as well as I.  However, poetry, like \r\nlove, when it is good (so strange how rare it seems such \r\nquality flies in through the windows we keep open or forget \r\nto close, how often that happens) can exhalt us, make the \r\nworld merrygorounding round us feel a grand ride, carbonate \r\nour bloodstream, banish our noonday nightmares.  Poetry, \r\nlike love, may be useless, like Auden said; but then again, \r\nI only know of Auden as a poet and a lover; any other \r\nqualities he had are obscured by how grandly he lived those \r\nuseless, extremist vocations.<br><br>\r\nI am not telling you anything useful; I am not telling you \r\nanything sensible.  For one thing, you are surrounded by \r\nsupportive friends, it seems, and they can advise you and \r\nhelp you and embrace you, cuddle you, coddle you, comfort \r\nyou.  I, though, am wilfully stubborn to commonsense \r\nworkarounds to loss.  I refuse strategies for surviving \r\nlife post-beloved.  I would rather it rain for the next one \r\nhundred years, and I walk the streets and sidewalks through \r\nthe sullen night, mourning and pitying myself and the \r\nidiocies I did and did not do that has landed me here, \r\n<i>sola, perduta Ã© abadonnata</i>.  You probably have \r\nsunnier itineraries in future, le.  I wish you luck.<br><br>\r\nInstead of this oversentimental clacktrack sodden with self-\r\npity and gratuitous incongruity, imagine instead I have \r\nwritten you a poem: and this poem, replete with idiotic \r\npuns and singsong rhymes out of Billy Bragg, made you whirl \r\nyour eyes and say aloud, to no one in particular, <i>What \r\nis this fool on?</i>  That would be enough, le: to stir you \r\nout of heartache, to make your eyes whirl round.  Tell the \r\nworld you were in love.  Otherwise, poetry, like love, has \r\nno other purpose.',4,0,0,0,'209.242.148.3','en'),(4718,1214,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','<p>\r\n\\/\\/\r\n</p><p>\r\nyou\'re just full of hot air. see jojo\'s remarks.</p>',6,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(4719,1218,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','i so completely understand. and have woken up most mornings \r\nfor the past week and a half with a very confusing girl in \r\nher underwear whose arm has draped lazily over my neck and \r\nwho has occasionally brought me mimosas.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(4720,1216,'2001-06-28 00:20:03',0,'kat','cant stop thinking\r\nno tears all fears\r\ngoing down quick\r\nsinking\r\nbeing alone\r\nthinking\r\nalways was solo\r\nits over\r\nno going back\r\nlost track\r\ndon\\\'t forget\r\ngot my bag\r\nsleeping on the floor\r\nfull circle and more\r\nthinking\r\nno tears all fears\r\nself conscious\r\ndreaming\r\nno movement\r\nslow bleeding\r\ncant stop thinking\r\nsleeping on the floor\r\none pillow\r\nalone\r\nno more time to be bored\r\njust creeping\r\non the backstep\r\nwish I could scream\r\nits all a bad dream\r\nno crutch anymore\r\nmade the turn\r\nno going back\r\none pillow is all I have\r\nround the tracks\r\ndon\\\'t get burned\r\nremember the worst\r\nlost my shirt\r\nleft me bleeding\r\ncant stop thinking\r\nembrace the hurt\r\nno tears all fears\r\nonly one pillow left\r\nno bed\r\nno ring\r\nno dreams\r\nwandering on the track\r\ngot pushed back\r\nnothing to feel\r\nfull circle\r\non the wheel',1,0,0,0,'12.64.31.162','en'),(4721,1214,'2004-02-03 19:35:30',533,'incitor','this whole thing gives me gas in the worst way.  pinky in \r\nthe air discussion of \\\'artistic\\\' expression is all well and \r\ngood,  however, through griece and his/her/its methods, \r\nmuch of what i loved best about this place is now gone to \r\nme.  swinney went from one of the finest little nooks i\\\'ve \r\nfound in over a decade of being online to just another BBS \r\nback when i was 13.  the same reason i distanced myself \r\nfrom that community, the same reason i\\\'ve ended so many \r\nfriendships over the last few years, is now the reason i \r\nfeel uncomfortable here.  there is no longer any point to \r\nsharing of my life, for i can never trust that i am seeing \r\nanything but another geek pretending to be more than he or \r\nshe is, just like when i was 13.  i was ridiculed for \r\nspeaking of my life, was accused of being a liar and \r\nworse.  even darwin, now my best friend, once was caught up \r\nin it, and stopped speaking with me for years.  funny thing \r\nwas, whenever i met these people who so assaulted my \r\nwriting, they were invariably nothing like they claimed; \r\nwhereas i was exactly what i had said all along.  saddest \r\nof all to me, is that i know tens of people just like \r\ngriece pretended to be.  to me, this persona was not \r\nanything new, was not art, could not be an experiment.  it \r\nwas just another known quantity, boring and sad.  ehhh.  \r\nforget it.',6,0,0,0,'172.166.144.201','en'),(4722,1214,'2001-06-28 01:33:18',0,'ratcatcher','It is semi-relevant here, don\\\'t you agree, to plug the most \r\nalmost-talented griecian cliche on the web?  Mark Driver \r\ncould drink an entire fifth of Jim Beam and misspell \r\ncondescending remarks about incitor without even picking \r\ngriece\\\'s teeth out of his knuckles.  \r\n\r\nhttp://www.blindwino.com/driver.html',3,0,0,0,'12.75.40.112','en'),(4723,1216,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','full circle on the wheel, indeed.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(4724,1218,'2001-06-28 02:07:12',0,'blurker','I know it\\\'s tacky to non-sequitir after such a provocative, \r\nwell-written piece, but I have ask... Where is the Richard \r\nHell cameo in Desperately Seeking Susan?  Ann Magnuson is \r\nthe cigarette girl, which raises a worse non-sequiter:  \r\nA.M. will be doing a semi-finished Rave Mom in San \r\nFrancisco soon and you should go.  I saw two of them in NYC \r\nand really dug them.  Sorry.  I should add, egg, that I \r\nreally liked this post (for non-movie trivia reasons), but \r\nI don\\\'t suppose that would be adding much.',1,0,0,0,'12.75.40.112','en'),(4725,1218,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'eggcentric movie fanatic','to blurker: <p>there is a scene in \\\"DSS\\\" in which \r\nmadonna is slowly trying to leave a hotel room with a \r\nsleeping man in it. Richard Hell is that sleeping man. \r\nLater, he is the one who is murdered (although you \r\ndont see any of that). madonna had stolen the historical \r\nartifact earrings from him. that was the cause of all the \r\nwacky trouble, remember?</p>\r\n<p> John Turturro also appears in this fine film, as the \r\nMC at the Magic Club.</p>',0,0,0,0,'216.175.93.231','en'),(4726,1065,'2001-06-28 02:36:06',0,'finnegan','nice, not bad, is this natural or are you on acid?\r\n\r\nHave you re