\r\ndon\\\'t think they really started to worry until the day i \r\nforgot how to get home from high school.<br>\r\n\r\nit\\\'s been under control with medication for years, but i \r\nstill regularly forget directions, miss freeway exits, lose \r\ndetails of last night\\\'s conversations, etc. folks get tired \r\nof hearing the epilepsy excuse from me and i get tired of \r\nhearing the \\\"did you forget your pills?\\\" question. and for \r\nall i know, all the medication in the world wouldn\\\'t help \r\nme remember. it\\\'s really hard to tell where the epilepsy \r\nends and pure simpleton idiocy begins. so i just say \\\"i \r\nforgot\\\" and take my lumps. over and over and over again. \r\nsigh.<br>\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.38.73.109','en'),(5136,1279,'2001-07-07 19:15:32',0,'jo','i\\\'m all with olivia on this one. if all the friends i\\\'d had \r\ncrushes on had stopped talking to me, i\\\'d have no friends \r\nleft. including elly and olivia.',1,0,0,0,'172.158.194.97','en'),(5137,1287,'2001-07-07 19:18:35',0,'jo','dude, this makes me think of zen and the art of motorcycle \r\nmaintenance. there\\\'s lots of talk in that about time gaps. \r\nabout losing whole days.',1,0,0,0,'172.158.194.97','en'),(5138,1288,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>this morning I put a \\\"krispy kreme donut\\\" paper hat \r\non sweepy and he commented that the same hat on \r\nyeti would transport us back to the good ole 1950s \r\nimmediately. we agreed that even without the hat, yeti \r\nhas the aura of a sweet \\\'50s good ole boy welcoming \r\nyou with sugar and a smile.</p>',0,0,0,0,'216.175.91.69','en'),(5139,1288,'2001-07-07 22:47:58',0,'auntie','me and mark and mandy have adopted yeti as one of ours. he \r\nwill always be our boy and a member of the family.  we love \r\nhim very much and when we talk about family stuff we always \r\nhope that he will come, too.\r\n\r\nyeti is the best thing elly ever brought home to us.',1,0,0,0,'24.162.119.106','en'),(5140,1279,'2001-07-07 23:53:15',0,'green','Im talking about when you abuse the fact < note abuse> that \r\nthese people are around and take them for granted...that is \r\npretty much what I was referring to. There will always be a \r\nbase attraction between all people, whether they be \r\ninvolved or not, it simply is a natural thing to wish to \r\nsurround yourself with persons whom you find attractive.\r\n\r\nWhen you abuse it though, that\\\'s a different story.',6,0,0,0,'64.20.45.214','en'),(5141,1293,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','I have two-toned aquafresh toothpaste. It has four nozzles \r\nat the tip. Two for white, two for blue. If you squeeze it \r\nfrom the end, only white comes out. To get this high-tech \r\ntoothpaste tube to function correctly, you are forced to \r\nsqueeze from the middle. I\\\'m convinced that this is a ploy \r\nto make you waste toothpaste and have to buy more sooner.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.146','en'),(5142,1293,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i do all of these things as well, except the \r\nobsession-with-scarcity-borscht toilet paper hoarding. ',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5143,1293,'2001-07-08 03:00:35',0,'dahlia','northern? oh man. remind me to go to the bathroom \r\nbefore i go to 5\\\'s! charmin! charmin ultra, unscented, is \r\nthe only way to go.',1,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(5144,1293,'2001-07-08 04:33:51',0,'kat','for the last three months i had no bathroom to call my own. \r\nwhat is the etiquette on toilet paper use when in another\\\'s \r\ndomain? i like to use lots of paper, but if it belongs to \r\nsomeone else that worries me. will they notice that half \r\nthe roll is gone? and even worse can their toilet handle \r\nit? do not ask me why i have this obsession. i often wonder \r\nif it is because during my formative adolescent years i \r\nlived in a rv. this meant using almost no paper at all [due \r\nto plumbing issues]. and now i waste. i waste. i waste. how \r\nhorrible of me. but i am very clean afterwards. as fresh as \r\na newly plucked peach.',1,0,0,0,'32.100.70.174','en'),(5145,1279,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','if your friends, fine. that\\\'s one thing. but if you\\\'re \r\nfriends with someone who you\\\'re secretly in love with, and \r\nyou don\\\'t do anything about it due to your low self-esteem, \r\nthen that isn\\\'t healthy. shit or get off the pot, i say.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.5.151','en'),(5146,1289,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','<BR><BR>i think it\\\'s almost impossible to create good \r\nart when you\\\'re unstable; but i also think the daily \r\ndoses of opiates or alcohol taken by the artists you \r\nmention may have created a baseline of stability in \r\ntheir day-to-day lives which enabled them to have \r\ncareers (albeit, in some cases, short ones).<BR><BR>a \r\ngood question people ask me these days is: why do you \r\nmake these little films of yours? and i\\\'ve come to the \r\nconclusion that it isn\\\'t about expression or fulfillment \r\nor need but because i don\\\'t want to work. ever again. no \r\nmore shit jobs. no more bosses. no more worrying that if \r\ni don\\\'t kiss ass i\\\'ll end up on the street. and that\\\'s \r\nvalid. and then i\\\'ll be free from work, and i can play, \r\nwhich is what art really is.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.5.151','en'),(5147,1293,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','all RVs should come equipped with a bidet, pumped by \r\na plastic foot pedal, sprayed clean with a little sprayer \r\nhose.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5148,1288,'2001-07-08 08:20:50',0,'liver','yeah, so yeti\\\'s hot.  what exactly is your POINT!?\r\nhot?  yes.  got it.',1,0,0,0,'64.81.72.119','en'),(5149,1293,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','<p>i squeeze from the middle but ALWAYS replace the cap.  I \r\nbuy unscented hypo-allergenic paper.  This upsets Kyla \r\ngreatly:  \\\"Why do you always get the BORING kind!?\\\" -\r\n \\\"Because it\\\'s good for your arse and it doesn\\\'t \r\nstink!\\\".</p>\r\n<p>when i get in the shower, i first wash my face with \r\nBlackmore\\\'s tea tree oil facewash.  Then i wash my upper \r\nbody with Dr Bronners Eucalyptis soap.  Then i wash my \r\npusseh with the same stuff.  Then i wash my back.  Then my \r\nlegs.</p>\r\n<p>Then i stand under really really hot water untill \r\ncondensation drips off the ceiling.  That grosses me out, \r\nso i hop out of the shower.</p>\r\n<p>on getting out, i dry off (face, chest, arms, back, \r\nlegs) then apply eye moisturizer, then face moisturizer, \r\nthen body moisturizer.  Then i apply tea tree deoderant, \r\nand brush my teeth with Tom\\\'s of maine, fennel.  Then i \r\nleave the bathroom.</p>\r\n<p>It always happens in this exact order.</p>',5,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(5150,1288,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','oh i think that was my point.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5151,1293,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>Fascinating.</p>\r\n<p>*cough*</p>\r\n',6,0,0,0,'64.172.164.74','en'),(5152,1279,'2001-07-08 10:39:33',0,'green','to matt: you hit it with two hammers\r\n',1,0,0,0,'64.20.45.31','en'),(5153,1293,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','how could you not enjoy my writing! it is powerful and \r\nexpressive. don\\\'t you understand that the toothpaste is \r\na metaphor???',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5154,1293,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p align=\"justify\"><font size=\"48\" color=\"red\" face=\"arial,  helvetica\"><b>\r\nIBUY</font></p><p align=\"justify\"> <font size=\"48\" color=\"black\" face=\"arial, \r\nhelvetica\">toiletpaper<br></font></p><p align=\"justify\"><font size=\"48\" color=\"red\" face=\"arial, helvetica\">INLOTS OF48.\r\n</b></font>\r\n</p>',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5155,1292,'2001-07-08 10:58:13',0,'green','i was drunk whilst writing this...\r\nI have to go pee now.\r\noh yeah......CREMATE!!!!\r\nin other words burn...burn...yeah-burn!',6,0,0,0,'64.20.45.31','en'),(5156,1293,'2001-07-08 11:01:49',0,'jim','<p align=\\\"justify\\\">\r\n<font size=\\\"48\\\" color=\\\"black\\\" face=\\\"arial,  \r\nhelvetica\\\"><b>I</b></font><font size=\\\"48\\\" color=\\\"blue\\\" \r\nface=\\\"arial,  helvetica\\\"><b>TWEEZE</b></font>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n',6,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(5157,1293,'2001-07-08 11:03:11',0,'jim','*hums Steve Reich*',6,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(5158,1293,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','it\\\'s all about saying stuff no one cares about',0,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(5159,1293,'2001-07-08 11:25:32',0,'jim','I care.',6,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(5160,1293,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','it\\\'s all about the bathroom. gimme the grafitti.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5161,1297,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','i think i drunk dialed \\\'the bend\\\' on friday night.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(5162,1297,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','are you drunk right now?',0,0,0,0,'216.175.93.225','en'),(5163,1297,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','drunk on L.U.V.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(5164,1293,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','always shampoo before soap, never after.',3,0,0,0,'216.175.104.235','en'),(5165,1298,'2003-05-10 16:09:14',79,'yeti','mr penis baby seal blood.',1,0,0,0,'64.51.232.102','en'),(5166,1299,'2001-07-08 19:57:36',0,'hh','i like gorge michael. \\\"Listen without prejudice vol 1\\\" is \r\nfine with me.',1,0,0,0,'24.93.61.58','en'),(5167,1293,'2001-07-08 20:03:05',0,'kat','wet hair n bod. brush teeth [squeezed from middle or bottom \r\ndon\\\'t matter]. wash face. shampoo. soap. this process \r\nbecomes disorganized a bit on those occasions when i decide \r\nto go skin free [ie. removal of body hair]. it is worth the \r\ndiscomfort of changing my habits one in awhile for the \r\nbenefit of feeling skin on skin. ...hairlessness everywhere \r\nis such a rush.',1,0,0,0,'32.102.91.254','en'),(5168,1299,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i think the difference is, bands such as phish or the \r\ndead inspire a brief pause of marked reverence by the \r\nperson identifying their music tastes. you didn\\\'t say, \\\"i \r\nlike classic and jazz and rock\\\", you said \\\"classical and \r\njazz and phish.\\\" a favorite band can often feel like its \r\nown genre, especially if there\\\'s a culture following it \r\naround. and people identify strongly with culture. (self \r\ndisclosure: not a phish fan.)',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5169,1293,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i like bodies.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5170,1299,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','s5: That\\\'s a good point. In my case, the culture doesn\\\'t \r\nplay such a big part in my liking them; I am mostly drawn \r\nto Phish because of their aesthetic sense. In fact, one of \r\nthe things that bothers me specifically is the way people \r\nidentify me with the culture (i.e. \\\"you must be a \r\nphishhead\\\") when I have given them no reason to do so. Fact \r\nis, I don\\\'t like most of the people who strongly identify \r\nthemselves as phishheads because they usually are pretty \r\none-sided. \r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.99','en'),(5171,1298,'2001-07-08 21:46:25',0,'baby animal','I won\\\'t get caught in your web, woman! I ain\\\'t here just \r\nto be some bitch\\\'s dinner!',5,0,0,0,'216.175.104.235','en'),(5172,1293,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','always poo before the shower, never after. i like using the \r\nbaking soda for rubbing into my skin, my legs. grab and \r\nshake, rub and rinse. hello leg! you are still there. i \r\nsometimes look down and am amazed at the muscle and flab \r\ncake that is my leg. hello there.',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(5173,1279,'2001-07-08 22:03:10',0,'bitchy chick2','ample parts = (*)(*)\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(5174,1299,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i get it. but i know someone who is also from south carolina who \r\nwould get it better. ',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5175,1299,'2001-07-08 22:26:15',0,'ty','what? who?',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.161','en'),(5176,1299,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','ix is horrified that i don\\\'t like phish.',3,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(5177,1299,'2001-07-08 22:36:53',0,'also','pink floyd<br>\r\n<br>\r\nand, is it just me, or does Primus have their own ID3 \r\ncategory?  Or is \\\"Primus\\\" a style of music as well as a \r\nband as well as a gas burner?',4,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(5178,1279,'2001-07-08 22:38:14',0,'o to jo','*bats eyelashes*<br>\r\n<Br>\r\n*giggles furiously*',1,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(5179,1293,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','not having to wash my hair is the best ever.  especially in \r\nwinter:  there\\\'s no period of freezing until your hair is \r\ndry.  that always used to get me, riding on the bus to \r\nwork, wet hair making me shiver, taking hours to dry.',3,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(5180,1300,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','when i\\\'m stuck on the bay bridge, waiting for 25 lanes \r\nof traffic to scoop out the two dollar toll, i roll down the \r\nwindows and listen to everyone else\\\'s stereos. there is \r\nno better collage of sound.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5181,1299,'2001-07-09 00:13:58',0,'jo','i don\\\'t have many rules about who i will and won\\\'t date, \r\nbut i will not, under any circumstances, date a phish fan.',1,0,0,0,'172.167.226.29','en'),(5182,1279,'2001-07-09 00:15:25',0,'jo to liv','oh, sure. play on my weaknesses. for shame.',1,0,0,0,'172.167.226.29','en'),(5183,1299,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i dated a phish fan and lived to tell the tale! we tripped \r\non acid to phish and he sang <i>come waste your time \r\nwith me</i> and i had a lot of glorious moments of \r\nhappiness laying in his bed listening to the words \r\n<i>oh to be prince caspian, afloat upon the waves</i>. \r\nhe would sit in his beanbag, in the dark, smoking and \r\nlistening to junta, which turned into my favorite album. \r\nbut i haven\'t bought any of the phish albums, even \r\nthough i like them. i just want to listen to phish when \r\nhe\'s around.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5184,1299,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','well, jo\\\'s comment kind of brings it all together at the \r\nend, doesn\\\'t it? that\\\'s exactly what I was talking about.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.178','en'),(5185,1279,'2001-07-09 01:43:50',0,'green','gimme sum of them ample parts ',6,0,0,0,'64.20.45.53','en'),(5186,1299,'2001-07-09 02:25:00',0,'jo','tyler, i don\\\'t think there\\\'s anything wrong with you at \r\nall, you seem perfectly nice and charming. i even know how \r\nyou feel! my favorite musician for a really long time was \r\nani difranco and i had the same sort of transcendent \r\nexperiences you described listening to her music and \r\nsharing it with fellow fans and i endured years of snarky \r\ncomments from people about it.<BR>\r\nbut i had to come to terms with the fact that that the \r\naverage ani difranco fan takes her music <b>way</b> too \r\nseriously, identifies themselves too strongly with her, and \r\nthus annoys their friends and aquaintances by talking about \r\nher a lot, quoting her, etc.<BR>\r\n(see also: tori amos, smashing pumpkins, nine inch nails, \r\nkiss, weezer. lots of musicians have similar cult-like \r\nfollowings that tend to isolate them from non-fans.)\r\n',1,0,0,0,'172.154.84.195','en'),(5187,1299,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<br><br><img \r\nsrc=\"http://www.progreviews.com/reviews/Rush-2112.j\r\npg\">',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5188,1299,'2003-07-24 15:44:23',165,'joker','hurrah for junta...<br>\r\nICULUS!!!!<br>\r\nFEE<br>\r\nFLUFFHEAD!!!!',1,0,0,0,'66.68.48.125','en'),(5189,1298,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','egg do you play the bass guitar?',3,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(5190,1300,'2001-07-09 03:08:55',0,'Friend','<br>\r\nI like to drive sometimes without having any place to go. I \r\nlike to turn the radio on loud and look at the world around \r\nme, sometimes I like to feel the air conditioner on my \r\narms.<br><br>\r\nAlso see:<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://members.aol.com/imreversible/private/julyeight1\r\n.jpg\\\">This</a> and <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://members.aol.com/imreversible/private/julyeight2\r\n.jpg\\\">this.</a><br><br>\r\nSometimes, it\\\'s okay to like consumerism.',1,0,0,0,'24.4.255.169','en'),(5191,1299,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','the bottom line is, if you like something that\\\'s a known \r\ntaboo, you should avoid coming out with it until you \r\nknow the coast is clear. i don\\\'t go around telling people \r\ni meet that i\\\'m an astrologer, for example, because i \r\nknow there\\\'s a taboo about it (\\\"oh, fucking new age \r\ncalifornia flake\\\"). on the flip side, by holding back \r\nthings, we risk shutting out possiblity. so, you know \r\nhow it goes. it\\\'s a constant game of reshuffling and \r\nplaying getting-to-know-you chicken. honestly i just \r\nwish that everyone would be more accepting.',2,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5192,1299,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','i like music. music, music, music. any kind. it makes me \r\njump up and down. with pure animal joy.<BR><BR>imagine if \r\none day they came and took away all your music. anything \r\nwould sound good after that. you\\\'d be like, \\\"goddamn, i wish \r\ni had some barry manilow or something.\\\" you can get into \r\nanything on some level at least.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.79.21','en'),(5193,86,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','what\\\'s a \\\"perisher?\\\"\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.79.21','en'),(5194,500,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','matt, just who the hell do you think you are, son? and do \r\nyou want to be called \\\"matt\\\" or \\\"matthew\\\"? please let us \r\nknow. we have to put down SOMETHING on the form here.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.79.21','en'),(5195,1300,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','Nothing wrong with liking consumerism. It\\\'s what we\\\'ve got. \r\nMight as well enjoy it. I mean otherwise what would we all \r\nbe doing? Look at the life of the average peasant in 1500; \r\nI can handle a couple Pier One\\\'s and Blockbuster Video\\\'s \r\nand Bed, Bath and Beyond\\\'s, long as I ain\\\'t gotta dig \r\ntrenches and pick turinps all day.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.147','en'),(5196,1299,'2001-07-09 04:06:47',0,'starlajo to jo','<BR>\r\n<BR>\r\noh jo! i used to be one of those scary smashing pumpkins \r\nobsessed people from the age of 13-16/17ish... i was always \r\ndiscussing b-sides or websites or whatever with the couple \r\nof other girls at my school who came up to me when i was 15 \r\nand said \\\"i heard you\\\'re a big sp fan.\\\"',0,0,0,0,'203.96.111.200','en'),(5197,517,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','<BR>1. going to the greek restaurant, picking fights with \r\nthe waitress, and drinking too much retsina<BR>2. pretending \r\nto be sober around parents<BR>3. smoking hash up in the \r\nattic with roger and eddie, thinking it would cure my \r\nincipient hangover<BR>4. staying up all night with a \r\nheadachey, spanikopita-flavored buzz<BR>5. getting into a \r\nthree-way with roger and eddie when it should have only been \r\na two-way at most. maybe even a one-way. or a no-way. \r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.79.21','en'),(5198,1300,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<pre><tt>\r\nBEGIN ARGUMENT\r\n\r\n    TOPIC = \\\"anti-globalization\\\"\r\n    ID = 4723\r\n\r\nEND ARGUMENT\r\n</tt></pre>',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5199,1300,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','the really beat thing to comtemplate is the next phase after \r\nthis, coming around the bend shortly, when things will be \r\nbuilt to last, scarcity will be nonexistent, machines will \r\ndo all undesirable labor, and we will live in harmony and \r\njoy forever. it\\\'s coming. you can smell it in the air. all \r\nchoices will be available to all people. you don\\\'t want to \r\ndeal with money? fine. there will be stores with free things \r\nin them. need some food? go into the store and walk out with \r\nsome. energy will be free, as well as education. it won\\\'t be \r\nnecessary to own a car if you don\\\'t want one. america is the \r\nonly place where everybody thinks they have to have a car. \r\namerica is full of shit sometimes, i think. things are going \r\nto choice around here, boyo. or not.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.79.21','en'),(5200,1299,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','It\\\'s like that line in \\\"Being John Malkovich\\\" where John \r\nCusack is on a date with the hot girl from the office and \r\nshe asks him to tell her about himself. The first thing he \r\nsays is \\\"Well, I\\\'m a puppeteer...\\\" and she says, \\\"Check!\\\" \r\nand runs out.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.147','en'),(5201,406,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','panda bear, panda bear, i am with you always, even unto the \r\nend of you.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.79.62','en'),(5202,541,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','if not for my mommy and daddy, i would be dead by now, \r\nsurely. or in prison. i am very thankful for them.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.79.62','en'),(5203,1303,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','damn, this makes me miss my sweetie. all i\\\'ve got here \r\ntonight are ravens. and they will NOT shut up.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.79.62','en'),(5204,1300,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','coming around the bend.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.102.50','en'),(5205,1298,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to o','no. i can play three chords sub-competently on the \r\nregular guitar. I have in the past played \\\"gigantic\\\" and \r\n\\\"about a girl\\\" really slow on the bass. i can sing in a \r\nsophisticated avant garde falsetto, and have a high \r\nrange of volume.  i can play keys. wanna start a band?',0,0,0,0,'216.175.102.50','en'),(5206,1304,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','often... when on the highway... the only feeling i can\r\nfeel is that i\\\'m careening out of control.  free fall \r\nfree fall free fall.  like that feeling when you lean back\r\nin a chair and starts to lean too far and then you catch\r\nyourself.<br><br>this sensation happens most often on 580.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(5207,1300,'2001-07-09 08:59:43',0,'moebius, at home, finally','<br>there came a point, oh, perhaps a year ago, when the \r\ncommute seemed to rule my life.</br>\r\n\r\n<br>at one point during this time, i was asked by a friend \r\nto contribute something funny to his famous humor-oriented \r\nweb magazine. but all my first ideas involved writing what \r\ni guess i knew about best back then: what i had come to \r\nthink of as \\\"The Long Drive.\\\" most of them were funny-\r\nstrange, not funny-haha, so i gave up.</br>\r\n\r\n<br>my favorite piece was an early-David-Byrne-type ditty \r\nabout a man who drove the same route each day, usually over \r\nan hour each way. he would fall into a trance of sorts \r\nduring the drive, only waking up as he parked. each day the \r\nlandscape changed slightly--so slightly he doesn\\\'t notice. \r\nand over the course of a few years buildings disappear, \r\ntrees replace other trees, hills and valleys trade places. \r\nand one day he realizes he\\\'s driving to a different \r\nworkplace, returning to a different home, and essentially \r\nliving someone else\\\'s life. </br>\r\n\r\n<br>i\\\'m not commuting anywhere at the moment. and it feels \r\nso good.</br>',2,0,0,0,'205.184.149.162','en'),(5208,1299,'2002-03-15 00:17:55',129,'moebius','<br>there was a time when i was oh so judgemental about \r\npeople\\\'s music tastes. but then i realized it was patently \r\nridiculous to cut perfectly fine people out of my life just \r\nbecause they thought Hootie and the Blowfish (for example) \r\nwere the last word in musical achievement.</br>\r\n\r\n<br>now i have grown and evolved or whatever and live with \r\nsomeone who listens to three things: musicals, cabaret \r\nsingers, and the Cowboy Junkies. she can\\\'t fathom most of \r\nmy music. and and this is okay: I like the Cowboy Junkies \r\ntoo.</br> ',2,0,0,0,'205.184.149.162','en'),(5209,1298,'2001-07-09 09:56:08',0,'o to egg','well, i have a band with the lovely kyla.  but i\\\'ll do a \r\nside project!  i can do:  nothing.  maybe tambourine?  i \r\ncan stand and admire you while you do melodical things.  \r\ni\\\'ll be a groupie!  as long as i get to give you head after \r\nthe shows.  or during.  you know, whatever.',1,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(5210,1305,'2001-07-09 10:26:01',0,'tomato','dude, please consider the co-op thing or at least make \r\nsure you have your own locked door.  i dated this girl in \r\nbiology when i was attending the university of oregon \r\nand she lived in a co-op (which i figure is the same as \r\nsant cruz -- eugen that is) and basically the only way i \r\ncan explain the uncleanliness is:  PUBLIC HAIR AND \r\nPISS.<p>\r\n\r\nmake sure you have your own room, piss at the corner \r\nstore.\r\n<p>\r\n\r\n(disclaimer:  i am eating marmite on toast in san \r\nfrancisco)',1,0,0,0,'165.247.213.2','en'),(5211,1304,'2001-07-09 10:28:48',0,'tomato','freeways make me feel uneasy, but only in big city \r\ninterchanges -- even sober.<p> \r\n\r\ngive me two lane oregon highways anyday.  watch out \r\nfor the trees!',0,0,0,0,'165.247.213.2','en'),(5212,1298,'2001-07-09 10:32:42',0,'tomato','non squitor to o:  i made a poster today that is gonig to \r\nbe printed out cmyk (ooo boy) based on something i \r\nmade on the guitar.  basically, i played a song straight \r\ninto the computer, a illus program that i made made \r\n(two made\\\'s?) a poster out of it. <p>\r\ngoogle=max/msp=nato++ (graphical video/audio \r\nprogramming environ.)',0,0,0,0,'165.247.213.2','en'),(5213,1266,'2001-07-09 12:05:27',0,'shane','chia... you should steal that old page thing!\r\n\r\nPS come visit me at the end of September........\r\n\r\nCome on, why not?!\r\n',2,0,0,0,'211.47.0.121','en'),(5214,1305,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','MARMITE IS SO WRONG!  Get some vegemite down ya.',3,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(5215,428,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','can peter play the banjo yet?',4,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(5216,1293,'2001-07-09 13:28:01',0,'puppy','i use conditioner instead of shaving cream... someone \r\nrecently told me that flossing everyday will add about 6 \r\nyears to your life; most heart disease originates as \r\nbacteria in the mouth (don\\\'t know if it\\\'s true). I don\\\'t \r\nreally floss too often. But I don\\\'t smoke. So I should die \r\nwhen I am expected to.',0,0,0,0,'192.35.232.99','en'),(5217,1289,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','  I think I\\\'m in love with Jade.  The people I hang out \r\nwith are so boring.  That\\\'s it.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5218,1305,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>that is a good description, tomato.  PUBLIC HAIR AND\r\nPISS.  it is really all about the filth.  i love filth.  why\r\ntry to fight it. there is nothing better than hillbillying\r\naround barefoot covered in grime.  i love it.  they are all\r\na bunch of filthy people you know.  disgusting.</P>',3,0,0,0,'205.179.19.62','en'),(5219,1303,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>\\\"bobby bobby digi<BR>\r\nstuck to your ass like a victory secret wedgie</P>\r\n',3,0,0,0,'205.179.19.62','en'),(5220,1305,'2001-07-09 14:45:21',0,'kat','you should have moved in with me. i use half a toilet paper \r\nroll in one sitting. even my dog wipes her ass. [on the \r\nlawn]',1,0,0,0,'32.100.70.159','en'),(5221,1300,'2001-07-09 15:47:27',0,'bmg','<p>hmmm, seeing <a \r\nhref=\'http://members.aol.com/imreversible/private/julyei\r\nght1.jpg\' target=new>this</a> and <a \r\nhref=\'http://members.aol.com/imreversible/private/julyei\r\nght2.jpg\' target=new>this</a>, I remember driving \r\naround Albuquerque right before the sun goes down \r\nwith my friends jeff and kim. Central and San Pedro? I \r\nthink back to my best driving stories, and the first one \r\nthat comes to mind is the mindless journey austin and i \r\ntook to wyoming... a long but dry story. Another drive I \r\nremember is the drive from palm springs to phoenix, \r\nwhich i did every weekend for a year or so. I remember \r\nburrying the needle some where deep in the mahove desert \r\n      scared to death that the boogy man was out there \r\nwaiting for me to stop and pee... seeing meth labs \r\nburning in the distance, and seeing not a single \r\nbillboard for nearly two hours.  A friend from cali is \r\nstaying with us this week, he left L.A. at 1:00pm on \r\nmonday, and arrived tuesday at 1:00pm... he is a \r\nbadass. Driving is fun, when your destination has \r\nnothing to do with work. I can\'t stand the billboards in \r\ncalifornia, they consume the sky and block the great \r\nview... decadence is driving with the windows down and \r\nthe a/c on full / turn the vent on and turn off the radio \r\nlisten to the ambient music that the we humans make... \r\nsometimes the sound frightens me, sometimes it \r\nexcites me. i am blown away by the sounds of us \r\nhumans, i like watching people pretend not to see me \r\nsinging to myself... i just blew a snot on my keyboard.',1,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(5222,1305,'2001-07-09 16:03:40',0,'bmg','<p>you used to collect beer bottles of your own tabaco \r\nspit when you lived in the co-op... now that is sick. you \r\nburped more, and you constantly stank like pachouli, \r\nsometimes cigars.there were naked girls on the porch, \r\nand i wasn\'t sposed to notice that... one girl started up a \r\nconversation with me once, while naked on the porch, \r\nasked me why i couldn\'t get past without looking at her \r\ntits, i was looking at her bright orange pubic hair... a \r\nstrawberry patch, and i tried not to look at her... \r\nsometimes i would eat dinner there, and get strange \r\nlooks, and i thought i should live there too. never \r\nhappened, still might one day. i like roommates, the \r\nmore the better the fun.</p>',1,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(5223,1293,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Pong Moll','<p>Hm. What\\\'s a bathroom?</p>',1,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(5224,1304,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','<p>Driving in jersey blows. It\\\'s anarchy.</p>\r\n',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(5225,1305,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','co-ops!  WOO!  how fun it would be to move into a co-op 5 \r\nyears after doing that whole thing.  all the meetings, the \r\nfilth, the bananas, the \\\'bible\\\', the <i>issues</i>.  \r\nspontaneous tribal drum jams with the crockery, and \r\nconfused, naked hippies sitting on the porch trying to \r\nconvince you that <i>you\\\'re</i> the one with the issues.  \r\ngood luck on getting voted in, aus.  ',2,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(5226,1303,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','  Before I ever had a girlfriend, I didn\\\'t need it so bad.  \r\nNow, I sometimes crave it to the exclusion of all else, but \r\nwhen offered up to me, I realize it\\\'s not what I really \r\nwant.  So, I find comfort in the glances of beautiful women \r\nor a warm embrace, but it\\\'s the ravens I\\\'m actually in love \r\nwith, and they\\\'re the only ones who ever loved me in return.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5227,1300,'2001-07-09 17:54:30',0,'qq','when i\\\'m in miles of backed up traffic on the freeway i go\r\nin between the lanes and it puts me into a state of\r\nhyper-concentration that\\\'s almost like meditation. it\r\neliminates everything from my consciousness except what i\\\'m\r\ndoing: putting the bike into the little pockets of space\r\nbetween cars, watching everything, reading other drivers to\r\nsee who\\\'s going to dart from one lane to another, who is\r\noblivious and staring straight ahead with a blank stare.\r\nwatching their little glances over their shoulders or the\r\nrepositioning of their hands on the wheel that\r\ntelepathically announces their intentions. it clears your\r\nmind, because there\\\'s no room to think about anything right\r\nthen. \r\n\r\n ',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.10','en'),(5228,1308,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','Buck up, son. Do good work, take your time, go the extra \r\nmile. Your ego tends to be less fragile when you really, \r\nreally bust your ass for something. Then, you can gaze down \r\ncondescendingly at those who fail to grasp your genius.\r\n<p>\r\nRewrite everything. Believe it or not, I changed three \r\nsentances just composing this little comment. It\\\'s a way of \r\nlife.\r\n<p>\r\nex. \\\"...tends to be...\\\" started as \\\"is\\\". \r\n<p>\r\n\\\"...composing...\\\" was \\\"writing\\\"\r\n<p> \r\n\\\"...fail to grasp...\\\" was \\\"don\\\'t understand\\\" and before \r\nthat \\\"don\\\'t get\\\". have confidence in your good taste.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.244','en'),(5229,1305,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>im getting a fourth roommate. 4 is the number of \r\ndeath. last time i lived with 3 friends, people cried and \r\nthrew things. </p>\r\n<p> but I love the sound of people chattering while I fall \r\nasleep. I grew up in a house that always had people in \r\nit, refugees, extended family, neighbors, just lots of in \r\nand out, with the front door rarely locked and people \r\nyelling through the screen to announce themselves. in \r\nthailand people live super close together and it breaks \r\ndown your sense of individuality --an American myth \r\ncherished by people who quote the same commercials \r\nand read the same celebrity magazines in line at the \r\ngrocery store and buy the same new technology to keep \r\nup with the Joneses. </p>\r\n<p> I love coming home to people dancing in the \r\nkitchen. I love when jay calls at 6 and asks me whats \r\nfor dinner.  I like commun-er-ty.</p>\r\n<p>there is a lot of work in managing people\\\'s habits \r\nand needs, but it teaches you a lot and it makes you \r\ncloser.</p>',0,0,0,0,'216.175.102.3','en'),(5230,1300,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','letting the days go by, let the water hold me down/letting \r\nthe days go by, water flowing underground/into the blue \r\nagain/after the money\\\'s gone/once in a lifetime, water \r\nflowing underground',1,0,0,0,'64.132.148.219','en'),(5231,1305,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','yes. you are really related to all the people on earth, and \r\nall living things, when it comes down to it. they are all \r\nyour family. we will be rediscovering this shortly. trust \r\nwill be very important. and love will continue to hold \r\neverything together.',1,0,0,0,'64.132.148.219','en'),(5232,1308,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','aren\\\'t you the one who wrote \\\"the day my life changed?\\\" \r\nthat was one of the most moving things i\\\'ve ever read. \r\nyou\\\'re already a great writer. everybody on here is a great \r\nwriter. so witty and concise and expressive. just keep at \r\nit and don\\\'t doubt yourself.',1,0,0,0,'64.132.148.219','en'),(5233,1300,'2001-07-09 19:30:28',0,'puppy','same as it ever was.<br>\r\nsame as it ever was....',1,0,0,0,'192.35.232.99','en'),(5234,1308,'2001-07-09 19:49:27',0,'puppy','to matt: thanks. that is very flattering to hear (read). \r\nLife is weird that way though. You know me as the author of \r\nthat particular piece and that was a particularly moving \r\npiece for you... which is a good thing and I definetly \r\nenjoy the fact that you enjoyed it.\r\n\r\n<p>But I also know myself for all the crap and drivel I\\\'ve \r\ncreated and sometimes I get mired down in that... Take, for \r\ninstance, David Shickler. He wrote a beautiful and funny \r\nshort story called \\\"The Smoker.\\\" One of the best bits of \r\nwritting I have seen in a long time. It was released in the \r\nNew Yorker as an excerpt of his novel, \\\"Kissing in \r\nManhattan.\\\" I haven\\\'t read the novel yet (it just came \r\nout), but the reviews I have heard about it aren\\\'t that \r\ngood, with the exception of that one chapter...\r\n\r\n<p>I think I have a fear of succeeding? or following \r\n(sustaining) success? I\\\'m not sure what my issue is, but I \r\ndo know that I have one....',1,0,0,0,'192.35.232.99','en'),(5235,1310,'2001-07-09 20:00:18',0,'jay','o, to be jobless<br>\r\nthe zen of the mop can teach<br>\r\ndirty gals the way.',1,0,0,0,'63.203.225.62','en'),(5236,1310,'2001-07-09 20:04:46',0,'fernando','<br>\r\nI saunter back there<br>\r\ndish still empty. Floors are mopped.<br>\r\nLess dust. I\\\'m hungry.',1,0,0,0,'63.203.225.62','en'),(5237,1300,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>\r\n<a \r