 dont think we have ever cleaned the \r\ninside of the toilet, and its freaking me out. ',0,0,0,0,'216.175.101.202','en'),(5256,1298,'2001-07-10 01:20:21',0,'kat','suckling baby seal blood is fine, but i have issues with \r\nthe groupie head thingy.',4,0,0,0,'32.100.71.70','en'),(5257,1298,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','i don\\\'t really have a problem with groupies giving head. and \r\nbtw, my band is playing on july 25th. heh.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(5258,1300,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon to austin','so you are saying big bay bridge blowjobs aren\\\'t out of the \r\nquestion?\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(5259,1308,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','you should read \\\"the tao of pooh\\\" and \\\"the te of piglet.\\\" \r\nthe second one especially deals with the fear of success, \r\nthe nagging little thoughts of, \\\"how will i, a tiny little \r\ncreature ever get to be something great, something grown up \r\nand good and right and at peace with myself?\\\"<BR>you aren\\\'t \r\ngoing to wake up in the middle of the night one of these \r\nnights with the blue fairy at your bedside, and all of a \r\nsudden, -poof- you\\\'re a real boy. you have to grow up on \r\nyour own. the buddha man said, \\\"you are the light; you are \r\nthe refuge; there is no place to take shelter but yourself.\\\"\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.9.225','en'),(5260,1309,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','if chevy can\\\'t make it, see if you can get paula poundstone. \r\ni bet she\\\'s getting some good material right about now.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.9.225','en'),(5261,1305,'2001-07-10 04:50:21',0,'maria','oh baby. that is SO my life back at school. and shush about \r\nthe filthiness and the hippies : it really depends on the \r\nco-op you join. my co-op last year wasn\\\'t like that *at \r\nall*. it really depends on the membership. i heart co-ops. \r\nconsensus is SO hard, and all we did last year was talk \r\nabout how much we hated it. but still. what else is there,  \r\nyou know? everything is a struggle, and i love being a part \r\nof it. sigh. this was a great post. i tried to e-mail you \r\nbut couldn\\\'t. sigh. i miss my lovely rural geek enclave and \r\nour wacky co-op system very much. thanks austin swinney. ',1,0,0,0,'172.129.231.186','en'),(5262,1298,'2001-07-10 04:57:13',0,'kat','okay. let\\\'s edit this....i have no problem with head. \r\ngetting or giving. it\\\'s the groupie thing. period. \r\n[wrangling the issue down to it\\\'s essence]',4,0,0,0,'32.100.70.93','en'),(5263,1300,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','but the question is, who blows who?',0,0,0,0,'216.175.101.202','en'),(5264,1310,'2001-07-10 07:38:25',0,'jim','<br>\r\nbold cheer, gain and tide;<br>\r\ncascade dawn, ivory joy.<br>\r\nProcter and Gamble.<br>\r\n',6,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(5265,1310,'2001-07-10 07:39:04',0,'jim','<br>\r\najax dynamo:<br>\r\nvel, crystal white octogon.<br>\r\nColgate Palmolive.<br>',6,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(5266,1310,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p>\r\nbunnies, kittens, tiles.<br>\r\nfrom our lab to your bathroom<br>\r\nprocter and gamble<br>\r\n</p>',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5267,1314,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','\\\"point of assness\\\"\r\n',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5268,1314,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=538.tx\r\nt\\\">monkeyass over donkey</a>',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5269,1316,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p>lulu, muffin. honey baby sweetie. i\\\'m sure delaware is darling, \r\nbut california is wicked, just wicked.\r\n</p><p>\r\nhang in there. i live to remove the proverbial oscar meyer weiner \r\nfrom your ass.\r\n</p>',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5270,1316,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','the ever present container of milk, lulu. just think about \r\nit. someday we will be driving at dawn together again, \r\nlistening to them announce the school lunch. we will \r\nfall in love all over again. I am counting white boys in my \r\nhead, lulu. they dance on my face like in a busby \r\nberkeley number. white boys dressed as robots. white \r\nboys in garbage can hats. we can fix it in post, lulu. we \r\ncan erase all the clown faces of the world and replace \r\nthem with cowboys. soylent white boys. eat me.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.101.202','en'),(5271,1310,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>I want normalcy<br>\r\nbathroom tile and lover-bots<br> \r\nhaunt me in my sleep</p>',1,0,0,0,'216.175.101.202','en'),(5272,1314,'2001-07-10 10:30:32',0,'oh','oh oh oh i so identify with this.  i have monkeyassed over \r\ndonkey with my friend who should be a good friend and i \r\nshouldn\\\'t have messed with things but i am all full steam \r\nahead all the time and fuck fuck fuck.<br>\r\n<br>\r\ni fucked up, or something.  i wanted the wrong thing.  i\\\'m \r\nsorry.<br>',3,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(5273,1313,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','how come noone ever comments on poetry?',0,0,0,0,'216.175.101.202','en'),(5274,1310,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p>\r\nbeing in transit<br>\r\nshe circles in the hallway<br>\r\nupstairs or downstairs<br>\r\n</p>',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5275,1314,'2001-07-10 11:35:58',0,'Zelig','some people are real freaks. and they are not ashamed.',5,0,0,0,'24.93.61.58','en'),(5276,1308,'2001-07-10 13:21:51',0,'puppy','i have read the tao of pooh, but it was long ago (maybe \r\neight years now). I also saw Benjamin Hoff speak at UT; \r\nthis was also about eight years ago.\r\n\r\n<p>The really interesting thing about Hoff\\\'s appearance was \r\nthat he was incredibly late; apparently his plane was \r\ndelayed or something. The crowd was a little peturbed and \r\nso was he... but his frustration was strange, kind of a \r\ncool smoldering frustration that soon withered....',0,0,0,0,'192.35.232.99','en'),(5277,1310,'2001-07-10 13:33:44',0,'LULU','<P>BLAH BLAH BLAH<BR>\r\nBLAH BLAH BLAH BLAH BLAH<BR>\r\nBLAH BLAH BLAH<BR></P>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(5278,1313,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i don\\\'t like poems about poo.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5279,1310,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','lulu, you got the syllables wrong.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5280,1312,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','ix is outside smoking right now. i want to be there. im \r\nstrung out. I need to suck on something. I am going to \r\nlook for sucky candy or bananas.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5281,1318,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','a security guard would be good for you.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5282,1318,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','yeah, i\\\'m running into a lot of that lately. people who know \r\na little bit are dangerous. \\\'cause they\\\'re \\\'fraid to admit \r\nthey don\\\'t know the rest. and very often they are jackasses.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.9.62','en'),(5283,1318,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<P>I find the best way to deal with people like that is to \r\njust be patient and not get pissed off.  He was prolly \r\npicked on a lot as a kid and expects that kind of \r\ninteraction with people he doesn\\\'t know, so he tries to cut \r\nit off at the pass by being the asshole first.  By taking \r\nthe bait, you just end up feeding his expectations and \r\nexacerbate the situation.</P><P>Now, I could very easily be \r\ntotally wrong, not knowing any of the people involved, but \r\nit kinda sounds like Philip is just an insecure, geeky kid \r\nwho is overcompensating because of all the mean words he \r\nheard from his peers as a kid.  I\\\'d venture a guess that if \r\nyou were nice to him, you might find a sweet, innocent, \r\nawkward boy hiding behind a shit-head facade.</P><P>Then \r\nagain, he could be fucking prig down to the core and \r\ndeserve to have his testicles used as the ball in a game of \r\nping pong.  Once you find out what he\\\'s really like, you \r\nshould act accordingly.</p>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5284,1316,'2002-03-05 20:17:36',17,'austin to le','<P>but le, i thought you put it there?</P>',3,0,0,0,'205.179.19.62','en'),(5285,1317,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Pee Moll','<p>It is interesting to see this message, and other recent \r\nones, and the idea of working at friendships. It\\\'s totally \r\nforeign to me. Maybe this is why I have no friends? Should \r\nit be any other way?</p>',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(5286,1314,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','<p>aww, poor joe. you know, it\'s okay. really. no one is \r\ngoing to die from a little social awkwardness. it happens. \r\nif you care, wait a few weeks and say hi again. chances \r\nare, no one would have remembered, and everything will be \r\nfine. i beat myself up over social things too... but it\'s not neccesary. something something about the test of time. the good ones will stick around.\r\n</p><p>\r\ni like you. you should come over and have cookies and tea!\r\n</p>',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(5287,1318,'2001-07-10 18:23:13',0,'bmg','<p>Bravo, a wonderful performance. I especially liked \r\nthe fight scenes.</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(5288,1318,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','can you fire philip and hire me? I can do avid (in 1999).',0,0,0,0,'216.175.101.202','en'),(5289,1317,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','i have a hard time believing in astrology. let\\\'s examine my \r\nforecast from cainer\\\'s website.\r\n<p> \r\n<font=\\\"8\\\">\r\n  \\\"It would seem that circumstances favour you now. You are \r\nambling, almost accidentally, into serendipitous \r\nsituations. Coincidences keep occurring. These are not, on \r\ntheir own, dramatic but they have the potential to bring \r\nbreathtakingly positive change. All you need is the ability \r\nto see that potential - and then to seize it. This requires \r\nnothing more, really, than a little faith and imagination. \r\nFirst you have to trust that there are good things to be \r\nseen if you look. Then, you just have to look cleverly - \r\nand inventively!\\\"\r\n<p>\r\nthe only  halfway predictive phrases are \\\"circumstances \r\nfavor you now\\\", and something about coincidences. The rest \r\nis advice that could apply to anyone.\r\n</font>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.213','en'),(5290,1320,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','Alas, the DMV is not the great equalizer we wish it could \r\nbe.  There exists people who, for a price, will whore \r\nthemselves out to those who do not wish to stand in line.  \r\nYep, power of attourny papers are signed and the wealthy \r\nnever have to go to the DMV, ever.  The rich will always \r\nenjoy privledge by trodding upon the backs of the poor.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5291,1320,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','Hmmmm.... thinking about going to the DMV.... I grew up in \r\nIdaho.  Every time I\\\'ve gone, I\\\'ve been greeted by an empty \r\nroom and a jovial, aged sherrif\\\'s deputy who would shuffle \r\naround and look the other way while I stole license \r\nlamination covers.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5292,1320,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','Being rich is ok. I\\\'d like to be rich, I think, so I could \r\nhave freedom. Yeah, yeah, mental freedom, freedom from \r\nprejudice...I have those anyway. Mostly. I want the freedom \r\nto not have to go wash dishes tonight for 8.50 an hour. The \r\nfreedom to sit on a porch on a high floor of a tall \r\nbuilding and drink vodkas-and-tonic while listening to \r\nMozart on my new Bose system. And, maybe, not having to go \r\nto the damn DMV. Is that so wrong?',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.13','en'),(5293,1319,'2001-07-10 20:14:40',0,'stella','I\\\'d have to agree with almost everything you\\\'ve said. I \r\nstarted flying when I was two. I\\\'ve flown MANY times. all \r\nover the world. Every time I am due to fly, I get anxious \r\nand my dreams are yucky for a week or two in advance. It \r\nseems to get worse the older I get. \r\nLast year, I was travelling a lot for work. I was flying all \r\nover the place, a few times a month. That\\\'s when it was the \r\nworst for me. Almost constant anxiety. And then one day I \r\nstruck up a conversation with my plumber. Seems he\\\'s a \r\nformer Air Force pilot. It was like hitting pay dirt! I \r\nsucked his brain dry of everything having to do with flying; \r\naccidents and the probability of occurance, how that shit \r\nstays up in the air, all of it. \r\nAfter that, I felt immensly better and now am not so bad \r\nabout the whole deal. My outlook these days is that if I die \r\nin an airplane crach, what a way to go!!',0,0,0,0,'168.100.203.247','en'),(5294,1319,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i am also afraid to fly. i dream endlessly of crashing \r\nairplanes. but this will change, it has to.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5295,1319,'2001-07-10 20:28:21',0,'puppy','I recently bought tickets to Florida on a web site that is \r\nscrewing me over; I am afraid that this is giving my plane \r\nbad ju-ju. I no like it :(',1,0,0,0,'192.35.232.99','en'),(5296,1317,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<P>Mollster: I agree.  I don\\\'t have the time or energy to \r\nwork on friendships.  They are either there, or they\\\'re \r\nnot.  That means I have a really small number of friends, \r\nbut the ones I\\\'ve got are there for good.</P><P>\r\nTyler: The crap you read in magazines and newspapers is \r\ntotal bullshit, naturally.  One twelfth of the population \r\ncan\\\'t all have the same day even though the con artists try \r\nto make us believe the contrary.  On the other hand, a \r\nfriend of mine had her complete chart done once, and the \r\nthings she was told were eerily accurate.  We used to argue \r\nabout the validity of astrology all night long, and I \r\neventually came to accept that there is something to it.  \r\nIt\\\'s all the con artists pawning themselves off as \r\nlegitimate pracitioners that give it such a bad rap.  I was \r\nand still am skeptical, but my friend found a convincing \r\nway to incorporate the reality of astrology into my own \r\nwarped belief system, so I have to give it some respect.</P>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5297,1320,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','Yeah... spending 8 hours a day in a skyscraper staring at a \r\ncomputer monitor under florescent lights is making my brain \r\nrot.  I want to spend my days doing yoga, taking dance \r\nclasses, and learning how to code, but the realities of \r\nfood and rent get in the way of that.  Let\\\'s go Lotto!!!',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5298,1318,'2001-07-10 20:56:18',0,'bmg','<p>did i tell you that I went to ACC? Also, I can develop \r\ndigital photo\\\'s?</p>',1,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(5299,1317,'2001-07-10 21:09:20',0,'bmg','<p>Funny thing jsut happened. I went to my favorite \r\nastrology site, astro.com, where you can enter all your \r\ninfo(chart stuff) and then when you go to the site it will \r\ngive you a fairly detailed projection... well, k-dogg at \r\ntimes has used my computer, therefore her horriscope \r\npops up firs. Occassionaly I check in on K-dogg, just to \r\nsee how she is doing. Well, i checked it out and it was \r\nexactly the same as mine. I was born on 10may75 she \r\nwas born 17june72 - both at different times... so does \r\nthis mean that she and i are in the same mood er \r\nwhat? it said:</p>\r\n</p><p><strong>\r\nEquilibrium\r\n</strong></p><p>\r\nThis is a time of psychological and emotional \r\nequilibrium, when the different aspects of your \r\npersonality are in tune with each other. You can face \r\nyour daily life with less effort than usual, which is bound \r\nto have some consequences\r\nin your material universe as well. Relations with friends \r\nand close neighbors will be very harmonious, and you \r\nmay make some new friends. People will be at ease \r\nwith you today because you are at ease with yourself. \r\nThe routine discussions, negotiations and transactions \r\nof everyday existence will offer no obstacles. This is an \r\nespecially good time to think about your personal and \r\nemotional life. Strains in that area can be corrected \r\nnow, because you are relatively at peace with yourself \r\nand with others, and communications about personal \r\nmatters should be easy. </p>',1,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(5300,919,'2001-07-10 21:22:11',0,'nice','cool',0,0,0,0,'134.117.83.123','en'),(5301,1320,'2001-07-10 21:27:55',0,'Mostly','I just like to look at the shoes of everybody in the DMV. \r\nYou can tell what type of a person is sitting across from \r\nyou just by looking at his shoes. <br><br>\r\nBut I haven\\\'t been to the DMV in awhile because we have \r\nthis express thing. For fifteen dollars extra, you get in \r\nout and on your way very quickly. This is where the people \r\nwith the nice shoes that have no wear on the soles go. \r\nMaybe it should be souls.',1,0,0,0,'24.4.255.168','en'),(5302,1317,'2001-07-10 21:32:37',0,'the unknown','\\\"To have a friend, be a friend.\\\"\r\n(unknown)\r\n\r\ni dont think that you realize what a friend is. There are no \r\nexpectations when there is friendship. You expect, you \r\nexpect way too much. So you left Ottawa, did you think that \r\neveryone was going to drop everything and agree with your \r\nselfish expectations of friendship. The people that drifted \r\naway from you while you lived there, why did they do that \r\nand now are so adiment about keeping the frienship glued \r\nwhile it was falling apart before . Why did your bestfriends \r\npull away from you when you left? Its your expectations and \r\nselfishness that lead to this. If only you could have \r\nrealized that you were slowly destroying your friendships \r\nwith those closet to you, then maybe, perhaps, you wouldnt \r\nbe writing about it today!',3,0,0,0,'134.117.83.123','en'),(5303,1319,'2001-07-10 21:32:50',0,'sometimes','I cry during takeoff and landing. But usually only when \r\nnobody is there to hold my hand.<br><br>\r\nI have been in eleven airports since May. I fly a lot. I \r\nusually never have anybody to hold my hand.',1,0,0,0,'24.4.255.169','en'),(5304,1320,'2001-07-10 21:37:24',0,'puppy','Here in Texas, we can do a whole lot of that DMV stuff via \r\nmail (actually, we call the DMV the DPS; which is weird, \r\ncuz I didn\\\'t grow up here; where I grew up, we called it \r\nthe DMV, so I frequently call the DPS the DMV... I also \r\ncall yard sales \\\"tag sales\\\"....) Hey. My parenthetical was \r\nlonger than my statement...\r\n\r\n<p>Anyway, the DPS/DMV here has your photo (well, not \r\n*your* photo) on file, so anytime you \r\nlose/renew/update/whatever your licence, you just fill out \r\na form you can get mailed to you (or downloaded from the \r\nInternet) and then send it in with a $xx.00 check... pretty \r\nsweet.',1,0,0,0,'192.35.232.99','en'),(5305,1318,'2001-07-10 22:39:34',0,'bulwinkle j','i went to wassamatta U. and i can throw a great forward pass\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(5306,1316,'2001-07-10 22:48:32',0,'lulu to austin','ooh austin.',0,0,0,0,'216.244.30.44','en'),(5307,1316,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon to lulu','ooh lulu!\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(5308,1319,'2001-07-10 23:37:11',0,'chi chi','<p>\r\nwow. this makes me feel better about my irrational fear. \r\ni fly to the middle-east and back twice a year, and to \r\noregon frequently and i alway get super anxious.<br> i \r\nalways run around like a headless chicken before my \r\nflights, and think about all the horrible things that could \r\nhappen.<p>i lied. just thinking about this now is \r\nmaking me anxious.',0,0,0,0,'64.165.201.205','en'),(5309,1320,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>\r\n<tt>Satan incarnate lives in the New York City DMV.  Thats \r\nwhy I\\\'ve lived here for seven years and still carry an \r\nexpired, out-of-state license.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'209.244.180.50','en'),(5310,1314,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','and this was said to me last night:  ah, pissoff, i can\\\'t \r\nbe bothered with your games.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nand i just thought i was going for honesty.<br>\r\n<br>',4,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(5311,1316,'2001-07-11 00:03:22',0,'s5 to s5','???',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5312,1316,'2001-07-11 00:55:34',0,'kat','boy don\\\'t i feel left out',5,0,0,0,'32.102.109.157','en'),(5313,1318,'2001-07-11 00:56:09',0,'jay','I love you Lulu. I\\\'m in tears reading this.',1,0,0,0,'63.203.225.62','en'),(5314,1319,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','i have this one fantasy that has never been fulfilled yet, \r\nof coming off the plane all vaseline over the lens mae west \r\nstylie, and someone will be there, with flowers and kisses \r\nand little mooing noises. someday. i have yet to convince \r\nmy current boy that it\\\'s worth it, dang it.',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(5315,1316,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','yeah, i agree. the inside jokes on this site really get \r\ntiresome. if you\\\'re going to talk about something, give a \r\nlittle exposition first so everybody can appreciate it, not \r\njust the inner circle.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.9.201','en'),(5316,1316,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','how about we don\\\'t do that. boy that would suck, if i had \r\nto provide a glossary whenever i talk to my friends in \r\npublic. maybe not everything is about you!',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5317,1310,'2003-05-10 16:09:14',79,'yeti','I gaze with dismay<br>\r\nAt the wreckage in my life<br>\r\nAnd realize; I move soon!<br>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'64.51.232.102','en'),(5318,1316,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','maybe it is. who knows?\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.9.201','en'),(5319,1316,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','this publication purports to publish articles, to allow \r\ncontributors and others to comment on those articles, and to \r\nindex those contributors. kind of like an interactive \\\"new \r\nyorker.\\\" to have comments that feel like a continuation of \r\nconversations begun on chat or wherever offends those who \r\nare not privy to such. it\\\'s just common courtesy. if you \r\ndon\\\'t want to engage in public discourse and conduct \r\nyourselves in the realm of common decency, then take the \r\nfucking thing off the internet or password protect it or \r\nsomething. and watch how you talk to people you know nothing \r\nabout.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.9.201','en'),(5320,1316,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','then again, i\\\'m not going to fight with anyone. do \r\nwhatever you want.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.9.201','en'),(5321,1316,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','hi matt. do you want me to hug you? i\\\'m a hugger.',6,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5322,1316,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p>bunnies and kittens:</p>\r\n<p><img \r\nsrc=\\\"http://www.saturn5.com/steve/images/nice.jpg\\\"></\r\np>',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5323,1316,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','yes, please hug me. i\\\'m just about at the end of my rope. \r\ntying a knot and hanging on to the end of it. which is \r\nprobably a byproduct of burning myself down inside writing. \r\ni\\\'m sorry. i love you.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.9.201','en'),(5324,1316,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','i\\\'m going to take some meds and go to sleep now. thanks. \r\nnighty-night.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.9.201','en'),(5325,1316,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','huggers don\\\'t ask, they just do.<BR>\r\n<BR>\r\ns5 is an impostor.',3,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(5326,1316,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','by that, i do NOT mean i\\\'m going to try to overdose and \r\ncommit suicide. i wouldn\\\'t want anybody to contact the \r\npolice in my town and tell them to send an intervention team \r\nout here. i mean i\\\'m going to take some medication (zyprexa \r\n15 mg and paxil 10 mg) which i am prescribed and which i \r\ntake as a last resort if all else fails and get in my bed \r\nand go to sleep. sign off for the night. i haven\\\'t been \r\nsleeping well. i\\\'m writing a script about the russian \r\nrevolution and how it was financed by these american guys \r\nand everything is melting together and it\\\'s getting hard to \r\nseparate the fact from the fiction. i feel my personality \r\nmoving into rasputin territory. so i just need to take a \r\nlittle breather and sleep for a day or so. you guys take \r\ncare. \r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.9.201','en'),(5327,1321,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','man, that\\\'s beautiful.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.80','en'),(5328,1319,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','I think a plane crash would be an awesome way to die. The \r\nexcitement! No lingering illnesses, no tearful goodbyes, no \r\ndrama--most crashee\\\'s don\\\'t have much warning. I mean, \r\nyou\\\'re going to die sometime, no matter what. The odds of \r\ndying in a plane crash are so small(about one in 100,000 \r\naccording to my father, an airline pilot. that includes \r\nprivate planes.) that you would just have to say \\\"Hey. \r\nHow \\\'bout that. Fuck it.\\\"',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.80','en'),(5329,1319,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','everyone talks about the odds. it\\\'s not about the odds. \r\nit\\\'s loss of control. disconnecting from the ground. you \r\ncan\\\'t reason away a phobia. i would fly if i were the pilot.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5330,1316,'2001-07-11 05:01:27',0,'bmg','matt has a point tho. people i have refered to the site \r\nhave told me that they cannot seem to follow due to the \r\nhidden/inside comments that seem to flow much like chat \r\nroom conversations within a select circle of friends. i \r\nhave been here for some time, entire time, and often i am \r\nleft scratching my head as to what this has to do with that \r\nand so forth... just not wanting this to become another \r\nboring blog that follows no structure. I am not suggesting \r\nwe apply rules or more structure, only a little less \r\nsecretive substance so that we all can laugh, cry, and be \r\naware of eachother... mang, i am off topic huh! \r\n(mang=inside lingo for ???) These articles travel thousands \r\nof miles to readers all over the world, which is great and \r\nkeeps me coming back to learn more about all of you... now, \r\ni am going to be quiet, as i am sure i am in trouble for \r\nbeing sooo off topic... sorry, people. ',1,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(5331,1316,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','ok, i\\\'m back. try not to wet your pants. got the pills down \r\nmy throat and i\\\'m chillin\\\' like bob dylan. i\\\'m not saying \r\ndon\\\'t chat or don\\\'t email people - i\\\'m saying just divide \r\nyourself: be here when you\\\'re here and be in chat when etc. \r\nthe thing is i\\\'m just jealous cause i can\\\'t chat with this \r\nold mac of my parents and/or i\\\'m too lazy to learn how to do \r\nit. it\\\'s all about you, isn\\\'t it, mattie? me, me, me. well, \r\ni\\\'m not tired yet. just very relaxed. maybe working off a \r\ngood fuck would do the trick. go find roger and eddie and \r\nsee if they want to smoke some bowls and get in the jacuzzi. \r\nrub a dub dub, three men in a tub. the butcher, the baker, \r\nthe orthodox quaker. yeah, i think so.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.79.65','en'),(5332,1316,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','now that i think about it, this site is the one place where \r\ni don\\\'t censor myself. with my friends, my coworkers, my \r\nlovers, i show each selected facets of myself. even in the \r\nprofessional writing i do, i don\\\'t let myself go the way i \r\ndo here. so i guess i\\\'m using this site for therapy, in a \r\nway. perhaps i need to integrate my personality. cause it \r\nseems really fragmented, now that i reflect upon it. and i \r\nguess it\\\'s the contact i\\\'m making with you all and the \r\nsimualtaneous contact with this higher, better, previously \r\nunknown self of mine that is what i value about this \r\nsite.<BR>i don\\\'t think my town is a healthy community. i \r\ndon\\\'t think the relationships i have with my family, lovers, \r\netc. are necessarily healthy. i waver between wanting \r\nsomeone to take care or me and wanting to be my own man. i \r\ndon\\\'t know. i think i\\\'ll go back to athens or somewhere else \r\nthat has a similar positive, openminded vibe. someplace like \r\nswinney.org would be if it was a town. \r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.79.65','en'),(5333,1319,'2001-07-11 06:03:20',0,'Joanna','I always cry at airports.  Always.  But I\\\'m not afraid of \r\nflying.  I guess I\\\'m just afraid of leaving people, or of \r\npeople leaving me.  ',1,0,0,0,'203.97.2.242','en'),(5334,1316,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>it is true, there is quite a bit of jabber jaw that goes \r\non here on the world\'s greatest website.  it was not intended \r\nto be a jabber jaw joint.  that just happens.  people get \r\ntogether and they get serious, then they get playful, but \r\nthey still get serious every now and then.  there is lots of \r\nmuck jabber, but then there are some genuine flowery \r\ndiscussions that go on.  i\'m working on another project that \r\nwill cut down on the jabber jaw.  it will also be on \r\nswinney.org.  there will be twoooooo great tasts that taste \r\ngreat together.  but enough about the future.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\none of the things i like about reading people like lulu\'s \r\nstuff is the effect it has on my writing style.  inevitably, \r\njust like i would pick up a laugh or a mannerism from a \r\nfriend, i find my sels slipping into this mode where i think \r\ni am sooooooooo cool, just completely golden.  a style that i \r\ndefinately got from our pal lulu whom i adore.  sure, some \r\nmay think she is boring, but i think she is wonderful.  in \r\nthis website full of cliche\'s, she is the most extreme of \r\ncliche\'s, a substanceless sassmouth.  and she takes a few \r\nelements of personality that her victim might leak and \r\nexploit, extrapolating into a fireworks show of assanine \r\nstereotypes and more cliche.  lulu is so cool.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nas for he inside joke about the hot dog, there was not one.  \r\ni might as well have said matt put the hot dog in lulu\'s ass.  \r\nhow would i know?  there was no inside story here.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\n<a href=\"http://www.sugarandspice.org/camping/index.html\"><img src=\"http://www.sugarandspice.org/camping/thumbs/IMG0012.jpg\"></A></P>\r\n',3,0,0,0,'64.174.154.112','en'),(5335,1316,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p>\r\n<img \r\nsrc=\\\"http://themeatjoy.com/images/hangintherebaby.jp\r\ng\\\"></p>',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5336,1310,'2001-07-11 07:16:42',0,'lulu','dammit, i\\\'m never gonna get this shit right.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(5337,1310,'2001-07-11 07:16:42',0,'lulu','dammit, i\\\'m never gonna get this shit right.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(5338,1318,'2001-07-11 09:11:20',0,'lulu to egg','dude, we\\\'re hiring. get your ass down here.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(5339,1318,'2001-07-11 09:20:36',0,'lulu to the thug','i love you too, you big lug.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(5340,1318,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','you don\\\'t get egg. she\\\'s ours.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5341,1317,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','^ hi stinder. how are you? stop invading my domain. \r\n',6,0,0,0,'142.214.129.50','en'),(5342,1322,'2003-07-24 15:44:23',165,'joker','it depends on who\\\'s around...',2,0,0,0,'66.68.48.125','en'),(5343,1319,'2001-07-11 13:17:40',0,'puppy','to s5: yeah&#151;I think I would fly too, if I were the \r\npilot. Maybe it\\\'s a control thing... I generally don\\\'t like \r\nriding in cars when other people drive... However, most of \r\nmy friends don\\\'t have cars, so I am the one driving most of \r\nthe time anyway...',1,0,0,0,'192.35.232.99','en'),(5344,1320,'2001-07-11 13:23:32',0,'essemar to Peter','I heard about a satelite DMV office on west 34th street \r\npast the Kmart there that few people know about.  \r\nSupposedly, you can actually get in and out of there in \r\nless then half an hour.  Or course, I\\\'m carrying an out of \r\nstate license myself.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5345,1321,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','Life can really suck sometimes.  I was living with this \r\nwonderful girl for two years and had to break it off last \r\nDecember.  I\\\'m still hurting.  I know that I\\\'ll feel \r\nalright about it some day, but I\\\'ll never be the same \r\nperson again.  If you feel the need, you can send me an \r\nemail.  I\\\'m living in NYC too.',2,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5346,1322,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','I find that if you spend enough time in a bar drinking beer \r\nsomething will eventually happen.  Oh yeah, smile a lot too.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5347,1305,'2001-07-11 14:04:51',0,'kd-o-g','<P>adam:  \\\"Confused, naked hippies sitting on the porch \r\ntrying to convince you YOU\\\'RE the one with issues.\\\"</P>\r\n<P>HAhaHahA!</P>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(5348,1322,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','Get a job. Hell, get two or three.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.130','en'),(5349,1321,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>\r\n<tt>I couldn\\\'t say it.  I thought I was about to, and then \r\nthis metallic, bitter, cramping taste seized my dry mouth, \r\nand I couldn\\\'t make the words - any words.  MY whole face \r\nfelt limp.  I managed an Ooouuhhhh..? and turned, walked \r\nhome.  My unconscious body language did get a strong \r\nmessage across, though.  An hour after my post, she came \r\nhome and we discussed.  No good or bad, just discused - \r\nthats a start, maybe.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nessemar: you\\\'re a strong man whereas I\\\'m too hopeful.  I \r\nread your other posts regarding what seems to sound very \r\nfamiliar.  Maybe I delude myself, but I continue to hope \r\nthat things aren\\\'t that far-gone yet.  3.5 years... most of \r\nit better than the recent few months, in all, good enough \r\nto think there\\\'s some future, yet, if I\\\'m willing to be \r\npatient, not pushy/smothery, wise and less emotional.  It \r\njust puts me in a dark mood to feel like I feel now, to \r\nhurt, remembering what was, and to see where this might be \r\ngoing.  I\\\'ll be in touch if things develop along the route \r\nof your experiences... I can imagine you might have some \r\nvaluable insights.</tt>\r\n',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5350,1322,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i am never bored. being bored is like death.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5351,1316,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','yeah, that\\\'s me lately. cat totem. in freefall. no \r\ncircadian.<BR>at other times, it\\\'s rabbit. or snake. or \r\nmonkey. but i\\\'m striving for bear. i\\\'m really trying for \r\nbear.<BR>(for some reason, this comment reminds me of sam \r\njackson\\\'s monologue at the end of \\\"pulp fiction.\\\" maybe \r\ncause it\\\'s not far from it.)\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.10.35','en'),(5352,1322,'2001-07-11 15:18:50',0,'bmg','just this morning I was speaking to k-dogg about boredom \r\nand loneliness... recently i came to the conclusion that \r\none, or at least myself, must keep busy and focused on \r\nliving goals, living today right now. live today, if you \r\nlive in yesterday you will be burdened with the \\\"should of, \r\ncould of\\\'s\\\" and if you live for tomorrow you will be \r\nburdened with never experiencing today - thus your life \r\nwill seem dull... go out, live, be alive... or as joker \r\nonce said, \\\"i am going down town to be a person, and do \r\nwhat person\\\'s sometime do...\\\" er something like that... \r\nenroll yourself in that art class you have allways dreamt \r\nabout, become that artist that you dream of. Go swim in the \r\nlake, take yoga, buy a bike, take a walk and become that \r\nhealthy body that you and other\\\'s dream of... go, be a \r\nperson now. and of course, SMILE. ',1,0,0,0,'198.214.190.236','en'),(5353,1318,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to lulu','the thug wouldnt take the motherfuckin cat. I think the \r\ncat is falling in love with me. what do I do.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.101.202','en'),(5354,1324,'2001-07-11 17:15:10',0,'wb','loud bitch',2,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(5355,1324,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon\\\'s addendum','On the spot, the lustre king of the albany bowl, DANCE DANCE \r\nREVOLUTION for only a dollar. Left arrow, down arrow, left \r\nleft left, right, up, up, down. It was at the three lefts and \r\na simultaneous up that I dropped the ball and suddenly the \r\nscreen is flashing FAIL FAIL FAIL. Yeah. What else...I can\\\'t \r\nreally remember exactly except that the bartender asked me at \r\none point if i was flirting with the security guard.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(5356,1321,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<P>Yeah, body language.  It took me months to finally, \r\ndefinitively walk away, and all the while she knew and \r\nconvinced herself that she didn\\\'t.  I think I was secretly \r\nhoping she would be the one to make the break, so she could \r\nbear the guilt.</P><P>I don\\\'t know what your exact \r\nsituation is, but I hope that it\\\'s just a couple bumps on \r\nan otherwise smooth road.  Mine was one where I *knew* I \r\nhad to get the hell out of there, but emotional bonds tied \r\nmy tongue.</P><P>Peace out, Dude!</P>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5357,1322,'2001-07-11 18:19:33',0,'stella','<P>as the guy in Shawshank Redeption says\\\"\r\n\\\"A man\\\'s(woman\\\'s) gotta to something to take his(her) mind \r\noff of the waiting\\\"\r\n</P><P>\r\nOr some shit like that.</P>',0,0,0,0,'168.100.203.247','en'),(5358,1324,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','yes, writers are like gays, aren\\\'t they? they so often do \r\nhappen in the best of families (**exasperated sigh**).',1,0,0,0,'64.132.148.219','en'),(5359,1324,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','we treat writers in the south the same as we do eccentrics: \r\nwe don\\\'t hide them up in the attic, just trot them out for \r\nthe guests to see. kind of like a circus animal more than a \r\nprofession.',1,0,0,0,'64.132.148.219','en'),(5360,1324,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon the fag','hi. yeah.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(5361,1324,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','hi. i\\\'m polysexual and a writer. don\\\'t think i was being \r\nhomophobic.',1,0,0,0,'64.132.148.219','en'),(5362,1324,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','pol