17/kitty.jpg\\\">',3,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(5546,1348,'2001-07-16 04:46:33',0,'human interest','\r\nNEW YORK (CNN) -- A mother cat who raced into a burning \r\nBrooklyn building and rescued her five kittens is recuperating with \r\nher litter at an animal clinic. \r\n<br><br>\r\nWith her eyes blistered shut, her paws burned and her coat \r\nsinged, the cat -- nicknamed Scarlet for her patches of red fur -- \r\ndarted into the flames and pulled out her kittens, one by one. \r\nOnce all the kittens had been rescued, their mother conducted a \r\nhead count, touching each kitten with her nose to make sure they \r\nwere all there.\r\n<br><br>\r\nFirefighter David Gianelli found the feline family outside the \r\nbuilding Friday and took them to an animal shelter, where the \r\nmother and babies are receiving treatment.\r\n<br><br>\r\nHundreds of people have offered to adopt the cats.\r\n',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5547,1348,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','<a href=\\\"http://www.theonion.com/onion3723/pet-\r\ncare_tips.html\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">Pet Care Tips</a><br>',3,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(5548,1348,'2001-07-16 06:49:39',0,'sawks','<br><a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.abcnews.go.com/sections/world/Daily\r\nNews/canada010713_cat.html\\\">!!!!</a>',1,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(5549,1349,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','<p> That was me :/ </p>',1,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(5550,1348,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p><img \r\nsrc=\\\"http://www.saturn5.com/steve/images/nice.jpg\\\"></\r\np>',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5551,1348,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i want to make this perfectly clear. the kitten and bunny \r\npicture isn\\\'t that cute. nowhere near as cute as the \r\nkitten romping through the field.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5552,1348,'2001-07-16 11:01:50',0,'Joanna','\\\"It is not known why Daigle was giving his parrot a \r\nshower. \\\" - I think we should have a competition on Swinney \r\nwhere everyone writes a story that starts with that line.  ',2,0,0,0,'203.97.2.242','en'),(5553,1348,'2001-07-16 11:03:22',0,'Joanna','<I>Also:</I>\r\n<BR><BR>\r\n<B>Vancouver ducks slip through the quacks </B>\r\n<BR><BR>\r\n16.07.2001 \r\n<BR><BR>\r\nVANCOUVER - When a family of ducklings fell down a \r\nVancouver sewer grate their mother did what any parent \r\nwould do. \r\n<BR><BR>\r\nShe got help from a passing police officer. \r\n<BR><BR>\r\nOfficer Ray Peterson said the mother duck grabbed his leg \r\nwhile he was on patrol. \r\n<BR><BR>\r\n\\\"I thought it was a bit goofy, so I shoved it away,\\\" he \r\ntold the Vancouver Sun newspaper. \r\n<BR><BR>\r\nBut the mother duck again grabbed Peterson\\\'s leg, and then \r\nwaddled to a nearby sewer grate where she sat down and \r\nwaited for him to follow and investigate. \r\n<BR><BR>\r\n\\\"I went up to where the duck was lying and saw eight little \r\nbabies in the water below.\\\" \r\n<BR><BR>\r\nPolice removed the heavy metal grate with the help of a tow \r\ntruck and used a vegetable strainer to lift the ducklings \r\nout. \r\n<BR><BR>\r\nMother and offspring then waddled to a nearby pond. \r\n<BR><BR>\r\n- REUTERS \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'203.97.2.242','en'),(5554,1346,'2001-07-16 17:08:22',0,'jay','I think I have to disagree with you there, ty.  First off, \r\nI think you\\\'re underestimating how difficult it is to \r\nachieve true honesty in writing, to actually articulate, \r\nhonestly and completely, a thought. And, writers do need to \r\nstruggle to figure out what is they have to say. Yes, as \r\nKerouac proved amply, honesty, when one strives constantly \r\nto achieve it in writing, is the key to beautiful and \r\ncompelling thoughts sometimes. But as Kerouac also amply \r\nproved, there\\\'s a lot of tedium in recording one\\\'s life, \r\nunstructured and without linear direction. \\\"On the Road\\\" \r\nwas heavily edited, as many don\\\'t realize, and it\\\'s evident \r\nhow much more punctuation and sort-of structure was imposed \r\non it by an editor, in contrast to a book like \\\"The \r\nSubterraneans\\\" which was not \\\"edited\\\" in any traditional \r\nsense.<p>\r\nBut our honest thoughts are not always original just \r\nbecause we thought them, and in order to have a literary \r\ncareer you have to combine the achievement of honesty with \r\nsome awareness of what\\\'s come before, and what it is you \r\nwant to say about your culture, or about the human \r\ncondition. There may not be all that many \r\nuntouched \\\"original\\\" thoughts, but the only way to have \r\nyour work be unique is to \\\"find a voice\\\" as they say. It\\\'s \r\ntrue this voice is already in you, but you\\\'ve got to find \r\nthe pathway to it, hone it, allow it to flow freely. On top \r\nof all that, you\\\'ve got to learn the rules of storytelling \r\n(you gotta learn em to break em...), and that can take \r\nyears, cause the rules are not terribly simple.',3,0,0,0,'63.203.225.62','en'),(5555,1350,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','<p>\r\nhi. when i saw you on sunday, i felt about the same way.<br>\r\naustin: sims, you look like you don\\\'t want to be here.<br>\r\nsimon: blah, i guess i don\\\'t.<br>\r\n</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(5556,1338,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','hiking!? cough cough. \r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(5557,1351,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','<BR>a man drinks himself sick in a bar, pukes down his \r\nshirt front. he laments that his wife will kill him for \r\nruining his shirt, staying out so late, etc.<BR>his friend, \r\nnext stool over, ushers him into the men\\\'s room, cleans him \r\nup, says, \\\"just tuck a twenty dollar bill into your breast \r\npocket, tell her the guy next to you got sick, gave you the \r\ntwenty to pay for the dry cleaning.\\\"<BR>so they rock on for \r\nawhile, he finally gets in around four a.m. his wife is \r\nlivid. she asks what happened to his shirt. <BR>\\\"relax,\\\" he \r\ntells her. pulls out the money, hands it over.<BR>\\\"but \r\nthere\\\'s forty dollars here,\\\" she says. \\\"what\\\'s the other \r\ntwenty for?\\\"<BR>\\\"oh, i almost forgot to tell you,\\\" he \r\nsays. \\\"he shit my pants, too.\\\"',1,0,0,0,'63.31.55.121','en'),(5558,1350,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','in the car we listened to \\\"sunday morning coming \r\ndown\\\" by johnny cash.',0,0,0,0,'209.86.7.131','en'),(5559,1353,'2001-07-16 21:26:36',0,'lou reed','i like wall projection movies, plastic Inevitable baby.',1,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(5560,1353,'2001-07-16 21:48:26',0,'jim morrison','i want to wander mexico on peyote, embrace the lizard, \r\nscream at the gods, turn into a eagle and go insane.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(5561,1353,'2001-07-16 21:50:59',0,'ray','hi, im ray, the keyboardist of \\\"the doors\\\" fame. jim and i \r\nmade films of girls freaking out and screaming at ucla film \r\nschool. the girls often bared their breasts. you might have \r\nseen this chapter in our lives depicted in oliver stone\\\'s \r\nfilm \\\"the doors,\\\" now available on dvd.',1,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(5562,1353,'2001-07-16 21:52:22',0,'jimi hendrix','to morrison: heh. yeah man. that would be wild... whatcha \r\ndoin tonight?',0,0,0,0,'192.35.232.99','en'),(5563,1353,'2001-07-16 21:56:59',0,'jimbo','nothing but existing, man, nothing but existing.',1,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(5564,1353,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','someone is trying to make me cry. ',0,0,0,0,'209.86.7.131','en'),(5565,1353,'2001-07-16 22:03:09',0,'janis','you dicks. leave her alone',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(5566,1353,'2001-07-16 22:36:08',0,'RL','you chillins y\\\'all just settle down now....it\\\'s bad you \r\nknow.',1,0,0,0,'32.102.110.201','en'),(5567,1353,'2001-07-16 22:54:44',0,'lou reed','I wasn\\\'t trying to goof at all. How can u be here without \r\na thick skin?',5,0,0,0,'24.93.61.58','en'),(5568,1353,'2002-03-05 20:17:36',17,'austin to egg','<BR>\r\nyum girls smell like <BR>\r\nrose petals, pez, my little ponies