639,1360,'2001-07-18 06:58:53',0,'wb','she looks 35 but is 49 and she needs a plane ticket?\r\n<BR>\r\ni think the mantra is always: jpegs, jpegs, jpegs. you can \r\nnever have too many jpegs. \r\n<BR>\r\nbeware of what is now called the \\\"napkin\\\" jpeg. this is a \r\njpeg that is composed or selected out of a large group of \r\npictures, you know, \\\"just the right one.\\\" this jpeg is what \r\nthe person wants you to see, but when you meet them you go: \r\nhuh, you look nothing like your jpeg! just the right angle. \r\na black and white low quality web cam helps a lot. keyword: \r\nshadows. \r\n<br>\r\nsouthwest airlines. \r\npeace.',1,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(5640,1360,'2001-07-18 07:00:48',0,'wb','oh sorry. i realized the 49 year old is your mom. i guess i \r\nbased my comments more on ix\\\'s comments than reading \r\ncarefully. \r\n<br>\r\nno, really, your mom is pr_tty, no matter what jpegs. sorry.',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(5641,1356,'2001-07-18 08:50:55',0,'confused','mazol tov?',0,0,0,0,'203.96.111.201','en'),(5642,145,'2001-07-18 10:50:33',0,'cynic','- too bad they don\\\'t love you.',3,0,0,0,'64.172.164.74','en'),(5643,1359,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>\r\n<tt>Once I had a dream that little wormy snakes were \r\nslithering into my mouth; i then woke up and vomited - for \r\nno reason.  I hadn\\\'t been sick or drinking or anything.  \r\nWeird.  I guess the old sobconscious can play its tricks \r\nnow and then, too.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5644,1360,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','Hey Green, I\\\'ve got a cell phone that came with a bazillion \r\nfree minutes that I never use.  I\\\'ll call.  Just thought \r\nI\\\'d warn you first, but I can\\\'t sell you a jizzoint.  I \r\ndon\\\'t smoke, mostly because every time I have one of three \r\nthings has happened: 1. I immediatly passed out.  2. I \r\nvomitted.  3. I wandered down the middle (yes, the middle) \r\nof city streets looking for Doritos.<P>Weed bad.  Single \r\nmalt Irish whiskey good.</P>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5645,1360,'2001-07-18 15:00:53',0,'huh','weed makes you vomit? veeery interesting reaction.',0,0,0,0,'168.100.203.247','en'),(5646,1360,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','Yeah, weed plus alcohol, every single time.  I spent the \r\n1999-2000 New Year\\\'s clutching to a toilet bowl to keep \r\nfrom falling off the floor and hitting my head on the \r\nceiling wilst listening to people chant, \\\"10,9,8...\\\"  I \r\nthink I managed to empty the entire contents of my \r\ndigestive track down to my colon over the course of that \r\nevening.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5647,1362,'2001-07-18 17:46:43',0,'uhuru','<p>I do hear what you are saying about feeling like people \r\naren\\\'t seeing you as a human being.  Oftentimes I have met \r\npeople like this in a \\\"professional\\\" arena.  People in the \r\n\\\"professional\\\" arena are often very immature and socially \r\nretarded.  I don\\\'t know why.  I usually enjoy hanging out \r\nwith computer geeks because they\\\'re not fronting this big \r\n\\\"professional\\\" persona. Then again I am generally just \r\nagainst small talk and must seem socially retarded myself \r\nto those who engage in it.  I just drift away, mind \r\nwhirring with important (to me anyway) observations about \r\npeople\\\'s body language and energy, and my blocks and their \r\nblocks, and our interaction at an ethereal level, and what \r\nthey are saying underneath the inane blather about tv and \r\nweather and sports and things that don\\\'t matter to me at \r\nall.</p>\r\n<p>as for politeness, I see it differently.  when I am \r\nbeing the person I want to be, I will hold the door for \r\nwhoever is behind me (for example).  I will take care of \r\nthose around me and not wake people up with loud footsteps \r\nand clean up my messes.  when I am in my most graceful \r\nself, politeness comes from the center, a true caring for \r\nmyself and the people I encounter.  I like what you said \r\nabout dancing with the other person.  it\\\'s also being aware \r\nof other people\\\'s space and needs.  living in the city I \r\nsee many people who are not only impolite, they seem \r\ndetermined to tell the whole world to fuck off whenever \r\nthey get the chance, in whatever form they can.  it\\\'s \r\nreally amazing--like people who throw still-smoking \r\ncigarette butts on the ground in front of you, or shove you \r\non the bus, or spit as you\\\'re walking by.  Amazing.</p>\r\n<p>I honor you as a unique and beautiful human being, in \r\nessence completely one-of-a-kind and phenomenally \r\nspecial.</p>\r\n:)',1,0,0,0,'216.185.7.75','en'),(5648,1360,'2001-07-18 17:58:17',0,'huh','Yes, weed makes me vomit too when I smoke whilst drunk. \r\nEvery time. When I smoke whilst not drunk, it just makes me \r\nparanoid as FUCK. I want so bad to be a pot smoker. But, \r\nalas, it is not to be.',0,0,0,0,'168.100.203.247','en'),(5649,1364,'2001-07-18 17:58:58',0,'wb','she just needs some space, dude.',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(5650,1364,'2001-07-18 18:01:35',0,'wb','she has a craving for oranvagina.',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(5651,1362,'2001-07-18 18:02:24',0,'jp to uhuru:','I\\\'m not sure why I brought up the politeness thing. It \r\nwasn\\\'t like I encountered extreme rudeness, just some \r\npeople not bothering to say hello or goodbye.<BR>\r\nActually looking back on it I think I was overly sensitive \r\nor naive about things. This group wasn\\\'t any different than \r\nwhen I was still working there. I just expected something \r\ndifferent. I wouldn\\\'t want anyone to have to put on some \r\npolite front, but then again I don\\\'t really like being \r\ntotally disregarded either.<BR>\r\nThanks for the nice words. ;)<BR>\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.172.123.228','en'),(5652,1364,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','you say, \\\"ok honey im going over here for a little while, \r\nbeep when you want me.\\\" she will miss you. go on a \r\ntrip or something.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.105.140','en'),(5653,1362,'2001-07-18 18:13:50',0,'kat','it has been a hard lesson for me to learn that not everyone \r\nis going to be my friend...and that not everyone is going \r\nto think of friendship in the same terms as i do. being \r\ndeeply empathic is overrated. it only means that i find it \r\neasy to be drawn close to others. the little pains come and \r\ngo with the days as people i thought i had bonded with \r\ndon\\\'t call, don\\\'t write, blah blah. but then weird shit \r\nhappens...out of the blue i get a letter from someone i \r\nhadn\\\'t spoken to in seven years. they are ecstatic to have \r\nfound me. or another one, who can\\\'t even find the time to \r\nemail calls to tell me what an inspiration i\\\'ve been to \r\nthem. the world is too busy. that is my theory. people \r\nexpend so much energy trying to survive, to stay sane, to \r\ndeal with their families that someone else get\\\'s the short \r\nend of their emotional stick. people have forgotten how to \r\nrelax and just enjoy...other people i think. [furniture? i \r\nknow how that feels. i am the girl who had a birthday party \r\nthree weeks ago. that would be the party where absolutely \r\nnoone i invited showed up. and i was so tired from work i \r\ndin\\\'t even care.]',4,0,0,0,'32.102.110.228','en'),(5654,1362,'2001-07-18 18:21:02',0,'stella','So many times I have made plans to go meet ex-coworkers for \r\na drink or whatever and every time, without fail, I have \r\ncome up against that indifference. It\\\'s the crappiest \r\nfeeling in the world. <br>\r\nI truly enjoy people, especially people whom I spend a lot \r\nof time with. I spend a lot of time at work and once I\\\'ve \r\nleft a specific work environment, I almost sentimentalize \r\nthe experience. So when I go back to the environment (or a \r\nlikeness of it; ie drinks with that group) I get excited and \r\nlook forward to the time. On  the other side, when I\\\'m in a \r\nwork environment and someone who has left comes back to \r\nvisit or have drinks, I am almost always the only one to be \r\ntruly happy and excited to see that person. <br>\r\nBoth of these scenarios are crap. But this is what you get \r\nfrom a society that values \\\'things\\\' over people.',0,0,0,0,'168.100.203.247','en'),(5655,1363,'2001-07-18 18:27:45',0,'stella','<P>\\\"it has been a year and i thought i would know your \r\ninsides  much more by now.\\\"</P>\r\n<P> that pretty much sums up my relationship</P>\r\n<P> the question is, do I take the chance that moving in \r\nwill make us closer, or do I follow my guts and run for dear \r\nlife?\\\"</P>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'168.100.203.247','en'),(5656,1364,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','ew, orange soda. barf.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(5657,1363,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<P>From experience: Moving in brings you closer in \r\nproximity only.  The intimacy is there or it isn\\\'t; it \r\ncan\\\'t be forced.</P><P>At 22, I feel like a decrepit, dirty \r\nold man (my thirty-something co-workers shoot me evil \r\nglares when I accidently let that thought slip \r\nout).</P><P>Some people need more space than others.  I \r\nlived with a girl who needed to spend every free moment she \r\nhad with me whereas I had things to see, places to go, \r\npeople to do. :)</P><P>Seriously, we had \r\ndifferent \\\"togetherness\\\" needs.  I would get frustrated \r\nthat I was spending so much time with her and neglecting \r\nother activities that didn\\\'t involve her, and she would be \r\nmiserable and lonely when I was off doing my own thing and \r\nshe was in the apartment alone.  I think that\\\'s one of the \r\nthings that tore us apart.</P><P>She says that she never \r\nreally knew me after living together for two years.</P>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5658,1363,'2001-07-18 19:05:36',0,'stella','Are you an Aquarius?',0,0,0,0,'168.100.203.247','en'),(5659,1364,'2001-07-18 19:26:19',0,'truth','sometimes they don\\\'t come back. it\\\'s a slow nice way out.',5,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(5660,915,'2001-07-18 19:58:36',0,'cyantist','so this got posted after all.  heh.',1,0,0,0,'64.172.164.74','en'),(5661,1364,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>\r\nah, there\\\'s the rub.  she has space - i\\\'m cool with that - \r\neveryone needs space and time and the like, me included.  \r\nits just this rollercoaster thing - this dragging me around. \r\n When i\\\'m not around, she calls me, makes plans to see me, \r\nmeets me anywhere, calls me at work, calls me at home, calls \r\nme on the cell, texts me, muses about what we\\\'re going to \r\ndo that evening or that weekend- and i go to great effort to \r\nbe patient, fulfill her needs and be there when i can and \r\nwhen she needs me.  When i am around, though, she\\\'s \r\nindifferent, and we never do any of the things she\\\'s thought \r\nup, proposed to me, suggested.  We meet, and she gets \r\nbusy all of a sudden.  it\\\'s like all that emotional need she \r\noverflows with when i\\\'m not there completely disappears when \r\nwe get together. i\\\'m not saying its some terrrible thing, \r\njust hard (and damn confusing) to figure out.  especially \r\nsince this just kaboom started after several years of \r\nrational, balanced good-relationship vibes.  she won\\\'t talk \r\nabout it now.  i\\\'m definitelye at a loss, but not as bleak \r\nas i might have come off as...<br>\r\n<br>\r\nand i <b>do</b> like orange soda.  \r\ndiet-slice-orange-mandarin.  ummmmmmmmm. i\\\'m going to go buy \r\nsome now at gristede\\\'s.',3,0,0,0,'209.246.96.239','en'),(5662,1364,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<P><I>Love is like a flame and time spent apart like the \r\nwind.  A small flame will be extinguished by the gentlest \r\nbreeze, but the strongest gale can only stoke a raging fire \r\nto greater heights.</I></P>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5663,1363,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','who? me? I\\\'m a taurus, but I act nothing like it.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5664,1366,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','Trust... You\\\'ve got to have complete trust in a person for \r\nthings to work all happy nice in the end.  Even a slight \r\nbreach can fuck things up in the long run.<P>I get \r\nintuitions about people/things and they are usually right, \r\nbut sometimes they\\\'re wrong.  I say look in your heart and \r\nthrough that into his and see what you can see.  And don\\\'t \r\nthink too hard about it.  Thought clouds intuition.  I\\\'d \r\njust do whatever feels right.</P>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5665,1366,'2001-07-18 20:55:54',0,'wb','the _admitted_ ex-cheater. what other kind is there? ',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(5666,1367,'2001-07-18 20:57:11',0,'wb','<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0395977894\\\">rea\r\nd it and weep</a>',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(5667,1367,'2001-07-18 21:11:26',0,'hh','<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0671600419/qid=\r\n995490579/sr=1-1/ref=sc_b_1/002-2552565-2267232\\\">rea\r\nd it and grow</a>',1,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(5668,1364,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','how bout the sex? are you getting her off enough?',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5669,1363,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','heh.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5670,1366,'2001-07-18 21:36:25',0,'uhuru','<p>hooray for intuition, and hooray for dreams...however, I \r\nwould not take the dreams literally.  Certainly they may \r\nmean that you have fears about living together, but the \r\nreality of the decision needs to be viewed in light of the \r\nconcrete and sensate matter (as opposed to an intuitive \r\nmatter) that it is.  Whether or not to trust him is an \r\nintuitive decision.  Whether or not to live with him is a \r\nsensate decision.  Your intuition points you in a \r\ndirection, and it is up to your sensate function to \r\ninterpret the message of the intuition into reality.</p>\r\n<p>as for cheaters, I don\\\'t believe at all that \\\"if he\\\'s \r\ndone it once he\\\'s bound to do it again.\\\"  I say this \r\nbecause for one reason or another, I\\\'ve cheated on \r\nboyfriends in the past, but by no means do I consider \r\nmyself chronic cheaterwoman because of it.  In my current \r\nrelationship I don\\\'t want to cheat.  Because I\\\'m committed \r\nin a true and deep way, seeking out other relationships or \r\nencounters just doesn\\\'t appeal.  Give this man the benefit \r\nof the doubt based on the him you know now, and not his \r\npast mistakes or choices.</p>\r\n<p>back to the sensate: to concretize the message of your \r\ndreams seems very important.  to talk about it, draw it, \r\ndistill its true meaning (not what the books say, what your \r\nheart and psyche are conspiring to tell you), and to \r\nmeditate on this decision as a decision of physical place--\r\n(ie how does your body react to the idea of living with \r\nthis person?  does it get all melty warm, or clammy and \r\nwithdrawn?  what does the body\\\'s wisdom tell you?).  </p>\r\n<p>may your intuition and your sensate functions work in \r\nharmony to guide you to where you want to be.</p>',2,0,0,0,'216.185.7.75','en'),(5671,1367,'2001-07-18 21:42:11',0,'puppy','<A \r\nHREF=\\\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0385334206/pupp\r\nyvaugn\\\">read it and <strike>weep</strike> laugh</A>',0,0,0,0,'192.35.232.99','en'),(5672,1366,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<br><br>\r\n[begin polyamory discussion #379]<br>\r\n[end polyamory discussion #379]<br>',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5673,1366,'2001-07-18 22:03:30',0,'uhuru','why is it most polyamourous couples I meet give me the \r\nmajor creeps?  maybe they\\\'re nervous because everyone they \r\nmeet suspects that the couple is trying covertly to draw \r\ninnocent singles into their lascivious web of debauchery.  \r\nmaybe they\\\'re on drugs.',4,0,0,0,'216.185.7.75','en'),(5674,1366,'2001-07-18 22:30:56',0,'a thought','or maybe you\\\'re projecting.',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5675,1366,'2001-07-18 22:33:17',0,'wb','why do they give you the creeps? maybe cos the poly womyn \r\ndo ass to ass? could that be it? ',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(5676,1369,'2001-07-18 23:12:31',0,'the enquirer','TEETH and hairy man are having an affair! shocking pics, page \r\n62!\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(5677,1369,'2001-07-18 23:27:27',0,'big chin','love the dance mag story. you capture the annoyances and \r\nvagaries of the magazine world in a wonderful way. plus,i \r\nparticularly love the paragraph on your photo guy and you \r\nand brooks.\r\n\r\nhas anyone told you lately that YOU RULE!!!',4,0,0,0,'64.12.106.41','en'),(5678,1369,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','ladies and gentleman, the above is my mother.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(5679,1353,'2001-07-19 00:00:24',0,'bark','last night i woke up to the neighbors cows in our garden.  \r\nabout a half a dozen mostly shadows slowly destroying our \r\ngood stuff.  i chased them off.  they came back later.  i \r\nwent out again and made loud gun noises. they ran and \r\nstayed away.  the tomatoes are beautiful this year, dozens \r\nof huge plants. i want to see them ripe.    ',3,0,0,0,'12.110.65.79','en'),(5680,1369,'2001-07-19 00:02:43',0,'Ursula Von Utte','Simon, what could i possibly say about that but...SOCKO!! \r\n(not really...but sort of...just wanted use the word socko \r\ni guess). \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nP.S. Brooks is a monkey ',1,0,0,0,'64.29.36.15','en'),(5681,1087,'2001-07-19 00:05:07',0,'Mike','What price now, for a shallow piece of dignity?',1,0,0,0,'165.84.104.2','en'),(5682,1364,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','<p>this pretty much explains the tail end of my \r\nrelationship with one of my ex lovers.</p>\r\n<p>here\\\'s what i was feeling:  we\\\'d been together 4 years.  \r\ni was restless, feeling like i was too young to settle for \r\nmediocre sex for the rest of my life, feeling like i had to \r\nspell everything out for him, realising that the \\\"we do \r\neverything together\\\" awesomeness was now becoming a drag \r\nand that i needed to get myself together.</p>\r\n<p>things my boyfriend could have done to make things \r\neasier on me and perhaps keep us together:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>give me space.  leave me alone for a whole week.  make \r\ndates with me, on weekends, to do things which were fun and \r\nnew. just put SOME effort in instead of whining at me.</li>\r\n<li>do new sex stuff.  anything new.</li>\r\n<li>try to re-establish himself as a lover and not a family \r\nmember or best friend.  this has to do with the sex and the \r\nspace.</li>\r\n<li>make a future for himself that didn\\\'t rely on me.  make \r\nplans for himself.  have an awesome life which doesn\\\'t need \r\nme to be in it.  this is perhaps the most important thing, \r\nbecause, apart from making me respect him more and see him \r\nmore as an individual, it would have made the transition \r\nfrom long-term relationship boy to single boy much easier \r\non him, if we had still broken up.</li>\r\n</ul></p>\r\n<p>there\\\'s nothing sexier than confidence and \r\nindependence.  the end.</p>',3,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(5683,1087,'2001-07-19 00:55:25',0,'msp','we don\\\'t talk about love.  we only want to get drunk.',3,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(5684,1364,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','are you getting her off mentally enough, though? most times, sex \r\nbegins in the head, not the crotch. or it begins with head, \r\ni forget which. mrow!',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(5685,1363,'2001-07-19 01:27:43',0,'answer','im a cancer and my man (?) is a scorpio',1,0,0,0,'198.81.16.48','en'),(5686,1360,'2001-07-19 01:30:12',0,'green','call me people \r\n\r\ni need some JD SALINGER SUPPORT\r\n\r\nthe babanafish i have become\r\n\r\nnow we dance',1,0,0,0,'198.81.16.48','en'),(5687,1367,'2001-07-19 01:54:36',0,'green','cool you dance. i do film\r\nall of it.\r\nyeah\r\nyou new yorker.....\r\ndid you vote Nader?',1,0,0,0,'198.81.16.48','en'),(5688,1364,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i feel that most relationships would be better off if \r\npeople would simply listen, rather than hope for explicit \r\ninstructions. sometimes \"i\'m too tired to cook\" means \r\n\"surprise me with dinner tonight\". or etc. that goes for the bigger things too.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5689,1364,'2001-07-19 03:03:11',0,'o to s5','<p>totally.  when you start to think it\\\'s annoying to have \r\nto think up nice things to do for your partner based on \r\nhints they\\\'ve given or things they\\\'ve said, then it\\\'s time \r\nto wonder why you\\\'re in the relationship at all.</p>\r\n<p>it\\\'s no fun to have to spell everything out all the \r\ntime.</p>\r\n<p>i hate having to tick \\\"constructive\\\" all the time.</p>\r\n',3,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(5690,1369,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','hello, where are the pictures of Cutey?? cmon, share.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.105.140','en'),(5691,1353,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','is this the bark who once offered to buy me a strap-on?',0,0,0,0,'216.175.105.140','en'),(5692,1366,'2001-07-19 03:51:30',0,'stella','<P>to wb: the _found out_ ex-cheater.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>to uhuru: thanks. One thing. Maybe two. The only reason \r\nwhy I put in my article that he is an admitted ex-cheater \r\nwas to help compartmentalize why I might dream that he\\\'s \r\ncheating. I don\\\'t believe in \\\"once a cheater, always a \r\ncheater\\\", and I\\\'m not of the belief that he\\\'ll cheat, which \r\nis why dreaming that he would  gives me pause. As for the \r\nrest, well, that\\\'s pretty much my whole problem. I need to \r\nthink about this, not feel, but it\\\'s hard to detact the \r\nfeelings when the sensory (the dreams) are so intense. The \r\nbest advice that I\\\'ve gotten so far is to rely on my trust. \r\nAnd on the fact that thinking about being in the same bed \r\nwith him every night makes me warm and tingly. </P>',0,0,0,0,'168.100.203.247','en'),(5693,1363,'2001-07-19 04:01:32',0,'kat','<p>yes. living together means you get to know each other \r\nbetter. but sometimes what you learn about the other is not \r\nwhat you hoped for. sometimes it just means that you \r\nrealize this is a person who does not want you to know \r\nthem. closed off from others. if you are not that happy \r\nbefore the big move in, then shacking up is not going to \r\nhelp. learn how to ask for what you want. do not point \r\nfingers and say you, you, you. simply say, hey...this is \r\nwhat i need. this is what i want from a relationship. what \r\nare your boundaries? what are you willing to give? to \r\ncompromise? to share? or not share? in the end...is this \r\nsomeone you can grow with?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>everyone involved ends up changing. thus is life. are \r\nyou both prepared for that?</p>',3,0,0,0,'32.102.64.210','en'),(5694,1363,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','i dont think people should move in together. at least, \r\nnot lovers. maybe friends. if you MUST be nearby every \r\nsingle fucking day, the ideal situation is if you live in \r\nseperate apartments in the same building. or \r\nsomething like that. like, on the same farm, but in \r\ndifferent bunkers. then you can sneak into his bunker,  \r\nhe can sneak into your hen house, you can squawk and \r\ntussle your feathers, my lil duckling. um. what was this \r\ncomment meant to be about i forget.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.105.140','en'),(5695,1363,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','or at least separate bedrooms.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5696,1367,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','i go to mcdonalds sometimes too. it\\\'s comfort food, all the \r\nway. my roomate and i have a pact that if one of us wins, \r\nwe split the money. good luck!',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.53','en'),(5697,1363,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','as an old man of almost 24, my advice is...oh shit. I don\\\'t \r\nknow what i\\\'m doing either. try to enjoy it! oh yeah, and \r\nhang out with steve. steve\\\'s cool. hi steve.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.53','en'),(5698,1369,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','*whimper*',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(5699,844,'2001-07-19 08:15:30',0,'deadeyes','R.E.M is amazing. i saw them live back in \\\'99. From what i \r\nremember, i fell in love that night. Plus Radiohead is one \r\nof my main loves. I have yet to see them live, but The \r\nBends would have to be my favourite.\r\n\r\ncheers\r\n\r\nxo',3,0,0,0,'24.141.64.203','en'),(5700,1372,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','i hate the word \\\"shoppe\\\". like \\\"fudge shoppe\\\". anything \r\n\\\"ye olde\\\" can fucking bite it too. yee oldie fudgie shoppy.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.105.140','en'),(5701,1364,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>\r\ns5; weeb:  i\\\'ve gotten quite good at listening (as opposed \r\nto simply hearing) so thats doubtfully an issue.  Mentally, \r\nthings are good (good point, weeb...).  Physically, her sex \r\ndrive has bottomed out inexplicably.  I\\\'m not griping, per \r\nse, as theres tons more to live than sex, but its \r\ndisappearance after several years of a good presence is a \r\nbit disconcerting... i think the new challenging job is a \r\nbig factor.  yikes.  oh woe is me, poor grad student, heh \r\nheh.\r\n\r\n',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5702,1367,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<tt>breakfast of champions, heh.  i like that book.  i \r\nmoved to nyc for specific motives, also, and have found \r\nthat working a 40+ hour week really does cut into those \r\nmotives.  thats the one inescapable thing that really \r\nbothers me nowadays.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5703,1372,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>\r\n<tt>I have that same angst against stuff that uses \\\"k\\\"s \r\nisntead of \\\"c\\\"s... i,e: \\\"Kuntry Kitchen\\\" or \\\"Kooky the \r\nKlown\\\'s Magic Birthday Strip-o-Gram for Kids\\\" or \r\nwhatever.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5704,1372,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>\r\n<i>Oh, and I also wanted to say:</i>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<tt>\r\nI like how you mentioned liking your friend\\\'s no-prentense \r\nhouse dancing style.  I agree, people are waay too \r\nserious/image conscious at clubs, especially some of the \r\ntrendier ones here in NYC (they get downright awful \r\nsometimes).  Nothing, offhand, seems as libberating as \r\ngetting out there and baring it all in a flailing dance \r\nlacking self-consciousness... it may look silly, but its \r\nintense.  One of my most intense and memorable club moments \r\noccurred when I was tripping out on a good dance vibe and \r\nwas in this totally non-rhythmic dancing trance.  as the \r\nmusic finally slowed, i realized that people were watching \r\nand... woah.. i didn\\\'t feel self-conscious.  beautiful \r\ngirls and guys floated past and said things like, \\\"you go, \r\nman!\\\" and \\\"you rock! you are so cool!\\\", \\\"i want what you\\\'re \r\non!\\\" unsolicited.  That was freakin cool.  I felt damn \r\ngood.</tt>\r\n\r\n',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5705,1374,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<tt> yes, i like to drive people to reality-check \r\nepiphanies sometimes... baaad.  sometimes i hate letting \r\nuncomfortable situations persist, so i just jump in and \r\ndeal straight, with little regard to the outcome, just that \r\nthe situation is immediately remidied- sometimes it pisses \r\npeople off but its better than languishing in an \r\nuncomfortable situation</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5706,1376,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>\r\n<tt> i grew up in tennessee, and therefore perk up \r\neverytime i hear the word...</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5707,1374,'2001-07-19 12:06:47',0,'slm','<i>ad hominem</i> attacks are not always wise.',0,0,0,0,'206.40.244.66','en'),(5708,1374,'2001-07-19 13:04:59',0,'lou','hey.  i loved that mailing list and it was my baby, and the \r\nattitude you think i had back then is mostly your \r\nimagination, and if you came at me without the four year \r\nold crankiness and the presumption that just because you \r\nwere on the mailing list and are old school it means i \r\nshould take you seriously even if you have nothing to say, \r\ni wouldn\\\'t talk to you as though you are four years old and \r\nsilly.',6,0,0,0,'165.247.53.42','en'),(5709,1371,'2001-07-19 13:23:40',0,'stella','If you\\\'re arguing on a daily basis with someone, then I \r\nwouldn\\\'t hesitate to say that you need some time away from \r\neach other. Soon. That\\\'s not supposed to be a part of any \r\nnormal relationship, loves or friends, or family for that \r\nmatter. ',0,0,0,0,'168.100.203.247','en'),(5710,1371,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','Wow.... if you just changed the year to 2000, I could have \r\nbeen the one writing this.<P>*warm hug*</P>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5711,1371,'2001-07-19 13:46:44',0,'puppy','actually, it depends on what kind of arguments.... if you \r\nare arguing about the same thing day in and day out, i\\\'d \r\nsay that there are some issues (you both probably need to \r\nlearn to listen and communicate better). but, if you really \r\naren\\\'t arguing *every* single day, then i\\\'d consider that \r\npretty normal. relationships where the participants *never* \r\nargue are the ones that are doomed....',2,0,0,0,'192.35.232.99','en'),(5712,1378,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>\r\n<tt> I like the way you put those feelings to text - the \r\nactual words you choose, the images they conjure.  thats \r\nuseful writing. glad the past 365 days have been \r\nbetter.</tt> ',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5713,1372,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','Coolest club going experience:<P>\r\nSimilar to Peter\\\'s, but I ended up being forced to dance in \r\nthe cage with a cute little goth chick and a couple gay men \r\nin their BVDs.  I also ended up getting offered a job as a \r\ngo-go dancer that night... The fullmoon can really excite \r\npeople\\\'s sexuality.</P>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5714,1372,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>\r\n<i>2nd Best Club Experience regarding self-\r\nconsciousness:</i>\r\n<br>\r\n<tt>Inhibitions finally dissolved and floating on a good \r\nemotional/group vibe, I somehow found myself dancing \r\nshirtless on the platform in front of the booth (which is \r\ninteresting for me, as I\\\'m usually more reserved in public \r\nvenues).  Anyways, as I\\\'m trancing out I manage to make eye \r\ncontact with the dj (who incidentally looked like dr. \r\nmingele to me at that moment, dissecting some poor track \r\nand pouring its soul, overflowing, into the next).  Looking \r\nup from the decks, lifting his fingers to point me out to \r\nthe other dj\\\'s/booth-groupies, he began to blow me kisses, \r\nshouting \\\"KEEP DANCING!\\\".  Coooool.  busted the door open \r\non my center chakra.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5715,1371,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>\r\n<tt>Ok, so which is more useful:  \\\"Time Apart\\\" \r\nor \\\"Meaningful Discussion to Repair Recurring Problems\\\"...?\r\n</tt> ',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5716,1370,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>\r\n<tt><i>incidence of \\\"i, me, my\\\", etc:</i><br>\r\n13<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<i>incidence of \\\"you\\\" or variations thereof:</i><br>\r\n3<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<i>my favorite \\\"s-words\\\" in this poem:</i><br>\r\nshroud, shelter, safe, see, secret. <br></tt> \r\n\r\n',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5717,1370,'2001-07-19 14:43:14',0,'thought','there are no other \\\"s-words\\\" mentioned....',3,0,0,0,'192.35.232.99','en'),(5718,1370,'2001-07-19 14:44:04',0,'thought','... besides \\\"shall\\\"',0,0,0,0,'192.35.232.99','en'),(5719,1373,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','Just to be a devil\\\'s advocate...<P>\r\nYou\\\'d prolly touch more lives in a positive way by being a \r\nteacher.  As far as groups that are getting the ass end in \r\nour society, I\\\'d have to say kids are it.  They have no \r\nvoice of their own in our political system, and various \r\ngroups seem to use children and schools as political \r\nweapons rather than really caring about the kids they \r\npropound to help.</P><P>\r\nI guess what really got me about school was all the \r\nteachers who didn\\\'t seem to give a fuck.  Here was a kid \r\nwho was obviously very intelligent but extremely \r\nuninterested.  Instead of having teachers who tried find \r\nways to excite me intellectually, I was either ignored or \r\nchastized for being lazy (even though I was getting A\\\'s and \r\nB\\\'s).  I probably would have done some cool stuff in school \r\nand not dropped out if I had only had a teacher who really \r\ninspired me.</P><P>\r\nYou should follow your heart and do what will make you \r\nhappy, but consider the difference you can make in a \r\nchild\\\'s life. ;)</P><P>\r\nThen again... lawyers have a much higher standard of \r\nliving...</P>',2,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5720,1370,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>\r\n<tt>precisely</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5721,1378,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','clearly a rollins fan',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(5722,1371,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','I\\\'d say \\\'time apart.\\\'  It gives you a chance to get away \r\nfrom the mind-games people in relationship tend to play \r\nwith eachother and figure out what you\\\'re really thinking \r\nand want.  Then with a more clear understanding of what\\\'s \r\nin your own head the \\\'Meaningful Discussion to Repair \r\nRecurring Problems\\\' will be much more productive.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5723,1376,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','<p>\r\nyou\'re lucky to even know me<br>\r\nyou\'re lucky to be alive<br>\r\nyou\'re lucky to be drinking here for free cos i\'m a sucker \r\nfor your lucky pretty eyes<br>',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(5724,1381,'2001-07-19 15:26:24',0,'puppy','i wrote <a href=\\\"http://www.puppyvaugn.org/2001/07/17.php\\\" \r\ntarget=\\\"_blank\\\">an entry</a> about this in my journal. \r\nwell, kinda about this...\r\n\r\n<p>i have been struggling with the idea of being \\\"forced\\\" \r\nto live in a society where we are \\\"expected\\\" to work 40 \r\nhour work weeks, etc., when i could be living as a hunter-\r\ngatherer and only have to \\\"work\\\" 6 hour days, three days a \r\nweek (that\\\'s right, they can meet all their basic needs by \r\nworking only 18-20 hours a week)....\r\n\r\n<p>but then i realized: i don\\\'t have to pursue all of my \r\ndreams *now*. there is a later. so, why not work a silly \r\njob, save up some money and retire early? then, i can do \r\nwhatever i want to do and with no regret! besides, hunter-\r\ngatherers don\\\'t have a very good retirement portfolio...',1,0,0,0,'192.35.232.99','en'),(5725,1377,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','I was talking to someone about the weather in Idaho when I \r\nwas suddenly struck with the smell of rotting leaves, the \r\nfeel of cold biting winds, and the sights of Halloween \r\ndecorations appearing on people\\\'s houses.  Yeah, autumn \r\nkicks ass.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5726,1353,'2001-07-19 15:38:13',0,'bark to egg','essentially',0,0,0,0,'12.110.65.49','en'),(5727,1373,'2001-07-19 15:44:00',0,'tyler to essemar','I know, that\\\'s why I wanted to be a teacher, but it\\\'s just \r\nnot practical in this day and age. As a guy, for one thing, \r\nthere\\\'s the very real chance of being accused of improper \r\nconduct, and the money\\\'s just not there. Also, at least \r\nthree-quarters of the kids aren\\\'t going to listen to me. I \r\nwas like you in school I think, I hated school, was bored, \r\netc. I wish I had had a teacher to inspire me, but that\\\'s \r\nwhat college professors are for. You turned out alright \r\ndidn\\\'t you?',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.228','en'),(5728,1381,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','yes! yes! that\\\'s what I\\\'m saying! money=freedom! it\\\'s not \r\nso bad if you\\\'re smart and can make a lot, then you can \r\nhunt and gather all you want.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.228','en'),(5729,1370,'2001-07-19 15:51:50',0,'chi chi','<p>\r\nso i\\\'m selfish and i like s-words. so what.',0,0,0,0,'64.165.201.89','en'),(5730,1373,'2001-07-19 15:53:35',0,'puppy','<p>a friend of mine is teaching at a high school out in \r\npennsylvania. he\\\'s teaching history and literature at an \r\nalternative school for \\\"bad-behavior\\\" kids. but it sounds \r\nreally cool. the owner of the school has a huge ranch \r\n(which the school is on), so part of the kids\\\' education is \r\nto go out and chop some wood or trail maintenance, or \r\nwhatever.... anyway, it got my juices flowing again to go \r\nback to school and maybe start teaching. i have always \r\nloved teaching.\r\n\r\n<p>before i moved to texas, i used to give drum lessons. i \r\nloved it. it was wonderful to be able to see my students be \r\nable to come in and then leave with a new excitement for \r\nmusic and usually with new skills to help them play better. \r\nwhen i moved down here to austin, i started coaching pop \r\nwarner football (for those who don\\\'t know what that is, it \r\nis like little league for football). that was great. i got \r\nto hang out with kids of so many different backgrounds and \r\nabilities... that was a lot of fun. i had to quit though. i \r\ndidn\\\'t want to, but i couldn\\\'t afford to get certified. i \r\nwas dead broke at the time, and i couldn\\\'t afford the $20 \r\nor whatever it was that was required to get certified to \r\nteach. oh, well.\r\n\r\n<p>i also have a few friends that went on to become \r\nlawyers... generally, the money they make is better than \r\nthat of a teacher. however, that sense of frustration, of \r\nnot making a difference, etc., is still prevelant. one \r\nperson i know became a lawyer to represent children in \r\ndivorces/abuse/orphans, etc., she left the lawyering \r\nprofession because she found out that she didn\\\'t make a \r\ndifference to the kids as a lawyer; she had more impact as \r\na social worker... now there\\\'s a good paying job...\r\n',1,0,0,0,'192.35.232.99','en'),(5731,1374,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','i SO enjoy fucking with assholes. it makes life just a \r\nlittle more worthwhile, but you have to be careful in \r\npicking which asshole with which to fuck.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.228','en'),(5732,1374,'2001-07-19 16:18:44',0,'ix to tyler','<p>\r\n<ignoring your possible double entendre>\r\n<p>\r\nbut at what point do you become an asshole yourself?\r\n<p>\r\nit\'s easy to set up a \"good guy vs asshole\" scenario but it \r\noften becomes hypocritical.\r\n<p>\r\ni find it more consistent and less dramatic to just publicly \r\nacknowledge that i\'m an asshole. then i don\'t have to\r\nto keep explaining my behavior!',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(5733,1374,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>\r\n...yes, you do have to be careful.  Yesterday, I saw a \r\npretentions corporate-bitch walking down broadway, gabbing \r\naway on her hands-free phone, arguing and flailing her \r\nhands, gesturing.  she was taking up like 70% of the \r\nsidewalk, whic is very impolite to do during rush hour to \r\nthe express train on one of manhattan\\\'s busiest \r\nintersections.  So, I have her a hearty, sarcastic, \r\ndroning \\\"Excuuuuuussseeeee MEEEEEEEE PLEASE!\\\"...\r\n<br><br>\r\n...to which she absolutely freaked and started trying to \r\npummel me.  Turns out she was crazy and was talking to \r\nherself (see how i always give people the benefit of the \r\ndoubt on the first impression?).  thankfully some garbage \r\nman intervened and kept her from slicing me from behind, \r\nha.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5734,1372,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','i\\\'ve never had a good time at ye olde buttstick',3,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(5735,1369,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon to egg','shut up, you\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(5736,1382,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://members.aol.com/bluchipart/interviews/hick\r\ney.htm\\\">dave hickey</a> is from texas',0,0,0,0,'216.175.105.140','en'),(5737,1374,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','You gotta love New York.  Just the sheer random craziness; \r\nI\\\'ve got stories....<P>\r\nAnd those hands free cell phones just make stuff harder.  I \r\nwas taking a leak in a public restroom and the guy next to \r\nme <I>starts talking to his penis!!!</I>  I thought shit \r\nlike that only happened in movies.  Then I looked and \r\nnoticed he was talking on a cell phone.  You can\\\'t tell the \r\ncrazies from the yuppies.....',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5738,1381,'2001-07-19 17:46:23',0,'kat','<p>money isn\\\'t bad...but not at the expense of losing \r\nyourself. in all our struggle to have these \\\'things\\\' we \r\nthink we must have to survive or be succesful it\\\'s easy to \r\nforget that our soul needs to be fed.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>there is always time to follow your passions.</p>',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.150','en'),(5739,1370,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','\\\"shh\\\". that is the same hush noise as when you pat my \r\nhead and i cry like a teen.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.105.140','en'),(5740,1381,'2001-07-19 17:53:22',0,'puppy','to kat: exactly! but just because you save money, doesn\\\'t \r\nmean you are wanting to acquire things.... if you had a \r\nmillion dollars right now, would you acquire things or quit \r\nyour job and follow your dreams?\r\n\r\n<p>me? i\\\'d invest it, live off the interest and travel, or \r\ngo to school, play some music, etc.... maybe take a bad \r\npaying job (i.e., a teaching position as tyler posits) and \r\nmake a difference....',1,0,0,0,'192.35.232.99','en'),(5741,1374,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>\r\n<tt>essemar: no doubt... the only things i hate more than \r\nthe hands-free confusion are the nextel phones that allow \r\ntwo-way chatter, like a CB radio, complete with loud \r\nsquawking and beeping and having to hear both sides of the \r\nconversation... if i have one more bus ride that involves \r\nme sitting between a hands-free-er on one side and a nextel \r\nbabbler on the other side, i\\\'m gonna implode!.  I swear.  \r\nand all their conversations are always like \\\"whatchoo gonna \r\ndo today, baby? i\\\'m knockin\\\' offa work early today, baby, \r\ngonna get me some sushi\\\" or something in that vibe...\r\n</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5742,1382,'2001-07-19 18:58:59',0,'kat','i slept in and did not go to the surf thing. i missed it, \r\nbut i didnt miss it. i was still hungover from that dang \r\nmovie. we should have had some brain tonic.\r\n\r\n\r\n',4,0,0,0,'32.100.70.169','en'),(5743,1381,'2001-07-19 19:22:10',0,'kat','<p>all i\\\'m saying is that there should be balance.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>i see too many of my friends come home tired and cranky. \r\nthey have no energy to do much because they are working \r\nhard to get what they think they should have so they can \r\nplay later....but you know, that\\\'s no guarantee that you \r\nwill ever feel like you have enough to cut loose and play. \r\nit\\\'s no guarantee that later you\\\'ll have time or space to \r\ndo the dream thing.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>i do not have a million dollars and i still aquire \r\nthings. ...and i never really did have the \\\'job\\\' to quit \r\nbecause the only choice for me was to follow my dreams. i\\\'m \r\nnot always comfortable with my bank account levels, but \r\ni\\\'ve tried the other path and it suffocates me. so i do \r\nwhat i do to make myself happy.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>[there is more to wealth than money]</p>',3,0,0,0,'32.100.70.169','en'),(5744,1382,'2001-07-19 19:23:05',0,'Phoofe:','brain tonic?!',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5745,1382,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','dave hickey wrote one of my favorite books ever, \"air \r\nguitar\". it just happens incidentally that it\'s writing about art. there\'s stuff \r\nabout his hippie childhood, and about jazz and about his \r\nfather, mixed in with some really startlingly good stuff about art history. recommended. ',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(5746,1382,'2001-07-19 19:30:43',0,'brain','<p><a href=\\\"http://www.africola.de/\\\">mmm...so good, so \r\nyummy, so peppy.</a></p>',1,0,0,0,'32.100.70.169','en'),(5747,1382,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','me and dave are becoming good friends.  we work on hot rods\r\ntogether.',1,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(5748,1374,'2001-07-19 19:50:39',0,'jo','hi.<BR>\r\nanna is a really good friend of mine.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(5749,1374,'2001-07-19 19:52:10',0,'jo','wherein joanna learns that she should read the comments to \r\nposts before she posts her own comment because obviously \r\nanna rushed in and defended herself. like the fucking \r\nrockstar girl that she is. hi anna banana.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(5750,1381,'2001-07-19 20:13:35',0,'puppy','i completely agree with you kat. don\\\'t let money run your \r\nlife; in fact, what i am saying is make the money work for \r\nyou....\r\n\r\n<p>if i was 20 again, this is what i would do:<br>\r\nsave $35/week, which is about $1840/year. assuming a 10% \r\nreturn on my money (the s&p index has done better than \r\nthat, historically), i\\\'ll have saved $500,000 by the time i \r\nam 55 years old. a male born in 1981 is predicted to live \r\nto about 78 years old. that means i\\\'ll have another 23 \r\nyears to live, and i can do so on a \\\"salary\\\" of $50,000 per \r\nyear (by living off of the interest).\r\n\r\n<p>and that\\\'s by saving an average of $35/week. there might \r\nbe times in my life where i can afford to save more than \r\nthat.... i have come to the conclusion that if i have a job \r\nthat let\\\'s me save at least $35/week, no matter how silly a \r\njob it might be, i am succeeding. soon (relative term), i \r\nwill be free of a job, and i won\\\'t have to succumb to the \r\nwhims and follies of holding down a day job....\r\n\r\n<p>that\\\'s all i am saying.... you don\\\'t have to lose \r\nyourself in the hunt for money, in fact, you can make it \r\nwork for you and liberate yourself entirely!!!!',2,0,0,0,'192.35.232.99','en'),(5751,1377,'2001-07-19 20:31:38',0,'green','hey essemar when you gonna call me?\r\nhuh....you Nuuu Yorkahh.\r\nhmmmmm.?\r\n\r\nI love Halloween\r\nbest holiday\r\nbest day\r\ndrink so much\r\n',1,0,0,0,'138.23.189.113','en'),(5752,1372,'2001-07-19 20:42:48',0,'green','the best is when you dance great in non-club situations...\r\nbut i agree with the \\\"shoppe\\\" and \\\"k\\\" dislike.',1,0,0,0,'138.23.189.113','en'),(5753,1374,'2001-07-19 21:20:40',0,'jo','okay so. having said that. there are definitely a few (i \r\nmean a few. two or three.) people online with whom i do not \r\nget along and who\\\'ve, in the past, treated me like shit in \r\nsome way. and no, i don\\\'t have the urge to contact them. i \r\ndon\\\'t call up the kids i went to middle school with and \r\nsay, \\\"nyah nyah,\\\" either, i just don\\\'t see the point. and \r\nthat\\\'s what that type of behavior is likened to, in my \r\nmind. i realize that people use the internet to keep tabs \r\non their enemies, but why would you continue to reintroduce \r\nthat type of negativity in your life when you could be \r\nusing that time to chat with friends? or to go outside? or \r\nread a book? it just seems like a waste, to me.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(5754,1378,'2001-07-19 21:40:19',0,'stella','Actually, I\\\'m not really a Rollins fan. I can\\\'t say that \r\nI\\\'ve ever heard any songs/writings from Rollins. Although, I \r\ndid once hear a brief interview with him. That, I did like.',0,0,0,0,'168.100.203.247','en'),(5755,1374,'2001-07-19 22:15:54',0,'lou','hi, jo. i adore you. (i adore you, too, slm, but you knew \r\nthat.)  \r\n\r\nalso, i agree with you. because, hello, what is the point?  \r\nkeeping tabs on people is one thing, but deliberately going \r\nout of your way to make sure they know you\\\'re a big baby \r\nwith nothing better to do is another. \r\n\r\nit\\\'s all about keeping it on the downlow, yo.',6,0,0,0,'165.247.53.42','en'),(5756,1370,'2001-07-19 22:40:35',0,'chi chi','did i really shhhhush you? i thought i just let you soak \r\nmy shoulder with your angst ridden tears.',0,0,0,0,'64.165.201.89','en'),(5757,1381,'2001-07-19 22:52:00',0,'jo','i really need to get into the habit of saving 10% of my \r\npaycheck.<BR>\r\nbut i should probably wait until i have a little more money \r\nor i would just dip into that account every two weeks.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(5758,1382,'2001-07-19 23:02:04',0,'patsy clown','<a href=\\\"http://www.iskip.com/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">skip to me \r\nlu skip to me la</a> ',1,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(5759,1381,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','<p>in this day and age there is no excuse to be not doing \r\nwhat you want to be doing.</p>',4,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(5760,1382,'2001-07-20 00:48:10',0,'kat','i saw some girl skipping across the street the other day. i \r\nthought she looked pretty stupid. the smile on her face was \r\nway too big...like one of those pageant debs. gross.',6,0,0,0,'32.102.64.31','en'),(5761,1374,'2001-07-20 01:47:47',0,'kat','<p>unresolved issues are unresolved issues. like \r\ncancer...they can eat away at you. maybe the wounds here go \r\ndeeper than you think. maybe what it takes to get over that \r\nis to simply acknowledge it. ask for an apology. it is the \r\nasking that is important, not the getting. the other \r\npossibility is that the whole situation is simply a \r\nconstruct of something else that happened in the past. \r\nsomething you can\\\'t resolve openly because it is too far \r\ngone...so the repetition becomes the target for your angst. \r\ni\\\'ve found when something keeps nagging at me, it means i \r\nhave to step up to the plate and deal with it. don\\\'t pick \r\nat the wound...cauterize it. and maybe sometimes that means \r\nhaving to swallow your pride.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>even the nicest of folks need to kick themselves in the \r\nass once in awhile.</p>',3,0,0,0,'32.102.64.31','en'),(5762,1376,'2001-07-20 01:54:02',0,'kat','i have always thought of this place, my home...as rugged \r\nand raw. it is a place that wants you. but it is totally \r\nunforgiving.',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.31','en'),(5763,1376,'2001-07-20 02:04:57',0,'trouble','\\\'but don\\\'t you know i\\\'m very happy - you know me well, i\\\'m \r\neven happy......\\\'\r\n\r\ni\\\'m in tennessee and i\\\'m in hell but at least i have all my \r\nliz phair cd\\\'s goddammit.  c\\\'mon detroit, grab me by the \r\nballs and pull me back home.',4,0,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(5764,14,'2001-07-20 04:27:00',0,'dj1_luna','I didn\\\'t write this by the way. I don\\\'t know why it has my \r\nname.',6,0,0,0,'24.93.61.58','en'),(5765,1244,'2001-07-20 04:34:03',0,'kat','<p>some of this = stolen inspiration. i still want the road \r\nthough. always the road. vancouver for thanksgiving? or \r\nmexico?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>[destabilizing] i almost always choose this.</p>',4,0,0,0,'32.102.90.251','en'),(5766,992,'2001-07-20 04:41:36',0,'feelsgood','is that <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.actionlove.com/msg.htm\\\">cupping</a> ....or \r\n<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.devolution.com.au/templates/t3a/t3aservices\r\n.html\\\">cupping</a>?',1,0,0,0,'32.102.90.251','en'),(5767,1367,'2001-07-20 08:42:18',0,'GREEN MATE`','i got your message THANX\r\nyou have a good voice. both my friend and i agree\r\nvery planned wording though nonetheless\r\nyou dancing boy\r\nyou\r\ntalk to you over email\r\nYO',1,0,0,0,'152.163.197.68','en'),(5768,1382,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','smtzs. it feels so biblical.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5769,1381,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','the other day i said outloud, \"... and i\'m going to be 27 \r\nsoon\" - and i stopped dead in my tracks with disbelief. \r\nnot because 27 is such a big number, but because i \r\nhave been feeling time accelerate, for the first time, at a \r\npace that i can\'t keep up with anymore. my 20s have \r\nbeen a whirlwind, i can\'t even remember which year \r\nwas which. when i turned 21 i bought myself \r\nalcohol for the first time. since then it\'s been one big \r\nblur.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5770,1376,'2001-07-20 09:33:51',0,'ticks','Such good music, and so different from album everyone knew \r\nher for, back in the day. I was just thinking of that, \r\nolder, disc today - how funny. <br>\r\n<p><i>I bet, <br>\r\nYou\\\'ve long since passed <br>\r\nUnderstanding <br>\r\nWhat it takes to be satisfied...\r\n</i>\r\n',4,0,0,0,'206.97.79.187','en'),(5771,1374,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Veer Moll','<p>I usually ignore those I dislike strongly. I don\\\'t \r\nreally need to express my feelings to them; to consider \r\nthem at all, even to acknowledge that they exist, is an \r\ninsult to myself.</p>\r\n',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(5772,1377,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','<p>Autumn, autumn, it\\\'s my favorite season by far. It makes \r\nme moody and sentimental, sometimes it even makes me desire \r\ncompanionship and othersuch foolishness things. The onset \r\nof autumn also marks the Satritain new year, a time for \r\nwildness and innonence and violence and newness.</p>\r\n',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(5773,1372,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','Non-club situations... My best friend and I used to \r\nfantasize about beating eachother up with gallon milk jugs \r\nin the gorcery store.  We also used to push eachother \r\naround in the cart whilst shopping.<p>I like the \r\nwhole \\\"shoppe\\\" and \\\"k\\\" thing.  I think it\\\'s \\\'kewt\\\'.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5774,1383,'2001-07-20 15:19:04',0,'ghost','<p>shadowplay [\\\'sha-(\\\")dO-\\\'plA]</p>\r\n\r\n<p>1 : partial darkness or obscurity within a part of \r\nspace : 2 a : to engage in mischievous sport or \r\nrecreation : b : to have arcane sexual relations : 3 : an \r\namorphous reflected image : 4 : to move aimlessly about : \r\n5 : shelter from danger or observation : 6 : to take \r\nadvantage [playing on fears] : 7 : an imperfect and faint \r\nrepresentation : 8 : to move or operate in a lively, \r\nirregular, or intermittent manner [shapeshift] : 9 : \r\npervasive an