09',0,'chi chi','<br>yeah. us immigration/customs sucks. JFK is the \r\nworst. we stopped flying into there. when i used to fly \r\ninto <br>SEA-TAC from the middle east i would always \r\n\\\"cross that line\\\" (i personally couldn\\\'t see it) and the \r\nsame time \\\"that the light went on\\\" (what?! where, what \r\nlight?) to indicate that it was time for a \\\"random\\\" search.\r\nrandom search my ass. every time i flew in i had one. \r\nand i\\\'m us citizen. ',0,0,0,0,'64.168.23.72','en'),(5795,1386,'2001-07-21 18:12:13',0,'chi chi to le','<br> that only in tap water though, right?',0,0,0,0,'64.168.23.72','en'),(5796,1387,'2001-07-21 18:23:20',0,'feltchboy','i am thinking of a nice cool, dark and rainy place',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(5797,1387,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','we\\\'ve already started having kids. five of my friends are \r\nexpecting.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5798,1376,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to Alanna','<br>\r\n<tt>i grew up \\\'round \\\'bouts chattanooga.  (chattavegas to \r\nthe locals...).  ever heard of it?</tt>',3,0,0,0,'209.244.100.232','en'),(5799,1388,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','hm. i\\\'m a \\\"maybe\\\" person. i tend to go after other \r\nmaybes.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5800,1388,'2001-07-22 01:51:06',0,'jo','hey peter, when i come visit nyc, can we get coffee?',1,0,0,0,'172.173.148.120','en'),(5801,1386,'2001-07-22 04:53:14',0,'wb','if you were really paranoid you wouldn\\\'t be writing about \r\nit on this web site. \r\n\r\nyou could call the CIA and complain. ',0,0,0,0,'151.197.237.74','en'),(5802,1383,'2001-07-22 04:53:47',0,'wb','forlorn?',0,0,0,0,'151.197.237.74','en'),(5803,1387,'2001-07-22 07:21:59',0,'fetchy','tonight i ran into a one night lover<br>\r\ni never called her back<br>\r\nshe appologized for blowing me off<br>\r\ntold me that she wanted to see me more<br>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(5804,1386,'2001-07-22 07:47:16',0,'green','its a bitch \r\ni was in israel for a bit about a month ago. the mid east \r\nis not as bad as the media makes it out to be.\r\nhey, to them its a way of life.',2,0,0,0,'216.179.224.45','en'),(5805,1386,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','green. that is the most ignorant remark ive ever heard \r\nregarding the middle east. the situation in the occupied \r\nterritory, an area you probably wouldnt have been allowed \r\nnear if you tried, is serious. killing is not a way of life. \r\nstop thinking the world is us vs. them and maybe you will \r\nunderstand that most of the conflict going on in the world \r\ntoday is a product of years of exploitation and severe \r\npoverty. \\\"they\\\" want the same things we want and have over \r\nhere in n.america. \r\n',5,0,0,0,'142.214.129.50','en'),(5806,1390,'2001-07-22 21:39:38',0,'tomato','street protests don\\\'t do much.  protesters instigate the \r\npigs, the pigs instigate the protesters.  people die \r\noutside of the \\\"red zone\\\".  just a nuisance to the G8.<p>\r\nthe news corps. are owned by the other corps who have \r\nbought off the pigs and the politicos.<p>\r\nwhat we need is public education, the evil doers need \r\nto be exposed in a way that the normals will understand \r\nand not view as some leftist whiny protestor rant.  the \r\nprotestors should be wearing three piece suits and \r\ncarrying briefcases.<p>\r\nor you could just phone up your local pop star and have \r\nhim talk to putin and blair over some champagne on a \r\nluxury yacht.<p>\r\n<img \r\nsrc=\\\"http://www.sadtomato.org/images/bono.jpg\\\">',4,0,0,0,'209.86.2.144','en'),(5807,1390,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<a href=\\\"http://indymedia.org/\\\">the independent media \r\ncenter</a> has excellent coverage on such matters. \r\nplease tell your friends! don\\\'t fight the media, be the \r\nmedia.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5808,1390,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','What information is spreading to the masses? Nobody has \r\nsaid what the protesters are protesting against, at least \r\nin the mainstream press. You yourself say \\\"don\\\'t invest\\\", \r\nbut you don\\\'t say why, or make any arguments, etc. I don\\\'t \r\nsee what the big deal is.',2,0,0,0,'63.10.151.153','en'),(5809,1390,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','Well, yes, I see that they are protesting against \r\nglobalization, but why is globalization bad? It seems \r\ninevitable to me, as scarce resources are tapped and \r\ndistributed, that companies will become multinational. It \r\nultimately lowers costs, so what\\\'s the problem? Are you \r\ngoing to stop driving a car or wearing clothes? Food is \r\nharvested with machines, which burn oil and use rubber \r\ntires, and metal parts, otherwise bread would be $10 a loaf \r\netc. ',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.153','en'),(5810,1390,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p>there are numerous books written on the subject. i \r\nsuggest you read <a \r\nhref=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/15675\r\n11961/\">globalize this!</a> as a starting point. and \r\nbecause globalization will be one of the most important \r\ntopics of this century, it\'s best to start educating yourself \r\nnow.\r\n</p><p>\r\nglobal trade is not inherently bad; the protestors are \r\nfighting against <b>how</b> global trade has been \r\norganized. some major themes: (and i\'m going to paste \r\nheavily from email i\'ve posted elsewhere)\r\n</p><p>\r\nglobal trade organizations are never elected by the \r\ncitizens they supposedly represent. they are appointed \r\nby their cronies, and they represent major corporations. \r\nthese agencies meet behind closed doors\r\nand have the power, by treaty, to repeal laws of other \r\ncountries. what this means is, when you vote in \r\namerica, it\'s pointless: trade organizations now hold \r\nthe monopoly on political power.\r\n</p><p>\r\nwe\'re seeing the emergence of a one-world \r\ngovernment, blind to public input, that supports\r\nprofits before the rights of the individual, and before the\r\nsovereignty of nations. through global trade \r\norganizations, corporations have the power to sue other \r\ncountries, to remove any pesky human rights and \r\nenvironmental laws as they see fit, for the purpose of \r\nmaximizing profits.\r\n</p><p>\r\nsince globalization, the yardstick for laws has become, \r\nquite simply, \"is this law a barrier to global trade?\" this \r\nsounds innocent, until we see that child labor laws, \r\nenvironmental standards, pollution controls, building \r\ncodes for factory safety, etc are all considered to be \r\nbarriers to trade. this gives, say, nike, the legal right to \r\nsue another country for complaining that too many of \r\ntheir 9 year old workers have had their fingers chopped \r\noff.\r\n</p><p>\r\nthe main objection by the protestors is not global trade, \r\nbut the fact that citizens are specifically not invited to the \r\ntable. many groups have presented alternatives - plans \r\nbased on democracy and accountability - to the current \r\nstructures, but unfortunately, the discussions are \r\nclosed. \r\n</p><p>\r\nthe protestors are not against global trade. they are \r\nopposed to global trade as it exists today: a closed, \r\nundemocratic system, that directly touches every citizen \r\nof every nation.\r\n</p><p>\r\nthis is a really tough movement to follow. the problem \r\nhere is that globalization affects so many people in \r\ndifferent ways, that there\'s no single protest group with \r\na quick and easy soundbite. also it\'s still a young \r\nmovement. as it gains momentum and respect, i expect \r\na more unified front to emerge.\r\n</p><p>\r\nthis is a battle of public perception, as shaped by large \r\nmedia organizations, controlled by advertising dollars.  \r\nwhat you read in the paper and see on tv is unlikely to \r\nbe fair journalism. do you really think the president of \r\ntime-warner would allow a full-scale public awareness \r\nmedia campaign, that specifically targets their \r\nadvertisers? their first duty, remember, is always to the \r\nshareholders.\r\n</p><p>\r\nin summary, the problems with globalization are (1) it \r\neffectively dissolves the rights of all nations to govern \r\nthemselves, (2) the organizations (WTO, et al) are closed to public \r\ninput and accountability, (3) their policies directly \r\nthreaten human rights and environmental standards, \r\n(4) mass media coverage, faced with a conflict of \r\ninterest, has no ability to report on the real issues at \r\nhand, and (5) the anti-globalization movement itself has \r\nno concrete, unified public face at this time, and thus is \r\nseen as \"the radical leftists tossing bricks through \r\nwindows\" due to the coverage by corporate media.\r\n</p>',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5811,63,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','<p>dropping the kids off at the pool has got to be the \r\nabsolute tops, number one, all time best of show euphemism for a dump i have heard in all of my short pitiful lifetime.\r\n</p><p>\r\ni salute you, austin swinney. if you were here, i would \r\nthrow money at you.</p>',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(5812,1390,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','oh.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.34','en'),(5813,1391,'2001-07-23 03:52:25',0,'duncan','I like it.',3,0,0,0,'61.10.144.104','en'),(5814,1390,'2001-07-23 04:22:01',0,'wb','good points steve.\r\n<br><br>\r\na few things tho,\r\n<br><br>\r\n\"what this means is, when you vote in america, it\'s \r\npointless: trade organizations now hold the monopoly on \r\npolitical power.\"<br><br>\r\n\r\ni disagree. it is not pointless. its important to remember \r\nthat we do live in a \"representative\" democracy, which of \r\ncourse is based on electing people to represent the people. \r\nso the reason why \"the people\" aren\'t brought to the table \r\nat the G8 is because those are the leaders and the point of \r\nthe conference is its a conference for the leaders. <br><br>\r\n\r\nit is true that commercial interests have too much control \r\nand control in areas that the money gives them an unfair \r\nadvantage. but voting as a citizen is not pointless. part \r\nof the problem is not just those big evil corporations, \r\npart of the problem is in fact that american citizens are \r\nsomewhat satisfied with how things are and don\'t vote \r\nthemselves. <br><br>\r\n\r\nonce everyone is either too apathetic or too convinced \r\nthat \"the man\" runs everything anyway and that voting is \r\npointless, that\'s when all the bad stuff will come true.\r\n<br><br>\r\nlike i said that time at dinner, i dont think there is a \r\nconspiracy by the media to fuddle the reporting of these \r\nprotests, i think it is simply too complex to report in \r\nless than 30 seconds. and most americans aren\'t that \r\ninterested in this kind of news. americans do not \r\nunderstand globalization because they are concerned with \r\nwhat is on american television, american music, american \r\nmovies. i don\'t think you can blame the ignorance of \r\namericans about world news on the media or the corporations \r\nthat own them and make the media lame and awful. that\'s too \r\neasy. the media is most interested in making money, getting \r\nratings. above all. and time and time again people want to \r\nsee football stars in car chases, interns having sex, \r\nmurder mysteries, etc. etc. ',0,0,0,0,'151.197.234.220','en'),(5815,1390,'2001-07-23 04:51:30',0,'tomato','wb:  i agree more or less on the mainstream media as \r\nentertainment point, sensationalistic and spectacle, et \r\nal.  but what of the actual corporations and the power \r\nthey hold today?  isn\\\'t it a bit too much?<p>\r\n\r\nshouldn\\\'t there be a death penalty for corporations?<p>\r\n\r\nlike, oh exxon, you fucked up the alaska shoreline, you \r\nare dead now, your assets are for sale, bye-bye.<p>\r\n\r\nthey have constitutional rights, just like the rest of us.  \r\nmaybe they should be put to death like the rest of us \r\nare?',1,0,0,0,'165.247.200.241','en'),(5816,1390,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','thanks for the feedback wb. i agree that the word \r\n\\\"pointless\\\" doesn\\\'t convey the message i\\\'m trying to get \r\nacross. as far as the media conspiracy theory goes, \r\nthere have been a number of interviews with protest \r\norganizers that never make it past the editors. *shrug* \r\nbtw the death penalty sucks.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5817,1390,'2001-07-23 05:33:03',0,'tomato','to s5: \r\n\r\n<p>yeah the death penalty does suck.  but for corporate \r\nentities?<p>\r\nfor the human death penalty we should instigate a \r\nnational holiday:  execution day.  every form of \r\ncommunication (newspapers, mags, every tv channel, \r\nevery radio broadcast) should carry live, the executions \r\nof that year.<p>\r\ntwo possible outcomes: 1) the people will feel sick and \r\nsee it for what it is or 2) it will turn into some WWF \r\nmedia orgy and people will have parties on execution \r\nday, light off firecrackers, and drink budweiser out of \r\n40\\\'s.<p>\r\n\r\ndunno.',1,0,0,0,'165.247.200.241','en'),(5818,1390,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','never underestimate the american appetite for glorified \r\nguts and gore.',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5819,1386,'2001-07-23 06:35:12',0,'chi chi','<br>\r\nyeah, \\\"the situation\\\" over there is some serious shite. \r\nand every time i come back to the US after being in that \r\npart of the world (saudi arabia and egypt are as close \r\nas i want to be) i\\\'m constantly reminded at how, not \r\nmisinformed, but.. i guess malinformed the US media \r\nlikes to keep the public (yes, this is another conspiracy \r\ntheory).  <br>\r\nwhen i\\\'m over in egypt the only all english all the time \r\nchannels we have are CNN international, and BBC \r\nworld. and yes they are part of huge news-media \r\nconglomerates, but they tell it a bit more harshly. and \r\nthey are not always \\\"a palestinian suicide bomber killed \r\n9 isrealis today in another horrific act\\\" but more like \r\n\\\"tensions are mounting as isreali police forbid UN relief \r\nworkers into palestinian camps\\\"... i guess what i\\\'m \r\ntrying to say is that over there the news is more \r\nimpartial (but not completely so)... <br>\r\npersonally i tend to stop listening when the whole topic \r\ncomes up. it\\\'s too much for me. the conflict goes way \r\nback. but not forever. and it is not a muslim vs. jew thing \r\neither, something many americans (who have \r\nsucceeded in pestering me into discussion the issue) \r\ndo not realize. it is an arab vs. new isreali settler \r\nconflict. many arab (palestinian) jews have been forced \r\ninto relocation camps, or have been killed ( by isreali \r\npolice) in conflicts arising from resettling.<br>\r\nall anyone wants is to live in peace. to have a home. \r\nsecurity, a job. a life. a place where you can raise kids \r\nand not worry that they\\\'ll be killed in the cross fire.\r\n<br> growing up in saudi arbia i met a lot of \r\n\\\"palestinians.\\\" they were kids who considered \r\nthemselves palestinian and had immense palestine \r\npride even though they had never been there. many of \r\nthem were born outside palestine, and had never set \r\nfoot there. they were refugees. born and raised in \r\ncountries that did not give them nationalities, they were \r\ncitizen\\\'s of a non-extant nation.  many had family back \r\nthere. or they had. most could give you an upsettingly \r\nlong list of people they new who had died. to me it \r\nseemed hopeless. but to them that was all they had. \r\nhope for a time when they could go back to their \r\nhomeland. hope for a time when there would be a \r\nhome land.\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.160.46.205','en'),(5820,1388,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>\r\njo: definitely.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\ns5: admittedly, i might be a maybe person, too, but thats \r\nanother writing, for another day...',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5821,1393,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>\r\n<tt>\r\n\\\"Go screw a donkey with a nickel\\\"...\r\n</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5822,1384,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>\r\n<tt>tall women are cute.  go tall girls.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5823,1387,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>\r\n<tt>this made me feel good</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5824,1383,'2001-07-23 11:47:43',0,'kat','desperado in vitro. wanna take my breath away?',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.68','en'),(5825,1394,'2003-07-24 15:44:23',165,'joker','yesterday was one of those days or phat austin in the \r\nsummer.  yeah, yeah, it may be hot, but the day was filled \r\nwith outdoors, starting with disc golf at pease park where \r\nthe wizard of mauz and myself dueled exquisitely along the \r\ndensely wooded shores of shoal creek, shoal creek, that is \r\nto say, the creek of shoals.  then there was lots of \r\ncycling down to far west to spend time with mscreant and \r\ndalia and to feel the baby kick, the baby kicked, the baby \r\nKICKED ME which makes me giddy.  then there was more disc \r\ngolf, but this time at the less challenging but nicer, \r\nzilker park, where the wizard of mauz and i again dueled to \r\na standoff and then ended the long daylight hours with a \r\nfrigid dip in zilker springs.  this morning i am quite \r\nexhausted, slightly more sun-browned, sore all over my \r\nshoulders, and content to be.',1,0,0,0,'66.68.48.125','en'),(5826,1390,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','<p>Globlization, fine. Let\\\'s globalize. Sounds good. I\\\'m \r\ncontent to let the Important People do whatever they want. \r\nAll hail the Global Empire; if our shit-headed civilization \r\ndeserved anything better, these assholes would hang.</p>',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(5827,1393,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<br>I walked away from you,<br>\r\nand I didn\\\'t think you would follow.<br>\r\nYou never said the word, \\\'leave\\\'<br>\r\nbut actions speak louder than words.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nWhy did you follow?<br>\r\nJust to twist the knife?<br>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5828,1398,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','me too. let\\\'s go to bed now, mollmoll. it is morning, daytime. we \r\nneed our rest.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5829,1383,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','Hey Kat, I\\\'ve got a vacuum cleaner that really sucks!<P>\r\n[<I>Grinning wildly</I>]',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5830,1398,'2001-07-23 15:15:54',0,'zelig','enjoy modernity, you ain\\\'t leaving it.',4,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(5831,1394,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>\r\n<tt>i visited muir woods in 1986... thinking back, it makes \r\nsense why all my memories of the place include people \r\nwearing jams, pastel mesh tank-tops, OP gear and pink \r\nconverse all-stars with turquoise slouch-socks. yikes</tt>\r\n',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5832,1395,'2001-07-23 15:56:57',0,'leonard','looks like you\\\'ve seen the <b><a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.rcpsych.ac.uk/press/preleases/pr/pr_188.htm\r\n\\\">light</a></b>.',6,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(5833,1394,'2001-07-23 15:58:40',0,'leonard','in 9th grade our p.e. coach, mr. muir, would send us out \r\nonto the track to do laps while he was in his office \r\ngetting handjobs from the girls in 12th grade.',1,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(5834,78,'2001-07-23 16:00:24',0,'leonard','i\\\'m not sure what you\\\'re talking about.',1,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(5835,1388,'2001-07-23 16:08:50',0,'jo','good. you\\\'re neat.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(5836,621,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','Wow... beautiful, intense, sincere.  I just want to sit in \r\nthe cool night air with some beers, or maybe some Jager \r\nMeister, and listen to the stories and know all the details.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5837,1383,'2001-07-23 17:12:52',0,'ghost to ess','<p>hush now child...can\\\'t you see she\\\'s flirting with \r\nsomeone else?</p>',1,0,0,0,'32.102.90.20','en'),(5838,1398,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','now is the very best time to be alive ever.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.16','en'),(5839,1398,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<br>\r\nNew York City in the 80\\\'s.  Or a bohemian in Paris.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5840,1383,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<br>\r\n<I>[pouts and sulks away]',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5841,1374,'2001-07-23 20:06:08',0,'k','i would like to know what \\\"group project\\\" means.  the lzls \r\nthemselves were not REALLY a group project. i did them \r\nmostly by myself (people filled in and whatnot).  the things \r\nthat came about because of them were.  the different \r\nwebsites and stuff.  and no, it didn\\\'t last or work out.  \r\nwelcome to the lives of 15 year olds, ya know?\r\n\r\ni have also found it very helpful not to say things about \r\npeople or situations you don\\\'t know much ',0,0,0,0,'205.188.195.59','en'),(5842,1398,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','there isn\\\'t any yesterday or tomorrow; there\\\'s just the one \r\nBig Day chopped up into segments by sleep. and it\\\'s the \r\nbest day i\\\'ve ever known. if you don\\\'t like it, do \r\nsomething to change it. it\\\'s perfect either way.',1,0,0,0,'64.132.148.219','en'),(5843,1383,'2001-07-23 22:26:00',0,'kat','all i wanted was a ride on the motorcycle...*blushing*',1,0,0,0,'32.102.110.84','en'),(5844,1395,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter:','<br>\r\n<tt>actually its just cheap Lucky film... oversensitive to \r\ncolors in/near the red spectrum.  oh, and who\\\'s bright idea \r\nwas it to call seasonal affective disorder \\\"SAD\\\"?  was that \r\nsome attempt at humor? oh well. i\\\'m off to expose myself... \r\nto red/near red and white light.',3,0,0,0,'63.210.217.78','en'),(5845,1374,'2001-07-23 22:52:27',0,'slm to k','sometimes you say the right things and we ALL appreciate \r\nyou for it.',0,0,0,0,'206.40.244.67','en'),(5846,1400,'2001-07-24 00:01:14',0,'kat','<p>someone gave me moonshine once. homemade tennessee. in a \r\nmason jar filled with grapes. it burned in my chest. i \r\nthought it must be like drinking solar flares. or more true \r\nto reality...like having to swallow my pride.</p>\r\n',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.120','en'),(5847,1400,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','i drank moonshine a few weeks ago. i liked it.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(5848,1392,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','hey hi.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(5849,1402,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>a.) i realized last night that I am a sucker for art \r\nmagazines. there is just something about holding a \r\nsmooth chunk of visual treats on your lap. matter!</p>\r\n<p>b.) i realized that last night that for now i am over \r\nsmoking. i dont feel that desire anymore. my friend \r\nmargaret invented the word \\\"duvel\\\" to mean \\\"the feeling \r\nyou get when you see someone you once loved, but no \r\nlonger love.\\\" that is me, with smoking, today. duvel.',0,0,0,0,'209.86.7.60','en'),(5850,1394,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>\"this is like one of my top ten good times.<br>\r\ngirls burst into snorting laughter.<br>\r\n\"you are joking.\"<br>\r\n\"no...i am at the ocean and there is a nice foggy light \r\nabove it and i have a human blanket across me...\"<br>\r\nsnorting miss piggys on the beach hoot with doubt. \r\nbeached baby seals are not sarcastic i suppose.<p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'209.86.7.60','en'),(5851,1402,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','<p>\r\ni am addicted to magazines. i can\\\'t help it.\r\n</p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(5852,1374,'2001-07-24 01:02:38',0,'lou to slm & jo & k:','and i love my friends. so much. like unbelievably!  there \r\nare some people who rock my world so much that i find it \r\ntough to understand why other people exist.',6,0,0,0,'165.247.53.42','en'),(5853,1404,'2001-07-24 01:35:35',0,'kat','my dog and i are so alike. wriggling our asses at those who \r\ncatch our eye. giving big \\\'pet me\\\' eyes. we do not bite or \r\nscreech. we simply lick you to do death with bouncy languid \r\nexuberance. a paradox of passion. we luv you long time.',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.120','en'),(5854,1404,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','in half an hour i get to go home and sit on the throne.  i \r\ncan\\\'t wait.',0,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(5855,1402,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','is that tonka shovelling bush?',0,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(5856,1404,'2001-07-24 01:46:47',0,'stella','\\\"shits in an unauthorized location\\\" is my favorite phrase \r\ntoday. ',0,0,0,0,'168.100.203.247','en'),(5857,1387,'2001-07-24 03:46:25',0,'Rude','yes, yes - it\\\'s all so incestuous.  or perhaps we\\\'re just \r\nlacking in creativity.  ',1,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(5858,1404,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','<BR>\r\n<I>\\\"so wonderfully, wonderfully, wonderfully, wonderfully \r\npretty\\\"</I><BR>\r\n\r\nI\\\'ve never had a pet. I really want to be a cat\\\'s friend.',0,0,0,0,'203.96.108.242','en'),(5859,1404,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i have secret affection for fernando.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5860,1402,'2002-04-12 05:27:03',57,'weeb zu adamajah','it sure is.',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(5861,1404,'2001-07-24 04:51:03',0,'chi chi','<br>i have great love for fernando.<br>\r\ni\\\'m begining to fear that he might be my soul mate; and \r\nthat in a previous life he did something that caused him \r\nto come back as a poor cat living with people who \r\novertly and subvertly mock him.<br>\r\nwe have great understanding. i leave him alone, and he \r\nleaves me alone. or we meowl at each other and run \r\naway.',0,0,0,0,'64.165.201.247','en'),(5862,1394,'2001-07-24 05:11:25',0,'chi chi (goat)','<br>\r\n<i>you</i> found muir woods? i believe egg, our \r\nfearless leader, knew where it was all along. i had faith \r\nin her ability to lead us to the tops of the world to find \r\nthe redwoods nestled in the valley. <br>\r\nas i recall you were sorta poopy up there on echo ridge.',0,0,0,0,'64.165.201.247','en'),(5863,1404,'2001-07-24 05:19:15',0,'justino','kitty been done wrong it seems like - he\\\'s seen his mama \r\nmade into strings on a tennis racket, then he was carried \r\nover molten lava on that racket, holding all his pain \r\ninside of him and keeping it cool, fernando sez i will \r\nmaster this\r\n\r\nand meanwhile he\\\'s come back awake this morning in a giant \r\nloft filled with screeching weirdos and they give love in \r\nfits and starts and he\\\'s got to get food in his gut, \r\nbecause maybe, he thinks, maybe there\\\'s some security in \r\nfattening myself up.  then i can be like mama, and even if \r\nthey take me away, i\\\'ll still be remembered for my soft \r\ntummy.\r\n\r\nthe question remaining for his human compatriots - how does \r\nfernando measure familiarity?  to be on living terms with \r\nhim is usually a fingersniff and then a near-brush; he\\\'s a \r\nmaster of distance flirtation; like a gliding dancer on a \r\ndancefloor populated by swinging singles, he drifts by with \r\na calculated casual expression and brushes on your body \r\nwith a hint of seduction and moves on.  a tragic cat.',4,0,0,0,'216.27.176.53','en'),(5864,1400,'2001-07-24 05:24:00',0,'BrewGuru99','It\\\'s not hard to swallow. Just find your place in the \r\nworld, decide what is important, and turn it all into blcak \r\nand white.',0,0,0,0,'64.20.45.200','en'),(5865,1405,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','The day I learned that Santa wasn\\\'t real, I also began \r\ndiscomforting questions to my mom about God. No one has \r\nsatisfactorily answered them yet.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.107','en'),(5866,1404,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to \\\"justino\\\"','what is this, stream of consciousness improv karaoke \r\nhour??',0,0,0,0,'216.175.93.188','en'),(5867,1404,'2001-07-24 05:56:22',0,'ghost','<p>it takes one to know one...doesnt it?</p>',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.29','en'),(5868,1404,'2001-07-24 06:06:32',0,'fernandez','<FONT SIZE=\\\"+2\\\"><i>jou peoples doan know sheet abouts me, \r\nmangz.  not sheet!  jou piece off up dee goddamn fucking \r\nriver mangs. FUCK JUSE ALL!</i></FONT>\r\n',6,0,0,0,'64.174.154.159','en'),(5869,1404,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to ghost','touch&eacute;',0,0,0,0,'216.175.93.188','en'),(5870,1400,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','brown = error condition',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5871,1388,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i always think of it like this- it\\\'s easy to be \r\nmiserable, but being happier is tougher, cooler, and much \r\nneater.  life is just plain miserable sometimes, but its \r\nour efforts to sort things out, to make sense about it, to \r\nenjoy it that makes us neat.  thats why i admire so many \r\npeople on swinney.org... through all their different \r\nefforts and writings and thoughts, theyre so neat in so \r\nmany ways.<br>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5872,1402,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>too much packaging foreplay in this world is \r\nright... why do i find myself ordering things, only to find \r\nthat when they\\\'re delivered, the biggest thrill is seeing \r\nthat ups-boxed goodness sitting on my apartment step, \r\nwaiting to be ripped open?  more often than not, the vibe i \r\nget from recieving something is more powerful than the \r\nthing itself. is that weird?  ok, people, feed my fetish \r\nand send me fancily wrapped empty boxes.  i\\\'m a whore for \r\nmail.',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5873,1404,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>\r\n<tt>the kitty i live with rubs back and forth on my legs, \r\ndoign figure 8\\\'s, while I try to use the bathroom.  major \r\npet peeve.  if i dont aquiesce, she sits there and stares \r\nat me...</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5874,1407,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>nyc would be <i>far</i> more fun if there were, \r\nwithin a thousand mile radius of here, even a drop of acid \r\nto be consumed.  unfortunately, there\\\'s not. pffrt.<br><br>\r\ns5: i like reading you<br></tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5875,1400,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>\r\n<tt>growing up in tennessee, they used to make moonshine \r\nout of corn and giant, yellow-y muscadine grapes. strong \r\nstuff.  you could always tell who was makign it as you \r\ncould smell it from 100 feet away. </tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5876,1407,'2001-07-24 13:02:40',0,'tip','peter: i used to live in CT, well within your thousand mile \r\ncondition; take the train to Bridgeport or New Haven. \r\nYou\\\'ll find something.',1,0,0,0,'192.35.232.99','en'),(5877,1405,'2001-07-24 13:04:03',0,'will','Not one more Christmas apart.',1,0,0,0,'198.214.178.232','en'),(5878,1405,'2001-07-24 13:16:28',0,'deb','What are you talking about? Santa IS real. \r\nDoes love know what\\\'s real?',1,0,0,0,'64.12.102.22','en'),(5879,1401,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<I>love me...</I>\r\n<P>Hot summer nights, drinking cold beers -- <br>\r\nsmoking cigarettes.<br>\r\nSweat-moist skin sliding across skin.<br>\r\nCold showers to battle heat.<br>\r\nRumbling trains and roaring street noise<br>\r\nignored...<br>\r\nin the cacoon of our mutual infatuation.</P><P>\r\nEventually, bitterness got in the way, replaced the love.  \r\nThat\\\'s become the aftertaste she leaves in my mouth.  I \r\nneed a machette to cut through the weeds and find the sweet-\r\nsalt taste of her skin.</P><P>\r\nIf only I had abandonned the garden before the weeds over-\r\nran it.  Then I could have the memories of a perfect \r\nEden.</P>',2,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5880,1407,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','<p>I used to know a girl who would always find loads of \r\nstuff up in CT. And not just the staple crops of \r\npsychedelia -- really rare stuff that I\\\'d always been dying \r\nto get my hands on. What\\\'s the deal with that place?</p>',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(5881,1401,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>\r\n<tt>I still have the love.  Its the proverbial sharpening \r\nstone for my machette, the weed-killer, the fertilizer for \r\nmy garden which admittedly does require more tending than \r\nits worth, but is still beautiful in certain seasons, \r\nalthough some of the finer, rarer flora have died.  Trying \r\nto match it\\\'s current state to my beautiful memories can be \r\nan obsessive undertaking at times, ha.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5882,1407,'2001-07-24 13:44:59',0,'tip','there\\\'s nothing else to do in CT; really.',1,0,0,0,'192.35.232.99','en'),(5883,1407,'2001-07-24 13:46:49',0,'puppy','<i>s5: I like reading you.</i>\r\n\r\n<p>that sounds vaguely sexual....',0,0,0,0,'192.35.232.99','en'),(5884,1404,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<br>true story:\r\n<P>Tristan was planting some flowers in the garden.  Steph \r\nwas folding laundry in their bedroom when she noticed their \r\ncat having a bowel movement in the closet, so she ran out \r\nonto the balcony and screamed, <i>\\\"TRISTAN, HE\\\'S SHITTING \r\nIN THE CLOSET!!!\\\"</i> which the neighbors interpreted \r\nas...</P>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5885,1407,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','i think i enjoyed this article best of all. I like to read \r\nyou, s5!! I want to read you all night long!!',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.154','en'),(5886,1407,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to Puppy','<br>\r\n<tt>..yes, writing is sexy sometimes</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5887,1405,'2001-07-24 16:07:24',0,'Pandora','<gasp!> Deb! What are you doing here! Actually, now that \r\nyou mention it, I think Santa may live down the street.  My \r\nsister and I see him bicycling topless back and forth to \r\nthe gas station, picking himself up a case of Coors Light \r\nin a can every other day.  Guess he can\\\'t get enough of the \r\nice cold refreshment.',4,0,0,0,'168.215.102.189','en'),(5888,1407,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','Just make sure you wear your reading glasses.  I know it \r\nfeels better without them, but you know... safe reading and \r\nall.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5889,1409,'2001-07-24 17:43:55',0,'kat','<p>i dreamt the other day that i was the cook in a greasy \r\ndiner working the midnight shift. it was very surreal. i \r\nstill remember the feeling i had picking up an onion. \r\nholding it up to check how fresh it was. the sound of \r\ncutting it. wiping my hands across the apron i was wearing. \r\nit was all about the texture, the smell, the lighting.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>oh wait, let me correct something...i was the MALE \r\ncook.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>i often have dreams where i play a male role. sometimes \r\ni even meet myself in my dreams and give her/me the good \r\none.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>i like those kinds of dreams.</p>',1,0,0,0,'32.102.109.118','en'),(5890,1409,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','there are pictures all over the ground. if you just look at \r\nthe ground when youre walking around. youll have a \r\nwhole family album. I collected pictures from this one \r\nlady\\\'s life at more than one salvage yard. at the san \r\npablo junkyard they call her \\\"the famous lady\\\". she is a \r\nredhead, looks like ann margaret. I am a part of her \r\nchristmas, holiday, love life, and motherhood.\r\n<p> will you mark your wedding day on the swinney.org \r\n2002 calendar? \\\"passover\\\". \\\"vernal equinox\\\". \\\"full \r\nmoon\\\". \\\"leonard\\\'s wedding [another one bites the dust]\\\" \r\n</p>',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(5891,1409,'2001-07-24 18:52:56',0,'leonard to egg','before you learn to walk, before you learn to rock... you \r\nlearn to rollerskate.',6,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(5892,1409,'2001-07-24 19:16:33',0,'kat','<p>ahhhh. rollerskating.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>those days of darkened rooms with peaches n herb, topped \r\nby abba. mixed in with some lowdown kool & the gang. real \r\nrollerskating. red satin jackets and dove shorts. tube \r\nstocks with stripes pulled up to your knees. chewing on \r\ncandy cigarettes. kissing yourself and your friends just to \r\nsee who had the best lip gloss. feathered hair for both \r\nboys and girls. shooting the duck. gliding \r\nbackwards....trying to catch the eye of the new kid.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>yea, i remember those days. i even owned my own pair of \r\nrink approved skates. that was the shit.</p>',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.23','en'),(5893,1411,'2001-07-24 19:57:11',0,'leonard','when i was in paris, i went to a crematorium and walked \r\nalong the hallway, where the ashes were kept, and i was \r\nreading the names of the ashes. i came across the name: \r\nLeopold Fucker, and i thought, \\\"wow, he must have dropped \r\nhis seed all over the town.\\\" ',6,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(5894,1412,'2001-07-24 21:02:17',0,'chi chi','<br> i remember learning how to smoke on the roof of \r\nmy J/H. \r\n<br> i also remember i got teased about my \r\ndevil-spawn hair.\r\n<br> besides that i think i\\\'ve managed to block most of \r\nmy memories...',0,0,0,0,'64.165.201.247','en'),(5895,1411,'2001-07-24 21:04:19',0,'trouble','first \\\'dingleberry\\\' this morning and now \\\'fucktong\\\'... you \r\nare the dictionary of wonderful words for tuesday.  thank \r\nyou.',1,0,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(5896,1412,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','i first smoked with that girl amy on the roof of her parents\\\' \r\nhouse. marb reds. she wore a stretched out faded old bikini \r\nwith cherries, i think.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(5897,1412,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>your memory of what people were wearing is the \r\nclearest series of details that strings the story together. \r\nand its not about a superficial obsession with \r\nappearances as fashion-talk might seem to be \r\n(although it\\\'s that too), but a concrete expression of \r\nmemory. not \\\"i felt this\\\" but \\\"I saw this\\\". it is evidence \r\nthat you can locate with certainty on your personal \r\ntimeline.</p> <p> my favorite thing to wear in 5th grade \r\nwas a big red blazer. and my hair was feathered, and \r\nyes I had dangly earrings in primary colors, geometric \r\nshapes. also, my sister\\\'s orange leggings that when \r\nshe found in a ball on my floor would get me a charly \r\nhorse.</p> <p> today I am wearing a pink blazer that my \r\nmother would wear in the 80s. I mean, literally, it is my \r\nmother\\\'s pink blazer with shoulder pads. she would \r\nlean down to kiss me on her way out at night when the \r\nbabysitter came. the smell of wax, alcohol, and roses. \r\nlipstick, hairspray, and moisturizer. </p>',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(5898,1376,'2001-07-24 21:19:00',0,'Harley','\\\"She likes to have all events and people under as much \r\ncontrol as possible.\\\" This statement basically \r\noverlooks all of the growing that I have done in the past \r\n7 or 8 years.   But that\\\'s OK.\r\n\r\nAbout clinging to the passing clouds, ephemeral \r\nphenomena: there is some important difference \r\nbetween clinging and loving. \\\"He who kisses the joy as \r\nit flies lives in eternity\\\'s sunrise.\\\"\r\nI am not sarcastic enough.\r\nTomorrow I go to Tennessee, my eden and my land of \r\nthe dead, to cling to the dead, or to mourn them.',1,0,0,0,'216.175.93.188','en'),(5899,1412,'2001-07-24 21:23:39',0,'big chin','omigawd, i so forgot about the red jumpsuit!! i hope i \r\nwasn\\\'t the one that picked that out for you to wear!',2,0,0,0,'205.188.193.189','en'),(5900,1412,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','listen, chin, i dressed myself as far as i recall. and i was \r\nsmashing, really smashing, i tell you, miss frosted perm!\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(5901,1411,'2001-07-24 21:54:54',0,'jeff koons to egg','you have come to bring us things that make us happy. now, \r\nfack off.',6,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(5902,1407,'2001-07-24 22:10:51',0,'\\\'D\\\'','Yep. I was tripping. And who was fucking with whom, may I \r\nask?! giggle. ~loa',1,0,0,0,'216.103.75.148','en'),(5903,1407,'2001-07-24 22:27:13',0,'stella','Um, no offense Peter, but I\\\'m in NY and I can find acid very \r\neasily. ',0,0,0,0,'168.100.203.247','en'),(5904,1407,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','i\\\'m not even there and i bet i could find it! heehee\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(5905,1410,'2001-07-24 22:32:51',0,'slm to alanna','so why can you NOT just let it go, then?  i\\\'m confused.',0,0,0,0,'206.40.244.66','en'),(5906,1410,'2001-07-24 22:39:04',0,'lou to slm','why WOULD she let it go? she keeps harping on it and we \r\nkeep paying attention to her.  really, it\\\'s our fault. \r\nactually, it\\\'s my fault. i\\\'m such an internet vulture. \r\ndidn\\\'t you know? i would have thought it obvious. i just \r\nattack EVERYONE. randomly. for absolutely no reason at all!',6,0,0,0,'207.237.128.1','en'),(5907,1410,'2001-07-24 22:40:00',0,'dork','i think i\\\'m just confused about what this is all about here.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(5908,1410,'2001-07-24 22:45:43',0,'lou to slm again','also, five bucks says she wrote that email to herself.  or \r\nmaybe chrissy wrote it to her. i keep telling him that he \r\nneeds to work on his writing, but he keeps saying that i\\\'m \r\njust jealous that HE is wasting away while *I* eat the ziti.',6,0,0,0,'207.237.128.1','en'),(5909,1410,'2001-07-24 22:47:00',0,'lou to dork','this is about alanna pretending she\\\'s three years old \r\nagain, and that negative attention is good attention \r\nbecause at least it\\\'s attention!  but what can you do, \r\nexcept give her enough rope to hang herself with.  oh, the \r\ntrials and tribulations of being an internet vulture!',6,0,0,0,'207.237.128.1','en'),(5910,1410,'2001-07-24 22:50:17',0,'dork','woah boys and girls, let\\\'s be nice here.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(5911,1411,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','why are cheesy celebrities so attracted to my posts?',0,0,0,0,'216.175.93.188','en'),(5912,1410,'2001-07-24 22:52:47',0,'lou to dork','or not.  slander vexes me and always has.',6,0,0,0,'207.237.128.1','en'),(5913,1411,'2001-07-24 22:53:15',0,'mike kelley','i want to be egg\\\'s boyfriend\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(5914,1411,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','i want to go out with tim hawkinson. or austin swinney.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.93.188','en'),(5915,1411,'2001-07-24 22:54:34',0,'adrian piper','*steals egg\\\'s newspaper*\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(5916,1410,'2001-07-24 22:55:06',0,'slm to anna','chrissy can\\\'t help it.  he\\\'s spent his whole life running \r\nfrom the emptiness that haunts him.  (and also, trying to \r\nfuck the loneliness away.  oh chrissy.)',0,0,0,0,'206.40.244.66','en'),(5917,1411,'2001-07-24 22:55:24',0,'chris burden','shoot me, egg!\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(5918,1410,'2001-07-24 22:56:48',0,'lou to slm','i don\\\'t care who/what he fucks. i just wish he would eat \r\nsomething. and pull up his goddamn pants already. i mean, \r\ncome on. crack kills.',6,0,0,0,'207.237.128.1','en'),(5919,1411,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to chris burden','can i come and be your pupil? you can lock me up in a \r\nlocker baby.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.93.188','en'),(5920,1410,'2001-07-24 22:58:34',0,'slm','also, i did not mean anna.  no no.  who is this \r\nanna?<br><Br><Br>i meant lou.  of course i \r\ndid.<Br><Br><br><Br>(and ps, we all know that low-slung \r\npants are very emo-funk-industrial fusion.)',0,0,0,0,'206.40.244.66','en'),(5921,1411,'2001-07-24 22:58:58',0,'eva hesse','Im the hottest.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.93.188','en'),(5922,1411,'2001-07-24 23:00:38',0,'nancy holt','too bad rob\\\'s dead, we could threeway\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(5923,1410,'2001-07-24 23:01:40',0,'lou to slm','i have no idea who this anna person is.  you must be \r\nhallucinating things again. like that time you hallucinated \r\nthat our names were anna and stephanie and we were at a \r\nstabbing westward concert and chris hall was wearing low-\r\nslung red pants. HELLO. like that would EVER happen. \r\nstabbing westward is SO FAR AWAY from emo-industrial-funk-\r\npunk-indie-glam fusion that it\\\'s almost silly to even \r\nmention them in the same sentence.',6,0,0,0,'207.237.128.1','en'),(5924,1410,'2001-07-24 23:05:03',0,'slm','i do not think<Br>that i can top that.',0,0,0,0,'206.40.244.66','en'),(5925,1410,'2001-07-24 23:06:37',0,'lou to slm','you should at least try! at the very least. don\\\'t give up. \r\nyou can do it! put your back into it!  (hahahaha.  ice cube \r\nis SO my secret boyfriend. chrissy is just gonna have to \r\ntake the backseat here.)',6,0,0,0,'207.237.128.1','en'),(5926,1410,'2001-07-24 23:12:55',0,'slm','i think his heart may break in twain.  and we can\\\'t have \r\nthat.  no rending of the hearts, no beating of the breasts \r\n(ahaha), no melodramatic \r\npost-punk-indie-pop-glam-retro-deathmetal-prog-fusion love \r\nsongs for YOU.<br><Br><Br>for lest we forget, you are an \r\ninternet vulture.',0,0,0,0,'206.40.244.66','en'),(5927,1410,'2001-07-24 23:18:13',0,'lou to slm','but don\\\'t you understand? once i break his heart by \r\nchoosing the ever-so-talented ice cube over the ever-so-\r\ntalented chrissy, he can write more songs about drinking \r\nwine, taking baths, laying naked on the floor...and how can \r\nwe forget SURFING?!  oh yes, he is a man of many facets. \r\ndare i say almost....Renaissance man esque?  sans hyphen!',6,0,0,0,'207.237.128.1','en'),(5928,1410,'2001-07-24 23:24:19',0,'slm to lou','he has depth.  he\\\'s a very complicated rockstar.  he has to \r\nmake many choices in his life -- not only about \r\ngroupie-fucking, not only about which rocksluts to allow on \r\nthe spacious tourbus, oh NO!  his life is HARD -- he has to \r\nwork out how not to alienate his literate fans, he has to \r\ndeal with dumb asses at mcdonald\\\'s how FORGET TO GIVE HIM \r\nFORKS, i mean, can you even eat pancakes without forks?  \r\nwhat about sticky fingers?  the flies will follow you for \r\ndays!<Br><Br>he\\\'s complex.  oh yes.  he has to deal with \r\nmany artistic challenges.  such as tears rolling off his \r\nface and dying in the rain.',0,0,0,0,'206.40.244.66','en'),(5929,1410,'2001-07-24 23:31:26',0,'lou to slm','flies? flies?  no no. you\\\'ve got it all wrong. it\\\'s the \r\nFLYS that are after him, i tell you.  and once my dangerous \r\nblack and blue spikes get done with him, there will be no \r\nmore groupies trying to get on the tour bus. you\\\'ll see.  \r\n<P>\r\n(unfortunately, after that, every time i reach out i will \r\nfeel him pull away-ay-ay-ay-ay, but what can you do? he has \r\nto learn that i won\\\'t tolerate his negative attitude. he\\\'s \r\nbringing down the team. that\\\'s really why they cancelled \r\nthe rest of the tour. the guys didn\\\'t want chrissy to look \r\nbad to his oh-so-literate, jeff buckley-loving fans, \r\nthough, so they said it was because andy needed surgery. i \r\nknow the truth though.)',6,0,0,0,'207.237.128.1','en'),(5930,1410,'2001-07-25 00:06:23',0,'slm','john 8:32',0,0,0,0,'206.40.244.66','en'),(5931,1410,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','this smacks of someone else\\\'s drama\r\n',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5932,942,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','revisiting this article after a few months in the sticks i\r\nmust say that i just wish i had a nokia 7100 series signal\r\npickup on mine.  the signals in santa cruz area are really\r\ndifficult with the 6100s.  i have to climb a pine tree to\r\nget a signal.  whereas, snafu has a 7100 and though it is a\r\nflimsy joke, it picks up signal like it is in outer space.',3,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(5933,1415,'2001-07-25 00:37:31',0,'leonard','austin and i went to eat once and i covered and then he \r\nsaid i\\\'ll get you next time. then we went out like 3 times \r\nafter that and he \\\"forgot\\\" each time. then he moved up \r\nnorth. i feel so scammed.',2,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(5934,1415,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','mm whiteboy nipples.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5935,1416,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','you write really really well',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.206','en'),(5936,1415,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>I\\\"LL HAVE YOU SLUTS KNOW</P>\r\n<P>i gave snafu TWENTY DOLLARS on the way back to his car\r\nfor the movie ticket and the pizza.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>you will get your beers and sandwiches.</P>',5,0,0,0,'20