?',0,0,0,0,'206.40.244.66','en'),(5949,1410,'2001-07-25 02:58:37',0,'lou','drama. melodrama. oh, the octoroon! oh, tragedy! oh, \r\nkierkegaard. oh oh oh. new kids on the block! <!--oh, no \r\npatience.-->',6,0,0,0,'165.247.53.42','en'),(5950,1410,'2001-07-25 03:58:00',0,'slm','*hand*staple*forehead*<Br><Br><br>an A for effort, but the \r\nwhole piece just didn\\\'t come together.  three stars out of \r\nfive.',0,0,0,0,'206.40.244.66','en'),(5951,1410,'2001-07-25 04:05:06',0,'lou to slm','\r\nhey, it\\\'s the effort that counts.  don\\\'t i even get extra \r\ncredit for tying new kids on the block to kierkegaard!? i \r\nmean, come on--soren is EVERYONE\\\'S cover girl.  (oh oh oh \r\noh oh, oh oh oh.  come on. you can hear donny in your mind. \r\ndon\\\'t deny it! it\\\'s invasive! it\\\'s permeating the fibre of \r\nyour being, your very existence!  oh...but kierkegaard was \r\nalmost existential, wasn\\\'t he. so...it\\\'s permeating the \r\nfibre of what might be your being, if you thought it was!  \r\nbut what is was? what is thought? what is being? rock the \r\nhouse with der Angst! raise your hands in the air! \r\nrepresent! STEPthefuckUP, y\\\'all!)',6,0,0,0,'165.247.53.42','en'),(5952,1410,'2001-07-25 04:09:06',0,'donnie to lou','yo, girl. you smell like hibiscus. also, you spelled my \r\nname wrong. <!--hi, this is lou, and i cannot believe that \r\ni spelled his name wrong! i SUCK.-->',6,0,0,0,'165.247.53.42','en'),(5953,1410,'2001-07-25 04:16:14',0,'starchy to donnie','but can a name be spelled wrong when it\\\'s just letters that \r\nare the representations of sounds?<Br><br>what IS a \\\"name,\\\" \r\nanyway?  what is \\\"is\\\"?  what is \\\"what\\\"?<br><Br>what???  \r\nwhat?!',0,0,0,0,'206.40.244.66','en'),(5954,1410,'2001-07-25 04:17:03',0,'lou to donnie','man. i am so sorry. but you were never my favourite, and i \r\nalways called you dennis cheese, anyway.  it\\\'s just . . . \r\nit\\\'s just that you pale in comparison to joey joe.',6,0,0,0,'165.247.53.42','en'),(5955,1410,'2001-07-25 04:18:50',0,'donnie to starchy','man, your problem is that you watched too many commericals \r\nfor the 90210 dolls during Swans Crossing. <P>\\\"did you see \r\n90210 last night?\\\"<BR>\\\"did you see brandon at my locker \r\nthis morning?\\\"<BR>\\\"WHAT?\\\" \\\"WHAT?\\\" \\\"WHAT?\\\"',6,0,0,0,'165.247.53.42','en'),(5956,1410,'2001-07-25 04:29:07',0,'starchy to everyone','i don\\\'t know WHAT you\\\'re talking about.  i would never watch \r\nSwan\\\'s Crossing.  that\\\'s so plebeian.  and as we all know, i \r\nam an intellectual.',0,0,0,0,'206.40.244.66','en'),(5957,1407,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','im getting more of a routine. im coming around to the \r\nidea behind your hair. Ive always thought you looked \r\nwashed out and albino, a cyborg of a young man with \r\nno blood. but then the other night at covered wagon I \r\nfiggered out that you are meant to be seen in the dark, \r\nlit by contrasty hellfire (that would be the Mac shade if \r\nyou could purchase lighting gels as cosmetics). you \r\nare an evil pilgrim/prince of darkness/bloodsucker. but \r\none on tv or a music video, not in real life. hubba hubba \r\n*eats knuckles*',0,0,0,0,'216.175.89.89','en'),(5958,1376,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to harley','wow, i do forget how long it has been. I am secretly an \r\nathlete and you are secretly a drug addict!',0,0,0,0,'216.175.89.89','en'),(5959,1416,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to essemar','if you bring the coke, you can snort it off my tits.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.89.89','en'),(5960,1410,'2001-07-25 05:02:39',0,'jo','holy shit. hi.<BR>\r\nis anyone else getting the wayne\\\'s world, \\\"i always just \r\nwanted to open a door to a room where a bunch of ninjas \r\nwere training,\\\" kind of feeling?<BR>\r\num. hi.',1,0,0,0,'172.144.131.231','en'),(5961,1415,'2001-07-25 05:05:09',0,'jo','austin leans really nicely.<BR>\r\nhe\\\'s, like, the best leaner i know.',1,0,0,0,'172.144.131.231','en'),(5962,1410,'2001-07-25 05:21:03',0,'jo','<a href=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?\r\nid=1223.txt\\\">DNR</a>.',1,0,0,0,'172.144.131.231','en'),(5963,1406,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','*salvation',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.126','en'),(5964,1406,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','i\\\'m not liking this. it feels rushed. anybody else?',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.126','en'),(5965,1406,'2001-07-25 05:31:01',0,'chi chi','<br>yeah, it just skimmed over his emotion... in part1 \r\nyou got more into what the guy was feeling... and \r\neverything happened is jumps',2,0,0,0,'64.165.201.247','en'),(5966,1412,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','<p>In 5th grade or maybe 6th grade I started wore black \r\ncargo pants, boots and these featureless black long-sleeved \r\nshirts. This is all I wore and I had many pairs of \r\neverything. They were the only clothes I had. My hair was \r\nalmost shaved on one side and long on the other, covering \r\nhalf of my face. This uniform lasted for several years. I \r\nhad no friends and barely spoke to anyone, I was only \r\ninterested in ice sculpting and astronomy. It was unreal \r\nand awkward, but one of the happiest times of my life.</p>',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(5967,92,'2001-07-25 08:51:15',0,'sean','you should <a href=\\\"http://www.mydojo.com\\\">practice \r\ntraditional karate</a> @ rod sanford\\\'s place in santa cruz.',1,0,0,0,'204.210.6.65','en'),(5968,1420,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','Who is lou?',1,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(5969,1410,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','<p>You will all be destroyed.</p>',5,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(5970,1410,'2001-07-25 09:35:16',0,'sierra','lou/anna/agro internet vulture/whoever the hell you are ::\r\n\r\nFor the record, I wrote that email to alanna and yes you were \r\na complete asshole to me many eons ago. I let bygones be \r\nbygones since you weren\\\'t worth wasting my time arguing about \r\nyour intellectual inferiority issues. However, since the \r\nsludge has been brought up from the bottom of the pond, I \r\nthought I\\\'d take one last chance and sling some at you.\r\n\r\nBy the way, I firmly believe in karma sucka. What goes around \r\ncomes around. \r\n\r\nLou, you seem to be getting mighty worked up over this \r\nthread. You alright over there? Or just bored with no life?\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'64.81.56.250','en'),(5971,1417,'2001-07-25 09:59:13',0,'green','that was moving,honestly. saying you want to be a real boy, \r\nbut do not rest on the mirrors others can be. look at you, \r\nand let that suffice until that person in need of \r\nassistance comes your way',1,0,0,0,'198.81.17.48','en'),(5972,1410,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','shh.',5,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5973,1410,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<img src=\\\"http://gee.kz/peter/yc.jpg\\\">',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5974,1420,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt> readers making assumptions about what they read is \r\nnatural, don\\\'t you think?  i mean, when you pick up a book \r\nand read it, you form your own opinions, insights and \r\nassumptions, no?  I\\\'ve never seen a novel or paper or essay \r\nwith a disclaimer regarding humility, tact and the like... \r\njust a thought...</tt>\r\n\r\n',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5975,1417,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>being a life-preserver can be a real drain, so be \r\ncareful... some people life-preserve your own life right \r\nout of you. i really liked this read</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5976,1420,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','communication works just fine without faces and eyes. \r\nthere\\\'s subtext in every story.',5,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(5977,1413,'2001-07-25 11:28:56',0,'spudlee','i really liked reading this entry. i actually learnt \r\nsomething about you. that is all.\r\n\r\nemail me when you get a chance eh?\r\nleigh xo\r\n\r\nps. i accidently hit the enter button before i typed \r\nanything and i got this nasty little message: \r\nCommenting on this site is not like some other cultures. \r\nLess is not more. Please back up and try again.\r\n\r\nhow very snotty! (and terribly wanky. really. no one likes \r\na twat)',2,0,0,0,'63.12.1.86','en'),(5978,1413,'2001-07-25 11:29:49',0,'spudlee','and they dont even allow you to have line breaks. bugger.',2,0,0,0,'63.12.1.86','en'),(5979,1416,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i really identified with this piece... neat, \r\nessemar.  i want to treat you to a few drinks at the \r\nholland bar sometime.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5980,1410,'2001-07-25 11:51:00',0,'no','<img \r\nsrc=\\\"http://www.wannabesuperheroes.org/is/silly/mighty3foote\r\nr.jpg\\\"><Br><br>chrissy = chump.<br>we = having a good time, \r\ndon\\\'t you know.<Br>you = missing the joke.',0,0,0,0,'206.40.244.66','en'),(5981,1410,'2001-07-25 11:51:46',0,'or','is that chimp?',0,0,0,0,'206.40.244.66','en'),(5982,1420,'2001-07-25 12:09:48',0,'lou is','my best friend, and i love her.<Br><br><Br>and while, yes, \r\nthere\\\'s subtext to every story, think about how many people \r\nreally can be aware of it.  sometimes there\\\'s too much \r\nhistory to sum up and process so that other people can be \r\naware of the context to a given \r\nsituation.<Br><br><Br>[<i>constructive</i>]',0,0,0,0,'206.40.244.66','en'),(5983,1413,'2001-07-25 12:10:51',0,'deb','and they don\\\'t censor their comments nearly as much as \r\ntheir actual posts ;)  no personal offense, just \r\nobservation.  Well, King William the 2nd, another job well \r\ndone.  I was supposed to go to that base, as you know.  \r\nFortunately, I can just rely on you to fill me in on what I \r\nmissed!',2,0,0,0,'205.188.193.176','en'),(5984,1416,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<P>tyler: Thanks, I really appreciate that.  I\\\'ve \r\ndefinitely gotten better since coming here.  Being exposed \r\nto more styles, having practice, and letting go (i.e. not \r\nbeing graded).</P><P>\r\nkat: [<I>crosses eyes and sticks tongue out.</I>]</P><P>\r\negg: When I get to sf, <B>you\\\'re mine bitch!!!</B></P><P>\r\npeter: I will gladly aquiesce to your overtures.  In fact, \r\nsince I\\\'m feeling in a giddy mood this morning, I\\\'m going \r\nto be a freak like Green and post my phone number: 917/586-\r\n4483.</P><P>\r\nkat: [<I>while looking other way, spills beer down front of \r\nyour shirt; feels really bad about it; being drunk, removes \r\nown shirt and offers to trade</I>]<br><I>*derisive smile*',1,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5985,1410,'2001-07-25 13:23:00',0,'lou to sierra','actually, just bored at work all day.  that email seemed \r\nmighty worked up to me. are you sure you let it go?<P>also, \r\nnow i am sad, because i am almost completely positive that \r\nit had been chrissy who wrote that letter.  i think i am \r\ngoing to have to drown my sadness in...coffee. mmmmmcoffee.',6,0,0,0,'165.247.53.42','en'),(5986,1418,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<p>Yeah, I was the Crow one year at a Halloween party.  I \r\ngot really drunk.  My friend Abbass commented the next day \r\non the large number of people he saw who had black lipstick \r\nsmeared across their faces.  I have my moments (especially \r\nwhen I can add the Bradon Lee aura to my own), but most of \r\nthe time you wouldn\\\'t notice me.</P><P>\r\nSo, I didn\\\'t realize I needed a public reaching out.  \r\nUmm.... thanks.  I\\\'ll try calling more often.',1,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5987,1420,'2003-07-24 15:44:23',165,'joker','two thoughts:<br>\r\nwords don\\\'t mean, people mean (which is to say, meaning is \r\nimputed by the reader, always)<br>\r\nwith all the potential meanings of the completely arbitrary \r\nsounds and symbols we collectively agree on and stamp with \r\nthe concept, \\\"language\\\", it\\\'s truly a wonder anyone ever \r\nunderstands anyone else',1,0,0,0,'66.68.48.125','en'),(5988,1418,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','yeah you seem pretty cool essemar. don\\\'t let it go to your \r\nhead.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.171','en'),(5989,1414,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<p>Mmmmm.... that\\\'s intense.  I grew up with my \r\ngrandparents which gave me a different sense of mortality \r\nand a morbid fear of growing old.  I remember visiting my \r\ngreat-grandma, first at her apartment, then at the \r\nretirement home, then the nursing home, and finally her \r\nfuneral.  I cried for days when my grandpa died.  Nowadays, \r\nevery time I call my grandma I hear about which of her \r\nfriends died last week.</p>...and the music plays on.',2,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(5990,1420,'2001-07-25 14:49:26',0,'John','<p>It is indeed natural to make assumptions while reading. \r\nThe difficulty I have is the failure to classify assumptions \r\nas such and instead regard them as established fact, with a \r\nconcomitant rush to judgement.</p>\r\n<p>Regarding human communication, I don\\\'t think there\\\'s any \r\nsubstitute for face-to-face communication. I will readily \r\nconcede that all communication is ultimately mind-to-mind, \r\nbut I continue to assert that humans rely heavily on \r\nmeta-communicative gesticulative signals when parsing \r\nmessages from one another, and these, while certainly not \r\nindispensible, are of enormous importance, and add critical \r\nvalue. Gregory Bateson, in his excellent compilation \\\'Steps \r\nto an Ecology of Mind\\\', was able to elucidate how \r\nschizophrenia was created in a child by repeated exposure to \r\ncommunication from the mother which contained contradictory \r\ncommunicative and meta-communicative data. That bespeaks the \r\nimportance of it, I would think. \r\n<p>At any rate, tact and sensitivity are indispensible, \r\nalong with a healthy dose of humor, particularly the ability \r\nto laugh at oneself. My lou is gaining in that all the time, \r\nand I am happy for her. I admire her honesty, but of course \r\nI do not always agree with her conclusions. At times I wish \r\nshe\\\'d be more tactful, because people apparently have gotten \r\nhurt. Sometimes it\\\'s necessary, but usually there\\\'s a better \r\nway.</p>\r\n<p>This is great. Greetings and respects to all.</p>\r\n<p>Love to my lou</p>',2,0,0,0,'207.99.41.217','en'),(5991,1420,'2001-07-25 15:11:08',0,'lou','tact is just not saying true stuff. i\\\'ll pass!  i\\\'ll take \r\ntwice the dose of humour, and three times of the ability to \r\nlaugh at oneself.<br><br>and, if it\\\'s available, i\\\'d also \r\nlike some coffee. :)<br><br>(also, i believe the phrases we \r\nare looking for here are these: <b>jumping to \r\nconclusions</b> and <b>ad hominem</b> !  i was pretty sure \r\ni had more to say, but i don\\\'t think so anymore.  except \r\nperhaps, that while i am a huge suppourter of the internet \r\nand all the various communication methods it provides, \r\nexperience has taught me that absolutely nothing compares \r\nto face-to-face and heart-to-heart.)',1,0,0,0,'207.237.128.1','en'),(5992,1420,'2001-07-25 15:12:17',0,'Lou','who the hell is john??',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(5993,1420,'2001-07-25 15:34:44',0,'lou','oh, i see.  how confusing. one of us is a capital L and one \r\nis a lowercase!  perhaps i should be 10u. that would be... \r\nk00l.',1,0,0,0,'207.237.128.1','en'),(5994,1415,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','wow this reminds me-- wasn\\\'t there supposed to be \r\nan \\\'austin swinney got a job\\\' dinner party where he takes \r\nout all his unemployed friends?? i totally forgot til now. \r\n<i>[best friendly/still waiting]</i>',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(5995,1416,'2001-07-25 16:04:18',0,'kat to ess','<p>\\\"thanks luv. so sweet of you to offer your clothes, but \r\ni don\\\'t think i could possibly wear anything that has \r\nBritney Spears face plastered all over it.\\\"</p>\r\n\r\n<p>[kat proceeds to win $500 in wet t-shirt contest now \r\nthat her previously hidden assets are revealed]</p>',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.197','en'),(5996,1415,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','well either sex or a conversation; ideally both.',0,0,0,0,'205.230.22.137','en'),(5997,1424,'2001-07-25 16:48:40',0,'jay','thank you for this. we all need reassurance that such a \r\nthing exists.',1,0,0,0,'63.203.225.62','en'),(5998,1424,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','word. does this mean le was a \\\"fat baby\\\".',0,0,0,0,'216.175.106.165','en'),(5999,1415,'2001-07-25 16:50:56',0,'kat to ix','i concur',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.197','en'),(6000,1414,'2001-07-25 16:53:37',0,'jay to chi chi:','this is a passionate piece of writing. and a good one. I \r\nguess death can bring that out in a person, even one as \r\nlevel-headed as you.',2,0,0,0,'63.203.225.62','en'),(6001,1415,'2001-07-25 16:55:11',0,'bmg','<p>i have spent the last year cleaning his room that he \r\nleft in shambles when making his move to california... i \r\nhad to peel a sock of the wall inside the closet and \r\nremove the snot under the desk that he left... no telling \r\nwhat else is under there... I have been collecting his \r\nmail in a huge plastic bag because he is unaware of \r\nhow to forward his mail... hey austin, did I ever send you \r\nyour tax return and your student loan statement?</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(6002,1412,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','i have a sneaking suspicion that \\\"assbutt\\\" is my little \r\nsister. what is this? old home week?\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(6003,1410,'2001-07-25 17:07:12',0,'dude, my board','<img\r\nsrc=\\\"http://www.mavsurfer.com/mavsurfer_00/editorial/image_photo/shark_photo2.jpg\\\">',4,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(6004,1415,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','remember when i took you and psycho-steph out for mexican \r\nwhen i got a job...?  well, i know of a nice restaurant in \r\ndowntown scruz.  *hint hint* ',2,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(6005,1416,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<P>That\\\'s alright.  You\\\'d probably want to keep the shirt \r\nanyway, so I wouldn\\\'t be able to cover up the N\\\'Sync boys \r\ntatooed on my chest.</P><P>\r\n[<I>Esse proceeds to jump onto the table and dance.  He \r\nfinds $500 the next day... stuffed into this pants.</i>]',1,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(6006,1420,'2001-07-25 17:31:55',0,'jo','hi john, you rock hardcore.<BR>\r\nyour daughter is a blessing. she regularly makes my life \r\nricher, more beautiful; she makes me laugh a hundred times \r\na day. i\\\'m hugely fond of her.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(6007,1425,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>Sam likes grey weather<br>\r\nGot up early for shower<br>\r\nSwinney before food.</p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'216.175.106.165','en'),(6008,1407,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','is fucking with tripping people bad juju? i guess it could \r\njust be harmless fun....',1,0,0,0,'64.132.148.219','en'),(6009,1416,'2001-07-25 17:45:12',0,'jo','</i></i>all these actions commands make me feel like i\\\'m on \r\nan IRC channel in high school.<BR>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(6010,1425,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<P>Yummy Hostess(tm) cake<br>\r\nI\\\'ve been losing lots of weight<br>\r\nIt evaporates</P>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(6011,1415,'2001-07-25 17:47:10',0,'jo to ix','oh ix. you have won my heart.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(6012,1407,'2001-07-25 17:49:58',0,'jo','i\\\'d like to give props to both s5 and rob brezsny, as they \r\nboth routinely rock my planets.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(6013,1420,'2001-07-25 17:57:36',0,'john','to jo: Thanks. She is a huge blessing and much more.\r\nto lou: (sigh)O dear, dear one, you have taken the same line \r\nsince you were 10, and even though it is not my intent to \r\nbore this convocation with our family quibbles, once again \r\nI will try to elucidate the difference between tact and \r\ninsincerity. \r\n\r\nAcc. to m-w, tact is \\\"skill and grace in dealing with \r\nothers. TACT implies delicate and considerate perception of \r\nwhat is appropriate <e.g. questions showing a lack of \r\ntact>.\\\" Please explain to me how this implies \\\'not saying \r\ntrue stuff\\\'.',2,0,0,0,'207.99.41.217','en'),(6014,1426,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','don\\\'t tell anybody but i think i might be a little in love \r\nwith egg\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(6015,1426,'2001-07-25 18:19:58',0,'jo','\\\"Im beginning to realize that one needs many different \r\nkinds of lovers.\\\"<BR>\r\nTESTIFY!<BR>\r\nyou are so smart!',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(6016,1420,'2001-07-25 18:27:52',0,'lou to john','either something IS appropriate, or something is NOT \r\nappropriate. if something is not appropriate, then couching \r\nit in pretty language is not going to change that--and vice \r\nversa.<br><br>if we want to talk about being able to \r\ndiscern what is appropriate and what is not appropriate, i \r\nthink that\\\'s more insight and common sense and a keen \r\nperception of the attitudes of those you\\\'re speaking to \r\nthan tact.<br><br>also, i would rather be blunt and plain-\r\nspeaking, and just say what is on my mind. and i think it \r\nwould save a lot of trouble if everyone else did that, \r\ntoo.  there is nothing wrong with being compassionate, and \r\nchoosing the right words so that people listen to the \r\nmessage and not the way it\\\'s delivered, but tact is usually \r\ntaken too far. i am anti-taking tact too far, to the point \r\nof dishonesty. etc.',1,0,0,0,'207.237.128.1','en'),(6017,1426,'2001-07-25 18:30:16',0,'preacher','<p>\r\ncan i get a WITNESS!?<br>\r\nooh baby, TESTIFY!<br>\r\n</p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(6018,1425,'2001-07-25 18:38:30',0,'chi chi','<br>\r\nit makes me tired.<br>\r\nall this gray weather we have.<br>\r\nwhen is it summer?',0,0,0,0,'64.165.201.247','en'),(6019,1425,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<PRE>\r\nhi request tracker,\r\ni am to install this thing.\r\nno one uses them\r\n</pre>',4,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(6020,1426,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<P>Sam sounds like my best friend Josh; he reminds me that \r\nI\\\'m a lazy sack of shit and also does the dishes at my \r\nhouse unprovoked.  Oh, and Simon, I think everyone is a \r\nlittle in love with egg.</P>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(6021,1425,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<P>Awake, one AM<br>\r\nBedsheets covered in my sweat<br>\r\nSauna-esque outside</P>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(6022,1414,'2001-07-25 19:06:15',0,'chi chi to jay','<br>\r\namazing, no? little chi chi can actually emote.\r\n\r\npassion in death.<br>\r\nthis was supposed to be  cathartic . perhaps deep \r\ndown the motivaters were level headed.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.165.201.247','en'),(6023,1407,'2001-07-25 19:09:42',0,'jack','names the planets after you\r\n<hr>\r\n<hr>\r\n<hr>\r\n<hr>\r\n<hr>\r\n<hr>\r\n<hr>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n',3,0,0,0,'64.152.168.65','en'),(6024,1420,'2001-07-25 19:12:13',0,'tactmaster','couching something in \\\"pretty language\\\" still says the same \r\nthing, imo. but allows for the person you are talking to to \r\nactually listen and perhaps think it over rather than \r\nautomatically getting defensive and freaked out.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(6025,1416,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<P>Hey, Peter, check out this review of the Holland Bar I \r\nfound on City search:</P><P>\r\n<I>\\\"I\\\'ve been in dive bars all over the city, and Holland \r\nis the only one I was scared to go into. The kind of place \r\nwhere everyone lined up at the bar turns around and stares \r\nat you as you walk in. And you know, deep down, you know \r\nthat you do not belong here.\\\"</P></I>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(6026,1420,'2001-07-25 19:35:24',0,'lou to tactmaster','hi, that was already stated.  \\\"there is nothing wrong with \r\nbeing compassionate, and choosing the right words so that \r\npeople listen to the message and not the way it\\\'s \r\ndelivered...\\\"<br><br>my issue is with the fact that \r\ngenerally speaking, in my experience, the pretty language \r\ntends to obscure the meaning rather than enhance it.  etc. \r\netc. etc.',6,0,0,0,'207.237.128.1','en'),(6027,1425,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,