:52',0,'Myself','\\\"Home is the place that when you go there, they have to take you in\\\" - Death of a Hired Man.\r\n\r\n\r\nI doubt I\\\'m best friendly. So I\\\'m checking nicely supportive. My ego extentions, however, range all over the the board.',2,0,0,0,'152.163.213.78','en'),(6066,1426,'2001-07-26 02:27:01',0,'yes sir','Amen, jo. ',1,0,0,0,'208.143.2.221','en'),(6067,1426,'2001-07-26 02:31:11',0,'ticks','tick to kat: Obsessed is bad. Obsession with anything tends \r\nto lead to fucking problems. Or problems fucking, pick as \r\nyou wish. <br><br> But some general concern can\\\'t be all \r\nthat bad, can it? ',0,0,0,0,'208.143.2.221','en'),(6068,1431,'2001-07-26 02:49:43',0,'romano','<BR>Austin: Why would you say that?  I swear that I don\\\'t \r\nunderstand some of the humor on this site.  If I met some of \r\nyou in person, I don\\\'t think I would like you: so I guess \r\nthis site is a good equivocator.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.17.71','en'),(6069,1420,'2001-07-26 03:04:38',0,'romano','<BR>One also runs the danger of making others think one is \r\nan asshole and not wanting much to do with one....\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.17.71','en'),(6070,1422,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>odd.  i just tonight finished reading \\\'crash\\\'... i \r\nwent and looked up this one (that i wrote sometime last \r\nyear) and posted it in honor of the moment.<br><br>\r\nsome people on swinney are psychic, i swear...<br><br>damn \r\nthe fates that its so hard to keep a car in nyc.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'64.152.171.209','en'),(6071,1431,'2001-07-26 03:38:20',0,'bmg','for the first two years of knowing austin, its been since \r\n91 or so, i thought he was the biggest asshole in the \r\nworld... i still think he is an asshole, but i don\\\'t like it \r\nwhen other people call him an asshole...i love him very \r\nmuch.',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(6072,1426,'2001-07-26 03:53:42',0,'kat','as i said...wanting to please ain\\\'t bad. *wink* ',1,0,0,0,'32.102.109.14','en'),(6073,1420,'2001-07-26 03:59:24',0,'mir','yeah, well, everyone\\\'s an asshole to someone.  once you get \r\nover wanting everyone to like you, it\\\'s a whole lot easier \r\nto live your life the way you feel it should be lived.  \r\nunfettered.  spiritually responsible.\r\n<br><br>\r\n(this above all: to thine ownself be true, and it must \r\nfollow, as the night the day, thou canst not then be false \r\nto any man.)',0,0,0,0,'206.40.244.66','en'),(6074,1429,'2001-07-26 04:07:25',0,'mir','am i the only one who thinks this poor girl needs to eat \r\nsomething?',0,0,0,0,'206.40.244.66','en'),(6075,1431,'2001-07-26 04:26:08',0,'leonard','austin is a fuckbag, but in a good way of course.',1,0,0,0,'209.179.132.97','en'),(6076,1431,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','actually, i laughed when i read what austin wrote, because \r\nthat fetus picture is pretty fucking scary. this is no way \r\nreflects on my sincere congratulations on your impending \r\ndaddyhood. (you\\\'re going to be one of those daddys that \r\ndoesn\\\'t shirk his half the work caring for the kid, right? \r\nbest friendly!)',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(6077,1434,'2001-07-26 05:11:33',0,'<p>joker','<font color=\\\"red\\\">and i saw in the turning so clearly<br>\r\na child\\\'s forgotten mornings<br>\r\nwhere he walked with his mother<br>\r\nthrough the parables of sunlight<br>\r\nand the the legends of the green chapels<br>\r\nand the twice-told fields of infancy<br>\r\nthat his tears burned my cheeks<br>\r\nand his heart moved in mine</font><br>\r\nd. thomas</p>',2,0,0,0,'66.68.48.125','en'),(6078,1431,'2001-07-26 05:21:17',0,'kat','<p>i have often joked with my bun in the oven friends about \r\nmy fear of \\\'alien\\\' baby. he lives in my tummy...ready to \r\ndestroy [this is a true phobia i have and comes up as my \r\nmain argument for the lack of children i\\\'ve given birth too \r\nas i hit those oh-so-tragic clock ticking \r\nyears].............oh, wait a minute. i think that\\\'s Austin \r\nliving in my tummy. i sure do love that boy\\\'s meatballs.</p>',1,0,0,0,'32.102.109.14','en'),(6079,1429,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','skinny girls #0',6,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(6080,1424,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','the phrase \\\"fat babies\\\" makes me feel vaguely sick.  like \r\nthey\\\'re dumplings on a skewer.  i don\\\'t like the thought of \r\nbabies.',3,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(6081,1428,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','green: Why do you say you don\\\'t envy people who have good \r\nrelationships with their parents?',3,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(6082,1429,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Veer Moll','bzzzzzztt I\\\'m with you on that one mir ... zzztt girl needs \r\nsome food or some muscle or something i don\\\'t know zttt over',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(6083,1430,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Veer Moll','<p>Dude, can I hang out with this kid? He sounds awesome. \r\nVery cool post,  btw, you have great style.</p>',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(6084,1431,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Veer Moll','Dude. That fetoid is in attack-mode. I swear.',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(6085,1429,'2001-07-26 11:40:40',0,'hh','someone has to love waifs. they need love too.',1,0,0,0,'24.28.73.144','en'),(6086,1424,'2001-07-26 13:46:46',0,'auntie','yes, elly was a fat baby, but not a dumpling.  she just was \r\nnot one of those skinny babies that look unhealthy.  breast \r\nfed babies are supposed to be pudgy, it\\\'s how you know all \r\nis well.  there is nothing sweeter than the back of a \r\nbaby\\\'s neck.  you kiss them there and they always make \r\nlovely baby noises and when they smile somewhere in the \r\nworld a bit of darkness recedes into light.',0,0,0,0,'24.162.119.106','en'),(6087,1420,'2001-07-26 14:11:29',0,'john to all','I am amazed that this produced so much interaction. Thanks \r\nto all. Some thoughts:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>To my dearest lou : as so often happens, we agree while \r\nseeming to disagree. You abhor falsehood, rightly, as do I. \r\nYou value discernment of appropriateness, as do I. There is \r\nno contention. Our differences, as often happens, are in the \r\nrealm of semantics. I love you :-)</li>\r\n<li>to mir : I have been a very enoumous sphincter to an \r\nunusually large number of people, but that had nothing to do \r\nwith being true to myself. It had more to do with my own \r\nstupidity. I agree wholeheartedly that to live responsibly \r\nmeans not people-pleasing. I would add, though, that to \r\nalienate people without good reason is not the best course \r\nto take. It is not for me to ridicule someone because they \r\ndon\\\'t see what I see.</li>\r\n<li>to tactmaster : Thanks for the commentary. I agree with \r\nyou, and the older I get the more I see the truth in \r\nit.</li>\r\n<li>to romano: Been there, done that, my friend, all too \r\nmany times. </li>\r\n',2,0,0,0,'207.99.41.217','en'),(6088,1424,'2001-07-26 14:15:30',0,'will','congratulations on your 29th.',2,0,0,0,'198.214.178.232','en'),(6089,1426,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to burt','you obviously havent done me. ask anyone, I come on a dime.',0,0,0,0,'209.86.6.198','en'),(6090,1436,'2001-07-26 15:36:32',0,'wolfwood','radioactive honey kisses are #1!',1,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(6091,1426,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to kat','when visit? email. put the robot in your kangaroo pouch and let\\\'s all dine.',0,0,0,0,'209.86.6.198','en'),(6092,1429,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','\\\"the sensation of liquids\\\"? what is this, a Palmolive ad? \\\"ooh Madge, I soaked in \r\nyour sensation of liquids.\\\"',0,0,0,0,'209.86.6.198','en'),(6093,1424,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','geez yr making me feel like calling my mom.',0,0,0,0,'209.86.6.198','en'),(6094,1438,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>that man looks liek his name should be \\\"Bucky\\\".</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6095,1438,'2001-07-26 17:40:31',0,'robotit','<PRE>\r\n10:25:36 robotec9: oh mang.\r\n10:25:49 egglit: why are you asking what the fuck is today\r\n10:25:58 robotec9: babies, friends getting money\r\n10:26:02 robotec9: grandmas dyin\r\n10:26:07 robotec9: what is going on?\r\n10:26:33 egglit: this is life mang\r\n10:26:42 robotec9: i cant cope\r\n10:26:44 egglit: lets get involved!\r\n10:26:48 egglit: lets get married!\r\n10:26:51 egglit: lets join in!\r\n10:26:56 robotec9: BABIES, RICHES!\r\n10:27:04 egglit: babies ARE riches!\r\n10:27:15 egglit: you can put them to work in the field\r\n10:27:47 egglit: ive decided i am going to drop out of the\r\nrat race, urge eve to purchase land and appoint myself\r\nartist in residence of land Land\r\n10:28:02 robotec9: great\r\n10:29:00 egglit: cmon my robot run away with me\r\n10:32:27 robotec9: i\\\'m dying\r\n10:32:29 robotec9: dying.\r\n10:32:33 egglit: huh?\r\n10:32:37 robotec9: babies\r\n10:32:38 robotec9: riches\r\n10:32:40 egglit: everyone is dying, and the universe is\r\nexpanding\r\n10:32:46 egglit: get with it ma joad\r\n10:33:19 robotec9: i love this mad moll SCIENCE poem.\r\n\r\n\r\no destabilizing\r\n</PRE>\r\n\r\n',4,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(6096,1438,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>\\\"he thinks he is losing his mind<BR>\r\nand he feels it going.\\\"</P>',4,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(6097,1438,'2001-07-26 17:57:25',0,'kaneda','where does this term \\\"mang\\\" come from ?',5,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(6098,1429,'2001-07-26 17:59:02',0,'PlasticBono','\\\"she feels like water in my hands\\\" - Paul Hewson.',2,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en');
INSERT INTO `comments` VALUES (6099,1428,'2001-07-26 18:02:20',0,'green','to mad moll: i dont envy people who have good relationships.\r\nenvying people is bad. Plus i wouldnt be who i am now if my \r\nparents werent the way they are',2,0,0,0,'198.81.16.159','en'),(6100,1416,'2001-07-26 18:05:24',0,'green','to essemar: i tried to do the tp thing ill email you what i \r\ngot \r\n\r\nits big brother....',0,0,0,0,'198.81.16.159','en'),(6101,1438,'2001-07-26 18:16:20',0,'ghost to robo','word',4,0,0,0,'32.102.91.53','en'),(6102,1438,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','he looks more like a Gerhard.',0,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(6103,1441,'2001-07-26 19:10:06',0,'adamabot','<pre>but, love grows with <processing> time</pre>',3,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(6104,1440,'2001-07-26 19:18:11',0,'kat','my belly demands \r\nfood offerings tasty sweet\r\nall is pieceful again\r\n',1,0,0,0,'32.102.91.53','en'),(6105,1440,'2001-07-26 19:19:17',0,'kat','<p>my belly demands<br>\r\nfood offerings tasty sweet<br>\r\nall is pieceful again</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<i>...until i forget the tags that is.</i>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'32.102.91.53','en'),(6106,1441,'2001-07-26 19:20:47',0,'ghost','and ghosts never fade away...',3,0,0,0,'32.102.91.53','en'),(6107,1440,'2001-07-26 19:23:06',0,'kat','duh, i can\\\'t think<br>\r\n<b>peaceful</b> <i>DAMMIT!</i>',6,0,0,0,'32.102.91.53','en'),(6108,1441,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','<p>i got your terrorism under control<br>\r\nlike danny glover<br>\r\nyo i\\\'m touching people<br>\r\nlike a stearing wheel cover<br>\r\nand you\\\'re takin a turn at ninety-five<br>\r\nyou\\\'re running like a naked little albino girl covered with \r\npollen<br>\r\nand i\\\'m the BEE HIVE<br>\r\n</P>',0,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(6109,1440,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>heavy metal time<br>\r\nold friend brings teenage boy fun<br>\r\nspontaneously',0,0,0,0,'209.86.6.198','en'),(6110,1436,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','i was told today that a man who is really good at catching katfish is called a \r\n\\\"katdaddy\\\".',0,0,0,0,'209.86.6.198','en'),(6111,1440,'2001-07-26 20:31:26',0,'chi chi\\\"','<br>\r\nmidnight madness, here<br>\r\ndawn creeps ever so slowly.<br>\r\nlay in crumpled sheets.>br>',0,0,0,0,'64.165.201.247','en'),(6112,1442,'2001-07-26 21:06:22',0,'exposition','i always wonder about these aim posts. does the other \r\nperson know you are going to post their conversation ?',5,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(6113,1442,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','you ask permission. if they say yes, you post it.',0,0,0,0,'209.86.6.198','en'),(6114,1442,'2001-07-26 21:10:29',0,'robotit','<PRE>\r\nrobotec9:  i am about to post above 20 lines under the <a\r\nhref=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=1438.txt#6095\\\">science\r\npost</A>\r\nrobotec9:  objections? \r\nrobotec9:  objections? \r\negglit:  no \r\negglit:  im the wordiest ho you got \r\n</PRE>',3,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(6115,1442,'2001-07-26 21:18:44',0,'robotit to jayper3000','<P>you make me want to be gut wrenching.  i wonder if i have\r\nit in me to be so.  i think you make it sound really\r\nattractive.  on the other hand, i know you have a theatrical\r\nnature.  gut wrenching for you may be just a tool.  i dont\r\nthink i have to wrench my guts to want to run away to\r\ncolorado with an S.O.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>as a matter of fact, i write ann landers <a\r\nhref=\"http://www.mcsweeneys.net/2000/11/30landers.html\">EVERY\r\nDAY</A> since i met my most recent heart beating woman.  ann\r\nseems to think we have a healthy relationship.  she thinks\r\nour explorations with role playing and furry animal masks is\r\na sure sign of luv and that we are well on our way to\r\ncorrecting our spelling.</P>',3,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(6116,1442,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','colorado? what\\\'s in colorado? I thought it was vegas or cuba. simon says she \r\nknows she is in love when someone makes her want to move to denver.',0,0,0,0,'209.86.6.198','en'),(6117,1442,'2001-07-26 21:47:59',0,'Cha-ka','Oganza Bi Sa Sa! ',4,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(6118,1441,'2001-07-26 21:48:47',0,'Cha-ka','Oganza Bi Sa Sa! ',6,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(6119,1442,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','that\\\'s it!@ that\\\'s totally it. it\\\'s love when it makes you \r\nwant to move to colorado or a little cabin in the woods \r\nwhere you can split wood, carry water, rise bread together. \r\nwackachika wackachika!@',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(6120,1442,'2002-03-05 20:17:36',17,'austin re: colorado','<P>i think what simon was going for was that she WOULD NEVER\r\nUNDER ANY SANE CIRCUMSTANCES move to colorado.  so if she\r\nfound herself wanting to move to colorado chasing some girl,\r\nthen she is really in love -- a state of total\r\nirrationality.</P>',3,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(6121,1442,'2001-07-26 22:19:49',0,'jay to OMS','I admit to a theatrical nature. I like to moan alot about \r\nhow tired I am, and I\\\'m a nightmare when I\\\'m sick.  But on \r\nthe subject of love, the Real is very dear to me. I don\\\'t \r\nact, or I try hard not to. The only time I\\\'ve ever been in \r\nlove it was pretty gut-wrenching. Maybe, to speak in \r\nhackneyed astrology talk, that is expected in the Pisces-\r\nScorpio union: crazy sex and even crazier emotions. We were \r\nall over the place, laughing, crying, jealous, mean, \r\nsensitive, caustic.  I don\\\'t know if everyone gets to have \r\nrelationships like that, where it takes you 2 years to \r\nbreak up and you cry, you honestly can make each other cry, \r\nat the drop of a hat. No theatrics. Real, messy tears. I\\\'m \r\nnot sayin this is the only brand of love there is, but I do \r\nbelieve that honesty\\\'s got to take the place of play-acting \r\nat some point, and that the play-acting is all well and \r\ngood if it\\\'s founded upon an honest exchange.',1,0,0,0,'63.203.225.62','en'),(6122,1430,'2001-07-26 22:22:02',0,'Felicity','You can hang with him any time...as long as you understand \r\nthat his behavior may be a bad influence on you.  (It helps \r\nif you understand German, too, because he speaks both \r\nDeutsch und Englisch and tends to get the two mixed up in \r\nhis little toddler mind.)',3,0,0,0,'216.42.125.249','en'),(6123,1442,'2001-07-26 22:28:36',0,'leonard','OMS: Open Mouth Syndrome',4,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(6124,1442,'2001-07-26 22:33:36',0,'translator','OMS=Old Man Swinney',2,0,0,0,'63.203.225.62','en'),(6125,1442,'2001-07-26 22:53:16',0,'leonard','OMS=One Minute Swinney',6,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(6126,1442,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','Orgasmidextrous Mr. Swinney',0,0,0,0,'209.86.6.198','en'),(6127,1442,'2001-07-27 00:43:35',0,'swinney','fans, please.  leave me some modesty.',2,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(6128,1442,'2001-07-27 00:54:09',0,'dirty girl','the phrase \\\"Mr. Swinney\\\" sounds so naughty. reminds me of \r\nthose fantasies of humping your gym teacher and screaming \r\nout his name with an emphasis on the \\\'mister\\\' part. ',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(6129,1442,'2001-07-27 01:11:40',0,'schoolgirl','for me it was my history teacher. he taught a History of Labor Movements class, \r\nHistory of Civil Rights, History of Constitutional Law...oh my god, im think im \r\ngonna tinkle. he had a young daughter and was always pulling little girl barrettes \r\nout of his pocket. teach me, daddy!',0,0,0,0,'209.86.6.198','en'),(6130,1441,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','Austin Swinney\\\'s Existential Angst',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(6131,1442,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i\\\'ve been gut wrenching. it\\\'s tiring. bring on the sarcasm.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(6132,1442,'2001-07-27 04:17:53',0,'wb','i  read that \\\"fuckin lil bra\\\" \r\n\r\neveryone has their cutsie love chatty lingo, i dont \r\nthink it is right to judge her. she is sarcastic but she \r\nhas a heart. she isnt without passion like so many \r\nwho go thru the motions of \\\"real romance\\\" which are\r\nbasically sad attempts to recreate moments \r\nseen in such films as \\\"jerry macguire\\\"\r\n\r\negg is saying: this is not that film you liked when you \r\nwere 15, this is not an hour long drama starring coke \r\nbitches from LA. this is me, im real and what will \r\nhappen between us is real because we have moved \r\npast a fantasy that somebody we have never met has \r\nwritten for us. she is priming the scene for real \r\nromance by liberating herself (and whoever the \r\ncomments are directed at) from all the rest of that.\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,'216.10.221.86','en'),(6133,1440,'2001-07-27 04:25:03',0,'wb','is it just me--- i find mentions of coffee in books and \r\nwhatnot written after say 1994 problematic...i get this \r\nwincing feeling that praising it is part of this \\\"java\\\" \r\nculture that starbucks brought to our country. \\\"im \r\ngetting wired on my double capp to the x treme\\\" that \r\nkind of shit. in  my mind its in the same place as \r\npeople talking about the \\\'thrill\\\' of staying upall night \r\nworking on a dot com project.  ',0,0,0,0,'216.10.221.86','en'),(6134,1442,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','wayne. suddenly you are on my side. I dont get it I also dont know what the first \r\nsentence of your comment means. also, I would like to note that EVRY fucking \r\nCOMMENT ON THIS SITE DEGENERATES INTO PORNY TALK. its like \r\npeople just come on here looking for an excuse to textually hump! my story was a \r\nserious document of a serious conversation about romance and relationships. \r\ngrow up people.',0,0,0,0,'209.86.6.198','en'),(6135,1442,'2001-07-27 04:28:36',0,'adult','\\\"porny\\\"? is that some sort of cute porn that\\\'s out there?',6,0,0,0,'24.28.73.144','en'),(6136,1442,'2001-07-27 04:35:21',0,'baby','I think <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=1221.txt\\\">porny</a> is like \r\n\\\"pony\\\" meets \\\"horny\\\". a horse motif. others think it\\\'s just the adjective form of porn. \r\n\\\"pornographic\\\" is just too long. not as fun.',0,0,0,0,'209.86.6.198','en'),(6137,1442,'2001-07-27 05:04:22',0,'wb','egg: my little porny, im always on your side you just \r\ndont always know it.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nre: the first sentence, you wrote \\\"fucking libra\\\" and i \r\nread it as \\\"fucking lil bra\\\" because i am not into \r\nastrology and when i see the word libra i don\\\'t always \r\nparse it right away.  ',0,0,0,0,'216.10.221.86','en'),(6138,1442,'2001-07-27 05:48:03',0,'kat','<p>you are all RIGHT...i say do what you feel when you feel \r\nit. say it. you can\\\'t change nobody...and you ain\\\'t gonna \r\nchange yourself. that being said: EVERYTHING changes, no \r\nmatter what. yes, i know this doesn\\\'t make sense. welcome \r\nto the world of love. welcome to the world [period].</p>\r\n\r\n<p>enjoy the ride...</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'32.102.90.160','en'),(6139,1442,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>\\\"porny\\\" is good.  i happen to like \\\"pornesque\\\".</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6140,1442,'2001-07-27 14:04:06',0,'erin to auntie','colorado is quiet hideaway love, denver is growing new love - \r\nain\\\'t much there yet, but its hopeful. maybe simon wants to \r\nmove to rocky mountains and sometimes there isn\\\'t a better \r\nreason then love.  chief niwot\\\'s curse..rational thought \r\nain\\\'t a priority or really much of a factor.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'129.105.107.217','en'),(6141,1448,'2001-07-27 21:16:36',0,'dza','ha!  i like it.',0,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(6142,1448,'2001-07-27 23:00:30',0,'ghost','y\\\'all need to stop worrying so much about fitting in here. \r\njust do what you do when you feel like doin it. the more \r\nyou add to the stew...the better it tastes.',1,0,0,0,'32.102.109.187','en'),(6143,1436,'2001-07-27 23:48:25',0,'kat','nobody has quite caught me yet....i wouldn\\\'t mind having a \r\nlovely around, to call daddy now and then.',4,0,0,0,'32.102.109.163','en'),(6144,1436,'2001-07-27 23:52:51',0,'kat','<p>ps: in Oklahoma there is school of thought on catfish \r\nhunting. it is hands-only, and folk have been known to \r\nloose digits in the process. this is called \\\'noodling\\\' and \r\nto the people who do it, it\\\'s a sacred thing.</p>',1,0,0,0,'32.102.109.163','en'),(6145,1448,'2001-07-28 00:05:02',0,'Pandora','good grief I haven\\\'t laughed that hard in a long time. I\\\'m \r\nreally truly glad you had the \\\'guts\\\' to share the tale.  \r\nI\\\'ll say bravo, because I\\\'m sure you don\\\'t want an encore.',0,0,0,0,'148.74.246.11','en'),(6146,1447,'2001-07-28 00:08:09',0,'felicity','i\\\'ll tell ya what i\\\'m thinking...i\\\'m thinking i\\\'m pretty \r\nembarrased because i got ahead of myself reading, and the \r\nway the words wrap on my screen the words \\\"was picking\\\" are \r\nat the end of a line.  my brain was quite certain that the \r\ntwo words that began the next line would be \\\"my nose.\\\"  \r\n\r\n<em>i\\\'ve really got to stop picking my nose while i\\\'m \r\ndriving</em>',2,0,0,0,'216.42.125.249','en'),(6147,1440,'2001-07-28 00:47:00',0,'chi chi','friday, five-forty.\r\nmust cross bay bridge to san-fran.\r\nbe ready ready at eight.',0,0,0,0,'64.165.201.247','en'),(6148,1440,'2001-07-28 00:47:59',0,'chi chi','oops <br>\r\nfriday, five-forty. <br>must cross bay bridge to san-fran. \r\n<br>be ready ready at eight. ',0,0,0,0,'64.165.201.247','en'),(6149,1448,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','is the a name for people who fetishizes shit stories? seems \r\nlike they all follow the same formula, or are very similar.',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(6150,1448,'2001-07-28 02:19:37',0,'trouble','weeb, i\\\'m not sure... the guide to popular feces-related \r\nprose neglected to mention any such name.  however, i am \r\nabsolutely positive that a name exisits and while it \r\ndoesn\\\'t quite suit a one-time \\\'shit for giggles\\\' weak \r\nstorywriter like myself i\\\'m sure it does apply to those \r\nwith more of a serious facination with the doo-doo.<P>it\\\'s \r\na friday, i felt like a single ode to the natural exits at \r\nmy own expense however formulaic it might have seemed.<p>if \r\ni can smile, then anybody can.',4,0,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(6151,1448,'2001-07-28 06:05:32',0,'kat','you never told us what your wife thought of the whole thing.',2,0,0,0,'32.102.64.224','en'),(6152,1451,'2001-07-28 07:24:14',0,'jo','i really like \\\"busy being 22.\\\"<BR>\r\nit reminds me of a favorite song lyric of mine: \\\"i was \r\nkissing you when i should have been in college.\\\"',1,0,0,0,'172.168.224.209','en'),(6153,1448,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','yeah. what was the wife\\\'s reaction?',0,0,0,0,'64.51.232.102','en'),(6154,1446,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','random capitalization + anime = insane?<br><br>\r\n:)))))))))))))))))',0,0,0,0,'64.51.232.102','en'),(6155,1448,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','Nice.',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(6156,1450,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','Dude, what do you think about Syndicate being named best \r\nD\\\'n\\\'B label by Knowledge?  I read the story in The Eye \r\nabout Syndicate and the ICE party hapening this weekend \r\nwhile I was at work tonight and I was reading the \r\ninterview/story with Mystical.  And then there was the \r\nfront page of the Entertainment section of the Star last \r\nSunday: <b>Toronto Jungle, Global \r\nRumble</b>.<br><br>Whatever, the best d\\\'n\\\'b tape I own is \r\nthis really old Sniper tape simply called <i>Drum and \r\nBass</i>.<br><br>Ram Records is putting out some really \r\ngood material lately.',1,0,0,0,'64.229.76.128','en'),(6157,1447,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','But, were you disappointed when you found out I wasn\\\'t \r\npicking my nose while driving?  Did that detract from the \r\noverall story?  If it did, maybe I can do a re-write for \r\nyou to morph it into more of a Seinfeld episode.',3,0,0,0,'64.229.76.128','en'),(6158,1446,'2001-07-28 12:43:32',0,'englishteacher','Correct grammar + internet = not necessary',1,0,0,0,'24.28.73.144','en'),(6159,1440,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Quad Moll','<p>It\\\'s all <i>so</i> 1990\\\'s, I don\\\'t see how they can \r\nstand it.</p>',0,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(6160,1451,'2001-07-28 17:39:14',0,'green','beautiful',1,0,0,0,'198.81.17.182','en'),(6161,1448,'2001-07-28 18:39:14',0,'trouble','being true to self she drank more than her little frame \r\ncould handle and fell deeply asleep in the car, but not \r\ndeep enough apparently because she saw fit to awaken every \r\nnow and then to tell me i was driving too fast or too crazy \r\nfor her tastes and that she smelled something \\\'odd\\\'.  i \r\nsimply grunted a few times so that it couldn\\\'t be said i \r\nwas ignoring her (which i was of course).  i wanted to \r\nremind her that i drank twice as much as she, tell her that \r\nmy ass and guts were working a search and destroy mission \r\non my insides and that the \\\'odd\\\' odor she smelled was \r\nnothing compared to the messy hell that was about to \r\nsurface but i couldn\\\'t say anything so i just continued my \r\nonward course home before i lost complete and total bowel \r\ncontrol.  she somehow managed to sleep through my breakneck \r\nstop once we got to the house and i left her in the car as \r\ni ran to the door.  an hour or so later i went out to get \r\nher and after waking her i was treated to a tiny drunken \r\nwoman berate me for everything under the sun with the \r\nexception of current human rights violations in china \r\n(which if i gave her more time, i would have been \r\nresponsible for eventually).  the humor i found in the \r\nmidst of my situation would have been lost on her so we \r\ndidn\\\'t bother to discuss it. <P>in the <A \r\nHREF=\\\"http://www.liz-phair.com/eig.htm#Divorce%\r\n20Song\\\">end</A> such arguements will cease to exist.',2,0,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(6162,267,'2001-07-29 08:02:56',0,'leonard','nice white socks, aus.',3,0,0,0,'209.179.128.109','en'),(6163,90,'2001-07-29 15:14:08',0,'Mike','Buck up boyo ,we will go camping and take the pain away!',0,0,0,0,'206.224.71.188','en'),(6164,1450,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','to be honest. Sniper IS/WAS the best dj in toronto with \r\nregards to the jungle. However im privy to some information \r\nthat made me lose all respect for the man. He almost beat me \r\nup at a party once. He has beaten kids up at parties for \r\nbumping into him, and he has threatened other dj\\\'s accusing \r\nthem of trying to \\\"take over\\\" the toronto scene and make \r\nsyndicate lose \\\"power\\\". \r\n<br>\r\nto be honest, i dont give a fuck. jungle isnt my mainstay \r\nthese days. I listen to a lot of bhangra, ska, and dub \r\nreggae. I still listen to 93-95 jungle and when i find a \r\ngood electro track i wiggle. hiphop is still a bit \r\ninteresting and the smiths still make me feel fuzzy. right \r\nnow im listening to a really good track called Rasool \r\nRastakhiz.mp3. I dont know what language its in, but its \r\nreally chillaxin. \r\n<br>\r\nboom chick boom chick just doesnt row my boat. never did. \r\nnever will. \r\n',6,0,0,0,'24.43.182.49','en'),(6165,1450,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','p.s  RAM is putting good stuff out you are right. i saw \r\nshimon about a month ago though and he sucked. \r\n<p>\r\ni too own the sniper tape \\\"drum and bass\\\". its not that old \r\ntho. its from about 97. if you want some good tapes....give \r\nme an email chiam@gee.kz and ill hook you up with some stuff \r\nif you\\\'d like. TAPE POWER. \r\n',6,0,0,0,'24.43.182.49','en'),(6166,1452,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','there were ten in the bed and the little one said, \\\"roll \r\nover!\\\" so they all rolled over and one fell out, there were \r\nnine in the bed and the little one said, \\\"roll over!\\\" ...so \r\nthey all rolled over and one fell out.  there was one in \r\nthe bed and the little one said, \\\"good night! good night!\\\" ',1,0,0,0,'63.31.55.144','en'),(6167,1452,'2001-07-29 22:04:26',0,'kat','i like this swintry...i really like this.',4,0,0,0,'32.102.109.247','en'),(6168,1450,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','I fucking hate prima donnas.  Especially DJ prima donnas.  \r\nI was and still am pretty big into going to see DJ\\\'s just \r\nfor the music.  I never went to parties to meet people.  \r\nMost of the people I would talk with at parties weren\\\'t \r\npeople I\\\'d wish to assosciate with outside of that \r\nenvironment.  It\\\'s shitty to find out that someone is an \r\nasshole when you actually respect them.<br><br>Yeah, I \r\nremember reading about you seeing Shimon at Turbo.  My \r\nroommate (Mook) was spinning at a party in Pittsburgh the \r\nweekend before that, he went on before Shimon and said he \r\nwas great there.  Maybe he just had a bad night or got too \r\ndunk and/or high while in Toronto?  Kerbkrawler (out on \r\nVirus) by Ed Rush & Optical is a good new track.  Ram \r\nRaiders Pt. 3 has some sick tracks on it too.  (Ahh to live \r\nwith a d\\\'n\\\'n DJ has <b>many</b> benefits =)).<br><br>Also, \r\nhave you heard Dillinja\\\'s Cybotron album?  It\\\'s a great \r\nalbum.  Totally worth the wait.  Dillinja is just a god.  \r\nAs far as in the wholeeeeee wide world, J Majik has been \r\nand remains my favourite dnb DJ.  Ever since I first \r\nheard \\\'Your Sound\\\'.<br><br>When I was in Ottawa for Canada \r\nday, staying at Simon\\\'s and Adam\\\'s place, the one night \r\nAdam put on this tape of pakistani classical music that he \r\nheard on the radio one night and just had to tape.  It was \r\nreally good.  Just listening to a little Squarepusher right \r\nnow.  Are you checking out the Plaid/Squarepusher/Mira \r\nCalix show on the 22nd?  It\\\'s going to be soooooooo good.',1,0,0,0,'64.229.76.128','en'),(6169,1454,'2001-07-29 23:31:57',0,'deb','maybe the editors understood.  love is one of those things. \r\nyou have it, and you want it to be right. you don\\\'t have \r\nit, and you pray that the connection will show soon, or \r\nthat you\\\'ll both get over whatever it is that\\\'s holding you \r\nback. but it all continues to be a mystery. never ends.',1,0,0,0,'205.188.197.52','en'),(6170,1446,'2001-07-30 02:08:32',0,'ty','My english teacher said the proper grammar is always \r\nimportant, to make sure that you are being clear. And \r\nspelling isn\\\'t grammer.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.72','en'),(6171,1455,'2001-07-30 02:23:16',0,'trouble','there isn\\\'t anything worse than an unfulfilled sunday \r\nmorning.  foggy sunday mornings (is there any other kind?) \r\nmove into foggy sunday afternoons and things never seem \r\nquite right with the world.  it would seem that sundays \r\nwere made for being let-down every now and then... i just \r\nhave no use for such a day.',1,0,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(6172,1455,'2001-07-30 02:36:15',0,'ghost','such days are perfect for drinking hot tea and taking naps.',1,0,0,0,'32.100.70.26','en'),(6173,1454,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','I always say, as long as it still bothers you, you\\\'re \r\nprobably not that bad. ',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.72','en'),(6174,267,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','o my god, you look 16.',0,0,0,0,'209.86.7.13','en'),(6175,267,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','dude, you\\\'re all wearing the same coloured shirt.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nis that a display house?<br>\r\n<br>\r\no<br>',4,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(6176,267,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','men in front, women in back. need i say more.',0,0,0,0,'64.51.232.102','en'),(6177,1453,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','Experiment on!  I enjoyed reading this.  You and Tyler are \r\nadding a nice new twist to the Swinney experience.  In \r\nfact, thinking of Ty, when the hell is he coming with the \r\nnext installment of his story?',2,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(6178,1455,'2001-07-30 16:51:14',0,'leonard','i saw my first \\\"Blueberry Juice\\\" at the drive-in. she was \r\ngiving it to him like there was no tomorrow. ',2,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(6179,267,'2002-03-05 20:17:36',17,'austin to o','it is all fake.  they are all robots, except me, as evident\r\nby the white socks.',3,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(6180,1455,'2001-07-30 17:25:15',0,'kat','there is much to be learned at the drive-in....and i always \r\nenjoy the flea market. it\\\'s a bit of everybody and \r\neverything all in one dirty place.',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.83','en'),(6181,1446,'2001-07-30 17:27:25',0,'kat','i like Rufus',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.83','en'),(6182,1461,'2001-07-30 17:49:09',0,'kat','<p>this post makes me hungry. i want to be at Willy\\\'s place \r\nlicking the wallpaper and munching plates. didn\\\'t you \r\nknow...everything inside is eatable. i mean edible. i mean \r\nyou can eat everything inside.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>that Wonka man is so nasty.</p>',1,0,0,0,'32.102.109.18','en'),(6183,1459,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>Maybe it isn\\\'t so much that we\\\'re trying to figure \r\nout how to grow into the ideal adults we always thought we \r\nwould be someday, but that we\\\'re losing the naivety that \r\npercieved that that ideal existed in the first place...?\r\n</tt> ',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6184,1461,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','fizzy lifting drinks + walt whitman = hangover.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'209.86.7.13','en'),(6185,1461,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>this post made me happy for some reason... \r\nthanks.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6186,1461,'2001-07-30 18:13:41',0,'big fella','Oh, Kat... yer so oral...',1,0,0,0,'63.203.225.62','en'),(6187,1459,'2001-07-30 19:22:49',0,'green','lets be bums on californ beaches and \r\nsomeone will find you and snatch your \r\nphotocopying hands and be like you you\r\ni want you to dance dance for me me \r\n',5,0,0,0,'138.23.189.113','en'),(6188,1461,'2001-07-30 19:59:38',0,'ghost','<p>big engines between thighs, and rumbling mechanics are \r\ncalling swinney....</p>\r\n\r\n<i>[and kat too]</i>',1,0,0,0,'32.102.109.18','en'),(6189,1463,'2001-07-30 20:17:00',0,'trouble','amen brother, amen.',1,0,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(6190,1463,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','redheds are hot.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.108.113','en'),(6191,1459,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<br>My ex and I used to fantasize about moving to Florida.  \r\nShe would sell snow cones on the beach and I would teach \r\nthe geriatric crowd how to Foxtrot and Waltz.  We almost \r\neloped and did it with visions of beach bungalows, swollen \r\nbellies, and toddlers underfoot.<br>\r\nWhatever... I\\\'ve only recently figured out that I\\\'m not \r\nperfect and life isn\\\'t always a dream; maybe I am starting \r\nto grow up.  So, Peter, when you gonna buy my that drink?',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(6192,1461,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','fuck, i miss summer. and fall. and winter. grrr.',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(6193,1461,'2001-07-30 22:39:28',0,'leonard','i don\\\'t know what to say. here is all i know about nothing:',1,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(6194,267,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','is that your dad?  he is my notion of your average american \r\nman.',3,0,0,1,'203.45.52.132','en'),(6195,1459,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Vileness Moll','<p>So long as I never accept the unacceptable, I\\\'ll be \r\nokay. Easier said than done.</p>',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(6196,1461,'2001-07-30 23:28:45',0,'john cage','i have nothing to say, and Im saying it.',0,0,0,0,'66.32.60.46','en'),(6197,1463,'2001-07-31 01:45:16',0,'deb','\\\"you were almost kind, you were almost true\\\"',2,0,0,0,'152.163.213.176','en'),(6198,78,'2001-07-31 01:54:17',0,'deb','imagination doesn\\\'t need to be sure.',2,0,0,0,'152.163.213.176','en'),(6199,1461,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>\r\n\r\ni don\'t want to let egg steal the narrative here.\r\n\r\n</P><P>\r\n\r\nit is Monday morning and as much as writing makes me want to vomit, i\r\nwill add my version of this little audi commercial before i even read\r\nher version.\r\n\r\n</P><P>\r\n\r\nSaturday night i did not go to housness\'s party because i wanted to\r\nget up in time to leave at 10 on Sunday for the beaches.  never mind\r\nwhat beach.  who cares about details, not us, ever.  so that is what i\r\ndid.  i had a beer, and embraced the tired steak stuffed lethargia on\r\nthe couch, slowly grasping that i was going no where tonight, knowing\r\nmy cell phone was down four flights of stairs and across the street\r\nwhere no one could reach me.  peter would call.  elly would call.\r\ndrinking would call.  i told ix i would drink with him.  sitting on\r\nthe couch after dinner, all these people and plans slipped away.\r\n\r\n</P><P>\r\n\r\nSunday morning wake up comes easy.  coffix.  left over muffin from\r\nSaturday.  i would regret not eating breakfast later, but for the time\r\nbeing i was wanting to stick to the plan.  leave at ten.  ten o clock\r\nrolls around, and jay decides he is coming but he is not ready.  egg\r\nis screaming that goat is burning her in hell like always and the\r\nworld needs to swirl up into goats ass like a drain.  i am thinking,\r\ngood god, the griswalds are going to the lake.  frantic everywhere.\r\negg and i rush to the store, me staying a comfortable distance behind\r\nthe grocery shopping machine bred for the one characteristic of\r\nswimming down lanes and pulling down items like a shark.\r\n\r\n</P><P>\r\n\r\nback at the raging bend of the highway that is egg\'s world, jay is\r\nready and arwa is arriving looking as though it was her wagon that\r\nrode her to the bend, or just drug her by the big toe screaming from\r\nbed, pulling bed sheets, hissing, fighting.  good morning goat.  goat\r\nbrings the wagon queen family truckster, silver with all leather\r\ninterior (good for cleaning up those spills -- Men\'s Magazine, July,\r\n2001, article, <i>33 things to waste your money on and feel good about\r\nit</i>.)  which is good because the first thing egg does upon loading\r\nthe car up is spill the goat\'s 40 oz insulated mug of coffix forming a\r\nrather serene pond of steaming brown nestled in the creamy leather\r\nthighs of goat\'s driver\'s seat.\r\n\r\n</P><P>\r\n\r\nwe drove for hours, seaming to heap upon hours, through the miles of\r\nPG&E stomping grounds, experiment sights, underground nuclear fusion\r\nreactors, milky blue coolant tanks, fields of discarded pipe.  Past\r\nacres of warehouses, and trucking depots, the live stock yards of\r\nhuman consumption, sheep, family farms and fruit stands.  finally we\r\narrive at the destination, what turns out to be not the lord\'s lake,\r\nbut man\'s lake.  a dammed river with water clear to about six feet.  a\r\nwatering hole for \"locals only.\"\r\n\r\n</P><P>\r\n\r\nwe were not local, so we could not swim in any of the local\'s dumb\r\nbeaches.  we tried.  they said not only could we not swim there, but\r\nthat we could not use profane language.  we were going to argue with\r\nthem about our rights to the land based on my 1/8 Cherokee heritage,\r\nbut they said there were no Cherokee around here, that would not\r\nfloat.  furthermore, that we were cussing up a storm and that alone\r\nwas reason enough to keep us out -- to protect the young ears of their\r\nchillun.  yes.\r\n\r\n</P><P>\r\n\r\ndejected, we sought beach refuge elsewhere.  we finally fond a slope\r\nof rock cliff just off the road in to town where the locals and\r\ntourists who either did not have the ten dollars for yearly beach\r\nadmission, or cussed, or were Hispanic, or smoked pot, or peed in the\r\nwater, or had too many tattoos .. swam. that was us.  we secured a\r\npiece of secondary real-estate next to the nice diving rock which was\r\nbeing occupied by teenage lovers.  life was good.\r\n\r\n</P><P>\r\n\r\nafter swimming a few minutes, i got out to pick the leeches off my\r\nlegs and stomach, and eat some food.  most of what went on after that\r\nwas hopping in and out of water.  cold, hot, cold hot.  i am happy to\r\nsay that despite my day in the sun, i have no sun burn.  i owe my\r\npristine condition to jayperOhOh.  his tanned highness taught me the\r\nways of the skin tanners.  i applied and re-applied 15 spf sun block\r\nand got in touch with my bedouin brothers with a fashionable head\r\ndress that chi chi lent me.\r\n\r\n</P><P>\r\n\r\non the way home we played pee games at a road stop.  egg peed in hover\r\nmode while jayperOhOh peed between her thighs.  i peed in the sink,\r\nand chi chi held the door so we could all see what we were doing.\r\nthen jayperOhOh assaulted the convenience store clerk with airborne\r\npomegranates and we jumped into the wagon and were off.  it is at this\r\npoint that egg\'s nice little article happens.\r\n\r\n</P>\r\n\r\n\r\n',4,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(6200,1461,'2001-07-31 02:38:36',0,'kat','peeing and spooge. you people are beautiful.<br>\r\n[best friendly]',1,0,0,0,'32.102.90.214','en'),(6201,1467,'2001-07-31 02:50:06',0,'ghost','<p>there is no-one to blame. or everyone. this is not \r\ndeath...only equilibrium. things will balance themselves. \r\nalways. eventually. did we all really think that making \r\nmillions on paper was going to last forever? did we all \r\nreally think that buying the 5 cent plastic parrot from \r\nTaiwan wasn\\\'t going to somehow affect our quality of living?\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>big. bigger. better. faster.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>if all you care about is cumming, well then all you\\\'ll \r\nget is an empty climax. those are a dime a dozen. cheap \r\nenough for everyone to have two.</p>',4,0,0,0,'32.102.90.214','en'),(6202,1467,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<h1><font color=\\\"red\\\">DOOM</font></h1>',6,0,0,0,'64.10.140.136','en'),(6203,1467,'2001-07-31 03:18:33',0,'cyantist','we do what history should have taught us.  my great \r\ngrandmother lived through the depression, and i learned a \r\ngreat deal from her how to survive.  she still reuses \r\nplastic baggies until they can no longer seal.  she folds \r\nher aluminum foil and uses it again until it just can\\\'t \r\nbe.  she is careful about everything she does and she just \r\nstopped consuming so much.\r\n\r\nthat\\\'s our problem auntie.  we think that buying things is \r\nsooo important.  well, it isn\\\'t!  we can get by without \r\nmany of the things we own.  \r\n\r\ni\\\'m not saying that the depression will be as bad as it was \r\nthen, but i have no doubt that it is going to be hard for \r\neveryone.  \r\n\r\nthe best things for us to do, is come together as a \r\ncommunity and help each other out.  if you see a friend \r\nstruggling to get a job, and you are better off, let them \r\nmow your lawn or do some errands for you.\r\n\r\nthings are bad, but that is because we put too much faith \r\nin products that weren\\\'t tangible and we over valued them.  \r\nnow that they are valued at what they are really worth, we \r\npanic.  \\\"oh my god.. we can\\\'t have everything for free \r\nanymore.. oh no!\\\".\r\n\r\nto be honest, i blaim companies like AOL.  the mega \r\ncorporations that took advantage of the stock climb and the \r\nhype.  AOL drove thousands of ma and pa isps into the \r\nground, while collecting a membership base.  they \r\noffered \\\"UNLIMITED\\\" internet access and set the standard \r\nfor the FREE internet craze that was going to happen in the \r\nyears to come.  in order to compete, you had to GIVE your \r\nservices away.\r\n\r\nhere\\\'s an idea, \\\"let\\\'s make all our money in \r\nadvertisement!\\\"  \\\"it works for television\\\".  well, just \r\nbecause it works for television, it doesn\\\'t mean that the \r\ninternet is the same sort of medium or has the same affect. \r\n\r\nhowever, don\\\'t blame yourself.  it isn\\\'t your fault.  how \r\ndo we stop giants like aol and time warner?  well, i guess \r\npart of us are to blame for jumping on the IPO bandwagons \r\nand working for companies like nbci.. (cough).\r\n\r\nwe made so much money and most of us (not all .. thank \r\ngoodness)  didn\\\'t save that much of our earnings.  now, \r\nwe\\\'re feeling the burn, because along with those empty \r\nshelves.. there\\\'s no job positions for us to fill.\r\n\r\ndo you know that i\\\'m overqualified to work in a coffee shop \r\nand they would turn me down in most places in order to fill \r\nthe position with someone who would work harder. (they \r\nassume).  \r\n\r\noh, and we should have gone to college.  some of us \r\ndidn\\\'t.  we couldn\\\'t resist the glitter of the town that \r\nhas drawn people since 1848 and the last gold rush.  \r\n\r\nwhat do you expect out of a city that attracted nothing but \r\ncapitalistic entrepreneurs even back then?  \r\n\r\nyes, you aren\\\'t in san francisco, but much of the burn you \r\nfeel eminates from here.  it spread like a virus.  (no pun \r\nintended)\r\n\r\nyes, hackers and spammers have scared people off, but it is \r\npart of the electronic frontier that excites people.  it\\\'s \r\nlike cowboys and indians all over again.  but, do hackers \r\nreally create the viruses or is it mcaffee?  hrm, i wonder.\r\n\r\ni dunno auntie.  you can sit and worry about all of this, \r\nor you can reach out and help people who are in need when \r\nthe time comes.  i would just brace yourself and ride with \r\nit, because in my opinion.. it is going to be fun.',1,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(6204,1466,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','<p>I probably would\\\'ve been one of the people to say \\\'no\\\'. \r\nYou say that seems ludicrous to you, but (from my \r\nperspective at least) saying \\\'yes\\\' is just as crazy when \r\nsome things are taken into consideration.</p>\r\n<p>I don\\\'t believe in the freedom of speech; I believe that \r\nwhat we like to think of as \\\'freedom\\\' is nothing more than \r\nthe indifference of a power-monopoly which can rarely be \r\nthreatened by anything we say, and when it is threatened \r\n(or more likely: annoyed), the system finds ways to filter \r\nout what it doesn\\\'t want to hear.</p>\r\n<p>I don\\\'t believe in rights; to me the idea no longer has \r\nany meaning. I think having rights leads the public into a \r\nvery false sense of security and I think it makes societies \r\nweak. \\\'Rights\\\' were originally concieved of in a time when \r\nthe power of the government was precarious and when the \r\npossibility popular revolution was a real one. Since the \r\nrulers and the ruled could threaten eachother, it became \r\nadvantageous for both parties to draw up a treaty (a \r\nconstitution and bill of rights) and work together. This \r\nmakes sense, not because anyone is \\\'free\\\', but because the \r\ntrue source of power in any system (violence or the threat \r\nof violence) is held by both parties.</p>\r\n<p>But we don\\\'t live in that world anymore. We\\\'ve become \r\ntotally removed from the source of true power. \\\'Rights\\\' \r\nhave no power beyond their capacity to be enforced, and we \r\nlive in an age where the public is uninformed, divided, \r\ncomplacent, unarmed and ultimately powerless. Thinking \r\nthat \\\'rights\\\' mean anything becomes ridiculous when you \r\ntake this into account -- it is like thinking that between \r\ntwo parties, one extremely powerful and one extremely weak, \r\nthat the stronger party will refrain from changing the ways \r\nit enforces and interprets the original agreement to suit \r\nits own interests for the sake of being \\\"nice\\\" or \\\"fair\\\". \r\nAnd I certainly don\\\'t believe that.</p>\r\n<p>So I guess my point is that, for the above reasons, I \r\ndon\\\'t take things like peaceful protests, handing out \r\nflyers, etc very seriously at all. I\\\'m not saying those \r\nthings are totally in vain, I suppose it\\\'s better than \r\nignoring our problems, and I certainly admire the awareness \r\nand dedication it takes to do those things consistently, \r\nbut it\\\'s not something I feel is effective enough to make \r\nme want to participate in any way.</p>',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(6205,1462,'2001-07-31 03:36:30',0,'cyantist','<p>first off, i wanted to tell you that i really appreciate \r\nthis post.  these kinds of posts are what drew me to \r\nswinney in the beginning.  i\\\'m begging you to keep writing \r\nhere.  fuck.. just keep writing.</p>\r\n<br>\r\n<p>this is a personal question, but do you mind if i ask \r\nwho the dead woman\\\'s brushes are?</P>\r\n<p>i know it is hard to believe that anything in this world \r\ncan be changed, but i can attest that i can be.  they \r\nhappen as small miracles.  perhaps, you can donate your \r\ntime or your art to cancer foundations and do everything \r\nyou can to help people living with cancer have better \r\nlives.  there may be no cure, but helping sure beats them \r\ndying lonely or full of desperation.</p>',1,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(6206,1466,'2001-07-31 03:44:32',0,'cyantist','question:<br>\r\n<p>do you think that perhaps the beliefs that you stated \r\nabove make you apathetic?</p>\r\n<p>from what you have explained to me, you are saying that \r\nyou\\\'ve pretty much given up on the idea that we can have \r\nany sort of say over what happens in our day to day lives \r\nand that we are living as calm and complacent cows.  i \r\ndon\\\'t disagree with you, btw.. i believe this is the case \r\nfor most americans.  i witnessed it today.  so, isn\\\'t that \r\npart of our problem?  people have stopped caring.\r\n</P>\r\n<p>when i was 16 or so.. i exited a movie theater with my \r\nfriend after watching a thought provoking film, and the \r\nfirst thing i saw after leaving was a safeway.  i turned to \r\nmy friend and i said, \\\"what do you think the public would \r\ndo if i blew up every convenience in this town.. starting \r\nwith that one.\\\"  \\\"do you think they would get up from \r\nbehind their television and actually do something about it?\\\"\r\ni came to the conclusion that we are self centered as \r\npeople and as long as we don\\\'t feel the burn of our lack of \r\nfreedom, we just sort of accept it and trudge on.  it isn\\\'t \r\nthat bad now, but the  more complacent we become and the \r\nmore we forget our constitutional rights.. the more we give \r\nup the meaning of what it means to be free.</p>\r\n<p>i\\\'m sorry you feel this way, and i wonder what path led \r\nyou to this belief.  i wish i could light a fire in you to \r\ncare more about the world around you.</p>',1,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(6207,1466,'2001-07-31 03:53:00',0,' cyantist','<p>btw.. i do believe you are right with your statement, \r\nbut i\\\'m just saying that we shouldn\\\'t sit around and do \r\nnotihng about it.  i understand that this may be regarded \r\nas a losing battle.. but i don\\\'t give up because we can \r\nmake a little difference here and there.  we\\\'re not going \r\nto change the entire system and make it effective for \r\neveryone.  however, it scares the shit out of me that a \r\nperson like dmitri can get arrested for something he \r\ndiscovered and talked about.  he\\\'s not a criminal.  we \r\ncan\\\'t let the \\\"power\\\" get away with this.</p>',1,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(6208,1458,'2001-07-31 03:55:20',0,'cyantist','hrm, interesting.  perhaps you can describe in more detail \r\nwhat this means to you and how you got there.. etc.  i\\\'m \r\ncurious.  how did you meet these people?',1,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(6209,1457,'2001-07-31 03:56:54',0,'cyantist','mmm.. nice.',1,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(6210,1456,'2001-07-31 03:57:59',0,'cyantist','more detail!  what did you end up doing?  that sounds like \r\na fun trip!',1,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(6211,1449,'2001-07-31 04:00:30',0,'cyantist','wow, i wish i could have frank conversations with my mom \r\nlike that.  my mother and i can\\\'t talk about anything and \r\nit makes me happy to know that there are great \r\nrelationships out there that foster this sort of \r\ncommunication.',1,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(6212,1449,'2001-07-31 04:00:31',0,'cyantist','wow, i wish i could have frank conversations with my mom \r\nlike that.  my mother and i can\\\'t talk about anything and \r\nit makes me happy to know that there are great \r\nrelationships out there that foster this sort of \r\ncommunication.',1,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(6213,1445,'2001-07-31 04:06:28',0,'cyantist','<p>this is pretty cute, but perhaps you could try \r\napproaching the relationship with less drugs :)  i noticed \r\nthat the entire story seemed to revolved around drugs and \r\nhow you interact with this girl on them.  perhaps i\\\'m \r\nreading it wrong and it was just your birthday.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>she probably does like you.  have you asked?</p>',1,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(6214,1456,'2001-07-31 04:17:48',0,'kat','this really dig this tyler post. mostly because it lacked \r\ndetail. not everything needs to be held under a microscope.',1,0,0,0,'32.102.90.214','en'),(6215,1467,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','for my part, i\\\'ve stopped wearing underwear. that way, i\\\'m \r\nnot spending money or resources washing them, buying new \r\nones, etc.  i would go bare-ass naked if they\\\'d let me.  but \r\nno.  and they say this is a free country.  i could \r\nunderstand if i had a less-than-perfect body. sure, they\\\'d \r\nwant to me stay covered up then. but not this buff brooding \r\ngreek god who walks the earth among them.  just cause their \r\nstuff ain\\\'t tight enough. i encourage everyone to go \r\nknickerless.  it\\\'ll make you smile.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.10.36','en'),(6216,1467,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','and they say i\\\'m not right. pshaw. the nerve.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.10.36','en'),(6217,1458,'2001-07-31 05:38:05',0,'Treetop','Well, it all began with a quest for three pounds of \r\nkindness...  Which never came into view.  The hippies were \r\nmy friends (Jas & Hops).  The trippy psycho girl (dawn) was \r\npicked up at a liquer store by Hops.  So all three of us \r\nare sitting on the side of the road way out in the country \r\nfor four hours waiting on three pounds.  We get the hell \r\nout of there after the crrazy girl starts buggin out.  Hops \r\ndecides to hitch to Arcada. Jas and I take some molly and \r\nend up safely in San Fran by daylight.  Jas is a great \r\ndriver\r\n\r\nWhat a daze...  ',1,0,0,0,'172.171.92.41','en'),(6218,78,'2002-03-05 20:17:36',17,'austin to leonard','get the fuck out of my archives you hozer.\r\n',6,0,0,0,'64.174.154.180','en'),(6219,1458,'2001-07-31 05:40:57',0,'Treetop','Oh yea, thanks for adding the title.  I was a little spaced \r\nout.  My synapse is working fine now :)',1,0,0,0,'172.171.92.41','en'),(6220,1467,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','everything will be fine. it\\\'s just fine.',1,0,0,0,'64.10.134.51','en'),(6221,1467,'2001-07-31 06:39:23',0,'cyantist','- takes of underwear.  *meep*',1,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(6222,1456,'2001-07-31 06:42:37',0,'cyantist','heh, and you don\\\'t have to assume that i am.  i\\\'m just \r\nexcited about the post and wanted more information.  rar!',3,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(6223,1456,'2001-07-31 06:43:09',0,'cyantist','rar i tell you.. RAR!',1,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(6224,1458,'2001-07-31 06:59:07',0,'punchline','<br><br>... so then the hippy says to the rabbi, he sez, \r\nwhaddya mean you only take tips!?',6,0,0,0,'64.10.134.51','en'),(6225,1467,'2003-05-10 16:09:14',79,'yeti','everything is wrong.',1,0,0,0,'64.51.232.102','en'),(6226,1456,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','\\\"oil pan\\\" is the other good excuse. use that one if you\\\'ve \r\nalready used \\\"fuel pump\\\".',3,0,0,0,'64.10.134.51','en'),(6227,1461,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to austin','you are condescending and irreverent. ',0,0,0,0,'216.175.103.2','en'),(6228,1461,'2001-07-31 07:53:27',0,'chi chi AKA goat','<br>\r\nthat\\\'s the last time i let either you (OMS) or egg tell our \r\ntale. you left out some facts:<br>\r\n1.jayperOhOh did kiddie-pee-pee in the lake<br>\r\n2.buellah\\\'s <i> gravel guard</i> came off. (BTW the \r\naudi people can\\\'t fix it for weeks up on weeks, let\\\'s \r\nhope the ducktape tolds)<br>\r\n3.OMS is a manly man cause he fixed my car, while egg \r\nand jayperOhOh are our weakest links, <i> \r\ngood-bye</i><br>\r\n4.<b><i> I </b></i>drove for hours and hours <br>\r\n5.i made primative rock structures<br>\r\n6. OMS almost drowned trying to kiss underwater while \r\nsimultaneously trying not to ingest lake-kiddie-pee-pee \r\nwater<br>\r\n7. my ass was sore from driving. oh and i have a bruise \r\non my knee<br>\r\n8. you have no beduin brethren my white friend.<br>\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.172.44.162','en'),(6229,1458,'2001-07-31 08:50:29',0,'treetop','We are talking about a metemorphosis.  We are talking about \r\ngoing from a caterpillar to butterfly.  We are talking \r\nabout how to become a butterfly.\r\nI mean:  The caterpillar isn\\\'t walking around\r\nSaying:  \\\"Man, I\\\'ll soon be a butterfly.\\\"\r\nBecause:  As long as he\\\'s busy being a caterpillar he cant \r\nbe a butterfly.\r\n\r\nIt\\\'s only when caterpillarness is done that one starts to \r\nbe a butterfly.  And that again is part of this paradox...\r\nYou cant rip away caterpillarness.\r\n-----\r\nThe butterfly:\r\n\r\nI am without form\r\nwithout limit\r\nbeyond space beyond time\r\nI am in everything\r\neverything is me\r\nI am the bliss of the universe,\r\neveryting am I\r\n',1,0,0,0,'152.163.207.137','en'),(6230,1471,'2001-07-31 08:54:43',0,'kat','the first night of sleeping in one\\\'s own bed after travel \r\nis almost a religious experience. it must be done alone, \r\nwith great ceremony.',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.22','en'),(6231,1466,'2001-07-31 09:10:37',0,'moebius\\\' turn to rant','<p>I guess I stand somewhere between Cyan and Moll on this \r\nissue: I\\\'m not going to go so far as to say \\\"rights\\\" mean \r\nnothing, but I also don\\\'t see much effectiveness in the \r\ngarden variety peaceful protest, either.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I suppose I picked up this jaded attitude after four \r\nyears at UC Santa Cruz, where just about every day there \r\nwas a student march for this or that, maybe about 3,453 \r\ndifferent political action groups anyone could belong to \r\n(who cares if half of them contradict the others?), and \r\nstudent occupations of the administration building were so \r\ncommon they became part of the daily routine. And did the \r\nworld at large change? Oh, perhaps, in a grand unified \r\nchaos theory sort of way. A militant vegan PAC flapped its \r\nwings somewhere in the Santa Cruz forest, and over in \r\nBoston a family decided to see what would happen if they \r\nstopped eating steak and hamburgers for awhile.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I ended up in San Francisco a bit tired of career \r\nprotesters who rail against \\\"the system\\\" in the effort to \r\nreverse injustice and \\\"raise the city\\\'s consciousness.\\\" In \r\nthe end it often seems like so much chatter, so much \r\nprosetlyzing and preaching. And this sucks, because there\\\'s \r\nanother side of me that <i>believes</i> in standing up to \r\ninjustice. I guess I just think it\\\'s best if you do that in \r\na constructive, informative, concrete way.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If you want to impress me, DO SOMETHING TANGIBLE. Donate \r\nyour time to a homeless shelter. Teach kids(and adults, for \r\nthat matter), to read. Go to law school, pass the bar, take \r\na vow of poverty, and become a tenant rights lawyer. Get a \r\ndegree in architecture, get involved in urban planning and \r\ncity politics, and see to it that the space set aside for \r\nyet another Home Depot gets turned into sustainible housing \r\ninstead. Build daycare centers for disadvantaged children. \r\nProvide emotional and physical support for AIDS and cancer \r\npatients. Recycle. And so forth.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Then again--on the other hand--there does seem to be \r\nevidence that if you keep turning up the volume of those \r\nmarches, eventually someone notices--as in the example of \r\nlast week\\\'s anti-globalization riots in Europe. But the \r\ntangible result there is still negligible. How soon \\\'till \r\nthese protests are turned into the next hit reality TV \r\nshow? (\\\"Which protester will *not* survive \r\ntonight\\\'s \\\'instructional action?\\\' Tune in at 8 and find \r\nout!\\\")</p>',3,0,0,0,'205.184.158.107','en'),(6232,1467,'2002-03-15 00:17:55',129,'moebius','<p>and yet, every day, that lazy ol\\\' sun keeps rolling on \r\nthough the sky (even when it seems to be overcast, natch). \r\nHow can this be?</p>',1,0,0,0,'205.184.158.107','en'),(6233,1466,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Hedaijha Moll','<p>My beliefs might make me seem pathetic to someone like \r\nyou, and possibly to others here, since \\\"saving the world\\\" \r\n(in some way) is a value that\\\'s probably shared by a lot of \r\nthe people here. It\\\'s a view I can appreciate and respect, \r\nbut it\\\'s not one that I can share.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It\\\'s not that I\\\'m indifferent. My problem just isn\\\'t \r\nwith any particular issue -- pollution, globalization, \r\ncivil rights, animal rights, etc -- I have a problem with \r\nthe fundamental course our civilization has taken in the \r\npast few centuries. Therefore, doing anything to make it \r\nlast any longer would be dishonest and self-defeating.</p>\r\n',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(6234,1472,'2001-07-31 13:30:35',0,'hh','\\\"all over your body\\\" i meant. oops.',1,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(6235,1457,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','ooooh...your words are so BIG...',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.35','en'),(6236,1472,'2001-07-31 14:11:12',0,'ty','must they be SO beautiful? sometimes it\\\'s just surreal.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.35','en'),(6237,1466,'2001-07-31 14:14:50',0,'ty','I think that we have rights. One of the things that \r\ninspired me to be a lawyer was the victories over the \r\ntobacco companies. It may not be easy, but the rules apply \r\nto everyone. Look at the FBI. Look at the crackdowns on the \r\nIRS. Look at Bill Clinton. We have a great system of laws. \r\nNo one can break them for long.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.35','en'),(6238,1472,'2001-07-31 14:17:20',0,'woolfwood','such beauty does exist.',1,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(6239,1459,'2001-07-31 14:26:32',0,'ty','I would move to Florida. That sounded like a great idea. Or \r\ngo to school, school is the key to happiness and success. \r\nOr at least success. If you can\\\'t be happy with success, \r\nyou suck.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.35','en'),(6240,1463,'2001-07-31 14:28:09',0,'ty','maybe you are a prisoner BECAUSE you don\\\'t like being told \r\nyou can change things.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.35','en'),(6241,1463,'2001-07-31 14:41:17',0,'wolfwood','maybe its hard for people to accept that sometimes change \r\ncan\\\'t/won\\\'t happen.',2,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(6242,1472,'2001-07-31 15:02:18',0,'wb','nice fonts',0,0,0,0,'151.197.238.30','en'),(6243,1459,'2001-07-31 15:49:21',0,'fool','I thought that once, about school - so I went back. In fact, \r\nI\\\'m there now, in class. I\\\'m older than any of the other \r\nstudents, and the grad student pretending to teach us has a \r\nvery limited mastery of the English language.  <br> School \r\nmay well be one key to success, but unless you have the \r\nluxury of studying something you love, rather than simply \r\nsomething that you could get the funding for, it can be a \r\ndemoralizing experience. <br> Or maybe I\\\'m just too old for \r\nthis, and missed the point, eh? ',2,0,0,0,'156.56.128.11','en'),(6244,1461,'2001-07-31 15:54:06',0,'szajic','it\\\'s not really crucial, I know, but I think it\\\'s kind of \r\ninteresting.  I asked google and its good friend jeeves about \r\nplankton and sperm.  as it turns out, human sperm are more or \r\nless pretty fixed in size: about <a href=\\\"http://\r\nwww.cellsalive.com/howbig.htm\\\">60 microns</a> long, say 10 \r\nmicrons for the head and 50 microns for the tail.\r\n<p>\r\nplankton on the other hand can be <a href=\\\"http://\r\nwww.chebucto.ns.ca/Science/SWCS/plankton.html\\\">almost any \r\nsize</a>.  while what we typically think of as plankton are \r\nlarger than sperm, there are important \\\'nanoplankton\\\' which \r\nare 0.2-2 microns long (really small!)\r\n<p>\r\nponder this next time you\\\'re doing fun sexual stuff with \r\nsomeone in a reasonably large body of water.  sploosh.\r\n',3,0,0,0,'130.91.196.77','en'),(6245,1445,'2001-07-31 16:13:25',0,'SSJ3 Gostu','ask? i can\\\'t just ask, that would be breaking the rules. :)\r\n\r\nbut, yeah, it was just my birthday-',1,0,0,0,'208.58.87.82','en'),(6246,1472,'2001-07-31 16:17:58',0,'kat','okay...sorry but this chick is frighteningly skinny. i love \r\nthe waifs, but whatever happened to voluptuousness? must we \r\nall look like crack addicts with oversized lips to be \r\nconsidered beautiful?',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.62','en'),(6247,1461,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to szajic','the VERY REASON i posted that was so that an industrious person such as \r\nyourself would get me the answers. god bless america and the internet!!!<br>\r\n-satisfied customer.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.103.2','en'),(6248,1472,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','it takes all sorts to make a world. some men are afraid of flesh. some women are \r\nafraid of food. what can you do?',0,0,0,0,'216.175.103.2','en'),(6249,1472,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>the most beautiful woman i\\\'ve ever seen is 5\\\"10, \r\n150lbs, and has enough muscle to almost beat me arm-\r\nwrestling. she\\\'s no waif, and wuite honestly, i\\\'ve never \r\nseen a more \\\'ideal\\\' looking lady. just my two cents.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6250,1461,'2001-07-31 16:57:03',0,'leonard to john cage','4\\\'33\\\" ',0,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(6251,1472,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<br>I briefly dated a girl once who was 5\\\'10\\\" and weighed \r\n125lbs.  At dinner she would typically eat all of her meal \r\nand some of mine.  I have a ballet instructor who is about \r\n100 lbs. of pure wiry muscle.  She\\\'s frequently accused of \r\nbeing anorexic, but she seems to eat her own body weight in \r\nfood every day.<P>\r\nI get really hot for waifish women, as it seems many other \r\npeople here do too.  I have a tendency to think of these \r\nthings in terms of biology/evolution.  Being rail thin in \r\nmodern society (much like being more \\\'voluptious\\\' in \r\nearlier times) is a status symbol.  It means that you have \r\nthe money and the free time to eat healthy (i.e. non-fatty) \r\nfoods and hit the gym to work out.  (In earlier times, \r\nbeing chubby was cherished because it meant you had enough \r\nmoney to eat.)  Biologically, we want to make babies with \r\nsomeone who is healthy and socially important.  Being thin \r\nis a symbol for both of these things.</P><P>I love this \r\npost, btw.  I\\\'ve always dreamed of writing poetry all over \r\na woman\\\'s body and eating sushi off her belly.</P>',4,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(6252,1471,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>i saw a vancouver police squad beat a homeless man to the\r\nground and start kicking him.  i\\\'m not sure what the\r\nhomeless man did.</p>\r\n\r\n<P>a woman next to me said, \\\"look, they are beating up that\r\nhomeless man.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>then they were gone.</P>',3,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(6253,1459,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>sorry for the delay, essemar. i put your number in \r\nmy phone then went out of town for the week, ack.  gonna be \r\naround later this week or next??</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6254,1471,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<br>Whoa... that\\\'s trippy.  I\\\'m always listening to people \r\ntell me how much cleaner and better Canadian cities are \r\nthan American, then I hear something like this.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(6255,1472,'2001-07-31 17:33:41',0,'ghost','<p>\\\"Being thin is a symbol for both of these things.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>there is a woman i use to see in town. i did not know \r\nher personally but she was part of the crowd i ran in. she \r\nwas the flame that all moths came too. the kind of person \r\nothers gravitated towards. she had a dirty mouth and was a \r\nnasty bitch, but she was sexuality incarnate. Cyndi was her \r\nname. and she was not a waif...or even close to it. i don\\\'t \r\nknow if other people saw in her what i saw, but i have to \r\nthink they did. you couldn\\\'t help it. they way she wore her \r\nlipstick, and the messiness of her hair. sexy curvy flesh \r\nshe was.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>i have noticed that most men are intimidated by fleshy \r\nwomen. 170lbs of raw muscle and the right womanly \r\nproportions to match. yea i have better definition and \r\nbigger biceps than most guys i find myself with. i am \r\nnovelty...and have yet to discover the man who truly adores \r\nmy gender bending disposition.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><i>[you all have been brainwashed]</i></p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'32.102.64.62','en'),(6256,1470,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Moon Moll','<p>I think I fear immortality, or the idea of immortality, \r\nmore than death. I like the idea of being intimately \r\ntemporary, of coming and going without effort or fear.</p>',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(6257,1468,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<P>I\\\'ll dance with you Deb.  I may not be the person you \r\nwant, but I\\\'ll never say \\\'no,\\\' especially if the music is \r\nbeautiful.  I just love to dance, so no matter who asks, I \r\nwill always say... <I>\\\'yes\\\'</I></P>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(6258,1472,'2001-07-31 17:47:37',0,'chapulin','not brainwashed at all. just a different taste that yours. \r\nwhy is it so hard to respect someone\\\'s preferance?',3,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(6259,1472,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Quth Moll','<p>I like girls who are small but could still beat me up. \r\nEspecially when they have dark hair and short tempers.</p>\r\n',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(6260,1474,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','i like \\\"rodential\\\".  ew.',2,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(6261,1474,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>\r\n<tt>\r\nevery dog in New<br>\r\nYork City shits on my side<br>\r\nwalk my front door stinks<br>\r\n<br>\r\nwhy can\\\'t yuppie man<br>\r\nstoop to pick up the shit from<br>\r\nhis beloved Spot?<br>\r\n<br>\r\nbetter he stain his<br>\r\narmani-esque suit than to<br>\r\nstink up my hood, yo<br>\r\n<br>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6262,1470,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','It wouldn\\\'t be so bad to re-invent yourself each one hundred\r\nyears or so.  I hope re-incarnation pulls through because I\r\nyearn to experience the future as much as I yearn for a\r\nlarge glass of cold water right now.<br><br>I wish to see\r\nhow things are going to unfold.  Perhaps as I age, I will\r\nthrow away these wishes however, for the moment, this is how\r\nI feel.<br><br>Maybe it also has something to do with that\r\ndesire to leave your mark on the world.  What better way to\r\ndo that than to simply never <b>leave</b>?',3,0,0,0,'64.229.76.128','en'),(6263,1474,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<img src=\\\"http://www.splendidezine.com/reviews/jun-4-01/\r\ncharm.gif\\\" align=\\\"right\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" width=\\\"180\\\" height=\\\"179\\\">\r\n',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(6264,1472,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<br>Yeah, Mollie, I think I\\\'d dig a chick like that too.<P>\r\nBtw, I spent two years of my life with a girl who is 6\\\'2\\\", \r\n170 lbs, first-string college b-ball player, and able to \r\ndrink anybody you know under the table.  She was soft and \r\ncurvy and could kick my ass.  I was totally in love with \r\nher.</P><P>The other explanation for America\\\'s love of \r\nwaifish women is simply Ghost\\\'s comment concerning \r\nbrainwashing.  We are so inondated with images from the \r\nmedia of beautiful = anorexically skinny that we can\\\'t help \r\nbut buy into the propoganda Hollywood deluges us with.</p>\r\n<P>Yes, everyone has different tastes, but you have to \r\nadmit that certain universals must exist.  Even though I \r\nprefer tall and thin, I know I could find beauty in short \r\nand squat.</P>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(6265,1472,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','how l