ed?  that \r\nwould make sense.. actually.',1,0,0,0,'24.221.161.16','en'),(6339,1485,'2001-08-02 13:59:54',0,'will','I once married a girl from Rancho Cucamonga.<br />\r\nI once had sex in the back of a van on a dirt road \r\nsomewhere in or around Hesperia.<br />\r\nThat doesn\\\'t help you any... but, you know, places and \r\ntimes.',4,0,0,0,'198.214.178.232','en'),(6340,1484,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>\r\n<img src=\\\"http://www.rhodamine.org/swinney.gif\\\">',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6341,1484,'2001-08-02 15:52:32',0,'ghost','i dig jim\\\'s banner, like a bad rag to read on Sunday \r\nmorning. but then...how could one resist the tempting \r\ncurves of peter\\\'s el camino. hubba hubba.',1,0,0,0,'32.102.109.141','en'),(6342,14,'2001-08-02 18:23:08',0,'dimbleberry junior','it probably has your name on it because whoever wrote it put your name on it.',0,0,0,1,'194.213.50.221','en'),(6343,1482,'2001-08-02 16:36:01',0,'jo','hi, i cook, sew, quilt, do crafty projects. i don\\\'t \r\nconsider any of these to be \\\"women\\\'s work,\\\" i don\\\'t do them \r\nbecause i feel that it makes me more feminine. they\\\'re \r\n<b>fun</b> and <b>neat</b> and they make me <b>happy</b>.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(6344,1482,'2001-08-02 16:37:45',0,'jo','although i couldn\\\'t keep a clean house if you held a gun to \r\nmy head. <BR>\r\nif everything i own is on my floor, at least i don\\\'t have \r\nto go looking for it.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(6345,1487,'2001-08-02 17:02:06',0,'green','you were real\r\nand not too many people are. they can see through it ( \r\nalthough it seems now as if all of us are working for a \r\ncorporation)',1,0,0,0,'208.179.105.129','en'),(6346,1488,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>i like this.  i stare out at the landscape and read the\r\nmoon\\\'s reflections often.  one of the beauties of santa cruz\r\nis the many opportunities to absorb nature.  there are hills\r\nand beaches, trees.  lots of high points and points of no\r\nobstruction.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>egg was here last night.  she was not here for long.  i\r\nwanted to show her some of the nice places i have found\r\nhere.  we did not have time though.  and off egg goes to new\r\nyork on saturday, leaving me here to find more places.</P>\r\n\r\n',2,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(6347,1489,'2001-08-02 17:12:32',0,'kat','wow. hug? beer? email? i feel for you. you and Green. ',1,0,0,0,'32.102.109.141','en'),(6348,1489,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt><i>uh, uhm, oh, itch, stratch, uhhh, too close to \r\nhome...</i></tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6349,1485,'2001-08-02 17:27:19',0,'leonard','i saw a dirty strip show in ontario, ca. i still feel dirty.',6,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(6350,1489,'2001-08-02 17:32:50',0,'BrewGuru99','God I\\\'m so sorry.',0,0,0,0,'63.68.91.141','en'),(6351,1484,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','i cant really get enough of pale white ass, im sorry.',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(6352,1488,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','i only want to see places in santa cruz from the back of \r\na motorcycle.',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(6353,1485,'2001-08-02 20:24:19',0,'leonard','<p>here\\\'s the <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://showerhead.org/the_party/party.html\\\">dirty</a> \r\n        party.</p>',4,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(6354,1484,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P><IMG SRC=\"http://swinney.org/gal/banners/rev_bgwhite3k.gif\">\r\n<BR>\r\n<BR>\r\n<IMG SRC=\"http://swinney.org/gal/banners/rev4k.gif\">\r\n</P>',3,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(6355,1485,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','people who know me, take note: I want a policeman to \r\nstrip for me on my birthday. wherever I happen to be on \r\nthat day. and i want him to be LEAN and BUFF. and a  \r\nreal policeman. a pro. you cant just send steve5 in a \r\nuniform.',0,0,0,0,'4.18.197.3','en'),(6356,1491,'2001-08-02 22:29:52',0,'kat','there is a point of no return driving this road. the \r\nhighway over the hill. if you drive it enough it becomes an \r\naddiction. the g\\\'s of each downhill curve calling your \r\nname. daring you to push it faster. harder. longer. it\\\'s \r\nthe rush you crave. there is a point where you can let go. \r\nwhere the machine underneath you knows. knows your next \r\nturn, your next breath, your next thought. this is the \r\nplace where danger and life become one. where you say to \r\nyourself...<i>\\\'i am beyond death and not of this world\\\'</i>',4,0,0,1,'32.102.91.115','en'),(6357,1490,'2001-08-02 21:20:38',0,'BrewGuru99','I try so hard. I want to be good at this life. I want to \r\nmake the world change its path for the better. I want to \r\nsee my passions grow and work and progress. I want to be in \r\nlove and stay in love.<BR>\r\n<BR>\r\nI\\\'m still learning.',0,0,0,0,'63.68.91.141','en'),(6358,985,'2001-08-02 21:24:39',0,'B-p','Hi I\\\'m B, I\\\'m an INFP and probably a 4. Note though (and \r\nthis is the point that I\\\'d like to make) that I\\\'m at the \r\nextreme end of IN, and right near the middle with the FP (I \r\nwas an INTJ when I was last tested in High School) The \r\ndanger with the Kiersey/M-B test is that it can polarise \r\nthings into F or T, when in reality its a continuum, \r\nslightly F, mostly F, etc.\r\np.s. O, notice what you said: \\\"i respect, or even \r\n<EM>envy<EM> people who can believe so totally in \r\nsomething, like some people do with religion.\\\" Is envy not \r\nthe dark side of a 4? (yeah ok so was it just a figure of \r\nspeech?) My own beliefs tend to be somewhat fluid, but \r\ncertain factors are quite fixed, namely the existence of \r\nsomething that can\\\'t be percieved with the 5 senses, but \r\nwhich, when understood, makes the universe make sense.\r\n',4,0,0,0,'202.49.180.133','en'),(6359,1491,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>it does not take much interaction with egg to realize\r\nmost of her perceptions revolve around sex.  she ran into\r\nher cousin\\\'s uncle at <A\r\nHREF=\\\"http://saturncafe.com/\\\">saturn cafe</A> and mentioned\r\nthat she thought the man\\\'s brother\\\'s nervous energy seemed\r\n\\\"really perverse\\\".  probably it is just nervous energy.  but\r\nwho can tell?</P>\r\n\r\n<P>jayperOhOh, her roomate and best friend is always\r\nalerting her audiences that everything egg says should be\r\ntaken with a grain of sex.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>if i am wrong, sue me.</P>',3,0,0,1,'205.179.19.31','en'),(6360,1491,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','that was wrong of me to say about the brother-in-law\\\'s \r\nuncle. but i think it\\\'s more just that everything is \r\ngenuinely about sex and Im the only one on this \r\nblooody earth who aknowledges it! ',0,0,0,1,'4.18.197.3','en'),(6361,1491,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','i feel dirty today!\r\n',0,0,0,1,'63.195.92.218','en'),(6362,1490,'2001-08-02 22:01:48',0,'deb','love is enigmatic. embrace what you can actually touch.\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'152.163.213.201','en'),(6363,1490,'2001-08-02 23:30:44',0,'kat','the learning never ends. and neither does the trying. the \r\nbest you can shoot for is \\\'knowing\\\' that this is so.',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.10','en'),(6364,1485,'2001-08-03 00:36:26',0,'felicity','Care package on the way.  Granted, it\\\'s just stuff I had \r\nlying around the office, but the coolest stuff I could \r\nfind.<UL TYPE=square>Here\\\'s what\\\'s coming:<li \r\ntype=square>one package microwave popcorn<li>two sticks of \r\nchewing gum<li>random condiments from my condiment \r\ndrawer<li>a pack of latte mix (pretty gross...sorry)<li>a \r\nyard sale sign (in case you need to make some extra money to \r\npay that phone bill)<li>a sheet of little metallic star \r\nstickers (i stick \\\'em on stuff to make me feel like i\\\'ve \r\naccomplished something great, a-la-grade school)<li>two \r\ncrayons (one should never be without a crayon or two)<li>a \r\nblack legal pad (complete with notes from my last two monday \r\nmorning meetings) and a \\\"green\\\" pen with which to write \r\nfantastical stories upon the tablet.</ul>\r\nSorry, no soap or bobby pins...but i hope it helps.<br>\r\n<img src=\\\"http://www.infoblvd.net/tribadv/cp.jpg\\\">',2,0,0,0,'216.42.66.175','en'),(6365,1485,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>i am sending you some pamplets such as, \\\"Is It\r\nDepression?\\\" and \\\"Dating Dangers\\\".</P>\r\n\r\n<P>knowledge is power.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>P.S., i am putting in one on \\\"Internet Dating\\\" because\r\nyou should just have it.  also one on \\\"21st Century\r\nDrinking\\\" and \\\"Self Esteem\\\" and \\\"Rave and Club Drugs\\\".</P>\r\n\r\n<P>we must stay informed.</P>',3,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(6366,1485,'2001-08-03 02:08:01',0,'kat','<p>i have the soap part covered...and some other doodads. \r\ndoodads are always fun. you\\\'ll make me smile if you send \r\nsomething back.</p>\r\n\r\n<P>1840 41st Ave. Suite 102-PMB120<br>\r\nCapitola, CA 95010</p>',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.243','en'),(6367,1482,'2001-08-03 02:18:35',0,'lou to jo','testify, girlfriend. <br><br>(also, i loathe that some \r\nactivities are considered \\\"womanly\\\" and others \\\"manly\\\" just \r\nbecause a greater percentage of women/men participate in \r\nthem.  i do not approve of that at all.)<BR><BR>(that was \r\nnot a criticism, btw, just a statement of me.)<BR><BR>(you \r\nknow.)',4,0,0,0,'165.247.53.42','en'),(6368,985,'2001-08-03 05:52:53',0,'B-p','please excuse the missing closing EM tag. My blood sugar \r\nwas low.',5,0,0,0,'202.49.180.133','en'),(6369,985,'2001-08-03 05:53:42',0,'B-p','</EM>',5,0,0,0,'202.49.180.133','en'),(6370,71,'2001-08-03 06:33:42',0,'alanna','<P>\r\nwhere above los angeles?\r\n</P>\r\n<P>\r\nyou should go to <A \r\nHREF=\\\"http://www.mentryville.org/\\\">mentryville</A>.&nbsp; \r\nit\\\'s a ghost town, and there are mountain lions and \r\nrattlesnakes.&nbsp; bring a friend. =)',3,0,0,0,'198.182.157.102','en'),(6371,1485,'2001-08-03 10:34:33',0,'green','whosoever just placed their addy in the hands of public \r\nawareness, let it be known, I will mail thee such things as \r\nsuper absorbant tampons, bobby pins, drawings, deoderant \r\n(only halfway used), some TP ( now I have some), lube, and \r\nsome chapstick if I.m slightly burgeois-ee on that day..( \r\ni.m trying to say  BOO-szchee....you know Richie....what I \r\ncall Esssemar on a good day.\r\n\r\noh and bye the way\r\n\r\nHEY RAT BASTARD!',1,0,0,0,'66.12.171.62','en'),(6372,1493,'2001-08-03 10:39:36',0,'green','wow...that.s a tale of TWO Tens',1,0,0,0,'66.12.171.62','en'),(6373,1490,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt><i>\\\"And it is not that they contain so much \r\npassion.... but that they deserve it\\\"</i>.  Thanks for \r\nputting that to words.  I\\\'m going to paraphrase you the \r\nnext time my better half questions why i have such emotion \r\ninvolving her- someone should be passionate about her, and \r\nif its not she, herself, then let it be me.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6374,1493,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i thoroughly enjoyed reading this, for what its \r\nworth...</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6375,1493,'2001-08-03 12:36:20',0,'by the way:','one dollar can also buy you a roll of <a \r\nhref=\\\"www.shitbegone.com\\\">Shit-be-Gone</a> toilet paper.  ',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6376,1493,'2001-08-03 15:03:59',0,'felicity','\\\"seeds were laid\\\"...I must have been pretty tired when I \r\nwrote that.  \\\"planted\\\" is a much better verb.  Glad you \r\nliked it, though.\r\n',2,0,0,0,'216.42.67.145','en'),(6377,1493,'2001-08-03 15:31:59',0,'chapulin',' what about the father? is there a sequel coming? nice \r\nstory.',1,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(6378,1493,'2001-08-03 16:14:51',0,'felicity','I\\\'ll have to work on the sequels.  Right now, the father is \r\nan amazingly supportive part of both his son\\\'s and my life. \r\n You can, however, read a more recent chapter in my \r\nmotherhood experience <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=1430.\r\ntxt\\\">here</a>. (...if you missed it the first time)',2,0,0,0,'216.42.67.145','en'),(6379,1496,'2001-08-03 16:31:52',0,'not_loco','*yawn*',6,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(6380,1496,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','dude, tell \\\'em all to SUCK IT and EAD while they\\\'re at it.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(6381,1496,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','what did the donation box say?',0,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(6382,1494,'2001-08-03 19:11:44',0,'trouble','i\\\'d say the everybody fits neatly into your pie chart of \r\nthe social enigma.  you either speak what you feel all the \r\ntime or you want to speak what you feel and don\\\'t for \r\nwhatever the reason or you do both which is the worst \r\nbecause your views are forever on trial within you (and if \r\nthey are not then they should be).<p>i tend to fit in the \r\nlatter and it\\\'s a bitch sometimes, it\\\'s easy to doubt \r\nyourself when you can rally against some things and cower \r\nto others.<p>great post, when you get around to reviewing \r\nmy case, please be sure to review all the facts... i can\\\'t \r\nbe held responsible for everything on my rap sheet.',1,0,0,0,'64.183.57.4','en'),(6383,1496,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Uncle Moll','<p>China can eat lead!</p>',1,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(6384,1496,'2001-08-03 19:53:01',0,'china','hey, EAD, man\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(6385,1494,'2001-08-03 19:56:53',0,'mir','problem is, of course, that people tend to think they\\\'re so \r\ngreat for speaking what they see as The Truth but then they \r\njust think that other people are rude or bitches or \r\nassholes when THEY speak what THEY see as The \r\nTruth.<Br><Br><Br>kind of a double-edged sword, isn\\\'t it?\r\n<!--if you say you have you\\\'re a slut, but if you haven\\\'t, \r\nyou\\\'re a prude.  or are you a tease? -->',0,0,0,0,'208.191.101.182','en'),(6386,1496,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','sign me up.',0,0,0,0,'209.86.7.41','en'),(6387,1494,'2001-08-03 20:30:35',0,'LURKERdaddy','You should be a Karma Policewoman then.',1,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(6388,1496,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>isnt that sweet, lulu is sad she cannot go.  =-( boo boo</P>',2,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(6389,1496,'2001-08-03 21:30:20',0,'chi chi','<br> i\\\'m with you. fuck america, fuck customer support, \r\nfuck the dolphins, fuck sony, fuck \\\'em all. \r\n<br> oh and fuck the VST people too.',0,0,0,0,'64.168.23.203','en'),(6390,1496,'2001-08-03 23:22:53',0,'LurkerDaddy','then get the fuck out.',6,0,0,0,'24.28.73.144','en'),(6391,1497,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p>passion, i tell ya, it\\\'s overrated.</p>\r\n<br><br>\r\n<tt>\r\n&gt; i wish i had a boy to play with.<br>\r\n&gt; one who would do exactly as i said.\r\n</tt>\r\n<p>you don\\\'t really want that do you! it would be no fun. it would \r\nbe fun at first then boring. do you think? tho i understand the \r\npurity of what you\\\'re asking for - a lack of complication.</p>\r\n<p>i always check destablizing too</p>',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(6392,1497,'2001-08-04 01:57:20',0,'ghost','the top and bottom are at war within me...',4,0,0,0,'32.100.71.80','en'),(6393,1499,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','like',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(6394,1498,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','<BR>that\\\'s kinda like everything.<BR>that\\\'s kinda like life.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.5.82','en'),(6395,1499,'2001-08-04 03:54:55',0,'kat','i am getting use to being alone. it is hard sometimes. \r\nhaving had six years of a best friendly ghost at my side. i \r\nam getting along at being alone. it is hard sometimes. \r\n[sigh]',4,0,0,0,'32.102.109.20','en'),(6396,1499,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','i always thought i was gonna die alone. something (maybe \r\nsomebody) came along and broadsided me. i\\\'ve come to believe \r\nthat we have this sweet goofiness in us, but you can only \r\ntap into it with another person. it can be anybody, and \r\nthat\\\'s the sheer beauty and awe of it, that it can be \r\nanybody. it knocks me out. it\\\'s something primal, \r\narchetypal, this love thing. it can really be anybody. the \r\ncashier at the corner store. your neighbor. anybody.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.10.166','en'),(6397,1499,'2001-08-04 05:12:35',0,'ghost','<p>the body seems to know of its own what to do and where \r\nto do it and how.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>it says: <i>c o n n e c t . . .</i></p>\r\n',4,0,0,0,'32.102.109.20','en'),(6398,1087,'2001-08-04 11:07:58',0,'B-p','what does it mean that so many people come to feel the same \r\nway independently? The detatchment, I mean, that leads to \r\nself-injury. From what is one detatched? Whence does it \r\ncome? Why is reality sometimes not real enough? \r\n\r\nBe Here Now said Baba Ram Dass and others. \r\n\r\np.s. like the healing blood image. not sure if i like the \r\nimplication that the dream girl had to bleed, to heal. \r\nWould she have been in pain?',2,0,0,0,'202.89.149.67','en'),(6399,1500,'2001-08-04 11:25:21',0,'Joanna','I ate tempura for my dinner, my mummy cooked it for me in a \r\nbout of \\\"Joanna is a vegan\\\" ness.  (I didn\\\'t tell her I ate \r\nsalami and brie on my toast this morning).  She was so good \r\nand cooked while me and my sister and dad ate ourselves \r\nsilly that I declared her to be a true communist, and so \r\nnow I am calling her Chairman Mum.  This is also because \r\nshe was conceived in Communist China.  They had friends \r\naround after dinner and I told them to go and plough the \r\nfields instead of playing games.  I\\\'m in a silly mood \r\ntoday.  ',1,0,0,0,'203.97.2.242','en'),(6400,1501,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','i like elly\\\'s site too. i look at it frequently. she sure\r\nhas an interesting life! all that nakedness.',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.89','en'),(6401,1498,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt><i>czr & ito:</i>\\\"...house music is what we all \r\nneed... it gets our spirits up, and it makes us wanna get \r\ndown...\\\"',3,0,0,0,'206.133.180.229','en'),(6402,1501,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','hi',4,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(6403,1500,'2001-08-04 16:33:09',0,'liver','<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.brentronics.com/imprints/2001/31_afroken/im\r\nages/l_luv.jpg\\\" target=\\\"_new\\\">\r\n<img border=0 \r\nsrc=\\\"http://www.brentronics.com/imprints/2001/31_afroken/ima\r\nges/s_luv.jpg\\\"></a>',2,0,0,0,'64.81.72.119','en'),(6404,1501,'2001-08-04 17:48:55',0,'kat','<p>welcome to the fold fuzzy...</p>\r\n<p>i too followed a link path here via elly\\\'s site. i am \r\nnow caught up in her tattoo. it makes me want another one. \r\nreminds me of when i got mine </p>\r\n<p><img \r\nsrc=\\\"http://lefteyelazy.com/roadtrip/images/photos/californi\r\na/fly.jpg\\\"></p>\r\n<p>the day before i left santa cruz for my roadtrip...and \r\nproceeded to leave bits of my skin all over arizona, new \r\nmexico, and texas.</p>',1,0,0,0,'32.102.109.70','en'),(6405,1502,'2001-08-04 18:09:53',0,'kat','hanging out at the Saturn is a possible alternative to egg-\r\nfilled foods. come eat with me....',1,0,0,0,'32.102.109.70','en'),(6406,1502,'2001-08-04 18:47:15',0,'ghost','<p>visions of a hamburger</p>',4,0,0,0,'32.100.71.54','en'),(6407,1499,'2001-08-04 18:58:15',0,'deb','i guess we all want to reach out to someone... or have \r\nsomeone reach out to us =\\\\',1,0,0,0,'64.12.103.38','en'),(6408,1502,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','<p>\r\nmang, since we can\\\'t make souffles without eggs for the next \r\nthree weeks, perhaps we should sit around and drink beers and \r\nstare out the window and occasionally nod at one another.\r\n</p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(6409,1498,'2001-08-04 19:43:26',0,'nipples','Stoo you are the man, but you need to get the hell out of \r\nthe capital region.  that place is dead, and it\\\'s probably \r\nkilling you...or at least your soul...\r\n\r\nthere\\\'s a line in \\\'Shine\\\' where the father tells his \r\nson: \\\"Music is the only thing that won\\\'t let you down, \r\neverything else will let you down...\\\"\r\n\r\ni believe it.',0,0,0,0,'198.182.157.96','en'),(6410,1498,'2001-08-04 20:55:06',0,'SSJ3 Gostu to Nips','<p align=\\\'justify\\\'>\r\nhaha! who is this?</p>\r\n<p align=\\\'justify\\\'>\r\nactually i moved to SF about three months ago, so- there \r\nyou go. send me email!</p>',1,0,0,0,'208.58.87.82','en'),(6411,1502,'2001-08-04 21:18:39',0,'bmg','go get some egg in oakland, mang! This is insane.',1,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(6412,1502,'2001-08-04 21:22:25',0,'asstin to slimon','<P>we can pull the beers out of a cooler and stare at your camino waiting for God \r\nto fix it.</P>',3,0,0,0,'216.175.99.106','en'),(6413,1502,'2001-08-04 22:29:34',0,'kat','visions of a hottub filled with naked people, robots, \r\nghosts, and beer. [which will not be happening anytime soon \r\nsince my roommates kidlings are visiting]\r\n\r\n<p><i>*grumpy*</i></p>',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.70','en'),(6414,1502,'2001-08-04 22:34:42',0,'slimon to asstin','dude. the broken camino is available for viewing tomorrow \r\nafternoon. for a ride to marin and some beers. call the \r\ncellie.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(6415,1501,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','Yeah... all that nakedness.  What freedom!  Not a day goes\r\nby that I do not damn the shackles that clothes force me to\r\nlive by.  Sigh, such is life though.<br><br>Kat, that\\\'s a\r\nnice tat.  Does the symbol have some sort of meaning or is\r\njust one of those <b><i>\\\"this looks cool\\\"</i></b> deals? \r\nAnd by leaving bits of your skin at the places you visit is\r\nlike spreading yourself around, in a way.  It\\\'s leaving a\r\nlittle bit of yourself in that other place so that a part of\r\nyou will always be there.  At least that\\\'s the way I\r\nrationalize leaving things at other people\\\'s places, in\r\nother cities/countries/whatever.  What is more personalized\r\nthan pieces of <b>you</b>?<br><br>Anyway, it\\\'s 8:14, I\\\'ve\r\ngot to leave to get to work soon.  Sigh, tonight is going to\r\nbe bus-ay because <a\r\nhref=\\\"http://www.toronto.com/profile?fid=17&id=357537\\\"\r\ntarget=\\\"new\\\">Caribana</a> is going to be in full swing\r\ntonight.  Party party party!  Shoot me now.',1,0,0,0,'64.229.76.128','en'),(6416,1501,'2001-08-05 01:26:17',0,'kat','<p>leaving parts of you in other places...</p>\r\n\r\n<p>i told my family that when my time comes i want to have \r\nmy ashes scattered out on the ocean. that way i can keep on \r\ntravelling, maybe someday being everywhere all at the same \r\ntime. i like that thought.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>the tat is something i drew for myself, partly a \r\nmandala...if you know me and you know the story behind the \r\nphoenix then you\\\'d probably figure out why i ended up with \r\nit. infinite rebirth by immolation....</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n',4,0,0,0,'32.102.109.86','en'),(6417,1502,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','there are virtual eggs available on the internet. the \r\ninternet. they have that on the east coast of this great \r\ncountry, can you not fuckin believe it?',0,0,0,0,'216.243.8.16','en'),(6418,1502,'2001-08-05 04:45:15',0,'ps','whatever they are telling you is \\\"eggless\\\" pad thai is just \r\nsomething they scrape the egg off in the back. there are \r\nstill egg particle-scrapings stuck in there.',0,0,0,0,'216.243.8.16','en'),(6419,1498,'2001-08-05 04:55:43',0,'nipples','AWESOME!!  so you\\\'ve really done it?  chillin\\\' with the \r\ndugster in SF...\r\n\r\ni WILL email you...but right now this is too much fun.\r\n\r\nit\\\'s clear you haven\\\'t purged your need to write...perhaps \r\nanother protoculture is in order...',0,0,0,0,'198.182.157.90','en'),(6420,1501,'2001-08-05 06:11:04',0,'chaya','hi, i like ink.  even more to the point: i\\\'ve been \r\ncollecting images of phoenixes (phoenices? phoenixi?) from \r\nwhence i will fashion an entirely different phoenix that i \r\nwill have drawn on my body somewhere.  i just don\\\'t know \r\nwhere yet.',1,0,0,0,'158.252.218.116','en'),(6421,1499,'2001-08-05 07:31:50',0,'chaya','some things: i think the sweet goofiness is always there, \r\nwhether or not you\\\'re specifically exhibiting it for \r\nanother person.  the kicker is that sometimes you meet \r\npeople whose sweet goofiness resonates with yours on a \r\ndeeply meaningful level and you get to make beautiful sweet \r\ngoofy music together.  it\\\'s neat as fuck and way better \r\nthan any other kind of high could ever hope to be.  \r\n[sidebar - i think that this particular connection is part \r\nof what people are chasing when they eat big piles of \r\ndrugs.  i have a whole theory about it.  you can ask me to \r\ntell you about it sometime.]<br><br>also: i wrote something \r\nabout connecting to lots of different kinds of people a \r\nwhile ago and i think maybe you might appreciate it.  it \r\nconveniently resides <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?\r\nid=590.txt\\\">here</a> on swinney.org for your perusal.  i \r\nwrote some other stuff about it too actually, but you\\\'ll \r\nhave to be a secret spy internet stalker and track it \r\ndown.  right ok then.<br><br>\\\"nice supportive\\\"',2,0,0,0,'158.252.208.35','en'),(6422,1501,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','ix, i\\\'m your number one fan! hi.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(6423,1502,'2001-08-05 08:55:47',0,'chi chi','<br><i>eggy</i><br>i had breaky by myself. *sigh*',0,0,0,0,'64.168.23.91','en'),(6424,1503,'2001-08-05 12:31:26',0,'ghost','it is six am. i was awake at 4am. the nightmares woke me. \r\nthere was noone around to hold onto afterwards. so i had to \r\nturn on the light. ',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.29','en'),(6425,1503,'2001-08-05 13:02:27',0,'deb','hmm. i was awake still at 2am, and stared at the cieling \r\nfrom my bed for longer... who knew. we all though we were \r\nalone, and here we weren\\\'t.',2,0,0,0,'152.163.213.212','en'),(6426,1503,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','9:10am... can\\\'t sleep.<br><br>My body hates me!',4,0,0,0,'64.229.76.128','en'),(6427,1502,'2002-03-05 20:17:36',17,'austin to chi chi','<P>8:24 am.  \\\'nando let me sleep in.  i went to feed him.  lola showed up too.  it is \r\nlike an animal farm out there.  but what i really have to say is that i saw chicken \r\napple sausage in the fridge.</P>',3,0,0,0,'216.175.101.152','en'),(6428,1503,'2001-08-05 17:18:43',0,'sims','good morning! woah boy, it\\\'s early. well, it\\\'s 10. but still!\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(6429,1498,'2001-08-05 20:05:34',0,'SSJ3 Gostu','ooooh! everybody\\\'s sooo mysterious these days :)-\r\n<BR>\r\ni have thought about a new page, and eventually it\\\'ll \r\nprobably happen, but- who knows.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'208.58.87.82','en'),(6430,1498,'2001-08-05 20:15:47',0,'nippster','by the way, if you want your David Holmes Cds back- just \r\ngive me your address   ; )',0,0,0,0,'198.182.157.95','en'),(6431,1498,'2001-08-05 20:24:43',0,'john holmes','my cds? when did i make cds? oh wait, you said david! my bad!\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(6432,1505,'2001-08-05 20:50:52',0,'kat','i am finding these swintries too enticing and sticky. stop \r\nit.',1,0,0,0,'32.100.70.241','en'),(6433,1504,'2001-08-05 21:55:47',0,'deb','but you know, sometimes that\\\'s the hardest question to \r\nanswer...',2,0,0,0,'64.12.102.41','en'),(6434,1501,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','My mom wants to be cremated when she dies.  She used to have\r\nnightmares about being buried alive and being conscious\r\nwhile her body is being eaten by worms and sutff.  I used to\r\nthink that was really morbid, but not so much anymore.  I\r\nwouldn\\\'t mind my ashes being spread in the ocean, or fired\r\ninto space or something.  I\\\'d really like them to be buried\r\ninto a polar ice cap and let global warming take care of\r\nreleasing them in the future.<br><br>Yeah, I definately want\r\nmy ashes to be ice-capped.',3,0,0,0,'64.229.76.128','en'),(6435,1504,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','But formulating the answers is just part of the fun. \r\nSelf-discovery and what-not, you know?  You get some\r\ninteresting answers.',3,0,0,0,'64.229.76.128','en'),(6436,1503,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>the first few weeks that I knew you I had trouble \r\nsleeping. I did not want to admit it then but it was partly \r\nbecause I had a freakout, knockout, knock-down, drag-out \r\ncrush on you.</p>\r\n<p>the ladies in this house woke up at the CRACK OF FREAKIN \r\nDAWN today and tried their best to yank me up for 2 hours \r\nand help them chop their friggin fruit. i was in the heat \r\nof a baby shower all day and ended up falling asleep uncle \r\nswinney-style in the middle of hte party in the middle of a \r\nstrange living room and waking up with little patterns \r\nindented on my skin from the classy couch upholstery. they \r\nslapped me around and put me in the car, and now theyre \r\ntelling me we have to get up at EIGHT EFFIN AM tomorrow to \r\ndo some godforsaken activity, one that no doubt involves \r\ngrilled meat and/or pork rinds. Im having a gay ole time \r\nhere lemme tell you.</p>',0,0,0,0,'216.243.8.227','en'),(6437,1504,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','<BR><BR>all the little lifeforms upon this little \r\nearth<BR>multiply and die and return into rebirth<BR>all the \r\nlittle children growing up in space<BR>adding their small \r\nstories to the history of our race<BR>here on \r\nearth...<BR>this reminds me of joseph campbell, \r\ntranspersonal stuff, how we\\\'re all expressions of the same \r\nconsciousness - people, plants, animals, unseen spirit \r\nhelpers....\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.9.169','en'),(6438,1494,'2001-08-06 02:28:21',0,'alanna','yah.&nbsp; it does get pretty tricky.&nbsp; i\\\'ve limited \r\nmyself to not sweating the small stuff and only voicing my \r\nconcern when i see a very glaring ickness.',3,0,0,0,'198.182.157.105','en'),(6439,1500,'2001-08-06 02:30:33',0,'alanna','woo! post number 23!',1,0,0,0,'198.182.157.105','en'),(6440,1494,'2001-08-06 03:34:17',0,'allison r.','if you say you have you\\\'re a slut, but if you haven\\\'t, \r\nyou\\\'re a prude.  or are you a tease?',4,0,0,0,'165.247.53.42','en'),(6441,1494,'2001-08-06 04:01:25',0,'mir','thank god SOMEONE catches references to \\\'80s movies.',0,0,0,0,'206.40.244.66','en'),(6442,1503,'2002-03-08 04:52:47',65,'le to egg','the east coast is bad egg. people get up early there and smoke \r\nless pot.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(6443,1494,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','<p>Saturday March 24, 1984.</p>\r\n<p>Shermer High School, Shermer, Illinois.</p>\r\n<p>Dear Mr. Vernon</p>\r\n<p>We accept the fact that we had to sacrifice a whole \r\nSaturday in detention for whatever it was that we did \r\nwrong. What we did WAS wrong.  But we think you\\\'re crazy to \r\nmake us write this essay telling you who we think we are, \r\nwhat do you care?  You see us as you want to see us... in \r\nthe   simplest terms and the most convenient \r\ndefinitions.</p>\r\n<p>You see us as a brain, an athlete, a basket             \r\ncase, a princess and a criminal. Correct?  That\\\'s the way \r\nwe saw each other at seven o\\\'clock this morning.</p>\r\n<p>We were brainwashed.</p>\r\n                                                  ',3,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(6444,1506,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','be honest. call him and say, \\\"i\\\'d really prefer if you \r\nweren\\\'t around wednesday night.\\\" he might act wounded, but \r\nit\\\'ll be good for him to come to grips with things. you want \r\na whole person, somebody who isn\\\'t weak and not an asshole. \r\nand there are plenty of them around.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.5.183','en'),(6445,1494,'2001-08-06 04:47:09',0,'kat','y\\\'all are gonna give me nightmares if you keep this up. \r\n[molly ringwald=gross]',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.107','en'),(6446,1506,'2001-08-06 04:50:23',0,'kat','i agree. be honest about what YOU want/need. don\\\'t \r\nsugarcoat it with the possibilities by mentioning your \r\nother ex or mom or whoever. that makes it a little easier \r\non you, but it also gives the other person a chance to keep \r\ntheir foot in the door. be emotionless, honest, and dont \r\never let \\\'em cross your boundaries.',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.107','en'),(6447,1507,'2001-08-06 04:56:34',0,'kat','don\\\'t worry, once you get older the only people who turn \r\npervy on you are the ones you *don\\\'t* like anyway. the ones \r\nyou wish had secret pervy thoughts about yourself are \r\ncontent to be just platonic friends. such is life. when \r\nyou\\\'re happy you\\\'re flooded...when you want it, you ain\\\'t \r\ngettin it.',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.107','en'),(6448,6,'2001-08-06 05:09:13',0,'bmg','go to sleep young man.',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(6449,1494,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','i luv molly ringwald.',4,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(6450,1494,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','<p>it was one of my favourite movies.</p>\r\n<p>Well, if you say you haven\\\'t...you\\\'re a prude.  If you \r\nsay you have...you\\\'re a slut!  It\\\'s a trap. You want to but \r\nyou can\\\'t but when you do you wish you didn\\\'t, right?\r\n</p>',4,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(6451,1503,'2001-08-06 06:18:14',0,'liver','they only smoke less pot because the pot is really freakin\\\' \r\nbad. back in pittsburgh we paid top dollar for a bag of \r\nbrown shake and stems and seeds AND WE LIKED IT!\r\n',6,0,0,0,'63.202.215.130','en'),(6452,1509,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p>on the new moon, i was camped near a lake in the lower part \r\nof the sierra mountains, here in california USA. moonless, the sky \r\nwas nothing but a curtain, a bed of stars, like <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://bud.com/99/02/tkles/23.elly.dylan/\\\">woody \r\nguthrie</a> sings about california. \r\n</p><p>\r\nmy companion was ryan shaw. we spoke of the moon then, in its \r\nabsence, while the stars reflected off the lake and the chipmunks \r\nreadied themselves in the bushes for an impending dawn attack of \r\nour food bag.\r\n</p><p>\r\nryan mentioned some girl, a hippie, a woman who said that \r\nlooking at the full moon could give her an orgasm. i stammered in \r\nresponse, after a pause. during the pause i had an intense \r\nmemory of standing in the middle of 27th street barefoot on the \r\npavement, looking up at a full moon and calling everyone in my \r\ncellphone to tell them about it. of riding the j church through \r\ndolores park as the moon rose over the city to the left of us and \r\nhow everyone on the train was mezmerized by it but no one \r\nspoke, almost in silent reverence. \r\n</p><p>\r\ni remembered breathing fast and shallow on the sight of that \r\nmoon. my heart coming up to my throat. \r\n</p><p>\r\ni remembered breathing fast and shallow before a few orgasms in \r\nmy life. my heart coming up to my throat.\r\n</p><p>\r\nafter the pause, i responded to ryan\\\'s somewhat incredulous tale \r\nof the woman who came when she saw the moon, i said \r\nsomething like \\\"that doesn\\\'t seem that far fetched.\\\"',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(6453,1508,'2001-08-06 07:54:10',0,'green','its ounds like you two are doing better..we are ...are you ?\r\nnice writing...good',1,0,0,0,'64.30.217.93','en'),(6454,1507,'2001-08-06 10:36:55',0,'deb','hah. i think i completely understand.',2,0,0,0,'205.188.197.39','en'),(6455,1506,'2001-08-06 10:53:23',0,'deb','trust me, nothing is sugarcoated. the truth is that i don\\\'t \r\nwant him there, and i DID tell him that. the boy has a god \r\ndamn mind of his own.  the only thing this could be is an \r\nexplosive situation...and i have no idea how to make it not \r\nhappen....<sigh>',2,0,0,0,'205.188.197.39','en'),(6456,1508,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>better... perhaps, if not more best-friends than \r\nanything else.  we\\\'ve been together a total of about 12 \r\nhours this week (probably half of them spent sleeping, the \r\nrest spent eating, and discussing why each of us feels that \r\nthe other is too good for us, ha). life\\\'s twists and turns \r\nare certainly interesting nowadays, and still very \r\nconfusing. thanks for the good thoughts, though!</tt> ',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6457,1507,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<tt><i>1. \\\"...if I could I would date myself...\\\"</i> amen, \r\nsister.  2. among the most hurtful feelings is watching a \r\ngreat platonic friendship head south when someone gets \r\npervy, gets the wrong idea, or doesn\\\'t take hints.  3. \r\namong the best feelings is a controlled, well-timed \r\nperviness in a lover that rears its head at the perfect \r\nmoments. ',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6458,1506,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>your time is too valuable to waste on somethign \r\nthat you know isn\\\'t good for you...</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6459,1504,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>thats why swinney.org is so cool... usually you \r\nhave to know someone a while before they\\\'ll divulge the \r\nbest story they\\\'re holding... here, you get to hear it as \r\nyou get to know the person, and even sometimes from someone \r\nyou don\\\'t even know.  its been really interesting to watch \r\npeople, strangers, form an image of themselves in my mind, \r\nbased solely on their well-chsoen words. and there are new \r\nthoughts each day, heh heh.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6460,1502,'2001-08-06 13:21:32',0,'jo','egg\\\'s job in my life is to ruin thai food for me. she \r\ndoesn\\\'t know that, but it is.<BR>\r\nalso: all pants all the time.',1,0,0,0,'172.162.184.132','en'),(6461,1494,'2001-08-06 13:53:35',0,'bender to kat','\r\nwell, we wouldn\\\'t speak for you. we don\\\'t even know your \r\nlanguage.',4,0,0,0,'207.237.128.1','en'),(6462,1509,'2001-08-06 14:09:49',0,'lou','i would always rather be alone than be with dubious \r\npeople.  or in an unstable relationship. there is nothing \r\nwrong with being alone. a lot of the time it\\\'s good. \r\nsometimes it is lonely.\r\n\r\n(also, i am glad you decided to pay attention. :))',1,0,0,0,'207.237.128.1','en'),(6463,1507,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<p>heh, heh..... I AM <B>PERVY</B> ALL THE TIME!!!  Does \r\nthat bother you Green?  Did you write this about me?  I\\\'ll \r\nbe your little lust bunny.</P>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(6464,1508,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<p>tantalizing breathless breast upon which every head will \r\nrest.  I had a dream of sleeping, breathing; warm hands \r\nfeeling, clutching, needing.  Slowly drowning discontent; \r\nrefilling all I\\\'ve spent.</p>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(6465,1509,'2001-08-06 15:01:06',0,'jo','i <a href=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?\r\nid=523.txt\\\">always prefer being alone</a>. i greatly prefer \r\nlonely to smothered.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(6466,1509,'2001-08-06 15:09:19',0,'lou to jo','amen.',1,0,0,0,'207.237.128.1','en'),(6467,1505,'2001-08-06 15:18:56',0,'wolfwood','<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.jamestheband.com/music/lyrics/displayTrack.\r\ncfm?Track=40\\\">Getting \r\nAway With It </a> ',1,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(6468,1508,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<tt>Word.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6469,1507,'2001-08-06 16:24:53',0,'pornluvr','i want to lick your nipples.  all of you. i want to do the \r\nhumpty dance all over your pubic area and spontaneously \r\ncombust in a fit of heated amourous passion!',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6470,1509,'2001-08-06 16:25:01',0,'jo','(you\\\'re cute.)',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(6471,1494,'2001-08-06 16:34:05',0,'jo','mmm bender. and some of them i just consider.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(6472,1509,'2001-08-06 17:49:33',0,'kat','i dig that relationships book. i\\\'ve taken friends to the \r\nbookstore for the sole purpose of showing them that book.',4,0,0,0,'32.102.90.192','en'),(6473,1507,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<b>porny?</b>',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(6474,1510,'2001-08-06 19:48:47',0,'green','freaky\r\nare you having problems with your significant other?',2,0,0,0,'138.23.189.113','en'),(6475,1509,'2001-08-06 19:56:22',0,'oh please','barf-o-rama',6,0,0,0,'208.191.101.182',