s that seem vivid to that extent.',6,0,0,0,'208.143.2.204','en'),(6489,1512,'2001-08-06 22:14:04',0,'editor','status-fying?\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(6490,1510,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>green: yep, some rockiness, but i think the dream is \r\nmore than that, for some reason...?  who knows.<br>\r\n<br>tick: yeah, it was uncanny and vivid as all get out... \r\nthe colors and setting and lighting in it were like the \r\nwildest trip...</tt>',3,0,0,0,'64.152.162.140','en'),(6491,1512,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>Sassy-fying!</tt>',3,0,0,0,'64.152.162.140','en'),(6492,1512,'2001-08-07 00:59:54',0,'i was a lively dancer','<img src=\\\"http://saturn5.com/~egg/jay.jpg\\\" alt=\\\"i was very \r\nchahming\\\">',0,0,0,0,'216.243.8.103','en'),(6493,1509,'2001-08-07 02:41:44',0,'lou to ghost','cantankerous is a <b>FINE</B> word.  props.',1,0,0,0,'165.247.53.42','en'),(6494,1512,'2001-08-07 03:52:56',0,'ghost','<p>ahhh the personals...</p>\r\n\r\n<p>wouldn\\\'t that be an interesting poll? to see how many \r\nswinnys have done the personals thing and how and if and \r\nwhat they got from it.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>[and while i\\\'m writing this i notice i\\\'m constantly \r\ncreating typos...using the word \\\'want\\\' instead of what i \r\nmeant. funny that]',3,0,0,0,'32.102.89.143','en'),(6495,1511,'2001-08-07 04:14:47',0,'two thoughts::','1. dish ran away with spoon\r\n<br><br>\r\n2. \\\"i climbed out the window with my shadow in a spoon, \r\ndancin on the roof shootin\\\' holes in the moon\\\"',1,0,0,0,'209.246.105.201','en'),(6496,1512,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','if someone could send their smell through the computer, I \r\nwould sign up for personals.',0,0,0,0,'216.243.8.103','en'),(6497,1512,'2001-08-07 04:35:44',0,'jo','when i think about personal ads, i think: if the people in \r\nmy life that i\\\'ve truly loved, truly fallen for, wrote \r\npersonals and i read them in a newspaper, would i respond?\r\n<BR>\r\nwithout a doubt, no.<BR>\r\nnow, if they anonymous websites that i happened to stumble \r\nacross and started to read without realizing the writer, \r\nwould i be enraptured, would i send them email professing \r\nmy <b>big fat monster textcrush</b>?<BR>\r\nwithout a doubt, yes.',1,0,0,0,'172.130.127.29','en'),(6498,1515,'2001-08-07 04:50:12',0,'kat','it is the uncertainty that makes it all worth living for.',1,0,0,0,'32.102.89.143','en'),(6499,1512,'2001-08-07 05:03:43',0,'kat','the only person who ever found my website and emailed with \r\na bigfatmostertextcrush on me was some 50-something MARRIED \r\nman who was into S&M and had dreams about killing his wife.\r\n\r\n<p>[thank you but i didn\\\'t need that kind of crush]</p>',4,0,0,0,'32.100.70.39','en'),(6500,1510,'2001-08-07 05:06:46',0,'ty','sometimes dreams dont really have any meaning, especially \r\njust before you wake up. it\\\'s just your brain entertaining \r\nitself. personally, i dream about tornados a lot. every \r\ntime, in the dream, i say to myself, goddam. all those \r\ndreams about tornados and i\\\'m finally seeing one in real \r\nlife, but of course it\\\'s just another dream. I wonder what \r\nwill happen if i ever DO see one in real life. will i wake \r\nup?',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.23','en'),(6501,1515,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','babies rock. i lovvvvvve babies. i wouldn\\\'t want to give \r\nbirth to one, but they are awesome and beautiful.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.23','en'),(6502,1515,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','swollen with pride, i need to point out that I searched on \r\ngoogle to find a reference to \"...symphony out \r\nof...swallowing our own tongues\", and i linked this <a target=\"window\" href=\"http://www.artbyte.com/mag/mar_apr_01/letigre_content.shtml\">artbyte</a> \r\nthingy without realizing that it is written by my very own \r\n10 yr pal poopchute!',0,0,0,0,'216.243.8.103','en'),(6503,1512,'2001-08-07 05:13:47',0,'Joanna','I like to read the personal ads, because sometimes they\\\'re \r\nreally really funny, and sometimes I like to wonder what \r\nI\\\'d write if I was to place an ad, but if I wouldn\\\'t \r\nrespond to an ad, why would anyone that I would want to be \r\ninvolved with respond to my ad?  \r\n\r\n<BR><BR>\r\n\r\nExcept that sometimes I feel like web pages are kind of \r\nlike personal ads, only you\\\'re generally looking for mind-\r\nconnections, not hot-loving (<A HREF=\\\"http://hubris.co.nz\\\" \r\nHubris.co.nz</A> - Hey Fellows, I\\\'m single). And sure, \r\ntextual loving is all very well, but it\\\'s not the same \r\nthing.  ',1,0,0,0,'203.97.2.242','en'),(6504,1514,'2001-08-07 05:16:43',0,'brian and robert','if you\'re just staring at your walls/ observing echoing \r\nfoot-falls/ of tenants wandering distant halls/ then this \r\none is for you./ if children playing all around/ to you is \r\nnoise, not pleasant sound/ and you\'d be lost, on the \r\nplayground/ then this one is for you./ you slip past \r\nstrangers in the street/ there\'s no one that you care to \r\nmeet/ longing for your TV seat/ then this one is for you./ \r\nall alone a life you lead/ a silent diner, where you feed/ \r\nyou bow your head, pretend to read\r\n<b>\r\nthen this one is for you.</b>',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.23','en'),(6505,1513,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','that sorry ass beeyatch.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.23','en'),(6506,1515,'2001-08-07 05:20:53',0,'chi chi','<br> speeding off to meet your gentlemen friend.<i> \r\nthick black eyeliner and red red lips.</i>\r\n<br> the road stretches on, and some joni playing. <i> \r\nCalifornia I\\\'m coming home / Oh will you take me as I \r\nam / Strung out on another man / California I\\\'m coming \r\nhome</>\r\n<br> pondering what happened, remembering old \r\nconversations. <i> sunday nature outings, mushrooms \r\nat venice on the bay, picking up living ecosystem \r\nhitch-hikers on route 1 </i><br>\r\nthe future stands before you, and your path ahead. <i> \r\npiscine fire dragon, the way is marked </i>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.160.46.81','en'),(6507,1515,'2001-08-07 05:26:16',0,'jo','i am such an egg-fan.',1,0,0,0,'172.130.127.29','en'),(6508,1512,'2001-08-07 05:32:31',0,'</a>jo','i get (and have sent) a fair number of textcrush emails. \r\nmost are from chumps, it\\\'s true. sometimes it\\\'s a little \r\ninsulting when someone professes their love for you based \r\non reading your website and you\\\'re like, \\\"dude. you can\\\'t \r\neven form sentences. fuuuuuuck why do the losers always \r\ncrush on me?\\\"<BR>\r\nstill, i\\\'ve had good luck with seeking out websites and \r\nsubsequent friendships with like-minded people, people very \r\nsimilar to the friends i\\\'ve made in my normal day-to-day \r\nlife.<BR>\r\nelly, for instance, often reminds me very much of my ex. i \r\neven have a tendency to walk towards both of them with my \r\nhead bowed forward because that\\\'s the part of my body that \r\ncraves their attention. pet my head, fill my ears with \r\nstories, please.',1,0,0,0,'172.130.127.29','en'),(6509,1512,'2001-08-07 05:32:58',0,'kat','ps: i\\\'ve been posting personals for about a year now. i\\\'ve \r\nactually met some pretty damn awesome folks that way...and \r\nit wasn\\\'t always about sex either. i still laugh when i \r\nread them though.',4,0,0,0,'32.100.70.39','en'),(6510,1514,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','the tires are the things on your car that make contact with \r\nthe road',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(6511,1515,'2001-08-07 06:21:09',0,'why','is everything in italics',0,0,0,0,'216.243.8.73','en'),(6512,1515,'2001-08-07 06:23:34',0,'</i>songs','<p>joni mitchell: \\\"will you take me as I am, strung out on \r\nanother man.\\\"</p>\r\n<p>calvin johnson: \\\"who\\\'s gonna love me the way that I \r\nam?\\\"</p>',0,0,0,0,'216.243.8.73','en'),(6513,1515,'2001-08-07 06:42:24',0,'people would','love you more, calvin johnson, if you didn\\\'t have the most \r\nirritating and sonically offensive voice of all time.',1,0,0,0,'172.130.127.29','en'),(6514,1512,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','upon second reading, i think this is very clever. but also \r\nheart-wrenching. I was thinking on the plane about what i \r\nsaid about mcsweeney\\\'s and how satire was too glib, or too \r\none-liner-esque for me. You have used satire to be sincere. \r\noh jay, your booty shakes the most.',0,0,0,0,'216.243.8.73','en'),(6515,1515,'2001-08-07 06:52:43',0,'calvin to people would','give it to me give itto megive ittomegiveittome',0,0,0,0,'216.243.8.73','en'),(6516,1516,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','welcome to my world.',0,0,0,0,'216.243.8.73','en'),(6517,1516,'2001-08-07 07:28:37',0,'chi chi','<i> this world is my world, this world is your world<br>\r\nfrom obnoxious cats, to weird random acts<br>\r\nthis world is my world.....</i>',0,0,0,0,'64.160.46.81','en'),(6518,1515,'2001-08-07 08:03:49',0,'lulu','<p> the ripping labia is a rite of passage to ultimate womandom, dear. <br>\r\n but,  fear it not, friend for i hear your labia is durable and strong and able to leap tall buildings and stop \r\nbullets dead in their tracks. <br>\r\ni also hear from my friend, Hank, that your labia has teeth and bites.<br>\r\ni imagine any woman with a labia like this has already reached the ultimate womandom and needs not the \r\nexperience of ejecting a slimy mammal the size of an adolescent kangaroo out of her hole.<br>\r\nhuevo, sweet dear, you are evolved...<br>\r\nyou are the ONE...<br>\r\nyou are the one the others have children for...<br>\r\nyou are the one we, the repressed, tamed labia women strive to become...<br>\r\nyou are the one with the chomping labia named marge.<br>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(6519,1517,'2001-08-07 08:20:13',0,'JAy Whiteside','well i think that you might like my friends: ronnie, \r\ndonnie, connie, billy, willy, oh and dont forget lonnie. \r\nthese are some of the coolest people youll ever meet, no \r\njoke. ',4,0,0,0,'209.179.146.37','en'),(6520,1510,'2001-08-07 13:06:04',0,'tylerdurden','Perhaps it\\\'s during sleep that we are truly awake. Awake to \r\nthe <i>reality</i> around us. Perhaps you have seen a \r\ntornado. Many tornados, only to dream that you wished you \r\ncould.',3,0,0,0,'217.32.149.92','en'),(6521,1512,'2001-08-07 13:41:37',0,'will','i want but i don\\\'t want to work.\r\ngive but don\\\'t expect reciprocation.\r\n\r\nlike a bad R&B single.\r\n\r\ngod, i love this generation!',4,0,0,0,'198.214.178.232','en'),(6522,1520,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>Great stuff, essemar, for real. I like writing that \r\ni can stop and <i>think</i> about.  Nice.  Speaking \r\nof \\\"nice\\\".. not to digress, but yesterday i was crossing \r\n72nd street and this big fat n\\\' greasy mullet passed this \r\nbusiness woman, and grunted \\\"NIIICE!!\\\" at her, while \r\ncraning to check out her ass.  She turned around and \r\nliterally- for real- <i>kicked him in the ass</i> while \r\nutering a equally loud \\\'fuck you\\\'.  That rocked.  it has \r\nnothing to do with your writing, of course, but i just felt \r\nlike sharing that story with someone.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6523,1521,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>man, i <i>like</i> that picture</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6524,1514,'2001-08-07 14:57:24',0,'Jah to ix','M\\\'kayyyyy....',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6525,1522,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>Ahh, the life of the fluctuating time-clock.  My \r\nlife is so much better having a job like this, also.  As \r\nlong as I get my projects finished in reasonable time, I \r\ncome and go as I please- Imagine how happpy our work-force \r\nwould be if everyone could work within tehse constraints?\r\n</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6526,1522,'2001-08-07 16:21:58',0,'lou','i don\\\'t think i know too many people, actually, who would \r\nbe happy working like this. i don\\\'t even know if i am.  i \r\nalways feel as though somehow, even though i get all my \r\nwork done, my company isn\\\'t getting their money\\\'s worth \r\nfrom me, because maybe a total of 4 hours are spent on \r\nworking, on average, every day.  guilt guilt guilt. oh the \r\nlife of a jewish catholic!  (it\\\'s an ethnicity, i swear. \r\nthese things are passed down through genetics.)\r\n<br><br>also, though, i love working like this. i only wish \r\nthat i really could set my own hours, and come in at night. \r\ni am not a fan of the daylight. i am also not a fan of \r\nmornings. in general.',1,0,0,0,'207.237.128.1','en'),(6527,1522,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<p>On a good day, I\\\'ll get an hour of actual work done on \r\nthe job, but I\\\'m always required to be here from 8:30am-\r\n4:30pm.  I used to feel guilty about it.  Sometimes I \r\nstress that someone will notice what an incredible lazy \r\nslug they hired and fire me.  Butt.... in this strange way, \r\nI feel like they are getting their money\\\'s worth.  My own \r\nself-inflated ego.<p></P>You get your work done.  You kcik \r\nass.</P>',4,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(6528,1518,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>\r\n<b>A Random Statement Taken from Quotes on Things Sitting \r\non my Desk:</b><br><br>\r\nDeliver to 535 East 70th Street<br>\r\nthe 2 CPU product ID used for<br>\r\nmaking glycine-rich Haupt\\\'s<br>\r\ncheap airfare, weather and tips for those of you who \r\nhave<br>\r\nimages of collagen and proteoglycan in bovine cartilage.<br>\r\nFor your information only,<br>\r\nDelaware Diamond Knives<br>\r\ncan repair your waterlogged cell-phone;<br>\r\nrequests should be sent to the Cornell University<br>\r\nglassware supplier<br>\r\n<i>only</i> when logging into the voice mail system.<br>\r\nThis study provides a framework wherein<br>\r\nused vinyl, discount cartridges and slipmats<br>\r\ncan ease the inflamatory symptoms associated with<br>\r\nA journey into America\\\'s Heartland.<br>\r\nHere\\\'s your PIN, Peter- use it when<br>\r\nthe MTA provides free transportation for<br>\r\ninpatient therapy.<br>\r\n<br>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6529,1519,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','you said you were going to write a piece about my \r\nunbreakable labia.',0,0,0,0,'216.243.8.83','en'),(6530,1515,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<img src=\\\"http://atari.saturn5.com/~egg/duck.jpg\\\" \r\nalign=\\\"left\\\"><p>i just woke up to a zoo in the living room \r\nnext to me. i slept with my breasts all akimbo and my \r\ncheetah panties sticking out and there are two toddlers \r\nchecking it out. apparently my sister\\\'s old roommate wanted \r\nto come show off her goods today.</p>\r\n<p> the little blonde girl likes me. they said, \\\"kendra, do \r\nyour <i>diamonds are a girl\\\'s best friend</i> dance for \r\namy.\\\" she stood up (the three year old), ground her pelvis, \r\nthrew one arm in the air and shouted \\\"GIMME THE ICE OR NO \r\nDICE!\\\" and then later i hear her mother musing \\\"i dont \r\nknow, i htink the babysitter watched MTV with her, AGAINST \r\nMY WISHES. she might be doing some britney speeyaz \r\nmoves.\\\"</p>\r\n<p>*cracks open a coke*</p>\r\n<p>it\\\'s gonna be a long week. does anyone know where i can \r\nget a little ducky-assed undies suit like the one here?</p>',0,0,0,0,'216.243.8.83','en'),(6531,1519,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to egg:','<br><tt>its so uncanny- i just emailed your labia-of-steel \r\npiece to my girlfriend, as she\\\'s said the <i>exact</i> same \r\nthings you said there... sometimes almost word for word. \r\nyikes, thats freeky. once again, swinney gets into the old \r\npsyche in weird ways.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6532,1522,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>some of my friends that punch the ole clock claim \r\nto see it as fate worse than death.  i love knowing that if \r\ni work efficiently/intelligently/quickly/hard, i can go \r\nhome, paycheck in hand, work-ethic fulfilled, and still \r\nhave time for a nap and a life.  it prevents me from \r\nwasting time online (with the exception of swinney-visits, \r\nhi.) or schmoozing with co-workers (who i don\\\'t connect \r\nwith much anyway as they\\\'re all much older) so \\\'the man\\\' \r\ngets 100% pure work out of me.  i\\\'m here maybe 4 hours most \r\ndays.  in any other setting, i don\\\'t think i could churn \r\nout even 4 hours of daydreaming in a day. dif\\\'rent strokes \r\nfor dif\\\'rent folks, but i like to see work as something \r\nthat suistains my life (not vice versa) so i get my work \r\ndone and get out, no workplace languishing here.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6533,1517,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<tt>Very fly. My eye enjoyed your entry. you\\\'re seemingly \r\nyearning y\\\'s... very lovely entry.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6534,1517,'2001-08-07 17:19:05',0,'referee:','two points deducted for double use of \\\'very\\\' and \\\'entry\\\'.\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6535,1507,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i think \\\'mons veneris\\\' is less sexie than \\\'pubic \r\narea\\\'<tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6536,1503,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>we wake up at dawn cause we\\\'re so coked up, you \r\nknow.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6537,1522,'2001-08-07 17:48:31',0,'kat','it is 11am and i have yet to even take a shower, or get \r\ndressed, or make my bed. in fact i keep getting back into \r\nbed. i am feeling feral.',1,0,0,0,'32.102.110.237','en'),(6538,1503,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','being coked up is cool. this is the \\\"me\\\" generation. bring on the \r\nbelted sweater dress and cutoff flashdance sweatshirt.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(6539,1515,'2001-08-07 17:56:24',0,'le, regarding egg\\\'s labia','i had ducky ass undies when i was a child. i referred to them as my \r\nFANCY PANTS. i have recently discovered that they have ADULT \r\nSIZED RUFFLE ASS FANCY PANTS at the costume shop way down \r\nfillmore. let\'s go there when you give up the east coast next.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(6540,1524,'2001-08-07 18:05:3