2','en'),(6585,404,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i used to work for a cheesy t-shirt printer in savannah and it was \r\nmy job to make the screens for the shirts. i took screens that \r\nalready had the emulsion painted on them and used a really \r\nunglamorous method of attaching patterns to them and exposing \r\nthem to light. i don\\\'t know if that\\\'s anything like what you\\\'re \r\ntalking about. it involved a light table and a garden hose. ok.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(6586,1529,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i wanna go to a club where all they play is up-\r\ntempo <a href=\\\"http://www.muzak.com\\\"><b>MUZAK</b></a>.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6587,1529,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>also... i <i>hate</i> those guys that come up to \r\nyou in times square with a clipboard and flashy clothes and \r\nsay \\\"Hey Buddy, do you <i>like</i> sketch comedy?!\\\" and \r\nthen try to hit you up to buy tickets with some schtick \r\nabout how great the act they\\\'re promoting is.  I\\\'ve taken \r\nto answering them, without missing a beat, with \\\"Hey Buddy, \r\nI hate sketch comedy, but i\\\'m waaaay into amateur \r\nproctology. wanna give it a whirl?\\\".  And it works.  They \r\nturn around and walk off without fail.  Mean, perhaps, but \r\na guy can only take so much sassy sketch comedy promotion \r\nin a day.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6588,1527,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i feel you, green.  two years ago, while in school, \r\ni had a B in an important biochem class.  so that i could \r\nspend an important day with the object of my smitten \r\naffection (who is now, at the moment, breaking my heart in \r\na sublime way), i skipped the final, and scored a nice \r\nround D.  it was worth it at the time.  now that i\\\'m waging \r\nwar with grad school applications, its come back to haunt \r\nme in a big ol\\\' nasty way.  add to the fact that said girl \r\nis flaking on me, and i\\\'m at a loss.  moral of the story? i \r\ndont know.  i just <i>empathize</i>, and being an emotional \r\nperson, thats good for me.  i did manage to stay on a \r\nsports team for 4 years, and get up every morning at 5:10am \r\nto go dawdle in the Harlem River- i agree, such is \r\ntheraputic.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6589,1517,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','i say fucky too.  fucky and sucky, but not at the same time\r\nusually, unless i\\\'m singing along to 2 live crew.',4,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(6590,1532,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','and <a href=\\\"http://www.airdisaster.com/\\\">this</a>.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(6591,1532,'2001-08-08 13:35:58',0,'damn','i think that site is porny for some folks',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6592,1531,'2001-08-08 13:38:31',0,'Barry Manilow','<br><tt>They were young and they had each other, who could \r\nask for more? At the Copa, Copacabana, the hottest site \r\nnorth of Havana... music and passion were always the \r\nfashion at the Copaaaaaaa, they fell in love!</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6593,1530,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>\\\"why did you yell fire when you fell into the \r\nchocolate?\\\"...\\\"because no one would have come if I had have \r\nyelled \\\'CHOCOLATE!\\\'\\\".',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6594,1526,'2001-08-08 13:41:03',0,'ben folds','gimme my money back, you bitch.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6595,1519,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>at the Jersey shore, they call the floating tampons \r\n<i>\\\"Beach Whistles\\\"</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6596,1532,'2001-08-08 14:25:36',0,'Jamazon','crash \\\'n burn',6,0,0,0,'217.32.129.44','en'),(6597,1530,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','Ahhh.... poor Kat doesn\\\'t have a boyfriend... I <i>hear</I> \r\nstrategically placed peanutbutter and a friendly dog can be \r\nbetter than a man.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(6598,1531,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','From now on, Barry Manilow will represent the me who stands \r\nfrozen like a dear in the headlights of beautiful eyes \r\nstaring at me, smiling at <i>me</I>.  Then, while I\\\'m \r\nwalking away (instead of towards), Barry will kick me in \r\nthe back of the head, sing <i>Copa Cabana</i>, and dance \r\nmerengue.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(6599,1531,'2001-08-08 15:09:05',0,'Sean Bateman','The eyes... those eyes of Barry Manilow.  They peer deep \r\nwithin my soul, beaming through their Ambervisionâ„¢ \r\nspectacles.  I dreamed I took Mr. Manilow for a ride on the \r\nback of my motorcycle once, you know.  He giggled through \r\nthe traffic circles, cha-cha-ed through the 4-way-stops, \r\nand grasped his arms tightly around my torso, cleching deep \r\ninto my sinews.  Barry Manilow.  Riding with me.  Later \r\nthan night, we made love quietly on my dorm-room floor; all \r\nthe while, those eyes, sweet crooning gems, pierced deep \r\ninto my soul, and enflamed me with the ardour of the \r\n<b>SALSA</b>!',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6600,1530,'2001-08-08 15:10:42',0,'Haute Frijoles','straight from the nut is best, i always say.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6601,1531,'2001-08-08 15:35:13',0,'Patrick Bateman','I hate Barry Manilow. Although I could eat him <i>with</i> \r\nsalsa. Rock\\\'n\\\'roll.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6602,1530,'2001-08-08 15:38:06',0,'green','essemar you PERVE\r\ngood work Kat....the word pervy is there\r\nAnd to FELICITY THANKS FOR THE STUFF IT JUST CAME IN THE \r\nMAIL YESTERDAY',1,0,0,0,'198.81.16.26','en'),(6603,1527,'2001-08-08 15:40:42',0,'green','thanx peter. what u wrote has helped. i supose i hould just \r\ntrain with the x-country team....even though I wont be ON \r\nIT...',1,0,0,0,'198.81.16.26','en'),(6604,1537,'2001-08-08 15:47:40',0,'Jamazon','pornographic?',4,0,0,0,'217.32.129.44','en'),(6605,1537,'2001-08-08 15:52:09',0,'Mr. T','This be some of that <b>Porn<i>y</i></b> jibba-jabba. I \r\npitty the poor fool!',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6606,1533,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>no, but I can smell my co-worker\\\'s b.o.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6607,1531,'2001-08-08 15:53:53',0,'Bret Easton Ellis','why, scooter my daisy heads!',6,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6608,1537,'2001-08-08 15:58:36',0,'will','Oh, the horror!  The horror! <br />\r\nThe horrible unfairness of it all!',4,0,0,0,'198.214.178.232','en'),(6609,1532,'2001-08-08 15:59:25',0,'<i>B</i>est <i>F</i>riendly','burn! Burn!',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6610,1537,'2001-08-08 16:06:34',0,'Dude','I prefer women that go braless.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6611,1531,'2001-08-08 16:08:09',0,'chew on this','',2,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6613,1533,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','being a mentally ill person, this offends me. it continually \r\namazes me that, in today\\\'s p.c. society, racist, sexist, and \r\nhomophobic comments are all taboo, but crazies are fair \r\ngame.  mental illness could happen to you, and there\\\'s a \r\ngood chance it will affect someone in your family or someone \r\nyou know.  open your mind up a little bit.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.79.117','en'),(6612,1531,'2001-08-08 16:08:55',0,'chew on this','\r\n<img src=\"http://apeculture.com/Manilow_Music_of_My_House.jpg\">',2,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6614,1531,'2001-08-08 16:11:40',0,'<b>I have Seen the Lights</b>','<center><img \r\nsrc=\\\"http://w3.one.net/~erikog/mc/disco/manilow.jpg\\\">',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6615,1531,'2001-08-08 16:12:50',0,'Those suck. dig this one:','<img \r\nsrc=\\\"http://w3.one.net/~shlybluz/jmoore/manilow/manilow1.jpg\r\n\\\">',2,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6616,1530,'2001-08-08 16:17:26',0,'kat','thanks Ess...i know you have hands-on experience when it \r\ncomes to flesh alternatives, but really sex is not the \r\nproblem. booty is always available if i should choose to \r\ntake advantage of it.\r\n\r\n<p><i>[the heart is a lonely hunter]</i></p>',3,0,0,0,'32.102.110.65','en'),(6617,1531,'2001-08-08 16:21:31',0,'kat','wow, i never realized he was one of the muppets before.',1,0,0,0,'32.102.110.65','en'),(6618,1531,'2001-08-08 16:30:54',0,'Kiff to Kat','<center>And artistic, too:</center>\r\n<br>\r\n<center><img src=\\\"http://www.nealportnoy.com/neal/new%\r\n20stuff/images/manilow.gif\\\"></center>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6619,1533,'2001-08-08 16:34:14',0,'bmg','coming from a manic depressive family (that daily pops \r\nprozac, zoloft,  effexor, luvox, and others -) I find this post \r\ndisgusting, and just plain shitty... but that is also why I \r\nlaughed so hard when I read it.  The joke around my \r\nhouse when someone gets fucky, wacky whatever, is to \r\nsay this in a loud and obnoxious voice \\\"Did we forget \r\nour Prozac today, [name of family member]? \\\" \r\nSometimes, this is the case, but there are other times \r\nwhere this triggers the family member to realize that \r\nthey are being hard to deal with resulting i them \r\ncalming down. This of course has gone on since i was \r\na little boy, three of my family members were able to \r\nkick the habbit (prozac, ridilin) and i think the others are \r\ngoing to continue being mental. I swear, laughing and \r\ntalking about the shit make it a lot easier to deal with... \r\ntime for my medicine. ',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(6620,1531,'2001-08-08 16:34:33',0,'<b>burn, burn!</b>','<img src=\\\"http://www.audiomixers.com/images/manilow.GIF\\\">',6,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6621,1531,'2001-08-08 16:35:43',0,'Barry, his-self:','<img \r\nsrc=\"http://www.telegraph.co.uk/graphics/ads/b/boxoffice/man\r\nilow.jpg\"></tt>aged to perfection!',4,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6622,1531,'2001-08-08 16:37:04',0,'beelzebubba','<br></tt>It\'s not Barry Manilo, but its good.<br>\r\n<img src=\"http://www.the-\r\nforum.com/ephemera/images/rrs012.jpg\">',2,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6623,1531,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','</center><br><img \r\nsrc=\"http://royaltyfreemusic.com/pic18.JPG\" \r\nalign=\'left\'><tt>I don\'t know about you, but these here \r\nfellas make me all hot and bothered. Dig the feathered frolets and Barry\'s nice sporty yet casual know-how.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6624,1530,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>in my adolescent days, my mom and i had a talk that went something like...\"Peter, guys dont seem to realize that when a girl wants sex, she can, unlike him, snap her fingers and a eager throng of men will appear for said duty.  love is not so simply acquired, and is so much more sought after. when the sex has come and gone and coem back again, love is nice to have around.\" gotta love being a teenager and having sex-talks with mom.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6625,1527,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i took very few credits my senior year as i had \r\nfulfilled all the requirements already.  unfortunately, \r\nNCAA didnt want to let me compete without my requsite 12 \r\ncredits.  so, i just practiced with the crew team anyway, \r\nhad a blast, stayed in shape, and... ended up competing \r\nwithout NCAA ever being the wiser. shhh!</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6626,1532,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','I have a friend who is going to be taking her first flight \r\nin a month or so.  I probably don\\\'t want her to see this.',1,0,0,0,'64.229.68.109','en'),(6627,1504,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','I agree with Peter.  This is an interesting forum, more so \r\nthan IRC or something similar because it is written \r\npieces.  You do have the potential to write total fiction \r\nhere and, depending on how careful and skillful you were, \r\ncould probably fool some people quite easily.  But somehow \r\nI doubt that a lot of the people here are writing fiction.',3,0,0,0,'64.229.68.109','en'),(6628,1537,'2001-08-08 17:37:22',0,'mojo','I used to drive a long commute without a shirt or bra on.  I\nloved the attention it provided, even if it was a tad\npaltry.<br>\nBut let\\\'s get really wild -- let\\\'s get sexy on public\ntransit. Stories, stories?\n  ',2,0,0,0,'64.10.134.128','en'),(6629,1537,'2001-08-08 18:02:38',0,'bmg','i would like to go <a href=\'http://www.sss.org/texnude/hhpix.html\' target=new> hippie hollow</a> this weekend - get \r\nnaked, bake in the sun - look at old and young men and \r\nwomen... Hippie hollow is the place of my first nude \r\nexperience, i was eight and i remember a woman on a \r\nraft nude... i wasn\'t sure how to react other than stare at \r\nher. then we all jumped in the water naked.',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(6630,1530,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<p>... and that\\\'s why I wish I was gay.</P>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(6631,1530,'2001-08-08 18:15:20',0,'carson mccullers','yes, dear, the heart is in fact a lonely hunter.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(6632,1537,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','i think this is cute\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(6633,1530,'2001-08-08 18:57:27',0,'kat','buddha is that you? smart ass...',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.133','en'),(6634,1530,'2001-08-08 20:52:05',0,'deb','i had/have a friend exactly like that. 40ish yr old pervert \r\ntype boy... but extremely honest. what can i say?',2,0,0,0,'205.188.200.58','en'),(6635,1530,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon to kat:','no, it was me.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(6636,1540,'2001-08-08 23:48:58',0,'chi chi','i\\\'m a dry heat kind of person, i love the heat, i crave it. \r\nbut if it\\\'s too humid then it\\\'s icky..<br>\r\nactually where i grew up was desert, but on the coast \r\nand humid, so in the spring when the rest of the country \r\nhad sand storms, we would have mud storms. <br>\r\nicky moist sandy air.',0,0,0,0,'64.168.23.62','en'),(6637,1540,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','i like the sticky heat. also, i love this diner in brooklyn \r\non graham st. near the L stop. danielle\\\'s, i think. maybe. i \r\nforget. but during the week, the breakfast special is, or \r\nwas, $1 for two eggs any style, toast, potatoes and coffee. \r\nthey also made homemade donuts. and my favorite waitress was \r\nmissing her two front teeth. she gave me bacon to give to my \r\ngirlfriend\\\'s dog who waited outside howling at me to finish.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(6638,1540,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','all of those things sound good. especially the donuts.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(6639,1529,'2001-08-09 01:11:13',0,'liver','hm.  i suddenly find myself yearning for sassy sketch \r\ncomedy promotion.  ',3,0,0,0,'63.202.215.130','en'),(6640,1527,'2001-08-09 01:34:32',0,'green','yeah...thats a nice story peter.\r\ngee, i want to quit my job\r\n',1,0,0,0,'198.81.17.151','en'),(6641,1540,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','i like your pics, but do they have to be so big and in the \r\ntitle? ',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(6642,1541,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','never too early to buy me flowers. never. i can email you \r\nmy address.',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(6643,1533,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','if i sell everything i own and cash in my 401k i could just\r\nmake it in!',4,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(6644,454,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','february is my worst month and best month. you have \r\npoignant moments in february. you wake up, and decide that \r\nyou will simultaneously succumb to and revolt against this \r\nfoul day. you lay in bed with the cat or a man and call in \r\nsick. or take bong hits and listen to Piano Magic and write \r\npoetry. or just watch a Tartovsky film in bed. oh, there \r\nare so many things for a self-indulgent person to do in \r\nfebruary! and having a partner in crime makes it delicious. \r\ni am going to bookmark this comment to look at for february \r\n2002. <b>ps</b> maybe let\\\'s have a \\\"feb-in\\\" in february. \r\nhot soup sharing and sad whispering about the rain and the \r\npast. <b>ps</b> im batty as hell!',0,0,0,0,'216.243.8.198','en'),(6645,1533,'2001-08-09 03:48:48',0,'mr. happy','<img \r\nsrc=\\\'http://swinney.org/journals/images/