ort runs over my apartment. the \r\nsound gets louder and louder as they go by, and i always \r\nask: is this the one that crashes into my building? i think \r\ni\\\'d never know if it hit, that\\\'s what freaks me out. alive, \r\ndead. lights out.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.186','en'),(6654,454,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','you like \\\"andrei rublev\\\"? that\\\'s what february\\\'s about - \r\nfaith. faith that spring will come again.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.79.93','en'),(6655,665,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','serendipity\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.79.93','en'),(6656,777,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','try swinney.org tattoos on the forehead\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.79.93','en'),(6657,999,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','i\\\'ve never been brave enough to ask anybody else for money \r\nlike that. whenever somebody asks me for something, i give \r\nit to them. i think, \\\"they might be an angel.\\\"\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.79.93','en'),(6658,1537,'2001-08-09 06:11:50',0,'kat','i once slept in a crackhouse on fifth...right off the music \r\ndrag. well okay, it wasn\\\'t a real crackhouse but it came \r\nclose. frightening bathroom stink. someone screaming on the \r\nother side of the wall at 4am. one room and six sleeping \r\nbodies...all of us on the floor. \r\n\r\n<p><i>word to the wise: if your boyfriend is taking you out \r\nof town and swears a buddy will let you crash at his place, \r\nget ye to the nearest motel 6...and worry about the bruised \r\nego later on. \\\"what, you don\\\'t trust me?\\\"</i></p>',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.11','en'),(6659,1111,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','the boy looked at johnny<BR><BR>horses horses horses \r\nhorses<BR><BR>do some research on totem animals\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.79.93','en'),(6660,1539,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i think you did the right thing. it is easy to blow someone \r\nup to hateworthy when they\\\'re never really in your space. \r\nshe will come back down to normal girl with flaws and good \r\nthings too, when you\\\'re with her in the flesh. ',0,0,0,0,'63.93.104.209','en'),(6661,111,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','sometimes i want to do the taoist thing and withdraw from \r\nsociety. for years. go off and become superhuman or \r\nsomething. live in a cabin and never see anybody. build up \r\nmy qi. lay the groundwork for immortality.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.79.93','en'),(6662,222,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','i\\\'m 31 and i live with my parents. i wish i had the luxury \r\nof wondering when to call them.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.79.93','en'),(6663,1540,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','smaller. not in the title. ',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(6664,111,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','captains log: i started to say something here about not \r\nbeing ordinary, but then i thought \\\"who am i to give any \r\nadvice about life?\\\" and decided not to.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.186','en'),(6665,333,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','sometimes i will call myself the matt mccord. like \\\"the bill \r\ndoss.\\\"\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.79.93','en'),(6666,333,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','why don\\\'t you shut up and go to bed.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.79.93','en'),(6667,333,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','come shut me up\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.79.93','en'),(6668,444,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','(sings) let\\\'s go to heaven in my car<BR><BR>(regular matt \r\nvoice) speaking of which, i got a car recently. \\\'90 (or \r\n\\\'91?) dodge dynasty. driving for the first time in eight \r\nyears was surreal.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.79.93','en'),(6669,111,'2001-08-09 06:37:55',0,'tyler --fuck it :','you are a really good writer, elly. you should take it \r\nseriously; using the internet as a forum is great, but \r\nimagine what picasso\\\'s life might have been like if he had \r\npainted all his works on billboards over the highway or on \r\nthe sidewalks of New York, as he might well have done had \r\nhe not had formal training. having something to devote your \r\nlife to outside of the commonplace(relationships, money-\r\nthese are important but ordinary) makes time hum and \r\ncrackle and float by. you are living with purpose. ',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.186','en'),(6670,555,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','all those people were really saying, \\\"i love you.\\\" but they \r\ndidn\\\'t know it. and you didn\\\'t know it.<BR><BR>yeti. i miss \r\nyeti being around. we love you yeti, wherever you are.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.79.93','en'),(6671,111,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','as opposed to living ON purpose. or living in a porpoise.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.79.93','en'),(6672,594,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','and there\\\'s another mia. we miss you, chia.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.79.93','en'),(6673,344,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','this reminds me of william saroyan: \\\"resurrection of a \r\nlife\\\". kinda sublime.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.79.93','en'),(6674,536,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','sometimes openness can be a very spiritual thing. what would \r\nhappen if i told all the secrets i have?  i guess what needs \r\nto be secret has a way of staying secret.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.79.93','en'),(6675,1542,'2001-08-09 07:05:04',0,'heiney','i\\\'m like cryin\\\' and shit over here.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(6676,1542,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','all my friends are ones i made in the last 3 or 4 \r\nyears.  sometimes i wonder about the ones from before, \r\nwhat they\\\'re doing. i think they might even have \r\ndisappeared. if i don\\\'t see them anymore, are they \r\nstill there?<BR><BR>my mom and dad like to talk about \r\nthe rapture: all the christians will disappear just \r\nlike that. i like to think if such a silly thing \r\noccured, it would be more gradual, taking place over \r\nyears and years. you would just lose track of them.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.79.93','en'),(6677,1542,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','now that i wrote that, and i got stuck in old email, Im \r\nnostalgic and fucky as hell. I cant dam up the real shit \r\nfo