l be packing up and moving away \r\nthis time. ',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(6863,1563,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','also, <a href=\\\"http://www.diaryland.com\\\">diaryland is \r\ncute</a> too.',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(6864,1563,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','mister richard smoker?',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(6865,1562,'2001-08-10 16:40:21',0,'ghost','never never NEVER apologize for raw emotional outbursts. it \r\nis a beautiful thing. languish in it awhile....it will \r\ndrive you to find the things you need most. maybe not a \r\nmove, but something else? ',1,0,0,0,'32.102.109.115','en'),(6866,1563,'2001-08-10 16:49:09',0,'jeff & bruce','will meet you in the bar',0,0,0,0,'12.110.65.60','en'),(6867,1562,'2001-08-10 17:16:13',0,'erbie','ooh what a fun post to respond to.  because don\\\'t you know, \r\nI wish I had all that time on my hands.  here is what I \r\nwould do:\r\n\r\n-practice guitar\r\n-paint with watercolors, very slowly and patiently\r\n-write poetry on thick white paper with a black brush pen\r\n-write letters to all the friends I miss\r\n-take really long walks and sing to myself\r\n-invite my employed friends to come and visit on weekends\r\n-meditate\r\n-breathe\r\n-choreograph dances to music I hear in my head (or to TV \r\ncommercials--sometimes this makes them more bearable)\r\n-get a kitten and spend a lot of time petting it\r\n-stretch a lot\r\n-make huge yummy salads with sprouts and red peppers and \r\nsunflower seeds and vinaigrette\r\n-breathe\r\n-ground out all of the anxiety that floats ambient in my \r\nday to day consciousness\r\n-wiggle and squirm\r\n-make bread\r\n-take baths\r\n-draw all of those characters who talk to me in my head \r\n(especially the curmudgeon, who says when things are going \r\nwell, \\\"This\\\'ll never last.\\\"  What does he look like?)\r\n-make some kickass costumes--gluing rhinestones onto \r\npantyhose and then wrapping the pantyhose all around my body\r\n-poke the dirt with a stick\r\n-watch the water roll down\r\n-breathe\r\ne',1,0,0,0,'216.185.7.75','en'),(6868,1566,'2001-08-10 17:19:55',0,'ghost','<p>blasted futures need no <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.superbad.com\\\" \r\ntarget=\\\"_blank\\\">release</a>.<br>\r\nyou were here<br>\r\nriding last nights wind.<br>\r\nflesh <a href=\\\"http://www.anilgupta.com/images/LP.jpg\\\" \r\ntarget=\\\"_blank\\\">carved</a>...with\r\ncolorless eyes.<br>\r\ni knew your shadow.<br>\r\nmetal <a href=\\\"http://www.bodym.com/perfpup.htm\\\" \r\ntarget=\\\"_blank\\\">mercury</a><br>\r\nfreak.</p>\r\n',4,0,0,0,'32.102.109.115','en'),(6869,1559,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','\r\nthis is a great quiz. i think i might take it this saturday \r\nor something. sit down with sharpened No#2\\\'s, and lots of \r\nwhiteout. rubber cement. some nice glue sticks. some smells \r\nare just inspiring enough without you having to actually \r\nuse them.',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(6870,1563,'2001-08-10 17:42:41',0,'green','I am starting my own journal.so chill\r\n ...anybody want to write...for me???\r\nevery thing written posted...it isnt up yet but will be at \r\npondjuice.com\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'152.163.194.181','en'),(6871,1563,'2001-08-10 17:55:04',0,'green','Diary land is GROSS and SCARY',6,0,0,0,'198.81.17.54','en'),(6872,1563,'2001-08-10 19:25:51',0,'i think it\\\'s cute','http://simon-fk.diaryland.com/older.html\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(6873,1563,'2001-08-10 19:26:18',0,'and i\\\'m a dork','<a href=\\\"http://simon-fk.diaryland.com/older.html\\\">hi</a>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(6874,1563,'2001-08-10 19:50:01',0,'jo','also livejournal has the comments aspect, too. ',1,0,0,0,'64.12.96.200','en'),(6875,1563,'2001-08-10 20:01:55',0,'brewguru99','What is the purpose of it all then!\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nWhy would anyone post on here at all? I understand that \r\nAustin would like to maintain a clean website with good \r\ncontent, but that is what their approval process for each \r\nsubmission is for. If they didn\\\'t think it merrited it\\\'s on \r\nplace on the site then it would\\\'ve gotten blocked.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nSimply because several submissions are by one person does \r\nnot degrade their individual quality. Each one must be \r\nrated as a unique entry, no relation to any others.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nEnvy of another writer should not exist on here. Let the \r\nsite be filled with good content, not sparse article \r\nwriters.',3,0,0,0,'66.12.171.62','en'),(6876,1563,'2001-08-10 20:06:59',0,'green to brewguru99','i agree \r\nso FUCK Y\\\'ALL',6,0,0,0,'198.81.17.29','en'),(6877,1563,'2001-08-10 20:07:40',0,'nihilism','what <i>is</i> the purpose of it all, anyway?',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(6878,1568,'2001-08-10 20:20:03',0,'green','yeah i remember that game. Dont worry i am unemplyed as \r\nwell and if you ever come to california you can sleep on my \r\nfloor.\r\n\r\nokay.well. \r\ntake care.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'198.81.17.29','en'),(6879,1568,'2001-08-10 20:22:26',0,'chi chi','oh yes! and how about <font color=\\\"#FF0000\\\">\r\nRedrover</font>?',0,0,0,0,'64.168.22.20','en'),(6880,1563,'2001-08-10 20:30:12',0,'existentialism','maman died today....',6,0,0,0,'198.81.17.29','en'),(6881,1568,'2001-08-10 20:46:33',0,'Treetop','To green.  Thanks so much for the offer.  I already live in \r\nSan Francisco.  I am not unemployed by choice.  There are \r\nnot many jobs here at the moment.  Maybe it is a good time \r\nto start a business, or a revolution, or feed the ducks...',1,0,0,0,'172.149.134.233','en'),(6882,1568,'2001-08-10 20:53:26',0,'redrover','redrover, send chi chi on over.',0,0,0,0,'172.149.134.233','en'),(6883,1568,'2001-08-10 21:03:03',0,'puppy','i, too, have thought that the time is ripe to begin a new \r\nadventure, begin a business, create my own rules. i may end \r\nup becoming a freelancer; however i think i would prefer \r\nhaving an actual \\\"storefront.\\\" it\\\'s much more romantic...',0,0,0,0,'192.35.232.241','en'),(6884,1562,'2001-08-10 21:12:40',0,'puppy','hi mr. bmg :) miss you too. erbie is right, by the way. and \r\ncongrats on going back to school! that rocks! really and \r\ntruly... i\\\'ll e-mail you later.\r\n\r\n<p>i know it\\\'s really hard to do things when you think you \r\nshould be doing something else; e.g., play guitar when you \r\nshould be finding work. but work is really nothing more \r\nthan a part of life, just as everything else is, and so we \r\nshould <i>savor</i> each moment and turn it into what we \r\nwant it to be.\r\n\r\n<p>i wish i could go home from work, right now, and do one \r\nof the things that erbie mentioned... *sigh*',0,0,0,0,'192.35.232.241','en'),(6885,1568,'2001-08-10 21:14:07',0,'Treetop','to puppy.  We could open a little shop, a little shop that \r\nsells things.  We could call it Grasshopper.  Have you seen \r\nmy grasshopper momma?  Oops, I blew it, its a moth...\r\n\r\n(taken from Jim)',0,0,0,0,'172.149.134.233','en'),(6886,1552,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','buff fireboys...mmm...\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.5.204','en'),(6887,1568,'2001-08-10 21:17:56',0,'puppy','hehe... the street i live on is called \\\"Grasshopper.\\\"',0,0,0,0,'192.35.232.241','en'),(6888,1568,'2001-08-10 21:23:22',0,'Treetop','Puppy, it is destiny then...',0,0,0,0,'172.149.134.233','en'),(6889,1568,'2001-08-10 21:33:41',0,'puppy','what would we sell? grasshoppers? moths? changlings?',0,0,0,0,'192.35.232.241','en'),(6890,1568,'2001-08-10 21:47:36',0,'treetop','Selling things like exquisite clothes and fabric from India \r\n(manufatured in mexico of course).  We could start a server \r\nfarm.  We could sell greens hair.  Never sell your soul...',0,0,0,0,'172.149.134.233','en'),(6891,1551,'2001-08-10 22:07:23',0,'chia to peter','you read the book too eh? god damn political philosophy \r\nclasses! i hate the author. i know the book was apology but \r\nwhatever it was dumb. ',6,0,0,0,'24.43.182.49','en'),(6892,1563,'2001-08-10 22:27:48',0,'genet','eat a dick!\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(6893,1568,'2001-08-10 22:44:53',0,'puppy','we could sell green hair. or, maybe a sod farm. that could \r\nbe relatively easy. although we\\\'ll need to have kids, so we \r\ncan have someone to mow the lawn....',0,0,0,0,'66.68.153.82','en'),(6894,1563,'2001-08-10 22:59:41',0,'kat to green n brew','um...i think you\\\'re misunderstanding. you might or might \r\nhave not noticed that most folks on here also have their \r\nown journals. fanatics they are. they just want you in the \r\nfold. part of the flock. immersion. expansion....what have \r\nyou. or simply wanting to see another facet of you. i don\\\'t \r\nthink it was intended as alienation.',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.196','en'),(6895,1563,'2001-08-10 23:11:25',0,'brewguru99','to kat: then what is the purpose of this site?',0,0,0,0,'66.12.171.62','en'),(6896,1568,'2001-08-10 23:13:44',0,'Kids','Hey, can we borrow thirty bucks to go to the mall?\r\n\r\n(Note* Mall security guards do not make good babysitters)',0,0,0,0,'172.149.134.233','en'),(6897,1563,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','we\'ve been over this. there\'s even a <a \r\nhref=\"http://swinney.org/journals/faq.phtml\">faq</a>. in \r\ngeneral it\'s pretty tacky to raid the fridge and adjust the \r\nheat, until everyone feels cozy with you.',3,0,0,0,'63.204.27.202','en'),(6898,1563,'2001-08-10 23:30:30',0,'Treetop to green','Would you like a beer? or some chi?  Hmmmm, Chi-beer!',0,0,0,0,'172.149.134.233','en'),(6899,1563,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<PRE>\r\nSubject: RFC #1 GREEN\\\'S FIX\r\n\r\nOhkay,\r\nSUMMARY:\r\n\r\nsummary is i am making a user table to speed things up and\r\nexclude more than one post per person on the front\r\n\r\nPROBLEM:\r\n\r\npeople like green are submitting three posts a day and some\r\npeople dont want to\r\nlook at them all.  editors dont want to be forced into\r\nchosing favorites\r\nand desciding which one to post which to trash just because\r\nthere were\r\nthree in a row.\r\n\r\nSOLUTION?:\r\n\r\ncreate a user table:\r\n\r\nCREATE TABLE articles_user\r\n        (user_id int(11) NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY\r\nauto_increment,\r\n        username varchar(20) NOT NULL,\r\n        most_rescent int(11),\r\n        total_submitted int(11));\r\n\r\n\r\nmysql> desc articles_user;\r\n+-----------------+-------------+------+-----+---------+----------------+\r\n| Field           | Type        | Null | Key | Default |\r\nExtra          |\r\n+-----------------+-------------+------+-----+---------+----------------+\r\n| user_id         | int(11)     |      | PRI | NULL    |\r\nauto_increment |\r\n| username        | varchar(20) |      |     |        \r\n|                |\r\n| most_rescent    | int(11)     | YES  |     | NULL   \r\n|                |\r\n| total_submitted | int(11)     | YES  |     | NULL   \r\n|                |\r\n+-----------------+-------------+------+-----+---------+----------------+\r\n4 rows in set (0.00 sec)\r\n\r\nPopulate it:\r\n\r\nINSERT INTO articles_user (username, total_submitted)\r\n        SELECT DISTINCT username, count(username) AS\r\ntotal_submitted\r\n        FROM articles_info\r\n        GROUP BY username;       \r\nThen add this to the submission into the database process:\r\n\r\n  $res = @mysql_query(\\\"UPDATE articles_user SET\r\nmost_rescent=$article_id,\r\ntotal_submitted=total_submitted+1 WHERE\r\nusername=\\\'$username\\\'\\\");\r\n\r\n  if ($res == false) {\r\n\r\n  # res one failed, go res two\r\n  # this is a new username to swinney.org\r\n\r\n  $res = @mysql_query(\\\"INSERT INTO articles_user\r\n(\\\'username\\\',\\\'most_rescent\\\',\\\'total_submitted\\\') VALUES\r\n(\\\'$username\\\',$article_id, 1);\r\n\r\n  }\r\n\r\ner something like that...\r\n\r\nhere is the submit page, ALL WHO GO THERE, PH33R:\r\nhttp://swinney.org/cgi/cvsweb.cgi/swinney.org/journals/submit_article.phtml?rev=1.8&content-typ\r\ne=text/x-cvsweb-markup\r\n\r\nTHEN when selecting out articles to exclude the likes of\r\nGREENS:\r\n\r\nselect article_id, articles_info.username, title FROM\r\narticles_info LEFT JOIN articles_user ON\r\narticles_info.article_id=articles_user.most_rescent where\r\narticles_user.most_rescent<>\\\"NULL\\\" ORDER BY article_id DESC\r\nLIMIT 5;\r\n\r\nonly more efficient because that one takes: 8 rows in set\r\n(2.11 sec)\r\nOR BETTER YET:\r\n\r\non the last query, snafu said:\r\nSELECT article_id,articles_info.username,title FROM\r\narticles_info,articles_user WHERE\r\narticles_info.article_id=articles_user.most_rescent AND\r\narticles_user.most_rescent ORDER BY article_id;\r\nthis way it takes 8 rows in set (0.01 sec)\r\n*nice*\r\n\r\nMK?\r\n</PRE>',4,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(6900,1563,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','oh yea,<BR> <FONT SIZE=\\\"8\\\">SUCK IT!</FONT>',4,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(6901,1563,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','ascii art.',3,0,0,0,'63.204.27.202','en'),(6902,1563,'2001-08-11 01:24:18',0,'tom','<i>come down of the cross...we need the wood</i>',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.196','en'),(6903,1568,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>a mall security guard once lectured me, \\\"don\\\'t let your\r\nlittle head think for your big head.\\\"  he let that happen\r\nand had a kid at 18.  i think he was about 23 at the time. \r\ni was in the process of being busted for riding my\r\nskateboard.  i just nodded my head and agreed that it would\r\nbe bad to let my little head think for my big head.  he let\r\nme go.</P>',3,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(6904,1568,'2001-08-11 01:58:23',0,'kat to tree','well come on up to the mountains...at least for a visit. my \r\nroom is not Hawaii but it has a nice view and a wiggly hula-\r\ngirl.',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.196','en'),(6905,1564,'2001-08-11 02:26:26',0,'deb','yea.. it\\\'s 10\\\"30 friday night\r\nfight club is on now\r\n\\\"you\\\'re not your job... you\\\'re not how much money you have \r\nin the bank... you\\\'re not the car you drive...\\\"',2,0,0,0,'152.163.213.181','en'),(6906,1562,'2001-08-11 03:32:50',0,'sic','i get restless too...maybe it is a good thing you dont know \r\nme...we would cause too much trouble ;)',0,0,0,0,'63.151.67.78','en'),(6907,1566,'2001-08-11 03:47:14',0,'sic','i am in love with wolfwood. if i had more time i would make \r\na shrine to that hot smoking priest. meoooow',0,0,0,0,'63.151.67.78','en'),(6908,1566,'2001-08-11 03:50:23',0,'bmg to sic','I can give you woolfwood\\\'s phone number.',0,0,0,0,'198.92.132.154','en'),(6909,1566,'2001-08-11 04:07:47',0,'sic to bmg','you would be my new best friend if you did *roar*',0,0,0,0,'63.151.67.78','en'),(6910,1570,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','i keep thinking about my father\\\'s funeral. how i would want \r\nto speak. what i would say. how i\\\'d sing \\\"perfect day,\\\" \r\naccompany it on the organ.  this makes me want to cry, but \r\nit has a way of sharpening your affections, makes you \r\nappreciate your people more. because someday they WILL die, \r\nand you will terribly miss all those times they pissed you \r\noff, irritated you, embarassed and mistreated you, took you \r\nfor granted. you would give anything to have your worst day \r\nwith them back.<BR><BR>and someday you will miss yourself \r\nlike this, too. so enjoy the fool and the saint that you \r\nare.  you\\\'re a star, baby.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.5.39','en'),(6911,1570,'2001-08-11 04:37:34',0,'sic to matt','aww *twinkle in eye*',0,0,0,0,'63.151.67.78','en'),(6912,1571,'2001-08-11 06:05:09',0,'kat to loveliest egg','are you trying to woo me with gobstoppers? don\\\'t you know \r\nhow fixated i am on that movie? because of that movie? i am \r\nfixation...and 93% perspiration, 6% electricity, 4% \r\nevaporation, and 2% butterscotch ripple. you can\\\'t forget \r\nthe ripple.\r\n\r\n\r\n',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.87','en'),(6913,1571,'2001-08-11 06:18:57',0,'xepmom','Applause (loud). There are some in my family who are \r\nwhisperers and mumblers. No one can understand us but our \r\nintimate little group. We bleep half-words, nod in agreement \r\nand skitter away. The others speak clearly with flawless \r\ndiction. They are such a pleasure to listen to.   \r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.174.154.182','en'),(6914,1571,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to kat','we are the musicmakers.',0,0,0,0,'216.243.8.25','en'),(6915,1571,'2001-08-11 06:33:05',0,'ghost','my relations are all loud and brassy. gatherings involve a \r\nbattle of vocal achievements...whoever can talk the loudest \r\ngets to talk. which often involves several repetitions of \r\nthe same comments/stories/arguments. i guess it was my \r\nnature to be the quiet one, the listener. but really i just \r\nfelt much more entertaining to watch the show then be a \r\npart of it. i am known as the \\\'family shade\\\'.',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.33','en'),(6916,1566,'2001-08-11 08:47:27',0,'sic','i cant wait...wolfwood be my man! you are one hot ass \r\npreacher...woo!',0,0,0,0,'4.16.224.124','en'),(6917,1563,'2001-08-11 08:56:27',0,'GREEN','I AM A JEW SO FUCK The cross',6,0,0,0,'64.30.217.44','en'),(6918,1570,'2001-08-11 15:28:50',0,'bmg','I had a dream that my mother passed away as well. In the \r\ndream I was looking to my evil step-mom for support, and \r\nshe was just as cold as allways. So, I start sobbing, I \r\nwake myself up I am crying so hard. when I wipe the tears \r\nfrom my cheak I notice that I wasn\\\'t crying at all I was \r\ndrooling... I hadnt slept well for the past three days, \r\nthat was a nap dream...',1,0,0,0,'198.92.132.154','en'),(6919,1568,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','janice is a nice name for a duck. ',6,0,0,0,'24.43.182.49','en'),(6920,1569,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','<p>That sorry bastard.</p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(6921,1571,'2001-08-11 17:20:03',0,'jo','my family is loud loud loud. and hysterical, and talks over \r\none another and there\\\'s affection thick in the air. \r\nsometimes it\\\'s too much for me and i have to go away. i \r\ntake a bath or go have a smoke on the porch; when i was a \r\nkid, i would take a book into the closet with an ittybitty \r\nbooklight to avoid being found. i\\\'m a lot better at it now \r\nbut it took me 20 or so years and i hope that if i ever get \r\nhitched, my family doesn\\\'t scare away the person i love. ',1,0,0,0,'64.12.106.66','en'),(6922,1571,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','egg, i liked this so so much. very nice...',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(6923,1572,'2001-08-11 17:52:56',0,'kat','B O L O G N A',4,0,0,0,'32.100.71.49','en'),(6924,1571,'2001-08-11 18:39:53',0,'leonard to egg','you are better than what\\\'s on tv.',2,0,0,0,'209.178.129.120','en'),(6925,1571,'2001-08-11 18:39:54',0,'leonard to egg','you are better than what\\\'s on tv.',2,0,0,0,'209.178.129.120','en'),(6926,1572,'2001-08-11 18:42:06',0,'leonard','yeah, my bologna has a first name, it\\\'s a-u-s-t-i-n.',6,0,0,0,'209.178.129.120','en'),(6927,1569,'2001-08-11 18:59:59',0,'Treetop','I was pulled over last week for riding in the passenger \r\nseat without a seatbelt.  The bastard wrote me a $75 \r\nticket.  Damn state troopers...',0,0,0,0,'172.149.134.233','en'),(6928,1570,'2001-08-11 19:31:05',0,'xepmom','The mommas and daddys are going to pass away, as in die. \r\nTheir hope is to do it before you do -- that would be the \r\nreal bad thing. I know it\\\'s scary to profess great love for \r\nfamily -- I was unable to tell my parents that they meant \r\nanything to me because we were not close enough.  Like you, \r\nhowever, I sometimes have the grief dreams. I like them \r\nbecause they hint at a level of emotion I usually don\\\'t feel \r\nwhen awake.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.174.154.84','en'),(6929,1569,'2001-08-11 20:25:56',0,'chi chi','god. yeah oregon state troopers or what ever they are \r\nare assholes. i had an undercover cop follow me for \r\nover an hour i was going 80 (25 over the speed limit) \r\nand the schmuck just followed, i thought he wanted to \r\nbe my driving buddy... <br>\r\nstoopid idiot that i am i wanted to see what my new car \r\ncould do uphill, so at the next hill i gunned it.. 80 - 85- \r\n90  sirens lights the mega phone all come out of no \r\nwhere. the guy had the gall to ask me if i saw him \r\nbehind me. <i> um, no you asshole, officer-sir! you \r\nthink i would have gone 90 in a 60 zone if i knew you \r\nwere a FUCKING COP!</i>',0,0,0,0,'64.168.22.95','en'),(6930,1570,'2001-08-11 20:47:10',0,'kat','<p><i>\\\"they hint at a level of emotion I usually don\\\'t feel \r\nwhen awake\\\"</i></p>\r\n\r\n<p>if i could be so lucky. i am all torrid emotion all the \r\ntime. i think i am cursed.</p>',4,0,0,0,'32.100.71.49','en'),(6931,1569,'2001-08-11 20:55:39',0,'treetop to chi chi','I was in Oregon!  How did you know?  Psychic eh!  I was on \r\nmy way back from Crater Lake and I had to ask my friend to \r\ndrive because I had a small case of elevation sickness.  *\r\n(Going from sea-level to 8 thousand feet with a stuffy nose \r\nis not very comfortable.)  Anyway, the very next day she \r\ngot pulled over again and the pig wrote her and the \r\npassenger a ticket for not wearing a seatbelt.       \r\n<Please wear your seatblet in Oregon>',0,0,0,0,'172.149.134.233','en'),(6932,1572,'2001-08-11 21:30:01',0,'sic','aus everyone wants a piece of that hot programming ass',0,0,0,0,'63.151.67.78','en'),(6933,1568,'2001-08-11 21:31:25',0,'treetop to kat','I would love to visit the mountains.  Have any pictures of \r\nthe view? Hula girl? :)',0,0,0,0,'172.149.134.233','en'),(6934,1568,'2001-08-11 21:32:44',0,'treetop to puppy','Build it and they will come...',0,0,0,0,'172.149.134.233','en'),(6935,1571,'2001-08-11 22:35:26',0,'green','loud is good egg. loud is very good. try a jewish, italian, \r\nspanish, lithuanian with a pinch of mexican and native \r\namerican....It gets LOUD at my house.',1,0,0,0,'198.81.16.179','en'),(6936,1568,'2001-08-11 23:18:20',0,'kat','the view from my bedroom...<br>\r\n<img \r\nsrc=\\\"http://www.lefteyelazy.com/images/photos/home/morningvi\r\new.jpg\\\">\r\n\r\n[hula girl introductions happen only for those who visit \r\nrealtime]\r\n',1,0,0,0,'32.100.7