t likely they \r\nwere the same pros that broke in the first time.  \r\n\r\n<BR><BR>\r\n\r\nI don\\\'t live in that street anymore.  ',1,0,0,0,'203.97.2.242','en'),(6973,1579,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>ugh- that sucks.  my entire car got stolen once, \r\nwhich was really awful as it was literally brand-new.  to \r\nmake matters worse, i didn\\\'t know its registration # or \r\nlicense or anything yet, so it made it basically impossible \r\nto locate.  ahhh, the helpfulness of the nypd.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6974,1579,'2001-08-13 14:30:25',0,'bark','isn\\\'t it weird that they left you the motorcycle money?  I \r\nwonder why.  <nudge> ',0,0,0,0,'12.110.65.22','en'),(6975,1579,'2001-08-13 14:35:42',0,'jo','my friend erin\\\'s car got stolen last week. her 83 cutlass \r\nwas stolen from the parking lot of her complex. her 83 \r\ncutlass! why would you steal that car?<BR>\r\nshe\\\'s decided to take it as a karmic message, too.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(6976,1579,'2001-08-13 14:47:08',0,'puppy','sorry to hear your tale, se&ntilde;or swinney. that really \r\nstinks. but, as you said, what will be will be. I had a \r\nfriend who <i>did</i> take the time to put the face plate \r\nof his stereo in his trunk, only to have it stolen from his \r\ntrunk, causing all sorts of extra damage that wouldn\'t have \r\nhappened if he had just left it in the dash...',0,0,0,0,'192.35.232.241','en'),(6978,1579,'2001-08-13 15:56:46',0,'justino','Good musing Austin, sorry for the initiating incident.  I \r\nthink you might be right to go ahead and use this passing \r\nto consider your relationship with this city; perhaps you \r\nmust live in Oakland now.  No more weed, beer and pussy in \r\nOakland without paying local taxes.  This break-in could be \r\na disguised invitation.<p>\r\n\r\nI was a visitor, I moved here, now I have a quieter Oakland \r\nexistence after an armed robbery and a car breakin.  Now I \r\nhave a crappy stereo that no one steals (replaced lost \r\nplastic knobs with wooden seat cushion beads); I leave my \r\ndoors unlocked and neighborhood wanderers regularly go \r\nthrough my car and take my loose change.  When you plant \r\nyour crops, you should plant enough for the birds to eat \r\nand the thieves to take.<p>\r\n\r\nYou dig so much into your raped car, and there are many \r\ncircumstances that augment that aggrevation.  Still, you \r\ndon\\\'t mention any more about the lost laptop.  Was there \r\ndata on it that mattered?  Was it your active buddy?  Your \r\ninternet umbilical?  Losing my laptop would be the notable \r\nevent for me I think; Linda Wirthheimer and Terry Gross I \r\ncould get back quick.',4,0,0,0,'216.27.176.53','en'),(6979,1579,'2001-08-13 15:57:58',0,'justino','then again, as you alluded to, your stereo and laptop might \r\njust have been your local Oakland tax payments.  ',2,0,0,0,'216.27.176.53','en'),(6980,1583,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','also, what is \\\"mang\\\"?',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(6981,1580,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','communication.  sharing.  only knowing a perspective and\r\nattempting to distribute it to those who might be\r\ninterested.  wanting to ignite emotion in others.  knowing\r\noneself better than anything else in the world.  ',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(6982,1583,'2001-08-13 16:08:57',0,'Doktor','the weird spacing is probably due to the fakt that the \r\neditors were stoned while approving posts',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(6983,1583,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','saucer of milk, table two!',0,0,0,0,'63.93.104.235','en'),(6984,1583,'2001-08-13 16:18:46',0,'bkute','y ask w h y [ ? ] ',5,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(6985,1583,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','i think spacing is sometimes used to indicate continuation \r\nof a line, sometimes it is for readability, sometimes it is \r\nto indicate cadence at which words are to be read, \r\nsometimes, as in your link, it is \r\n<P>just</P><P>the</P><P>way</P><P>paragraph</P><P>tags</P><P\r\n>are</P><P>displayed.</P><CENTER><P>mk?</P></CENTER>',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(6986,1579,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>regarding my laptop, it was merely a glorified and high powered terminal covered in stickers.  i do all my work on remote servers.  in fact, i do all my work on this site.</P>\r\n<P>i am going to have to pick up mister hall\'s narrative \r\nhere and say that if in fact the theft of my stereo and \r\nlaptop was oakland\'s tax, then san francisco must have a \r\ntax too:</P>\r\n<PRE>\r\nrobotec9: hey\r\niamtheBMG: hi\r\nrobotec9: what is the lamest thing that could happen\r\nto you this morning with out anyone getting hurt?\r\nrobotec9: when you hypothetically woke up got ready for\r\nwork and left the house?\r\nrobotec9: and you worked in san antonio\r\nrobotec9: an hour and a half away\r\nrobotec9: also, it was the subject of a major\r\nmotion picture this summer\r\nrobotec9: no pressure\r\n</PRE>',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(6987,1580,'2001-08-13 16:44:17',0,'xepmom','to xep: I love you.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.174.154.232','en'),(6988,1582,'2001-08-13 16:58:30',0,'green','no prob...keep the blab running...it\\\'s great',1,0,0,0,'12.80.20.234','en'),(6989,1583,'2001-08-13 17:10:07',0,'kat','fucking mang, he stood me up!',4,0,0,0,'32.102.110.112','en'),(6990,1580,'2001-08-13 17:11:42',0,'kat to everyone','i want to ignite your emotions. come to me, i am here for \r\nyou.',4,0,0,0,'32.102.110.112','en'),(6991,12,'2001-08-13 17:12:34',0,'bmg','having a job was cool... on the nights i couldn\\\'t sleep, I \r\nwould go to work and work. my mind would drift into \r\npatterns of the words on the screen, i would see how \r\nlong I could go with my vision distorted on purpose... \r\nwhile working... just typing away at some perl hack \r\nre-aranging sentences and paragraphs. sometimes I \r\nwould do some evil handy work for the people that \r\nworked on my stuff after me... and they would be \r\npleased... i would be pleased, and the boss was \r\npleased... other times I would do not so extraordinary \r\nwork and no one would be pleased... i miss the dark \r\nhours of working, i hated the days... the days killed my \r\nsoul cause I would have to see this girl that I had dated \r\nfor a while, lusted for a long while... and then had to see \r\nher doing the same with a friend of mine that worked \r\nright next to me... ugh.',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(6992,136,'2001-08-13 17:20:44',0,'iona','<img src:\\\"http://www.jessejoker.org/images/ioana.jpg\\\"> \r\ngive me your money, sucka!',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(6993,1582,'2001-08-13 17:21:03',0,'The cynical essemar','She\\\'s just setting you up for a bigger fall.  Dump the \r\nbitch before she plunges the venomed dagger into your back.',6,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(6994,1579,'2001-08-13 17:21:18',0,'kat','i was just talking with my mom the other day about how your \r\nperspective can change so drastically once you\\\'ve been \r\nthrough a situation that equals violation. it amazes me \r\nwhen i visit friends who never lock their doors or close \r\ntheir windows at night. i long for this freedom. she knew \r\nwhat i meant, both of us never forgetting the time our \r\nlittle apartment was broken into. just me and her living \r\ntogether and coming home to a wide open door and space full \r\nof destruction. we were shell shocked.',2,0,0,0,'32.102.110.112','en'),(6995,136,'2001-08-13 17:21:32',0,'iona','<img src=\\\'http://www.jessejoker.org/images/ioana.jpg\\\'> \r\nfuck',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(6996,1582,'2001-08-13 17:31:18',0,'essemar the Romantic','<p>\r\nI looked into your eyes tonight<br>\r\nand saw the glimmer of a light<br>\r\na warmth rekindled deep within<br>\r\nto burn away all of our sin</P>\r\n<p>\r\nThe portal of your soul reopenned<br>\r\nand let your spirit soar into night<br>\r\nI saw above our love had ripened<br>\r\nas you lifted us on wings of light.</P>\r\n<p>\r\nThe tale of bliss so rarely told<br>\r\nhas filled my heart and made me bold<br>\r\nto bask inside the light you shine<br>\r\nand make sweet love to she who\\\'s mine</p>',1,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(6997,1583,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','if you don\\\'t like obnoxious spacing, I recommend you never\r\ntry to program in Python.  :-)',3,0,0,0,'24.167.21.142','en'),(6998,1583,'2001-08-13 18:30:47',0,'Treetop','</head>\r\n<body>\r\nThe falling flower\r\n<br>I saw drift back to the branch\r\n<br>Was a butterfly.\r\n<p>Fallen flowers rise\r\n<br>back to the branch--I watch:\r\n<br>oh...butterflies!\r\n<br>~ Moritake(1452-1540)\r\n</body>\r\n</html>',0,0,0,0,'172.169.100.55','en'),(6999,1579,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','packing tape.  the ultimate theft deterrent.  (i hope)',0,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(7000,1579,'2001-08-13 19:14:33',0,'bmg','i didnt know the answer to robotec\\\'s question... still \r\ndon\\\'t know... and he never told me, and i feel left in the \r\ndark. what happened on the way to work?',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(7001,1583,'2001-08-13 19:24:12',0,'wb','ix you are one of those fucking engineer types. you do not \r\nlook at the clouds and see faces, shapes and BEAUTY you \r\nlook at the clouds and see only water vapor. <BR><BR> DAMN \r\nYOU AND YOUR SCIENCE TRYING TO KILL OUR MAGIC<BR><BR><BR> \r\nTHERE IS MAGIC IN THIS SPACING! <BR><BR> EVERYTHING IS NOT \r\nLINEAR, you fuck sludge.',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(7002,1583,'2001-08-13 19:31:02',0,'ghost','fuck sludge?  nice...very very nice. [two points for wb]',1,0,0,0,'32.102.110.112','en'),(7003,1583,'2001-08-13 19:55:39',0,'treetop','</head>\r\n<body>\r\n<font color=\\\"#3333FF\\\"></font>&nbsp;<font \r\ncolor=\\\"#3333FF\\\"></font>\r\n<center>\r\n<p><font color=\\\"#3333FF\\\">tangled </font><font \r\ncolor=\\\"#FF0000\\\">Emotion</font><font color=\\\"#3333FF\\\"></font>\r\n<p><font color=\\\"#3333FF\\\">fuck sludge </font><font \r\ncolor=\\\"#FF0000\\\">On</font><font color=\\\"#3333FF\\\">\r\nmy shoe</font><font color=\\\"#3333FF\\\"></font>\r\n<p><font color=\\\"#3333FF\\\">irrelevant </font><font \r\ncolor=\\\"#FF0000\\\">Suggestions</font>\r\n<br><font color=\\\"#3333FF\\\"></font>&nbsp;\r\n<br><font color=\\\"#3333FF\\\"></font>&nbsp;<font \r\ncolor=\\\"#3333FF\\\"></font>\r\n<p><font color=\\\"#FF0000\\\">Freedom</font><font \r\ncolor=\\\"#3333FF\\\"> expression</font><font \r\ncolor=\\\"#3333FF\\\"></font>\r\n<p><font color=\\\"#3333FF\\\">utility </font><font \r\ncolor=\\\"#FF0000\\\">Of</font><font color=\\\"#3333FF\\\">\r\nspacing</font><font color=\\\"#3333FF\\\"></font>\r\n<p><font color=\\\"#3333FF\\\">try it for </font><font \r\ncolor=\\\"#FF0000\\\">Yourself</font></center>\r\n\r\n</body>\r\n</html>',0,0,0,0,'172.169.100.55','en'),(7004,1582,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>essemar: you might be right, i\'ll have to admit, we did have a good weekend together, though. all this was probably\r\nthe empathy and chemicals talking, ha.  speaking of which- when you\r\ngonna join us?</tt>',3,0,0,0,'63.210.217.168','en'),(7005,1579,'2001-08-13 20:19:07',0,'dude','where\\\'s my car?',0,0,0,0,'64.168.21.85','en'),(7006,1580,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','Sometimes I lie awake at night, staring at the ceiling, and \r\nI imagine an etheral figure drift down through the plaster, \r\ncoming closer and closer until I can feel her light.  Then, \r\nher lips gently touch mine, and she bursts into dark.',3,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(7007,1582,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','Hey, that was essemar the Cynic talking.  You shouldn\\\'t \r\nlisten to him.  He\\\'s pretty harsh.  Of course, essemar the \r\nRomantic tends to be pretty doey eyed and stupid.  The \r\ntruth is there somewhere in between.<br><br>I\\\'ll give you a \r\ncall about this weekend.  I think egg will be joining us, \r\nunless she has decided that I\\\'m a lecherous ax murderer.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(7008,1582,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>...she\'d be right, then!</tt>',3,0,0,0,'63.210.217.168','en'),(7009,1579,'2001-08-13 20:49:37',0,'kdog','*whining* Ohhhhhhh nooooo.  sorry aus.  ',1,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(7010,1583,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','see?\r\n<pre>\r\n[14:07] &lt;le&gt; i guess you\'re male so you want to somehow involve science and\r\n[14:07] &lt;le&gt; mathematics, but if you just eat what is right for your\r\n[14:07] &lt;le&gt; nutrition and subsistence you\'d be fine. it\'s a more organic\r\n[14:07] &lt;le&gt; process that counting calories\r\n</pre>\r\n<p>\r\nthe gender card is played. and then:\r\n</p>\r\n<pre>\r\n[14:10] &lt;wb&gt; obviously there is some grey zone in the dealings with the\r\n[14:10] &lt;wb&gt; body but it is true that it operates in a machine like way in\r\n[14:10] &lt;wb&gt; the area of calories, fat storage and all of that\r\n</pre>\r\n<p>\r\ni\'m a white yuppie west coast american machinist without a soul.\r\n</p>',0,0,0,0,'209.228.10.196','en'),(7011,1583,'2001-08-13 21:15:01',0,'wb','oh good christ. i played the MACHINA card.',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(7012,1583,'2001-08-13 21:16:12',0,'wb','btw ix, i feel violated that you pasted things i said in \r\nprivate chat on livejournal.com',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(7013,1580,'2001-08-13 21:17:14',0,'ghost','that was me ess...next time i\\\'ll bite you so you know for \r\nsure.',1,0,0,0,'32.102.110.18','en'),(7014,1583,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','don\\\'t ask me to compromise my art.',0,0,0,0,'209.228.10.196','en'),(7015,1583,'2001-08-13 21:18:02',0,'wb','<bcm> too much carbs => long digestion cycles',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(7016,1583,'2001-08-13 21:18:49',0,'wb','(bcm) <BR>too much carbs 8==============D long digestion \r\ncycles',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(7017,1585,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i envy you that you can put these feelings into\r\nwords, so crisply. nice.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'64.152.169.13','en'),(7018,1581,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>lugubrious, rainy day, gray, long nap, reading\r\nswinney, bleak, finally finding color in green</tt>',3,0,0,0,'64.152.169.13','en'),(7019,1583,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>What\\\'s a soul <i>anyway</i>?  And regarding\r\ndigestion.. a friend of mine just paid 185$ for a colonic in\r\nChelsea. Hm.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'64.152.169.13','en'),(7020,1580,'2001-08-13 21:42:16',0,'Doktor to Geist','do you do sexual favors, also?',3,0,0,0,'64.152.169.13','en'),(7021,1584,'2001-08-13 21:44:20',0,'lou','but one will turn into two, and so on, and then eventually \r\nyou\\\'ll grow apart because you will be an adult and your \r\nlover will still be a child, and you will both be \r\nstagnating. (oh, wait, sorry, that\\\'s <I>my</i> life!) \r\nwaiting isn\\\'t the ultimate redemption unless you know \r\nbeforehand that the tree you are watching as you wait will \r\nbe bearing fruit.  unfortunately.',1,0,0,0,'207.237.128.1','en'),(7022,1579,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>DUDE. some guy, right NOW, right HERE, just picked\r\nup my laptop and closed it, and started to pick it up while\r\nI was two feet away getting a drink. Shit. Now he has the\r\nnerve to tell me he was just trying to get a closer look at\r\nit... indeed!</tt>',1,0,0,0,'64.152.169.13','en'),(7023,1584,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>what if the fruit, unripe as it were, has been so\r\ngood in the past that it\\\'s worth the risk waiting?</tt>',3,0,0,0,'64.152.169.13','en'),(7024,1584,'2001-08-13 22:04:10',0,'lou','i think maybe then you might just have to use your good \r\njudgement.  it\\\'s a risk--but what isn\\\'t?  some risks are \r\nworth taking, and others are chalked up as a learning \r\nexperience...even if you don\\\'t learn from them.  good luck.',1,0,0,0,'207.237.128.1','en'),(7025,1583,'2001-08-13 22:26:59',0,'jo','i don\\\'t feel that i need to explain my art to you, warren.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(7026,1585,'2001-08-13 22:34:21',0,'jo','yes.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(7027,1585,'2001-08-13 22:39:54',0,'lunchbox','you are NOT jealous of people who feel nothing for other \r\npeople.  you wouldn\\\'t have it any other way.  you are just \r\nenvious of the way they can cut ties so smoothly.',0,0,0,0,'206.40.244.66','en'),(7028,1585,'2001-08-13 22:41:58',0,'maria','i can sympathize.\r\n\r\n(hi lou!)\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'172.141.218.40','en'),(7029,855,'2001-08-13 23:18:44',0,'bmg','this came up in chaos today... and i re-read it cause i \r\ndidn\\\'t remember writing it... but the second i read it i \r\nhad this eerie feeling that at the time I was writing this \r\nwas this at about the same time that my <a \r\nhref=\\\'http://swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=879.txt\r\n\\\'>friend passed away</a>. Coincidense, probably - but \r\nit was an eerie feeling nonetheless...',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(7030,1585,'2001-08-13 23:20:35',0,'lou to lunchbox','fly, fatass, fly.<br><br>and yes. i think that\\\'s more to \r\nthe point. i am always tied; but people who feel nothing \r\nannoy me with their blase attitudes and irreverence for \r\nrelationships.  six of one, half-dozen of the other, and i \r\nthink i misused the semi-colon. ach.',6,0,0,0,'165.247.54.157','en'),(7031,855,'2001-08-13 23:21:10',0,'bmg','oops, wait a sec - it was the day before... trash day is on \r\nfriday not saturday... this is not an X-file afterall...',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(7032,1585,'2001-08-13 23:22:52',0,'lou to maria','HI! but also, i\\\'m sorry. for you and for anyone else who \r\ncan.',1,0,0,0,'165.247.54.157','en'),(7033,1584,'2001-08-13 23:54:17',0,'kat re Peter\\\'s comment','oh damn...this is so where i am right now.\r\n',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.215','en'),(7034,1584,'2001-08-14 00:13:48',0,'treetop','\\\"Don\\\'t shake the tree when the fruit ain\\\'t ripe.\\\"      \r\n~Loose Lucy',0,0,0,0,'172.159.34.57','en'),(7035,1583,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','<p>this is so typical ix</p>\r\n<p>le, i tried to convince him to stop calorie counting \r\ntoo.  there is such a thing as common sense.  use it.</p>',4,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(7036,1581,'2001-08-14 00:43:04',0,'nobody_on_swinney.org','thanx pedro',1,0,0,0,'198.81.16.31','en'),(7037,1581,'2001-08-14 00:43:04',0,'nobody_on_swinney.org','thanx pedro',1,0,0,0,'198.81.16.31','en'),(7038,1584,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>and to push the metaphor- too much unripe fruit\r\ngives a bad stomach ache!</tt>',3,0,0,0,'64.152.163.236','en'),(7039,1585,'2001-08-14 01:01:49',0,'fatass','also, i\\\'m not sure that continuing to care is really the \r\nbest thing.  for ANYONE involved.  including \r\nyou.<Br><br><br>you hate people until they prove you wrong \r\nand then they\\\'re in for life?  no.  that\\\'s not how it works. \r\n and being decent to assholes doesn\\\'t mean compassion, or \r\ncaring, or anything like that, and you\\\'re right, being \r\ndecent is just that: being decent.<br><Br><Br>and i don\\\'t \r\nknow where i\\\'m going with this, but i think that there comes \r\na point where you have to let go or you hold yourself back, \r\nand it\\\'s not about hating or not caring or being blase -- \r\nand it\\\'s not even about protecting yourself.  it\\\'s about \r\nassimilating what you\\\'ve learned and DOING SOMETHING WITH IT \r\ninstead of doing the same goddamned thing over and over.',0,0,0,0,'206.40.244.66','en'),(7040,1577,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>all this paranoia is starting to get to me. right now im \r\nnestled into the murderous wooded western countryside of \r\nmassachusetts and i cant sleep in general beause im \r\nterrified for my life. because you can see the stars, and \r\nyou know that means SOMOENE IS COMING FOR YOU.</p>\r\n<p>ps: i put lobster in the summer pasta dish. its a MIND \r\nSCRAMBLER. made it for ralph and dotty.</p>',0,0,0,0,'205.188.195.202','en'),(7041,1585,'2001-08-14 03:07:26',0,'lou to lunchbox','BUT. if i continue to do the same thing over and over \r\nagain, at least i will get good at it.<br><br>also, by the \r\nway, i didn\\\'t say it made sense! who makes sense? not me. \r\never. anyway. so the point...is gone because i lost my \r\ntrain of thought. so.<br><br>it\\\'s just all frustrating.',5,0,0,0,'165.247.54.157','en'),(7042,1583,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','the spacing makes you slow your digestion down, and taste \r\nevery word.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.28','en'),(7043,1583,'2001-08-14 04:15:04',0,'ix to pseudo-hippy girls','<p>\r\nwhy do you persist in claiming that nutrition is not a\r\nscience? if it wasn\'t, why would there be a nutritional\r\nsciences department at my university? why would\r\nnutritionists be fully qualified medical doctors?\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\ngod, if you please just send me a nice math-oriented girl, i promise i\'ll go to church every sunday.\r\n</p>',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(7044,1583,'2001-08-14 04:22:51',0,'tyler, not taking a side','Look at it this way. So many variables affect nutrition, \r\nand your body\\\'s response to it, such as physical activity, \r\nseason, shit probably even mood, that science may not be \r\nable to function as efficiently -on a personal level- as \r\nour own intuition. For example, the brain is a computer; we \r\nstudy computers, it\\\'s a legitimate science, yet we can\\\'t \r\nget one to park a car or write a symphony, now can we?',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.28','en'),(7045,1579,'2001-08-14 04:33:58',0,'Robert Siegel','stay tuned, as we repeat the same 4 news stories you just \r\nheard on another show, almost verbatim, because we take \r\nthem right off the wire without doing any real reporting. \r\nAlso, I edit the onion at www.theonion.com. did you know \r\nthat?',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.28','en'),(7046,1583,'2001-08-14 04:36:13',0,'sawks','<hr>\r\n<a href=\\\"http://www.calculusgirls.com/\\\"><img \r\nsrc=\\\"http://www1.calculusgirls.com/images/tn_newbumper1.jpg\\\"\r\n></a>',1,0,0,0,'210.8.201.242','en'),(7047,1584,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','when life gives you lemons, lobby your government for lime\r\nhandouts instead.  or something.  typing in the 120 seconds\r\nleft of today doesn\\\'t leave much room for a point. :-)',1,0,0,0,'209.163.146.106','en'),(7048,1585,'2001-08-14 04:49:29',0,'danielle','hi lou!\r\n\r\ni\\\'m the same way you are, definitly. i\\\'m a cancer as well \r\nand i\\\'m not the second coming of christ so maybe it is the \r\ncancer thing.\r\n\r\nand peter: lou is very good at putting things into words, \r\neven if she doesn\\\'t think so ;)\r\n',1,0,0,0,'24.68.193.134','en'),(7049,1589,'2001-08-14 07:09:45',0,'kat','Marie Bais Des Anges',4,0,0,0,'32.102.91.153','en'),(7050,1589,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','<a href=\\\"http://us.imdb.com/Title?0168629\\\" \r\ntarget=\\\"new\\\">Dancer In The Dark</a>',3,0,0,0,'64.229.65.19','en'),(7051,1590,'2001-08-14 07:40:42',0,'kat','there is something here that i really connect with. maybe a \r\nperspective from the other side of the coin. i\\\'m \r\nexperiencing an intensely unfamiliar and frustrating \r\ntransition of being the aggressor. i never use to be that \r\nway...but i ended up in a relationship that demanded it. \r\neither i grasped for what i wanted, or got nothing. it \r\nsuffocated me. why should i be with someone who hasn\\\'t the \r\nenergy or courage or inclination to declare his desires? i \r\nfound it boring, and depressing, and emotionally draining. \r\ni am NOT a leader....i am not your leader. i am certainly \r\nnot a follower either, but i definitely aint here to be \r\nyour momma. the weirdness is that since i\\\'ve been on my own \r\ni see that i am stuck in this sort of dominating position. \r\nwhat i find bizarre is that the men im attracted too are \r\nvery outspoken and yet it seems they turn completely \r\npassive once i have spent a certain amount of time with \r\nthem. it makes me worry that i am a soul sucker...a \r\nvampire. leaching them of life. what a horrible thing to \r\nbe! friends have said that i\\\'m emotionally overwhelming at \r\ntimes. too intelligent. too questioning. im not sure what \r\nthis means. i feel cursed. the person that i see as me is \r\njust a happy go lucky little kid with lots of passion and a \r\nbig heart for sharing and inquisitiveness/hunger for \r\neverything else. maybe i just like people too much. i think \r\nof so many people i know as friends, it\\\'s hard to remember \r\nthat maybe they don\\\'t see it the same way. they already \r\nhave friends to fill their time. i don\\\'t worry so much \r\nabout the possible horrible things that might happen if i \r\nget involved with someone that i\\\'m attracted too...i only \r\nworry that if i don\\\'t i could lose the chance at something \r\nthat might turn out to be amazing. enjoy it for what it is? \r\nwith no expectations? i dont know...this is pointless 1am \r\nlate night rambling. i know nothing.',4,0,0,0,'32.102.91.153','en'),(7052,1590,'2001-08-14 07:48:53',0,'bmg','3am rambling... i know nothing either... i think we are \r\ncoming from the same side of the coing, actualy... ',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(7053,1589,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','there is this one movie i saw involving prisons in asia \r\nthat i don\\\'t recommend on mushrooms.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(7054,1583,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','you cock.  stop putting words into my mouth.  some things\r\nare so obvious that you don\\\'t have to do the math to work it\r\nout.  hamburgers every lunchtime == bad for you.\r\n\r\nlike, duh.  just fucking use your brain.  it\\\'s how we\r\nfigured out maths, doofus.',5,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(7055,1588,'2001-08-14 12:16:43',0,'Herr Doktor','stop smoking krak before bed, perhaps?',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7056,1589,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i guess it\'s a little more mainstream, but <a \r\nhref=\"http://us.imdb.com/Title?0180093\">Requiem for a \r\nDream</a> <i>really</i> got to me. some of it close to \r\nhome, some of it unbelievably surreal, all downright sad.  \r\ni was depressed for a week afterwards, yet somehow can\'t \r\nforget this film.  i recall leaving the theater in an \r\nintrospective downer haze and almost getting plowed over by \r\na cab; i took my boot and kicked the cab\'s rear fender as \r\nhard as I could- the driver slammed on his breaks and \r\njumped out to accosts me, but upon seeing the delerious \r\nlook that must have been on my face, he just turned right \r\naround and drove off. i\'d have never done that on any other \r\nday. somehow, i can\'t forget this film.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7057,1589,'2001-08-14 13:28:33',0,'zooberries','E.T.',1,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(7058,1589,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<p><u>Boys Don\\\'t Cry</u> really kicked the shit out of me.  \r\nMovies people may not have heard of:<br><u>Ju Dou</u> <i>\r\n(chinese)</I><br><u>The Hairdresser\\\'s Husband</u><i>(Le \r\nMarie de la Coifeusse)</i></p>',3,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(7059,1592,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>as a new yorker, i\'ve often wished that there was some way that you could share empathy, to give someone that \"i know what you\'re going through, and it\'s going to be ok, somehow\" nod, or the hug that they probably need desparately.  sadly, i don\'t think its possible.  to escape \r\nthis harsh reality, i tend to spend weekends regressing deeper into closely knit groups of friends, parties or clubs where, at worst, theres a false/superficial shared sense of empathy and caring, emotion and affection.  the harshest reality i\'ve ever had is to step out of such an \r\nenvironment and have a cabbie gyp me or a commuter or pedestrian give me that \"fuck you- you don\'t exist in my world\" look, or to smile at someone and have them give you the finger.  it really sours me.  if only there were some way to bridge this gap, some sign or symbol you could \r\npassively display to someone to let them know, without patting them on the back and risk getting stabbed, cursed or worse.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nyes, freaky shit definitely happens on the 1/9 train.  in my 6 years of commuting on it, i\'ve seen a shooting, watched pre-giuliani-esque hookers getting busted, watched the homeless spew crack-riddled vomit on passengers, and most recently observed a fat college student doing PCP and performing feats of superhuman strength, lifting his body, horizontally, from the railings and doing other one-armed gymnastics that he probably couldn\'t have undertaken othewise, all to the astonishment of his \'sitter\' and the rest of us.  ahh, NY, anything goes here.  it might be a lonely hell of a city, but its shiny and dirty and beautiful and i love it.</tt>\r\n',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7060,1588,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>Lately, I\\\'ve been having a very odd recurring \r\ndream; the same every time.  It places me in a depression-\r\nera dust-bowl town somewhere in the plains-states.  the \r\ntopsoil has eroded away, leaving barren fields and brown \r\ndirt blowing everywhere.  I ride an old rusty bicycle to \r\nthe main town square where I pass a giant rusty water-\r\ntower.  I go into a dilapidated old general store and buy \r\ntheir single remaining plant- a cactus, and grinning, I \r\nknow at least <i>it</i> will grow.  A friend tells me this \r\ndream is probably an artifact from a previous life.  Odd.  \r\nmaybe i\\\'ll write an entry about it.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7061,1589,'2001-08-14 14:16:59',0,'Herr Doktor','All this mish mash mumbo jumbo of foreign films and obscure \r\nartsy movies.  Show me <A HREF=\\\"http://us.imdb.com/Title?\r\n0097438\\\">Gleaming the Kube</A> anyday, and I\\\'ll shed a tear \r\nfor you.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7062,1589,'2001-08-14 14:25:02',0,'Animal Chin','I quite prefer <A \r\nHREF=\\\"http://www.justpushplay.com/searforanchi.html\\\">The \r\nSearch for Animal Chin</A> as far as skate-rat films go.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7063,1583,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','<p>\r\nand veggie burritos for lunch every day is no better. which\r\nwas my original point to elly. just cos you\'re vegan doesn\'t\r\nmean you can\'t overeat.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nwhat exactly is so upsetting about my reasoning? \"hm i eat a\r\nburrito every day, which is a big pile of starch, which\r\ntakes a really long time to digest and makes me totally\r\nincapable of activity during the early afternoon, and which\r\nis higher in calories (5/gram) than a grilled chicken breast\r\n(protein, 2-3/gram).\" is that threatening somehow? in what way\r\nis that not \"working it out\", \"using my brain\", \"common\r\nsense\", \"duh\"? how else am i supposed to know \"what is right\r\nfor my nutrition and subsistence\"?\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nwhat i learned from trying a vegan diet:\r\n</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>\r\nmy body feels more energetic when a higher proportion of my\r\ndiet comes from fruits and vegetables\r\n</p>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>\r\ni actually enjoy eating many vegetables\r\n</p>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>\r\nthere are nice healthy tasty substitutes for many of the\r\ngross things i used to eat. case in point: boca burgers\r\n</p>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>\r\neating five rolls of veggie sushi fills your belly just as\r\nmuch and generates just as much waste as eating five rolls\r\nwith fish. way, way too much.\r\n</p>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>\r\nsometimes i want some meat and/or cheese, and i\'m\r\nok with that, and fuck off if you don\'t like it.\r\n</p>\r\n</ol>',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(7064,1591,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<p>last saturday someone i barely know called to invite me \r\nout just to hang out he showed me the office where he works \r\nthe arcade games the climbing wall the gym the basketball \r\ncourt then we had some marvelous tibeten food comfort food \r\nthen we watched a play a good friend of his had written and \r\ndirected and all this time we talked and laughed and \r\nbitched and made plans and built fantasies and destoyed \r\nrealities i live my life for the moments not the tedium</p>',6,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(7065,1583,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<p>I went to Marlboro College, and a friend of mine there \r\nwanted to go all protein in his diet.  The problem?  They \r\ndidn\\\'t always serve some kind of meaty dish at every meal.  \r\nThere was <i>always</I> a vegetarian <i>and</I> a vegan \r\ndish for those pursuing that life-style, but it was not \r\nuncommon for there to be <i>nothing</I> for the \r\ncarnivores.  After talking to some people about it, I found \r\nmany people who want to eat meat for every meal.  Didn\\\'t \r\nthe Eskimos subsist purely on animal products?  Whatever, I \r\nthought I had a point make, but I seem to have broken the \r\ntip.</P>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(7066,1579,'2001-08-14 16:20:14',0,'Christina Aguillara','i was lost, but now i am found.',2,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(7067,1583,'2001-08-14 16:32:56',0,'kat','<p>was just reading <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.metroactive.com/metro/eating1-0131.html\\\" \r\ntarget=\\\"_blank\\\">this</a>...</p>\r\n<p>balance. i think that\\\'s the key to everything in life. \r\nwell, that and knowing yourself. what\\\'s good for one person \r\nmay not be so wonderful for another.</p>',2,0,0,0,'32.102.109.76','en'),(7068,1577,'2001-08-14 17:31:07',0,'chi chi to egg','mmm lobster. just this saturday i was sitting at your \r\ntable, flipping through martha living, and they had this \r\ngreat looking dish with LOBSTER in it. i told \r\njayperOhOh to make it for me. also a berry tart. mmm \r\nmm.<br>\r\nwhen are you coming home egg? i miss you.',0,0,0,0,'64.172.44.13','en'),(7069,1589,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','Stroczek.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.5.203','en'),(7070,1585,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>hooray; i\\\'m a cancer too.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7071,1592,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','I realized I couldn\\\'t live in New York when I was 18 \r\nbecause I am too absorptive. I really do go and talk to \r\npeople who are crying, partially out of curiousity. Oout \r\nthere in California, we just sit in our cars and look \r\nstraight ahead, even when someone is trying to flag you \r\ndown to get into the lane.',0,0,0,0,'216.243.8.131','en'),(7072,1592,'2001-08-14 17:49:49',0,'also','Im hoping that we can take drugs and avoid others together \r\nsometime this week. SWINNEY.ORG EAST COAST',0,0,0,0,'216.243.8.131','en'),(7073,1590,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','i would say to give her another chance. sometimes people \r\nact like assholes when theyre nervous. everyone gets all \r\nfreaky when theyre trying to hook up a lil luv. especially \r\nif shes hot, you could get some ass out of it and then be \r\nfree of responsibility if she turns out to be a jerk. ',0,0,0,0,'216.243.8.131','en'),(7074,1591,'2001-08-14 18:00:48',0,'SUCK IT','hi lulu!\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(7075,1592,'2001-08-14 18:09:32',0,'maria','SWINNEY.ORG EAST COAST : REPRESENT!!\r\n',6,0,0,0,'172.186.101.115','en'),(7076,1588,'2001-08-14 18:41:47',0,'treetop to peter','I like it, you should write it...',0,0,0,0,'205.188.209.166','en'),(7077,1592,'2001-08-14 19:09:03',0,'lou','last night as i was waiting for the L train, instead of the \r\nobnoxious headache-inducing drums that are usually played \r\non the platform, there was an opera singer.  she was \r\nblack/hatian/whathaveyou, and her voice was so gorgeous, \r\nand she was accompanying herself on one of those mini casio \r\nkeyboards.<br><br>and everyone was laughing at \r\nher.<br><br>so i gave her all of the money i had in my \r\npockets (which was about $6, but still), and smiled at her \r\nuntil the train came.<br><br>maybe it doesn\\\'t make a \r\ndifference to do stuff like that, and maybe she didn\\\'t \r\ncare, but it made <b>me</b> feel better.<br><br>(yeah, i \r\ncould never leave nyc for a long time, i don\\\'t think. \r\nthere\\\'s just something about this place. the pollution is \r\nin my blood.)',1,0,0,0,'207.237.128.1','en'),(7078,1585,'2001-08-14 19:11:10',0,'lou','to danielle & peter: thank you and happiest birthdays!',1,0,0,0,'207.237.128.1','en'),(7079,1583,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<p>Yo, that\\\'s right, Bitch.  Buddha fucking kicked ass; he \r\nwas all about that moderation shit.  I got that crap \r\ngrilled into my head by my father for, like, twenty year, \r\nDude..... Yeah Man, that\\\'s the bomb.</P>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(7080,1588,'2001-08-14 19:56:37',0,'Treetop to Herr Doktor','</head>\r\n<body>\r\nPlease stay off <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://buttsacrossamerica.com/buttshot_pages/golden_ga\r\nte_bridge.html\\\">crack</a>\r\n</body>\r\n</html>',0,0,0,0,'205.188.209.166','en'),(7081,1594,'2001-08-14 20:45:52',0,'maria','i like this. ',2,0,0,0,'172.163.109.32','en'),(7082,1594,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','i was just in nyc for a week and stayed at one of my old \r\napartments and armed myself with takeout margaritas and packs \r\nof old gold cigarettes and went out on the town. i thought \r\nabout writing a \\\"swinney\\\" about it, but it seemed too dirty \r\nto discuss. now, all of a sudden, i\\\'m driving to tex-ass on \r\nsaturday. now there\\\'s an adventure story.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(7083,1594,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i\\\'m optimistic too. it\\\'s hard to be an optimist. no one \r\nwants to hear it.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(7084,1591,'2001-08-14 21:48:29',0,'lulu','give it time essemar, this guy\\\'ll screw you over, take my \r\nword.  if you live for the present, then more power to \r\nyou...don\\\'t think about what\\\'s gonna happen in the future, \r\ncause shit, that\\\'s far away.  i assure you tho, there is no \r\nsuch thing as altruism.',0,0,0,0,'209.179.224.9','en'),(7085,1594,'2001-08-14 21:56:09',0,'lulu','optimism shmoptimism.  who said being optimistic is a \r\nmust.  there\\\'s hope in pessemism, too, buddy...it brings a \r\nwhole new light to reality that optimism filters out.  suck \r\nit, jay!',0,0,0,0,'209.179.224.9','en'),(7086,1593,'2001-08-14 22:26:28',0,'jo','wait. so. you\\\'re saying they <b>are</b> making that movie \r\nor you wish that they were with those actors?<BR>\r\nthat\\\'s one of my favorite books and i can\\\'t see anyone as \r\nattractive as johnny depp being the narrator. that\\\'s just \r\nthe thing; the narrator would need to be homely or you \r\ndon\\\'t sympathize with his jealous hatredlove of his best \r\nfriend\\\'s beauty.<BR>\r\nalso who to play his suicidal wife?',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(7087,1592,'2001-08-14 22:33:27',0,'green to esse:','call me yo. i have unemployment woes. she would ve thought \r\nyu were a perve. just kidding',1,0,0,0,'198.81.17.59','en'),(7088,570,'2001-08-14 22:41:13',0,'green','is this menstrual?',1,0,0,0,'198.81.17.59','en'),(7089,1583,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','i don\\\'t give a shit what you eat.  i just don\\\'t like your \r\nattitude',6,0,0,0,'203.45.52.132','en'),(7090,1594,'2001-08-14 23:15:25',0,'fernando','no, misery just loves company.\r\n',3,0,0,0,'63.203.225.62','en'),(7091,1590,'2001-08-14 23:15:31',0,'bmg','i was a lil harsh, i don\\\'t think i really meant all that... i \r\nthink i will see her again.',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(7092,1590,'2001-08-14 23:35:57',0,'chi chi to egg','what kind of mills alum are you? get some free ass! \r\n\r\n<br>\r\nto bmg: it\\\'s all about first impressions. don\\\'t waste your \r\ntime.',0,0,0,0,'64.172.44.13','en'),(7093,1590,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','i agree with egg on this one.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(7094,1592,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to egg:','<br><tt>swinney east coast fellas got good drugs to \r\nboot</tt>',3,0,0,0,'209.246.84.152','en'),(7095,1594,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','\\\"oh jay,...\\\"',2,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(7096,1588,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i think doktor is my dealer...uh oh</tt>',3,0,0,0,'209.246.84.152','en'),(7097,1588,'2001-08-15 01:34:17',0,'treetop','</head>\r\n<body>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<br>Things could be <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.cutoffmyfeet.com\\\">worse</a>\r\n</body>\r\n</html>',0,0,0,0,'205.188.209.166','en'),(7098,1583,'2001-08-15 02:32:19',0,'moebius, back on track, here','<p>ix, you might also ask: why bother with any sort of \r\ngraphic textual design in books, magazines, etc. why not \r\njust always present everything in plain ol\\\' Courier or \r\nArial font? (then again, if you\\\'re wondering about this \r\npoetry spacing issue, you\\\'re probably wondering about that, \r\ntoo...)</p>\r\n<br>\r\nanyway, i figure <br><br>\r\nfolks<br><br>\r\ngenerally<br><br>\r\n<blockquote>go   for<br><br>\r\n<blockquote>the<br>\r\n<blockquote>wacky<br></blockquote></blockquote>   \r\nspacing<br><br>\r\n simply because<br><br>\r\n<center>they can.<br></center>\r\n<p>(but man, I think poets would give all that up if they \r\nhad to code their wacky poetry breaks and spacing in HTML \r\nalla the time...)</p>\r\n<p>anyway, \\\'nuff said there...go on back to the anti-\r\nvegitarian or whatever it is conversation that I\\\'ve not \r\nread yet...</p>',1,0,0,0,'205.184.158.55','en'),(7099,1581,'2001-08-15 02:37:13',0,'BrewGuru99','<FONT Color=008800 Size=-2>Beautiful.</FONT>',0,0,0,0,'66.12.171.62','en'),(7100,1596,'2001-08-15 02:50:21',0,'x','What was wrong with this one?',0,0,0,0,'66.12.171.62','en'),(7101,1595,'2001-08-15 03:36:29',0,'bmg','I like this... and i liked your pictures on your site too.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(7102,1597,'2001-08-15 03:57:11',0,'Treetop','</head>\r\n<body>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<br>Identifying the basic theme sets the tone for the \r\ninterpretation:&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\nYou are riding a bicycle into the town square and stop at a \r\nstore.&nbsp;\r\nYou pass an empty water tower.&nbsp; You buy a plant during \r\na drought.&nbsp;\r\nThe plant will live because it requires little water...\r\n<p>Riding a bicycle could symbolize traveling through \r\nlife.&nbsp; The drought\r\ncould represent a period of little growth.&nbsp; Buying a \r\ncactus shows\r\nthat you are investing or in something that will survive \r\nduring this period\r\nof little growth...\r\n<p>These are my thoughts, but I am no expert.&nbsp; You are \r\nthe best interpreter\r\nof your dreams.\r\n<br><a href=\\\"http://www.dreamloverinc.com/dream.htm\\\">Dream \r\ndictionary</a>\r\n</body>\r\n</html>',0,0,0,0,'205.188.209.166','en'),(7103,1594,'2001-08-15 03:57:41',0,'Amy','i didnt say the web is dead.',0,0,0,0,'216.243.8.142','en'),(7104,1591,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<blockquote>no such thing as altruism</blockquote>\r\n<p>\r\nbullshit\r\n</p>\r\n<p>if there were no such thing as altruism, this site would\r\nnot exist.  counterproof by instance of item subject to\r\nblanket negation, QED</p>',6,0,0,0,'209.163.146.106','en'),(7105,1595,'2001-08-15 04:04:39',0,'Treetop','</head>\r\n<body>\r\nI really like your <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.netcowboy.com/gallery2.html\\\">sketch</a>...\r\n</body>\r\n</html>',0,0,0,0,'205.188.209.166','en'),(7106,1590,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to chi chi','i am a Feminist with a capital eFF. I dont see any reason \r\nwhy a woman who obviously is asking for free ass wouldnt \r\nhave any trouble giving it up. In fact, I bet she would \r\nlike it, from the sounds of her! In fact, I bet if bmg bent \r\nher over his kitchen table and then asked her to cook \r\nbreakfast wearing nothing but a thong painted with duckies, \r\nshe\\\'d like that too! its a free sex market, get with it \r\npeople!!',0,0,0,0,'216.243.8.142','en'),(7107,1595,'2001-08-15 05:51:56',0,'netcowboy','Ah, ain\\\'t you guys the nicest?! I got home from the book \r\ndiscussion and our home alarm won\\\'t stop going off. It \r\nbeeps every two minutes. Suburban Troubletime. \r\nFinally, a technician is coming out to fix it. Maybe he\\\'ll fix \r\neverything else too.',1,0,0,0,'24.161.203.57','en'),(7108,1594,'2001-08-15 06:22:11',0,'wb','AMY YOU SAID IT',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(7109,1597,'2002-03-15 00:17:55',129,'moebius','<p>hey, I have nothing to say about yr dreams actually \r\nother than I basically agree with Treetop there. I \r\npersonally never try hard to figure out my dreams--they\\\'re \r\nso strange and offbeat sometimes I just like to marvel at \r\ntheir weirdness. I also see in them a deep well of \r\ncreativity that I\\\'d like to do a better job of \r\ntapping.</p><p>\r\nno, I just wanted to say that I continue to be inspired by \r\nyour slice-o-life storybits. thanks.</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'205.184.146.239','en'),(7110,1592,'2001-08-15 06:56:47',0,'green to egg','meaning that they wish to snort these good east coast drugs \r\noff of your  tee-tahs',1,0,0,0,'198.81.16.151','en'),(7111,1598,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','hm?',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(7112,1590,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','my opinion is that you should just fuck.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(7113,1591,'2001-08-15 07:59:47',0,'lulu','this site is a self indulgent hootenanny for ninny\\\'s like \r\nyourself.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(7114,1594,'2001-08-15 09:38:43',0,'lulu to fernando','company is misery\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(7115,1597,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>treetop: your interpretation actually smacks of my \r\nreality right now.  i don\\\'t know why i didn\\\'t notice the \r\nobvious connections before- thanks.<br><br>moebius: thanks \r\nfor the encouragement. it\\\'s good knowing someone reads \r\nthem.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7116,1595,'2001-08-15 11:18:01',0,'Herr Doktor','your sketch looks like things i\\\'ve seen while tripping',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7117,1588,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>that\\\'s downright <b>CREEPY</b>.</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7118,1593,'2001-08-15 12:04:24',0,'dj1_luna','<p>this is my casting. no such movie is in the works. I \r\nwould either have Gabrille \r\n  be both catherine and the wife or have <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://us.imdb.com/Name?B%E9art,%\r\n2BEmmanuelle\\\">Emmanuelle \r\n  B&eacute;art </a>play the wife</p>',1,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(7119,1593,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','if that\\\'s a messy office, you are a seriously neat person.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.89','en'),(7120,1599,'2001-08-15 13:02:02',0,'Doktor','this is an honest question: what\\\'s the draw of anime?',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7121,1591,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<p>No such thing as altruism...... this is true.  I was \r\njust talking about an evening that I was planning on \r\nspending at home turned into a nice evening out.  Day to \r\nday tedium is shitty.  99% of life is pretty boring and \r\nlame.  It\\\'s that 1%, the moments, that make life worth \r\nliving.  If you haven\\\'t had a really good moment in a \r\nwhile, 100% of life can seem shitty.</P>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(7122,1598,'2001-08-15 13:02:36',0,'Doktor','there\\\'s more to life than getting laid. i get laid all i \r\nwant and am still depressed.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7123,1596,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>forgot to put a title and cancelled submision, but \r\na half-second too late. someone in the know, kill this one \r\nplease, but leave the version titled \\\"dream a little \r\ndream\\\"... thanks</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7124,1591,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>thats why i live for the weekend. if you play your \r\ncards right, out of the possible 168 hours in a week, you \r\ncan make at least 55 of them worth living.  Thats almost a \r\n33% return, thus making 1/3 of your life worthwhile. \r\nHm.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7125,1591,'2001-08-15 13:10:11',0,'Herr Doktor','i\\\'m too selfish to know the meaning of altruism',6,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7126,1598,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<p>Yeah, there was a time in my life when I had a \r\ngirlfriend who would have sex whenever I wanted, and I \r\nstill got depressed.  Getting laid isn\\\'t everything, but it \r\nis still a very nice thing, a very pleasant, nice feeling \r\nthing.</p><p>btw, I am one of the YOU who will <i>never</i> \r\nget laid.  Thanks Green for listening to me bitch and \r\nsaying nice things to me.</p>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(7127,1598,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>after finally experiencing the emotive conglomerate \r\nof sex/love/spiritual-connection, all in the same moment, \r\nthe idea simply \\\"getting laid\\\" wanes a little more than it \r\nused to. its like smack; once you get the good stuff, \r\nthere\\\'s no going back. thats why i, like a junkie waiting \r\nin line, endure all my ongoing relationship melodramas- the \r\nfix is <i>so</i> worth it</tt>',3,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7128,1594,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>Manhattan: the only place where you can see a \r\nhomeless guy d/l his email on a palm VII</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7129,1599,'2001-08-15 13:52:47',0,'woolfwood','I think its one of those things were u either like it or \r\nnot. a matter of taste. mainly a love of animation and art \r\nand fiction.',1,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(7130,1599,'2001-08-15 14:05:15',0,'Doktor','again, a legit question not meant to incite- i\\\'m just \r\ncurious, and you seem cool: anime fans that i know seem \r\nrather obsessive and weird about it, as if theyre part of \r\nsome obscure coolness, as if its chic.  last i heard, i \r\nhadn\\\'t seen alot of rabid spiderman fans, even though thats \r\nart and fiction.  is it just that anime is more \r\nintellectual? whats the deal? like, if i were to post \r\nvignettes about Danger Superman Slut, I can guarantee \r\nthey\\\'d be no wherenearly as interesting as your posts.  and \r\ni do really likeyour posts!  I just am anime-ignorant and \r\nwant to know more.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7131,1598,'2001-08-15 14:11:05',0,'green to essemar','your\\\'re welcome.\r\nI may soon be taking up that offer to sleep on your floor',1,0,0,0,'198.81.17.153','en'),(7132,1599,'2001-08-15 14:19:42',0,'woolfwood','actually there is no relation between Danger Slut and \r\n