elt even worse when I thought \r\nabout how I could\r\nhave been more of a friend to him.&nbsp; He really had no \r\nfriends.&nbsp;\r\nI was the only person he talked to in the class.&nbsp; \r\nEveryone made fun\r\nof him.&nbsp; Nobody wanted to sit next to him.&nbsp; The \r\nteacher had placed\r\nme next to him.&nbsp; I had that sick feeling at the bottom \r\nof my throat.&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; The next day I hoped to see him walk \r\nin.&nbsp; He\r\nnever did.&nbsp; I had dreams that he was still \r\nalive.&nbsp; I was nice\r\nto him in my dreams...\r\n</body>\r\n</html>',0,0,0,0,'172.151.236.189','en'),(7256,1604,'2001-08-17 05:45:54',0,'maria to jo','thanks, girl.\r\n\r\nyou da bomb. ',1,0,0,0,'172.167.9.107','en'),(7257,1601,'2001-08-17 05:49:23',0,'maria','i don\\\'t get it?',0,0,0,0,'172.167.9.107','en'),(7258,1607,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','macy\\\'s dressing room (while wearing expensive ballgown). in a \r\ndoorway in soma. out on the playa at burning man. on an airplane \r\nunder a blanket.',4,0,0,0,'63.93.104.225','en'),(7259,1607,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','i don\\\'t really see why guys are so horrified about\r\nswallowing their semen. i don\\\'t think it tastes very good,\r\nit\\\'s not something i\\\'d choose to do often, but the concept\r\nin itself is not disgusting. most guys are on top of the\r\nworld when a girl swallows. silly double standard.',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(7260,1607,'2001-08-17 11:12:58',0,'Doktor','swallowing your semen = easy cleanup!',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7261,1607,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','oh my god. i wish i hadn\\\'t even read that. that\\\'s why god \r\nGAVE us double standards! besides, i wouldn\\\'t ask a girl to \r\ndo that anyway, if she found it as even remotely disgusting \r\nan idea as me. \r\n<p>\r\nps- people in the military are fucked in the head to begin \r\nwith, oh 8 times out of 10.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.208','en'),(7262,1605,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','what the fuck are you talking about? did you ever actually \r\nreally -listen- to any of the music? or were you too busy \r\njudging other people? \\\"loaded people\\\" will like it? their \r\nmusic is extremely well-composed and arranged. people who \r\nappreciate beauty, form, craftsmanship, inspiration, \r\nspontaneous creation, and dedication like it.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.208','en'),(7263,1605,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','by the way, i reread your poem, and it doesn\\\'t mean \r\nanything. like in a grammatical sense that is. you just \r\nthrew random phrases together, and it\\\'s like \\\"poof! I\\\'m a \r\npoet!\\\" don\\\'t be that guy. class project: look \r\nup \\\"pretension\\\" in Webster\\\'s.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.208','en'),(7264,1607,'2001-08-17 14:22:21',0,'bmg to tyler','yes you are right... but i think your percentage is wrong, \r\nyou see it is the 15% of the military that makes the rest \r\nlook bad... the remaining 85% are people, people going \r\nthrough life just like you and I. There is prejudice \r\neverywhere. That 15% really made me sad, I loved the \r\n85%. ',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(7265,1614,'2001-08-17 15:26:52',0,'Pervy','You can cough on my deli shit any day, Baby.',6,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(7266,1607,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','tyler, you really need to take a trip out of the provinces.',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(7267,1611,'2001-08-17 16:25:39',0,'sims to adam','huh. that\\\'s really nice. i like when it works like that.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(7268,1612,'2001-08-17 17:26:40',0,'auntie','one thing i learned with years is that people die.  the \r\nolder you get, the more they fall out of the circle of \r\nlife, and the falling often takes people you wish you had \r\nsaid or done something to, with, or for.<br><br>\r\n\r\nthe first few times this happened to me, i was young, and i \r\ndidn\\\'t know what to do.  all those regrets eating my \r\nsoul... it was more than i could bear. <br><br>\r\n\r\nafter some time passed under my belt i realized that the \r\nprocess of living gives all of us the opportunity for vast \r\nmansions of rooms filled with regrets and sorrow.<br><br>\r\n<ul>\r\n<font face=\\\"verdana\\\" size=\\\"2\\\"><b><em>\r\ngod grant me the serenity to accept the things i cannot \r\nchange<br><br>\r\nthe courage to change the things i can<br><br>\r\nand the wisdom to know the difference<br><br>\r\n</em></b></font>\r\n</ul><br><br>\r\n\r\nyou can\\\'t change what happened yesterday, but you can learn \r\nfrom this how not to let it happen again.  you can learn \r\nhow to reach out to the unlovable and do a kind thing, you \r\ncan remind yourself with your sorrow, and someday, the \r\ncircle will be unbroken.<br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'24.162.119.106','en'),(7269,1617,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','did you get any phone numbers?',0,0,0,0,'209.246.96.195','en'),(7270,1617,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','Austin should add \\\'self-indulgent\\\' as a category in the \r\nsubmission form, and yes Egg, I did get a phone number.  \r\nI\\\'m not sure what I\\\'m going to do with it though.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(7271,1617,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','was it the sassy brunette? inquiring minds want to know. \r\nfrench her',0,0,0,0,'209.246.96.195','en'),(7272,1617,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to J2 (AKA essemar)','<p>I want to thank you for being there though, even though \r\nyou played cards with complete strangers and not us. You \r\nreally got us through. mama gonna get you thru!!!</p>\r\n<p>i got my freakin tickets, and im going to wear my booogie \r\nnights dress and sneak in the back to suck Philip Seymour \r\nHoffman\\\'s porksword, thats all that matters! god bless \r\namerica! thank you, boys of brooklyn and the upper west \r\nside! thank you, peter and essemar! thank you austin \r\nswinney, for coding this fabulous site! thank you, all the \r\nboys on SWINNEY.O',0,0,0,0,'209.246.96.195','en'),(7273,1621,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','HEY I GOT YOU GUYS A PRESENT TOO WHAT ABOUT ME',0,0,0,0,'63.93.104.218','en'),(7274,1617,'2001-08-17 20:14:44',0,'treetop','Some bar...\r\n\r\n  Spro Praha  \r\n  Velkoobchod  \r\n  Bubenska\\\' 14, Praha 7',0,0,0,0,'172.144.160.243','en'),(7275,1621,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','HAHHAHAHA HA HA HA YOU GUYS ARE REALLY TOO TOO CUTE',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(7276,1605,'2001-08-17 20:53:57',0,'treetop to tyler','</head>\r\n<body>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<br>Of course I listened to the music. I\\\'ve seen over 40 \r\nshows.&nbsp; The\r\nmusic was my drug.&nbsp; As far as my writing is concerned, \r\nit does MEAN\r\nsomething.&nbsp; It means a lot of things.&nbsp; Not that \r\nyou would UNDERSTAND\r\nbecause, its not spontaneous and well composed at the same \r\ntime.\r\n<br>&nbsp;\r\n<br>Please look up the word, \\\"oxymoron\\\".&nbsp; Then read \r\nwhat you just\r\nwrote: \\\"Their music is extremely well-composed... and \r\npeople who appreciate..spontaneous\r\ncreation like it\\\"\r\n<p>You know, phish has similar lyrics.&nbsp; They don\\\'t \r\nreally SEEM to\r\nmean anything.&nbsp; Of course they mean something to the \r\nwriter, but the\r\nwriter leaves the interpretation open to the \r\nlistener.&nbsp; You can find\r\nyou own meaning within their lyrics.&nbsp; For instance, \r\nwhenever I hear\r\n\\\'Foam I think of being really drunk and swirling \r\naround.&nbsp; \\\'Tweezer\r\nmakes me think of acid.&nbsp; And of course there \r\nis \\\'Fluffhead...&nbsp;\r\nThat one explains itself.\r\n<p>Im not trying to burn you, Im just saying that when you \r\nlash out at\r\nsomeone for their ideas you should be very careful in what \r\nyou <a href=\\\"http://sugarmegs.org/hunter.swf\\\">say</a>.\r\n<p>~peace\r\n</body>\r\n</html>',0,0,0,0,'172.144.160.243','en'),(7277,1612,'2001-08-17 21:10:37',0,'mojo','I have never lost a loved one, but experienced the pain of \r\nit through watching my father lose his best friend.  She \r\nwas young, in her mid 40s, and very healthy and vibrant.  A \r\nfootball coach and a school teacher, single mother of a 10-\r\nyear old boy.  She was diagnosed with a fatal blood \r\ndisorder at a regular check-up, and given ONE WEEK to get \r\nher affairs on order.  She died four days later.<br>\r\nI keep waiting for the day when reality will drop into my \r\nlap, that phone call that indicates someone I love has \r\ndied.  How will I deal with it?  With strength, or will I \r\ncrumble?  Will I be the blubbering person in the corner of \r\nthe wake, who cannot be soothed?  Or will I make a rousing \r\neulogy at the funeral, and host a grand retrospective party \r\nin their honor?<br>\r\nI wonder sometimes if people from my high school days have \r\ndied and disappeared into the aether of my life.  I may \r\nnever know.',3,0,0,0,'216.232.156.58','en'),(7278,1617,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>Aww guys, I had a blast.  Ess, you blew us off, man. Hey, aren\'t you glad we didn\'t stay up on your roof? Life is lived in the little moments, I think. How was work this morning? I fell asleep in the fume hood.  Let me know if you wanna chill Sat. nite. Egg, you should join us!  <b>egg:</b> i got an \r\nemail from Slick Poppa.  Glad you got your tickets, though.  \'ll have to admit, though, the true art for me was in the co-chillin.<br>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'66.65.49.22','en'),(7279,1622,'2001-08-17 21:39:59',0,'l-box','people don\\\'t change as much as we like to think they do.  \r\nthe angle of our perception just shifts.<Br><BR><br><i>[best \r\nfriendly, OF COURSE.]</i>',0,0,0,0,'206.40.244.66','en'),(7280,1622,'2001-08-17 21:47:59',0,'also, though','sometimes people have really good excuses for being late.',0,0,0,0,'206.40.244.66','en'),(7281,1621,'2001-08-17 21:55:55',0,'auntie','your present requires a writing all it\\\'s own because there \r\nis a story to tell and i am too sleepy to write it and \r\nbesides you know i love the BOYS better, LOL!<br><br>\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,'24.162.119.106','en'),(7282,1605,'2001-08-17 22:41:40',0,'whisper','</head>\r\n<body>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<br>Btw, There are better bands out there.&nbsp; You could \r\ntake for instance,\r\nthe String Cheese Incident.&nbsp; It seems to me that most \r\nof the phish\r\nhangers-on have now jumped on SCI tour...&nbsp; I base this \r\nobservation\r\non the Shasta show a couple of weeks ago.&nbsp; Then there \r\nis Widespread\r\nPanic.&nbsp; WSP was my first counter cultural music \r\nexperience back in\r\n89 when I was a freshman in high school.&nbsp; Phish is \r\ngone, and Trey\r\nwants to write pop music.&nbsp; Good for him...&nbsp; The \r\nmusic is where\r\nit all begins.&nbsp; The scene just follows who ever is \r\nconvenient.&nbsp;\r\nExample:&nbsp; \\\"Hey bro, did you bring back any good drugs \r\nfrom the show?\\\"&nbsp;\r\n\\\"Yea duuude, its double dipped and double stacked.\\\"&nbsp; \r\nMy fav lot phrase\r\nis \\\"What the fuck, its only a buck!\\\"\r\n<br>&nbsp;\r\n<br>&nbsp;\r\n</body>\r\n</html>',0,0,0,0,'172.144.160.243','en'),(7283,1605,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','Some of their stuff is spontaneous, some is composed. Some \r\nof it is improvisation within the framework of a written-\r\nout composition. I don\\\'t understand things that make no \r\nsense, like the first poem of your post. Please don\\\'t try \r\nto compare it to song lyrics, which of course are a part of \r\na larger work. A poem means what it\\\'s words and phrases \r\nmean, which in this case is nothing. Unless it\\\'s written in \r\nsome kind of secret code. \\\"It means something to ME\\\" is a \r\nbullshit modern art copout. Here\\\'s an example:\r\n<p>\r\nFire and ice swirl around my head\r\nthe green frog smiles, satisfied\r\nthe fool laughs\r\ninside a puff-cloud\r\ni am free\r\n<p>\r\nsome people think that kind of thing is high art, but i \r\njust made up some profound-sounding shit.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.237','en'),(7284,1616,'2001-08-17 23:01:14',0,'mojo23','God loves Atheists.  So do I.',3,0,0,0,'216.232.156.58','en'),(7285,1617,'2001-08-17 23:03:01',0,'kat','swinney boys = hubba hubba = we stay up way too late = \r\nfrench kiss = hardware addiction',4,0,0,0,'32.100.71.176','en'),(7286,446,'2001-08-17 23:03:08',0,'mojo','nice, round and white. Just like the last time I see it.<br>\r\nI miss your nice, round, white ass.<br>\r\nYours, too, le, even if I haven\\\'t seen it up close.',1,0,0,0,'216.232.156.58','en'),(7287,600,'2001-08-17 23:06:40',0,'mojo','what could go terribly wrong?<br>\r\nif it looks like shite, just cut it off.  Her hair\\\'s short, \r\nright? just ask le, bald is beautiful!',1,0,0,0,'216.232.156.58','en'),(7288,458,'2001-08-17 23:12:13',0,'mojo','We\\\'re all stupid and boring.<br>\r\nWe write about the most exciting moments (or most \r\nexcrutiatingly boring moments) of our lives for each \r\nother\\\'s solicited comments.',3,0,0,0,'216.232.156.58','en'),(7289,703,'2001-08-17 23:18:05',0,'mojo','mmm. transformers and house music and booty shaking.  mmm',2,0,0,0,'216.232.156.58','en'),(7290,1622,'2001-08-17 23:57:31',0,'lou to lunchbox','sometimes people DO have really good excuses! like the tire \r\non the bus they are on blew out and it was tedious and \r\nawful!  now i feel bad, but it\\\'s okay because we are having \r\na really good time listening to bad mp3s and sewing! you \r\nshould be here, lb!<BR><BR>ps, maria, i like you lots!',1,0,0,0,'165.247.55.211','en'),(7291,1605,'2001-08-17 23:59:02',0,'treetop to ty','</head>\r\n<body>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<br>I like what you just wrote.&nbsp; It is abstract, and I \r\n<b>do</b> find\r\nmeaning within your words.&nbsp; Of course I have to \r\n<b>think</b> and relate\r\nyour words to my experiences.&nbsp; So maybe I went a \r\nlittle overboard\r\nby posting a whole article that is too abstract.&nbsp; I \r\nwanted to get\r\nfeedback, and I did.&nbsp; Within the comments, a \r\nconversation has developed...\r\n<p>As for the first part of my post, those were random \r\nthoughts that went\r\nthrough my mind as I sat at a bar.&nbsp; Of course I could \r\nelaborate on\r\nthose thoughts, but I would rather the reader \r\n<b>generate</b> their own.&nbsp;\r\nWhile I was sitting at the bar, I thumbed through a book on \r\nastrology and\r\ncame across the personification about the tiger.&nbsp; The \r\npoem was unsigned.&nbsp;\r\nMy analysis of the poem is that the tiger is overwhelmed \r\nwith self righteousness.&nbsp;\r\nBut after all, he is a tiger...\r\n</body>\r\n</html>',0,0,0,0,'172.144.160.243','en'),(7292,1605,'2001-08-18 00:29:41',0,'whisper','/head>\r\n<body>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<br>Elaboration:\r\n<p>I have a blue sharpie in my back pocket.&nbsp; We had \r\njust smoked some\r\nhash from India in the DJ booth.&nbsp; It is part of the \r\ncultural blessing\r\nof this certain tribe to wrap the hash with corn \r\nhusks.&nbsp; <font color=\\\"#3333FF\\\">OM\r\nSHIVA OM</font>&nbsp; When you smoke this hash, it gives \r\nyou a slight dizziness\r\nas if you body is sliding to the side but you head is \r\nfloating upwards.&nbsp;\r\nThe DJ&nbsp; a snakebite and pulls me out of my \r\ntrance.&nbsp; The conclusion\r\nof our conversation:&nbsp; Columbus sailed to America \r\nbecause he thought\r\nhe could provide a faster trade route from Spain to \r\nIndia.&nbsp; I go back\r\ninto my trance.&nbsp; I am pulled out of my trance \r\nagain.&nbsp; This time\r\nthe DJ is talking to me about how the bar has a homely feel \r\nto it.&nbsp;\r\nKinda like cheers.&nbsp; Everyone knows everyone.&nbsp; \r\nAnyway, he was\r\ntelling me the German word for that feeling is \r\nGemitlichkeit &lt;SP?>.&nbsp;\r\nWe both took German in high school.&nbsp; So I am \r\nthinking, \\\"yea, its good\r\nto have that.&nbsp; That feeling is all you need, its good \r\nto have that\r\nin your head.\\\"&nbsp; And then the trance returns...\r\n</body>\r\n</html>',0,0,0,0,'172.144.160.243','en'),(7293,199,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','this is sublime',0,0,0,0,'63.10.151.232','en'),(7294,1624,'2001-08-18 04:28:27',0,'lou','\r\nit is good to not want to be in new jersey. if anyone ever \r\nwanted to be in new jersey, i\\\'d be scared for them. i \r\ncannot think of a good reason to be in new jersey, except \r\nfor Denny\\\'s (which can also be found in upstate new york, \r\nPA, and CT), or maybe to stop two angels from walking \r\nthrough the arch of a church that is really in pittsburgh...',1,0,0,0,'165.247.55.211','en'),(7295,1624,'2001-08-18 04:33:40',0,'maria','i am in new jersey. the only good thing about where i live \r\nis that dunkin donuts is up the block, but i could get that \r\na lot of other places, you know? \r\n\r\n',6,0,0,0,'172.157.64.185','en'),(7296,1624,'2001-08-18 04:52:33',0,'lou to maria','that is exactly my point. there is NOTHING that new jersey \r\nhas that cannot be found in several other states.  states \r\nthat, may i point out, are not ASS. etc.',1,0,0,0,'165.247.55.211','en'),(7297,1626,'2001-08-18 06:01:14',0,'ty','and then, the funky disco sdtrk starts up...Roxy \r\nEntertainment Presents...A Mark Rammstein \r\nProduction...Cheryl Badd...Rosy Cheeks...\\\"Where the Girls \r\nAre\\\"...(c)1986',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.167','en'),(7298,1617,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to peter','YOU GOT AN EMAIL FROM SLICK POPPA???? tell me more. ',0,0,0,0,'63.210.213.246','en'),(7299,1624,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','A. why are you in new jersey and B. WHAT OF SLICK POPPA??',0,0,0,0,'63.210.213.246','en'),(7300,1625,'2001-08-18 09:55:52',0,'loureed','makes me wanna listen to (Paranoia Key Of E )\r\n',3,0,0,0,'24.27.26.62','en'),(7301,1626,'2001-08-18 09:56:52',0,'theb\\\'s','play me some \\\"she\\\'s leaving home\\\"',3,0,0,0,'24.27.26.62','en'),(7302,1616,'2001-08-18 10:00:32',0,'question','are pictures a no no now ?',1,0,0,0,'24.27.26.62','en'),(7303,1623,'2001-08-18 11:12:53',0,'Treetop','Whenever you ask for mike\\\'s hard lemonade its an automatic \r\nlicense checking event.',0,0,0,0,'172.144.160.243','en'),(7304,1624,'2001-08-18 11:57:26',0,'lunch b.','i have to say that i 