wn.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(7623,1653,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','<p>yeah swinney, i\\\'ve heard that story before and i don\\\'t\r\nthink it was about your grandparents friends</p>\r\n<p>best friends?  i think just maybe it means that i\\\'m kind\r\nof perverted.</p>',4,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(7624,1657,'2001-08-24 00:37:58',0,'deb','pushing out of bed. floggings. can we say domestic dispute? \r\nhow horrible... ;)',2,0,0,0,'205.188.196.57','en'),(7625,1653,'2001-08-24 00:39:44',0,'deb','but why did you use it twice? was it something about the \r\ntooth brush that turned you on? what was it?',2,0,0,0,'205.188.196.57','en'),(7626,105,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','damn',2,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(7627,1660,'2001-08-24 01:18:41',0,'deb','the terror of waking up from a dream where you\\\'re happy, \r\nonly to find out that you\\\'re still very alone.',2,0,0,0,'205.188.196.36','en'),(7628,1653,'2001-08-24 02:44:32',0,'liver','how come no one ever moons me on fillmore?\r\n',5,0,0,0,'63.202.215.130','en'),(7629,1653,'2001-08-24 03:32:39',0,'szajic','the burglars shoving <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.waste.org/mail/?list=wallace-l&month=0004&m\r\nsg=393\\\">toothbrushes up their asses</a> vignette also \r\nappears in <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.plastic.com/altculture/01/04/11/1558232.sht\r\nml\\\">DFW</a>\\\'s <em>Infinite Jest</em>, though I have no idea \r\nwhether it surfaced as an urban legend before or after \r\nthat.\r\n<p>\r\nalso, jo: I am shocked, shocked that you\\\'d use your \r\nroommate\\\'s mach3!  those cartridges are expensive, yo.',3,0,0,0,'63.48.18.60','en'),(7630,1660,'2001-08-24 03:48:49',0,'ty','oh god. now i\\\'m all depressed. ',0,0,0,0,'63.10.151.132','en'),(7631,632,'2001-08-24 05:15:28',0,'huevita','cats do it the same way dogs do it, except that a male cat \r\nhas a knob on the end of its dick that would make it deeply \r\npainful, if not impossible, for the female to retract \r\nshortly after ejaculation. i am a cat person and I like it \r\ndoggy style.',0,0,0,0,'216.243.8.76','en'),(7632,1638,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','none of these comments make any sense, and you are all dumb \r\nassholes.',0,0,0,0,'216.243.8.76','en'),(7633,1660,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','This isn\\\'t one of those dreams that needs interpreting.  It\r\nclearly maps out things for me.  This is an illustration of\r\nthe source of my insomnia, of the dark cloud that hovers\r\nover my every move.  It\\\'s a map, showing me what it is I\r\nwant but am too afraid to ask for.  It\\\'s my major weakness.\r\n Please don\\\'t exploit it.',3,0,0,0,'64.229.64.167','en'),(7634,632,'2001-08-24 09:57:42',0,'Jamazon','Doggy is good. In my experience, lots of women love it cus \r\nof the deeper penetration. My lady likes it.<BR><BR>\r\n\r\nWhat about \\\'woman on top\\\' That kicks ass if ur lazy like \r\nme. Is there a name for that?',1,0,0,0,'217.32.159.66','en'),(7635,1653,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','olivia, ix, yeti, le. when the fuck are we going out for \r\nbeers? ',1,0,0,0,'64.81.65.205','en'),(7636,1658,'2001-08-24 10:50:35',0,'Jamazon','Now. You see. I would have left it open for a sequel. But \r\nthat\\\'s just me.',6,0,0,0,'217.32.159.66','en'),(7637,1642,'2001-08-24 10:56:58',0,'Jamazon','This has proved much more controversial than i ever could \r\nhave imagined...',1,0,0,0,'217.32.159.66','en'),(7638,632,'2001-08-24 12:09:22',0,'Dr. Dre','\\\"aint nuthin but a g thang baby, girls on top cause i\\\'m \r\nlazy\\\"',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7639,632,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>doggy is a favorite here.  girl on top is \r\n<i>best</i>, however.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7640,1653,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>did someone mention <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.urbanlegends.com/classic/toothbrushes_on_va\r\ncation.html\\\">the toothbrush urban legend</a>?</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7641,1660,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>my dream-life is generally much more vivid, \r\nexciting and <i>happy</i> than my real life.  i do hate \r\nwaking up, sometimes</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7642,1661,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<a href=\"http://elly.org/misc/lonesome_kicker/\">lonesome \r\nkicker</a>',0,0,0,0,'216.27.183.161','en'),(7643,1653,'2001-08-24 12:19:09',0,'jo to s','you are not shocked. i was between razors. it was only a \r\ncouple of months.<BR>\r\ni also made him dinner almost every night and for the \r\nmonths when he had vertigo and couldn\\\'t leave the \r\napartment, i did all his errands. so cartridges, \r\nschmartridges! i had some karma coming at me!<BR>\r\nthey are <b>nice</b> razors.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(7644,1661,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>\'lonesome kicker\'...nice.  i think i\'m going to go \r\nread that every time i start feeling down or the effects of \r\nself-sympathy. it sort of puts things in perspective.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7645,1664,'2001-08-24 14:13:36',0,'Herr Doktor','most useless thing= Hummel figurines',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7646,1638,'2001-08-24 15:55:55',0,'marcie','You sound like James Brown should be YOUR gynecologist, too.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.5.232','en'),(7647,1665,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','more useless advice:<br><br>Are you still in contact with \r\nhim?  I found the only way to deal with the girl I lived \r\nwith for two years was to completely break all contact with \r\nher.  Right after I moved out, every time I heard her voice \r\nor read an email from her, it would just cause more salt \r\ntears to cascade into the open wounds festering in my \r\nheart.  I had to surgically remove her from my life, \r\ncompletely.  That (and dating a model) was what finally got \r\nme functional again.<br><br>Warm hugs are really nice too.',1,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(7648,1653,'2002-03-05 20:17:36',17,'austin to le, o','<P>i dont see why i cant pass an urban legend off if i want\r\nto.  it is a good story.  i think it is funny.</P>',3,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(7649,1666,'2001-08-24 16:47:15',0,'Pandora','Obviously something is there, beneath the surface, that \r\nkeeps you running. Don\\\'t ignore it -- while the desire \r\nmight be there, as well as the fuel from a good friendship, \r\nthese \\\"inklings\\\" shouldn\\\'t be overlooked. They can save you \r\nfrom pain and torment.\r\n\r\nOf course, they may also prevent you from gaining an \r\namazing experience.\r\n\r\nGood luck.',1,0,0,0,'168.215.102.189','en'),(7650,1660,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','Despite the odd, if slightly unnerving ending, I did wake up\r\nwith a smile on my face.',3,0,0,0,'64.229.64.167','en'),(7651,1666,'2001-08-24 17:01:49',0,'ghost','question...if you <i>both</i> realized there were deeper \r\nfeelings for each other why scram? \r\n\r\n<p>i have an incredibly deep connection with one of my male \r\nfriends. i love him so much that sometimes i wonder why the \r\nhell am i not with him. he says all the things i ever \r\nwanted a guy to say to me. but when that moment came...the \r\none where someone pours their heart out, i knew the only \r\nthing i could do was be honest. to say that yes, i loved \r\nhim like no other. and yes, he meant the world to me. but \r\nthat for many reasons i wasnt willing to take the \r\nrelationship to a different place. right now he means more \r\nto me as a friend/brother then he would as a lover. things \r\nwere awkward for awhile but we never lost touch. and i \r\nthink we are even closer now. i have to admit it was so \r\ntempting to go to that other place.</p>',1,0,0,0,'32.102.109.216','en'),(7652,1665,'2001-08-24 17:18:17',0,'Nastchenka','i\\\'m never one to write fairy tales--but this happened to my \r\nmom and dad--he walked away from her after 10 years of \r\ndating, she left, cut him out of her life for three years \r\nand he finally realized what he\\\'d lost and came back and \r\nasked her to marry him. She put him through hell and then \r\nagreed. Now they\\\'re dirt poor driving a pickup truck with 3 \r\nkids, one a dyke, one a punk rocker and one a gun-totin\\\' \r\npsycho. ',3,0,0,0,'199.4.18.2','en'),(7653,1651,'2001-08-24 17:19:04',0,'ty','Do seasons ache? Or do you ache when they change, like \r\narthritis or something? Or do you ache slowly, like the \r\nseasons change slowly? Or dop they ache slowly, and you \r\nchange? Oh, now I\\\'m all confused.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.28','en'),(7654,1664,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','does this make any sense? hello in there...',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.28','en'),(7655,1666,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','there isn\\\'t much difference between friendship and love, \r\neven romantic love. people make way too big a deal out \r\nof \\\"where they are in a relationship.\\\"',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.28','en'),(7656,1666,'2001-08-24 17:33:50',0,'ghost to ty','yea. but nothing is black and white...and its in the shades \r\nof gray where people get lost. where it helps to try and \r\ndefine things at least a little bit. it would be nice to \r\nthink we could have open and honest relations with those we \r\nlove, but we are after all only human. expectations get in \r\nthe way. differences of opinion. wants and needs. i may not \r\nreally understand or know why i feel or think the way i \r\ndo...but it makes sense to share what i can whenever \r\npossible.',3,0,0,0,'32.102.109.216','en'),(7657,1666,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','and who is this lucky girl?',0,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(7658,1539,'2001-08-24 18:12:49',0,'Ariel (another one)','Jolayne, holy holy shit. This whole thing is so eerily \r\nfamiliar that it\\\'s creeping me out. We will talk much \r\nmuch much more.\r\n\r\nLove and support to you, my emotional double.',1,0,0,0,'65.4.10.102','en'),(7659,1664,'2001-08-24 18:31:35',0,'artistiko','you must be familiar with s.o.c, no?',1,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(7660,1664,'2001-08-24 18:44:35',0,'dork','SOC IT TO ME BABY\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(7661,1658,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','bob could return as a ZOMBIE FLESH EATER in THE RETURN OF BOB \r\nIS ME.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(7662,1666,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','I myself am about to make one of those potentially stupid\r\nmoves and tell a good friend of mine that I love her as more\r\nthan just a friend.  In fact, I\\\'m going to meet her at work\r\nshortly.<br><br>This could get interesting.',1,0,0,0,'64.229.64.167','en'),(7663,1666,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','sigh.',0,0,0,0,'216.27.183.161','en'),(7664,1666,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','sigh sigh\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(7665,1666,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','there are few simple heuristics in life (successful ones \r\nanyway).  one is: <b>Don\\\'t Screw The Crew.</b>  Love does \r\nnot mix with Work.  Becuase if it goes south, you have all \r\nthat stress mixed in with the smelly shitbag of emotions \r\nwork carries around anyway.  Not A Good Scene.',1,0,0,0,'24.167.21.142','en'),(7666,1664,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','most useless thing: a broken i486dx2-66 cpu.  too ugly to \r\neven make a good necklace from.  The runner up is all the \r\nmicrosoft software I \\\"aquired\\\" back in the day (the days \r\nbefore gaining Enlightenment, namely, Unix).',1,0,0,0,'24.167.21.142','en'),(7667,1664,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','because at least the M$ junkware I can use for coasters.',1,0,0,0,'24.167.21.142','en'),(7668,1666,'2001-08-24 23:12:28',0,'bmg','<p>sigh, sigh, sigh. </p>\r\n<p>so when the conversation started to get thin, our \r\neyes would meet and we would just smile - as if we \r\nhad just done it. An awkward and unsettling moment for \r\nthe both of us. Me looking at her, her looking at me and \r\nlittle or no conversation inbetween. Part of me was like, \r\nOKAY fuck this, lets just bring it up - get it out in the \r\nopen and talk about it... just then the light turned green, \r\nmy car goes into motion, and my emotion flew out the \r\nwindow. A few more conversations about this and that, \r\nbarely scraping the top of the surface. I could tell that it was bothering \r\nher as much that is was bothering me. Usually talk \r\ncomes easy with the two of us, both of us are loud \r\nmouths. Tension won\'t be broken just yet... we are \r\ngoing out for drinks at 9. Alcohol will do atleast one of \r\ntwo things... i\'ll let ya\'ll know later. -- what the fuck am i \r\ndoing? </p><p>I asked austin earlier, how is it that I get \r\nmyself into these things... when i want it, its not there... \r\nwhen i dont, it is there... No reply from austin.</p>',1,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(7669,1665,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','hang on. you can ride this out. ',0,0,0,0,'216.27.183.161','en'),(7670,1653,'2001-08-24 23:21:11',0,'da','hey also, that urban legend (or maybe it isn\\\'t!) makes an \r\nappearance in <i>infinite jest.</i>',2,0,0,0,'128.111.96.65','en'),(7671,1653,'2001-08-25 03:54:02',0,'hmm','is it lying when it\\\'s for the cause of a good story? \r\npersonally, dishonesty is a turn-off, but i guess it\\\'s not \r\nillegal. all a matter of personal preference.',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(7672,1666,'2001-08-25 04:00:08',0,'thebreedgirl','and...so...how\\\'d it go?',1,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(7673,1665,'2001-08-25 04:19:19',0,'oprah','you gonna <i>make</i> it <i>ba</i>by.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.73','en'),(7674,1662,'2001-08-25 04:30:41',0,'deb','don\\\'t you  hate it? you think you\\\'ll do good deeds and \r\nit\\\'ll all be ok cause you\\\'ll be repaid someday, somehow; \r\nbut we all end up screwed over in the end.',3,0,0,0,'64.12.102.22','en'),(7675,1664,'2001-08-25 04:32:50',0,'deb','old hummel figurines are useful for money when they\\\'re old\r\n\r\ncrayons make the world go round\r\n',2,0,0,0,'64.12.102.22','en'),(7676,1665,'2001-08-25 04:41:59',0,'kat to oprah','<p>i\\\'m gonna make a baby???  <i>eewwwwwwwwwww</i></p>\r\n<p>[destablizing]</p>',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.38','en'),(7677,1666,'2001-08-25 04:51:32',0,'ghost','<p>well if you didnt live so far away i\\\'d ask you out on a \r\ndate.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>i\\\'d look you in the eye. i\\\'d say, \\\'bmg...let me show you \r\nmy world.\\\'</p>\r\n\r\n<p>[jealous]</p>',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.38','en'),(7678,1666,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','bmg is really cute.',0,0,0,0,'216.27.183.161','en'),(7679,1666,'2001-08-25 07:13:45',0,'bmg','<p>breed girl! - wow, is this one of the lovely Garden \r\nGirls??? Gee, how could I be so lucky. Lemme tell yah \r\nbout them breed gardin girls! Yikes, watch out, they\\\'ll \r\nsteal you heart!</p>\r\n<p>ghost, le - blush, blush - ya\\\'ll needn\\\'t flatter me so! \r\nTwo beautiful ladies such as yourselves teasing me as \r\nsuch!!! Shame on both of you!</p>\r\n<p>yah, well - it went as usual. I realized when she \r\ncame to my door, an hour late and high, that it was \r\ngoing to be more of the same. Not much said, drinks \r\nwere drank and people were seen. We ran into my ex \r\nthere, which made for odd feelings... (damn austin is \r\nso small). The night ended without a heart breaking, \r\nromantic ending. Sorry folks!</p>\r\n<p>I\\\'m going to date myself for a while. I am not high \r\nmaintenance, I clean up after myself, I cook for myself, I \r\ntalk to myself, and I find myself rather sexy; all good \r\nreasons to comit to myself.</p>',1,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(7680,1666,'2001-08-25 07:38:30',0,'jo','bmg is precious precious. ',1,0,0,0,'128.83.46.130','en'),(7681,1650,'2001-08-25 07:42:26',0,'jo','ummmm i\\\'ll pass.',1,0,0,0,'128.83.46.130','en'),(7682,1650,'2001-08-25 14:10:38',0,'bmg','ughhh... mah luhngs awe fihne.',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(7683,1666,'2001-08-25 14:24:56',0,'Joanna','Hi BMG, I would like to marry you. I cook really well.  I \r\nkeep myself clean.  I have child bearing hips.  ',1,0,0,0,'203.97.2.242','en'),(7684,1666,'2001-08-25 20:56:42',0,'kat','this world of Swinney.O always makes me think of Peter \r\nGabriel\\\'s ...<i>games without frontiers</i>',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.248','en'),(7685,1668,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p>this is wholly unrelated but:</p>\r\n<p>i lived downstairs from you when i was 12. i don\\\'t remember \r\nvery much about it because i\\\'ve done too many drugs and have a \r\nproblem dealing in memories and other things relating to linear \r\ntime, but i do remember some stuff. \r\n</p><p>\r\ni remember that you dislocated your shoulder from carrying a \r\nheavy bookbag too much, and i remember something about not \r\nbeing allowed to hang out with you guys on sunday because of \r\nsome rules? and... i remember seeing you guys on new years eve \r\none year and you had stayed up all night playing board games. \r\n</p>\r\n<p>for those of you that weren\\\'t there, i looked like this:</p>\r\n<p><img src=\\\"http://elly.org/img/yearbook2.jpg\\\"></p>\r\n<p>i am the second from the left. you will note that the boy \r\npictured next to me is josh manthey, the younger brother of <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://dir.yahoo.com/News_and_Media/Television/Programm\r\ning/Shows/Reality_Television/Survivor/Season_2__Australia/Manth\r\ney__Jerri/\\\">jerri manthey</a>, who some of you tv viewers may \r\nknow from the popular reality television show, \\\"survivor\\\".</p>',4,0,0,0,'216.27.183.161','en'),(7686,1668,'2001-08-25 22:50:37',0,'deb','yea, i don\\\'t hate myself either... :(',2,0,0,0,'152.163.201.176','en'),(7687,1668,'2001-08-25 23:44:54',0,'felicity to le','of course i remember you.  i actually found a letter that i \r\nwrote to you but never sent a couple of days ago.  i must \r\nhave written that letter when i was 12 years old, judging by \r\nthe content, the less than skilled art that graced the \r\npages, and the fact that I still referred to you as \r\n\\\"Lizard\\\".<BR><BR> \r\ni\\\'m still trying to figure out how i could dislocate my \r\nshoulder, though.  Sure, the bookbag was heavy, but we lived \r\n50 feet from the front door of the schoo.  Man....I \r\n<b>was</b> a total dork.',1,0,0,0,'216.42.124.244','en'),(7688,1668,'2001-08-26 01:40:05',0,'kat','i am STILL a dork.',1,0,0,0,'32.100.71.230','en'),(7689,1669,'2001-08-26 07:51:50',0,'will','This should be a song.<br /><br />\r\nIt could be my anthem.<br /><br />\r\nEspecially now.  We broke up.  End soap opera.',1,0,0,0,'152.163.207.66','en'),(7690,1637,'2001-08-26 08:01:44',0,'will','move more center-city and pay enormous rent!  wonderful \r\nidea!  ',6,0,0,0,'152.163.207.66','en'),(7691,1669,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p>\r\n<img src=\\\"http://steve.org/images/broodingcats.gif\\\">\r\n</p>',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(7692,949,'2001-08-26 09:00:13',0,'Evan','Either Kurt Vonnegut or Aldous Huxley (because those are the\r\nonly authors that i have read in the last 3 years) wrote\r\nthat the best that we can do is to paying attention to how\r\nwe react to different situations throughout our lives to\r\nbetter realize our nature. The more experiences remembered\r\nthe better.  if we\\\'re lucky we\\\'ll try not to make the same\r\nmistakes too much.<br><br>\r\n\r\njournals are good for getting that perspective.  i think.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nEvan<br>\r\n<a href=\\\"http://koax.org\\\">www.koax.org</a>  ',2,0,0,0,'66.68.121.96','en'),(7693,1669,'2001-08-26 13:00:47',0,'Bitch','I never once claimed I was anything but. I wish it would \r\nstop being such a freaking surprise to everyone.\r\n\r\nLife was a little simpler before he stepped in. I didn\\\'t \r\nintend to crush his toes.',4,0,0,0,'66.66.233.39','en'),(7694,1669,'2001-08-26 14:15:03',0,'will','This isn\\\'t my fault at all.  Don\\\'t even attempt to make it \r\nsound as if it were.<br /><br />\r\nYou aren\\\'t absolved simply because you say, \\\"Well, yes, I \r\nam a bitch, I thought you knew!\\\"  That only deepens your \r\nguilt... because you know and yet still refuse to change, \r\nstill put yourself in situations where others will be hurt \r\nby your irresponsibility.<br /><br />  \\\"I don\\\'t change.\\\"  \r\nDon\\\'t expect anything else to, then.',2,0,0,0,'172.155.199.10','en'),(7695,1669,'2001-08-26 14:59:10',0,'deb','Please, don\\\'t flatter yourself.  \\\"You\\\'re so vain, you \r\nprobably think this song is about you...\\\"  You\\\'re not the \r\nonly one.',6,0,0,0,'205.188.196.23','en'),(7696,1669,'2001-08-26 15:05:54',0,'bitch to bitch','somehow i doubt anyone was surprised',5,0,0,0,'205.188.196.23','en'),(7697,1669,'2001-08-26 16:17:36',0,'maria','i hate the word \\\"bitch\\\". especially because women who are \r\ncalled this are usually judged by a disgusting double \r\nstandard : if a man were to act the way that \\\"bitches\\\" do, \r\nit\\\'s usually called \\\"aggressiveness\\\". same goes for that \r\ngem of a word \\\"slut\\\". so, if i ever call anyone a bitch, \r\nit\\\'s usually referring to a boy and it\\\'s usually someone wh \r\nois just really cranky to me. \r\n\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nregarding the little catfight going on in the comments, the \r\npeanut gallery would like to say that you really should \r\nhave known something like this was going to happen, and \r\nsaying you have no fault in this is really really \r\nincredibly childish and stupid. --no one-- is ever not at \r\nany kind of fault in those kinds of situations. wise up. \r\n\r\n\r\n',2,0,0,0,'132.162.231.185','en'),(7698,1669,'2001-08-26 16:21:26',0,'deb','maria, i see no cat fighting, really. i see bitterness, \r\nplain and simple.  i also don\\\'t believe anyone of the \r\npeople involved claimed to not be at fault at all. you \r\ncould wise up yourself a little, you know. and i mean that \r\nin the \\\'nicest possible way.\\\'',3,0,0,0,'152.163.201.213','en'),(7699,1669,'2001-08-26 17:26:06',0,'yeti to maria','<p>Come on. People being assholes are people being \r\nassholes. Call it what you want. Bitch, dick, cocksucker, \r\nasshole, fuckbag. Doesnt matter.</p>\r\n<p>Do you really think that men have the luxury of acting \r\nin a way which most of us would determine as unacceptable \r\nbehavior without some sort of judgement that holds similar \r\nconnotations to the word \\\'bitch\\\'?</p>\r\n<p>If anything, I suppose I\\\'m at fault for going easier on \r\nwomen in terms of the standards I hold them to for \r\nbeing \\\'good people\\\' or \\\'bad people\\\'. I think I\\\'m much \r\nharder on men, and most hard on myself.</p>\r\n<p>Now, the slut thing is disturbing and disbalanced. I \r\nhope that changes in the next 5 or 10 years.</p>\r\n<p>huh.</p>',1,0,0,0,'216.27.183.161','en'),(7700,1669,'2001-08-26 19:00:13',0,'truth','YOU are INCREDIBLY childish AND stupid MARIA; so SPEAK for \r\nYOURSELF.',6,0,0,0,'152.163.213.179','en'),(7701,1669,'2001-08-26 19:02:47',0,'maria','anonymous attacks are childish and stupid. \r\n\r\n',6,0,0,0,'132.162.231.185','en'),(7702,1669,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','<BR>ding-dong. fart machine. poophead. double \r\nloser.<BR><BR>no, you are.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.10.127','en'),(7703,1669,'2001-08-26 19:17:20',0,'maria','do i know you? ',0,0,0,0,'132.162.231.185','en'),(7704,1670,'2001-08-26 19:24:13',0,'.','it is a frolick!',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(7705,1668,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','they say from this valley you are going. i will miss your \r\nbright eyes and sweet smile.<BR><BR>don\\\'t listen to me or \r\nlisten to me. but...not everybody needs the drugs. does \r\nanybody? maybe. there are other things you could try first. \r\nif you want to. are you worth it? i love you.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.10.127','en'),(7706,1670,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','yesss.  tummies. rubbing them together. then you get sweaty \r\nand get those suction sounds going when they slide together \r\nthen separate. kissing and sliding together. no \r\nfriction.<BR><BR>i like the whole thing. belly, tits, ass, \r\narmpits. fingers, fingers, little toes.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.10.127','en'),(7707,1669,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','you talkin\\\' to me, mama?\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.10.127','en'),(7708,1670,'2001-08-26 20:58:23',0,'.','uh?',0