ard of oz, don\\\'t do it at all.',1,0,0,0,'172.171.208.165','en'),(7720,1666,'2001-08-27 05:00:13',0,'jo','<a href=\\\"http://www.mmmbed.com/pictures/2001/bmg/\\\">recent \r\npictures of bmg</a>. muahahaha. isn\\\'t he adorable? awwww.',1,0,0,0,'172.171.208.165','en'),(7721,1671,'2001-08-27 05:13:56',0,'kat','i am sorry le, but i dont think an all swinneyboy shower \r\nscene would even keep me here. not even if it included \r\npygmy goats and monkies.<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<i>i am comin to get you mang...i am comin to get you</i>',4,0,0,0,'32.102.109.150','en'),(7722,1666,'2001-08-27 05:20:07',0,'bmg','i\\\'ve got goos bumps, and all giggly with excitement! i\\\'m \r\ngonna have ta comfaskate dat camera jo! ',1,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(7723,1666,'2001-08-27 05:22:51',0,'bmg','i have big eyebrows, huh. kinda like furry catapillars.',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(7724,1671,'2001-08-27 05:22:53',0,'huevita','chase skirt. *pfft*',0,0,0,0,'216.175.103.245','en'),(7725,1666,'2001-08-27 06:36:54',0,'ghost','nice delicious lips...',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.32','en'),(7726,1671,'2001-08-27 07:04:18',0,'s5 to austin','load up honda. head east on I-80. call me when you hit \r\nreno.',1,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(7727,1671,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','oh and bring egg. you\\\'ll need 28 gallons of water.',1,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(7728,1671,'2001-08-27 07:42:45',0,'mojodog','but then who will take care of me????',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.125','en'),(7729,1671,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p>i have cold feet now. it is 2:42am. i am packing canned goods. \r\ni am concerned. what if i hate it! how will my stuff get home! who \r\nwill be my friend? i know i\\\'ll be lonely surrounded by so many \r\npeople.\r\n</p><p>\r\nthe two-day beginning of bman angst begins.\r\n</p><p>\r\nok i\\\'m ready.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n',4,0,0,0,'216.27.183.161','en'),(7730,1671,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<br><br>\r\n3:20am. still in san francisco. chaya is watering my \r\nplants. gear is packed into bins. i am deciding between \r\na nap or ephedrine. i want to be there i want to be there \r\ni want to be there. coming soon: rental van 3-D tetris.\r\n<br><br>\r\na thought: going to burning man is like volunteering for \r\nmercury retrograde.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(7731,1671,'2001-08-27 10:57:49',0,'green','fuck BURNING MAN ...it is just as corporate as going to \r\nknotts or disneyland...when was paying for someone to pick \r\nup your trash at the end of the week so expensive...and \r\nit\\\'s supposed to be some concept involving man\\\'s self \r\nsufficient talents....yet you need someone to watch over \r\nyou so no chaos occurs?....that\\\'s ok. BURNING MAN is as \r\ncorporate as a pair of guess jeans with the triangle brand \r\npatch ripped off...\r\n\r\nhave fun. i.ll do better things with 200+ \r\ncreate an environment rather than buy a ticket for it...\r\n',3,0,0,0,'64.30.217.22','en'),(7732,1666,'2001-08-27 11:03:15',0,'Joanna','and now I really want to marry you, after seeing pictures \r\n(I love being shallow!).  I think Le is right and we should \r\nmove to Utah, and be like that family that\\\'s in the news \r\nright now because the husband has gone to jail and the five \r\nwives are standing by him.  <BR><BR>\r\n\r\nI\\\'m unemployed right now, I have a lot of time on my \r\nhands.  ',1,0,0,0,'203.97.2.242','en'),(7733,1671,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','so?',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(7734,1672,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','everyone\\\'s breaking up again!',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(7735,1668,'2001-08-27 11:22:43',0,'Doktor','i need the drugs.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7736,1672,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>we both agree we probably shouldn\'t, but some things are inevitable.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7737,1671,'2001-08-27 11:51:22',0,'bmg','green, sounds like you really wanna go to burning man. \r\nyou should of coincided the quiting of your job with the \r\nlast pay check and road trip to burning man... who \r\nknows it might of changed your life. There is allways \r\nnext year! ',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(7738,1671,'2001-08-27 13:30:51',0,'Brian Bendis','I don\\\'t think green wants to go at all. i think she knows, \r\nyou know..that it Sucks. i think that\\\'s what she is saying. \r\ndid you go? did it change your life?',6,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(7739,1671,'2001-08-27 13:43:03',0,'trouble','\\\'...i did nothing and it was everything i thought it could \r\nbe\\\'',1,0,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(7740,1671,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>corporate, schmorporate.  burning man sounds like \r\n<i>fun</i>. I\\\'m not against paying to have a good time- \r\nI\\\'ve paid more for movies/books/music/drugs/records/gear in \r\nthe past month than the cost of burning man, so whats the \r\ndifference? just my two cents.  best friendly.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7741,1671,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','you really should experience the event before you diss it.',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(7742,1672,'2001-08-27 14:50:00',0,'jo','peter, it takes a lot of courage to break up while you \r\nstill want to be together rather than when you\\\'re \r\nambivalent (or, much worse, hateful) towards one \r\nanother.<BR>\r\ngood luck.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(7743,1671,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','<BR><BR>every summer my dad\\\'s family goes to cumberland \r\nisland national seashore, off the georgia coast. every year \r\ni dread going. it\\\'s hot as hell, the campsites are in thick \r\nwoods so there\\\'s no breeze, the mosquitos can be fierce.  \r\ncold showers only.  daily 16-hour encounter therapy \r\nsessions with my tribe, most of whom i wouldn\\\'t choose to \r\nbe around if they weren\\\'t related to me.<BR><BR>midway \r\nthrough the first day, i tell myself, \\\"yes, it\\\'s confirmed: \r\nyou ARE crazy to know how it is and come back here every \r\nyear.\\\"<BR><BR>and then the magic kicks in: playing games; \r\nexploring the island and the ruins of the carnegies\\\' summer \r\nhome; sneaking out to sleep on the beach during what, if we \r\ntime our 3-day slot right, is the height of the sea \r\nturtles\\\' nesting season.  it recharges my \r\nbatteries.<BR><BR>it isn\\\'t corporate: it\\\'s a national park, \r\nprobably shouldn\\\'t be privatized (which would no doubt lead \r\nto development), but does corporate=bad? i guess there are \r\ngood and bad corporations. is burning man a for-profit \r\nenterprise? i doubt it. i wouldn\\\'t go to disney world by \r\nmyself, but i love taking my niece there, seeing it through \r\nher eyes. flexibility. you can change your mind, and it\\\'s \r\nok.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.5.210','en'),(7744,1671,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','I always dont make plans to go and then on like the first \r\nday I want to change my mind and go, and then its too \r\nlate. I will be doing laundry and going to see ween with \r\nix. and then I am going to vegas to see men in thongs. \r\nfyi.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.91.205','en'),(7745,1672,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','better to do it now while you both still have all your \r\nlimbs.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.91.205','en'),(7746,1672,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>for three years, we were so \'in love\' that we \r\nintegrated each other so deeply in our respective lives, \r\nfamilies, activities.  now as a result, we\'re more brother-\r\nand-sister-ish than \'lovers\'. as the \'passion\' isn\'t \r\nforthcoming, we decided it was time, and god, do i hate it. \r\nmeanwhile, i\'m losing sleep and busying my time playing \r\nthe \'what if?\' game. i also constantly ask myself if we \r\ncould still be in a relationship without passion; would it \r\neventually come back if we actually <i>tried</i>, and if \r\nso, how to regress to that, etc etc, ad nauseum.<br><br>So, the question of the day, people: <b>Can</b> (not should) you still be in a relationship when there\'s no current passion? Knowing us, chances are it woulc come back soon enough....</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7747,1671,'2001-08-27 15:48:37',0,'bmg ta bendis','<p>nah, I haven\\\'t gone... and yes I think it would alter my \r\nlife, every time I experience something new it alters my \r\nlife. I could stay at home and be like stagnant water and \r\nnot change. I could sit and watch movies all day, day-\r\ndreaming about getting out and exploring myself and this \r\nworld, or I could go out and do it... I have never heard \r\nanyone coming back from burning man and trash it... must be \r\nan experience that few have had. I think green should go, \r\njust cause she fears it being as she said, she could go and \r\nmake a report about it and post on swinney how much she \r\nhated it.</p><p>thats just my opinion. I plan to go at some \r\npoint in my life, first I want to go to a rainbow \r\ngathering.</p><p>I did a three month survival package in \r\nthe north eastern boarder of Thailand (sound like fun?). \r\nThree months of no showers, besides a wash cloth in the \r\nappropriate places, no power (besides the vehicles we had), \r\nno women (I was disapointed that the women were not allowed \r\nto go), and no a/c. We did have communications set up, and \r\nI actually got to call home from the field. That time there \r\nwas intense, hot, and full of action. It changed my life... \r\nSometime I might write some stories about it... if ya\\\'ll \r\nare interested in hearing stories from the dark side of the \r\nmilitary and government...</p>--<i>best friendly</i>',1,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(7748,1672,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to petey','<p>Ive been in that exact situation before, and I have no \r\nanswers. After youve been together for awhile, the \r\nquestion becomes, what, if not passion, binds me to \r\nyou? there are a lot of things besides passion that keep  \r\nyour attention on someone. I mean, if you end up \r\nsticking around for years, the \\\"passion\\\" is bound to \r\nmutate, change, die out. If it is not supplemented with \r\nsomething else that is just as essential or better (deep \r\nemotional intimacy, cerebral understanding, spiritual \r\nconnection, insane domestic compatibilty, etc) then \r\nthat;s the end! </p> <p>It\\\'s my general belief that if you \r\ngo about your business and do your own thing, fortunes \r\nof passion are unexpectedly showered onto you. if not a \r\nreignition of your longtime love, then perhaps \r\nsomeone/something new.</p>\r\n<p>p.s. I love \\\"someone/something\\\". anything with \r\n\\\"slash\\\". there is a sleater-kinney song: \\\"now im walking \r\nto your house/cause i really wanna figger you out/it\\\'s \r\nalways something/someone new every day, as long as \r\nim not looking for me.\\\"</p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'216.175.91.205','en'),(7749,1671,'2001-08-27 15:58:35',0,'Brian Bendis to xi','who\\\'s said I hadn\\\'t been? it was opinion.',6,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(7750,1671,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to bmg','my family is from Isaan (northeastern thailand)! come \r\nto california and tell us stories, I will make sticky rice.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.91.205','en'),(7751,1672,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','that is without a doubt my favorite sleater-kinney song.',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(7752,1671,'2001-08-27 16:12:17',0,'ix to bendis','my comment was directed at green.',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(7753,1673,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>wow, this is actually one of the more eloquent and \r\nintelligently written things I\\\'ve seen on here in a while. \r\nwrite more.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7754,1670,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>yes, stomach, tummies. good things. my favorite \r\nspot to stop and play with, twiddle the navel ring, tickle \r\nthe area right under the belly-button. a fav of mine, for \r\nsure</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7755,1664,'2001-08-27 16:27:53',0,'Doktor','old crayons make the world go around? fuck gravitation!',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7756,1671,'2002-03-05 20:17:36',17,'austin to burning man','<P>ok, i want to go:</p>\r\n<PRE>\r\nThere seems to be some confusion about a \r\ncouple things which I would like to clarify:\r\n\r\n1) Hours: Hours for any project funded by \r\nthe Corporation for Corporate Corporation are \r\n8:00 AM - 4:30 PM unless you have worked out\r\nanother arragement with your supervisor. This\r\nmeans generally you are expected to be here at\r\n8:00. If you are a few minutes late, no one is\r\ngoing to give you a hard time. You are not\r\npunching a clock. If you are going to be more \r\nthan 15 mins. late, then please let your \r\nsupervisor know.\r\n\r\nQuestions? Let me know.\r\n\r\n-- supervisor\r\n</pre>\r\n<P>--BURN! BURN!</p>',6,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(7757,1671,'2001-08-27 16:59:12',0,'robonez','<PRE>\r\nrobotec9: why arent you at burning man?????\r\nleonard: i went to burning crotch instead\r\nleonard: it was a gas\r\n</PRE>',4,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(7758,1671,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','has you peeped bobby\\\'s site yet today \r\n(perceptions.diaryland)?\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.77.187','en'),(7759,1671,'2001-08-27 17:03:13',0,'wb','i _do_ like being left behind. welcome to the story of my \r\nfucking life. <BR><BR>\r\n\r\ngiven that i dont have this special weekend to express \r\nmyself, let it all hang out, its pretty tough being non \r\ncreative person with no outlets. its frustrating really. if \r\ni could just save the hundreds of dollars, then i would \r\nhave a captive audience. people would point at me and go: \r\nhey you have hundreds of dollars for weekend warrior \r\nadventures too! we are brothers! they would hug me and tell \r\nme that i was special. they would show me hidden things in \r\ntheir pubis. we would connect. we would call it spiritual. \r\n<BR><BR>\r\ndriving back into The City i would think that i live in the \r\nexact right place and i\\\'m just being myself.',6,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(7760,1672,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','<BR><BR>you just going through a dry spell?  try some time \r\napart.  the thing is, do you love her?  and do you want to \r\nhave to start over with someone else?  (just from an energy \r\nefficiency standpoint)<BR><BR>what do your instincts tell \r\nyou? just cause you don\\\'t fuck doesn\\\'t mean you can\\\'t still \r\nenjoy an incredibly intimate relationship.  maybe you fucked \r\ntoo much. people have varying energy requirements. check out \r\ntantra. or open the relationship up beyond the two of you. \r\nor hang around some kids with her. just do something new. \r\n<BR><BR>alone time is good time, too.  growth time.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.77.187','en'),(7761,1671,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','blech.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(7762,1674,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','it\\\'s important to be earnest. and openness is big, big \r\nmedicine.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.77.187','en'),(7763,1674,'2001-08-27 17:35:17',0,'jon bon jovi','then what is bad medicine again?',0,0,0,0,'216.175.91.205','en'),(7764,1674,'2001-08-27 17:39:53',0,'chapulin','doesn\\\'t huevo mean egg?',2,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(7765,1674,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','sarcasm. or wack ofay muthafuckas thinkin they got \r\nskillz. i forget which:p\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.77.187','en'),(7766,1671,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to wb','toni morrison\\\'s <i>Sula</i> : \\\"and like any artist without \r\na medium, she became dangerous.\\\" cmon wayne, lets \r\nfashion a 6 ft papier-mache Middle Manager Man! you \r\ncan put on a diaper and do your interpretive dance \r\naround it singing \\\"I am BABY NEW YEAR\\\" while my \r\nupstairs neighbors \\\"jam\\\" on the digeridoo! Ill make a \r\nbra that double functions as a match-lighter which \r\ninflames my Nils and Lars nipples and ill shake my \r\nflaming pasties in the face of Manager Mang to set him \r\non fire. oh god it will be a hoot.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.91.205','en'),(7767,1674,'2001-08-27 17:54:30',0,'corny','porny, forlorny, acorny, sigorny, bjorny, horny, californy, \r\nscorny, etc\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(7768,1671,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','machine gun jumblies! how\\\'d i miss those?',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(7769,1672,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','<p>at some point in all relationships, you will have to stop \r\ntreating your lover like a lover, and treat him like a good \r\nfriend. what i mean is, sometimes you have to give them \r\nspace, and give them love, but ease off them a little bit. \r\n</p><p>\r\nif you\'re unhappy, it\'s not the end of the world to take a \r\nlittle time off, or make some changes. it sounds corny! and \r\ncheesy!! but maybe it\'s time to learn something new \r\ntogether, start taking french classes, go to a sunset \r\nconcert, and just be together. don\'t try to force it, don\'t \r\nhave expectations, just hang out like friends. this is of \r\ncourse, after you have made the decision whether you still \r\nwant this person in your life. do you?\r\n</p><p>\r\na little kindness goes a long way. having sex isn\'t the \r\nonly intimacy. perhaps the people in the relationship need to relearn how to fall in love with each other. be kind. be loving. perhaps there is a seed still there. perhaps you\'re better off looking for someone else.\r\n</p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(7770,1669,'2001-08-27 20:36:27',0,'whore','you are BITCHES! all of you! hi!\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n\\\"best friendly\\\"\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(7771,1674,'2001-08-27 20:52:55',0,'jo','oh don\\\'t worry. your love is still like bad medicine.<BR>\r\n(it\\\'s what i need.)',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(7772,1671,'2001-08-27 21:10:47',0,'treetop','</head>\r\n<body>\r\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; I will not be at burning man \r\neither.&nbsp; For $200+\r\nthis year you can stick a candle in your glory hole and \r\nlight it.&nbsp;\r\nBesides, there are other things going on for Labor Day \r\nweekend.&nbsp; In\r\na musical sense you could check out <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://members.aol.com/wgeneral/meetwavy.html\\\">Wavy\r\nGravy\\\'s</a> annual <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.pignic.com\\\">pignic</a> in Laytonville,\r\nCA.&nbsp; The <a href=\\\"http://www.jambase.com/search.asp?\r\nvenueID=4828\\\">line-up</a>\r\nof bands is pretty nice.&nbsp; I highly recommend going if \r\nyou live in\r\nCalifornia.&nbsp; Send me an <a \r\nhref=\\\"mailto:sshkdwnst@aol.com\\\">email</a>\r\nif you would like to get a group together.\r\n</body>\r\n</html>',0,0,0,0,'172.157.106.120','en'),(7773,1671,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','i\\\'d rather go to blow buddies\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(7774,496,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','once a bunch of us broke into a doll factory and i stole some \r\nheads and voiceboxes for my roommate. i\\\'m looking around for \r\nthe pictures to show you but i can\\\'t find them! oh well.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(7775,1671,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','but i\\\'m in sf',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(7776,1671,'2001-08-27 23:42:48',0,'Dork13','</head>\r\n<body>\r\nHahahaha!&nbsp; <a href=\\\"http://blowbuddies.com/\\\">Blow \r\nbuddies</a>!\r\n</body>\r\n</html>',0,0,0,0,'172.163.238.179','en'),(7777,1673,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','God damn, Ix. Everybody leaves town and you become fuckin \r\nWilliam Shakespeare. That was beautiful, man, really, \r\nreally great. Really. We need to hang out. Want to come to \r\nSC? First game\\\'s on Friday. It\\\'s on me.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.106','en'),(7778,1673,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','ps--I understand about not jumping right into a scene like \r\nthat, I would probably be the same way. I mean, all that\\\'s \r\ncool I guess, but it sort of rings a little desperate and \r\nfalse to me. I mean, come on. That\\\'s just people trying to \r\nstop time for a while, to have something \\\"they\\\'ll never \r\nforget\\\", etc.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.106','en'),(7779,1673,'2001-08-28 00:52:12',0,'joni mitchell','<PRE>Bows and flows of angel hair and ice cream castles in \r\nthe air \r\nand feather canyons everywhere, I\\\'ve looked at cloud that \r\nway. \r\nBut now they only block the sun, they rain and snow on \r\neveryone. \r\nSo many things I would have done but clouds got in my way. \r\n\r\nI\\\'ve looked at clouds from both sides now, \r\nfrom up and down, and still somehow \r\nit\\\'s cloud illusions I recall. \r\nI really don\\\'t know clouds at all. \r\n\r\nMoons and Junes and ferris wheels, the dizzy dancing way you \r\nfeel \r\nas every fairy tale comes real; I\\\'ve looked at love that \r\nway. \r\nBut now it\\\'s just another show. You leave \\\'em laughing when \r\nyou go \r\nand if you care, don\\\'t let them know, don\\\'t give yourself \r\naway. \r\n\r\nI\\\'ve looked at love from both sides now, \r\nfrom give and take, and still somehow \r\nit\\\'s love\\\'s illusions I recall. \r\nI really don\\\'t know love at all. \r\n\r\nTears and fears and feeling proud to say \\\"I love you\\\" right \r\nout loud, \r\ndreams and schemes and circus crowds, I\\\'ve looked at life \r\nthat way. \r\nBut now old friends are acting strange, they shake their \r\nheads, they say \r\nI\\\'ve changed. \r\nSomething\\\'s lost but something\\\'s gained in living every day. \r\n\r\nI\\\'ve looked at life from both sides now, \r\nfrom win and lose, and still somehow \r\nit\\\'s life\\\'s illusions I recall. \r\nI really don\\\'t know life at all.</PRE> \r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.29.73','en'),(7780,1673,'2001-08-28 01:20:44',0,'ix to tyler','i\\\'m actually going to be in rock hill sometime in the next month or two. \r\ndoubt i\\\'ll make it to columbia tho. but tailgate hard, raise a bud for me \r\nand knock back some bojangles. go cocks!',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(7781,1673,'2001-08-28 01:21:42',0,'ix to joni','wow! i never knew. what album?',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(7782,1673,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','shoot man, that\\\'s right around the corner. You oughta ride \r\ndown, have a few beers.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.106','en'),(7783,1673,'2001-08-28 03:38:37',0,'JM','i see clouds from both sides now.',1,0,0,0,'24.27.26.62','en'),(7784,1673,'2001-08-28 05:19:32',0,'cyantist','i\\\'ve never gone for many of the same reasons.  (though i\\\'ve \r\nnever tried).  i\\\'m always afraid that i\\\'d see the true \r\ncolors of some people that i\\\'d rather not see.  i\\\'m also \r\nafraid that it would shock me and make me afraid.\r\n\r\nyou should go next year.  i might even go myself.',1,0,0,0,'24.221.170.252','en'),(7785,1676,'2001-08-28 05:55:40',0,'huevita','S.O.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.105.179','en'),(7786,1673,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','i am reminded of <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.bud.com/98/09/tkles/07.wb.rv/\\\">wayne\\\'\r\ns piece</a> on bud.com on RVs.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.91.218','en'),(7787,1674,'2001-08-28 09:31:52',0,'huevita','there was something else i forgot to note.\r\n<p> this handy ascii for the big \\\"D\\\"<br>\r\n8=====D<br>\r\nmakes a lot of sense to me because \\\"8\\\" is infinity \r\nturned on its side, and it stands for the BALLz. cajones. \r\nthe seed that perpetuates life forevermore. and that \r\nperpetuation equals, for whatever quantity of equality, \r\nthe big \\\"D\\\". sideways forever = D.  and then there is the \r\nfable about asian women having sideways vaginas. I \r\nhave not found that to be true yet. </p>',0,0,0,0,'216.175.91.218','en'),(7788,1670,'2001-08-28 10:43:57',0,'Jamazon','i like to blow raspberries',6,0,0,0,'217.32.131.250','en'),(7789,1676,'2001-08-28 11:07:09',0,'kdog','your password has passed beneath my feet hundreds of times, \r\nand i think of you each time.  ',1,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(7790,1676,'2001-08-28 12:11:30',0,'bmg','<p>i stepped on it once, and I thought I might have \r\nbroken your back...</p><p>you know my 2000 \r\npassword, and now that you mention it i think that the \r\ncertain word does have special meaning in my life... but \r\nI think i was in need of a new password and the a U2 \r\nsong happened to be playing, and I heard the word. If \r\nyou ever decide to change passwords make sure that it \r\nis long enough. I made the mistake of changing my 6 \r\nletter password, which has changed austin, to another \r\n6 letter password. The problem is that a lot of sites now \r\nrequire 8 letters, this is a pain in the ass. I cant stand \r\ndisrupting the original password... Thinking back on \r\npasswords, I realize that all of them start with the letter \r\n\\\'d.\\\' I have a weird fascination with the letters \\\'d\\\' and \\\'y\\\' \r\nthis day is brought to you by the letters d and y. thanks.',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(7791,1676,'2001-08-28 14:00:27',0,'puppy','yo, i still use my UT password (and sometimes username). it \r\ntook me a semester to remember mine, too. in fact, it\\\'s so \r\nconfusing, i don\\\'t mind telling it to people, because i \r\nknow they won\\\'t remember it.... (i tell it to people, but i \r\ndon\\\'t write it down...)',1,0,0,0,'192.35.232.99','en'),(7792,1672,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>you guys.  thanks for the advice. very on point. \r\nyes, we both still love each other, we\'re just a little \r\nburned out on the passion side of things, and its almost \r\ngone on too long this way.  add a tendency to be depressed \r\nto the mix, and its no good.  we talked at length yesterday \r\nand decided we were friends before we were lovers, \r\nand friends still- soul-mates, actually- and would always \r\nseek each other in the end... its just working through the \r\nnow and present that sucks. thanks for your tips, we\'ll see \r\nhow it goes. most of the tedious (yet somewhat appropriate) emotionality is because we had out \'breakup discussion\' while coming down after rollin all weekend.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'209.246.107.76','en'),(7793,1677,'2001-08-28 15:47:02',0,'Rent- boy','\\\"Choose life. Choose a job. Choose a starter home. Choose \r\ndental insurance, leisure wear and matching luggage. Choose \r\nyour future. But why would anyone want to do a thing like \r\nthat?\\\"',3,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(7794,1676,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','i can\\\'t remember my UT ACITS password anymore.  i keep a \r\nlong .txt file called SNs.txt on my hard drive and on a zip \r\nor two.  this contains all of my dozens of passwords and \r\nusernames.  without that file, i\\\'d be lost.  fuck.',3,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(7795,1673,'2001-08-28 18:44:29',0,'wb','it doesnt remind me of all of that. brian\\\'s is thoughtful \r\nand well-written.',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(7796,1673,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to wayne','wayne, look in the mirror and repeat after me: \\\"I am a \r\ntalented individual. I have as many gifts to share with \r\nthe world as ix.\\\" and since you got me on bud drunk last \r\nnight I have been alerted to my own past verbal \r\natrocities. so we are all feeling like stupid dickheads \r\ntoday.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.93.221','en'),(7797,1678,'2001-08-28 18:59:56',0,'baby fat','mmmmmmmm, cake!',1,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(7798,1580,'2001-08-28 23:27:40',0,'coyoboy','did this work?',4,0,0,0,'156.153.255.243','en'),(7799,1580,'2001-08-28 23:28:37',0,'hughey and the news','\\\"sometimes in my bed at night, I curse the dark and I pray \r\nfor light and sometimes the light\\\'s no-- consolationnnnn\\\"',6,0,0,0,'156.153.255.243','en'),(7800,1574,'2001-08-28 23:30:53',0,'hughey lewis and the newds','\\\'don\\\'t you know me i\\\'m the boy next door, the one you find \r\nso easy to ignore, is that what I was fighting for\\\'',1,0,0,0,'156.153.255.243','en'),(7801,1530,'2001-08-28 23:34:52',0,'coyotoeboy','i really like the salt rocks that accumulate at the bottom \r\nof a bag of snyder\\\'s of hanover old tyme pretzels-- they \r\nare the best part... maybe i\\\'m not getting enough salt in \r\nmy diet?',5,0,0,0,'156.153.255.243','en'),(7802,1497,'2001-08-28 23:36:19',0,'coytotyboy','\\\'we used to sit around and play \\\'puss in the corner\\\'-- \r\nshe\\\'d hit me in the puss and i\\\'d land in the corner.\\\'',3,0,0,0,'156.153.255.243','en'),(7803,1480,'2001-08-28 23:37:44',0,'huey dewis and the doods','\\\"walking on a thin line, straight off the front line, \r\nlabeled as freaks loose on the streets of the citaay.\\\"',5,0,0,0,'156.153.255.243','en'),(7804,1455,'2001-08-28 23:39:11',0,'coyoteboy','how come they never made salty pop rocks?',4,0,0,0,'156.153.255.243','en'),(7805,1436,'2001-08-28 23:40:34',0,'hooey lewis and the newz','\\\"they taught me how to shoot to kill, a specialist with a \r\ndeadly skill-- one i needed to have to be a survivor\\\"',4,0,0,0,'156.153.255.243','en'),(7806,1343,'2001-08-28 23:45:02',0,'prevertedungulate','yes there is still room for porn, for good porn, important \r\nporn, porn that makes me proud to be an enjoyer of porn, \r\nporn that makes you think, porn that makes a stink, \r\ninspiring porn, porn with edges, porn with guts, porn that \r\nkicks you in the nutz (sic), porn porn porn porn',5,0,0,0,'156.153.255.243','en'),(7807,1269,'2001-08-28 23:45:58',0,'hewey louis','or you can come up to my pad in montana, we can go duck \r\nhunting.',4,0,0,0,'156.153.255.243','en'),(7808,851,'2001-08-28 23:51:31',0,'coyoteboy','yes a good cigarette\r\nit certainly was\r\nmy last ciggie\r\never-- funny fag',5,0,0,0,'156.153.255.243','en'),(7809,582,'2001-08-28 23:54:57',0,'yeah','i really love dogs, but they make me sneeze.',6,0,0,0,'156.153.255.243','en'),(7810,1665,'2001-08-29 00:12:06',0,'coyoteboy','25 mg sertraline taken orally once daily. take with food. \r\ntake in the morning if you have problems with \r\nsleeplessness. try wellbutrin if the side effects get too \r\nbad.',3,0,0,0,'156.153.255.236','en'),(7811,1676,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','your password would be a cool band name',3,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(7812,1676,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','<p>\r\npersonally I think that OTPIE passwords are just like, the\r\ncoolest things.  almost as if you used swinney.org journal\r\nblurbs as a pwd gen.\r\n<P>\r\nWhat is OTPIE?\r\n<p>\r\nOne Time Passwords In Everything\r\n<p>\r\nit\\\'s this thing that sort of attaches to and augments\r\n<tt>login</tt> on a Unix system.  so it affects telnet, ftp,\r\nblah blah blah.  pretty much everything.\r\n<p>\r\nIt works by giving you a list (generated from some random\r\nbits and your super-extra-secret otpie phrase like\r\n\\\"ithinkbillgatesisarabidandaltogthertoocheekymonkey\\\") of\r\nwords.  like 100 of them at once.\r\n<p>\r\nexample:\r\n100:  MANG PRONY CALIFORNY FOO BAR BAZ\r\n99: PEAR DOG CREAM LICK BLOSSOM\r\n98: CAMEL STROKE ELM FENCE BOOB\r\n... (on down to 1)\r\n<p>\r\nand on each login, you type in your username and for the\r\npassword, the next sequence on the list.  even over\r\nplaintext channels.  Because, if a black hat sniffs it, it\r\ndoes them squatola good.\r\n<p>\r\n(And there is like a program where you can over a secure\r\nchannel \\\"check out\\\" your next sequence of wordz.)\r\n<p>\r\n<em>But don\\\'t lose that list or let it fall into the wrong\r\nhands!!!</em>  :-)\r\n<p>\r\nI\\\'d dig up an URL, but google would point you in the right\r\ndirection.',1,0,0,0,'209.163.146.106','en'),(7813,1676,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','wow, i never knew hats had noses. every day something knew. \r\ni must remember to keep my hair clean least i \r\noffend.<BR><BR>is it just <B>BLACK</B> hats? how about black \r\nhats with constellations and crescent moons on them? you \r\nthink they do? jesus, nothing is safe anymore. hats with \r\nnoses. what\\\'s next? computers with ears?\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.5.55','en'),(7814,1676,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','terazzo, rialto, corvair, zona, rosa, (one more - not \r\nyet).\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.5.55','en'),(7815,1676,'2001-08-29 05:10:33',0,'jo','adam: a band called barcelona did a song: \\\"<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.barcelonadc.com/frame.asp?p=sounds\\\">i know \r\nthe password to your shell account</a>\\\" which rocks pretty \r\nhard.',1,0,0,0,'172.158.96.157','en'),(7816,1676,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','oh, what the fuck. you only go round once.<BR><BR>\\\"wir \r\nplayin trust games here theday.\\\" - the mother superior\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.5.55','en'),(7817,1676,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','look at silly me. did all that and forget to type the word \r\nin. must be telling me something. (i was about to tell you \r\nthe password on my hotmail account.) should i? i\\\'ll bet \r\nyou\\\'d like that, you naughty things.<BR><BR>talk amongst \r\nyourselves and get back to me. see what the concensus is. \r\nlet me know if you think that would be a good thing or a bad \r\nthing.  or a vanilla thing.  but vanilla\\\'s a flavor, too, \r\nisn\\\'t it?\r\n',4,0,0,0,'209.208.5.55','en'),(7818,1665,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','looks like we have a kat fan on our hands.',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(7819,1677,'2001-08-29 10:53:43',0,'deb','the worst thing you can do, in choosing, is rule out the \r\nthings you know are wrong.  all that leaves is a shorter \r\nlist of choices.',2,0,0,0,'64.12.103.21','en'),(7820,1678,'2001-08-29 10:57:29',0,'deb','and now you\\\'re turning 25... you know on my 21st birthday, \r\na couple weeks ago, my mom ran out of candles for the cake. \r\ni didn\\\'t think i was THAT old; its not like we had to burn \r\ndown a wax museum to make candles.',2,0,0,0,'64.12.103.21','en'),(7821,1680,'2001-08-29 11:00:48',0,'deb','after high school, i find myself buying more music then \r\nbefore. now i find myself trying to find my own identity. \r\nbefore, i had to worry about just getting through the day. \r\nbut i\\\'m a sucker for good, strong, dramatic music...always.',2,0,0,0,'64.12.103.21','en'),(7822,1681,'2001-08-29 12:23:18',0,'Doktor','Getchoo MACK on!<img \r\nsrc=\\\"http://www.macktrucks.com/summerclearance/images/yellow\r\n_truck.jpg\\\">',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7823,1682,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>oh no. here we go <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?\r\nid=1532.txt\\\">again</a>.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7824,1680,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br>Music. i\\\'m finally confident enough not to feel weird \r\nabout buying alot of different music.  the people at the \r\nrecord store must think i\\\'m schitzo. Music is good, \r\ndefinitely, and can move you like nothing else.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7825,1681,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','<BR>\r\n<I>I like trucks I always will, big or small I like them \r\nstill. I like trucks</I>',0,0,0,0,'203.96.108.200','en'),(7826,1681,'2001-08-29 12:44:01',0,'Cypress Hill','\\\"ohhh shit i\\\'m rollin\\\' in a mack truck thats stolen, guess \r\nwhat i\\\'m haulin\\\'? ammo to bust my load!\\\"',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7827,1681,'2001-08-29 12:44:25',0,'Sisqo','Dumps like a truck?',6,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7828,1674,'2001-08-29 12:45:27',0,'Um','so does HORNY',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7829,1356,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','what does mazol tov mean?',0,0,0,0,'203.96.108.200','en'),(7830,1678,'2003-07-24 15:44:23',165,'joker','happy birthday dj.  i remember your last one...sorta.  at \r\nsome point i was banging on that rickety piano in the \r\nback.  you were doing shots and wearing a funny hat.  \r\nyou\\\'re always wearing a funny hat.',1,0,0,0,'66.25.186.181','en'),(7831,1672,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Quih Moll','<p>Bring a caribou buck to her house. After her family \r\neats, if she leaves the antlers out in the night for you, \r\ngo inside and love her. If her entrance is empty, however, \r\ndo not speak to her again. This is how you do it.</p>\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(7832,1356,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','oh! it means congratulations by the looks of some website i \r\nfound.\r\nsorry! i come from a country with a smallish jewish \r\ncommunity so i don\\\'t get to know things like this.',0,0,0,0,'203.96.108.200','en'),(7833,1681,'2001-08-29 13:01:32',0,'jo','um, i don\\\'t get it? four comments about trucks when austin \r\nwas talking about karate?<BR>\r\naustin, they don\\\'t expect you to be committed to that \r\nspecific dojo, do they? just the art? you can always \r\ncontinue karate somewhere else if you moved.',1,0,0,0,'172.136.56.146','en'),(7834,1680,'2001-08-29 13:04:35',0,'jo','music will always matter.',1,0,0,0,'172.136.56.146','en'),(7835,1675,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','<p>Yes, I too think this is good. Maybe I like it too much. \r\nI like being invisible, I love not feeling obligated to \r\nspeak. I hide in the basements of the libraries and on the \r\nbacks of the buses. This strategy doesn\\\'t land me many new \r\nfriends and my romatic life is a tundra with a frozen \r\ntumbleweed rolling across the nothing. But you can\\\'t have \r\neverything you know.</p>\r\n',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(7836,1680,'2001-08-29 13:16:35',0,'Madonna','Music makes the people come together',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7837,1681,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to Jo','<br><tt>i think it\\\'s some fragmented reference to his \\\'i am \r\ngoing to mack\\\' thing...</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7838,1678,'2001-08-29 13:19:14',0,'when i was 25','it was a <i>very</i> good year',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7839,1681,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Veer Moll','<p>I haven\'t fought in a long time and your post reminded \r\nme of it. In our fighting, the moves are called things like \r\nlunge, parry, riposte, feint, disengage, attack au fer, \r\nbalestra. A balestra is like a jump or leap towards your \r\nopponent. I\'m small, so I would often try to use this to \r\ncover ground, just jump right in and go right into a low \r\nattack. When it worked it felt so good, although getting \r\ncaught in mid-air is <a \r\nhref=\"http://sportsillustrated.cnn.com/features/1997/yearinpictures/perspectives/images/medium/othe04.jpg\">not cool</a>.</P>\r\n<IMG SRC=\"http://sportsillustrated.cnn.com/features/1997/yearinpictures/perspectives/images/medium/othe04.jpg\">\r\n<p>Reading your thing reminded me of it. I should take \r\nlessons again.</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(7840,1681,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','can you handle a little truth this morning? if not, skip \r\nthis comment.<BR><BR><BR><BR><BR>you still here? \r\nok:<BR><BR>*if the economy collapses completely, you will \r\nnot have a job. there will be no jobs. there will be no \r\nfood. there will be no life on earth. economics isn\\\'t just \r\nlimited to money and employment and shopping. its smallest \r\nunit of exchange is subatomic. the economy is a function of \r\nmood. you\\\'re making all this up as you go along, this \r\nreality, so have no fear.<BR><BR>*fucking is not the \r\nbe-all, end-all of human existence. yeah, it\\\'s nice, i know, \r\nand birds do it, bees do it, why can\\\'t i do it? so do it. \r\nbut consider the possibility that one day you may not want \r\nto. you might want to use that energy for other things, \r\nthings that are better than fucking. yes, you heard me \r\nright.<BR><BR>*god tests you, god tries you out. god seduces \r\nyou. one test is how well you commit to things. not just \r\nideas, but people, places, your body, everything. everybody \r\nneeds a home, roots, even if that home is the entire \r\nuniverse. karate might be your power thing. your road into \r\nthe mystery. i would be so excited to be doing that again \r\nfor the first time.<BR><BR>*real men ride long \r\nboards:p<BR><BR><BR><BR><BR>and, by the way, why\\\'d you take \r\nthat article down there grasshopper? i was trying to conduct \r\nme a little experiment.  take care. \r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.9.116','en'),(7841,1682,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','myself, i would have freaked the fuck out then sued them. \r\nbut that\\\'s just me. part of me, anyway.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.9.116','en'),(7842,1682,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','what nerve. sadistic motherfuckers.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.9.116','en'),(7843,1678,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'