ndments as you \r\nlike. And bathe in goat entrails while your at it, too. \r\nBecause let me tell you something. God is <i>such</i> a \r\nbore. I liked some of his earlier stuff -- Sodom and \r\nGomorra was cool -- but let\\\'s face it. Revelations was a \r\ngood try, but eh. Like \\\"oo, four horesmen\\\" \\\"aa, pestilence, \r\nI\\\'m so fucking scared\\\". Come on dude. No one buys that \r\nshit.</p>\r\n<p>Fact is, Satan is chic, he\\\'s covering new ground and \r\nhe\\\'s especially in tune with our generation. My cousin was \r\nin the Infernal Reserves -- it\\\'s a good way to get into \r\nSatan and the minions -- and it seemed like he had some \r\nreally great experiences. He got to see the Land of Nod, \r\nstomped on some newborns, ate some kittens, pushed pregnant \r\nwomen down flights of stairs, lit puppies on fire, etc. I \r\nthink he\\\'s really grown as a person.</p>\r\n<p>Just keep your mind open. Yaweh or Whomever isn\\\'t the be-\r\nall and end-all of your spiritual allegiances. If you\\\'re \r\nhaving trouble with the commandments, don\\\'t sweat it. Just \r\ntake your business elsewhere.</p>\r\n',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(7876,1684,'2001-08-30 01:30:03',0,'sparky','arff arff',0,0,0,0,'172.136.95.200','en'),(7877,1685,'2001-08-30 01:33:50',0,'doobielicious','have you seen Zabalawi?',0,0,0,0,'172.136.95.200','en'),(7878,1685,'2001-08-30 01:36:10',0,'artistiko','Lucifer Morningstar is chic you say? hmmm...following \r\nsomeone who ceased to fear and then got burned. hmmm..  ',1,0,0,0,'24.27.26.62','en'),(7879,1684,'2001-08-30 06:40:57',0,'fernando','fucking bastards, you don\\\'t know my nightmare...just get that fucking beast outa my food gahdammit.  and \r\nyou wonder why i\\\'m so hungry all the time, it\\\'s because that beast, lola keeps chowin\\\' on my food,  fuckin-\r\na.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(7880,1687,'2001-08-30 12:24:42',0,'pandora','\\\"...alive below the waist..\\\"',1,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(7881,1682,'2001-08-30 12:31:38',0,'Jamazon','pocket rocket?',1,0,0,0,'217.32.141.66','en'),(7882,1687,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>(<i>Chemistry Dork Warming, beware!</i>) This curry \r\npiece caught my eye as I\\\'m a major fan of east indian \r\nfoods; consequently, it got me thinking about some things I \r\nrecall from work/school about some positive effects of why \r\nwe might crave \\\"spiciness\\\" (besides teh obvious reasons of \r\ntaste, excitement, etc).  Whether curry or peppers, \r\nspiciness generally comes from a family of substances \r\ncalled capsaicinoids (check spelling on that) (or for all \r\nyou budding chemists out there, something like 8-methyl-n-\r\nvanillyl-6-nonenamide, a very versatilve chemical indeed- \r\nnote n-methyl/amide groups).  Capsaicinoids have been shown \r\nto act on the central nervous system by causing a long-\r\nlasting selective desensitization to soem key aspects of \r\nthe body\\\'s pain response.  It works by \r\nreducing/neutralizing some key biochemical substances \r\ncalled \\\"neurotransmitters\\\" that are found in nerve endings \r\nthat are involved in carrying the pain signal to the \r\nbrain.  These are some of the same chemicals that influence \r\nserotonin/dopamine precursors, and in essence, indirectly \r\ncontrol mood, sensitivity, and depression (as well as a ton \r\nof limbic responses- kinda like prozac, mdma, ephedrine, \r\nand a mess of other things, good and bad).  A purified \r\nsynthetic hodgepodge of capsaicinoids have been marketed as \r\na rheumatoid arthritis treatment under the name \\\"Zostrix\\\", \r\nand research has very recently shown that Zostrix might \r\nalso have some kind of effect on balancing depression, lack \r\nof concentration, and loss of sleep.  If any of those apply \r\nto you, and you crave peppers or curry, eat up.  your body \r\nmight be trying to tell you something.  Ok, thats my \r\nofficial two cents worth.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7883,1685,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>don\\\'t et me started about roaches.  as far as the \r\n10 commandments and spirituality... yikes. i still don\\\'t \r\nknow what to think.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7884,1677,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>I <i>want</i> an item of clothing that typifies \r\n<i>leisure wear</i>.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7885,1688,'2001-08-30 13:48:02',0,'comsumer','vaporware! ',4,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(7886,1688,'2001-08-30 14:10:20',0,'Garbageman','dude, i wish that chiamattt guy would comment on this- \r\nseems like his type of thing.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7887,1681,'2001-08-30 14:45:23',0,'tyler to matt:','How\\\'d you get so smart, buddy-row?',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.102','en'),(7888,1685,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','Down here we call those monster flying roaches \\\"palmetto \r\nbugs\\\", because it sounds so much nicer. I actually have \r\nseen the little ones, and they are a slightly different \r\ncolor. I think they\\\'re two different species, and the \r\npalmetto bug might not be a roach <i>per se</i>. As for the \r\nTen Commandments, I wouldn\\\'t trust someone with a really \r\nstrong opinion either way. It\\\'s good advice though. We have \r\nright-and-wrong built into us is my theory, because I know \r\nwhen what I\\\'m doing is right, and when it\\\'s wrong, \r\naccording to the facts I have at the time. So <b>NO \r\nEXCUSES, PEOPLE</b>, do the right thing.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.205','en'),(7889,1690,'2001-08-30 16:29:23',0,'addendum','<p>what I think about after having coffee or beer is \r\npersonal.</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(7890,1690,'2001-08-30 16:32:08',0,'thus','<p>if resources are low, a little time with myself is \r\nprobable. </p><p>yah, I have a lot of time on my \r\nhands... no pun intended.</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(7891,1690,'2001-08-30 17:01:05',0,'jo','i chose beer last night, coffee the night before.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(7892,1688,'2001-08-30 17:05:33',0,'puppy','well said. I, too, have frequently lamented about this... i \r\nthink cigarettes can be lumped into your list of Coke, \r\nNike, et. al.\r\n\r\n<p>I had an interesting conversation with a friend of mine \r\nregarding a similar topic: How much is choosing certain \r\nproduct \\\"personal choice\\\" and how much of it is manipulated \r\nby ad agencies...\r\n\r\n<p>Without a doubt, most of our purchases are made from \r\npersonal choice; I prefer Coke over Pepsi. No amount of \r\nadverstising will make me change my mind. However, why do I \r\nchoose Coke over tap water? Why do others choose tap water \r\nover Coke? Water, in general (not necessarily tap) is a \r\nrequirement for life, thus requires no advertising. I will \r\ninately seek out water. I had to be taught to like Coke.\r\n\r\n<p>Still, I am aware that I am being manipulated and I am \r\naware that I buy things that are not essential to my \r\nsurvival. I have been educated about the power that \r\nadvertisments can have. Yet, sometimes I forget, succumb to \r\nthe pressure, and buy a DVD player, even though I already \r\nhave a very good VCR...',1,0,0,0,'192.35.232.99','en'),(7893,1690,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','coffee and beer are the two things that make your cum \r\ntaste like total disgusting ass vomit. drink a tall glass of \r\nwater. oh and cigarrettes make your crotch taste like \r\nmashed maggots too. think of the ladies who are \r\nhungry for your juicy flow! dont give them a rotten fruit to \r\nsuck.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.105.202','en'),(7894,1690,'2001-08-30 17:26:22',0,'bmg','i\\\'m gonna be sick, thanks egg.',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(7895,1671,'2001-08-30 17:41:49',0,'coyoboy','<p>yeah,<br> i\\\'m out of lock step with the alterno-burning \r\nman crowd.</p> <p>speaking as the resident american indian, \r\ni find the BM attempt at tribalism to be a bit laughable-- \r\n<br>chaotic, forced- yes <br>tribal- no</P>',5,0,0,0,'156.153.255.243','en'),(7896,1687,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion',