:39:20',75,'tyler','Do you think about what it means to her if her business \r\nsuffers? Do you think she would cry if she employed people \r\nwho weren\\\'t up to the job and lost her business? Would she \r\nbe able to pay the rent? Is she a person?',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.27','en'),(7954,1684,'2002-03-05 20:17:36',17,'austin about fernando','<P>last night / this morning fernando jumps on the bed promtly at \r\n 5 and yowls.  i respond with a pillow.  he \r\ndisappears.  no more out of fernando.  about 6:30 i \r\nappear to be awake so i get up and take a shower.  i \r\nfeed fernando.</P>\r\n<P>all day he sits on the edge of egg\'s desk behind the \r\nscanner cloaked by the clothes rack.  he does not want \r\nto be bothered.  is he always like this?  i in my \r\ninsecurity think he must be angry with me.  he should \r\nbe over on the bed where he belongs during the day, \r\nand the night for that matter.  i didnt say to him, \r\n\"fernando, i am giving you the pillow because you are \r\non the bed.\"  i clearly said, \"fernando i am giving you the \r\npillow because you are yowling at five in the \r\nmorning.</P>\r\n<P>what is with the cold shoulder then?  i dont think i \r\nwas being unfair.  he knows he is waking me up.  why \r\ndoes he not know why i am pillowing him?</P>',4,0,0,0,'216.175.105.67','en'),(7955,1684,'2002-03-05 20:17:36',17,'austin on fernando','<P>just an update on fernando, he is on the bed now.  i \r\nhad to feed him a little extra to make up for what may \r\nhave been some coarse action on my part this \r\nmorning.  he is sleeping off in his FULL TUMMY.</P>',3,0,0,0,'216.175.105.67','en'),(7956,1694,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','most people don\\\'t really care about travelling.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.176','en'),(7957,1697,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','\\\"...and that\\\'s a pretty nice haircut...\\\"',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.176','en'),(7958,1694,'2001-09-02 06:34:17',0,'Jim','</head>\r\n<body>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<br>Do you know the warm progress under the stars?\r\n<br>Do you know we exist?\r\n<br>Have you forgotten the keys to the Kingdom?\r\n<br>Have you been borne yet and are you alive?\r\n<p>Let\\\'s reinvent the gods, all the myths of the ages.\r\n<br>Celebrate symbols from deep elder forests.\r\n<br>[Have you forgotten the lessons of the ancient war?]\r\n<p>We need great golden copulations.\r\n<p>The fathers are cackling in trees of the forest\r\n<br>And our mother is dead in the sea.\r\n<p>Do you know we are being led to\r\n<br>Slaughters by placid admirals,\r\n<br>And that fat slow generals are getting\r\n<br>Obscene on young blood?\r\n<br>Do you know we are ruled by TV?\r\n<p>The moon is a dry blood beast.\r\n<br>Guerrilla bands are rolling numbers\r\n<br>In the next block of green vine,\r\n<br>Amassing for warfare on innocent\r\n<br>Herdsman who are just dying.\r\n<p>O great creator of being,\r\n<br>Grant us one more hour to perform our art\r\n<br>And perfect our lives.\r\n<p>The moths and atheists\r\n<br>Are doubly divine and dying.\r\n<p>We live, we die\r\n<br>And death not ends it.\r\n<p>Journey we more into the Nightmare.\r\n<br>Cling to life, our passion\\\'d flower,\r\n<br>Cling to cunts and cocks of despair.\r\n<br>We got our final vision by clap.\r\n<br>Columbus\\\' groin got\r\n<br>Filled with green death.\r\n<p>(I touched her thigh and death smiled.)\r\n<p>We have assembled inside this\r\n<br>Ancient and insane theatre\r\n<br>To propagate our lust for life\r\n<br>And flee the swarming wisdom of the streets.\r\n<p>The barns are stormed,\r\n<br>The windows kept,\r\n<br>And only one of all the rest\r\n<br>To dance and save us\r\n<br>With the divine mockery of words.\r\n<br>Music inflames temperament.\r\n<p>(When the true King\\\'s murderers\r\n<br>Are allowed to roam free,\r\n<br>A thousand Magicians arise in the land.)\r\n<p>Where are the feasts we were promised?\r\n<br>Where is the wine,\r\n<br>The New Wine.\r\n<br>(Dying on the vine.)\r\n</body>\r\n</html>',0,0,0,0,'172.152.56.91','en'),(7959,1700,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','you nasty little man\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.9.30','en'),(7960,1701,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','<p>\r\ni\'ve felt exactly the same way a few different times in my\r\nlife, and i\'ve treated it as a sign to move far away:\r\ncarolina to new york to california to australia. have to say\r\ni\'ve been generally pleased with the results.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nthe question of the hour, for me at least, is: what do you\r\ndo when you yourself are one of those second-rate\r\nsame-old-played-out-story friends? pretty difficult to move away from yourself...\r\n</p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(7961,1701,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','No, you really can\\\'t move away from yourself, except by, \r\nwell, getting crazy drunk or doing heroin or something. But \r\nyou can change, as long as you aren\\\'t dead. \r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.195','en'),(7962,1701,'2001-09-02 17:25:41',0,'ty','ps-you\\\'re coming to hang out, right? right? make a new \r\nplayed-out bullshit friend?',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.195','en'),(7963,1693,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Pee Moll','If we\\\'re going to make meaningless generalizations about \r\nsomething, can we pick a topic little less <b>done</b> than \r\ngender x or gender y? If you have to be vapid, at least \r\nhave the courtesy to be interesting about it.\r\n',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(7964,953,'2001-09-02 23:44:33',0,'treetop','</head>\r\n<body>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<br>Last night I went to this free party in Berkeley.&nbsp; \r\nIt was on a\r\nconstruction site.&nbsp; Cars lined the main road.&nbsp; We \r\nhad to walk\r\nback into the wilderness for some time.&nbsp; We came upon \r\ntwo busses which\r\nwere perpendicular to each other.&nbsp; The DJ was spinning \r\nin an old yellow\r\nschool bus.&nbsp; Speakers blasted hard-core techno which \r\nsounded like\r\nshock therapy.\r\n<p>Its amazing how no sound carries when there is nothing \r\nto bounce it\r\nback.&nbsp; People wandered around in the groves of shrubs, \r\nsinging, playing,\r\nfrolicking...&nbsp; My friends blue pocket strobe light \r\ncreated streaks\r\nof color as he danced twirling in circles.&nbsp; We sat on \r\nthe edge of\r\nthe bay, downing beers and laughing at the insanity of this \r\nplace.&nbsp;\r\nNowhere in the middle of somewhere.&nbsp; A Japanese guy \r\njust caught a\r\nfish.&nbsp; It looks real nice.&nbsp; I wouldn\\\'t eat \r\nanything that came\r\nout of the bay.\r\n<p>5:30 am...&nbsp; It started to get light outside so we \r\ndecided to get\r\nback to the city.&nbsp; There was a cop car hanging out \r\nwhere everyone\\\'s\r\ncars were parked.&nbsp; \\\"Please move your cars or they will \r\nbe ticketed!\\\"&nbsp;\r\nI don\\\'t think anyone at this point cares about getting a \r\nticket or moving\r\nthier car.&nbsp; We wait until he is a good distance away \r\nfrom my auto\r\nand slip inside.&nbsp; Im glad someone can drive :)\r\n</body>\r\n</html>',0,0,0,0,'64.12.102.151','en'),(7965,1701,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','yeah maybe. i\\\'ve only got three days in the thrill but i might be able to \r\nmake it down. <a href=\\\"mailto:swinney@maz.org\\\">email me</a> so i \r\nhave your address.',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(7966,1701,'2001-09-03 10:53:41',0,'Jamazon','yep...i moved to Ireland',1,0,0,0,'217.32.129.200','en'),(7967,1699,'2001-09-03 10:56:39',0,'Jamazon','You are not special. You are not unique. You are the all \r\nsinging, all dancing crap of the world',1,0,0,0,'217.32.129.200','en'),(7968,1696,'2001-09-03 10:58:03',0,'Jamazon','Get out. Find a new one.',1,0,0,0,'217.32.129.200','en'),(7969,1698,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','I still live here, you can come say hi to us anytime. Sorry \r\nI was not so social tonight, I was too busy trying to stop \r\nmyself from sneezing and snotting all over the place. MMMM \r\nsexy. \r\n\r\nI like you!',1,0,0,0,'64.81.65.205','en'),(7970,1704,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P><a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=\r\n1673.txt\\\">bud did you read ix\\\'s post about burning \r\nman?</a> it is better.  all in fun, burning man.</P>',3,0,0,0,'216.175.104.46','en'),(7971,1704,'2001-09-03 17:26:47',0,'bmg','<p>i drank a mexican martini and smoked a joint  last \r\nnight... it was lots of fun. i haven\'t smoke out in a long \r\ntime, i think that smoking pot is like pressing the reset \r\nbutton on my mac... it takes a long time to reboot and \r\nbecome operational again. </p>',1,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(7972,1696,'2001-09-04 01:26:51',0,'countrywesternboy','<p>there is solace and yes there will be others, but where \r\nyou are now is real. </P><p>pain is real, loneliness is \r\nreal, self doubt is real like cold turkey withdrawal. your \r\nconnection fired the pleasure centers, now you must do \r\nwithout.</p> <p> Time is the only real cure.</p> good luck \r\npilgrim.',2,0,0,0,'12.81.84.21','en'),(7973,1704,'2001-09-04 01:30:11',0,'Doktor','it is five ayy-emm and you are liss-sinn-ing to los angeles.',0,0,0,0,'63.210.212.193','en'),(7974,1693,'2001-09-04 01:35:32',0,'coyoboy','i must remember to try that next time...',6,0,0,0,'12.81.84.21','en'),(7975,1196,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>note to self, check pockets before putting pants in \r\nthe washing machine.</P>\r\n<TT>:-(</TT>',4,0,0,0,'216.175.88.103','en'),(7976,1704,'2001-09-04 05:05:06',0,'jo','<a href=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?\r\nid=785\\\">great minds</a>, etc.',1,0,0,0,'172.142.233.170','en'),(7977,1673,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i enjoyed reading this. burning man definitely amplifies \r\nboth the best and the worst in everyone.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(7978,1704,'2001-09-04 11:20:50',0,'Jamazon','If I was drunk i would be happy.',1,0,0,0,'217.32.123.221','en'),(7979,1687,'2001-09-04 11:23:21',0,'Jamazon','Indian Ass Fire....That would be a kickass name for a band \r\ndon\\\'t you think?',1,0,0,0,'217.32.123.221','en'),(7980,1707,'2001-09-04 11:26:39',0,'Doktor','<BR>\r\nhelp me help you help<BR>\r\nspin me round and round and round<BR>\r\ni move fore and aft<BR>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7981,1687,'2001-09-04 11:27:45',0,'Doktor','\\\"some like it hot and some sweat when the heat is ON\\\"',6,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7982,1709,'2001-09-04 11:34:51',0,'Jamazon','<p>\r\nI sometimes think it\\\'d be cool to get your brain formatted, \r\nzeroed, wiped. All your preconceptions erased\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nTo a baby, everything is new. Everthing is intersting. \r\nNothing is mundane. Nothing is familiar. Babies don\\\'t get \r\nbored. Babies don\\\'t get depressed. They experience the \r\nworld around them for what it is.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nIf only we could do the same.\r\n</p>',1,0,0,0,'217.32.123.221','en'),(7983,1709,'2001-09-04 12:37:55',0,'sawks','<br>\r\njamazon, you need to try eating some DRUGS<br>\r\n*constructive*',3,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(7984,1694,'2001-09-04 12:46:43',0,'kini','\\\"travelling is a brutality. it forces you to trust \r\nstrangers and to lose sight of all that familiar comfort of \r\nhome and friends. you are constantly off balance. nothing \r\nis yours except the essential things - air, sleep, dreams, \r\nthe sea, the sky - all things tending towards the eternal \r\nor what we imagine of it.\\\"\r\n<br>(pavese)\r\n<p>hi, i like being off balance. ',1,0,0,0,'61.8.19.87','en'),(7985,1709,'2001-09-04 12:56:07',0,'doktor','i was gonna say.. thats why the good lord invented drugs, \r\nmy boy! manna fro mheaven set to reformat our cognitive \r\nstores.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7986,1710,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>I watched the most beautiful full moon on the \r\nhorizon this weekend while camping in PA. I walked around \r\nin crisp, purpleish moon shadows all night. Something as \r\nbeautiful as a sunset/rise/moon/etc can really transcend \r\nthe physical \\\'place\\\' you are and make anywhere beautiful \r\nand memorable.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7987,1710,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','also, i\\\'ve been flushing my toilet repeatedly, just to \r\nwatch it flush.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(7988,1709,'2001-09-04 13:25:19',0,'Jamazon','<p>drugs cost money...</p>',3,0,0,0,'217.32.123.221','en'),(7989,1707,'2001-09-04 13:27:30',0,'Jamazon','<br>You spin me right round baby right round<br>\r\nLike a record baby<br>\r\nRight round...',1,0,0,0,'217.32.123.221','en'),(7990,1710,'2001-09-04 13:29:04',0,'Jamazon','<br>How come you\\\'ve always got something so intersting to \r\nsay Peter? :)',1,0,0,0,'217.32.123.221','en'),(7991,1707,'2001-09-04 14:03:23',0,'Kylie','I\\\'m spinning around<BR>\r\nMove out of my way<BR>\r\n<I>and look at my ass! think this will help me sell records?\r\n</I>',1,0,0,0,'203.97.2.242','en'),(7992,1710,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>s5: one summer, i was living on the galapagos.  one afternoon, we drove our boat (as close as we could tell on the gps) to the equator and flushed the toilet- and the legend is rather true- the water flushed straight down with a giant suck.  a few minutes north our south, and you get the typical vortex. i must have busied myself with this phenomenon for several hours, and got really angry when i had exhausted our boat\'s 75 gallon fresh water flush tank.  interestingly, your shadow looks like a black pool under your feet on the equator. its uncanny. i have a picture of me standing on the line in equator park at high noon and i have no visible shadow at all, which was quite surreal. there was no moon there that summer, and the nights were dark except for the phytoplankton glowing in the sea; they looked like stars reflecting in the ocean.<br><br>\r\njamazon: drugs</tt> ',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7993,1709,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>not if you know the right people</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7994,1704,'2001-09-04 14:09:51',0,'And the Radio Man','says it is a beautiful night out there, and the radio man says, \"rock and roll lives\".',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7995,1707,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>regard my port and <br>\r\nstarbord turning round and up<br>\r\nand up, gyroscope.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7996,1701,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to ix','<br><tt>thats when you reinvent yourself</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7997,1700,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>ix, i like your writes. they have content>average \r\non here. write more, please.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7998,1699,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to green','<br><tt>maybe you\\\'re meant to do more than make sandwiches?\r\n</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(7999,1710,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','17 <i>thousand?</i> Oh my god. I had no idea it was that \r\nhuge. I think the closest I came to anything like that was \r\nthe Phish new year\\\'s eve 2000 show in the Everglades. There \r\nwere like 70,000 people there, and let me tell you--I was \r\nregretting it. Too many people. It felt severely diluted. \r\nMy personal theory is that there is only so much \\\"good \r\ntime\\\" to go around at an event like that, and your share \r\ngets smaller and smaller the more people show up.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.221','en'),(8000,1710,'2001-09-04 15:07:32',0,'Doktor','what about the great times that only an awkwardly small \r\ngroup, like 2 people, show up for? i think theres a happy \r\nmedium.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8001,1711,'2001-09-04 15:21:52',0,'Doktor','at least <i>someone</i> got lucky this weekend. that is the \r\npoint here, right, the conquest? lucky you.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8002,80,'2001-09-04 15:33:25',0,'Garbageman','i love this piece, mang.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8003,1699,'2001-09-04 15:59:33',0,'texass','fruits, nuts, and flakes live in california. texas only has \r\nsteers and queers. The dating pool is much smaller in \r\ntexas. but i know from having lived near there, that \r\nRiverside is depressing, because it has none of the \r\nabove. you should move, and renunciate.',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8004,1699,'2001-09-04 16:45:08',0,'jo','? what?',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(8005,1711,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','get a dildo.',6,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(8006,1700,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','my posts are uncommon cos i rarely think of something\r\ninteresting enough to share.',0,0,0,0,'209.228.10.196','en'),(8007,1700,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','but thanks :)',0,0,0,0,'209.228.10.196','en'),(8008,1711,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','this is depressing. maybe he thought you liked him. why\\\'d \r\nyou sleep with him if you didn\\\'t? i mean this is just dumb. \r\ndoes that make you <i>cool</i> or something?',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.86','en'),(8009,1711,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','casual sex in your own bed is tricky. i recommend \r\nexploits at his place. home should stay private and \r\nsafe.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(8010,1705,'2001-09-04 18:23:37',0,'treetop','will you marry me?',0,0,0,0,'172.131.95.80','en'),(8011,1709,'2001-09-04 18:35:28',0,'pusherman','Im your momma, Im your daddy, im that whisper in the \r\nalley...',0,0,0,0,'172.131.95.80','en'),(8012,1710,'2001-09-04 18:44:29',0,'Treetop to ty','I was at that show.  I heard it was more like 100 \r\nthousand.  They only sold 70 thousand tickets.  I ran into \r\nso many pe0ple who had snuck in.  That festival was a lot \r\nof fun.  It was great that nothing much went wrong, the \r\ncops were chill, and they kept the porto-lets cleaned.  I \r\ndon\\\'t care if the world explodes!',0,0,0,0,'172.131.95.80','en'),(8013,1710,'2001-09-04 18:44:54',0,'ps:::::','cheese cake',0,0,0,0,'172.131.95.80','en'),(8014,1711,'2001-09-04 18:47:59',0,'sounds like`','a power trip to me',0,0,0,0,'172.131.95.80','en'),(8015,1711,'2001-09-04 18:48:42',0,'chew em up','& spit em out',0,0,0,0,'172.131.95.80','en'),(8016,1710,'2001-09-04 19:05:11',0,'ghost','<p>people fed me wherever i went. i held hands with whoever \r\nwas close. took showers with total strangers. slept like a \r\nbaby. fed people fruit by hand. wandered around alone under \r\nthe moon. was bathed in ice and kisses. laughed until i \r\ncried. cried until i laughed. words were whispered in my \r\near. danced in the middle of the street. danced \r\neverywhere.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>it all felt totally natural. the perfect thing. safe. \r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>and everyone was beautiful</p>\r\n\r\n<p><i>everyone was beautiful</i></p>\r\n',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.188','en'),(8017,1711,'2001-09-04 19:40:41',0,'Dr.Helmer','true, this is not flattering at all.  one can assume he \r\nwanted this kind of treatment[ ? ] ',5,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(8018,1711,'2001-09-04 20:16:38',0,'a dirty boy','i prefer to do my meaningless fucking in places like club \r\nbathrooms. or other people\\\'s beds. a lot easier to sneak off. \r\nand no one has to feel sad that the person they just fucked \r\nwon\\\'t touch them after.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(8019,1710,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','<p>what not to do with your rental van after being in the desert for a week and on an empty stomach: GO FOOD SHOPPING AT \r\nRAINBOW. record scores were reached. but now i am invincible. *noshes vegan cheesecake*</p>',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(8020,1710,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p>caught in a duststorm at night, far from camp but still \r\nhearing the sounds. all i could see was dust, the moon, and \r\nmy dear friends who were with me. safe. safe. safe. and \r\nhappy. \r\n</p><p>\r\nover and over i hear people say that they won\\\'t go, they \r\ncan\\\'t go, it\\\'s sold out, it\\\'s too much, it\\\'s overrated. \r\nshow me one other place on earth that is anything like \r\nburning man and maybe i\\\'ll start to agree.\r\n</p>',4,0,0,0,'216.27.183.161','en'),(8021,1711,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mashed Moll','It all sounds so wonderful.',0,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(8022,1710,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','<p>Well, you can always do it yourself, at any time, under \r\nany number of different circumstances, free of charge, free \r\nof commentary, free of anything. Assuming, that is, you \r\ndon\\\'t need other people to make you happy, or large crowds \r\nto have an amazing experience, which I suppose is an \r\nassumption that might not fly with some of the people \r\nhere, \\\'everyone is beautiful\\\', \\\'we are the \r\nworld\\\', \\\'kumbaya\\\', etc., but to each his own.</p>\r\n',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(8023,1710,'2001-09-04 21:25:34',0,'treetop','I\\\'ve found several places like this, but sadly they always \r\nseem to come to an end.  \r\n  \\\"Off to the side I fall but I hear a sweet call.  My \r\ngypsy eyes is comin\\\' and I\\\'ve been saved.\\\"',0,0,0,0,'172.131.95.80','en'),(8024,1694,'2001-09-04 21:53:17',0,'treetop','</head>\r\n<body>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<br>Being a libra, I face balance.&nbsp; Not only do you \r\nhave to trust\r\nstrangers when you travel, they also have to trust \r\nyou.&nbsp; Its what\r\nbinds you together as travelers.&nbsp; I have backpacked \r\nall over.&nbsp;\r\nI have found that fellow travelers like to look out for \r\neach other.&nbsp;\r\nAnd yes, you do <i>give up</i> a lot of conveniences and it \r\n<i>will</i>\r\nupset your daily routine.&nbsp; But you gain much more, \r\nbroaden you experiences,\r\nand learn new things about people and life.\r\n<p>I like to balance things...\r\n<br>my moon is aires\r\n<p>hi :)\r\n</body>\r\n</html>',0,0,0,0,'172.131.95.80','en'),(8025,1694,'2001-09-04 23:14:10',0,'editor','  thats aries mr libra',0,0,0,0,'172.131.95.80','en'),(8026,1706,'2001-09-04 23:26:57',0,'dingoatemybaby','I thought you were talking about that restaurant at 16th \r\nand mission!',4,0,0,0,'156.153.255.134','en'),(8027,1699,'2001-09-04 23:32:36',0,'texass','hi jo, its me.',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8028,1711,'2001-09-05 01:11:39',0,'Joanna','It\\\'s fiction, it\\\'s not finished yet. ',1,0,0,0,'203.97.2.242','en'),(8029,1711,'2001-09-05 01:54:37',0,'I hunt elv