ear really isn\\\'t, and so on and so forth.  ',1,0,0,0,'203.97.2.242','en'),(8118,1721,'2001-09-06 14:37:32',0,'Doktor','<i>taps fingers.  frowns.</i> ok.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8119,588,'2001-09-06 14:42:36',0,'jo','it\\\'s a pretty cute fucking nose.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(8120,588,'2001-09-06 14:49:39',0,'Doktor','<i>I\\\'d</i> do her!',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8121,1720,'2004-07-27 05:00:32',578,'Netfong','if your mind says \"OBEY\" and you do not, then what are you \r\nobeying besides just another part of your mind? this \r\ndoesn\'t make any sense. you always obey your mind. you \r\ncannot act in any way that isn\'t obeying your own mind, \r\notherwise, you wouldnt be able to act at all, and even there is acting in not acting!<br><br>there is obeying in not obeying.<br><br>by choosing to not obey you are indeed obeying something, the however fleeting thought that says \"hey man, dont obey that!\"<br><br>\r\nthere is minding in not minding.<br><br>you are subject to everything on an infinity of minute levels.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8122,1721,'2004-07-27 05:00:32',578,'Netfong','intereseting story- its a good story, indeed, fun to read. \r\nhowever, it does smack a bit of \\\"i\\\'m having vicarious \r\nadventures throuth my characters by creating extremely \r\ncontrived situations that i\\\'d never do/could do in real \r\nlife\\\". just my worthless two cents worth! \\\"best friendly\\\".',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8123,1717,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>if i had to say goodbye to someone i loved, \r\nunsurely, i\\\'d wish it to be during an eclipse, on an \r\nafternoon with rare scenery that i wouldn\\\'t be reminded of \r\neach new day, in odd lighting that is both memorable and \r\nnot often relived.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8124,1720,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Nostalgia Moll','<p>Now now. Let\\\'s not throw around poor \\\'infinity\\\' like \r\nsome mental chewtoy.</p>',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(8125,1720,'2001-09-06 15:49:39',0,'Jamazon','On a long enough timeline, anything is plausible.',1,0,0,0,'217.32.159.215','en'),(8126,1717,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','kat, you really need to cheer up\r\n',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(8127,1721,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','rhetorical question alert: can\\\'t somebody tell a story\r\nwithout some knucklehead deciding it\\\'s autobiographical?\r\n<p>\r\ni\\\'m enjoying this story cos i am curious about the\r\nmotivations for behavior like this.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(8128,1721,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','ps: nice tao of steve bit there at the end. what will happen\r\nnext?',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(8129,1716,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','a while back, i was driving my car down 14th street. i looked \r\nup and saw a street cleaning sign that said NO PARKING \r\nmondays from 12-2PM. i checked the clock on my dash--1:30. oh \r\nshit! i thought, where did i park? i wonder if i got a \r\nticket!? i bet i did! fuck! then i looked down at my hands on \r\nthe steering wheels and remembered that i was, in fact, \r\ndriving my car.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(8130,1715,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','leave the birds alone',0,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(8131,1717,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','after spending 8 hours in a car with a sleep deprived kat \r\nlast week, i can say she\\\'s a pretty cheerful person! ix, \r\nyou\\\'re mean. you know things people write online aren\\\'t a a \r\n1:1 map to to how they always feel. ',0,0,0,0,'216.27.183.161','en'),(8132,1716,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','<p>i often try to <b>ctrl+z</b> things that i do in real \r\nlife.</p>',0,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(8133,205,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','*grinds teeth* *drools*\r\n<br><br>\r\ni just want you to know.. i know we\\\'ve never met before \r\nbut... i just feel your energy so strongly right now.. you \r\nare so special',0,0,0,0,'216.27.183.161','en'),(8134,1720,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','<p>thanks for titling this article \\\"O B E Y.\\\"  it made me \r\nremember that i had a shepard fairey OBEY(ANDRE) sticker in \r\nmy back pocket :) it\\\'s warm.</p>  ',0,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(8135,1721,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','living vicariously through fiction/art/music == #1',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(8136,588,'2001-09-06 18:12:14',0,'today i','wrote a song about elly, this is how it goes:\r\n<p><i>oh elly<BR>\r\nyou came and you brought me some tofu<BR>\r\nand i pet your head<BR>\r\noh elly<BR>\r\nyou make requests with wide-open eyes<BR>\r\nand sentences full of question marks<BR>\r\nand i think that you\\\'re swell...</i></p>\r\n<p>this goes on for a while longer, is sung to the tune \r\nof \\\"mandy,\\\" by barry manilow, and never rhymes or fits any \r\nbeat or pattern.</p>',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(8137,588,'2001-09-06 18:22:14',0,'oh and another','song about elly, this time to the tune of apples in \r\nstereo\\\'s \\\"stream running over\\\":\r\n<p><i>there\\\'s an elly in the bed, under blankets<BR>\r\nshe\\\'s never waking up, not ever</i></p>',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(8138,1721,'2001-09-06 18:39:31',0,'Dr.Helmer','if everything posted here was autobio then a lot of you \r\nneed to be committed immediately',6,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(8139,1721,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','<BR><BR>you said a mouthful there, doc.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.5.196','en'),(8140,1717,'2001-09-06 18:52:46',0,'coyo','it\\\'s really easy to say something negative about what \r\nsomeone else has done-- a culture of critics. i love kat!',6,0,0,0,'156.153.254.42','en'),(8141,588,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i only know one person who constantly rewrites the lyrics to \r\n\\\"mandy\\\"',0,0,0,0,'216.27.183.161','en'),(8142,1716,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','Give your brain the three-finger salute.',2,0,0,0,'64.229.64.167','en'),(8143,1721,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','<p>drhelmer/matt: what, having a one night stand?! plu-leez.\r\n</p><p>it really strikes me as hilarious the small minded\r\nsactimonious head waggling of some of the comments here.\r\nwhat exactly are you all offended at? a girl goes out to a\r\nbar and has a one nighter. fuck, it\'s not earth shattering \r\nby modern standards. \r\n</p><p> and what is this pseudo penance she has to\r\ndo for it? like some guy is going to actually confront\r\nsomeone who is only interested in a one nighter. being used\r\nfor an all nighter (consenting, under the influence) is NO\r\nEXCUSE at all to physically threaten the girl and   verbally harass her. if someone is standing in front of\r\nme (unconsenting,\r\nand totally out of line), penning me in, pardon ME, you better believe i would take that as\r\nan act of aggression and react accordingly. \r\n</p><p>\r\ni want this girl to tell her story. her fiction should not\r\nbe censored by some boys bleating foul play because she\r\nhappens to be having fun. and no, i wouldn\'t change my mind\r\nif the circumstances and sexes were reversed. one nighters\r\nhave their own code of ethics, and the story didn\'t say\r\nwhether she had lied about her intentions or not. and if (as\r\na lot of these things work) nothing was said, passions were\r\nexchanged without real assurances of a future relationship--\r\nyeah, then it\'s just a fuck, and you can\'t go on about how\r\nyou were expecting more etc etc for fucks sake. in these modern times, as much as we want it to guarantee something, fucking usually doesn\'t amount to anything approaching a promise.\r\n</p><p>\r\n\r\none night stands. you\'re allowed to have them. don\'t assume\r\nyou know all about the intentions involved without explicit\r\ndetails. \r\n</p><p>\r\nand if you\'re going to write about this sort of thing, give\r\nyour audience a clue. </p>',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(8144,1711,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','i liked it. it sounds honest and has a good cadence. don\\\'t\r\nbow down to pressure from your readers.',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(8145,1715,'2001-09-06 20:09:38',0,'leonard','get some sun, dave. geez.',6,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(8146,1717,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','ok',0,0,0,0,'209.228.10.196','en'),(8147,205,'2001-09-06 21:11:24',0,'treetop','</head>\r\n<body>\r\n::Smiles with kindness:)\r\n<br>\\\"Every quantum of energy is interchangeable with every \r\nother one, and\r\nthere is continuous change: continuous transformation of \r\nenergy from one\r\nform to another.&nbsp; Thus everything in the universe is \r\ninterrelated.\\\"\r\n~ Ram Dass\r\n<center><img \r\nSRC=\\\"http://www.fractalus.com/cheshirecat/g10.jpg\\\" BORDER=0 \r\nheight=184 width=238></center>\r\n\r\n</body>\r\n</html>',0,0,0,0,'172.170.117.178','en'),(8148,1721,'2001-09-06 21:11:38',0,'reverend','TESTIFY! CAN I GET A WITNESS!\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(8149,1721,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','I\\\'m talkin\\\' about sin-ah! I\\\'m talkin about <b>fornication-\r\nah!</b> ',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.27','en'),(8150,1721,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','i think it\\\'s a really good piece.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nundecided on whether it\\\'s fiction or not.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nalso, weeb kicks ass.',2,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(8151,1721,'2001-09-06 21:54:32',0,'editor','it has promise. go back, fix up some awkward spots and we\\\'ll \r\ntalk.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(8152,1721,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Pee Moll','<p>weeb: Maybe I\\\'m missing something here, but I don\\\'t \r\nreally see anyone lighting torches and launching a crusade \r\nagainst the practice of sleeping around. No one seems \r\nparticularly offended by the idea, much less suggesting \r\ncensorship, so uh, out of curiosity, what are <i>you</i> \r\nreacting against?</p>\r\n',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(8153,1605,'2001-09-06 22:05:54',0,'A. Einstein','\\\"A new type of thinking is essential if mankind is to \r\nsurvive and move towards higher levels.\\\"',0,0,0,0,'172.170.117.178','en'),(8154,1721,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','weeb is reacting to the comments posted to the bottom \r\nof part 1, which is linked above.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(8155,1721,'2001-09-06 22:16:17',0,'hype','*snap snap',0,0,0,0,'172.170.117.178','en'),(8156,1718,'2001-09-06 22:37:11',0,'treetop','</head>\r\n<body>\r\nwords without fury\r\n<br>bless to communicate love\r\n<br>of crystal wisdom\r\n</body>\r\n</html>',0,0,0,0,'172.170.117.178','en'),(8157,1721,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','omigod, weeb said something to me. i\\\'m so happy i could \r\nshit.<BR><BR>i wasn\\\'t talking about this article. i didn\\\'t \r\nreally even read it. just kind of skimmed through it. i was \r\njoking, affirming what the dr. said about us all being \r\ncertifiable if what we write on here is autobio. \r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.9.172','en'),(8158,1721,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','If you say so.',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(8159,998,'2001-09-06 23:59:31',0,'chukimo','carry weapons? sure, if it makes you feel safe -- but your \r\nattitude, the way you carry yourself, and what you are \r\ndoing will normally determine wether or not a potential \r\nattacker becomes a real one. I grew up in the mid-cities \r\narea of LA and have travelled all over the \\\"bad\\\" areas of \r\nSouth Central LA, East LA, Oakland, SF, Cleveland, New \r\nYork, Bronx--at night, young and unafraid. Im a white male \r\nof light-medium build (5\\\'8\\\" / 165lb), and I look alot like \r\nhowdy doody. I have had guns/ knives pulled on me, \r\nthreatened verbally, and even got in a couple fights, \r\nalthough Im not a very good fighter, speed and quick wit \r\nwill get you very far. Don\\\'t be afraid but be prepared if \r\nyou are-- and if you do carry a weapon, remember that it \r\ncan be taken away and used against you much easier than you \r\nthink ... about half of the homeless people you see are \r\nmentally deseased, most of the others have emotional / \r\npsychological difficulties for as many different reasons \r\nyou can imagine, some of these reasons are self-inflicted \r\n(like drugs and alcohol abuse) your friend is obviously one \r\nif the first half andshould be receiving continual hospital \r\ntreatment, the others who could probably hold down jobs if \r\nthey wanted to, are sucking away a lot of the support that \r\nis available for the homeless\r\n\r\nN.B. who the hell are all you people? you have some cool \r\nstories to read hpoe you dont mind my response / inquiry',3,0,0,0,'64.63.65.33','en'),(8160,1721,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon to matt','hi, is there any reason to get snide there, snidely?\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(8161,1718,'2001-09-07 00:07:05',0,'treetop','</head>\r\n<body>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<center>\r\n<br>A cheerful sight\r\n<br>did I see upon passing\r\n<br>a brother in need\r\n<br>of my of minds laughing\r\n<p>A happy hitchhiker\r\n<br>blooms flowers of tone\r\n<br>in my day so twisted\r\n<br>I had set out alone\r\n<p>Kindred souls are we\r\n<br>of the didgeridoo\r\n<br>we play crystal music\r\n<br>for the lot of you\r\n<p>We vibrate our energy\r\n<br>inside and outwards\r\n<br>to heal minds and souls\r\n<br>of their backwards\r\n<p>A winding road\r\n<br>we did proceed to follow\r\n<br>until darkness was upon\r\n<br>our journey\\\'s hallow\r\n<p>Or destination it seems\r\n<br>brought us too much gaze\r\n<br>as little elf said \\\"park over there\\\"\r\n<br>in her oh\\\' so stony haze\r\n<p>This story is not over\r\n<br>but I must say see ya\\\'s\r\n<br>I have to taste beer\r\n<br>their paying me for my ideas</center>\r\n\r\n</body>\r\n</html>',0,0,0,0,'172.170.117.178','en'),(8162,1717,'2001-09-07 00:20:24',0,'kat','ix is okay...he knows...i\\\'m just a melancholy girl at \r\nheart. but i still know how to smile. and feel it.',4,0,0,0,'32.102.109.53','en'),(8163,1499,'2001-09-07 00:42:58',0,'to matt','wow that was beautiful, nice poem',0,0,0,0,'64.63.65.33','en'),(8164,1499,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','yeah, nice matt',1,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(8165,1635,'2001-09-07 02:27:15',0,'you','are bitch-food.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8166,1499,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','thank you very much.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.10.100','en'),(8167,1718,'2001-09-07 03:20:30',0,'ty','mmm\\\'kay.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.17','en'),(8168,1722,'2001-09-07 06:29:08',0,'ghost','i was afraid to call you. maybe it\\\'s too late. maybe you \r\nwont like my voice. maybe you\\\'ll think im silly. i sent you \r\nan email instead.',4,0,0,0,'32.102.109.227','en'),(8169,1722,'2001-09-07 06:50:51',0,'bmg','<p>I am imagining it... and I will save it, and read it over \r\nand over again.</p><p> silly? who am i to think anyone \r\nsilly? </p><i>and its never too late to call.</i>',1,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8170,1718,'2001-09-07 07:48:58',0,'southpark','Smoking mari\\\'juana is bad mmmm\\\'kay...',0,0,0,0,'172.170.117.178','en'),(8171,205,'2001-09-07 08:06:10',0,'tree2zu','</head>\r\n<body>\r\n\r\n<center>Slide to the side\r\n<br>translucent tranquility.\r\n<br>zuzu was her guru\r\n<br>on the plane\r\n<br>of her transparent reality.\r\n<p>on the other side\r\n<br>unreality is her <b>bliss.</b>\r\n<br>it takes all you can\r\n<br>then releases it to <b>the</b> everything.</center>\r\n\r\n</body>\r\n</html>',0,0,0,0,'172.170.117.178','en'),(8172,205,'2001-09-07 08:11:51',0,'everything','everything',0,0,0,0,'172.170.117.178','en'),(8173,1722,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>lately, when i get to feeling the gloom-n-doom \r\nfeelings, i get my ass up, and go for a run in central park-\r\n you\\\'re right, running exorcises (exercises?) lots of \r\nstuff. and hey, it gets you in shape too. nice combo- kinda \r\nlike mdma, ha.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8174,1723,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>what do you guys know, besides that each other \r\nknows what the other knows?</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8175,1561,'2001-09-07 12:27:18',0,'Garbageman','Dude, this is the <i><b>WEIRDEST</i></b> thing I\\\'ve ever