6','en'),(8213,1722,'2001-09-07 23:25:56',0,'bmg','i run twice a day evey other day, usually - less it rains. \r\nbetween 6-8 is best for me, both am and pm. In the am, \r\ni get a better work out than the pm, but in the pm i can \r\nfeel my breathing improve. zoloft, hmmm. never tried it. I \r\nrun at the pace of a bear, slow, methodical, kapha-type. \r\ni try not to eat after sun down. i try to wake before sun \r\ncomes up... sometimes a bit of depression is exactly \r\nwhat I need, in this particular case it helped me. without \r\nbeing depressed every now and then, I wouldn\\\'t know \r\nwhat happy is like. ',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8214,1725,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>it is a funny thing about retirement.  i wouldnt mind \r\nworking a little in my older age, programming if that is \r\nstill what i do.  it doesnt seem like such a big deal until \r\nyou meet someone whose hands dont work at fifty five \r\nbecause they have arthritis.  and then you, or i, think i \r\nam a programmer.  well, i will probably be sick of \r\nprogramming by then.  i\\\'ll work at disney world in orlando \r\nand commute from my retirement home.  but then you, or i, \r\nmeet someone whose feet have been removed because of \r\ndiabetes mellitus.</P>\r\n<P>oh what is this job that i have and find so expendable?  \r\nit puts 12% of my yearly paycheck in a 401k after the first \r\nyear, i can add more if i want.  i dont put anything in the \r\n401k though because i dont know how i could work there more \r\nthan a year.</P>',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(8215,1728,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','celery is no friend of mine. but \r\nmaybe weeb could sway me. hmm ...\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.156.225.151','en'),(8216,1723,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','rhinoceros - smashing pumpkins\r\n<BR>\r\n<I>\\\"she knows, she knows, she knows.... how\\\'s it\\\"</I>',0,0,0,0,'210.55.167.105','en'),(8217,1728,'2001-09-08 01:09:01',0,'ty','I love vanilla. <a \r\nhref=\"http://www.shanks.com/v