ry altogether.  The \r\nsimple refreshing crunch is the point!  It tastes like \r\nwater with a dash of the essense of spring added for colour \r\nand, yes egg, subtle bitterness, like munching fresh mown \r\ngrass.<br>\r\nbut crunchy!<br>\r\nspread with cheese whiz (or vegan alternative) for easy \r\nsnax for kids and hungry, unemployed IT folx alike!  A \r\ncrowd-pleaser!<br>\r\nThrow the leaves in a salad.  They\\\'re cheap and add flavor \r\nto anything, like soup and curries.<br>\r\nIf you\\\'re munchy and don\\\'t really wanna eat, celery is the \r\nsecret.  You can chow on it until your teeth fall out and \r\nnever get full, and because it takes more energy to chew \r\nand digest it than it provides, it\\\'s better for you than \r\naerobics. <br>\r\nScrew rolfing, I\\\'ll take celery anyday.<br>\r\n(and it comes with it\\\'s own dental floss!)',1,0,0,0,'64.10.136.13','en'),(8230,1726,'2001-09-08 23:51:45',0,'Gemma','Most enjoyable.',0,0,0,0,'210.55.36.4','en'),(8231,1710,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','it was called fucking amal in .au, too.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nix and i went to see it.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nwho did the lunch/shoes thing for me?  kyla?',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(8232,1710,'2001-09-09 02:07:39',0,'ix to egg','i seem to have forgotten that scene. please refresh my\r\nmemory.',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(8233,1725,'2001-09-09 07:41:18',0,'bmg','if you can get a job that is. or you can roll it over to a \r\nbus, and take all your friends on a journey round the \r\nAmerica\\\'s! ',1,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8234,1710,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','<BR>\r\nthe lunch/shoes thing was from me.\r\ni am so nice, yes i am!',0,0,0,0,'203.96.108.202','en'),(8235,1729,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','mirror father mirror',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(8236,1725,'2001-09-09 17:50:25',0,'jo','BUS! BUS! BUS! BUS!',1,0,0,0,'172.134.82.172','en'),(8237,1729,'2001-09-09 20:17:01',0,'horse','galloping',4,0,0,0,'216.27.183.161','en'),(8238,1653,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','did i say that recently, i slept in swinneys bed on his \r\nunwashed sheets?  doing things to swinneys stuff \r\nwhile he\\\'s not there is really fun.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(8239,1710,'2001-09-10 01:00:03',0,'sawks to o','<br>\r\ni was there too, biyaaaaatch :P',2,0,0,0,'203.10.110.132','en'),(8240,275,'2001-09-10 01:24:11',0,'mogs','obsidian is black volcanic glass, have a look on the shores\r\nof Lake Taupo and you will find some.',4,0,0,0,'203.109.250.83','en'),(8241,1730,'2001-09-10 03:53:54',0,'ghost','<p>exploring the possibilities<br>\r\nof communicating</p>\r\n<pthrough variations</p>\r\n<p><br>\r\nof</p>\r\n<p>breathlessness.</p>',4,0,0,0,'32.102.109.248','en'),(8242,1730,'2001-09-10 04:03:36',0,'ghost2','<p>variations of...</p>',5,0,0,0,'32.102.109.248','en'),(8243,1730,'2001-09-10 04:04:17',0,'ghost','<p>through</p>',6,0,0,0,'32.102.109.248','en'),(8244,1730,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','i am inspired by my friends and this third grade goof-ass \r\nworld.  friday i was inspired to make a public service \r\nannouncement about driving nice.  this third grade goof-ass \r\nworld initiated the idea, but only in the context of my \r\nfriends who would make it possible.  first, i thought the \r\np.s.a. was funny to me because i thought of lulu acting in \r\nit. second, i though it was possible because s5 wants to do \r\nvoice overs. third, i thought it might actually happen \r\nbecause egg likes to make videos.  maybe it will happen, \r\nmaybe not.  but the question was...</P>',3,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(8245,1729,'2001-09-10 05:04:36',0,'treetop','I went to a party last night inside of a mirror',0,0,0,0,'172.138.25.59','en'),(8246,1726,'2001-09-10 10:53:56',0,'Kate','This seems so much more realistic than the last segment - \r\nmore like the first. I\\\'ve been on that toilet baby. nice.',2,0,0,0,'203.97.2.242','en'),(8247,1731,'2001-09-10 11:39:00',0,'kat','<p>i dream a lot. before i left town to escape i was having \r\nhorrible dreams. night terrors. waking up with the sweats. \r\nfearful. i\\\'d been chased. hunted. haunted. i didnt dream at \r\nall the week the i was gone. and now i dream of questioning \r\nthings. i am searching. and it always has something to do \r\nwith desert and love....</p>\r\n<p>my best friend sets me on a journey. she needs my help. \r\ni\\\'m riding a ferry. i have nothing but one small bag. i am \r\nbarefoot and covered in dust. i am content. willing to do \r\nanything for her.</p>\r\n<p>friends come to visit my home. they are hungry. we eat \r\nsome kind of lavish feast. i keep finding things to give \r\naway. there is glitter everywhere. they paint themselves \r\nand are laughing and crying. telling me they love this \r\nplace. i look outside through the window and see nothing \r\nbut desert.</p>\r\n<p>i am walking at night through a city of tents. i am \r\nalone with the wind roaring around me. i lay down to sleep \r\nand wake to find myself being held by a female friend of \r\nmine. someone i work with. though we don\\\'t hang out very \r\noften i have always felt very close to her. she is \r\nundressing me and petting me. the wind is still roaring \r\noutside. i can hear music...and we are laughing softly. \r\nkissing. and i am thinking to myself, why must this end?</p>\r\n<p>i dont know what any of these dreams mean. i dont feel \r\nthat they need to be deciphered at all really. i am just \r\nhappy that the anger i felt before i left is \r\ngone....gone...gone...gone.</p>',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.131','en'),(8248,1730,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>When she was in 7th grade, my good friend made a \r\n<i>public service announcement</i> for the state of new \r\njersey, to promote recycling.  The crazy thing is that now, \r\n11 years later, she still hears it on the radio from time \r\nto time.<br><tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8249,1653,'2001-09-10 12:16:27',0,'Everyone to Austin','<I>Please</I> auction some more of your personal items on \r\neBay so that we can all have a shot at ownign a piece of \r\nthe rock that is austin swinney!',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8250,1731,'2001-09-10 12:38:43',0,'ty','well i\\\'m glad too. thanks for the comment.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.145','en'),(8251,1728,'2001-09-10 13:22:52',0,'Jamazon','Celery !== Food',4,0,0,0,'217.32.131.168','en'),(8252,1734,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','<BR>\r\nsomeone was too tired to put her paragraph tags in.\r\nyeah. it was me. ok? jo=forgetful\r\n\r\nmaybe i could hand you a bunch of the tags and you could \r\nuse them in your head where you see fit. work out your own \r\nparagraphs. that cool with you?',0,0,0,0,'210.54.236.27','en'),(8253,1735,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>techno is good; trance is good, also.  but, booty \r\nshakin\' is <i>best</i>.  i just moved into a new apartment- \r\nits half underground, half at sidewalk-level.  saturday \r\nnight, i put my speakers in the window (at sidewalk level) \r\nand mixed trance for 2 hours.  my neighbor turned off his \r\nsalsa and came over to sift through my records.  drunk \r\ncolumbia students were attracted from nearby cannon\'s pub, \r\nand delighted me by dancing on my sidewalk, two feet in \r\nfront of my window for an hour or so.  i could only see \r\nthem from the hips down, and they were definitely shakin\' \r\nbooty.  as i said, booty shakin\' is a good thing, indeed. \r\npeople should shake booty more often.</tt>  ',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8254,1734,'2001-09-10 13:59:13',0,'kini','<p>and sydney loves you!',0,0,0,0,'61.8.19.70','en'),(8255,1734,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>what pretty town names: St. Kilda, Prahran, Surry \r\nHills... ahh, the mystique of new places!</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8256,1735,'2001-09-10 14:07:37',0,'bmg to peter','<p>i wanna come over and sift through your records, \r\nand dance in the street. </p><p>bailar salsa, \r\nmerengue, cumbia,\r\nsonidos africano y mas! its all good.</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8257,1735,'2001-09-10 14:15:40',0,'bmg','<p>my little apple<br>\r\nsweat and tart<br>\r\ncut in half <br>\r\nmakes two<br>\r\none for me<br>\r\nand <br>\r\none for you<br>\r\n-our little apple<br></p>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8258,1735,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to BMG','<br><tt>If you (or anyone else for that matter) ever find yourself \r\nin nyc, on the corner of 108th street and Broadway on a \r\nweekend-night, follow the music... <i><b>Bailaremos toda la noche!\r\n</i></b></tt>  \r\n',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8259,1734,'2001-09-10 14:53:09',0,'Jamazon','<br>Australia is<br>\r\nNice but so is New Zealand.<br>\r\nThey are nice and hot.',1,0,0,0,'217.32.131.168','en'),(8260,1735,'2001-09-10 14:55:31',0,'Jamazon','An all time classic and the soundtrack to my schooldays \r\nis \\\'Josh Wink - Higher State of Consciousness\\\' The Dex and \r\nJonesy Remix was done on a Commodore Amiga you know ;)',1,0,0,0,'217.32.131.168','en'),(8261,1730,'2001-09-10 14:59:02',0,'Jamazon','I beleive it went something like this....*ahem*<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<i>There once was a man from Nantucket<br>Who kept all his \r\neggs on one bucket...</i>',1,0,0,0,'217.32.131.168','en'),(8262,1730,'2001-09-10 14:59:30',0,'Jamazon','in even!',1,0,0,0,'217.32.131.168','en'),(8263,1735,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>I actually caught josh wink at <a \r\nhref=\"http://www.centro-fly.com\">centro fly</a> two weeks \r\nago. although some of his stuff was cheez (spoken word at a \r\nclub?), the crowd literally freaked out when he \r\nspun \'<a href=\"http://www.cdnow.com/cgi-bin/mserver/SID=1057309897/pagename=/RP/CDN/FIND/album.html/ArtistID=WINK*JOSH/ITEMID=388254\">higher state</a>\' for like 30 minutes. definite old-\r\nschool acid. i went home and hugged my 303.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8264,1735,'2001-09-10 15:21:52',0,'jo','dig, i named my first fish \\\"snyder\\\" after gary snyder. he \r\nis righteous, homes.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(8265,1733,'2001-09-10 15:25:37',0,'jo','new apartments are good, peter. they\\\'re a convenient way to \r\nstart seeing your life in new terms. homes are muy \r\nimportante; i hope this one treats you kindly.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(8266,1733,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>yes, yes, yes!  things are off to a great start, \r\nhere.  all i needed was a slight change of venue and more \r\nspace, a few blocks up the street; same life, better place- \r\nnow i can <i>live</i>.  i discovered that a basement room \r\nhas yellow walls with a sky/clouds mural on the \r\nceiling.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8267,1736,'2001-09-10 16:09:24',0,'Doktor','d00d, your3 so \\\'1337.',6,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8268,1722,'2001-09-10 16:55:43',0,'coyoboy','sure, depression, in the secular sense can be an important \r\nspice, much like seasoned salt, added to the french fries \r\nin the diner of life (pardon my metaphor).\r\n\r\nbut if you find yourself unable to get up, get out of bed, \r\nand your days are full of the spice of depression only-- \r\nthen vitamin Z (zoloft or some other) is worth thinking \r\nabout. \r\n\r\nThough it seems like everyone is on the stuff these days, \r\nthere is a fine line between regular old, good-for-you \r\ndepression, and the stuff you need to see someone about.',3,0,0,0,'156.153.255.134','en'),(8269,1722,'2001-09-10 16:56:59',0,'crowboy','moll-- you don\\\'t eat no caribou',6,0,0,0,'156.153.255.134','en'),(8270,1735,'2001-09-10 17:09:54',0,'kat','my little apple<br>\r\ncomes from spain<br>\r\nborn to shake booty<br>\r\nsee those hips move?<br>\r\nshe likes the feel<br>\r\nof two hands<br>\r\non her apple<br>\r\nas the music<br>\r\nmoves her to another place\r\n',4,0,0,0,'32.102.109.234','en'),(8271,1735,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt><a \r\nhref=\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?\r\nid=1115.txt\">Apple Season</a>. Once I was volunteering at \r\nan inner-city community center, and this little kid was out \r\nin the front lobby, breakdancing like i\'ve never seen \r\nbefore, and chanting at the top of his lungs: <i>\"booty, \r\nc\'mon, booty SHAKE. booty-SHAKE-booty, booty SHAKEDATBOOTY, \r\nc\'mon booty shake, booty-shake-booty\"</i>, etc... there \r\nhave been moments where i\'d have liked to have been that kid, \r\njust for 5 minutes.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8272,1738,'2001-09-10 17:20:12',0,'Sara Goldfarb','i had the oranges and blues, <i>and</i> the electro-shock-\r\ntherapy... look how i ended up. <b>i\\\'m gonna be on TV!!</b>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8273,1737,'2001-09-10 17:24:33',0,'Patrick Bateman','<br><b>Memory List:</b><br>\r\n<br>\r\n<b>Objects:</b><br>\r\nDrills, coat-hangers, Dean & Deluca seasoning salts. Pen \r\nknives.  Videos to return. Armani blazers to get dry-\r\ncleaned.<br> \r\n<b>People:</b><br>\r\nEvelyn, Sean, whores, dealers.<br>\r\n<b>Places:</b><br>\r\nLe Cirque. The Rainbow Room.  Sylvias.  Tribeca Grill.<br>\r\n<b>Words:</b><br>\r\nMoney, sex, death, greed, power, coke, snuff, torture, \r\nlove, happiness, spasm, death, killer.<br>\r\n<b>Music:</b><br>\r\nHuey Lewis, Genesis.<br><br>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8274,1738,'2004-07-27 05:00:32',578,'NetfÃ¶ng!','see the changes;<br><hr>\r\n1.   they are gold;\r\n2.   they are silver;<br>\r\neat the rancid; ransom; dancer.\r\n<hr>Hmm, nameless comments!  ',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8275,1737,'2001-09-10 17:30:50',0,'kat','my favorite time was visiting gramma. she let me stay up \r\ntill midnight. we\\\'d turn out all the lights and curl up on \r\nthe couch to see the late show. john wayne usually. i \r\nsnuggled up to her side and she would whisper secrets to \r\nme...about who that actor was or why the did things the way \r\nthey did. she would run her fingers through my hair. i long \r\nfor this still...movies at midnight. under blankets. curled \r\ntogether. ',4,0,0,0,'32.102.109.234','en'),(8276,1738,'2001-09-10 17:33:09',0,'kat','rancid ransom dancer....what nice images that leaves me \r\nwith. i must steal that sometime.',4,0,0,0,'32.102.109.234','en'),(8277,1734,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','st kilda reprazent!',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(8278,1737,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>there was a <i>hoot-owl</i> that lived in my vast \r\nback yard when i was growing up.  my older brother taught \r\nme how to make owl-like calls by blowing into my cupped-\r\ntogether hands in a certain, special way.  on summer \r\nevenings when school was out, he and i would go up in the \r\ntreehouse or up on the deck (after the treehouse had long \r\nrotted) and \\\'talk\\\' to the owl; surprisingly, he\\\'d sometimes \r\nhoot in response to our well-intended cacophony. one summer \r\nevening, it rained on me late in the evening, waking me \r\nfrom where i had fallen alseep on the deck, and i heard the \r\nowl.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8279,1738,'2001-09-10 17:36:31',0,'',' ',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(8280,1738,'2001-09-10 17:39:21',0,'Felix da Housecat','<i>speed seduction in a magazine, endless passion in a \r\nlimousine, invisible hand shakes the tambourine, see \r\nyourself on the silver screen</i>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8281,1738,'2001-09-10 17:41:07',0,'Doktor to Kat','I prefer \\\"prancing winsome romancer\\\".',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8282,1734,'2004-07-27 05:00:32',578,'NetfÃ¶ng!','New. Zealand. Girls. Are. Hot.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8283,1738,'2001-09-10 17:55:47',0,'kat to Doktor','somehow that only makes me think of blazing saddles.',4,0,0,0,'32.102.109.234','en'),(8284,1738,'2001-09-10 17:57:12',0,'Mungo','likes beans<hr>\r\n<B><h1><i>F A R T ! ! ! </B></H1></I>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8285,1738,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>Benjamin Franklin said that eating asparagus \\\"will \r\nmake our winds toothsome\\\" and that \\\"drinking turpentine \r\nwill give our waters a scent like roses\\\". just an \r\ninteresting couple of thoughts...</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8286,1737,'2001-09-10 20:00:51',0,'leonard','j\\\'aime ceci beaucoup. il m\\\'incite a vouloir se toucher dans \r\nles endroits que je ne puis pas decrire en ce moment.',2,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(8287,1729,'2001-09-10 20:26:36',0,'matt to treetop','boy, are you on DRUGS?!? :)',1,0,0,0,'64.132.148.219','en'),(8288,1737,'2001-09-10 20:48:15',0,'english','I like this much. it encourages me has to want to touch \r\nitself in the places which I then not decrire in this \r\nmoment. ',0,0,0,0,'24.27.26.99','en'),(8289,1737,'2001-09-10 20:56:13',0,'jo','decrire = describe',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(8290,1734,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','god, i miss australia.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nin a moment of weakness, i admitted to my lover that i \r\nmiss new zealand as well.  i do.  i miss it so much.  \r\nthinking about ponsonby and grey lynn and \r\nkarangahape road and the events of my life that \r\noccured in that area, it makes me want to cry.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nit\\\'s not always warm in australia.  especially in \r\nmelbourne, it gets REALLY cold in winter.  and REALLY \r\nhot in summer.  living next door to the desert will do that \r\nfor you.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nanyway.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(8291,1735,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','although i shouldn\\\'t, and although it makes me a music \r\nsnob, my hackles still rise when people refer to john \r\ndigweed and sasha as techno.',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(8292,1732,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','joanna, you rock',1,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(8293,1728,'2001-09-10 22:02:04',0,'sarah','<p>lovich = extra super celery</p>\r\n\r\n<p>sort of like how cilantro = extra super parsley</p>\r\n\r\n<p>a good variation on bugs on a log is to make it with \r\nbean mash instead of peanut butter and raisins. celery is \r\nsuper road trip snacking, because it is its own funny-\r\nshaped plate. ya.',1,0,0,0,'207.107.254.248','en'),(8294,1739,'2001-09-10 22:28:21',0,'kat','word',4,0,0,0,'32.102.109.222',