\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">i was thinking of you</a> \r\nwhile there...</p>',1,0,0,0,'32.102.109.167','en'),(8317,1738,'2001-09-11 09:20:59',0,'tomato','i love montana.',1,0,0,0,'209.162.48.216','en'),(8318,1737,'2001-09-11 09:54:04',0,'Jamazon','Bof!',4,0,0,0,'217.32.163.219','en'),(8319,1739,'2001-09-11 10:10:04',0,'leonard','Mon singe conduire l\\\'autobus!',1,0,0,0,'217.32.163.219','en'),(8320,1735,'2001-09-11 11:14:14',0,'bmg to sawks and o','<p>reciting my own text here:\r\n</p>\r\n<pre>\r\nSasha. Digweed. Nick Warren.\r\nA little trance, mixed with some down tempo.\r\n</pre>\r\nnot destablizing, just constructive.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8321,1742,'2001-09-11 11:21:06',0,'tomato','people in sf are generally just about too fucking cool to \r\nhang out with.  just keep that in mind and everything will \r\nbe ok.',1,0,0,0,'209.162.48.216','en'),(8322,1735,'2001-09-11 11:35:38',0,'Vomit','fucking genre pretensions suck. good music is good music, \r\ncall it whatever you like. i know more about music than all \r\nof you put together and i\\\'d never be so pretensious as to \r\npoint out the difference between techno, trance, \r\nhouse, \\\'electronica\\\', etc... ',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8323,1736,'2001-09-11 12:39:20',0,'lulu','suck it, pajamajon.  ',2,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(8324,882,'2001-09-11 12:43:23',0,'Garbageman','Dude. More TUBE, MORE Tube, please, yes, thank you much.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8325,1736,'2001-09-11 13:19:10',0,'Jamazon','gladly',4,0,0,0,'217.32.132.109','en'),(8326,1739,'2001-09-11 14:12:14',0,'jo','stop talking about your monkey, dude.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(8327,1510,'2001-09-11 15:59:30',0,'Jamazon','an omen perhaps?',1,0,0,0,'217.32.156.35','en'),(8328,1739,'2001-09-11 16:41:48',0,'leonard','designer imposter! i would never do such a thing.',4,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(8329,1742,'2001-09-11 16:42:48',0,'leonard','i love that image. do you have more?',2,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(8330,1742,'2001-09-11 16:57:40',0,'kat','i recently told a friend that i was giving up on the job \r\nsearch. that i am disillusioned. disenfranchised. \r\ndiappointed. they said...what\\\'s the big deal? we all work \r\nin cubes. you can too! yes right...but somehow i find \r\nsomething morally wrong with this \\\'business image\\\' \r\nmentality. i am applying for creative positions. promotions \r\nand development. they want to pay me to create, but are \r\noffended by the possibility that i might have my own \r\npersonality? i am supposed to shut this off when i walk in \r\nthe office? yes folks you too can have an imagination and \r\nbe a robot in a vacumn. this makes no sense.',4,0,0,0,'32.100.71.202','en'),(8331,1744,'2001-09-11 17:18:06',0,'bmg','<p>i just want to huddle around with all my friends. eat \r\nsoup, eat fruit, and be with friends. thats it. silence \r\nwould be best. </p>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8332,1744,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','no one bombs australia. people bomb the US. i live in the \r\nUS. i don\\\'t like being bombed. ergo: ______',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(8333,1744,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','australia is really nice.  i like it there.  we don\\\'t get \r\nbombed.  no one really hates us.  we\\\'re just kind of \r\nnice.  we should really give land back and make \r\namends to the aboriginies.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(8334,1744,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>i am shocked. i really am.  there is now other way to put\r\nit.</P>',4,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(8335,1744,'2001-09-11 17:30:49',0,'kat','my friends in Oklahoma are emailing. what do you say? what \r\ncan you do? it took me three years to work up the courage \r\nto visit the bombing site. nothing can make me leave. this \r\nis my home.',1,0,0,0,'32.100.71.202','en'),(8336,1744,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','shadok woke me up with the news this morning. i thought it \r\nwas an elaborate game he invented just to snap me out of \r\nbed. oh god. how terribly fucked. i still hear planes from \r\nthe top of the hill.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(8337,1744,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','i am the only one at work watching it on my machine.',0,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(8338,1744,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','i got out of bed all hungover and wandered into the hall \r\nwhere my roommate said, hey did you hear the stuff that is \r\nhappening? and i said, no, what happened? and she said, we\\\'re \r\nunder attack. the world trade center and some planes and the \r\npentagon. i don\\\'t really know. i\\\'m like, what you are \r\nkidding.<br>\r\nnow no UPS to ship my magazine. i\\\'m going home.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(8339,1744,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','how do you think your <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=\r\n131.txt\\\">party</a> will handle the crisis, darlin?',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(8340,1744,'2001-09-11 17:59:41',0,'bmg','i say we all turn our computers off, grab some crayons \r\nand color for a while. take a nap. drink some water... ',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8341,1744,'2001-09-11 18:03:38',0,'kat','btw: i disagree with justin\\\'s comments. there is no such \r\nthing as perfection. there are always loopholes. the US has \r\nbeen living in a bubble. i didn\\\'t realize this till i lived \r\nin London. if you ever spend an extended period of time in \r\neurope it will really open your eyes to what babes in the \r\nwoods we are.',4,0,0,0,'32.100.71.202','en'),(8342,1744,'2001-09-11 18:05:09',0,'sic','plan to donate some blood...food...whatever \r\nprayers,thoughts you can',0,0,0,0,'172.168.43.56','en'),(8343,1744,'2001-09-11 18:24:43',0,'ghost','all of Disney corp parks have been closed. DISNEYLAND is \r\nclosed. i know it seems petty to be touched by this. but \r\nthe Land of Dreams closed? okay. this is real. whatever \r\nhappens we cannot lose our dreams.',4,0,0,0,'32.100.71.202','en'),(8344,1744,'2002-03-05 20:17:36',17,'austin to egg','<P>i have put him in <a\r\nhref=\\\"article.phtml?id=1744.txt#8340\\\">contact with\r\nbmg</a>.</P>',3,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(8345,1744,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','there is a beach burn tonight at ocean beach in san \r\nfrancisco, stairwell 28, for those who want to join.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(8346,1744,'2001-09-11 18:46:55',0,'mscreant','i\\\'m pregnant and anemic. my doc says i cannot donate \r\nblood... what else can be done?',2,0,0,0,'66.69.227.53','en'),(8347,1744,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','wtcbombing.org.net.com are all taken.',3,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(8348,1742,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','they just want you to do your job and have a professional \r\nappearance. no one takes you seriously when you are all \r\npierced and tattooed and dressed funny and have strange \r\nhair, especially if you are trying to sell them something. \r\ni personally don\\\'t care what anyone else chooses to look \r\nlike, but i maintain a conservative appearance for two \r\nreasons. 1)The way I look or dress has nothing to do with \r\nmy creativity or personal philosophy, and 2)It helps my \r\ndaily life in many ways--I don\\\'t like to attract attention, \r\nand I don\\\'t want people making huge assumptions based on my \r\nappearance.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.246','en'),(8349,1744,'2001-09-11 19:16:17',0,'Moll','School shut down. Trains shut down. Buses shut down. Phones \r\nbusy. Had to walk and walk and walk in the general \r\ndirection of my town until I found a friend. F-15\\\'s and \r\nother warplanes flying overhead from Fort Dix en route to \r\nNYC. Great strangeness.',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(8350,1746,'2001-09-11 19:16:48',0,'AmyLouisegg','well, whats it gonna be, roasted chicken or tuna \r\ncasserole? make up your mind, ma joad. I wish Id \r\nnever said that to you about the water.',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(8351,1746,'2001-09-11 19:25:26',0,'huevitahuevita','<p>I was just watching the footage again, and \r\nreminiscing with jay about the last time we were in that \r\nbuilding. the tallest pair in NY! the proud phalli of our \r\ngreat nation.</p>\r\n<p>and I remembered laying in his bed this morning \r\nwhile he read cnn out loud. In most of my daily life I \r\nscorn the phallus as symbol of power, and complain in \r\nbars about military spending over heath care or \r\neducation. But when I imagine my house on fire I hope \r\nfor protection. And secretly, the phallus comforts me. \r\nAnd admittedly, I have been living under its cruel and \r\noppressive protection my entire life. Who am I? A \r\nthoughtful piece of snatch living in deep affluence \r\nmoaning about violence I have never experienced.</p>\r\n<p>What scares me most is the carnage-lust alighted \r\nin the voice of every wolf I talk to. It is more than just \r\nconcern for our safety. It is affirmative excitement for \r\ncultural chaos. it is a hard-on for violence. I am trying to \r\nreconcile my psychosexual lust for the phallus and my \r\ndesire to live in a world where aggression is \r\nconsidered primitive. </p>',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(8352,1746,'2001-09-11 19:38:02',0,'jay','I just remembered why you want people you really love \r\naround you in life. Why you shouldn\\\'t stay where things \r\ndon\\\'t feel right. Because yeah, we all come together when \r\nwe\\\'re afraid, and we forget our petty differences, but who \r\nwants to be with someone they don\\\'t really love, listening \r\nto them screech about the disaster in that timbre of voice \r\nthat always got on your nerves? What do you do when the \r\nwar\\\'s on, and you\\\'re not in love?',1,0,0,0,'66.32.25.42','en'),(8353,1743,'2001-09-11 19:47:12',0,'leonard','i\\\'m sure they didn\\\'t teach you how to hold a chainsaw like \r\nthat in lumberjack school. geez us, watch yr wood//',6,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(8354,1745,'2001-09-11 19:56:33',0,'trouble','the sun poured down here this morning and the sun shines \r\nthere now.  people died here today and people will die \r\nthere tomorrow.  everybody knows that nobody ever \\\'wins\\\' \r\nbut everybody seems to keep trying.  sigh.',1,0,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(8355,1746,'2001-09-11 20:09:47',0,'jo','yeah. vanderslice\\\'s \\\"<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.johnvanderslice.com/html/lyrics_insound_tex\r\nt.html\\\">i miss the war</a>\\\" comes to mind.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(8356,1746,'2001-09-11 20:11:28',0,'jo','(that song sort of makes light romance of war. don\\\'t hold \r\nme responsible for john vanderslice\\\'s weirdness.)',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(8357,1745,'2001-09-11 20:13:56',0,'bmg','gulp.',1,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8358,1744,'2001-09-11 20:18:23',0,'ix to steve','if the us ever gets in a war with china, australia will be\r\nbombed. count on it.',0,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(8359,1744,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','but will that happen?  i don\\\'t think the chinese are \r\nresponsible for the wtc thing.<br>\r\n<br>\r\ni wonder what australia\\\'s official position is on helping \r\nthe usa out.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nthe more i think about it, the more horrific it seems.  i \r\nthink people who are reacting to these crashes with \r\nindifference and casualness are in shock.  it really is a \r\nbig deal, wherever you live.<br>',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(8360,1744,'2001-09-11 21:24:13',0,'stuart murdoch','it\\\'s been a bloody stupid day.',6,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(8361,1744,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','or we could colonize io.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(8362,1744,'2001-09-11 21:36:32',0,'ernie brewer','don\\\'t worry stew we\\\'ll grease those bastards.',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(8363,1744,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','i wasn\\\'t trying to link the chinese to this horror. i was\r\npointing out that wherever a person goes, they live under\r\nthe shadow.',0,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(8364,1744,'2001-09-11 21:45:45',0,'Mike','I still can\\\'t believe it,I hope austin doesn\\\'t leave the \r\ncountry because of this.\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,'206.224.71.189','en'),(8365,1744,'2001-09-11 21:55:51',0,'jo','i hope that no one does. ix is right; none of us is \r\nsheltered, anywhere, from this possibility.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(8366,1744,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','antarctica?',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(8367,1744,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','mars needs women.',0,0,0,0,'66.32.27.86','en'),(8368,1742,'2001-09-11 23:15:13',0,'kat','it goes a lot deeper than just how you look Tyler. its \r\nabout wanting art and really cranking out widgets. <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.metroactive.com/cruz/kinkade-0136.html\\\" \r\ntarget=\\\"_blank\\\">read\r\nthis</a>.',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.199','en'),(8369,1743,'2001-09-12 01:26:29',0,'treetop','murderer!',0,0,0,0,'172.151.151.115','en'),(8370,1746,'2001-09-12 01:33:04',0,'treetop','Twelve Monkeys...',0,0,0,0,'172.151.151.115','en'),(8371,1747,'2001-09-12 01:39:44',0,'stella','<P>*sigh*</P>\r\n<P>I live in NY, about 20 minutes from the chaos. I know \r\npeople who haven\\\'t been accounted for yet. Friends and \r\nco-workers today at work screaming and crying because their \r\nbrothers and husbands work in the WTC and haven\\\'t been, \r\ncan\\\'t be, located. </P>\r\n<P>Chiamatt, I agree with your points. I typically read what \r\nyou write and think to myself, \\\"Wow, good point.\\\" I know \r\nfor a fact that the rhetoric is bullshit and that the US \r\ncauses it\\\'s share of pain and chaos. But please, not so soon \r\non this one. Let\\\'s let the government say the only things \r\nthat they can say for right now, because right now, there \r\nare SO MANY more important things to do besides criticize. \r\n</P>',0,0,0,0,'168.100.203.247','en'),(8372,1747,'2001-09-12 01:40:05',0,'erin','as always the power of language here is immense. it is never \r\njust \\\"us\\\" or \\\"them\\\" never just \\\"right\\\' or wrong.  more wrong \r\nor more right. yes i feel remorse for those who die on other \r\nsoil. yes i feel a deeper sadness for what happened in new \r\nyork and dc today because I KNOW people who were hurt. i \r\nfeel no need to apologize for the inconsistency in my grief. \r\nyes i feel empathy when someone in your family dies, goddamn \r\ni feel sadder when one dies in mine. i know you are speaking \r\nto a greater \\\"you\\\" then just to me. let me ask you a \r\nquestion in light of yours.  is it MORE acceptable that it \r\nhappened here? do you believe it MORE deserved? where are \r\nyour boundaries of acceptable carnage. should we shrug and \r\nsay \\\"well, hell, heh heh...guess we deserved that one.\\\"\r\nsigh. i don\\\'t know.\r\ni have many wishes now. none of them wil',0,0,0,0,'64.12.102.158','en'),(8373,1744,'2001-09-12 01:41:22',0,'Gruss gut','I like Switzerland',0,0,0,0,'172.151.151.115','en'),(8374,1747,'2001-09-12 02:00:34',0,'jo','email that i just sent to a friend:\r\n<tt><p>From: joanna vaught<BR>To: dustin<BR>\r\nSubject: Re: hi\r\n<p>\r\n\r\n> i didn\\\'t do it.<BR>\r\n><BR>\r\n> that\\\'s all i\\\'m allowed to say at this time.\r\n<p>\r\nso you know, when our school represented israel at model \r\nun, i was close\r\nto everyone on that team and i heard and read all the \r\nresearch of israel\\\'s\r\ndefense and stance on their relationship with the \r\npalestinians.\r\n<p>\r\nand in the face of that much mutal hatred, you can only ask \r\nyourself, \\\"how\r\ncan you hate groups of people this much? how can you not \r\njust wake up and\r\nrealize that they\\\'re not the enemy, they\\\'re your brother, \r\nthey\\\'re just\r\ntrying to keep their families safe, just like you.\\\"\r\n<p>\r\ntoday, watching the footage of the palestinians celebrating \r\nin the street,\r\npassing out cakes, laughing and saying smugly: \\\"there \r\nshould have been\r\nmore,\\\" i kept thinking, \\\"soulless. heartless. enemy, enemy, \r\nenemy.\\\"</tt>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'172.163.124.58','en'),(8375,1747,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','<p>\r\nill answer your question. i dont think what happened today \r\nin nyc and d.c is deserved of any city. I dont think any one \r\nperson on this earth should go through what the thousands \r\nwent through today. however, i do beleive this. \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nafter ww2 europe was devastated by death, war, and \r\ndevastation. whole cities were in ruin due to the \r\ncatastrophic effect of modern war. economies were in ruin \r\nand whole groups of people were on the move and without \r\nanything to their name. europe had become a \\\"third world\\\". \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nthe united states, a country late into the war, and except \r\nfor pearl harbour was untouched by a war at home. u.s, like \r\ncanadian troops, were always on the front, but never on the \r\ndefensive of home turf. for this reason the united states \r\nwas economically capable of drafting what we now call the \r\nmarshall plan. a plan to rebuild a once prosperous part of \r\nthe world; propelled into the third world by war. the \r\nmarshall plan pumped millions of dollars and aid...dollars \r\nand aid that re-built europe into what it is today; 26% of \r\nthe worlds gdp. \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nnow i ask you this. why is it that the richest country in \r\nthe world cannot spend that same ammount of money in the \r\nregions of the world most poor; raising their standards of \r\nliving and education to the standards that which we in the \r\nwestern hemisphere take for granted?\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nwhen i can walk upto a man woman or child in ethiopia or in \r\nthe west bank, and the only care on his mind is what kind of \r\ncar he wants...ps2 or xbox. when i hear this, i know that \r\nthe united states has helped. \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\ncall me what you will. i am an idealist. i am a socialist. \r\nhowever if people would just start paying attention to whats \r\ngoing on around them, things would change. I pay attention \r\nand i still have time to watch porn, play video games, work, \r\nride my bike on the boardwalk, goto movies, talk to people \r\nabout bman on icb, and most importantly sleep. with 2/3 of \r\nthe voting population not voting, i am not encouraged, and i \r\nfind myself looking at a population that wants a quick \r\nclosure to this horrific act. however i think generations \r\nare needed. ',1,0,0,0,'24.43.182.49','en'),(8376,1747,'2001-09-12 02:46:33',0,'wb','ill call you what you are: a fucking joker. \"whew\". just \r\nkeep your mouth shut from now on.\r\n\r\n<BR><BR>\r\n\r\n_chiam_ whew, i just wrote a very long answer to erins \r\nquestion to me<BR>\r\n_chiam_ on swinneyorg<BR>\r\n_chiam_ i need to go have a smoke. im so baked.',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(8377,1747,'2001-09-12 02:57:35',0,'BjB','<p>I wish I was writing many of you under better \r\ncircumstances, but as many\r\nof you know, I am an employee of Lehman Brothers in NYC and \r\nmy office is\r\nlocated at 1 World Trade Center (the one with the antenna) \r\non the 38th\r\nfloor. I had been at the office since 6:45am because of \r\nmeetings, and\r\nyes, I was in the building when it all happened. </p><p>\r\n\r\nSince many people are trying to ask me what happened, I \r\nfigured that I\r\nshould write everyone in one email so that not only do you \r\nknow that I\r\nam alive and physically unharmed, but so that you can hear \r\nmy experience\r\nas a first-hand witness.\r\n</p><p>\r\nFirst, I must say that this is by far one of the most \r\ndisturbing days of\r\nmy life. I have seen some things today that no person \r\nshould ever have\r\nto see.\r\n</p><p>\r\nTuesday mornings I have a meeting at 7:30am in the \r\nneighboring World\r\nFinancial Center building (where I used to work when I was \r\nwith\r\nMerrill). I had just come back and was sitting at my desk \r\nfor about 10\r\nminutes before I heard and felt the first attack. The sound \r\nof a\r\nthunderous BOOM was heard with the jostling and swaying of \r\nthe WTC 1\r\nbuilding. The feeling was something akin to someone \r\ngrabbing you by the\r\nshoulders and swinging you back and forth a few times. \r\nStartled by this,\r\nI looked out the window just a few feet away to see glass, \r\nthousands of\r\nsheets of paper and large metal pieces raining down from \r\nabove. My first\r\nreaction was that the top of the building blew off by some \r\ngas explosion\r\nor that a plane or helicopter had clipped the top of the \r\nbuilding.\r\nWanting to go closer to the window and look out, the better \r\nof my senses\r\ncame about and I grabbed my wallet, keys and Palm Pilot \r\n(they were right\r\nin front of me) and ran to the emergency stairwell.\r\n</p><p>\r\nIt\\\'s funny how nobody really knows where the stairwell is \r\nuntil\r\nsomething like this happens.\r\n</p><p>\r\nAs mentioned above, I am on the 38th floor. It took me 20 \r\nminutes to get\r\ndown. The stairs are only wide enough for two people \r\nabreast, and\r\nseveral times the flow of person traffic stopped. Around \r\nthe 20th floor,\r\nwe started seeing lots of smoke. Around the 9th floor, the \r\nfiremen,\r\nrunning up the stairs, passed by with the look of \r\nuncertainty in their\r\neyes... water started rushing down the stairs like a river \r\na few floors\r\nfurther below.\r\n</p><p>\r\nAt this point, nobody knew what was going on. The \r\ntemperature in the\r\nstairwell was rising due to the amount of people trying to \r\nget out, and\r\nthe sounds of men and women getting nervous didn\\\'t help the \r\npeople\r\ntrying to cling to their sanity. I don\\\'t think the people \r\non the lower\r\nfloors had any idea to what extent things were going on, \r\nand I don\\\'t\r\nthink the people on the upper floors had much time to think \r\nabout it.\r\n</p><p>\r\nExiting the stairs in the upper lobby of the building \r\n(still inside)\r\nflashed a scene to the fountain area outside (the area \r\nbetween the two\r\ntowers that people may remember Homer Simpson had a boot on \r\nhis car in,\r\nif you saw that one). Completely evacuated, but the sound \r\nof \\\"pebbles\\\"\r\nbrought me to look out the large windows to see a the \r\noutside raining\r\nglass, debris and burning \\\"stuff\\\". The direction that \r\neveryone was\r\nrunning was towards a covered bridge that runs between the \r\nWTC and the\r\nWorld Financial Center (across the west side highway, going \r\ntowards the\r\nwater). I wish I didn\\\'t but from this point until after I \r\nhad crossed\r\nthe highway, I had saw several bodies.. one thing that you \r\nnever want to\r\nsee is someone falling 80 stories to the.. well, I\\\'ll leave \r\nit there.\r\nYes, I saw \\\"the whole thing\\\". We had to quickly run across \r\nfrom our\r\nbuilding to the building where the bridge is.\r\n</p><p>\r\nWalking quickly towards the water, I finally got a chance \r\nto look back\r\nat the building. At this point, I had no idea that there \r\nwas anything\r\nwrong with the WTC 2 building (the one without the antenna, \r\nsecond hit,\r\nit was the one that was the first to fall and was hit more \r\nin the\r\nmiddle). Making it closer to the water, the sight of one of \r\nthe tallest\r\nbuildings in the world in flames makes you a bit terrified, \r\nbut very\r\nthankful that you made it out.\r\n</p><p>\r\nIn a bit of a daze, I continued to walk north along the \r\nwaterfront on\r\nthe west side of Manhattan. I had found a friend of mine \r\nfrom Merrill\r\nLynch (Brian Yarrington) walking in the same direction and \r\ntried to talk\r\nabout other things.. not really able to complete sentences, \r\nI tried\r\nborrowing his cell phone to call my family (who were no \r\ndoubt _FREAKING_\r\nout), but cell reception wasn\\\'t happening. At some point, I \r\nhad been\r\nable to look back and notice the size of the damage to WTC \r\n1. I still\r\ndid not know that WTC 2 had been hit.\r\n</p><p>\r\nAbout another three quarters of a mile down the road, I \r\nfinally saw the\r\ndamage that had been done to WTC 2 and had overheard \r\nsomeone talking\r\nabout a bomb going off in that building. Continued to walk \r\nhome.\r\n</p><p>\r\nThese days I have been living in the West Village between \r\n6th and 7th\r\navenues around Christopher St. and West 4th. I had said \r\ngoodbye to my\r\nfriend Brian and started walking east into Manhattan\\\'s \r\nGreenwich\r\nVillage. I had stopped on Hudson street to talk with some \r\npeople who\r\nwere standing in the street listening to the news on a car \r\nstereo. I\r\ntold my story, declined some help and \\\"you should see a \r\ndoctor\\\" talk and\r\ncontinued walking towards my apartment. Somewhere between \r\nBleeker St.\r\nand 7th avenue, I see and hear the screams of people on 7th \r\navenue\r\n(about 50 ft. away) looking in the direction of the towers. \r\nAsking what\r\nhad just happened, people told me that WTC 2 had just \r\ncollapsed (the\r\nfirst collapse). About this time, I saw my apartment\\\'s \r\nsuper, a woman\r\nnamed Ana, and just went over to her and threw my arms \r\naround her.\r\n</p><p>\r\nI finally went back to my apartment and tried to call my \r\nfamily on a\r\nnormal phone. No such luck, the phone system was extremely \r\nclogged.\r\n</p><p>\r\nEventually I made it over to 6th avenue and bumped into an \r\nacquaintance\r\nfrom the office (he sat a row away from me). We turned to \r\nsee the WTC 1\r\nbuilding collapse into nothing.\r\n</p><p>\r\nFunny, as we were parting ways, I started to say \\\"See you \r\ntomorrow...\\\"\r\n... I stopped after \\\"See you...\\\" when we realized that we \r\nshould just\r\nfinish the sentence with \\\"when I see you..\\\"\r\n</p><p>\r\nWell, it took me three hours to write this. I apologize to \r\nthe people\r\nwho have been worried about me for the last few hours, but \r\nknow that I\r\nam safe and only a little shaken up.\r\n</p><p>\r\nPeace.<br>\r\n-BjB</p>',6,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8378,1747,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt to wb','no i am not a joker. people who actually know me will know \r\nthis. yes. i was baked, but that has no bearing on how i \r\nwrite and how i think about the world today. i find it \r\nridiculous that you would post something i had said on icb \r\nand attribute it to my response. if you think that because i \r\nwas baked that i was less serious and less respectful \r\ntowards those who have seen things they never thought they\\\'d \r\nsee well then you are a very wrong person. i am very mad at \r\nyou right now. i dont even know you. you dont even know me, \r\nyet you think you can come on here and try and ruin my \r\ncreditability with those who read what i have to say. i \r\nspeak of a tragic situation. i lash out at no one, yet you \r\nfind it in your best interest to try and make me look like a \r\n\\\"joker\\\" as you put it. what was your point? ',6,0,0,0,'24.43.182.49','en'),(8379,1747,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt to bjb','can you please email me? chiam@gee.kz',3,0,0,0,'24.43.182.49','en'),(8380,1747,'2001-09-12 03:34:57',0,'I hunt elves','yes you are an idealist. thinking of utopia while some are \r\nin the middle of a man made hades. ',4,0,0,0,'24.27.26.99','en'),(8381,1747,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','i\\\'m glad you made it brother.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.221','en'),(8382,1747,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','by the way, fuck you \\\"chiamattt.\\\" we do not do anything \r\nlike this. also the assassinations in palestine are nothing \r\nyou wouldn\\\'t do if you were faced with suicide bombers and \r\nshit every day, not to mention the fact that we have bent \r\nover fucking backwards to try and get a resolution between \r\nthe two nations, asking israel to let the palestinians have \r\npalestine, and oh by the way don\\\'t they seem happy to see \r\nus get fucked up? you you pompous son of a bitch, we went \r\nto kosovo to stop innocent people from being killed, and by \r\nthe time we knew what was going on in Rwanda, it was over. \r\nwe don\\\'t just randomly bomb people\\\'s houses, schools, \r\nhospitals, or skyscrapers, we bomb military installations \r\nand give plenty of warning first through diplomatic \r\nchannels, so they can get everybody out, unless we are \r\nfired on. oh and i\\\'m sure you want to say something about \r\nmy post, no i didn\\\'t like it, but i didn\\\'t think it was \r\nwrong either, i just didn\\\'t like how everybody thought it \r\nwas fourth-of-july fireworks instead of people dying.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.221','en'),(8383,1746,'2001-09-12 04:08:52',0,'bmg','i miss clinton too. by the way, what word did bush say that \r\nwas the wrong word??? i didnt catch that.',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8384,1747,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','oh, goddammit, i\\\'m sorry. sorry man.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.221','en'),(8385,1747,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt to tyler','like i said, i wish people would start paying attention.',6,0,0,0,'24.43.182.49','en'),(8386,1749,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','*hugs*',1,0,0,0,'24.43.182.49','en'),(8387,1749,'2001-09-12 04:42:13',0,'bmg to le','<p>I wanna re-enlist because of this... north korea sent \r\nempty nuclear missiles over japan a few years back. empty \r\nthreat and all, but it sure did scare the shit out me and \r\nmy battalion. shoved into a plane, flown to korea - \r\nthinking \"oh my god this is it.\" but quoting Gunny Dan \r\nDaly \"Come on, you sons of bitches! Do you want to live \r\nforever?\"...</p>\r\n<p>\r\n\"There are only two kinds of people that understand \r\nMarines: Marines and the enemy. Everyone else has a second-\r\nhand opinion.\"</p><p> and \"Our Country won\'t go on forever, if we \r\nstay soft as we are now. There won\'t be any AMERICA-because \r\nsome foreign soldiery will invade us and take our women and \r\nbreed a hardier race!\"-<br>\r\nLT. GEN. LEWIS \"CHESTY\" PULLER, USMC</p>\r\n\r\n<p>i miss being around patriots... I hope there is a \r\nnewfound patriotism in this country - i really do. i think \r\nit would breed better leaders and less people detracting... \r\nFuck those people who say shit, honor those people who do \r\nshit. Stand up, grab a hand, go give blood, make your \r\nstance known. Just don\'t fucking talk about it!</p>\r\n<p>swinney followed me onto a military base once, he has \r\nheard the language that i speak right now... i consider \r\nmyself a pacifist. today is different, in a lot of ways.</p>',1,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8388,1749,'2001-09-12 04:45:29',0,'bmg','<p>i wanna eat bullets and drink motor oil right now.</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8389,1749,'2001-09-12 05:01:43',0,'ghost','walk softly....go easy. i could think of nothing else but \r\nthis today. \r\n\r\n<i>go easy</i>',4,0,0,0,'32.102.109.159','en'),(8390,1749,'2001-09-12 05:47:12',0,'tomato','i think we need to watch our civil liberties after this.  not \r\nonly is the military, as you pointed out, going to be on \r\nhigh alert but back here we are going to be losing \r\nprivacy rights, etc now tthat here is an excuse for it.\r\n<p>\r\nhope your dad is ok.',1,0,0,0,'209.162.48.221','en'),(8391,1747,'2001-09-12 06:12:29',0,'MP','Globalisation is THE mechanism for eliminating world \r\npoverty, for the nations of Africa for developing countries \r\nin South America and elsewhere direct aid is a policy that \r\nhas been shown to fail. The enemies of globalisation, the \r\nlimp wristed embittered politicing of the left condemn \r\nthese countries to a never ending litany of dictators, \r\nextremist left and right wing governments and economic \r\nstagnation. Economic Growth can only be realistically \r\nachieved through foriegn investment, through the global \r\nmobilisation of capital and people. Socialist polemic will \r\nnot afford the peoples of Ethiopia or anywhere else the \r\nchoice of a car or game console. Look to SE Asia if you \r\nwant to see the experiment in progress. \r\nOr as I think about it why not look to our own economic \r\nhistory how quickly we forget.\r\nI\\\'m tired of post-modern moral relativism, there is a right \r\nand wrong yes it\\\'s arbitary and culturally determined but \r\nit makes it no less valid for these reasons. This is a war \r\nof values and no quarter should or can be given. The \r\nideologies of fundamentalism, the irrational fear of \r\nglobalisation and moral relativism have no legitimacy in a \r\nglobal society. That affront to human decency that is the \r\nTaliban in Afghanistan and all other regimes of that ilk \r\nshould have been destroyed before it was allowed to start. \r\nIt is the view that we can live with these differences that \r\nthe global community can negoitate with capricious and \r\nirrational states that must in some way be held responsible \r\nfor this act.\r\n\\\"We are right and you are wrong\\\" it\\\'s no more complex than \r\nthis, don\\\'t be fooled by bullshit rhetoric that suggests \r\notherwise. I can think of nothing that is more worthy of \r\ndefence that one\\\'s moral code than the product of western \r\ncivilisation even with all it\\\'s failings. \r\nIn case the subtle difference between using cruise missiles \r\nand passenger jets is lost on some of us..... I don\\\'t \r\nrecall America [or Australia, the country in which I live] \r\never strapping 90 odd people unwilling to a bomb and \r\ndeliberatly attacking a civilian target without \r\nprovocation ....... then again I could be wrong...\r\n',5,0,0,0,'203.20.36.20','en'),(8392,1749,'2001-09-12 06:35:26',0,'chi chi','<br>\r\ni know what you mean about heightened military \r\nsecurity. i was in western saudi arabia during the gulf \r\nwar. all of thirteen, what a grown up i thought i was. i \r\nhave rarely been so terrified. i remember the onset of \r\ndesert storm: my dad was onsite in medina, while we \r\nwere in jeddah. my mom, not wanting to be alone with \r\ntwo kids in an apartment on the edge of town took us to \r\nher mother\\\'s house to spend the night. \r\n<br>\r\nwe had \\\"preparedness drills\\\" at school. classroom \r\nwindows were sealed, and a box of bottled water \r\nplaced in each room. the drill: an alarm would go off, \r\nwe\\\'d all get under our tables, and the teacher would \r\nstuff a towel under the door in the event of gas attacks.  \r\nfrench students came with their embassy issued \r\ngas-masks. families from  dhahran and riyadh fleeing \r\nto jeddah after they had scud attacks out there.\r\n<br>\r\ni now sit here in california in relative safety. i wonder \r\nabout my parents who just today left london for cairo, i \r\nhave yet to hear from them. my family in saudi arabia is \r\nglued to the television trying to find out everything they \r\ncan. i wonder what this means about the future, for \r\nthem over there. for me, so proud to be first generation \r\namerican, yet trying to reconcile that with being arab.\r\n<br>\r\ni feel for all people touched by this. \\\"this is not my war, \r\nkeep your war away from me.\\\" the anger, resentment, \r\nshock and grief. this is the crucial time, words spoken \r\nin anger, actions taken in the heat of the moment. this \r\nmore than ever is the time to reflect.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.168.21.213','en'),(8393,1742,'2001-09-12 06:37:02',0,'Treetop','</head>\r\n<body>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<br><b>To Leonard:</b>&nbsp; Hi, this guy\\\'s <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.psy-eye.de/\\\">site</a>\r\nhas some interesting eye candy.&nbsp;&nbsp; \\\"<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.uni-\r\nkoblenz.de/~eyerq/pics/organicshrine.html\\\">Organic\r\nShrine</a>\\\" is actually my current wallpaper.\r\n<p><b>To Kat:</b>&nbsp; Hey, I bet Kinkade paints pictures \r\nof naked women\r\nin his basement.\r\n</body>\r\n</html>',0,0,0,0,'172.138.89.21','en'),(8394,1749,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Squashed Moll','<p>I kind of want the world to end. But even so, today I \r\nsaw fighter jets. I thought about war and about wanting to \r\nhelp. I even thought the words: \\\"my country\\\". Strangeness. \r\nI\\\'ve always liked people who are actually in the military, \r\nall of the ones I\\\'ve known have been fucking saints. \r\nAlthough I\\\'m sure they\\\'ve always been able to tell that I \r\ndisagree with their politics, they\\\'ve never judged me \r\nbecause of it or held it against me, and I guess I can\\\'t \r\nhelp but return the favor.</p>\r\n<p>Things might get crazy now. Maybe, after a time, the \r\ncraziness will become such that everything fucking ends. I \r\nhope that happens; human beings deserve much more than this \r\nshithead civilization. We have so much more energy to us \r\nthan what we\\\'re allowed to use. At least that\\\'s what I try \r\nto think sometimes.</p>\r\n<p>I just wish it didn\\\'t have to be so terrifying and \r\npainful. I wish we could change in a way that didn\\\'t \r\ninvolve driving eachother crazy until we\\\'re fucking ramming \r\neachother\\\'s buildings with airplanes. Does that make sense? \r\nThe horizon I\\\'ve looked at for my entire life won\\\'t look \r\nthe same anymore. It will just be a smudge. And so some \r\ndipshit temp on the 105th floor is trying to type out a \r\nmemo when he notices <i>a fucking jumbo jet about to slam \r\ninto his boss\\\'s office</i>? Why? Because he happens to work \r\nat a tourist attraction? Because some general pulled out of \r\na conference on race issues on the other side of the planet \r\na week earlier? Because it\\\'s the will of <i>God?</i> We \r\nshouldn\\\'t exist. <i>We are ramming eachother\\\'s buildings \r\nwith airplanes full of people because a supernatural being \r\nwants us to.</i> This is a fucking stupid species. We\\\'re \r\nall fucking retarded.</p>\r\n<p>Anyway. Sorry for the rant, dudes, be well.</p>\r\n',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(8395,1748,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','does anyone have numbers for any of them?',0,0,0,0,'206.170.1.39','en'),(8396,1744,'2001-09-12 10:18:24',0,'Henry Kissinger','you should have leestened to me, meester president.',4,0,0,0,'212.161.41.80','en'),(8397,1747,'2001-09-12 10:20:45',0,'Jamazon','<p>\r\nI think everyone should calm down here. Chaimatt has made \r\nsome valid points but i think maybe the timing was a little \r\nout. Now, obviously these terrorists did what they did for \r\na reason. This wasn\\\'t a mindless act of terrorism. Let\\\'s \r\nnot forget that they died too, they obviously believed very \r\nstrongly in their cause. Why they did what they did, we \r\ndon\\\'t yet know.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nTo deny that American Foreign Policy can be hypocritical \r\nand xenophobic at times is to close your eyes to the truth.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nI don\\\'t not think anyone would condone what happened \r\nyesterday. I certainly wouldn\\\'t and neither would chiamatt.\r\n</p>',1,0,0,0,'217.32.148.105','en'),(8398,1749,'2001-09-12 11:20:59',0,'kdog','<P>no us.  no them.  </P>\r\n<P></P>\r\n<P>we each bear responsibility for this and all other \r\nactions.  how can you have peace and harmony in society \r\nwhen the individuals of that society (all societies) have \r\nno peace and harmony within themselves?</P>\r\n<P>in the end this question points to the ground zero of \r\nall conflict and suffering.</P>',2,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8399,1749,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','i hope that your dad will be ok and that you will be ok too.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.47','en'),(8400,1748,'2001-09-12 15:16:35',0,'Jamazon','<p><b>I know Peter is at 749 west end avenue. That\\\'s North Manhattan i think ?? i\\\'m not big on NY geography. I emailed him and heard nothing back. Does anyone know where he works? </p>\r\nHopefully he\\\'s just not had time to check his email with all the chaos</p>\r\n<p>\r\nI hope he\\\'s ok</b></p>',1,0,0,0,'217.32.148.105','en'),(8401,1747,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','how about just shutting the fuck up for a while. have some respect. save \r\nyour criticisms for a less emotional time.',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(8402,1747,'2001-09-12 15:47:15',0,'Jamazon','Jesus, you people are touchy. Read my comment \r\nagain....slowly. I\\\'ve not critised anything or anybody. I \r\ndon\\\'t appreciate your tone. Especially at a time like this.',3,0,0,0,'217.32.148.105','en'),(8403,1747,'2001-09-12 16:49:11',0,'crowboy','seriously, bad timing, wait a bit before you \r\nstart \\\'digesting it\\\' publicly through your theories and \r\nideas and such.',3,0,0,0,'156.153.254.42','en'),(8404,1747,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','<p>\r\ni dont think my timing was off. these were my thoughts on \r\nthe subject. If i had written a reactionary article calling \r\nfor death and destruction to those responsible, irrational \r\nacts of revenge...would my timing have been better?\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\ni will not shut the fuck up. i will not keep my mouth shut. \r\ni say what i want when i want because we live in a free \r\nsociety. all those who think i am not sensitive to those who \r\nlost friends family and co-workers can ignore me. \r\n</p>\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'24.43.182.49','en'),(8405,1747,'2001-09-12 17:08:23',0,'to MP','in the 1980\\\'s the united states navy shot down an iranian \r\npassenger flight over the persian gulf and never \r\nappologized. ',5,0,0,0,'24.43.182.49','en'),(8406,1747,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','Some un-bridled thoughts i have at the moment:\r\n\r\ni try to disassociate myself with \\\"america\\\" and associate \r\nmyself with \\\"people\\\".  all this just makes me sad. \r\nsometimes i feel ashamed to be an american, living on the \r\nbloody backs of the less fortunate.  other times, i feel \r\nlike it is my duty to enjoy my priviledged place in the\r\nworld becuase i know that all humans, given the choice, \r\nwould choose this over poverty, oppression, and disease.  \r\nif i was living in the third world and saw a first world \r\ncitizen scorning and throwing away his blessed place in \r\nhuman society i would be angry at him for taking his good\r\nfortune for granted.  the decision i usually come to is to \r\nbe thankful for my life and that my responsibility as a \r\nhuman is to live life to the absolute fullest i can \r\n(without hurting anyone else, of course).\r\n\r\n',3,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(8407,1747,'2001-09-12 18:20:52',0,'crowboy','Good Citizenship Tips (excerpt from the Onion)\r\n...Engage others in tense, unproductive political arguments \r\nthat break down into embarrassing exchanges of personal \r\nattacks. ',4,0,0,0,'156.153.255.126','en'),(8408,1749,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','<p>\r\ni have a confession. the only way i know how to process \r\nthis is to mourn for the buildings. the towers were an \r\nessential, beautiful shining monument of my childhood, and \r\ni am sad they are gone. in a totally different room the \r\nmourning for the event as a public event is stored, along \r\nwith the clamoring surrounding the event.  but this \r\nmourning for the buildings lives in a different place, \r\nwhere twilight falls on a snow covered city, quiet except \r\nfor the deep gongs of the church at the corner. i\'m \r\nsomewhere between seven and ten years old. i know i am \r\nalmost home when i can see the towers over catherine street.\r\n</p><p>\r\nthe street slopes downhill to the bay. i can see the water, \r\na block away, dark and sparkling with reflected lights \r\nwhere i\'m to turn left. it has been snowing heavily the \r\nlast couple of days. the towers are grey in the distance \r\nand it\'s beginning to snow again. i am supremely content.\r\n</p><p>\r\nnow, when i make the obligatory post-college visits to my \r\nparents who live in brooklyn, i always made the pilgrimage \r\nto the corner of catherine and madison street, again \r\nheading home to 38 monroe street Apt EH10, and saying hello \r\nto the grey towers in the distance. the streets kept \r\nshrinking. the towers are larger than you would think, like \r\na rising moon. they are much higher than the buildings \r\nacross the street, but you can take them in at a glance, \r\nunlike when you\'re at their base. they lean away at their \r\ndistinctive angle. clouds moved quickly between them \r\nsomewhere in the middle. at christmastime, they glowed red \r\nand green on top.\r\n</p><p>\r\ni stopped to visit them a year ago, and they were \r\nbeautiful. how can they be so beautiful? i will not believe \r\nthey are gone. i can\'t believe they are gone.\r\n</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(8409,1748,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','heh.... haven\\\'t had a chance to check out Swinney until \r\njust now.  It\\\'s nice to know that you guys are concerned.  \r\nI talked to Peter yesterday on the phone.  I\\\'m glad to \r\nhear that people were able to make it out of the WTC.  It \r\nseriously isn\\\'t as bad as it could have been.  If those \r\nbuildings had <i>fallen over</I> right away instead of \r\ncollapsing an hour later.....  I\\\'m still a little in a state of \r\nshock at how many people must have died yesterday \r\nand the fact that parts of NYC look like a war zone.',0,0,0,0,'63.23.117.194','en'),(8410,1747,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','The media is analysing and commenting on it and have been\r\nsince the whole thing began.  No-one has been dissing them\r\nfor their bad timing.',3,0,0,0,'64.229.71.182','en'),(8411,1750,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','<p>\r\nexcerpt: an email from my best friend in nyc, little nick:\r\n<br>\r\ni am so fucking scared:<br>\r\ni was in manhattan on bway, everyone screaming crying- \r\nsomeone yells \\\' the\r\ntowers fell down!\\\'<br>\r\nim totally scared, running aorund, to the east village to \r\nfind someone i can<br>\r\ntalk to, ran into kid congo who calmed me down ( !), then \r\nfound out the<br>\r\nbridge was open and ran across with thousands of people<br>\r\nmanhattan is closed.<br>\r\namaerica is closed.<br>\r\nthis is war<br>\r\n</p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(8412,1750,'2001-09-12 20:41:28',0,'adam','i can\\\'t imagine',0,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(8413,1747,'2001-09-12 21:07:05',0,'Gordon Sinclair','<p>A Tribute To The United States\r\nWidespread but only partial news coverage was given to a \r\nremarkable\r\neditorial broadcast from Toronto by Gordon Sinclair, \r\nCanadian television\r\ncommentator. For more information about Gordon Sinclair or \r\nthe following\r\nbroadcast, please see this.  What follows is the full text \r\nof his\r\ntrenchant\r\nremarks as printed in the Congressional Record:\r\n</p><p>America: The Good Neighbor.</p><p>\r\nâ€œThis Canadian thinks it is time to speak up for the \r\nAmericans as the most\r\n\r\ngenerous and possibly the least appreciated people on all \r\nthe earth.\r\nGermany, Japan and, to a lesser extent, Britain and Italy \r\nwere lifted out\r\nof the debris of war by the Americans who poured in \r\nbillions of dollars\r\nand\r\nforgave other billions in debts. None of these countries is \r\ntoday paying\r\neven the interest on its remaining debts to the United \r\nStates.\r\nWhen the Franc was in danger of collapsing in 1956, it was \r\nthe Americans\r\nwho propped it up, and their reward was to be insulted and \r\nswindled on the\r\n\r\nstreets of Paris. I was there. I saw it.\r\nWhen earthquakes hit distant cities, it is the United \r\nStates that hurries\r\nin to help. This spring, 59 American communities were \r\nflattened by\r\ntornadoes. Nobody helped.\r\nThe Marshall Plan and the Truman Policy pumped billions of \r\ndollars into\r\ndiscouraged countries. Now newspapers in those countries \r\nare writing about\r\n\r\nthe decadent, warmongering Americans.\r\nIâ€™d like to see just one of those countries that is \r\ngloating over the\r\nerosion of the United States dollar build its own airplane. \r\nDoes any other\r\n\r\ncountry in the world have a plane to equal the Boeing Jumbo \r\nJet, the\r\nLockheed Tri-Star, or the Douglas DC10? If so, why donâ€™t \r\nthey fly them?\r\nWhy\r\ndo all the International lines except Russia fly American \r\nPlanes?\r\nWhy does no other land on earth even consider putting a man \r\nor woman on\r\nthe\r\nmoon?\r\nYou talk about Japanese technocracy, and you get radios.\r\nYou talk about German technocracy, and you get automobiles.\r\nYou talk about American technocracy, and you find men on \r\nthe moon - not\r\nonce, but several times - and safely home again.\r\nYou talk about scandals, and the Americans put theirs right \r\nin the store\r\nwindow for everybody to look at . Even their draft-dodgers \r\nare not pursued\r\n\r\nand hounded. They are here on our streets, and most of \r\nthem, unless they\r\nare breaking Canadian laws, are getting American dollars \r\nfrom ma and pa at\r\n\r\nhome to spend here.\r\nWhen the railways of France, Germany and India were \r\nbreaking down through\r\nage, it was the Americans who rebuilt them. When the \r\nPennsylvania Railroad\r\n\r\nand the New York Central went broke, nobody loaned them an \r\nold caboose.\r\nBoth are still broke.\r\nI can name you 5000 times when the Americans raced to the \r\nhelp of other\r\npeople in trouble. Can you name me even one time when \r\nsomeone else raced\r\nto\r\nthe Americans in trouble? I donâ€™t think there was outside \r\nhelp even during\r\n\r\nthe San Francisco earthquake.\r\nOur neighbors have faced it alone, and Iâ€™m one Canadian who \r\nis damned\r\ntired\r\nof hearing them get kicked around. They will come out of \r\nthis thing with\r\ntheir flag high. And when they do, they are entitled to \r\nthumb their nose\r\nat\r\nthe lands that are gloating over their present troubles. I \r\nhope Canada is\r\nnot one of those.â€\r\nStand proud, Americans!\r\n</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8414,1742,'2001-09-12 21:13:46',0,'leonard to treetop','grassy ass.',6,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(8415,1742,'2001-09-12 21:54:15',0,'crowboy','kat: how do you live if you don\\\'t work?',2,0,0,0,'156.153.255.126','en'),(8416,1742,'2001-09-12 22:11:03',0,'pimp','ohhhh, she works!',0,0,0,0,'172.146.89.97','en'),(8417,1742,'2001-09-12 22:14:00',0,'grassy ass','   yes leonard?',0,0,0,0,'172.146.89.97','en'),(8418,1742,'2001-09-12 22:16:01',0,'Treetop to Leonard','Dee naada',0,0,0,0,'172.146.89.97','en'),(8419,1750,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','people are even scared in columbia, sc where i live. there \r\nis a state trooper on every side of the capitol building \r\ndown the street, even today. <br>\r\nmy roomate got me up at nine am on the 11th, saying \\\"check \r\nthis out, man.\\\" i staggered into his room, and saw the \r\nfirst tower on fire. we figured that a plane had hit it, \r\nwhich would be unusual, but keep in mind i didn\\\'t realize \r\njust how big that hole was, never having seen a building \r\nthat big. the biggest one here is 27 stories. so i \r\nfigured, \\\"it\\\'ll suck trying to put that out\\\", and i thought \r\nabout getting another hour of sleep in. then as i watched, \r\ni saw the second plane hit. boom. (here comes the part that \r\ni am building up to). Barrett said, \\\"why do they keep \r\nflying into it?\\\" for about one full second i was sure that \r\nthere was some desperate mistake being made, something to \r\ndo with computers maybe, <i>making</i> the pilots fly into \r\nthe towers. then of course i figured it out.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.230','en'),(8420,1747,'2001-09-12 23:25:03',0,'ashley to jamazon:','<p>\r\nyes, lets not forget the terrorists are dead too. what is \r\nit you\\\'re trying to express here? is that tragic too? what? \r\ncommentary on the tragic nature of human existence?\r\nlet us mourn the loss suffered by a terrorist group \r\nyesterday, how my heart goes out to them. fuck you, eat my \r\ntone.<br>\r\n(note: <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.torontostar.com/NASApp/cs/ContentServer?\r\npagename=thestar/Layout/Article_Type1&c=Article&cid=10002891\r\n17654&call_page=TS_News&call_pageid=968332188492&call_pagepa\r\nth=News/News\\\" target=\\\"_new\\\">reportedly</a>, Osama bin Laden \r\ndropped to his knees and praised Allah when he was told \r\nabout the attacks.)\r\n<p>\r\noh and:<br>\r\n\\\"To deny that American Foreign Policy can be hypocritical \r\nand xenophobic at times is to close your eyes to the truth.\\\"\r\nrepackaging critisism as truthspeaking is some low shit. or \r\nmaybe you just don\\\'t think about what you say.<br>\r\nxenophobic indeed, jamazon.co.uk.\r\n<p>\r\nchiamatt: yep, and this society has left me free to \r\nridicule your lack of tact.\r\n<p>\r\nfuck this, i\\\'m going back to worrying about how to fit my \r\nxbox into my suv.\r\n\r\n',6,0,0,0,'63.203.225.62','en'),(8421,1742,'2001-09-12 23:47:00',0,'kat','<p>to crowboy: i wake up in the morning. i eat fruit & \r\nfibre. i take a dump. you call this not living???</p>\r\n\r\n<p>to pimp: say that again and i\\\'ll pop a cap in your \r\nass.</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p><i>[best friendly]</i></p>',1,0,0,0,'32.100.69.5','en'),(8422,1750,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i was going to post something about all this but \r\ncan\\\'t put it it words yet. some images: a lecturer at the \r\nhospital i work at saying \\\'oh fuuuuuuck...\\\' and gesturing \r\nout the window to the WTC, all of us looking over just in \r\ntime to see it fall. a woman collapsing. a man pushing a \r\nbody into the emergency room in a shopping cart. a \r\nconstruction worker bawling, hugging me, saying over and \r\nover \\\"my wife is with jesus\\\". all phones dead. net down. \r\nsubway bombs, bomb-squad on the GWB, buildings collapse. \r\nwhat could i <i>possibly</i> say?</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.242','en'),(8423,1742,'2001-09-13 02:41:52',0,'treetop','::lights incense::',0,0,0,0,'172.147.211.44','en'),(8424,1747,'2001-09-13 03:48:01',0,'disco','Finally the American Forgien Policy has caught up with the\r\nUS.  I feel bad for those who were, killed, and lost loved\r\nones etc.  This was bound to happen.  For once its US\r\ndigging loved ones out of the rubble, not some forgien\r\nstate.  Feels shitty doesnt it.  Do unto others.  Cheers,\r\n\r\ndisco',1,0,0,0,'24.112.139.52','en'),(8425,1747,'2001-09-13 03:50:28',0,'and another','http://www.tompaine.com/opinion/2001/09/11/index.html',1,0,0,0,'32.102.109.9','en'),(8426,1751,'2001-09-13 04:07:10',0,'ghost','i\\\'ve just always thought of you as ALL coyote.',1,0,0,0,'32.102.109.9','en'),(8427,1747,'2001-09-13 05:14:29',0,'bmg','disco: <p>you are implying that we haven\\\'t had to do it \r\nbefore, digging the remains of our own citizens out of \r\npiles of rubble, and that now we will know what it is like! \r\nDo you know what it is like?</p> <p>Deductive logic, valid \r\nmaybe, but not a sound argument. implying that we haven\\\'t \r\nwhen have before. i think we are all aware that killing \r\nsucks</p>\r\n<p>\r\n>Finally the American Forgien Policy has caught up with the \r\nUS. <br>\r\nImplies that our foreign policy has been, wreckless, self-\r\ncentered, or what?\r\n</p><p>\r\n>This was bound to happen.<br>\r\nbound to happen again, law of averages.\r\n</p><p>\r\n>For once its US digging loved ones out of the rubble, not \r\nsome forgien state.<br>\r\n</p><p>\r\nFeels shitty doesnt it. <br>\r\nIt feels shitty watching any destruction doesn\\\'t it.\r\n</p><p>\r\n>Do unto others.<br>\r\neye for an eye? you really believe in that?</p>\r\n\r\n',3,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8428,1751,'2001-09-13 05:45:26',0,'sarah','<p>my roommate\\\'s big tough guy brother (editor of Phat \r\nmagazine. ya) describes his hair in terms of those exact \r\npeople: brando, elvis. every barber understands elvis and \r\nthus you can get a hip punk pompadour haircut for $7 \r\nanywhere. \r\n\r\n<p>i like when tough guys describe their hair styles. a \r\nhell\\\'s angel in the seat behind me on the bus one time knew \r\nmore hairstyle names than i did. whatever a fade is is what \r\nhe always got, because his gang leader used to always get \r\none at MagiCuts. his friend had something involving \r\nfeathering. also they argued about whether wearing hats \r\nwould make you go bald at a young age (the fade guy learned \r\nthat in prison).\r\n\r\n<p>i feel kind of silly writing about hair right now. when \r\nis it respectful to start talking about hair again? i don\\\'t \r\nhave anything necessary to say about how i feel bad about \r\nall the building crash people... should i be quiet for \r\nawhile instead?',1,0,0,0,'207.107.254.186','en'),(8429,1751,'2001-09-13 05:54:30',0,'boardranter','it\\\'s ok to talk about the pedestrian bits of daily life.\r\n\r\nperhaps its trite to say \\\'life goes on,\\\' but it does. \r\n\r\nfor me, its somehow worse to try to argue, and rationalize \r\nthe unthinkable (especially when high). \r\n\r\ni think a fat forum is fine.',3,0,0,0,'12.81.66.71','en'),(8430,1751,'2001-09-13 05:54:39',0,'highboardranter','it\\\'s ok to talk about the pedestrian bits of daily life.\r\n\r\nperhaps its trite to say \\\'life goes on,\\\' but it does. \r\n\r\nfor me, its somehow worse to try to argue, and rationalize \r\nthe unthinkable (especially when high). \r\n\r\ni think a fat forum is fine.',3,0,0,0,'12.81.66.71','en'),(8431,1747,'2001-09-13 06:15:46',0,'to disco','ever hear of Earthquakes?',5,0,0,0,'24.27.26.99','en'),(8432,1747,'2003-05-10 16:09:14',79,'yeti','You insensitive fucks. I dont think that many US citizens, \r\nor human beings gloat over the death of others. Of loss of \r\nfamily or friends. Of destruction of property. It\\\'s \r\ndisgusting to me that you are mixing US politics and human \r\nlives together. Do you think that any of us want to see \r\nanyone die?<br><br>\r\nGrow up.',6,0,0,0,'216.27.183.161','en'),(8433,1747,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','furthermore:\r\n<br><br>\r\n<img src=\"http://www.gee.kz/peter/yc.jpg\">',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(8434,1747,'2001-09-13 08:47:18',0,'Jamazon to Ashley','<P>I wish people would pay more attention before replying. \r\nRead my comment again. The point i was making is that this \r\nwasn\\\'t a *mindless* act of terrorism as people were saying. \r\nI said \\\"remember the terrorists died too\\\" What i meant by \r\nthis was not that we should feel sorry for them. That\\\'s \r\njust stupid.</P>\r\n<P>I was pointing out that this happened for a reason. The \r\nterrorists obviously had a reason for what they did. They \r\ngave up their lives for something they believed in. Why \r\nthey did what they did, i\\\'m sure we will find out sooner or \r\nlater.\r\n</P>\r\n<P>\r\nNow can we *please* stop this bickering. Thousands of \r\npeople lie dead on the streets of downtown manhattan. </P>',1,0,0,0,'217.32.151.146','en'),(8435,1747,'2001-09-13 08:49:44',0,'Jamazon','<p>\r\nI\\\'m just re-reading my last comment and i\\\'d like to point \r\nout that i don\\\'t condone what the terrorists did in any \r\nway, shape or form. Whether they had certain beliefs or \r\nnot, it is still wrong to crash planes into buildings and \r\nkill people.\r\n</p>',1,0,0,0,'217.32.151.146','en'),(8436,1750,'2001-09-13 09:04:55',0,'Jamazon','<p><b>All i can say is i\\\'m glad you\\\'re ok. And you \r\nPeter.</b></p> <p><b>I just heard on the news here that as \r\nmany a 500 British people are still missing, feared \r\ndead.</b></p>\r\n<p><b>This isn\\\'t just an attack against the USA. It\\\'s an \r\nattack against the entire Western World. This is echoed by \r\nNATO in Brussels, who have pledged full military support \r\nfor anything you americans plan on doing in \r\nretaliation</b></p>',1,0,0,0,'217.32.151.146','en'),(8437,1749,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>interesting, weeb. i thought some of those same \r\nthoughts, <i>mourning for the buildings</i>. the mantra for \r\nfinding your way back to the train after partying in the \r\nvillage or any other spot downtown? <i>look for the \r\ntowers</i>. coming back from jersey?<i>look at the \r\ntowers</i>. coming home to nyc from anywhere? <i>look at \r\nthe towers</i>. no more towers to look at.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8438,1748,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<Br><tt>yes, ok here. thanks for caring, you guys, it makes \r\na person feel good. a friend of mine is a rescue worker \r\ndown there- he claims he\\\'s carring a small piece of the \r\nrubble on him daily until he can come to peace with this. \r\nas for me, i\\\'m just sleeping alot and not working much.  \r\nkeep the humanity in mind- there\\\'s tons of people who have \r\nlost so much.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8439,1750,'2001-09-13 12:58:47',0,'kat to Jamazon','i was just saying this to someone yesterday...that there \r\nwere people from all over the world in that building. noone \r\nis left untouched.',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.211','en'),(8440,1752,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','That\\\'s a pretty big gun, dude.',0,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(8441,1749,'2001-09-13 13:14:58',0,'kat','i know what weeb is feeling. i lived in Santa Cruz when the \r\n89 earthquake hit. so much of the media was focused on the \r\ncity and the freeway collapse....i dont think people \r\nrealized how isolated we were. highway 17 was closed for \r\nmonths. our entire downtown was almost completely \r\ndistroyed. my friends and i use to each lunch on Pacific \r\nAve often, it really was the soul of this town. it is not \r\nthe same. and i think this to myself everytime i go down \r\nthere. it will never be the same. .......twelve years \r\nlater, there is still one building that hasn\\\'t been \r\nreplaced by a Gap or Starbucks. it is a gaping wounded \r\npiece of earth surrounded by chainlink fencing. in a way \r\ni\\\'m glad. i would much rather have this reminder than some \r\nsugarcoated attempt at forgetting. people died in this \r\nplace on that day. October 17th. i will not forget.',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.211','en'),(8442,1752,'2001-09-13 13:46:32',0,'Gavin','i dont hunt, mind you, or kill e\\\'er a living thing. i just \r\nlike to shoot clay pigeons and trap.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8443,1752,'2001-09-13 14:02:41',0,'Jamazon','Dude, your one danger dude. With your guns and your \r\nchainsaws. And you\\\'re Welsh.',1,0,0,0,'217.32.151.146','en'),(8444,1752,'2001-09-13 14:05:42',0,'Gavin','well, i\\\'m finnish now, officially. so swinney.org makes it \r\nto finland!  no, i\\\'m not dangerous- i dont want you all to \r\nget the wrong idea- i\\\'m as peace-loving and gentle as any \r\nman alive.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8445,1510,'2001-09-13 14:21:50',0,'Gavin Cruickshank','This is freaky, uncanny, and downright scary, especially \r\nafter the events of this past week.  The news has ripped \r\nthrough an otherwise normally quiet Europe, like nothign \r\nelse.  Wow.  I\\\'m speechless for all of you, especially the \r\nNewyorkers.',2,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8446,1752,'2001-09-13 14:22:45',0,'Jamazon','Once a Welshman, always Welshman. Tom Jones can\\\'t hide it \r\nand neither can you. Shirley Bassey anyone?',4,0,0,0,'217.32.151.146','en'),(8447,1752,'2001-09-13 14:32:08',0,'Gavin','Tom Jones [<i>the welshman with the golden voice!</i>] is \r\nneither vicious or gruff.  Shirley Bassey isn\\\'t a true \r\nWelsh, although sexy.  I am a native of Finland now anyway, \r\nso none of this concernes me.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8448,1752,'2001-09-13 14:47:07',0,'Jamazon','You can\\\'t hide behind you Pseudo-Finnish-Nationalism. They \r\nknow where you are Gavin. And they\\\'re coming to get you.',4,0,0,0,'217.32.151.146','en'),(8449,1752,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','that\\\'s a really nice shotgun. i have been thinking of \r\ngetting one like it, a beretta.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.51','en'),(8450,1747,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','is it really? well, i\\\'m glad you cleared that up for us.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.51','en'),(8451,1752,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','if you want a good shotgun, get a mossburg 590. its teh \r\nshotgun teh u.s marines use. 3000 consecutive shots without \r\nbarrel melt. ',4,0,0,0,'24.43.182.49','en'),(8452,1752,'2001-09-13 17:39:12',0,'leonard','why are you shooting trees? harmless little trees. first \r\nyou cut them down, and then you shoot them! what, do you \r\nwork for the mafia? why you! i bet you smoke cigarettes, \r\nand write letters on yellow legal paper! blasted tree \r\nmurderer. you will pay!',6,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(8453,1752,'2001-09-13