\nnader smells bought, too.  (pardon my french:))\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.9.227','en'),(8540,1762,'2001-09-16 16:13:36',0,'jerry falwell','obviously, you are gay or catholic, most likely just \r\nanother dirty hippie.',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8541,1762,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','ugh.',6,0,0,0,'24.43.182.49','en'),(8542,1753,'2001-09-16 17:54:09',0,'jo','this is the first song oof and i listened to in the car \r\nwhen i picked him up from the airport friday night. that\\\'s \r\nweird.',1,0,0,0,'172.157.221.199','en'),(8543,1762,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','yeah, i\\\'m gay and catholic and straight and muslim and a \r\npagan and a lesbian and a white man and an old asian lady \r\nand just everything. and a hippie and a republican and a \r\ngreen and a fascist and a star and a squirrel and a nut and \r\na doctor. i am the cosmos and beyond. and you are two. just \r\nerase those pencil lines in your mind and just love and BE. \r\nor don\\\'t be. your choice. spread the joy, motherfucker.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.10.56','en'),(8544,1762,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','and in need of a little nappie. excuse me.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.10.56','en'),(8545,1762,'2001-09-16 19:13:28',0,'treetop','::Throws birkenstock at jerry falwell::',0,0,0,0,'172.137.169.25','en'),(8546,1761,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','If you dig <i>Dots And Loops</i> you would probably, or\r\nalready do, enjoy <b>The Sea And Cake</b> and\r\n<b>Broadcast</b> (are amazing).  You should also check out\r\n<i>Polyfusia</i> by <b>Seefeel</b>.  <i>Felt Mountain</i> by\r\n<b>Goldfrapp</b> is also good.  The best thing for breaking\r\ninto <b>any</b> style of music is to have someone who\r\nalready has a very wide grasp of said genre and a lot of\r\nexperience dealing with it.  They are excellent for making\r\nsuggestions and easing you into things with music that is\r\nmore  <i>accessible</i> to a non-fan.  Here are some other\r\nnames you may be interested in checking out: <b>Plaid</b>,\r\n<b>Red Snapper</b>, <b>Speedy J</b> (<i>A Shocking Hobby</i>\r\nis a good album), <b>4 Hero</b>, <b>Orbital</b> is pretty\r\naccessible, <b>Aphex Twin</b>\\\'s <i>Selected Ambient Works\r\nVol. 1</i>, <b>Autechre</b>, <b>&micro;-ziq</b>, <b>Mira\r\nCalix</b>, <b>B12</b>...<br><br>Want me to continue?',1,0,0,0,'64.229.71.182','en'),(8547,1759,'2001-09-16 19:42:23',0,'leonard','i see the way you\\\'re looking at the trees and i don\\\'t like \r\nit. just leave them alone.',6,0,0,0,'209.179.131.131','en'),(8548,1761,'2001-09-16 20:01:02',0,'bmg','<p>i just bought a magazine, first magazine in like a \r\nyear or more for me. I bought it cause it had a Dj \r\nSpooky disk on the cover, the magazine is called nest... \r\nanyway, I am a spooky fan - and this disk has got some \r\ngreat sounds... a gathering of the tribes type feel. pretty \r\ncool. ',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8549,1761,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','Is that Spooky disk a special magazine-only dealie or is it\r\nsomething available via other means?  I have some Spooky and\r\ndig what he\\\'s done.  <i>Songs Of A Dead Drummer</i> is a\r\ngreat release.',2,0,0,0,'64.229.71.182','en'),(8550,1761,'2001-09-16 21:17:50',0,'bmg','it is magazine only. i will post mp3s if you or anyone \r\nelse wishes?',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8551,1761,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt><i>Discovery</i> is a grand record.  Its one of the \r\nfew \\\'house\\\'-ish records i spin regularly. It and the Jaxx\\\'s \r\n<i>Rooty</i>. <i>Harder, better, Faster</i> is a nice song- \r\nLately, I\\\'ve been spinning in my apartment alot and starting \r\nsidewalk mini-parties outside my sub-terranian apartment.  \r\nEveryone, young and old, spanish, black, and white always \r\nlike <i\\\\>Harder, Better</i>... they also like <i>Face to \r\nFace</i> and <i>Too Long</i>.  But by far, the best is \r\n<i>Digital Love</i>.  The first time I heard that track, I \r\nwas rollin in a club downtown, and peaked the very second \r\nthat hard guitar-ish riff kicked in.  It totally blew my \r\nmind and I still love that song.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.242','en'),(8552,1763,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>random personal glimpse: i finally ended it with my \r\nformer lover, and although it makes me pensive at moments \r\n(less and less frequently as time passes), the good feelings \r\nof \\\"my old self\\\" that i have now are overwhelming.  They \r\nmake me very happy in the midst of any sadness. i definitely \r\nreccommend it for anyone teetering on the edge.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.242','en'),(8553,1761,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt><b>oh and BMG:</b> i saw spooky spin once with the \r\nfreight elevator quartet up at columbia\\\'s film school. it \r\nwas awesome- i caught the show in minidisk- i can mp3 it if \r\nyoud be interested...</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.242','en'),(8554,1761,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','nest is a brilliant magazine. they once printed a spread \r\nabout three inmates in a women\\\'s prison, and the \r\ninterior design choices they made when decorating \r\ntheir cells. i plan to resubscribe.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(8555,1761,'2001-09-16 23:04:23',0,'bmg','<a href=\'http://www.lepard.org/mp3s/\' target=new>here</a>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8556,1761,'2001-09-16 23:11:05',0,'bmg','tah petah:<p> and yah, I am interested!</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8557,1762,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','obviously you\\\'re a paranoid freak.',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(8558,1762,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','at whom was that comment directed?\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.5.76','en'),(8559,1762,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','this really pisses me off. the word \\\"freak\\\" comes up again. \r\ni don\\\'t care if you used that word in reference to me or \r\nsomeone else - it strikes me as prejudice. in its own way, \r\nit\\\'s as loaded as \\\"nigger\\\" or \\\"faggot\\\" or \\\"bitch\\\" or \r\n\\\"towelhead\\\" or any of ten thousand other sweet litt