i will.',2,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(8572,1763,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i think the only way to live with a lover is to be sure you \r\nare on equal grounds. with everything. space, money. having \r\nyour own space is key too.',0,0,0,0,'216.27.183.161','en'),(8573,1762,'2001-09-17 06:29:40',0,'jerry falwell','if yall weren\\\'t a bunch of stinky, dirty, filthy hippies - \r\nI\\\'d pray for you. That goes for all you catholics too. Fuck \r\nthe ACLU.',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8574,1762,'2001-09-17 06:33:32',0,'G dubya','<p>I vow to <a \r\nhref=\'http://www.austin360.com/statesman/editions/sunday/new\r\ns_1.html\'>smoke</a> all ya\'ll out, Texas style!!! YEEEEEEEE \r\nHAAAAAAA!!!! YIPPPEEE KIIIIEEEE YIIIIIIEE YAAAAAY \r\nMOTTTTHERRRR FUCKKKKERRRRS!!! <p></p>Whose got the pipe? Papers anybody???</p><p>Can anybody roll a muthafukin joint here???</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8575,1758,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','s5: sometimes i think you take this stuff way too \r\npersonally. i mean that in a nice, supportive way. people \r\ngotta vent, man. they\\\'re probably much healthier doing it \r\nhere than say at their kid\\\'s birthday party--that\\\'s my \r\nopinion.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.183','en'),(8576,632,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','man that was beautiful what your mom wrote. tearing up over \r\nhere. ',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.183','en'),(8577,1760,'2001-09-17 08:05:53',0,'jay','<p>things around me:</p>\r\n<p>Pack of cigarettes (I\\\'m smokin again for the war effort)\r\n<br>\r\nCopy of Grace Paley\\\'s \\\"Wants\\\"<br>\r\nThe remote control to the TV, shoved straight up my ass so \r\nit don\\\'t work no more<br>\r\nCopy of \\\"Chet Baker Sings\\\"<br>\r\nThe desire to be anywhere in time but right now, even the \r\nSpanish Inquisition<br>\r\nBad dreams, insomnia<br>\r\nMy ever-present drinking problem<br>\r\nA few Ativan, not prescribed to me (popular among \r\nhousewives in the 70s, takes the \\\"edge\\\" off)<br>\r\nAn email from my mother telling me to drive back east, \r\ndon\\\'t fly.<br>\r\nReminder note to call unemployment<br>\r\nA dictionary and a thesaurus.<br></P>\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'66.32.27.192','en'),(8578,1758,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i don\\\'t think people need to vent as much as they do. i \r\nalso don\\\'t believe in support groups. hired clowns are \r\nworse for children than violent parental outbursts. oral \r\nsex isn\\\'t sodomy.',6,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(8579,1760,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','on my desk: clutter, trash, cat hair, uneaten popcorn, \r\nwires. canned air. bombay sapphire. juice bottles. \r\nmoldy coffee cup. snow globes. nipple clamps. dead \r\nbatteries.',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(8580,1759,'2001-09-17 09:27:53',0,'Jamazon','<p>\r\nGavin sees a tree<br>\r\nGets this urge to cut it down<br>\r\nChainsaw! Cut! cut! cut!\r\n</p>',1,0,0,0,'217.32.146.34','en'),(8581,1760,'2001-09-17 09:33:09',0,'Jamazon','<p>\r\nA piece of paper with phone numbers written on it that i \r\ndon\\\'t recognise<br>\r\nA pen<br>\r\nThe PHP 4 Bible<br>\r\nA magazine cut out of a cow with big udders<br>\r\nA black 3.5\\\" floppy disk<br>\r\nA fear of World War\r\n</p>',1,0,0,0,'217.32.146.34','en'),(8582,1761,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','Yeah, if you want to get turned on to <b>Orbital</b>, go buy\r\nthe album <a\r\nhref=\\\"http://www.cdnow.com/cgi-bin/mserver/SID=1583845067/pagename=/RP/CDN/FIND/album.html/artistid=ORBITAL/itemid=1201227\\\"\r\ntarget=\\\"buy_me\\\">Orbital 2</a>.  It\\\'s still my favourite\r\nOrbital release, even after all these years.',1,0,0,0,'64.229.71.182','en'),(8583,1763,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to le et. al.','<br><tt>amen. space, particularly.  moving from a one-\r\nbedroom that I shared with my lover to a 5 bedroom that is \r\nall mine has made me a different person, completely.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8584,1765,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>Gavin, you just plain kick ass.  I think I want \r\nyour life! <i>\\\"best friendly\\\"</i></tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8585,1758,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to s5','<br><tt>the comments are just useless rind, usually.  the \r\ntrue fruit is in the articles.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8586,1003,'2001-09-17 12:17:28',0,'Gavin Cruickshank','Le, I think you are Cool.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8587,1759,'2001-09-17 12:18:55',0,'Gavin Cruickshank','<BR>Lets not be wankers.<BR>\r\nI do not kill trees for sport.<BR>\r\nI live forestry.<BR>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8588,1765,'2001-09-17 12:31:21',0,'Jamazon','Gavin. You\\\'re like Action Man or something. I never knew \r\nWelsh people could be so kickass.',1,0,0,0,'217.32.146.34','en'),(8589,1764,'2001-09-17 12:36:37',0,'Jamazon','they say that smell is our oldest sense. Because it\\\'s been \r\nwith us throughout our entire evolution it is entirely \r\nintegrated within our brains making it the most powerfull \r\nsense we have.<BR><BR>I\\\'ve seen reports of Altzheimers \r\npatients being helped to recover memories with the use of \r\nsmells from their childhoods.',1,0,0,0,'217.32.146.34','en'),(8590,1764,'2001-09-17 12:39:47',0,'Doktor','good point, peter. i\\\'ve discovered similar associations \r\nwith smells before, for sure.  i also remember jody foster \r\nin <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/6302271967/qid=\r\n1000730305/sr=1-3/ref=sc_v_3/002-9304272-\r\n8548018\\\">Candleshoe</a> associating the strong scent of \r\nlilacs with some vague but important childhood memory... \r\ncool.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8591,1764,'2001-09-17 13:36:52',0,'Joanna','I have big smell associations also.  Probably the strongest \r\nis the smell of rum, which always takes me back to New \r\nYears Eve 95/96 when I was drinking a lot of rum&coke and I \r\nfirst made out with a boy and subsequently became \r\nheadoverheelssmitten.  ',1,0,0,0,'203.97.2.242','en'),(8592,1764,'2001-09-17 13:43:00',0,'Garbageman','dude, that same hting happened to me with gin!  cool. now, \r\neverytime i smell or taste it, i get taken back to good \r\nmemories. i like this post. it made me stop and think of \r\nsomething i haven\\\'t considered.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8593,1766,'2001-09-17 13:46:30',0,'Jamazon','Is this about me?',1,0,0,0,'217.32.146.34','en'),(8594,1766,'2004-07-27 05:00:32',578,'NetfÃ¶ng!','...if you want it to be',4,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8595,1760,'2001-09-17 14:35:02',0,'ghost','vague passionate words, overflowing infatuation, shadowy \r\nerotic pictures',1,0,0,0,'32.102.109.216','en'),(8596,1761,'2001-09-17 14:55:58',0,'bmg','i just happen to have a promo copy of Orbital - the \r\naltogether... i\'ll just go ahead and post that too.<a \r\nhref=\'http://www.lepard.org/mp3s/\' target=new>here</a>, for one \r\nday only.',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8597,1758,'2001-09-17 15:01:04',0,'bmg','what if best friendly had a <em>lulu</em> pink shade? \r\nburn, burn could have a dark color?',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8598,1758,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>...and i might add, i often contribute to the \r\nuseless rind.  i do savor the fruit, though, and contribute \r\nwhen i can.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8599,1758,'2001-09-17 15:35:26',0,'Jamazon','I weed in my pants.',0,0,0,0,'217.32.146.34','en'),(8600,1767,'2001-09-17 16:16:18',0,'leonard','this made me all sweaty. suck it.',6,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(8601,1767,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>nice story!  i liked the bit about watching someone \r\nsleep. i like watching lover\\\'s sleep while the sun rises \r\nover them.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8602,1767,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','austin, you should be writing for money. you got the goods.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.5.10','en'),(8603,1767,'2001-09-17 17:10:41',0,'Private Writer','a writer for <i>moooney</i>...',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8604,1767,'2001-09-17 17:13:48',0,'kat','down a few blocks from the country club is a bus station \r\nthat sits on the very edge of Cattown. you can sleep there \r\nwithout hassle. then when you wake breakfast is just a \r\nshort jaunt to the right, deathway 17 a glance to the left.',1,0,0,0,'32.102.109.216','en'),(8605,1761,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','I have that promo as well.  I wasn\\\'t so impressed with The \r\nAlltogether.... I enjoyed <i>Middle Of Nowhere</i>, \r\nthough.  Alltogether let me down.  I think there were three \r\ntracks on it I enjoyed.  Then again, I only listened to the \r\nalbum once, so perhaps I should give it another listen and \r\nI might actually enjoy it more than I did (not) the first \r\ntime.',1,0,0,0,'141.117.243.130','en'),(8606,1761,'2001-09-17 17:44:13',0,'treetop to bmg','you are tha bomb :)',0,0,0,0,'172.129.130.81','en'),(8607,1762,'2001-09-17 17:48:42',0,'treetop','rolls alabama thumpers',0,0,0,0,'172.129.130.81','en'),(8608,1761,'2001-09-17 17:53:54',0,'bmg','<p>yah, I agree fuzzy... it let me down too, but i think i \r\nwas let down cause i expected so much... i have given it \r\na good listen to in the past couple of months - and \r\nthough its not my favorite, i like it... some of the songs I \r\nhear and think to myself, \\\"yah, I remember that song, its \r\nallrigh...\\\" then I realize that it is not an old song but a \r\nnew one... it kinda grabbed me later on... I didn\\\'t like, \r\nmaybe understand is a better description, bjork when \r\n<em>debut</em> came out... some three years later I \r\npopped it in and fell in love with it... </p><p>treetop - \r\nthats why they call me the bass master general. (not \r\nbass as in fish)...',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8609,1758,'2001-09-17 17:59:53',0,'jedgar','and don\\\'t forget to buy those stocks!',3,0,0,0,'156.153.255.243','en'),(8610,1768,'2001-09-17 18:02:51',0,'bmg','<p>Hey, dirty, baby I got your money <br>\r\nDon\'t your worry, I said hey. <br>\r\nBaby I got your money </p>\r\n<p>Hey, dirty, baby I got your money <br>\r\nDon\'t your worry, I said hey. <br>\r\nBaby I got your money </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Yo! so I glanced at the girls, girls glanced at me \r\n<br>\r\nI whispered in their ear, wana be with me? <br>\r\nYou wana look pretty though, in my video <br>\r\nOl\' dirty on the hat and I let you all know <br>\r\nJust dance! if you caught up in the holy ghost trance \r\n<br>\r\nIf you stop! ima put the killer ants in your pants <br>\r\nI\'m the O-D-B as you can see <br>\r\nEvery eye, don\'t you be watching me <br>\r\nI don\'t want no problems cause I put you down <br>\r\nIn the ground where you can not be found <br>\r\nI\'m just dirt dog trying to make sum bunny <br>\r\nSo give me my streaks and give me my honey <br>\r\nRadio, yes all day, everyday <br>\r\nRecognize I\'m a fool and ya luuuuuuuuuuv me! <br>\r\nNone of you nmph better look at me funny <br>\r\nNmph you know my name now give me my money! \r\n<br></p><p>\r\nhook till fade with odb sayin shit\r\n</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8611,1767,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','i read the whole thing and i really enjoyed it.  it felt \r\nlike it was written in kind of a sleepy-eyed sunday \r\nafternoon trance.  it reminded me of my drive down the \r\ncoast yesterday.  sleeping bags make me sweat.',1,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(8612,1761,'2001-09-17 18:07:35',0,'The Arcives Speak!','<br>\r\nYou are a beautiful female. He is a black jetta with \r\nbooming bass in the trunk. You are walking down the street. \r\nYou hear the sound of raw bass vibrating through the air. \r\nYou feel it in your spine. You get excited. Perhaps a \r\nlittle wet. You want to know who has this sexual effect on \r\nyou. Who is this sound? Who is the man that goes thump in \r\nthe night?!\r\n<br><br>\r\n<b>The Bass Master General has entered the room.</b> ',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8613,1761,'2001-09-17 18:15:09',0,'bmg','haha!  i do like to make bass. \r\n',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8614,1763,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','mental space too-- space to make mistakes, space to be \r\nspazzy, space to be spacy. oh yes. space is sexy.',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(8615,546,'2001-09-17 19:29:02',0,'Mighty blue nothing','shut up Matt.',0,0,0,0,'206.224.71.189','en'),(8616,1768,'2001-09-17 19:34:06',0,'ghost to bmg','=)',1,0,0,0,'32.102.109.216','en'),(8617,1765,'2001-09-17 19:56:17',0,'PartyTron','I read about Gavin on his interesting site and E-mailed him. \r\nHe reccommended I come look at this amasing site. I do like \r\nit, although I do not understand it. I hope I do not do \r\nsomething bad by posting here and you not knowing me, \r\nmeanwhile! Thank you, {PT}.',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.242','en'),(8618,1767,'2001-09-17 21:21:51',0,'byob','Bring Your Own Blanket',0,0,0,0,'216.175.99.230','en'),(8619,1767,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','i read this twice. it is very difficult to wage war against \r\nyou when you are such a heartthrob.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.99.230','en'),(8620,1767,'2001-09-17 21:44:13',0,'leonard','i read this again and it still makes me sweaty! so go suck \r\nit!',6,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(8621,1769,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>it seems that we are all doing a lot of dreaming. \r\nwaking dreams included. do not turn on the television. If \r\nwe keep listening to our dreams, not \\\"dream\\\" as in \r\npeewee\\\' s bike dream or my dream to go to thailand, \r\nbut those real moments of hysteria that wake us over \r\nand over, and images we cant explain, we will \r\nunderstand this week better. and you can be a writer, \r\nand not a worried housewife, or at least both,  and not \r\ndead.</p>',0,0,0,0,'216.175.99.230','en'),(8622,1769,'2001-09-17 21:57:24',0,'kat','this is the best jayper post i ever read',4,0,0,0,'32.102.91.115','en'),(8623,1768,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>on a day when you cant make up your mind about \r\nmusic, might i suggest  five cds on \\\"shuffle\\\"? you have \r\nto have a five player for it i guess.</p>',0,0,0,0,'216.175.99.230','en'),(8624,1753,'2001-09-17 22:06:38',0,'beck',':)',0,0,0,