,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','And now, from the boys who brought you war, recession, and \r\ncriminal campaign capers, the Republicans present, a Tricky \r\nDick entertainment spectacular, ladies and gentlemen, give \r\nit up for: America\\\'s New War!',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.69','en'),(8637,1769,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','well, i like you. i love you. how about that? i wasn\\\'t \r\nsaying that to be mean. i\\\'m just calling them like i see \r\nthem and trying to offer encouragement.<BR><BR>nobody\\\'s \r\ngoing anywhere. we all might as well try to get along \r\nand stop being so ly offended. me included.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.9.59','en'),(8638,1769,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','that was \\\"easily\\\" offended.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.9.59','en'),(8639,1763,'2001-09-18 01:36:47',0,'a bitter film','<a \r\nhref=\\\"http;//members.aol.com/sshkdwnst/asf/lifeasaguy.asf\\\">L\r\nife\r\nas a guy</a>',0,0,0,0,'172.138.75.64','en'),(8640,1761,'2001-09-18 01:37:07',0,'kat to Fuzzy','you are seeing <i>HER</i>!!! on fuck i am so insanely \r\njealous. kim and i tried to get tickets to the Oaktown \r\nshow. they were SOLD OUT in five minutes (or so their story \r\ngoes). i would do wild crazy things for the person who \r\ncould take me to that show. wild crazy everlasting \r\ngobstopper kinda things.',4,0,0,0,'32.102.109.248','en'),(8641,1763,'2001-09-18 01:38:40',0,'use this one...','<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://members.aol.com/sshkdwnst/asf/lifeasaguy.asf\\\">L\r\nife\r\nas a guy</a>',0,0,0,0,'172.138.75.64','en'),(8642,1770,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon L','See them walking hand in hand across the bridge at \r\nmidnight. Heads turning as the lights flashing out are so \r\nbright. And walk right out to the four line track. There\\\'s \r\na camera rolling on her back. On her back. And I sense a \r\nrhythm humming in a frenzy all the way down her spine.\r\n',4,0,0,0,'32.102.109.248','en'),(8643,1762,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','Hmm. I\\\'m trying to think of way of raising the bar in terms \r\nof oversensitivity, but this thread has really left me hard-\r\npressed. Holy shit, do we need to sit down and come to a \r\nconsensus before someone is allowed to have an individual \r\nthought? Can I say this? Can I not say this? Can I have \r\nthis idea? Can I use these words to have this idea? Should \r\nwe sit in a circle and come up with a Correct Way of \r\nThinking, xerox it, mail it to family and loved ones, \r\nxxxooo???????\r\n',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(8644,1770,'2001-09-18 03:07:43',0,'pauline kael','kiss kiss, bang bang.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.10.129','en'),(8645,1768,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','when the film changes faster than the soundtrack can \r\npace.',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(8646,546,'2001-09-18 03:40:11',0,'jo','wow. i really needed to read that old comment of mine just \r\nnow. fortuitous.',1,0,0,0,'172.145.170.17','en'),(8647,1772,'2001-09-18 03:50:27',0,'shirt police','put a shirt on!',2,0,0,0,'209.179.134.53','en'),(8648,1772,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>When I first watched the <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.powersof10.com/powers/eames/statio\r\nn_86.html\\\">Eames film</a> about the Polaroid SX-70, \r\ntears welled up in my eyes. I get sentimental about \r\nthings like that the same way old guys get nostalgic \r\nabout historical baseball games. oh, hold me.</p>\r\n<p>nice pics, pete. yr lookin good too.</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(8649,1773,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','why does the sky look so much bigger there?',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(8650,1764,'2001-09-18 05:56:19',0,'sarah','<p>our olfactory nerves are tangled up with the limbic \r\nsystem of the brain, i think, which is the emotional sort \r\nof processing area. i like that. also i think it is funny \r\nthat partial explanations for random things are my most \r\nfrequent contribution to conversations. i associate \r\neverything :)',0,0,0,0,'207.107.254.248','en'),(8651,1769,'2002-04-12 05:27:03',57,'weeb to matt','a litt