n spite of its charm, it\\\'s lost me many a grand photo. i \r\nonce snapped like 5 shots of a feathery-mullett guy on the \r\njersey transit train wearing a jersey that said \\\"SWINNEY\\\" \r\non the back, but i was crestfallen- they all blurred. ahh, \r\nto have a digital camera. i\\\'m going to have to break down \r\none of these days and mature past old-skool analog.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8730,1778,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>in the apartment i just moved into, there\\\'s a \r\nbuilding-front <i>right</i> next to mine that i noticed \r\nalways seems to be hopping.  as my window is at sidewalk \r\nlevel, i spin tunes alot for the people that loiter around \r\nthere for hours, day after day. their favorites are <i>ring \r\nmy bell</i>, <i>funky town</i>, <i>tsop</i>, and for some \r\nreason <i>sweet dreams are made of this</i>, among other \r\nthings. they seem to be a disco-y crowd, but i\\\'m turning \r\nthem on to house.  well, to make a long story short, i just \r\nfound out that the building there is a half-way house that \r\nserves the community in the treatment of drug-abuse, and \r\nthe fine folks that loiter there are its esteemed patrons \r\nwho are required to check in several times a day. hmm. i \r\nalso discovered a small notice on the building front that \r\nperscribes <i>double</i> the penalties for anyone violating \r\nany drug possession/distribution/usage laws within 500 feet \r\nof the building. gulp.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8731,1778,'2001-09-19 11:39:18',0,'Jamie','So you\\\'ve moved to a good area then',1,0,0,0,'217.32.126.109','en'),(8732,1778,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>its actually a fairly nice neighborhood... i was \r\nquite surprised. it also happens to be the most \r\ninconspicuous and grandiose looking halfway-hosue i\\\'ve ever \r\nseen!</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8733,1773,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','digital cameras are much worse for high speed action \r\nphotos. i\\\'ve had good luck with my canon AE-1, which i \r\npicked up at a second-hand store a while back for not \r\nvery much.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(8734,1775,'2001-09-19 12:07:51',0,'Jamazon','<br>\r\nPoision from above<br>\r\nGet up close and chop them down<br>\r\nDeath to all the trees',1,0,0,0,'217.32.126.109','en'),(8735,1773,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i have an old manual slr which i may have to bust \r\nout...</tt> ',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8736,1775,'2004-07-27 05:00:32',578,'NetfÃ¶ng!','Gavin, is this <i>really</i> you? I found it on Jamazon\'s \r\nsite. I think you have a <i>super</i> haircut, by the \r\nway.<br>\r\n<img \r\nsrc=\"http://www.gavincruickshank.fi/images/my_info/me/016.jp\r\ng\">',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8737,1775,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>Woah... the resemblance to David St. Hubbins of <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.spinaltap.com\\\"><i>Spinal Tap</i></a> fame \r\nis uncanny!</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8738,1773,'2001-09-19 14:02:55',0,'ronald mcdonald','s5 is the hamburglar in disguise',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.24','en'),(8739,1773,'2001-09-19 14:12:47',0,'tenacious d','flarna is an angel in disguise',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(8740,1773,'2001-09-19 14:13:53',0,'Gavin Cruikshank','<a href=\\\"http://www.jamazon.co.uk/index.php?\r\narticle=73\\\">Robble, robble</a>!',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8741,1774,'2001-09-19 14:46:57',0,'Don Quixote','\r\n<P>i only miss you in my sleep. \r\n<P>i only miss you when my pride lets my heart speak. \r\n<P>but all i wanna do is miss you tonight. \r\n<P>all i wanna do is miss you tonight.',1,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(8742,1773,'2001-09-19 15:10:23',0,'Gavin Cruikshank','When i think about you i touch myself',1,0,0,0,'217.32.126.109','en'),(8743,1773,'2001-09-19 15:11:31',0,'Gavin Cruikshank','I did not post that last comment. someone is dillying with \r\nmy identity!',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8744,1780,'2001-09-19 16:00:30',0,'you','bet\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.9.62','en'),(8745,1780,'2001-09-19 16:15:03',0,'rob brezsny','you should read my book.',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(8746,1778,'2001-09-19 16:47:55',0,'erbie','i live next door to a halfway house, too.  its inhabitants \r\ndon\\\'t often dance.  doesn\\\'t seem like they have much \r\nenergy.  if i could infuse them with a disco vibe i \r\ndefinitely would.  it\\\'s a very funky scene.  my own mini \r\nmegacities.  this movie i saw last night megacities has \r\nleft me in a stupor.  it\\\'s very very good.',1,0,0,0,'64.105.32.155','en'),(8747,1774,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','tori amos in straight black hair is just wrong. i want the \r\nold tori back!',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(8748,1774,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to weeb and peter','it looks like tori is in fact pulling a thorough Cindy \r\nSherman. her new album, according to my informant  \r\nAgent Jayper Double 0, contains \\\"all covers; songs \r\nwritten by male artists from a female perspective\\\". Im \r\nall for it. Im dying to hear it, actually. and the photos \r\nshow her in all manner of hairstyle, so I dont think you \r\nneed to worry that she got a makeover, weeb. WIGS!',0,0,0,0,'216.175.108.100','en'),(8749,1780,'2001-09-19 18:05:36',0,'jo','<font size=1>i hated breszny\\\'s book.</font>',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(8750,1762,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','thanks.',6,0,0,0,'24.43.182.49','en'),(8751,1780,'2001-09-19 18:43:39',0,'what','...does brezny\\\'s book have to do with this?',5,0,0,0,'32.102.64.24','en'),(8752,1781,'2001-09-19 19:55:08',0,'trouble','life is ripe with eery parallel these days, hidden meanings \r\nand similarities abound.  spooky.',1,0,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(8753,1780,'2001-09-19 20:10:48',0,'brezsny\\\'s book','contains a poetically wordy personal ad with \\\"cosmic\\\" \r\nlanguage wrapped into it. maybe more than one \\\"crazy \r\nwacky\\\" personal ad with figurative embellishments and \r\nhyper hypertext.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.88.156','en'),(8754,1774,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','i heard it has a cover of raining blood on it. i\\\'m looking\r\nforward to hearing that. my flatmate is apparently tori\\\'s #1\r\nfan so i\\\'m betting it won\\\'t be too difficult.',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(8755,1774,'2001-09-19 20:19:31',0,'agent orange','here\\\'s all the <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.toriamos.com/gallery.php\\\">Wigs</a> you can \r\nhandle. ',1,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(8756,1780,'2001-09-19 20:20:57',0,'brezny','i am a bullshit artist hear me roar',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(8757,1781,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','my parents have the following cats:<br>\r\n<br>\r\nBono:  a big black bruiser, with a tiny meow (like mike \r\ntyson)<br>\r\nBeatrice:  a small, slinky calico.  a snobish loner who \r\nwill rip you a new one if you pet her wrong.<br>\r\nFat Sausage:  a missile-shaped little blackie with the \r\nperfect mix of affection and sly cat-coolness.<br>\r\n<br>',2,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(8758,1781,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','when i lived with The Shut-Ins<tm>, we had the following \r\ncats:<br>\r\n<br>\r\npricilla: the queen of all cats. eats food with her dainty \r\npaws. hunts and kills any new kittens who come near. is \r\ntotally buff. most likely does kitty-push-ups while we \r\nsleep.<br>\r\nmanilla: sad little tiny kitty who has incurred the wrath of \r\npricilla. i wish i had photos of their steel-cage death \r\nmatch. poor manilla finally freaked out and ran away.<br>\r\nthrillah: brother of manilla. HUGE. GIGANTIC. has no balance. \r\nfalls off stuff. likes to make out. nibbles on ears. looks \r\nnot unlike david duchophony.<br>\r\nweird waiter: pricilla\\\'s girlfriend. who came down from a \r\nhole in the ceiling.<br>\r\njudas: the gangsta cat who lives in the hall. has matching \r\nscars on his cheeks, black teeth and a bit off ear. he walks \r\nyou from one end of the hall to the other.<br>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(8759,1780,'2001-09-19 21:32:37',0,'ghost','when i wrote this [february i think] i was just daydreaming \r\nabout being in the Catina waiting for some mysterious sexy \r\nHarrison Ford type to come along that i could seduce.\r\n\r\n<p><i>okay...so sue me for being a kid of the 70\\\'s</i></p>',4,0,0,0,'32.102.109.127','en'),(8760,1338,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','HIKING.',5,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(8761,1781,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','<br>when bubba and i lived in the House of Commons, there \r\nwas a cat we affectionately called \\\"Fucker\\\".<br>\r\neach foot on Fucker had 7 or 8 toes.<br>\r\nhe was a freak.<br>\r\nwe also called him \\\"Fingaz\\\", and \\\"Mr. Hands\\\".<br>\r\none did not fuck with Fucker, if you know what i mean.<br>',3,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(8762,1338,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','<i>hitch</i>-hiking is a good way to flee a two ton bison \r\non catalina island.',3,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(8763,1338,'2001-09-19 23:17:51',0,'dude','what\\\'s up?\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(8764,1338,'2001-09-19 23:18:07',0,'bro','chillin. what;s up with you?\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(8765,1338,'2001-09-19 23:18:18',0,'dude','chillin chillin\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(8766,1780,'2001-09-19 23:45:26',0,'I want to be a cowboy','and you can be my cowgirl',0,0,0,0,'172.163.55.223','en'),(8767,1781,'2001-09-20 02:25:17',0,'jo','dude. bono is such a good cat name!',1,0,0,0,'172.173.114.245','en'),(8768,1774,'2001-09-20 02:28:10',0,'jo','mmmmm. <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.toriamos.com/gallery/bitmaps/characters/Tor\r\niBlackseethrough.jpg\\\">that\\\'s nice</a>.',1,0,0,0,'172.173.114.245','en'),(8769,155,'2001-09-20 02:29:34',0,'seattle','must be 65% barbarian.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.17.32','en'),(8770,604,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','you and me both, sister.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.17.32','en'),(8771,1782,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>Ok, then.  <i>Now</i> post the Trish story.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.255','en'),(8772,1784,'2001-09-20 02:50:23',0,'ghost','i once lived in a small warehouse in what we call out here \r\nlittle mexico. it had three deadbolts plus the door handle \r\nlock. it had a bathroom...but no shower. there was no \r\nkitchen. it was a warehouse. i lived there by myself. i was \r\nsixteen.',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.238','en'),(8773,1774,'2001-09-20 03:21:46',0,'thom','Been thinking about you, and there\\\'s no rest, \r\nshit I still love you, still see you in bed. \r\nBut I\\\'m playing with myself, and what do you care \r\nwhen the other men are far, far better. ',1,0,0,0,'24.27.31.133','en'),(8774,845,'2001-09-20 04:53:32',0,'treetop','fish tacos?',0,0,0,0,'172.156.141.6','en'),(8775,1782,'2001-09-20 07:41:37',0,'green','life is ssoooooooooooooo boring rite now.\r\nfly me to NY for 6 days',6,0,0,0,'216.67.100.68','en'),(8776,845,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','-',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(8777,1781,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','today austin called my cat \\\"yorca of the floor seas\\\"',4,0,0,0,'216.27.183.161','en'),(8778,1781,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>for some reason, in quickly glancing through these \r\ncomments, i momentarily perceived the last one as reading \"Yo, RCA get \r\nthe floozies\". not that my interpretation has any relevance \r\nhere, but i thought it was amusing, unless your cat <i>is</i> a floozie.</tt>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8779,1784,'2001-09-20 12:03:30',0,'anonymous new yorker','i hate that fucker. he harasses me incessantly each time i \r\ngo to the west side market',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8780,1784,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>yes, for some reason, the previous tennant \r\ninstalled mucho locks on the place.  <i>maybe they knew \r\nsomething i dont know</i>, or maybe they were just \r\nparanoid. there\'s even three locks on the basement service \r\ndoor, that appears to have been cemented/welded/sealed shut \r\neons ago.  my friend says three locks are better feng shui \r\nthan two, and especially four.  maybe that was the reasoning.<br><br>i\'ve never \r\nexperimented with it, but i surmise that i could completely \r\nremove my apartment door, and it would be completely safe, \r\nalbeit a bit drafty. its a good building with good people. \r\nthey\'d probably come in and hang out and watch cable.  the \r\nother day a fellow tennant apologized profusely for like 5 \r\nminutes because her dog, upon passing me in the hall, \r\nwagged his tail and it tapped my leg. those types of people \r\ndon\'t thieve, usually.<br><br>\r\nits only the half-way house next door that shakes my \r\nconfidence, and even then, not in thievery.  the thing that \r\nworries me there is that the top of my window is usually \r\ncracked and open to get a breeze.  i\'ve noticed that its at \r\nside-walk waste level.  the half-way-ers have a bad habit \r\nof urinating near that end of the street. i fear those two \r\nworlds will someday collide, leaving me with quite a \r\nproblem.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8781,1786,'2001-09-20 13:00:27',0,'Jamie','i think i love you. And your missus...',6,0,0,0,'217.32.149.145','en'),(8782,1786,'2001-09-20 13:13:27',0,'Analyst','It appears that she is making a gesture or some sort, \r\nperhaps approximating the dimensions of Gavin\\\'s genetalia.  \r\nOr, perhaps she\\\'s re-enacting Gojira\\\'s trampling of Tokyo.  \r\nYeah, thats more like it.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8783,1785,'2001-09-20 13:17:06',0,'wolfwood','i would love not to feel real. reality hurts.',1,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(8784,1785,'2001-09-20 13:52:12',0,'Rick Springfield','you know i\\\'s wishin\\\' i had Jesse\\\'s Girl; how can i find a \r\nwoman like that?!',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8785,1785,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','I like to dream.  Someone told me last night that the way I \r\nmove makes him think I\\\'ll float away at any minute.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(8786,1785,'2001-09-20 13:56:52',0,'essemar\\\'s bad advice','You gotta Zen that shit!!!!  You\\\'re outta control and the \r\nmore you try to control the more outta control you get.  \r\nJust let go and keep your eyes open.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(8787,1783,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','[<i>mouth open plaintively</I>] chirp! chirp!',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(8788,1786,'2001-09-20 14:26:05',0,'jo','is she being a little teapot?',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(8789,1785,'2001-09-20 14:28:04',0,'Stoner to Ess','<br><tt>yes, in scarcely perceptable ways, you undulate \r\nwhen you walk and talk and gesture. its quite ethereal for \r\nsuch a person of substance.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8790,1783,'2004-07-27 05:00:32',578,'NetfÃ¶ng!','lay off the joe and get a more sane shift, fuzzkins!',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8791,1786,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>I\\\'d have to wager that she\\\'s either doing an anti-\r\nrain-dance (which I would do for <i>that</i> view!) or an \r\ninterpretive dance entitled \\\"Gavin is Truly the Mack\\\". \r\n<i>\\\'best friendly\\\' for real...</i></tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8792,1786,'2001-09-20 15:02:32',0,'Jamie','Are you the real Gavin Cruickshank? ',1,0,0,0,'217.32.149.145','en'),(8793,1786,'2001-09-20 15:08:08',0,'ghost','i have been to Inverness. then somehow i ended up in \r\nOklahoma. i think Gavin should visit Oklahoma. it would be \r\ninteresting to see what he would do there.',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.155','en'),(8794,1786,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','wonderful.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8812,1787,'2001-09-20 18:14:50',0,'For the Record','Peter never said it was <i>\\\"more \\\'real\\\' than anything else \r\nwritten on this site\\\"</i>. \\\'best friendly\\\'.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8795,1786,'2001-09-20 15:27:57',0,'Jamie','Someone is just posting the gavin photos here i \r\nwager.\r\n\r\n',4,0,0,0,'217.32.149.145','en'),(8813,1787,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>Thats right. I happen to enjoy the extrmemely <i>high \r\ncontent</i> of very real and intelligent writing on this \r\nsite, and hold many of the writers in high esteem.  Deep in a very inebriated state last night, I \r\nrequested this article- at the time, I had some cosmic \r\ninsight that made it seem <i>really</i> important for everyone to read, which of \r\ncourse I can\'t recall now for the life of me, ha...maybe it seemed more pressing to hear the story elaborated on in person. Maybe its cause I\'m bouncing back from a sordidly failed relationship, who knows.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8796,1785,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','taoists believe that, ultimately, we do not exist. they also \r\nhave certain practices, wherein, they do not have sex, live \r\napart from society and each other, view food as medicine and \r\nvice versa, and, as a result, live forever. so there are \r\ntradeoffs made.<BR><BR>if you want to feel more grounded in \r\nreality, less spacy, open up your heart chakra. the easiest \r\nways to do this, if you don\\\'t do yoga or qijong, are to \r\nsing, wear green shirts or hold green stones over your \r\nbreastbone, and put yourself last and others first \r\nsometimes. practice acts of charity. if somebody asks you \r\nfor money on the street, consider giving them a dollar. i\\\'m \r\nnot saying give money to everybody to asks. do that in any \r\nbig city, and you\\\'ll be broke before long. but if there\\\'s \r\nsomebody who asks like they genuinely need it, why not? what \r\nwere you going to do with that buck? it takes a lot to ask \r\nsomebody for money. try it sometime.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.5.186','en'),(8797,1787,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>Ahh, a refreshing story of reality.  Although I do \r\nremember, from the bowels of last night\\\'s haze, ranting on \r\nand on about how I prefer stories that fit all on one \r\nscreen, I can\\\'t remember specifically why I was so obsessed \r\nwith this story. It just amuses me for some reason and \r\nrings true somehow.  Thanks for posting it...</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8798,1786,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','she\\\'s doing that thing you\\\'d do if somebody poured a \r\nbucket of water on your head. you suck the breath in, \r\nand your arms go <BR><BR>\\\"i\\\'m a student of human \r\nmoves.\\\":)\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.5.186','en'),(8799,1786,'2001-09-20 16:22:21',0,'Jamie','Cheers\r\n',1,0,0,0,'217.32.149.145','en'),(8814,1789,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','When I was in grades seven and eight, I was in a Kickboxing\r\nclass.  Kickboxing was fun.  I think that was a rather bad\r\ntime in my life to be involved in something like that,\r\nthough.  Unable to appreciate/care enough.  And then I went\r\nto highschool and discovered the drugs(TM).  Then it was all\r\nover.',1,0,0,0,'64.229.90.24','en'),(8800,1786,'2001-09-20 16:51:06',0,'jo','wow. wow! intrigue, intrigue.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(8801,1786,'2001-09-20 16:57:23',0,'Sick Police','i like the rants',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8802,1783,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','The highlight of that lecture came <b>after</b> I wrote\r\nthat, when my bag suddenly slowly slid off my desk onto the\r\nfloor.  It was really loud and everyone, including the prof\r\nstopped and stared at me.  I just kind of looked around,\r\nlaughed and picked my bag up.  Meanwhile the friends seated\r\naround me where shaking their heads in shame.<br><br>Reminds\r\nme of the time I shouted <b><i>\\\"Screw you, ya old\r\nbastard!\\\"</i></b> at my Computational Theory prof back in\r\nMarch of this year.  That was spot on.',1,0,0,0,'64.229.90.24','en'),(8803,1785,'2001-09-20 17:17:35',0,'ERROR; Thief','You have gotten to this page because your were linked to \r\nfiles on our server (http://www.toonamiarsenal.com/) from \r\nan outside source. Zogg and TylerL do not appreciate having \r\ntheir files leeched, and as such have instituted this \r\nsystem. Here\\\'s what to do if you were refered here by... \r\n<BR><BR>\r\nA