Man-Pride</i>.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8809,1786,'2001-09-20 18:01:59',0,'rant','....i\'m getting sick of seeing links to other sites every \r\ntime i visit swinney. <i>hey come visit my site, read the \r\nweird conversation there! this guy came here from \r\nmy site!</i> what is up with this? the last time this happened some really cool people quit posting on swinney. does this \r\nhave to happen again?',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.155','en'),(8811,1787,'2003-07-24 15:44:23',165,'joker','is the moral to this story supposed to be, don\\\'t get \r\ninvolved with people you don\\\'t meet face to face? why does \r\nPeter think of it as more \\\'real\\\' than anything else written \r\non this site? and what would Tara\\\'s side of the story be?',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.155','en'),(8810,1787,'2004-07-27 05:00:32',578,'NetfÃ¶ng!','I don\\\'t get it.  Why were you all \\\"please dont let that be \r\nher\\\"? Or was she <i>exiting</i> the frat house?',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8815,1789,'2004-07-27 05:00:32',578,'NetfÃ¶ng! to Fuzz','i hear you, man. some of us take our bruises and punches in \r\ndifferent ways.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8816,1784,'2001-09-20 18:29:41',0,'ty','all you have to do is to go postal on his ass, one good \r\ntime. grab him by his grimy shirt, and shake him, and \r\nscream at him to shut his fucking mouth and leave you \r\nalone. homeless people get a big kick out of how much shit \r\nwe are actually willing to put up with, and they always \r\npush your self-control/fear/whatever buttons, and nothing \r\ngives me more pleasure than to see them get some back, \r\nespecially from a dork like me who they think is a dead \r\nwinner.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.40','en'),(8817,1789,'2001-09-20 18:32:59',0,'F <b>---&gt;</b> N','True, true.<br><br>And you <b>really</b> don\\\'t want to take\r\nyour punches via emu digestion.  Like, really.  I once saw\r\nemu\\\'s running in circle\\\'s around their pen at an animal\r\nfarm.  It was frightening.  I think that even turned me off\r\nemu\\\'s.  My life-long dream of running an emu farm will\r\n<b>never</b> come to pass now.  Those three emu\\\'s ruined it\r\nfor the rest of them.',1,0,0,0,'64.229.90.24','en'),(8818,1787,'2001-09-20 18:33:57',0,'note','true. Peter did not say that exactly...but he implied [a \r\nrefreshing story of reality] that this article in \r\ncomparison to others had more truth to it. \\\'refreshing\\\' is \r\ntypically used in context to mean that you have not \r\nseen/heard/read/eaten something of that nature in quite \r\nawhile. ',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.155','en'),(8819,1787,'2004-07-27 05:00:32',578,'NetfÃ¶ng!','I feel refreshed every day when i wake up, and every day, i \r\nwake up to the same old shit. same routine, different day, \r\ni still feel refreshed :-) Maybe I\\\'m just thick.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8820,1787,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to note','<br><tt>it <i>did</i> when i was terrifically stoned. does \r\nthat clear things up? i was trying to not be so blunt, heh \r\nheh... end of story. no more nit-picking necessary, thanks.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8821,1784,'2001-09-20 18:40:41',0,'thought','or as you have done simply ignore the guy. aggression is \r\nnever a good answer. you could always quote passages from \r\nthe Dune trilogy to him....<i>\\\"It is by will alone I set my \r\nmind in motion. It is by the juice of Sapho that thoughts \r\nacquire speed, the lips acquire stains, stains become a \r\nwarning. It is by will alone I set my mind in motion.\\\"</i>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.155','en'),(8822,1787,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<p>You always here the <i>When Harry Met Sally</i> stories, \r\nbut rarely the ones about the failures.  I think Peter \r\nmumbled something along those lines last \r\nnight.</p><p>There\\\'s no moral to the story.  It was just an \r\nunusual reaction to a romanticized situation.  Tara herself \r\nwas very attractive.  Tall, blond, a lean swimmer\\\'s body.  \r\nIt\\\'s just that when I saw her, I instantly <i>knew</i>... \r\nIt\\\'s like when you meet someone and get an immediate vibe.  \r\nI always trust my intuition because it\\\'s usually right.</P>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(8823,1784,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to Ty','<br><tt>nice approach- I got a kick out of that because I \r\nwas once on my way to sell back a textbook.  To make a long \r\nstory short, they wouldn\\\'t buy it back (it cost me like \r\n$200) so I stormed out of the bookstore to be greeted by \r\nEddie.  He harangued me for the zillionth unsuccessful time-\r\n <i>\\\"Howdy Slim, spare a dime for a brother?\\\"</i>- and I \r\ntossed him the book, with a \\\"dont ever say I didn\\\'t give \r\nyou anything\\\" sort of look.  I spotted him carrying it \r\naround for a month or so. It was quite rewarding to \r\nrepeatedly see a addled, junkie old ex-con toting a shiny \r\nnew \\\"Partial Diff. Eq. and Multidimensional Analysis\\\" text \r\naround.  Soon after, our friends at the NYPD ran Eddie into \r\nRikers\\\'s Island for a month or so for repeated crack and \r\nassault charges.  A large bleeding-heart throng of Columbia \r\nstudents bailed out their gritty urban sage, returned him \r\nto his stoop near the Banco Popular, where he continues to \r\nhurl bizarrely insightful quips at passersby, as well as \r\ndemands for change.  Only now, he does it without the \r\nbook.  Last time I passed him, he was waiving a gold lame \r\nmini-skirt in the air and singing the National Anthem.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8824,1784,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to thought','<br><tt>i know. i always do. i never actually lock all \r\nthree locks on my apartment, either.  it just sounded \r\npoetic to say i did.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(8825,1784,'2001-09-20 19:07:02',0,'ghost','<i>The spice must flow.</i>\r\n',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.155','en'),(8826,579,'2004-07-27 05:00:32',578,'NetfÃ¶ng!','i like this story. that was very kind of you. i did a