larks, and they love \r\nyou.',2,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(8935,1793,'2001-09-21 22:48:24',0,'kat','austin works in the right place for making pamphlets. it is \r\napproximately 2 miles from my house, one halfmile from the \r\nliquor store, and one mile to the smoothie place.',4,0,0,0,'32.102.109.210','en'),(8936,1805,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p>you need something with good arch support. delias \r\nshoes never have that. may i recommend some birki \r\nclogs or a good pair of hiking boots? \r\n</p><p>\r\nmaybe if we\\\'re lucky now olivia will say \\\"HIKING\\\" in the \r\nnext comment.\r\n</p>\r\n',4,0,0,0,'216.27.183.161','en'),(8937,1805,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','peter: do you have big feet? <a \r\nhref=\"http://www.oddballshoe.com\">oddballshoe.com!</a>.',4,0,0,0,'216.27.183.161','en'),(8938,1792,'2001-09-21 23:34:24',0,'robertredford','hey batter batter, swing!',4,0,0,0,'156.153.255.236','en'),(8939,1805,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','HIKING.<br>\r\n<br>\r\ni\\\'m such a fucking crowd pleaser.',5,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(8940,1782,'2001-09-21 23:43:18',0,'deb','i think everyone hurts as much as the next person, but yea, \r\nanother candlelight vigil, and i\\\'m going to start doing \r\nother things with those candles...',2,0,0,0,'152.163.213.59','en'),(8941,1783,'2001-09-21 23:45:57',0,'deb','but did they ever ask? ;)\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'152.163.213.59','en'),(8942,1807,'2001-09-22 00:00:28',0,'Rabbit in yer headlights','UNKLE rocked 1998. laid it down. so brilliant i dont mind \r\nhe\\\'s so lazy.',1,0,0,0,'24.27.31.133','en'),(8943,1805,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to le','<br><tt>thankyouthankyouthankyou! they actually <i>have</i>\r\nsome cool shoes in my size that dont cost 200$! yes, i have\r\nbig feet. lets just say the fact that that size sells upto\r\n22 is rather helpful...</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.255','en'),(8944,1805,'2001-09-22 00:32:41',0,'silent observer','bmg wears new balance',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8945,1805,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','i wear new balance.',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(8946,1782,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','all holes filled with hard candle',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(8947,1807,'2001-09-22 00:55:40',0,'teknoligiez','Massive Attack? Underworld? are you out there?',1,0,0,0,'24.27.31.133','en'),(8948,1805,'2001-09-22 01:05:18',0,'bmg','i wear tastle cole-haans, with shorts on.',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(8949,1798,'2001-09-22 01:05:37',0,'treetop','I wonder if she was from france',0,0,0,0,'172.145.161.227','en'),(8950,1798,'2001-09-22 01:08:29',0,'oh yea, Royal w/cheese','  When I was there there was a lot of anti Mc\\\'e\\\'dees going \r\non.  I remember seeing a sticker someone had stuck on the \r\ndoor of a Mcdonalds.  It had uncle sam sitting on a \r\ntoilet.  The toiled had the golden arches on it and was \r\nactually a Mcdonalds.  I was going in to use the restroom.  \r\nThe Irony...  ',0,0,0,0,'172.145.161.227','en'),(8951,1806,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Droll Moll','I\\\'ve seen this show before, except then it was Richard \r\n<i>cour de Lion</i> and Salah al-Din al-Ayyubi. The New War \r\nis pretty typical: great special effects and a shitty cast \r\ncompared to the original. At least this time <i>we\\\'re</i> \r\nthe ones with the big guns, but still, I hate remakes.',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(8952,1804,'2001-09-22 01:32:34',0,'I like big butts','and I cannot lie',0,0,0,0,'172.145.161.227','en'),(8953,1793,'2001-09-22 01:37:55',0,'treetop','Mmmm, Bushmills smoothies :)',0,0,0,0,'172.145.161.227','en'),(8954,1808,'2001-09-22 01:55:32',0,'treetop','evil backwards is live..  Thank you Miles Davis..Live Evil',0,0,0,0,'172.145.161.227','en'),(8955,1793,'2001-09-22 02:34:35',0,'sting','mommins. word.',1,0,0,0,'24.27.31.133','en'),(8956,1811,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','\\\"a bootleg of your love\\\" is a nice turn of phrase.',0,0,0,0,'206.170.32.241','en'),(8957,1808,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','<p>I think \\\"they\\\" are evil insofar as they blew something \r\nup that was close to my house and killed a slew of people \r\nwho, in one way or another, might have just as easily been \r\nme.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>But if I put my American-ness aside, I\\\'d probably \r\nconsider what they did to be a cunning and courageous \r\n(imagine spending months, maybe years, training for your \r\nown death) attack against a perfectly legitimate enemy. \r\nYes, as human beings, corporate executives, office workers, \r\nand other assorted civilians <i>are</i> responsible for \r\ntheir own actions and do possess some degree of free-will, \r\nhowever stifled. We live (<i>I live</i>) in a kind of \r\nfantasy world where we\\\'re totally detached from the effects \r\nof the organizations we lead and work for. We breath life \r\ninto an infrastructure which decides the fate of global \r\ntrade, how to bully the third world, how to get away with \r\ndoing x and y, how to prop up such-and-such regime, etc, \r\nand we do this with relative impunity. That is, until \r\nsomeone gets clever and starts wiping out our ergonomic \r\ndeskspace with several tons of commercial passenger jet. \r\n[Insert: Flaming Dilbert cartoons raining from the sky, \r\ncharred stress-toys floating in the Hudson.]</p>\r\n<p>I guess I\\\'m just saying that it wasn\\\'t unprovoked, and \r\nthat I don\\\'t think they\\\'re \\\"evil\\\" (just desperate) or that \r\nthe people celebrating it are \\\"crazy\\\" (just voiceless), and \r\nthat I don\\\'t think we can blame it all on the Big Guys in \r\nCharge.</p>\r\n',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(8958,1787,'2001-09-22 02:49:43',0,'deb','I had not seen that movie, ever, until not too long ago. I \r\nwas watching it and I got upset because after they had sex \r\nand started to argue I thought the movie was going to have \r\na bad ending; and my friend encouraged me to believe that.  \r\nYou never know, that tall blonde girl might have done \r\nsomething and become beautiful...or reversed whatever the \r\nproblem was... and you might see her in 5 years.',1,0,0,0,'205.188.201.201','en'),(8959,1793,'2001-09-22 02:50:49',0,'treetop','Was Judi Booty our waitress?   Hehe...',0,0,0,0,'172.145.161.227','en'),(8960,1789,'2001-09-22 02:55:45',0,'deb','i was thinking about stuff like that recently, too. i \r\nthought that after i finished my emt classes and had more \r\ntime, i\\\'d take up kickboxing or karate or something... just \r\nfor the opportunity to kick the crap out of SOMETHING.',1,0,0,0,'205.188.201.201','en'),(8961,1793,'2001-09-22 02:58:28',0,'Hi :)','I like to boogie.  Im going out now.',0,0,0,0,'172.145.161.227','en'),(8962,1800,'2001-09-22 03:18:30',0,'Doktor','some poo-poo heads think you suck. well, i think youre a\r\nfuckin genius! fo\\\' real, dawg. keep it real, yo. peace out.',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.255','en'),(8963,1811,'2001-09-22 03:21:49',0,'Anonymous to Protect da Guilty','i\\\'m soooo rollin right now and just read this piece and i\r\nfeel it. its beautiful in a blue-note sorta light.\r\n<i>bootleg of your love</i> atthe same time delights me, and\r\nbeckons me to fix teh <i>Exact same issue, i feel</i> in my\r\nown life.  thats for sparking the healthy introspection,\r\nyour writing has made its mark.  Thank you!',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.255','en'),(8964,1792,'2001-09-22 03:23:41',0,'deb','kava kava pills??? or just tea?',2,0,0,0,'205.188.201.201','en'),(8965,1793,'2001-09-22 03:26:55',0,'deb','hey. you can buy me liquor, too, you know.',1,0,0,0,'205.188.201.201','en'),(8966,1798,'2001-09-22 03:31:28',0,'deb','the mcdonalds up the street from me burnt down not too long \r\nago when an employee (who just graduated from the fire \r\nacademy, btw) got pissed cause he didn\\\'t get a raise. he \r\nlit the couch in the employee lounge on fire. now they sell \r\nburgers out of a trailer on the side while they gut and \r\nrebuild.',3,0,0,0,'205.188.201.201','en'),(8967,1802,'2001-09-22 03:34:45',0,'deb','interesting how someone who was not would have so many \r\npictures of the same person doing SO many different things.',3,0,0,0,'205.188.201.201','en'),(8968,1811,'2001-09-22 03:35:38',0,'author','blush. and i meant to type artistico as the name. oops.',1,0,0,0,'24.27.31.133','en'),(8969,1804,'2001-09-22 03:36:55',0,'deb','yup. i felt about the same way when my car was stolen. \r\nexcept the cop did not offer me a ride to work. he \r\nsaid \\\'did you check the lot to see if they just moved it?\\\' \r\nas if i had searched the 20 building complex...',3,0,0,0,'205.188.201.201','en'),(8970,1793,'2001-09-22 03:52:29',0,'kat','<p>to treetop: yea, i think she was our waitress. but at \r\nsome point it seemed like we had three our four different \r\nones.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>to Hi: i like to boogie too.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>to deb: if you want to spend a week driving over to my \r\nhouse and babysit my Spazdog, then you too shall be the \r\nrecipient of a bottle o\\\' brain tonic.</p>',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.122','en'),(8971,1805,'2001-09-22 03:57:27',0,'jo','i don\\\'t really like tennis shoes. but birki clogs are a \r\ngood suggestion; i always like wearing yours when you\\\'re \r\naround, els. i will get myself a pair.<BR>\r\nand they\\\'re good for show-attending?',1,0,0,0,'172.157.187.251','en'),(8972,1807,'2001-09-22 04:03:50',0,'jo','sometimes, my friend jason goes \\\"AHOOOOOOOEEEEEEE!\\\" and i \r\nsay, \\\"that was for brooklyn.\\\"<BR>\r\nprops to mos def. best hip hop record i\\\'ve ever owned.',1,0,0,0,'172.157.187.251','en'),(8973,1808,'2001-09-22 04:05:27',0,'jo','thank you, alan. this was really interesting.',1,0,0,0,'172.157.187.251','en'),(8974,1807,'2001-09-22 04:29:01',0,'cynn','massive attack and the marquis de sade.',4,0,0,0,'216.8.153.107','en'),(8975,1807,'2001-09-22 04:47:26',0,'kat','i am partial to the Tribe\\\'s...Love Movement.',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.122','en'),(8976,1807,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','mmmm... mos def.\r\n\r\nalso: dj shadow\\\'s stem long stem is real good for listening \r\nto when you are angry on the bus.',1,0,0,0,'210.54.208.205','en'),(8977,1792,'2001-09-22 05:28:48',0,'kini','in tonga, (traditionally) the kava root is chewed up by \r\nyoung girls before it gets spat out, mixed up with water, \r\nstrained through a cloth, and handed out to drink.\r\n\r\n<p>in fiji, i like to sit in the village under my mango \r\ntree as the sun sets over the ocean and the men tell \r\nstories around the yaqona bowl.\r\n\r\n<p>in this part of the world kava abuse CAN be a problem. \r\nhere, in australia, it exists mainly in the aboriginal \r\ncommunities of the northen territory. we actually have a \r\nnational code of kava management.\r\n\r\n<p>hi.',1,0,0,0,'61.8.19.82','en'),(8978,1808,'2001-09-22 05:38:01',0,'ty','my definition: evil is one person or group of persons \r\nharming another person or group of persons, whether by \r\nnegligence or concious action, except in extreme cases of \r\nself-defense. Also, the evil party must be aware of the \r\nfact that it is harming the innocent party.\r\n<br>\r\nit exists and is preacticed by almost everyone on a daily \r\nbasis. \r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.175','en'),(8979,1803,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','homeric.',3,0,0,0,'216.27.183.161','en'),(8980,1803,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','one can only hope names have been changed to \r\nprotect the innocent.',4,0,0,0,'206.170.1.33','en'),(8981,1808,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','\\\"the evil party\\\" would be a good name for a horror flick. \r\nthe plot: four college freshmen girls go to their first \r\ncollege party, only to discover by the end of the night \r\nthat the doors are locked and all the other party goers \r\nhave become the walking undead. her friends freshly \r\nkilled by zombies, \\\"sheila\\\" (brunette) manages to \r\nescape alive, leaving with a bloody arm and the one boy \r\nwho didn\\\'t turn undead (... or did he?!)',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(8982,1807,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','<i>She was showin\\\' me her tanlines and her tattoo, playin\\\'\r\nSade\\\'s Sweetest Taboo.  Burinin\\\' candles, all my other plans\r\ngot cancelled... Man I smashed it like an Idaho\r\npotato.</i><br><br>Uhhh, brilliant?',1,0,0,0,'64.229.83.107','en'),(8983,1812,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','Look for positivity from unknown sources.<br><br>Don\\\'t yield\r\nto negative feelings, make them work for you.',1,0,0,0,'64.229.83.107','en'),(8984,1812,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','people really don\\\'t take the time to get to know people. \r\nthis is true for most people, not just you. everyone is \r\nbanking on everyone else being simple. the people who are \r\ncomplex get shit for it, and no one tries to understand. \r\nbut you know, after years of being unknown there are a few \r\npeople, maybe three, four, who really REALLY know me. who \r\ntook the time and were patient and know me. so don\\\'t give \r\nup hope. i\\\'m a difficult person and some people rose to the \r\nchallenge. i don\\\'t think i used up the last batch of those \r\ntype of people.',4,0,0,0,'216.27.183.161','en'),(8985,1812,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','<br>',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(8986,1811,'2001-09-22 11:42:32',0,'Bob','\\\"These memories I got they can strangle a man\\\"',1,0,0,0,'24.27.31.133','en'),(8987,1807,'2001-09-22 14:01:21',0,'jo','\\\"brilliant\\\" was applied to UNKLE. i said \\\"best\\\" about mos \r\ndef. there are times his lyrics fail but his sound is so \r\nincredible that i don\\\'t care.',1,0,0,0,'172.157.187.251','en'),(8988,1807,'2001-09-22 15:07:53',0,'sawks','<br>\r\nmos def needs to give up on the singing thing (except \r\nfor tree never grown, that was nice)<br><br>\r\nhe\\\'s at his best (imho) over a dj premier beat, but then \r\nso is everyone else...\r\n',3,0,0,0,'144.132.9.80','en'),(8989,1812,'2001-09-22 15:52:34',0,'horse','<img border=\\\"0\\\" \r\nsrc=\\\"http://www.lefteyelazy.com/images/photos/misc/galloping\r\n.jpg\\\" width=\\\"351\\\" height=\\\"252\\\">',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.54','en'),(8990,1807,'2001-09-22 17:32:46',0,'Fuzz-2-Jo','Wait... I shouldn\\\'t write <b>anything</b> just before I am\r\nabout to pass out.  I meant that I thought Mos Def\\\'s lyrics\r\nwere brilliant.  Now I see how my comment could have been\r\ninterpreted as sarcasm.<br><br>My bad.  And I like Mos Def\\\'s\r\nvoice.  The Pish Posh remix of Blackstar is superb.  That\r\ntrack turned me on to Mos Def.  Plus, he ruled in <a\r\nhref=\\\"http://us.imdb.com/Title?0215545\\\"\r\ntarget=\\\"movie\\\">Bamboozled</a>.',1,0,0,0,'64.229.83.107','en'),(8991,1812,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>voice, hair, body, sex. im intrigued by this list. i have \r\nnever fallen for anyone <i>regardless</i> of what they \r\nlooked like, but the physical qualities were always an \r\nextension of who the person was and not some kind of \r\ncompliance with pre-set \\\"hot booty\\\" criteria. me and my \r\nbody, they are me. my mind is inside my body. there is \r\nno seperating them. if somoene were to love me, it \r\ncould never be love for just the cold brains on top, but \r\nthe whole warm vessel that houses and nurtures it too. \r\nor vice versa - how can someone be in love with a \r\npussy, or more absurdly, a haircut? </p>\r\n<p>but then again, im starting to realize that men think \r\ndifferently. elementary?</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.32.60.152','en'),(8992,1792,'2001-09-22 18:42:25',0,'kavaboy','I\\\'ve heard of this, but is kava abuse worse than the grog \r\n(that is, alcohol abuse)? It seems that the white \r\ngovernment finds anything the natives are up to to be a \r\nthreat.',3,0,0,0,'12.81.85.242','en'),(8993,1812,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','Maybe you need to use different terms in this discussion?  I\r\nthink that <i>love</i> for anyting less than a person in\r\ntheir entirety is simply <i>lust</i>.  Being attracted to\r\nsomeone just becuz they is aesthetically pleasing isn\\\'t\r\nlove.  Conversely, just being attracted to someone with a\r\nhuge mellon (I mean intelligence-wise, not a giant head,\r\nalthough I\\\'m sure there\\\'s people who dig that sort of thing;\r\nI\\\'m just not one of them).  You\\\'ve got to want, and get, the\r\nwhole package.<br><br>Anything less is pointless.  Sure,\r\nrelationships exist for less than true love.  Hell, even\r\nmore than enough marriages probably occur for two people in\r\nlust (just look at some divorce stats to back up <b>that</b>\r\ntheory).<br><br>I don\\\'t personally agree with just labelling\r\nthe whole of men as thinking differently (when different\r\nequates to lovin\\\' a lady for just her ass or a haircut). \r\nMaybe I\\\'m being ignorant, or being hopeful that there are\r\nmore guys like me, who won\\\'t settle for anything less than\r\nthe real deal, whole package (with all the extras included).\r\n Maybe I\\\'m too picky, or stupid but whatever.  I don\\\'t think\r\nI could ever love anyone not wholly and truly, nor would I\r\nexpect any less from someone I\\\'d let get close enough to me\r\nbe in such a position as to express something more than\r\n<i>like</i>.<br><br>Does any of this make sense?',1,0,0,0,'64.229.83.107','en'),(8994,1803,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','\\\"She didn\\\'t taste as bad as she smelled.\\\" Sexy. Very sexy.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.5.188','en'),(8995,1812,'2001-09-22 21:18:09',0,'bob marley','wake up and live',0,0,0,0,'172.141.172.252','en'),(8996,1803,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt><i>\\\"One night in Bangkok makes a hard man\r\nhumble\\\"</i>... perhaps the same applies to the City.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.255','en'),(8997,1792,'2001-09-23 01:20:36',0,'kini','god, no. of course it\\\'s nowhere near as bad. accordingly, \r\nthe number of regulations and programs in place to stem \r\nalcohol abuse far outweigh those for kava abuse.\r\n\r\n<p>the kava management code aims to (as far as i can tell) \r\nstop a small problem becoming a huge problem, you know? \r\nit\\\'s not out there so \\\"white people\\\" can control what \r\nthe \\\"natives\\\" get up to every night. it\\\'s common sense, \r\nreally.\r\n\r\n<p>but anyway. back to you. i think you have to start \r\ndrinking a dozen cups of the stuff a night in the long term \r\nbefore the festy skin lesions start and your liver gets \r\nsickly. all is well!',1,0,0,0,'61.8.19.123','en'),(8998,1804,'2001-09-23 03:12:36',0,'<p>joker',' i surrendered my bike to whoever wanted it last week, by \r\nnot locking it up at night.  people say, \\\"god, what an \r\nidiot you are...\\\"  \\\"you put too much faith in humanity\\\" \r\netc.  but i prefer to believe that whomever it was that \r\nneeded it, used it for some great virtuous purpose.  and \r\neveryday i walk out of the building by the bike-rack, \r\nexpecting it to be there.  it will be, in one way or \r\nanother.  that is the way of all things.  bless you.</p>',1,0,0,0,'66.69.227.53','en'),(8999,1804,'2004-07-27 05:00:32',578,'NetfÃ¶ng!','i\\\'m deeply pained by whomever decided to take advantage of\r\nnaivity. its ruined countless lives, mine included.',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.255','en'),(9000,1803,'2001-09-23 06:14:24',0,'ty','ha ha ha ha ha. ha ha. ha.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.249','en'),(9001,1792,'2001-09-23 06:23:39',0,'kavaboy','we bandage ourselves with chemicals trying to soothe \r\nourselves into modernity, it\\\'s not working...',5,0,0,0,'204.27.188.1','en'),(9002,1812,'2001-09-23 06:27:46',0,'Mulder','Trust no one.',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(9003,1803,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','Shit..... people I know are starting to invade Swinney.  \r\nThe above stuff happened <i>in my bed</I>.  I personally \r\nthought Jo was kinda cute, but she did have really small \r\nboobs.',0,0,0,0,'63.208.119.28','en'),(9004,1803,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','god essemar. so you\\\'re saying that not only is this a TRUE \r\nSTORY, but you actually maintain a friendship with the \r\npurveyor of such mean comments?',0,0,0,0,'216.27.183.161','en'),(9005,1737,'2001-09-23 13:59:26',0,'BBQ','my brain',3,0,0,0,'213.1.129.17','en'),(9006,1813,'2001-09-23 15:53:51',