tanza','da bagno',0,0,0,0,'172.141.172.252','en'),(9016,1819,'2001-09-23 19:48:47',0,'please','insert comment here',0,0,0,0,'172.141.172.252','en'),(9017,1815,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt<i>Peecheezed off</i>... heh</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.255','en'),(9018,1803,'2001-09-23 21:24:17',0,'Hallett','well, what can i say?  allot of it, in truth, is exagerated \r\nfor the sake of taking something and just going way way way \r\nto far with it.  of course one could go farther, but who\\\'d \r\nwant to?  maybe somebody, but not me, not today, not with \r\nsomething that actually happened.  it was a terrible \r\nexperience, one that i am ashamed of.  why am i sharing it \r\nwith swinney?  good question.  i don\\\'t know, perhaps \r\nbecause essemar said he would if i didn\\\'t (*and there you \r\nare pretending to be surprised by it), but more just to \r\nfind out peoples reactions. am i evil?  am i scum?  yes \r\nprobably.  you don\\\'t know the half of it, and still i hope \r\nfor the worlds forgiveness.',3,0,0,0,'172.152.108.128','en'),(9019,1803,'2001-09-23 21:35:59',0,'Manly Man','I actually <i>prefer</i> girls with small boobs.',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.255','en'),(9020,1812,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','Well, thanks.  Yeah, I guess I do have standards but that\r\ndoes mean a lot of lonely evenings by yourself.  I guess in\r\nthe end you look back and realise it was all worth it, but\r\nright now, I\\\'m not so sure.  <i>The end</i> is a ways off, I\r\nhope.',3,0,0,0,'64.229.83.107','en'),(9021,1820,'2001-09-23 23:20:12',0,'david lynch','I used to live in the Wilma building in lovely downtown \r\nMissoula, Montana. The name \\\"missoula\\\" is a Salish word \r\nthat means \\\"bad place by the water.\\\" Creepy. But the \r\ndialogue of Isabella saying \\\"hit me, hit me\\\" is all me.',4,0,0,0,'12.81.84.88','en'),(9022,1792,'2001-09-23 23:22:01',0,'kavaboy','and natives (aborigines, or american indians like me) are \r\nthe canaries in the coal mine.',3,0,0,0,'12.81.84.88','en'),(9023,1803,'2001-09-23 23:30:30',0,'jeanpaulsartre','The fundamental experience of being is that metallic taste \r\nin my mouth-- nausea.',5,0,0,0,'12.81.84.88','en'),(9024,1738,'2001-09-23 23:31:27',0,'montanaboy','montana is great, if it wasn\\\'t built on your homeland...',4,0,0,0,'12.81.84.88','en'),(9025,1706,'2001-09-23 23:33:25',0,'coyote','you shouldn\\\'t be telling my stories until after the first \r\nsnow.',4,0,0,0,'12.81.84.88','en'),(9026,1819,'2001-09-24 01:23:19',0,'right','...and the Editors have been sleeping???',6,0,0,0,'32.102.109.8','en'),(9027,1803,'2001-09-24 04:01:20',0,'maria to jo','word to that. i wonder if there are any boys out there who \r\nhave similar stories about me? <br><Br>\r\n\r\nterrifying, indeed. ',4,0,0,0,'132.162.231.185','en'),(9028,1819,'2001-09-24 05:49:59',0,'editor #13','eh. yah... actualy, this post makes about as much \r\nsense as any I have seen in a while... *yawn*<br>I \r\ndouble dog dare someone to say something REAL. \r\nImpress me.',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(9029,1821,'2001-09-24 06:05:06',0,'whatever dude','roll tide ROLL!',0,0,0,0,'172.149.213.20','en'),(9030,1803,'2001-09-24 06:08:03',0,'ghost','this isn\\\'t really about the girl, so it\\\'s not the story \r\nthat bothers me...it\\\'s the fact that someone could think so \r\nlittle of themself. his actions reek of desperation and \r\nself-loathing.',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.104','en'),(9031,1821,'2001-09-24 07:26:27',0,'Alan','* Sat, Oct 27 - 2001 *\r\n\r\n - Castration Day for the Cocks in Knoxville, Tennessee - \r\n\r\nWelcome to 107,000 screaming fans all armed with a well \r\nsharpened pair of scissors!',4,0,0,0,'64.160.52.231','en'),(9032,1823,'2001-09-24 08:38:29',0,'bmg','<p>austin needs to do a little manicuring on his own nails \r\nthere...<br>\r\nhe is everywhere. i have swinney resin scattered throughout \r\nmy house. he invades my computer, my answering machine... \r\nand i still find his socks - i found bits of his mind in an \r\nold notebook of mine... in a notepad of mine, i found a \r\nletter to a lover... i didn\'t read it - but thought about \r\nposting it... </p>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(9033,1815,'2001-09-24 09:14:25',0,'Jamie','Il mio nome Ã¨ Jamie',1,0,0,0,'217.32.139.150','en'),(9034,1803,'2001-09-24 09:17:39',0,'Hallett','yes, please, tell me who i am.  yes i\\\'m being sarcastic, \r\nbut at the same time i really DO want to know exactly what \r\nothers think.  it is a judge of both who i am and how well \r\ni write.  \r\n\r\nfor all the females out there; please don\\\'t think this is \r\nin anyway typical of the way guys talk about woman.  in my \r\nexperience they don\\\'t talk about them that much at all.  \r\nthis story was an experiment in peoples reactions, in my \r\nown reaction.  partially i am seeking forgivness (although \r\ni\\\'m not sure i\\\'ve done anything wrong) but mostly i just \r\nenjoy the opportunity to be completely honest (freedom of \r\nthe facelessness of the web).  this was a one time \r\nexperience.\r\n\r\ni invite and appreciate all the comments you have to give.  \r\ni truly do.  i should also mention that i am rather drunk \r\n(a result of my girlfriend breaking up with me today -a \r\ncompletely other and much much longer story).\r\n\r\nthanx',3,0,0,0,'172.139.93.239','en'),(9035,1803,'2001-09-24 09:39:20',0,'girls','you mean we haven\\\'t cornered the market on porney gossip?',1,0,0,0,'66.32.60.152','en'),(9036,1821,'2001-09-24 12:05:08',0,'Tennessean','\\\"On days of a home game, the Tennessee Vol\\\'s Neyland \r\nStadium becomes one of Tennessee\\\'s most populated spaces- \r\nmore than most of the state\\\'s largest towns!\\\"',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9037,1803,'2001-09-24 13:08:52',0,'barbie','<p>I think maybe you are gay.</p><p>which is cool, \r\nreally. I have some great gay friends. When ken breaks \r\nmy heart, I call up one of my gay friends and have them \r\ntalk shit about the new girl for me. Ken sleeps around a \r\nlot, but I don\\\'t mind as long as he brings home the \r\nmoney. At first I did mind, and then I met jo - and she \r\nrocked my world.</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(9038,1803,'2001-09-24 13:18:51',0,'Virile Man','I dunno. I still like girls with small boobs.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9039,1823,'2002-06-12 21:13:52',93,'chiamattt','its the swinney co-op. very socialist. ',6,0,0,0,'24.43.182.49','en'),(9040,1823,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>I think Commandant Swinney should get into the NYC \r\nMayorial race before they let Giuliani snap up a third term-\r\n They extended the race (and his tenure) indefinitely due \r\nto the WTC incident, so Mister Swinney probably has time to \r\nget his name out there. Then again, there\'s always write-\r\nins on the ballot.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9041,1803,'2001-09-24 13:42:44',0,'barbie','<p>there are some great plastic surgeons I know. I could \r\ngive her their names?</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(9042,1803,'2001-09-24 13:55:38',0,'Virile Man','breast reduction, nipple enlargement!',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9043,1824,'2001-09-24 14:41:25',0,'trouble','interesting... don\\\'t you think it would be more a power \r\nover a persons will rather than just their ability to \r\nsupport anything you bring forth?  and if that\\\'s the case \r\nthe majority of television networks already have that \r\npower.  on a similar note of dreams and related mental \r\nimagery, i have deja-vu to the max right now reading your \r\npost and typing my subsequent reply.  wierd.',1,0,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(9044,1824,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>thats the freaky thing. the dream was chock-full of \r\ninteresting little vignettes where this ability was put to \r\nuse (none of which i can now remember). I do recall \r\n<i>never</i> using it to overtly take control of a person\'s \r\nwill, foremost; just to get strangers to vouch for me. \r\nLike, how can a cop ticket you when 45 people pull over \r\nright behind you and start saying, \"Officer, there must be \r\nsome glitch! he wasn\'t speeding! we all were passing him!\" \r\nand the like. sadly, it was put to rather banal (albeit strange) use; such a \r\nboring life i lead, heh.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9045,1824,'2001-09-24 14:56:29',0,'De Ja Vu','maybe you are Peter\\\'s psyche',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9046,1819,'2001-09-24 14:58:10',0,'Moo','we know who you are!',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9047,1824,'2001-09-24 15:10:49',0,'trouble to peter','no, it just means you were using the force for good rather \r\nthan evil like the good jedi you are.  the taking over of a \r\npersons will can really only be for evil and fiendish \r\npurposes.  (insert ghoulish laugh and image of one rubbing \r\nhands together looking down with eyebrow raised)',1,0,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(9048,1824,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>I thought it\\\'d be a good topic for a movie. you \r\ncould take the \\\"evil-rule-the-world\\\" route (overdone \r\nalready), but i think the dead-pan \\\"get myself out of \r\nspeeding tickets\\\", etc. would be a much more humourous \r\nroute.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9049,1824,'2001-09-24 15:19:46',0,'A Good Movie','with <a href=\\\"http://209.237.157.45/ram/71646.RAM\\\">this</a> \r\non the soundtrack.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9050,1824,'2001-09-24 15:25:26',0,'trouble to peter','i vote for jim jarmush to direct.  i\\\'d like to see those \r\ncircumstances in tokyo, denmark, detroit, isreal and a 5th \r\nas yet unknown location.<br>\\\'my name is helmut\\\'...',1,0,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(9051,1824,'2001-09-24 15:34:25',0,'Tom Tykwer','i\\\'d do it. i agree- i think you should hilight a single \r\nvignette several times over several different times, in \r\nseveral different places. kinda like my hit film <i>run \r\nlola run</i>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9052,1824,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>wow, this discussion has cleared my writer\\\'s block \r\nfor the first time in a year or so. i think i\\\'ll write this \r\nall up in a short story before someone else does, ha.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9053,1824,'2001-09-24 15:38:43',0,'trouble','ooooh, franka potente!  thank you tom for bringing franka \r\npotente into my life via your wonderful film.  yum.',1,0,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(9054,1824,'2001-09-24 15:39:06',0,'trouble to tom','ooooh, franka potente!  thank you tom for bringing franka \r\npotente into my life via your wonderful film.  yum.',1,0,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(9055,1824,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>whomever posted the link to harrison crump\\\'s <i>Get \r\nBoogie</i>, you\\\'re too much (and a little creepy)- thats \r\nlike my favourite song. Although, for the score, I might \r\nhave to consult the Bangalter/De Homem-Christo duo.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9056,1824,'2001-09-24 15:45:44',0,'trouble to peter','on behalf of swinney readers everywhere i ask that you be \r\nsure to share your story when it\\\'s completed.',1,0,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(9057,1824,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>certainly. i\\\'ll be writing tonight.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9058,1792,'2001-09-24 17:00:23',0,'kavadreamboy','i think that kava kava has the effect of increasing my REM \r\nsleep, the dream sleep, because I\\\'m having the most vivid \r\ndreams-- and remembering them, which is unusual for me.\r\n\r\nthis morning it was svea driving downtown (billings, mont.) \r\nin the back of some guys old car, like a dodge dart. we \r\nwere going to meet the pack, the usual assortment of social \r\ncronies (the kids tend to run in packs).\r\n\r\nthe guy driving was some red haired scraggly guy, but a \r\ncharmer, he kept looking back at us and smiling. ah, svea i \r\nthink he was into you.\r\n\r\nbut he dropped us off at the wrong place, not downtown but \r\njust on the suburban edge of downtown. and we started \r\nwalking.\r\n\r\ndoes kava make anyone else dream so much?',5,0,0,0,'156.153.255.243','en'),(9059,1803,'2001-09-24 17:01:59',0,'Patrick Bateman to Hallett','We should meet and talk. But first I have to return some \r\nvideotapes.',6,0,0,0,'212.161.41.80','en'),(9060,1803,'2001-09-24 17:06:23',0,'Sean Bateman to Patrick','<tt>Rock\\\'n\\\'Roll, dude.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9061,1805,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','you evil people. you have inspired some serious new shoe \r\njonesing. mmm vegan birkenstocks ... ',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(9062,1805,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','ew clogs. ew hiking. etc.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(9063,1805,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','oh and p.s.--clark\\\'s are cute\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(9064,1808,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','Am I evil? / Yes I am / Am I evil? / Yes I am, I am man...\r\n\r\n_James Hetfield\r\n\r\n//\\\\/\\\\\\\\ETALLICA  GRRR',3,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(9065,1803,'2001-09-24 17:41:52',0,'Sean Bateman','And I don\\\'t look a thing like James Van Der Beek.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.77.139','en'),(9066,1819,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Art Moll','Is it a post? Is it not a post? Does it redefine \\\"post\\\"?',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(9067,1820,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Helmut von Moll','That is like my favorite fucking movie ever.',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(9068,1823,'2001-09-24 18:15:32',0,'the blair witch','sometimes i look like the incredible hulk too. why is my \r\nmouth always open.',0,0,0,0,'66.32.60.152','en'),(9069,1823,'2001-09-24 18:17:48',0,'fashion consultant','why is that girl wearing a plaid shirt like it\\\'s the early \r\n90s.',0,0,0,0,'66.32.60.152','en'),(9070,1823,'2001-09-24 18:27:36',0,'maybe','it is the early \\\'90s in cali. there\\\'s a time zone \r\ndifference, you know.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.9.26','en'),(9071,1823,'2001-09-24 18:52:07',0,'leonard','it good to see that austin is still wearing the same \r\nclothes he was wearing when i last saw him.',3,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(9072,1819,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','this post is so \\\"post-post\\\"\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(9073,678,'2001-09-24 19:37:54',0,'trouble','what does it say about the human condition when almost \r\neverybody knows of somebody who stopped fighting and just \r\nsaid \\\'i quit\\\'?<br><br>thank you for the post, it took me \r\nback to high school and made me think of ally, nobody could \r\nhave saved her either and my guilt stays with me to this \r\nday.',3,0,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(9074,1823,'2001-09-24 19:42:12',0,'bmg','<p>clearly the woman in plaid has invaded austin\\\'s \r\ncloset, or his trunk. That shirt has got to be austins. I \r\nbetcha that the woman in question took it from him after \r\ntaking his virginity.\r\n</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(9075,1823,'2001-09-24 19:55:53',0,'just like','a viking',1,0,0,0,'64.132.148.219','en'),(9076,1823,'2001-09-24 20:56:41',0,'huevitahuevita','actually, austin invades my closet.\r\n<br><img \r\nsrc=\\\"http://atari.saturn5.com/~egg/pink1.md.jpg\\\" \r\nwidth=\\\"300\\\" height=\\\"213\\\" border=\\\"0\\\"><br>\r\n*pinkhoodie*',0,0,0,0,'66.32.60.152','en'),(9077,1823,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','that shirt was my dad\\\'s. i dont believe he knows that \r\nflannel is early 90s.',0,0,0,0,'66.32.60.152','en'),(9078,1826,'2001-09-24 21:05:14',0,'Captain America','<p>Buy Buy! it\\\'s a sale on wall street now. I gave money \r\nto this <a href=\\\"http://www.howardstern.com\\\">cause</a>.</p>',1,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(9079,1827,'2001-09-24 21:52:19',0,'kat','i had a three hour conversation last night. i did not get \r\nenough sleep. it took me an hour and a half to get to work \r\nthis morning. i was tired and traffic was bad. i missed my \r\nbreakfast. starving. \r\n\r\n<p><i>yea. today is exquisite</i></p>',1,0,0,0,'32.102.110.215','en'),(9080,1827,'2001-09-24 22:04:26',0,'Blood Roses','Food is such a good way to feel alive. I\\\'m sad and i\\\'m \r\ngoing to PF CHANGS to feel better. some noodles can save \r\nmy life.',1,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(9081,1827,'2001-09-24 22:31:35',0,'bmg','Juan, get your ass over here - so I can kiss it.',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(9082,1827,'2001-09-24 22:52:46',0,'curiousboy','kat: does this mean you got a job?',3,0,0,0,'156.153.255.243','en'),(9083,1819,'2001-09-24 23:43:06',0,'Treetop','</head>\r\n<body>\r\n&nbsp;<font color=\\\"#990000\\\"> I am curious, does this post \r\nreflect <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.aracnet.com/~lavatech/bong/freebonghit.html\r\n\\\">marijuana</a>\r\nor the <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.channel2000.com/news/stories/news-19991106-\r\n173057.html\\\">toilet</a></font>?\r\n<center>\r\n<p><img SRC=\\\"http://sugarmegs.org/dancingleaf.gif\\\" NOSAVE \r\nheight=112 width=150></center>\r\n\r\n</body>\r\n</html>',0,0,0,0,'172.140.88.229','en'),(9084,1826,'2001-09-24 23:57:24',0,'treetop','It seems to me that the problem with investing today is \r\nthat many people have recently been burned and are very \r\ncautious as to which company they invest in.',0,0,0,0,'172.140.88.229','en'),(9085,1827,'2001-09-25 00:24:28',0,'jo','dude. now i\\\'m singing blood roses to myself. dammit \r\ndammit.<BR>\r\nwould anyone like to come to austin java company and study \r\nfor the GRE all night with me? oh really? what a fucking \r\nsurprise. hate hate.<BR>\r\n(hi, please let me come home to <a \r\nhref=\\\"mailto:joanna@unpopular.com\\\">happy email</a>.)',1,0,0,0,'172.143.180.83','en'),(9086,1828,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','where is .nu?\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.9.45','en'),(9087,1828,'2006-07-06 18:08:16',754,'Camilla Henrikke','.nu? I dunno. I think it\\\'s a small island somewhere. Heh.',3,0,0,0,'130.67.15.248','en'),(9088,1828,'2003-05-10 16:09:14',79,'yeti','.nu is the TLD for Niue.<br>\r\n<a\r\nhref=\\\"http://www.odci.gov/cia/publications/factbook/geos/ne.html\\\">Look\r\nhere.</a><br>\r\nHi Camilla, and welcome to swinney.org\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.109.213.61','en'),(9089,1827,'2001-09-25 00:58:23',0,'kat','just woke up. starving. i will send happy email to anyone \r\nwho wants it. this is my job.',4,0,0,0,'32.102.109.23','en'),(9090,1828,'2001-09-25 00:59:19',0,'copycat','gavin?',0,0,0,0,'172.140.88.229','en'),(9091,1827,'2001-09-25 01:01:42',0,'sleepy','<a \r\nhref=\\\'mailto:bmg@lepard.org\\\'>ME,ME,ME,ME,ME,ME,M\r\nE,ME,ME,ME,ME,Me</a>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(9092,1828,'2001-09-25 01:08:00',0,'ladies and gentlemen','<H1>The Internet\\\'s Own Camilla!</H1>\r\n<P>\\\"best friendly\\\"</P>',1,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(9093,1828,'2001-09-25 01:33:00',0,'I like','Oslo',0,0,0,0,'172.140.88.229','en'),(9094,1828,'2006-07-06 18:08:16',754,'Camilla Henrikke','Why doesn\\\'t people believe that I am \\\"the real Camilla\\\"? Do \r\nemail wallflower@wallflower.nu if you STILL don\\\'t believe \r\nme and I shall reply and confirm. =}',6,0,0,0,'130.67.15.249','en'),(9095,1828,'2004-07-27 05:00:32',578,'NetfÃ¶ng!g','geez, ppl!',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.255','en'),(9096,1827,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','i could use some happy email. somehow my mood \r\nhas taken a turn.',0,0,0,0,'66.32.60.152','en'),(9097,414,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>when i was at the omega institute in new york, eve \r\nbrought me to the book store and made me look \r\nthrough an alex grey book. psychedelia bothers me. but \r\ni am trying to open my mind, MAN. i am going to try to \r\nfinish the rob brezsny book before i see her again.</p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'66.32.60.152','en'),(9098,1829,'2001-09-25 04:18:26',0,'abused','my parents made me rake them leaves...',4,0,0,0,'12.81.66.95','en'),(9099,1828,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','yay, i\\\'m glad to see camilla. ',0,0,0,0,'206.170.1.97','en'),(9100,414,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p>i wouldn\'t really call alex grey\'s work \"psychedelic.\" maybe, \r\nbut more than that i see him as a medical artist with a \r\nsoul. he makes paintings of the spiritual body as it has \r\nbeen seen in a few different religions and cultures - the \r\nchakra system, the energetic system of the body. for \r\nenergyworkers, people who do reiki or other energy \r\nwork, people who research electromagneticfields in the \r\nbody, etc, alex grey\'s work is really important. \r\ngroundbreaking actually. \r\n</p><p>\r\nthe \"sacred mirrors\" project is a really amazing body of \r\nwork - it\'s a group of  life size portrayals of humans, \r\npainted in standing positions, with the same frame (a \r\nvery intricate frame with symbols from different religious \r\norigins). the viewer stands in front of each painting and \r\nsees a \"mirror\" of themselves in the painting: a black \r\nwoman, a black man, a white woman, a white man, an \r\nasian woman, an asian man. the body, with skin. the \r\nskeleton alone. the muscular system alone. the \r\nnervous system alone. the spiritual self, the energetic \r\nself. the pregnant woman. \r\n</p><p>\r\nsure, his work is really obvious, and maybe that is \r\npsychedelic and hippie in nature: we are all one, we are \r\nthe same, etc. the thing that gets me about it the sheer \r\ndetail. the accuracy and sterile detail that he uses to \r\nportray the non-sterile self is really fascinating to me. it\'s unapologetically stark but done with such care. i love it.\r\n</p><p>\r\nhe\'s done a lot of work that\'s less obvious. like riding on \r\na crowded subway, seated underneath and ad that was \r\na picture of his face, for one hour. \r\nhe went to the north pole and it was art: \"polar \r\nwondering\"\r\n</p><p>\r\ni dunno. i am a convert. but this is why i want to go to \r\nschool for \"philosophy and religion\" or \"art and religion.\"\r\n</p><p>\r\ni\'m going to a weekend workshop presented by alex \r\ngrey at <a href=\"http://www.ciis.edu\">ciis</a>. it\'s totally \r\nfucking hippified and i\'m really *really* looking forward \r\nto it.\r\n</p><p>\r\nrob brezny, i dunno. his writing style seems egotistical.\r\n</p> \r\n',4,0,0,0,'206.170.1.97','en'),(9101,414,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<p>ok, i\\\'m looking at the new work up on his <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.alexgrey.com\\\">site</a>, and i can see \r\nhow you could look at it and think \\\"psychedelic.\\\" but try \r\nlooking at it from this perspective - we don\\\'t have much \r\nwell known modern day spiritual artwork. think of mister \r\ngrey as a historian for a modern day conciousness of \r\nreligion. if you want \\\"psychedelic,\\\" go down to the head \r\nshop and buy a tie dye tapestry, my friend!\r\n</p><p>\r\nsorry, i\\\'m feeling a little punchy. i have a cold and i\\\'ve \r\nbeen up too long. i feel like i don\\\'t exist and nothing i do \r\nmatters. not in a bad way, i\\\'m just in this really \r\nunrealistic bubble of snot and sleep dep.\r\n</p>',4,0,0,0,'206.170.1.97','en'),(9102,1826,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Dumb Moll','What\\\'s a stock?',0,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(9103,1829,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Fire Moll','When I was a child, we would make a giant pile of the \r\nleaves, and light them on fire. There would be much smoke. \r\nFather would put a partridge on a spit. Mother\\\'s eyes would \r\ngrow wild in the light. Burning meat.',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(9104,1828,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','mmmmmmmmmmmmm. caaaa meeeeeee laaaaaaa.....',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.162','en'),(9105,1828,'2004-07-27 05:00:32',578,'NetfÃ¶ng!','i think camilla is cute. cute, camilla, cute.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9106,414,'2001-09-25 14:01:43',0,'jo','\\\"his writing style seems egotistical.\\\"<BR>\r\ni would have said \\\"self-aggrandizing new age bullshit,\\\" but \r\nto each his own.<BR>\r\n(and i <b>really</b> like his column. devoted reader. i \r\nwanted to like the book!)',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(9107,1831,'2001-09-25 14:05:56',0,'trouble','is it anywhere near normal to be wide awake at anytime of \r\nday anymore?  <br><br>swinney.org seems to be one big \r\nsupport group for those of us who either don\\\'t sleep well \r\nor don\\\'t sleep with any regularity.  <br><br>hi, my name is \r\ntrouble and i can\\\'t sleep much anymore.',1,0,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(9108,1831,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>I\\\'m sleep-confused. I used to like my 8 hours a \r\nnight. Then I started sleeping from noon-5p and midnight-\r\n5am. That worked for some of college, then my sleeping \r\nschedule fell all to hell. I jsut slept a few hours here \r\nand there when i could, and stayed up all night a few times \r\na week. now i sleep from 2am-6am. that would have been \r\nunthinkable for me a few years ago, but now i really like \r\nmyelf more; not that it has anything to do with the sleep, \r\nor this article, for that matter, but i thought i\\\'d \r\nshare.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9109,1828,'2001-09-25 16:03:23',0,'critic','this is obviously not her writing style',0,0,0,0,'172.153.2.45','en'),(9110,1828,'2001-09-25 16:12:49',0,'Worbairn\\\'s Hacky Mucky','critic, if ye\\\'er so sure a ye\\\'erself, whyn\\\'tya go an poost \r\nye\\\'ar name!',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9111,1830,'2001-09-25 16:13:44',0,'Worbairn\\\'s Hacky Mucky','i was celebratin, ye knoow!',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9112,1787,'2001-09-25 16:14:25',0,'Worbairn\\\'s Hacky Mucky','what e\\\'re thes \\\"harry and sally\\\" shite?',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9113,44,'2001-09-25 16:36:28',0,'bmg','<p>you are special, <em>very special</em>.</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(9114,1828,'2001-09-25 17:10:34',0,'critic','Yes?  ',0,0,0,0,'172.153.2.45','en'),(9115,1828,'2001-09-25 17:24:35',0,'critic to','Worbairn\\\'s Hacky Mucky:  Oh, yea, I\\\'d really like for you \r\nto take on my personality also.',0,0,0,0,'172.153.2.45','en'),(9116,1828,'2001-09-25 17:26:33',0,'Worbairn\\\'s Hacky Mucky','you\\\'re still being defensive ;)',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9117,1828,'2001-09-25 17:41:37',0,'critic','well, who are you? ;)',0,0,0,0,'172.153.2.45','en'),(9118,1828,'2001-09-25 17:45:38',0,'Worbairn\\\'s Hacky Mucky','i am <a href=\\\"http://www.nadir.com\\\">Nadir</a>, long-time \r\nreader, first time commentor.  and you, my esteemed friend, \r\nare...?',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9119,1828,'2006-07-06 18:08:16',754,'Camilla Henrikke','critic: I usually just write lists for grocery shopping and \r\nI really am your uncle. ;)',6,0,0,0,'213.172.193.29','en'),(9120,1828,'2001-09-25 18:14:07',0,'jo','hi.<BR>\r\nwhat the fuck?',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(9121,1829,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','ah sweeping, my childhood friend.  ',0,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(9122,1828,'2001-09-25 18:18:39',0,'critic','  I am the critic and I dance under the moon.  The truth is \r\nmy sight and I sing its tune.  I am the critic and I live \r\nin a maze.  I see the path out of your phase.',0,0,0,0,'172.153.2.45','en'),(9123,1831,'2001-09-25 18:36:15',0,'Alan','That must be why I ended up here.  I have suffered from \r\ninsomnia for years.  The only solution that even came close \r\nto getting me to sleep were drugs that made me wake up \r\nfeeling like Medussa.  That only lasted for about a week \r\nand I decided that no sleep was a better solution.\r\n\r\nActually, its not true that I cant ever sleep.  I can sleep \r\nvery well in the fifteen minutes before I am supposed to \r\nwake up.  I think my body has decided that it wishes to \r\nsleep in any time period that I must definitely have to be \r\nawake.\r\n\r\nAlan',4,0,0,0,'198.211.32.155','en'),(9124,1824,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','...unless I come to your place and make you smoke weed and \r\nspin records.',4,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(9125,1824,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','...unless I come to your place and make you smoke weed and \r\nspin records.',4,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(9126,1829,'2001-09-25 18:52:10',0,'bmg','<p>sweeping has allways been my place to escape... <br>I am \r\npicturing young momma and poppa bmg raking leaves... the \r\nthought makes me quiet.</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(9127,1824,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>ess, I\\\'ll be doing that anyway ;)</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9128,1829,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','momma and poppa bmg.',0,0,0,0,'66.32.60.152','en'),(9129,1831,'2001-09-25 19:31:12',0,'kavaboy','kava kava does really help me sleep. just a little bit and \r\ni\\\'m all sleepy tired, then because it somehow doesn\\\'t \r\ninterfere with REM sleep (unlike alcohol or many sleeping \r\npills) i wake up feeling refreshed.',5,0,0,0,'156.153.254.42','en'),(9130,1831,'2001-09-25 19:34:31',0,'trouble','all this kava talk as of late, i must try this new and \r\nwonderous substance.  i hold little hope though, i think \r\ni\\\'m sleep challenged.',1,0,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(9131,1828,'2001-09-25 19:35:17',0,'jo','you do a lot of drugs and probably write poetry about the \r\ndark cavernous abyss of your pain. ',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(9132,1828,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','who doesn\\\'t?\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.5.96','en'),(9133,1829,'2001-09-25 19:46:12',0,'kat','foggy morning porch swings blankets and fall leaves apron \r\nstrings baking cookies arms around my waist fireplace crisp \r\nautumn air swirling breeze looking out the porch screen \r\ndogs woofing unseen ghosts away full moon snowflakes \r\ncandlelight fresh bread rising warm hands steamed windows \r\nlong cold nights misty breath ....',4,0,0,0,'32.100.70.217','en'),(9134,1834,'2001-09-25 20:04:20',0,'dude, you said','\\\"soaping up and feeling good.\\\" tee hee.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.5.96','en'),(9135,1834,'2001-09-25 20:08:46',0,'artistik0','the bed is just too big without her...',1,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(9136,1834,'2001-09-25 20:11:01',0,'leonard','<a href=\\\"http://www.wastedchicks.com/\\\">wasted chick. </a>',5,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(9137,1829,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','...training for cross-country, running miles through \r\nrolling wheat fields, walking off into dusty sunsets, that \r\nsmell, the moon dancing behind windblown trees, leaves \r\ncrunching underfoot, the smell of leaves, Halloween \r\ndecorations, Christmas shopping, the first swirling flakes, \r\nbut most off all, that autumn smell...',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(9138,1833,'2001-09-25 20:40:51',0,'erbie','under no circumstances must you hold on to preconceived \r\nnotions, ideals, fears, or baggage.  you are free to let it \r\ngo.  it may not be easy.  i have found that the way i \r\ndefine \\\"being in love\\\" now is that the person i am with \r\nsomehow enables me to love free of jealousy or past/future \r\ntrips.  i call it magic, but it actually is quite \r\nchemical.  chemicals can be magic.  and his particular \r\nmakeup of chemistry somehow makes me love him and not feel \r\njealous of any of his exes or worried about his attraction \r\nto other women.  it is directly related to the way he \r\nsmells (totally divine).  this is weird--i never cease to \r\nfind it weird myself--but true.  in other relationships \r\nwhere the guy did not smell so good to me/feel so good \r\nphysically (from flesh all the way to invisible particulate \r\npheromones and even down to the intangible energy level), i \r\nwas much more prone to jealousy, obession, and heavyness in \r\ngeneral.  when the chemistry\\\'s right, i feel, these \r\nattachments can be let go of more easily.  they\\\'re just a \r\nsmokescreen anyway.',1,0,0,0,'64.105.32.155','en'),(9139,1828,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i dunno. under the influence of psychoactives,i\r\nwrite about <i>beautiful</i> things. happy things. things i\r\ncouldn\\\'t even begin to touch with my status-quo-realist\r\npersonality and ego intact.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.255','en'),(9140,1833,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i\\\'ve recently been relationally-deflowered, and its\r\nno fun a-toll. btw, fine readers, essemar actually\r\n<i>can</i> hook up continuous one-night-stands for himself,\r\nthis skill being inextricably linked to the sex appeal of\r\nhis rat-tail mini-mullet ;)</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.255','en'),(9141,1833,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','dude, jpegs?\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(9142,1834,'2001-09-25 21:18:38',0,'Hallett','for me it\\\'s going to bed.  and more so finding little \r\npeices of evidence of her.  like the ticket stub i found in \r\nmy pocket yesturday, i dare not think of some of those \r\nabsolutely spectactular moments we shared.  but the higher \r\nthe high, the lower the low; balance.',2,0,0,0,'64.158.83.98','en'),(9143,1833,'2001-09-25 21:29:31',0,'Hallett','with your first love you notice so many details and quirks \r\nthat become endearing and a symbol of your understanding of \r\nwho that person is.  what\\\'s scary is when someday you \r\nrealize that those quirks, those things you found so \r\namazingly special, are shared by many others.  but we can \r\ngo much much deeper than quirks, than a first love.  \r\nexperience makes us dynamic, and that allows for much more \r\npossibility.  we can always go deeper, and give more.',4,0,0,0,'64.158.83.98','en'),(9144,1833,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mashed Moll','Life is better with lower standards. Love? No. Tolerance? \r\nYes.',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(9145,1837,'2001-09-25 23:16:22',0,'john','hey baby\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(9146,1837,'2001-09-25 23:16:40',0,'ho','you datin\\\', sugar?\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(9147,1837,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','hi chi chi!\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(9148,1837,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>yesterday I was walking down west macarthur, or \r\nshall we say, \\\"hooker row\\\", and someone beeped at \r\nme. I looked across the 4 lane road and saw this man \r\nwho looked a whole lot like ix (from that distance). I \r\nthought, hey! ix got a car and came to get me for an \r\nadventure.</p>\r\n<p>am I fool? the guy flipped a bitch and pulled over on \r\nthe side of the road, where he rolled down the window \r\nand leaned towards the door, and I instantly realized it \r\nwas not ix, it looked nothing like ix. I immediately \r\nmumbled \\\"oh sorry I thought I knew you but I dont\\\" and \r\nhe cut me off saying, \\\"you look familiar!\\\" and i yelled \r\n\\\"yeah i made a mistake\\\" and booked my ass down the \r\nstreet, when he yelled after me, \\\"Yr good lookin!\\\"</p>\r\n<p>wb suggested the guy thought I was a streetwalker. \r\nI guess standing on the road or sitting on a bench is an \r\ninvitation to be fiddled with?</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.32.60.152','en'),(9149,385,'2001-09-25 23:32:42',0,'dude mang','this is rad\r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(9150,1832,'2001-09-26 01:02:15',0,'bmg','<p>ahhh... sweeping. I love sweeping.</p><p>when I \r\nwas a little kid my parents would send me off to my \r\ngrandparents farm for the summers. I would get to drive \r\ntractors, collect cantelopes and watermelons then eat \r\nthem. I can remember evenings walking through the \r\ncotton fields back to farm house all sticky from working, \r\nplaying and eating fruit. I would see my grandfather \r\ntending to the vegtables in the garden...</p>\r\n<img src=\\\'http://www.lepard.org/post/farmin.jpg\\\'>\r\n<img src=\\\'http://www.lepard.org/post/farmin0.jpg\\\'>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(9151,1830,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','who are the satritains?',0,0,0,0,'216.27.183.161','en'),(9152,815,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','didn\\\'t go to boston. stayed in brooksville. all summer.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.5.2','en'),(9153,1830,'2001-09-26 02:30:50',0,'The Satritains','are an internationally renowned doo-wop group from \r\nLomaville, Kentucky.  Whenever a member dies, they are \r\nreplaced with one of the many young hopefuls back in \r\nLomaville.  Kinda like Menudo.  Their biggest hit, to date, \r\nhas been \\\"Holler \\\'Mercy!\\\' When You\\\'ve Had Enough.\\\"  They \r\nare available for tractor pulls, inaugurations, and bar and \r\nbat mitzvahs. Contact International Creative Management \r\nfomoinfo.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.5.2','en'),(9154,1832,'2001-09-26 02:45:03',0,'ty','Welcome! This is our farmhouse. This time of year, the \r\nclusterflies can get pretty bad, and there\\\'s nothing you \r\ncan do, but swat them. ',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.15','en'),(9155,1833,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','everyone sees the quirks, but you are the only one who \r\nrealizes how special they are, and you feel the need to \r\nshow her as well. that\\\'s love; you can change the pronouns \r\nto fit your situation.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.15','en'),(9156,1834,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','Now I ain\\\'t gonna say that I <i>masturbate</i> in there, \r\nbut sometimes I like to soap \\\'im up real good, and wash \\\'im \r\nreal fast.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.15','en'),(9157,1834,'2001-09-26 02:57:11',0,'you','nasty little man\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.5.2','en'),(9158,1834,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>hey, i like showers as much as the next guy, soapin\\\'\r\nup, gettin\\\' clean; purely for bath purposes.  although, i\r\nmust be candid- one of my more sensual experiences involved\r\nhaving my hair washed. intense scalp scrubbing, heh.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.255','en'),(9159,1838,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','miss ya, shorty.',0,0,0,0,'66.32.60.152','en'),(9160,1833,'2001-09-26 03:05:29',0,'Mulletia','Note, Simon: a very patriotic essemar!<br><img\r\nsrc=\\\"http://www.mulletsgalore.com/mulletpix/classifications/X/amer/americandream.jpg\\\">',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.255','en'),(9161,1837,'2001-09-26 04:40:47',0,'kat','being human is invitation to be fiddled with...',4,0,0,0,'32.102.109.28','en'),(9162,1838,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','to keep from getting overwhelmed by lists, only put three \r\nthings on it. put everything else on a separate list so you \r\ndon\\\'t forget, but put it somewhere else. you sleep first \r\nthough!!\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(9163,1833,'2003-05-10 16:09:14',79,'yeti','dude, that\\\'s a pretty powerful mullet',0,0,0,0,'216.27.183.161','en'),(9164,1833,