nrolling it in toilet paper, and sucking on sweet death.  \r\nThat\\\'s how much I <i>love</i> smoking.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(9263,1843,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i hit the unfiltered luckies when i need a smoke. \r\ngood enough to do the trick, bad enough to keep me from \r\nwanting more too often. i just have a bad habit of chain-\r\nsmoking the whole pack in like 5 minutes, though.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9264,1800,'2001-09-27 15:12:47',0,'Jamazon','Who thinks i suck?',1,0,0,0,'217.32.156.32','en'),(9265,1843,'2004-07-27 05:00:32',578,'NetfÃ¶ng!','i\\\'ve been trying to quit since like may, but somehow, i\\\'ve \r\nended up smoking more. imagine that. ooh, the draw of the \r\nparliaments is too strong!',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9266,1843,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','I was thinking about living in a monastary for a month in \r\norder to quit smoking.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(9267,1843,'2001-09-27 15:27:52',0,'jo','i was just telling lou on the phone about smoking sampoerna \r\nxtra\\\'s out the window of bedroom when i was 15.<BR>\r\n\\\"smoke clove cigarettes and drink vermouth like i was 17, \r\nthat would be a scream.\\\"',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(9268,1843,'2001-09-27 15:28:48',0,'jo','ess: i\\\'m taking up knitting. mostly because: KNITTING! is \r\nso great. but also because it will give me something to do \r\nwith my hands while my friends are smoking and i\\\'m. wishing \r\ni were dead.',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(9269,1843,'2001-09-27 15:33:29',0,'(oh, also)','<a \r\nhref=\\\"http://www.intelihealth.com/IH/ihtIH/WSIHW000/24479/24\r\n549/250734.html\\\">clove cigarettes are worse for you than \r\nregular cigarettes.</a> i had a friend go to the hospital \r\nbecause she was <b>coughing up blood</b> from smoking 7 \r\nclove cigarettes one night. ',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(9270,1843,'2004-07-27 05:00:32',578,'NetfÃ¶ng!','i simply adore cloves and am majorly sketched to hear that \r\nbad news... ignorance is bliss! someone tell me smoking \r\nincreases the libido or something... something, please!',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9271,1843,'2001-09-27 16:30:35',0,'american spirit big chief','We created American Spirits in blue, extra blue and yellow \r\npacks as a way to get the whiteman back for smallpox.',4,0,0,0,'156.153.254.41','en'),(9272,1828,'2006-07-06 18:08:16',754,'Camilla Henrikke','Jesus fucking christ, I(being the owner of \r\nwww.wallflower.nu) DID post this entry. Is that so weird? \r\nEmail wallflower@wallflower.nu and I will confirm it. Geez.',6,0,0,0,'213.172.193.29','en'),(9273,1843,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','I can\\\'t actually quit smoking completely, for one simple \r\nreason: smoke breaks.  I can\\\'t imagine sitting at my desk \r\nfor a full 8 hours.<br><br>NetfÃ¶ng!: Read some old \r\nadvertising from circa 1920\\\'s.  They used to extoll the \r\nvirtues of cigarettes in cleaning out the lungs and making \r\nit easier to breathe.  The truth is, cloves are \r\nhorrendously bad for you.  Clove oil has a natural \r\nanesthetic in it which keeps you from feeling your lungs \r\nbeing shredded.  Without that smoking a clove would be an \r\nincredibly painful experience.  Also, cigarettes are the \r\nleading cause of impotence in young men.',2,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(9274,1828,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','It\\\'s just weird that someone people on this site have been \r\nlusting after is actually posting here out of the blue.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(9275,1843,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','american spirit cigarettes = hippy killers',4,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(9276,1843,'2001-09-27 17:30:12',0,'chi chi',' i smoke american spirits and i\\\'m no hippy.<br>\r\nbut i also started them when i was attempting to quit 2 \r\nyears ago.. i had managed to cut down to 2 smokes a \r\nday, but those camels were fast burning, and i figuiresd \r\ntwo american spirits would last me longer.',0,0,0,0,'64.172.45.37','en'),(9277,1844,'2001-09-27 17:49:59',0,'jimmynofun','music is over',4,0,0,0,'156.153.254.41','en'),(9278,1844,'2001-09-27 17:56:02',0,'bmg','<p>i crave good music.</p><p> kdogg and i saw buken \r\nand conrad at rave party in houston... we didn\\\'t realize it \r\nwas bukem until we left, saying \\\"who was that? that \r\nwas fabulous!\\\"\r\nthen we realized it was bukem, and it just made sense \r\nthat we liked it...\\\"of course it was him!\\\" I fell asleep to \r\nbukem last night. I haven\\\'t heard the new one... can\\\'t \r\nwait.</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(9279,1833,'2001-09-27 17:58:47',0,'essamar','I don\\\'t KNOW!!!',4,0,0,0,'172.171.213.254','en'),(9280,1844,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','My roommate has been at two parties where Bukem was supposed\r\nto play and he ended up not making either of them.  Two\r\nyears ago in Miami for the WMC, his records were stolen so\r\nhe couldn\\\'t play his set and they slotted Juan Atkins in his\r\nstead (the MC didn\\\'t even know who he was introducing:\r\n\\\"Uhmmm, Juan Atkins from, uhm, Detroit?\\\" [reading off a\r\ncard]).  I guess that wasn\\\'t so bad, seeing one of the\r\ngodfathers of Techno instead of Bukem isn\\\'t so bad.  Then\r\nagain at DEMF this summer, Bukem cancelled for some reason I\r\nhave since forgotten.<br><br>My roommate is cursed to never\r\nsee Bukem live.  I hope he comes here sometime in the near\r\nfuture.  I really want to check him out live.  He\\\'s totally\r\ngot his own style and everything he touches is magic.  And\r\nConrad is totally not your standard MC, he\\\'s just on some\r\nother shit, entirely.',1,0,0,0,'64.229.74.80','en'),(9281,1843,'2001-09-27 18:16:09',0,'Alan','my friends (most of who are non-smokers) laugh when at end \r\nof a hike (or short walk in our case), my cousin and i are \r\nwinded.  we will be standing there sweating and breathing \r\nas if we are going to die.  the first thing we do before we \r\neven catch our breath is reach for a smoke.  i will not \r\neven be able to really take in a big draw on a cig but the \r\nlittle bit i do pull through feels so so good.',2,0,0,0,'198.211.32.155','en'),(9282,1840,'2001-09-27 18:27:57',0,'kat','i was on the phone last night with bmg...he said <i>deep \r\ndicking</i> three or four times.\r\n\r\nhe really likes that.',4,0,0,0,'32.100.67.180','en'),(9283,1843,'2001-09-27 18:28:55',0,'glaxowelcome','try new zyban(tm) for your quitting smoking jones...',3,0,0,0,'156.153.254.41','en'),(9284,689,'2001-09-27 18:30:35',0,'bmg to chris','<p>shut up, dork.</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(9285,1843,'2001-09-27 18:30:57',0,'runboyrun','i quit smoking by replacing the habit with the habit of \r\nrunning. it\\\'s a pastime cannot keep up and smoke at the \r\nsame time. and it worked.\r\n\r\nit also helped with the inevitable weight gain that happens \r\nwhen you quit.\r\n\r\nbut still years later smoking remains a powerful attraction.\r\n\r\n',3,0,0,0,'156.153.254.41','en'),(9286,1828,'2001-09-27 18:33:34',0,'thanking you','thanks you',4,0,0,0,'156.153.254.41','en'),(9287,1840,'2001-09-27 18:35:13',0,'gmb','<p>heh. heh... Kat said <em>deep \r\ndicking</em>.</p><p> i wonder which he likes, giving or \r\nreveiving? hehehe... I am regressing... I am now \r\n14.</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(9288,1840,'2001-09-27 18:43:02',0,'Dr. Frank-n-Furter','i know which he prefers...',1,0,0,0,'32.100.67.180','en'),(9289,1840,'2001-09-27 18:44:12',0,'bmg','<p>Whats <em>up</em> Doc? =)~</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(9290,1828,'2006-07-06 18:08:16',754,'Camilla Henrikke','Hooray for lust?',3,0,0,0,'213.172.193.29','en'),(9291,1845,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','why did somebody think this was not camilla? are you \r\ncamilla? the woman with the cheekbones?',0,0,0,0,'66.32.60.152','en'),(9292,1844,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>would anyone rip either or both of bukem and/or \r\nstereolab (did i get my boolean expressions right)?</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.32.60.152','en'),(9293,1844,'2001-09