nd the White Stripes.  what does this matter?  \r\nnothing, i just like promoting the White Stripes these \r\ndays.  go figure.',1,0,0,0,'216.142.219.138','en'),(9303,1845,'2001-09-27 21:01:45',0,'Alan','all of this talk about being the real... makes me wonder if \r\ni am the real alan.  techinically, i am not.  alan is my \r\nmiddle name and this is the first time i have used it for \r\nanything.  before it was always that funny name in between \r\nmy first and last names on checks, credit cards, and my \r\ntrusty passport.  i have never really had any connection to \r\nit.  so, i guess by using it here, i am trying to build a \r\nrelationship with my middle name.    \r\n\r\nis being the real \\\"camilla\\\" anything like being the real \r\njohn prine?  i must get out of my cave more.  people are \r\naccusing people of impersonating people i have never heard \r\nof.  its one crazy world.\r\n\r\nalan uh or is it',2,0,0,0,'198.211.32.155','en'),(9304,1845,'2001-09-27 21:08:28',0,'prince charles:','tampon, deodorant, whatever -- come to me camilla parker \r\nbowles on the back of a white steed wearing nothing at all \r\nbut fDS',3,0,0,0,'156.153.254.41','en'),(9305,1844,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','You used the <b>E</b> word.  I dislike that word. \r\nElectronic, I can deal with; but you append an <i>a</i> to\r\nit and I get all squeamish.',6,0,0,0,'64.229.74.80','en'),(9306,1843,'2001-09-27 23:07:12',0,'huevita','personally, <font size=\\\"5\\\" point-size=\\\"20\\\"><b>I prefer to \r\nsmoke cock.</b></font>',0,0,0,0,'66.32.60.152','en'),(9307,1843,'2001-09-27 23:17:49',0,'bmg','<p>heheh... egg said <em>smoke cock</em></p>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.76.248','en'),(9308,1847,'2001-09-27 23:21:55',0,'chi chi','for me it\\\'s the twinkling tune of the icecream truck as it \r\ncomes down my street. i believe in magic, in fairies, \r\nand giants. i believe there is no thing as too much \r\nicecream',0,0,0,0,'64.172.45.37','en'),(9309,1847,'2001-09-27 23:26:30',0,'eerbie','deja vu is also magical for me.  it reminds me that time is \r\nnot linear at all, but all happening at once.',3,0,0,0,'64.105.32.155','en'),(9310,1847,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to chi chi','you are such an incredible cornball.',0,0,0,0,'66.32.60.152','en'),(9311,1847,'2001-09-27 23:31:03',0,'chi chi to egg','better to be a cornball, and be excited over the icecream \r\ntruck, then crazy and excited over a shantytown.',0,0,0,0,'64.172.45.37','en'),(9312,1846,'2001-09-27 23:31:57',0,'huevita','multiple nicknames are such a BOTHER.',0,0,0,0,'66.32.60.152','en'),(9313,1847,'2001-09-27 23:33:00',0,'chi chi','speaking of which the icecream truck just came rolling \r\npast. i\\\'m trying the tutone \\\"artificially flavored vanilla \r\nicecream in a quiescently frozen confection shell\\\"',0,0,0,0,'64.172.45.37','en'),(9314,1847,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','dont say shantytown, you WHORE!!!!! whatever you do, \r\ndont say shantytown, you lascivious slam hound!!! youll \r\ngive away your whorish secrets.',0,0,0,0,'66.32.60.152','en'),(9315,1847,'2001-09-27 23:39:28',0,'chi chi','listen here egg, i can say whatever the fuck i want. \r\nSHANTYTOWN!!!! SHANTYTOWN!!!!!',0,0,0,0,'64.172.45.37','en'),(9316,1843,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','i predict there will be some swinney.org cock smoking action\r\nthis weekend.',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(9317,1843,'2001-09-28 00:03:36',0,'what,','ix is going to give the D to essemar to help him quit \r\nsmoking?',0,0,0,0,'66.32.60.152','en'),(9318,1847,'2001-09-28 00:52:59',0,'ghost','ha ha...i just emailed egg to say i Shantytown sounded fun. \r\nand i hadn\\\'t even read this yet.',6,0,0,0,'32.102.109.108','en'),(9319,1847,'2001-09-28 00:58:14',0,'ps','there are <a href=\\\"http://images.burningman.com/index.cgi?\r\nimage=3100\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">more exciting things</a> to run \r\nafter than just the ice cream truck...',1,0,0,0,'32.102.109.108','en'),(9320,1848,'2001-09-28 01:01:00',0,'ghost','maybe he is simply confused and doing what he can to try \r\nand figure it all out like the rest of us.',4,0,0,0,'32.102.109.108','en'),(9321,1848,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>i really think you have to reconsider this judgement upon\r\npeople based on a scrap of evidence like an eminem cd.  you\r\ndont really know how that person got it or why.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i owned two eminem cd\\\'s at one time.</P>\r\n<P>austin - 2</P>\r\n<P>i bought them both at a best buy in el paso, texas, on my\r\nway to los angeles, california.  it was a good three years\r\nafter the whole eminem on the cover of\r\npeople/time/newsweek/nyt/wham/playboy/etc bananza.  i was\r\ndriving allong and i thought, i have no oppinion about him. \r\nall this time people have been getting riled about eminem\r\nand his wife beating, drugs, and attempts to be a good\r\nfather anyway.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>isnt there an eminem thread <a\r\nhref=\\\"http://swinney.org/journals/search.phtml?search_this=eminem\\\">up\r\nin this biatch somewhere</a>?</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i listened to them both a few times, maybe three.  i\r\nliked some of the songs.  some i thought were stupid and\r\nplayed to seventeen magazine.  some of the songs were like\r\nnothing i had heard before, genius?</P>\r\n\r\n',3,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(9322,1848,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>oh and tori amos?</P>\r\n<P>egg - 1</P>',4,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(9323,1846,'2001-09-28 01:21:23',0,'MultipleMan','ok. if you say so.',1,0,0,0,'24.27.31.48','en'),(9324,1848,'2001-09-28 02:07:02',0,'I hunt elves','Elitist or someone who has taste?',1,0,0,0,'24.27.31.48','en'),(9325,1848,'2001-09-28 02:08:28',0,'asstin','<P>hi</P>\r\n<P>yes, what is it about eminem that people dont write him\r\noff as a sort of 2LiveCrew?\r\n</P><P>\r\nwell, i dont have my notes on me regarding his few albums,\r\nbut i think it became obvious to me early on in the\r\nlistening that he was trying to do/show some things:</P>\r\n<UL>\r\n<LI>anger some people who get a few seconds into the\r\nnewsbite and clench their fists\r\n<LI>people slip up and do wrong at times\r\n<LI>people intentionally do wrong things at times\r\n<LI>sometimes people are right in doing so, from a\r\nperspective\r\n<LI>express some of the frustrations of being poor and\r\nhaving aspirations\r\n<LI>express some of the frustrations of working very hard\r\nand being told \\\"no\\\"\r\n</UL>\r\n<P>of course it is difficult to keep from projecting. \r\nforemost what the listener takes away from the albums is a\r\npersonal preferences.  it is not all for one and one for\r\nall.  the \\\'intro to teenage psychology\\\' songs might not\r\nappeal to someone like me who is past that stage in life,\r\nbut the concept of \\\"Tired of having to deal..\\\" definately\r\nstrikes a chord in my soul.  some days i want to stay in bed\r\nknowing that i will be critiziced at work.  and my attitude\r\nat that time is coined in the phrase SUCK IT.  but i get up\r\nand go to work anyway hoping for the day i can give up or\r\nhave the nerve to make my own way in the financial web that\r\nmotivates me.  no i am not going to \\\"..grab the steel\\\", but\r\ni sure like listening to that song that goes:</P>\r\n<BLOCKQUOTE>\r\nTired of having to deal.\r\n<BR>\r\nTired of having to deal with\r\n<BR>\r\nthe bullshit without grabbing the steel.\r\n</BLOCKQUOTE>\r\n<P>it has a nice rythm to it, very nice.  the way he bebops\r\nthose lyrics out is soothing.</P>\r\n<P>another point of interest is his progression.  in his\r\nfollow up album he has an intro that you might describe as\r\n<I>hypertextual</I>, egg.  he describes getting fan mail\r\nfrom some guy out in america, and although he is reading it\r\non the album he did not have time to reply to the letters.\r\nthen one day he finally sits down to write the letter of\r\nreply only to realize that that particular fan commited an\r\nimmitation of his fictional murder scenario described in one\r\nof his songs where he slits his girlfriend\\\'s through and\r\nputs her in the truck and drives to the ocean with his\r\ndaughter to take mommy swimming.  the realization that is\r\nwell executed and give the listener a genuine sense of\r\nregret for having enjoyed the song, maybe, but certainly a\r\nsense of his own regret should that event of immitation\r\ncrime actually be carried out.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>and the beats are slammin\\\'.  maybe i will have some more\r\non this topic later.</P>',3,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(9326,1848,'2001-09-28 03:47:59',0,'ty','It\\\'s all about the Benjamins. Baby.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.175','en'),(9327,1843,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','read Emerson. he will tell you how to quit.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.175','en'),(9328,1848,'2004-07-27 05:00:32',578,'NetfÃ¶ng!','how can i hate Eminem\\\'s music so much but still think he\\\'s\r\ncute, just so? hm.',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.255','en'),(9329,1843,'2001-09-28 05:21:43',0,'jo','\\\"cocksmoker\\\" is my favorite term of affection, ever.<BR>\r\nas in: \\\"hey, surrender control of the remote, cocksmoker.\\\"',1,0,0,0,'172.165.149.253','en'),(9330,1848,'2001-09-28 05:38:07',0,'misunderstood','people should have an iq/maturity test before being allowed \r\nto listen to eminem.\r\nhe\\\'s actually fucking clever.\r\nmy take on eminem is that he is trying to make us wonder \r\nwhy we are laughing and raise awareness of these \r\nsituations.... that just aren\\\'t confined to hiphop.\r\n\r\ni don\\\'t think he\\\'s much of anything the media make him out \r\nto be.\r\n\r\nyeah, and i\\\'m a girl, okay?\r\n',0,0,0,0,'210.54.208.205','en'),(9331,1844,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','Bukem was meant to play here in NZ last year, but he got \r\nbusted with pot in customs and was sent home.\r\n\r\nWho in their right mind tries to bring pot into NZ? It\\\'s \r\nlike... It\\\'s almost as silly as trying to bring it in to \r\nJamaica.',0,0,0,0,'203.96.111.200','en'),(9332,1848,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>on a very personal level, i find his commitment to \r\nfatherhood to be an asset to the community.</P>\r\n',3,0,0,0,'64.174.154.94','en'),(9333,1848,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>I have had two experiences with eminem. That day \r\nin Sweden and then some other time later. I lied about \r\nhaving heard all the sound-bites- all of my information \r\nabout his possible intentions or \\\"genius\\\" come from \r\n(verbally-spouted)  theories of young men I know \r\npersonally. I have honestly not read one single article \r\nabout his personal life or his own words about his \r\nwork, and I know he was arrested or something in the \r\npast few years. Unfortunately, I am not a journalist and \r\ndont worry about embellishing/lying when Im having an \r\nemotional fit.</p>\r\n<p> The thing about hearing this \\\"beating\\\" or \r\n\\\"hyper-beating\\\" or \\\"conceptual beating\\\" that got on my \r\nnerves is that I have no interest in the possible \r\nambiguity of its intention. The sound itself is odious to \r\nmy ears in a visceral and intuitive way. Perhaps this \r\nreaction only reveals my sensitivity to any suggestion of \r\ngender-based violence. it\\\'s hard to say.</p>\r\n<p>I was trying to impart the revelation I experienced \r\nfrom hearing \\\"97 bonnie..\\\" (which Im not sure Ive ever \r\nheard the original of)covered by a female, which made \r\nme actually read the lyrics and re-examine my visceral \r\nreaction.</p> \r\n<p>Just while we are keeping score, I did not purchase \r\nthe tori amos record. It is Jay\\\'s. I will listen to it a lot \r\nthough.</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.32.60.152','en'),(9334,1848,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to misunderstood','ive never laughed at anything ive heard by eminem.',0,0,0,0,'66.32.60.152','en'),(9335,1848,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>ok, a few more things. This bit about his desire to \r\n\\\"anger people who clench their fists a few minutes into \r\nthe news bite\\\" doesnt strike me as anything to \r\ncongratulate him for. Ive probably brought this  up \r\nbefore, but George Lucas once said that its not hard to \r\nmake people cry. Just strangle a puppy onscreen! In \r\nthe same way, it doesnt take much to anger a woman \r\nlike me. Just flippantly record sounds of violence! woop \r\ndee fuckin do. so then maybe ill sticker his cds in the \r\nrecord store saying \\\"this guy is a prick\\\", and does \r\nanything but media exchange take place? And I just \r\ndont appreciate questions about violence against \r\nwomen being obscured by such a media circus.</p>\r\n<p> I mean, let\\\'s say hypothetically that he is trying to \r\nbegin some kind of public dialogue about domestic \r\nviolence. if he is honestly using his own lyrics as a sort \r\nof reverse propoganda, then why doesnt he explicitly \r\nsay that outside of the music? If he is using these \r\nserious scenarios merely as attention-getting fodder, in \r\nsome way, he doesnt take them seriously. I dont think \r\nthe issue of a man beating his spouse to submission \r\nor death as justifiable is up for debate. I dont think he \r\ntakes it for granted that his listeners will understand the \r\nambigious nature of his words. and maybe he is \r\nowning up to that in this self-referential song that austin \r\ndescribed, but is aknowledgement enough? there is a \r\nheavy responsibility in this game he is playing, the \r\nproverbial shouting \\\"fire\\\" in a crowded building and \r\nthen running away.</p>\r\n<p>and the real question I have is, <i>why</i> is he \r\ninterested in creating such simple reactions? In other \r\nwords, this \\\"hypertextual\\\" song content sounds clever to \r\nme, but it doesnt answer why he wrote the original \r\nsong outlining such a scenario in the first place. Is he \r\nsaying, \\\"oh you guys im really sorry i didnt mean for you \r\nto ACT IT OUT...\\\", and if so, what exactly <i>did</i> he \r\nmean? It keeps everything in too ambiguous a place for \r\nsuch a LOADED LOADED LOADED subject to live. </p>',0,0,0,0,'66.32.60.152','en'),(9336,1847,'2001-09-28 09:05:53',0,'jim','jim',0,0,0,1,'66.92.4.146','en'),(9337,1845,'2001-09-28 09:32:33',0,'Jamie','tampon - deodourant? How are these things the same?',1,0,0,0,'217.32.161.0','en'),(9338,1848,'2001-09-28 09:34:42',0,'jim@thisishomemade.com','',0,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(9339,1848,'2001-09-28 10:10:53',0,'sean','the <a href=\\\"http://www.salon.com/ent/music/feature/2000/06/07/eminem/index.html\\\">critics</a> love him. <b>austin</b> can i have my eminem cd\\\'s back?',1,0,0,0,'158.252.216.207','en'),(9340,1842,'2001-09-28 10:28:49',0,'Jamie','I you think that shits scary you should try living in \r\nNorthern Ireland.',4,0,0,0,'217.32.161.0','en'),(9341,1848,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','but is it art?',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(9342,1845,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','...anything that gets to cuddle up inside Camilla\\\'s kootch.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(9343,1847,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','The girl I met in Central Park agreed to go out with me \r\nthen backed out the next day because I gave her a bad deja \r\nvu.<br><br>I wish I could move back to that wonderous \r\nshanty town.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(9344,1848,'2001-09-28 13:12:41',0,'i, too','<p>have boys in my life that expound on eminem. from an <a \r\nhref=\\\"http://sent.diaryland.com\\\">email to one of them</a> \r\nrecently:</p>\r\n<tt><p>> My argument is that rather than exisiting as a \r\nmere simplistic and<BR>> misogynistic rant, Eminem\\\'s tracks \r\nform a highly mediated, reflexive<BR>> and self conscious \r\npastiche of the kinds of images flying around in<BR>> what \r\nRushkoff refers to as the \\\'datasphere\\\' and indeed, uh, \r\neveryday<BR>> life. Um, that\\\'s very wanky (and impromptu!) \r\nbut I think I can back<BR>> it up (although I really \r\nhaven\\\'t given much thought as to how yet...)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>yeah i want further exploration of that, please.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>because you were saying, i think, that people who listen \r\nto eminem are in\r\non the joke, meaning: \\\"understand the artist, understand \r\nthe intention.\\\"</p>\r\n\r\n<p>but to say that he\\\'s just reflecting the images that \r\nsurround him is\r\nsaying: \\\"understand the world he lives in, understand the \r\nartist.\\\"</p>\r\n\r\n<p>so which is the case? are you saying that we should \r\nall \\\"get\\\" eminem\\\'s\r\njoke because he\\\'s eminem or because he\\\'s a rap artist at \r\nthe turn of the\r\ncentury?</p></tt>',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(9345,1847,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i quite enjoyed snorting coke and sleeping on a cardboard box in a shantytown of sorts, once.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9346,1851,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','Why can\\\'t I have meaningless flings?  Why am I so overly-\r\nambitious?  Why am I so damned discontent?',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(9347,1851,'2004-07-27 05:00:32',578,'NetfÃ¶ng! to essemar','plurghh. you sound like patrick bateman. those three \r\nfactors for me arent as interrelated as i once thought. i \r\nused to program my personality by them, instead of vice-\r\nversa. as for now, i\\\'m staunchly trying to invent \r\na \\\"meaningful fling\\\". we\\\'ll see.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9348,1848,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','I\\\'ve always wondered what the male version of the \r\nterm \\\'misogyny\\\' is.  (It\\\'s not \\\'misanthropy,\\\' which refers \r\nto general hate of people despite its etymology.)  Does \r\nsuch a word even exist in english?  Maybe women aren\\\'t base \r\nenough (like men) to actually hate an entire gender, \r\ntherefore making such a term unnecessary.  Or maybe, women \r\nas a gender are much more deserving of our disgust?  Or are \r\nwe going to fall back on the old standby of blaming it on \r\nthe patriarchy.<br><br>Oh yeah, regarding M an\\\' M, my \r\nopinions tend to be pretty simple.  I think he\\\'s just \r\nexploiting some loaded topics in order to get media \r\nattention and sell records.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(9349,1848,'2001-09-28 14:08:56',0,'Did I Hear someone say','<blink><b><i>BLING?</b></i></blink>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9350,1851,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','heh... the grass is always greener.  No matter how much you \r\nhave, you will always want more.  I just saw some \r\nreflections of my own life in what you wrote.  It\\\'s the \r\nsame thing, only turned inside out.<p>I\\\'ve also had some \r\ngreat meaningful flings.</p>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(9351,1851,'2001-09-28 14:22:59',0,'bret ellis','hey patrick, dont you have some videos to return?',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9352,1845,'2001-09-28 14:37:07',0,'Jamie','ya dirty harlem globetrotter',1,0,0,0,'217.32.161.0','en'),(9353,1845,'2001-09-28 14:45:52',0,'secret admirer','i\\\'d climb up in camilla\\\'s kootchie any day!',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9354,1853,'2001-09-28 14:46:34',0,'jo','my steak is a little mealy, did someone drop it?',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(9355,1853,'2001-09-28 14:52:04',0,'Doktor','so, let me see: apples are blue and steaks are red... no \r\nwait, uh, im confused.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9356,1845,'2001-09-28 15:11:12',0,'Jamie','she has good bone structure',2,0,0,0,'217.32.161.0','en'),(9357,1846,'2001-09-28 15:26:15',0,'I have','27 aliases on swinney.org',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9358,1851,'2001-09-28 15:28:34',0,'Titus','welcome to the winter of my disconent',1,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(9359,1848,'2001-09-28 15:29:45',0,'littlearsonist','geez her cover of Real Men was really awesome and more \r\nimportant maybe?',1,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(9360,1848,'2001-09-28 15:34:52',0,'Critic','<i>Fuckin-A</i>, man. Have you ever heard a <i>worse</i> \r\nrendition of \\\"happiness is a warm gun\\\"? That one was \r\nbutchered in a way that only Tori could do it.  I think I\\\'m \r\ngonna cut an all-male cover-album of Tori\\\'s songs. And \r\nbutcher them. Badly. Hooray for Masculinity!</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9361,1848,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>the breeders do a fantabulous cover of it. \r\n(\\\"happinesss...\\\")</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(9362,1853,'2001-09-28 15:56:00',0,'kat','the fun part comes when you dig someone so much that you\\\'re \r\nboth willing to spend hours trying to see things from their \r\npersepective...and finding ways to share yours.',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.116','en'),(9363,1853,'2001-09-28 16:13:24',0,'eerb','i tripped on this as a child...asking my mom, well, what \r\ndoes red REALLY look like to YOU?  Cause I know what it \r\nlooks like to ME, but how do I know my EYES aren\\\'t \r\ndifferent?<br>\r\nI think one of the best parts about the psychedelic \r\nexperience is the expansion of perception which enables you \r\nto trust that the true essence and fabric of reality is \r\nmore multifaceted than any human organ can normally \r\nperceive.<br>\r\nstill, in the final analysis of the great color debate,sub- \r\nvs. objective reality is a wash.  my blue is mine, and can \r\nnever belong to anyone else.  i can describe the way the \r\nsky looked last night as i rode over the hill at dusk...the \r\ndeepening green where the sun had disappeared, the golden \r\nglow of headlights streaking past, the gradual indigo \r\ndeepening above my head, the warming and burning of my \r\nlungs as the hill got steeper, my gears clicking, thoughts \r\nhumming, almost sideswiped by an inattentive yuppie on a \r\ncell phone...do you see that blue?  the whole world felt \r\nblue at 7:00 last night.  can you see it?',1,0,0,0,'64.105.32.155','en'),(9364,1848,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','i think it is his attitude problem that is so much fun to\r\nlisten to.',3,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(9365,1848,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','I\\\'ve heard a Helmet cover of Bj&ouml;rk\\\'s <i>Human\r\nBehavior</i> on this Music For Our Mother Oceans\r\ncompilation. It was... interesting.  A hippie friend of mine\r\nowns the disc.',2,0,0,0,'64.229.74.80','en'),(9366,1848,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>i have nothing more to say about eminem, and i am\r\nsuprised i have found anything at all.  which leads me to\r\nexamine my own reason for defending him.\r\n</P><P>\r\ni have bopped my head to some eminem songs and mumbled\r\ncool.  i dont think i would ever be able to argue him\r\noutside of his misogynist label.  i cant even spell\r\nmisogynist without referencing the text.  maybe tori just\r\nwanted to sell a few more albums on top of her already\r\nbazillion copies a year.  i dont think anyone would say\r\neminem does not problems.</P><P>one of my ex girlfriends, k*\r\nsaid it best, \\\"he clearly has issues with women.\\\"  i agree. \r\ni dont identify with his mind on women.  but i listened and\r\nwondered why, why, WHY? would he be rapping about heinous\r\nacts and at the same time constantly refering to is daughter\r\nand being friends with his daughter, and being there for his\r\ndaughter.  it is fucked.  it is so fucked it puts a smile on\r\nmy face.  and i mutter, \\\"ha ha, WTF\\\"  if he was just talking\r\nabout killing her mom, then i would be bored and repulsed,\r\nonly.  not intrigued.</P>\r\n<P>to borrow some humor from sick twisted film, the psycho\r\nin silence of the lamb that was making a woman suit out of\r\nskin from women.  if it were only that, it would not be\r\nfunny, just sick.  but he says, \\\"it puts the lotion in the\r\nbasket,\\\" while stoking his poodle, and then poses with his\r\ndick between his legs.  and large portions of the audience,\r\nperhaps all male, gasp, utter a choppy haha and say,\r\n\\\"WTF\\\".</P>\r\n<P>again, what speaks to me are his raps about\r\ndissatisfaction in the work place.  i\\\'m not shaving my head\r\nand walking around in a white tee shirt, saggy blue jeans\r\nand high tops, but i do wear a white tee shirt on occasion,\r\nand sometimes i shave my head.  it really has nothing to do\r\nwith eminem.</P>',3,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(9367,1854,'2001-09-28 17:15:19',0,'mohandas','western civilization? it\\\'s a good idea',4,0,0,0,'156.153.255.243','en'),(9368,1848,'2001-09-28 17:17:48',0,'arete','we talk about celebrities the way the ancient greeks talked \r\nabout gods and goddesses, as if they mattered in our lives \r\nof going to the store, school, work, commute, pick up the \r\ncleaning, cook some ramen.',3,0,0,0,'156.153.255.243','en'),(9369,1848,'2001-09-28 17:21:27',0,'oldteenybopper','music is what helps us teeny boppers cope with our hormone \r\ndriven urges, we\\\'ll get over it. when i\\\'m 30 i will be \r\nlistening to perry como.',4,0,0,0,'156.153.255.243','en'),(9370,1848,'2001-09-28 17:23:15',0,'40year old','and when you are 40 you will listen to <b>nothing at \r\nall</b> (emphasis mine). I know because i\\\'m going \r\nprofoundly deaf from all the crap I poured in my ears over \r\nthe years-- another young person\\\'s fad grown stale.',6,0,0,0,'156.153.255.243','en'),(9371,1848,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','i think it\\\'s pretty simple. guys that listen to \r\nmisogynistic works don\\\'t feel threatened because they\\\'re \r\n_guys_ and the hate rolls off their backs. they can listen \r\nto the beat underneath the death cries. it\\\'s not their \r\nthroats that\\\'s being jokingly slit. hey more miller lites! \r\nbut women (understandably) get upset. because they\\\'ve live \r\nwith the threat of violence, where ever they go, all the \r\ntime. i go down to get a fucking burrito down the street, \r\nand i get crotch danced by disgusting old men. we live with \r\na different reality, with a different fear. enimen prolly \r\nhas no concept of the trauma and disgust his music elicits \r\nin women and doesn\\\'t care. too bad most men aren\\\'t open to \r\nrealizing that. that\\\'s why i immediately understood where \r\negg was coming from. depending on my mood, i would fucking \r\nthrow that radio out the window.',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(9372,1848,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','<BR><BR>celine\\\'s <U>journey to the end of the night</U> is \r\nhighly racist and anti-semitic, but is also one of the best \r\nbooks of the twentieth century. i don\\\'t think he was doing \r\nit as ironic post-modern stance, either.<BR><BR>at some \r\nlevel, it\\\'s worth tolerating everything, even intolerance, \r\nand connecting to people on their terms, not yours. what \r\ncomes after political correctness? not a return, i think, to \r\nbigotry, but a transcendence of even the tendency to be \r\nrepulsed by it. some people are prejudiced. does that make \r\nthem evil? they might engage in evil actions, but they \r\nthemselves are not. ostracizing the bigot isn\\\'t any more \r\nproductive than the bigotry itself. it\\\'s hard to say, isn\\\'t \r\nit. i don\\\'t know. and i think that\\\'s all we can really say \r\nabout it, that we don\\\'t know what the answer is and enjoy \r\nlife anyway. and teach our children to keep their minds \r\nopen. \r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.9.83','en'),(9373,1848,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','<p>also, does this sound like a guy who\\\'s on the cutting \r\nedge of women\\\'s rights to you?: \r\n</p><p>\r\n\\\"He (Enimen) was charged Tuesday with carrying a concealed \r\nweapon and assault with a deadly weapon. Michigan \r\nprosecutors say Eminem was spying on his wife late Sunday \r\nnight in a Hot Rocks Cafe parking lot in Warren, Mich., and \r\npulled a gun on a bartender after seeing him kiss his wife. \r\nEminem faces up to nine years in prison if convicted on \r\nboth charges.\\\" - Salon \\\"invisible Man\\\" by Eric Boehlert \r\n</p><p>best fucking friendly.</p>',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(9374,1842,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','hi, yeah. \r\n',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(9375,1848,'2001-09-28 17:45:59',0,'me','i am 32. i listen to ODB.',5,0,0,0,'32.102.110.31','en'),(9376,1848,'2001-09-28 17:56:11',0,'me','i\\\'m 36 and I listen to leif garret (remember him?)',4,0,0,0,'156.153.255.243','en'),(9377,1848,'2001-09-28 18:02:22',