nd cocks of despair. \r\nWe got our final vision by clap. \r\nColumbus\\\' groin got \r\nFilled with green death. \r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,'172.173.195.145','en'),(9447,1861,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','on second thought, this post rocks. and so do you tyler! \r\nyou are the coolest.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.67','en'),(9448,1861,'2001-09-30 05:21:27',0,'paola','\\\"this person\\\" - how he dare go against the party line? \r\ndoesn\\\'t he know there\\\'s rules around here? quick - jump on \r\nhim and fuck his shit UP. teach him you can\\\'t have a \r\ndiffering opinion. \\\"this person.\\\" who is he? he can\\\'t be one \r\nof us. look at the shit he posts.<BR><BR>grow up.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.5.19','en'),(9449,1853,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','can you prove that the universe exists independantly of \r\nyou? nope. it exists only as a reflection in your mind. if \r\nyou do not percieve it, it does not exist, for you. when \r\nyou die, the universe ends. for you. so...you...are...the...',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.67','en'),(9450,1861,'2001-09-30 06:09:05',0,'jo','\\\"i touched her thigh and death smiled.\\\"<BR>\r\ni, too, have <a href=\\\"http://www.mmmbed.com/doors/\\\">j.m.\\\'s \r\npoetry memorized</a>.',1,0,0,0,'128.83.219.85','en'),(9451,1861,'2001-09-30 06:11:22',0,'treetop','hi jo :)',0,0,0,0,'172.173.195.145','en'),(9452,1861,'2001-09-30 06:14:40',0,'jim m','  The moon is a dry blood beast. \r\nGuerrilla bands are rolling numbers \r\nIn the next block of green vine, \r\nAmassing for warfare on innocent \r\nHerdsman who are just dying. \r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,'172.173.195.145','en'),(9453,1861,'2001-09-30 06:17:56',0,'solon','what are the rules of swinney.org? I\\\'m a newby and can\\\'t \r\nfigure this clique out. somebody suss me please.',4,0,0,0,'204.27.188.1','en'),(9454,1848,'2001-09-30 06:19:30',0,'george','i\\\'ll just see you at folsom at the \\\'Rimming Eagle\\\'-- ciao',5,0,0,0,'204.27.188.1','en'),(9455,1861,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','\\\"rules\\\"\r\n',0,0,0,0,'66.122.218.90','en'),(9456,1861,'2001-09-30 07:53:53',0,'treetop','  It seems to me that there are no defined \\\"rules\\\". But, \r\nkeep in mind that you must account for what you say.  \r\nPersonally, I like diversity outside of the \\\"norm\\\".  Not to \r\nsay that this particular post tickles my fancy.  I do \r\nhowever find a sense of interest in the comments that it \r\nhas generated.  :)',0,0,0,0,'172.173.195.145','en'),(9457,1861,'2001-09-30 07:55:15',0,'treetop','and yes, i think le does rule :)',0,0,0,0,'172.173.195.145','en'),(9458,1861,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i\\\'m not a newbie, and i still can\\\'t figure this clique out.',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(9459,1859,'2001-09-30 09:44:12',0,'Hallett','MmmmHhmmmm.',4,0,0,0,'172.138.65.75','en'),(9460,1861,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','uhm hi, do we need to register our nicks now? i did not \r\nsay the second comment on this post. someone used my name to put that there. grr. very unhappy. ',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(9461,1861,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','i think you guys are afflicted with a serious case of Cock \r\nEnvy, and you need to work this out with a professional. \r\n<br>\r\nby the way...\r\n<br>\r\nit was a joke, obviously, i don\\\'t think that needs to be \r\nspelled out for anyone. austin, don\\\'t call me \\\"this person\\\" \r\nlike you are better than me and i am a dumbass hillbilly. \r\ni\\\'m sure you <i>never</i> make tasteless jokes. what do i \r\ndeserve? is somebody coming to my house to kick my ass? am \r\ni supposed to sit around crying because somebody said \r\nsomething mean on a website that like 35 people read? \r\n<br>\r\nweeb(tm), does this mean you really don\\\'t think i am cool?\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.165','en'),(9462,1861,'2001-09-30 18:20:06',0,'Critic','<i>\\\"i think you guys are afflicted with a serious case of\r\nCock Envy\\\"</i>... i see statements like this and assume that\r\nthey\\\'re probably <i>intended</i> to rabble-rouse. whats the\r\npoint? um, ok, so you really stuck it to us with that\r\nstatement!<br><br>a lesson that i learned, finally, that\r\nmade my life (and those around me) much better was the old\r\n\\\"think before you speak\\\" lesson. I grew wise enough to not\r\nsay about half of the things that i really wanted to, and my\r\nlife got happier. people reacted to me much nicer, and i\r\ndiscovered myself saying fewer things that i later\r\nregretted.<br><br>\r\nnot that thats the ase here, or that we shoudl censor, or\r\nthat we cant have open minds, or any of those usual, tired\r\narguments. it just seems unfriendly to rabble-rouse.',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.255','en'),(9463,1861,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','sometimes the rabble needs rousing:)<BR><BR>if you \r\ndon\\\'t agree with someone, you can discuss your \r\ndifferences of opinion in a rational manner, without \r\ngetting hostile or ostracizing them. we\\\'re all \r\ndifferent. and like i said, nobody\\\'s going anywhere, \r\nso we might as well make an effort to get along. \r\nlisten to me - i\\\'m so pious, aren\\\'t i?<BR><BR>if \r\nsomething on here pisses you off or unnerves you, go \r\nwith it - explore that avenue.  we\\\'re here today to \r\nleave nothing in this world undone, to see things from  \r\nevery possible viewpoint, to try everything, to fully \r\ninteract with reality and practice for when we become \r\nall things. that\\\'s why they call it \\\"expanding your \r\nconsciousness.\\\"<BR><BR>or you could just ignore it, \r\nkeep your blinders on. that\\\'s valid, too. it\\\'s not any \r\nbetter or worse than option 1.<BR><BR>have a nice day.\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.208.10.164','en'),(9464,1861,'2001-09-30 20:08:53',0,'Critic','...and sometimes us old Fogeys get tired of rabble-rousing\r\nfor the sake of rabble-rousing. devils advocate, just trying\r\nto prove a point for no reason, etc, etc...<br><br>\r\nwhy fuss over something so stupid? stick to things you care\r\nabout,write about them, etc. now <i>thats</i> why wecome\r\nback. sophomoric little snippets musign about \\\"cocks\\\" arent\r\nexactly filet-mignon grade fare, here, please!',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.255','en'),(9465,1858,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','oh yes.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.90.172','en'),(9466,1861,'2001-09-30 21:41:03',0,'i guffawed','when it ran on the Onion (www.onion.com). so why not steal it, and publish it here, let\\\'s hear it for cocks!',3,0,0,0,'204.27.188.1','en'),(9467,1848,'2001-09-30 21:42:51',0,'rubber dude','damn this latex is getting hot, it must be 90 degrees out here today. And my cock and ball harness is \r\nchafing me.',3,0,0,0,'204.27.188.1','en'),(9468,1848,'2001-09-30 22:05:09',0,'Lil\\\' Kim','you should all go buy my album, \\\'Notorious K.I.M.\\\' - it \r\nfeatures the hummable gender challenging ditty \\\'Suck My \r\nDick\\\' and other fun things.',2,0,0,0,'195.40.196.236','en'),(9469,1861,'2001-09-30 22:37:19',0,'I hunt elves','sex always sells. also a away to get lots of comments.',1,0,0,0,'24.27.31.48','en'),(9470,1848,'2001-09-30 22:39:42',0,'duct tape','dont forget your butt plug',0,0,0,0,'172.173.195.145','en'),(9471,1861,'2001-09-30 23:51:15',0,'Bocephus','ok, so you have lots of comments. <i>now what?</i>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.255','en'),(9472,1861,'2001-10-01 00:57:43',0,'00','<img \r\nsrc=\\\"http://www.laurasmith.com/Bush_as_Arab.jpg\\\">',6,0,0,0,'209.162.48.52','en'),(9473,1861,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','i didn\\\'t steal it, i made it up. it\\\'s my baby, ugly or not, \r\nwritten in good taste or not, whether you think it\\\'s funny \r\nor not. it certainly has raised some discussion, \r\ncommunication, and honest opinions. so...\r\n<p>\r\nLet\\\'s give a cheer, Carolina is here, we\\\'ll let the \r\nGamecocks lead the way...',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.204','en'),(9474,1848,'2001-10-01 06:07:41',0,'maria','i have a soft spot for lil\\\' kim. her gender challenging \r\nditty is quite hummable and perfect female empowerment \r\nmusic... ',2,0,0,0,'132.162.231.185','en'),(9475,1864,'2