ou think i would drive to \r\nsanta cruz for mr. swinneydotorg? no. i want the cave. \r\ni\\\'m never believing anyone again.',0,0,0,0,'64.165.201.19','en'),(9502,1865,'2001-10-01 22:56:47',0,'mmmm!','heroin!',1,0,0,0,'209.162.48.144','en'),(9503,1868,'2001-10-01 23:19:51',0,'ghost','chi chi wants the cave....come and visit my mystery spot.\r\n',5,0,0,0,'32.102.109.156','en'),(9504,1868,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','alright ... what happened in shantytown after i left?? \r\n(and should i have left the paddle behind?) btw dinner \r\nwas lovely - best massamun curry i\\\'ve had yet. yum \r\nyum.',1,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(9505,1868,'2001-10-01 23:41:00',0,'chi chi to ghost','will have to be blindfolded?',0,0,0,0,'64.165.201.19','en'),(9506,1868,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','don\\\'t you mean the cavern?',0,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(9507,1868,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','<blink><b>BEST FRIENDLY</b></blink>',0,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(9508,1869,'2001-10-02 01:26:02',0,'trouble','i love the layout and enjoy \\\'articles\\\' better than \\\'entries\\\' as i view everybody who posts here as journalists of sorts.  writing about and revealing themselves.  (nice supportive)',0,0,0,0,'24.181.44.135','en'),(9509,1869,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','the layout and new features ROCK ASS.  jim, swinney and ix, you should be proud.<br>\r\n<br>\r\ni like articles, so it seems like less of a teenage girls journal and more serious.  but also, it doesn\\\'t really matter. and i myself have a teenage girls journal.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(9510,1869,'2001-10-02 01:29:33',0,'deb','not bad, cept it\\\'s a pain in the ass that the articles that i\\\'ve already read don\\\'t stay red... then i have to remember. too much work for me, damnit :)',3,0,0,0,'152.163.213.202','en'),(9511,1869,'2001-10-02 01:31:28',0,'jim','I have only a slight preference for \\\"entries\\\".  I\\\'ll do whatever the majority of comments here suggest is the right thing to do as far as that particular term goes.',6,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(9512,1869,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>originally, I crinkled my nose at \\\"ye olde fonte\\\". but I now see that it is more punk-renaissance than \\\"ye olde\\\". it\\\'s like, \\\"ye olde FUCKIN fonte, and who cares if you think its awkward, FUCKE!\\\" punk medieval, like mary timony. I see the light! do you hear me, friends! I celebrate you!! </p><p>also, i like very much being able to scroll through last/next entry, and a convenient link to the user\\\'s journal from the top. oh this is the swinney ive been dreaming of. </p>\r\n<p>when will you show what \\\"category\\\" the person checked at the bottom of their comments and submissions?</p>\r\n<p>*BEST FRIENDLY*</p>',6,0,0,0,'216.175.90.172','en'),(9513,1869,'2001-10-02 01:32:32',0,'hi','is there still a problem with logging in? cuz it says it doesn\\\'t remember my password but now my name is taken so i can\\\'t try again.',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(9514,1869,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','also, I like \\\"entries\\\" better, because the writing isnt always an \\\"article\\\". personally, I write \\\"stories\\\" and \\\"essays\\\".',0,0,0,0,'216.175.90.172','en'),(9515,1869,'2001-10-02 01:33:31',0,'jim to deb','links you have viewed should be displaying purple, links you haven\\\'t should be blue.  ',6,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(9516,1869,'2001-10-02 01:34:30',0,'jim to hi','yah, the registration system is borked.  as soon as it works you should be able to log in with the password you originally registered with.',6,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(9517,1869,'2001-10-02 01:35:05',0,'jim to egg','dunno about the comment category thing.  ask austin.',6,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(9518,1869,'2001-10-02 01:35:29',0,'hi to jim','thank you, sir',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(9519,1869,'2001-10-02 01:38:16',0,'jesus','thanks you too...',1,0,0,0,'24.181.44.135','en'),(9520,1869,'2001-10-02 01:38:47',0,'jim to deb','that blue and purple may be a little too similar.  I\\\'ll experiment a little.',6,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(9521,1869,'2001-10-02 01:39:11',0,'jo','dear jim. you rock my ass. this is beautiful.',1,0,0,0,'172.140.78.179','en'),(9522,1869,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to jim','can i tell you sometime how i feel about the word \\\"borked\\\".',0,0,0,0,'216.175.90.172','en'),(9523,1869,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p>first of all, the new design looks great. clean, simple - this is really good work, jim. and i like being able to login now. i bet that will become more useful as time goes on and new features are added.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>a minor thing - the article display should have the title as more prominent than the blurb, as before. previously, the title was larger and stood out more, with the blurb reading as parenthetical to the title. i liked that. now it runs together as one long title, and is harder to notice on the page.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>finally, the shift from \\\"article\\\" to \\\"entry\\\" rubs me the wrong way. i was first drawn to this site because it encouraged people to post <i>writing</i> rather than \\\"i did this and that today\\\" journal entries. and sure, many of the articles lean heavily towards journal entries, but that\\\'s always felt like a side effect rather than the focus. so i guess what i\\\'m saying is, i\\\'m much more excited about reading articles than journal entries. (there. i said all that without making one comparison to livejournal.)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>everything else rocks my greek ass. i\\\'m even gonna click \\\"best friendly\\\".</p>',1,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(9524,1869,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','oh yeah. the comments are much more readable. i like the bold usernames. *smooch*',1,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(9525,1869,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','also the cool way to see if there were any articles waiting to be activated is gone.  POOS!',1,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(9526,1869,'2001-10-02 01:55:10',0,'jim to jo','aw, thanks!',6,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(9527,1869,'2001-10-02 01:55:1