>',2,0,0,0,'64.229.74.80','en'),(9537,1869,'2001-10-02 02:32:41',0,'jim','so far, Sabbath Black makes people think of things ye olde, heavy metal, punk rock, and beer.  I feel good about this.',6,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(9538,1869,'2001-10-02 02:41:19',0,'Alan','I am lame and lazy so I will simply say thanks for the effort on the site.\r\n\r\nAlan',2,0,0,0,'198.211.32.155','en'),(9539,1869,'2001-10-02 02:47:50',0,'the webby comittee','*cat call*',1,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(9540,1869,'2001-10-02 02:55:33',0,'jim','oh oh, one other thing:\r\n\r\ntitle bars now display useful information.  for example, if you bookmark an article, the name of the article will appear in your Bookmarks menu.  you can bookmark entries pages, search results and more.  one possible usage of this is to bookmark a search of your username, to facilitate regular ego-searching.',6,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(9541,1869,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','sexy',1,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(9542,1869,'2001-10-02 03:03:17',0,'jim','\r\nwe here at swinney.org are all about providing you with the best possible user experience.',6,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(9543,1869,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','nice ass',0,0,0,0,'216.175.90.172','en'),(9544,1869,'2001-10-02 04:05:46',0,'question','jim.. login still down?',1,0,0,0,'24.181.44.135','en'),(9545,1867,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','i believe that a child\\\'s name should not be where parents choose to display their creativity. a too-interesting name might distract people from his or her accomplishments or special qualities.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.218','en'),(9546,1869,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','login down!<br>\r\nmy server is down!<br>\r\ni can\\\'t get my email!<br>\r\nthe internet broke<br>',0,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(9547,1869,'2001-10-02 06:14:01',0,'jim','registration is fixed.   if you registered an account earlier today you will need to re-register.  smooches.\r\n\r\n',6,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(9548,1869,'2001-10-02 06:15:59',0,'jim','oh hey, another cool feature for logged in folks: your username gets prefilled on all submission forms.  just another way that swinney.org makes your life more productive.',6,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(9549,1869,'2001-10-02 06:37:11',0,'kat','you people rock...i want to make love to y\\\'all.',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.121','en'),(9550,1869,'2001-10-02 06:43:28',0,'jim','who am I to dissuade you?',6,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(9551,1869,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','hey, you had your chance!',0,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(9552,1870,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','a large proportion of guns are used against their owners. think twice. always expecting the worst can be a self-fullfilling prophecy.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(9553,1870,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','one day, my dad will give me the .38 that my great grandfather used to carry. i\\\'ll keep it unloaded and locked away, maybe take it target shooting sometimes. i am a good shot. i don\\\'t like violence, but i also respect elegant machinery. ',4,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(9554,1869,'2001-10-02 08:53:03',0,'me','lovely, marvelous, spiffy, in a short thought-very fucking nice.',1,0,0,0,'152.163.195.213','en'),(9555,1870,'2001-10-02 08:56:57',0,'tomato','when i move to OR and then MT, i\\\'ll get a gun again i think.  trigger lock, etc.  responsible.\r\n<p>\r\ni also want to shoot a deer up there, clean it, then eat it.  this may \\\"shock\\\" some weak stomached vegans or veggies, but i feel as if i must do that to get close to what i eat, to kill something with my hands, to clean it in the hills, to see its eyes.  i need to be closer to my food to know it.  to get through. to thank it.',1,0,0,0,'209.162.48.153','en'),(9556,1870,'2001-10-02 08:58:50',0,'tomato','and, sorry, vegans or veggies should at least try farming too.  the key is closeness to food, to see what\\\'s involved.<p>\r\n(end hippie eugene rant)',1,0,0,0,'209.162.48.153','en'),(9557,1870,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','i don\\\'t have a problem with people who hunt, clean, cook and eat animals.  i think a lot of vegans are not opposed to meat eaters doing these things.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nsome vegans don\\\'t want to hurt the bambis but some are just opposed to the mass production and awful treatment of animals that make up your sunday roast dinner, and as you point out the isolation between the meat on your plate and the cow in the field.<br>',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(9558,1870,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','some vegans would rather you hunted with a knife than a gun, where there\\\'s a mutual understanding that combat is taking place, and both sides have an equal chance of injury or escape. just like how all other animals hunt their prey. point-and-click to clear memory is still an abstraction to your dinner plate.',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(9559,1870,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','also, living on a sailboat would rock.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(9560,1870,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','ABSTRACTION, that\\\'s the word i was looking for.  you sure are smart, s5!',1,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(9561,1870,'2001-10-02 09:23:41',0,'tomato','that\\\'s a technological abstraction. \r\n<p>\r\nhow far must one take it?  down to hand to hand combat with a deer?  what is natural and what is not?  \r\n<p>\r\nwe invented tools, guns, etc.  i am not talking about going out and taking an animal with claymore mined ambushes and a squad of marines, i am talking about knowing the animal, knowing the habitat, tracking, etc.  like fly fishing as opposed to bait fishing.\r\n<p>\r\nand you\\\'re right, the sailing thing would rock.  5k, can\\\'t believe it.',1,0,0,0,'209.162.48.153','en'),(9562,1870,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','actually i\\\'d be really impressed if you set up a minefield. also: sailing! YEAH!',1,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(9563,1870,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','you know how i feel about this ryan. \\\"veganism\\\" was on the list of topics posted inside the isuzu trooper. right between \\\"shitting\\\" and \\\"whether we have to shit\\\"',4,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(9564,1869,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i vote that the blue and purple are, in fact, too similar',0,0,0,0,'216.15.97.21','en'),(9565,1869,'2001-10-02 11:08:11',0,'Joanna','Best friendly - bozo list idea is fantastic. ',1,0,0,0,'203.97.2.242','en'),(9566,1858,'2001-10-02 11:08:21',0,'Jamie','don\\\'t i get credit for the poems pete?',1,0,0,0,'217.32.134.134','en'),(9567,1858,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>Ahem, jamie... <i>regards link at top called \\\"text\\\"</i>...</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9569,1869,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','the bozo filter isn\\\'t my idea. the internet\\\'s howard rheingold got very upset with me when i designed salon.com\\\'s table talk 1.0 without a bozo filter feature. i didn\\\'t understand then, but now i have a bit more experience with online community. long live the bozo filter.',0,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(9570,1858,'2001-10-02 12:25:06',0,'Jamie','oh yeah... duh',1,0,0,0,'217.32.134.134','en'),(9571,1867,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','I have an unusual name in real life, and I\\\'m really glad I do.  It made being a kid kinda tough, but being a kid is going to be tough regardless.  Now, people think it\\\'s cool, and I\\\'m never one of three people turning his head when someone yells, \\\"Chris!\\\" (I know you all know at least one - if not two or three - person named Chris.)',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(9572,1869,'2001-10-02 13:03:09',0,'trouble','now while i kind of like the idea of a filter for a few personal reasons has anybody thought about the possibility of it acting as a feature that might alienate some of swinney.org\\\'s fans?  truth be told (and this is <b>not</b> negative in the least, more a simple truth) its tough to break into what is at times a really tight clique and because everbody both readers and more importantly the authors value each others opinions and respects each others work a filter such as this \\\'might\\\' work as a feature to hinder the readers (self included).  i have found some real gems of written material here that i would not have seen if i had acted on a negative comment i saw or listened to a friend say less than flattering things about an entry and/or its author.  now, before you throw your hands up and proclaim me \\\'crazy for thinking such a thing about me\\\' and \\\'i would never act so rash\\\' we all know it happens, has happened and probably will happen and this <b>isn\\\'t</b> a condemnation.  my little thought has now swearved into a plea for a little restraint i guess... behind some of the \\\'bozo\\\'s\\\' hides a potential diamond.  *best friendly*',1,0,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(9573,1869,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<p>I have a feature request: Nav buttons at the top of an entry that lets me scroll through entries in chronological order.  That way I could more easily browse through the most recent posts without going back to the entries page.  Does that make sense?</p><p>btw, \r\n\r\nI agree with trouble.  I\\\'m not sure why, but the argument somehow just makes a lot of sense to me.</p>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(9574,1869,'2001-10-02 14:07:58',0,'jo','i was just wondering, can i do a little dance of some sort about how much i like this redesign? some sort of exaltent dance, possibly with \\\"whoop whoop\\\"s and arms waving in the air, possibly to a kool & the gang song?',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(9575,1869,'2001-10-02 14:13:52',0,'trouble','ess, that was not an argument (i hope that\\\'s not the way it was perceived) it was more a poorly punctuated ramble about the hope i have that the \\\'bozo\\\' feature doesn\\\'t deter potential writers from posting because of the idea of being ignored (by an automatic filter and not by a concious response to reading the post) and to ask those who think of using it not to make snap judgements about ignoring a user or users.  if i had my coffee before i wrote it i \\\'might\\\' have made a little more sense... but then again.',1,0,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(9576,1870,'2001-10-02 14:15:43',0,'jo','this is reminding a lot of sarah vowell\\\'s essay (and also a chapter in her book) \\\"shooting dad.\\\"',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(9577,1867,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>your name <i>is</i> cool. first and last. although, i\\\'m a bit pissed that your real name isnt Jim <i>Kebober</i>.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9578,1869,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to Jo','<br><tt>i just scored four kool-n-tha-gang records from a guy on the street yesterday for <i>$1</i>. i spent all night last night listening to <i>jungle boogie</i>, <i>ladies night</i>, and [of course] all of <i>new york city cool</i> at +8% speed. damn. i\\\'ll spin if you dance.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9579,1871,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','<p align=left color=red>it\\\'s all good, man. you do what you have to to get by. i\\\'m sure if there were something better you could be doing right now, and it were <i>practical</i>(big consideration), you would be doing it.</p>',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.44','en'),(9580,1871,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','<p>wait--you <i>are</i> doing it. grad school.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.44','en'),(9581,1871,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>...but after grad school? ack. i\\\'m just a perfectionist, i think, or mildly obsessive. i want to be in a fruitful, rewarding career <i>now</i>. i dont want to wait for grad school to start, or end for that matter. i dont want to have to work. what i <i>need</i> is to win the lottery, heh.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9582,1870,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','the situations i am envisioning that might require a gun would be: 1)catching a shark 2)being assaulted in a remote part of the carribean. lots of people down there do not like white people, and most of them are very poor. it can be a dangerous place--most of the countries down there are 3rd world once you \\\"leave the resort\\\". plus, it\\\'s hard to call 911 when you are 500 miles from the U.S.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.44','en'),(9583,1871,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','Quit your bitching Peter.  At least you\\\'re not a high school drop-out, and I know that your job is much nicer than mine.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(9584,1870,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>...and don\\\'t forget pirates! gun if you must, but I\\\'d invest the gun-money in a <i>premium</i> shortwave radio reciever/transmitter. a coast-guard smackdown would probably hit harder than a few shots from a briny 45 anyway.</tt> ',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9585,1871,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>perhaps. but you make alot more <i>$bling$</i> than i, heh heh.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9586,1868,'2001-10-02 16:37:44',0,'jo','i like \\\"ungrateful slut.\\\" i need to use this more.',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(9587,1868,'2001-10-02 16:40:34',0,'Mike','The mug at the top is my neighbor.',0,0,0,0,'206.224.71.189','en'),(9588,1867,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to peter','im pissed about that too.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.90.172','en'),(9589,1867,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>yes. so many potential thrills are lost now that i cant call up Big Ess and say, \\\"Guten Tag, Meeeester Kee-BOB-ber!\\\". humph. I think i\\\'ma change my name to <i>Antwerp Luxembourg Schnitzel</i> in retaliation.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9590,1870,'2001-10-02 17:06:03',0,'black beard','ARRRRRR!',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(9591,1869,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','<p>i like the fact that the year slot in the date at the top of the entries has five digits, so we can post until the year 99,999.</p>',1,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(9592,1868,'2001-10-02 17:42:53',0,'ghost','it was all for the robot...[inner turmoil over scheduling confusion which has resulted in...well, more confusion. i hold noone responsible]...it was all for the robot.',1,0,0,0,'32.102.109.129','en'),(9593,1