\\'t even drive cars. sheash! ',0,0,0,0,'64.165.201.19','en'),(9723,1882,'2001-10-04 07:03:50',0,'\\\"frisco\\\"','i don\\\'t see a shout out for the 5-1-0 on here either, missy',0,0,0,0,'166.90.33.171','en'),(9724,1882,'2001-10-04 07:15:47',0,'chi chi','listen up y\\\'all the East Bay will kick all your scrawny asses. any day.',0,0,0,0,'64.165.201.19','en'),(9725,1862,'2001-10-04 07:25:08',0,'Hallett','At the age of 25 it\\\'s: <p>1. Travel<p>2. Art<p>3. Love<p> But I suspect that at the age of 45 priorities will change.',0,0,0,0,'172.173.101.250','en'),(9726,1880,'2001-10-04 07:26:53',0,'Hallett','you gonna give me a place to live Peter?',0,0,0,0,'172.173.101.250','en'),(9727,1862,'2001-10-04 07:29:44',0,'tomato','why?',4,0,0,0,'209.162.48.124','en'),(9728,1848,'2001-10-04 08:34:45',0,'some jerk with an opinion','<p>\r\nI think there\\\'s no ways to look at Eminem, or  anyone in the media who speaks about or represents violence.  \r\n</P>\r\n<p>\r\n1.  He\\\'s an entertainer.  In which case his words shouldn\\\'t be taken seriously;  they should be considered a blockbuster movie, something to be taken with a grain of salt, and ignored altogether.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\n2.  He\\\'s an artist, with something to say.  This is where it gets dodgy because now he\\\'s taken seriously.  (This seems to be the opinion of most folks).  \r\n</p>\r\n<P>\r\nIn this case, the defense I think should be brought forth is that he didn\\\'t create the violence.  The violence is here, has been around for quite some time... and he is speaking about it (which few people have really done in a serious fashion).   Certainly some of his songs condone violence.  He seems to be a rather fucked up individual.  But he is not the cause of the violence that goes on in America, and I think we  would be better served by looking at the cause of violence instead of crucifying its poster boy.\r\n</P>\r\n<P>\r\nI mean, which would mess your head up more, listening to an eminem song or see your dad beat up your mom?  Eminem\\\'s characters are dark, and not designed to be worshipped.  Any halfway intelligent kid listening would realize that he\\\'s not someone you want to be when you grow up.  ',3,0,0,0,'63.194.91.214','en'),(9729,1886,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','this is really good and i like it a lot.',0,0,0,0,'216.27.183.161','en'),(9730,1882,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','they wear snowshoes there.',0,0,0,0,'216.27.183.161','en'),(9731,1880,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to Hallett','<br><tt>er, coincidently, my flatmate is moving out in like 2 weeks. there\'s a realistic chance i actually <i>might have</i> a room in my cavernous paint-peeling place for a lucky mofo or two. so, anyone with $521.70 should feel free to <a href=\"mailto:peter@rhodamine.org\">submit</a> headshots, bribes, sexual favors or free drugs to me posthaste.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9732,1886,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>this <i>is</i> good. that being said, with no disclaimer, let me just say that i\'m sitting here at work listening to <a href=\"http://www.cdnow.com/cgi-bin/mserver/SID=559905419/pagename=/RP/CDN/FIND/album.html/ArtistID=N.W.A./ITEMID=24443\"><i>\"straight outta compton\"</i></a>, and this entry matches the meter of eazy-e\'s verse in an uncanny way.  jay, i suppose that makes you a <i>lyrical masta\'</i>.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9733,1883,'2001-10-04 12:25:19',0,'an admirer','hi, this is awesome.',1,0,0,0,'203.96.111.200','en'),(9734,1853,'2001-10-04 12:27:42',0,'Jamazon','That\\\'s what i\\\'m talking about. Does any of this exisit? As you\\\'re reading this right now, do i exisit? Did i write this, or am i just a part of your own little universe dreamt up by you? I\\\'m pretty sure i exisit. But how am i to know. maybe i don\\\'t. Maybe you don\\\'t. I can\\\'t put this into words. it doesn\\\'t make sense as words.',1,0,0,0,'217.32.158.65','en'),(9735,1883,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>I was gonna sell my kidney on ebay, t