\\\"http://www.mmmbed.com/stars/cancerIII/page1.jpg\\\">i can convince</a> little sara, crashed out on my couch, that she wants them, too',0,0,0,0,'172.141.174.96','en'),(9840,1902,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','i got to meet Lou Holtz the other day. that\\\'s about the extent of my famous-people meetings, now that i think about it. well, i met melvin seals from jgb, and Col. Bruce Hampton, but those were easy. ',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.141','en'),(9841,1902,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','i want to party on your pussy baby, cause she\\\'s stone cold bush. suck my kiss, you sexy mexican maid! ',0,0,0,0,'216.175.99.186','en'),(9842,1900,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>i love bridge to terabithia. i still wear slips and smudged black eyeliner ocassionally and i truly wish courtney love still did the same. when she began her transformation into whatever it is she is doing now, my friend noah wrote this haiku:</p>\r\n<p>courtney love sucks<br>\r\nsucks sucks sucks sucks sucks sucks sucks<br>\r\nhave you seen Bazaar?</p>\r\n<p>when i saw le tigre last year Johanna Fateman had her hair all teased up and she was wearing something zebra with pointy boots. fashion-wise, she is a cross between the haute-class of chi chi and the cheap-cha-cha-playmate-punk of egg. she\\\'s the classy ho of the bunch. my hero.</p>',0,0,0,0,'216.175.99.186','en'),(9843,1902,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','the circus made me feel a lot of funny feelings.  it made me happy to be seeing circus.  the level of skill and lack of fear in the performers amazed me.  una, the rope girl, did the most impressive rope act i\\\'ve ever seen.  she was better than cirque du soleil.  really.  it was original, not the same tricks rehashed over and over.  cirque du soleil is supposed to be the end all be all of circus and here was una, performing at cell space in front of a hundred or two hundred sf nutjobs who paid $5 less because they came dressed as clowns.  and i wondered why she chose to be part of the bindlestiffs instead of that giant corporate world-reknown entity.  she gave me hope.  she reminded me that you do what you love because you love it, not for the recognition of where it might bring you.  Corn Mo was the soft and gentle rocker i wanted to be friends with.\r\n<p>\r\nthe circus also made me sad.  the marching band specifically.  i do not like that form of entertainment.  that sort where YOU WILL ENJOY THIS BECAUSE WE SAY SO and if you don\\\'t enjoy it they shove it down your throat so hard they make it impossible to breathe.  it\\\'s a great concept... the rowdy kids of band camp, but please, let people be themselves and if it\\\'s not their thing, it\\\'s not their thing.\r\n<p>\r\nit also felt like Cell Space Event #109323b.  i don\\\'t know how many shows i\\\'ve seen there by how many different groups or how many parties or how many gatherings or how many whatevers.  no matter what the event is, the crowd is the same.  it\\\'s a good crowd.  it\\\'s a crowd filled with creativity and energy and life and spontaneity and down and dirty primal instincts.  it\\\'s a crowd that looks like it feels really really good.  it\\\'s also a crowd that\\\'s self righteous in its freedom.  and if you\\\'re not free like them then why are you there?  it\\\'s not a crowd that allows for quiet people.  it\\\'s like being in burningman mode all the time at cell space.  i suppose that\\\'s what a lot of people long for when they leave the playa and that\\\'s where they go to get it.  i guess i\\\'m just not free enough... not hip enough... not <i>something</i> enough to get it.  i revel in my silence and inwardness.  i laugh on the inside. but people take that as stodgy or depressed or unhappy to be there.  no, it\\\'s just reflection.  it\\\'s taking it all in to be processed later.  I guess that\\\'s not allowed.  you must live in the now and be here now and enjoy it RIGHT NOW! because there\\\'s no time for reflection when the world is zooming past at 1000mph (hmm... at the equator.  how fast does it spin in sf?  37 degrees north... less than 500mph? things move slow up here.  ok. whatever).\r\n<p>\r\nmaybe i am just stodgy and depressed but i\\\'m really not unhappy about being in those places until people tell me so and once they do it makes me want to disappear and run away and live in the woods and have chickens and eat their eggs and make tacky macrame and just sell it by the roadside in a place that no ones ever heard of.  but it sure doesn\\\'t mean i don\\\'t like the circus.\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(9844,1902,'2002-10-04 04:15:39',409,'rachel','<p>\r\ni really wasn\\\'t sure what to expect when i went\r\nto the cirkus with xep and eric but i went because\r\ni have enjoyed various things that i associate\r\nwith xep like the sf circus school show and \r\ncirque du soleil and so on. it was nice to see\r\npeter and le and aimee, and meet matt, who \r\nneeded a ride home to berkeley.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\ni thought it was going to be massively crowded\r\nbecause lots of people i know were talking about\r\ngoing, but even though i got there later than i\r\nhad planned, xep had saved me a super nice seat!\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\ni mentioned to xep one point that i felt not weird/interesting/hip enough to be there; \r\ni can really understand the thoughts xep described about the adamant nature of the \\\'underground\\\' culture of san francisco. i like seeing people dressed in crazy ways, it doesn\\\'t make me uncomfortable to see them act outrageously, but i\\\'m just not like \r\nthat. i don\\\'t feel as though i\\\'m repressing\r\nany kind of outpouring of creative behavior\r\nor emotion, i just don\\\'t feel the need or desire\r\nto wear nothing but ruffled panties and sfpd\r\nstickers on my nipples, or walk around trying \r\nto make people notice me. and sometimes i feel\r\na bit pressured to affect some sort of crazy\r\nbehavior. but when i change my appearance or behavior, it\\\'s because i have some sort of \r\ninternal motivation. my closest friends tend\r\nto be the same way, from what i can tell. i \r\nlike knowing that they are not putting on some\r\nsort of show.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nhowever, i really liked the extra action \r\nmarching band. i think it\\\'s mostly because i \r\nreally enjoyed being in a huge marching band \r\nin high school. i like the big sound and \r\noverwhelming percussion. i tend to like big \r\nbombastic symphonic orchestral music too.\r\nanything that just overwhelms my senses and emotions and disables my tendency to analyze and determine what my reaction *should* be, i \r\nenjoy. \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nthe best part of the cirkus i thought was corn\r\nmo. he was excellent at providing the music\r\nfor all the acts, and when he sang alone, \r\nespecially in his first set, his voice just\r\nblew me away with its power and intensity. \r\nyay! i got his cd! screw flea! corn mo is \r\na real rock star! :)\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nbesides that, i thought the \\\'brother-sister\\\' \r\ntrapeze team were really excellent. at times\r\nfor other acts like the sword swallowing and \r\nthe contortionist i had to close my eyes so \r\nas not to feel sick watching. \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\ni was very glad to have gone. maybe i will\r\nemail corn mo and tell him how much he rocks.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nanyway. i don\\\'t keep a journal, but maybe i \r\nshould because i obviously wrote a lot more here\r\nthan i intended. hi le, xep. you\\\'re nice.\r\n</p>\r\n',2,0,0,0,'207.214.90.67','en'),(9845,1902,'2001-10-07 21:47:24',0,'tomato','people in SF are way too fucking cool for me.  too cool for school.',2,0,0,0,'209.162.48.67','en'),(9846,1902,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','fuck em. what difference does it make whether or not they think you are whatever enough? i mean did somebody say something to you? tell them to go piss up a rope. rule number one for being cool: don\\\'t give anybody else a hard time.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.172','en'),(9847,1901,'2001-10-07 23:24:11',0,'green to hallet','where did you get such an awesome name?\r\nlet us just get essemar to adopt us both...since i am in same boat, as you',2,0,0,0,'198.81.16.44','en'),(9848,1887,'2001-10-07 23:26:38',0,'green','that sounds like good fun',2,0,0,0,'198.81.16.44','en'),(9849,1902,'2001-10-08 02:20:09',0,'ghost','le and i talked for hours while on the way to burning man. we both wanted quiet and sleep and yet we talked and talked...and somehow this felt right. and i thought that when i finally got to burning man i would be wild and crazy and not at all my usual quiet self, and yet i was even more silent than normal. and this felt right. i almost did not talk at all while there. i spent hours sitting with strangers not talking, and we had a wonderful time. i even sat in the Goat and didn\\\'t talk. just sitting, listening, while people asked me...why are you here? what can you tell me? i just laughed and smiled. it felt right. quietness is an emotion, an answer, a thing, in and of itself. listening to the unspoken. words often get in the way of what is really being expressed.....i wander in silence, and i wander in words. often.',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.154','en'),(9850,1903,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','I know <b>exactly</b> where you\\\'re coming from on this.  I wish I could offer some advice and wisdom, but I cannot.  I don\\\'t know how to stop it, either.',2,0,0,0,'64.229.67.178','en'),(9851,1903,'2001-10-08 03:18:06',0,'jo','yeah, deb. i know exactly what this is like. good luck.',0,0,0,0,'172.132.182.168','en'),(9852,1893,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>i miss texas-mexican food so much that i cannot even begin to eat california-mexican food.</P>\r\n<P>The Air War Over Afganistan is playing out and i want a breakfast taco from taco wars, or tomale house, or that place on south congress, what is it called?</P>\r\n<P>texas-mexican food is the best, number one, all time greatest food in the history of me.  it is a good reason to visit, and a good reason to move back.  it is a good reason to start a mexican food restaurant in california called, Mexican Food, Texas Style.</P>\r\n<P>in another room i swear i just hear a news caster call bin laden an \\\'asshole\\\'.  i wish.  that would be rad.</P>',1,0,0,0,'64.174.155.79','en'),(9853,1899,'2001-10-08 05:32:59',0,'alana','<p>i am sorry.<p>\r\n<p>i shall smile for you you in the face of the sun.</p>\r\n<p>don\\\'t feel alone.</p>',4,0,0,0,'203.212.154.208','en'),(9854,1893,'2001-10-08 06:18:59',0,'jo','the place on s. congress is guero\\\'s, austin, home of <a href=\\\"http://www.wellyeah.com/chat/benpinesforaustin.txt\\\">the world-famous, crave-em-day-and-night, fish tacos</a>. i had some for lunch today. sara and i have decided that if we tell them we have to know the ingredients of their special sauce for dietary concerns, they\\\'ll tell us. good lord, i hope so.',0,0,0,0,'172.149.143.108','en'),(9855,1899,'2001-10-08 06:23:12',0,'jo','auntie, i\\\'m grumpy for you. i don\\\'t think anyone here knows what it would be like to have their husband and best friend over there right now. i think that you should bust your ass down to austin and let the kids down here spoil you. bmg and i will take you out for good food!',0,0,0,0,'172.149.143.108','en'),(9856,1902,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i\\\'m glad the cell space exists. i\\\'m glad there are people who do freaky things, even though sometimes they are trying really hard to be freaky for the sake of being freaky. but it\\\'s all okay. i\\\'m glad these things exist because the alternative is that they don\\\'t exist. of course there is attitude present but i\\\'m happy enough to sift through it all and find the little corner where i can sit back and watch the parade of san francisco do its thing. much like rachel, i also don\\\'t feel compelled to wear green styrofoam tits on my forehead.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(9857,1905,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<ol>\r\n<li> making soup\r\n<li> packing and unpacking\r\n<li> keeping philodendrons alive\r\n<li> talking to strangers\r\n<li> mothering inanimate objects\r\n<li> squeezing yeti\'s blackheads\r\n</ol>',4,0,0,0,'66.123.206.34','en'),(9858,1902,'2001-10-08 13:42:20',0,'me','my friend danny used to be in the bindlestiff family circus, i dont know if he still is....\r\nwas there a geeky little blonde boy who is a contortionist?? just wondering...',0,0,0,0,'152.163.205.64','en'),(9859,1905,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>\r\n1. whistling <br>\r\n2. cracking my knuckles<br>\r\n3. mixing records<br>\r\n4. writing<br>\r\n5. dreaming<br>\r\n</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9860,1905,'2001-10-08 14:24:44',0,'jo','<ol>\r\n<li>keeping my checkbook balanced</li>\r\n<li>sending postcards</li>\r\n<li>neck massages</li>\r\n<li><b>neck kisses</b> - oh lordy i\\\'m good at that</li>\r\n<li>telling stories</li>\r\n</ol>',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(9861,1893,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>burritoville... gristede\\\'s... are you in nyc?</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9862,1901,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>\'hallett\'. definitely sounds like a cop-name; i can almost hear it, down at the station-house, \'hallett, get back to the precinct!\' or something like that. thats cool. all my names are too bland to be a cop-name.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9863,1898,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>painful flashback. i actually knew a fella in college that was obsessed with skull-fucking (<i>Squicking</i>, as he called it); he <i>actually</i> did the old melon trick. He heated them in his microwave and then went to work, <i>squicking</i> away. We used to bug him that his room smelled of honeydew.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(9864,1893,'2001-10-08 14:41:18',0,'Jamie','i wish i could pay someone to make burritos for me. But i must make my own. Because i\\\'m in stupid Ireland...',1,0,0,0,'217.32.142.181','en'),(9865,1905,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','<ol>\r\n<li>moving countries</li>\r\n<li>changing my mind</li>\r\n<li>being unemployed</li>\r\n<li>being in love</li>\r\n<li>organising lives that are not my own</li>\r\n</ol>',3,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(9866,1905,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','i should add:<br>\r\n<br>\r\n6. &nbsp;&nbsp;fucking<br>',3,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(9867,1905,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>1. changing what i am doing\r\n<BR>2. eating food\r\n<BR>3. drinking coffee in the morning\r\n<BR>4. doing what i want to do, eventually\r\n<BR>5. ?\r\n</P>',2,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(9868,1893,'2001-10-08 16:41:18',0,'jo to peter','yes she is, hence the \\\"mexican food in nyc is not mexican food\\\" comment. ',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(9869,1907,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','Fuck, I forgot to give this a title.  Ummm.....\r\n<p>\r\n\r\ntitle: Wow, this is what it\\\'s like to be a slut.\r\n<br>\r\nblurb: It\\\'s actually kinda fun.</p>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(9870,1905,'2001-10-08 17:08:54',0,'stats','we did this <a href=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=517\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">all before</a> didn\\\'t we?',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.147','en'),(9871,1902,'2002-10-04 04:15:39',409,'rachel','<p>\r\nthere was a blonde guy from australia\r\nwho was a contortionist. i forget what his\r\nname was offhand. he was pretty excellent,\r\nthough.\r\n</p>\r\n',2,0,0,0,'207.214.90.67','en'),(9872,1906,'2001-10-08 17:14:16',0,'ghost','\\\'living\\\' is not about what you do...it\\\'s about being true to yourself.',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.147','en'),(9873,1906,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','Shit... I was wondering what happened to you guys.  It worked out well though.  I had a friend down from Boston this weekend, and a new friend I met on Friday.  I wouldn\\\'t have been able to squeeze you into my busy schedule.  I still left about twenty messages on P\\\'s voicemail.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(9874,1893,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','Hey, Lou.  I always get the chicken fajita burrito for lunch.  There\\\'s a Burritoville across the street from my office.  What do you usually get?  I really do want to know.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(9875,1905,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>1. daydreaming<br>\r\n2. laughing<br>\r\n3. farting<br>\r\n4. making \\\"to do\\\" lists into fine art drawings<br>\r\n5. making home movies into video art</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(9876,1905,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','I could fill in austin\\\'s number 5.',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(9877,1889,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','<p>anything you make is copyrighted whether or not you put a &copy; on it.</p> :)',3,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(9878,1905,'2001-10-08 17:34:58',0,'skinky','1. reading\r\n2. playing DOOM (hey, I know it\\\'s out of date, but it\\\'s a useful skill, really)\r\n3. listening to NPR\r\n4. going to bookstores\r\n5. farting (in that order)',1,0,0,0,'156.153.255.243','en'),(9879,1904,'2001-10-08 17:37:35',0,'missoula 1989','we broke up, \r\ni slept in the basement apartment\r\nonly getting up at midnight\r\nto go to the bridge down by the school\r\nand smoke with the bums\r\n\r\ni rode my tenspeed around and around\r\nand slept with your hooded sweatshirt\r\nfinding your hair, peices of you\r\nleftover in my life\r\n\r\nbut i got over you\r\ndidn\\\'t i?\r\n12 years later\r\nafter the stalking court case\r\nand the injunction\r\nand finding of facts\r\n\r\nafter the felony \r\nand misdeameanors\r\nand seizures?\r\n\r\nwe got over eachother didn\\\'t we\r\nor and the slander\r\nand liable case\r\nyes that too',3,0,0,0,'156.153.255.243','en'),(9880,1906,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>er, um, ah. ack. sorrrrry. i was occupiedfor most of this weekend. i had hoped to get together later this week, but the damn war got in my way.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.127','en'),(21236,3662,'2004-07-29 23:52:32',83,'adamajah','*C*H*I*A*',2,9,93,0,'216.206.179.50','en'),(9881,1905,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','<p>1.  sitting and thinking<br>\r\n2. 