t>i think they get quite <i>enough</i> electro-shock treatment at teh half-way house...</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(9987,1913,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>rachel, its hard to understand because you\'re at a different maturity level than you were when you were a teenager; admittedly, though, behaviour trends seem to be hitting an all-time low. <br><br>I used to ride the B train home every day, and my commute overlapped the school-day\'s end. It only took me a week or so to learn not to ride in the last car of the train- as soon as I got to the 103rd street stop, school kids would flood in and <i>fuckin\' wreak havoc</i>; i\'m talking arguments, fights, flinging cups of soda on the walls of the car, destroying shit, and screaming and yelling ghetto narratives that would leave even Eazy-E blushing apologetically. when i was in school, i was a happy (albeit naive) guy. i don\'t think anything ever happened in my life that could have motivated me to yell and scream like those kids.  then again, even if anything did, i\'m not sure that it would be an excuse to carry on like that.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(9988,1915,'2001-10-09 23:19:53',0,'wb','this post reminds me a little bit of \\\"american pyscho\\\" i dunno why.',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(9989,1911,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','pussy cats!  mrow!',1,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(9990,1915,'2001-10-10 00:23:35',0,'ryan','it\\\'s the detail.  (i just read that book)',1,0,0,0,'209.162.48.203','en'),(9991,1916,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','ryvita and vegemite.<br>\r\n2 minute noodles (ramen).<br>\r\ni ate peanut butter toast for lunch for a month, to save money to visit sf.<br>\r\ncups of tea.<br>\r\npotatoes!<br>\r\n<br>\r\nthis is not so much desperation food but poor food.<br>',3,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(9992,1915,'2001-10-10 01:01:13',0,'Patrick Bateman','Tuesday: met evelyn for lunch at \\\'Faces\\\'. picked up the new Genesis album. Dropped clothes off at cleaners. Returned videos. Picked up Spiced Salt blend at Dean and Deluca...',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(9993,1916,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','the little raisin bran muffins that my grandmother forces on me when i visit.<br><br>\r\negg burritos with cheese and sour cream<br><br>\r\nfried bologna sandwiches with mayo',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.202','en'),(9994,1912,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','run outside with a metal baseball bat, when they are sitting there, and hit the railing as hard as you can. if one of them attacks you, as long as you are on your stoop feel free to defend yourself with said bat. METAL, i can\\\'t stress that enough. they will think you are crazy after that, and leave you alone.\r\n<P>\r\nbroken bottle pieces superglue to metal very well too. make sure to paint them to match!',1,0,0,0,'63.10.152.202','en'),(9995,1912,'2001-10-10 01:54:29',0,'Hallett','Why not buy a video camera, set it up in an obvious place.  If it didn\\\'t scare them away then at least you\\\'d have some interesting footage to work with and, if it ever came down to it, definitive proof of what was going on.  But you could make some kind of Jerry Springer on the Street show.  Perhaps using the Mr. Rogers theme song.  -hey did anybody know that Mr. Rogers was a sniper in Vietnam? ',0,0,0,0,'172.157.118.99','en'),(9996,1916,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<li>ramen<br><br>\r\n<li>and, from the critical path days, brown rice from the never-cleaned rice cooker, with maple syrup poured all over. mmm good! thanks marcy for this one.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(9997,1916,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>\\\'Smoky Bean Soup\\\'<br>Taylor Pork Roll<br>street-vendor pretzel</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(9998,1912,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>to bad glass is illegal and they\\\'d steal the videocamera.  i <i>do</i> like the bat idea. perhaps i could out-crazy them enough to make a lasting impression...</t>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(9999,1915,'2001-10-10 02:33:48',0,'fern','i also object to my name. fern!? is this some not so subtle reference to my hair?\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.168.23.149','en'),(10000,1915,'2001-10-10 02:46:14',0,'Victor Ward','shit, i\\\'m outta xanax.',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10001,1915,'2001-10-10 03:04:08',0,'lulu','\\\"fern\\\"...bwahahahaha....you\\\'re name is \\\"fern\\\"...hahahahhahahaha.',0,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(10002,1916,'2001-10-10 03:38:13',0,'trouble','i\\\'m a sucker for the little cheese and peanut butter vending machine crackers.  those and coffee almost 3 times a day keep me warm and regular.  i\\\'m also partial to the warehouse club size tub of animal crackers... that stuff lasts for months!  damn, i got the munchies now.',1,0,0,0,'24.181.44.135','en'),(10003,1916,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','today i went to the gas station and got some ritz bitz cheese bites. mang, it filled me up.',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10004,1912,'2003-03-05 23:09:34',129,'moebius','<p>I just thought of something...back in the late \\\'80s a trend developed among certain suburban convenience stores that were having problems with loitering heshers, potheads, and gutter-punks: they installed speakers in front of the store and blasted them with classical music! In general, it worked.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I\\\'d start with bucolic, romantic stuff like Debussy, maybe some Mozart. Avoid the Wagner and Beethoven symphonies, that might just amp \\\'em up.</p>',1,0,0,0,'205.186.177.83','en'),(10005,1915,'2001-10-10 05:20:31',0,'kat','i see a lot of food, as i work for a caterer. today we served banana chimichangas. braised with brown sugar and pecans, rolled in a flour tortilla, deep fried, sprinkled with powdered sugar then topped with vanilla ice cream and hot caramel syrup. our conversation ended with how overheated caramel makes a nice alternative to napalm. it literally burns itself into the skin so that you cannot wipe it off.',1,0,0,0,'32.100.70.230','en'),(10006,1914,'2001-10-10 05:25:33',0,'ghost','chocolate and coffee at Noon for lunch. and i dont friggin care if i\\\'m too broke...come hell or highwater i WILL have that three dollar cup of espresso dammit!!!',4,0,0,0,'32.100.70.230','en'),(10007,1916,'2002-03-15 00:17:55',129,'moebius','<br>\r\nOver the past few years most of my desperation food moments were found in corporate breakrooms when I was too swamped to really break for lunch. Since I\\\'ve never quite gotten in the habit of bringing a lunch to work, I\\\'d end up scrounging around and eating ancient cup-a-soup type things or third-rate bagels left over from \\\"bagel day\\\" two days earlier.\r\n<br><br>\r\nand then this summer, when I had to go on an absolute-zero-fat diet to ward off an incipient heart condition, <i>everything</i> seemed like desperation food for awhile. but I\\\'ve since adjusted, as long as I can sneak a choccychip cookie once in awhile.<br> ',1,0,0,0,'205.186.177.83','en'),(10008,1916,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','\r\nthose dry dry dry toy-sized granola in foil in the vending machines. plain boiled TVP. plain sprout bread (eww, mushy AND lumpy). hmm, of course ramen too. usually i just down a lot of water so i don\\\'t eat yucky things at all. then i cook. when cooking hungry, i drink lots of wine.\r\n\r\npicky picky weeb!',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(10009,1916,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','graham crackers.',0,0,0,0,'66.123.206.12','en'),(10010,1916,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','yewr crazy! i love graham crackers in soy milk. mmmmmmmm',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(10011,1916,'2001-10-10 05:51:19',0,'jo','okay so maybe this is from growing up poor, but your desperation food is totally food that i buy on a regular basis for regular consumption. when asked the other day what i would want my last meal ever to be, if i were on death row, say, i answered: \\\"grilled cheese sandwich, tomato soup, big yummy salad. banana pudding with sliced up bananas and nilla wafers for dessert.\\\"<BR>\r\nam i simple to please or just simple?',0,0,0,0,'172.128.105.242','en'),(10012,1916,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','but when you\\\'re really hungry, graham crackers suck. hey weeb, i just said the following things to you on chat, but you\\\'re idle!\r\n<br><br><tt>\r\n/m s5 my brakes are fucked up. do you know how to tighten coaster brakes? i bet\r\n weeb knows<br>\r\n/beep weeb<br>\r\n/w @weeb<br>\r\n<br>\r\nGroup: mung     (mvl) Mod: weeb          Topic: beans<br>\r\n &nbsp;&nbsp;*weeb          6h19m    5:42pm  weeb@en.gage.org  (nr)<br>\r\n/m weeb DEAR WEEB<br>\r\n/m weeb I HAVE A QUESTION ABOUT BICYCLES<br>\r\n&lt;*s5*&gt; weeb\r\n<br>/m weeb PLEASE INDICATE IF YOU WOULD BE WILLING TO PARTICPATE IN MY DESIRE FOR\r\nANSWERS\r\n<br>/m weeb SINCERELY,\r\n<br>/m weeb ELLY\r\n</tt>',4,0,0,0,'66.123.206.12','en'),(10013,1916,'2001-10-10 05:58:34',0,'jo','my desperation foods: plain tortillas, popcorn, pasta. starches starches, some more starches.',0,0,0,0,'172.128.105.242','en'),(10014,1916,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','/m le ',0,0,0,1,'63.197.69.58','en'),(10015,1916,'2001-10-10 06:08:21',0,'silly weeb','<p><pre>\r\n/m le HI ELLY\r\n/m le YES THAT IS AGREEABLE\r\n<*le*> hi!\r\n/m le i am laughing\r\n<*le*> what do i do!\r\n<*le*> the brakes, they don\\\'t work very well!\r\n/m le aww\r\n<*le*> takes ten feet to stop!\r\n/m le oh yer fucked\r\n<*le*> very bad, run into planters and trash cans!\r\n</pre></p>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(10016,1909,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','I think the coolness of a position is frequently in direct relation to the shittiness of the application process / thickheadedness of the cockslappers in in HR there.  Oh well, good luck!\r\n(Kiss your elbow and jump up for luck.  If  you can spin around completely while in the air it\\\'s extra mojo.)',1,0,0,0,'209.163.146.106','en'),(10017,1916,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','Critical Pants?  That sounds like me after I\'ve had cheap greasy texmex for breakfast at the the little taqueria close to where I work (well, the little taqueria I like, there are three others).  Just one ... more ... function ... <em>NOWRUNTOTHESHITTERREALLYQUICKLIKE</em>. hahahaha...',1,0,0,0,'209.163.146.106','en'),(10018,1916,'2001-10-10 06:57:52',0,'cleanup gnome','</em> think I missed an end-em tag there.',1,0,0,0,'209.163.146.106','en'),(10019,1915,'2001-10-10 08:26:56',0,'author','the \\\"American Psycho\\\" tone was intentional. ',1,0,0,0,'216.175.93.164','en'),(10020,1910,'2001-10-10 09:16:22',0,'Hallett','after over $1000 dollars in various tickets and late fees, after getting my license suspended.  after getting my motorcycle impounded.  after month\\\'s of trying to negotiate the release of my license from the dinky little town court of Dekalb (which is only open from 7:30pm-8:30pm on tuesdays).  after having to call the Judge at home where she talked to me as she washed her dishes and made her kids lunch for the next day.  after all of this, I am finally ready to rejoin the throngs of car owning Americans.  it\\\'s good to be back.  cheers to all of you speeders and double parkers.',0,0,0,0,'205.188.198.181','en'),(10021,1916,'2001-10-10 10:28:30',0,'updating le','i think i figured it out. there\\\'s a little knob next to the pedal that when tightened or loosened seems to affect the sensitivity of the brakes. things were just cooler in 70\\\'s.\r\n<br><br>\r\nhi, i\\\'m nocturnal and bored! welcome to pointless swinney comments and submissions!\r\n',0,0,0,0,'66.123.206.147','en'),(10022,1917,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>there\\\'s a vendor who parks his cart on the corner near where i work every day. he sells not only potatoes, but also <i>yams</i>. if that isnt the coolest thing, he also sells baked <i>purple yams</i>, available with a variety of toppings, including tofu sour cream.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10023,1893,'2001-10-10 12:41:53',0,'lou','um. ew.',4,0,0,0,'216.175.64.134','en'),(10024,1916,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','meat pies',0,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(10025,1917,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','Dear Abbey:<p>Soooo..... I\\\'m trying to decide wether or not to loan Hallett $1,000 so he can move to NYC into Peter\\\'s place.  He\\\'s a dear friend, and I\\\'d love to have him around, but I\\\'ve got a story about an accordian that demonstrates his level of fiscal responsibility.  I certainly can\\\'t <i>give</i> him $1,000.<br>sincerely,<br><b>not</b> ridiculously wealthy beyond my wildest dreams in NYC.</p>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(10026,1917,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>so many ~500$ shares are popping up all over the upper west side; everyone should move here. but, is there something going on that i dont know about? yes, the room in my place might still be available. rent discounts for whacking the addict neighbors. hallett, you shoulda <i>kept</i> the accordian.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10027,357,'2001-10-10 14:20:57',0,'trouble','ok.  i was nice about this the first time this post was in the rotation but now... today of all days when the White Stripes are playing david letterman tonight and i am still living far from my hometown... it\\\'s just painful.  i have to move.  no getting around it.  back home to detroit or to chicago?  anybody got a quarter?',1,0,0,0,'208.255.153.146','en'),(10028,1918,'2001-10-10 14:25:40',0,'jo','HI ELLY I\\\'M GLAD YOU\\\'RE WRITING A LOT.<BR>\r\nokay now i\\\'m going to actually go read what you wrote.<BR>\r\nNICE SUPPORTIVE!',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(10029,357,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i purchased a stripes record online, and it was stolen. ups says it was signed for by \\\"Superintendant Bill Smythe\\\". never heard of anyone named that. i want my record, dammit.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10030,1918,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>this is a comfortably fragmented, fun-to-read piece. i like it. especially the obtuse cat part.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10031,1916,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','$1 McDonald\\\'s double cheeseburger.  If I have them in my fridge, I\\\'ll put sprouts in it to pretend that I\\\'m healthy.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(10032,1916,'2001-10-10 14:31:58',0,'Richard Simmons','and do you eat <i>these</i> with your usual 1/2 lb of mayo? <i>stop the insanity!</i>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10033,357,'2001-10-10 14:38:39',0,'trouble','props to Superintendant Bill Smythe for having good taste.  too bad you got screwed though.  find somebody who has the cd and steal it from them.  in retrospect, thievery and this band seem to go hand in hand.  i accidentally borrowed a friends copy a long time ago and then when i saw them in concert later i saw people stealing the discs from the merchandise table.  the people working the booth didn\\\'t seem to mind either.  in the end i guess karma will come back to Superintendant Bill Smythe, me and the thieves at the concert but until then... i\\\'m rocking the fuck out.',1,0,0,0,'208.255.153.146','en'),(10034,357,'2001-10-10 14:39:28',0,'jo','i was just thinking, on the drive to work, about how i\\\'ve seen a LOT of music this year, average of 3 shows a week probably, and i think the two white stripes shows were the top two shows so far.',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(10035,1915,'2001-10-10 14:41:22',0,'bret easton ellis','more people should read <u>rules of attraction</u>, i think that\\\'s my best book.',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(10036,357,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>unfortunately, it was a not-so-easy-to-find white-label vinyl. i think Sup\\\'t. Bill Smythe just has a thing for grabbing ups boxes, although he might be an audiophile, who knows.  my bldg\\\'s super is named alberto rodriguez, and he never steals my packages.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10037,357,'2001-10-10 14:42:02',0,'trouble','(rubbing hands together, raising eyebrow and smiling devilishly) my fiendish plan to elevate the White Stripes is working.... (insert ghoulish laugh here)',1,0,0,0,'208.255.153.146','en'),(10038,1909,'2001-10-10 14:43:47',0,'jo','this is in such direct contrast to my hamlet-like inability to make a decision that i devoured this entry, egg.',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(10039,1915,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i\'m currently reading <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0679743243/qid=1002725209/sr=1-1/ref=sr_1_3_1/107-3887088-1645351\"><i>the informers</i></a>. not his best, but definitely a refreshing revisit to the same so-cal flava\' as <i>less than zero</i> and some familiar characters like the batemans and the usual assortment of gay-drug-dealing-manwhores. i like this book.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10040,1918,'2001-10-10 14:48:52',0,'trouble','yes, this is a fun post although it left me thinking... how the hell can somebody be so in tune to their surroundings during a low blood sugar induced haze?  it\\\'s amazing and i\\\'m jealous now of your ability to recall such detail.  shit, i\\\'m lucky if i remember my name when my blood sugar crashes. *best friendly*',1,0,0,0,'208.255.153.146','en'),(10041,1912,'2004-07-27 05:00:32',578,'NetfÃ¶ng!','yea. if you\\\'d stop spinning gawdamned house and play a little pachelbel or something pretty, theyd probably go ;-)',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10042,1918,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','well. it\\\'s a catch, cuz i noticed a lot of things in this sort of overly detailed acid haze of being low blood sugar, but was unable to carry on practical business like finding the stupid application. i got it a couple of days later. heh.',0,0,0,0,'66.123.206.147','en'),(10043,1912,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>how about eno\\\'s <i>three variations on the canon in d</i>? thats the closest i have.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10044,1912,'2001-10-10 14:58:28',0,'trouble','i think you should play the soundtrack to Beat Street or maybe the entire Afrika Bambatta catalog BUT don\\\'t bother with the Breakin\\\' 2 soundtrack unless you want them to revolt...  see this way at least then you can have something to watch.<br><br>\\\'let the poppers pop and the breakers break\\\'',1,0,0,0,'208.255.153.146','en'),(10045,1912,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>nooooo way! they adore bambaata\'s <i>planet rock</i>. once, i threw that on amidst <i>ring my bell</i>, <i>tsop</i>, and <i>funkytown</i> and a haggard old guy actually came up to my window and quite profoundly shouted, \"don\'t stop! planet ROCK! b-boy busy gotta gotta pop-n-lock!\" see why this is problematic?</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10046,1916,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','Hey... I <i>like</i> mayonaise.  It\\\'s left over German influence.  French fries fried in lard (the way they\\\'re supposed to be, not <i>fucking conola oil</i>) smothered in mayo... yummy!  Then there\\\'s <b>putine</b>!  God, I\\\'m getting a woody just thinking about it all.',1,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(10047,1916,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>dude. my fam is as deutsch as they come and i never heard anything about mayo!</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10048,1918,'2001-10-10 16:37:50',0,'leonard','next time you\\\'re at the new college, look up patrick james dunagan and mr. tom clark (genius). tell \\\'em leonard said hello.',1,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(10049,1918,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','i wandered into the new college library the other day. it was strange. small, but dense. but nothing looked like anything i would want to read or check out. an aging hippie came in and smiled at me then went away. i wandered around the quiet corridors happily. the cafe kind of scares me a little.',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(10050,1917,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','\r\nthere\\\'s 500$ rents here too in san francisco- as a second roommate in nice little houses on nice little streets like dearborn and in the heart of castro valley. very different from last year\\\'s rents of $1100+ per person...',3,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(10051,1917,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>oooooh, i want to live in a <i>house</i>! i\\\'ll trade a stint in my apartment for a stay in a nice <i>house</i> somwhere. maybe the market is finally crashing. goody- now i can get that $10k loft i always wanted for only $5k!</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10052,1918,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','<p>i like it.   especially the \\\"wobbling in an oval\\\" part (haha).  i was reading it for a little while, and then i scrolled down, and down, and down, and well i don\\\'t think i\\\'ll finish it.  but, that\\\'s not because i don\\\'t like it.  it\\\'s because my eyes hurt in the morning.</p>',1,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(10053,1918,'2002-03-15 00:17:55',129,'moebius','<br>ok, ok, here\\\'s my favorite: \\\"The cat was yowling. It yowled more realistically than any other cat I had heard yowling before.\\\"\r\n<br><br>\r\nI love that line...it would never occur to me to think of such a thing. Now I know I\\\'m going to return home tonight, stare at my two itinerant feline companions, and wonder if they\\\'ve been faking it all this time. I wouldn\\\'t put it past them. (But even if that turns out to be so, I won\\\'t kick them to the curb.)<br>',1,0,0,0,'148.87.1.170','en'),(10054,1918,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','The two words that go together best in the english language: <em>Fuckin\\\' cat!</em> (Or: \\\"Why do we call them cats?  Because all the other monosyllabic Anglo-Saxon curse words were taken.\\\")\r\n<br><br>\r\nDon\\\'t get me wrong, I love cats.  But they are little fuckers.',1,0,0,0,'66.25.29.204','en'),(10055,1916,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','<p>\r\npoor food:<br>\r\nbagels from food not bombs toasted with margerine and nutritional yeast, and occasionally as a special treat, a slice of tofu.<br>\r\ntortillas toasted on the burner.<br>\r\nsauted onions, perhaps with a carrot or two thrown in.<br>\r\n</p>',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(10056,1916,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>witnessed last night at the c-town grocery at 110th and manhattan ave: one woman, four kids; 1 lb. tripe, one onion, two pork trotters, 1 5lb. bag of potatoes. cost? $3.71, on govt. assistance card. <i>thats</i> desperation food. we have it pretty good, after all.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10057,1918,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','yeah.... <b><i>FUCKIN\\\' CAT!!!</B></I>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(10058,1916,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','shit... that\\\'s how I was eating <i>before</i> I got food stamps.  Once I got the gov\\\'t aid, I was livin\\\' on steaks and frozen pizza.  <p>(disclaimer: this was years ago I did this.  I am now a productive member of society.)</p>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(10059,1916,'2001-10-10 18:26:20',0,'sims to ess','when i was on food stamps as a kid and for a minute a couple years ago... it was mostly cheap vegetables, rice and beans. and that\\\'s what i eat still, more or less. and p.s. i\\\'m no productive member of society!',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(10060,1916,'2001-10-10 18:27:12',0,'sims to peter','and what that lady was buying sounds like menudo to me. and really, it\\\'s pretty good. although it sounds disgusting',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(10061,1915,'2001-10-10 18:31:19',0,'Brett Ellis','Hi, I write a book anytime I get time away from inhaling bales of coke and hanging out with the actresses of \\\"Sex and the City\\\"',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(10062,1916,'2001-10-10 18:37:01',0,'ryan','<pre>\r\n\r\nA large saucepan (see note below)\r\n1 calf\'s foot (about 1 to 1 1/2 pounds)\r\n2 pounds honeycomb tripe\r\n1 large onion\r\n3 cloves garlic, peeled\r\n6 peppercorns\r\n2 teaspoons salt, or to taste\r\n4 quarts of water\r\nA comal or griddle\r\n3 large chiles anchos\r\nA spice grinder\r\nA large chile poblano, peeled or 2 canned, peeled green chiles\r\nThe calf\'s foot\r\n1/2 cup canned hominy (1 pound) drained (see note below)\r\nSalt as necessary\r\n1 scant teaspoon oregano\r\n</PRE>\r\n<P>\r\nHave the butcher cut the calf\'s foot into four pieces. Cut the tripe into small squares. Put them into the pan with the rest of the ingredients. Cover with water and bring to a boil. Lower the flame and simmer uncovered for about 2 hours, or until the tripe and foot are just tender but not too soft. Meanwhile, toast the chilies well. Slit them open and remove the seeds and veins from the chile poblano, cut it into strips, and add to the meat while it is cooking. Remove the pieces of calf\'s foot from the pen, and when they are cool enough to handle, strip off the fleshy parts. Chop them roughly and return them to the pan.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nAdd hominy and continue cooking the menudo slowly, still uncovered, for another 2 hours.\r\n\r\nAdd salt as necessary. Sprinkle with oregano and serve (see note below).\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nThis amount is sufficient for 7 or 8 people. It should be served in large, deep bowls with hot tortillas and small dishes of chopped chile serranos, finely chopped onion and wedges of lime for each person to help himself, along with Salsa de Tomate Verde Cruda to be eaten with tortillas.\r\n</P>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'209.162.48.76','en'),(10063,1916,'2001-10-10 18:37:38',0,'br','we need more of those.',0,0,0,0,'209.162.48.76','en'),(10064,1918,'2001-10-10 18:44:47',0,'jo','see, els, you were worried that people wouldn\\\'t like this piece or it would be too long and rambly to capture attention spans but more people have cited lines and responded positively to this than other pieces recently.',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(10065,1918,'2001-10-10 19:04:44',0,'trouble','i agree with jo.  this piece was a real visual for the minds eye.  i\\\'ve read it twice now to make sure i didn\\\'t miss anything the first time around.<br><br>\\\'but tendrils in a chaotic spiral\\\'... hmmm.',2,0,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(10066,1916,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','<p>i thought getting the chicharron tacos would be cool.  it put me in a state of desperation.  remember, bubba?  ew. </p>',3,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(10067,1918,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>yes. wrote more things like this please le. i used to eschew the long-ass pieces on here, now im finding that i actually <i>prefer</i> them, as theyre usually more insightful, especially once the writer has a chance to \\\'warm-up\\\' some. jay\\\'s recent post was like that; good. and i like your point of view, to boot. it makes sense.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10068,1912,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>now, my one of my half-way-haus neighbors is <i>dipping</i> <i>[thats as in \'skoal\' for those of you who are fortunately urbane enough to not know what \'dipping\' is]</i> and actually <i>spitting</i> the shit on my window. heads are gonna roll, i assure you. one of you texas folks- fill me in on the best way to confront a dipper!</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10069,1917,'2001-10-10 19:57:53',0,'leonard','i wonder what kind of jobs they have in fucksville?',2,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(10070,1912,'2001-10-10 20:02:39',0,'trouble','do people still say the person spotted dipping has a \\\'boot lip\\\'?  do what i did back in high school, walk up behind one of the them and wack them on the back real hard and make them swallow that shite.  i used to love doing that to the rowdy bunch that loved their dip, its a bonus if they ingest and then expell rapidly because i hear the bile burns like hell for some reason.  *constructive*',3,0,0,0,'208.255.153.146','en'),(10071,1917,'2001-10-10 20:04:27',0,'Mayor o\\\' Fucksville','fuckin\\\', bonin\\\', shite like that. general screwin\\\' around.',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10072,1920,'2001-10-10 20:18:44',0,'trouble','goddamn, that\\\'s two posts today that make me question whether or not i go through life with my eyes open, do i notice anything going on around me?  i apparently do not.',1,0,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(10073,1920,'2001-10-10 20:21:42',0,'leonard','oakland is quite the <a href=\\\"http://www.ebbc.org/hypermail/ebbc-talk/2000/1157.html\\\">fashionable</a> town.',1,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(10074,1920,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>geez. people out there sure do wear alot of hats! i probably dont see two hats in a whole day here, if that many. people should wear more hats. i\\\'m going to the store now; i think i\\\'ll dig out a hat to wear. surely i have one around here some place...</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10075,1910,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>i am now a card carrying driver of the California roadways.</P>\r\n<P>but first i had to fail the test.  they let me take it again.  according to ann, that is not kosh.  she had to go back the next day when she failed it.  so i got special treatment.</P>\r\n<P>it was more stressful than the SAT, taking that quiz.  my head is splitting.  i have not eaten anything since brekky and i drooled all over the answer sheet.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>unfortuneatly i forgot to tell them i was in for a drivers license with motorcycle attachment like xep did.  xep said they dont know what from what when you turn in an out of state license as i did.  if you tell them you had a motorcycle license with it, they will maybe believe you.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>next up, insurance and registration.</P>',3,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(10076,1912,'2001-10-10 23:39:09',0,'Green','FInd the city ordinances on razor wire then ask your super. No ONE will fuck with razor wire....',0,0,0,0,'198.81.17.46','en'),(10077,1910,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to Austin','<br><tt>...good luck. im still driving on a year-expired out-of-state tag cause its so tedious and expensive to register my damn car. ack.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10078,1907,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>Congratulations, essemar, you are now qualified to live in San Francisco and call yourself an \\\"artist.\\\"</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin',5,0,0,0,'24.221.170.233','en'),(10079,1907,'2004-07-27 05:09:45',82,'a FAN','hey, darwin, eat a bowl of dicks.',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(10080,1913,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','i think i was more afraid of teenagers when i was one.  i feel like i could crush them like little bugs now.  at the time, however, i had no sense of self worth or self preservation.  i thought everyone had a reason to want to abuse me.\r\n<p>\r\nnow it\\\'s easy for me to think, \\\"bah, you\\\'re just teenagers\\\" and i think they pick up on that.  recently i went and visited a friend at her highschool.  we walked down the hallway together between classes so it was filled with lots of teenagers doing their teenager thing.  i felt no fear though.  i think they sensed it.  no one said a single word to me except one 15 or so year old boy who looked at my motorcycle helmet and said \\\"Arai... coooool\\\".  (that brings up all sort of other consumer idenity in our youth but that\\\'s an entirely different tangent.)  it was bizarre to be in a high school without the ever present fear that tainted my entire high school experience.  i think i could have gotten so much more out of it if i had just learned to not be afraid.  that\\\'s probably the case in all aspects of life actually.  just learn not to be afraid. (hah)\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(10081,1907,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','YAY - darwin is back!!',1,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(10082,1907,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>Hey, at least when <u>I</u> make snide comments, I have the balls to put my name on them.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin',1,0,0,0,'24.221.170.233','en'),(10083,1907,'2001-10-11 01:39:22',0,'sarah forbes keough','sorry, pumpkin cake, i like using funny little names from time to time. i think they\\\'re a laugh a minute.',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(10084,1920,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','<br>\r\noakland fashion is ALL about the hats.  no really.  it\\\'s all about the hats.  those sunday church going hats... oh man.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(10085,1907,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','your middle name is FORBES? i feel that explains a lot.',0,0,0,0,'66.123.206.44','en'),(10086,1920,'2002-03-08 04:52:47',65,'le to trouble','egg walks around with a notebook and sometimes when you\\\'re talking to her she\\\'ll laugh loudly, repeat what you said back to you with a quirky rephrasing, squint, and then write something down in her notebook. ',4,0,0,0,'66.123.206.44','en'),(10087,1907,'2001-10-11 02:45:14',0,'amy r.u. squires to sarah fk','will you call me \\\"pumpkin cake\\\" from now on',0,0,0,0,'216.175.89.229','en'),(10088,1920,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','in totally unrelated other news besides the fact that this takes place in oakland, I was at the ruby room in oakland the other night, and in the girl\\\'s toilet room I saw these words: \\\"little sarah is sexy because she is 21 and so trashy\\\". also, on the toilet seat itself was written \\\"little sarah is sexy\\\". Now I am wondering for a number of reasons if \\\"little sarah\\\" is someone I know. is it? only one person here can tell me. SPeak up. ',0,0,0,0,'216.175.89.229','en'),(10089,1920,'2001-10-11 03:02:54',0,'trouble to le','while i could see using a notebook to record such information being a start to my being keen to the goings on around me i\\\'m wondering if this doesn\\\'t indicate a bigger problem.  i think i need to be more open to the things i remember... wait, that sounds ridiculous.  <br><br>what i mean is i can pick the things out of the day that really pissed me off and recall them in meticulous detail but the random things like ordering lunch, talking with a co-worker (unless its some real salacious shit) and checking out the folks around me in general doesn\\\'t register.  it\\\'s a funk i\\\'m in... the changing of the seasons before i was ready i think fucked me up.  thanks for the insight on eggs\\\' extra nifty way of recalling things... the both of you rock with the swintries.',1,0,0,0,'24.181.44.135','en'),(10090,1910,'200