 who aren\'t act out of habit.  the latter bores me.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n',6,0,0,1,'66.92.4.146','en'),(10166,1921,'2001-10-11 19:24:16',0,'jim to Peter','<p>\r\nwow, I couldn\\\'t disagree with that more.  I think one of society\\\'s greatest problems is this epidemic lack of obsession, this apathy, this approaching everything with a safety net of irony and distance. people who are obsessed with something act out of passion, people who aren\\\'t act out of habit.  the latter bores me.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n',6,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(10167,1921,'2001-10-11 19:28:38',0,'','<br><tt>er, jim, i meant the <i>stalker</i> variety of obsession. no, apathy is bad, yes. passion is good, yes. i couldnt agree with you more. but, i guess i\'m just not the type who finds himself smitten with someone, pours over their webpages, and begins obsessing over them, thats all. <i>\'best friendly\'</i> ',0,0,0,1,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10168,1921,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to jim','<br><tt>er, jim, i meant the <i>stalker</i> variety of obsession. no, apathy is bad, yes. passion is good, yes. i couldnt agree with you more. i guess i\\\'m just not the type who finds himself smitten with strange entities, pouring over their webpages, obsessing over them, thats all. </i>\\\'best friendly\\\'</i>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10169,1921,'2001-10-11 19:30:12',0,'ummm','passion + habit = terrorist attacks',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.37','en'),(10170,1921,'2001-10-11 20:09:55',0,'jim to ummm','<p>\r\npassion + habit = a lot of things.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nwhen I talk about passion and intensity lately people invariably mention how passionate and intense the terrorists were, as if to suggest that passion and intensity should be added (alongside butter knives, nail clippers, shaving razors, curbside check-ins and freedom) to the list of things we can\'t carry with us anymore.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>  \r\nthat scares me more than jet planes, more than anthrax.\r\n</p>',6,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(10171,1921,'2