ly<br>2. making woman feel spectacular -emotionally/spiritually<br>3. making woman wish they\\\'d never met me.<br>4. traveling<br>5. any kind of visual art except sculpture and painting.<br>note: i would never call myself an artist and mean it, i would never call anyone an artist.',0,0,0,0,'172.158.161.144','en'),(10185,1921,'2002-03-05 20:17:36',17,'austin to jim','does passion scare you more than megadeth and slayer too?',4,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(10186,1921,'2001-10-11 23:16:09',0,'justino','<p>\r\nberlin\\\'s best song is \\\"riding on the metro\\\" but for this thread it has to be \\\"<a href=\\\"http://www.totse.com/en/ego/can_you_dance_to_it/berlnsex.html\\\">Sex (I\\\'m a)</a>.\\\"\r\n</p>',2,0,0,0,'210.197.80.13','en'),(10187,1923,'2001-10-11 23:42:31',0,'Samuel L. Jackson','No, I usually just sock \\\'em on the jaw and yell \\\"Pop goes the weasel\\\"...',3,0,0,0,'195.40.196.181','en'),(10188,1921,'2001-10-11 23:43:35',0,'Professor A. Hall','<p>Ahem.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Let\\\'s take a historical view of this \\\"which came first, Justin or the Chicken\\\" question:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I present this exhibit A, from within a few months of <a href=\\\"http://www.links.net/vita/sf/egg/pix/mindfuck.lg.jpeg\\\">the initial meeting</a> of ARUS and JAH:</p>\r\n\r\n<a href=\\\"http://www.links.net/vita/sf/egg/\\\"><img src=\\\"http://www.links.net/vita/sf/egg/pix/harlot.lg.jpeg\\\" alt=\\\"holy harlot\\\" border=1 width=276 height=419></a><p>\r\n\r\n<p>As we can see, circa 1996, Egg was the more <a href=\\\"http://www.links.net/vita/sf/egg/pix/pinkpixie.lg.jpeg\\\">lively looking</a> of these two younger people.  It probably stems in large part from these, the Chickens:</p>\r\n\r\n<a href=\\\"http://www.links.net/vita/sf/egg/pix/lolita.lg.jpeg\\\"><img src=\\\"http://www.links.net/vita/sf/egg/pix/parents.lg.jpeg\\\" alt=\\\"cock a doodle doo!\\\" border=1 width=460 height=325></a><p>\r\n\r\n<p>The roots of Amy\\\'s particular sort of genius clearly rest largely between these two folks and all they had in mind for their offsprung.</p>\r\n\r\nWhat affect did ARUS have on JAH?  Proof is profuse, but dirty crotch.  We have this photo, taken mid-stride, to evidence the changes in progress:<p>\r\n\r\n<a href=\\\"http://www.eggthings.com/blood/\\\"><img src=\\\"http://www.links.net/vita/sf/egg/pix/me.blood.md.jpeg\\\" width=216 height=144 border=1></a><p>\r\n\r\n<p>Finally, we turn to a photograph by <a href=\\\"http://www.links.net/vita/sf/scoot/pix/shadeshead.lg.gif\\\">Professor Bremser</a>.  This, taken as the end of JAHARUS was in site</a>.  Here we see the evident long term damage to both parties resulting from this relationship:</p>\r\n\r\n<a href=\\\"http://www.links.net/vita/sf/egg/pix/heart.lg.jpg\\\"><img src=\\\"http://www.links.net/vita/sf/egg/pix/thaibrunch-upset.lg.jpg\\\" alt=\\\"the end\\\" border=1 width=348 height=470></a><p>\r\n\r\nKnowing why it didn\\\'t work is a mystery of the ages, though the advent of their discontent was <a href=\\\"http://www.links.net/vita/sf/egg/pix/script.jpg\\\">liberally</a> strewn about.',1,0,0,0,'210.197.80.13','en'),(10189,1921,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','let\\\'s get on with 2001, people.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.101.59','en'),(10190,1923,'2001-10-11 23:56:33',0,'nowhere girl to bmg','Most definitely. I will email instructions for bathtub ministrations and available timeslots immeadiately.',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.37','en'),(10191,1893,'2001-10-12 00:50:55',0,'lou','orange is the new pink!<P>\r\n<font size=1>burn! burn!</font>',6,0,0,0,'216.175.64.134','en'),(10192,1923,'2001-10-12 01:03:12',0,'hardcore','bathtubgirlhoax#669',4,0,0,0,'172.166.93.30','en'),(10193,1923,'2001-10-12 01:21:01',0,'wha','the...?',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.37','en'),(10194,1893,'2001-10-12 01:22:13',0,'sims to austin','that\\\'s funny cuz growing up in the mission, i\\\'m so not into texmex style. i\\\'m all about mission-style. i guess it\\\'s just what you\\\'re used to. on that note, i\\\'m leaving work and heading straight to cancun for a burrito. smooches.',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(10195,1923,'2001-10-12 02:10:41',0,'hardcore','fuk',6,0,0,0,'172.166.93.30','en'),(10196,1921,'2001-10-12 02:28:57',0,'leonard to egg','tru dat.',3,0,0,0,'209.178.128.135','en'),(10197,1921,'2001-10-12 02:37:49',0,'hardcore','bite me jim',0,0,0,0,'172.166.93.30','en'),(10198,1923,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>1. bmg <i>is</i> funny<br>2. we used to have one of those old-school footytubs when i was growing up. it was quite nice for bathing and rubber-ducky time.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10199,1922,'2001-10-12 03:59:37',0,'lou','this is why i don\\\'t ride the bus.  the train all the way, yo. i\\\'d rather walk than ride the bus. except the shuttle bus. i love the shuttle bus.',2,0,0,0,'216.175.64.134','en'),(10200,1922,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'peter to lou','<br><tt>i am lucky. i get to take the train to the bus. i can even take the local or express, and end up at the same bus stop.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10201,1922,'2001-10-12 05:14:08',0,'lou to peter','except you still have to take the bus. i don\\\'t think the bus can be rationalized. not in any way. not express, not local. only shuttle bus.  i wish the train went to more parts of nyc, in less roundabout ways.',4,0,0,0,'216.175.64.134','en'),(10202,1922,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to lou','<br><tt>the busses have hissy brakes that wake me up at night, too. if the train went further east, the city would be on the right track, and i could ride the rails all the way to work.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10203,1921,'2001-10-12 05:33:06',0,'Green','The above is a fictional story. All names, events, and places are not meant to represent actual people, occurances, or locations and are merely coincindental. It is not a definitive statement on the swinney world. It does not offer any solutions. It is however a highly personal cronical. As such, we hope it will provide insightes into our highly sexual and competitive swinney society. Any taking this entry as fact please bear in mind that you suck.',6,0,0,0,'172.182.189.21','en'),(10204,1921,'2001-10-12 06:41:41',0,'Leonard Cohen','i smell a post called \\\" the history of them all\\\".',1,0,0,0,'24.27.31.48','en'),(10205,1918,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','there is a hollow space that cats occupy, somewhere behind the meat in my head. it is where your head was at when you said the man\\\'s eyes were \\\"hidden from you forever\\\". someplace hollow and minty green and cool, like the cinder block that you put your hand on in the school bathroom or cafeteria at ramona quimby, age 8, time and place. this is how to describe memory. I want to read more things like this.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.101.59','en'),(10206,1907,'2001-10-12 07:49:00',0,'cyantist','austin: so, how\\\'s that working out for you?  being clever?',2,0,0,0,'24.221.170.119','en'),(10207,1907,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>Thanks, essemar. Yeah, incitor is a nice guy. One of my few true friends on this has-been planet, orbiting a cold, indifferent sun.</p>\r\n<p>Glad to know someone appreciates my efforts.</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n',1,0,0,0,'24.221.170.233','en'),(10208,1922,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','i used to take the m104 ( or the 4, i cant remember?) bus a lot, from columbia to work on the upper east side when i was dating a columbian. oh and i also lived on frat row for a summer. I relished taking that bus because i got to look out the window and see the city rollin and hoppin. part of the payoff of new york is the physical environment, and people are so often trapped in their rat-routine that they require themselves to block out a lot of delicious stimuli in order to survive and get where they are going. wherever that is.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.101.59','en'),(10209,1907,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','i\\\'d like to hear sunday gossip about darwin\\\'s sex life.',0,0,0,0,'216.175.101.59','en'),(10210,1907,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','oh also, this thing about going home with a model. it reminds me of a \\\"sex in the city\\\" episode. I was walking on avenue A when i was visiting in august and i saw what could only be described as a MODEL!  and i whispered to my friend, \\\"wow, a model!\\\" and he was all, \\\"yeah theyre all over the place, duh.\\\" except im telling you this for a fact, I lived and worked there and we did not have models on the bowery or anywhere else around there in 1995. i guess, for the boys, this is an asset? for a low life prick-slut like me, it means \\\"there goes the neighborhood\\\".',0,0,0,0,'216.175.101.59','en'),(10211,1907,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>ive never seen any models here, although rumor has it that they exist. come to think of it, ive seen very few \'famous people\' here in the city. no wait, i take that back. i saw dick van dyke at the ollies noodle shop in midtown once. he was being a noisy asshole, and my gf at the time <i>shhhh!</i>-ed him. she also said \'shut up, fucker\'. to dick van dyke. how cool. from thence on, she was known as The Girl Who Shhhed Dick van Dyke.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10212,1922,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to egg','<br><tt>i like the m*4 busses. they take me to the museum. sometimes i think it would be a better idea to give up the rat routine and just sit here on my ass, on the bus and train, and strictly soak this place in. you dated a columbian <i>and</i> lived on skeez, uh, i mean FRAT row? had you no interest in self longevity? heh heh.</tt>\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10213,1924,'2001-10-12 11:32:10',0,'editor','dude. you started your piece with \\\"ok. so\\\"',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10214,1926,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>any craic? i like this. it reminds me of <a href=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=1597.txt\\\">this</a>.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10215,1561,'2001-10-12 12:36:59',0,'Flancie','this is the strangest post on swinney',4,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10216,1923,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','I have a rubber lobster that squeaks.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(10217,1907,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','egg, Peter: You guys should come hang out at my dance studio in Soho.  The neighborhood is teaming with overly-tall overly-skinny women in little black dresses.  I think the two of you should go around offering them kabobs and putine.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(10218,1907,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>is that the place where you danced <i>under</i> savion glover? ive been the posterboy for Lazy Slug lately. it might actually take the prospect of tall women in little black dresses to get me off my ass. although, id gladly get up for a kebab. maybe i should just watch tv.</tt>\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10219,1907,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','No... the studio where my tutelage <i>under</i> Savion Glover occurrs is on 57th above the Hard Rock.  The best thing to look at there is the teeny-bopper tourists.  Well, that and the toned, athletic dancers I take classes with.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(10220,1876,'2001-10-12 14:28:54',0,'geo','<p>anyone else find something a bit strange about the syntax of the dude\\\'s messages?</p>',1,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(10221,1918,'2001-10-12 14:57:38',0,'geo','I think that this is what my teachers meant when they told me to elaborate. This is a really fun visual thing you\\\'ve written, it seems to go in slow motion though it isn\\\'t slow to read. \r\n\r\nAlso, I hate college paperwork. I\\\'m glad you got to experience the cat since you had made the trip, even if you never got the application.',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(10222,1918,'2001-10-12 15:02:37',0,'jo','(hi, george.)',0,0,0,0,'172.169.120.183','en'),(10223,1924,'2001-10-12 15:34:03',0,'erbie','snort. sigh.',4,0,0,0,'64.105.32.155','en'),(10224,1924,'2001-10-12 15:41:31',0,'all the little piggies go','snort, snort, sigh.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10225,1921,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt><b>55</b> comments. my, my.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10226,1922,'2001-10-12 16:13:31',0,'geo','<p>ha. I love public transportation. There\\\'s something great about relationships of mutual recognition. You never really talk to the people, but they\\\'re comforting to see. Like the bus people, or even better, when the guy at the coffee stand on 34th and Madison knows your order (small coffee with cream and a bigass croissant), even though he serves a million people a day.</p>\r\n<p>I like that you have publicly acknowledged these people you see everyday. Now there\\\'s some kind of record of them for the day when you change bus routes or cities.</p>\r\n<p>Also, I love that you play a commuter-beat-matching game. I think I would play the same game if I rode your bus.</p>',2,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(10227,1921,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','I concede defeat.  You know what I\\\'m talking about <b>BITCH</B>!<p>So.... 56 comments.  Has anyone else noticed that that\\\'s how many comments Auntie\\\'s infamous \\\"doggie-style vs. missionary\\\" article got?  Does this mean Swinnites are more obsessed with Justino and Egg then sex?  Does the record for most commented upon article pass to this one? or is there an article I\\\'m not aware of that has recieved more?  shit....</p><p><h6>btw, anyone notice my most recent article with 54 comments?</h6>:-)</p>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(10228,1907,'2001-10-12 16:55:05',0,'ghost','smell of the new girl...is not me. not new. i have not left anything. anywhere. with anyone. not worth writing about. wondering about. holding back. locked inside. no longer. stupid. pointless. twisted. slut dreams. fruit cake. hot honey tea. burns me. freaks me. do you need this. i am not tall. not short. not fat. not thin. i am not your fucking daydream. only a glance. over the shoulder. not there. not here. wanting. wanting. wanting. wanting. passion and gutwrenching. youth. useless. no sense. no reason. recollections. it only works if you are willing to let go.',4,0,0,0,'32.102.109.102','en'),(10229,1907,'2001-10-12 16:56:34',0,'ghost','oh...im sorry i didn\\\'t realize this was a contest. \r\n\r\n<i>hello/goodbye</i>',1,0,0,0,'32.102.109.102','en'),(10230,1922,'2001-10-12 17:10:19',0,'jo to geo','george, peter\\\'s post was a sort of inspired/prompted by <a href=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=1920.txt\\\">egg\\\'s</a>.',0,0,0,0,'172.139.85.108','en'),(10231,1921,'2001-10-12 17:52:59',0,'for green','<p><img border=\\\"0\\\" src=\\\"http://www.gee.kz/peter/yc.jpg\\\" width=\\\"225\\\" height=\\\"272\\\"></p>',1,0,0,0,'32.102.109.102','en'),(10232,1907,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','i smell her hair... squeezed together in crowded hallways. who is she? her image lingers in the places we meet. in my mind. in my longing. hot honey tea. soothes me. calms me. i need this. a dream... as i write. she is tall. short. fat. thin. she is my fantasy. fear. she looks my way. i look away. mouth frozen. heart thumping. run away. run away. run away. adolescent fears. romantic desires. poetry lost in the wind. she doesn\\\'t know. i exist. and i cry. can\\\'t approach. ephemeral beauty. she disappears. like a ghost.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(10233,1907,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','ehhh.... it\\\'s not really a contest.  Some bizzare sibling rivalry kicked in when we noticed how many comments we were getting.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(10234,1806,'2002-04-20 20:49:51',273,'Quinn','Not that you\\\'ll ever see this, \\\"Droll Moll\\\" but you are a fool to think you\\\'ve \\\"seen this one before.\\\"  If you lived in NYC, like a friend of mind who had the fragments of WTC (including a burnt human torso)  rain through his fucking window, you wouldn\\\'t be so goddamn flippant.',0,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(10235,1922,'2001-10-12 18:47:37',0,'geo to jo','I know. Is that what that linky thing is up at the beginning?',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(10236,1922,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to geo','<br><tt>the lady at york/72 has my coffee waiting; i should have done her justice in this piece, ha. i just stopped and thought: i\\\'ll be making this <i>exact</i> commute for the next at least <i>eight</i> years (if grad school goes as it should). wow. by that time, i should have perfected the <i>Salsa and Toll-Box Funky Breaks</i> collection.</tt>\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10237,1806,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>a friend of mine dropped off a piece of the WTC here at my place- it fell on/broke his shoulder while he was fleeing wtc1; he says its his lump of bad luck for me. if i keep it, no harm should come my way as it stands for eons of bad luck already come. today, a doctor i work with told me he doa\\\'d a woman who was wheeled into the er in a shopping cart after tower 2 fell. sorry to rant. i just needed to get that off my chest. thanks.</tt>',0,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10238,793,'2001-10-12 19:37:03',0,'green velvet','im from la la land.',6,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10239,1921,'2001-10-12 19:53:23',0,'wb','i don\\\'t know why she had the glass in the cleavage. i dunno if brian asked for it. i think regardless of who asked for it, she wanted it. she wanted it badly.',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(10240,1907,'2001-10-12 20:05:21',0,'ghost to ess','mmm...thank you for the response. i still wish i\\\'d seen more of you out on the playa. i must have passed by you a million times. both of us rolling naked in the dust and not knowing it.',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.111','en'),(10241,1907,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>id pay good money to be <i>rollin</i> naked in the dust right now.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10242,1928,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>1. have you heard anything from hole\\\'s \\\"pretty on the inside\\\" album? such as \\\"when I was a teenage whore\\\"? it is worth your time. </p>\r\n<p>2.  the first two songs that come to mind in which your \\\"stop\\\" phenomenon occurs is, the pixies \\\"where is my mind?\\\" and cibo matto\\\'s \\\"spoon\\\". both of which are fine songs, imho. so suck it.</p>',0,0,0,0,'216.175.101.59','en'),(10243,1928,'2001-10-12 20:51:52',0,'wb','right. right. cibo matto i have heard that one. there are songs on the radio also. lucinda williams. jewel im sure does it. nelly fartado. explain nelly fartado.',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(10244,1928,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>one of my favorite <a href=\\\"http://audio.satelliterecords.com/ram/82280.RAM\\\">songs</a> uses \\\'stop\\\'. it is quite a gimmick, though.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10245,1927,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','hi quinn. ',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.44','en'),(10246,1928,'2001-10-12 21:35:55',0,'wanky wankerson','see, and here i thought the \\\"stop\\\" gimmick started with m.c. hammer!',0,0,0,0,'63.110.193.71','en'),(10247,1929,'2001-10-12 22:20:02',0,'kat','someone must give in',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.111','en'),(10248,1929,'2001-10-12 22:20:29',0,'morphing','someone must give in...both should',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.111','en'),(10249,1929,'2001-10-12 22:21:00',0,'into','without both giving in',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.111','en'),(10250,1929,'2001-10-12 22:21:29',0,'silent','it wont work',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.111','en'),(10251,1929,'2001-10-12 22:22:28',0,'erotic','torture to give in....torture to not',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.111','en'),(10252,1929,'2001-10-12 22:23:11',0,'ghost','time to let go? or time to lose?',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.111','en'),(10253,1929,'2001-10-12 22:27:07',0,'i','am tired of dancing alone...',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.111','en'),(10254,1928,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','janes addiction: also guilty of the gimmick.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(10255,1927,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','there\\\'s a war?',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(10256,1929,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','<pre>\r\n/status name lupine\r\n[=Change=] Group is now named lupine\r\n</pre>',0,0,0,0,'66.123.206.70','en'),(10257,1930,'2001-10-13 01:13:55',0,'only slightly relevant','that feeling of being embarrassed for someone else?  in my family, we\\\'ve made up a word for it: TUFA.  TUFA is an acronym; the letters stand for Totally Unbelievably Fucking Annie.  (Annie being the feeling you get when you watch Annie and keep changing the channel because you are so ridiculously embarrassed for every single person taking part in that spectacle.)',0,0,0,0,'63.110.193.71','en'),(10258,1928,'2001-10-13 01:37:44',0,'wb','peter, hate to break it to you, that song sucks.',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(10259,1929,'2001-10-13 01:38:47',0,'wb','anthrax hand',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(10260,1928,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to wb','<br><tt>um. <i>ok</i>.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10261,1928,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','<i>That song</b>; I\\\'m pretty sure Dave Clark spun that in his set at iDance this year.  I\\\'ve had a thing for Dave Clark ever since that time at Uncharted Waters, when he spun right after Jeff Mills and totally blew his set out of the water (no pun intended).<br><br>Speaking of Mills, <i>that song</i> uses the same bell sample from Jeff Mills\\\' <b>The Bells</b>.',2,0,0,0,'64.229.85.192','en'),(10262,1928,'2001-10-13 02:31:23',0,'</i>The W3C','Close your tags, infidel!',6,0,0,0,'64.229.85.192','en'),(10263,1928,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>thats the one. im spinning it right now, out my basement window, for my hood, ha.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10264,1928,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Malixious Moll','Oh god, is there a post-9/11 world already?',0,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(10265,1928,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','i  have my doubts about dave clarke but i \\\'m a big fan of  jeff mills\\\' \\\"the bells\\\"!  ding-da-ding-ding, ding-da-ding-ding!',2,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(10266,1928,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to Moll','<br><tt>post 9/11 is <i>so</i> here! the scene is breathing again, alas. <i>ding ding...</i></tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10267,1929,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Puss Moll','I have found that if both give in, weakness is created in the tribe. Both must hold fast until the life of one becomes intolerable. Obedience ensues.',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(10268,1929,'2001-10-13 04:26:24',0,'thought','giving in might not be the most appropriate phrase....simply giving might do. letting go is better. open. owning each other? obviously this was the motivator. owning. not on the whole healthy. dancing....the push and pull. unconcious movement of emotions. unspoken. yes. it is all in the dance.',1,0,0,0,'32.100.71.57','en'),(10269,1921,'2001-10-13 05:06:38',0,'BrewGuru99','Hmmm... Seems the swintry record lies elsewheres with 60 at the moment to this 58+1. (We probably should consider the number of comments by the author himself/herself and deduct those from the sum.)\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nNot like it all matters tho, this was just an obnoxious attempt at getting swin ratings.',0,0,0,0,'198.81.17.39','en'),(10270,1921,'2001-10-13 05:08:40',0,'green','<P> i know....I am <I> soooo</I> obnoxious. \r\nbut o well. Have you read the other stuff?</P>',6,0,0,0,'198.81.17.39','en'),(10271,1930,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>wow, that first paragraph made your english class sound like this site. heh.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10272,1921,'2001-10-13 05:11:58',0,'Bozo Filter','you are the weekest green. <b><i>Goodbye.</b></i>',6,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10273,1851,'2001-10-13 05:43:06',0,'Doctor Man','hmm. you were stoned <a href=\\\"http://www.rhodamine.org/aly/aly11.jpg\\\">here</a> also. are you ever sober?',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10274,1921,'2001-10-13 06:21:45',0,'jim','<p>\r\n\"the new design\" had 62.  with this comment, this swintry ties with it.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n',6,0,0,1,'66.92.4.146','en'),(10275,1876,'2001-10-13 07:54:17',0,'kittykat','it\\\'s been a long time since i\\\'ve been on here to check up on my friends, but it sounds like dude needs to die real quicklike.',3,0,0,0,'216.88.65.165','en'),(10276,1928,'2001-10-13 08:28:43',0,'wb','a few more instances of the \\\"stop\\\" issue:<BR>\r\n-macy gray (on her hit single) <BR>\r\n-u2 (on an older song where the last words are \\\"stop it\\\")<BR><BR>\r\n\r\nis it just me of does macy gray\\\'s raspy chortle voice sound a bit \\\'developed,\\\' like she heard billie holiday and went: i want that.',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(10277,1914,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','wiffle farts?',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.66','en'),(10278,1930,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','agreed. i think we should have one day each week (maybe on thursdays) when no one posts a single comment. comment-free thursdays.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(10279,1931,'2001-10-13 10:55:14',0,'OKmoon','as opposed to the \\\"Just\\\" video that will only frustrate.',1,0,0,0,'24.27.31.48','en'),(10280,1927,'2001-10-13 11:02:25',0,'one reporter\\\'s opinion','<a href=\\\"http://www.narconews.com/goff1.html\\\">check THIS crazy shit out... yeesh.</a>',0,0,0,0,'64.170.190.204','en'),(10281,1928,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>That\\\'s <a href=http://www.daveclarke.com>Dave Clarke</a>.</p>\r\n<p>And I find tech-housey-tribally music (like peter posted) really mindbogglingly boring. However, I have demanding taste in techno, so feel free to ignore me as a techno snob.\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin<br>\r\nTechno Loving Fact Checker',3,0,0,0,'24.221.170.233','en'),(10282,1931,'2001-10-13 12:13:42',0,'yaaaa','lets all smother ourselves and runaway with drugs!!!',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.46','en'),(10283,1931,'2001-10-13 12:52:57',0,'ghost','chocolate and good lovin does so much more for me than pot ever did. when necessary i can survive on chocolate alone. <p><i>*twothumbsupforbubblebathsnhotteataswell*</i></p>',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.46','en'),(10284,1931,'2001-10-13 17:10:47',0,'bmg','<p>what is radiohead?</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.81.166','en'),(10285,1928,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to Darwin','<br><tt>you have a good point. alot of house is spun strictly for its shake-your-ass motivtion. and as your average scenester\'s sense of time is smothered either in chemicals or the music (or both), boredom isn\'t much of an issue. in my set last night, that <i>boring</i> song was flanked by <i>Belt Frictional Problem</i> (<a href=\"http://www.cdnow.com/cgi-bin/mserver/SID=1216456996/pagename=/RP/CDN/FIND/album.html/artistid=ATKINS*JUAN/itemid=1386241\">Juan Atkins</a>) and <i>O.M.D.I.L.Y.</i> (<a href=\"http://shop.hooj.com/cookiesql.cgi?task=showproduct&session=100751105&id=kult020\">Snitzer & McCoy v. Humate</a>; heavy mix- try that at +6%). I also tossed in some <i>La La Land (vogt remix)</i> (<a href=\"http://www.green-velvet.com\">Green Velvet</a>). i typically like to throw in as much Hardfloor or emmanuel top as the househeads can tolerate, although i\'m not sure you\'d call any of this techno(?). links are for you to <i>fact-check</i>. whats your favorite piece of techno?</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10286,1931,'2001-10-13 17:53:21',0,'ryan','the teevee is one of the few mass mind control devices that the populace actually procures themselves.  90% of the time with much excitement, sense of duty, and lust.  it is dangerous.',6,0,0,0,'209.162.48.145','en'),(10287,1931,'2001-10-13 18:28:02',0,'dork','the teevee is only a mind control device ...<i>if you\\\'re stupid.</i> i dont know about you, but i\\\'m smart enough to be ableto handle teevee without being terribly persuaded one way or the other.',3,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10288,1931,'2001-10-13 18:42:04',0,'kitty2dakat','first of all, i don\\\'t smother myself with drugs. 2nd of all i\\\'m sorry i threw a suggestion to some of you people.  3rd, tv doesn\\\'t control my mind...drugs do.  :)  go hug a tree.  have a nice day!',3,0,0,0,'209.144.25.91','en'),(10289,1930,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','That feeling of being embarassed <i>for</i> people; I get that, too.  In my case, it is for people with annoying cell phone rings that go off in crowded public places (such as busses, busy streets, restaurants, etc.).  All of a sudden the cell phone that the rough-looking thug guy, across from you on the bus, is sportin\\\' begins to blast out the <i>Under The Sea</i> theme from The Little Mermaid and you can\\\'t help but want to crawl back inside your shell, or back to a time when cell phone\\\'s didn\\\'t exist.<br><br>Maybe I\\\'m just suffering from wireless envy.',2,0,0,0,'64.229.85.192','en'),(10290,1930,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','under the sea, that was really funny.\r\n<br><br><BR>\r\nhow \\\'bout steve-free fridays? that has a nifty ring to it...like a special at Applebee\\\'s.\r\n<br><br>\r\njust kidding.',1,0,0,0,'63.10.151.53','en'),(10291,1931,'2001-10-13 21:12:20',0,'jim to dork','that might be true if it wasn\\\'t for scientifically established concepts like the subconscious mind, and the effect message repetition is proven to have on it.',6,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(10292,1931,'2001-10-13 22:31:28',0,'kitty2dakat','i really didn\\\'t expect austin or bmg to have such narrow minded friends...that kinda sucks.  why is it anyone\\\'s concern if i like to get high and listen to music after a bad day?  if that\\\'s not what you like to do, then...don\\\'t.  go judge someone you actually know, if you must.  at least that would make a bit of sense.  peace.',3,0,0,0,'209.144.25.91','en'),(10293,1931,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to Kitty','<br><tt>dont sweat it. i get high on all sorts of shit and listen to music all the time, especially on weekends. i even have a fw friends on here who do also, but would never admit it, so there! we\'re not <i>all</i> bad, heh heh...</tt>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10294,1931,'2004-07-27 05:00:32',578,'NetfÃ¶ng! to peter & kitty','thats right. alot of us do it, we\\\'re just kinda reserved about it. i do it. youre among good company.',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10295,1931,'2001-10-13 23:16:07',0,'kitty2dakat','thanks kids.  :)',0,0,0,0,'209.144.25.91','en'),(10296,1927,'2001-10-13 23:29:03',0,'sospirando','<p>\r\non \\\"compromise\\\":\r\n\r\n\\\"From the viewpoint of dominant class interests, the less the dominated dream the dream of which I speak, in the confident way of which I speak, and the less they practice the political apprenticeship of committing themselves to a utopia, the more open they will become to \\\'pragmatic\\\' discourses, and the sounder the dominant classes will sleep.\\\" \r\n\r\n-Paulo Freire, from Pedagogy of Hope\r\n\r\nkeep hope alive.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n',3,0,0,0,'64.170.190.204','en'),(10297,1931,'2001-10-13 23:41:19',0,'repeat after me','...we all wank out our arsholes on this site. Never take anything anyone says too seriously. It\\\'s the kind of party where you stick your dick in the mashed potatoes.',1,0,0,0,'32.100.71.204','en'),(10298,1929,'2001-10-13 23:45:28',0,'ghost','sorry for being so vapid with my comments yesterday. restless roadtrip dust is stuck in my head.\r\n\r\n<p><i>i love this post. i love this post. i love this post. i loves this post.</i></p>',4,0,0,0,'32.100.71.204','en'),(10299,1933,'2001-10-14 02:02:22',0,'ghost','<b>*sigh*</b>',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.76','en'),(10300,1928,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>Those border on techno..</p>\r\n<p>My personal favorites for techno are : Subhead, Justin Berkovi, Neil Landstrumm, DJ Argonic, Deitrich Schoenmann & the hidden agenda crew, Tobias Schmidt, Si Begg, the Downwards camp.</p>\r\n<p>You know. Crunch, whirr, bleep. With some funk, but probably not \\\"shake-your-ass\\\"</p>\r\n-darwin\r\n',2,0,0,0,'24.221.170.233','en'),(10301,1928,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to Darwin','<br><tt>neon rocka is good.  ahh, but some \'shake-your-ass\' can help pay the bills.  double ahh about the <i>crunch-whir-bleeeep</i>- if youre ever on the east coast, feel free to come play with my <a href=\"http://www.rhodamine.org/pics/buchla.jpg\">buchla music box</a>!</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10302,1933,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','huh?',0,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(10303,1932,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<P>people have to learn their lessons on their own time.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>however, compromises must be made.  no one likes a person who does not compromise.  i often find myself impatient and waiting on other people.  i try to swallow time and remember that despite my plans, it does not matter if i am twenty or thirty minutes late because that is to be expected nowadays.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>i like to be on time, but often i am late.  i like to be with friends, but often they are late.  and whenever i have gone through this with friends that do not make compromises, i wait for them when they are late, and get dumped when i am, and that is not worth trying to be ontime.</P>',3,0,0,0,'216.175.92.7','en'),(10304,1931,'2001-10-14 16:58:30',0,'jo','(i gotta give props to quoting the dick in mashed potatoes, yo. mad props.)',0,0,0,0,'172.148.6.70','en'),(10305,1934,'2001-10-14 17:26:44',0,'french canadian man','O, this girl. With girls this age, you can do nothing nice for them without being a letch. The prettier they are, the uglier they make everyone around them. I know this is what they\\\'re thinking -- <i>je le sais!</i>\r\n',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(10306,1935,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i was only just getting used to seeing yvonne around.<tt> :(</tt>',0,0,0,0,'66.123.206.173','en'),(10307,1927,'2001-10-14 23:24:34',0,'green','i find nationalism of any kind to be a dangerous thing. And there is quite a bit of it strewn over the entire country. You see flags on every suburban, on the homes, on everything. It all boils down to economics. that is the end all conclusion to why people are unhappy...there is an immense hatred towards the american people that covers half the globe and more. what can i say...i despise what has been molded as the \\\"new\\\" american dream. a dream of acquiring more and more