bout those words.</p><p>Yeah, I get depressed sometimes and need to be alone, but most of the time when I feel like that I want someone to pop by and hold my hand, smile at me, scruff my hair, and make me chicken soup.</p>',1,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(10357,1940,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>at first i was nervous... will i ever get my <i>white blood cells</i> back? it makes me put some trust in humanity; some trust in <i>Metal Head</i>. not too risky as i see him daily on the bus. now we have a topic to talk about- thats truly groundbreaking for commuting NY\\\'ers!</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10358,1932,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>more people should be willing to be shoulders. You. Thats right, <i>you reading this</i>: be a shoulder sometime.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10359,1933,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','Hey, Wolfwood, I really like the stuff you write.  There\\\'s a neoimpressionist/anime feel to the words you choose.  I don\\\'t think enough people appreciate the raw beauty language can have apart from any meaning it may try to convey.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(10360,1934,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<p>I <i>love</i> generalizations.  They give you a simplified view of the world which allows our tiny brains a chance to actually grasp at least an allegory of what\\\'s happening around us. =)</p> <p>Problems with generalizations only arise when people think they actually apply to everyone and forget to treat people like individuals.</p>',1,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(10361,1942,'2001-10-15 21:54:10',0,'chi chi','i\\\'m with you on the disbelieving dog people. a few months ago egg and i spent a day on the beach. apparently it was our fault that we sat in the dog designated lavatory. i don\\\'t know how many came and pissed in front of us. but there was this one beast who came a shat not 5 feet from us. when the owner finally showed up an hour later, she basically accused egg and i of lying when we told her her dog had shat there, and would she please clean it up. ',0,0,0,0,'64.168.21.153','en'),(10362,1940,'2001-10-15 22:19:39',0,'green','good story\r\nahhhh, you should invite him over he seems like my type',1,0,0,0,'198.81.17.53','en'),(10363,1941,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','zazel did nothing but make me cackle with evil mocking laughter.',0,0,0,0,'210.54.254.35','en'),(10364,1942,'2001-10-15 23:26:32',0,'wb','yes, chi chi. and this is an important point left out. god for fucking bid you would say anything to these people. because in CA you sure don\\\'t want to be the one to harsh anyone\\\'s mellow.<BR><BR> as with the example of the frisbee people clearing the field, it\\\'s this quiet battle, a twilight battle if you will, between the savages and the civilians. if you say something it\\\'s public.',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(10365,1942,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Malixious Moll','<p>In Newark we have a park. It is, quite possibly, the ugliest and most unfriendly park in the world, quite befitting to the city and to New Jersey in general. It is called:</p>\r\n<p><b>MILITARY PARK</b></p>\r\n<p>It is basically a giant concrete crater. That\\\'s it. A large cement basin on the corner of two highways. I\\\'ve never seen anyone in it.</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(10366,1933,'2001-10-16 00:20:10',0,'jim','<p>\r\nI also really liked this.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nunfamiliar narrative styles scare people.  don\'t let it keep you from writing.\r\n</p>\r\n',6,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(10367,1942,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','no skaters??',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(10368,1942,'2001-10-16 00:25:52',0,'ghost','you live in a big city. there are humans there. most people are not perfect most of the time. my attitude towards stuff like this has mellowed over the years. i realize by virtue of being alive i\\\'m no saint and probably on occasion generate activity that might not please others. i own a dog. i pick up her shit almost all the time. i pick up other dogs shit. i do not like walking or sitting in shit either. i keep her on a leash almost all the time. mostly because she is a high anxiety shapeshifting crafty mutt who will disappear on me. i don\\\'t usually take her to parks unless its a dog park...because i too would like to relax when im at the park. but where i attempt to be a good dog owner i fail miserably in other areas. i am sure that many touristy folk...and old folk...and law enforcement folk are not happy with the fact that i tend to drive over Deathway 17 at speeds way above the posted limits. i do this six to ten times a week. that and loud music are the two things that make my commute sane. its a big city we all live in. i am not perfect. i need to release my anxiety somehow. someway. frisbee at the park might be a safer alternative for me.\r\n\r\n<p>*bestfriendly*</p>',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.99','en'),(10369,1942,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','chickens trapped in a small cage have two choices: peck each other to death, or wait peacefully for death. it\\\'s all about attitude, baby.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(10370,1940,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','i like this a lot.',2,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(10371,1942,'2001-10-16 02:06:03',0,'jay','I\\\'m not sure it\\\'s all that constructive to divide people in the park into \\\"savages\\\" and \\\"civilians.\\\" I mean, I hear ya on a lot of your peeves, and I\\\'m no stranger to malevolent bitching about infringements on my peace and personal space, but to hear this take you would believe that the only civil folk to sit in the park are the readers. A park is a public space, and unfortunately in dealing with the public, particularly in a larger American city where social mores can get a bit lax (because everyone assumes everyone else in town is a heathen, a pervert, or a slob), you take the wheat with the chaff, and if the inconsiderate grate too much on one\\\'s finer sensibilities, one packs it up and leaves. One yearns for the country, for fields that are not city parks, for this very reason: Isolation is the only means to achieving the sort of peace that excludes intrusion.',3,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10372,1937,'2001-10-16 02:23:51',0,'deb','wedding wasn\\\'t the point. it doesn\\\'t matter if you don\\\'t know what it is your\\\'re missing...',0,0,0,0,'152.163.201.214','en'),(10373,1942,'2001-10-16 02:31:05',0,'wb','it is all about civilians and savages. notice that even though what i wrote is long i never say \\\"there should be rules.\\\" or laws or any of that. the savages need rules \\\"no frisbee, no sports, no dogs.\\\" <BR><BR>civilians are proud of living free, but they know that with freedom comes a sense of personal responsibility. <BR><BR>\r\nyour solution is a typical one of the 20th century american urban dweller, to leave, for the country, for the suburbs. leave the savages behind in the city! why shouldn\\\'t the sportos go far out into the suburbs to find the large sports fields, dog lovers fields for their imprisoned beasts? my solution is stay ask for change, lead by quiet example and, when neccesary, shame them out of their behavior. the city can be a better, more civilized place. look what happned in nyc and some of the other cities of the east in the past decade. it\\\'s possible!',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(10374,1943,'2001-10-16 02:34:46',0,'deb','but you\\\'re wrong.  i\\\'m pissed at the media. i don\\\'t need to know about anthrax every day.  all they do is spread panic.  panic panic. i\\\'m tired of it all. i don\\\'t want to hear another word about war, anthrax, drafts... wake me up when it\\\'s over.',0,0,0,0,'152.163.201.214','en'),(10375,1943,'2001-10-16 02:39:05',0,'jay','I\\\'m really torn on this subject. Yes, quite obviously, our president is a fool and an idiot. But I believe, and I think not wrongly, that there are a whole lot of people putting a great deal of thought into this, and that at least some of them are quite informed and intelligent. The thing is, a Democrat, or even a Rhodes Scholar, is just as capable of making a blunder in wartime as a Republican, or a buffoon. We could lay back and turn the other cheek, but I\\\'m not sure, for all my pacifist feelings, if I could fathom laying down and quietly accepting my fate while getting kicked in the gut. I do not believe, for all of America\\\'s hubris, that we\\\'ve committed any terrible wrongs in the Middle East. Most our leaders have only sought to help in the peace process, and it\\\'s the problematic role of a superpower to have your hands in a few different pots. It\\\'s up to history to understand and parse out the consequences. So therefore, I want to see lunatics squelched, put in their place. I don\\\'t believe in an eye for an eye, but I do believe that we still live in a world where, despite all the peace we as Americans have enjoyed for a while, a military is necessary, conflict is inevitable, and if you threaten and kill, you deserve more than a stern reprisal and a judicious trial. In other words, the age of war isn\\\'t over, and the spoiled lot of our generation may just have to swallow this and move on, hoping for some semblance of peace eventually, in our lifetime.',2,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10376,1943,'2001-10-16 02:42:41',0,'jay','I also think it\\\'s a fallacy to believe, as terrorist would love for us to believe, that we are gravely in danger every day of our lives. Something awful could happen tomorrow, but it\\\'s not because of something the U.S. has done. It would have happened to someone, somewhere, no matter what. It just has to be stopped. I\\\'ve been saying all along wake me up when it\\\'s over, but now I\\\'m starting to realize that for all my will to escape, I don\\\'t want to sleep away a year or two of my life.',3,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10377,1940,'2001-10-16 02:49:25',0,'jo','peter. you are a good man.',0,0,0,0,'172.162.165.170','en'),(10378,1942,'2001-10-16 03:02:57',0,'jay','<p>First of all, my solution was not simply \\\"escape to the country or the suburbs,\\\" it was \\\"accept intrusion, or leave.\\\" I suppose there is a third choice which is to throw a fit and try to make your grievances known to all those around you, but in a democratic space, the quiet and annoyed tend to defer to the noisy and inconsiderate because the quiet are, quite often, out-numbered. If your favorite park has no rules against dogs, for instance, you should perhaps go to a park that has such a rule. I\\\'m sure there must be some in San Francisco, just as there are parks where dogs are allowed off their leashes. As for these other atrocities, on a beautiful day in a city that rarely sees sun, you\\\'re just bound to run into assholes who annoy you, whooping it up in public, enjoying the day as you are, but in a different way.</P>\r\n<p>Secondly, as someone who lived in New York for six years, all of which were during the Giuliani administration, the \\\"cleaning up\\\" and \\\"civilizing\\\" of the city to which you refer is a topic of a great deal of controversy. It is not, in fact, the Gen X liberals who have celebrated the triumph of these feats, as it has been the wealthy, conservative, or racist who have sung the praises of the mayor for getting the \\\"savages\\\" off the streets and out of sight. There are still homeless people (though somewhat less visibly-- not because they\\\'ve been given shelter or employment, but, I suspect, because they were herded into a warehouse one night in Queens and left for dead), and there are still assholes by the dozen in every city park you enter. When people visit New York, or get to know New Yorkers, in fact, one of their most noticeable characteristics I think is a certain stalwart resignation that their personal space will be violated, and their sensibilities insulted on an hourly basis. This is something I\\\'ve noticed that is peculiar to Californians: they put a high price on their personal space, and on their privacy. Unmolested by the world inside their car, they\\\'re easily upset by other drivers because they had been existing under the impression that the world was as controllable and ordered as the the radio dial. And San Franciscan, in particular, strike me as the most control-conscious and suburban-longing of all city-dwellers.</P>\r\n<p>Sorry to be quite so talkative, but I feel fairly strongly about this. To live in a city is to accept chaos, or savagery if you that\\\'s what you want to call it. We have laws, and parks have rules, and big cities have big police forces, because the more people you pile into a small space, the more chaos ensues, the more crap you gotta take from the next guy.</p>',3,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10379,1943,'2001-10-16 03:42:55',0,'science dork','anthrax is <i>not</i> highly infectious, contrary to popular belief- it is very infective, but its hard to get- it requires direct entrance into the bloodstream.',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10380,1940,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>mmm.<i>good</i> is this giant, juicy cabbage knish i\\\'m eating now. this here is the truth.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10381,1942,'2001-10-16 04:02:21',0,'wb','The first time I visited NYC was in the early 80s as a kid. Living in Philadelphia and having friends living there I visited frequently in the late 80s and early 90s. As a tourist whose been there at least once a year, I can see that it is a much nicer place now than it was. <BR><BR>Less homeless on the streets might be part of it, but not a major part. It is now a cleaner city than San Francisco. They might have better garbage guys there, but I think the civilians who live there don\\\'t throw shit on the street, out their car windows like the savages do here. <BR><BR>I think the average New Yorker has a better idea of what it means to be a citizen there. Over the summer I visited and went sat with a friend for a few hours in Tompkins Sq Park. There was much less space than the parks in SF, but people respected that space, nobody would have thought of doing the stuff I outlined above. Less than a decade ago this was a park of drug dealers, open IV and crack use, urinating and defecating. Some of that is still there, but it was mostly people (of all races) sitting, drinking a beer, having a conversation...<BR><BR>Everyone I know who has lived in NYC since before 1990 agrees that it is a nicer place now. Regardless of what white liberal, rich or gen x, thinks this or that, do you think NYC has declined? <BR><BR>\r\nThe savages I\\\'m talking about in this piece are white, with income and homes, people with free time, college educated people. People who should have developed some common sense, some manners, some consideration. Indeed, there is no bigger asshole in our society than a white male.\r\n<BR><BR>Philadelphia is much like New York in the attitude of the local people. I disagree with you about chaos. There is a big difference between hustle and bustle and chaos. The important difference is that, sure, you live in a city, people occasionally bump into you on the street, people honk, you almost get hit by an idiot on a bike in a hurry, you get splashed by a taxi.<BR><BR> The difference between these east coast cities and the west coast is that they are aware of those around them. If they are doing the same things I describe in the parks, there is a sense that they are being assholes, of \\\"Yes, I am doing this.\\\" Like I described with the smokers, at least they _know_ that what they are doing interferes with somebody else\\\'s personal space. There is an honesty there. There is the \\\"I see you\\\" moment. Even if it is \\\"I see you and guess what fuck you I\\\'m playing soccer.\\\" The dog owners I describe see you and look right through you.  <BR><BR>I agree with you that people here are affected by the time spent in the cars, they like personal space or expect it more. I\\\'m saying that more than the east, because of the car time, it has gotten so bad that they aren\\\'t even aware of when they are infringing on other people\\\'s personal space. This disconnect is where real chaos comes in.',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(10382,1942,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>you would get <i>so</i> nailed for dealign in Tompkins Sq. now, ha. the the only problem with living in nyc is that people let their dogs shit <i>everywhere</i> and arent terribly good about cleaning it up; particularly here on the upper west side.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10383,1943,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>is <i>the president going to get us all killed</i>? i dont think so. i dont like bush, but i certainly dont think hes leading me to death. just my two cents. <i>\\\'bestfriendly\\\'</i></tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10384,1943,'2001-10-16 04:24:42',0,'sospirando to jay:','<p>\r\nhow do we achieve a \\\"semblance of peace in our lifetime\\\" if we don\\\'t ourselves demand it?</p>',3,0,0,0,'64.170.190.204','en'),(10385,1724,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>this is an interesting story</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.48.134','en'),(10386,1943,'2001-10-16 04:39:53',0,'00','<img src=\\\"http://globalsecurity.org/military/systems/aircraft/images/atengun2X.GIF\\\">',1,0,0,0,'209.162.49.187','en'),(10387,1943,'2001-10-16 04:47:02',0,'sospirando','<p>\r\n<i><b>that\\\'s</b></i>creepy...</p>',0,0,0,0,'64.170.190.204','en'),(10388,1942,'2001-10-16 05:04:15',0,'jay','We are in agreement about the lack of consideration of Californians. The greatest fallacy is to believe that the happy, outwardly friendly attitude made famous by (southern) Californians means that Californians are nice and thoughtful citizens. There is a terrific self-importance and lack of humility that seems to come with life out here. It\\\'s either the cars, or the self-help culture, or the lack of any real history, or just some perniciously contagious attitude that spreads from person to person as they become indoctrinated in the way of life. Most of what you describe above <i>could</i> have taken place in New York, it\\\'s just that there aren\\\'t as many parks to lounge in there, at least on the grass, and there aren\\\'t quite so many frisbee throwers.',2,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10389,1943,'2001-10-16 05:19:28',0,'jay to sospirando','<p>If I\\\'m not mistaken, in history, peace has never come about by demanding it, but rather, by fighting for it. Believe me, if I was drafted, I wouldn\\\'t stand by these words and go to war. However I know there are people who would, and I only respect them for their courage. Is violence evil? Yes. Is war stupid? Absolutely. But this world is chock-full of stupid people who do stupid things, and who will not be reasoned with. There are a great many leaders, nations, groups, etc., who would rather see me and my family dead and bleeding than reason with me. Pure objectivity is an impossibility when passions are inflamed, so all that\\\'s left is battle, and a hope that someone submits or surrenders. Do you think now, or a few weeks ago, would be a fine time to submit, or to peaceably sit down at a negotiating table? If you do, you\\\'re a silly person. What have the American people, or our government, actually done to deserve being terrorized? To use anything but force is to say, \\\"Oops. We\\\'re sorry we upset you. We won\\\'t interfere in anything in the Middle East ever again. You guys straighten it all out, and just leave us to our happy little isolationist selves.\\\"</p>\r\n<p>If you were a world leader today, and you were faced with Adolph Hitler, on a mad mission to conquer all of Europe in the name of Germany and exterminate thousands of people who didn\\\'t fit his idea of human perfection, and he sent battleships across the Atlantic to conquer New York, would you simply try to set up meeting?</p>',4,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10390,1943,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<a href=\\\"http://www.tuxedo.org/~esr/jargon/html/entry/Godwin\\\'s-Law.html\\\">godwin\\\'s law</a>',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(10391,1942,'2001-10-16 06:19:15',0,'ryan','speaking as an oregonian that is currently \\\"doing time\\\" in california/sf, i must say that i have never really encountered this much filth.\r\n<p>\r\ni am amazed at the amount of smokers that throw butts on the ground (mine go into the can).\r\n<p>\r\ni am also amazed that in my four short years here not less than five times have i been waiting for a bus on market street and seen someone throw the detritus of their McMeals right into the street.  this has also happened at least five times on the bus itself, the jackasses throwing their shit out the window.\r\n<p>\r\ni could care less about fucking dogs -- sometimes the site of them makes me kind of horny.  what i cannot stand though, is people throwing their shit everywhere when the city has been nice enough to put those big trash cans everywhere. ',1,0,0,0,'209.162.49.187','en'),(10392,1943,'2001-10-16 06:21:48',0,'ryan','<i>\\\"I do not believe, for all of America\\\'s hubris, that we\\\'ve committed any terrible wrongs in the Middle East. \\\"</i>\r\n<p>\r\nwhat?\r\n<p>\r\nread some history.',1,0,0,0,'209.162.49.187','en'),(10393,1921,'2001-10-16 06:22:31',0,'lulu','BWAHHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHA!',0,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(10394,1936,'2001-10-16 06:25:03',0,'lulu','hey green....<br>\r\n<p>BWAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHA!</p>',0,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(10395,1942,'2001-10-16 06:27:39',0,'lulu','hey jay....<br>\r\n<p> B W A H A H A H A H A H  A H A  H A H A H A  H A H A H A H  A HA H A H  A H A . . . . . . P  P F F F T T H  A H A H A H A  H A H A H  A H A H A H  A H A H A H H A H  A H A H A H A HA H A H A  H AH A H A !</P>',0,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(10396,1943,'2001-10-16 06:31:14',0,'leonard to s5','brilliant.',2,0,0,0,'66.122.134.26','en'),(10397,1943,'2001-10-16 06:51:31',0,'origami','<p>Well, the arguments that we must step up to the plate and retaliate would hold more weight with me if we actually knew for certain who committed these acts.  It\\\'s all well and good to attack with full force when our enemies are screaming thier guilt from the highest mountains, but for us to mobilize forces in a very politically and emotionally precarious location without solid evidence to back it is like the kid who gets hit with a spitball in 2nd grade yelling \\\"I\\\'m going to get whoever did that!\\\".</P>\r\n\r\n<p>I just think we\\\'re jumping the gun, and I don\\\'t think we want the entire fundamentalist Islamic world on our case.  If we\\\'re going to attack, let\\\'s be absolutely sure.</p>',1,0,0,0,'172.149.121.181','en'),(10398,221,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p><b>October 15, 2001</b>: sometimes people make fun of me for remembering dates diligently, but Im fascinated by seasonal happenings. for instance, I realized when adamajah came to visit during austin\\\'s birthday that it was the <a href=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=40.txt\\\">year anniversary</a> of  swinney.org. hey, someones gotta keep tabs on this stuff.</p>\r\n<p>I am particularly fascinated with this entry because of the section where austin says he wants to send his last girlfriend in NY a plane ticket to visit him. You see, I did that in December of 2000. I sent my last boyfriend in NY a plane ticket to visit me in California. That very week. cmon, it is intriguing, no?</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10399,1921,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','<p>\r\nnumber of comments per post  == dubious measure of superiority a la dick size.\r\n</p><p>\r\ni hate pointing out the obvious here, but the number of comments doesn\\\'t mean squats-diddly.</p>',4,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(10400,1935,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','her spot on market seems to have been replaced by <b>big</b>-white-haired trannie person.  i like her.  she is crazy in all the right ways.',0,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(10401,1942,'2001-10-16 08:32:06',0,'ryan','sight.  that sucks.',0,0,0,0,'209.162.48.227','en'),(10402,1943,'2001-10-16 08:35:22',0,'jay to ryan','I\\\'ve read some history. I am not ignorant of the arguments here. What\\\'s your point? The infidels have stuck there noses where they don\\\'t belong... such is the way of the world. Palestinians have a right to be angry for being forcibly moved from their land. Saudi Arabians have a right to believe their government has invited the protection of infidels and has no religious right to rule. Jews have a right to a homeland. The thousands of people who lost their lives last month had a right to live. What\\\'s your point.',3,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10403,1943,'2001-10-16 08:51:57',0,'ryan','my point is that this country\\\'s gov (the US) is often viewed as an imperialist gov.  forget the religious bullshit.',0,0,0,0,'209.162.48.227','en'),(10404,1943,'2001-10-16 09:31:26',0,'sospirando','<p>\r\n<a href=\\\"http://www.progressive.org/0801issue/nagy0901.html\\\">\r\nand these people didn\\\'t have a right to live?</a> </p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\ndo we have to continue in this stupid cycle or can we struggle for peace? do more innocents have to die over there just \\\'cause some innocents who happen to live here died? is what we\\\'re doing now going to stop anyone from carrying out some more <a href=\\\"http://www.cnn.com/2001/HEALTH/conditions/10/16/anthrax/\\\"> gnarly shit</a>, or just bring on more of it? are you ready for WWIII or should we chill? Pakistan and India are already <a href=\\\"http://www.cnn.com/2001/WORLD/asiapcf/south/10/15/india.pakistan/\\\">getting a little funky</a>, and both have nukes. do you really wanna go there?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nwhere\\\'s the <a href=\\\"http://www.globalresearch.ca/articles/CHO110A.html\\\"><b><i>evidence</i></b></a>, Massa Bush? i\\\'m willing to believe you, the past 9 months of turning yr back on the world and the American citizenry below a certain tax bracket notwithstanding. but some things i\\\'m not willing to take on faith. bin Laden was the guilty party 2 hours after this whole thing happened. how do they know that, prior to any investigation? and if they knew that, <a href=\\\"http://www.copvcia.com/stories/oct_2001/krongard.html\\\"> what else do they know?</a></p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nand why, for a country that proclaims to live by \\\"rule of law\\\", is turning bin Laden over to an international court not even being <b>talked about </b>as an alternative? the Taliban has offerred to do so. twice. justice isn\\\'t good enough, though, is it? definitely no good for Lockheed Martin, Boeing and Raytheon.  <a href=\\\"http://www.tompaine.com/news/2001/10/11/index.html\\\">and what does Big Oil have to say about all this?</a></p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\ni don\\\'t think anyone\\\'s saying \\\"do nothing\\\". <a href=\\\"http://www.thenation.com/doc.mhtml?i=20011029&s=falk\\\">but the broad-stroke military solution isn\\\'t the only solution available here.</a>let\\\'s hope it\\\'s not, for all our sakes.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nPEACE!!!</p>',3,0,0,0,'64.170.190.204','en'),(10405,1943,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','can i get a \\\'yes\\\' for tibet!',6,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(10406,1943,'2001-10-16 09:49:42',0,'tibet','yes!',0,0,0,0,'64.170.190.204','en'),(10407,1943,'2001-10-16 10:01:02',0,'ryan','tibet, leonard peltier, keep tahoe blue, mumia = SUV political action.',0,0,0,0,'209.162.48.227','en'),(10408,1940,'2001-10-16 10:24:28',0,'Terry','I never knew i dreamt of melting rocks; converstaions with dust and air. The day i saw the lizards was a defining moment. That\\\'s where it all began...',1,0,0,0,'217.32.154.67','en'),(10409,1934,'2001-10-16 10:28:13',0,'Terry','I couldn\\\'t find the gibbons or the emus. \\\"They must have gone underground\\\" i thought to myself. Why? I don\\\'t know; but it was the only logical explanation at the time. It wasn\\\'t until my tussle with the lizard king that it all became crystal clear.',1,0,0,0,'217.32.154.67','en'),(10410,1934,'2001-10-16 10:32:22',0,'Jamie','It\\\'s evolutionary. A male human interacts with a female human in order to \\\"Get it on\\\" with said female human. Other than that, the male human has no other reason for interecting with the female human. They talk far too much and get in the way of hunting bears and stuff.',1,0,0,0,'217.32.154.67','en'),(10411,1926,'2001-10-16 10:35:56',0,'Terry','<p>Crack was never my drug of choice. I was far too good for that. Crack is the drug of choice for HIV ridden prostitutes from here to timbuktu. I preferred something a little more upmarket.</p>',4,0,0,0,'217.32.154.67','en'),(10412,1943,'2001-10-16 11:03:16',0,'anonymous for obvious reasons','<p>Sure the jewish people are entitled to a homeland but that doesn\\\'t mean they can just steal one from someone else (the palestinians)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nTo say that american foreign policy hasn\\\'t contributed to the current situation is naive. Of course, no-one is saying it\\\'s entirely america\\\'s fault. that would be an equally misguided statement. But the american government does have a habit or marching into countries and (pardon the phrasing) pissing large numbers of people off.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nFor example. In the 1980s, The US military accidentally shot down an Iranian Passenger jet. Fair enough. it was obviously an accident. A very unfortunate one at that.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nAmerica never apologised.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nIt is understandable why a substantial percentage of the worlds population is \\\"anti-american\\\". Of course this does not condone terrorism. but recent events have highlighted the fact that America is just one of many countries. Sure, it\\\'s a big, flashy country. But it isn\\\'t invulnerable. \r\n</p>',1,0,0,0,'217.32.154.67','en'),(10413,1943,'2001-10-16 11:37:44',0,'devils advocate','what land in the world <i>hasn\\\'t</i> been stolen from someone else? if it exists, its a minority, i think...',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10414,1943,'2001-10-16 11:45:07',0,'Jamie','Antarctica?',1,0,0,0,'217.32.154.67','en'),(10415,1943,'2001-10-16 11:52:55',0,'Jamie','Dudes, i just read that story about the US cutting off Iraq\\\'s water supply....<BR><BR>\r\nSurely this is against the geneva convention. You can\\\'t intentionaly kill civilians. Thats just plain wrong. If this is true; i\\\'m shocked.',1,0,0,0,'217.32.154.67','en'),(10416,1943,'2001-10-16 11:57:33',0,'Taliban','Yes. We hate you Americans. But we asked for evidence of Osama\\\'s guilt on more than one occasion. You were not forthcoming. Would your government extradite someone without a shred of evidence? We offered to hand him over to a international court. twice. you ignored us. Now you are bombing the shit out of us so you can forget it. He\\\'s fucked off into the mountains anyway. We don\\\'t have a fucking clue where he is. That is all.',1,0,0,0,'217.32.154.67','en'),(10417,1939,'2001-10-16 12:03:52',0,'Jamie','<br>\\\"thrusts ass into sky, smiles\\\" <br>is \\\"smiles\\\" two syllables?',1,0,0,0,'217.32.154.67','en'),(10418,1939,'2001-10-16 12:32:51',0,'Mister Grammar','Um, yes... \\\"SMY-uhls\\\". but thanks for playing!',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10419,1939,'2001-10-16 12:36:16',0,'Jamie','i guess it depends on your accent...',1,0,0,0,'217.32.126.239','en'),(10420,1934,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','Ahhh... Jamie, you\\\'ve answered your own concern.  The female needs to spend time interacting with the male in order to determine wether or not he is acceptable evolutionary material.  Males have a lot of sperm to waste.  Females have only a limited number of eggs.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(10421,1943,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','<h1>FREE MUMIA</h1>',2,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(10422,1934,'2001-10-16 13:06:23',0,'Jamie','oh the other hand. I\\\'d happily <i>interact</i> with Netfong. She\\\'s one hot human female!',1,0,0,0,'217.32.126.239','en'),(10423,1943,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p><img src=\"http://www.saturn5.com/steve/images/nice.jpg\"></p>',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(10424,1934,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>this here is the truth</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10425,1940,'2004-07-27 05:00:32',578,'NetfÃ¶ng!','\\\"terry\\\", im reading ur story. i like it.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10426,1934,'2004-07-27 05:00:32',578,'NetfÃ¶ng! to jo','yes! generalisations suck!',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10427,1934,'2004-07-27 05:00:32',578,'NetfÃ¶ng! to peter','boh!',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10428,1943,'2001-10-16 14:09:37',0,'stella','If anyone has any doubt about America\\\'s foreign policy, please read a cute little book by Noam Chomsky titled \\\"What Uncle Sam really wants\\\". It\\\'s really *quite* interesting. ',0,0,0,0,'168.73.245.56','en'),(10429,1943,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>free mumia... ahh, for the heady days when all nyc was was a huge artsy drug den, an unyielding giuliani-hating, mumia-freeing march with easy-to-jump-turnstiles and 5$ club covers. now, we\\\'re all waving our american flags, having babies, voting republican, drinking microbrews and going on studio tours at p.s. 1.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10430,1943,'2001-10-16 14:16:55',0,'bubba to stella','If anyone has any doubt about America\\\'s foreign policy, they should tactfully shove it up their ass or go discuss it on some politically-oriented bbs. isnt there some rule making taboo topics of politics and religion in your average public forum? im growing so weary of all this debate. debate on tv, debate at home, debate in the car, debate on swinney. ',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10431,1943,'2001-10-16 14:27:24',0,'stella to bubba','Oh, poor little one... can\\\'t handle big people topics. Perhaps you should find yourself a nice little hole in the ground and go hide in it if you can\\\'t deal. \r\n',0,0,0,0,'168.73.245.56','en'),(10432,1943,'2001-10-16 14:31:24',0,'bubba to stella','i was just making a point, not necessarily against you. your reply seemed a bit gruff. sorry if i pissed you off. <i>however</i> please regard the difference between <i>being able to deal</i> and <i>being tired of dealing</i>. i think that is the duality in play here. oh, i can deal quite well, thanks, im just sick of doing so and sick of the unending, droll politika.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10433,1943,'2001-10-16 14:39:50',0,'stella','<p>it seemed to me that you were suggesting that I shove it up my ass. if you were not, apology accepted perhaps next time if you\\\'re making a general statement, you shouldn\\\'t direct the comment to one person in particular. </p>\r\n<p>yes, the topic is old. yes, there are more than likely a LOT of political bbs out there that are red hot with politcal debate. no, swinney isn\\\'t a forum dedicated to this kind of subject matter. swinney, as far as I know, isn\\\'t dedicated to anything but writing. that\\\'s one big reason why I like swinney. anything goes. ',0,0,0,0,'168.73.245.56','en'),(10434,1943,'2002-04-20 20:49:51',273,'Quinn','<p>It is just as easy to wave a flag of peace as it is to wave an American flag.  This isn\\\'t anything like The Gulf War, or Vietnam...it doesn\\\'t fit under any banners or solutions or easy political labels.  What are we saying when we say that we shouldn\\\'t attack Afganistan?  A regime that pulls out a woman\\\'s fingernails if she wears nail polish, that blows up the religious history of a country, that labels and kills individuals based on their personal faith (sound familiar?).  \r\n\r\n<p><i>Ah, me...war is wrong.  Yes.  War is wrong.  War is wrong.  And war is wrong.  Give peace a chance and Give peace a chance, a chance is what peace deserves.  Put a daisy in a rifle barrel and give peace a fucking chance.</i>\r\n\r\n<p>War has killed Afgani civilians already.  This is true.  This is a ethical delimna: the sacrifice of the few for the many.  If we do things right in Afganistan and back up our present military action with assistance to the Northern Alliance after the Taliban falls (and it will fall), Afganistan will see a better future.  If Afganistan sees a better future it will no longer be a place for terrorists to hide.  \r\n\r\n<p>These things won\\\'t manifest in a year, or even five years.  A decade of healing may have to be done before we see the benefits of the present conflict and this is only if the United States is responsible and sticks around after we \\\"get Bin Laden.\\\"\r\n\r\n<p>I mean, we have no choice but to get the terrorists don\\\'t we?  There has to be a way to bring an end to global terrorism.  We can\\\'t tollerate another Sept. 11, can we?   We can\\\'t just sit back and wait for it to happen.\r\n\r\n<p><i>Sing lalala and war is wrong.  Sing and pound the drum.  Sing lalala and war is wrong.   War is awful dumb.</i>\r\n\r\n<p>I hate war and love peace.  Of course I do, don\\\'t we all?  A friend of mine called Bush \\\"war-mongering.\\\"  That is a very igorant thing to say.  Nobody wants war.\r\n\r\n<p>Bush is stoopid Bush is dum....but what would you have done?\r\n\r\n<p>Hey...we\\\'ve got a crisis here of epic proportions.  Bigger than epic...UNIVERSAL PROPORTIONS.  I am so confused by it all I don\\\'t know how to feel.  I used to protest wars...and now I watch CNN.\r\n\r\nHope for the flowers.\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(10435,1943,'2001-10-16 15:07:34',0,'bubba','Terrorism has killed American civilians already. This is true. This is a ethical delimna: the sacrifice of the few for the many. If we do things right in America and back up our present military action with assistance to the Northern Alliance after the Taliban falls (and it will fall), Afganistan will see a better future. If Afganistan sees a better future it will no longer be a place for terrorists to hide. \r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10436,1943,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to s5','<a href=\\\"http://www.faqs.org/faqs/usenet/legends/godwin/\\\">shadok showed me this</a> more accurate explanation of godwin\\\'s law. In order to actually end the thread, you have to have equated the person with whom you are arguing to a Nazi, not just invoke the name \\\"hitler\\\".',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10437,1942,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','$0.02:<p>New Yorkers, for the most part, aren\\\'t hesitant about voicing their annoyance, very loudly, when annoyed.  If I were to engage in any of the \\\"savage\\\" behaviour detailed above in Central Park, I would immediately be yelled/bitched at, and if I were to choose to persist, I\\\'d probably get the shit beat out of me.  Punishment can be a very effective deterent.</p><p>Btw, once you get out of mid-/downtown Manhattan, the streets are covered in garbage.  NYC is my trashcan.</p>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(10438,1942,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>this much is true. once, i was walking with a friend past the bowling green in Central Park, and she was having a smoke. one of the all-white-clad lawn bowlers actually yelled at her and said <i>\"dont smoke so close to the green, missy!\"</i> even though we were a solid 10 feet away.<br><br>and there <i>is</i> alot of garbage around. i love how anti-litter people have such a double-standard, throwing their ciggarette butts on the sidewalk while yelling at someone for littering. by biggest gripe is the dog poop thats freakin <i>everywhere</i>. they need to ban dogs from nyc. dogs and cars. yeah! who needs either here? get a cat and a bike, or get a date and ride the train, yo.</tt>\r\n\r\n \r\n',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10439,1942,'2001-10-16 16:47:30',0,'wondering','...it is one thing to vent about pet peeves and release some misguided frustrations, but it is really another thing altogether to start categorizing and classifying as \\\'savages and civilians\\\' or \\\'us and them\\\' or...well hopefully you get the picture. Is segregation the answer? \r\n\r\n<p><i>star bellied sneech</i></p>',1,0,0,0,'32.102.109.121','en'),(10440,1944,'2001-10-16 16:49:36',0,'kat','awwww...and here i thought you hated that job. *sniffle* *sniffle* *sob* *sigh*',1,0,0,0,'32.102.109.121','en'),(10441,1943,'2002-04-20 20:49:51',273,'Quinn','I don\\\'t get it bubba.  Why the one word change?',0,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(10442,1943,'2001-10-16 17:32:05',0,'bubba','two word change. trying to make a point',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10443,1942,'2001-10-16 17:33:38',0,'wb','Smokers are a whole other subject Peter. Yes butts on the ground is most certainly litter. Beyond that the TV ads say 50,000 people die a year of second hand smoke. Even if half that is true, it\\\'s an outrage. Think that we are going to war over 5,000 people dead. When we have an industry which enables 10 times that number to be killed innocently. Certainly anyone who puts other people in harm because of their petty addiction is a savage. <BR><BR>In terms of civilian vs. savages. The word civilian simply means citizen. The word savage means not civilized. It also means crude, etc. I never mentioned segregating anyone. I never mentioned laws or rules. But indeed, based on your behavior in a city, how you treat other people, not only the people you know, but sometimes more importantly strangers, determines how civilized you are.',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(10444,1943,'2001-10-16 17:43:06',0,'tibet','<p>\r\nactually... i\\\'ve changed my mind. leave me out of this one. i\\\'ve got enough going on here to worry about as it is.</p>',0,0,0,0,'64.170.190.204','en'),(10445,1943,'2002-04-20 20:49:51',273,'Quinn','<p>Bubba,\r\n\r\n<p>Okay, I see the other word change, but I still don\\\'t get it.  Can you use your own words and define it for me?   \r\n\r\n<p>It seems that you are trying to flip-flop the argument, to make me see it as if Afganistan was initiating some kind of action.  But that doesn\\\'t bear out in actuality, so I just don\\\'t get it.  \r\n\r\n<p>Help?',0,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(10446,1943,'2001-10-16 17:54:04',0,'bubba','no more help. im just a simpleton whos merely churning the waters to see how pretty the stirred up silt and muck looks when it glimmers on the water\\\'s surface. ',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10447,1941,'2002-04-20 20:49:51',273,'Quinn','a big Pablo Neruda fan are we?  ',0,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(10448,1944,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>I have a sassy co worker that shouts <i>\"Work it, Boy!\"</i> every time she passes me sitting here at my workomputer. it makes me feel good. Yo, Austin: <i><b>\"Work it, Boy!\"</i></b></tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10449,1943,'2002-04-20 20:49:51',273,'Quinn','Then just fergit it, Bubba-licous.  I don\\\'t really care.',0,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(10450,1943,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','<p>wow.  i just read that whole goddamned thread - probably the longest thread i have actually endured.  i have to say that i am not disgusted, but actually impressed with how much you all are thinking about this, and with how thought out <i>some</i> of your opinions are.  whether you are right or wrong, kudos to all you guys who are using your mind today.  :)</p>\r\n<p><b>swin.org people are cool people</b></p>  ',1,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(10451,1945,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','karma yoga',1,0,0,0,'64.132.148.219','en'),(10452,1946,'2001-10-16 18:53:00',0,'wb','<b>RE:</b>not voting. Democracy is a gift. Voting is a gift. People who say they don\'t vote as some sort of statement generally think they are above going through the pesky task of thinking about who to vote for. And they are above having to regret who they voted for. They are above the idea of voting for somebody who doesn\'t believe in everything they believe in. They are elitist.\r\n\r\n<BR><BR>\r\n\r\n<b>RE:</b> making an artist\'s statement every week. This sounds like a stupid piece of advice. Couldn\'t that time be spent developing one\'s art? Isn\'t the job of an artist to focus that voice or vision so that it doesn\'t need a \"statement\" to explain it, so that it\'s realized to the point of making sense (or not) and above all connecting with people. <BR><BR>\r\nI don\'t know much about art and the art world. I\'m more on the books side of the creative world. What I see there are these \"great white male\" authors writing diatribes and editorial pieces about what kind of novel society needs. In literary magazines that are not read by many general readers they try to figure out the next big thing for \"real novels\" (as opposed to the novels that they have decided don\'t count because they aren\'t \"art\"). I\'ve read some artist statements, we get two of the art magazines here at home and it can often be the same thing. <BR><BR>It seems that the art that I connect with, the books that I connect with come from a place that is different than this kind of thinking and planning. These statements, these manifestos are the moment of pause where the writer or artist tries to calculate what the audience wants, what would be seen as clever and smart. Let\'s try to come up with something that\'s \"new.\" What would make him or her popular, the next Jackson Pollack, the next David Foster Wallace. It\'s the calculation of a breakthrough, the prediction of a breakthrough, rather than the senseless hard work and time engrossed in the craft that naturally leads to one.  <BR><BR> What this \"statementing\" seems to want to avoid is the scary reality that you can be an artist or a novelist and bust your ass for 20 years and never make or write something that people want to spend their time with, let alone pay for. The literary manifesto attempts to remove this risk. Not only are you spending time figuring out what is new, what is next, what is neccesary, you are making sure you are in the \"new pack\" of writers executing this next wave.<BR><BR>\r\nI have this feeling that the reason why the mainstream doesn\'t care about artistic novels (and certain visual artists) is not because they are dumb or uneducated, but because they don\'t have time for art that comes out of a really good statement. They don\'t care if it looks good on paper. They don\'t care if a novel is a clever idea. They want to connect. <BR><BR> <b>RE:</b> not making art after 9/11. This is also stupid. Art is important in this world. Art comforts people. Art makes people think. Art makes people consider other options. Art makes the world a better place. <BR><BR>Current events\r\nknock you down and donâ€™t care if you get back up. Art is different; art knocks you down, but helps you get back up. ',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(10453,1946,'2001-10-16 19:01:11',0,'lou to wb','YES.',1,0,0,0,'207.237.128.1','en'),(10454,1946,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>maybe to have saved you some rampage time, wayne, i should add that the advice about practicing an art statement had to do with the fact that Im applying to graduate school, and I have to ahve a good one to get in, because of competition they need some weeding-out process. like subscribing to Word of the Day to prepare for the gre. nothing more, nothing less.</p>\r\n<p>but that fact does discourage me from wanting to go back to school. I like the idea of practice, of regularly exercising your ability to create and think, and I think in some ways when you lose the banality of your work routine you risk becoming \\\"soft\\\". more often than not when i walk through art these days I become aware of the patterns and genres that repeat themselves, and how words prop them up as having context and significance. I am deadly bored of that practice. </p>',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10455,1946,'2001-10-16 19:09:52',0,'wb','well the quote you put up there re: statements, that was in reference to \\\"in order to get into grad school\\\"?\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(10456,1946,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','also, a good statement is more like a brief journal entry than it is a manifesto about the world to come. it is like a good title. it emphasizes the intention of the work without trying to \\\"invent meaning\\\" by itself. it is a practice, like doing steps at the barre as a ballerina. you dont show the audience your exercises, but it all contributes to how you perform on stage. some visual artists are purely visual and care only about images or forms, and perhaps writing would do nothing for them. But my verbal voice enters into my physical process and is not consistently seperate from it. ',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10457,1946,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to wb','yeah, that was my teacher\\\'s advice about how to write a good statement as part of the application. i could have been more clear about that but i didnt think it was important to this entry, which was more generally/poetically about \\\"getting soft\\\" than whether or not people should write \\\"artist\\\'s statements\\\". ',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10458,1946,'2001-10-16 19:16:17',0,'wb','right. for some reason the scene from the courtney love documentary just came to mind; where the ex boyfriend shows lists that she wrote about how to become famous (\\\"befriend michael stipe\\\"). <BR><BR>when\\\'s jay going to join the fray on this one?',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(10459,1946,'2001-10-16 19:18:03',0,'wb to egg','Well I think despite my \\\"rampaging\\\" I was talking about getting soft. Giving into the thinking that \\\"art doesn\\\'t make the world a better place\\\" \\\"art is only as good as the statement\\\" and just that mindset of statementing is what i think of when I think of artists getting soft. ',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(10460,1946,'2001-10-16 19:19:51',0,'','\\\"Smitty\\\" Jennifer Jason leighs wise cracking pal at the news desk was played by Bruce Campbell,not Sam Raimi ,although they are old friends.',0,0,0,0,'206.224.71.189','en'),(10461,1946,'2001-10-16 19:19:58',0,'Mike','\\\"Smitty\\\" Jennifer Jason leighs wise cracking pal at the news desk was played by Bruce Campbell,not Sam Raimi ,although they are old friends.',0,0,0,0,'206.224.71.189','en'),(10462,1942,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','are jay and wb falling in love?',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10463,1942,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to jay','i disagree that there is a \\\"lack of any real history\\\" in california. they just didnt teach you that in prep school because new england/ new york is the most egocentric \\\"culture\\\" in this world! theyll have you believe history was <i>invented</i> in the banks of the Hudson! that the Met was erected before the Coliseum!',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10464,1942,'2001-10-16 19:35:04',0,'ps','i laugh out loud when i read any portion of this. also, I do like to watch dogs fuck in the park. but thats just me.',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10465,1946,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt><i>[artistic droooool]</i> both my right and left brains are madly in love with barbara kruger.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.121.20','en'),(10466,1946,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to mike and wb','oh, Im sooo embarassed! I think of bruce as sam\\\'s alter-ego, and I think sam co-wrote \\\"hudsucker\\\". ps, wayne: jay is still in bed. ',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10467,1945,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>this is beautiful. i have a friend who, as part of his rather orthodox spiritual dictums, cherishes the written word. once, i stood on a stack of textbooks to reach something, and he, tactfully and sublimely stooped to offer a word and gesture of pennance to the books (and their encapsulated writing/efforts/wisdom) for my dishonouring them with the sole of my foot. he says, admittedly sheepish in today\'s age, that if one disgraces a book with their feet, they thus disgrace the author of the books. <br><br>His words were, <i>\"if the Creator embodied you as a book, you would understand\"</i>. How interesting you read your prose regarding that very topic.<br><br>Maybe this is different than your and my beliefs, but i think its a rather profound spin on such things. books. beautiful and respected, <i>especially if you are one</i>.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.121.20','en'),(10468,1946,'2001-10-16 20:22:03',0,'trouble','\\\'uber-tard\\\', damn that\\\'s good.<br>*best friendly*',1,0,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(10469,1943,'2001-10-16 20:34:28',0,'trouble','a view from the sidelines reveals the following observation:<br><br>suddenly everybody is Andy Rooney?  knee-jerk patriotism combined with sudden scrutiny of our media makes for an lesson in repetition... you have all heard it before.<br>*nice supportive*',2,0,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(10470,1943,'2001-10-16 20:38:50',0,'God','<b>time for a new topic, people!</b>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.121.20','en'),(10471,1946,'2001-10-16 20:45:46',0,'wb','Clearly Jay must be an artist thinking about his statements to still be in bed after noon.',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(10472,1947,'2001-10-16 20:50:10',0,'tolstoy','nothing rekindles memory like a smell',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10473,107,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','you bitch! im going to go get a coke right now. have you ever considered doing commercials? uh, excuse me miss, are you a MODEL? well uh, heh i only ask cuz yr so PRETTY...',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10474,1946,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','<BR><BR>\\\"musicians are the angels of the earth.\\\" - sun ra<BR><BR>this holds true for artists as well as mothers, brickmasons, children, those who pump out shit-houses, soldiers, kings, criminals, animals, everybody.<BR><BR>it takes a lot to create something, chiefly overcoming your own fears. my hat\\\'s off to anybody who tries.',1,0,0,0,'64.132.148.219','en'),(10475,1947,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','tolstoy. wowie-zowie. i was purusing the encyclopedia the other day, and came across ol\\\' leo. he was something. a writer, a teacher, an ascetic, a martyr. i\\\'ve never read anything he wrote. i\\\'m beginning to think i received a half-assed education at ye olde hernando high school. where it smelled like rednecks and pine-sol.',1,0,0,0,'64.132.148.219','en')