to hell! mercury retrograde can eat it.',6,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(10481,1948,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p>aren\\\'t they cyoot?!</p><p>\r\n<img src=\\\"http://www1.umn.edu/bellmuse/mnideals/prairie/fieldguide/images/vole.jpg\\\"></p>',6,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(10482,107,'2001-10-17 11:07:18',0,'jim','Life tastes good.',6,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(10483,1946,'2001-10-17 13:15:03',0,'jo','really? the six-year-old in me is in love with bruce campbell. he\\\'s dreamy.',0,0,0,0,'172.144.119.42','en'),(10484,1532,'2001-10-17 13:23:22',0,'Addendum','<a href=\\\"http://www.flight404.com/\\\">www.flight404.com<a/>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10485,1946,'2001-10-17 14:23:23',0,'jo','i\\\'ve had <a href=\\\"http://www.mmmbed.com/sullengirl/thousandwords/pictures/abortionpc.jpg\\\">one of kruger\\\'s images</a> as a postcard for a few years and at one point scanned it and had it up on my site. an aquaintance photoshopped it to say \\\"playground\\\" instead of \\\"battleground,\\\" which i thought was interesting because it seemed like something kruger would have done.',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(10486,1948,'2001-10-17 14:24:06',0,'ty','andioulle = \\\"ann-dewey\\\"',0,0,0,0,'63.10.151.154','en'),(10487,1948,'2001-10-17 14:32:01',0,'jo','i really like dividing up music by how dangerous it is, i think that\\\'s a <B>FINE</B> division. my friend austin, when trying to categorize my eclectic music tastes once, said that i like music that <i>slaps you around and then smiles at you afterward</i>, and i thought that was pretty great but i think now i will tell people that i like <i>dangerous</i> music, as that is far more apt. props to you.',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(10488,1950,'2001-10-17 14:34:08',0,'jo','seriously, come visit austin. hang out. maybe this next week when elly is here. we have much to discuss.',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(10489,1949,'2001-10-17 14:53:14',0,'wb','This quote from Don Delillo seems related:<BR><BR>\r\nThe novel is the dream release, the suspension of reality that history needs to escape its own brutal confinements. \r\n<BR><BR>\r\nFiction is true to a thousand things but rarely to clinical lived experience. Ultimately it obeys the mysterious mandates of the self (the writer\\\'s) and of all the people and things that have surrounded him all his life and all the styles he has tried out and all the fiction (of other writers) he has read and not read. At its root level, fiction is a kind of religious fanaticism, with elements of obsession, superstition and awe. \r\n\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(10490,1946,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i like the one that goes <i>\\\"when i here the word culture, i take out my checkbook\\\"</i></tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10491,1950,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>a bored soul likes to travel. when?</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10492,1950,'2001-10-17 15:17:22',0,'ghost','<i>\\\'you dont know what love is...until you\\\'ve loved the love you had to lose\\\'</i>',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.161','en'),(10493,1951,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>thats because bigfooters are magic</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10494,1722,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>inspired by this piece, i have code-named the gigantic rats that live on my stoop and in my apartment\\\'s outdoor trash-bins \\\'fattycakes\\\' in order that i might discuss them with my flatmates without arousing the suspicion of innocent bystanders. i dont want people thinking i live in a dump, you know.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10495,1950,'2001-10-17 16:30:43',0,'lou','how come everyone is going to austin after i\\\'ve already left? i think this is a plot.',4,0,0,0,'207.237.128.1','en'),(10496,1948,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','*tucks the little vole in her shirt*',0,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(10497,1950,'2001-10-17 17:05:15',0,'jo to peter','i don\\\'t know, take advantage of the fares. you can fly austin -> nyc roundtrip for $200 now, i\\\'m sure it\\\'s the same going to the other way. consult <a href=\\\"http://calendar.yahoo.com/joannavaught\\\">the calendar</a> for reference if necessary.',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(10498,1950,'2001-10-17 17:07:34',0,'jo to lou','this obviously means that you should have stayed, duh.',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(10499,1950,'2001-10-17 17:32:33',0,'trouble to jo','with calender for all to see i would like to offer a change regarding the appearence of the White Stripes.. it has been said that they have been or will be rescheduled for the 29th.<br><br>my apologies to you peter for using your excellent post to pass on this information.  but you know where i live now and you know i have so very little to be excited about these days.',1,0,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(10500,1950,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to jo','<br><tt>i see 178$. this is good. i\'ll be in touch. ooh, white stripes! white stripes!</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10501,1950,'2001-10-17 17:35:22',0,'lou to jo','um. yeah. duh, actually.  i think there are only three places in the world that i want to be right now--but i guess what is really going on is that i want to be with a bunch of Very Specific People, and they are all in different places.  what i know: i do not want to be here, at work.',4,0,0,0,'207.237.128.1','en'),(10502,1950,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>three places i\'d rather be now, than at work:<br><br>\r\n1. in <a href=\"http://www.centralpark.org\">central park</a><br>\r\n2. on <a href=\"http://www.jekyllisland.com\">jekyll island</a><br>\r\n3. at <a href=\"http://www.satelliterecords.com\">satellite records</a><br></tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10503,1950,'2001-10-17 18:05:48',0,'lou','1. st louis<BR>\r\n2. austin<BR>\r\n3. home, in bed, drinking cocoa, watching TBC.',1,0,0,0,'207.237.128.1','en'),(10504,1950,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<ol><li>On my girlfriend\\\'s couch smoking a ciggie and petting her cat.<li>Hanging out in Deborah\\\'s apartment watching <u><i>Strictly Ballroom</i></u><li>Lying in bed curled up with Erin.</ol>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(10505,1950,'2001-10-17 18:29:36',0,'trouble','<b>1.</b> lafyette coney island in detroit, watching the steam rise from the streets<br>\r\n<b>2.</b> sitting along the navy pier in chicago with a cup of coffee looking back at the skyline<br>\r\n<b>3.</b> row 50 of the detroit institute of arts theater watching an animation festival with favorite jeans and shirt',1,0,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(10506,1946,'2001-10-17 19:24:15',0,'jo','\\\"everything that\\\'s interesting costs a little bit of money.\\\"<BR>\r\n(not kruger. ethan hawke\\\'s character in <i>before sunrise</i> but hey it\\\'s a nice point.)',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(10507,1950,'2001-10-17 19:27:46',0,'jo','this is interesting seeing as how a few days ago, lou was in my apartment in austin and we were watching <i>strictly ballroom</i>.',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(10508,1946,'2001-10-17 19:54:17',0,'lou to jo','you and me and five bucks.',4,0,0,0,'207.237.128.1','en'),(10509,1950,'2001-10-17 20:32:06',0,'Ya Ya','\\\"you must not be so afraid\\\"',2,0,0,0,'156.153.255.236','en'),(10510,1945,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','\r\nwho wrote this poem?',0,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(10511,1950,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<br>\\\"A life lived in fear is a life half lived.\\\"<p>Deborah has <b>never</b> seen <i>Strictly Ballromm</i>.  That\\\'s so fucked up.  Especially since she\\\'s a dancer.</p>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(10512,1949,'2001-10-17 20:51:41',0,'jay','That\\\'s perfect. What book is that from?',1,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10513,1945,'2002-04-20 20:49:51',273,'Quinn','(c)2001 Quinn Skylark',0,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(10514,1950,'2001-10-17 21:48:50',0,'lou','i think that everyone should have to see Strictly Ballroom.  especially anyone who appreciates (a) music, (b) costuming, (c) dancing, (d) paul mercurio.  also required watching?  The Girl in the Watermelon.  (and Spy Kids.)',1,0,0,0,'207.237.128.1','en'),(10515,1951,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i like to clutch a yeti and suck my thumb',4,0,0,0,'207.105.89.225','en'),(10516,1953,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','<FONT SIZE=8><TT>\\\\M/</TT></FONT>',0,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(10517,1953,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','dude, anthrax',6,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(10518,1953,'2001-10-17 23:52:30',0,'leonard','turn off your television.',6,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(10519,1953,'2001-10-18 00:14:33',0,'t.v.','<PRE>\r\n*>click<*\r\ndeath\r\ndeath\r\nanthrax\r\n*>click<*\r\nsilence.\r\n*>click<*\r\ndeath\r\ndeath\r\nanthrax\r\ndeath\r\nsaundra leavy\r\n*>click<*\r\nsilence.\r\n*>click<*\r\nDEATH\r\noverspending\r\nDEATH\r\ncut into social security\r\n*>click<*\r\nbombing\r\ndeath\r\nbombing\r\nDEATH\r\n404\r\n*>click<*\r\ndeath\r\ndeath\r\nanthrax!\r\nanthrax?\r\nANTHRAX!\r\n*>click<*\r\n</PRE>',3,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(10520,1953,'2001-10-18 00:31:01',0,'anthrax','<p>\r\n<a href=\\\"http://www.anthrax.com/nfws.htm\\\">we have nothing to do with any of this, we swear!</a>\r\n</p>',0,0,0,0,'64.170.190.204','en'),(10521,1946,'2001-10-18 00:39:27',0,'sospirando','barbaras ehrenriech AND kruger rule O.K.!',0,0,0,0,'64.170.190.204','en'),(10522,1953,'2001-10-18 01:47:36',0,'trouble','quinn my man, a long time ago you gave me some advice.  at the time i will admit it caused me some minor irritation because i was a practicing, disciplined and even an outspoken believer in it and i didn\\\'t feel the need for your advice, but in retrospect i can say with all honesty i appreciated it just the same and i even worked a little harder at it.  please now allow me now to return the favor using your own text:<br>\r\n\\\'- learn how to meditate\\\'<br>\r\n\\\'- learn how to meditate\\\'<br>\r\n\\\'- learn how to meditate\\\'<br>and then you followed it up with:<br>\\\'meditation teaches you how to live-in-the-world. it does not solve problems. it calms one down and makes worldly problems diminish in importance.\\\'<br>in closing let me add the most important part of this comment. <b>* nice supportive *</b>',2,0,0,0,'24.181.44.135','en'),(10523,1953,'2001-10-18 01:51:13',0,'lulu','hey quinn...<br>\r\n<p>BWAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHA!</p>',0,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(10524,1953,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','<pre>\r\n*>click<*\r\nyou\\\'re watching the Daily Show on Comedy...\r\n*>click<*\r\nnext...on HBO...he started out as a small-time...\r\n*>click<*\r\n...now, we\\\'re going to add a little garlic...a little more garlic...a little MORE garlic...\r\n*>click<*\r\n\r\nI luv TV\r\n</pre>\r\n',1,0,0,0,'65.140.49.65','en'),(10525,1950,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<ol><li>in a capoeira roda</li>\r\n<li>biking in the woods</li>\r\n<li>djing a party</li>\r\n</ol>',2,0,0,0,'24.221.170.233','en'),(10526,1950,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','peter are you coming to austin? !!! ??? i will feed you TURBODOG if you do.',4,0,0,0,'66.123.206.37','en'),(10527,1950,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i am <i>trying</i> to. the evil airline fates are being cruel, however!</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10528,1950,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','long live turbodog.',2,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(10529,1950,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','so i was playing the white stripes and sawks came in and asked \\\"who\\\'s this?\\\" and i said \\\"it\\\'s the white stripes\\\" and he said \\\"oh, thought so.  they toured with the rock and roll machine [nz band, friends of sawks - ed] a while back.  yeah, i hung out with them.  man that meg white sure can drink!  she slams them back and then plays worse than on the album!\\\".<br>\r\n<br>\r\ni think it\\\'s pretty cool that sawks hung out with the white stripes.',2,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(10530,1950,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>the premier reason why i like the stripes (besides the fact that their music is <i>good</i>) is: 1. jack white\'s singing voice 2. the drum banging 3. the guitar banging ... if it takes getting schnookered for them to make those sounds, then drink, drink!</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10531,1953,'2002-04-20 20:49:51',273,'Quinn','<p>I work for a media company....soaked in knowledge I am...web sites, newspapers, television, radio programming, magazines...these things compose my day...too much knowledge can get to you...but it\\\'s my freakin\\\' job...what can I do?\r\n\r\n<p>n\\\'thanks mr. trouble.  i appreciate yr words.  i will try to meditate instead of drinking myself senseless like I\\\'ve been doing of late.\r\n\r\n<p>and to lulu, your schtick is rather tiresome.  didn\\\'t you hear?  irony is dead.  or is that ironing?  i\\\'m not sure.  ',0,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(10532,1950,'2001-10-18 13:56:17',0,'jo','i\\\'d like to make a toast to jack white\\\'s EYES while singing, particularly his cover of \\\"jolene.\\\" JESUS LORD!',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(10533,1945,'2001-10-18 13:57:35',0,'jo','hi, i too would like to throw in my belated comment that this is beautiful work.',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(10534,1950,'2001-10-18 13:58:51',0,'jo to els','elly, peter IS coming, and it\\\'s going to overlap with a day of your visit! so there will be much turbodog consumption indeed, my friends. long fucking live turbodog!',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(10535,1950,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i\\\'ve played the white stripes on several road trips now; and everytime he sings \\\"... to the valley below\\\", i just *happen* to be driving into a valley, i just *happen* to have another cup of coffee (for the road) from the last truckstop. i love when music does things like that. it\\\'s like they knew.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(10536,1950,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to s5','<br><tt>i love that sort of uncanny, cosmic timing. my favourite instance was when i was listening to a song who\\\'s refrain included <i>\\\"and all the whores on bleeker street they wear their blissful grins, caused by the drugs they take to relieve them of their sins\\\"</i>. suddenly, i realized that not only was i on bleeker street, but i was pretending not to notice the aggressive hookers while focusing on the random young man who was writhing in the gutter outside the waverly in some withdrawl fit.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10537,1950,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to jo and elly','<br><tt>er, do i <i>want</i> to know what a turbodog is?!</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10538,1950,'2001-10-18 15:14:59',0,'jo to peter','it\\\'s a louisiana beer that they serve at my favorite bar, showdown, for $7/pitcher. it\\\'s so fucking good.',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(10539,1950,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','don\\\'t believe them. \\\"having a turbodog\\\" is really one of those things like \\\"bagpiping\\\" or \\\"teabagging\\\".',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(10540,1950,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>nice. my entire family hails from louisiana, actually, but way back.</tt> ',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10541,1954,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>if its any consolation, i had an interesting conversation this past weekend that went something like:<br><br>\r\n<i>her grandmother:</i> \"why aren\'t you kids married with a kid yet?!\"<br><br>\r\n<i>me:</i> \"well, considering that we haven\'t even been together for going on several months now, thats not very likely\"<br><br>\r\n<i>her grandmother:</i> \"so when <i><b>are</b></i> you kids gonna get married and have a kid?!\"<br><br><i>sigh...</i></tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10542,1954,'2001-10-18 15:33:49',0,'stella','<p>ugh.</p>\r\n<p> A co-worker reminds me that my biological clock is ticking and that \\\"I\\\'d better get on it\\\"... as if I signed some kind of agreement with mankind to procreate. </P>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'168.73.245.56','en'),(10543,1954,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter, needlessly digressing','<br><tt>not that its my place to say, but i\'m gonna say it anyway... i hate how society has a way of making public domain out of certain things that are quite private. when a good friend of mine was pregnant, she was pushed to the verge of freaking out by all the strangers who maniacally rushed towards her in stores, on the train, on the street, grinning, reaching out, wanting to pat/touch/feel/rub/look-at her stomach, asking all sorts of personal questions about it... and this in nyc, where people <i>never</i> approach you unless they\'re insane or homeless. yikes. i cant blame anyone for <i>not</i> wanting to have a kid.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10544,1950,'2001-10-18 15:56:56',0,'stella','<P>\r\nAbita is yummy too!</P>\r\n<P>\r\nI\\\'m going back to New Orleans in three weeks...! I am going to eat crawfish and oysters with my oyster-shucker friend, Samuel. I am going to listen to whatever local music I can find. I am going to be sexually agressive with Rick until he can\\\'t take it anymore. And I\\\'ll come home happy.</P> ',0,0,0,0,'168.73.245.56','en'),(10545,1950,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i want a beignet from cafe du monde</tt>   \r\n',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10546,1950,'2001-10-18 16:06:22',0,'stella','<P>Mmmm. </P>\r\n<p> chickory coffee. </P>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'168.73.245.56','en'),(10547,1950,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to new orleans','<br><tt>you tease me! i want a muffaletta from the deli on decatur street. i want chicory coffee. i want jax beer. i want pecan pralines. i want an oyster po\\\'boy from holmes cafeteria. i want strange euro smokes from the monteleon. i want all these things while riding the st. charles streetcar.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10548,1950,'2001-10-18 16:27:14',0,'trouble','minor observations of the white stripes outside of their celebrity skin.<br>meg and jack used to frequent this bar just outside of detroit (i saw them a few times there... i\\\'m in no way stating i <b>know them</b>), meg did indeed like to drink and seemed often annoyed when guys tried to hit on her only <i>after</i> they find out she can play drums.  jack seemed the quiet sort who was always writing and stealing the orange rings and cherry\\\'s from the foo-foo tray at the bar.  he was always talking to the bartender and this drunk who used to hang out around the corner.  after seeing quite a few of their concerts and seeing them at other local detroit bands concerts just hangning out i can say without a doubt that they are one of the most fan friendly musical units i have encountered and they will play <i>anywhere, at anytime, for just about anything</i>.  i am so happy so many of you dig this band.',1,0,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(10549,1953,'2001-10-18 17:45:42',0,'we\\\'re with you, quinn...','<p>\r\n<img src=\\\"http://www.mnftiu.cc/mnftiu.cc/images/war.015.gif\\\">\r\n</P>',1,0,0,0,'64.170.190.204','en'),(10550,1953,'2001-10-18 17:51:43',0,'lulu','oh quinn....<br>\r\n<p>BWAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHA!...<br>\r\n*sigh*</P>',0,0,0,0,'64.14.248.62','en'),(10551,1950,'2001-10-18 18:02:22',0,'jo','i got to tell meg that her tank top was on inside-out. she ran her finger along the seam, turned to me and said in conspiratorial-girl style, \\\"THANK you.\\\" and beelined to the bathroom.',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(10552,1954,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','',0,0,0,0,'64.132.148.219','en'),(10553,1954,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','about the age thing: do like i do, when people ask how old you are - tell them you don\\\'t know, you\\\'ve stopped counting. this gives them pause.',1,0,0,0,'64.132.148.219','en'),(10554,1950,'2001-10-18 18:08:43',0,'jo','okay also! i have a <b>serious</b> ongoing <a href=\\\"http://www.mmmbed.com/makemesleepy/2/\\\">love affair with new orleans</a>. if anyone is considering roadtripping there, i think what they should do instead is fly into austin and a bunch of us should go together.',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(10555,1955,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','it\\\'s times like these that i\\\'m glad i\\\'m not around too many people that much. humanity, as a whole, i love. one on one, they get a little tricky on you.',1,0,0,0,'64.132.148.219','en'),(10556,1950,'2001-10-18 18:24:31',0,'stella','<p>two words. jazz fest.</p>\r\n<P>we\\\'re considering either flying in and camping on the outskirts or getting a group together and road-tripping.</P> \r\n<P>you haven\\\'t lived until you\\\'ve experienced jazz fest. </P>',0,0,0,0,'168.73.245.56','en'),(10557,1954,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','when i hear \\\"i\\\'ve stopped counting\\\", i always add 10 years to my first guess.',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(10558,1950,'2001-10-18 19:36:57',0,'jo','fuck YEAH jazz fest.',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(10559,1950,'2001-10-18 20:06:25',0,'stella','<P>my bestest memory from jazz fest:</P>\r\n<p>sitting under a bush (if you\\\'ve been there, you understand why) my lover, heavily buzzed from drinking Fosters all day, sunburned, eating crawfish and boiled red potatoes, thinking \\\"this is quite possibly the best day of my life\\\"</P>',0,0,0,0,'168.73.245.56','en'),(10560,1950,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>my favorite memory from jazz fest: eating oysters that were only hours old while walking around the fairgrounds in major sensory overload.</tt> ',1,0,0,0,'66.65.121.20','en'),(10561,1956,'2001-10-18 20:32:23',0,'stella','<p>monomenot....doot doo di doo doo</P>\r\n\r\n<p>!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!</P>\r\n\r\n<p>fozzie bear</P>\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,'168.73.245.56','en'),(10562,463,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>the diner near my apartment serves <i>\\\"Disco Fries\\\"</i>\\\" a pound of french-fries, covered with melted swiss and cheddar, and then ladeled over with gravy.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.121.20','en'),(10563,1958,'2001-10-18 21:23:14',0,'lou','it\\\'s the anonymity of existing here, the fact that nobody gives a shit about you that <i>allows</i> you to thrive. it takes a certain kind of person to understand and find solace, inspiration, comfort, and love in being ignored.',1,0,0,0,'216.175.66.79','en'),(10564,1958,'2001-10-18 21:26:06',0,'jo would like to refer you to','the conversation we had the last night you were here about being ignored, on the street, in nyc. you love it?',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(10565,1958,'2001-10-18 22:29:53',0,'lou to jo','knowing that no matter what you do nobody is really going to care is waaaay different from not walking down the street and hearing, \\\"hey, baby, nice ASS.\\\"  it\\\'s a fine line, but it\\\'s a line.',6,0,0,0,'216.175.66.79','en'),(10566,1958,'2001-10-18 22:50:39',0,'jo to lou','that\\\'s fair. <BR>\r\nwhat i\\\'d like to do now is vehemently disagree with you and then end up agreeing with you. that\\\'s always fun!',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(10567,1952,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','bjork - \\\"vespertine\\\". kristin said, \\\"this album is really just for her hardcore fans.\\\" I said, \\\"I am a hardcore fan!\\\" and she said, \\\"well then, this album is for you.\\\" it hugs me. it\\\'s brimming with love.',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10568,1952,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','miss kitten and the hacker make me feel dirty. the couple songs i\\\'ve heard off the new bjork album make me feel pretty and dreamy. the other day i was listening to up against the wall redneck mother by jerry jeff walker and that made me feel like a good country boy. also, the liquid sky soundtrack has been making me feel exactly the way i\\\'d like to feel.',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(10569,1958,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i like knowing that if i wanted to, i could dance, <i>completely naked</i> in the median of broadway, and no one would give two fucks. not even the cops.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.121.20','en'),(10570,1958,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','they might if there were thousands of you and some dude was trying to take your picture. i\\\'ve seen it.',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(10571,1958,'2001-10-19 00:25:21',0,'jim to simon','hahahahaha.  I was just coming here to make that exact same comment.',6,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(10572,1952,'2001-10-19 00:38:02',0,'bmg','<p><img src=\'http://images.amazon.com/images/P/B00000J7SS.01.LZZZZZZZ.jpg\'></p>',0,0,0,0,'66.68.81.166','en'),(10573,1958,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>dudes. the \\\'american morning\\\' photographer! when i was in college, that guy was on campus once trying to get people to sign on. he said \\\'no jewelry, makeup or clothes\\\'. they were to shoot at 125th and west side hwy, but the shoot got broken up by cops first.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.121.20','en'),(10574,1954,'2001-10-19 01:09:01',0,'sospirando','<p>\r\n(also nearing 30, male and single)... i for one am glad that women like stella exist. in my old age, i was beginning to wonder. go stella, go stella...\r\n</p>',0,0,0,0,'64.170.190.204','en'),(10575,1958,'2001-10-19 02:05:23',0,'green','how is any of this Hegelian?\r\n',0,0,0,0,'198.81.17.173','en'),(10576,1958,'2001-10-19 02:09:50',0,'Green','hegel would not believe that one could be \\\" in love\\\" with the arts. For in order to make a correct value judgemnt on art one must separate art from the passions, something which Nietzsche onjects to greatly, and look at it from a universal social point of view. As well as being able to reason the necessity the art lends to society as well as its universality and the \\\'disinterest\\\' upon which it should be contemplated. It\\\'s in \\\"Hegel\\\'s Aesthetics\\\". But then again you were being abstract.\r\n\r\n(aphilosophystudent)',1,0,0,0,'198.81.17.173','en'),(10577,1949,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','that quote *is* perfect. it seems like the thing i would want to remember to say to someone i work for-- he dismisses the whole idea of religion and of faith and religious passion. i think he\\\'s missing out on what makes man more than animal, the ability to believe in somethin purely on faith. passion is so beautiful, all it\\\'s many ways of being.',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(10578,1953,'2002-04-20 20:49:51',273,'Quinn','<p>Lulu, I truly love you.\r\n\r\n<p>Your *sigh* speaks volumes.\r\n\r\n<p>Thank you.',1,0,0,0,'209.110.250.78','en'),(10579,1958,'2004-07-27 05:00:32',578,'NetfÃ¶ng!','don\\\'t worry, peter. <i>i</i> get it, but then again, i know about you and hegel. good thing i speak german too :P im gonna move to nyc soon, i think.',1,0,0,0,'66.65.121.20','en'),(10580,127,'2001-10-19 02:46:46',0,'greetings','from another era of swinney',6,0,0,0,'66.65.121.20','en'),(10581,1960,'2001-10-19 03:56:26',0,'Truant','let me be the first one to call you crazy.',1,0,0,0,'66.65.121.20','en'),(10582,1960,'2001-10-19 03:57:21',0,'dong buh','what?',1,0,0,0,'66.65.121.20','en'),(10583,1960,'2001-10-19 03:58:11',0,'salt','and salt and salt and salt.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(10584,1954,'2001-10-19 04:08:22',0,'kat','32...never been married...never had kids...two closest female friends...32 and 39...have never been married...never had kids...we also get that \\\'look\\\' and those comments...another symptom of the herd mentality...get away! get away! get away!!!',1,0,0,0,'32.102.90.187','en'),(10585,1954,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>on marriage: katherine hepburn (an \\\"old maid\\\" at death, but possibly a dyke) put it best when she said \\\"why exchange the admiration of many men for the criticism of one?\\\"</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10586,1958,'2001-10-19 06:09:10',0,'trouble to peter','peter, you\\\'re fucking <i><b>killing me</b></i> here buddy...  killing me.  i\\\'m accepting donations at this point to help me pay for a move, i\\\'ll do anything.<br><b>*burn! burn!* (but in the best and nicest possible way)</b>',6,0,0,0,'24.181.44.135','en'),(10587,1951,'2001-10-19 07:49:56',0,'sean','<p>i thought the whole <a href=\\\"http://www.skepdic.com/bigfoot.html\\\">Yeti myth</a> was disproven and exposed as a grand hoax last year. austin are you sure you believe in Y