ur little comment could add.<BR><BR>but this is really good stuff.  keep it up.',1,0,0,0,'209.208.9.123','en'),(10821,1986,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','<p>ditto.</p>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(10822,1985,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','<p>sounds like the musak version of a dre beat.</p>',0,0,0,0,'64.120.104.101','en'),(10823,1986,'2001-10-29 18:41:39',0,'conscience','who ever said <i>comments</i> were some type of standard? you post. people comment if they feel like it or are motivated to. comments have nothing to do with anything. are you implying we should post some drivel just because we remotely liked an entry? i prefer to read it and enjoy the immediate visceral quality and move on.',0,0,0,0,'66.65.50.61','en'),(10824,967,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to le','<p><b>october 29</b>. i just realized that mirah has a lyric about \\\"sugar in my bowl\\\" </p>\r\n<p><i>i really like it, this rock n roll<br>\r\nmakes me want a little sugar in my bowl.</i></p>\r\n<p>but i was referring to the nina simone,</p>\r\n<p><i>i want a little sugar in my bowl<br>\r\ni want a little sweetness down in my soul<br>\r\ni could stand some lovin oh so bad<br>\r\ni feel so funny, i feel so sad.<br>\r\n....whatsa matta daddy, cmon save my soul<br>\r\ndrop a little sugar in my bowl, i aint foolin.</i></p>\r\n<p>i like to write about music without directly addressing music. my heart is flaring inside out today and I have to wonder if it is that I put sugar in the coffee, or took a pill yesterday, or am expecting blood, or want to procrastinate with swooning, or am a tard. </p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10825,1986,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','ditto.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(10826,1986,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','<BR><BR>i don\\\'t know. i stay confused. i always thought communication was a two-way street.<BR><BR>i was talking to a fellow swinneyite about this last week: the jist was that, for me, posting on here kind of feels like wrapping my material around rocks and throwing them down a well.  he said to get to know some of you outside of swinney.<BR><BR>i guess if i was writing novels, i would get feedback via critical opinion or book sales. i don\\\'t know.',1,0,0,0,'64.132.148.219','en'),(10827,1986,'2001-10-29 21:37:54',0,'ghost','<p>i saw you down by the salted railroad tracks past Pacific last week. you had blood on your hands and black raven shoes. i knew we spoke from the same place when you mentioned my boat was stuck in dry dock. we both laughed when i said i was a professional at doing everything the hard way.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>coffee and covert operations tomorrow at 8?</p>',4,0,0,0,'32.102.90.144','en'),(10828,1981,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','yeah, we\\\'ve been debating switching out the tagline.  we were never serious about it, but unfortunately the web doesn\\\'t have an explicit humor tag, and a lot of people take it the wrong way.  the main stumbling blocks to changing it are 1) our inability to agree on anything better 2) our inherent laziness (I mean, come on, how lazy do you have to be to run a news site where your users contribute most/all of the news? hehe)',1,0,0,0,'66.25.29.204','en'),(10829,1987,'2001-10-29 22:24:06',0,'chat','<P>\r\n[14:22] chiam> the seats in the back come out for extra space. <BR>\r\n[14:22] chiam> yeah only cost me 2.8 million u.s<BR>\r\n[14:22] chiam> ample cupholder capacity<BR>\r\n[14:22] chiam> am/fm cassette<BR>\r\n[14:22] chiam> no cd<BR>\r\n[14:22] chiam> but lots of cb.<BR>\r\n[14:25] chiam> she does thirty miles to the gallon. <BR>\r\n\r\n</P>',2,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(10830,1987,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','probably gets better gas mileage than the Ford Expedition (Excursion?) too... :-)',1,0,0,0,'66.25.29.204','en'),(10831,1986,'2001-10-30 00:44:59',0,'just','what the hell are you talking about?',1,0,0,0,'209.208.25.199','en'),(10832,1987,'2001-10-30 01:01:17',0,'people','who cannot use apostrophes correctly should cease using them 