 brutish and damaging on the surface is in fact nature\\\'s necessity.',0,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(10841,1984,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','dickie:<br><img src=\"http://www.charlotte.com/justgo/movies/wallpapers/1024ripley4.jpg\" height=\"175\" width=\"233\">',0,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(10842,1989,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','<p>\r\n&lt;&lt; No, I have never seen a screen do that. I think is fake because, kids turning sprinkler systems on and off via computers? I mean that is totally fake! &gt;&gt;\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nis he joking? he must be, even tho i don\\\'t get it. cos you can totally get a web interface for your sprinkler system.\r\n</p>',0,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(10843,1989,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','maybe i should change my nick to LogIn.',0,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(10844,1984,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to ix','I have never heard it put so eloquently.',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10845,1989,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','\\\\/\\\\/3 |2 l33T3s+!!  j00 w1|| pHj34r |_|5!!!',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(10846,1989,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>mmm. PBX.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10847,1992,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>the art of <i>flying</i> is tedious when the viscosity of the air is always changing.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10848,1984,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','on second thought, after re-reading this post and then wayne\\\'s brilliant satire, I\\\'ve confirmed that his comments in no way illuminate anything about the above writing except to mercilessly and inaccurately mock it. sometimes, the critic is just a dick.',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10849,1984,'2001-10-30 16:35:45',0,'dickie','<br>porny porny,<br>\r\nput ya hands on my ass<br>\r\nporny porny!',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10850,1984,'2001-10-30 16:53:37',0,'essemar to egg','This article can be read as very empowering and feminine, a glorification of this woman\\\'s place in her world, but that doesn\\\'t change the fact I got a chub when I read it.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(10851,1984,'2001-10-30 17:09:03',0,'sex p0lice','how do we know lin is a girl?!',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10852,1990,'2001-10-30 17:11:35',0,'','<br><tt>i am the lazy<br>\r\nwaiting for Eris<br>\r\nto kiss<br>\r\nenchantment back my way<br></tt>\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,1,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10853,1990,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i am the bored<br>\r\nwaiting for Eris<br>\r\nto kiss<br>\r\nenchantment back my way<br></tt>\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10854,1984,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to essemar','i didnt say anything about this article being \\\"empowering\\\" or \\\"feminine\\\", or about the gender of \\\"lin\\\". all i said was that wayne can be a dick.',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10855,705,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','soggy biscuit with a mrs. johnson\\\'s doughnut.',4,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(10856,1990,'2001-10-30 19:54:22',0,'ty','that\\\'s a nice poem but i don\\\'t understand the first stanza:<br>i am the world\\\'s girl--\r\nthe evil dawn\r\n\r\n<br><br>\r\nwhat did you mean by that?\r\n',1,0,0,0,'65.140.48.181','en'),(10857,1992,'2001-10-30 19:58:39',0,'ty','there is nothing holding you back. this is frickin\\\' <i>america</i>. ',1,0,0,0,'65.140.48.181','en'),(10858,1984,'2001-10-30 21:20:26',0,'essemar to egg','I didn\\\'t mean to sound like I was putting words in your mouth.  That wasn\\\'t my intention.  I was just thinking about the different levels one can look at things.  On an artistic level, this article has some very elegent imagery/metaphor with regards to self-image.  You could even look deeper and consider its implications of the filter our society puts on self-image and masculine vs. femine notions of power and self-expression.  It is also, in its way, the most erotic thing I\\\'ve every read on Swinney.  wb\\\'s comments expressed exactly what I was thinking when I finished reading the piece the first time.  Therefore, I thought his words were quite germane and welcome.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(10859,1992,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','Well... gravity does hold me back regardless of wether I\\\'m in the US or Istanbul.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(10860,1990,'2001-10-30 21:44:26',0,'ghost','fucking whinyass crybaby Water sign...LOSER...get ye gone Satan...back...BACK...i say! yo mama lives in a ditch...HOPELESS romantic...dork! now drink yer coffee and eat yer cake...n just shut yer piehole okay?\r\n\r\n<p><i>*bestfriendly*</i></p>',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.198','en'),(10861,1992,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','that\\\'s true.',1,0,0,0,'65.140.48.114','en'),(10862,1991,'2001-10-30 22:04:58',0,'ketchup advisory board','maybe you aren\\\'t getting enough ketchup.',1,0,0,0,'65.140.48.114','en'),(10863,1991,'2001-10-30 22:51:33',0,'ketchup','i am evil.',0,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(10864,1986,'2002-10-04 04:15:39',409,'rachel','it is very dark here. you may be eaten by a grue.\r\n',0,0,0,0,'65.200.105.130','en'),(10865,1984,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>Wasn\\\'t <i>Germaine</i> one of the Jackson 5?! no wait, that was <i>Jermaine</i></tt>.',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.61','en'),(10866,1990,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>hopeless! romantic! <i>dork!</i> arrrrrgh!</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.61','en'),(10867,1990,'2001-10-31 00:11:22',0,'kat','<p>-----Original Message-----<br>\r\nFrom: mojo-kat [mailto:kat@lefteyelazy.com]<br>\r\nSent: Monday, October 29, 2001 7:04 PM<br>\r\nSubject: ?<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\narrrrrrrrrrrrrrrggggggggggggggggggggggg<br>\r\n</p>',6,0,0,0,'32.102.109.123','en'),(10868,1989,'2001-10-31 01:08:43',0,'leonard','this is so like |-|3 |_|_[]. it makes me laugh. ',1,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(10869,1984,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p>\r\ncritics ruin art. in the process of engineering art for the masses, they force the artist away from pure expression. show me a piece of art, i\'ll show you two opposite opinions. why should i care about yours? why should the public? why should a dollop of negativity bear more weight than the aesthetic of the artist? opinion is nothing more than fashion; and fashion is fickle, often hideous.\r\n</p><p>\r\nwhat is relevant to others is frequently irrelevant to me. thus i see no point in favoring one group at the detriment of another. perhaps the collective critic is the true champion of the lowest common denominator.\r\n</p><p>\r\ni prefer sincerity in art to technical perfection. perfection brings me no closer to beauty; likewise, bludgeoning the artist away from happiness and pride in their work, pushes them further away from sincerity.\r\n</p>',5,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(10870,1984,'2001-10-31 03:21:36',0,'ghost to s5','amen',1,0,0,0,'32.102.109.123','en'),(10871,1984,'2001-10-31 03:27:16',0,'jo','<p>because criticism and commentary go hand in hand. to say there should be no art criticism means no book reviews? music reviews? no pitchforkmedia? is it only criticism if you\\\'re saying something that can be perceived by even one person as negative?</p>\r\n<p>art criticism can be a good thing and as much as it destroys or upsets some artists, it fuels others. yes i create for myself but i also create to throw it out into the public and see what people think. if all i got were rave reviews, i might stay mediocre. i need criticism to spurn me on. to make me say: \\\"you\\\'re wrong about me, and here\\\'s WHY,\\\" and make something even better.</p>\r\n<p>there\\\'s a long history of artists who only created their best work (and i use \\\"best\\\" meaning the work they themselves were most proud of) after critics snubbed, mocked, even judged cruelly the work they had been doing. pollock comes to mind mostly because i just saw that film but a quick thumbing through art history books will turn up countless others.</p>',0,0,0,0,'128.83.177.71','en'),(10872,1992,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','anything is possible in america... except living on minimum wage.',0,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(10873,1984,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p><b>to reiterate</b>:wb is sometimes a clever critic, and I believe that criticism is a healthy cultural practice. but sometimes, he\\\'s just a dick. \\\"dick\\\" meaning he acts only with the intention of exposing the weakness or insecurity of another, sometimes at the service of an inexplicable whim, and sometimes to mask and soothe his own insecurities. in the case of quoting inane madonna lyrics as a way of mocking lin, I believe he commented here because the devil made him be a dick, for no reason but to make the evil lord chuckle. I cant say I didnt chuckle. but I have been living in the cruel and whimsical world of wb for years now and I know how to chuckle most of the time, savoring what layers of sincere genius lie between the devil\\\'s teeth and discarding the meaningless cruelty that sometimes fuels this vehicle of expression [excuse my lengthy mixed metaphor im delirious]. lin knew nothing of wb and might have thought that \\\"she\\\" sucked because wb was just being a dick. i thought some brief explanation of wb\\\'s role in various textual communities would encourage others who might have suffered at the hand of his \\\"criticism\\\" to chuckle as well. that is all.</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10874,1984,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p>\r\nreviews are necessary, but they are different than opinion pieces. well-written reviews lead me to more of what i like, regardless of what the reviewer likes.\r\n</p><p>\r\nwhat if criticism beats down and obscures more great artists than it props up?\r\n</p>',6,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(10875,1984,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','once, tuggy and i had a conversation about whether a genre of art needs a body of critics to have high standards. i think we had this conversation in the context of online journals. i almost always think tuggy is right but i\\\'m undecided on this one. i\\\'m not sure that art benefits from critics setting standards. i\\\'m not sure it suffers either. i think there\\\'s room for people who like critics and the standards and context they impose, and room for people who disregard the critics. in fact i think if there need s to be criticism, there also needs to be a faction that thumbs its nose at the critics.\r\n<br><br>\r\nmax\\\'s: no critics allowed',4,0,0,0,'216.27.183.161','en'),(10876,416,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>this <i>is</i> neat.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.61','en'),(10877,1984,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to s5','<p>having made something that was *passionately* disliked by many people, I can say for myself that forcefully BAD reviews encourage me. I mean, generally, I DIG negative, or even just tenacious, criticism way much more than people coming into my house, looking at my artwork and giving a weak smile, and asking no questions, stupid or not, and making no attempt at assessment. criticism is attention. validation. conversation. communication. aknowledgement.  I can\\\'t imagine being \\\"beaten down\\\" by \\\"bad\\\" criticism. if Ive been told I suck, it just gives me something to cackle against with my defiant fist. and i would say there are a lot of -makers who also thrive on that energy of opposition. </p>',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10878,1984,'2001-10-31 05:50:38',0,'jim','<p>\r\nart criticism serves three purposes admirably:\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>providing data to those art consumers who cannot or choose not to form their own opinions about what art moves them;\r\n\r\n<li>providing an outlet to those art creators who cannot or choose not to create their own work, and instead rely on discussing the work of others to express themselves;\r\n\r\n<li>providing a meter to those art creators who believe that the true worth of their work can come from anyone but themselves.\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nthe decision to participate in this system is in left largely to each individual consumer, critic and artist. it can and does exist in parallel to the system where artists create work motivated purely by passion and without thought to audience, consumers choose art on the basis of whether or not it makes them feel all crazy inside, and critics don\\\'t get invited to parties.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nI don\\\'t believe that \\\"critics ruin art\\\" anymore than I believe criticism is any kind of  \\\"necessity\\\".  I choose not to give any self-appointed arbiter of taste that kind of power over the art I experience or the art I create.  \r\n</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n',6,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(10879,1984,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','hey, did i mention that coke bought odwalla? man, does that suck.',6,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(10880,1984,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','UUUGGHHHHHHHH!!~!!!!!!!!!!!!<br>\r\n<br>\r\n[burn burn]',6,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(10881,1984,'2001-10-31 13:30:09',0,'trouble','adding to the thread, i read/saw recently an interview with billy bob thornton (at least i think it was billy bob).  in it he was discussing the movie making process and how the idea of \\\'test audiences\\\' was ridiculous.  showing the movie to a select bunch of \\\'average\\\' moviegoers, gauging their reactions and based on those reactions, editing the final version.  he brought up the idea of picasso showing paintings to average folk on the street and then going back and \\\'editing\\\' his art or trashing it all together based on their reactions.  i agree with the notion that critics are a good thing if their only goal is to be constructive.  <br>all i have is a nickel so i\\\'ll leave the remaining three cents in the cup.  *best friendly*',1,0,0,0,'208.255.153.146','en'),(10882,1984,'2001-10-31 14:08:34',0,'The Critic','<img src=\\\"http://www.egr.msu.edu/~mccreer4/images/critic.gif\\\"><br><a href=\\\"http://www.egr.msu.edu/~mccreer4/portrait2.htm\\\">for the critic in all of us</a>',0,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10883,1994,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','so you ARE going to wear a costume!',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10884,1984,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','wow, i missed a discussion on the value of art critics. haha! hmm. heh.',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(10885,1994,'2001-10-31 18:45:03',0,'stella','would the cape indicate that Captain penis isn\\\'t circumsized?',0,0,0,0,'168.73.245.56','en'),(10886,1994,'2001-10-31 18:48:37',0,'teacher','can this story be read at public school? is there an animated version coming soon? i\\\'m sick of snoopy',1,0,0,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(10887,1984,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','critics are too invited to parties. who else is going to write about the party in index or paper?',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(10888,1984,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i stopped buying odwalla a while ago, after oof gently pointed out to me that all their juice sucks and is made with OJ anyway. i\\\'m not surprised coke bought them. odwalla has sort of become a symbol of hippies in button down suits to me. frat boys with hemp jewelry.',4,0,0,0,'216.27.183.161','en'),(10889,1984,'2001-10-31 21:30:15',0,'stella','fresh samantha is better anyway.\r\nor buy a juicer. ',0,0,0,0,'168.73.245.56','en'),(10890,1995,'2001-10-31 21:34:02',0,'leonard','<p><a href=\\\"http://www.dvdmoviecentral.com/ReviewsText/nekromantik.htm\\\">Nekromantik</a> is pretty creepy, too.</p>',1,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(10891,1995,'2001-10-31 21:44:47',0,'trouble','\\\'showgirls\\\' was some pretty scary shite too... <shiver>',1,0,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(10892,1995,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','perhaps try: <a href=\\\"http://us.imdb.com/Title?0084464\\\">PANDEMONIUM</a>',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(10893,1995,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','Perhaps we\\\'re forgetting the most important Halloween movie of all: <a href=\\\"http://us.imdb.com/Title?0077651\\\" target=\\\"movie\\\">Halloween</a>.  I know that\\\'s what I was watching tonight 365 days ago.',1,0,0,0,'64.229.76.52','en'),(10894,1995,