DING TO KNOW MORE ABOUT WHAT HAPPENED FROM THIS HAIR ADVENTURE. <a href=\\\"mailto:joanna@unpopular.com\\\">PLEASE FILL ME IN</a>. preferably with PICTURES.',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(10901,1997,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','testify!',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(10902,1995,'2001-11-01 00:54:56',0,'redrum','the Shining....heeeeeeeeeeeeeeerrrrrrrrre\\\'s JOHNNY!',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.178','en'),(10903,1982,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>Isn\\\'t \\\"the other people place\\\" Drexcyia doing non-electro stuff?</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin',1,0,0,0,'24.221.170.233','en'),(10904,1997,'2001-11-01 01:25:23',0,'PAGAN','People Against Goodness and Normalcy',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10905,1982,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>just downloaded some mp3s. listened in tub while reading. sounds like competently programmed but ultimately forgettable electro.</p>\r\n<p>What about this album impresses you so?</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n',3,0,0,0,'24.221.170.233','en'),(10906,1999,'2001-11-01 03:17:45',0,'dude','you said \\\"panis\\\"',1,0,0,0,'209.208.10.156','en'),(10907,1982,'2002-04-12 05:27:03',57,'weeb to darwin','\nthat\\\'s a really good way to say \\\"your taste sucks\\\" without actually saying it. sheesh.',0,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(10908,2000,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','we\\\'ll have to wait \\\'til 2020 if we want to have our adult posse on a halloween full moon. thing is, i don\\\'t think i\\\'m going to be grown up by then.',1,0,0,0,'209.208.10.156','en'),(10909,1998,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','nice. article 1996 was good, too. ancestor worship is tops. most americans know notalot about their geneology.',1,0,0,0,'209.208.10.156','en'),(10910,1999,'2001-11-01 03:34:16',0,'dumb','i also misspelled halloween.',6,0,0,0,'208.58.87.82','en'),(10911,1982,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>All I said is I don\\\'t understand why he\\\'s impressed by it and asked him for clarification. All other value judgements are your inference.</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n',3,0,0,0,'24.221.170.233','en'),(10912,1982,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','snipe snipe snipe.',0,0,0,0,'216.27.183.161','en'),(10913,1984,'2001-11-01 04:36:18',0,'lin','<p>some facts about this piece, and thanks for the discussion. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>This piece was in no way planned out to be erotic, but in my processes of creating artwork and writing of all kinds I have found others always see an underlying framework of sexuality. </p>\r\n<p> I don\\\'t think I suck, though I was origionally disappointed that there wasn\\\'t much other commentary. I encourage criticism so that I can try to find any flaws, but I generally tend to ignore it anyway.</p> \r\n<p>There are lots of people who will tell you that you should never divulge the meaning you brought with you when exposing work to others, and giving a detail of what you think things should mean, because art is entirely subjective.</p>\r\n\r\n<p> In this case I think my intentions have become a sort of sideline point. I will retain them for future writing. Next time I won\\\'t use the word thigh, if I can help it.</p> \r\n\r\n',3,0,0,0,'24.112.33.4','en'),(10914,1995,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','carnival of souls. seconds. testament. stroszek.',1,0,0,0,'209.208.9.69','en'),(10915,1982,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>le, what are you trying to say here? Is it impossible that I honestly don\\\'t understand what about the music resonates with the author enough to post here about it? Could it be possible that I really want clarification?</p>\r\n<p>Or, is it more likely that I am a big <a href=\\\"http://www.klangundkleid.ch/toys/actionfigures/detail.asp?ID=4480\\\">meanie</a> who wants to snipe at people\\\'s musical taste?</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n',1,0,0,0,'24.221.170.233','en'),(10916,1982,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i wasn\'t trying to say anything but \"gee, people are sniping at each other here.\" it wasn\'t a character judgement, much as you might like it to be because then you\'d have a reason to argue with me. it was actually just me saying the word \"snipe\" three times because i sort of like the word and because i noticed tension in this thread.',4,0,0,0,'216.27.183.161','en'),(10917,1982,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>ok. I agree, there seems to be some hostility in this thread. maybe my 3 second music review seemed insultingly blunt or something.</p>\r\n<p>thanks for the clarification.</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin',2,0,0,0,'24.221.170.233','en'),(10918,1984,'2001-11-01 05:22:03',0,'jo','',0,0,0,0,'172.137.194.44','en'),(10919,1984,'2001-11-01 05:23:14',0,'jo','dammit fucking dammit. tab not enter, tab not enter.<BR>\r\nhi. i liked your piece. i think it happened to spawn some dialogue that was mostly unrelated to the piece itself, but. don\\\'t take that personally, it happens all the time.',0,0,0,0,'172.137.194.44','en'),(10920,1995,'2001-11-01 05:25:15',0,'wb','no need to stay true to your liberal arts education, nobody will report ya! obvious or not, \\\'halloween\\\' is a fucking classic.',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(10921,2000,'2001-11-01 05:29:25',0,'bobgoblin','favorite halloween candy...<i>SMARTIES!</i>',0,0,0,0,'32.102.91.184','en'),(10922,1995,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to wb','there is nothing in my liberal arts education to encourage my love of \\\"Sleepaway Camp\\\". I actually dont really like the movie Halloween. I was trying to be kind, but youve driven me to admit it.',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10923,1995,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','now i want hostess cupcakes. may contain beef fat.',4,0,0,0,'216.27.183.161','en'),(10924,1984,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','hi lin. you rock.',1,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(10925,1997,'2001-11-01 06:09:13',0,'ghost','<p><img border=\\\"0\\\" src=\\\"http://swinney.org/journals/images/851_1.jpg\\\" width=\\\"381\\\" height=\\\"196\\\"></p>\r\n<p>i want to play dress-up in knee highs and pigtails and find someone who\\\'ll let me call them daddy</p>',0,0,0,0,'32.102.91.184','en'),(10926,1455,'2001-11-01 06:12:54',0,'kat','oh shit...the first time i ever had Pop Rocks was at this drive-in. im surprised i didn\\\'t lose my virginity there too.',1,0,0,0,'32.102.91.184','en'),(10927,1984,'2001-11-01 07:32:26',0,'wb','i guess i get the last word. <BR>\r\n-neither the author or myself held the original post up as art.<BR>\r\n-while the lyrics might have been a bit tongue in cheek, only the humorless would consider it \\\"criticism\\\"<BR>\r\n-since the former college art students steered the thread from the joys of being a dick to the world of art...regarding the role of criticism in the art world: art would be more ignored than it already is if it wasn\\\'t for the space that critics hold in newspapers (of course you don\\\'t see art criticism on network tv, non-npr radio, etc etc). keep in mind that many times critics are saying \\\"go see this\\\"<BR>\r\n-to the artists: at least the critics care enough to say your shit does, in fact, stink. isn\\\'t the attention all you were after in the first place?',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(10928,811,'2001-11-01 07:43:34',0,'Buck','Rolls and rolls of tape methinks\r\n\r\n',3,0,0,0,'209.178.170.55','en'),(10929,1995,'2002-10-04 04:15:39',409,'rachel','tonight we watched \\\'the prince of darkness\\\'\r\nand \\\'the thing\\\'. both excellent halloween \r\nnight movies. sadly, not too many kids came\r\nto the door, so we have a lot of candy left\r\nover. if you like nerds, charms blow-pops,\r\neyball gumballs, candy bracelets, and poprocks,\r\ncome on by. \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\ni can\\\'t avoid speculating that the reason there were so few kids tonight is that their parents are hysterically scared. bah. \r\n</p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'207.214.90.66','en'),(10930,1984,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','UUGGHHHHHHHHH!!!!!!!<br>\r\n<br>\r\n[angry detractor]',5,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(10931,1995,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i saw lots of kids out tonight in sf. i was surprised. where did they all come from!',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(10932,1997,'2001-11-01 12:09:50',0,'Daddy','count me in!',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10933,1999,'2001-11-01 12:15:05',0,'dude','you said \\\"too girls\\\"',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10934,1984,'2001-11-01 12:46:36',0,'jim to wb','wayne, that last post sounded exactly like that little speech Jerry Springer gives at the end of his show; that one that sums up in the most superficial way possible the past sixty minutes of ecstacy and horror and the human condition that he\\\'s just finished serving up to you at four in the morning.\r\n',6,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(10935,1995,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','just watched <b>the lost boys</b> - also for the scary movie list.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(10936,811,'2001-11-01 14:34:08',0,'Grant Morrison','Hi, I\\\'m Grant Morrison, acclaimed and possibly mildly insane Scottish comic book genius, and author of such great reads as KILL YOUR BOYFRIEND and THE INVISIBLES. Now Marvel are letting me write X-MEN. They must be mad! I\\\'m filling it with telepathic BDSM and theories about human evolution.\r\n\r\nP.S. That picture is the cover of New X-Men #116, part three of the three-part \\\'E Is For Extinction\\\' storyline, and was drawn by Frank Quitely, my also-Scottish mate. I know it\\\'s a bit porny, but that\\\'s just Frank.',2,0,0,0,'212.161.41.80','en'),(10937,1995,'2001-11-01 15:38:29',0,'bark','seconds Lost Highway',0,0,0,0,'12.110.65.19','en'),(10938,1982,'2001-11-01 15:52:25',0,'critic','darwin, it definitely wouldn\\\'t be the <i>first</i> time you derided someone\\\'s musical tastes... <i>\\\'best friendly\\\'</i>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10939,1984,'2001-11-01 15:57:04',0,'jo','wow and i would have thought one random ugggghhh per thread would have been enough but apparently we need two.',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(10940,1984,'2001-11-01 16:11:58',0,'make that three','ugggghhh!',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10941,1984,'2002-03-08 04:50:26',86,'egg to wb','hey, dont blame it on me, all I said was that you can be a dick. it was ix who was saying that critic thing, and he was being funny. some of us were in on the joke.',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10942,1984,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','I must say that this is the most fun I\\\'ve had on Swinney in a while.  Tongue in cheek serious argumentation and confused intentions always make for an excellent farce.<p>\r\n\r\nAAAAAAAAARRRGGHHHH!!!</p><p>Lin, you rock.  Keep writing stuff for us muse over.  We obviously enjoyed it very much.</P><p>...and keep using the word \\\'thigh.\\\'  I like that word a lot.</p>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(10943,1984,'2001-11-01 17:47:51',0,'wb','keep on musing in the free world, fuckos.',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(10944,2000,'2001-11-01 18:28:46',0,'Professor Swinney','<B>*Switches Weeb*</B>, NO!  you will rot your teeth out!  little childred are only allowed to have apples and carrots for halloween.  nothing else.  popcorn maybe.  and celery. that is all.',4,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(10945,2000,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i was always fond of the <i>popcorn ball</i> myself</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10946,1995,'2001-11-01 19:42:19',0,'mightybluj to rachel','you know it!  JC\\\'s \\\"the Thing\\\" has got to be the scariest movie of all time in my book.   i won\\\'t let my dog in my room when i got to bed after viewing it.  ',1,0,0,0,'204.64.42.245','en'),(10947,1995,'2002-03-05 20:17:36',17,'austin to s5','you dog! you watched the lost boys with out me, and i live here :-/ no respect.',3,0,0,0,'205.179.19.31','en'),(10948,2000,'2001-11-01 20:15:38',0,'trouble','i used to be quite fond of the pennies taped up in counts of five.  mcdonalds gift certificates rocked too, what can i say...  we were poor',2,0,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(10949,1999,'2001-11-01 22:00:20',0,'yeah','fuck! i did, didn\\\'t i? shit, that\\\'s what i get for not proof reading before submitting. but i did use the word vindicated- and that\\\'s what?, like four syllables?- so i think i still come out the winner.',4,0,0,0,'12.146.203.137','en'),(10950,1995,'2001-11-01 22:35:58',0,'pumpkin','<p>I thought those peanut butter cakey things were called \\\'Tasty Kakes\\\'... I remember them too.. they werer yummy</p>',2,0,0,0,'216.136.25.122','en'),(10951,1984,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','\\\"the useless fade in time\\\"',0,0,0,0,'64.132.148.219','en'),(10952,2001,'2002-09-09 00:01:42',195,'matt','joseph buck, you rock like the rock \\\'n roll.  go on doing.',0,0,0,0,'64.132.148.219','en'),(10953,811,'2001-11-01 23:32:39',0,'grant','who exactly do you think gives a fuck?',0,0,0,0,'64.132.148.219','en'),(10954,1995,'2001-11-01 23:52:03',0,'jo','yeah they <b>totally</b> still make the tasty kake variety of this snack food. before it was available in texas, my mom used to have our relatives in philly ship them to us because she\\\'s <b>just that</b> addicted to their deliciousness.<BR>\r\nthey\\\'re good a little frozen, too.',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(10955,1995,'2001-11-01 23:54:00',0,'jo to s5','where they all came from was parents who said, \\\"let\\\'s go trick-or-treating in the rich neighborhood because they give better candy and are less likely to kill us!\\\" at least that\\\'s what we all did when we were kids.',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(10956,1984,'2001-11-01 23:54:15',0,'huge_wobbly_penis','*wobble*',2,0,0,0,'140.174.185.248','en'),(10957,1995,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','mostly in their own neighborhoods; i saw them around the lower haight and the mission.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(10958,1984,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','oh, and i thought one snarky bullshit opinion was enough per thread.  obviously fucking not.',6,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(10959,1999,'2001-11-02 00:51:00',0,'hungrynow','so tell us ///what was upstairs?\r\n',0,0,0,0,'12.20.43.1','en'),(10960,1997,'2001-11-02 00:56:38',0,'averageamerican','i may be confused but that doesn\\\'t mean we can\\\'t fuck like pagans and smear choclate....i just choose not to deprive anyone else of their chocolate and fucking priveldges.',0,0,0,0,'12.20.43.1','en'),(10961,2001,'2001-11-02 01:05:23',0,'uh yea','quantity equals quality? only those who live and produce their medium 24/7 can be called true artists? ...this is such an elitist attitude. you\\\'re gonna miss out on a lot of great stuff and amazing people thinking this way.',4,0,0,0,'32.102.91.205','en'),(10962,1989,'2001-11-02 02:35:24',0,'deb','heheh...the good \\\'ol BBS days...',0,0,0,0,'205.188.193.152','en'),(10963,1992,'2001-11-02 02:42:52',0,'deb','but what is art?\r\n\r\nyou could live on minimum wage if you lived in a cardboard box, maybe.',0,0,0,0,'205.188.193.152','en'),(10964,1995,'2001-11-02 02:50:40',0,'deb','who needs scary when you can watch Nightmare before Christmas. Cartoon fun for any freakish holiday...',0,0,0,0,'205.188.193.152','en'),(10965,1992,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','art fart',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10966,1984,'2001-11-02 02:56:28',0,'fuck','shit fucking fuck goddamn!  bullshit fucking fuck.',6,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(10967,1984,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','constructive.',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10968,1995,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>mmm. tasty kakes. when i lived in brooklyn, i lived across the gowanus pkwy from a tasty kake bakery. year round, the air smelled like a mixture of artificial-berry flavouring and the ny harbour.',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.61','en'),(10969,1984,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','<p><img src=\\\"http://steve.org/images/nice.jpg\\\"></p>',6,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(10970,1995,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>a. I dont know what this tasty kake crap you guys are talking about is, but I posted to pals about the funny bones and this guy sent me <a href=\\\"http://www.hometownfavorites.com/shop/catalog.asp?c=dessert\\\">this url</a> where I can order funny bones to my heart\\\'s content. the only problem is that I have to order a minimum of $20 and the funny bones are only $4 and I really only need one box.</p>\r\n<p>2. I used to have a copy of  \\\"The Lost Boys\\\" that my friend and neighbor Liz had taped off of cable. I have seen that movie over a dozen times. I have also seen Some Like It Hot, Bus Stop, Gone With the Wind, Weird Science, and some other weird ones over two dozen times. I have a head full of garbage. It is my lifelong goal to empty out the garbage, and I dont think Ill make it before I croak, because I keep opening it up and filling it with fresh piles of new garbage, like swinney.org.</p>',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10971,1995,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','sometimes the garbage grows tentacles.',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(10972,1984,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','it\\\'s all over when we bring out the fluffy bunnies.',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(10973,1982,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','Darwin, are you asking me to convince you to like this album?  What do you want from me here?  You don\\\'t like the album, I do.  Go team.  Is there something wrong with this situation?',3,0,0,0,'64.229.76.52','en'),(10974,1984,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','GGGGUUUUHHHHGFUUUUUUCCCKKKKK<br>\r\n<br>\r\n[constructive]',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(10975,1997,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Wsht\\\'qui\\\'jit\\\'ong Moll','In my country, eat yak.',1,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(10976,1984,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','maybe we can break the record for the most comments!',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(10977,1984,'2001-11-02 04:39:17',0,'GWAR','How do you hide money from the hippie /<br>\r\nput it under the soap!',1,0,0,0,'64.229.76.52','en'),(10978,1984,'2001-11-02 04:48:02',0,'life tastes good','<p>\r\n<img src=\"http://vagabondage.com/~jim/corbiscoke.jpg\">\r\n</p>',6,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(10979,1984,'2001-11-02 05:24:01',0,'arrrrrrrrrrrrgggggggghhhh','object insertion porn is totally uncalled for. thanks.',6,0,0,0,'32.102.91.205','en'),(10980,1984,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','nice, i didn\\\'t know corbis cataloged porn too',0,0,0,0,'207.214.220.220','en'),(10981,1984,'2001-11-02 06:05:47',0,'jim','<p>\r\ndoes that mean you haven\'t seen their camgirls catalog either?\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<img src=\"http://vagabondage.com/~jim/damnthiscorbis.jpg\">\r\n</p>',6,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(10982,1984,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','shut up! i\\\'m gonna take away your photoshop privileges, young man!',0,0,0,0,'207.214.220.220','en'),(10983,1982,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>I want to understand what it is that you like about this album that makes it so distinctively good. Like I said, it sounds like pretty non-distinctive electro to me.</p>\r\n<p>As the above unnamed critic has stated, I have often derided other people\\\'s taste in music. In an effort to understand why people like things that I don\\\'t, I\\\'m trying a new approach. The new approach, specifically, is asking people <u>why</u> they like the music that they do that I don\\\'t.</p>\r\n<p>\r\nIs that more clear?\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'24.221.170.233','en'),(10984,2001,'2001-11-02 06:45:59',0,'Buck','Hi, my name is Buck. What\\\'s yours? As i said in the last paragraph this is not all either/or. Yes a great novel, symphony, or painting will come from the wayward mail carrier. But whether they continue to create depend upon their conditions, commitments, and attention to the muse. But the other point I made is important. Choice. Some artists have no choice but to create work, next meal, be damned.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,'209.178.170.26','en'),(10985,2001,'2001-11-02 08:35:05',0,'jim@thisishomemade.com','',0,0,0,1,'66.92.4.146','en'),(10986,2001,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','hey buck! nice to see you found your way to swinney.org :)\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,'203.96.111.200','en'),(10987,1986,'2001-11-02 09:03:14',0,'shane','I have really enjoyed reading this piece.\r\nThank you, and would you mind if I shared it with my class of 4 students? Please email me at breaker2g@hotmail.com with a reply',0,0,0,0,'211.115.44.214','en'),(10988,811,'2001-11-02 09:49:12',0,'Daniel Clowes','Yeah, Morrison, you and your spandex-clad goons can go fuck a tree. Buy Ghost World everyone!',1,0,0,0,'212.161.41.80','en'),(10989,2001,'2001-11-02 09:53:57',0,'jim','<p>\r\nsome artists like drinking cold, cold lemonade.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nsome artists don\\\'t write Christmas cards.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nsome artists abhor puppies.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nsome artists wear elaborate underwear.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nsome artists prefer sleeping on their stomachs to sleeping on their backs.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nsome artists wear sunglasses at night.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nsome artists are too busy thinking about their work to fuck.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nsome artists are too busy fucking to think about their work.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nsome artists have no choice.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nsome artists do.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nthis is all trivia.  the moral of your story rings so true to me, but the trivia you present as evidence gets me down.   your attempt to establish devotion as a metric for artistic worth fails for me because the conception of devotion you use as a foundation is so narrow.  \r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nthat daily route your wayward mail carrier follows which you superficially identify as that thing standing between she and her muse IS her object of devotion, THE place from which her words or her music or her paint is borne from.  for her, the work which you hold up to honor is a tiny part of her experience of that and, in turn, a tiny part of her existence as an artist.  that you don\\\'t recognize the rest as art is not her failure.  \r\n</p>\r\n',6,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(10990,2004,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','this is from dan savage. he\\\'s running masturbation horror stores. here\\\'s the <a href=\\\"http://www.sfweekly.com/savage/index2.html\\\">full column</a>. i fucking love dan savage.',4,0,0,0,'66.123.206.47','en'),(10991,2001,'2001-11-02 11:02:03',0,'Buck','Starlajo. Many thanks.',0,0,0,0,'209.178.170.138','en'),(10992,2001,'2001-11-02 11:19:50',0,'Buck','Hi Jim. Yeah you are right about our mailcarrier. Her experience may inform her artistic process. But there is that other kind of artist where the process, and relationship with the medium itself is so a part of them that everything else falls aside. Therefore the Jimi example. Quantity does not equal quality, but can sure help the artist improve. I think this is why so few novelists who have their first/only published have it blow up, or even rarer, to have it talked about in 50 years time. Regardless, all this is tough to explain. Enigmas wrapped in riddles stuck in fortune cookies after Peking Duck at Sam Woo\\\'s in Monterey Park. As I have said, I am working on this for something elsewhere. But I appreciate what ya said. Mas! Be well.',0,0,0,0,'209.178.170.138','en'),(10993,2004,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>small world. i was just reading this <a href=\\\"http://www.villagevoice.com/issues/0143/savage.php\\\">same article in the voice</a> this morning on the way to work.  why do they always have to put BIG, <i>giant</i> ads for sex toys on the opposite page? I always attract some interesting stares from the codgery upper east side folk.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10994,2003,'2001-11-02 13:50:47',0,'critic','wow, a shameless, unsolicited plug for your site! <i>thanks</i>.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10995,1982,'2001-11-02 14:10:27',0,'','Fuzzy, while youre at it: if you could also <i>please</i> explain whether you prefer boxers over briefs and provide a concise statement explaining your tastes, why you see one to be superior to the other, and how this all applies to <i>me</i>. I really <i>just want to understand</i>. (Actually, what I <i>really</i> want is to get flustered up in pretense and overintellectualize the fact that my tastes are far superior to yours.)<br><br>Also, if you could please annotate your tastes in food, films, and art, that would be great... I think it would provide enough fodder to keep my wheels spinning for a while.<br><br>\r\n<i>[ok, sorry for the sarcastic rant folks, but for real... some things are just a <b>matter of personal taste</b> and require no qualification, explanation, or pseudointellectual digression]</i>\r\n<br><br>ok, thats my two cents. please dont rip[ me apart for saying it...',1,0,0,1,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10996,1982,'2001-11-02 14:12:17',0,'critic','Fuzzy, while youre at it: if you could also <i>please</i> explain whether you prefer boxers over briefs and provide a concise statement explaining your tastes, why you see one to be superior to the other, and how this all applies to <i>me</i>. I really just <i>want to understand</i>. (Actually, what I <i>really</i> want is to get flustered up in pretense and overintellectualize the fact that my tastes are far superior to and more eclectic than yours.)<br><br>Also, if you could please annotate your tastes in food, films, and art, that would be great... I think it would provide enough fodder to keep my wheels spinning for a while.<br><br>\r\n<i>[ok, sorry for the sarcasm, but for real... some matters are just merely <b>a matter of personal taste</b> and require no explanation, qualification, or pseudointellectual digression. this whole discussion is as dumb as someone yelling at me because i prefer my asparagus steamed over sauteed]</i><br><br>thats just my two cents. please dont rip me apart for it. thanks!',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(10997,2004,'2001-11-02 14:24:44',0,'sawks','<br>\r\nmy friend evan got busted by his grandma while trying to blow himself, i dont think i can leave this thread without mentioning that...\r\n',3,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(10998,811,'2001-11-02 15:24:04',0,'jo','dear daniel clowes, when you have a spare minute, can you drop me a line, because i would really like to discuss with you the differences between the graphic novel and the movie, particularly the terry zwigoff influences and the fact that terry turned seymour into a clone of himself and minimized the josh role to almost nothing and how this reflects on enid\\\'s character.',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(10999,1984,'2001-11-02 15:35:07',0,'kat','le let me suck on her popsicle at burning man. i guess i could have run after the naked punk boys and gotten my own, but it just tastes so much better when it belongs to someone else!',1,0,0,0,'32.102.64.157','en'),(11000,2005,'2001-11-02 15:38:20',0,'ghost','i exist for times like this.',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.157','en'),(11001,1984,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>why does food always taste so much better when it belongs to someone else?! some of my best meals lately have been my flatmate\\\'s, whom i stole from the fridge, of course.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(11002,2005,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>water signs, unite!</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(11003,2005,'2001-11-02 15:59:54',0,'jo','shout out to water signs.',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(11004,1992,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','There was a point in my life when I was spending $50 a week on rent and another $15 on food.  Those were the entirety of my expenses.  Now, I spend $800 a month on rent plus another $130 on utilities and around $100-150 a week on food and other sundry expenses.<p>I was a lot happier back when I was living on $65 a week.  That was one of the best times of my life.</p>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(11005,1992,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>the tenfold economy change of living in nyc v. anywhere else is a hassle, too. in austin, i was amazed that i could get a GRAND dinner for like 5$! i was on a wild spending spree all weekend, as i could buy funky clothes, records and tons of other stuff for the price of coffee, bagel, times, and a metrocard</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(11006,2004,'2001-11-02 17:17:23',0,'wb','oh im sorry, i thought somebody on the site actually experienced this. apologies for stealing from a free weekly.',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(11007,2002,'2001-11-02 17:37:58',0,'jack frost','yeah. the snow is coming. dont you fucking worry. ',6,0,0,0,'24.43.182.49','en'),(11008,1984,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','hey le, has anyone ever told you you look like punky brewster?\r\n<br><br>\r\n*best friendly* hee haw',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(11009,2003,'2001-11-02 18:50:13',0,'it\\\'s','skullfucking time.',1,0,0,0,'209.162.48.40','en'),(11010,2004,'2001-11-02 19:48:45',0,'jay','<p>yeah, sorry... it was me. I\\\'ll take the credit. I didn\\\'t feel like it deserved a full post as it wasn\\\'t an original piece, but it did deserve further viewing. </p>\r\n<p>My own horrors only involved getting caught in an awkward position by my Lithuanian grandmother once and having her pull up a chair and say, \\\"Jou play vich yourself?\\\" and then getting up nervously and leaving, having not come up with anything further to say after I denied it.</p>',2,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(11011,1999,'2001-11-02 19:58:58',0,'squishy cheese','and fruit salad',6,0,0,0,'12.146.203.228','en'),(11012,1982,'2001-11-02 20:31:31',0,'Blue Meanie','<img src=\\\"http://www.klangundkleid.ch/img/toys/590340_RingoAndBlueMeanie-Actionfigur-16cm-YellowSubmarine-Beatles-39CHF.jpg\\\"><Br>Meanie! Meanie! Careful, or we\\\'ll sic the <a href=\\\"http://www.klangundkleid.ch/toys/actionfigures/detail.asp?ID=5274\\\">apple bonkers</a> on you!',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.61','en'),(11013,675,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','no, baseball bats!',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(11014,675,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>when i lived in tennessee, my neighbor had a silver el camino with <i>flames</i> painted down the right side. he didnt have enough cash to get the other side done, and mused, for years, that he\\\'d \\\'go back and get it done someday\\\'. thats life. living day by day with only one side of your camino decorated with flames.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.61','en'),(11015,675,'2001-11-02 21:45:16',0,'ice cube','\\\'fresh el camino rollin\\\' kilo g\\\'',1,0,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(11016,2003,'2001-11-02 22:28:07',0,'unamerican','this ad is fucking with your head.',6,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(11017,2004,'2001-11-02 23:37:02',0,'wb','i don\\\'t know what i would do if i got caught by a grandparent. i guess you didn\\\'t roll over and die, so i probably wouldn\\\'t either, but still.',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(11018,2005,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','sine rulz',1,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(11019,1984,'2002-06-27 20:39:15',240,'xep','<br>\r\nmaybe the world is blind or just a little unkind... dunno <br>\r\nseems like you can\\\'t be sure of anything anymore... although <br>\r\nyou may be lonely then one day you\\\'re smiling again <br>\r\neverytime i turn around i see the girl who turned my world around ... standing there<br>\r\neverytime i turn around her spirit\\\'s lifting me right off the ground<br>\r\nwhat\\\'s gonna be? guess we\\\'ll just wait and see\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<bold><blink> PUNKY POWER!!!!</blink></bold>',6,0,0,0,'209.228.7.6','en'),(11020,2005,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','he\\\'s a fish, i\\\'m a crab. what a fantastic love affair.\r\n\r\nswimmy swimmy swish!',1,0,0,0,'64.81.65.178','en'),(11021,2005,'2001-11-03 05:07:12',0,'jo','i know i should be crushing on fish or scorpions but lately i wouldn\\\'t mind a bull around to keep me grounded and set me straight and give me long lectures to which i don\\\'t feel like listening. in other words, it would be nice to have someone around to <b>kick my ass.</b>',0,0,0,0,'172.135.39.44','en'),(11022,2005,'2001-11-03 05:08:16',0,'jo','(oh and snuggle. kick my ass and snuggle.)',0,0,0,0,'172.135.39.44','en'),(11023,2005,'2001-11-03 05:45:05',0,'sinew','by the way, I missed you guys',1,0,0,0,'64.81.65.178','en'),(11024,2005,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter, <i>rereading</i>','<br><tt>wow; this is truly <i>beautiful</i>.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.61','en'),(11025,1992,'2001-11-03 06:52:07',0,'green','i have no job\r\n\r\n67 cents in the bank and no income\r\n\r\nalso i am a packrat and love cilindrical tubes made of cardboard\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,'198.81.17.167','en'),(11026,1982,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>\\\"critic\\\", I\\\'m curious as to what you\\\'re trying to accomplish here. You claim to have some knowledge of my history of debates over matters of taste and appear to think yourself qualified to judge my motivations. If you know me this well, why don\\\'t you feel comfortable using your real name to insult me?</p>\r\n<p>According to your assessment, I\\\'m a \\\"psuedo-intellectual\\\" who \\\"over-intellectualizes\\\" matters that don\\\'t deserve examination in order to \\\"keep [my] wheels spinning.\\\" You also imply that I don\\\'t really want to understand, instead preferring to stroke my ego by getting \\\"flustered up in pretense.\\\"</p>\r\n<p>Without going too deeply into the psychology behind a wildly insulting personal attack posted behind a pseudonym, I have to admit that I am truly baffled.</p>\r\n<p>Perhaps I wasn\\\'t clear enough as to <u>what I want</u>and <u>why</u>. Fuzzy posted a glowing review of a piece of music that seems to be important to him. Apparently, it\\\'s important enough to share with a public audience which is free to comment on it. He suggests that readers \\\"Go buy it, or download it. Or something, just get it.\\\" I <u>did</u> this. I spent time hunting down the mp3s, downloading them, listening to them and then communicating my impressions to him.</p>\r\n<p>Isn\\\'t that what a public discussion forum is about? A person shares something, the others experience it for themselves and then report that experience? Instead, I\\\'ve been showered with accusations and disrespect. I notice that Rachel hasn\\\'t been castigated for sharing her (affirming) experience of this music. I submitted a comment with a differing viewpoint from the author of the article, and people seem really threatened! I\\\'m extremely confused as to why commenting on a post in the \\\"comment\\\" section warrants such a virulent response.</p>\r\n<p>Is swinney.org a one-way street where people write things and nobody is allowed to disagree with them in any way or question them about their beliefs? If you (\\\"critic\\\") really believe this, why even have a \\\"comments\\\" section? So everyone can pat each other on the back and make sexual innuendo? What is the purpose of a discussion forum where people are reviled for.. discussing?</p>\r\n<p><u>Someone</u> in this article certainly is posting in bad faith. I invite readers to examine this article and the comments closely and render their own judgements.</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin \r\n',4,0,0,0,'24.221.170.233','en'),(11027,1982,'2001-11-03 08:30:11',0,'cyantist','along with acronym \\\"DNR\\\", i think we need a new one for \\\"FE\\\", which stands for \\\'flame enabler\\\'.  they are kind of like the peopl e that make you drink when you are an alchoholic.  before entirely reading a post, they immediately get as insulted as possible and cry out to the public, \\\"oh my gosh!  can you believe that he/she said that?\\\"  they are usually the first people to react, yet retreat when other people take the bait and begin to fight or flame.  meanwhile, they look innocent, but they are far from innocent.  usually misunderstandings stem from such people.  i\\\'ve noticed a trend here. <br><br>\r\nFelix the FE has an emotional response to everything posted by someone they don\\\'t like and therefore become irrational and avoid parsing any of that person\\\'s post or email. It\\\'s all over from there.\r\n<br><br>\r\nfor this reason the typical FE is one of the most closed minded, discussion killing individuals on the internet. <br><br>\r\nbut, don\\\'t worry FE\\\'s, just like all disorders.. there is a self-help program for this too.  All you have to do is:\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>sit back and read the entire post and perhaps try to think out of the box by pretending that it is written by someone else.\r\n<li>imagine that people change and evolve over time and aren\\\'t always trying to insult you.\r\n<li>perhaps realizing that sometimes it is *you* that has the problem and not everyone else.\r\n</ol>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\nso if you don\\\'t like my \\\"opinions\\\", please feel free FE to DNR.  thanks.',1,0,0,0,'24.221.170.119','en'),(11028,1982,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','darwin: you know, from your own history online, that the way you state things tends to put people on the defense. so you should know, because you\\\'re an aware human with an ability to learn from historical data, that saying the album seemed \\\"ultimately forgettable\\\" to you, then saying \\\"why does it impress you?\\\" is a challenging way to ask someone why they like something. i read it as <i>prove to me why this album is worth your time, or anyone\\\'s</i>. i\\\'m glad that you\\\'re making an effort to understand other people, or phrase things in the form of an open ended question instead of just saying \\\"dude, that sucks\\\" but in this case, the question was almost more condescending than it would have been if you would have just said \\\"dude, this album sucks, i don\\\'t like it.\\\" at least then it would have been a personal statement of your taste that didn\\\'t really challenge fuzzy to somehow explain to you why he (she?) likes something. with the challenge you seemed to intimate that you were somehow the authority.\r\n <br><br>\r\nalso, i think it\\\'s lame that everytime someone gets grumpy at your for your classically bad ways of trying to stir up some kind of debate or discussion that would be interesting to you, you say \\\"what, no one is allowed to dissent here? we\\\'re all patting each other on the backs here? this is a forum where no one can ask questions?\\\" in your own defense, as if it\\\'s <i>our</i> problem that we don\\\'t do well with your mannerisms of intellectual challenge, when <i>you\\\'re</i> the one who has repeatedly had problems communicating online. over and over when you\\\'re called on a fact about yourself that you know to be true, that fact being that you phrase things in ways that make people feel insulted or challenged, you act like there\\\'s something wrong with the community you\\\'re communicating within. like we\\\'re all nazis: <i>DO NOT ASK QUESTIONS. MOVE ALONG.</i>. it\\\'s an annoying tactic and i officially label that particular argument of yours to be tired and useless now. \r\n<br><br>\r\ni see that you have made steps to understand how better to elicit the constant justification and explanation that you demand from the people around you, but you\\\'re still a long way off from learning how to get that kind of info out of people without them being totally defensive. i don\\\'t think you\\\'re a dick or a bad person, i think you just don\\\'t communicate in ways that other people deal well with, and i think you should either a) get used to these kind of reactions from people and work within that framework (which would mean, not getting upset when people get upset with you) or b) continue thinking about why people often react this way to you, and continue to learn why that is, and work on it. \r\n<br><br>\r\n<tt>[x]</tt> constructive\r\n',3,0,0,0,'207.214.220.247','en'),(11029,2005,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','yay. nice things are nice. yay.',1,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(11030,2004,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','\\\"my friend evan\\\"',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(11031,2005,'2001-11-03 18:27:12',0,'stats','crabs have a unique gift for finding true love in the most unnoticed things. ghost, peter, and jo are all crabs. and now we know sine is too. rock on you beautiful Cancerians. you are a flame for the world.',1,0,0,0,'32.102.91.110','en'),(11032,1982,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>le, you should be a psychiatrist. seriously, that was pretty insightful and complete.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.61','en'),(11033,2005,'2001-11-03 21:39:32',0,'jo','sine and i have the same birthday: july 17. right, is that right? i thought i remembered that.',0,0,0,0,'172.154.34.138','en'),(11034,2005,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','that\\\'s 10 days before my birthday. but i\\\'m no water sign. rrar! hi.',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(11035,2005,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to jo','<br><tt>same birthdays are interesting; kat and i have the same birthday, too. two minutes apart. wow.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.61','en'),(11036,2005,'2002-10-06 17:40:35',261,'sine','july 17, yep. jim is july 16!',1,0,0,0,'64.81.65.178','en'),(11037,2005,'2001-11-04 06:27:56',0,'Garmonbozia','wow. maybe there\\\'s some continuity in this astrology shit after all...!',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.61','en'),(11038,1321,'2001-11-04 07:57:57',0,'kat','<i>sometimes love is just altogether too big to grasp</i>',4,0,0,0,'32.102.64.108','en'),(11039,2007,'2001-11-04 08:01:46',0,'uh,','is this supposed to be satire? if so, you\\\'ve hamstrung it by not providing any context or narrative. it doesn\\\'t go anywhere and doesn\\\'t say anything other than, \\\"ha, aren\\\'t people who practice some religions funny?\\\"',1,0,0,0,'209.208.77.247','en'),(11040,2007,'2001-11-04 08:03:15',0,'dude','you said \\\"ream\\\"',0,0,0,0,'209.208.77.247','en'),(11041,2007,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','I thought L. Ron Hubbard was dead!',1,0,0,0,'65.140.48.180','en'),(11042,2008,'2001-11-04 16:19:55',0,'gay asian raver','yeah, i shaved my head, also, as well-- then dyed it blonde. now i\\\'m told i look like a \\\'gay asian raver.\\\' but also a complete bastard as well.',1,0,0,0,'63.14.201.42','en'),(11043,2005,'2001-11-04 16:51:16',0,'jim','it\\\'s true, I am.  sine, you are sweet to remember.',6,0,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(11044,2008,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','leonard, you are a fucking bastard.',3,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(11045,2010,'2001-11-04 18:30:39',0,'ghost','<i>i am lost in my clothes and noone here will shave me</i>',1,0,0,0,'32.100.71.217','en'),(11046,2007,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>satire... or stoner. this vaguely smacks of the <a href=\\\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1559500409/qid=1004900194/sr=1-2/ref=sr_1_10_2/103-5700306-4425419\\\"><i>Principia Discordia</i></a>... <i>\\\"i am chaos. i am the substance from which your artists and scientists build rhythms\\\"</i>.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.61','en'),(11047,2010,'2001-11-04 19:02:31',0,'','<br><tt>i am covered with throws and no one here will crave me.</yy>\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,1,'66.65.50.61','en'),(11048,2010,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i am covered in throws and no one here will crave me.</tt>\r\n\r\n',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.61','en'),(11049,2008,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>hmm. i saw a swinney.org graffiti in the Pearl art store in chinatown...</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.61','en'),(11050,1984,'2001-11-04 19:06:39',0,'him-a-hymn-unto-HIM','This fight for identity is interesting because I feel that most people my age have very little sense of spirituality.  I know that they will often piece together strings of philosphical thought from Nitche to Derrida couple it with some form of Buddhism (yoga tantric vipasana) and marry it all together with a healthy dose of cynicism.  It\\\'s all contrived like a a Hal Hartley movie. It\\\'s as if we self-consciously manufacture spirituality without having any faith in the spiritual character.  There is nothing wrong with being an actor, but eventually we hit the wall of sincerity and our ego come crashing down. \r\n\r\nIt all boils down to the social need to know, based on our scientific drive to comprehend the world through our five senses; like water droplets collecting on our skin, you feel as if something is there and very tangible, yet it is only there temporarily, set to evaporate upon the moment your attention is distracted.  \r\n\r\nWe are at a distance from our senses. We are at a distance when we try to understand Derrida. We are  a distance when we practise yoga.  How do we close the gap?\r\n\r\nSuspend your disbelief in your un-knowledge. Humble yourself.',2,0,0,0,'24.68.8.198','en'),(11051,1984,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','yes, many people told me i looked like punky brewster when i was a kid. and now, just the other day, jweis accused me of DRESSING like punky brewster. i think. ',4,0,0,0,'209.86.5.4','en'),(11052,1982,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','how about that new tenacious d album?',0,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(11053,1982,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','how about that new tenacious d album?',0,0,0,1,'61.9.128.141','en'),(11054,1982,'2001-11-05 01:36:11',0,'youequals','<img src=\\\"http://www.gee.kz/peter/yc.jpg\\\">\r\n<br>best friendly!',1,0,0,0,'209.86.5.4','en'),(11055,2010,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i am covered in gnomes and no one here will pave me.',4,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(11056,2010,'2001-11-05 03:45:01',0,'green','i am covered in sores and noone here will lay me',0,0,0,0,'198.81.17.26','en'),(11057,2010,'2001-11-05 03:46:49',0,'BrewGuru99','I have big sweaty pores and all of them will drain me',0,0,0,0,'198.81.17.26','en'),(11058,2011,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>im jealous of your nanowrimo writing; you seem to have a good plan. i\\\'m almost finished with mine, and i still have no plot!</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.61','en'),(11059,2011,'2001-11-05 05:31:27',0,'ghost','<i>\\\"i\\\'m almost finished with mine, and i still have no plot!\\\"</i>\r\n\r\n<p>...this sounds like my life.</p>',4,0,0,0,'32.102.91.43','en'),(11060,2011,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','sounds like Thomas Pynchon.',1,0,0,0,'65.140.49.42','en'),(11061,2011,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','there is something wonderful about microsoft word\\\'s word count feature.  im doing nanowrimo too.  i can write much better in microsoft word than emacs.  emacs wants me to be terse and concise.  ms word just wants me to spray characters like a fool.  i am a little behind because i dont have my computer to work on in oakland at egg\\\'s.  i think i have three thousand words.',3,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(11062,2011,'2002-03-05 01:46:04',17,'austin','also, i dont like thomas pynchon.',4,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(11063,2011,'2002-03-08 04:59:53',174,'Mad Moll','I write, or used to write, short fiction. But haven\\\'t lately. But the idea was: short short short. So I don\\\'t nanowrimo. This is also why I too am not a big fan of Pynchon\\\'s biggiesized masterpieces.\r\n\r\nLately I\\\'ve been wanting to write the screenplay for a zombie movie. Not out of any interest in horror, or in movies, but out of a sense of civic duty. I think the zombie movie needs a comeback in a big way.\r\n',6,0,0,0,'24.190.43.87','en'),(11064,2011,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','i love pychon. he\\\'s the friend you listen to ramble on and on and on and he\\\'s brilliant and funny but it gets so overbearing you start ignoring him until he says something REALLY FUCKING BRILLA and then you fall over in astonishment and jealousy. cymbals. and then it\\\'s back to snoozing through all the filler.',2,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(11065,2008,'2001-11-05 08:41:37',0,'leonard to aus','i learned it from watching you, all right?',6,0,0,0,'209.178.128.160','en'),(11066,1982,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>So yeah. I\\\'ve noticed that there are some people who have problems parsing terse statements online. There is, however, a significant number of people who don\\\'t. I think I\\\'ll spend my time talking to <i>them</i> online, and talk to other people offline.</p>\r\n<p>wrt your second point re stifling discussion. I really do feel that people waste stunning amounts of time BSing and couching their words in nonthreatening language online. On the one hand, I should by now be able to remember this, and stay out of discussion venues with low signal-to-noise ratio. I periodically forget, and send a terse post to a forum where someone is likely to react poorly. Like my response to your \\\"snipe\\\" comment, I am often extremely sensitive to having to justify every short statement that someone reads venom into. I admit it, I sometimes react poorly when someone steps up to defend themselves from an attack I\\\'m not actually making. It should be noted, however, that my statements are not the only cause of hysterical hissy fits. As Cyan mentioned, sometimes people just throw hissy fits if they perceive that someone (esp someone they don\\\'t like) is challenging their beliefs in any way. Note that this is not the only reaction that a person can have to this kind of challenge, whether it is real or inferred. </p>\r\n<p>In fact, in <a href=\\\"http://swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=1928\\\">this post</a> I mention that I find music that Peter posted about \\\"mindbogglingly boring.\\\" What was Peter\\\'s reaction? Did he freak out at me for killing his buzz? No! He proceeded to EXPLAIN why he liked his music. In fact, he even sent me an email! We had a nice discussion!</p>\r\n<p>While I\\\'m sure that I could be more non-threatening to people on the Internet, I\\\'m not sure that I care to bother. The vast majority of people I have had functional discussions with online don\\\'t seem to get threatened by me. If I have to spend hours explaining that I\\\'m REALLY REALLY NOT TRYING TO PICK A FIGHT, it\\\'s not worth my time. I\\\'ve been responding to posts in various forms for long enough that I\\\'m <i>tired</i> of flame wars. Text postings (thread style) are so low-bandwidth, I think I\\\'d rather spend the time doing other things.</p>\r\n<p>One last point. People who feel compelled to make snide comments behind fake names in message forums fit <i>my</i> definition of \\\"chump.\\\" It wasn\\\'t impressive when you made a fake account on a BBS in order to talk shit without it reflecting on you, and it isn\\\'t impressive on the web. Regardless of what anyone might think about me, at least I\\\'ll never have to fear being a coward who won\\\'t stand behind his words.</p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n\r\n',3,0,0,0,'24.221.170.233','en'),(11067,1982,'2001-11-05 09:20:15',0,'cyantist','<br>ix: s/how about that new tenacious d album?/how bout them mets?/g.   you are awesome.',0,0,0,0,'24.221.170.119','en'),(11068,2011,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','update. i wrote a thousand more words tonight and i didn\\\'t use my deity scheme at all. i guess i\\\'ll save it for when i run out of ideas. beer helps. ',4,0,0,0,'165.247.220.38','en'),(11069,1982,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to darwin','<br><tt>...ha. and in regard to that conversation: i ended up being exposed to a genre i had glossed over, and now own alot more music that i had been completely unexposed to a few weeks ago. good exchanges benefit everyone involved.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(11070,2011,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','i should write a novel in emacs just to show you it can be done.',0,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(11071,2011,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>or even better yet, write a novel <i>about</i> emacs...</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(11072,2010,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','I always take more showers in the winter because it feels so nice to stand in a hot shower on a cold day.  You don\\\'t drink hot chocolate in the summer, do you?',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(11073,2010,'2001-11-05 14:04:38',0,'critic','i have plenty of foes and noone here will lathe me ',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(11074,2010,'2001-11-05 14:13:26',0,'J.M.','I didn\\\'t fuck Fawn, but I did make out with her before she passed out, at which point I called her boyfriend and had him carry her home.<p>btw, if Fawns bf ever reads this, he\\\'s going to fucking kill me.  I\\\'m so glad I didn\\\'t end up giving her any kind of hickey.  I only ended up with some scratch marks down my chest.</p>',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(11075,2004,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','Laurie burst into my room once after I said, \\\"Just a minute.\\\"  She knocked and waited ever single time from that point on.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(11076,2011,'2001-11-05 14:21:55',0,'jo','beer helps. a lot. god bless shiner bock.<BR>\r\nalso: dear almost finished peter. you\\\'re such a nice guy, i really enjoyed hanging out with you while you were here. BITE ME.',0,0,0,0,'172.146.149.132','en'),(11077,1982,'2001-11-05 14:25:26',0,'jo','i think that\\\'s a tribute to peter\\\'s easy-going good-natured personality. i would have DNRed, myself.',0,0,0,0,'172.146.149.132','en'),(11078,2011,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to jo','<br><tt>i never said it was <i>good</i>; as a matter of fact, its endless pages of senseless babble as my <i>\\\"imposed structure\\\"</i> is to write while under the influence. i read some of it to essemar, and he said something to the effect of \\\"i have <i>no idea</i> what you\\\'re saying, but it sounds pretty\\\".</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(11079,2011,'2001-11-05 15:54:55',0,'jo','oh. right on, then.',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(11080,2011,'2001-11-05 18:04:14',0,'don','<IMG SRC=\\\"http://www.perival.com/delillo/underworld.jpeg\\\">',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(11081,2011,'2001-11-05 18:23:42',0,'jo','as long as we\\\'re talking about weird coincidences of that nature, you should <b>really</b> go watch ryan adams\\\' <a href=\\\"http://www.ryan-adams.com/\\\">new york, new york</a> video, which was taped on september 7 & 8. it\\\'s CREEPY.',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(11082,2005,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','Is aquarius a water sign?  I know the little symbol is a water-carrying dude.  I was born at 8:52pm on Feb 1 1978 in Houston (TX, USA) if anyone wanted to look at my natal chart to see what it says about a mostly-lurking member of the swinney nebula.  :^)',1,0,0,0,'66.25.24.179','en'),(11083,2011,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','Hey, when you all finish the novels you should post them here (or a link to them or something)!\r\n:^)  I think somebody should write a novel in vi about emacs, just to pinch RMS\\\'s hairy goat ass.',1,0,0,0,'66.25.24.179','en'),(11084,2001,'2001-11-05 19:03:12',0,'concerneed citizen','an artist can\\\'t help him/herself. they are a conduit through which the greatest good finds expression. re: cg jung',3,0,0,0,'64.229.144.80','en'),(11085,2005,'2001-11-05 19:23:58',0,'nope','aquarius is air.',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(11086,2001,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','<p>i think the idea of the artist as an exalted guide to the \\\"greatest good\\\" is totally dung. i think an artist should approach her work as a plumber does. cmon people its the year 2001. we know by now that the ability or the \\\"calling\\\" to create is no more a mandate from god than the urge to blow up buildings. its all a lot of passe rhetoric of determinism and jabba jabba. just go about your business and keep your feelers out and make stuff and quit sprinkling 20th century fairy dust all over it.</p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(11087,2015,'2004-07-09 19:12:25',72,'essemar','kat, honey, I understand you.  You should come to NYC, and we\\\'ll dance and sweat and revel in a chemically altered state without sleeping in a city that doesn\\\'t allow it.  We\\\'ll forget about those cruel people who say we don\\\'t love them when we really do, who make us feel not good enough, like we don\\\'t deserve them.  They don\\\'t deserve us!!  We know who we are, and it\\\'s when we allow someone to take our identity away that the hurting really starts.',0,0,0,0,'198.45.19.20','en'),(11088,2016,'2001-11-05 20:41:38',0,'2016','pinko!',1,0,0,0,'209.162.48.24','en'),(11089,2016,'2001-11-05 20:50:30',0,'good ol\\\' moebius','<p>I was out of work from April through September...it helped me psychologically to to tell friends I was \\\"on sabbatical.\\\" And in that respect it was great--I finally chance to taste a bit of the slacker life I\\\'d pretty much given up around \\\'95, when the whole tech gold rush thing started getting in gear.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>My feeling about those job sites is that they\\\'ve mostly become scams in the months since the tech downturn started. I heard reports that Hotjobs continued to post job openings long after they were filled--just so the desperately unemployed would salivate a bit and think their cup was running over with open positions. Sigh.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If I were you I\\\'d give up on most of those jobsites alltogether--or at least take their info w/a grain of salt. You\\\'ll find more reliable information directly at the source--websites of the companies you\\\'d like to work for--and at places like craigslist.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>And at the risk of sounding a bit Rush Limbaugh here, I kind of doubt federalizing the job search sites would solve much. If you think \\\"capitalist bureaucracies\\\" are bad, you\\\'ve clearly not spent enough time at the DMV....</p>',3,0,0,0,'148.87.1.170','en'),(11090,2002,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','OpenGL is <em>cool</em>.',1,0,0,0,'66.25.24.179','en'),(11091,2010,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','You shouldn\\\'t fool around with people that are attached.  It\\\'s downright <em>tacky</em>.',5,0,0,0,'66.25.24.179','en'),(11092,2016,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','the problem of inefficient information dissemination is I think insurmountable, i.e. information distribution in the real world will only asymptotically approach perfection becuase perfect information dispersal mechanisms are presently impossible to fabricate.  this is especially true where some economic gain can be derived from having some iota of information whereas others don\\\'t.  (\\\"we have X jobs site Y doesn\\\'t\\\" \\\"I can get the beans for $Z/Kg when the going rate is Z+1\\\" \\\"grid square FOO has oil under it\\\")  presuming the economic factor is removed, there are still all the ordinary communications inefficiencies (e.g. how do you make sure that the One Big Job Database has every job submitted to it?).  i feel your pain though, searching for jobs sucks.  i\\\'m very lucky to be in a job that\\\'s both semilucrative and very enjoyable.',1,0,0,0,'66.25.24.179','en'),(11093,2008,'2002-10-04 04:15:39',409,'rachel','it really bothers me that people seem surprised when i just fucking change the water bottle myself.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\neven d. expressed surprise the other night when we were making soup and he asked me to get water, and his water cooler was out, so i changed the bottle instead of waiting for him to do it when he got done with making onion cakes. i\\\'m a big girl. i can lift heavy things. why shouldn\\\'t i change the damn water bottle myself?\r\n</p>\r\n',0,0,0,0,'65.200.105.130','en'),(11094,2008,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','i sort of miss office banter',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(11095,1982,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','Well, aren\\\'t we all a bunch of drama queens.<br><br>Okay, Darwin, The Other People Place.  Personally, I enjoy that slow electro-y style.  As I said in the original post, it reminds me a lot of Black Dog Productions\\\' Bytes and I <b>really</b> love that album.  That alone means that anything I find which has a similar sound will be something which I would highly enjoy.  The songs themselves may not be highly memorable in their own right, but the album as a whole gives me a great sense of peacefulness when I listen to it.  It\\\'s a very pleasant feeling album.<br><br>I have to say, though, I am impressed that you downloading some tracks.  I rarely (if ever) check out music that people I don\\\'t know suggest.  Even though I am the kind of person who enjoys learning what kind of music people like and then throwing similar things at them for their enjoyment; if I don\\\'t know a person and they do not know me, I probably wouldn\\\'t enjoy what they\\\'re talking about, unless they mention it is similar to something I already know and enjoy.  Maybe I\\\'ve limited myself to discovering (...being led to...) music I would actually enjoy, but that\\\'s just me.<br><br>Also, I\\\'m a ginormous <a href=\\\"http://www.warprecords.com/\\\" target=\\\"new\\\">Warp</a>nut.  There is not a single release on Warp (that I have so far) which I do not enjoy.  That\\\'s an impressive thing for a music label to accomplish.  Most of my friends are in the same boat with me on that vein of thinking, too.  Warp simply puts out good music.  Perhaps because a lot of us took similar musical paths to what we know and enjoy today, we\\\'re more likely to find certain things interesting for the same reasons.  For someone such as yourself (or anyone else for this matter) who probably did not take the same journey as I did, it might be difficult to understand.  Everyone with more than a casual interest in music makes certain choices and allows themselves to be opened to new styles or variations on styles at certain points.  I know that for a long time I was really into punk and then I started getting into electronic music and there was some overlap.  In April, I went and saw Propagandhi play here in Toronto.  Two weeks before that I was being musically assaulted by the poundings of Aaron and Chris Liberator.<br><br>Diversity.<br><br>I don\\\'t know if this helps at all, but let me know.<br><br>With all the killing and flesh-eating, it looks like we forgot about the love.',3,0,0,0,'64.229.79.200','en'),(11096,1982,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','And just for the record:  <b>briefs</b>.',1,0,0,0,'64.229.79.200','en'),(11097,2015,'2001-11-06 01:05:04',0,'kat','<i>*meow*</i>',1,0,0,0,'32.100.71.221','en'),(11098,2010,'2001-11-06 01:07:19',0,'green to orion and esse','i agree\r\nit is fucking tacky and to do so results in bad karma explosion by your scrotum\r\ntell your furry friends to have fun\r\ni hate chocolate especially milk.\r\n\r\nits all about <B> SOY</B>',4,0,0,0,'198.81.17.182','en'),(11099,2011,'2001-11-06 01:45:19',0,'auntie','i get to be in the book.  there are advantages to spawning le\\\'s from loins.',0,0,0,0,'24.162.119.106','en'),(11100,2011,'2001-11-06 02:57:11',0,'jo','i keep announcing to people that they\\\'re going to be in my book.<BR>\r\nand, while true, most of this is just foreplay for the moment when, on december first (also my friend harley\\\'s birthday, hooray sagittarians!) i declare, \\\"you were <b>so</b> in my novel.\\\"',1,0,0,0,'172.168.171.213','en'),(11101,2015,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter to ess','<br><tt><i>chemically altered states</i> have a knack at taking away your identity also...</tt>',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.61','en'),(11102,2011,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i just realized that my story only has four characters: a Woman in Debt, a Voodoo-Practicing Piece of Trailer Trash, a State Trooper, and Fifth Avenue. my story is quickly digressing into babble. im ruminating regarding continuing with it.</tt> ',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.61','en'),(11103,2010,'2002-10-18 20:39:20',75,'tyler','i fucked her.',1,0,0,0,'65.140.48.116','en'),(11104,2010,'2001-11-06 04:00:51',0,'critic','i wouldn\\\'t fuck her, strictly based on the fact that her name is <i>Fawn</i>.',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.61','en'),(11105,2010,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','remmeber fawn hall',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(11106,2022,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','two things: brian\\\'s brother really DOES work in a school! and, these two have the same eyebrows.',4,0,0,0,'165.247.204.152','en'),(11107,1982,'2002-03-05 20:16:36',214,'darwin','<p>well, I figured if you cared enough to post a message gushing about it, it was worth the listen. I am also a world-class mp3 guy, so it wasn\\\'t too hard to get.. =)</p>\r\n<p>In any case, I can understand where you\\\'re coming from. I admit, it was nice music to take a bath to. I\\\'m not too much of a fan of most downtempo, although I rather like ambient. I think for me, if it\\\'s going to have beats, the beats have to kick. If the beats don\\\'t kick, then I want some good lyrics or singing (dub, hip-hop). So you can probably see why groovy atmospheric electro doesn\\\'t do it for me.. =) Also, I think the only warp music I\\\'ve heard is Autechre (mm) and some Squarepusher albums. It seems like some of those guys are kinda stuck in a rut now, tho. Like the laptop brigade has caught up with them, or something.</p>\r\n<p>I am a huge fan of diversity, which is why I am glad to now have a musical collection which contains more music than I could possibly listen to in the next 20 years. At last count, I have ~250 CDs full of 192k/s mp3s. Even if I listened to them back to back all day every day, it\\\'d still take YEARS to listen to it all. Yet, for some reason, I keep downloading them. I have to say I have heard tons of stuff that I would NEVER have heard otherwise, like a symphony orchestra playing the music from \\\"the legend of zelda\\\" or bootlegs of obscure hiphop acts &c &c &c. In fact, today a guy I know released Johann_Sebastian_Bach_-_The_Complete_Bach_(153cd)_(2000)-HiT2000, which is, as the name indicates, a 153 set of the complete recordings of JS Bach. =)</p>\r\n<p>Thanks for answering my question, proving once more that despite all the computations, you can just dance to that rock n\\\' roll station.</p>\r\n<p><i>Hibbert: Hmmmm. Through the midst of all the killing and skin-eating, somehow we forgot the looovvve.<br>\r\nMoe: Yeah, ain\\\'t that always the way, you get nuts with the skin-eating.</i></p>\r\n<p>\r\n-darwin\r\n\r\n\r\n',2,0,0,0,'24.221.170.233','en'),(11108,2022,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','except my brother is an english teacher and jv football and girls softball coach, not the principal. but still.',0,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(11109,2016,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','you complain about \"capitalist bureaucracy\" and in the same breath argue that <u>more government</u> is the answer? what is the color of the sky in your world?',0,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(11110,2022,'2001-11-06 09:17:11',0,'wb','and the same shape face, the \\\'im a 