merican attitude that caused everyone to hate us in the first place. oh, you nitwit.',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(11181,2029,'2001-11-08 01:03:20',0,'jay','Jeez, you sure are insightful, Fuzzy. Why don\\\'t you take your enlightened and brilliant mind elsewhere, or better yet, go watch a DVD and stop upsetting me with your thoughtless drivel.',6,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(11182,2029,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','yeah, dude, that <i>sucks</i>',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(11183,2029,'2001-11-08 01:12:11',0,'ryan','<a href=\\\"http://www.dack.com/war/\\\">Am I a Terrorist or a Member of Al-Qaeda or a Taliban Fighter or Not?</a>',1,0,0,0,'209.162.48.114','en'),(11184,2029,'2002-10-03 18:45:24',70,'Fuzzy','I guess I\\\'m glad I\\\'m not American, then.  My country is too busy <i>peace-keeping</i> Afghanistan to be bombing the fuck out of them, or something.<br><br>There, perhaps you\\\'d rather enjoy my sterotypical Canadian viewpoint on the matter.<br><br>And thanks to whomever for the graphic.',3,0,0,0,'64.229.79.200','en'),(11185,2029,'2001-11-08 01:29:03',0,'Jean ChrÃ©tien','There are no Canadian \\\"peace-keepers\\\" in Afghanistan.',0,0,0,0,'209.162.48.114','en'),(11186,2029,'2001-11-08 01:52:45',0,'','oh dear. heaven forbid there is someone pro war. i wonder if in 1945 the president would of asked us to send a dollar to the japanese children.',4,0,0,0,'24.27.31.56','en'),(11187,2025,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','i don\\\'t dilute either.  it seems fine, and i don\\\'t feel dried out afterwards.  i use lavender.  mmm.  also, papaya goop by nature\\\'s gate rocks the party.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(11188,2029,'2001-11-08 02:10:42',0,'Cartman','Dude, blame Canada. As a wise man once said, \\\"They know not why they suck.\\\"',4,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(11189,2001,'2001-11-08 02:19:55',0,'Buck','Hi Egg- My name is Buck, how are you? No dung there. My goal was to mention two ways of approaching creative work, and in each way legitmize both. That someone is inherently an artist in a medium is few and far between, and to the outside world is mostly viewed by responses of \\\"when is he/she gonna get a real job?\\\" On the other hand someone who has the day gig as a mailcarrier/neuro surgeon/cook at restaurant may kick themselves and long to be an artist, while creating the best work they can which informs their lives should not be frowned on either, and provides a real service to people already. SHould their work be judged less? Should they kick themselves? Don\\\'t think so. Be well.',3,0,0,0,'209.178.170.30','en'),(11190,2001,'2001-11-08 02:52:47',0,'dear buck','do you realize you\\\'re saying one thing in your post, and another in replies? if this is some kind of article or theory or project you\\\'re working on, you might want to take that into consideration.\r\n\r\n<p>*constructive*</p>',3,0,0,0,'32.102.64.149','en'),(11191,2030,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','losing my passport at the last minute has always been my greatest fear.  last time i flew back to .au from sf, i couldn\\\'t find it anywhere.  s5 and i searched the house up and down, but it was nowhere to be found.  finally it was found next to the shredder under his desk.  coincidence, or cosmic message?',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(11192,2029,'2001-11-08 04:03:45',0,'oh good lord','\\\"would of?\\\" WOULD HAVE. WOULD HAVE. JESUS.',0,0,0,0,'172.155.95.104','en'),(11193,2029,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','hi jo :)',4,0,0,0,'209.86.4.173','en'),(11194,2030,'2001-11-08 04:14:33',0,'jo','elly, i\\\'m the opposite way. i\\\'m so <b>terrified</b> of being in situations like that that i go to ridiculous (in my mind) lengths to prepare against them. for instance, i\\\'m leaving for boston on saturday. and instead of being SUPER FUCKING EXCITED because i get to see STEFAN and KRISTY, two of my best friends in the whole world, i\\\'m angsty and nervous and stupid because travelling means that things are up in the air. well, literally but also figuratively. what if my flight is late? what if i lose my wallet? what if i leave something on the plane? what if i miss the train from providence to boston? all easily remedied things, should they happen, but i worry regardless.<BR>\r\nand then, of course, none of those things ever happen and everything is <b>fine</b>.<BR>\r\nso instead of wasting time by beating myself up because i\\\'ve fucked up, i waste time by WORRYING that i will fuck up. both are ridiculous.<BR>\r\ni wish i could grow up and realize that even when things aren\\\'t completely in my control, completely planned, they\\\'ll work themselves out.',0,0,0,0,'172.155.95.104','en'),(11195,2030,'2001-11-08 04:41:39',0,'ghost','are you sure you wrote this? are you sure it wasn\\\'t me who you were thinking of when you wrote this? hmmmmm....the line IS thin. and i cross it every time.',4,0,0,0,'32.102.109.83','en'),(11196,2030,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','why does s5 need a shredder?',0,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(11197,2030,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','presumably to shred the passports of innocent australians?',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(11198,2030,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','update: i am feeling better since i wrote this. sorry for the outburst. ',0,0,0,0,'209.86.4.173','en'),(11199,2029,'2001-11-08 05:38:35',0,'pogo','are you guys seriously unloading on fuzzy for being first \\\'stereotypically American\\\' and then for being Canadian.\r\n\r\nI\\\'ve met the enemy and he is us.',6,0,0,0,'12.81.84.212','en'),(11200,2029,'2001-11-08 06:56:25',0,'us','we\\\'re unloading on fuzzy, regardless of nationality, because she wrote a dumb post.',3,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(11201,2030,'2001-11-08 06:58:50',0,'chi chi','i\\\'m like jo. i get all freaked out about all the possabilites. anything that could go wrong i worry about. i </i>hate<i> air travel. first it\\\'s the fear, and it\\\'s never nor will be about terrorists, i\\\'m more afraid of mechanical or human error.(my friends all scoff. this is a stupid fear considering how much i do travel by air)(in a recent survey for british airways i determined that in the past 12months i have been on atleast 27 planes) but more than that everything before. do i have/know where the tickets are, my passport (do i need just the american, or do i need the egyptian), do i have a ride? have i packed the right clothes? enough underwear? tooshbrush, contacts, glasses? have mailed in my rent check? did i clean the bathroom? all the dishes? take out the trash?\r\n',0,0,0,0,'64.168.20.1','en'),(11202,2030,'2001-11-08 06:59:33',0,'me','</i>damn',0,0,0,0,'64.168.20.1','en'),(11203,2029,'2001-11-08 07:06:29',0,'chi chi','i don\\\'t feel there was anything wrong with the statement  \\\"sucks to be them\\\". barring nationalities, and who is doing what to whom, it does suck to be them right now. every afghani person is in a position/world/life that i personally hope and pray never to have to face. <br> was he supposed to say \\\"lucky bastards\\\"?',0,0,0,0,'64.168.20.1','en'),(11204,2030,'2001-11-08 07:47:53',0,'auntie','you are not insane.  you are not even on the edge of insane.  everyone feels like they live in a bubble outside of reality, because everyone feels like they are playing a role imposed upon them by circumstances, peer groups, family, money, and some wild media representation of how life SHOULD be.<br><br>\r\n\r\nyou lost your passport.  you flaked out on something you wanted to do, more than once.  oh well, life goes on...<br><br>\r\n\r\ni am a firm believer in karma, god, or some mysterious force with no name.  there is a REASON you didn\\\'t get on the plane today, and someday you will maybe know what that reason is.  maybe not.<br><br>\r\n\r\nin the meantime, go get a new passport, you have cuter hair now than you did in your last passport picture.  take a nap. the people who did you all those favors did them because they love you, and you would do the same for them if the situation were reversed.<br><br>\r\n\r\ndon\\\'t beat yourself up.  learn from mistakes. if you have to make the same mistakes ten times before you learn, oh well, that\\\'s your karma.<br><br>\r\n\r\ni have many mom things to say about this, all of them end with -- i love you, you are not nuts, everything will be alright.',1,0,0,0,'24.162.119.106','en'),(11205,2029,'2001-11-08 08:51:19',0,'ryan','maybe it was just the flippancy of it.  like, oh i got my coffee, and by the way they are dropping these bad ass eight ton bombs on people on the other side of the world that make mushroom clouds even though they aren\\\'t nuclear. <p>\r\nwe\\\'re all doing that, getting our coffee, taking shits, but not all of us write about it and then make a flippant remark about GW\\\'s new war.',0,0,0,0,'209.162.49.188','en'),(11206,2029,'2001-11-08 09:06:51',0,'ryan','fuck you <b>ryan</b>.',0,0,0,0,'209.162.49.188','en'),(11207,2030,'2001-11-08 09:56:15',0,'alana','dude. these things happen. be kind to yourself.',3,0,0,0,'203.212.136.244','en'),(11208,2029,'2001-11-08 12:34:45',0,'critic','<img src=\\\"http://imagem.webphotos.iwon.com/1000017357/1000017357_1031200124620PM0.3895792.jpg\\\">',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(11209,2030,'2001-11-08 17:20:15',0,'wb','elly, this post definitely documents some frustration and i hope you work through it. having known plenty of people with this sort of problem, i believe it\'s one of three possible things:<BR>\r\n1. mental disturbance: chemical imbalance, stress about something that makes you not think about something else, pyschological trauma that distracts.<BR>\r\n2. drugs<BR>\r\n3. choice. (conscious or subconscious). i usually don\'t buy it when people say either they are a creative free spirit who can\'t seem to meet me on time for lunch dates, etc. same as those writers who hold up drinking as a neccesity to write. same goes for this idea of being \"on a different spiritual plane\" than the rest of us. most often it really means \"im too special to deal with the rest of society\'s petty bullshit.\" seems a little spoiled american, \"ET\" for me (if aliens land they will pick my back yard, cos i\'m special syndrome). the drunk writer, the absent minded \"free spirit\" is all too cliche\'d. i\'d hate to link swinney to this page, soil our fine web site, but it makes some sense for <A HREF=\"http://www.oprah.com/phil/advice/phil_advice_lateness.jhtml\"> the \"choice\" of being flakey</A>\r\n\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nand oh yeah i found this on the internet and i can\'t believe this guy painted this painting in 1989!:\r\n<IMG SRC=\"http://www.beatthief.com/images/passport.jpg\">. ',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(11210,2030,'2002-03-08 04:50:11',86,'egg','oh wayne, you and your tough love.',0,0,0,0,'66.47.229.243','en'),(11211,2032,'2001-11-08 17:54:44',0,'Dwayne Schneider','<p>Well son, let me tell ya...i aint no Gary Snyder, but the name sounds kinda the same so i thought it might be okay to write a little note. What ya need son is a good friend who\\\'ll give ya an ass whuppin now and then, along with some beer drinkin. There aint nothin like praying at the god of porcelain while havin someone there to tell ya you deserved every bit of it. Anything but beer and yer just foolin yerself. All the rest is just for sissies who can\\\'t stand to face the wrath...and that\\\'s what you need to do. Face the wrath, no matter how good or how bad. You just gotta face it and then git out the door and go to work. Nothing wrong with an honest days trade. Somebody\\\'s gotta work the plumbin and fix the pipe.<p>\r\n\r\n<p>...oh yea, and when yer lonely just come on by my <a href=\\\"http://www.patharrington.com\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">website</a>. I\\\'ll share a joke or two with ya.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>[X] best friendly</p>',1,0,0,0,'32.102.109.65','en'),(11212,2032,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','hey bmg.  what\\\'s going on?  is it cold as fuck in austin yet?',2,0,0,0,'66.13.23.218','en'),(11213,2032,'2001-11-08 18:31:21',0,'jo','it is not cold as fuck yet. i went swimming on sunday. the water was cold but, according to two kids who just spent 4 years in new hampshire, no colder than how the water is in the northeast in the middle of the summer.',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(11214,2030,'2001-11-08 18:44:34',0,'jo','<p>so, um. here\\\'s a story.</p>\r\n<p>two years ago, my best friend lost complete control of his life. he was an insomniac and when he did sleep, it was either restless or it was hard as a rock - he slept for 10 and 12 hour stretches and had a hard time waking up.</p>\r\n<p>he had a really hard time making it to his classes so he started failing them despite the fact that he knew more about some of these subjects than his professors did.</p>\r\n<p>he worked for his parents in his hometown half an hour away and frequently was between an hour to three hours late to work. he was dating me, and i was living in a town 45 minutes away, and was over an hour late every time he came to visit me. two times that he was supposed to visit me, he fell asleep and my worried phone calls didn\\\'t wake him, so he effectively stood me up.</p>\r\n<p>and at the time i thought it was just him. that he was flaky and unreliable and that was just part of who he was.</p>\r\n<p>two years later, he\\\'s moved away. he manages a coffeehouse where he pulls 10 and 12 hour shifts, happily showing up at 6 AM some mornings to open up. he\\\'s uber-responsible.<BR>\r\nhe called me last week to tell me that he had to fire someone because she was coming into work late and had missed a shift and i nearly reeled from the irony.</p>\r\n<p>so what i\\\'m saying is this: maybe he finally found something that he cared about. maybe he finally got in an environment where he was challenged and where he knew that if he fucked up, there would be no apologies, no chance to fix things.</p>\r\n<p>i don\\\'t know, it\\\'s just a story. but this got me thinking.</p>\r\n<p>[x] constructive</p>',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(11215,2016,'2001-11-08 18:45:27',0,'wb','there is a nationalized job board for government jobs. <BR><BR>\r\ni found this part of the post amusing:<BR>\\\"what i have found in my journeys to the many sites out there is that there is so much redundancy. the \\\"job site\\\" scene is bloated and full of redundant information. \\\"',0,0,0,0,'216.103.215.241','en'),(11216,2030,'2002-03-08 04:52:53',65,'le','i just came back from the passport office! i will have a new passport for tomorrow. i rebooked the airline tickets too. everything is ok.\r\n<br><br>\r\n',4,0,0,0,'165.247.216.221','en'),(11217,2030,'2001-11-08 19:24:41',0,'jo','HOORAY! YAY AUSTRALIA!',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(11218,2030,'2001-11-08 19:50:40',0,'australia','HOORAY! YAY LEPETER! ',1,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(11219,2001,'2001-11-08 19:58:54',0,'Buck','It would be odd if your name was Deer Buck, but anyway,i am aware of that, it is work in progress yeah? that is the reason why i brought it here, to see if it has a good beat and people can dance to it, and trusting the wise folks of swinney to help me work the kinks out. I have also added a better intro using a metaphor about life on an aircraft carrier... thanks much. ',0,0,0,0,'209.178.171.99','en'),(11220,2030,'2001-11-08 20:07:01',0,'drew','<p>travel papers.  argh.  once we nearly couldn\\\'t go to san diego because margaret couldn\\\'t identify herself adequately by the standards of the fuckhead airlines.  i keep telling myself i\\\'m going to gather up that sort of stuff and put it in one place.  someday i might.</p>\r\n<p>sleep.  i hate insomnia.  i\\\'ll deprive myself of sleep rather than risk it.  this may sound stupid and bow-tie but try setting an alarm for when you want to get up.  make it superloud and put it in the farthest corner from your bed.  no matter when you go to sleep, get up when it goes off and don\\\'t go to bed again until 8 -- or 9 -- hours before the appointed time.  if you do this for a few days and avoid caffeine and sugar too close to bedtime (eek!  i KNOW!) your body should accept the abuse and behave.</p>\r\n<p>but i agree with your most excellent mom that we all feel that alien-on-earth thing to some degree, or at least all the \\\"we\\\" you would want to know about.  i feel it right now more than ever, now that i don\\\'t have to pretend every day that i\\\'m some kind of mad technobusiness archon.</p>\r\n<p>have a good trip.  i hope i\\\'m here when you get back.</p>',0,0,0,0,'65.12.14.45','en'),(11221,2025,'2001-11-08 22:41:57',0,'me to egg','where do you get dr bronners?',2,0,0,0,'207.189.39.18','en'),(11222,2025,'2001-11-08 22:54:49',0,'at','hippy stores yo.',0,0,0,0,'209.162.48.88','en'),(11223,2032,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','ah, Barton Springs?  burrrrr*shiver*',0,0,0,0,'66.13.23.218','en'),(11224,2030,'2001-11-08 23:09:11',0,'drew','forgot to mention...cats are very good for waking you up earlier than you want them to.  especially the kind that bite your toes when they\\\'re hungry or want to play.',0,0,0,0,'65.12.14.45','en'),(11225,2033,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','i wish i could hire you at this magazine.',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(11226,2033,'2001-11-08 23:52:30',0,'oh, that\\\'s right','nobody cares.  HM.  what am i, chopped liver?',0,0,0,0,'63.110.193.71','en'),(11227,2033,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','what huh',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(11228,2033,'2001-11-09 00:08:59',0,'lou to simon','hire me! hire me! yes!',1,0,0,0,'216.175.68.86','en'),(11229,2033,'2001-11-09 00:09:16',0,'lou to chopped liver','that\\\'s right, bitch. step UP.',4,0,0,0,'216.175.68.86','en'),(11230,2033,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','where do you work now?',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(11231,2030,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','huzzah!',0,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(11232,2030,'2002-09-05 18:42:54',18,'ix','is that drew from avantgo?',0,0,0,0,'61.9.128.141','en'),(11233,2026,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','egg: is that a russian folk tale?  (I had to read &lt;&lt;Masha i Myedvyed&gt;&gt; in russian 2, which apparently is like the canonical russian folk tale (\\\"Masha and the Bear\\\" for those of you in the audience that don\\\'t speak pa-rooski).)',1,0,0,0,'66.25.24.179','en'),(11234,2033,'2001-11-09 01:01:19',0,'lou','tor books. and really, to be honest, it\\\'s a fabulous gig and i love it there. i\\\'m just unsatisfied, on the whole, with the grunt work.',4,0,0,0,'216.175.68.86','en'),(11235,2029,'2002-03-04 07:14:25',185,'orion','the mushroom cloud pattern is hardly unique to nuclear weapons or big ass conventional ones.  has to do with the pressure/temperature dynamics IIRC, even small explosions will make a little mini-mushroom.\r\n\r\n<p>  wrt \\\"sucks to be them\\\", well, life sucks in that part of the world.  real bad.  nothing particularly new about that.  ideally, after we get through with our retaliatory mud moving, we\\\'ll try to make life a little better there by reconstructing a functioning physical and governmental infrastructure.  foreign sovereignty? blow me: www.rawa.org  societies that don\\\'t respect the basic rights of their citizens on that scale deserve to be externally unfucked.  [China (tibet) and Isreal (palestine) are two other countries that IMNSHO deserve a big american boot up their ass.]  foreign sovereignty is another way of saying that countries and cultures are more important than individual humanity.',4,0,0,0,'66.25.24.179','en'),(11236,2030,'2001-11-09 01:10:56',0,'erbie','<p>believe me, going to a shrink is just as hard as any other responsible act.  last night i skipped, and i left her this long message saying, uh sorry, you know how i am, i don\\\'t feel well, i don\\\'t have the energy to deal with my idiosyncrasies today, etc etc etc.  felt pretty awful about it for around 2 hours.  then as i was in the shower i pictured myself counseling someone many years down the road, and saying understandingly, ah yes.  when i started therapy it was like pulling teeth to get me to go.  i hated it.  every week i ground my teeth as i rode up that damn hill.  some weeks i flaked and stayed home and watched tv instead and sent the therapist guilty checks enclosed in arty greeting cards.  i understand.  i understand.</p>\r\n<p>you know when you\\\'re paying your therapist to give you some peace and quiet, you really need some time to yourself.  she left me a message today and i haven\\\'t listened to it yet.</p>',1,0,0,0,'64.105.32.155','en'),(11237,2033,'2002-09-16 21:29:19',82,'simon','hang in there, pal, it\\\'ll get better.',0,0,0,0,'63.195.92.218','en'),(11238,2033,'2001-11-09 01:14:26',0,'lou','ha. ha. ha. ahaha.',6,0,0,0,'216.175.68.86','en'),(11239,2033,'2002-09-01 23:16:03',57,'weeb','since you\\\'re getting paid to show up, why don\\\'t you just work on your own shit on company time? write that novel, steal their resources for something- they must have lots of stuff you can play with. maybe you can take a course online. maybe you can sneakily start doing other work and then demand a promotion. with all that time, i\\\'m sure you can think of something.',1,0,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(11240,2033,'2002-03-05 20:15:16',59,'s5','i\\\'m with weeb. do things on your own that will expand what you know and what you can do, especially things within the context of your career. make better use of your time; give yourself a promotion. failing that, masturbate more often in the company restroom. or daytrade.',3,0,0,0,'65.84.40.62','en'),(11241,2033,'2001-11-09 02:36:05',0,'leonard','it could be worse... management could be aliens that worship a guy who used to wear a captain\\\'s hat. ',1,0,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(11242,2029,'2001-11-09 03:43:53',0,'critic','hah. i make a fuckin mushroom cloud every time i smoke trees.',1,0,0,0,'66.65.50.61','en'),(11243,2033,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>ahh, work: the place where i do private web-work and get paid more than i do for my actual job there; the place that i can steal.. er, <i>appropriate</i> snazzy new tech gear. i love work,