NGELFIRE! DAMN YOU TO HELL!',0,0,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(13257,2275,'2002-01-21 15:52:29',0,'coke-whore','i <i>adore</i> snow also.',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(13258,2274,'2002-01-21 16:29:04',0,'blue stocking','what i really really can\\\'t stand is being forced to listen to really bad music in an enclosed space e.g. being inside a bus shelter in -20C weather, with someone listening to their discman so loud the panes of glass are shaking, and they always have bad taste. always. <scream>',0,0,0,0,'216.191.251.36','en'),(13259,2274,'2002-03-08 04:52:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>thats probably because those of us with good taste in music also have the social tact to not crank the volume up so high, heh. i have noticed, though, that alot of us urban folks like the volume boost as it drowns out the cacophony of commuters arguing, amateur lyricists freestyling on the subway, and crack-thugs fighting on the corner.  in that regard, im considering <a href=\"http://www.sonystyle.com/computing/prd.jsp?pid=350\">these</a>. i tried them out at the sony world store here, and they do rock.</tt>',1,0,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(13260,2246,'2002-04-20 20:49:51',273,'Quinn Skylark','I really, really like Aquavit.  Especially ice cold. It\\\'s probably the best clear liquor I\\\'ve ever had.  Only I can\\\'t get my hands on it as often as I like.  My local liquor store doesn\\\'t carry it and I\\\'m forced to go out of the way, and get it from a store that\\\'s far from the subway.  Then its a trudge back from the store to the Orange line, where I can finally get the bottle home.  But I like Aquavit, I like the caraway/rye taste---it makes me think of smoked fish and statuesque blonde women.  What could be better than that?',0,0,0,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(13261,2246,'2002-01-21 18:34:40',0,'better, maybe...','statuesque women that smell like fish?',1,0,0,0,'24.29.138.17','en'),(13262,2274,'2002-01-21 18:57:19',0,'drew to peter','i had a very specific band in mind with my transsexual freaks from manhattan phrase: fischerspooner.  in case it wasn\\\'t clear, i too know and listen to much better music than craig david.  i simply don\\\'t delude myself that most people share my opinions on the matter, or will realistically be likely ever to do so.',0,0,0,0,'65.12.14.45','en'),(13263,2280,'2002-01-21 18:59:28',0,'Scapegoat','<p>There is something about bunkering down with your signifigant other during an Ottawa winter that can\\\'t be beat.</p> ',1,0,0,0,'64.229.168.200','en'),(13264,2274,'2002-01-21 19:19:45',0,'ryan','what\\\'s good taste?',0,0,0,0,'209.162.48.143','en'),(13265,2278,'2004-08-24 18:01:43',83,'adamajah','<p>i saw BHD last night and was a little disappointed.  cinematography, sets, action, and even acting, was pretty darn good.  however, the movie was a big mess.  there was no sense of accomplishment, which might have been realistic, but makes for a bad feature.  i went in expecting an even better, more graphic, Saving Private Ryan - which is what people were telling me it was, but it wasn\\\'t.</p> \r\n<P>there was a build up, but no climax - just \\\"i\\\'m going back in!\\\", \\\"let\\\'s get outta here!\\\", \\\"i\\\'m going back in!\\\", \\\"let\\\'s get outta here!\\\", over and over again.</p>\r\n<p>and yes, if ridley wanted to portray the event with more honesty, it should have been more graphic, showing how grown men weren\\\'t the only victims and participants in the raid.</p>\r\n<p><b>the movie was executed with indecision - there was no real commitment to realism or entertainment.  ridley, make up your mind!</b></p>   ',0,0,0,0,'66.13.23.218','en'),(13266,2282,'2003-03-07 17:56:26',69,'starlajo','In August/September 1991 when I was 10 going on 11, I stayed in a hotel in Buena Park, that was opposite Knotts Berry Farm.  We had fun.  I liked the roller coasters.\r\n\r\nPeople asked us if we were from Australia and I would screw my face up and say \\\"No! New Zealand!\\\"',2,0,0,0,'210.54.242.102','en'),(13267,2280,'20