e reads this site. better than family reading it.</tt>',1,162,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(14321,2420,'2002-02-19 12:19:31',66,'Peter','<br><tt>love is the act of pulling pubes from between your front teeth.</tt>',1,76,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(14322,2419,'2002-02-19 12:22:53',66,'Peter','<br><tt>today my neighbor came by from across the hall; she\\\'s a painfully hip girl with the little glasses and kate spade shoulder-bag. she has a puppy Bichon that she walks on a pink string, and was complaining that said dog had repeatedly soiled her Ikea sisal carpeting.  standing at my door, looking in, she said <i>\\\"i wish my place was more like yours... nothing between your feet and the bare floors except dirt\\\".</i> oddly, i think she meant it as some kind of compliment.</tt>',1,493,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(14323,2422,'2002-02-19 13:11:13',65,'le','blotter\\\'s been hard to find lately, period. i think making acid is out of style.',0,83,0,0,'216.27.183.161','en'),(14324,2422,'2002-02-19 13:19:53',66,'Peter','<br><tt>maybe some young entrepeneur with an owsley-ish soul will come along and tap into what must be a huge demand.</tt>',1,122,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(14325,2431,'2002-02-19 14:21:07',67,'trouble','lotus, i\\\'m so happy you found swinney.  this was another great piece.',1,72,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(14326,2429,'2002-02-19 14:31:14',67,'trouble','admittedly, i\\\'ve had difficulty getting into your style of writing javorai.  i guess it\\\'s just my contention that to really <i>feel</i> or enjoy poetry you must be open to any interpetation of what the author is conveying and i just haven\\\'t been open enough.  <i>this piece connected though</i>.  kudos.  i need to go back and check out your other stuff, maybe i can see something different.',1,400,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(14327,2420,'2002-02-19 14:38:19',67,'trouble','love is the act of laying still afterwards.  opting to clean each other like monkeys <i>later.</i>',1,98,0,0,'216.82.34.12','en'),(14328,2429,'2002-02-19 14:44:19',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i like poetry; ive always had trouble getting on target with interpretations, though. i think it had to do with a kooky teacher i had in high school, who taught us to all find bizarrely interesting imagery in poems. now, its as if i subconsciously search for the most sordid or devious interpretation possible, by default. im a <i>poetry lech</i>!</tt>',1,360,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(14329,2419,'2002-04-20 20:49:51',273,'Quinn','le, very nice piece...\r\n\r\n<p>Our upstairs neighbors used to be so quiet, but they recently had a baby and now they bang around up there all the time.  I don\\\'t know exactly why a baby changes how their feet impact the floor, but it has changed up there.  \r\n\r\n<p>They drop things now.  Big booming sounds come through the floor at strange hours.  Often they move something with metal wheels because they grind on the hardwood floor.  \r\n\r\n<p>I\\\'m not the complaining type.  I\\\'ve lived in some pretty crappy conditions, so a little neighborly noise isn\\\'t going to kill me, so let \\\'em be noisy up there.  It really isn\\\'t THAT  bad.\r\n\r\n<p>But the odd thing is that they never made significant noise before.  When Mrs. Skylark and I  moved in, they told us \\\"if we ever get to loud, just let us know and we\\\'ll try to keep it down.  Nice neighbors!  But we never heard anything more then an occasional footfall.  Nonetheless, whenever we\\\'d meet them on the stairs, \\\"If we ever get to loud...\\\"  and we\\\'d tell them that we never hear them.\r\n\r\n<p>But we hear them now.  I don\\\'t know what it is about having a baby that can make a couple walk more heavily on the earth, but our upstairs neighbors surely do.',0,1232,65,0,'198.185.18.207','en'),(14330,2420,'2002-02-19 15:41:53',74,'jo','thank you all for getting me thinking about oral sex at 9:40 AM on a work day.',0,78,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(14331,2420,'2002-02-19 15:54:08',66,'the male mind to jo','welcome to the male mind, 24/7, jo! :)',1,38,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(14332,2420,'2002-02-19 16:26:15',74,'jo','you guys must get tired. because i was thinking about what a good band mates of state is and how much i like black tea and this email i\\\'m writing to my friend and this work i have to get done before lunch and all of a sudden BAM! oral sex. and it\\\'s amazing how much harder it is to multi-task when you have lovin\\\' on the brain.',0,336,0,0,'216.141.109.62','en'),(14333,2420,'2002-02-19 16:28:52',66,'another male','and its harder to actually get that shit done when you have a raging hard on. yuck.',1,83,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(14334,2431,'2002-02-19 16:35:48',156,'lotus','i\\\'m still sort of dizzy, but i love it here! you should thank my friend hool for introducing me to swinney. btw, i went back and read all your articles, and God, i got totally caught up in your words. you are so expressive and vivid!',0,236,67,0,'216.191.251.36','en'),(14335,2420,'2002-02-19 16:55:31',123,'dcc','at least when you\\\'re sitting down you can get *some* things done when you\\\'re cock is talking sex time. aren\\\'t you glad you have that great desk job now? you can think about getting laid all day and no one will be the wiser. well, except everyone on here ...',3,266,0,0,'204.92.73.229','en'),(14336,2420,'2002-02-19 17:38:03',185,'orion','for some reason I\\\'m reminded of the Wolf chili commercials.  (\\\"How long since you\\\'ve gotten laid?  WELL THAT\\\'S TOO LONG!!!\\\")  And yes, I\\\'m a guy and thoughts of sex or boobies or something like that are usually not too far from the front of my mind... :-)  Like there\\\'s anything <i>wrong</i> with that.\r\nAs far as going downtown, I think the key point is SOAP and WATER, for both genders.  And, well, you don\\\'t have to take that shower alone...',1,468,0,0,'66.25.24.179','en'),(14337,2425,'2002-02-19 17:41:25',176,'Scapegoat','Similar feelings abound this was one of my most recent entries on my site - <br><br>\r\n\r\nEngines are starting to burn again as I recapture an older sense of self, one that is my most powerful incarnation to date. Here\\\'s to being able to let go of      everything and the power that ability brings. \r\n',0,302,0,0,'64.229.167.194','en'),(14338,2420,'2002-02-19 17:42:44',185,'orion','speaking of inexplicable wood, and this is something I\\\'ve confirmed happens to other people, what\\\'s up with the Calculus Woody?  Namely the wood you get about 40 minutes into an hour calculus lecture.  Your classmates are all unappealing nerds, your professor is an incomprehensible chinese gnome, wtf?  What is there about partial derivatives that merits this?  Strangely, it only happened to me in calculus, once I started taking the higher maths (linear algebra, diff-eq, etc.) it went away.  My theory is that your body is trying to remind you that you aren\\\'t dead from boredom, and the higher maths provoked enough of a fear response in me to not need this.',1,671,0,0,'66.25.24.179','en'),(14339,2435,'2002-02-19 17:49:28',185,'orion','heh.  i have like four pairs of black jeans that are currently, shall we say, not up to the task of containing a man of my substance.  (I used to be 5\\\'11\\\" and 130 pounds, now I\\\'m more like 6\\\'0\\\" and 240.)  Actually I think I may have given those all away now.  I mean, I think I can probably get back down to 36 or so (from 40) but the only way I\\\'d hit 31/32 again is if my kidney died (again), and that doesn\\\'t seem like an acceptable tradeoff. ;-)  It takes at least a year for a pair of jeans to get really good,\r\nmuch like a pair of boots.',1,563,0,0,'66.25.24.179','en'),(14340,2420,'2002-02-19 17:52:20',66,'Peter','<br><tt>calculus (with the possible exception of the <i>fourier transform</i> and <i>finite element analysis</i>, of course) generally failed to get me i nthe mood. i think it has something to do with boredom, though. when surrounded by utterly bland banality, whats better to get the old wheels a-movin\\\' than a little debaucherous fantasizing?</tt>',1,352,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(14341,2435,'2002-02-19 17:54:50',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i, myself, am hurting for cool shirts. i will gladly dip into my surplus of pants for anyone willing to cough up a shirt or two.</tt>',1,141,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(14342,2434,'2002-02-19 17:54:59',185,'orion','illegal loft?',1,13,0,0,'66.25.24.179','en'),(14343,2434,'2002-02-19 18:01:13',176,'Scapegoat','<b>\\\'Olde English\\\'</b> reading those words makes my head hurt, and as I remeber that experience did take place in a rent controlled hovel.',0,143,0,0,'64.229.167.194','en'),(14344,2434,'2002-02-19 18:01:47',82,'simon','hahahahahaha. it\\\'s so true.',0,30,0,0,'198.136.186.46','en'),(14345,2434,'2002-02-19 18:05:15',66,'illegal loft','hi. im a cool, cheap place to live that resides in an industrially zoned warehouse. i have no bathroom or kitchen, short of whatever you rig or splice from the existing services. i am generalyl serviced by sketchy freight elevators. i am in the part of town youre fraid to walk in at night. acdcording to city ordinances, i am illegal to live in.',1,346,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(14346,2434,'2002-02-19 18:09:13',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i love my rent-control hovel, however, the call of post-9/11-vacated lofts of dubious legality is rather strong. if i move, i will have to schlep two (2) 64oz. bottles of OE and more house compliations than you can shake a stick at.</tt>',1,245,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(14347,2434,'2002-02-19 18:16:42',66,'The Midtown Party Pack','<br><br><b>The <i>Midtown</i> Party Pack:<br>\r\n<i>conspicuously shipped in a faux-sharkskin briefcase:</i><br>\r\n<UL TYPE=\\\"square\\\">\r\n<LI>car service\r\n<LI>co-op inherited from parents\r\n<LI>dental dams\r\n<LI>herbal ecstacy\r\n<LI>6-pack of Corona\r\n<LI>J. Lo Remix cd\r\n</UL><br><br>',1,281,0,0,'204.168.247.48','en'),(14348,2434,'2002-02-19 18:16:47',82,'simon','hey old pal, i lived in you for a couple years in williamsburg unt