ge',2,75,0,0,'144.132.122.131','en'),(19107,3151,'2002-11-19 02:42:54',124,'gus','this is SF we walk a lot here. \r\n<p>\r\naustin, you are funny. I will go ride with the boys next time, even I do weigh them down. ',0,128,0,0,'64.163.213.252','en'),(19108,3152,'2002-11-19 06:06:11',65,'le','that is really fucked up.',0,25,0,0,'216.27.183.162','en'),(19109,3152,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','i saw you there about 10 minutes after.  you were wearing your new domini dress.',6,80,65,0,'64.81.243.3','en'),(19110,3152,'2002-11-19 13:27:10',65,'le','weirder. i guess eve and i walked by. we were on our way to get produce for some extravagant thai dish eve plans on. ',0,117,0,0,'216.27.183.162','en'),(19111,3151,'2002-11-19 22:35:29',74,'jo','walking home is THE best way to sober up.',0,41,0,0,'146.6.172.208','en'),(19112,3151,'2002-11-20 16:02:19',66,'Peter','<br><tt>taking a cab sure isnt, thats for sure, heh. especially when youre really faded and the cabbie dumps you out on the back of some random hill, a mile from your destination, in the middle of the night in SF, claiming \\\"my shift is over!\\\" ugh!</tt>',1,258,74,0,'204.168.247.130','en'),(19113,3148,'2002-11-21 00:16:25',64,'Joanna','\\\"Was I drunk?\\\" is my favourite line in the world to use.  \r\n\r\nThat and \\\"I like bears\\\". ',1,99,0,0,'130.216.131.85','en'),(19114,3155,'2002-11-21 04:28:11',17,'austin','i have a similiar problem with michael jackson.  today i thought i saw him dangling a babby out of a 4th story hotel balcony.',0,125,0,0,'64.2.58.24','en'),(19115,3155,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','when you visit, i\\\'ll let you use his toothbrush.',6,51,0,0,'64.81.243.3','en'),(19116,3152,'2002-11-21 05:39:19',175,'Paul G','<p>Melissa is one of the best women that I know.  As a girl, she was homeless for quite a while; she lived in a car with her mother and siblings.  She never finished high school; she got a G.E.D.  She started working for the State, in Corrections.  She had a child; the father isn\\\'t around now.  She\\\'s still a cop, and a good one too.  She found a way to preserve her womanhood in an environment that is dominated by really aggressive males - in both orange and also blue.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Sometimes it strikes me that there isn\\\'t too much difference between the profiles of all the people who are at the margins of civil society - or who are actually outside of it.  The people who are homeless, or members of criminal organizations, or working in criminal justice, or who are involved in the arts - or even prostitution, they all are the same, in a way.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\\"Outsider\\\" is a term that gets bandied about a lot by rather lame individuals who spend their entire lives padding around on carpeting under artificial light.  But, there\\\'s something to the idea that - for some of us - what we are, or who we are, forces us towards unconventional modes of being.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The shooter and the one who was shot are both where they are because in some way they are expendable.  I think.</p>',0,1298,0,0,'66.19.51.149','en'),(19117,3155,'2002-11-21 07:02:51',176,'Scapegoat','Based on some pictures I have been shown I thought I saw Austin chilling at the Rivoli here in Toronto last month. Perhaps he is everywhere all at once.  ',0,154,0,0,'65.95.140.108','en'),(19118,3155,'2002-11-21 08:09:24',124,'gus','I see austin swinney everywhere I go. Last night he was at the bar drinking beer and whiskey, the day before he was walking out of a house on ramona street, ignoring me as I walked past him with my groceries. a day before that he was on a motorcycle ride with my boyfriend.\r\n<p>\r\nIt might be because he moved in around the corner, but who can be sure. it\\\'s a real mystery.',0,375,0,0,'64.172.57.94','en'),(19119,3155,'2002-11-21 11:18:34',64,'Joanna','Are you comparing yourself to Michael Jackson? ',1,47,17,0,'203.97.2.243','en'),(19120,3155,'2002-11-21 12:41:11',93,'chiamattt','ive never seen austin swinney. i did see jesus once, but that was a long time ago in a land far far away. the gospel according to chiamattt.',6,140,0,0,'61.37.53.62','en'),(19121,2849,'2002-11-21 12:42:45',93,'chiamattt','ive heard that bad spelling is a sign of genious. ',1,50,0,0,'61.37.53.62','en'),(19122,3155,'2002-11-21 14:48:27',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i thought i saw austin driving a tugboat down the east river the other day. actually, i didn\\\'t really think that... but, how cool would it be if austin had a secret tugboat-driving alter ego?</tt>',1,207,0,0,'204.168.247.130','en'),(19123,3154,'2002-11-21 18:44:55',195,'matt','you said it, mama',1,17,0,0,'209.208.108.241','en'),(19124,3155,'2002-11-21 21:32:46',64,'Joanna','And in an update, this morning I dreamt I DID go visit s5 and o, in San Francisco which was actually Hamiltron - a terrible sub city here in NZ - and I went to a party filled with Swinneyites (except none of them were real people from here) and one guy was tottering around off his tits on cocaine, and ended up overdosing, and people tried to shock him awake and they used so much electricity that they ended up setting his body on fire. It was really very very horrible and traumatic. \r\n\r\nMoral of the story is: Please kids, don\\\'t do drugs if I ever make it to San Fran.',1,575,0,0,'130.216.131.85','en'),(19125,3143,'2002-11-21 23:00:49',416,'Taxman','Candy rules.',1,12,0,0,'207.28.199.1','en'),(19126,3154,'2002-11-21 23:15:45',366,'eunoia','Your article made me sick, I mean it could have made me spew. I am so sensitive about sex right now. Things didn\\\'t work out with the last one, the last one who made me crazy, she has a borderline personality disorder, my cousin said. But still I could give her many orgasms without even trying. Committment became scary for her. I felt like this whole sex war thing became turned around in front of me, as I was the sensitive one who wanted some attachment to emotion and caring and she was the cold mechanical one who just wanted a good fuck and nice dinner made for her. We remain really good friends, but my current relationship I just use as something to quiet down my own pain. I hate this feeling of rejection that is associated with love, this shame, this weird self-image. Love is not free, but sex is cruel and cold. I guess I thought it was something different, but really it\\\'s just a bunch of nerve-endings set a blaze. Is life just a grab-bag? yours to take advantage of, or are there people who still just want to be together because they feel right? I feel like the older I get the smarter I get the more cold and unfeeling I get. I think about sleeping with whores more everyday, why not, that way I don\\\'t have to feel to achieve satisfaction. If I only had the bankroll and big hunfry teeth and scars on my back to prove my manhood...',1,1359,0,0,'193.167.219.184','en'),(19127,3155,'2002-11-22 00:17:15',195,'matt','that would be me, the one on the <B><I>ko-kaine</B></I>',1,55,0,0,'209.208.111.99','en'),(19128,3157,'2002-11-22 02:30:50',176,'Scapegoat','I can relate to the sentiment of this letter',0,44,0,0,'65.95.140.108','en'),(19129,3157,'2002-11-22 19:45:49',427,'hopper','<p> Of course (and knowing her, after sending the letter, I realized she  \r\nwould)  she got hung up at the whole concept of \\\"ticket\\\". </p>\r\n\r\n<p> The unavoidable, and unfortunate, truth of such a situation is that\r\nmost people who can see the stars don\\\'t seem to have much need for\r\ndescriptions of earth. </p>\r\n  \r\n<p>\r\nSo - for the record - trying to stretch 2 years of a relationship into a\r\nthird when one party has remained to finish a degree, and the other has\r\ngone off to China with the peace corps is a fool\\\'s quest: it must be\r\nattempted, despite the fact that one knows from the beginning that it is\r\nalmost certain to fail. And it just as painful when it does. \r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<i>[Why am I sharing this here, with you, a quasi anonymous crowd? Hell\r\nif I know.  It\\\'s not advice that will be useful to anyone else I know. But\r\nmaybe it will come in handy to one of you.]</i>',3,894,0,0,'129.79.18.233','en'),(19130,3155,'2002-11-22 23:42:02',90,'leonard','The other day, I thought I saw Austin flicking a booger on to a door knob in my crappy office but it was just a fond memory.',1,124,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(19131,3155,'2002-11-23 00:07:15',86,'egg','last week when i was in LA i saw <a href=\\\"http://www.annawaronker.com/images/photos/SPRadio1_02/Annaband.jpg\\\">austin</a> play guitar for this girl Anna Waronker. We dated for a while and he never told me he played guitar!',0,227,0,0,'199.4.104.129','en'),(19132,3075,'2002-11-23 11:32:07',366,'eunoia','<p>You are my favorite writer on Swinney, I appreciate all your cold realism. You have this really strong voice that comes through in your writing that bleets with cynicism and hopelessness.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I think I feel like your character, which is female from what i gather. Weird because I am not female. I use expressions like \\\"fitting into my own skin.\\\" Maybe we all feel restless, but good hygene is important. That manic compulsion of routine keeps us from jumping off cliffs and bridges.</p>',0,501,0,0,'193.167.219.184','en'),(19133,2597,'2002-11-24 12:50:23',366,'eunoia','hey you like to garden too. Exciting news. I am in finland now and there is like permafrost where I live so I try to do indoor gardens but they always wilt and die because its too dry and hot in my space. *Blum* I like your story though--brought many happy rememberances.',1,271,57,0,'193.167.219.184','en'),(19134,3158,'2002-11-25 01:35:02',124,'gus','next you\\\'ll be telling us that the woman you took to the zg for some cold beer and hot sex was the pubic hair neighbor\\\'s daughter.\r\n<p>\r\nFrankly, I don\\\'t believe a word of it!',0,184,0,0,'64.172.58.76','en'),(19135,3158,'2002-11-25 02:09:46',57,'weeb','this is great.<br><br>\r\n\r\nalso, this is great.<br><br>\r\n\r\nalso, i want a motorcycle bike. with sidecar and a helmet with fake sideburns. ',1,137,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(19136,3158,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','you rule austin',6,15,0,0,'64.81.243.3','en'),(19137,3158,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','you know what?  i love this most because now i know that austin has the same thoughts that run through my mind when some ass is trying to tell you what to do.  unfortunately i have the feeling he actually does what i do, which is to stare at my feet and nod impotently while imagining them suffering by my hand.',6,311,0,0,'64.81.243.3','en'),(19138,3158,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','luckily i have s5 now who is quite content to be an asshole back.  he is the best.  he steers me away from crying children, sends back my food at restaurants, tells off telemarketers and karate chops people who don\\\'t mind their own bizness.  yeah.',6,250,0,0,'64.81.243.3','en'),(19139,3158,'2002-11-25 07:09:38',90,'leonard','Austin, let me know if you need me to write a letter.',1,53,0,0,'216.249.108.153','en'),(19140,3158,'2002-11-25 09:58:36',175,'Paul G','It was so violent.  And it was so funny - <i>at the same time.</i><br>\r\nIt made me think that you were German.',0,110,0,0,'67.195.57.45','en'),(19141,3158,'2002-11-25 16:38:07',66,'Peter','<br><tt><A href=\\\"http://swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=2383\\\">germans have senses of humor?</a></tt>',1,112,175,0,'204.168.247.130','en'),(19142,2383,'2002-11-25 16:41:05',66,'Peter','<br><tt>update: this happened again, as it does every friday and saturday night; the comedians come in for the kill, i dodge them.<br><Br>except that this week, i had just bought kraftwerk\\\'s <i>computer world</i> from a sidewalk vendor, and was carrying the record under my arm. when i passed the comedians, i decided it had been long enough that i could resurrect the <i> am german...</i> line. needless to say, it worked perfectly. i was the picture of aryan humor-less-ness!</tt>',1,485,0,0,'204.168.247.130','en'),(19143,2383,'2002-11-25 18:08:54',67,'trouble','revisiting this article through another leads me to conclude that the phrase <i><b>\\\"Yo! Step your bitch-ass back, fucktard!\\\"</i></b> is now my new favorite phrase and i\\\'m actively seeking some sort of t-shirt distribution deal.  paul germanos you will get some kind of cut i assure you.\r\n',1,297,0,0,'63.70.119.94','en'),(19144,3158,'2002-11-25 19:18:15',175,'Paul G','Haha.  Yes, you are right: If you laugh at a comedian\\\'s comedy, then you are not German.<br>\r\nBut, if Austin rode up to a comedian, struck him violently in the groin, and you laughed at that...well, then you would be very German, indeed.',0,240,66,0,'67.195.31.95','en'),(19145,3158,'2002-11-25 19:40:17',66,'Peter','<br><tt>or, you\\\'d be a <i>new yorker</i>, heh.</tt>',1,54,175,0,'204.168.247.130','en'),(19146,3152,'2002-11-26 04:29:17',120,'joyrider','hm.  you and s5 attract weird cosmic dissonance.  hakim bey should write an essay about you.',2,92,0,0,'12.252.211.253','en'),(19147,3149,'2002-11-26 04:30:39',420,'thanatos',':) . . . smiles... what a great reprieve to read your little ramblings... i escaped to swinney, to step back from the stress of corporate deadlines and 4th quarter quotas... i can relate to your man in the street, until today, though i have sold out, i still peek into my fantasy, my dream of pursuing a pure life, ... he seems to have done so, and so have other great thinkers of the past . . . i hope i will not perish, without at least a taste of a pure life.',2,462,0,0,'63.193.245.138','en'),(19148,3144,'2002-11-26 04:35:44',420,'thanatos','... waiting for Part Two . . .',0,30,0,0,'63.193.245.138','en'),(19149,3152,'2002-11-26 06:31:18',66,'Peter','<br><tt>s5, breaker of horses! o, erisian goddess o\\\' chaos!</tt>',1,67,0,0,'66.108.187.249','en'),(19150,3158,'2002-11-26 16:25:53',142,'oof','you made me think of that really sweet and earnest way that 5 has of telling someone to shove it up their ass. such a fetching boy. *swoon*',1,139,62,0,'65.101.48.189','en'),(19151,3158,'2002-11-26 17:37:17',17,'austin','you really should write a letter.',1,33,90,0,'205.216.79.13','en'),(19152,3158,'2002-11-28 20:21:03',314,'eve','^-^ Germans <i>do</i> have a sense of humor. If you think otherwise, then you\\\'ve met the exceptions. Germans have a harsher sense of humor, it takes more to get them to laugh, and in some point, the joke has to be personal and have some cut. \r\n\r\nGood article, by the way Austin =)You didn\\\'t strike me as the violent type, but for poodles and pubic hair, I see it\\\'s possible.',0,383,0,0,'80.139.176.61','en'),(19153,3158,'2002-11-28 22:55:44',17,'austin','it is all a big show!  i am working on my Robert Ludlum writing style.',1,70,314,0,'206.30.205.106','en'),(19154,3162,'2002-11-29 18:36:10',175,'Paul G','Once upon a time, a holiday meal was an event through which a family became closer.  The type of food that was prepared helped people to remember who they were, and where they came from; or so it seemed to me.<br>\r\nWhether I was in my family\\\'s home, or in my girlfriend\\\'s home, some Greek/Italian/Syrian cooking was always a part of - if not the whole of - the meal.<br>\r\nThen one year it seemed like things changed.  On a Christmas Eve, when I should have been stuffing grape leaves, I ordered a pizza, instead.  My mum and sister laughed when they found out what I had \\\"cooked\\\" for them to eat.<br>\r\nEven if it\\\'s not a good idea to do everything that way that it was done in the past, it\\\'s almost always good to remember; or so it seems.<br>\r\nThis was a great \\\"day after\\\" piece: it captured the mood of street quite nicely.  There is a certain \\\"emptiness\\\" about the holidays, as surely as there is a \\\"fullness.\\\"',1,949,0,0,'67.195.182.41','en'),(19155,3162,'2002-11-29 23:55:48',262,'szajic','<p>In Massachusetts, after Thanksgiving, and until the New Year, licensed liquor stores are open on Sundays.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>This year, as a way to parry the inevitable question - \\\"well, I know you\\\'re vegetarian, but you\\\'re not going to eat turkey on Thanksgiving?\\\" - I broke down and bought turkey.  A fifth of Wild Turkey.</p>',2,334,0,0,'66.30.28.227','en'),(19156,3162,'2002-11-30 04:53:51',59,'s5','<a href=\\\"http://www.nowandzen.net/unturkey.html\\\">the now and zen unturkey</a>',0,83,0,0,'64.81.243.3','en'),(19157,3163,'2002-11-30 23:39:14',57,'weeb','<p>\r\nsometimes i think life is just a dream, i disembody myself when i feel like life is too much to take in. i don\'t want to lose control, so i let go of control. same difference? i don\'t know.\r\n</p><p>\r\nrisk is when the universe threatens and what we push back when we reach out for that bar and hold it out and up. \r\n</p><p>\r\ndon\'t be afraid to be afraid.</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n',1,609,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(19158,3163,'2002-12-01 00:02:47',240,'xep','pike. sweep. seven.',0,19,57,0,'144.132.122.131','en'),(19159,3162,'2002-12-01 03:44:45',124,'gus','Right before dessert at my parents house on thanksgiving this year, we started to go around the table and tell eachother what our \\\"porn name\\\" was. We did this because what could be a more wholesome way for a loving family and it\\\'s guests to share with eachother over pie?\r\n<p>\r\nMy mom (porn name \\\"blackie dauer\\\" had been drinking wine all day (prefaced by a martini apertif and followed by a champagne digestif) so when it was aarong\\\'s turn to tell his porn name, and he said loudly and proudly with a porny gleam in his eye, \\\"Kitty Woof-Woof Leroy\\\", my mom burst into (yet another set of) giggles and champange flew everywhere as her glass clanked into her plate.\r\n<p>\r\nYes. I think we do all feel a little closer now. Possibly too close. Please pass the champange. I need some more.',0,808,0,0,'64.172.57.189','en'),(19160,3163,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','it\\\'s at times like this that i kinda wish there were always safety nets.  it is thrilling that there are not but i still kinda wish there were.  just in case.\r\n\r\nplease be careful in the air xep!  i never worried about you before but now i do.',6,246,0,0,'64.81.243.3','en'),(19161,3163,'2002-12-01 10:12:08',240,'xep','christian is sitting in a hammock beside me drinking a beer.  everyone is ok.  it\\\'s all ok.',0,94,0,0,'144.132.122.131','en'),(19162,3163,'2002-12-01 21:00:49',57,'weeb','\r\noh you are making me pine for the trapeze. i miss tumbling too. and also trampoline! oh sigh. soon!',1,101,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(19163,3162,'2002-12-02 00:47:02',17,'austin','one time i didnt have any food on thanksgiving and the only place open was ken\\\'s donuts in austin.  so i had ken\\\'s donuts for breakfast lunch and dinner.',2,159,59,0,'205.138.150.254','en'),(19164,3162,'2002-12-02 02:54:13',82,'simon','i drove all over san jo desperately looking for coffee on thanksgiving and had to settle for some flavored abomination from boston market, the only thing i could find open.',1,172,0,0,'66.167.204.146','en'),(19165,3138,'2002-12-02 04:58:51',180,'auntie','when i was very young, there was a war in vietnam and boys i knew went there and got killed and maimed, and the one thing i am very sure about is that the voices of the people were not heard because we stood in the street and sang anti-war songs.  \r\n<br><br>\r\nthe voices were heard when young people with no money and no power began going to the polls and actually voting.\r\n<br><br>\r\ni voted for the first time when i was 19, just married, in 1972.  i have never missed voting in election or primary, and that includes the many times, including this year, that i voted absentee.\r\n<br><br>\r\ni may have mentioned it before on this place - but the most important elections are actually the peediddly local commissioner and school board races -- those people who become county commissioners today have aspirations of becoming us senators and congressmen.\r\n<br><br>\r\nbtw, the congressman has a shitload more power than the state senator. pay very close attention to those people.  presidents are very interesting and special, but they president can\\\'t vote on a bill, he can only veto it.\r\n ',3,1088,0,0,'24.162.106.240','en'),(19166,3165,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','you\\\'re so sweet, alana.',6,26,0,0,'64.81.243.3','en'),(19167,3168,'2002-12-02 15:18:49',66,'Peter','<br><tt>its all about the aftest.</tt>',1,38,0,0,'204.168.247.130','en'),(19168,3168,'2002-12-02 17:40:30',82,'simon','i like this one.',1,16,0,0,'209.172.115.210','en'),(19169,3001,'2002-12-02 18:24:10',251,'Jamie','<p><b>Postscript:</b></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Caroline left me for a 40 year old. I\\\'m now back in England working for the same company i was when i left :-(\r\n</p>',6,151,0,0,'172.183.58.169','en'),(19170,3001,'2002-12-02 18:27:05',251,'Jamie','sometimes choices make themselves',4,33,0,0,'172.183.58.169','en'),(19171,3001,'2002-12-02 18:31:23',66,'Peter','<br><tt>my ex is dating a 45 year old puerto rican construction worker; i say, let \\\'em have her!</tt>',1,104,251,0,'204.168.247.130','en'),(19172,3164,'2002-12-02 18:36:51',195,'matt','where in athens did you live?',1,29,0,0,'209.208.110.61','en'),(19173,3168,'2002-12-02 21:11:49',90,'leonard','I usually don\\\'t but right now I\\\'m LOLing. I\\\'m all tingly as well.',1,74,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(19174,3164,'2002-12-02 21:13:04',90,'leonard','HA. Buttplug and toothbrush in the same sentence.',1,49,0,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(19175,3165,'2002-12-02 21:14:02',180,'auntie','and for ralph emmert...\r\n<br><br>\r\nwho died the first week of may, 1991.  he was the first person i knew who died of the virus.\r\n<br><br>\r\nhe was loved by lex aka collared cougar.  they had been together 13 years.  when ralph got really sick and had to get a wheelchair, they put longhorn steer horns on it and made it look western, because ralph loved cowboys.  and fried chicken.  and dancing.  but most of all, ralph loved halloween, his favorite thing was getting the house all spooky for the kids and giving out the candy to the kids and oohing and aahing over their costumes.\r\n<br><br>\r\nwhen their neighbours figured out ralph and lex were gay, they were scared to let their kids go there on halloween.\r\n<br><br>\r\nwhen ralph died, his sisters would not let lex go to the funeral home.  they hated him, and blamed him for ralph dying.\r\n<br><br>\r\nover the years i have known and cared for dozens of people who died from aids. everyone thinks it\\\'s all over, that people don\\\'t still die from it, because it isn\\\'t in the news.\r\n<br><br>\r\nbut they do die from aids still. every minute of every day.\r\n<br><br>\r\ni will remember bruce for you, remember ralph for me.\r\n',1,1174,0,0,'24.162.106.240','en'),(19176,3166,'2002-12-02 22:35:10',421,'chimeres','Awwww... :)  \r\nYou were inspired!  Maybe i should be nicer to my brother, i\\\'m thinking now.',0,94,0,0,'207.113.161.50','en'),(19177,3161,'2002-12-02 22:50:04',421,'chimeres','You are inspiring me too, -- to stop thinking of sweet snacks and to get my blah studying done so I can go out and frolic too.  hehee, but in a *good* way, of course, for now... haha.',0,183,0,0,'207.113.161.50','en'),(19178,3161,'2002-12-02 22:54:33',420,'thanatos','hehe ... what to do in between crushes/flings; write about the last one . . . . i\\\'m thinking i should do an anthology or \\\"how-to\\\" on italian men and romance . . tee-hee!',2,178,421,0,'128.242.125.65','en'),(19179,3169,'2002-12-03 03:28:23',65,'le','what is going on? is this fiction? is this writing or did you post a chat log? ',0,79,0,0,'216.27.183.162','en'),(19180,3169,'2002-12-03 11:22:21',65,'le','ps. i don\\\'t like this',6,24,0,0,'216.27.183.162','en'),(19181,2217,'2002-12-03 19:48:42',74,'jo','p.s. after nearly eleven months, we broke up. we\\\'re still in love but it\\\'s not working. i am miserable, miserable, miserable.',3,131,0,0,'146.6.172.208','en'),(19182,3164,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','maybe you are moving the things.',6,32,0,0,'64.81.243.3','en'),(19183,3162,'2002-12-04 00:07:20',129,'moebius','<br>last christmas day i just had to get out of the house at one point and get some cafe time. i\\\'m not sure why--it had something to do with the fact that it was the first xmas holiday in ever that i wasn\\\'t with some format of extended family or other, and molls was taking a nap, and i was feeling stircrazy. so.<br><br>i was looking at about 4pm and city was graveyard quiet. i ended up at the <i>Horseshoe</i>, in the lower haight, which for whatever reason seemed to be keeping its usual hours. when i arrived there was a whole family of scandinavian people yukking it up, but they eventually left.<br><br>then a lovely but somewhat scattered-seeming girl showed up. she kept giving me the eye, and i kept looking back, like a fish caught on a hook. the next thing i knew she was talking to me and i was full of conflicted emotion, thinking of molls back home, thinking of this girl\\\'s friendly smile. i was sure this couldn\\\'t be a good thing.<br><br>but, ha, false alarm: she wanted to read my tarot. so i let her, maybe out of relief, and perhaps an interest in a little adventure before returning home. i don\\\'t know if she knew what she was doing; she seemed nervous, and she kept slipping up with the cards. she prophesied a variety of things for my future, mostly bad stuff. overall, it really freaked me out. made me wish i\\\'d never left home, never left molls alone, just did the good christmas thing and stuck around. i kept thinking <i>well that\\\'s what you get well, that\\\'s what you get.</i> i paid her more than she asked for and got the heck out of there.',1,1592,0,0,'148.87.1.170','en'),(19184,3162,'2002-12-04 00:12:27',129,'moebius','oh, and people go strolling around macys and the other downtown department stores after thanksgiving for a simple reason: to look at the animated store displays. this year it\\\'s mickey mouse starring in \\\"Twas The Night Before Christmas.\\\" animatronics! this is something my parents used to take us to do when we were kids. used to drive all the way up from Half Moon Bay for it.',1,385,0,0,'148.87.1.170','en'),(19185,3164,'2002-12-04 02:01:19',371,'Kyla','Whenever I drive my car at night, the streetlights turn off or on as I drive past.  I\\\'m sure my car is some sort of electrical black hole or something.  Perhaps you have similar effects on your light fittings?  :)',6,216,0,0,'203.97.2.243','en'),(19186,3162,'2002-12-04 05:46:08',421,'chimeres','<p>I always thought the best thing about holidays is breaking away from the innundating, psychotic family haze of the lunch/dinner table and wandering out into the world to find it utterly deserted and desolate.  Then going back home and realizing how bizarre but chronically addicting family is, and being glad to have one of the most crazy families to feed it.</p><p>Somehow, this year, i never found that desolation (everyone i hoped to avoid decided to take their yearly hike in tennessee valley with me, and i didn\\\'t even get closed out of any stores), so i\\\'m very glad to have read this posting to know the desolation is still there.</p>',0,649,0,0,'209.232.55.237','en'),(19187,3162,'2002-12-04 13:55:14',240,'xep','i ended up at the horseshoe last hexmas day also.  it wasn\\\'t what we wanted though... axum was the real destination but they did not exist when we needed them.  after some frustration the toronado won out and we spent the rest of the day with expensive beer.',0,261,129,0,'144.132.122.131','en'),(19188,3162,'2002-12-04 15:12:55',17,'austin','i refuse to be involved in tarot in any way because if what they have to say is good, i would rather be suprised.  if what they have to say is bad, i would rather not know.',3,172,129,0,'64.2.58.24','en'),(19189,3171,'2002-12-04 18:43:26',82,'simon','hmm. that makes sense, chia.',0,28,0,0,'209.172.115.210','en'),(19190,3171,'2002-12-04 19:14:48',124,'gus','americans have been drinking too much for 200 years. the british even longer, and in asia they\\\'ve been binge drinking and puking, even sometimes without the enzyme needed to digest it, for much longer than in the west. (in laos they drink 22 oz beers with breakfast as well as with other meals and between meals, and regularly chug lao lao, a Very strong and ancient rice liquor. They drink till they puke, then puke, then are ready to drink more).\r\n<p>\r\nI think you have some good points, but you can see I\\\'m totally unconvinced that you\\\'ve discovered the root of drinking too much.',0,592,0,0,'64.172.56.120','en'),(19191,3171,'2002-12-04 19:34:15',74,'jo','(binge drinking and puking and then drinking again is called \\\"boot \\\'n\\\' rally,\\\" very popular drinking method on college campuses. over and out.)',1,155,0,0,'146.6.172.208','en'),(19192,3170,'2002-12-04 19:37:39',17,'austin','you don\\\'t know him and don\\\'t care, so i would be rude once subtle didn\\\'t work.',2,87,0,0,'64.2.58.24','en'),(19193,3170,'2002-12-04 20:08:36',74,'jo','you know what? this only minorly creeped me out until i scrolled back up and read \\\"15 years old\\\" again. dude, 15. that guy needs to LET GO.\r\n<BR>\r\nin other news, i recently realized that i hadn\\\'t talked to an old flame in over a year and that his email address was bouncing and so i used people.yahoo.com to find him and either he\\\'s moved to roanoke, va or i will need to call his DAD to get his number, assuming his dad would even give me his number. so, uh. i\\\'m not really one to talk.',1,502,0,0,'146.6.172.208','en'),(19194,3171,'2002-12-04 20:53:34',154,'ryan','at some point i heard (from somewhere) that native americans were genetically disposed to alcoholism (not used to it and therefore never developed the required processes to cope with consumption).<p>when i was bumming around montana there was a festival on the blackfoot indian reservation that i took part in.  they roasted buffalo, danced, sang and banned the sale of alcohol on the entire reservation.  a common sight was the montona state troopers pulling over a car full of indians and confiscating their alcohol. (the reservation bordered a populated area of glacier national park).',0,588,0,0,'65.58.159.86','en'),(19195,3164,'2002-12-04 23:25:48',231,'alana','i think i lived on south milledge and then i lived in normaltown. all of athens was good :) the river, weaver d\\\'s, wuxtry mmm. \r\n\r\nalso, frodo purrs loudly.',3,159,0,0,'203.221.31.32','en'),(19196,3171,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','it\\\'s pretty common for japanese businessmen to drink till they puke or pass out on the train home.  apparently you can see them littering the sidewalks, passed out in their suits.',6,182,0,0,'64.81.243.3','en'),(19197,3170,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','heh.  my ex boyfriend won\\\'t talk to me at all, but i message him on irc every few months to ask him how he is.  i say, \\\"how\\\'re you?\\\" he says \\\"good.\\\"  i say \\\"still going to uni?\\\" he says \\\"yeah.\\\"  i say \\\"okay then.\\\" he says \\\"....\\\"  i guess it\\\'s kinda stalking but i figure that one day he will just break down and be nice to me.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nps it is stalking as soon as he continues to try to gain information on you, or enter correspondence with you, after you have told him many times that you are uninterested.',6,559,0,0,'64.81.243.3','en'),(19198,3171,'2002-12-04 23:37:52',370,'seanthecon','there have also been scientific reports about ethnic origin and DNA. basically it states that asians and isreali jews have a DNA composite that gives them an adverse effect to alcohol. i have no idea how legitimate this is, considering it was reported in the mainstream press, but its interesting to consider.',0,309,0,0,'209.52.190.35','en'),(19199,3171,'2002-12-05 02:09:08',174,'Mad Moll','Star Crafting. That\\\'s fucking awesome. I\\\'ve heard that some Koreans are actually professional Starcraft players, and that I guess software companies or promoters or whomever basically pay them to raise hell at tournaments in their name. I don\\\'t know if that\\\'s actually true, but props to Korea all the same.',6,319,0,0,'24.189.13.22','en'),(19200,3171,'2002-12-05 07:01:21',93,'chiamattt','well in korea there is a tv station that has starcraft on 24/7. a few years ago star craft was so big there was a breakfast cereal, backpacks, pencil cases, and toothpaste. I havnt really seen much of that stuff lately, but now the new game coming on strong is warcraft three. another fact is that two years ago some gamer from vancouver moved to korea to become a professional starcraft player...won the world championship and still works here playing games. its unreal. ',2,472,174,0,'61.37.53.41','en'),(19201,3170,'2002-12-05 17:57:07',57,'weeb','well, you are not required to keep in touch with him, as much as he believes otherwise. you can just route his emails to a folder for documenting his insanity if he does anything more incriminating, or you can route his emails to /dev/null.\r\n\r\n',1,244,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(19202,3162,'2002-12-05 18:41:02',129,'moebius','yeah, i suppose you could say that about most fortune-telling schemes and rituals. i\\\'ve got a schizoid break between my die-hard skeptic point of view and my dreamy romantic belief that nothing is impossible and \\\"magic\\\" (for lack of a better word) exists.<br><br>the skeptic side tends to get me into trouble by having me submit to a reading for a laugh. then the romantic side flips out when it hears bad news. rinse, repeat.\r\n\r\nalso, xep: drinking expensive beer on hexmas with pals sounds like a nice way to spend the day.',1,534,17,0,'148.87.1.170','en'),(19203,3171,'2002-12-05 23:05:10',83,'adamajah','games are evil.\r\n\r\nchia, stop spending all your dough on las drogas and send me my GTConcept ;)',0,95,0,0,'66.13.23.218','en'),(19204,3171,'2002-12-06 00:24:33',174,'Mad Moll','That is fucking cool. I want to move to Korea. I don\\\'t even like Starcraft that much, but there\\\'s just something overpoweringly cool about enjoying the game that much 