ten feel guilty or repetitive for the amount of time i spend talking about weather and seasons, but there really is something endlessly fascinating about it all. you hit upon it nicely; that seasons leave you and return (or you leave them, you may argue; we depart from each other simultaneously?) and every year they are new experiences even if they are supported by the history of what they have been in the past.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>experiencing the seasons change in a new city are oddly disconcerting. even though the weather here is basically the same, autumn felt so different. but maybe it doesn\\\'t really have much to do with geographical change, because every year autumn is a new season?</p>',1,727,234,0,'216.220.104.108','en'),(19353,3189,'2002-12-19 19:23:43',66,'Peter','<br><tt>\r\nI just ordered up a beer and sat down at the bar<br>\r\nWhen some guy walked in and said; \\\'Who owns this car?<br>\r\nWith the peace sign, the mag wheels and four on the floor?\\\'<br>\r\nWell, he looked at me and I damn near died<br>\r\nAnd I decided that I\\\'d just wait outside<br>\r\nSo I layed a dollar on the bar and headed for the door...<br></tt>',1,357,0,0,'204.168.247.130','en'),(19354,3189,'2002-12-19 19:58:17',129,'moebius','<br>Well we rolled up interstate fourty-four<br>\r\nLike a rocket sled on rails<br>\r\nWe tore up all a our swindle sheets<br>\r\nAn\\\' left \\\'em settin\\\' on the scales<br>\r\nBy the time we hit that Chi-Town<br>\r\nThem bears was a gittin\\\' smart<br>\r\nThey\\\'d brought up some reinforcements<br>\r\nFrom the Illinois National Guard<br>\r\nThere \\\'as armored cars, and tanks, and Jeeps<br>\r\nAn\\\' rigs of every size<br>\r\nYeah them chicken coops \\\'as full a bears<br>\r\nAn\\\' choppers filled the skies<br>\r\nWell we shot the line, an\\\' we went for broke<br>\r\nWith a thousand screamin\\\' trucks<br>\r\nAnd eleven long-haired friends of Jesus<br>\r\nIn a chartreusse microbus<br>\r\n\r\n...tales of <a href=\\\"http://www.narrowgauge.org/4x4/cw_pages/lyrics/bbr/convoy.html\\\">the four wheel cowboy</a>...',1,796,0,0,'148.87.1.170','en'),(19355,3001,'2002-12-19 21:36:44',251,'Jamie','additional: jamie is in love again. her name is chris and she is amazing :oD',1,76,0,0,'172.181.223.92','en'),(19356,3116,'2002-12-19 21:51:02',251,'Jamie','<p>i think i\\\'d like to meet this roberto fella</p>',1,53,66,0,'172.181.223.92','en'),(19357,3192,'2002-12-20 08:14:02',370,'seanthecon','aaaaahhhhhh to the spills and spoils of love. its never ending twists and torments. white is drained. white is blinding. beautiful piece me mon. i am tried and convicted. you are the judge and jury. aaaaaaaaaaaaahhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhh',0,233,0,0,'65.95.117.228','en'),(19358,3180,'2002-12-22 08:07:38',234,'etienne','sometimes summer changes you; sometimes the way you experience it changes summer.  (maybe?)<br><br>\r\n\r\nstill waiting for your homework assignment detroit :)',1,156,67,0,'203.96.111.237','en'),(19359,3180,'2002-12-22 08:08:11',234,'etienne','sent :D',1,7,122,0,'210.55.167.12','en'),(19360,3186,'2002-12-22 23:36:42',75,'tyler','sometimes, you are hated just because you exist. ',1,49,0,0,'165.247.165.75','en'),(19361,3192,'2002-12-22 23:41:41',75,'tyler','seperation and conjunction<br>\r\nhere and there<br>\r\n\r\nnear and far<br>\r\nblack and white<br>\r\none and zero<br>\r\nlove\r\n',1,117,0,0,'165.247.165.75','en'),(19362,3189,'2002-12-22 23:48:53',75,'tyler','<p>everything you write<br>\r\nseems to be about new york<br>\r\nit must be some place</p><p>\r\ni may go to school<br>\r\nat cardozo school of law<br>\r\nif i get lucky<br></p><p>\r\nit is in New York<br>\r\nstrange place for someone from here<br>\r\nsouth carolina</p>\r\n',1,256,0,0,'165.247.165.75','en'),(19363,3186,'2002-12-23 14:54:51',93,'chiamattt','The SOFA or status of forces agreement between korea and usa gives the US Military jurisdiction over its own troops when they commit a crime while on duty. The men charged and then court martialled were on duty and so where given to the US authorities. \r\nThis incident was a complete accident and, in fact, the driver of the vehicle was unable to see the two girls during the accident and if he could have seen them, the vehicle wouldn t have been able to stop in time to avoid the girls.\r\n\r\nEven the Korean police that were on the scene within minutes of the accident quickly settled their paperwork calling the incident an unavoidable accident. (it is certainly argueable that the korean police are somewhat inept... but that is another post).\r\n\r\nOnly later did this incident become a sort of national issue. And, for the record, G.W. Bush has apologised 3 times for the deaths of the girls and the most recent time it was a direct apology to the Korean Ambassador, which is what the vast majority of the korean protesters wanted. And, as a result, the \\\"leaders\\\" of the protests have rejected the apology.',2,1113,0,0,'61.37.53.26','en'),(19364,3186,'2002-12-23 14:55:27',93,'shanE','chiamattt didn t write that, shanE did.',0,39,0,0,'61.37.53.26','en'),(19365,3186,'2002-12-24 00:24:52',59,'s5','well! that settles that! all the paperwork was in order, so everything\\\'s peachy keen! thanks for clearing that up. kinda makes me wish my neighborhood was lucky enough to be occupied with all those generous military men.',6,223,93,0,'64.81.243.3','en'),(19366,3198,'2002-12-24 21:01:55',175,'Paul G','I wrote something last night.  And I used the words, \\\"leather-clad,\\\" too.  But I was writing about being 35 and alone, not 25 and with someone.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\nI still like to read about love.',0,195,0,0,'67.195.79.6','en'),(19367,2832,'2002-12-24 23:58:25',175,'Paul G','I miss you.',0,11,187,0,'67.195.79.97','en'),(19368,3198,'2002-12-25 16:29:35',74,'conor oberst','The last few months I have been living with this couple. Yeah, you know, the kind that buy everything in doubles.  They fit together, like a puzzle. \r\nI love their love and I am thankful that someone actually \r\nreceives the prize that was promised by all those fairy tales that drugged us. \r\nAnd they still do me. I\\\'m sick, lonely, no laurel tree, just green envy. \r\nWill my number come up eventually? Like love is some kind of lottery, \r\nwhere you can scratch and see what is underneath. It\\\'s \\\"Sorry\\\", \r\njust one cherry, \\\"Play Again.\\\" Get lucky.\r\n',0,566,0,0,'12.162.145.219','en'),(19369,3196,'2002-12-28 09:49:07',142,'oof','this is a comment.',1,18,0,0,'216.160.220.217','en'),(19370,3203,'2002-12-28 15:48:25',57,'weeb','oof. i have a little xmas present for you and lots of hugs when you get back. you have many people here who miss you. *hugs*\r\n\r\n\r\n',1,130,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(19371,2447,'2002-12-28 15:54:01',314,'eve','The saddest thing is that this always happens to children. Their parents are supposed to be the ones that help them, not destroy them. I\\\'m not a psychologist by any means, but I find often when looking at people with \\\"problems\\\" it can usually be blamed in some way from a bad childhood. No one is made of steel, and a bad childhood can create a lifetime of damage. And it\\\'s not deflecting the blame from the person with the problem, for me that is just the reality of the situation. Children are delicate mentally and physically, and without human attention and affection, an infant can die. And people still don\\\'t care. If someone is not ready to be a parent, they should not procreate, they should be sterilized. Just because they CAN have a child, doesn\\\'t mean they should or should even be allowed to. \r\n\r\nI\\\'m sure there have been a lot of neglegent parents (like my mother also was) that are really sorry for how badly they had raised their child. I\\\'ve heard enough I\\\'m sorrys and I did my bests. None of that really matters though, the damage is done, and everytime you see that person they are just a reminder of how much they fucked up. ',0,1172,0,0,'212.65.24.41','en'),(19372,3202,'2002-12-29 04:35:37',75,'tyler','I hope that your predictions are correct. Unfortunately, the nature of North Korea\\\'s government makes this unlikely. people in America complain about corruption and governmental oversight, and with good reason; people in power can and do sometimes become corrupt. It has a lot to do with how they came to power in the first place and their cultural history. The US, for example, became a well-run country for almost 100 years until the Civil War, which was of average length, and despite her ups and downs has done really well since. I attribute this to the fact that the US government, on a <i>practical</i> level, was modeled on the British, which was stable and several steps removed from feudalism, which I consider to be basically the rule of naked force. Some would argue that naked force maintains power here in the US today, and they are correct on a practical level--how do the police stop you when you are shooting at others? How are evicted persons removed from their dwellings? With force. Still, the <i>acquisition and control</i> of that force is governed by a higher level of order, representative democracy, as opposed to the feudal system of a hereditary nobility and the random element of, simply, whoever can get the most swords together in one place at one time. <br><br>\r\nThe North Korean government was born of feudalism and then Communist occupation. The South Korean government was born of feudalism and then, essentially, Capitalist occupation, under which it has thrived (by our sense of the word, anyway). The main point is this: the structures in place to support the power of those in charge, which can be likened to the structures that bring the police, fire trucks etc. when someone calls 911 (electric company, phone company, political/legal system, all the way down to the manufacturers of the emergency responder\\\'s shoes), are completely different in North Korea than in South Korea. If you took the 20 million NK\\\'s and all of a sudden gave them the authority currently held by the SK\\\'s, i.e. voting rights and more importantly <i>governmental oversight ability</i>, the NK system, built on a &quot;because I said so or you\\\'ll be shot&quot; basis, would collapse and lots of people would probably die. So their peaceful mixing is highly unlikely in my eyes.<br><br>\r\nThe good news is, to view the future of North Korea, we need only look to the past of the Soviet Union; you simply can\\\'t support a nation without engaging with other nations in trade etc., and the trade has to be natural, i.e. capitalist, where efficiency and quality are rewarded naturally, vs. the forced nature of trade in the former soviet bloc nations. North Korea\\\'s economy will most likely implode like the USSR\\\'s. This may have already begun, and NK\\\'s strange actions of late may be related to the beginning of this process. NK\\\'s leader is probably taking these drastic measures because his accountant has finally gotten it across to him that soon, they won\\\'t be able to make payroll for, or even feed, the shock troopers that keep the hungry peasant workers of NK out of his bedroom. And, get this, this is in a country where they <i>print their own money.</i> It\\\'s a doomed system. We, the US, need to be ready for some serious shit, as the walls fall down around the NK government leaders\\\' heads. Ready to rush in and stabilize things, so that, hopefully, the minimum amount of damage will be done to the land and its people.',1,3476,0,0,'165.247.165.141','en'),(19373,2447,'2002-12-29 06:36:29',66,'Peter','<br><tt>our cat\\\'s name is stella. i read this cause of the confluence in nomenclature.</tt>',1,94,151,0,'66.108.188.37','en'),(19374,3116,'2002-12-29 06:39:17',66,'Peter','<br><tt>yeah, he was neat. the landlady discovered his scheme (living in the basement here, unbeknownst to her) and evicted him last month, but oh well.<br><br>i must say, though, that its lots quieter around this place without his all night salsa parties, heh. </tt>',1,267,251,0,'66.108.188.37','en'),(19375,3189,'2002-12-29 06:44:14',66,'Peter','<br><tt>me, born in rural<br>\r\ntennessee, me living in<br>\r\ncosmopolitan<br><br>\r\n\r\nelectronicville.<br>\r\nits the margin between them<br>\r\nthat are these writings.<br><br>\r\n\r\n<i>[technically, though, this was about a parkway- a motorway- just like ones in any city or country; but, i understand your observation. come to nyc and you\\\'ll understand, i assure you.]</i>\r\n</tt>\r\n\r\n',1,380,75,0,'66.108.188.37','en'),(19376,3202,'2002-12-29 22:13:13',175,'Paul G','China.',0,6,0,0,'67.195.63.223','en'),(19377,2545,'2002-12-30 17:55:36',17,'austin','people have been falling for aarong\\\'s cat, Mina.\r\n<BR>\r\n<img src=\\\"http://www.divinia.com/kitty/mina_xmas.jpg\\\">',1,119,0,0,'24.175.65.27','en'),(19378,2545,'2002-12-30 17:59:34',57,'weeb','i have fallen head over heels for the doe-eyed mina. she caught me with her stare stare STARE of \\\"are you my savior? mew? muooooooo?\\\" talky talker cat. give me my heart back.',0,180,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(19379,2545,'2002-12-30 18:21:56',66,'Peter','<br><tt>ooh... update: a <A href=\"http://www.fonem.org/stellar.jpg\">super #1 cute wondercat</a> has come into my life since my last comment on this post. so cute. did i mention <i>cute</i>?</tt>',1,200,0,0,'204.168.247.130','en'),(19380,3196,'2002-12-31 00:47:38',18,'bcm','i love comments.\r\n',0,18,0,0,'12.127.67.66','en'),(19381,3196,'2002-12-31 02:56:00',66,'Peter','<br><tt>mmm, <i>comments</i>.</tt>',1,29,0,0,'66.108.188.37','en'),(19382,3194,'2002-12-31 02:59:19',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i really like the second and third paragraphs...</tt>',1,61,0,0,'66.108.188.37','en'),(19383,2545,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','i want all the cats.  yes please.',6,33,0,0,'64.81.243.3','en'),(19384,2545,'2002-12-31 13:51:08',66,'Peter','<br><tt>MEOW</tt>',1,17,62,0,'204.168.247.130','en'),(19385,3205,'2003-01-02 22:40:33',371,'Kyla','Damn.  Why don\\\'t I have someone to write something like this about me?  Shyeet.',6,82,0,0,'203.96.111.237','en'),(19386,3205,'2003-01-02 23:24:24',74,'jo','yeah. yeah. ditto.',1,18,0,0,'146.6.172.208','en'),(19387,3202,'2003-01-03 01:21:51',83,'adamajah','GTC Tokyo-Seoul !',1,17,0,0,'66.13.23.218','en'),(19388,3203,'2003-01-03 08:38:28',190,'dahlia','yes, dear. love love love, and more love.\r\n\r\nit\\\'s worth holding on. i promise.\r\n',0,83,0,0,'66.92.4.146','en'),(19389,3207,'2003-01-03 18:00:04',82,'simon','simonized? heh. cute.',0,21,0,0,'209.172.115.210','en'),(19390,3207,'2003-01-03 18:10:28',66,'Peter','<br><tt>heh. i thought the same thing when i saw <i>simonized</i>. it appears that your namesake is a waxing process.</tt>',1,122,82,0,'204.168.247.130','en'),(19391,3207,'2003-01-03 23:06:02',82,'simon','i just naturally assumed it had something to do with the somewhat pervy content of this post. ah well.',1,102,66,0,'209.172.115.210','en'),(19392,3207,'2003-01-04 15:48:11',175,'Paul G','In \\\'73 my family moved into a home that had - for a time - no working toilet.  As kids, we had to stand in the sink and pee.  It was really fucking weird.\r\n\r\n<p>There were two little garage/houses towards the rear of the property; each had a fireplace in it.  We used the fireplaces to melt wax; we made sand candles with the melted wax.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>One day, Mum made pancakes.  I started to eat them.  My throat burned.  I looked at the syrup bottle: it was filled with ants.  Ants taste hot and scratchy.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>There were so many weird bugs...</p>\r\n\r\n<p>A lot of your writing makes me remember those times in my life that were, well, sort of fucked up.  It\\\'s familiar - in a creepy sort of way.  Because, I want to forget a lot of that stuff, or put it behind me, or something...</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The genital/grape thing made me wince.  I dunno.  Could there be an \\\"average\\\" guy in the next piece?  Maybe an Italian-looking guy with a nice cock, who was able to cum like a horse?</p>',3,992,0,0,'67.195.31.108','en'),(19393,3208,'2003-01-05 08:11:46',17,'austin','sims,\r\n\r\n<br> you write at a brisk pace.\r\n\r\n<br>\r\nyou drunk gay lover,\r\n\r\n<BR>\r\naustin',1,86,0,0,'66.90.146.62','en'),(19394,3207,'2003-01-06 01:47:34',195,'matt','i was trying to think of an \\\"-ized\\\" adjective that started with s, and it was down to \\\"simonized\\\" or \\\"sodomized.\\\"<BR><BR>it didn\\\'t strike me until now that it could be construed as a reference to anyone on the site.  i wasn\\\'t thinking about simon at all when i wrote it.<BR><BR>i\\\'m saving \\\"sodomized\\\" for a future chapter.<BR><BR><I><B>best friendly</B></I>',1,390,0,0,'209.208.108.25','en'),(19395,3207,'2003-01-06 01:48:26',195,'matt','pervy?  you sure it\\\'s not sensual?',1,37,0,0,'209.208.108.25','en'),(19396,3208,'2003-01-06 10:57:33',175,'Paul G','This was really well written, and a nice slice of life.  It made me reflect upon the fact that I don\\\'t know any women who know how to cook.  I mean I haven\\\'t dated a single woman who really felt comfortable in the kitchen.  Odd.  I\\\'m always the one at the stove.',0,271,0,0,'67.195.71.75','en'),(19397,3208,'2003-01-06 18:23:58',82,'simon','that made me think about the last couple girls i\\\'ve dated. and mostly i was the one who cooked too.',1,102,175,0,'209.172.115.210','en'),(19398,3207,'2003-01-06 19:05:20',82,'simon','pervy is much better than sensual.',0,34,195,0,'209.172.115.210','en'),(19399,3208,'2003-01-06 22:55:50',195,'matt','this post made me really hungry.<BR><BR>what kind of drugs did you do over new year\\\'s?',1,89,0,0,'209.208.109.64','en'),(19400,3208,'2003-01-07 00:56:16',175,'Paul G','Maybe, this is one of those things that\\\'s unrelated to either gender or orientation, and has to do with ethnicity exclusively.  Like, if you are the one in the relationship who is Latin or Asian you will be the default cook - because when people talk about going out to eat, they talk about getting Italian, or Mexican, or Chinese, or Thai food.  No one ever says, \\\"Let\\\'s get English food.\\\"  Because, eating eels and kidneys is a punishment, not a reward.\r\n\r\n<p>I like cooking - a lot.  But, at some point it\\\'s just about the other person making the effort.  It\\\'s the same way with massage: I really like doing it; I will do it - happily - 90% of the time.  It\\\'s the idea that the other person should try - sometimes - for the sake of showing some concern.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Everything else having been said, it\\\'s really cool that you took the time to invest yourself in the preparation of a meal like that.  It seems to be one of the most essential ways of showing love and concern for another person.  And not too many people are willing to do it.  So, cheers.</p>',0,1082,82,0,'67.195.31.33','en'),(19401,3208,'2003-01-07 01:14:56',82,'simon','oh thanks. i also cooked a couple of chickens on the bbq. the food was pretty basic but good. someone brought  a salad.',0,119,175,0,'209.172.115.210','en'),(19402,3208,'2003-01-07 01:15:38',82,'simon','oh the usuals. a couple different powders followed by a handfull of pills later.',0,80,195,0,'209.172.115.210','en'),(19403,3171,'2003-01-07 18:29:38',443,'afr0bunny','well indians and pakistanis are also asian, but this doesnt really hold true for indians/pakistanis of dravidian and aryan descent. of course we are all overlooked as being asian too. wouldnt surprise me if the ppl doing the study didnt realize that we are asian also. ',3,269,370,0,'68.158.100.163','en'),(19404,3208,'2003-01-07 19:35:01',74,'jo','i think that\\\'s a pretty unlikely explanation. my ethnic friends neither cook more or less than my other friends. there are just some people, regardless of gender, sexual orientation, or race who enjoy cooking more than others do.',2,232,175,0,'146.6.172.208','en'),(19405,3208,'2003-01-07 22:36:06',86,'egg','i lived with a dude who would do most of the cooking, and it was often very \\\"white\\\" dishes - red beans and rice, chicken noodle soup, roasts- YUM. cmere sexy whitey!!!',0,173,175,0,'199.4.104.129','en'),(19406,2545,'2003-01-07 22:59:52',129,'moebius','we returned from two weeks of being away for the winter holidays, and the cats were ecstatic, overjoyed, thrilled beyond mortal comprehension to have us home.<br><br>and then we went to bed and they hopped up right along with us in a joyful rush to snuggle in and share the warmth after so many cold nights.<br><br>in the wee hours of the morning, molls woke up, because i was snoring again (imagine a tuvan throat singer being strangled over & over again and you\\\'re almost there). she turned to make me roll over and shut up but stopped short: i was on my back, miranda was cuddled neatly upon my chest, and i was slowly petting her in my sleep. i was snoring, she was purring: it was a midnight duet. ',0,706,0,0,'148.87.1.170','en'),(19407,3208,'2003-01-08 01:33:52',175,'Paul G','Haha.',0,5,86,0,'67.195.73.89','en'),(19408,3208,'2003-01-08 01:40:09',175,'Paul G','<p>I like you.  But, I like my explanation too.  Am I too attached to my own ideas?  Or, is there nothing in this world but will to power?  Is it enlightened or slavish to be still?  Sigh.  I just don\\\'t know, anymore.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I don\\\'t want to be understood to have said that certain people are somehow predisposed by virtue of their genes to be good cooks, or to take an interest in cooking.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>But, you know, in Latin America, and in the Mediterranean, and in the Asian Subcontinent, and in Southeast Asia, it\\\'s possible to grow many more types of intensely flavored foods than it is possible to grow in Northern Europe.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>And food, and cooking, seems to play a much more central role in the cultures that evolved in the aforementioned places than it does in Northern Europe.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I\\\'m sort of passionate about this, because I come from a \\\"mixed\\\" home.  So, please, it\\\'s not a lecture of any kind, but just an effort to share something that is really important to me, with you - because I care.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Think of all the things that came to Europe after the Columbian exchange: peppers, chocolate, coffee, tomatoes, beans, potatoes, corn, etc.  I was joking about it, but it\\\'s not too far from the truth to say that for centuries, food in Northern Europe consisted of barley, oats, sheep, and fish.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Food was responsible for slavery in the New World: it was the desire of the Portuguese and Spanish to grow sugar in Brazil and the Caribbean that lead them to begin to spirit away Africans; supposedly, only 5-10% of those kidnapped were taken to North America for work in cotton plantations.  And people wanted things like sugar, and pepper, because their food sucked.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I guess it\\\'s just the idea that there are cultures that tend to emphasize food and meals, and those that tend to de-emphasize food and meals in favor of other things.  Not that one or the other is better - just that there are differences.  And those of us who maintain the old cultures sometimes are at odds with our partners.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I\\\'d say it\\\'s just me, and I\\\'m full of crap, but my sister has had the same experience with her partners.  Maybe I\\\'m full of crap, anyway.  I don\\\'t understand too much, anymore.  I\\\'d still have to say that I\\\'ve had some sort of connection with my Cuban, or Italian, or Chinese girlfriends that has been missing in other cases - like some sort of...oh I dunno.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I bet simon\\\'s chicken was good.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>With respect,<br>\r\nPaul.</p>',0,2537,74,0,'67.195.73.89','en'),(19409,3208,'2003-01-08 07:10:55',82,'simon','heh. yeah the chicken was fucking good, fyi. but the thing i think is interesting...for me this whole post was about discomfort and trying to figure out how to be close to my sister again and not being sure what to say. the cooking was the easiest way to get around the real details and that\\\'s what became the topic of the comments. ---cheers, simon',1,352,0,0,'66.167.76.169','en'),(19410,2949,'2003-01-08 08:30:34',445,'ja luv','<p>yeah my bud drove you up there to portland like 6 years ago.  You looked older.  You started making out with some chick in a really frightening basement.  He excused himself.  I told him he should have atleast seen if you wanted a nice 3some or something.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>but yeah.. peace, yo.  Down with the Bushreich.</p>',3,320,0,0,'205.158.144.168','en'),(19411,3208,'2003-01-08 14:56:43',74,'jo','you didn\\\'t need to explain to me how almost every culture but the anglo-saxons have a strong relationship with cooking and with food. i get that. i took arms with your statement that ethnicity exclusively determined which partner in a given relationship cooked. exclusively. that hasn\\\'t been my experience.<BR>\r\nand i realize that when you couch these speeches in phrases like \\\"i like you,\\\" and \\\"because i care,\\\" it\\\'s because you\\\'re trying to soften the blow and emphasize the \\\"best friendly!\\\" of your point, but, and i can only speak for myself, it makes me feel condescended to. it would have been easier if you\\\'d just said, \\\"sometimes,\\\" rather than \\\"exclusively.\\\" then white girls like myself who cook up a storm while our ethnic boyfriends watch movies wouldn\\\'t feel the need to point out that it\\\'s not always the case.',1,874,0,0,'172.168.210.206','en'),(19412,2570,'2003-01-08 15:17:24',66,'Peter','<br><tt>by chance, i saw the last part of a documentary about the state of nevada on pbs this past weekend. there was a snippet at the end about burning man. they walked up to interview an amusingly dressed individual, who turned out to be none other than the unmistakable speed levitch.<br><br><i>continuity...</i></tt>',1,320,0,0,'204.168.247.130','en'),(19413,2949,'2003-01-08 16:28:05',17,'austin','WHOA now, I like Bush.  Simon does too.',3,39,0,0,'64.2.58.24','en'),(19414,3210,'2003-01-08 17:15:02',86,'egg','I really hope *I* was \\\"hot stuff\\\" and you wuz the \\\"snowbunny\\\".',0,74,0,0,'199.4.104.129','en'),(19415,3208,'2003-01-08 17:32:26',86,'egg','That\\\'s a fascinating parallel to the way that our domestic activities, or physical cravings, can manifest our emotional life. I find myself wicked hungry when Im emotionally needy. food is such a loaded subject, so dear and so indicative of cultural and relational dynamics that we read your post and eat up the red herring with a spoon.  ',0,342,82,0,'199.4.104.129','en'),(19416,2949,'2003-01-08 17:47:37',82,'simon','oh shit. i remember that. yeah that basement was fucked up.',1,59,0,0,'209.172.115.210','en'),(19417,3210,'2003-01-08 18:37:09',17,'austin','danh, i like this work. write some more here, please.',1,53,0,0,'64.2.58.24','en'),(19418,3210,'2003-01-08 20:38:54',66,'Peter','<br><tt>hi danh</tt>',1,18,0,0,'66.108.188.37','en'),(19419,3211,'2003-01-09 02:24:02',371,'Kyla','Don\\\'t bother dealing with God, you have to wait too long.',6,60,0,0,'203.97.2.243','en'),(19420,3211,'2003-01-09 03:47:16',168,'god','try living in the present moment. there are no problems or frustrations in the now. only in the past and in the future.',1,119,0,0,'64.175.184.131','en'),(19421,3211,'2003-01-09 04:05:45',67,'trouble','<p>this really resonated with me, i curse often and sometimes without hesitation.  i also see it as a release, i know full well that i look like an idiot sitting in my automobile in traffic mouthing every conceivable expletive in your direction because you cut me off, drove too close behind me,  etc, etc... but it\\\'s better than me waiting until we\\\'re stopped at the next light and i\\\'m pulling you out of your car by your ear and beating you to death in front of the rest of the working public.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>these days i have found a balance and i can hold my tongue better than i used to but you better believe that under the skin... lie words and phrases that carry true feelings and very real emotion.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>oh, and god?  what god?</p>\r\n\r\n*best friendly',1,767,0,0,'165.121.212.146','en'),(19422,3210,'2003-01-09 04:23:22',57,'weeb','i think i heard \\\"WOOOOOOOOOOOOOO OOOO OOOOOOO HOOOOOOOOO EEEYYYYYYYEAAAAAH\\\" at least a couple of times that night. yes, definitely a couple of times.',0,155,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(19423,3211,'2003-01-09 04:53:40',129,'moebius','<br>This reminded me of how, when I was a grade-school kid, I was afraid to say curse words because God might hear me. I was already fairly dubious of God\\\'s existence, but I figured it was best to err on the safe side.<br><br>I then went through a phase where, on the brief walk from the school bus stop to my front door, I would recite, in my mind, all of the curse words I could think of--the entire litany of filth available to me at that time: <i>fuck shit piss cock cunt ass asshole...</i> <br><br>I remember doing this day after day as I walked down that sunny suburban sidewalk (always being careful to avoid stepping on the cracks) but I no longer recall <i>why</i> I did it. Maybe it was a dare, a challenge, to see what God might do.<br><br>And of course, no lighting bolts or acts of grievious harm came calling, so I guess I eventually started saying them out loud, at first timidly and then louder and louder. Perhaps it was at that point that I inferred that what I\\\'d heard people say was true: maybe God was dead. Or at least deaf.',1,1052,0,0,'148.87.1.170','en'),(19424,3211,'2004-07-27 05:13:48',63,'o','the lack of cursing is make me feel more granny like, which i welcome.  i bake and sew and say things like \\\"deary me!\\\".  s5 has caught me slipping \\\"fucker\\\" into conversation a lot, to mean \\\"thing\\\", or whatever, which is a hard habit to kick.  good luck austie!  i am with you.',6,294,0,0,'64.81.243.3','en'),(19425,2949,'2003-01-09 06:19:02',444,'danh','<p>oh lord now \\\"ras vagrant\\\" is following me around.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>i barely remember my 1st trip to portland, but what really sticks out in my mind was attempting to sleep in that basement, and then the denizens upstairs started... well i don\\\'t know what they were doing.  Squaredancing?  Militia formations?  \r\nImpromptu game of broomball?  I still sometimes wonder what they were doing.  It involved a lot of noise and large amounts of bodies moving large amounts of mass from place to place, but no words were spoken. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>That was probably the first of many ridiculously long trips to watch Sleater-Kinney perform.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I am planning another one right now. </p>',0,681,82,0,'216.102.198.168','en'),(19426,3211,'2003-01-09 12:02:01',93,'chiamattt','my new years resolution was to tell people who dont say thankyou to FUCK OFF. yeah. ',6,84,0,0,'218.145.25.79','en'),(19427,3211,'2003-01-09 12:53:55',64,'Joanna','I was taught to swear by a boy called Brendan Vice, when I was 8. I was told that \\\"fuck\\\" meant \\\"have a baby\\\" and \\\"shit\\\" meant \\\"poo\\\" so I remember one afternoon walking home with two older boys, and we decided to swear at everyone we passed, so we alternated yelling \\\"FUCK!\\\" at people with \\\"HAVE A BABY\\\".  \r\n\r\nI think I was subconciously trying to do my bit for NZ\\\'s falling birth rate. ',1,425,0,0,'203.97.2.243','en'),(19428,2949,'2003-01-09 17:03:57',86,'egg','I dont understand, what is the appeal? is it just so OVERWHELMINGLY WONDERFUL and SPONTANEOUS each time you travel hundreds of miles to hear them play that awful song \\\"I WANNA BE YOUR JOEY RAMONE\\\" once more? or perhaps you are waiting to hear a redux of the cover of \\\"DUDE WHO LOOKS LIKE A LADY\\\"? see you next month.',0,328,444,0,'199.4.104.129','en'),(19429,3211,'2003-01-09 17:41:52',240,'xep','austin, get in your car, drive 467 miles north on 101.  turn right.  drive 9 miles up the river.  chill.  we\\\'ll be here waiting.',0,131,0,0,'198.88.153.110','en'),(19430,3211,'2003-01-09 17:48:36',17,'austin','xep, that is exactly where i would like to be right now instead of war dia