Swinney a check for god\\\'s sake.',1,414,17,0,'64.210.3.222','en'),(19436,3208,'2003-01-09 21:53:09',175,'Paul G','I was really upset.  And so I walked away from the computer.  I stood in front of a mirror in another room - combing my hair, and flexing.  I lost track of time.  I had spaghetti cooking on the stove, and it burned.  It was very ironic.',0,236,0,0,'67.195.71.186','en'),(19437,3208,'2003-01-09 22:16:05',82,'simon','you flex in front of the mirror when you\\\'re upset?',1,53,175,0,'209.172.115.210','en'),(19438,3208,'2003-01-09 23:50:39',17,'austin','<H1>H A H A H A H A!</H1>',1,25,175,0,'64.2.58.24','en'),(19439,3208,'2003-01-09 23:57:19',17,'austin','paul, i\\\'m picturing you with a red face, a black plastic comb, shirtless, alternately combing pomade into a \\\'The Outsiders\\\' style hair treatment, then flexing, and then combing, then flexing.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nand it is hysterically funny.',1,241,175,0,'64.2.58.24','en'),(19440,3208,'2003-01-09 23:57:57',17,'austin','reference:<BR><BR>\r\ntravis bickle.',1,34,175,0,'64.2.58.24','en'),(19441,3208,'2003-01-10 00:15:31',175,'Paul G','<img width=400 src=\\\"http://monograph.org/paul/combs01.jpg\\\">',0,55,0,0,'67.195.71.186','en'),(19442,3208,'2003-01-10 00:19:02',175,'Paul G','No, no - comb <b>and</b> flex.  For the first time in ages, I have pretty long hair and big arms.  And I feel like a sexy bitch.',0,128,82,0,'67.195.71.186','en'),(19443,3208,'2003-01-10 00:28:35',175,'Paul G','Navy blue mechanic\\\'s shirt with the sleeves rolled up, and the front buttons open - otherwise, you were dead on.  I love my sideburns.\r\n\r\n<p>I promised myself that I would drive for a month before renting <i>Taxi Driver</i>.  It was one month, last week.  And that movie is in the vcr, now.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The comb with missing teeth is my <i>working comb</i>; it goes in the right cargo pocket of my pants.  The bathroom door of the garage is locked open, and when I do my thing in the mirror I put on quite a show: <b>\\\"Come get some!\\\"</b>  Haha.  If I don\\\'t get killed it will be a miracle!.</p>',0,604,17,0,'67.195.71.186','en'),(19444,3208,'2003-01-10 16:21:22',195,'matt','paul schrader wrote that movie with a gun on the table.  he was, as they say, under duress.<BR><BR>my favorite part of that movie is when he\\\'s watching \\\"american bandstand\\\" and sees the couples dancing while jackson browne plays on the soundtrack.  he kicks the t.v. over.  i\\\'ve felt that alienated so many times, like everybody else in the world was enjoying life but me.  that movie\\\'s full of great moments, though.',1,432,0,0,'209.208.108.71','en'),(19445,3211,'2003-01-11 00:07:47',265,'chuckspeed','<p>dude.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>karma is totally fucked when someone as erudite, literate and kick-ass as sir Swinney is outta a job and dissed by a bum.</P>\r\n\r\n<p>shitfuck was my fave curse as a kid - one thing to fuck; another altogether to shitfuck.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>what happened to the bike?\r\n\r\n',0,280,17,0,'205.188.209.48','en'),(19446,3211,'2003-01-11 00:11:13',82,'simon','<a href=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=1411\\\">fucktong!</a>',1,83,0,0,'209.172.115.210','en'),(19447,3208,'2003-01-11 00:39:16',82,'simon','jpegs?',1,6,175,0,'209.172.115.210','en'),(19448,3211,'2003-01-11 01:04:46',17,'austin','i actually totally suck in the big scheme of things.  thanks for the sentiment though!',1,86,265,0,'64.2.58.24','en'),(19449,3208,'2003-01-11 11:23:48',175,'Paul G','Only for you, simon.  I will buy a digi-cam this weekend.  I\\\'ll even send a pose in the mechanic\\\'s shirt for free.  But if you want more, I\\\'ll need a credit card number and proof that you\\\'re over 18.  You seem so innocent.',0,234,82,0,'67.195.63.138','en'),(19450,3209,'2003-01-12 01:15:26',174,'Mad Moll','Why\\\'d you write this as a poem?',6,34,0,0,'24.189.207.213','en'),(19451,3209,'2003-01-12 02:27:15',195,'matt','uh, it just came to me that way?<BR><BR>no, i\\\'m trying to vary the chapters in terms of style, kind of like some theme and variation action going on.  i wanted to have some artistic shite in the mix.',1,202,0,0,'209.208.109.24','en'),(19452,3213,'2003-01-13 00:19:21',65,'le','i used to have a dog named \\\'sepia surprise,\\\' what a strange coincidence',4,77,0,0,'216.27.183.162','en'),(19453,3213,'2003-01-13 16:52:34',175,'Paul G','I keep a Phillips screwdriver in my bag; I call him, \\\"Mr. Stabby.\\\"',0,72,0,0,'67.195.79.219','en'),(19454,3211,'2003-01-13 22:20:25',75,'tyler','he seems to at least have you thinking, doesn\\\'t he?',1,54,0,0,'165.247.165.164','en'),(19455,3215,'2003-01-16 01:07:57',154,'ryan','<p>\r\nShe can kill with a smile<br>\r\nShe can wound with her eyes<br>\r\nShe can ruin your faith with her casual lies<br>\r\nAnd she only reveals what she wants you to see<br>\r\nShe hides like a child<br>\r\nBut she\\\'s always a woman to me\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nShe can lead you to live<br>\r\nShe can take you or leave you<br>\r\nShe can ask for the truth<br>\r\nBut she\\\'ll never believe you<br>\r\nAnd she\\\'ll take what you give her as long as it\\\'s free<br>\r\nShe steals like a thief<br>\r\nBut she\\\'s always a woman to me \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nOh, she takes care of herself<br>\r\nShe can wait if she wants<br>\r\nShe\\\'s ahead of her time<br>\r\nOh, and she never gives out<br>\r\nAnd she never gives in<br>\r\nShe just changes her mind \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nShe will promise you more<br>\r\nThan the Garden of Eden<br>\r\nThen she\\\'ll carelessly cut you<br>\r\nAnd laugh while you\\\'re bleedin\\\'<br>\r\nBut she\\\'ll bring out the best<br>\r\nAnd the worst you can be<br>\r\nBlame it all on yourself<br>\r\nCause she\\\'s always a woman to me \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nShe is frequently kind<br>\r\nAnd she\\\'s suddenly cruel<br>\r\nShe can do as she pleases<br>\r\nShe\\\'s nobody\\\'s fool<br>\r\nBut she can\\\'t be convicted<br>\r\nShe\\\'s earned her degree<br>\r\nAnd the most she will do<br>\r\nIs throw shadows at you<br>\r\nBut she\\\'s always a woman to me \r\n</p>',1,1296,0,0,'67.75.229.147','en'),(19456,3217,'2003-01-16 05:03:03',59,'s5','so then what happened?',0,22,0,0,'64.81.243.3','en'),(19457,3217,'2003-01-16 05:10:44',66,'Peter','<br><tt>hypothetically speaking, of course.</tt>',1,48,0,0,'66.108.188.37','en'),(19458,3211,'2003-01-16 10:24:49',187,'kandrer','i never doubted that God is behind every trouble we encounter. this whole life is a fight against Him. be strong, Austin! :)',1,124,0,0,'211.134.102.145','en'),(19459,3217,'2003-01-16 10:47:08',59,'s5','maybe it\\\'s one of those stories where one person starts and someone else picks up.',0,85,0,0,'64.81.243.3','en'),(19460,2821,'2003-01-16 11:53:46',187,'kandrer','hey Scapegoat! sorry, i did check back, but i was \\\'away\\\' for such a long time...<br>\r\ni am not sure if i am still understanding the point here. i don\\\'t think you should change anything in your way regarding this \\\'prejudice or not\\\' issue. you seem perfect to me.<br>\r\nyou know, in fact i think any kind of idea in people\\\'s mind is okay to me, even \\\"terrible\\\" ideas (i am not talking about you). only acts count. so coming back to what you said, i would just look at the <i>way</i> you fight.',1,514,176,0,'211.134.102.145','en'),(19461,3217,'2003-01-16 18:20:41',195,'matt','i\\\'m about to do that with <U>the infidels</U>.  :P',1,53,0,0,'209.208.110.134','en'),(19462,3211,'2003-01-16 18:23:54',195,'matt','i\\\'m beginning to suspect that, too.  it certainly explains a lot.',1,68,0,0,'209.208.110.134','en'),(19463,3217,'2003-01-16 18:36:52',239,'Poonlarp','do your <i>infidels</i> end up working at ikea? maybe one of them could be the man whol proportedly let all the folks in. you could write about his all-conquoring plan to score a complete <i>Poang</i> livingroom set.',1,216,195,0,'204.168.247.129','en'),(19464,3175,'2003-01-17 07:09:04',75,'tyler','it\\\'s 26 days before i was born.',1,34,129,0,'165.247.165.164','en'),(19465,3215,'2003-01-17 07:11:55',75,'tyl