ckets are $70 a pop.  he got it fixed in a couple weeks and it is much nicer than it ever was when i had it.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ni\\\'ve got a r80gs now that is a bit more reliable and generally in good running condition.  i hope i can keep it that way.\r\n',2,576,0,0,'64.2.58.24','en'),(20442,3432,'2003-09-22 22:22:21',124,'gus','I am lame, because everything I read this all I can think is that it\\\'s really more \\\"vocabulary\\\" than \\\"linguistics\\\" - I know. I am annoying.',0,154,82,0,'63.198.55.58','en'),(20443,3432,'2003-09-22 22:22:35',124,'gus','yah i meant \\\"every time\\\" yep.',0,35,0,0,'63.198.55.58','en'),(20444,3430,'2003-09-23 14:00:22',370,'chuck d','bring the noise dave. now I know you definitely have FLQ in your blood. vive le korea libre!',6,92,0,0,'193.91.64.34','en'),(20445,3429,'2003-09-23 15:41:00',57,'weeb','<p>\r\n<br>\r\nsitting across a table, elbows on a tea stained tablecloth, finger tracing a pattern in the dust, waiting and waiting\r\n<br>\r\nfor my tea\r\n</p>',1,152,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(20446,3432,'2003-09-23 17:35:38',82,'simon','i know it is but i decided to be wrong for fun',0,46,124,0,'67.31.26.60','en'),(20447,3428,'2003-09-24 08:17:45',428,'stephen','HAH. U R PRICELESS.\r\n\r\n<3\r\n-s',2,29,0,0,'67.124.236.91','en'),(20448,3211,'2003-09-25 05:19:51',57,'weeb','today i said GOD DAMN THIS THING at the copy machine and jose said \\\'you shouldn\\\'t damn anything to hell\\\' which amused me to no end because i\\\'m not sure if he was serious or not, because hes a big homo but if he was, i forgive him for his little idiosyncracies, BUT SO i said, \\\'i\\\'m can because i\\\'m a heathen\\\' \r\n<br><br>\r\nand then he proceeded to chase me around the store sprinkling me from his personal snifter of holy water',1,448,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(20449,3434,'2003-09-25 17:42:43',75,'tyler','how about iMotivate?',1,20,0,0,'66.245.115.146','en'),(20450,3435,'2003-09-26 14:26:03',82,'simon','dude! weeb! ',0,12,0,0,'67.31.23.65','en'),(20451,3434,'2003-09-27 18:44:10',90,'leonard','http://www.somethingawful.com/articles.php?a=1675',6,49,0,0,'67.118.80.121','en'),(20452,3435,'2003-09-28 04:07:46',57,'weeb','dude! sims!!\r\n<br><br>\r\nattention sims: we miss you lots. and then some.\r\n',0,74,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(20453,3435,'2003-09-28 08:34:06',66,'Peter','<br><tt>get arms that end in hex keys and tire tools, weeb, and you\\\'ll be my perpetual biking buddy! hi, too.</tt>',1,117,57,0,'66.65.21.254','en'),(20454,3439,'2003-09-30 04:42:34',17,'austin','Oh man, \\\"LOL!\\\"',1,20,0,0,'64.2.58.24','en'),(20455,3439,'2003-09-30 05:33:55',93,'chiamattt','My inner patch is full of thorns and tumbleweed. ',0,49,0,0,'61.40.66.81','en'),(20456,3438,'2003-09-30 05:36:15',93,'chiamattt','you are my inner patch. you are the cobwebs and calcium buildup.',4,64,0,0,'61.40.66.81','en'),(20457,3439,'2003-09-30 08:29:23',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i dont think marijuana is allowed on swinney.org!</tt>',1,62,0,0,'140.251.238.136','en'),(20458,3439,'2003-09-30 14:10:29',508,'edward','Sometimes I find it hard to understand the coherence and stuff. Just for my education could you please tell me the thought behind that \\\"oh man\\\"? Would appreciate it.\r\n\r\nI promised to write, and I\\\'m going to, just so you know.',0,234,17,0,'193.10.214.64','en'),(20459,3439,'2003-09-30 14:10:58',516,'Spiccoli','Why, you know you\\\'ve at least once, all of you.  An artist that has never done any drug is lying.  At least I mess with acid and stuff.',3,138,0,0,'65.132.36.35','en'),(20460,3439,'2003-09-30 14:18:57',516,'Spiccoli','I know Austin, you are probably thinking.  \\\"What kind of pothead stoner did we let in here.\\\"  Well, the kinda that\\\'s nice and draws with colored pencils, aparently.  ',0,175,0,0,'65.132.36.35','en'),(20461,3439,'2003-09-30 14:26:39',516,'Spiccoli','Oh, and I\\\'m not fucking 17.   I just look really young.  Why, did I put that picture there; because I was intoxicated.',0,121,0,0,'65.132.36.35','en'),(20462,3439,'2003-09-30 14:37:25',516,'Spiccoli','I DON\\\'T mess with acid that is. Gotta stop the wake n bakin.',0,63,0,0,'65.132.36.35','en'),(20463,3439,'2003-09-30 15:50:13',17,'austin','Hi Ed,\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nThe expression \\\'Oh man\\\' is a shortened statement that means something more like \\\'Oh man, get a load of this\\\' or \\\'Oh man, this is really funny\\\' or \\\'Oh man, did you just see that?\\\'  Things of that nature.\r\n',0,246,508,0,'64.2.58.24','en'),(20464,3439,'2003-09-30 16:23:35',508,'edward','Umm, well, that I did now. But I think the reason why you wrote it was because of the drugs-stuff.. so nevermind. Thanks anyway.',0,128,17,0,'193.10.214.64','en'),(20465,3438,'2003-09-30 16:28:07',516,'Spiccoli','Thats great.  I\\\'m just the little nerdy kid with glasses every one stares at, but never says anything to.  I\\\'m not the best, the worst, or anywhere between.  I\\\'m just off to the side some where staring off into a deep gaze of my ADD.',0,242,0,0,'65.132.36.35','en'),(20466,3439,'2003-09-30 18:17:21',239,'Poonlarp','welcome to spiccoli.org',6,23,17,0,'66.65.21.254','en'),(20467,3422,'2003-10-01 05:19:11',175,'Paul G','<p>\r\n<i>\\\"ate a burger\\\"</i>\r\n<br>\r\nteehee!\r\n<br>\r\ni bet you did...\r\n<br>\r\nbut, the offer is still good - even the offer to provide bail money...\r\n<br>\r\ntake care of yourself, sims.\r\n<br>\r\np.s. i checked, \\\"burn! burn!\\\" just to let you know that my feelings were hurt; nothing personal.\r\n<br>\r\np.p.s. maybe hool will bring his cam in the taxi, one night...\r\n</p>',6,371,82,0,'199.35.157.174','en'),(20468,3439,'2003-10-01 05:20:54',175,'Paul G','Poonlarp.',1,9,239,0,'199.35.157.174','en'),(20469,3439,'2003-10-01 09:53:27',234,'etienne','i am gobsmacked.',1,16,17,0,'210.55.37.53','en'),(20470,3439,'2003-10-01 14:35:34',93,'chiamattt','sometimes the six year old will put a pencil in her nose and wipe it on my pants. I shrug it off and tell her to finish writing her BIG F.',0,138,0,0,'61.40.66.81','en'),(20471,3436,'2003-10-01 14:54:14',93,'chiamattt','Spiccoli: I dont really care if you have ADD or if you are BIPOLAR. Should that make me think of you any differently? Should I \\\"cut you some slack\\\"? I think if we had everyone on this site bring up their medical records, we\\\'d find people who have had as hard a time. Im sorry people stared at you. Just be glad you have some people on this site warmly joking with you about something you wrote. If the SWINNEY.ORG team didn\\\'t like your shit, they really would not have posted it. Take a pill, sniff a bump, do what you do. Just chill out man. Hi im dave.  ',6,568,0,0,'61.40.66.81','en'),(20472,2634,'2003-10-01 17:39:15',516,'Spiccoli','The poser punk sorta seems like the guy off of SLC Punk.',0,56,0,0,'65.132.36.20','en'),(20473,3439,'2003-10-01 22:26:09',66,'Peter','<img src=\\\"http://image.pathfinder.com/teenpeople/images/yearbook99/spiccoli.gif\\\">',1,87,0,0,'66.65.21.254','en'),(20474,3439,'2003-10-02 03:18:59',57,'weeb','wow, i\\\'ve never seen a male GlamorShot (tm) before.',0,54,0,0,'63.197.69.58','en'),(20475,3432,'2003-10-02 06:05:32',93,'chiamattt','the word \\\"gook\\\" came from here in Korea. The korean word for \\\"american\\\" is \\\"me-gook\\\"...so when all the koreans were saying \\\"megook\\\" around the american soldiers during the Korean war, they thought they were saying \\\"im a gook\\\". ',1,257,0,0,'61.40.66.81','en'),(20476,3432,'2003-10-02 13:00:38',66,'Peter','<br><tt><A href=\\\"http://www.ku.edu/~ibetext/korean-war-l/2001/06/msg00348.html\\\">miguk</a>.</tt>',1,101,0,0,'66.65.21.254','en'),(20477,3439,'2003-10-02 14:07:45',508,'edward','wrong url: http://www.cannabinoid.com/users/spiccoli399396.shtml',0,64,239,0,'193.10.214.15','en'),(20478,3436,'2003-10-02 16:57:53',82,'simon','hi dave!',0,8,0,0,'67.31.3.129','en'),(20479,3439,'2003-10-02 16:59:25',82,'simon','you havent!? my friend seth has them done all the time. he\\\'s got a rather impressive collection.',1,99,57,0,'67.31.3.129','en'),(20480,3439,'2003-10-02 19:45:44',75,'tyler','this isn\\\'t really easy to say, but...sometimes, when i\\\'m all alone you know, and it\\\'s late, and i\\\'m pretty sure my neighbors are asleep...i like to play with my patch. i call it \\\'patch-time.\\\' but there\\\'s nothing growing in <i>there</i>, LOL!',1,262,0,0,'66.32.106.158','en'),(20481,3439,'2003-10-03 03:01:06',154,'ryan','anyone know where i can score some pcp?',0,39,0,0,'216.99.204.24','en'),(20482,3439,'2003-10-03 18:18:47',129,'moebius','damn, i was hoping this entry meant people would start swapping their favorite drug-trip stories. kind of like that spate of hilarious \\\"vomiting in public\\\" stories that swept through swinney a couple years back.',0,217,0,0,'148.87.1.171','en'),(20483,3439,'2003-10-05 04:56:20',17,'austin','<B>YEARS</B>, this site has been around for <B>YEARS</B>.  \r\n<BR><BR>\r\n*DESTABILIZING*',4,86,129,0,'64.2.58.24','en'),(20484,3433,'2003-10-06 01:40:05',66,'Peter','<br><tt>given my luck lately, im sort of glad i sold my car and bought a bicycle...</tt>',1,88,0,0,'66.65.21.254','en'),(20485,3445,'2003-10-09 20:58:32',372,'mews','<p>i have never puked in public. i feel, for my age, that ive failed somehow because of this. everyone else has Super Vomit Tales that they happily recount with a fond haze in their eyes, and i\\\'m always secretly annoyed that i cant join in. doing it on purpose just wouldn\\\'t be the same though i guess.</p>',0,312,0,0,'203.109.254.40','en'),(20486,3445,'2003-10-09 22:24:09',66,'Peter','<br><tt><A href=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=2061\\\">puke</a>...</tt>',1,94,0,0,'66.65.21.254','en'),(20487,3445,'2003-10-10 01:34:42',372,'mews','see?? everyone!!  :)',0,20,0,0,'203.109.254.40','en'),(20488,3445,'2003-10-10 01:34:58',372,'mews','<p>see?? everyone!!  :)</p>',0,27,0,0,'203.109.254.40','en'),(20489,3448,'2003-10-10 16:31:18',370,'seanthecon','that\\\'s nice chia. now where\\\'e the apology you owe me for ruining two years of my life. those were my \\\'balls don\\\'t smell like feces\\\' years. i can\\\'t get my girlfriend to go down on me now. she calls them \\\'shit balls\\\'. what are you going to do about that? don\\\'t forget the apology you owe my mother for impregnating her with your horse semen and the one you owe my father for impregnating him with your sheep semen. shit chia, this apology thing better just be the start of a trend.',6,506,0,0,'193.91.64.34','en'),(20490,3439,'2003-10-11 22:20:58',195,'matt','dude.  you\\\'re hot.<BR><BR>i think this picture\\\'s going in my leetle collection.\r\n',1,87,0,0,'209.208.110.228','en'),(20491,3445,'2003-10-13 00:57:26',195,'matt','my best puke was in the back of a cop car.',1,42,0,0,'209.208.109.123','en'),(20492,3445,'2003-10-13 01:58:46',66,'Peter','<br><Tt>careful... the last person i knew that repeatedly bragged about never puking (or puking in public, for that matter) soonafter got arrested... for mooning the entire world... from within the glass-ensconsed external elevator of the marriot marquis in times\\\' square... during the millennium new year\\\'s celebration. yep.</tt>',1,336,372,0,'66.65.21.254','en'),(20493,3448,'2003-10-13 12:02:56',65,'le','don\\\'t you have a cat? what is wrong with you?',0,48,0,0,'216.27.177.123','en'),(20494,3448,'2003-10-13 13:35:19',93,'chiamattt','good question. I dont really know anymore. ',1,43,65,0,'218.39.19.11','en'),(20495,3451,'2003-10-14 21:30:55',176,'Scapegoat','I read your comment about your possible regret and think of all the times that the same feeling has plagued me.<br><br>\r\nThe thing is those experiences make us who we are, regardless of whether we are still taking part in certain behaviours or not. The idea that someone\\\'s past may make someone uncomfortable is understandable but the possibility that there wouldn\\\'t even be a connection if not for the form that those past experiences have given us is something that I wouldn\\\'t want to risk.<br><br>\r\nI hope that what I\\\'m trying to say makes sense. I\\\'d fight the feelings of regret.<br><br>  ',1,608,0,0,'159.33.2.41','en'),(20496,3451,'2003-10-15 01:42:42',75,'tyler','even i am enough of a feminist to be upset by your adoption of the male v. female double standard when it comes to number of sexual partners.',1,141,0,0,'66.32.115.176','en'),(20497,3451,'2003-10-15 07:32:24',234,'etienne','what?  i thought it was more an individual regret rather than a \\\'because i\\\'m a chick and have slept with x number of people he\\\'ll think i\\\'m a slut because i like to propagate stereotypes about sluts v. studs\\\'.  mate.',1,231,75,0,'203.96.108.229','en'),(20498,3450,'2003-10-15 07:34:17',234,'etienne','it\\\'s the wanting that makes the difference',0,45,0,0,'203.96.108.229','en'),(20499,3451,'2003-10-15 13:47:49',392,'p.','I don\\\'t really recall clarifying my stance on male sluts as opposed to the female version.  I can see how his \\\"not liking\\\" whatever slutism might be in my past perhaps be misunderstood to be criticism, as opposed to what it is: a slight amount of jealousy over situations in which he had no control, and quite frankly don\\\'t matter any more.  It is a disagreement over a moral issue that no longer concerns us, sex without love; sex simply for the sake of sex, male or female.  \r\n\r\nAnd c\\\'mon.  The word \\\'slut\\\' makes you giggle at least little bit.',0,567,75,0,'12.13.167.78','en'),(20500,3447,'2003-10-15 17:11:38',93,'chiamattt','i liked this a lot. ',1,20,0,0,'218.39.19.10','en'),(20501,3451,'2003-10-15 17:16:24',75,'tyler','her sense of guilt reinforces the stereotype, see? she says explicity that she doesn\\\'t regret the <i>sexual activity by itself,</i> but only in light of a man\\\'s opinion. this in effect filters her self-image through a man\\\'s/society\\\'s prejudicial stereotypes, giving real weight to and making her complicit in those stereotypes, as i read it.',1,353,0,0,'66.32.157.57','en'),(20502,3451,'2003-10-15 18:42:44',234,'etienne','there\\\'s a difference between thinking about it because suddenly it might matter to someone you care about and thinking about it in terms of what the whole world thinks of you.  sometimes things like this are not buying into stereotypes, they JUST ARE.',3,254,0,0,'210.55.38.126','en'),(20503,3451,'2003-10-15 18:43:10',392,'p.','<p>You\\\'re correct in saying that it his perception that causes her misgivigs.  However, you\\\'re also making the assumption that it is her <i>sex in combination with her actions</i> that causes his. </p>\r\n\r\n',0,211,75,0,'12.13.167.78','en'),(20504,3445,'2003-10-15 18:43:20',17,'austin','Arrested for mooning!  I can\\\'t belive that.  Say it isn\\\'t so!\r\n<BR><BR>\r\n\\\"We have a possible MOONer in the Marriot elevator.  Send a officer to check it out.\\\"',2,170,66,0,'66.128.224.196','en'),(20505,3451,'2003-10-15 19:10:16',392,'p.','Actually, scapegoat, you\\\'re making perfect sense.  And I do agree.',0,69,176,0,'12.13.167.78','en'),(20506,3451,'2003-10-16 07:10:28',234,'etienne','i just watched \\\"best in show\\\". that woman with the geeky husband and all the men recognising her and alluding to shared sexual experiences made me think of this.',0,167,0,0,'210.55.125.154','en'),(20507,3445,'2003-10-17 02:36:50',372,'mews','<p>new years inhabits its own universe, and should be exempt from comparisons to everything outside it. can i also brag about having never seen a real life mooner? plenty of streakers, but no sly flashing or slapping of creamy  moonbuttock. not a one.  </p>',0,257,0,0,'203.109.254.40','en'),(20508,3451,'2003-10-17 03:39:53',75,'tyler','good point, p. ',1,15,0,0,'66.245.105.188','en'),(20509,3454,'2003-10-17 16:28:02',17,'austin','This is the greatest article I\\\'ve read in a long time.  You should perform it. Thanks!',1,89,0,0,'64.2.58.24','en'),(20510,3451,'2003-10-17 16:58:07',176,'Scapegoat','It took me a while to make peace with my collected experiences but I imagine them as a sort of crucible that has given me the ability to genuinely feel for a partner.<br><br>\r\nI wouldn\\\'t give that up.',1,203,392,0,'159.33.2.41','en'),(20511,3454,'2003-10-19 00:54:23',75,'tyler','this is awesome. where i live we have a grocery store called the fresh market. it is darker and quieter. even the labeling on the packages seems subdued somehow. it is also way more expensive.',1,192,0,0,'66.32.144.155','en'),(20512,3451,'2003-10-19 01:35:26',66,'Peter','<br><tt>only insecure jerks ask the \\\"how many\\\" question. he should realize that, after all that experience, if youre dating him, he must stack up pretty well in all aspects. thats like the hugest compliment, no?</tt>',0,222,0,0,'66.65.21.254','en'),(20513,3445,'2003-10-19 02:56:23',82,'simon','PRESSED HAM! --ps. i once got in trouble for mooning.',0,53,0,0,'12.236.164.112','en'),(20514,3455,'2003-10-19 19:02:15',175,'Paul G','this was both a pleasure to read, and also engaging...it made me think.',1,71,0,0,'199.35.155.73','en'),(20515,3455,'2003-10-19 20:02:02',17,'austin','Thanks Paul G.  I am always hesitant to post stuff like this because I know my logic is never fully explored and full of holes.  But then again, I was only walking down the street / thinking about a strange personals ad.',1,220,175,0,'64.2.58.24','en'),(20516,3438,'2003-10-19 21:54:57',477,'jehannum','<p>this absolutely rocked. and burger mayo on the crotch of black suit trousers is a bad look in anyone\\\'s language, especially when the office you work in isn\\\'t that far from the red light district...</p>\r\n\r\n<p>oh, and buy a sony ericsson, they\\\'re heaps better... :)</p>',1,279,0,0,'210.54.176.118','en'),(20517,3451,'2003-10-20 11:28:58',370,'seanthecon','c\\\'mon man. sex is fucking sex. everybody is weird and kinky about it. this has nothing to do with slut vs stud. there are many women who feel uncomfortable with the number of fucks their male partner has had in the past. and how can you not ask your partner how many? that\\\'s fucked up. everyone is curious. if you don\\\'t ask you\\\'re probably just insecure that your numbers won\\\'t match up. if people want to be hung up about sex that\\\'s their bobby brown prerogative, but life is like too $hort man, and you can\\\'t worry about who gets spanked and how gets to hump the chicken.',6,594,0,0,'193.91.64.34','en'),(20518,3455,'2003-10-20 16:38:25',82,'elvis costello','blaim it on cain/ don\\\'t blame it on me/ oh it\\\'s nobody\\\'s fault/ but we need somebody to burn',0,101,0,0,'12.236.164.112','en'),(20519,3455,'2003-10-20 17:42:31',17,'austin','...learn something new everyday.',1,32,82,0,'66.128.224.196','en'),(20520,3455,'2003-10-20 17:55:30',75,'tyler','it seems like, to have a social group, you need both positive and negative factors. positive in the sense that the group does or has the qualities of <i>x</i>, exhibits certain behaviors or attributes, and negative in the sense that the group does not do certain things or appear certain ways. if this is true, then what we call society, the group composed of \\\'average\\\' people, <i>does</i> then need social outcasts to help cement everyone else\\\'s status in the group. what if all these outcasts had their own secret society? see <u>The Crying of Lot 49</u>, by Thomas Pynchon. do i still owe you a book, or did you get the one about string theory?',1,656,0,0,'66.245.93.105','en'),(20521,3454,'2003-10-20 20:45:33',372,'mews','<p>no, thank you :)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>i\\\'m very willing to trade up in price for a more pleasant and relaxed  shopping experience. its nice to not be served by robots sometimes too</p>',0,178,0,0,'203.109.254.40','en'),(20522,3455,'2003-10-20 21:12:15',82,'simon','i love that book, i just bought it for my sister',0,48,0,0,'12.236.164.112','en'),(20523,3455,'2003-10-20 21:28:14',17,'austin','I got that string theory book.  I can\\\'t say I have read it yet though.  Perhaps some day.  <BR><BR> I tried to read the Crying of Lot 49.  I just coul