y writing appeals to some people...sometimes.  it\\\'s a good feeling i think.  maybe a little confusing.\r\n</p>',2,174,122,0,'64.175.32.199','en'),(20784,3526,'2004-02-04 23:49:28',83,'adamajah','<p>sixteenth notes echo<br>\r\nLars lives in my fingertips<br> \r\ncube-farm disturbance?<br>\r\n</p>',3,95,0,0,'216.206.179.50','en'),(20785,3526,'2004-02-05 03:50:04',66,'Peter','<br><tt>integration grape<br>\r\nno hula hoop dancing here<br>\r\nbreathe with the movement?<br></tt>',1,97,0,0,'66.65.23.42','en'),(20786,3528,'2004-02-05 03:56:46',239,'Poonlarp','<b>swinney scorecard:</b><Br>\r\n<i>use of \\\'secret\\\' in story... 13<br>\r\nuse of \\\'hooty hoo\\\' in story... 0</i>',6,118,0,0,'66.65.23.42','en'),(20787,3528,'2004-02-05 07:16:01',234,'etienne','yeah man, where\\\'s the hooty hoo?  there\\\'s not enough of that shit',2,71,0,0,'210.55.167.241','en'),(20788,3528,'2004-02-05 07:19:59',234,'etienne','p.s., i really liked this kandrer. you rock.',0,44,0,0,'210.55.167.241','en'),(20789,3526,'2004-02-05 18:27:48',75,'tyler','oh no, here we go\r\nagain with the haiku shit\r\nthanks a lot, assholes',1,68,0,0,'66.32.105.69','en'),(20790,3526,'2004-02-05 18:28:33',75,'tyler','oops, i forgot to<br>\r\nuse html as told<br>\r\nnow look at me go',1,62,0,0,'66.32.105.69','en'),(20791,3521,'2004-02-06 16:01:53',273,'Quinn','That is an unauthorized post.  Griece is dead.',0,46,534,0,'63.150.109.234','en'),(20792,3529,'2004-02-06 22:29:56',65,'le','i\\\'m confused. what exactly is your job?',4,42,0,0,'64.242.240.2','en'),(20793,3521,'2004-02-06 23:29:49',534,'griece','you take that back or i fuck you up nice and good, see?',5,55,273,0,'66.65.23.42','en'),(20794,3526,'2004-02-06 23:58:26',66,'Peter','<br><tt>pay pee poh pay pee<br>\r\npee, pee py picky py pee<br>\r\npy poh picky py</tt>',1,83,0,0,'66.65.23.42','en'),(20795,3529,'2004-02-07 09:34:46',533,'incitor','I do plainclothes investigations and loss prevention.  ',2,55,65,0,'64.175.32.199','en'),(20796,3528,'2004-02-07 20:08:41',187,'kandrer','mmm... i am not sure, but i am glad you like it. thanks a lot my dear :).',1,73,234,0,'221.119.220.254','en'),(20797,3530,'2004-02-09 03:35:49',93,'chiamattt','fuck this was cool. ',1,20,0,0,'211.214.6.90','en'),(20798,3535,'2004-02-10 18:58:12',66,'Peter','<br><tt>maybe life has been hard, finally, due to your golfball theft. id recommend taking them to the nearest body of water and dumping them in. <br><br>we have a similar fireplace/mantle that sits in obsolete stasis... get some new candles. candles that are only yours, and burn them in the fireplace.<br><br>create a life that is yours again from amongst the leftovers that you have from sharing its past with others.</tt> ',1,426,0,0,'156.145.58.57','en'),(20799,3530,'2004-02-11 07:37:16',83,'adamajah','First Swinney I read in months.',1,31,0,0,'216.206.179.50','en'),(20800,3535,'2004-02-11 14:53:13',228,'belly','being a writer isn\\\'t that hard if you really want to be one. trick is, you actually have to write stuff, instead of waiting for people to ask you to write stuff.<br><br>\r\n\r\n1. think of some story ideas. \r\n<br><br>\r\n2. email the editors of relevant magazines/newspapers/places in which writing is published with briefs. perhaps <i>golfing world</i> is a good place to start.\r\n<br><br>\r\n3. do some for free if you have to at first. \r\n<br><br>\r\n4. collect payment.\r\n<br><br>\r\n5. repeat/work on novel in spare time.\r\n<br><br>\r\n6. congratulations, you are now a freelance writer.\r\n\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nnote to self: do this.',0,615,0,0,'194.128.172.227','en'),(20801,3530,'2004-02-11 19:24:02',239,'Poonlarp','that\\\'s not true. you <a href=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=3526#20784\\\">commented</a> on one of my pieces merely a week ago.',6,152,83,0,'156.145.58.57','en'),(20802,3526,'2004-02-11 19:25:27',239,'Poonlarp','you people have no<br>\r\nwicked haiku skil-il-ils<br>\r\nbut im on fire<br>',6,72,0,0,'156.145.58.57','en'),(20803,1607,'2004-02-11 19:30:25',239,'Poonlarp','this is grand',6,13,0,0,'156.145.58.57','en'),(20804,3535,'2004-02-12 02:32:37',75,'tyler','this is exactly why i decided to go to law school.',1,50,0,0,'66.245.102.226','en'),(20805,3535,'2004-02-12 02:33:11',75,'tyler','also--i like to play golf. don\\\'t hate me, man. ',1,50,0,0,'66.245.102.226','en'),(20806,3535,'2004-02-12 03:54:54',66,'Peter','<br><tt>a golfing lawyer? no way!</tt>',1,38,75,0,'66.65.23.42','en'),(20807,3530,'2004-02-12 05:35:30',93,'chiamattt','hi adamajah. It is nice to see you are still alive and well. ',1,61,0,0,'218.39.19.69','en'),(20808,3530,'2004-02-12 05:35:32',93,'chiamattt','hi adamajah. It is nice to see you are still alive and well. ',1,61,0,0,'218.39.19.68','en'),(20809,3530,'2004-02-12 10:22:46',223,'shanE','That was a really decent piece of work. Provided me with some enjoyment. Thanks.',0,80,0,0,'218.145.25.75','en'),(20810,3535,'2004-02-12 15:24:20',273,'Quinn','Sorry Tyler, I\\\'m required to hate you.  You\\\'re a lawyer.  ',1,64,75,0,'63.150.109.234','en'),(20811,1607,'2004-02-12 21:05:41',228,'belly','<a href=\\\"http://www.nationallampoon.com/nl/08_features/WCS/cover.asp\\\">how to masturbate in the line of gunfire</a>',0,120,0,0,'81.178.198.52','en'),(20812,3536,'2004-02-13 15:00:07',273,'Quinn','Elvis stood on the corner with his hands in his pockets.  There was nothing to do, no place to go.  He watched the taxi cabs pass with patrons inside them.  They were going somewhere, had some purpose beyond their present.  Something else lay in their future even if was just going to the hardware store.  Elvis looked down at his two-tone shoes.  The shoelaces were doubleknotted.  He had polished them to a high gloss the night before.  He had expected to find his friends Troy and Carter on the corner, but that hadn\\\'t shown up yet.  Elvis rubbed his shoes on the back of his pants legs to make sure they\\\'d be clean when Troy and Carter finally arrived.  The three of them had strong opinions about their shoes, and Elvis did not want to be found lacking.',1,764,0,0,'63.150.109.234','en'),(20813,3536,'2004-02-13 18:14:29',66,'Peter','<br><tt>carter stood under a busted street light. while he waited for elvis, he studied the flickering shadows cast on the sooty, broken pavement below. <i>\\\"why the fuck is elvis always late?\\\"</i> he mused, while watching the broken glass glint from the nestled cracks under the penumbra cast by the snazzy homemade red-white-and-blue chuck taylor platforms he had stolen from troy the night before. see, troy had a short term memory problem caused by narcotics abuse, and was an easy mark when he needed new kicks. carter contemplated calling elvis on his cell, and would have too, if elvis hadnt \\\"borrowed\\\" it the night before so he could look like a pure playa to the other trannies. that damn elvis, always confusing the street numbers with the avenues, always standing on the wrong corner for the hookup. frowning, he walked off, figuring he\\\'d have to find a new, more reliable source for his <i>\\\"bulging beauties\\\"</i> fat-girl pr0n...</tt>',1,966,273,0,'156.145.58.11','en'),(20814,3530,'2004-02-14 06:09:35',83,'adamajah','<p>No, I wrote a haiku.  But I\\\'ll read it right now.  ;)</p>',2,63,239,0,'216.206.179.50','en'),(20815,3534,'2004-02-14 15:26:49',477,'jehannum','<p>please forgive my assumptions of empathy and affinity (see also \\\"this is the feeling...\\\" that i posted two minutes ago, and you will understand what is behind the rush of honesty)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>i offer you here (in friendship) a stream of consciousness so that you may (i hope) know that you are not alone</P>\r\n\r\n<tt>it\\\'s seeing his face pasted on top of yours when you talk to people the way does. cringing when you say things you have heard coming from his mouth. shout or nag a girlfriend the way he always spoke to you. wanting to change your name, to cling to just your first name and denounce him. chewing and grinding your teeth and making fists in the dark, wishing he could hear all the vitriol flying around in your head and wishing it would bring him to his knees. it\\\'s being angry at the world and driving friends away even when you love them, and hating them for leaving.</tt>\r\n\r\n<p>it is also several years on, after you nearly destroyed each other with pain. when you cried and threw things and screamed. where you live in a world where they know he is your son, and you just take the best of it for yourself and throw the rest aside. where it still takes you five days to calm down after seeing him, but you learn to play the political family game so that you can keep him happy and at arms length, and live your own life.<p>\r\n\r\n<p>again i apologise for my assumptions. you are your own person, and i wish you strength and happiness and future.</P>\r\n\r\n<p>please know that reading your article and replying, at the very least, gave me a tremendous feeling of worth and purpose at 4.23 in the morning. karma does exist, and we are all here for one another in some way.<p>',1,1696,0,0,'203.109.157.66','en'),(20816,3537,'2004-02-15 06:26:58',477,'jehannum','it is also the evening-after cringe factor of realising that in a fit of chemically-induced self-confidence and hippydom you have decided to share these thoughts with the world, and it is certainly the most arduous and largely ineffective proof-read and painful insertion of paragraph tags in the history of web publishing.',0,323,0,0,'210.48.81.175','en'),(20817,3538,'2004-02-15 08:04:31',266,'spleenless','I was on a research vessel near midway island when someone caught a big marlin.  I\\\'m not sure it\\\'s really possible for a marlin to show much in the way of expression on his face but I could swear he looked surprised to find himself on the deck of that ship being clubbed to death by hungry scientists.  If anyone had asked me, I probably would have voted to throw him back.  Nobody asked so I helped eat him later.  He was extremely tasty.',1,445,0,0,'63.193.168.40','en'),(20818,3537,'2004-02-15 22:09:06',228,'belly','as a friend and i marvelled early this morning: they\\\'re so little, but so <i>change</i>y!\r\n\r\nthis post matches my mood perfectly.',0,132,0,0,'81.178.193.0','en'),(20819,1200,'2004-02-16 02:12:32',534,'griece','yep!',0,4,0,0,'66.65.23.42','en'),(20820,3534,'2004-02-16 05:29:16',370,'seanthecon','i thought this said \\\'when you ate your dad\\\'. different story.',6,67,0,0,'67.68.51.181','en'),(20821,3537,'2004-02-16 12:31:34',75,'tyler','thats why i quit doing ecstasy--the cringe factor. but all you did was write an article on the web, not, say, grab the microphone in an enormous (ENORMOUS) bar in Charleston, so you could \\\'do a song.\\\'',1,206,0,0,'66.245.17.184','en'),(20822,3537,'2004-02-17 16:15:28',228,'belly','it\\\'s motherfucking tuesdays from hell and swearing NEVER AGAIN.',0,66,0,0,'194.128.172.227','en'),(20823,3536,'2004-02-17 16:56:05',273,'Quinn','The moon outside Elvis\\\'s hotel window was big as a dollop of butter on a stack of IHOP pancakes. He had opened the window to the night.  A cool breeze stirred the curtains.  Elvis had waited all night for Carter but he hadn\\\'t shown up. He had really needed to make this particular hookup \\\'cuz he was lacking in funds, not even sure where next week\\\'s rent was coming from.  In fact, just coming home today he\\\'d had to creep past the landlady\\\'s door trying to avoid the loose floorboards.  Elvis hated those unintentional run-ins with the landlady, the insistent demands for the rent, the threats, the insults.  He set Carter\\\'s cell phone on the table. The fact that Carter was without it meant that he could not be reached as he did not have a landline.  He could call Troy, but what good would that do?  That motherfucking junkie hadn\\\'t shown up either.  What good was friendship?  What good was integrity?  Didn\\\'t anyone honor their commitments anymore?  Elvis found a half full whiskey bottle in the cabinet, uncapped it and took a long hit.  Then, suddenly angry, he went over to the table and smashed Carter\\\'s cell phone with the hill of the whiskey bottle.  Pieces of Japanese plastic scattered around the room.  The whiskey bottle stayed intact.  He uncapped it and took another deep drink.',1,1326,0,0,'67.130.105.66','en'),(20824,3536,'2004-02-17 18:12:17',534,'griece','...and you know what they say about the moon acting as a harbinger of lunacy. was doubly the case for elvis, soggy as he was in the soothing, deadening elixer of whiskey and a sordid coctail of random under-the-table female growth hormones, incidentally, the last of his dose of goods from troy, that motherfucker. even carter couldnt be counted on to deliver some fucking porno. who can a he/she trust these days? broke, drunk and frustrated, elvis passed the remainder of the evening tesselating the fractured plastic cell shards into vaguely humanesque forms, writhing, copulating, homoerotic... images he fleshed out into visual fantasies shortly before passing out in a pool of his own vomit on the floor... hopefully the landlady wouldn\\\'t rear her ugly disfigured face before the pending hangover wore off...\r\n\r\n',5,821,0,0,'156.145.58.57','en'),(20825,1237,'2004-02-17 18:13:25',534,'griece','anyway.',5,7,0,0,'156.145.58.57','en'),(20826,1217,'2004-02-17 18:14:14',534,'griece','with some passing time spent in hindsight, ive finally begun forming answers to many of the existential questions that have plagued me in the past.',5,147,0,0,'156.145.58.57','en'),(20827,3536,'2004-02-17 19:16:32',273,'Quinn','...but the door was locked, thankfully, and Elvis had pushed a chair under the doorknob, barring the unexpected entry of his landlady.  \r\n\r\nWhen he came to, his face caked with sticky regurgitation.  He was shocked that he had passed out.  Two drinks?  He must have had more, but couldn\\\'t recall drinking that much.  He unfolded his limbs and shakily stood up.  \r\n\r\nThere was something happening to him.  He looked down at his chest and the buds of his incipient breasts there.  He reached under his shirt and touched his nipples which were exceptionally raw and tender.\r\n\r\nHe grimmaced and rubbed his face.  The drugs hadn\\\'t killed his beard yet.  He\\\'d have to shave before going out.  Elvis grabbed his shaving lotion and razor.  He carefully moved the chair from under the doorknob, and opened the door.  The bathroom was down the hall.\r\n',1,850,0,0,'67.130.105.66','en'),(20828,3536,'2004-02-17 19:30:45',239,'Poonlarp','en route to the bathroom, elvis\\\' head felt like the class dweeb getting pummelled in an elementary school dodge-ball game. except instead of soft rubber kickballs, it was shot after shot of whiskey that was making his head feel like a quickly sinking ship.<br><br>he raised his bare forearm to wipe the slurry of puke from his stubble, as well as the crust from his eyes, so dizzy that he wasnt sure which he was wiping clean... or, if he was actualyl just smearing the shit around his face.<br><br>\r\nthe latter must have been the case, as he was snapped back to clarity by the shreik of his landlady, who was coming up the staircase, trying to ward off the city pest-control inspector... to elvis\\\' credit, despite his long outstanding rent, the only thing she was concerned about at that very moment was how to get her head around the image of a half-nude, topless, puke-covered transexual man with a greaser coiff stumbling towards the shit-stinking communal bathroom... which was the source of the sub-code vermin in the first place...',6,1044,0,0,'156.145.58.57','en'),(20829,1237,'2004-02-17 19:35:19',273,'Quinn','Who brought griece back?  He is supposed to be dead.....  He was glad to be gone....',6,84,0,0,'67.130.105.66','en'),(20830,3536,'2004-02-17 19:53:05',273,'Quinn','...somehow Elvis got around the landlady, who stood stock-still, dazed by his outlandish appearence.  What the fuck was she so suprised about?  Up until her operation just a few years ago, she\\\'d had a prong dangling between her legs too.  Christ!  He looked at himself in the cracked bathroom mirror.  They were just breasts, and little ones at that.  He cupped them in his hands and lifted them a bit.  Maybe it was the Presely hairdo.  Carter and Troy told him constantly that he was going to need to change his style, but Elvis didn\\\'t have a solid idea for his next identity.  The bathroom wasn\\\'t all that bad once you got used to it.  Life stinks, it may as well stink like shit.  He lathered up with the shaving cream, put the razor to his ceek and scraped away the black bristles.  Outside the bathroom, the landlady had recovered from her reverie.  She pounded on the door, YOU GET YOUR SLIMY ASS OUT OF THEIR ELVIS!  She screamed, WHEN AM I GONNA GET MY RENT!?  Elvis calmly killed a cockroach that had attempted to crawl into his shaving kit.  AS SOON AS YOU GET RID OF THESE GODDAMN ROACHES!  I AIN\\\'T PAYIN\\\' YOU A DIME UNTIL THIS PLACE IS FIT TO LIVE IN!  He used a washcloth to towel the vomit and sour sweat from his torso, then turned, unlocked the door and pushed it hard.  The landlady went flying back and hit the wall.  Elvis squared himself on his feet.  I\\\'M ON RENT STRIKE, YOU BITCH.  YOU\\\'LL GET YOUR RENT WHEN YOU CLEAN UP THIS DUMP!  He stormed off down the hall, stomping his feet hard.  The landlady and the city inspector stared after him.  Then, behind him Elvis heard the city inspector speak to the landlady:  \\\"Do you have a roache problem in this building, ma\\\'am?\\\"  Elvis grinned to himself.  At best, he\\\'d bought himself another free week.',1,1802,0,0,'67.130.105.66','en'),(20831,3540,'2004-02-18 18:02:27',75,'tyler','<p>having both not-gone to college and then having gone, i have to say that the prospect of a life without college is more frightening than actually going. or i should say, the prospect of being an <i>intelligent</i> person and not going is a frightening one. college basically proves to a skeptical (and rightly so!) world that you have both the discipline to learn, and the capacity to apply, complicated concepts. without higher education, employers and others will assume that you do not possess that ability, no matter what your outward appearance may suggest, and they will treat you accordingly--in which case, i have noticed two main responses among the people i have known in life: 1) those people become fed up with taking orders from those less intelligent than themselves, and end up going to college after all; and 2) those people decide that maybe they aren\\\'t so smart after all, their minds fracture, and they adjust their self-images downward to fit the perception of society. </p>',1,1000,0,0,'66.245.17.184','en'),(20832,3540,'2004-02-18 19:43:20',66,'Peter','<br><tt>heres to never adjusting your self-image downward...</tt>',1,65,75,0,'156.145.58.57','en'),(20833,3540,'2004-02-18 21:05:51',75,'tyler','<p>i was thinking about my earlier comment in class just now, and i think i might have been a little too black-and-white on the subject. of course, there are very smart people who don\\\'t go to college and lead happy, successful lives. if you can figure out how to do that, i say go for it. </p><p>\r\nmy cautionary statement, though amended, still stands--most people i know who have been really smart and not gone to college of some kind, or who dropped out, have ended up pretty fucked up and unhappy. or what i consider worse, a kind of \\\'forced happy\\\' in a shitty situation. </p>',1,588,0,0,'66.245.17.184','en'),(20834,3540,'2004-02-19 03:44:11',534,'griece','life\\\'s all about forced happy in a shitty situation. ',5,56,75,0,'66.108.170.192','en'),(20835,3526,'2004-02-19 19:23:50',83,'adamajah','<p>spin clockwise six times<br>\r\noffice space is your lock-down<br>\r\nfoam-filled coaster whore<br></p>\r\n',1,104,0,0,'216.206.179.50','en'),(20836,3526,'2004-02-19 21:49:37',66,'Peter','<br><tt>pimpin\\\' like a cat<br>\r\non a mouse, pimpin\\\' all the<br>\r\nhoneyz in the house<br></tt>',1,99,83,0,'156.145.58.11','en'),(20837,3540,'2004-02-20 06:19:24',266,'spleenless','Every year you don\\\'t go to college it will get more difficult to talk yourself into going.\r\n<br><br>\r\nOn the other hand, it would have been useless for me to go straight out of highschool.  I was too busy taking drugs and crashing motorcycles.  I had no idea what I wanted to be when I grew up.\r\n<br><br>\r\nBack on the first hand, you may not suffer the same vices I did.\r\n<br><br>\r\nOn a third hand that\\\'s somewhat similar to the second one, I\\\'m finding that my age and experience give me a significant advantage over a lot of the younger students.\r\n<br><br>\r\nIt helps to have a lot of hands too.',1,604,0,0,'63.193.168.40','en'),(20838,3542,'2004-02-20 15:43:31',66,'Peter','<br><tt>nice story! this is how i feel every day, in every moment of my 12.5 mile commute on bicycle. every call is a close one, and every asshole driver deserves damage and a beat-down. yet, i keep this angst to myself, stay in stealth-mode, and get to work in one piece, having achieved the zen epiphany that is cycling through manhattan traffic without getting angry, scared, or killed. its good.</tt>',1,404,0,0,'156.145.58.57','en'),(20839,3541,'2004-02-20 17:41:41',82,'simon','dear jay, happy birthday. i think this poem is lovely. your friend, simon',1,73,0,0,'209.21.99.118','en'),(20840,3539,'2004-02-21 04:50:36',241,'linus van pelt','screw \\\'finding nemo\\\'. this is the feel good story of the year.',0,68,0,0,'24.192.68.235','en'),(20841,3539,'2004-02-21 07:23:07',370,'fresh freddy forint','fuck that nemo. be that nemo.',6,29,0,0,'24.69.255.236','en'),(20842,3542,'2004-02-21 21:43:12',122,'hool','i\\\'ve always found it funny how furious a motorist becomes when i, on my bike, give said motorist the middle finger, even when it\\\'s so obviously their own fault. ',0,167,0,0,'66.185.84.68','en'),(20843,3539,'2004-02-22 01:59:02',534,'griece','<i>*yawn*</i>',5,13,0,0,'66.108.170.192','en'),(20844,3539,'2004-02-22 19:26:32',370,'ballsack','fuck that yawn. i said fuck that yawn.',6,38,0,0,'24.69.255.236','en'),(20845,3542,'2004-02-22 19:34:17',266,'spleenless','My father used to ride an old BSA back in the early \\\'60s.  Back then people would avert their eyes and shuffle past meekly when he walked down the street in his leather jacket.  They were terrified of anyone that rode a motorcycle.\r\n<br><br>\r\nSometimes I wish that fear still existed.  Maybe motorcyclists should start taking over small towns again.  I\\\'ve done my part so I won\\\'t personally be participating in any take-overs.',1,435,0,0,'63.193.168.40','en'),(20846,3463,'2004-02-23 13:08:05',528,'oliver','vegemite weird? nah. it is only one of the best spreads in the world! it is legendary in australia. do they sell it in america?',1,127,0,0,'211.29.1.196','en'),(20847,3463,'2004-02-23 13:11:52',528,'oliver','try a vegemite and cheese sandwhich - melted. put it in the microwave for a bit. heaven on earth!!',1,98,0,0,'211.29.1.196','en'),(20848,3540,'2004-02-23 16:12:59',228,'belly','if i got sent back in time to go to university all over again i would:\r\n<br>\r\n1. study a little bit harder<br>\r\nand<br>\r\n2. be way more slutty',0,142,0,0,'194.128.172.227','en'),(20849,3542,'2004-02-23 18:34:05',75,'tyler','i chase asshole drivers like dogs chase cats. i have gained a lot of endurance by following them on my bike to the next light or stopsign. people  need reeducation sometimes. because i have almost been hit by a car, the adrenaline is pumping, and i really am ready to have a fistfight right there. people almost always pick up on that vibe, and back down. ',1,356,0,0,'66.245.17.184','en'),(20850,3540,'2004-02-23 18:40:08',17,'austin','if i got sent back, i\\\'d join a frat and get a business degree, and not study at all.',1,87,228,0,'64.2.58.24','en'),(20851,3542,'2004-02-23 19:14:33',66,'Peter','<br><tt>or, they back down then, and save the <i>really</i> vile lashing out for the next innocent cyclist they pass...</tt>',1,123,75,0,'156.145.58.57','en'),(20852,3540,'2004-02-23 20:34:08',122,'hool','<p>- this is assuming you\\\'re going to a university, and not a community college/trade school, though both are equally valid</p>\r\n\r\n<p>i found that the university experience, when done earnestly, will actually spit you out on the other side even <i>more</i> lost than when you came in, because the universe contained within your mind will have expanded exponentially.  it\\\'s a welcome surprise.</p>',0,402,0,0,'66.185.84.68','en'),(20853,3540,'2004-02-23 22:18:05',17,'austin','assuming you don\\\'t join a frat and go to business school!',1,60,122,0,'64.2.58.24','en'),(20854,3542,'2004-02-24 01:24:55',75,'tyler','they aren\\\'t the ones lashing out to begin with...it\\\'s more of a contemptous disregard for my safety. i am the one lashing out, and rightly so.',1,148,0,0,'66.245.17.184','en'),(20855,3542,'2004-02-24 16:26:00',66,'Peter','<br><tt>its taken me a while to come to this conclusion, but ive found that- at least for me- i get into alot less drama on the streets when i take the zen approach. subtlety, wariness, avoidance, even-temper... all good ways to stay safe and keep the general road-rage down (from both the cyclist\\\'s and driver\\\'s points of view); often, the fleeting fulfillment of vengence simply makes things harder on the rest of the cyclists who try to stay in stealth mode and avoid such aggro (and in the long run, rather futile) conflicts. <br><br>there\\\'s a good thread on this exact topic <a href=\\\"http://www.livejournal.com/community/bikepirates/350153.html\\\">here</a>.</tt>\r\n',1,682,75,0,'156.145.58.57','en'),(20856,3542,'2004-02-24 17:06:20',129,'moebius','road rage is road rage, folks. whether it involves two drivers, two cyclists, or a mixture of the above....',0,107,0,0,'148.87.1.170','en'),(20857,3543,'2004-02-24 19:47:56',82,'simon','dude. i work at 333 7th ave, 11th fl. weird. also, i walk to and from the kitchen to get water, steal ink for my printer and blank cds.',0,135,0,0,'209.21.99.118','en'),(20858,3543,'2004-02-24 21:59:51',57,'weeb','i <3 NY\r\n\r\ni have been secretly reading my programming perl book all morning. \r\n\r\nmy cow orkers and i pass little notes under the table when the boss isn\\\'t looking.',1,167,0,0,'67.95.211.226','en'),(20859,3542,'2004-02-25 01:42:02',175,'Paul G','<i>Hell\\\'s Angels</i>, p. 124 - among others, 1966-1967, ref. comment #3.',3,75,0,0,'206.68.117.82','en'),(20860,3530,'2004-02-25 01:49:02',175,'Paul G','you don\\\'t step up to the plate very often; but every time you do, you knock it out of the park.',1,98,0,0,'206.68.117.82','en'),(20861,3534,'2004-02-25 01:52:46',175,'Paul G','\\\"What is the son, but an extension of the father?\\\" - someone\\\'s proverb.',3,80,0,0,'206.68.117.82','en'),(20862,3543,'2004-02-25 02:09:53',122,'hool','<p>when i worked in various office environments, i tried my best to be a master time killer.  i always covered clocks of any kind, first thing i do on the first day.  take off watch.  hide system tray clock / command line timestamp.  post-it note over lcd time on desk phone.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>three to four 15 minute bathroom naps. find a stall, sit down, elbows on knees, head cradled in hands.  the long route to the bathroom.  \\\'meetings\\\' with workers. purchase store items one at a time to encourage frequent trips.</p>\r\n<p>cigarettes.  funny how the smokers can take frequent leave to smoke outside, but if a non smoker were to just go out and stand there, s/he\\\'d be not a Good Worker.</p>\r\n<p>arrive late, leave early</p>',0,728,0,0,'65.49.92.218','en'),(20863,3543,'2004-02-25 04:28:22',66,'Peter','<br><tt>when i worked the night shift last year, id go in the conference room and sleep on the big table during my 4-5am lunch hour. we usually took 1.5 hours for \"lunch\".  then, every hour, id go into the bathroom and sleep for about 15 minutes or so. it sucked ass so hard. id set my phone to wake me up; when my boss yelled at me for talking on my cell in the bathrom, i dont think she knew i was sleeping. so id get bitter and graffiti up the bathroom there with slurs about my workplace.  its a wonder i worked there as long as i did. i had to work extra hard, to boot, to cover for all the sleeping. but without me, no one could cut. so i guess that part was worth it.</tt>',0,616,0,0,'66.108.170.192','en'),(20864,3540,'2004-02-25 13:11:14',528,'oliver','we don\\\'t have frats in australia. uni\\\'s here are very different than america. by the way, i am going to uni now. i start next week. quietly going insane at the price of everything, but other than that, everything is going okay. I put my paranoia down to sheer nerves. ',1,274,0,0,'211.29.1.31','en'),(20865,3540,'2004-02-25 13:13:21',528,'oliver','and i\\\'m studying international business/international studies. yippee (can you hear the sarcasm?)',2,100,0,0,'211.29.1.31','en'),(20866,3543,'2004-02-25 18:22:40',74,'jo','i was going to write a swintry last year titled something to the effect of \\\"ways to keep you busy at your tedious dot com job\\\" but it ended up sounding more bitter than resourceful, so i trashed it. sissyfight.com, livejournal, and \\\"research\\\" were all included. obviously by \\\"research\\\" i mean everytime you become vaguely interested in some topic and spend a whole afternoon googling every piece of relevant information and then adding a bunch of books about it to your amazon wishlist.',0,504,0,0,'67.209.34.7','en'),(20867,3543,'2004-02-26 21:02:47',273,'Quinn','\r\n<P>When walking around the office, carry a file folder, and walk with intensity while muttering to yourself and glancing at your watch.\r\n\r\n<P>Drink the largest cup of coffee you can handle.  The caffiene makes time seem like its going faster.\r\n\r\n<P>Have two documents open at all time, your spreadsheet, powerpoint doc, HTML file...and whatever story you\\\'re working on at the time.  Use Alt-Shift to toggle between the daywork and your real work.\r\n\r\n<P>Learn how to tune out in company meetings while still picking up enough to ask one relevant question at the end.\r\n\r\n<P>Take lots of bathroom breaks.  Leave you computer on and send yourslef messages from a handheld computer.  If you\\\'re savy enough you can take control of you\\\'re desktop, open and close files, run programs.\r\n',1,789,0,0,'67.130.105.66','en'),(20868,3543,'2004-02-26 22:12:01',91,'jay','can\\\'t forget the ever-important playlist making.  it\\\'s all i do.  yesterday\\\'s inspiration: Silly Love Songs, and its companion list, Smart Love Songs.',1,159,0,0,'66.123.22.66','en'),(20869,3543,'2004-02-27 11:32:26',187,'kandrer','i am a bit surprised there was no comment about the \\\"good times to get a private moment to poo in the women\\\'s room\\\" part.<br>\r\nsociologically, i think it\\\'s a very rich question (while to \\\"keep busy\\\" we often do little better than monkeys: walking around, eating) <br>\r\ni also had this experience of the \\\"unpredictable mid afternoon window\\\" (i loved these words).<br>\r\nmaybe there is another moment: just 30 minutes before the usual end of the day time (like 4:30 if most people leave at 5pm). at this moment everyone away from his/her desk might look gone early; so people will try to go to the bathroom well before that time.\r\n',1,652,0,0,'220.214.6.96','en'),(20870,3543,'2004-02-27 14:13:18',66,'Peter','<br><tt>stealthy workplace masturbation is also a good way to kill some time...</tt>',1,84,0,0,'156.145.58.11','en'),(20871,3543,'2004-02-28 00:11:17',93,'chiamattt','im good at the stealthy workplace masterbation, though I have yet to do it at my current job. It just seems tooo dirty. ',1,120,0,0,'218.39.19.10','en'),(20872,3545,'2004-02-28 16:16:27',82,'simon','the palace at 4am is quite a different place than it is at 4pm.',0,63,0,0,'209.246.78.36','en'),(20873,3543,'2004-02-29 08:39:16',370,'seanthecon','i need a job.',6,13,0,0,'24.85.235.57','en'),(20874,1214,'2004-02-29 08:43:39',370,'freddy fucking forint','so this is where this yawn bullshit comes from. jesus fucking christ.',6,69,534,0,'24.85.235.57','en'),(20875,3545,'2004-02-29 17:13:26',65,'le','\\\"i slept in my bra again\\\"<br>\r\n\\\"i need to clean my room\\\"<br>\r\n\\\"assholes!\\\"<br>\r\n\\\"i need to clean my room\\\"<Br>\r\n\\\"i\\\'m cleaning my room\\\"<Br>\r\nle tigre<br>\r\n\\\"WHO\\\'S CALLING ME!?!?!!\\\"\r\n',4,220,0,0,'216.254.118.212','en'),(20876,3547,'2004-03-01 10:59:31',370,'seanthecon','this is like the passion of christ and dmx rolled in one. hey dave. i brought back my granville ale and pilsner and bought me a six of ironhorse. get $2.80 from the returns. and $8.12 for the ironhorse. except the fucker rips me off a dollar. and now i\\\'m looking for the cops. i wanna register my bike to get the insurance. i\\\'m leaving messages. but they\\\'re too busy busting grow-opts. one every hour. so now i won\\\'t get the insurance. i\\\'ve found the magic of flasks. southern comfort and golden retrievers. so i\\\'ve given up on mornings. fuck em. they\\\'re too early. don\\\'t drink and drive. get it-get it on the floor.',6,640,0,0,'24.85.235.57','en'),(20877,3543,'2004-03-01 16:57:04',66,'Peter','<br><tt>lets see... 888 7th ave is at like 55th street, yes? that means youre close to <a href=\\\"http://www.westerlyhealthfoods.citysearch.com/\\\">westerly</a>, which you may or may not have discovered yet. its good. they are on 8th at 54th, diagonally across from studio 54, incidentally...</a>',1,298,0,0,'156.145.58.57','en'),(20878,1214,'2004-03-02 00:21:56',175,'Paul G','It is possible to falsify reality [if by \\\'reality\\\' we mean the things our ideas represent] for the purpose of understanding it.  \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nBut it is also possible to falsify reality for the purpose of preventing another from understanding it.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nWords, numbers and such are products of the mind: symbols, and not the things themselves.  Granted.  \\\"This is not a pipe.\\\"  OK,ok.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nBut in the story of the cave, the shadows are generated through the machinations of puppet operators - seemingly for the purpose of gaining the intellectual attachment of the cave dwellers.  This appears to be an example of falseness for the purpose of manipulation.  It\\\'s a political activity.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nThere seems too to be a distinction [in that work] made between false things: even if knowable reality is false, it is less false than the shadows.  \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nMaybe Plato is a big liar.  I understand the purpose of the activity of the gadfly.  I wonder how to heal, well, and live happily once stung, though.  If everything is false, then in what is there meaning?  This is a problem.  \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nBlah,blah,blah.\r\n</p>',1,1146,534,0,'64.107.88.167','en'),(20879,3547,'2004-03-02 00:26:04',93,'chiamattt','p.s this was just drunk fiction of what happened in my head at club MB.',6,71,0,0,'218.39.19.10','en'),(20880,3547,'2004-03-02 00:51:22',83,'adamajah','So, you\\\'re not really 6\\\'2\\\"?',0,36,93,0,'216.206.179.50','en'),(20881,1214,'2004-03-02 02:02:45',534,'griece','whatever. whos plato?',5,21,175,0,'66.108.170.192','en'),(20882,1214,'2004-03-02 07:54:43',175,'Paul G','my plato.',1,9,534,0,'131.156.255.243','en'),(20883,3543,'2004-03-02 16:00:38',228,'belly','on poohing at work: \r\n<p>\r\ni used to be shy about it. i\\\'m not anymore (although this may be related to my new horrible job, which at least has nice stalls with floor-to-ceiling walls and doors). however, should you have less insulation/privacy, and should you meet someone at the handbasin whereupon you are embarrased about any possible auditory or olfactory information that person has obtained regarding your endeavours, i think a good think to do would be to look them directly in the eye, and blithely comment, \\\"bowel cancer\\\", perhaps with a wave of the hand or a shrug.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nthis might work better if it is just a temp job.</p>\r\n<p>\r\nin japan, women flush the toilet while they wee, so other people in the bathroom can\\\'t hear them. there are sound effects in fancy toilets, so you can disguise that incriminatingly human trickling sound with crashing waves, perhaps, or the twittering of tropical birds. \r\n</p>',0,935,0,0,'194.128.172.227','en'),(20884,1388,'2004-03-02 20:27:02',66,'Peter','<br><tt>oh wow, i vaguely remember writing this. that line <i>\\\"without me, no one could cut\\\"</i> has become my personal mantra recently. it has shown up in my dreams; it is important, somehow.</tt>',1,203,66,0,'156.145.58.57','en'),(20885,1153,'2004-03-02 20:30:25',66,'Peter','<br><tt>wow, my bag looks so much older now. i think i should redo the inventory and see how the things i carry have changed in the past few years...</tt>',1,154,0,0,'156.145.58.57','en'),(20886,3547,'2004-03-03 03:13:51',93,'chiamattt','haha need any japan only vids dude?',1,35,0,0,'211.214.6.90','en'),(20887,3548,'2004-03-04 02:57:41',175,'Paul G','I looked at snow.  I dreamed in white.',4,38,0,0,'206.68.117.82','en'),(20888,632,'2004-03-04 16:42:37',66,'Peter','<br><tt><i>still</i> wondering about the \\\"russian officer\\\", swinney...</tt>',1,81,17,0,'156.145.58.57','en'),(20889,3547,'2004-03-09 01:45:25',83,'adamajah','Gran Turismo 4: Prologue',1,24,93,0,'216.206.179.50','en'),(20890,3530,'2004-03-09 13:52:45',93,'chiamattt','I liked this again. ',6,20,0,0,'211.214.6.90','en'),(20891,3547,'2004-03-10 08:46:20',75,'tyler','chiamatt: as we say down here: you all right, boy. you all right.',1,65,0,0,'66.245.77.101','en'),(20892,3546,'2004-03-11 18:47:19',65,'le','so sweet.',4,9,0,0,'64.242.240.2','en'),(20893,2791,'2004-03-14 03:56:42',266,'spleenless','<br>\r\nI just read my own comment from a long time ago.  I live near the ocean now and I\\\'m going to school to get a marine biology degree.  I\\\'ve spent a total of about three months on four different research vessels.  I dive regularly in a tank full of tuna at the aquarium.  I\\\'ve met wild squid and octopuses doing their thing out in the ocean.  I got scared shitless by some sharks near midway island.  I may get an internship this summer working with an ROV (a robotic submarine kind of thing) and collecting data about squid.\r\n<br><br>\r\nI was a very bored programmer living in oakland and hating my job when I wrote that long time ago comment.  I better be careful or I\\\'m gonna break my arm patting myself on the back.\r\n<br><br>\r\n...of course the downside is that I\\\'m almost broke right now but who cares.  Viva la Squid!',1,839,266,0,'63.193.168.138','en'),(20894,3556,'2004-03-15 14:19:57',66,'Peter','<br><tt><i>\\\"thow ya hands in the air if yous a true playa; cmon lemme hear ya say oh yay-ER\\\"</i></tt>',1,107,0,0,'156.145.58.57','en'),(20895,3556,'2004-03-15 15:56:05',75,'tyler','\\\'burnt any issue\\\'-- in law school, that would mean burnt a child. in this article, i don\\\'t know what it means. \r\n<br><br>\r\nafter reading your other articles, i\\\'m going to go out on a limb here and guess that this piece is about your relationship with some dude. \r\n<br><br>\r\nswinney as group therapy.\r\n',1,313,0,0,'66.245.77.101','en'),(20896,3556,'2004-03-15 17:06:43',82,'simon','peter you beat me to it.',0,24,66,0,'209.21.99.118','en'),(20897,3556,'2004-03-15 19:08:34',534,'griece','group therapy? if you ask me, it sounds like this writer smoked mad trees and typed something up.',5,97,75,0,'156.145.58.57','en'),(20898,3557,'2004-03-18 01:33:04',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i like this. thanks.</tt>',1,33,0,0,'66.108.169.117','en'),(20899,3556,'2004-03-18 01:50:55',66,'Peter','<br><tt>s, b!</tt>',1,18,82,0,'66.108.169.117','en'),(20900,1151,'2004-03-18 22:52:36',75,'tyler','i liked it',1,10,0,0,'66.245.11.251','en'),(20901,3556,'2004-03-18 23:06:34',75,'tyler','i guess my comment was a little rude, arcy. a ghost from the past has appeared, to warn 