BR>\\\"the march of the wooden soldiers\\\"<BR>all you protest kids<BR>you can hear jack say, get ready, ah<BR><BR>sweet jane<BR>come on baby!<BR>sweet jane<BR>oh oh ah!<BR>sweet jane<BR><BR>some people, they like to go out dancing<BR>and other peoples, they have to work.  just watch me now!<BR>and there\\\'s even some evil mothers<BR>well, they\\\'re gonna tell you that everything is just dirt<BR>y\\\'know that women never really faint<BR>and that villains always blink their eyes, woo!<BR>and that, y\\\'know, children are the only ones who blush<BR>and that life is just to die<BR>and everyone who ever had a heart<BR>they wouldn\\\'t turn around and break it<BR>and anyone who ever played a part<BR>oh, wouldn\\\'t turn around and hate it<BR><BR>sweet jane<BR>whoa oh oh!<BR>sweet jane<BR>sweet jane<BR><BR>heavenly wine and roses<BR>seems to whisper to her when he smiles<BR>heavenly wine and roses<BR>seems to whisper to her when he smiles<BR>la lala lala la, la lala lala la<BR>sweet jane<BR>sweet jane<BR>sweet jane',1,1652,0,0,'209.116.42.32','en'),(21160,3648,'2004-07-20 21:26:56',17,'austin','\\\'Traana\\\'',1,14,538,0,'63.80.97.254','en'),(21161,3651,'2004-07-21 00:02:55',122,'hool','<p>hi paul. i really liked this.  in a bit of synchronicity, i dropped my toothbrush in the toilet a few days ago, while brushing my teeth.  the handle was wet and slippery as i brushed, and it squirted out of my hand and right into the toilet bowl.  the bowl had just been refreshed by a flush, fortunately.  i dumbly watched the brush bounce around the bowl before the brush head sank below the water line.  that was the end of my crest spinbrush.</p>',0,453,0,0,'65.49.92.218','en'),(21162,3653,'2004-07-21 06:52:58',533,'incitor','apologies for the typos.  i\\\'m drunkxor.',1,42,0,0,'24.5.141.120','en'),(21163,3646,'2004-07-21 07:11:03',72,'essemar','[note: I\\\'m replying to Incitor, but his name isn\\\'t appearing in the pull-down for some reason.]<br><br>\r\n\r\nhmmmm... I\\\'m not sure what to say to what you wrote, but I feel a reply is necessary if for no other reason than to say, \\\'I don\\\'t think poorly of you at all.  In fact, I think very highly of you.\\\'<br><br>I just have a strange way of showing my affection.<br><Br>Also... you know... I don\\\'t really know you at all.  All I know is the stories you care to share with us, and those stories remind of some people I really liked in my past who shared many of the traits enumerated above.  Take that how you will.<br><br>And remember to look me up if you\\\'re ever in NYC.  essemar@hotmail.com',4,715,0,0,'66.95.134.2','en'),(21164,3653,'2004-07-21 09:05:42',72,'essemar','<p>Just in case you\\\'re looking for comments from the peanut gallery...<br><br>Fuck her brains out.<br><br>\r\n\r\nI mean, as long as you don\\\'t anticipate any negative consequences from said course of action.  Weird and unwanted emotional attachments suck.  Diseases suck.<br><br>It sounds like to me that the only reason you don\\\'t get closer to this girl (physically or emotionally) is a desire to hurt yourself.  Don\\\'t let neuroses stand in the way of happiness.</p><p>Anyways... liked reading what you wrote.  Always impressed with the level of detail you include.  Very nice.  Also, responded to the comment you left on my article.</p>',1,646,0,0,'66.95.134.2','en'),(21165,3653,'2004-07-21 14:17:50',533,'incitor','<p>it\\\'s complicated.  darwin, when i first told him about the situation, asked me, \\\"could you date a whore?\\\"  i\\\'m sure that i can, for a while.  but i have absolutely no doubt that it would turn out...badly.  </p>\r\n\r\n<p>i call her Lamashtu for a reason though.  not simply because it\\\'s fun to name people.  when i\\\'m with her, she does erase things.  it\\\'s temporary, but it helps.  if each man has his hell, i tend to think we each have a thousand.  she takes some away, and adds others.  i cannot risk loving a creature that cannot love though.  i see the madness in me every day, i can\\\'t just fuck it away, and i should not encourage it through dangerous emotional entanglements.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>in the meantime, our time together provides us each with something we want.  and is, for me, fodder for my writing.</p>',1,834,72,0,'24.5.141.120','en'),(21166,3653,'2004-07-21 16:47:25',17,'austin','NOT WORK SAFE',1,13,0,0,'63.80.97.254','en'),(21167,3653,'2004-07-21 19:56:56',122,'hool','well, the article was flagged as \\\'adult\\\'. what about adding a \\\'not work safe\\\' flag option for articles?',0,115,17,0,'65.49.92.218','en'),(21168,3651,'2004-07-21 21:58:37',72,'essemar','I used to live in an apartment that had shelves above the toilet.  After one toothbrush and two hair brushes, I got into the habit of closing the lid completely.',6,161,0,0,'66.95.134.2','en'),(21169,3653,'2004-07-21 23:09:34',17,'austin','I said that as a joke.  On mailling lists I am on, when somebody sends porn, the subject will say <PRE>Sub: NOT WORK SAFE! you mom naked</PRE>',1,142,122,0,'63.80.97.254','en'),(21170,3653,'2004-07-22 02:00:35',533,'incitor','<p>;)</p>\r\n<p>it\\\'s easy for me to forget that lots of people actually can look at the web while working.  i only do during certain sorts of investigations, and even then, only long enough to get whatever we need.</p>\r\n<p>i hope the crudity was too bothersome</p>',1,265,17,0,'24.5.141.120','en'),(21171,3653,'2004-07-22 02:01:02',533,'incitor','errr...wasn\\\'t even',0,21,17,0,'24.5.141.120','en'),(21172,3653,'2004-07-22 02:11:57',17,'austin','Guys, I was only kidding!  Keep pouring smut into the trough.',1,61,0,0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(21173,3653,'2004-07-22 02:25:21',17,'austin','incitor, this was some great porno by the way.  even though it never really got to the porn, it was still quite porny.  i liked it.',1,131,0,0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(21174,3653,'2004-07-22 02:34:13',533,'incitor','<p>i had the feeling that last night was something worth sharing.  i\\\'d been feeling sort of poetic all day, so after such a bizarre \\\'date\\\', i knew it was time to share something new with swinney.org.</p>\r\n<p>she just called me about five minutes ago, and we may get together on friday.  i\\\'ll have to consider it.  even i, in my madness, can only handle so much torment during a given week.</p>\r\n<p>austin, essemar:  thanks for the kind words.</p>',1,458,0,0,'24.5.141.120','en'),(21175,3654,'2004-07-22 05:21:42',17,'austin','<P>Actually, I think you got kicked off for using strange fonts!</P>\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nJust yesterday I was browsing the archives and I thought to make a series of \\\"Historic Swinney Moments\\\".\r\n<BR><BR>\r\n<LI>Essamar\\\'s WTC article\r\n<LI>Olivia leaving\r\n<LI>sine and Peter hooking up\r\n<LI>The Art Contest / Fuck the Man Thread\r\n<P>I\\\'m glad you are back!</P>',1,358,0,0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(21176,3654,'2004-07-22 05:58:02',533,'incitor','<p><i>a revolution of intimate bloggery</i></p>\r\n<p>that\\\'s how i feel as well.  i guess that\\\'s why i returned here to end things.</p>',2,139,0,0,'24.5.141.120','en'),(21177,3653,'2004-07-22 06:47:35',72,'essemar','<p>heh...</p><p>I used to get involved with girls kind of like this and know to the core of my soul that getting too attached to them would lead to all kinds of shit.  Of course I would just go ahead and fuck the shit out of them anyways.  No willpower.</p>',2,257,0,0,'66.95.134.2','en'),(21178,3654,'2004-07-22 07:46:07',17,'austin','<P><i> i guess that\\\'s why i returned here to end things.</i></P>\r\n<P>yes, sometimes i want to kill myself when i end up on this site.</P>',1,140,0,0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(21179,3654,'2004-07-22 09:32:11',63,'olivia','<p>dude austin, that was so goth.</p>',6,37,17,0,'64.81.243.3','en'),(21180,3654,'2004-07-22 09:34:55',63,'olivia','<p style=\\\"font-family: georgia, verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; color: #333;\\\">also:</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\\\"font-family: georgia, verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: bold; color: #333;\\\">SWEET!!!</p>',6,224,0,0,'64.81.243.3','en'),(21181,3654,'2004-07-22 13:45:00',66,'Peter','<br><tt>oh wow, its o! hi o!<br><br>too bad you deleted all your articles. im glad youre back though. youll just have to write new stuff :D</tt>',1,144,63,0,'156.145.58.57','en'),(21182,3654,'2004-07-22 14:56:53',57,'weeb','wow, where was i? i didn\\\'t even know any of that happened!\r\n\r\noo now i get to await delicious writings by olivia!!@ *dances*',0,127,0,0,'66.92.219.22','en'),(21183,3654,'2004-07-22 17:11:23',533,'incitor','*laugh*  dunno about suicide.  i\\\'m just working on ending all personal contacts.',0,83,17,0,'24.5.141.120','en'),(21184,3654,'2004-07-22 18:12:09',66,'Peter','<br><tt><b>favorite swinney moment:</b><br><Br>\r\n<UL TYPE=\\\"square\\\">\r\n<LI><A href=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=632\\\">the russian officer</a>\r\n</UL></tt>',1,183,17,0,'156.145.58.71','en'),(21185,3653,'2004-07-22 20:55:14',122,'hool','<p>okay austin, all good</p>\r\n\r\n<p>incitor: i liked this, thanks for writing it. i\\\'m not very verbose in my praise on articles lately, but i still feel the need to support the ones i like a lot with the \\\"hi this was really good\\\" comment.</p>',0,250,0,0,'65.49.92.218','en'),(21186,3654,'2004-07-22 21:12:19',57,'weeb','wow i am sad. i don\\\'t remember the weeb imitation by austin. remind me!!@\r\n<br><br>\r\nalso groaning at the memory of that article. it\\\'s true that the internet rewards the basest of subjects. see swinney!\r\n<br><br>\r\n*ducks* ',0,228,0,0,'208.218.54.65','en'),(21187,3651,'2004-07-23 00:42:56',175,'Paul G','that was a great comment.  thank you.  but, most of all, i am glad that you laughed.\r\n<p>\r\nyou\\\'re bucking the whole trend here, don quixote de la notepad.  where are all the pictures?  templates?  you do realize it\\\'s difficult to get students in unversities to write.  and you want me to learn primitive html?  \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nyou\\\'re a mom \\\'n pop store on the web, competing against the walmarts, blockbusters, and starbucks.  you\\\'re a salmon trying to struggle against the current of society and over the dam of indifference.  swim little swinney!  swim!\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nof course it sucks at times.  and i\\\'m sorry for the rhetorical hyperbole.  but intellectual companionship is a difficult thing to find - not in reference to iq, but rather in regard to perspective.  you\\\'ve got balls like bukowski; don\\\'t let them get broken.  haha.\r\n</p>',1,859,17,0,'206.68.117.82','en'),(21188,3651,'2004-07-23 00:48:44',175,'Paul G','i feel the same about your stuff, peter.  and i admire your energy too.  thanks for not becoming fatigued!',1,106,66,0,'206.68.117.82','en'),(21189,3651,'2004-07-23 00:50:45',175,'Paul G','haha.  i still need to come to toronto and buy a pic from you!',1,62,122,0,'206.68.117.82','en'),(21190,3654,'2004-07-23 00:54:04',175,'Paul G','it was like watching my internet parents fight.',1,47,0,0,'206.68.117.82','en'),(21191,3653,'2004-07-23 05:57:34',533,'incitor','<p>why thank you!</p>\r\n<p>i take the craft of writing very seriously.  of course, i don\\\'t always care to craft what i\\\'m writing.  ;)  here i tried to let everyone see a part of my life, as close to how i emotionally experienced it as possible.  unlike most of what i\\\'ve written here on swinney, i wanted to make it something worth reading regardless of the content.  i think i came close to succeeding.  i like to think even i have something to offer people once in a while.</p>',1,487,122,0,'24.5.141.120','en'),(21192,3654,'2004-07-23 20:13:26',195,'matt','that post makes me miss all the people who aren\\\'t around anymore.<BR><BR><I>those were different times</I>',1,109,0,0,'207.239.93.170','en'),(21193,3654,'2004-07-23 23:07:51',574,'xiolablue','2001 was a nice year',1,20,0,0,'66.215.156.7','en'),(21194,3656,'2004-07-24 09:28:03',72,'essemar','<br>Dude... You know, I tried that thing where you cut all ties with people and just tell humanity to go fuck itself.  I thought it would be great not having to deal with people\\\'s shit, and... it kinda sucked.  When you\\\'re scrambling around in that pit it can be hard to tell up from down.<br><br>People like you and care about your well being.  You\\\'re just going to have to accept that.  And you might not like all of them, but you will find a couple who get you, who you like being around and talking to.  It doesn\\\'t all have to be that shitty.',6,558,0,0,'66.95.134.2','en'),(21195,3656,'2004-07-24 18:39:28',533,'incitor','i don\\\'t expect it will be great.  i think it\\\'s going to be bad, very very bad.  it\\\'s not to spite anyone, or because some people don\\\'t really understand me.  it\\\'s something i have to do because i love them.',1,221,72,0,'24.5.141.120','en'),(21196,3640,'2004-07-25 05:42:39',57,'weeb','i am feeling like a pressed ham.',0,32,0,0,'66.92.219.22','en'),(21197,3654,'2004-07-25 10:12:13',63,'olivia','13 comments cannot be let to stand.',6,35,0,0,'64.81.243.3','en'),(21198,3660,'2004-07-25 19:26:10',57,'weeb','i used to have (i still might) this dream, this dream of my perfect man, and he is tall, soft, dark, and kind. he pets my hair a lot. he\\\'s also a lumberjack and we live in alaska. it must be that i have this vague thing for lumberjacks. i like plaid.\r\n\r\nit\\\'s strange, i am perfectly happy in my current relationship, but still. the lumberjack remains.',0,357,0,0,'66.92.219.22','en'),(21199,3660,'2004-07-25 20:50:20',17,'austin','(weeb you have a lust for tree murderers?)',1,42,57,0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(21200,3656,'2004-07-25 20:54:49',17,'austin','btw, i fixed the problem with commenting directly to anyone with \\\"to\\\" in their name.  ',1,92,533,0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(21201,3662,'2004-07-25 23:30:51',83,'adamajah','<P>Is there a low-carb variation of this recipe? <br> \r\n<br> \r\n<br> ;p</P>',1,74,0,0,'4.62.253.33','en'),(21202,3662,'2004-07-26 01:08:19',93,'chiamattt','I just wish we could hear what the \\\'iron chef\\\' judges would say when eating this. voice overs and all. \r\n<p>\r\nalso. good god man!',1,135,0,0,'211.207.246.90','en'),(21203,3662,'2004-07-26 02:06:01',57,'weeb','wow i like this. maybe we could have a series of articles written about imaginary tv shows. it could be the shit.',0,113,0,0,'66.92.219.22','en'),(21204,3662,'2004-07-26 03:00:42',175,'Paul G','pic: <a href=\\\"http://www.otsue.jp/images/gallery/shamisen.jpg\\\">japanese demon with a banjo</a>.  i bet i know what\\\'s in his food bowl.',1,143,0,0,'206.68.117.82','en'),(21205,3656,'2004-07-26 03:31:41',533,'incitor','didn\\\'t know it was a problem.  but now that you\\\'ve brought it up, i guess i understand what was going on when people wanted to reply to me.  haha',0,151,17,0,'24.5.141.120','en'),(21206,3662,'2004-07-26 05:35:46',17,'austin','haha, that is a good one paul.',1,30,175,0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(21207,3663,'2004-07-26 05:36:14',17,'austin','Thanks for throwing some up here.',1,28,0,0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(21208,3660,'2004-07-26 06:39:17',17,'austin','hi tricia.  i forget that people have paintbrushes and use them for art.',1,72,0,0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(21209,3656,'2004-07-26 13:39:04',72,'essemar','I\\\'m calling bullshit on you.  I can\\\'t believe you make the lives of people any shittier than they are already making it themselves.  And as far as I\\\'m concerned, you\\\'ve actually made my life a little bit better.  cheers.',6,232,533,0,'66.95.134.2','en'),(21210,3662,'2004-07-26 16:51:14',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i see a <a href=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=1858\\\">series</a> forming here!</tt>',1,115,17,0,'156.145.58.71','en'),(21211,3662,'2004-07-26 18:11:09',538,'arcy','Indeed there is! After hopelessly searching in my cupboards not so long ago, for a non-existent box of KD, I came up with an idea to satisfy my artificial cheese craving. All I had was a bag of frozen cut green beans and a jar of \\\'cheese whiz\\\'; which was actually in one of the collectors edition NHL glasses! Its actually not bad, just steam the green beans and throw in enough CW to evenly coat the beans. I also added a squirt of \\\'miracle whip\\\' just to make it that much more creamier. Voila! Low carb cheesy beans, and you get a hearty helping of greens for the day! \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n',2,591,83,0,'142.204.189.110','en'),(21212,3658,'2004-07-26 18:29:43',538,'arcy','xiolablue:\r\n\r\nI shouldn\\\'t think you should feel so guilty about bringing your cats to a shelter. I volunteered for some time at a Humane Society in the city I last lived in and the only reason why they would put any animal down is because they are hopelessly ill or violent and not able to be adopted. Some where there for close to a year. I saw even the nastiest of abused cats go to amazing homes especially older people who expect nothing out of the cat but their company. I had to put my favorite pet down because of kidney failure due to diabetes several years back, and I regret constantly for not being in the room when they did it. I have reoccuring dreams about her being angry with me, pretty nuts but it still effects me deeply. I vowed to be in the thick of things when and if anything should ever happen to someone I care about, no matter how it will affect me.',1,877,0,0,'142.204.189.110','en'),(21213,3662,'2004-07-26 21:31:40',83,'adamajah','\\\"...I just threw up a little bit in my mouth...\\\"',0,54,538,0,'216.206.179.50','en'),(21214,3663,'2004-07-26 23:32:58',175,'Paul G','the relationship between personal identity and community membership is interesting.\r\nthere\\\'s the idea that we\\\'re social animals, and we can\\\'t realize our human potential alone.\r\nbut we don\\\'t get to choose the time and place of our birth, or our genetic inheritence either.\r\nso to the extent that those things shape our behavior, or affect the way that others treat us, we\\\'re sort of fucked.\r\nthat anyone should make it to the point where they are able think-through all of the bullshit foisted upon us is a freakish coincidence of luck and effort.\r\nthe litle girl in your story is of the kind who\\\'s probably more likely to win that lottery than are the kids who taunted her.\r\nthat\\\'s something to be thankful for.\r\n<p>\r\nthree of my grandparents emmigrated from europe; one came from asia.\r\nand your story made me think as much as austin\\\'s soy/mac story made me laugh.\r\nthanks!\r\n</p>',1,905,0,0,'64.107.88.142','en'),(21215,3662,'2004-07-27 01:07:32',93,'chiamattt','ok. cheese whiz and green beans. yo! That is so nasty. \r\n\r\n<p>\r\nalso ADAMAJAH! booooyaka dude!',1,94,0,0,'211.207.246.90','en'),(21216,3656,'2004-07-27 03:16:17',533,'incitor','thanks.  =)  but when you fire someone, and send them to jail for a felony, and you\\\'ve met all five of their kids (and held and/or played with them), you can\\\'t forget that you\\\'ve negatively impacted a human life.  sure, they should only blame themselves... but i have to say it\\\'s difficult to handle sometimes.',1,322,72,0,'24.5.141.120','en'),(21217,3662,'2004-07-27 03:18:23',63,'olivia','pine nuts taste like cheeze!  try that in a recipe, chef austie!!!',6,66,0,0,'64.81.243.3','en'),(21219,3664,'2004-07-28 00:32:35',175,'Paul G','i\\\'ve had my strangest dreams while sleeping on some moving thing: train/car/plane.  maybe it has something to do with the upright position?  vibration?  hmmm.  has anyone from this site ever wandered into one of your dreams?',1,227,0,0,'64.107.88.142','en'),(21218,3663,'2004-07-27 05:10:12',542,'glen','<p>\r\nI\\\'m just trying to fit in.\r\n</p>',2,40,17,0,'199.181.107.145','en'),(21220,3664,'2004-07-28 01:03:16',261,'Peter','<br><tt>certainly. sine is my dream-woman, having shown up in countless ones over the years. my first s.o dream included le, who was lecturing me on the merits of technics turntables over vestax. jo was in one, as a good witch dressed in brown. starlajo has been in more than her fair share, definitely. one even incluided you combing your hair. odd how the brain works, yes?</tt>',1,380,175,0,'162.83.176.112','en'),(21221,3664,'2004-07-28 01:05:42',261,'Peter','<br><tt>certainly. sine is my dream-woman, having shown up in countless ones over the years. my first s.o dream included le, who was lecturing me on the merits of technics turntables over vestax. jo was in one, as a good witch dressed in brown. starlajo has been in more than her fair share, definitely. one even incluided you combing your hair. odd how the brain works, yes?</tt>',1,380,175,1,'162.83.176.112','en'),(21222,3664,'2004-07-28 01:19:14',261,'Peter','<br><tt>certainly. sine is my dream-woman, having shown up in countless ones over the years. my first s.o dream included le, who was lecturing me on the merits of technics turntables over vestax. jo was in one, as a good witch dressed in brown. starlajo has been in more than her fair share, definitely. one even incluided you combing your hair. odd how the brain works, yes?</tt>',1,380,175,1,'162.83.176.112','en'),(21223,3658,'2004-07-28 03:04:02',574,'xiolablue','thanks arcy-i dont feel as guilty now\r\nthat we have winsston and linus...but it just sucks we did it',1,100,538,0,'66.215.156.7','en'),(21224,3662,'2004-07-28 03:06:07',574,'xiolablue','that actually sounds good',1,25,0,0,'66.215.156.7','en'),(21225,3666,'2004-07-28 20:49:19',579,'jamesagee','i was born in knoxville, tennessee on november 27, 1909.  after my father\\\'s death in 1916, i attended several boarding schools, the last of which was exeter, where i began to write.  two years after graduating from harvard, i produced a volume of poetry, <U>permit me voyage</U> (1934).  during the rest of the 30s, i worked for <U>fortune</U> magazine, which assigned me to write about tenant farmers in alabama.  photographer walker evans and i spent five years on the project.  published in 1941 as <U>let us now praise famous men</U>, it remains a singular and profound affirmation of the human spirit as well as an important sociological work.  if i do say so my damned self.<BR><BR>in 1939, i wrote a treatment for a screenplay of andre malraux\\\'s <U>man\\\'s fate</U>.  the movie was never made, but my interest in cinema was piqued.  i became a film critic for <U>time</U> and for <U>the nation</U>, where my reviews virtually invented modern film criticism.  they were collected as volume one of <U>agee on film</U> in 1958.  volume two contains the screenplays i wrote after 1948, including <U>the african queen</U>, filmed by john huston in 1951; <U>the night of the hunter</U>, filmed by charles laughton in 1955; and the unproduced <U>noa noa</U>, based on the journals of paul gauguin.<BR><BR>i had a hard time in the 50s because of self-doubt and the effects of years of alcoholism.  the autobiographical <U>the morning watch</U> appeared in 1950; my next book, the novel <U>a death in the family</U> (of which the above is the preface), was published after my death in new york city on may 16, 1955.  that book won me the acclaim i never received in life, including a pulitzer prize in 1958.  i was married three times, and had four children.',1,1763,0,0,'207.239.93.170','en'),(21226,3664,'2004-07-28 22:41:11',234,'etienne','darren and i got in the lift the other day with a woman who was going to the first floor.  i was giggling so hard - i just couldn\\\'t hide it.  it\\\'s only about ten steps to the second floor!',0,194,0,0,'219.88.223.161','en'),(21227,3664,'2004-07-28 23:43:04',175,'Paul G','odd, indeed.\r\nle was one of only two s.o people to invade my subconscious.\r\nabout 2 weeks ago i was asleep in my taxi, in the alley, when it began:\r\nwe were married.  my father was alive again - standing in the threshold of a doorway with my mother.\r\nthey were watching us.\r\nle began to complain about food that i had made.\r\n\\\"you expect me to eat this?\\\" she said.\r\ni tried to explain that it was a salad.\r\nshe held up a dead, brown leaf.\r\ni left the room and looked in a mirror: my hair and eyes had turned grey.\r\ni looked like an elf.\r\nthen, the two of us climbed rope-ladders to escape something.\r\ni woke, jumped from the taxi, and locked myself out - again.',1,666,261,0,'206.68.117.82','en'),(21228,3664,'2004-07-28 23:54:25',175,'Paul G','trix!',6,5,0,0,'206.68.117.82','en'),(21229,3520,'2004-07-29 02:54:01',57,'weeb','this made me very happy.',0,24,0,0,'66.92.219.22','en'),(21230,3666,'2004-07-29 04:13:54',261,'Peter','<br><tt>i grew up in tennesse, also. i think hunter s. thompson is a better writer than you. but then again, he grew up in kentucky.</tt>',1,137,579,0,'162.83.176.112','en'),(21231,3665,'2004-07-29 14:45:58',574,'xiolablue','i need some cash to get to new york',2,35,0,0,'66.215.156.7','en'),(21232,3667,'2004-07-29 15:11:55',17,'austin','<P>it would be funny if you didn\\\'t stop there.  got tattoos, got a motorcycle, decided that you are lesbian, and  moved to san francisco\\\'s mission.  keep us posted on this :-)</P>\r\n<P>i knew a woman in college who at about 55 ditched her family, bought a VW bus, left arizona and decided to go to college in texas.</P>\r\n<P>she said she got tired of giving.</P>\r\n<P>one day when a cop tried to give her a parking ticket, she gave him hell.</P>',1,448,0,0,'63.80.97.254','en'),(21233,3667,'2004-07-29 15:12:58',17,'austin','<P>and that sounds like destiny to me (not yours, blue, but this woman\\\'s in my comment).</P>',1,95,0,0,'63.80.97.254','en'),(21234,3667,'2004-07-29 16:41:46',574,'xiolablue','yeah. problem is I dont want lots of tatoos. Only one ...maybe.\r\nAnd I hate motorcycles.\r\n\r\nMaybe move to NY.\r\nHmmm. \r\n\r\nI will definately keep you posted. \r\nWhatever happens its fate',1,183,17,0,'66.215.156.7','en'),(21235,3667,'2004-07-29 19:37:41',66,'Peter','<br><tt>so did you marry <a href=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=1601\\\">brewguru99</a>?</tt>',1,115,574,0,'156.145.58.71','en'),(21237,3175,'2004-07-30 06:30:00',581,'SOLARIS','seriously, I have been noticing 11\\\'s as well, not one one one one, but 11\\\'s, I understand where you are coming from',2,121,0,0,'206.116.243.100','en'),(21238,3667,'2004-07-30 14:43:49',574,'xiolablue','yes I did.\r\nAnd we had major soap opera drama last night...I think I may post about it-maybe not.\r\n\r\nBut things are good.Or getting better.\r\nMaybe Im going through my pre mid-life crisis eh?\r\n\r\nI hear you got married as well. Belated congratulations. ',1,251,66,0,'66.215.156.7','en'),(21239,3667,'2004-07-31 19:29:40',122,'hool','<p>i think that people become boring, and unboring.  life remains constant, and thus a convenient scapegoat in general terms when you don\\\'t want to take responsibility for your actions or inactions.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>i \\\'work from home\\\' and there is much monotony in my daily schedule.  i work very, very hard at maintaining a life that i\\\'m interested in living, despite the repetitive stage.  boredom is always your fault, and you always deserve the unhappiness associated with it if you let it settle in.</p>',0,513,0,0,'65.49.92.218','en'),(21240,3660,'2004-08-01 02:14:22',577,'Tricia','(..i once had a lumberjack as a school mascot many many years ago... )Do lumberjacks still exist? I\\\'ve never seen one in real life. \r\nI actually found this guy from my dream last night and talked to him... :) Cheers to me!\r\nOh.. and, well I use paintbrushes, but haven\\\'t used them in a while, I paint little clay sculptures as well.. my teal paintbrush is waiting patiently behind the knobs of the kitchen sink.',1,417,0,0,'64.12.117.21','en'),(21241,3660,'2004-08-01 11:34:27',72,'essemar','<br>I had a great-uncle who was a lumberjack.  He was one of the toughest guys I\\\'ve ever known.  He used to make fun of my soft hands.',4,137,0,0,'66.95.134.2','en'),(21242,3664,'2004-08-01 16:31:40',74,'jo','ha. good witch.\r\n',2,17,0,0,'66.68.101.14','en'),(21243,3662,'2004-08-01 16:34:27',74,'jo','that looks so good. had you not included the picture, i may have been able to stave off trying this, but having seen the picture, i now have to drag my hungover ass to wheatsville and wander the aisles collecting my ingredients.',0,228,0,0,'66.68.101.14','en'),(21244,3667,'2004-08-02 04:43:18',574,'xiolablue','true...but not all boredom is self inflicted. More a mixture of both the self and the environment one is in.\r\n\r\n',1,112,122,0,'66.215.156.7','en'),(21245,3668,'2004-08-02 04:57:01',93,'chiamattt','what did he steal? ',1,19,0,0,'211.207.246.90','en'),(21246,3668,'2004-08-02 05:17:27',533,'incitor','around $700 of amphetamine precursors.  ',0,40,0,0,'24.5.141.120','en'),(21247,3671,'2004-08-02 16:40:16',74,'jo','whoa. i am sorry to hear this. the child psych 101 classes i took said that kids very rarely have good and convincing details for the stories they make up (unless they are either super-precocious or highly manipulative or both). at the risk of making you worry more, if i were you, i would follow my instinct and believe him. maybe have the \\\"i of course believe you, but you know how serious this is and if you\\\'re lying, it could really hurt daddy\\\" talk. good luck with whatever decisions you make. ',2,508,0,0,'216.142.229.132','en'),(21248,3671,'2004-08-02 16:47:54',17,'austin','Eek.',1,4,0,0,'63.80.97.254','en'),(21249,3671,'2004-08-02 16:50:05',17,'austin','I often wonder what to believe on this website where some people write truth and others write fiction.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nDad sounds like a numbnutz.',1,141,0,0,'63.80.97.254','en'),(21250,3670,'2004-08-02 18:18:35',72,'essemar','<br>whoa... dude... that\\\'s fucked<p>So, did you <i>run</i> away from the old guy or were you just walking away.</p><p>and btw, that was actually a brave thing you did, getting involved and all.  What were you supposed to do?  Show your manliness by beating the crap out of an 80-year old guy?</p>',3,299,0,0,'66.95.134.2','en'),(21251,3671,'2004-08-02 18:21:04',66,'Peter','<br><tt>uh, all this notwithstanding, why are you letting him stay in touch wit hdear ol dad? these events alone seem like jsut reason to curtail visitation...<br><Br>also: i witnessed <i>alot</i> of domestic violence when i was a kid, and i turned out ok... thansk to alot of effort from my single mom and a lil bit of professional help to help explain it when i was like 7. jsut a thought...</tt>',1,398,0,0,'156.145.58.71','en'),(21252,3671,'2004-08-02 18:22:05',538,'arcy','I will be going out and buying stock in Trojan asap. Some people are just not cut out for child rearing. Is it really always good to keep daddy in the picture?',2,159,0,0,'66.185.84.68','en'),(21253,3671,'2004-08-02 19:07:21',574,'xiolablue','wow-these things are always complicated and messy. Good Luck\r\n',1,62,0,0,'66.215.156.7','en'),(21254,3670,'2004-08-02 19:09:54',574,'xiolablue','I would have let the old man have the ball.\r\n\r\nHe\\\'s old and he\\\'s gonna die soon. While the kids in the pool have many years of brattiness left...\r\n\r\nHaving once been a lifeguard I so would have let the old man have the ball.But that\\\'s just me.\r\n\r\ncall me-say hi to you know who',1,286,72,0,'66.215.156.7','en'),(21255,3671,'2004-08-02 21:37:49',81,'felicity','The reason he still has contact with his dad is that I\\\'ve never said anything negative about him to Conner, so he has no reason to do anything but love him as unconditionally as a 5 year old can. (Too many male pronouns...sorry!)  I\\\'ve made it clear that if I hear anything of this nature happening again, that\\\'s it. Up until now, everything has been minor enough that it can be fixed in the two weeks between visits to Dad\\\'s.  This one just isn\\\'t that simple.',0,475,0,0,'216.42.122.249','en'),(21256,3671,'2004-08-03 02:03:47',17,'austin','<P><TT>i witnessed alot of domestic violence when i was a kid, and i turned out ok...</TT></p>\r\n<P>Uh, yeah, i dont think so.</p>',1,128,0,0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(21257,3671,'2004-08-03 03:23:50',66,'Peter','<br><tt>you dont thin i turned out ok? golly!</tt>',1,50,17,0,'162.83.176.112','en'),(21258,3666,'2004-08-03 21:51:31',82,'simon','i like that \\\'things i hate\\\' list you made with walker evans. that was funny.',0,82,579,0,'209.21.99.118','en'),(21259,3671,'2004-08-03 22:15:08',195,'matt','<B><I>fiction?</B></I><BR><BR>austin, are you saying people <u>lie</U> around here?  quel horror!\r\n',1,99,0,0,'207.239.93.170','en'),(21260,3670,'2004-08-04 00:11:08',175,'Paul G','genius!  it makes me wonder about the predicament of man in the year 2004.  and it also makes me wonder if the old man knew kung fu, had a knife, or possessed psychotic strength.  you rule.',1,189,0,0,'206.68.117.82','en'),(21261,3671,'2004-08-04 00:43:59',175,'Paul G','you don\\\'t have an incident; you have a pattern.  putting the child in the position of deciding what to say, and to whom, is pushing off the burden that the adults should be bearing.  you don\\\'t like dealing with stuff; how much less does your son - knowing what might follow his report.  children model; what other adult males are in conner\\\'s environment?  still, this happens a lot.  gah.  assuming this isn\\\'t simply a thought-provoking exercise...  ',1,462,81,0,'206.68.117.82','en'),(21262,3630,'2004-08-04 07:59:47',70,'Fuzzy','<p>The people demand a follow-up!</p>\r\n<p>We demand satisfaction!!</p>',1,70,0,0,'65.50.24.60','en'),(21263,3671,'2004-08-04 16:32:17',81,'felicity','It has already started to happen.  He\\\'s hit and kicked me a few times this week when he was angry.  We are going to see a children\\\'s domestic violence counselor next week, and decide the status of his father\\\'s visitation times based on the counselor\\\'s recommendations.',0,280,175,0,'216.42.66.181','en'),(21264,3671,'2004-08-04 16:58:43',81,'felicity','<p>As for positive male role models...I\\\'m currently on a self-imposed dating hiatus, but he still spends a lot of quality time with my father.  The male friends that I do have are all great with him as well.</p>\r\n<p>I\\\'m admittedly weak when it comes to deciding how honest to be with Conner about his father.  While I don\\\'t want to \\\"pull back the curtain\\\" and leave Conner even more confused and dissapointed, I know that it\\\'s just a matter of time before his father destroys the bond himself.</p>\r\n<p>Before he goes to sleep every night we try to say one nice thing about each of the important people in his life.  If you could see the look in his eyes when he talks about what a great softball player Daddy is or how Daddy is good at \\\"pretending Spiderman\\\" with him, it might give you a better idea of why I haven\\\'t cut him off yet.</p>\r\n<p>Ideally, I wouldn\\\'t be so spineless about this.  Then again, ideally, I wouldn\\\'t be put in the position to have to make this kind of decision.</p>',0,1022,175,0,'216.42.66.54','en'),(21265,3671,'2004-08-04 18:10:55',66,'Peter','<br><tt><i>I know that it\\\'s just a matter of time before his father destroys the bond himself.</i><br><br>here\\\'s hoping he doesnt do more than simply destroy the bond. i know its not my place to say it, but you might further consult some professional opinions about being more proactive about handling this situation. using healthy means, i have a feeling the quicker you handle this the better. merely my opinion, of course :)</tt>',1,438,81,0,'156.145.58.57','en'),(21266,3672,'2004-08-04 19:58:55',57,'weeb','i was trying to tell someone about this song too, a couple of days ago. it feels sad, like leaving behind something or someplace you love, hitching or walking, or amtraking. just leaving. the place leaves its mark on your skin like a coat of humidity, your eyes close and you can hear summer nights again, far far away, a long time ago, i loved you, she said.\r\n<br><br>\r\ngoodbyes. it makes me think of goodbyes.',0,411,0,0,'208.218.54.65','en'),(21267,3671,'2004-08-04 20:03:49',57,'weeb','i\\\'ve seen some domestic violence as a child. it shook me up, and made me feel sad, protective of myself, and ill. it would make me feel ill to see that from my dad, and i would probably be torn between loving him and hating him.\r\n<br><br>\r\ni know it\\\'s hard, but here is what i think: by ignoring it or accepting it, you are really telling the boy that this is okay. it\\\'s okay to hit someone else in anger, whether it is a spouse, son or stranger. is this something you really want your son to be acclimated to?\r\n<br><br>\r\ni would personally stop visitations with the father until he gets a grip, or apologizes, or make sure the father and the child always knows what is acceptable and what is not. love is not an excuse to cover up abusive behavior.',0,758,0,0,'208.218.54.65','en'),(21268,3671,'2004-08-04 20:06:52',57,'weeb','also just as a personal opinion, i have no doubt at all that Conner saw what he said he did. kids make up stuff, but they can\\\'t make up tiny little accurate details. his impersonating his dad is really a 5 alarm danger signal that you need to take firm action, and soon.',0,273,0,0,'208.218.54.65','en'),(21269,3317,'2004-08-04 22:18:48',582,'Evsterm','Vettes are the suckiest car in the world. If you have one you should sell it, and buy somthing that actualy goes fast.\r\n\r\nFrom,\r\nA muscel car hater',5,147,0,0,'24.118.98.90','en'),(21270,3671,'2004-08-05 00:40:20',175,'Paul G','story 1 - about a week ago i picked up a woman at 4:15 am.  she was missing a shoe, her eyes were swelling shut, her lip was cracked, and there was blood running down her nose.  i asked what happened.  \\\"a guy raped me and beat the shit out of me,\\\" she said.  and then she asked to be taken to an address on belmont.  i told her that we needed to go to the hospital, or the police station.  she refused.  conflict: it\\\'s her right not to report.  but, not only was she in need of medical attention, the person who attacked her was still at large in the neighborhood.  what about the rights of the other residents?  i dialed 911, and tried to talk to her until the police arrived; it took 10-15 minutes for them to get there.  it was too late.  another taxi driver took her money, and took her away.  why did she refuse help?  she had left her son at home alone, and was afraid that if discovered she would lose her child.  i suspect that she was working the street at night while her little boy slept.  the whole system failed her: hospital/police/911/me.  she\\\'s someone\\\'s mother.\r\n<p>\r\nstory 2 - my friend was married to a stripper; they got divorced.  she re-married, and recently had a child.  one week after the child\\\'s birth, her new husband took her mother for a ride on his motorcycle.  they had an accident; they were both killed.  so there she is: divorced, widowed, a stripper, with no family left alive, and a week-old child.  she\\\'s someone\\\'s mother.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nyou can make your situation work.  don\\\'t beat yourself up.  if you were really \\\"spineless\\\" you would let things drag on for years.  if i write something that makes you feel bad, tell me that i am a dick.  look at what peter and weeb wrote.  fight!  you\\\'re someone\\\'s mother.\r\n</p> ',1,1791,81,0,'206.68.117.82','en'),(21271,3670,'2004-08-05 01:02:53',122,'hool','<p>essemar: i just walked away from the guy.  there\\\'s no way i could reconcile punching an old man, unless he hit me first with a youthful punch.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>paul g: thanks. he moved too slow to seem threatening.  but i imagined a scenario where he kicked my unsuspecting ass with martial arts, in front of the kids.  would\\\'ve made for an even better story.</p>',0,365,0,0,'65.49.92.218','en'),(21272,3671,'2004-08-05 03:11:29',81,'felicity','What you say does make me angry. Not at you, but at myself for being unable to stand up for my kid.  I\\\'ve pored through all I can find about New York State custody laws (I couldn\\\'t begin to a lawyer) and I\\\'m still not sure that I can keep Conner from visiting his father. Even supervised visitation would require what seems like a more extreme situation on his part.  It would also appear that he could play the \\\"mental illness card\\\" (I\\\'m bipolar...who isn\\\'t?) with the same effectiveness as I could raise allegations of abuse.  I spoke with Conner\\\'s pediatrician today about the situation.  She believes his story (I took him to see her on Monday), and advised me to discuss my options with his new counsellor next week.  He\\\'s not due to go back to his father\\\'s house until the middle of this month, so if I have the backing of a mental health professional, I can file for sole custody and keep Conner out of his house for the time being.  Without that backing from someone \\\"official,\\\" I\\\'m not sure that I could get anywhere.\r\nConner is safe right now.  We\\\'ve talked at length about violence and why what he saw was wrong.  My sister, who was nearly killed by her ex-husband (who after a year in and out of courts still has joint custody of their son despite the domestic violence), seemed to get through to him about the gravity of the situation.\r\nI\\\'m going to spend the next week making sure my own ducks are in a row.  I\\\'ve had offers from friends and my employer to write character references to counter any accusations that I\\\'m not mentally stable enough to raise my son.  With the support of my family I\\\'ll handle any outbursts that might occur, and see what happens at the appointment next week.\r\nIn the mean time, it\\\'s nice to know that there are people out there who care enough about \\\"some stranger\\\'s kid\\\" to make me angry.',1,1900,175,0,'216.42.122.249','en'),(21273,3671,'2004-08-05 03:12:43',81,'felicity','that should read \\\"begin to afford a lawyer.\\\"',0,50,175,0,'216.42.122.249','en'),(21274,3674,'2004-08-06 14:59:07',57,'weeb','<pre>Jesus saves!\r\n\r\nthat is going to be my new expletive of choice.</pre>',0,74,0,0,'66.92.219.22','en'),(21275,3662,'2004-08-06 22:32:02',83,'adamajah','Wheatsville Food Co-op.  That brings back some memories.  ',0,58,0,0,'216.206.179.50','en'),(21276,3674,'2004-08-09 15:56:52',74,'jo','a dad of a pal of mine is fond of the curse: \\\"god FUCK america!\\\" because it is so offensive to nearly everyone. he\\\'s disabled and an old hippie who smokes a large amount of marijuana and has been known to shout this in public when frustrated. hooray.',2,259,0,0,'216.142.229.132','en'),(21277,3662,'2004-08-09 16:01:46',74,'jo','!!ALERT: THIS POST IS SO \\\"AUSTIN\\\" IT IS UPSETTING! ALERT!!\r\n<p>i don\\\'t actually like wheatsville that much because it\\\'s overpriced and the selection is shit and because although i like buying organic foods a lot, i also like the option of NOT buying them. i am also annoyed they have the largest selection of colors of manic panic in town but no el milagro chips. EL MILAGRO is austin-grown, man, their fucking factory is on 6th street, i park there when i go to emo\\\'s. anyway, they are randomly elitist in which products they\\\'ll stock and i like my elitism to be reliable, thanks.',4,599,0,0,'216.142.229.132','en'),(21278,3673,'2004-08-10 07:37:06',70,'Fuzzy','<p>Guess who heard a single cricket in the front yard of a house on Riverdale Ave. during his bike ride home at 2:45am this morning?</p>',1,136,0,0,'65.50.24.60','en'),(21279,3674,'2004-08-10 17:29:27',175,'Paul G','a mask, a quick glimpse, something turning...sometimes it is like the carnival.',1,79,0,0,'206.68.117.82','en'),(21280,3662,'2004-08-10 20:50:10',83,'adamajah','I can\\\'t really remember if I liked it or not.  I just remember it being close to the HOC, and having a good selection of Ben & Jerry\\\'s.  It was hard to find an open space on the bike rack sometimes. <br>\r\nI do know I liked Wheatsville better than Whore Foods.\r\n',0,267,74,0,'216.206.179.50','en'),(21281,3651,'2004-08-11 02:28:56',368,'haecceity','That was a great story, Paul.  I\\\'ve had a lot of days like that lately. ;)',1,77,175,0,'24.14.131.126','en'),(21282,3241,'2004-08-11 18:50:17',195,'matt','Clean up that mess and you won