...Makes for very amusing dinners',1,368,0,0,'138.23.2.197','en'),(21292,3677,'2004-08-15 17:04:19',17,'austin','Yay, therapy.  You need a house call from Dr. Octagon.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\n<img src=\\\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/B000005AM7.01.LZZZZZZZ.jpg\\\">',1,144,0,0,'209.237.231.200','en'),(21293,3677,'2004-08-15 20:06:10',82,'incitor','<p>it\\\'s strange, but i\\\'ve thought alot over the years about women faking orgasms.  i remember arguing with my ex-wife about it.  i was annoyed with her for faking (i only knew of course, because she told me over breakfast), and she was defensive over it.  it came down to me being irritated that she had fooled me into thinking she was satisfied - and therefore i\\\'d not been given the chance return the pleasure she\\\'d given me.  she was defensive because...well, frankly, i\\\'m not certain we ever figured that out.</p>\r\n<p>i suspect there are several reasons for women faking their orgasms, but of course, these are just my personal theories.  women commonly practice deception on a subconscious level, as a means for self preservation.  or so i\\\'m given to understand.  in a state of nature, perhaps a male would be angry if a woman were not as fully receptive to his sperm as she might be.  (orgasm seems to be conductive to uptake of the sperm.  i\\\'ve got a great video of the process somewhere.)  hmmm...i forget my other theories, i smell food.</p>\r\n<p>i\\\'m sort of lucky i guess, in that when i orgasm, i don\\\'t want to curl up, i want to do stuff.  usually i just wanna continue having sex.  at the least i\\\'m going to want to go out and walk around.  this has led me to favor women who let me know that they haven\\\'t had an orgasm, since barring heavy fatigue or anger, i\\\'m more than happy to continue the lovemaking until she\\\'s sated.  if she doesn\\\'t communicate clearly, she\\\'s not going to be as pleased with the results.  this applies to most sexual activities... or so it seems to me.</p>\r\n<p>but you know...whatever.  my two cents are discounted, as i haven\\\'t made love in five years.</p>',3,1742,0,0,'209.237.231.200','en'),(21294,3682,'2004-08-15 20:53:08',86,'egg','i happen to be visiting with 2 nephews, age 4 and 1, while reading this here. I come to such conclusions (\\\"I dont want children\\\") about every 8 minutes (on average). they really just don\\\'t interest me. i find family life intensely boring. I hope my mom doesn\\\'t read this. i just want him to grow up so i can make him mix CDs. today i got a chance to watch the cartoon of sleeping beauty. I liked the part where the witches make a dress and a cake and clean up with house with magic, that was righteous. all that other crap is snoresville.  ',0,552,0,0,'66.30.73.38','en'),(21295,3677,'2004-08-16 00:58:03',72,'essemar','<i>Well, really essemar, but for some reason I\\\'m logged in as egg.</i><p>I get the feeling that this going to be one of those high volume comment articles.  God we love to talk about sex.  Me included of course, so here is my very male, somewhat quirky view of the issue:<br><br>I don\\\'t give a fuck what a girl does in bed with me because, well, I\\\'m going to enjoy myself regardless.  That doesn\\\'t mean I\\\'m totally selfish.  If she wants me to try things, keep doing something, stop doing something, I\\\'m more than happy to oblige as long as I get some sort of vocal/somatic/grunting signal from her.  On the other hand, if she just wants to lay there doing nothing, making no noise, I can enjoy that too.  (Just don\\\'t bitch to me about not doing [blank] because no matter how hard I try, I can\\\'t read your mind.]  I\\\'m not saying \\\"your orgasm, your resposibility.\\\"  I\\\'m willing to work with you, but people are free to enjoy sex in whatever fashion they choose.<br><br>As far as faking orgasms specifically, I\\\'m against it in principle, but it really depends on the person.  For some men, so much of their masculinity is tied up in their sexual prowess that you\\\'ll really hurt their ego if you don\\\'t have the big O.  Others understand that a woman won\\\'t come every time and that it\\\'s okay; a woman\\\'s orgasm isn\\\'t as simple as inserting slot \\\'A\\\' into tab \\\'B\\\' and repeating until there\\\'s a big, gooey mess.  Just try to understand what your guy wants and needs from you, and make him understand that you don\\\'t have to \\\'<i>trip the light fantastic</i>\\\' every time.  I think another part of the problem is that men don\\\'t understand that women don\\\'t <i><b>need</i></b> to come the way we do.  We feel a certain urgency to come that women don\\\'t.  If a woman doesn\\\'t come, it\\\'s not the end of the world.  If a man doesn\\\'t, it is.<br><br>All that being said, I will now tell the world: I fake orgasms.  Not very often (I am male), but sometimes I just know it\\\'s not going to happen, so I fake it to avoid any hurt feelings.  Women seem to take it very personally if the man they are with can\\\'t come, so I do it to avoid awkward conversations.</p>',1,2242,0,0,'209.237.231.200','en'),(21296,3682,'2004-08-16 00:38:22',17,'austin','test.\r\n',1,7,0,0,'209.237.231.200','en'),(21297,3682,'2004-08-16 01:03:50',17,'austin','jay and egg are going to have an arranged pregnancy so that jay can have a kid.  that is my prediction.  jay will raise <i>it</i>, egg will make <i>it</i> mix tapes and hack together clothes for <i>it</i>.',1,205,0,0,'209.237.231.200','en'),(21298,3682,'2004-08-16 01:05:27',17,'austin','also, burpee tomatoes!',1,22,0,0,'209.237.231.200','en'),(21299,3677,'2004-08-16 14:39:10',584,'capslock','I thats the whole point. I don\\\'t want him to feel inadaquate. I guess the whole issue is that I don\\\'t really care if I reach max sometimes, but I think he does so....plus its the most fun in the world to hear him get off from my inclining vocalizations.',2,259,72,0,'127.0.0.1','en'),(21300,3677,'2004-08-16 14:39:13',584,'bmg','tell him to grind the corn.',1,27,0,0,'127.0.0.1','en'),(21301,3677,'2004-08-17 05:44:14',72,'essemar','ummm... so is there any actual problem with your sex life?  It sounds like you\\\'re enjoying it just fine, and that\\\'s the point, isn\\\'t it?<br><br>btw -- <i>\\\'intermittently flex the muscle down there that swallows whole\\\'</i> -- so fucking hot.  He\\\'s a lucky man.',6,277,584,0,'66.95.134.2','en'),(21302,3677,'2004-08-17 05:45:06',72,'essemar','That last comment was to capslock.',0,34,584,0,'66.95.134.2','en'),(21303,3677,'2004-08-17 06:34:15',17,'austin','asf',1,3,584,0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(21304,2893,'2004-08-17 14:32:28',75,'tyler','i\\\'m laughing as hard as i ever have--and i\\\'m from south carolina!',1,71,0,0,'68.222.239.6','en'),(21305,3682,'2004-08-17 14:45:02',75,'tyler','i would like to go back and be six or eight again, for a day. just because i can\\\'t remember what it was really like, to be physically so small.  ',1,148,0,0,'68.222.239.6','en'),(21306,3677,'2004-08-17 22:53:43',71,'dj1_luna','did u watch Six feet under this pas weekend? \\\"grind the corn\\\" was mentioned. random fact.',1,95,584,0,'207.8.101.10','en'),(21307,2290,'2004-08-18 04:15:32',538,'arcy','I\\\'m going back in time on this one. Not even sure if you ever thought this might happen. Maybe comfort is good. I often mistakenly confuse it with complacency. I think I like the idea that maybe in writing this the you from the past might catch a wave of recognition or insight.',1,281,0,0,'69.195.31.236','en'),(21308,3677,'2004-08-18 04:49:34',538,'arcy','Too much \\\"Sex in the City\\\" for you darlin\\\'!!',1,53,584,0,'69.195.31.236','en'),(21309,3682,'2004-08-18 20:12:51',175,'Paul G','a good read.',1,12,0,0,'64.107.88.142','en'),(21310,3683,'2004-08-19 03:43:21',533,'incitor','uh, dunno, i was really drunk when i wrote this shit.  if the mods had to clean up a really messy post (i already know you had to title it for me), i apologize.  and offer my thanks.',1,182,0,0,'24.5.141.120','en'),(21311,3677,'2004-08-19 03:59:05',538,'arcy','that last comment was for capslock',0,34,0,0,'69.195.31.236','en'),(21312,3683,'2004-08-19 07:29:37',533,'incitor','wasn\\\'t really complete, i finished it, but am too drunk and lazy to even consider preparing it for swinney.  uh, if for some reason you care about the rest, go find my fucking livejournal i guess.  bleh.  time to passout.',6,224,0,0,'24.5.141.120','en'),(21313,3684,'2004-08-19 17:08:05',91,'jay','It\\\'s the great dream, right, the return to the pastoral?  I think it\\\'s hard for modern kids to appreciate, what with all the urbane temptations on TV, which is why the populations of Nebraska and a lot of old farm towns are declining, everyone moving toward the cities, the coasts.  We all want what we have not got.  But my guess is it\\\'ll turn around, paradigms will change.  Corporate farming isn\\\'t sustainable, and the market for locally grown produce will only get bigger.  Small farms will find new ways of getting by, city folks buying up property and planting heirloom tomatoes.  I have a friend who wants to move to Vermont and make artisinal cheese.  I say it\\\'s a fine idea, and there are some folks making a nice living at it as we speak. ',1,764,0,0,'66.123.22.66','en'),(21314,3683,'2004-08-20 04:05:31',93,'chiamattt','I really liked this dude. Thanks. ',1,34,0,0,'211.207.246.90','en'),(21315,3683,'2004-08-20 04:25:27',533,'incitor','thanks.  i\\\'ve been sitting around since i wrote it, trying to figure out where i\\\'m going with it.  haha.  it\\\'s hard, because i can only write anymore when i\\\'m drunk.  but i can\\\'t come up with ideas while i\\\'m drunk.  pain in the ass.  grrrr.',2,258,93,0,'24.5.141.120','en'),(21316,3683,'2004-08-21 04:55:58',93,'chiamattt','sure. I can understand the \\\'write when you drink\\\' thing. I\\\'m mostly like that too, but these days I drink socially and not sitting at my desk. Its hard. I try to write swintries, but I have been unable to get anything I feel worthy onto the keyboard for a while now. anyway, I enjoy your posts a lot. keep it up.  ',0,323,533,0,'211.207.246.90','en'),(21317,3639,'2004-08-21 16:49:01',195,'matt','herr doktor, you aren\\\'t who i thought you were, but the apology still holds for you, too.',1,92,0,0,'207.239.93.170','en'),(21318,3684,'2004-08-23 07:27:49',17,'austin','Paul G., this is Austin.  I read this.',1,38,0,0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(21319,3684,'2004-08-23 22:10:44',175,'Paul G','yep.  i go to a particular \r\n<a href=\\\"http://nicholsfarm.com/\\\">vegetable farmer</a>\r\nduring the growing season here, in illinois. he, lloyd, did a stint in the navy, worked in baggage out at o\\\'hare, and then made the move to growing organic produce, along with his wife: doreen.\r\n<p>\r\ncorporate farming depends upon petroleum for many of its herbicides, pesticides, and fertilizers, in addition to the fuel that powers the machinery that plants, harvests, transports, and refrigerates its products.\r\nbut for the introduction of some new technology, it is difficult to imagine how places like ny, la, and chicago would feed their populations - absent petroleum.\r\none way or another, things are going to have to change.\r\n(add something about the abuse of cheap immigrant labor and scary biotechnology here...)\r\nmy vote is as yours: to return to the land.\r\nwe\\\'ll see what happens.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nsometimes you read a book, and then it sits on your shelf.\r\nother books keep finding their way off the shelf, and into your hands.\r\nif i\\\'m honest, i\\\'ll admit that the christian bible, nietzsche\\\'s <i>beyond good and evil</i>, machiavelli\\\'s <i>prince</i>, and hst\\\'s <i>hell\\\'s angels</i>, climb off my shelf a lot.\r\nand i keep some modern american poetry in my bag, along with a few platonic dialogues, and bukowski\\\'s <i>dirty old man</i> too.\r\n<i>hell\\\'s angels</i> has surprisingly little to do with motorcycles, and an awful lot to do with the experience of a particular class of american: marginalized, yet defiant.\r\nhst draws out the parallel between the outlaw subculture and hillbilly subculture - both of whom have had their symbols co-opted, if only parody, now.\r\nlooking into places like wisconsin, west virginia, kentucky, or the hill country in texas, i see people like my family - naturals with small machines and animals, and i hear hst telling their story.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nhi austin!\r\n</p>',1,1922,91,0,'64.107.88.142','en'),(21320,3686,'2004-08-24 05:59:55',17,'austin','dude, i\\\'d let the bitch have her way.  i recently went on a week long motorcycle trip with a viet nam vet., another guy, and my dad.  by the end of it, i was having a hard time keeping my cool and started to snap.  i get all sucked into the conservativism and start agreeing with them on some points.  but the points are things like we should not be in a war in iraq.  and i can go along with this just fine.  and everything is smooth until i say something like, \\\'jesus, i keep forgetting GW is a toadie pup tool who wouldn\\\'t be in office were it not for his dad who couldn\\\'t even get reelected.  junior is a failure at everything he ever tried to pull off legally or illegally.\\\' and my dad says, \\\'careful you are starting to sound like you aren\\\'t a republican.\\\'  i\\\'m not!  but then i\\\'m not a democrat either.  but then pops will turn around and say, \\\'al franken is really funny.\\\'  i\\\'m trying to figure out what we are talking about.  republicans who are sick of being republicans but can\\\'t concieve of anything else?  \r\n</P><P>\r\ni think people need to sort their shit out themselves.  look at the middle east, they have been steady sorting things out forever.  they are doing a great job with it and seem to be largely happy with themselves throwing rocks and missles and car bombs back and forth.  i dont see our need to be in on that.  oil shmoil.  who needs it.  i\\\'d rather walk than join the nut job ranks of muslims and jews in the middle east.  my nut job is just fine in san diego going insane.  \r\n</P><P>\r\ni bought camo converse all stars last weekend as some kind of externalization of the war bouncing around in my head.  i\\\'m showing my awareness.\r\n</P><P>\r\nthe more i listen to what people are saying, the more i wonder just how bad it has to get before we the people invalidate our own government.  the first civil war was north and south.  we could have another one but it wouldn\\\'t be that simple.  it would be more like one side of town versus another.  perish the thought.\r\n</P><P>\r\nor we could just elect kerry to placate us while they keep the war going in iraq.  we\\\'ll be more understanding about the war.  instead of saying we are going to have it wrapped up, we will just keep it going.  openly.  we can\\\'t leave now, we fucked it up!  that is what they will mean.  i say, man, we fucked it up and there is nothing we can do about it now so lets get the shit out of there.  let God sort it out.  if we can keep them from detonating a reagan era bomb in a major city we will be doing something positive.  that will be a positive impact.\r\n</P><P>\r\ni feel like a disenfranchised republican.  i like business.  i like making money.  i like other people doing it too.  some dude in the mountains who makes soap and drives down to town with a 20 year old pickup to sell it at the wholefoods, GOOD FOR HIM.  a biotech company wants to try and isolate the gene for aging so we live for tho hundred years, i\\\'m fine with that.  we need to have a longer view of life.  the bank wants to charge me $2 to use an ATM that isn\\\'t theirs?  fuck you guys, but ok.  but i am NOT down with stealing from other countries or selling them weapons to destabilize them, or starting wars to buy weapons.  i\\\'m down with lower taxes.  i\\\'ll pay more in taxes if it keeps the wife off my back.  i\\\'ve been liberal.  i\\\'ve lived with among them.  i\\\'ve felt the peer pressure to be vegan.  i\\\'ll make vegan food for the vegans.  vegans are nice.  i like my steak medium rare.  i like to wear suits sometimes, with pointy shoes. \r\n</P><P>\r\n i want the war in iraq part 2 to end.  i don\\\'t want us to get our asses handed to us as a reminder, though that will probably happen.  i support the troops because i\\\'m sure it is a nice life until you have to kill some total stranger who wants you dead, or you become an armless legless eating machine.  Newt Gingrich was on CSPAN the other day saying he expected the War On Terror to go on until 2070.  WHY?\r\n</P><P>there is no end to this.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>BURN! BURN!</P>',6,3946,0,0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(21321,3686,'2004-08-24 11:09:40',538,'arcy','Well I know it ain\\\'t my country but if all hell breaks loose you can bet we\\\'ll be in on it. Hello?! Canada\\\'s number one export of primary energy supply is oil, oh ya and you guys own all the companies that refine it. So whats the problem? I guess we\\\'re not as fun to play war with, we\\\'re like the pouty little sister that won\\\'t fight back and always ends up as a neighbourhood POW. No fun in that. ',1,416,17,0,'69.195.31.236','en'),(21322,3685,'2004-08-24 17:50:56',83,'adamajah','<p>This is almost as good as \\\"Geumho pussy crew\\\".\r\n\r\n\r\n\\\"We pause and smoke some crack out of a light bulb\\\"... hahaha</p>',1,132,0,0,'216.206.179.50','en'),(21323,403,'2004-08-24 18:04:34',17,'austin','just a reminder, this article kicks ass.',1,40,0,0,'63.80.97.254','en'),(21324,3686,'2004-08-27 01:30:56',93,'chiamattt','<img src=\\\"http://www.mapleleafweb.com/images/energy-graph.gif\\\">',0,69,0,0,'211.207.246.90','en'),(21325,3686,'2004-08-27 17:14:29',538,'arcy','That\\\'s exactly what I mean. The oil comes from us is refined by us and used by us, so what is affecting the gas prices by such an extreme factor? Whatever my brain starts to hurt when I go there. Cheers to having access to much appreciated public transit!',2,258,93,0,'142.204.189.82','en'),(21326,2926,'2004-08-28 05:59:08',586,'Landon','Youth is the only gift you can never return, relive , or keep for forever, and a dad is a dad nomatter what he did if you show love he will always remeber that and love you for it. even when hes 17 and says he hates you in a heated agrument about some idle highschool girl. if you show him true love he will never be able to let go of you and less then you could let go of him.',2,377,0,0,'67.76.61.54','en'),(21327,3684,'2004-08-28 10:54:21',120,'joyrider','reminds me of the cotton farmers in my hometown.  dying-breed mormons.  their kids all moved to mesa or left to work in the copper mines.',0,137,175,0,'69.144.196.130','en'),(21328,936,'2004-08-28 20:36:18',195,'matt','this is the future of an illusion.',1,34,0,0,'207.239.93.170','en'),(21329,3684,'2004-08-30 02:47:02',175,'Paul G','are they still hiring at the mines?',1,35,120,0,'206.68.117.82','en'),(21330,3684,'2004-08-30 03:58:06',175,'Paul G','i saw my uncle this weekend.  aged 71 years he still has a full pompadour, and he wanted to wrestle me for the dinner check.  he\\\'s my height and build, and he\\\'s got 15 pounds on me; it wasn\\\'t easy.\r\n<p>\r\ni don\\\'t know that i could do exactly what he did, even if i wanted to.  raising animals isn\\\'t my thing; the land up there is getting expensive; and the state of family farming is the subject of many odes.  \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nbut beyond all of that, i don\\\'t know that it would be satisfying.  there\\\'s got to be something more, something creative, something intellectual that\\\'s a part of it - in order to feel complete.  <a href=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=3686\\\">soap-making mountain-man</a> isn\\\'t me - at least it\\\'s not me yet.  the farm was my uncle\\\'s vision, in his time.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\ni do find that i am envious of his freedom, the natural beauty that he has enjoyed, and the successful relationship that he has been a part of.  i\\\'d like to find a way to bring those things into my life - without depriving anyone else in the process.  yeah there\\\'s a strong libertarian streak here as well, but it\\\'s tempered with compassion.  oh and if i could find a way at age 70 to keep my hair and whip dudes 1/2 my age, that would be cool too.  \r\n</p>',1,1309,17,0,'206.68.117.82','en'),(21331,3683,'2004-08-30 20:40:02',574,'xiolablue','wow-that was really a good story.\r\nI loved it.',1,46,533,0,'66.215.156.7','en'),(21332,3683,'2004-08-31 02:20:45',533,'incitor','thank you, i\\\'m glad you liked it.',2,36,574,0,'24.5.141.120','en'),(21333,3683,'2004-08-31 03:28:42',574,'xiolablue','your welcome.',1,13,533,0,'66.215.156.7','en'),(21334,3683,'2004-08-31 03:38:28',533,'incitor','the remainder just went up.  ah... life.',2,40,574,0,'24.5.141.120','en'),(21335,3689,'2004-08-31 03:59:02',533,'incitor','damn, i swear i was sober when i did my tags on this one!~  ah well.  obviously half of it should NOT be in italics.  haha',6,122,0,0,'24.5.141.120','en'),(21336,3685,'2004-09-01 02:23:41',75,'tyler','chiamatt, i listened to your version of \\\'ave maria\\\' the other night. i had almost forgotten how much i love it. do you have any more?',1,139,0,0,'66.32.152.168','en'),(21337,3690,'2004-09-02 00:20:07',57,'weeb','i have been not commenting on jay\\\'s articles, but i would like to profess my undying love for all of them. they bring me glee and joy.\r\n<br><br>\r\nright here, right now, i\\\'m telling you!',1,191,0,0,'208.218.54.65','en'),(21338,3688,'2004-09-02 00:57:22',66,'Peter','<br><tt>fuckin a, matt. you know what? i hate to say it, but since this piece is long, alot of people are gonna skip over it. i hope that those folks see this comment, you know, the part right here where it says <i>this here long piece is worth reading, yo</i>, and actually read it all. its not to be missed. not very easy to swallow, some of it, and fuck, much of it is downright troubling... but its *real*. definitely worth the 15 minutes i took reading it. thanks for bothering to type all that, and, you know, for parsing your life in such a readable way for us here on the intorweb.</tt>',1,594,0,0,'69.112.2.221','en'),(21339,3684,'2004-09-02 01:02:04',66,'Peter','<br><tt><a href=\\\"http://www.citynoise.org/index.php?article=260\\\">Yuba, Wisconsin: 1970 pop. 75, My Uncle\\\'s Farm</a> <i>by Paul G</i></tt>',1,146,175,0,'69.112.2.221','en'),(21340,3690,'2004-10-05 03:45:54',91,'jay','thanks, weeb.  i am heartened to have readers.  Oh, and does anyone have any clue how \\\"Mrs. Fields Cookies\\\" relates to this at all?  Like, what word did Google ads glom onto here?  Or is Mrs. Fields just the default ad when no decent content can be glommed upon?',1,268,0,666,'66.123.22.66','en'),(21341,3685,'2004-09-03 00:44:10',93,'chiamattt','yeah. you can visit my website. chiamattt dot com. I have an archive of music. ',0,79,0,0,'211.207.246.90','en'),(21342,3690,'2004-09-03 01:07:50',175,'Paul G','weeb is right: you kick ass.',1,28,91,0,'131.156.255.243','en'),(21343,3684,'2004-09-04 20:41:50',175,'Paul G','haha, peter.  pic #1, left to right: uncle, me, cousin, coco.  and that is the allis, pulling the manure spreader.  the real date is probably 1971, and my cousin and i are about 4 years-old.  i am struck that it seemed a good idea to everyone that we should ride on the fender - where we could easily fall to a painful, crushing death.  car seats, helmets, air bags and such?\r\n<p>\r\ni remembered your story <i>Suck Creek Crawdaddies: time passes fast nowadays</i> and simon\\\'s <i>i come from here: just the beginning</i>.  i really enjoyed reading those two articles again, along with the other pieces in this <a href=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=3082\\\">series</a>.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nit is hard to believe that several years have passed.  i wish that i could take what i have learned and who i have become back in time, and play my cards a bit differently - online and off.  i am probably not alone.  cheers for being there.\r\n</p>',1,951,66,0,'64.107.88.142','en'),(21344,3690,'2004-09-04 21:07:12',574,'xiolablue','beautiful! i love this poem...',1,30,91,0,'66.215.156.7','en'),(21345,3688,'2004-09-05 12:22:47',228,'belly','i second the <i>definitely worth reading</i> comment. thanks matt.',0,66,0,0,'81.178.113.16','en'),(21346,3695,'2004-09-06 16:17:50',195,'matt','tyler, you\\\'re a good man.',1,28,0,0,'24.92.189.219','en'),(21347,3695,'2004-09-07 20:13:49',66,'Peter','<br><tt>too bad everyone has a different take on <i>higher purpose</i>, huh?</tt> ',1,82,0,0,'156.145.58.11','en'),(21348,3695,'2004-09-08 01:10:00',533,'incitor','<p>i\\\'ve been thinking about this post for some time now.</p>\r\n<p>i believe the author means well.  but shit, i\\\'m tired of the cult of victimhood.  how is someone\\\'s pain worth more than another\\\'s life i wonder.</p>\r\n<p>i think back to my earliest lessons as a bouncer.  i remember how a man in pain will seek to externalize, inflict, his pain on another.  i failed to see then, and fail to see now, how it\\\'s okay to inflict pain merely because one hurting.</p>\r\n<p>i am sickened at how so many lack a basic understanding of the will-to-power.  i don\\\'t understand how the motives of some are ignored, or assumed to be reasonable, while the motives of others are assumed to be unreasonable.</p>\r\n<p>it is a fact of life, that the people on the bottom are not always victims.  they are not always moral or ethical.  their methods are not always acceptable. their ends are not always just.  why is this so hard to see i wonder.</p>\r\n<p>i\\\'m tired of arguing this i guess.  i don\\\'t have the will left to support what i\\\'m writing here.  night after night, for years, i\\\'ve had this conversation.  i care enough to say something even now, but i guess i don\\\'t care enough to put much effort into it.  everyone is welcome to their delusions of human motivations.</p>',4,1287,0,0,'24.5.141.120','en'),(21349,3695,'2004-09-08 04:03:42',17,'austin','i just bit through my tongue.',1,29,0,0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(21350,3695,'2004-09-08 18:19:57',57,'weeb','<p>\r\nButthead once said, \\\"this sucks like nothing has ever sucked before\\\".\r\n<br><br>\r\nsomeone hand me the pepto-bismol.\r\n</p>',6,151,0,0,'208.218.54.65','en'),(21351,3695,'2004-09-09 16:57:22',534,'griece','tyler, how you gonna be a good personal injury lawyer with this sort of attitude? or were you on ecstasy when you wrote this?',5,125,0,0,'156.145.58.11','en'),(21352,3688,'2004-09-09 19:30:28',82,'simon','hey matt. i was thinking fondly of you yesterday for some reason and thought i\\\'d say so. also i THIRD the worth reading comment.',0,131,0,0,'209.21.99.118','en'),(21353,3695,'2004-09-10 13:42:55',492,'bmg','War is our Business, Business is our WAR! ',0,42,0,0,'163.181.251.10','en'),(21354,3695,'2004-09-10 14:39:30',66,'Peter','<center><font size=\\\"20\\\"><font color=\\\"red\\\"><b><center><marquee>\r\nWAR IS PEACE<br>\r\nFREEDOM IS SLAVERY<br>\r\nIGNORANCE IS STRENGTH<br>\r\n</b></font></font></center></marquee>',1,182,492,0,'156.145.58.11','en'),(21355,3688,'2004-09-13 01:13:04',195,'matt','thanks.  i think fondly of you guys, too.  everybody\\\'s good people around here.  thanks for commenting.\r\n',1,108,82,0,'24.92.189.219','en'),(21356,3697,'2004-09-13 05:09:53',195,'matt','(727) 848-8550',1,14,0,0,'24.92.189.219','en'),(21357,3697,'2004-09-13 05:46:23',17,'austin','HA ha ha...  A/S/L/JPGS?!  just kidding.  i didnt get my mach on til i was in my early 20s.  i was way to psycho to deal with chicks prior to that.  now i am sane enough to deal with them for about 3 months.  then the shit hits the fan.',1,236,0,0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(21358,3697,'2004-09-13 05:52:09',17,'austin','i took the liberty of formatting your article for you...  just another way that service is job #1 on swinney.org.  or maybe i was trying to impress you with my html abilities.<BR><BR>i\\\'m a decade older than you are.',1,218,0,0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(21359,3696,'2004-09-13 06:12:04',17,'austin','often times, god is determined to fuck austin up.',1,49,0,0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(21360,3695,'2004-09-13 06:18:27',17,'austin','i think they are going to think you sound like a puto and plant a bomb in your car.  i\\\'m all for a truce, but they can go fuck themselves.  nobody should pander to those people or supplicate in any way.  i\\\'d sign off on their execution if we caught them all.  too bad we can\\\'t find them.  i\\\'m open to letting the ones we do catch rot in the worst of prisons. <BR><BR>i hope you don\\\'t end up specializing in arbitration. ',6,360,0,0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(21361,3697,'2004-09-13 08:02:57',231,'alana','i was in my 20s before i started getting an giving this sort of thing. now you can\\\'t stop me. i think it\\\'s all very dependant upon who you\\\'re surrounded by. move to san francisco. that\\\'s where all the beautiful loving humans are. \r\n\r\nalso, maybe hug a dog and cat. some dogs and cats can share an embrace. they can be really present. \r\n\r\nget out there, sweet kate. become yourself and forget about what you\\\'re meant to have  done and experienced by 18. or 21. or 40.\r\n\r\nyou are kate. you are perfect!\r\n\r\n',1,519,0,0,'150.101.156.40','en'),(21362,3697,'2004-09-13 13:33:10',66,'Peter','<br><tt>dont sweat it; compared to worldwide averages (despite whatever your social-group/mass-media/social-trends/demographic might fool you into thinking) youre probably right on schedule. fuck this meaningless drive to be sexually/socially mature by the time youre 15... thats just not how humans work in this more modern generation, no matter how anyone might strive to rationalize it. for what its worth, by 18, i also had yet to exchange passionate kisses. i was a virgin. now, at 27, looking back, i realize i have no regrets in how that timing worked out. i have lived and grown through many relationships since, some wonderfully physical, some not. some rife with kissing and fucking and lovemaking and all sorts of scandalous and banal couplings, some not. i used to wonder the same... <i>\"when will my turn come, dammit?!\"</i>... and now that im happily married and content in the most permanently fulfilling relationship ive ever had, i realize that those frustrations were just the ramblings of my horny 18-year-old mind. im really glad i wasnt wrapped up in relationships, at 18, that required more maturity and wisdom than i had at the time. looking back, everything happened in the right sequence, if not always the most physically fulfilling one, surely saving me many regrets. enjoy being young, and enjoy the novelty of growing into your sensuality... its an enlightenment you only get to experience once.</tt>',1,1379,0,0,'156.145.58.11','en'),(21363,3697,'2004-09-13 14:10:49',231,'alana','fuck yeah, <pre>peter</pre>.',1,28,66,0,'150.101.156.40','en'),(21364,3699,'2004-09-13 16:54:24',17,'austin','i dont understand.  somebody dumped you on the left, or you are losing your vision?',1,83,0,0,'63.80.97.254','en'),(21365,3697,'2004-09-14 02:28:05',234,'etienne','i definitely do not think that being sexually active before i was 18 helped any more than it hindered.  i know it doesn\\\'t seem like that now but chill!  ',1,156,0,0,'219.88.223.161','en'),(21366,3699,'2004-09-14 04:33:07',231,'alana','i lost my vision.<br>a medication took it away.',3,47,17,0,'150.101.156.40','en'),(21367,3699,'2004-09-14 05:01:48',17,'austin','that is messed up!  permanently?  or you can switch meds?',1,57,231,0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(21368,3699,'2004-09-14 05:04:21',234,'etienne','wow.  this is totally something that i fear happening because i am so visually impaired already, at 24.  thanks for sharing.',1,124,0,0,'219.88.223.161','en'),(21369,3699,'2004-09-14 15:07:13',231,'alana','austin: i\\\'m off the med that did it, but the side effect is irreversible.\r\n\r\netienne: i was 24 when this happened. five  years later, it\\\'s still the same. with luck it won\\\'t progress further. do you have a progressive 