-27 03:52:42',17,'austin','glad you liked it!',1,18,195,0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(21404,3704,'2004-09-27 18:16:46',195,'matt','i didn\\\'t understand the part about the lipstick, though.',1,59,0,0,'24.92.189.219','en'),(21405,3704,'2004-09-28 00:03:37',17,'austin','i think lipstick is widely understood to be doggie boner from the old your momma/chihuahua joke.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ni could be wrong.',1,125,195,0,'63.80.97.254','en'),(21406,3704,'2004-09-28 01:26:35',195,'matt','well, that is an intriguing premise - my mother and a chihuahua.  i\\\'ve never heard it.  please elucidate.<BR><BR>this reminds me of how i\\\'m always asking jamie, apropos of nothing, \\\"you know what the difference is between you and a fridgidaire?\\\"  and he\\\'s like, \\\"what?\\\"  and i\\\'m like, \\\"i dunno.  you tell me.\\\"  and i never tell him the punchline.<BR><BR>someday he\\\'s going to hear the joke somewhere, maybe from one of his redneck uncles or from the rednecks at his engineering firm.  better yet, i think i\\\'m going to drop in on him at work one day, as i do occaisonally with christie for one reason or another, and, with him sitting there, i\\\'m going to ask his boss, \\\"you know the difference between a homo and a refrigerator?\\\"  (only i won\\\'t say <B><I>homo</B></I>.  it will be something more colorful.)  and it\\\'s going to be funny.  especially when i see the look on jamie\\\'s face.  probably not too funny for jamie, though.',1,980,17,0,'24.92.189.219','en'),(21407,3704,'2004-09-28 02:41:20',17,'austin','<a href=\\\"http://www.woodhavenlabs.com/males-swollen.html\\\">\\\"we call it lipstick\\\"</a>',1,95,195,0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(21408,3704,'2004-09-28 04:09:10',195,'matt','<B><I>homo erectus</B></I>.  we got a lot of mileage out of that one in seventh grade.  i\\\'d forgotten all about that \\\'til just now.',1,137,0,0,'24.92.189.219','en'),(21409,3704,'2004-09-28 04:10:11',195,'matt','i found reading that page somewhat arousing.',1,44,17,0,'24.92.189.219','en'),(21410,3704,'2004-09-28 04:38:41',17,'austin','HA HA, EW.  i was more than a little disturbed that i was searching the internet for \\\"dog erection lipstick\\\".',4,115,195,0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(21411,689,'2004-09-29 03:04:52',195,'matt','i wonder how he\\\'s doing....',1,30,0,0,'24.92.189.219','en'),(21412,3703,'2004-09-30 00:02:15',175,'Paul G','thanks.  it\\\'s weird that sometimes things happen for a reason, and other times things just happen.  but, being human, we always want a reason - and sometimes try too hard to put reasons where they don\\\'t belong.\r\n<p>\r\nhealing from some injury or illness makes you really appreciate what you took for granted, before.  cheers.\r\n</p>',1,336,0,0,'131.156.159.145','en'),(21413,3705,'2004-10-03 07:01:28',195,'matt','how could you tell somebody they\\\'re \\\"shadowing\\\" you and to please fuck off?  how rude.  how arrogant. how nasty.<BR><BR>sometimes i wished i lived in a place where people were always coming and going, a place full of activity.  dorm life.  i miss that sometimes.  but, then again, i love having my own space.',1,317,0,0,'24.92.189.219','en'),(21414,3374,'2004-10-03 09:02:35',595,'tomhanks','<p>2003-06-08 chiamatt:\r\n\\\"We were staying at a Bungalow community called the Lamai Chalets\\\".</p>\r\n\r\nHi chiamattt\r\nOk more than one year ago you are stayed at Lamai Chaletâ€¦ .\r\nAt November 2003 I was also there. And I met Den, Tik and Pompui (the boss) too.\r\nThis year from Christmas to new-year I go back to Samui and want to stay at Lamai Chalet. \r\nDo you have the telephone number from Lamai Chalet? There is no homepage or contact address in the net (didnâ€™t find one).\r\n\r\nThanks for any help.\r\n\r\nGreetings from Switzerland\r\n\r\ntomhanks\r\n',0,544,0,0,'81.63.13.112','en'),(21415,3702,'2004-10-03 19:42:21',183,'ali','<p> I had to swtich my keyboard back to English in order to type this. <p>\r\n\r\nI have been through that countryside, that exact countryside (the beauty of the fixed route and it\\\'s relation to time always astounds me) about 50 times in the last 4 years. More, actually, but I can\\\'t keep track anymore. (har har) <p> \r\n\r\nYou are in Canada on those rails. The relation of that speeding rail, the wet grass (or snow covered piles of things) is a distinct image in my mind, priviledged because of this form of travel. The streaking drops tghat roll across the window blur together from one voyage to another, mixed with sunsets, sunrises, and stop announcements. There is no doubt in my mind where I am when I am on the rails. <p>\r\n\r\nEven as I rolled across the praries or through Quebec, I have never felt lost in those boxy green and beige chairs. I have witnessed mystery there, endured and enjoyed other people\\\'s lives. Death. Oakville. Brantford. Kingston. Winnipeg. Strathroy. Shawinigan. Jasper. After a while every stop becomes the same place.<p> I have never found a more fitting view of this country. Thanks for reminding me. ',1,1139,0,0,'66.185.84.196','en'),(21416,3705,'2004-10-04 05:01:49',93,'chiamattt','why were you sitting in the hall? I dont get it. ',1,49,0,0,'211.207.246.90','en'),(21417,3705,'2004-10-04 13:10:52',594,'HappyKitty','I was sitting in the hall to write a story about the action taking place around me as I was writing.\r\n\r\nThe beginning of the story is edited out in this version; if you\\\'d like, I could e-mail you the whole thing.',1,215,93,0,'138.73.15.94','en'),(21418,3706,'2004-10-04 13:50:35',66,'Peter','<br><img src=\"http://saturn5.com/~peter/rhodamine/images/lomo/liberty2.jpg\">',1,78,0,0,'156.145.58.57','en'),(21419,3702,'2004-10-04 20:13:27',538,'arcy','I find it relieving to know that there is a way from A to B thats not the 401. Its nice to think that my world is not as familiar as I thought it was.',2,150,183,0,'142.204.74.158','en'),(21420,3705,'2004-10-04 22:44:08',93,'chiamattt','sure. d m a t t e A T g m a i l . c o m',1,39,594,0,'211.202.80.222','en'),(21421,3707,'2004-10-05 16:00:38',66,'Peter','<br><tt><i>\"...DRIVE OUR TEENY LOLITAS WILD WITH HUMAN PHEROMONES MADE FROM PRE-OWNED INKJET CARTRIDGES...\"</i><br><br>this cracked me up in the biggest way. this piece is every possible spam gimmick thrown into one hilarious tirade. nice. hahahaha!</tt>',1,108,0,0,'156.145.58.57','en'),(21422,3709,'2004-10-05 17:40:09',82,'simon','1. heh, widget.\r\n2. huh? what?\r\n3. hi swinney. are you really in georgia?',0,73,0,0,'209.21.99.118','en'),(21423,3709,'2004-10-05 20:38:42',195,'matt','you got an ad for mrs. field\\\'s cookies over there.',1,53,0,0,'24.92.189.219','en'),(21424,3710,'2004-10-06 19:50:47',195,'matt','goddam, i know that tune.  give \\\'im a swift kick in the ass every time you go by, and see if that doesn\\\'t shape him up some.<BR><BR>no, don\\\'t.  love him is all you can do until he realizes that he can and needs to get better, however he wants to do that.',1,263,0,0,'24.92.189.219','en'),(21425,3709,'2004-10-06 21:18:11',66,'mesothelioma','<br>mesothelioma mesothelioma mesothelioma mesothelioma mesothelioma mesothelioma mesothelioma mesothelioma mesothelioma mesothelioma mesothelioma mesothelioma',1,155,0,0,'162.83.204.173','en'),(21426,3515,'2004-10-07 05:02:17',420,'thanatos','yes .. u r right ... why do i even bother to write about it ... why do we even write and succumbing to chronicle these myopic events in human existence that will not really matter later on?  ... no matter how grand of a theory, poetry, art, science or alligory we attempt to leave behind, at the end of the day, the true forces of destruction may obliterate all forms of illusions ... \r\n\r\ni don\\\'t know why i bother, good point, good point.',2,442,0,0,'67.101.98.164','en'),(21427,3689,'2004-10-07 10:53:59',65,'le','good stuff.',4,11,0,0,'67.164.14.63','en'),(21428,3704,'2004-10-07 10:57:10',65,'le','mr peepers.',4,11,0,0,'67.164.14.63','en'),(21429,3705,'2004-10-08 12:19:24',93,'chiamattt','carleton or oh U?',0,17,0,0,'211.202.80.222','en'),(21430,3711,'2004-10-09 17:43:49',93,'chiamattt','damn. are you writing about me?',3,31,0,0,'211.202.80.222','en'),(21431,3710,'2004-10-09 18:38:08',508,'edward','in a package.. as everything it seems. welcome.',1,47,0,0,'193.10.214.97','en'),(21432,3711,'2004-10-09 18:43:43',508,'edward','probably not, because it seems as if the person she is writing about does not see the world in an accurate way. so if your first thought is that the picture might be of you, you\\\'re probably wrong.. yep.',3,205,93,0,'193.10.214.97','en'),(21433,3704,'2004-10-10 14:02:16',295,'karenlee','Kommissar Erex! [If you are not familiar with inspector rex please say]',1,71,0,0,'203.194.6.250','en'),(21434,3703,'2004-10-10 14:04:51',295,'karenlee','oh dear pg, are you ok? are you all covered in scabby splotches? are they sure it\\\'s zoster? some of those spidies are quite nasty and would appear just like the zoster.',1,171,0,0,'203.194.6.250','en'),(21435,3711,'2004-10-10 22:36:41',175,'Paul G','it\\\'s like a thin person telling an obese\r\nperson that losing weight is a simple matter.\r\nor maybe it\\\'s like someone with money\r\nlaughing at a poor man\\\'s unfashionable\r\nclothes.\r\n<p>\r\nwhat\\\'s easy?  what\\\'s difficult?  why?\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nyou take those things in which you excell,\r\nand then compare yourself to someone who\r\nstruggles with them - for the purpose of?\r\n</p>',4,381,0,0,'192.203.136.254','en'),(21436,3711,'2004-10-10 22:44:40',175,'Paul G','this is - totally - every post-break-up scolding, ever.  or, it\\\'s the \\\"well they sucked at a,b,c and so i\\\'m glad i\\\'m not with them anymore,\\\" self-talk post-break-up...\r\n<p>\r\nbut all the isobel articles are penetrating, engaging, good-reads.  yep.',1,261,93,0,'192.203.136.254','en'),(21437,3711,'2004-10-11 04:04:15',65,'le','i am with paul g on this one.',4,29,0,0,'67.164.14.63','en'),(21438,3711,'2004-10-11 17:21:54',508,'edward','how long can you stand listening to the one complaining about how hard it is to lose weight, or the poor man\\\'s stories of how successful he once were.\r\n\r\nsometimes people got to shape up. here; look around and evaluate his life.',3,231,175,0,'193.11.88.235','en'),(21439,3711,'2004-10-12 00:31:37',552,'isobel','I should probably apologize for the rant, and yes I\\\'m probably a bad person for saying and thinking these things, but there is only so much you can do for one person before they have to start claiming their own accountability. The frustration lies in the fact that they are so quick to judge everyone with such unattainable expectations, that I thought it was so amazing that one person was so dedicated to their own dignity. I didn\\\'t realize it but you can actually betray yourself with too much dignity. I know this facade is built for the sake of protection, and I never know what to do when its all broken down and exposed.  ',2,635,0,0,'69.195.31.216','en'),(21440,3703,'2004-10-12 06:52:14',175,'Paul G','yep: better.  now i\\\'m going to take a class in \\\"tough love\\\" so that i can take responsibility for everything.  once i do that, my mother will grow younger, her memory will return, and she won\\\'t need to walk with a cane anymore.  \r\n<p>oh, and our current president is in the white house because he earned the position with his own efforts.  and babies born to women who smoke crack are stupid for choosing that too.</p>',1,430,295,0,'131.156.159.154','en'),(21441,3712,'2004-10-13 14:57:06',82,'simon','heh. we moved to a tiny town in pennsylvania from san francisco halfway through 4th grade. many parent-teacher conferences and school-changes ensued. in fact, i wrote a <a href=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=1412\\\">\\\"swinney\\\"</a> about it.',1,268,0,0,'209.21.99.118','en'),(21442,3712,'2004-10-13 16:49:31',17,'austin','...series...\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ni moved around allot to.  ultimately i gave up and went to a boarding school.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nhi jen!',1,120,0,0,'63.80.97.254','en'),(21443,3712,'2004-10-14 01:03:17',599,'jentifer','How kosher is it to reply to my own thingamabob? \r\n\r\nMy parents worked for the US Public Health Service so I spent most of my growing up days in small towns on or near reservations. \r\n\r\nMy favorite moving story: when we moved from Seattle I was only about 4 years old. I knew we were moving somewhere with an \\\"A\\\" in the beginning, and I guess my parents didn\\\'t teach me much geography. I told one teacher I was moving to Australia, a friend that we were relocating to Alambama, my grandma learned we were carting ourselves off to Alaska and my mother got a phonecall from my sunday school teacher asking if we needed any help learning German for our move to Austria. In the end it was only Arizona, and I was heartbroken when I learned I wouldn\\\'t have my own pony or a tent.',2,786,0,0,'66.74.35.133','en'),(21444,3711,'2004-10-14 03:32:59',175,'Paul G','all the art, literature and music that i like was made by people who struggled with adversity in their lives.  some of it is comic; some of it is tragic.  so, i guess that i can stand to listen to the complaints for quite a long time indeed.\r\n<p>\r\nwhat i can\\\'t stand is the thought that there is one \\\"shape\\\" for people.  and i reject the idea that everyone is responsible for, or capable of altering, the circumstances of their life.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nmany good people suffer, needlessly, because they are outside the  mean in some way.  and sometimes we are victims of the bad choices that others make.  and sometimes truly outrageous events cost innocent people their lives and/or happiness.  etc. \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nthe tone of this article was really hateful, as i read it.  sometimes, people need to make changes for the sake of their health, or whatever, ok.  but the article didn\\\'t read as being inspirational, or constructive, or in any way positive.  it read like someone throwing poop at someone else.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nand now a happy story about the way that life should be:\r\n<br>\r\nmy \r\n<a href=\\\"http://www.thedailystar.net/2004/02/16/2004-02-16__cul03.jpg\\\">\r\nwife and i</a>\r\ntook a ride in\r\n<a href=\\\"http://www.denvillenj.org/BarbieCar.jpg\\\">\r\nour car</a>,\r\nto our\r\n<a href=\\\"http://pamsthemes.com/barbie2/dream-house.jpg\\\">\r\nhome</a>\r\nin malibu.\r\nthe end.\r\n</p>',3,1384,508,0,'131.156.159.101','en'),(21445,3712,'2004-10-14 15:36:13',82,'simon','haha that\\\'s awesome. according to family legend, i had a fit when my parents picked me up from preschool and told me we were moving back to san franciscoâ€”at the time, we were in new jersey. they picked me up, put me in the back of the vw bus and i crawled out the window and ran to the steps of the nearby church and banged on the doors and yelled, i want to live here and do jazzercise! they taught it in the basement of the church. as far as i could tell, that\\\'s what churches were for.',1,494,0,0,'209.21.99.118','en'),(21446,3712,'2004-10-14 17:54:20',66,'Peter','<br><tt><i>\\\"i want to live here and do jazzercise!\\\"</i><br><Br>classic!</tt>',1,82,82,0,'156.145.58.11','en'),(21447,3712,'2004-10-14 17:56:55',66,'Peter','<br><tt>also: i really liked this article. it was fun to read, mostly due to having had a similar pencil, which i got from the cumberland science museum in nashville, tennessee. i was very frustrated when it had worn down to the nub, and all that was left was the rock-cylinder. whenever we would take our annual field-trip there, all the kids in my class would get all sorts of pencils from the gift-shop there; it was a sort of status thing, for the rest of the year, whoever had the coolest pencil from the science museum.<br><Br>then we all grew up and discovered other cities, drugs and sex. ahh well, all good things do pass, as they say.</tt>',1,649,599,0,'156.145.58.11','en'),(21448,3711,'2004-10-14 18:00:05',66,'Peter','<br><tt><A href=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=1475\\\">this</a> was my take on 