with the issues and research the candidates beforehand. it helps you decide.<br><Br><i>*best friendly*</i<</tt>',1,155,557,0,'162.83.193.107','en'),(21519,3723,'2004-10-24 15:20:28',74,'jo','i might have to not read swinney for the next week or so because if we have another <a href=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=3138\\\">discussion like this one</a>, i might go into cardiac arrest. because i have always thought people who didn\\\'t vote were fuckheads, but now i\\\'m actually <em>scared</em> and <em>enraged</em> by people who don\\\'t vote. i feel like i\\\'m being held hostage in my own country by people who are indifferent. that is much more upsetting to me than feeling like the country is being run by the religious right because the religious right is really just a small minority, they\\\'re hardly anything. the real power are the indifferent people, they are the real vote-swingers. what has to happen, you fucks, WHAT WILL MAKE YOU GIVE A SHIT?\r\n\r\n',4,796,0,0,'66.68.108.105','en'),(21520,3720,'2004-10-24 15:37:21',93,'chiamattt','you are all funny. the fact is. the american populous is lazy. lazy fucks who like to blame others for the problems. bush. kerry. what is the difference? the fact is, with either elected, nothing will change, and all anyone can talk about is how shitty bush is. do you think bush caused all the problems? bush is a result. bush is what happens when people become so fucking consumed. I hate to say it, but americans are lazy. I hate to say it, but americans like to blame \\\'the third man\\\' and americans just like to blame. blame. blame. blame. read the fucking books. do the fucking math. american politics, and american civil society has been corrupt since before pearl harbour. its pathetic. and to think that the american \\\'swinney.org\\\' is anything more than the \\\'norm\\\' is pathetic as well. whats my point? my point is that \\\'americans\\\' do nothing to change the way it is. they just pick one of two sides and go with it....it infuriates me. yes sure. there is the odd person who knows what is going on...and it maybe perhaps it is odd that it is the ones who do, that arent living in the u.s anymore. they left. its pathetic. the roman empire fell...and so will the u.s empire...for many of the same reasons...and most of you will just sit back and say \\\"i didn\\\'t see it coming\\\". ugh. pathetic. ',1,1327,0,0,'211.202.80.222','en'),(21521,3720,'2004-10-24 16:14:36',195,'matt','the united states of america is the greatest endeavor in, the highest achievement of human history, and it will be just fine.  not everyone is lazy.  not everyone is corrupt.  there are good people on the left and the right who are full of hope, who will do whatever it takes to make things right and make things better.  i, for one, am not going anywhere.  i\\\'m going to stay here and do whatever i can, however much or little that might be.<BR><BR>one candidate <U><B>is</U></I> better than the other, and i desperately hope he wins, but if he doesn\\\'t, there is still hope, and there will still be people who will do their utmost to ensure that democracy stays alive in this country.<BR><BR>your ill-informed, grad student blanket generalizations are wrong and are not helpful in the least.  if you don\\\'t have anything constructive to say, then please just shut the fuck up.',5,884,0,0,'24.92.189.219','en'),(21522,3720,'2004-10-24 16:33:19',195,'matt','</B>*closes tag*',0,16,0,0,'24.92.189.219','en'),(21523,3720,'2004-10-24 22:20:12',183,'lin','<p>I think you could say that chiamatt represents the rest of the world, the majority of which now seem to feel this way about americans. Anyone with two cents knows that defining the entire american culture in one way or another is just a blanket statement that cannot take into account the myriad of differences that exist. However, I think that it\\\'s ironic that this sort of blanket pessimism is reflective of how people within the US seem to view their sitution in regards to elections (one guy or the other), and also how other countries have now come to view the US. As a Canadian, I find it sad that \\\'we\\\' talk about Americans as if they don\\\'t live half an hour away from some of us.  We all have a lot of responsibility to take. We all like to point the finger.</p>\r\n',0,786,195,0,'66.185.84.196','en'),(21524,3720,'2004-10-25 00:14:25',534,'griece','yeah chiamattt, all americans are lazy. so are all the faggots. and niggers and kikes. fuckin catholics! damned women! fuckin yankees! pansy ass redneck white trash! flaky assed californians! fuckin flyover state hicks! damned homo canadians! fuckin towelheads! muthafuckin injuns! chinks! yellows! dykes! eurotrash! aryans! nazis! christians! ASSHOLES ALL!<br><br>generalized labels SUCK ASS and you should BE ASHAMED for saying what you said. youre way off base, dude, and though you may know alot of facts cause youve \"read the books\" and \"done your homework\" you need to learn to apply that knowlege to the real world in a mature, eloquent fashion- not in a way that appears intended to offend \"that group\" you speak so lazily of. and im not saying this as an \"american\" so much as i am saying it as a \"human. make fun of america all you want- it sucks in ALOT of ways, just like your country, or any other country does- no where is perfect, dude. please realize that making such sweeping epiphanies against any group- americans or otherwise- isnt really cool nowadays. this aint 1950- we try to be a little more civilly minded nowadays<br><br>and to go on and end this flame, let me just go on record as saying <b>\"HITLER!!!\"</b>. thank you. (BURN! BURN!)',6,843,93,0,'162.83.193.107','en'),(21525,3720,'2004-10-25 00:44:14',175,'Paul G','<PRE>\r\n     !!!!        \r\n  !!!!!!!!       \r\n!!!!!!!!!!!   O_O\r\n!!!  !!!!!!! /@ @\\\\\r\n      !!!!!! \\\\ x /\r\n      !!!!!!/ m  !m\r\n       !!!!/ __  |\r\n       !!!!|/  \\\\__\r\n        !!!\\\\______\\\\\r\n</PRE>',1,207,0,0,'206.68.117.82','en'),(21526,3720,'2004-10-25 04:07:42',82,'simon','whoa',0,4,0,0,'24.215.234.170','en'),(21527,3720,'2004-10-25 13:24:56',66,'Peter','<br><tt><img src=\"http://www.rhodamine.org/elvis.jpg\"></tt>',1,65,0,0,'156.145.58.57','en'),(21528,3720,'2004-10-25 16:18:01',74,'jo','lin, thanks for making it sound as if it\\\'s a new thing that most of the world views americans this way. that\\\'s nice of you. but the sentiment isn\\\'t new, it\\\'s as old as the hills, and like most national stereotypes, just as wrong. (oh except the ones about the french, everyone knows those guys are jerks. FREEDOM FRIES!) i am kind of surprised that dave, who i have previously thought was a pretty with it guy, would resort to such petty namecalling, but then again, i have now said in two different swintries that nonvoters were fucks, so. i\\\'m guilty of this as well.\r\n\r\n',3,587,0,0,'216.142.229.132','en'),(21529,3720,'2004-10-25 16:20:06',74,'jo','hey paul g, this series should really include stefan\\\'s article on how there is no good reason to be in iraq, that was an awesome swintry.',0,140,175,0,'216.142.229.132','en'),(21530,3720,'2004-10-25 16:23:02',74,'jo','http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=3298',0,53,175,0,'216.142.229.132','en'),(21531,3720,'2004-10-25 22:41:51',175,'Paul G','chia has always struck me as a thoughtful\r\nperson, with deep concerns about the \r\neconomy, politics, and war.  like you!\r\ni am thankful that there are people who are still engaged, and brave enough to voice their ideas in their own names.  witty and well-reasoned articles and comments are always more fun than, \\\"fuckfuck.\\\"  reading backwards, it\\\'s easy to miss s5, wb, jim, le, o, et al.\r\n<p>\r\ni started following DEAN early, because of you.  it seemed like the only real choice the american people had was in the democratic primary, this year.  either we dropped the ball, or it was knocked from our hands.  where do we go, now?  nader is being kept off the ballot here, in illinois.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nenergy policy, conservation of natural resources, ending offensive war, new farming, etc.  that\\\'s where i\\\'m at.  my candidates and advocates were marginalized.  why are we still so petroleum dependent?  you would think, if for no other reason, defense would push us away from a resource located primarily in the mid-east and russia.  it makes no sense.  increasing competition for diminishing natural resources = more war.\r\nand if a lot of hungry people with guns start moving about, there won\\\'t be anyplace that\\\'s terribly safe, anymore...\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\ni stole london.<br>\r\ni stole france.<br>\r\ni stole austin\\\'s squirrel,<br>\r\nfrom his underpants.\r\n</p>',1,1375,74,0,'206.68.117.82','en'),(21532,3722,'2004-10-25 22:56:42',175,'Paul G','though an alias has led to more than one blushing face, i want to say that i have enjoyed everything that you\\\'ve written here.',1,129,0,0,'206.68.117.82','en'),(21533,3720,'2004-10-25 23:20:52',74,'jo','i should have maybe finished my thought and said that it would be easy to just be like: \\\"dave is a meanie! what a mean jerk!\\\" but he\\\'s not, not at all. he\\\'s passionate. i am, too. which is why what he wrote doesn\\\'t anger me, he has a right to think and say whatever he wants. i respect him for feeling strongly. i wish more people did.\r\n\r\n<p>i really miss dean, paul. dean wasn\\\'t wishy-washy about shit. i think that really scared moderate democrats. it\\\'s a shame.</p>',0,489,175,0,'66.68.108.105','en'),(21534,3720,'2004-10-26 02:24:39',195,'matt','you should see the way i treat the people who are actually physically around me day-to-day.  you should see the way i treat myself.  i have a very ugly side that\\\'s been coming out more often now that i\\\'m not deadening it anymore.  but telling you about it does not excuse it.  i regret the inflammatory and hateful tone of my previous comment.  i regretted it about an hour after i posted it and had calmed down some.<BR><BR>chia\\\'s comment does not seem witty or well-reasoned.  at the time, as an american, i took it as a prolonged insult.  he apparently disagrees with griece, who suggested that a vote for nader would be a vote for bush.  he says, \\\"you people are funny,\\\" then goes into a diatribe about americans.  it really hit home when he said that the \\\"american swinney.org\\\" isn\\\'t any different from the norm.  that just tied us into the rest of his comments.<BR><BR>(i\\\'m presuming that griece is american.  they talk like an american, at any rate.  i would be interested in knowing who all has access to the griece avatar.  i know it used to be amy and lulu, but the neat thing is that now it could be anybody.)<BR><BR>i shouldn\\\'t have reacted in that fashion.  i should have gone away until i could respond like a civil human.  i respect everyone\\\'s right to have an opinion and express it and also reserve my right to question it.  in a respectful manner.  sorry.',1,1406,0,0,'24.92.189.219','en'),(21535,3720,'2004-10-26 02:28:41',534,'griece','the beauty of the internets (thanks, bush!) is that you should never know who i am. i am me. i am not amy or lulu or anyone else. i am griece. does it matter who i am? i am me. i think chia is a idealistic socialist who talks alotta talk but thats about it. what good are facts if they offend so much that they are useless?!',5,324,195,0,'162.83.193.107','en'),(21536,3720,'2004-10-26 02:30:47',534,'griece','also, i am not an american.',5,27,195,0,'162.83.193.107','en'),(21537,3639,'2004-10-26 02:33:13',534,'griece','\\\"i am whoever you say i am, and if i wasn\\\'t, then why would i say i am?\\\" ---eminem',5,91,195,0,'162.83.193.107','en'),(21538,3720,'2004-10-26 13:04:58',74,'jo','at a bar in brooklyn filled with swinneyites, over the span of about three hours, multiple people told me their and their friends\\\' aliases and i remember being surprised by them all. and now i don\\\'t remember a  <b>single one</b> when usually my memory for these things is razor sharp and i can parrot back entire conversations verbatim from months and years ago. i guess that i didn\\\'t care that much but i love a good secret. and a good vodka tonic.',0,458,0,0,'66.68.108.105','en'),(21539,3720,'2004-10-26 13:24:04',66,'Peter','<br><tt>heh heh heh... <i>great lakes</i> has a way of blotting out your short-term memory, you know. \\\'specially when chris is tending the bar ;)</tt>',1,153,74,0,'156.145.58.57','en'),(21540,3720,'2004-10-26 13:28:11',67,'trouble','to this day i have yet to see a good argument for the use of multiple aliases.  intentionally provoking people as the basis for stimulating new conversation or ideas is a good thing, always welcomed in my opinion, but why people feel the need to have that side of you kept separate from your other, more public, side has always struck me as silly.  everybody gets flamed every now and then, it comes with the territory.  doesn\\\'t it?\r\n\r\ni don\\\'t know... maybe i\\\'m old.',3,475,74,0,'24.225.168.121','en'),(21541,3720,'2004-10-26 15:58:11',74,'jo','yeah right on. that\\\'s why, to this day, the only alias i have is incitor. hahahaha.',0,86,67,0,'216.142.229.132','en'),(21542,3720,'2004-10-26 17:34:10',66,'Peter','<br>what if we\'re all aliases, and this site was peopled by a single, schitzo sycophant... who\'s name was <i>AUSTIN SWINNEY</i>... MUAHAHAHA! s.o wi11 pwnz j00 a11!<br><br>we have the \'alias thread\' every year. first, it was \'critic\', then \'griece\', then whoever. theyre inevitable on the internets. i have an alias on here (which i use when im writing something that i dont want filed under the \'peter\' alias). i know of more than one alias on here that are shared. ultimately, they serve as avatars for different personalities/moods, i like to think, and aren\'t meant so much as ways to anonymously flame someone. for most of the core of us here, who know each other face to face, on terms aside form this site, id like to think flaming isnt the point :) so that being said, lets not weather yet <i>another</i> tirade on aliases, thusly forcing austin to implement some half-baked identity-theft-thumbprint-scan-to-log-in mechanism, ok? if the aliases make you that insecure, feel free to just assume that anything said by someone who isnt someone you know in the flesh... is me. better? I KN0W ALL! or better yet, just make your own alias and have an argument with yourself.<br><br><i>*best friendly*</i></tt>',1,686,0,0,'156.145.58.57','en'),(21543,3720,'2004-10-26 17:44:15',606,'critic','totally.',1,8,0,0,'156.145.58.57','en'),(21544,3720,'2004-10-26 22:31:35',93,'chiamattt','my other alias is chiamattt',6,27,0,0,'211.202.80.222','en'),(21545,3723,'2004-10-26 22:38:17',93,'chiamattt','This is why I want Dubya to win another 4 years. Maybe when 100million americans lose their jobs, and out of that 100million, 50 million are drafted into a war in Iran the population will actually wake up and say \\\"shit, what happened?\\\"',1,241,74,0,'211.202.80.222','en'),(21546,3720,'2004-10-26 22:51:30',175,'Paul G','comments in full circle, returning to the subject of the article:\r\n<p>\r\n(Peter) <i>\\\"thusly forcing austin to implement some half-baked \r\nidentity-theft-thumbprint-scan-to-log-in mechanism,\\\"</i>\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\n(Revelation, 13:16) <i>\\\"And he causeth all, both small and great, \r\nrich and poor, free and bond, to receive a mark \r\nin their right hand, or in their foreheads,\\\"</i>\r\n</p>',1,390,0,0,'64.107.88.142','en'),(21547,3720,'2004-10-26 23:47:44',17,'austin','Yes, the end of days is triggered by too many humans to name.  We were screwed from the beginning with our screwing.  Even if the planet only had good christians, no heathens, no evil christians, the end of days would still arrive.  Eventually, there would be too many people to name.',1,284,175,0,'63.80.97.254','en'),(21548,3723,'2004-10-27 01:43:35',441,'yummy','<p>So shocking how many women don\\\'t vote...Is it not enough to remember that others suffered so we could have this privilege?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Check out the HBO movie Iron Jawed Angels. <br>\r\nhttp://www.hbo.com/films/ironjawedangels/synopsis </p>\r\n\r\n<p>It is a graphic depiction of just a small part of the battle women waged for voting rights. I am ashamed that there were times I took this for granted.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>On Nov. 15, 1917 forty prison guards wielding clubs and their warden\\\'s blessing went on a rampage against the 33 women wrongly convicted of \\\"obstructing sidewalk traffic\\\" ...all because they dared to picket Woodrow Wilson\\\'s White House for the right to vote.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>They beat Lucy Burn, chained her hands to the cell bars above her head and left her hanging for the night. They hurled Dora Lewis into a dark cell, smashed her head against an iron bed and knocked her out cold. For weeks, the women\\\'s only water came from an open pail. Their food was infested with worms. When one of the leaders, Alice Paul, embarked on a hunger strike, they tied her to a chair, forced a tube down her throat and poured liquid into her until she vomited. She was tortured like this for weeks until word was smuggled out to the press.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Woodrow Wilson and his cronies actually tried to have many of these women institutionalized on the grounds of insanity.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>........<br>\r\nIn 1848 The first women\\\'s rights convention in the United States is held in Seneca Falls, New York. A \\\"Declaration of Sentiments and Resolutions\\\" is signed by many present, outlining the issues and goals for the developing women\\\'s movement. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>It would be 1920...and 72 years...before women would be able to vote in the US.</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n',3,1764,0,0,'24.7.71.79','en'),(21549,3720,'2004-10-27 02:11:44',195,'matt','now lemme tell you a story.  the devil he has a plan.  a bag a\\\' bones in his pocket.  got anything you want.  no dust and no rocks.  the whole thing is over.  all these beauties in solid motion.  all those beauties gonna swallow you up.<BR><BR>hi hi hi hi hi.  one time too many.  too far to go.  i - we come to take you home.<BR><BR>and when they split those atoms.  it\\\'s hotter than the sun.  blood is a special substance.  they gonna pray for that man.<BR><BR>so wake up young lovers.  the whole thing is over.  watch out touch monkeys.  all that blood gonna swallow you whole.<BR><BR>hi hi hi hi hi.  what\\\'s that?  who\\\'s driving?  where we goin\\\'?  who knows?  i - we come to take you home.<BR><BR>how many people do you think I am?  pretend I am somebody else.  you can pretend I\\\'m an old millionaire.  a millionaire washing his hands.<BR><BR>rattle the bones, dreams that stick out.  a medical chart on the wall.  soft violence and hands touch your throat.  everyone wants to explode.<BR><BR>and when your hands get dirty.  nobody knows you at all.  don\\\'t have a window to slip out of.  lights on, nobody home.<BR><BR>click click - see ya later.  beta beta - no time to rest.  pika pika - risky business.  all that blood will never cover that mess.<BR><BR>hi hi hi hi hi.  so soft.  hard feelings.  what\\\'s that?  who\\\'s driving?  no tricks.  let\\\'s go.  i - we come to take you home.  i - we come to take you home.  hi hi hi hi hi.',1,1464,0,0,'24.92.189.219','en'),(21550,3724,'2004-10-27 05:46:33',195,'matt','i said \\\"please\\\".',1,22,0,0,'24.92.189.219','en'),(21551,3720,'2004-10-27 12:47:10',17,'austin','i am awake at 5:30AM because i was dreaming that the swinney family and the bush family were hanging out at crawford ranch.  we were all in the living room.  it was a christmas party or something.  it wasn\\\'t a nightmare.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ni was joking that bush sr should stop taking pictures with my camera because he was inadvertently taking pictures of classified materials.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nthis dream may be the result of my seeing a specific shirt while i was at the mall looking for a birthday present for somebody.  the shirt was a sort of forrest green cordoroy with tiny hunters, shotgun open over the arm, labrador following close.  i laughed and wondered who would wear such a thing.  bush would at crawford ranch.  i considered buying it as a joke.  but then realized that no on would think it was a joke, they would just make fun of it.  that wouldn\\\'t be laughing with me, so i didn\\\'t get it.  it would make a funny halloween cosume though.',1,950,0,0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(21552,3724,'2004-10-27 12:59:51',538,'arcy','Bottom line is the US shouldn\\\'t be in the middle east, and thank you for finally mentioning Vietnam. What about Panama? There is a patchwork quilt of military injustice that has smeared itself across the world and leads back to the US. This isn\\\'t new. This leader is no different, he is just an easier target. The way I look at it, it doesn\\\'t matter who gets into office, how many crutial decisions does Bush really make? He is a face to blame. He is not charismatic, he is not good-looking, he is religious, but in the bad southern, extremist sort of way. He is everything the US doesn\\\'t want to be reminded of, and so he will be voted out. Thats just how I see it from up here. There is more to deal with than just electing someone. Money is driving this war, and no one seems to have a problem with that. I guess the reality is that if we are complacent about our oil comsumption, then we can excuse ourselves from really being involved in how we get it. Maybe its not laziness so much as selfishness. If someone said tomorrow that we would be cutting off the middle east, drilling in our own beautiful Northern backyards to get this crud and that you would now be limited in the amount of driving you could do, would you really let him get out alive??? Ours is a society driven by oil, and oil based products how is voting Kerry in going to change any of that!',0,1376,0,0,'142.204.74.98','en'),(21553,3724,'2004-10-27 14:15:51',66,'Peter','<br><tt>if you havent seen <a href=\"http://boss.streamos.com/qtime/interscope/eminem/encore/video/mosh-rev/300_mosh-rev.mov\">this video</a> yet...</tt>',1,157,0,1,'156.145.58.57','en'),(21554,3724,'2004-10-27 14:18:37',66,'Peter','<br><tt><i>\"I just want to begin by saying that I think the appointed president of the United States right now stole the election and a incinerated American rights and freedoms\"</i><br><br>i totally agree. but what im wondering is that- if you think he stole it- why you also think its the voter\'s fault that he was \'elected\'? but whatever, thats just me nitpicking. <i>what i really wanted to say is this:</i><br><br>i agree with pretty much everything youre saying, and i can certainly empathize with your anger about it- im pissed as fuck too. speaking out is good- just maintain in the back of your mind an awareness that, despite the image of what you might percieve a \"stereotypical american\" to be, many of us are as furious as you... <i>more</i> furious even, as the blame is on <i>our</i> heads by proxy... and many of us are fighting to assure that we dont get four more years of this nightmare of fear, manipulation, lying, corruption and internationally conspicuous atrocity. fuck, the rage is even <a href=\"http://nodata.com/war/mosh.mov\">showing up on mtv</a> [hi, corporate capitalism]. we may not be a statistical majority, but were damned close to it, and i am 100% confident that we\'ll be enough to effect a change in 6 days... and though it may not be a change that will lead us straight into the promised land of political utopia, it sure as hell has more potential to led us <i>out</i> of our current political nightmare than any other choice we\'ve been offered. and realistically speaking, thats a substantial improvement. changing the world, as you know, takes time and happens through generations of decicive choices and actions. this is merely a single step- though a very prescient one to us living in today- to seek a better route for tomorrow.</tt>',1,341,0,0,'156.145.58.57','en'),(21557,3723,'2004-10-28 02:11:00',528,'oliver','in australia it\\\'s compulsory to vote. so a hell of a lot of careless voting goes on in these parts.',0,102,0,0,'129.96.120.254','en'),(21555,3723,'2004-10-27 17:30:34',538,'arcy','Did you know that women didn\\\'t get the right to vote in Quebec until 1940!',0,77,0,0,'142.204.16.10','en'),(21556,3724,'2004-10-27 18:06:36',492,'bmg','Dude, John Peel has fucking died, there are other things to think about other than the political situation of wherever...',1,121,0,0,'139.95.251.9','en'),(21558,3723,'2004-10-28 03:44:06',74,'jo','... is oliver ollee? if so, HI OLLEE!!!!!!!! if not, hey what\\\'s up random stranger.',0,86,528,0,'66.68.108.105','en'),(21559,3661,'2004-10-28 04:56:46',587,'ackman','Wow. This is good. Clarity. Understanding. Old judgements no longer cluttering the truth, but fodness remains. Feels like when I have the opportunity to stand on the other side of a fence I\\\'d hidden behind for too long (and maybe I\\\'ve had one toke too many and should shut the fuck up). Whatever. I liked it it alot. Thanks.',1,330,0,0,'67.119.12.24','en'),(21560,3720,'2004-10-28 05:43:44',175,'Paul G','<PRE>\r\n     !!!!        \r\n  !!!!!!!!       \r\n!!!!!!!!!!!  \\\\666/\r\n!!!  !!!!!!! /@ @\\\\\r\n      !!!!!! \\\\ x /\r\n      !!!!!!/ m  !m\r\n       !!!!/ __  |\r\n       !!!!|/  \\\\__\r\n        !!!\\\\______\\\\\r\n</PRE>',1,211,17,0,'131.156.159.149','en'),(21561,3708,'2004-10-28 06:16:35',587,'ackman','Nice, but you mught want to consider a coupla things next time:\r\n\r\na) Where ya wanna go?\r\nSeemed like you changed your mind a couple times as to what you wanted out of this bit. Also looks like you were in a hurry. Scribble when the feelin\\\' takes ya but maybe take a tiny, little bit o\\\' editorial time, eh?\r\n\r\nb) Pulp entertainment is fine - I\\\'d wager that your literary interest/addiction began comic books, ya? But, isn\\\'t it like, somewhat ironic that you find a place where one can write the same kinda parable/introspective character analysis/poetic/hero\\\'s journey/etc. that you\\\'ve been writing and hiding/burning for years and NOW you start writing harmless, fun pop-crap that...well, for the most part this stuff cost you little, if anything, emotionally and as a result you DON\\\'T come away from it with that that satisfying \\\"ahhh!\\\" like you used to get with the first toke on a cigarette/geez o\\\' the \\\"GoodLife\\\" in the morning. Relief. Release. \\\"Re\\\" - \\\"Lease\\\". Scribbling is The Respectable Jonze. But writing that other crap is like shooting sugar n\\\' K\\\'wha - hardly worth the expense and it don\\\'t feed the monkey. And when monkey don\\\'t eat...well, I don\\\'t need to tell You, do I? Go back to what you know. Vivesect your soul, spread out your thoughts for public examination like yesterday\\\'s used Kleenex. Humiliation?\r\nMaybe a little, but I wold think that you have at least built up some small increase in thickness of skin (if not a taste for a bit o\\\' the ol\\\' ultra-humiliation?) in this regard. Pick the scabs, damnit! Let the wound breath, and give the bacterial organisms a fighting chance - conflict is always more interesting than peace. \r\n\r\nc) if you\\\'re gonna write loaded, that previously mentioned editorial-time would probably be best utilized in a sober (less-loaded, at least) state. So, pull out and rework some of that old stuff. It\\\'s good; Iv\\\'e seen it. \r\n\r\nP.S. - I know that detoxing is hard but then, so was trying to put five bills up yer ar aweek while you were three months behind in rent. Stick with it bubbah. The \\\'worms in yer head\\\' can only eat so much. Ultimately, we\\\'ll starve \\\'em out (surprised they\\\'re not hungry already!-joking!), and grow some health mold or somethin\\\'. Now, get back to wrtiting (or reading)!\r\n',3,2349,0,0,'66.127.54.24','en'),(21562,3720,'2004-10-28 06:56:05',175,'Paul G','beer.  bush will win because most people would rather drink beer with him than kerry.\r\n<p>\r\nbush jr is like clinton or reagan: he smiles and makes people feel good.  kerry, gore, bush sr, mondale are all sort of creepy/dorky.  that is as deep as it runs.\r\n</p>',1,260,0,0,'131.156.159.149','en'),(21563,3724,'2004-10-28 09:24:53',261,'sine','it\\\'s going to work out fine, after Kerry and the \\\"reality-based\\\" people work out some of the pile of shit Bush has created in the past four years.\r\n\r\nIf Kerry doesn\\\'t win, i predict civil war II. the middle vs. the coasts.\r\n\r\nit\\\'ll be interesting to see the massive voter turnout on tuesday. it will happen. hopefully there won\\\'t be riot police blocking the minorities from voting.\r\n\r\nonion predicts another recount...but i have faith. i have to. i have absolute faith that Kerry will win this one.\r\n\r\n',0,520,0,0,'162.83.181.10','en'),(21564,2612,'2004-10-28 09:42:22',587,'ackman','I have had a recurring dream/nightmare since the age of four; pops up every now and then. I always play a four year old (\\\'play\\\' because I think of dreams as movies directed by my subconcious), and I\\\'m in what, by my standards at the time, is a large, vacant, unfurnished house. I\\\'m wandering from room to room and seem to have the understanding that a responsible adult is either outside or left me there for a bit. As I explore I periodically hear some other kids shoes echoing through the house as they run, but it doesn\\\'t seem to be a concern until I happen to catch a glimpse of the kid running down the hall outside one of the rooms I\\\'m in. The kid is wearing some kinda large, black, slightly bent conical Witch\\\'s hat. I call out to the kid and, when I receive no answer, it makes ther hair go up on the back of my neck. Despite my fear, I feel compelled to find and identify this other child. I continue to hear and catch glimpses of him and I keep finding myself in small rooms whilst he runs by in large hallways acdomadating increasingly large objects such as support columns and elaborate stairways ala Busby Berkely. I get progressively closer to catching the kid and finally, I catch up to him and he spins around giggling in a mad kinda way and his face is mine. I\\\'m absolutely terrified and scream bloody murder. This is typically when I wake up (apparently, I wake myself up with the screaming. It wasn\\\'t until I started sleeping with women that I found out that I scream in my sleep [rarely]). And, although it never occurs to me in my dream, when I was four I had demanded to dress up as a Witch for holloween (\\\'demanded\\\' as it was not exactly common for little boys to wanna be Witches in 1966) primarily based on my attraction to the conical black hats. Go figger.',0,1817,0,0,'66.127.54.150','en'),(21565,3724,'2004-10-28 22:43:03',175,'Paul G','i hope that you are right, and that i am wrong.',1,47,261,0,'206.68.117.82','en'),(21566,3715,'2004-10-29 00:31:55',83,'adamajah','<p>i like articles with pictures.</p>',1,37,17,0,'216.206.179.50','en'),(21567,3716,'2004-10-29 04:12:53',83,'adamajah','That was funny.  thnx!',2,22,0,0,'4.62.251.144','en'),(21568,3722,'2004-10-29 16:31:51',538,'arcy','thanks.',1,7,175,0,'142.204.16.10','en'),(21569,3714,'2004-10-30 07:05:19',189,'cyantist','it\\\'s too bad that you took that down.  it was rather nice.',3,61,0,0,'64.134.113.111','en'),(21570,3725,'2004-10-30 16:41:17',57,'weeb','elephant babies.\r\nelephant babies.\r\nelephant babies.',0,52,0,0,'66.92.219.22','en'),(21571,3645,'2004-11-01 17:56:00',538,'arcy','Curtains! what the hell. Meh, I guess I was tired writing this one.',0,67,0,0,'142.204.66.212','en'),(21572,3723,'2004-11-01 18:58:28',186,'ook','<p>for the last week, every time i walk past my usual polling station (i\\\'ve lived in this neighbourhood a lot), i have a mental reflex to remember to vote. i live in canada. we\\\'re not having an election.</p>',0,213,0,0,'207.6.176.119','en'),(21573,3725,'2004-11-01 20:48:46',90,'leonard','I hope you took pictures. ',1,26,0,0,'67.118.80.121','en'),(21574,2929,'2004-11-01 21:35:05',74,'jo','i can\\\'t believe it took me so long to comment on this post: all john irving novels are about prostitutes. he also writes about vienna a lot. vienna and whores, whores and vienna.\r\n\r\n(i have read every single john irving novel, no shit, even son of the circus and the fourth hand: you can\\\'t top hotel new hampshire. part of it takes place in a whorehouse in vienna.)\r\n\r\n(i guess a prayer for owen meany was pretty awesome, too.)',1,433,0,0,'216.142.229.132','en'),(21575,3725,'2004-11-01 22:23:17',93,'chiamattt','nope',0,4,0,0,'211.202.80.222','en'),(21576,3723,'2004-11-02 01:05:40',528,'oliver','1920??!!! shit. it was 1894 when women got the right to vote here in south australia. shit, 1920!! that\\\'s awful. \r\n\r\njo -  no i\\\'m not ollee.',0,146,0,0,'211.29.1.24','en'),(21577,3720,'2004-11-02 18:11:53',83,'adamajah','<p>That\\\'s weird.  Bush creeps me out and everyone I know, even republicans.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nIt\\\'s much more imaginable to be drinking a beer and throwing the pigskin around with Kerry than with the shifty, twitchy, awkward little man called Bush Jr.</p>',2,253,175,0,'216.206.179.50','en'),(21578,3720,'2004-11-03 00:33:03',175,'Paul G','dude.  granted i was drinking beer when i wrote this, and the more i drink the more bush makes sense, but here is the logic behind the seeming weirdness: in modern american history (since WWII) ten men have been elected into the white house.  six of those ten (60%) have come from the area between illinois and texas.  and every president who has served two full terms has come from that area.\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Truman, 48, missouri\r\n<li>Eisenhower, 52, 56, kansas\r\n<li>LBJ, 64, texas\r\n<li>Reagan, 80, 84, illinois\r\n<li>Clinton, 92, 96, arkansas\r\n<li>Bush Jr, 00, texas\r\n</ul>\r\ngiven that our population is in california, along the east coast, and around the great lakes, we ought to expect more presidents from those areas.  but it doesn\\\'t happen.  americans like people from the illinois-texas belt.  effete patricians from new england don\\\'t play well in our politics.\r\n<p>\r\nif kerry does win today, it\\\'s because he started wearing a ball cap and a coat that looks like a carhartt, while campaigning around milwaukee, detroit, and cleveland.  you know, he started doing <a href=\\\"http://www.cnsnews.com/storyimages/2003/John_Kerry_Hunt.jpg\\\">this</a> stuff.  junior bush is a nut-job for sure, but i believe that he likes to eat beef, watch nascar, cut things down with a chainsaw, and pray to jesus. <a href=\\\"http://www.whitehouse.gov/news/releases/2002/08/images/20020809-1_ranch8-515h.jpg\\\">this</a> is why the puppet-masters picked him to front their regime.  eh?\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\np.s. yes, i am angry at the democratic party for not running a \\\"real\\\" alternative.  kerry seems more like bush sr. than any other recent president.  blah!\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\np.p.s. here\\\'s to being wrong!\r\n</p>',1,1704,83,0,'64.107.88.142','en'),(21579,3724,'2004-11-04 12:27:39',93,'chiamattt','WHAT THE FUCK HAPPENED? ',1,24,0,0,'211.202.80.222','en'),(21580,3724,'2004-11-04 15:22:05',74,'jo','what happened is that you got <a href=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=3723#21545\\\">what you wanted</a>. four more years of dubya. i think that the voter turnout was over 60% for the first time since 1968 (don\\\'t know if there are final numbers on this yet) so we really CAME OUT to say WE HAVE OUR HEADS UP OUR COLLECTIVE ASSES.',3,353,0,0,'216.142.229.132','en'),(21581,3724,'2004-11-04 17:48:43',534,'griece','what the fuck happened? you know what the fuck happened. whats your point?  more than 50 percent of us turned out to vote, so you should be happy, right? as someone above said, we did what you were criticizing us for not doing in the past, didnt we? i for one am getting sort of tired of your whining and typecasting about all this. youre really preaching to the choir, dude, dont you get that? i think you arent sayin much aside from blaming us for shit we already knew well before you started going on and on about it, shit that isnt really our faults beyond the fact that were \"americans\" (which is pretty broad). i really dont mean any offense man, as you seem cool, but what the fuck is your point? ok, youre mad about bush. guess what? we are too. youre not saying anythign we havent thought/heard/felt before, dude. why dont you go visit the states that voted for bush and rant to them, ok? cause i betcha ten usd that no one on this site voted for bush, ok? california? australia? new york? canada? those are where most of us are from, and none of our states or countries voted for bush, ok? hell, even the stray texan and floridian here didnt even vote for bush. so youre preaching to the choir, dude, once again, and its sort of annoying, these ALL CAPS RANTS about how much fucking america fucking sucks and is fucking fuckity fuckfuck lazy fuckers fucking americans. we get it already. some dumbasses in america voted in a bum president. ok. its not the first time. i think its safe to say that half of americans suck. but half dont. and those of us that dont dont need to get lip from a fucking canadian about it. we already have to live with four more years of this shit, dont you understand that?<br><Br>chia, again, no offense man, but how about offering something a little more intellectual, constructive, thoughtful, factual or whatever or lay off the whining for a while, ok? otherwise, you start sounding like a troll.',5,1615,93,0,'130.219.136.216','en'),(21582,3724,'2004-11-04 17:55:25',534,'griece','haha, good one. <br><Br>\r\nchiamattt to jo : This is why I want Dubya to win another 4 years. Maybe when 100million americans lose their jobs, and out of that 100million, 50 million are drafted into a war in Iran the population will actually wake up and say \\\"shit, what happened?\\\"  \r\n ',5,290,74,0,'130.219.136.216','en'),(21583,3724,'2004-11-04 22:52:50',93,'chiamattt','yes. you are right. ',1,20,534,0,'211.202.80.222','en'),(21584,3724,'2004-11-05 22:50:05',175,'Paul G','it is of great value to be able to recognize one\\\'s\r\nenemies.\r\n<p>\r\nif you were vegan, you saw kerry kill small animals\r\nwith a shotgun.  if you were anti-war, you saw kerry\r\npromise to send more troops to iraq.  if you were\r\nlabor, you saw kerry married to a billionaire.  if\r\nyou wanted change, you saw kerry in government for\r\nover 20 years.  who was kerry?  why?\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nthis is a moment of clarity.  freedom supposes choice.\r\nchoice supposes recognition of the alternatives.\r\nallow for the possiblity that something good will\r\ncome from what is, and let go of the attachment to\r\nwhat you would have willed things to be.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nthere are things in the world that need you as they\r\nstruggle to come into being.\r\n</p>',1,730,66,0,'64.107.88.142','en'),(21585,3723,'2004-11-06 06:47:37',441,'yummy','<p>and then they come in...<br>\r\nwith their machines<br>\r\nand magic markers<br>\r\nand menthol breath</p>\r\n\r\n<p>here we go again, here we go again</p>\r\n\r\n<p>watching the suits<br>\r\nfucking our lives up</p>',4,203,0,0,'24.7.71.79','en'),(21586,3724,'2004-11-06 07:01:13',154,'ryan','GODS, GUNS AND FAGS -- that\\\'s what happened.',0,47,93,0,'216.99.197.120','en'),(21587,3724,'2004-11-06 07:01:58',154,'ryan','ryan meant to say GOD not GODS.  there is only one.  please don\\\'t arrest me.',0,79,154,0,'216.99.197.120','en'),(21588,2597,'2004-11-06 12:08:01',587,'ackman','In previous adventures, my roommates and I would go out on the veranda \\\"first thing in the morning \\\" (read: whatever time the first of us awakened - and then tortured the others into consciousness) dressed in our best bachelor bathrobes (read: blankets and the clothes you only wear when nothing else is clean)on saturday mornings and lip-sync to \\\"heard it through the grapevine\\\" or \\\"Respect\\\"; choose the classic Motown hit and we could fake knowing the lyrics. We had gotten lucky and were sharing a nice Victorian @ 22nd and south van ness, in our twenties and no one to medicate us. Anyways, a new donut shop opens two-blocks away and, in the midst of our morning scavenge for ciggies and coffee, we walk into this place on openning (coincidentally; we figured we\\\'d have to go all the way to Cala\\\'s for smokes). The guy tells us we\\\'re the very first customers and, if we show up within an hour of openning on saturdays, we get a free dozen of donuts! BET! Of course, we were there without fail every sat. prior to our \\\'gig\\\' on the veranda. Funny thing is, as we would shamble down to the donut shop for caffeine and sugar (breakfast of champion lip-sync\\\'ers) we would hear this rooster crowing somewhere to the west or south - we were never sure. We started listening for it. \\\'Tried triangulation - we were all lousy at geometry and we looked silly standing at the corners of intersections, donuts in mouth, hands cupped to ears, rotating our heads like wet-radar. We never found it. But after a few weeks, it occured to me that we typically got up pretty darned early in the morningespecially when we didn\\\'t have to. I discussed it with my \\\'mates and we discovered that there was alot about us, who we had become over time, that did not match the reputations we had with family and friends, which were much the same as the self-images we maintained subjectively (slacker, punk, funk junkie, irresponsible, etc.)so it seemed to us that we had actually \\\'grown\\\' in different ways - in good ways, mostly - and it hadn\\\'t been due to direct pressures from what-so-ever-authority we generally refused to respond to. I don\\\'t know what I\\\'m trying to say...chickens can be/are good.Or, I like hearing about gardening-like stuff in the City (I\\\'ve been in pseudo-voluntary exile to the south for almost ten years, and miss \\\'my\\\' sf)?\r\nYeah, that\\\'s the one (no sarcasm whatsoever)!\r\nGeez, I just looked at the screen and noticed I\\\'ve gone on long enough to whittle the right-hand slide bar to a nub. I apologize for the long windedness and unconciously working out my epiphaniac (?) memories in your space. Anyways, I liked this - your post that is. Makes me remember a time when I allowed myself to be ruled by a philosophy borrowed and cobbled out of the writings of the likes of Aimee Mann, Elvis C., S. Vega, Michael Penn, etc. I miss that. Think I\\\'ll pick it up again. Thanks Weeb.\r\n\r\nP.S- And, uh...I\\\'ll spew a bit less in the future.\r\n\r\nHope yer all havin\\\' a great saturday.\r\nP.P.S.- yeah, I know this will go unread, but that ain\\\'t what it\\\'s for fer me sometimes. Whatever good luck I can wish you all, you have.\r\nAchilles',1,3210,0,0,'66.127.54.196','en'),(21589,3731,'2004-11-10 23:37:37',175,'Paul G','artful, economic, and engaging - like all of your stuff.  but i see a skunk\\\'s head peeking out from under a big croissant, not a bird.',1,137,0,0,'131.156.159.180','en'),(21590,3731,'2004-11-11 03:40:27',370,'seanthecon','devil horns or jabba the hut\\\'s tail? personlly i can\\\'t stop looking at the naked chick. overall, probably the best place to smoke crack in the world.',6,155,0,0,'24.85.233.195','en'),(21591,3731,'2004-11-12 02:46:12',57,'weeb','that\\\'s a stencil of a steaming pile of butt birth.\r\n<br><br>\r\nnice.',0,70,0,0,'66.92.219.22','en'),(21592,3731,'2004-11-12 08:38:14',66,'sine','c\\\'est poo-poos!',0,18,0,0,'141.155.108.105','en'),(21593,3675,'2004-11-13 02:48:00',587,'ackman','Geez! This is embarrassing. I just read your article and it resonated SO much with me, in me, with something gone by for so long that it swept me up and -  selfish, self-centered asshole that I am, I went on about MY experience, MY hole-in-the-heart and...well, I really only just wanted to say that, in regard to this article - I know this. I feel this. I carry this too. And thank you for something that got a rise outta me. Sometimes, lately, I\\\'m a little-too-night-of-the-living-dead-extra-like, ya know-wud-I-meen? Anyways, I guess I\\\'ll post that other crap in my area. Thanks again, it\\\'s GOOD.\r\n\r\n ',1,613,0,0,'67.119.12.128','en'),(21594,3733,'2004-11-14 05:31:02',83,'adamajah','Of all the things I\\\'ve heard through walls from freak-neighbors, that\\\'s one thing I wouldn\\\'t mind.  Then again, I\\\'m drunk right now because McSwinney left a bottle of \\\'cragginmore\\\' in my kitchen.',2,213,0,0,'4.43.160.212','en'),(21595,3733,'2004-11-15 03:19:22',175,'Paul G','Tasting Note:\r\n<a href=\\\"http://www2.adhoc.net/scubi/whisky/scotch/malts/Gragganm.htm\\\">Firm body, malty smoky finish</a>\r\n?',1,128,83,0,'206.68.117.82','en'),(21596,3733,'2004-11-15 15:01:09',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i used to live in an old apartment in harlem where next-door resided a couple who seemed to perpetually exist in a tenuous balance between fighting and fucking... one would often lead to the other, then the other again, in the space of an afternoon. ultimately, it was more amusing than disturbing.</tt>',1,311,0,0,'130.219.136.216','en'),(21597,3734,'2004-11-15 18:31:33',587,'ackman','OMG! I wonder if I\\\'ll ever learn to a)stop long enough to edit or b) stop long enough to consider the rammifications of trying to write loaded/post-loaded-sleep-deprived. Anyways, thanks fer not tossing me out on me ear, an\\\' if\\\'n y\\\'all haven\\\'t yet, read Tyler\\\'s post.\r\nAchilles',4,295,0,0,'67.122.209.250','en'),(21598,3734,'2004-11-15 20:02:13',195,'matt','your name\\\'s achilles?<BR><BR>are you greek?<BR>are you hot?<BR>are you a little bit gay?',1,91,0,0,'24.92.189.219','en'),(21599,2769,'2004-11-16 03:33:06',486,'procyon','i was at the dorm laundromat the other day and a guy talked to me for a while about the fact that i am a girl but am currently working as a football referee. \\\"breakin\\\' down stereotypes there,\\\" he said. then as he left he said something like \\\"wouldn\\\'t it be a great story to tell people that we met doing laundry?\\\" i thought of this swintry.',2,358,0,0,'128.135.192.136','en'),(21600,3733,'2004-11-16 08:48:10',17,'anon','\\\'Damajah, STAY OUT OF MY 12 YEAR!\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nBACK OFF MY SCOTCH, GERMANOS!\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ni enjoy listening to neighbors get it on.  it is so scandilous.  i had a neighbor in my first college coop that was a screamer.  she would go on and on.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nthen flyinjlo my roommate in SF recently had this wasteoid of a girlfriend who would get drunk out of her mind.  i had to carry her out of a couple cars for flyinjlo.  he couldnt lift her himself.  he was usually trashed too.  and somehow, someway, she couldnt get her face out of the floorboard of a taxi cab, but yet she could get her face on his ... and start screaming.  i was amused for a while, but ultimately i wanted to go back to sleep.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nanother girlfriend i had... neither one of us made much noise, but when you live in a loft with 3 other people and her bedroom has no wall, only curtains, well...  they were bount to hear some sloshing around.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nOMG, i may have said too much.  i\\\'m in a drought.  most of my days are dedicated to working for beautiful women.  life sucks.',1,1059,83,0,'68.6.211.134','en');
INSERT INTO `comments` VALUES (21601,3733,'2004-11-16 08:49:09',17,'austin','like i like my women.... <TT>Firm body, malty smoky finish</TT>',1,63,175,0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(21602,3733,'2004-11-16 13:51:58',74,'jo','sloshing',0,8,0,0,'66.68.108.105','en'),(21603,3733,'2004-11-16 13:54:36',74,'jo','man, in austin, tx, rents are so good, hardly anyone i know has a roommate. i completely forgot about \\\"we have to be quiet because of your roommate\\\" sex. awww fuck. i am going to miss you, 600 sq. foot 1 bdrm for $495. you have treated me well these last 2 years.',0,269,0,0,'66.68.108.105','en'),(21604,3735,'2004-11-16 17:59:03',17,'austin','curled toes #1.',1,15,0,0,'63.80.97.254','en'),(21605,3733,'2004-11-16 19:29:42',66,'Peter','<br><tt>$495?! thats not <i>rent</i>, thats a night out!</tt>',1,61,74,0,'130.219.136.216','en'),(21606,3733,'2004-11-16 20:37:36',486,'procyon','\r\nprocyon: the question is what kind of odds you have of your friend\\\'s neighbors knowing who you are\r\nmy friend brian: know who you are how?\r\nbrian: by your groans?\r\nbrian: recognize you accross campus?\r\nprocyon: no, when you walk out in the morning\r\nprocyon: though i do groan loudly on the quads from time to time\r\nprocyon: i have to\r\nprocyon: otherwise i\\\'d be completely out of practice\r\nbrian: did you hear the Rockwell story?\r\nprocyon: no\r\nbrian: abbreviated version: he has the top bunk\r\nbrian: banged this chick\r\nbrian: pipe is by bunk\r\nbrian: pipe travels length of the hall\r\nprocyon: oh no\r\nprocyon: oh no\r\nbrian: entire floor hears girl\r\nbrian: Rockwell becomes a legend\r\nbrian: that kid is the Bond of WJ\r\nbrian: oh well\r\nbrian: I\\\'m off to bed\r\nprocyon: okay, have fun\r\nbrian: soon you\\\'ll be a legend in your dorm\r\nprocyon: hahahaha\r\nprocyon: it doesn\\\'t work that way for girls\r\nprocyon: i\\\'d just be a ho\r\nbrian: then you can make your partner into a legend\r\nprocyon: fair enough',2,1008,0,0,'128.135.192.136','en'),(21607,3733,'2004-11-16 20:38:19',486,'procyon','oh no, i forgot to put < b r > \\\'s in..',5,41,0,0,'128.135.192.136','en'),(21608,3733,'2004-11-16 22:29:12',175,'Paul G','some time after we split, i picked up my ex.  it was mid-summer, hot, and as we drove, we bounced up-and-down on the vinyl bench-seat of my truck.  she said it made her horny: the heat, the scent of us in the same small space, and the movement, all together.  bouncybouncy.  \\\"let\\\'s get a room,\\\" she said.\r\n<p>\r\nit was a dirty little motel, with a big dirty bed.  a mirror hung overhead.  there was the usual porn-per-view on the tv, and an unusual \\\"shelf\\\" at the other end of the room.  the shelf was carpeted; the carpet was greasy.  and then it started: the room next door was occupied by one Speedy Gonzalez who kept the headboard of his bed at red-line, crashing into the wall between us.  bambambam.  how the cheap paneling withstood the onslaught is beyond me.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nto this day i am convinced that the chinese mobsters who ran the motel had cameras behind the mirrors.  and if i ever go to peking i expect people to blush when they see me for the second time, \\\"ahhh, mistah juicy!\\\"\r\n</p>      ',1,1027,0,0,'64.107.88.142','en'),(21609,3733,'2004-11-16 22:54:36',175,'Paul G','show me the personal when you finish it: seeking youthful & petite blonde female with firm body, malty smoky finish, and curled toes.  knowledge of bad american food and good scotch whiskey required.  likes to \\\"ride bitch\\\" a plus.',1,236,17,0,'64.107.88.142','en'),(21610,3733,'2004-11-17 14:39:30',66,'Peter','<br><tt><i>mistah juicy</i></tt>',1,32,175,0,'130.219.136.216','en'),(21611,3733,'2004-11-19 07:54:44',195,'matt','let\\\'s look at this from another perspective:<BR><BR>have you seen her?  is she hot?  introduce yourself.  she might like you better than the guy she\\\'s fucking.<BR><BR>she sounds like a good time charlita.  i\\\'d totally go for it.',1,237,0,0,'24.92.189.219','en'),(21612,3736,'2004-11-19 18:57:53',17,'austin','sometimes a poem is all you got.',1,32,0,0,'63.80.97.254','en'),(21613,3736,'2004-11-19 19:01:22',66,'Peter','<br><tt>...and sometimes, its those stale crackers sitting on top of the fridge.</tt>',1,85,17,0,'130.219.136.216','en'),(21614,3736,'2004-11-19 22:28:27',175,'Paul G','something about the malleability of appearance..the need, pressure, or demand to change it...and an ethical quandry...with a human-animal analogy.  hmmm.  yay for more writing. ',1,177,0,0,'64.107.88.142','en'),(21615,3735,'2004-11-19 22:32:58',175,'Paul G','a romance/poetry/eros series...',1,31,0,0,'64.107.88.142','en'),(21616,3715,'2005-05-20 22:57:31',231,'alana','<img src=\\\"http://logy.org/~alana/melbs.jpg\\\">\r\n\r\nalana jonze, melbourne, australia.',3,88,0,3,'150.101.148.99','en'),(21617,3735,'2004-11-21 00:05:37',234,'etienne','i love these kinds of descriptions.',1,35,0,0,'222.152.45.27','en'),(21618,3569,'2004-11-21 00:14:35',234,'etienne','yes, that movie fucked with me.  it was hard to watch and beautiful to watch.',1,77,508,0,'222.152.45.27','en'),(21619,3737,'2004-11-22 16:59:18',66,'Peter','<br><tt>is it at all telling that the id of this entry is 3737? is it possible that 3737 is more powerful than 1111? ph33r!</tt>',1,128,0,0,'130.219.136.216','en'),(21620,3737,'2004-11-22 17:02:39',82,'simon','my ex girlfriend\\\'s birthday is 11/11/71. i always thought that was a little odd.',0,83,0,0,'209.21.99.118','en'),(21621,3737,'2004-11-22 17:06:20',66,'Peter','<br><tt>ha. you think thats odd? check <A href=\\\"http://www.nvisible.com/1111/1111intro.html\\\">this</a> out...</tt>',1,119,82,0,'130.219.136.216','en'),(21622,3737,'2004-11-22 17:09:39',124,'gus','My birthdate: 7/7/71 @ 11:11 AM. ',0,33,0,0,'67.101.113.170','en'),(21623,3734,'2004-11-22 22:47:48',587,'ackman','The name is Greek, but I\\\'m told I am quite French.\r\nAt my age/condition (read: minimal efforts towards maintenance) I\\\'m only hot when dehydrated.\r\nA little bit gay? I\\\'m sure we\\\'re ALL a little bit gay as well as we are all a little bit straight. I guess in my case it\\\'s like a 2mm Allen wrench - I\\\'m sure there\\\'s one in the tool case somewhere, just can\\\'t say I\\\'ve seen it.',1,400,195,0,'66.127.54.127','en'),(21624,3734,'2004-11-22 22:51:45',587,'ackman','Oops! Skipped the first question, the answer to which is: Yes!',1,62,195,0,'66.127.54.127','en'),(21625,3734,'2004-11-23 03:01:28',175,'Paul G','the last line of your first paragraph:\r\n<br>\r\n\\\"PRESTO! He\\\'s made you all disappear!\\\"\r\n<br>\r\nand the last line of my last parapraph:\r\n<br>\r\n<a href=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=2826\\\">\\\"Presto: I wish that you would appear, again.\\\"</a>\r\n<br>\r\nadd greek-french, belmont, epiphanic, long-winded, etc.\r\n<p>\r\nas poor as our justice system is, it has some worthy qualities: the right to notice of the charges against you; the right to confront and cross-examine your accuser in a public court; the right to present a defense of your own; etc..  through such a process, the truth is supposed to be most likely to appear.  i like the truth.  and without such rights, we are left like jospeh k. in kafka\\\'s <i>trial</i>.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nthis is why, for me, it is best to say what i have to say in my own name, directly.  the thing that i enjoyed most about the net in the past was that it allowed one to exchange words/pictures with people in other places - people with different values, backgrounds, etc.  it presupposed a certain level of trust.  and who really cared if you knew the people on-line, or would ever meet them?  the idea was to move beyone what was familiar to you, and grow from the experience.  who cared how \\\'professional\\\' their presentation was?  that\\\'s not the point.  and what\\\'s up with the homogenization, competition, falseness, and everything else that seems to characterize the current state of affairs? it\\\'s like television, or politics. *destabilizing*\r\n</p>',4,1531,587,0,'206.68.117.82','en'),(21626,3737,'2004-11-23 06:15:18',195,'matt','in the late \\\'70s, there was briefly an 11:11 club in athens.  it opened every night at 11:11.  it was basically an unlicensed bar.  at 256 w. clayton street.  later home to the third and fifth incarnations of the 40 watt club.',1,229,0,0,'24.92.189.219','en'),(21627,3737,'2004-11-23 17:50:21',17,'austin','<H1>2626</H1>',1,13,66,0,'63.80.97.254','en'),(21628,3296,'2004-11-24 19:54:00',195,'matt','all three of these are good alone, and then in all three, a woman figures prominently.  very nice.',1,98,0,0,'24.92.189.219','en'),(21629,3734,'2004-11-26 05:33:45',17,'austin','Paul Germanos, as usual i am too drunk to read your words.  I scanned them, though.  Franz Kafka?  how dare you get high brow on this rat hole?',6,143,175,0,'209.30.160.144','en'),(21630,3737,'2004-11-27 10:06:53',231,'alana','<p>an 11:11 club in athens?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>i\\\'ve been spiritually/psychically drawn to athens, ga from the age of 3. the older  i get, the more it all makes sense to me.</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n',1,178,0,0,'150.101.147.73','en'),(21631,3737,'2004-11-27 20:17:22',195,'matt','i\\\'ve lived in many cities in florida and mexico and also athens.  i think athens might be my favorite outside of brooksville.  it has that energy unique to college towns, but it beats the hell out of gainesville (the only other one i\\\'ve lived in) because it\\\'s small, all the townies know each other, and it\\\'s a cultural mecca.  where else is it very common to see rock stars buying condoms, drinking beer, eating pizza, or watching shows in the same places you do?<BR><BR>it really is magical.  it\\\'s a place of vast possibility.  i felt at home after my first few days.  i\\\'d like to live there again someday.  if not full-time, at least have a house there.  the only drawback for me is that it has more bars per capita than any other place i\\\'ve lived.  downtown (adjacent to the university) is saturated with them.',1,835,0,0,'24.92.185.89','en'),(21632,3735,'2004-11-28 15:33:35',477,'jehannum','wow, nice. i had a dream the night before last, about something that i can\\\'t quite remember. when i woke up, i felt a lot like this before i realised i was alone. for some reason i still felt all warm and fuzzy, like i wasn\\\'t really alone in the world and everything would be okay.',1,287,0,0,'144.136.74.116','en'),(21633,3738,'2004-11-29 20:46:43',195,'matt','keep looking up.  we\\\'re all rooting for you.  and praying for you.<BR><BR>something i like to tell myself when things are good or bad is that everything happens for a reason.  even if it isn\\\'t apparent until much later.',1,225,0,0,'24.92.185.89','en'),(21634,3738,'2004-11-30 05:19:39',67,'trouble','the bravery you\\\'ve shown here is inspiring.  i can only imagine what the full read must be like.  \r\n\r\ni\\\'ll be thinking of you.',2,132,0,0,'24.225.139.86','en'),(21635,3724,'2004-11-30 11:52:24',615,'idealogue','brilliant stuff, chia. \r\n\r\n\\\"American politics and American civil society has been corrupt since before pearl harbor.\\\" \r\n\r\nthe governments of any powerful or wealthy country throughout history have been corrupt. big shocker. tell me more, please. what\\\'s this? the most powerful country in the world is seeking to expand its power and assets? i never saw this coming.\r\n \r\n\\\"If Corporate Capitalism is what you are talking about then yes, the United States has proved itself. But if you are talking about education, health care, the government, and laws regarding narcotics, immigration and taxation, then you my friend are clearly mistaken\\\"\r\n\r\neducation? health care? in the private sector the united states has the best schools and doctors in the world. nowhere else even comes close. who you think should have access to them really depends on what your perspective of a good government is. nice facist world view. by the way, more americans have health insurance than you think and more \\\"underprivladged americans\\\" have grants to go to these good schools than you think. \r\n\r\nbefore you blame lazy americans, religious zealots and gun nuts for george bush, maybe you should realize that these elections are about as significant as flipping a coin to pick a new king. that\\\'s why no one participates really. john kerry wasn\\\'t really going to change anything. \r\n\r\nif you are opposed to what is shaping up to be absolute united states world domination, maybe you should blame the countries who you are putting on a pedestal. they\\\'re the ones not doing anything about it other than basically saying \\\"hey, thats bad\\\". maybe that\\\'s because they all have their fingers deep in the pie too. when hitler got out of control did countries who were opposed to him just sit on their asses like this?',6,1822,0,0,'65.49.100.30','en'),(21636,3724,'2004-11-30 21:19:23',195,'matt','oh, jesus christ, please don\\\'t start this up again.<BR><BR>let\\\'s move on.',1,79,0,0,'24.92.185.89','en'),(21637,3724,'2004-12-01 17:49:37',17,'austin','BRING IT!',1,9,0,0,'63.80.97.254','en'),(21638,3724,'2004-12-01 23:00:06',66,'Peter','<br><hr><tt>OH, ITS ALREADY BEEN BROUGHTEN!</tt><hr>',1,40,17,0,'162.83.133.151','en'),(21639,3724,'2004-12-02 01:58:07',57,'weeb','i smell troll butt',1,18,0,0,'66.92.219.22','en'),(21640,3637,'2004-12-04 05:35:27',587,'ackman','I was already starting to feel like the village idiot \\\'round here (okay, okay. \\\'Apprentice\\\' Village Idiot. But I gotta be getting close to Journeyman), but now I\\\'m REALLY confused. Gimme a bit to rub my few remaining nuerons together, an\\\' when I get a spark I\\\'ll formulate the question.\r\n',1,306,0,0,'67.117.130.45','en'),(21641,3637,'2004-12-04 06:33:05',66,'Peter','<br><tt>hi ackman, ive been around here a tad and i dont really know you. tell us about yourself.<br><br>i wanted to comment and say that this morning, the second i woke up, the words \\\"milton fazoo\\\" came into mind, and i couldnt realize why. now i know where that name was seeded from. strange how weird random bitz float thru your mind sometimes.<br><Br>but then again, i once dremt of <a href=\\\"http://rhodamine.org/blog/index.php?p=31\\\">coming on a manatee for the sake of an old woman\\\'s longevity</a>, so who knows these days?</tt> ',1,549,587,0,'162.83.168.187','en'),(21642,3637,'2004-12-04 11:28:05',587,'achilles','Hi, Peter.\r\nI\\\'m actually gonna think fer a little bit about how to answer yer question. An author friend of mine once told me \\\"Succinctness is the essence of good writing\\\", and I\\\'ve a tendency to long-windedness - and not the good kind (Bad writer! No biscuit!). As to Milton Fazzo, isn\\\'t that the psuedonym of one Boston Swinburne (or was it \\\'Austin? ;)). Anyways, I\\\'ll \\\'come down\\\' a bit and put a little something here - wherever \\\'here\\\' is. \\\'Wasn\\\'t the easiest thing finding this article. Bye for the moment!\r\n',1,551,66,0,'66.127.53.95','en'),(21643,3741,'2004-12-06 18:58:42',195,'matt','see, this is why i\\\'m never going to do interviews when i get famous.  stupid bullshit.  has nothing to do with doing the job.',1,128,0,0,'24.92.185.89','en'),(21644,3741,'2004-12-06 19:59:41',66,'Peter','<br><Tt>...id not bring <i>myself</i>, cause you know they say that no other known planets are capable of sustaining human life. why bother going if youre just gonna die once you get there?</tt>',1,194,0,0,'130.219.136.216','en'),(21645,3741,'2004-12-06 23:41:49',534,'griece','what teh fuck is co-op? were not all privvy to your shorthand, you know.',1,72,0,0,'162.83.168.187','en'),(21646,3741,'2004-12-07 02:48:08',538,'arcy','many sorries, its work term for school. i.e. they help you find summer jobs in your field that might lead to full time work. It never does but it generally pays relatively high so what the hell...',2,196,534,0,'69.195.31.216','en'),(21647,3734,'2004-12-07 04:39:17',175,'Paul G','<p>\r\n<a href=\\\"http://faculty.ncwc.edu/toconnor/428/428lect16.htm\\\">\\\"List of Antisocial Personality Disorder Traits</a>: \r\n<br>\r\nSense of entitlement; Unremorseful; Apathetic to others; Unconscionable behavior; Blameful of others; Manipulative and conning; Affectively cold; Disparate understanding; Socially irresponsible; Disregardful of obligations; Nonconforming to norms; Irresponsible.\\\" \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\n\\\"<b>Sociopathy</b> is chiefly characterized by something wrong with the person\\\'s conscience. They either don\\\'t have one, it\\\'s full of holes like Swiss cheese, or they are somehow able to completely neutralize or negate any sense of conscience or future time perspective. Sociopaths only care about fulfilling their own needs and desires - selfishness and egocentricity to the extreme. Everything and everybody else is mentally twisted around in their minds as objects to be used in fulfilling their own needs and desires.\\\" \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\n\\\"<b>Psychopathy</b> is a concept subject to much debate, but is usually defined as a constellation of affective, interpersonal, and behavioral characteristics including egocentricity; impulsivity; irresponsibility; shallow emotions; lack of empathy, guilt, or remorse; pathological lying; manipulativeness; and the persistent violation of social norms and expectations (Cleckley 1976; Hare 1993). The crimes of psychopaths are usually stone-cold, remorseless killings for no apparent reason. They cold-bloodedly take what they want and do as they please without the slightest sense of guilt or regret. In many ways, they are natural-born intraspecies predators who satisfy their lust for power and control by charm, manipulation, intimidation, and violence.\\\"\r\n</p>',1,1737,17,0,'206.68.117.82','en'),(21648,3741,'2004-12-07 04:53:06',565,'perogie','I wouldn\\\'t (purposefully) bring two things:\r\n\r\n1. Parades\r\n2. Disney\r\n\r\nBoth of these things are on my \\\"Things That Exist, But Shouldn\\\'t\\\" list.\r\n\r\nYou don\\\'t have to agree with me.  But my reason is that parades and Disney are just two of the things that you\\\'re supposed to love when you\\\'re a kid.  Your parents take you to see parades and Disney movies and theme parks.  But for all of the build up, with them asking you over and again how excited you are that you\\\'re about to see a parade, or Disney (or even a Disney parade), they\\\'re really not worth all the hype.\r\n\r\nI\\\'ve doubtless offended someone here.',0,637,0,0,'66.28.241.17','en'),(21649,3739,'2004-12-07 04:57:07',565,'perogie','I really liked this.  It even rhymes.\r\n\r\n',0,41,0,0,'66.28.241.17','en'),(21650,3734,'2004-12-07 06:15:33',195,'matt','is there something going on that the rest of us don\\\'t know about?  should we have a symposium or something?',1,110,0,0,'24.92.185.89','en'),(21651,3742,'2004-12-07 06:44:21',195,'matt','joanna vaught, my dear, if this ever sees fruition, you\\\'re getting a slice.<BR><BR>wow.  looking back over this, i come across as a real sophisticate, don\\\'t i?<BR><BR>also, anybody at all, please don\\\'t feel you need to contact him and enlighten him as to what a freak i am.  because i\\\'m not.  i\\\'m a good person.  i\\\'m a good man.  besides, i referred him to my work on here a long time ago.  he\\\'s been briefed.  he knows that my work here is, well... he knows about it.  moreso than.<BR><BR>in hollywood, they don\\\'t care what you do in the bedroom as long as you bring the goods to the table.  i just thought you guys would find this interesting.  i know you\\\'re on my side.',1,699,0,0,'24.92.185.89','en'),(21652,3443,'2004-12-07 17:10:30',618,'skwooshi1','I just found your writings on accident which I think is the case with most treasures.  I see you haven\\\'t written for some time and I hope you have not forgotten this space as I would love to hear more.  Life is definitely weird enough without fiction.  I have printed up your spiritual writings as I find that they especially suit my mood these days.  Would love to hear more.\r\n',0,381,0,0,'216.161.222.14','en'),(21653,3743,'2004-12-07 19:15:34',66,'Peter','<br><tt>sho ever said schitzo was bad? c\\\'mon, <i>crazy</i> is the spice of life!</tt>',1,88,0,0,'130.219.136.216','en'),(21654,3742,'2004-12-07 19:16:34',66,'Peter','<br><tt>nice. though, the title makes me think of the dumb \\\"captain\\\'s log\\\" jokes, for some reason...</tt>',1,114,0,0,'130.219.136.216','en'),(21655,3741,'2004-12-07 19:19:38',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i like parades. i used to love watching them march the elephants through downtown, trunk-to-tail and such. my hometown had a wicked veterans day parade, too, complete with tanks and jeeps and shit. it was alot of fun.</tt>',1,223,565,0,'130.219.136.216','en'),(21656,3742,'2004-12-07 22:08:33',74,'jo','man, i love me the SHIT out of some chris onstad.\r\n\r\nwhy would i get a slice? am i how you found out about achewood?\r\n\r\nif an achewood movie ever happened, i would never ever stop watching it. i would watch it on a loop.',1,220,195,0,'216.142.229.132','en'),(21657,3742,'2004-12-07 22:14:09',74,'jo','also, matt, i think he\\\'s the most like roast beef, not teodor. you have to be a lot like roast beef to think like roast beef. or maybe he used to be like roast beef and then he find the right anti-anxiety meds.<BR>\r\none time i wrote him and told him that roast beef reminded me so much of my friend ______ and he wrote back and ended the email with: \\\"tell your friend _____ that i said good luck.\\\"<BR>\r\nonstad forever. ',1,428,195,0,'216.142.229.132','en'),(21658,3742,'2004-12-07 22:32:38',195,'matt','yeah, you\\\'re how i found out about achewood.  you\\\'re due something.',1,73,74,0,'24.92.185.89','en'),(21659,3734,'2004-12-08 04:33:54',175,'Paul G','during the past year i\\\'ve written in only one place: here.  and i\\\'ve read only three things on a regular\r\nbasis: swinney, elly, and citynoise.  that\\\'s it.  all other ties have been cut.  yet...  \r\n<p>\r\n(1) during the past month or two, someone has been screwing with me.  here, someone has read what i\\\'ve written, and then used unique words and phrases of mine, in their own articles, without acknowledging what they\\\'ve borrowed.  plagiarism.\r\n<br>\r\n(2) so too, that person has mixed some truth with falsehood, for the purpose of\r\ndamaging my character in the previously mentioned articles.  libel.\r\n<br>\r\n(3) a uchicago.edu address has appeared in the stats (nov).\r\n<br>\r\n(4) on citynoise, someone has posted pictures of things that i\\\'ve posted pictures of - as if they wanted to best me in photography there, as in writing, here.\r\n<br>\r\n(5) during this same (2 month) period of time, i\\\'ve been the victim of identity theft, and fraud.  a line has been crossed.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nin the years that i\\\'ve been on-line, i\\\'ve had \\\"problems\\\" with only one person.  that person was employed doing web work for the uchicago press.  that person was a digital photographer, and their pics looked like those on citynoise, now.  that person wrote lies about me, on-line, like the lies here.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nnow, i\\\'ve been honest, and open, about who i am, and what i believe.  everyone has been able to interact with me: to question, to dialogue.  but, instead, these other things have happened.  if i ever became involved with anyone in \\\"real life,\\\" it was because i found them to be attractive, intelligent and interesting. i would, still, want them to be happy, no matter who they were with. and i don\\\'t want to throw their personal struggles out in public.  but if someone wanted my attention, or felt the need to tell me something, why not write to me, or have a conversation?\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nmaybe this is all a coincidence?  someone else screwing with me?  what does this look like to you?  you tell me.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\n<a href=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=3743#21653\\\">and then this...</a>\r\n</p>',1,2146,195,0,'206.68.117.82','en'),(21660,3734,'2004-12-08 04:56:31',66,'Peter','<br><tt>why did you link to my comment? i hope youre not saying im schitzo ;)</br><br>email me the details of whats concerning you on citynoise, and ill make sure it gets sorted. i have lots of nice info about all the users there...</tt> ',1,231,175,0,'162.83.168.187','en'),(21661,3734,'2004-12-08 05:15:39',74,'jo','...<BR>\r\n...<BR>\r\nseriously?',0,28,175,0,'66.68.108.105','en'),(21662,3741,'2004-12-08 05:51:27',565,'perogie','Maybe I should add \\\"generalizations\\\" to my \\\"things that exist, but shouldn\\\'t list,\\\" because a military parade would\\\'ve floated my boat quite nicely when I was a little kid.\r\n\r\nBut I think that\\\'s a generalization, too, and now I\\\'m torn.\r\n',0,261,66,0,'66.28.241.17','en'),(21663,3743,'2004-12-08 19:52:50',618,'skwooshi1','easy for you to say, you haven\\\'t been dealing with him for over 8 years off and on and off and on.  Time to break the cycle i think.\r\n',1,137,0,0,'216.161.222.14','en'),(21664,3743,'2004-12-08 20:06:54',66,'Peter','<br><tt>sure, i havent had to deal with your particular wacko, but i think its fair to say everyone\'s had an extended run-in with such a person in their life, though some have turned out better than others... but since its such a problem for you- and you cant go back in time- better to change it now than wait another 8 years, yeah?</tt>',1,197,618,0,'130.219.136.217','en'),(21665,3734,'2004-12-09 04:17:33',175,'Paul G','something weird began around sept/oct.  i gave my cell # to lit thousands of customers in the taxi, and i never had a problem - until then.  at that point i started getting crank calls.  the earliest evidence of fraud that i have, so far, dates to that time period too.  it\\\'s not something that i\\\'m imagining, because i\\\'ve got the statements and phone bills, and i\\\'ve had to spend the last three days dealing with the creditors, credit bureaus, police, etc.  and it\\\'s not over yet.  if the tone of my writing has been \\\'irked\\\' this is why.  sigh.  but for these events in my \\\'real life\\\' i wouldn\\\'t have paid attention to anything on-line.  i got rid of my isp about a year ago, and i\\\'ve only used my cards with reputable merchants.  i\\\'ve pretty much kept to myself, taking care of work, school, and mom.  and i\\\'ve done my stuff my way.  so i\\\'ve got to wonder what\\\'s up, eh?',1,917,74,0,'206.68.117.82','en'),(21666,3743,'2004-12-09 15:34:08',618,'skwooshi1','Exactly where I\\\'m at dude.  Right now I\\\'m working on killing the dream instead of chasing it....it isn\\\'t as easy as everyone keeps telling me it should be.  I shouldn\\\'t talk anyway, it\\\'s not like I\\\'m all there myself....I just can\\\'t seem to live in his world, but I like it enough to keep visiting for short vacations.',0,339,66,0,'216.161.222.14','en'),(21667,3743,'2004-12-09 16:13:35',66,'Peter','<br><tt>word. but sometimes its just easier to make a clean break when youre struggling with the idea. i had a similar game going on for 6 years or so, and was really relieved to have ended it, though it took me a good while to bounce back. after a little mourning anda rebuilding myself, i became a new man, and watched my life get about 1000x better, for what its worth. change can be a good impetus, sometimes :) good luck with it...</tt>',1,441,0,0,'130.219.136.217','en'),(21668,3707,'2004-12-09 19:33:03',239,'Poonlarp','yes.',6,4,0,0,'130.219.136.217','en'),(21669,3557,'2004-12-09 19:33:46',239,'Poonlarp','to give it a taste test. fuck grocery stores.',6,45,0,0,'130.219.136.217','en'),(21670,3536,'2004-12-09 19:34:18',239,'Poonlarp','then they all died. the end.',6,28,0,0,'130.219.136.217','en'),(21671,3526,'2004-12-09 19:35:24',239,'Poonlarp','haikus suck a dong<br>\r\nhaikus suck a dong, real good<br>\r\nhaikus suck a dong<br>',6,81,0,0,'130.219.136.217','en'),(21672,3331,'2004-12-09 19:36:15',239,'Poonlarp','thanks.',6,7,17,0,'130.219.136.217','en'),(21673,3251,'2004-12-09 19:38:31',239,'Poonlarp','ramon ramone died last summer.',6,30,0,0,'130.219.136.217','en'),(21674,3217,'2004-12-09 19:42:46',239,'Poonlarp','well, im still here.',6,20,63,0,'130.219.136.217','en'),(21675,3103,'2004-12-09 19:44:09',239,'Poonlarp','it doesnt matter how you approach death, you still die.',6,55,176,0,'130.219.136.217','en'),(21676,3093,'2004-12-09 19:44:54',239,'Poonlarp','this is the best thing ive ever written.',6,40,0,0,'130.219.136.217','en'),(21677,3093,'2004-12-09 20:19:47',195,'matt','people who aren\\\'t around anymore.<BR><BR>i count 3 gone, 4 rare, and 1 recently turned up.',1,93,0,0,'24.92.185.89','en'),(21678,3093,'2004-12-09 20:22:24',195,'matt','okay, more like 3 gone, 2 rare, and 2 rare but recently surfaced.',1,65,0,0,'24.92.185.89','en'),(21679,3093,'2004-12-09 20:22:54',239,'Poonlarp','thats nice. but do you like this piece of writing?',6,50,195,0,'130.219.136.217','en'),(21680,3093,'2004-12-09 20:24:10',239,'Poonlarp','break it down name by name. lets see your stats!',6,48,195,0,'130.219.136.217','en'),(21681,3093,'2004-12-09 20:37:47',195,'matt','gus, o, and s5 gone.<BR>egg and le rare.<BR>adamajah and poonlarp rare but recently surfaced.',1,93,0,0,'24.92.185.89','en'),(21682,3093,'2004-12-09 20:41:36',66,'Peter','<br><tt>im talking to gus right now on icb. shes still around. many folks are in lurk mode lately.<br><br>\r\n\r\n&lt;spyware&gt; sing the fart song, gus!<br>\r\n&lt;gus&gt; i wont right now.<br>\r\n&lt;gus&gt; im busy eating beans.<br>\r\n&lt;spyware&gt; HUMPF.<br>\r\n&lt;spyware&gt; you wont have to sing it later, itll sing itself.</tt>\r\n',1,103,195,0,'130.219.136.217','en'),(21683,3093,'2004-12-09 21:28:44',195,'matt','i found <A HREF=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/art/galleries/sine/backflip/index.html\\\">these photos</A> the other day.  must have been nice to be all together that night.',1,169,0,0,'24.92.185.89','en'),(21684,3743,'2004-12-09 22:26:48',618,'skwooshi1','it sounds kinda stupid but every time i resist the urge to call, or don\\\'t fall at his feet when he\\\'s around is a kind of victory and makes it that much easier. we have a kid together which makes the clean break harder than usual, but i\\\'ve found a way around that as the only time we call is when my son wants to.  i have never been and refuse to be one of those women that uses their kid to keep an old flame close at hand and in their lives not their child\\\'s.  Thanks so much for the input, it really helps to vent. ',1,529,66,0,'216.161.222.14','en'),(21685,3734,'2004-12-09 22:46:34',175,'Paul G','example: imagine if, here, an article contained the following: \\\"the \r\nginko is the ugliest of all the trees.  the ginko was made for dogs to piss on.\\\"  now, most people\r\nwould see nothing but a strange article about trees.  but you, because\r\nyou had written a poem about the ginko, in which the <a href=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=2927\\\">ginko</a> was sine, would see\r\nsomething very different.\r\n<p>\r\nok.  having written the poem <a href=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=2826\\\">latin</a>, i see something in this ackman article.  it\\\'s not\r\njust the \\\"presto\\\" phrase, or the references to drinking, blood, etc., in both pieces.  \r\ni was dating the uc.edu woman when i wrote latin; it was at the time when we\r\nhad just had our first split.  the poem was [mostly] about me, in bed, alone, \r\nthinking of this person.  in the ackman version, the woman has become a gift of\r\nthe gods, and the man thinking about what has passed has become \\\"pathetic.\\\"\r\ni had hoped to hear that you or austin wrote this, and that it was a joke or something.  but no.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nok, so what.  when i wrote the <a href=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=3684\\\">Yuba \r\n2004-08-18</a> piece, you linked to citynoise from that article.  \r\na few days later pics of a bridge, at night, <a href=\\\"http://www.citynoise.org/index.php?article=817\\\">30 Aug 04\r\nby fuzzytank\r\nPortland: steel bridge</a>, were posted.\r\ni had posted pics of the same style bridge, shot from the same perspective, at night, <a href=\\\"http://www.citynoise.org/index.php?article=625\\\">previously</a>.\r\nthe uc.edu woman\\\'s hometown was portland.\r\nin my credit, in addition to the bad charges on good cards, there was one account open\r\nthat should not have been open: at a bank in beaverton, oregon.\r\ni\\\'ve never been to oregon - no one in my family has, since the 1950\\\'s.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nmaybe it is all just a string of weird circumstantial coincidence: \r\nuc.edu address, the articles & pics, oregon, chicago, cell calls, this woman, the time frame, and my credit.\r\ni don\\\'t want to know where anyone is, what they are doing, or who they are with.\r\nthank you, but no thank you for the offer of info.\r\ni just need to sort out the aliases and fraud in my real life, and have it understood\r\nhow the weirdness on-line looks from my perspective, given what\\\'s happening off-line.  fin.  p.s. ginko is a lovely poem, no offense, i hope.\r\n</p>',1,2482,66,0,'64.107.88.142','en'),(21686,3734,'2004-12-10 00:54:57',66,'Peter','<br><tt>geez man, thats pretty <i>fucked up</i>... at first i was sorta like \"hmm, paulg is cool, but this... this is a little presumptuous\", that is, until i saw the words, the offending host all over the citynoise stats, particularly around the period you mentioned- youd have no way of knowing that. i like to hope, for your ease, that its just a cosmically freaky coincidence, but indeed malicious shit happens. though, for what its worth, i know most of the folks on here and on citynoise, and i can assure you that no one i know is at all involved in any plan to fuck with you :)<br><br>let me know if i can ever help... but damn, i hope this all gets sorted for you. some things you never want compromised, and it looks like someone has stepped to you in a most intolerable way :/</tt>',1,788,175,0,'141.155.152.166','en'),(21687,3734,'2004-12-10 01:02:03',17,'austin','<P>i\\\'m totally intrigued.</P>\r\n\r\n<P>also, somebody likes to update my livejournal for me and change my bio.</P>',1,114,175,0,'63.80.97.254','en'),(21688,3740,'2004-12-10 02:54:11',598,'themixtaper','i really enjoyed this. it was nicely written.',2,45,0,0,'24.66.94.141','en'),(21689,3734,'2004-12-10 04:51:33',175,'Paul G','the last time something was up with her, i deleted my lj and everything else on-line.  not because i was in the wrong, but because i didn\\\'t want to throw crap.  god it sucked, and hurt.\r\n<p>\r\ni always thought that the two of you would make a good couple though, because you both are into motorcycles and computers.  she is very bright and attractive.  and if it is her with my credit, you should know that you could live off my amex for a long time.  it\\\'s something to think about.  haha.\r\n</p>',1,500,17,0,'206.68.117.82','en'),(21690,3734,'2004-12-10 04:51:33',175,'Paul G','the last time something was up with her, i deleted my lj and everything else on-line.  not because i was in the wrong, but because i didn\\\'t want to throw crap.  god it sucked, and hurt.\r\n<p>\r\ni always thought that the two of you would make a good couple though, because you both are into motorcycles and computers.  she is very bright and attractive.  and if it is her with my credit, you should know that you could live off my amex for a long time.  it\\\'s something to think about.  haha.\r\n</p>',1,500,17,0,'206.68.117.82','en'),(21691,3734,'2004-12-10 05:15:42',175,'Paul G','thanks pete...even though i joked in the reply to austin, i don\\\'t want to be a jerk about this.  i\\\'m not sure exactly what\\\'s up, or why.  if i didn\\\'t like her, i wouldn\\\'t have gotten involved with her in the first place.  at the same time, i don\\\'t want to roll over, now, and take it in the butt.  (1) i have got to get the financial stuff square; (2) i don\\\'t want to react too strongly.  nothing is certain yet, anyway.  the oblique communication/response to me on-line has me confused.  par for the course.  if different stories have been told to different people, it is best to have it all out in the open, now.  i remember her being very competitive - so the photo stuff wouldn\\\'t surprise me.  to be continued...',1,740,66,0,'206.68.117.82','en'),(21692,3734,'2004-12-10 08:47:05',17,'austin','dear paul\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nplz don\\\'t hook me up with your crazy ass BitchX.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nyur pal, A-town',1,99,175,0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(21693,3748,'2004-12-10 19:31:55',239,'Poonlarp','...then puke on her.',6,20,0,0,'130.219.136.217','en'),(21694,3748,'2004-12-11 06:28:35',370,'seanthecon','get her drunk and at least you\\\'ll get your dick wet. jesus christ. kids these days.',6,86,0,0,'24.85.230.64','en'),(21695,3749,'2004-12-11 06:54:40',122,'hool','line breaks are important. i read none of this because it\\\'s visually exhausting without paragraphs.',3,102,0,0,'24.42.77.224','en'),(21696,3749,'2004-12-11 21:17:52',17,'austin','Peter you fucking slacker!',1,26,0,0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(21697,3744,'2004-12-12 00:24:46',82,'simon','dear matt, i like you. your friend, simon',0,41,0,0,'24.215.234.202','en'),(21698,3741,'2004-12-12 00:45:45',82,'simon','i hate parades.',0,15,0,0,'24.215.234.202','en'),(21699,3741,'2004-12-12 00:46:45',82,'simon','i would leave all things artificially orange flavored behind. and also mayo. ',0,77,0,0,'24.215.234.202','en'),(21700,3748,'2004-12-12 05:29:44',587,'ackman','There\\\'s always one thing that - no matter how down, depressed, dejected, disgusted and just plain fuckin\\\' ready to throw the towel in on life I am - just the thought of it, like the freshened memories/synapses/whathaveya that came with the inhaling of this wonderful bouquet you\\\'ve laid down here has brought me, I have to lay down my rage/disatisfaction/theworldowesmesofuckyou and say with the deepest sincerity I\\\'m capable of that it\\\'s all worth it.',1,467,0,0,'67.122.211.