inking about the iconography:  hearts, dollar signs, love, money - i thought, <I>a spade.  what does that look like?</I><BR><BR>and then it hit me.  kind of phallic.',1,219,0,0,'71.99.163.87','en'),(22343,3909,'2006-01-13 14:44:10',66,'Peter','<br><tt>humpf. i was hoping for something more dazzling, akin, perhaps, to the <i>cleveland steamer</i> or the <i>rusty trombone</i>...</tt>',1,140,195,0,'130.219.8.253','en'),(22344,2512,'2006-01-14 18:20:15',195,'matt','one, two, three<BR>i say, children, what does it all mean?<BR>whoa, whoa, whoa<BR>one, two, three<BR>i wouldn\\\'t lie to you.<BR>no more, no less<BR>that\\\'s a magic number.<BR>no more, no less<BR>what is it?<BR>no more, no less<BR>do the shang-a-lang.<BR>no more, no less<BR>anybody in the audience ever get hit by a car?<BR>no more, no less<BR>how high\\\'s the water, mama?<BR>no more, no less<BR>how high\\\'s the water, mama?<BR>no more, no less<BR>three feet high and rising.<BR>no more, no less<BR>three<BR>that\\\'s a magic number.',1,541,0,0,'71.99.163.87','en'),(22345,3914,'2006-01-14 22:36:26',17,'austin','i don\\\'t think i\\\'ve ever seen anything incoherent from you before.  i like it!',1,83,0,0,'69.17.112.117','en'),(22346,3912,'2006-01-14 23:35:30',251,'jamie','i once had a crush on samantha janus',0,36,0,0,'172.214.139.65','en'),(22347,3911,'2006-01-14 23:38:59',251,'jamie','this reads like a dream',0,23,0,0,'172.214.139.65','en'),(22348,3909,'2006-01-14 23:47:25',251,'jamie','<em>\\\"i guess theres jersey and shit. then a bunch of other shit. then california.\\\"</em>\r\n\r\nThis made me laugh. But may, i like your writing. This wouldn\\\'t go out of place on citynoise.org\r\n\r\nand wtf are cheese curds?',0,225,0,0,'172.214.139.65','en'),(22349,3891,'2006-01-14 23:58:06',251,'jamie','why does this sound familiar?... oh yeh',0,39,0,0,'172.214.139.65','en'),(22350,3894,'2006-01-15 00:03:30',251,'jamie','wasn\\\'t your last article about shitting yourself in public?',1,62,0,0,'172.214.139.65','en'),(22351,3914,'2006-01-15 07:47:32',82,'simon','i like it too. ',0,15,0,0,'24.193.163.174','en'),(22352,3914,'2006-01-16 17:17:07',66,'Peter','<br><tt>paulg. this is the best thing youve ever written.</tt>',1,62,0,0,'24.46.99.165','en'),(22353,2512,'2006-01-16 18:59:06',66,'Peter','<br><tt>my soul posse consists of three... and thats the magic number.</tt>',1,75,195,0,'24.46.99.165','en'),(22354,3911,'2006-01-16 19:00:44',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i totally know this girl.</tt>',1,38,0,0,'24.46.99.165','en'),(22355,3891,'2006-01-16 19:02:21',66,'Peter','<br><tt>148. 1+4+8=13. 13 is a prime number.</tt>',1,49,0,0,'24.46.99.165','en'),(22356,3894,'2006-01-16 19:03:23',66,'Peter','<br><tt>sh*te</tt>',1,18,0,0,'24.46.99.165','en'),(22357,3914,'2006-01-16 20:26:20',727,'netter','puts me all aflutter.  wowiez.',1,30,0,0,'69.108.96.172','en'),(22358,3914,'2006-01-16 20:45:07',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i watched <A href=\\\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0113967/?fr=c2l0ZT1kZnx0dD0xfGZiPXV8cG49MHxrdz0xfHE9bmV3IGplcnNleSBkcml2ZXxmdD0xfG14PTIwfGxtPTUwMHxjbz0xfGh0bWw9MXxubT0x;fc=1;ft=23\\\">new jersey drive</a> recently. ive also listened to <A href=\\\"http://finelinefeatures.com/crash/cmp/warm-lyrics.html\\\">warm leatherette</a> alot lately. <br><br>this piece of writing brought both to mind.',1,402,0,0,'24.46.99.165','en'),(22359,3914,'2006-01-16 20:57:09',82,'simon','i love warm leatherette. join the car crash set!',0,48,0,0,'24.193.160.213','en'),(22360,3914,'2006-01-17 01:13:26',66,'Peter','<br><tt>im town between abject excitement and horror to know that grace jones did <a href=\\\"http://saturn5.com/peter/music/grace_jones-warm-leatherette.mp3\\\">a cover of \\\"warm leatherette\\\"</a>...</tt>',1,209,82,0,'24.46.99.165','en'),(22361,3914,'2006-01-17 04:01:02',17,'austin','i think i like some other paulg stuff more!',1,43,66,0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(22362,3914,'2006-01-17 05:03:28',66,'Peter','<br><tt>oh, totally. im just saying this is fresh. and fresh is good.</tt>',0,74,66,0,'24.46.99.165','en'),(22363,3915,'2006-01-18 16:57:18',82,'simon','heh.',0,4,0,0,'24.193.160.213','en'),(22364,3915,'2006-01-18 19:58:16',66,'Peter','<br><tt>actually, i heard simon has a <i>giant</i> cock...</tt>',1,63,0,0,'130.219.8.253','en'),(22365,3915,'2006-01-19 00:46:49',195,'matt','yeah, the little ones so often do.  ;)<BR><BR>and the big ones.  :0',1,67,0,0,'71.99.163.87','en'),(22366,3914,'2006-01-19 02:46:31',175,'Paul G','Thank you.',1,10,0,0,'192.203.136.254','en'),(22367,3914,'2006-01-19 02:48:58',175,'Paul G','<p>\r\nOctober 16, 2005: \r\nAll I want to do is make it out of Illinois.\r\nEverything has died, failed, and broken again.\r\n(1) I lay around depressed; (2) I shoot myself in the head; (3) I get on the bike and ride away.\r\nOption Three in progress.\r\nFirst night on the road.\r\nMotel room in Missouri.\r\nBottle of hard liquor.\r\nPay-per-view:\r\n\\\"Reign of Tera,\\\" and then...\\\"Breathless.\\\"\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\n<a href=\\\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0085276/\\\">\\\"Breathless.\\\"</a>\r\nA favorite film.\r\nHe steals cars, and reads Silver Surfer.  \r\n(Reckless but kind, almost childlike innocence mixed with lawlessness?)\r\nShe\\\'s been told that she\\\'s special, all her life: beautiful, affluent family, education, promise of a professional career.\r\nIt hits close to home.\r\nWash-rinse-repeat.\r\nRomance, pregnancy.\r\nBelievable.\r\nAnd then...she agrees to run off to Mexico.\r\nA brief fantasy.\r\nEnd of the flick, back to reality, he\\\'s shot.\r\nOh so French.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nShe\\\'ll move on.\r\nThe Form.  The Meeting.  The Committee.  \r\nWhat was, for him, the slow death through obsequious behavior.\r\nMyrmidons.  Eunuchs.\r\nLaboring to build a system through which your own labor becomes obsolete?\r\nDoing what you think is wrong, for people that you hate, in exchange for the chance to grow old before dying?\r\nLeaving less hope of freedom for the succeeding generation?\r\nThe nutless bitches become legion.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nRemade for the People as <a href=\\\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0187078/\\\">\\\"Gone in Sixty Seconds.\\\"</a>  He and She don\\\'t read comics; they are comic book characters.\r\nCage and Jolie.  With a happily-ever-after ending.  Oh so American.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nScene: <a href=\\\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0100935/\\\">\\\"Wild at Heart.\\\"</a>  The match head\\\'s phosphorus bursts into flame.\r\nThat\\\'s it.  An explosion of heat and light...and then nothing.  Ash.\r\nThe slag heap in \\\"The Great Gatsby.\\\"  And worse.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\n\\\"Jet trails in the sky...\\\"\r\n</p>',4,1980,0,0,'192.203.136.254','en'),(22368,3914,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',82,'simon','<img border=0 src=\\\"http://www.symphonyspace.org/releases/photos/79/breathless_1.jpg\\\" width=400>',1,91,175,0,'24.193.160.213','en'),(22369,3914,'2006-01-19 15:30:41',82,'simon','oops! didn\\\'t realize that was so, uh, large.',0,47,0,0,'209.21.99.118','en'),(22370,3914,'2006-01-19 16:23:27',195,'matt','much more flavor than a big-ass picture of richard gere, anyway.',1,64,0,0,'71.99.163.87','en'),(22371,3914,'2006-01-19 18:13:11',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i bet thats what you tell <i>all</i> da bitchez...</tt>',1,63,82,0,'130.219.8.253','en'),(22372,3914,'2006-01-19 19:51:06',82,'simon','stop talking about my dick, dude. you said you would after i showed it to you...',1,80,66,0,'209.21.99.118','en'),(22373,3914,'2006-01-19 23:39:36',175,'Paul G','no, no.  not \\\"oops!\\\"  perfect.  \r\n<href=\\\"http://www.imdb.com/gallery/mptv/1228/Mptv/1228/2927_0056.jpg?path=gallery&path_key=0053472\\\">yes</a>, \r\n<href=\\\"http://www.nwfilmforum.org/superhits/breathless.jpg\\\">yes</a>, \r\n<href=\\\"http://www.moviemail-online.co.uk/images/large/breathless.jpg\\\">yes</a>.  i am thankful for you.  xoxo.',1,349,82,0,'192.203.136.254','en'),(22374,3914,'2006-01-19 23:42:19',175,'Paul G','<br>\r\nhttp://www.imdb.com/gallery/mptv/1228/Mptv/1228/2927_0056.jpg?path=gallery&path_key=0053472\r\n<br>\r\nhttp://www.nwfilmforum.org/superhits/breathless.jpg\r\n<br>\r\nhttp://www.moviemail-online.co.uk/images/large/breathless.jpg',1,225,0,0,'192.203.136.254','en'),(22375,3915,'2006-01-20 15:37:54',251,'jamie','this brought a lump to my throat for reasons i won\\\'t go into',4,63,0,0,'213.249.154.99','en'),(22376,3205,'2006-01-20 15:43:59',251,'jamie','i could watch her sleep forever<br>\r\ni could watch her sleep all night<br>\r\nand i wonder what she\\\'s dreaming of<br>\r\nwhen i am out of sight<br>\r\ni could watch her sleep forever<br>\r\njust the way she is tonight<br>\r\nas i think about the times we\\\'ve spent beneath a candle light<br>\r\nbut for now my baby\\\'s sleeping<br>\r\nand for now she doesn\\\'t know<br>\r\njust how much she means to me<br>\r\nand how i love her so\r\n',1,422,0,0,'213.249.154.99','en'),(22377,3915,'2006-01-20 15:49:34',195,'matt','wistfulness or nausea?',1,22,251,0,'71.99.163.87','en'),(22378,3915,'2006-01-20 15:54:25',251,'jamie','i wish it were nausea',0,21,195,0,'213.249.154.99','en'),(22379,3175,'2006-01-20 18:53:52',0,'Thaddeus','I am an 1111 person. This has been going on for years. It is not a fixation. I have had many situations happen to me with those numbers involved. It could also be binary code. Anyhoo. Thanks.',1,191,0,0,'24.210.86.4','en'),(22380,3916,'2006-01-21 15:50:42',86,'egg','you left out that he likes to blare \\\"hot for teacher\\\" while running red lights.',0,85,0,0,'128.6.30.199','en'),(22381,3916,'2006-01-21 16:03:30',82,'simon','i like the peeing on the cadillac engine to put out the fire story. herf lives!',1,79,0,0,'69.203.6.192','en'),(22382,3806,'2006-01-21 19:42:37',195,'matt','i said i\\\'d post this and never did:<BR><BR><B>COUSCOUS AROMATIQUE</B><BR><BR>serves 4-6<BR><BR>1 lb. couscous<BR>1/4 c. olive oil<BR>1 onion, cut into chunks<BR>2 carrots, thick slices<BR>4 baby turnips, halved<BR>8 sm. new potatoes, halved<BR>1 green bell pepper, chunks<BR>1 sm. fennel bulb, thick slices<BR>1-in. cube fresh ginger, grated<BR>2 garlic cloves, crushed<BR>1 t. ground turmeric<BR>1 t. ground coriander<BR>1 t. cumin seeds<BR>1 t. ground cinnamon<BR>3 T. red lentils<BR>14-oz. can tomatoes, chopped<BR>4 1/2 c. vegetable stock<BR>4 T. raisins<BR>salt and pepper<BR>rind and juice of 1 lemon<BR>harissa paste (opt.)<BR><BR>1.  cover couscous with cold water; soak 10 min.  drain; spread out on a tray for 20 min., stirring occaisonally with fingers.<BR><BR>2.  in a large saucepan, fry the veggies in the oil for 10 min.<BR><BR>3.  add ginger, garlic, spices; stir; cook 2 min.  add lentils, tomatoes, stock, raisins, salt, pepper.<BR><BR>4.  bring to boil; reduce to simmer.  by now, the couscous is ready to steam.  place in a steamer and fit it on top of stew.<BR><BR>5.  cover; steam gently for 20 min.  grains should be swollen and soft.  fork through; season well.<BR><BR>6.  add lemon rind and juice to stew; check seasoning.  if desired, add harissa paste to taste.',1,1291,0,0,'71.99.163.87','en'),(22383,3916,'2006-01-21 21:46:22',175,'Paul G','a good story.  ref: \\\"internet cash pyramid scheme,\\\" details would be helpful.',1,83,0,0,'192.203.136.254','en'),(22384,3914,'2006-01-22 07:48:19',682,'turandot','This is really different.  good good good',2,41,175,0,'72.14.140.105','en'),(22385,3916,'2006-01-22 10:54:01',66,'Peter','<br><tt>lol. herf. cocaine.</tt>',1,32,0,0,'24.46.99.165','en'),(22386,3916,'2006-01-22 20:34:27',400,'elaine','i like the safe',1,15,0,0,'62.56.36.111','en'),(22387,3916,'2006-01-23 15:11:30',251,'jamie','<p>i\\\'m stuck on the <em>\\\"all kinds of raunchy drunk sex\\\"</em></p>',1,74,0,0,'213.249.154.99','en'),(22388,3911,'2006-01-23 15:13:21',251,'jamie','don\\\'t we al',0,14,66,0,'213.249.154.99','en'),(22389,3911,'2006-01-23 15:13:34',251,'jamie','l',0,1,66,0,'213.249.154.99','en'),(22390,3724,'2006-01-24 09:43:47',195,'matt','WHAT THE FUCK HAPPENED?',1,23,0,0,'71.99.163.87','en'),(22391,3924,'2006-01-24 15:11:14',626,'catintheattic','10 a.m. the next day.  ate the rest of it over an hour ago.  high is substantially less than last night.',1,104,0,0,'71.99.163.87','en'),(22392,3924,'2006-01-24 16:51:35',626,'catintheattic','seems to be a consensus that perhaps there was not enough fat in the recipe, either.',1,84,0,0,'71.99.163.87','en'),(22393,3924,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',66,'Peter','<br><tt>re: the oil... i rarely use oil from packaged stuff (olives, sun dried tomatoes, mozarella) cause it often has alot higher moisture level, and tends to pop and sputter and smoke alot. i prefer to save it for seasoning and salad dressing.<br><Br>and stems and seeds? do they have much thc in them?<br><Br>and the addition of capers is deluxe. not only do they taste good, theyre naturally anti-gas. weed or not, this sounded like an interesting recipe, which ill probably recall somedday soon when im cooking, and try to vaguely replicate off the cuff...</tt>',1,566,626,0,'24.46.99.165','en'),(22394,3924,'2006-01-25 18:27:34',626,'catintheattic','yeah, you\\\'re right about the oil, now that i think about it.  i never considered that.<BR><BR>seeds and stems:  i don\\\'t know how much thc they have, but they turned the oil green.  probably due to something in them besides the active ingredient, though.<BR><BR>you know, i don\\\'t know why i like farfalle so much.  i think it\\\'s just the word.  reminds me of \\\"farfisa\\\".<BR><BR>a cooking anecdote:  i was making pad thai last night (sans weed).  in the middle of chopping some broccoli, my balls suddenly started to tingle, then burn.  the skin in front, just under the roast beef.  it got worse over the next few minutes.<BR><BR>i was like, <I>goddamn!  what is this?  this has got to be some kundalini shit!</I><BR><BR>then i realized that right before the broccoli, i was cutting up some dried chilies, handling them, getting the seeds out.  it hit me that i must have unconsciously (or not) touched that area.<BR><BR>i went in the bathroom and had a little sink wash, but they still burned.  i called my sister, the nurse, and asked for some advice.  she couldn\\\'t stop laughing for about half a minute.  then she told me to soak them in some milk and started laughing again.<BR><BR>i didn\\\'t try the milk thing.  it went away after half an hour.',1,1269,66,0,'71.99.163.87','en'),(22395,3925,'2006-01-27 19:14:10',66,'Peter','<br><tt>...he makes great tunes because he has awesome taste in music</tt>',1,74,0,0,'130.219.8.253','en'),(22396,3925,'2006-01-28 09:14:37',370,'seanthecon','amen motherfucker. amen. the revolution will not be blogged. let\\\'s get free.',6,79,0,0,'24.85.230.64','en'),(22397,3925,'2006-01-28 22:28:32',175,'Paul G','...maybe, it should be difficult for a just person to feel comfortable in an unjust society.  and sometimes we need to reach the point of collapse before we are willing to admit that there are problems with our associations - political, or romantic.  it\\\'s a profoundly human thing.\r\n<p>\r\nchia, you read like you are in a profoundly different place - relative to most of your pieces from korea.  but thank you for writing, again.\r\n</p>  ',1,439,0,0,'192.203.136.254','en'),(22398,3805,'2006-01-29 20:03:44',82,'simon','it\\\'s now been a year. i wish i could go back to sf and see our pals.',0,71,0,0,'24.193.163.91','en'),(22399,3929,'2006-01-29 20:11:52',400,'elaine','i like the top and tail, j',1,26,0,0,'62.56.34.70','en'),(22400,3926,'2006-01-30 18:35:55',508,'edward','I saw an interview with a London-based travel book writer or maybe travel bookshop owner. He said that the primary conceptual problem between the idea of going somewhere and actually going there, is that you bring yourself. At that time, I liked the way he put it into words... as I did now reading this text somewhat touching the same topic.',1,342,0,0,'193.10.214.31','en'),(22401,3925,'2006-01-31 01:00:55',93,'chiamattt','<p>\r\nA code of integrity has put him in a profoundly different place. At no time in his life has he ever felt so locked in. At no time in his life has he ever been compelled so strongly to uphold his end of the contract. He is bound by two contracts. Both concern a friend of his who argued in his favour and did extraordinary things. That is why he cannot just pick up and leave. As much as his life is a tangle of emotions, selfish thoughts and feelings, at the end of the day he will not rollover and put the reputation of his friend on the line. If his friend loses face in a society where losing face is an embarrassment not only to the individual but also to the individual’s family, he could not even begin to say that learning from the past, brings forth a better future. He has made mistakes before. He had dishonored and lost a good friend and vowed never to let that happen again. No matter where he goes or what he does, because of these contracts, he will not be able to change, at least his location, until October. He could change his life outside of work. He could change his life inside of work. He could change his attitude regarding life, work, friends, society, and the woman. He knows all of this. His energy is perhaps tied up in upholding his end of the contracts. \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nHe and his friend rarely speak anymore.\r\n</p> \r\n',0,1349,0,0,'211.253.15.130','en'),(22402,3925,'2006-01-31 05:56:45',66,'Peter','<br><tt>you should keep this going, chia. i think this entry is one that many people can relate to...</tt>',1,106,93,0,'24.46.99.165','en'),(22403,3925,'2006-02-01 00:50:20',93,'chiamattt','He recalls the past as a patchwork of moments, visions, and desires. He cannot say for sure which event came first or what happened when and where for every memory. His memories, especially of her, have long since been skewed and distorted by imaginary prologues and conclusions. He has, in part created a mythical past which when thought about at length is either false or exaggerated. Even when he sits down to write he has trouble figuring out what was real and what was made up. Did he love her or was that just a mythical love which only his dream world could know? Could he have lived a happy and full life with her? His honest answer is yes, but his realistic and agreeable answer is no. He cannot even say for sure that he loves his mother, father, brother, or friends. He does not love himself and though in the past he has said that it is easier to love someone else than to love yourself, he understands now that to know any kind of love, no matter what or who that love is directed at, he must learn to love himself; a daunting task for a man who cares little about his now, and thinks mainly about his then.  ',0,1122,0,0,'211.253.15.130','en'),(22404,2716,'2006-02-03 11:35:54',295,'karenlee','Wow, i am wondering what kind of defensive trip i was on back in 2002. What a weird answer to your question. please allow me to answer again: I make lots of things. I do not have a particular category, however i do like to carve stone. I also like fixing things. I really do not like the tone of my original comments. Even though I\\\'m sure they were meant in jest, as I am not nasty, I apologize anyway.',3,405,174,0,'220.236.47.132','en'),(22405,3929,'2006-02-03 14:32:15',251,'jamie','so i\\\'ve heard',4,16,400,0,'213.249.154.99','en'),(22406,3929,'2006-02-03 19:40:30',400,'elaine','only with heffalumps wearing really good socks',1,46,251,0,'212.225.62.217','en'),(22407,3926,'2006-02-07 03:14:17',175,'Paul G','<i>\\\"[...]the primary conceptual problem between the idea of going somewhere and actually going there, is that you bring yourself.\\\"</i>\r\n<p>\r\nThat quote, above, and the ideas of self, travel and change have been turning round in my mind for a week, or more.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nThe \\\"self\\\" seems like it can, and should, be a thing that is changeable.  So that when one participates in, or observes, something profound, e.g., war, prison, pregnancy, chilbirth, etc., one is different in some way afterwards.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nAnd I would hope that \\\"travel\\\" might be included in that list of transformational experiences.  It\\\'s not only a matter of the physical distance that allows one to observe phenomena from a different perspective, or the thought that travel provides one the opportunity to compare and contrast human constructions - political, religious, and such - but, sometimes, the discomfort of the trip, or the beauty/horror that one encounters actually alters the person - the \\\"self.\\\"\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nWhat I noticed about Amanda\\\'s trip diary/story was her connection to the place from which she came: the suggestion that it was good to know NZ was there, relatively green and unspoiled, away from the mess of the World.  A refuge?  Something like that.  The same sort of thing was alive in the heads of the English - as I knew them - before WWII.  And I\\\'m jealous.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nThe search for the transormational experience/trip implies a sense - at least a vague sense - that something is incomplete, or needs to be changed.  Discontentment.  [Tack on LSD, philosophy, Burning Man, motorcycles, teaching in Korea/Japan, piercing and such - as you please.]\r\n</p> ',3,1688,508,0,'192.203.136.254','en'),(22408,3930,'2006-02-10 02:16:33',83,'adamajah','That\\\'s some funny \\\'shit\\\'.  :-B\r\n\r\n(How did he get from a motorcycle to a car?)',2,87,0,0,'71.106.138.110','en'),(22409,3931,'2006-02-10 07:15:36',17,'austin','you are a beautiful writer.  i\\\'m really not very drunk.  just three drinks.  enough to appreciate.',1,101,0,0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(22410,3931,'2006-02-10 14:05:05',82,'simon','ames, this is so lovely. i\\\'ve been thinking about the One Memory since i spoke to you earlier.',1,97,0,0,'24.193.37.185','en'),(22411,3931,'2006-02-10 23:02:56',91,'jay','staggeringly good.  long live swinney.org!',0,42,0,0,'69.226.199.117','en'),(22412,3931,'2006-02-11 22:17:57',175,'Paul G','it\\\'s amazing when someone is able to bring together an unlikely combination of individual parts to make a harmonious whole: individual traits into a personality, personalities into a relationship, memories into words, words in a good story, and that terrible list of food into one stomach.  well done.',1,304,0,0,'192.203.136.254','en'),(22413,3930,'2006-02-12 05:35:08',240,'xep','I love the fact that this is not the first swinney entry about puking into one\\\'s helmet.',0,91,0,0,'69.17.112.129','en'),(22414,3930,'2006-02-12 07:20:46',17,'austin','i pretend this was an homage to the master.  otherwise, you are just a copy cat ho.  you can ride on the back of my bike anytime--but you have to wear your jeans backwards.',1,172,0,0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(22415,3930,'2006-02-13 00:29:34',66,'Peter','<br><tt>ew</tt>',1,15,0,0,'24.46.99.165','en'),(22416,3931,'2006-02-13 14:12:48',93,'chiamattt','this made me cry. thank you. I needed it. ',1,42,0,0,'58.226.158.76','en'),(22417,3930,'2006-02-13 14:50:42',251,'jamie','dude, i think you might have some issues there?',0,47,0,0,'213.249.154.99','en'),(22418,3930,'2006-02-15 02:23:37',93,'chiamattt','Oh my god! Dude, I could not contain my laughter at work, and I work in a very conservative office. I got some really evil eyes and the jig was up. They knew I wasn\\\'t working. \\\"dear god\\\". classic. ',1,206,0,0,'211.253.15.130','en'),(22419,3933,'2006-02-16 03:17:23',93,'chiamattt','good thing you didn\\\'t have nevada eggs in the center console. ',1,65,0,0,'211.253.15.130','en'),(22420,3933,'2006-02-16 13:56:54',534,'griece','Yea, fuck that shit.',5,20,93,0,'130.219.8.253','en'),(22421,3933,'2006-02-17 19:29:36',82,'simon','what\\\'s a nevada egg?',0,23,0,0,'209.21.99.118','en'),(22422,3933,'2006-02-17 20:07:41',534,'griece','why dont you read my last submission before asking questions.',5,61,82,0,'130.219.8.253','en'),(22423,3935,'2006-02-17 23:37:02',17,'austin','<P>fuckin\\\' a.</P>\r\n<P>the speakers are all blown in my car.</P>\r\n<P>as for your writing... <B>*</B><I>destabilizing</I><B>*</B></P>',4,134,0,0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(22424,3935,'2006-02-18 00:42:25',727,'netter','i\\\'ll take \\\"destabilizing\\\" as a compliment, \\\'cause i like that word so much.  ;)',1,91,17,0,'69.108.124.145','en'),(22425,3933,'2006-02-18 16:11:43',82,'simon','gotcha',0,6,0,0,'24.193.163.202','en'),(22426,3933,'2006-02-19 03:22:03',534,'griece','its kool i dont mean any offense. im just sayin. im a man of many dimensions. suckers gotta stay caught up to feel what im tryna lay down. and fuck those who cant follow. but youre smart. im sure you can do the maths. read my latest 4 entries. ill m ake better sense then man.',5,276,82,0,'24.46.99.165','en'),(22427,3872,'2006-02-19 03:23:01',534,'griece','whatever. fucl alla yall',5,24,0,0,'24.46.99.165','en'),(22428,3936,'2006-02-19 18:57:02',400,'elaine','or your doctor',1,14,0,0,'62.56.30.143','en'),(22429,3916,'2006-02-19 21:35:23',180,'auntie','i wonder if herf still has his green jammies?',1,45,0,0,'24.92.160.192','en'),(22430,3907,'2006-02-19 21:37:22',180,'auntie','i don\\\'t think so.  i think it refers to buckskins, as in skins.  but i might be wrong.\r\n\r\ni think it\\\'s too cold to swim just yet.',2,135,626,0,'24.92.160.192','en'),(22431,3936,'2006-02-19 21:43:35',180,'auntie','<p>a sad commentary on the professions we grew up admiring - but so true - both the legal and medical systems have so many built in flaws, you\\\'d think they were congress</p>\r\n\r\n',1,180,0,0,'24.92.160.192','en'),(22432,3937,'2006-02-20 22:52:56',93,'chiamattt','Is writing a book about getting it on a shelf? ',1,47,0,0,'58.226.158.76','en'),(22433,3937,'2006-02-21 01:01:47',180,'auntie','i don\\\'t know',4,15,93,0,'24.92.160.192','en'),(22434,3937,'2006-02-21 04:02:01',93,'chiamattt','If you have written something you are proud of and think people would be interested in reading it email me. You don\\\'t need an agent to get a book deal, and you don\\\'t need a book deal to get an agent. You just need to network. :)',1,234,180,0,'211.253.15.130','en'),(22435,3937,'2006-02-21 04:06:08',93,'chiamattt','Take a look at this. \r\n\r\n<a href=\\\"http://creativeandperformingarts.humber.ca/schforwriters/summerworkshop.html\\\">Summer Workshop</a> ',1,138,0,0,'211.253.15.130','en'),(22436,3936,'2006-02-21 08:27:02',93,'chiamattt','did you drop out of law school?',1,31,0,0,'211.253.15.130','en'),(22437,3937,'2006-02-21 21:03:45',682,'turandot','There\\\'s also the option of self publishing. What a friend of mine did was find an editor who has backing and connections, this helped smooth out a lot of problems in the writing and got the books in stores.',2,209,180,0,'206.19.233.2','en'),(22438,3935,'2006-02-21 23:22:18',175,'Paul G','i like it.  especially paragraph five: life \\\"swishing\\\" by, counted out the window of a moving car.  hand on lap.  sunshine.  good stuff.',1,142,727,0,'64.107.88.238','en'),(22439,3936,'2006-02-21 23:55:15',175,'Paul G','i think that it is true that you can only repeat a thing so many times before you begin to believe it.  and maybe it\\\'s not even a matter of repetition, but simply being exposed to something frequently that helps you to lose whatever loathing you once had for it.',1,265,0,0,'64.107.88.238','en'),(22440,3936,'2006-02-22 04:12:29',176,'Scapegoat','No, I haven\\\'t dropped out but god knows I have been close several times.',0,75,93,0,'70.30.233.101','en'),(22441,3939,'2006-02-22 19:44:50',82,'simon','hm. interesting.',0,16,0,0,'209.21.99.118','en'),(22442,3940,'2006-02-23 00:16:23',175,'Paul G','indeed.  i spent a lot of time looking at the 999 before i fabricated a centerstand for the kawasaki.  with a little help from autocad, i was able to produce this:<br>\r\n<img src=\\\"http://germz.org/img/motorcycle/stand.JPG\\\" width=\\\"300\\\" height=\\\"225\\\" border=\\\"1\\\" alt=\\\"e-mail critical dimensions for a quote\\\"><br>\r\nit doesn\\\'t say \\\"ducati\\\" but it does say \\\"germanos.\\\"',1,405,0,0,'64.107.88.238','en'),(22443,3940,'2006-02-23 05:03:00',93,'chiamattt','There was a Ducati dealership near my apt, but it has since gone out of business. Things that go fast cannot go fast in Seoul.',1,126,0,0,'211.253.15.130','en'),(22444,3940,'2006-02-23 05:08:38',93,'chiamattt','<p>\r\n<img src=\\\"http://autobai.com/acecart/bin/photo/citi110-e.jpg\\\">\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nThe Daelim Citi 100cc scooter. Actually pronounced \\\"Shitty Bek\\\" in Korean. C is often a Sh sound here. \r\n',1,197,0,0,'211.253.15.130','en'),(22445,3939,'2006-02-23 07:25:47',682,'turandot','Feelings of anger and vulnerability usually coexist, maybe the painting doesn\\\'t have bad mojo as much as it makes people feel vulnerable. I like the idea of the painting leaving your circle as all the harsh feelings fade. ',1,225,0,0,'72.14.140.105','en'),(22446,3939,'2006-02-23 10:39:18',400,'elaine','interesting take on it, thanks.\r\ni like the idea that the fire in it might have faded. \r\nof course i can\\\'t maintain total fury or even the bleakness that i felt then even if i wanted to, which i don\\\'t. i am working on a whole \\\'silly cow\\\' exhibition just now, and i am trying to get with the positive side, and to finally exorcise any lurking demons. ',1,362,682,0,'62.56.59.16','en'),(22447,3939,'2006-02-23 14:20:03',66,'Peter','<br><tt>occasionally, i find paintings on the street or in trash piles. often, ive taken them home and painted on them.</tt>',1,124,0,0,'130.219.8.253','en'),(22448,3939,'2006-02-23 17:40:08',400,'elaine','that could easily have been her fate, and i can\\\'t say i would be in the slightest bit pissed off about that. in fact the idea of her \\\'sleeping\\\' behind some other image seems quite comforting.',1,200,66,0,'62.56.43.93','en'),(22449,3940,'2006-02-23 23:25:42',682,'turandot','That homemade center stand is such a good example of postmodernism and bauhaus.',2,79,175,0,'206.19.233.2','en'),(22450,3940,'2006-02-24 00:21:16',66,'Peter','<br><tt>paulg: ill show you my kawasaki if you show me yours! more jpgs! for real!</tt>',1,87,175,0,'24.46.99.165','en'),(22451,3941,'2006-02-24 10:42:21',400,'elaine','i don\\\'t know what gives me worst shivers, the being slapped awake, or the devil nursey',1,89,0,0,'62.56.8.182','en'),(22452,3940,'2006-02-25 02:36:32',175,'Paul G','the white font on black adds to the rich-to-the-point-of-decadence feel of the piece; austin has a good aesthetic sense.  but i can\\\'t help but wonder if the ducati is a consciously employed metaphor, or subconscious employed expression, for something else: beautiful, dangerous, high-maintenance. ',1,300,682,0,'64.107.88.206','en'),(22453,3940,'2006-02-25 02:43:52',175,'Paul G','custom painted gas tanks, by sine.  as evidenced by the ducati, people are willing to spend for what they consider to be art on wheels.  lacquer, enamel, aibrush, brush, just tanks.  simple.  $$$.  when you get yours done, you will become a rolling billboard - bringing the vision to the people.',1,295,66,0,'64.107.88.206','en'),(22454,3940,'2006-02-25 07:55:42',66,'Peter','<br><tt><img src=\\\"http://saturn5.com/peter/ke100/ke_rebuild1.jpg\\\" border=\\\"1\\\"><br><br>it is in desperate need of a paintjob. im thinking lots of oldskool norton-orange.</tt>',1,184,175,0,'24.46.99.165','en'),(22455,3940,'2006-02-26 05:57:18',682,'turandot','I suppose it\\\'s good for a man\\\'s ego have complete and intimate understanding of how motorcyles work, even make modifications to your liking so she\\\'s juuuuuust right.',1,174,175,0,'72.14.140.105','en'),(22456,3942,'2006-02-27 03:29:46',82,'simon','i love you, jay. i\\\'m sitting here in the wreckage, post-amy\\\'s 30th party. i cracked the last beer and i\\\'m surveying the damage from the couch. we missed you, friend. and everything smells like frosting and whiskey.',1,223,0,0,'63.212.166.178','en'),(22457,3942,'2006-03-01 02:20:24',175,'Paul G','so good.',1,8,0,0,'64.107.88.238','en'),(22458,3942,'2006-03-01 19:35:39',727,'netter','so beautiful.',1,13,0,0,'69.108.127.209','en'),(22459,3942,'2006-03-01 19:35:40',727,'netter','so beautiful.',1,13,0,0,'69.108.127.209','en'),(22460,3946,'2006-03-03 16:20:43',82,'simon','haha.',0,5,0,0,'209.21.99.118','en'),(22461,3909,'2006-03-03 19:32:51',195,'matt','austin, these cheap-ass gold-plated nipple clips you sent me done turned my titties green.',1,90,0,0,'64.128.136.170','en'),(22462,3946,'2006-03-04 20:31:09',175,'Paul G','the \\\"expand your mind\\\" ad is disturbing.  i don\\\'t know why.  and his smile makes me feel like he\\\'s in on the joke.',1,126,0,0,'192.203.136.254','en'),(22463,3640,'2006-03-07 16:19:42',66,'Peter','<br><tt><A href=\\\"http://www.citynoise.org/article/3203\\\">homage to old shoes</a>...</tt>',1,93,0,0,'130.219.8.253','en'),(22464,3640,'2006-03-07 18:19:12',400,'elaine','i expect it smelled quite a bit of essence of you',1,49,0,0,'62.56.59.245','en'),(22465,499,'2006-03-10 17:12:18',195,'matt','five years.  wow.  doesn\\\'t seem like it.',1,43,0,0,'64.128.136.170','en'),(22466,500,'2006-03-10 17:13:39',195,'matt','i didn\\\'t know it was an article at a time type of proposition.  some kind soul activated both of them.',1,105,0,0,'64.128.136.170','en'),(22467,3947,'2006-03-13 17:52:46',66,'Peter','<br><tt>this was intense. reading it has given me a dull, throbbing headache.<br><Br>ive had dreams with some of these identical elements in them before.<br><Br>odd...</tt>',1,172,0,0,'130.219.8.253','en'),(22468,3940,'2006-03-13 17:56:45',66,'Peter','<br><tt>...yes, my next modification will be to make the rear brake actually <i>work</i>, heh...</tt>',1,101,682,0,'130.219.8.253','en'),(22469,3948,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',17,'flickr','<BR><img src=\\\"http://static.flickr.com/48/112578726_9d9e5552ed.jpg\\\" width=\\\"300\\\">',4,88,0,0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(22470,3355,'2006-03-20 04:34:23',17,'austin','why is there no porn series?',1,28,0,0,'68.6.212.249','en'),(22471,3355,'2006-03-20 16:34:24',66,'Peter','<br><tt>there should be... and youre just the man to do it...</tt>',1,66,17,0,'130.219.8.253','en'),(22472,3355,'2006-03-20 22:12:33',741,'mute','yeh, i haven\\\'t written anything <i>Dir</i>-tay in awhile.  it\\\'s about time.',1,81,0,0,'64.128.136.170','en'),(22473,3950,'2006-03-22 09:12:54',400,'elaine','super lovely londonist writing',1,30,0,0,'212.225.62.127','en'),(22474,3950,'2006-03-22 14:16:26',251,'jamie','ah you got i working then?',0,26,0,0,'213.249.154.99','en'),(22475,3950,'2006-03-23 17:40:59',742,'an_impossible_child','hey thanks you two, yeah i did it, by jove, i did it! :)\r\nxxxxx',0,63,0,0,'86.138.1.223','en'),(22476,3950,'2006-03-23 18:44:13',741,'mute','this woman in laredo explained to me once what a leyline was, and i told her that\\\'s what she had out her front door and around the corner.<BR><BR>har.<BR><BR>this is good stuff.  i wish i knew some of the references.  or had the energy to look them up.',1,255,0,0,'64.128.136.170','en'),(22477,3950,'2006-03-23 19:03:27',239,'poonlarp','What\\\'s a leyline?',4,20,0,0,'130.219.8.253','en'),(22478,3526,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',239,'poonlarp','dong dong dong dong dong<br>\r\ndong dong dong dong dong, dong dong.<br>\r\ndong dong dong dong dong',3,88,0,0,'130.219.8.253','en'),(22479,3950,'2006-03-23 19:13:05',741,'mute','<a href=\\\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leyline\\\">somethin\\\' like dis.</a>',1,79,0,0,'64.128.136.170','en'),(22480,3953,'2006-03-23 23:22:51',741,'mute','if you want to be want to be a great writer, just go ahead and do it.  don\\\'t worry about any of the extras.  or the consequences.<BR><BR>(there are a lot of great writers in the world that not many people know about.  on here, for instance.)',1,244,0,0,'64.128.136.170','en'),(22481,3953,'2006-03-23 23:37:10',741,'mute','<I>It\\\'s splendid to be a great writer, to put men into the frying pan of your imagination and make them pop like chestnuts.</I><BR>-Gustave Flaubert',1,151,0,0,'64.128.136.170','en'),(22482,3950,'2006-03-25 17:59:56',742,'an_impossible_child','thanks for that, references are quite londoney i guess, \\\'john\\\' is john keats, who either did become a proper doctor or at least studied medicine & alchemy i think (as i was walking, i came across a plaque saying how he & another man lived in this house while they were studying at the nearby hospital)...\r\n\r\num... yeah (sorry my brain isnt working too well today :P)\r\n',0,374,741,0,'81.154.142.70','en'),(22483,3953,'2006-03-26 04:00:34',17,'austin','[x]',1,3,0,0,'68.6.212.249','en'),(22484,3953,'2006-03-27 04:00:28',66,'Peter','<br><tt>have you considered a career in \\\"male modelling\\\"?</tt>',1,68,0,0,'24.46.99.165','en'),(22485,3953,'2006-03-27 17:42:10',142,'oof','eh, too easy.',0,13,66,0,'136.167.255.151','en'),(22486,3953,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',17,'austin','here is my feedbag for you:\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ni am picking up what you are putting down, but as someone who doesn\\\'t desire any recognition outside my friends, i don\\\'t strive to be considered an artist at all.  i would like to be considered a story teller some times.  i think i was at one point.  i could regale audiences with tales of far flung non-possibilities and no one corrected my spelling.  now i just sit on chat and tell lies full of spelling errors in chat rooms.  i think it is the down side of the internet that there is no more oratory in my life.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ni can\\\'t tell you what you should do or care about.  i can\\\'t even put myself in your shoes.  you are you, i am me.  all i can say is [x] i read it.  i assumed you posted it here for me to read, as you might an email to a mailing list or a bulletin on the stop light.  in the future, if you write me a letter, i\\\'ll try and write back.',1,878,142,0,'68.6.212.249','en'),(22487,3952,'2006-03-27 18:13:57',741,'mute','is this a little beyond the pale in some way?  the pederastic leanings, maybe?  a whiff of misogyny?<BR><BR>i just wondered.  comment whore that i am.  i\\\'ll bet you i\\\'m going to have just a lovely relationship with professional critics.',1,242,0,0,'64.128.136.170','en'),(22488,3953,'2006-03-27 18:48:57',142,'oof','I\\\'ve shared this with a few friends and gotten some feedback and I feel inclined to clarify myself a bit.\r\n\r\nWhen I talk about being great, I don\\\'t mean that I am trying to be or want to be the next great American novelist, or some grand notion like that. I do think that there are many, many people writing for public consumption these days, in some part due to the explosion of the Internet. Meanwhile, I also think reading culture is continuing its ongoing decline. \r\n\r\nSo I feel an imbalance between writers and readers. I think our ego-driven self-celebrating culture has driven more and more people to pursue sharing themselves through writing while simultaneously discouraging reading as culture. Put another way, in economic terms, our culture is producing more writing than it can consume. This over-production, in some way of thinking about it, constitutes waste.(*)\r\n\r\nMy only compulsion to write is to contribute something worthwhile. I don\\\'t want or need to contribute to the waste. I don\\\'t need to see my words on paper, just for the sake of themselves. I\\\'m not at all convinced I have anything worthy to contribute. That is the question I\\\'m asking myself. \r\n\r\nIf I don\\\'t have anything to contribute, I\\\'m content to stay quiet. The only way for me to find out, is to write. This public admission of my neuroticism surrounding this issue is step one in that effort.\r\n\r\n(*) I understand the argument that some will make that all writing is good writing, that waste is not possible, because the act of writing itself is meaningful enough for some, even if what is written is not read. I\\\'m not even sure I disagree with this argument, but I know that I myself am not motivated to write without an audience. Without an audience, I don\\\'t need to write. I can just think.',0,1808,17,0,'136.167.255.151','en'),(22489,3952,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i was wondering how many 14 year olds have actually heard/heard of neubauten... then i remembered that pretty much everyone i know thats been a fan of them has come from your neck of the woods. for real. its like metro tampa is to post-industrial what norway is to black metal.<br><br> and <i>frutier than a loquat enema</i>... thats a good one, honey white...</tt>',1,358,741,0,'130.219.8.253','en'),(22490,3953,'2006-03-27 19:00:19',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i gave up on writing some time ago. now, im putting all my energies into spittin\\\' maaad freesteez, ya huuuurd...<br><br>the mc is the new bard, yo.</tt>',1,163,0,0,'130.219.8.253','en'),(22491,3953,'2006-03-27 21:43:28',17,'austin','i wouldn\\\'t overlook writing for yourself to read.  i was at a show the other day talking to a friend of a friend that i don\\\'t know.  he bought a lucinda williams live album the other day that was recorded live in san francisco four years ago.  he was living in san francisco at that time.  he looked in his journal, because he always writes it in it everyday, to see what activity he was doing instead of going to that show.  fishing, he figured.  but instead his journal said something like, \\\"ate dinner.\\\"  that is all.  this meant he was depressed at the time.  he reflected on how lame it is to sit at home depressed instead of fishing or going to lucinda williams.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\ni also wouldn\\\'t overlook writing for one person. as a person interested in history, i enjoy reading journals.  i have a book of napoleon\\\'s journal entries by my bed right now.  i wish i had journals for deceased members of my family tree.  how many readers doesn\\\'t matter me so much as who the readers are.  if 100 years from now, my sister\\\'s kid\\\'s kid reads my journal, or reads swinney.org, then it is all worth it to me.  of course that is just one case that would make it all worth it.  \r\n<BR><BR>\r\nsomebody i have not met or talked to from this site told me once that i wrote something that caused them to want to write something for others.  that makes it worth while too.  and look at me, i write about barfing in helmets and dogs that like blondes, nothing lofty there.  no positive cultural contribution.  i\\\'m contributing to a handful of people\\\'s laughing with a snort.\r\n',1,1594,142,0,'68.6.212.249','en'),(22492,3953,'2006-03-30 21:50:00',175,'Paul G','I\\\'ve heard the same sort of questioning before.  But, previously,\r\nthe questions were posed by people\r\nwho were considering whether they ought to have children:\r\n<p>\r\n\\\"Do we, already, have too many people?\\\"\r\n\\\"Is it an act of arrogance to be so concerned\r\nwith my own genetic legacy?\\\"\r\n\\\"Into what environment am I bringing these children?\\\"\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nIn the article/comments:\r\n\\\"ego-driven self-celebrating,\\\"\r\n\\\"over-production,\\\"\r\nand, employing the metaphor directly:\r\n\\\"My ego and my insecurity might finally find their rightful home, \r\ntogether at last, \r\nas the two proud parents of my art.\\\"\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nThere does seem to be a parallel between producing art,\r\nand producing children: You - the artist, the parent - guess, try, hope,\r\nand then expose something through which you are vulnerable.\r\nWhile people plan, wait, and fail, other really good thing happen by accident.\r\nLife is funny, that way.\r\n</p>',3,946,0,0,'192.203.136.254','en'),(22493,3954,'2006-03-31 22:37:58',240,'xep','you know, griece, no one writes about pooh like you.  no one.  it is your special gift.',0,87,0,0,'69.17.112.129','en'),(22494,3954,'2006-04-03 01:46:42',93,'chiamattt','heh. ',1,5,0,0,'211.253.15.130','en'),(22495,3957,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',66,'Peter','<br><tt><i>\"...to give is to receive...\"</i></tt>',1,55,0,0,'130.219.8.253','en'),(22496,3953,'2006-04-04 19:33:57',142,'oof','hmm!',1,4,175,0,'136.167.255.151','en'),(22497,3957,'2006-04-06 17:23:38',742,'an_impossible_child','huh?',0,4,66,0,'81.154.142.70','en'),(22498,3957,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',66,'Peter','<br><tt>thats what <i>\'dare quam accipere\'</i> means... ;)</tt>',1,69,742,0,'130.219.8.253','en'),(22499,3959,'2006-04-12 00:09:43',66,'Peter','<br><tt>so why do you write as \\\"mute\\\" now?</tt>',1,53,0,0,'24.45.9.118','en'),(22500,3959,'2006-04-12 20:01:40',741,'mute','options.',1,8,66,0,'64.128.136.170','en'),(22501,2509,'2006-04-27 06:46:26',177,'pony','Bwaahaaha...i\\\'m reading this four years later and wondering why the hell I commented with a quote from Yoda.',4,111,0,0,'67.160.220.128','en'),(22502,2509,'2006-04-27 18:04:43',17,'austin','those were crazy, crazy times.\r\n<BR><BR>\r\nthe good old days.',1,60,177,0,'68.6.212.249','en'),(22503,3953,'2006-04-28 23:13:23',74,'jo','austin swinney, that is one of the greatest and most interesting little pieces of text i have ever read on this site. ',1,118,17,0,'66.179.216.253','en'),(22504,3953,'2006-04-29 07:58:12',17,'austin','bangin\\\'!  I still got it.',1,28,74,0,'68.6.212.249','en'),(22505,3953,'2006-05-01 12:02:28',400,'elaine','<p>and whomever.</P>\r\n<p>\\\"now i just sit on chat and tell lies full of spelling errors in chat rooms\\\"</p>\r\n<p> seems to me to be a perfectly legit writing form. art making in whatever medium is not necessarily about praise, but it is about communication, and about audience, even if the audience is small or transitory. as a person, no matter how veneralbly aged, i still feel totally misunderstood for large scads of time. whenever i manage to get something down into a word or picture form, if someone so much as tips me a wink or even so much as shrugs back i feel less isolated. the fact that i have somewhat \\\'professsionalised\\\' this activity does not detract from the exercise of trying to communicate, and the fact that it is about reaching out does not make it \\\'mere\\\' therapy.</p>',1,805,17,0,'62.56.9.75','en'),(22506,3954,'2006-05-01 12:15:39',400,'elaine','<p>i once shat myself while i was in my car. diarrhea is not soemething you can hang on to and is no respecter of circumstance. i sat in my own poo in my parking space, eyeing the route across the VERY overlooked square, and thinking about the stairs, and wondering about my strategy. i considered taking off what i was wearing and trying to manage the situation a bit in the car before going in, but i decided, in the end that that would be even messier, and the illusion of privacy in a car really is just an illusion. so i walked across the square, and up the three flights of stairs, stinking and slithering in my pants. it was disgusting. nothing happened, no one \\\'caught\\\' me, it was a purely internal, personal humiliation. and now i have shared it with you. feel the love.</p>',0,789,0,0,'62.56.9.75','en'),(22507,3954,'2006-05-01 15:10:32',66,'Peter','<br><tt><i>\\\"...stinking and slithering in my pants...\\\"</i><br><br>now thats imagery for you!</tt>',1,103,400,0,'130.219.8.253','en'),(22508,3954,'2006-05-02 23:00:10',17,'austin','wasn\\\'t it just a bit satisfying though?',1,42,400,0,'68.6.212.249','en'),(22509,3954,'2006-05-03 00:22:36',66,'Peter','<br><tt>cmon, aus10. have you shat your pants before? be honest...</tt>',1,71,17,0,'24.45.7.227','en'),(22510,3954,'2006-05-03 20:47:06',195,'matt','seems to me like every time i shit my pants, i just happen to be sans underwear.',1,80,0,0,'64.128.136.170','en'),(22511,3967,'2006-05-03 22:35:46',93,'chiamattt','dude, you should seriously think about chewing a few imodium every time you leave your home. heh',1,96,0,0,'58.226.158.76','en'),(22512,3970,'2006-05-16 17:44:03',82,'simon','haha! cherries! dude the other day i woke up from a dream where my magazine\\\'s entire staff was herded into the conference room where we were given ice cream and told the magazine was folding, effective immediately, and we were all fired.',0,240,0,0,'209.21.99.118','en'),(22513,3970,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',66,'Peter','<br><tt>dood, they were like the pickled maraschino cherries that you let rot in the jar in the fridge and shit. all over the floor, carpeted wall-to-wall. but yo, that 