',496,'chemicalpilate','Dude, balls, tripping, me.\r\n\r\nPancakes: cook a bunch on the weekend.  Put pairs of pancakes in ziplock bags and freeze them.  Microwave and toaster-over on weekday mornings for homemade goodness.  A SDB tried-and-true idea!',1,223,0,0,'69.17.112.117','en'),(22554,3996,'2006-10-05 05:34:39',705,'mjoyce','dude your sister is cute!',0,25,0,0,'24.130.107.33','en'),(22555,3996,'2006-10-06 23:21:51',251,'jamie','i second that',6,13,0,0,'81.179.99.62','en'),(22556,3996,'2006-10-07 03:35:38',82,'simon','bro, your sister is hot.',1,24,0,0,'72.78.6.71','en'),(22557,4000,'2006-10-08 19:20:04',195,'matt','article 4000',0,12,0,0,'72.184.213.54','en'),(22558,3996,'2006-10-10 02:00:12',175,'Paul G','Happy (belated) birthday, OMS!  I tried to post-up \\\"appendage\\\" pics, but: (1) I don\\\'t have a laptop; and (2) my little sister said, \\\"No fucking way.\\\"\r\n<p>\r\n<i>\r\n...and that was before she saw yours getting perved.\r\n</i>\r\n</p>',1,240,0,0,'192.203.136.254','en'),(22559,3996,'2006-10-19 02:30:31',240,'xep','macbook',0,7,0,0,'69.17.112.129','en'),(22560,3990,'2006-10-19 02:33:30',240,'xep','Choice fragments taken from spam rearranged into a more satisfying format:                                                              \r\n                                                                                \r\n                                                                                \r\nWhen I first arose screaming from my sleep                                      \r\nit was, indeed, raining.                                                        \r\nWe actually had to wait in a starting line,                                     \r\nbut there were no other people                                                  \r\nIs this technology helping in life                                              \r\neven if some of us get the rage?                                                \r\nI\\\'m glad Kendra \\\"smoked\\\" Craig.                                                 \r\nyou\\\'re allowed to do that,                                                      \r\nyou\\\'re just not allowed to share it.                                            \r\ncontrolling the display                                                         \r\nthis is perfect                                                                 \r\nTalk about reasons not to get up.                                               \r\nScratch that, it can be wrong and still great.                                  \r\nWe just like to judge.        ',0,1413,0,0,'69.17.112.129','en'),(22561,3999,'2006-10-19 22:00:58',155,'blue stocking','wow. there are lines in this that burn a person if they stand too close. \r\n\r\np.s. what the heck happened to swinney? it used to be so alive before. ',0,148,0,0,'67.70.129.155','en'),(22562,3996,'2006-10-19 22:01:27',155,'blue stocking','i don\\\'t have a laptop. i feel so left out.',0,45,0,0,'67.70.129.155','en'),(22563,3999,'2006-10-20 01:30:29',195,'matt','come to think of it, i know a disturbed young ma.',1,49,0,0,'72.184.213.54','en'),(22564,3999,'2006-10-20 01:32:14',195,'matt','entropy.',1,8,155,0,'72.184.213.54','en'),(22565,3996,'2006-10-24 20:47:52',17,'austin','i like how i intended for people to submit pictures in the same sort of pose, but all i got were cat calls to my sister.',1,120,0,0,'69.17.112.129','en'),(22566,3996,'2006-10-24 23:13:09',195,'matt','i looked at the comments page after noting that that bit of porno spam was article 4000 and saw that my comment was juxtaposed right after the three about your sister.  that wasn\\\'t intentional.  i was just remarking on that number being reached, be it by an unsolicited computer-generated submission or whatever.  sorry if it might have seemed otherwise.<BR><BR>and, you know, as far as the site goes, the community, people participating, whatever, it seems like this is the culmination of a process that started a few years ago.  i was in rehab from the beginning of \\\'04 until almost the end of april of that year, and when i got out, i noticed that traffic on here had markedly decreased.  i don\\\'t know if it had anything to do with whatever it was that happened with olivia (never got the story on that) or what, but it was exponentially less active.<BR><BR>and since then, regrettably, there\\\'s been some infighting, flame wars, bad blood.  and over the last few months, traffic has dropped off to virtually nothing.  i don\\\'t know if those two have anything to do with each other, or if people have just gotten bored, moved on....  the few regulars that were left are not so regular anymore.<BR><BR>which is all unfortunate.  because i feel like i got to know some of you better than real life people i\\\'ve known.  to the point where, at times, this was my only social outlet.  which isn\\\'t very healthy, i know.  i\\\'ll have to get out in the world and find some people i can relate to, which is all for the best, i suppose.<BR><BR>but i predict a renaissance.  maybe not for a year or two, but eventually.  everybody returns to their past haunts sometime or other.  nostalgia, the comfort of the known, the circular nature of human behavior.  you\\\'ll see.  ',1,1784,17,0,'24.26.7.38','en'),(22567,3996,'2006-10-25 19:14:55',66,'Peter','<br><tt>i check this site daily, as i have for more than half a decade. im sure im not the only one that just lurks, commenting now and then, making an arbitrary thought or two, waiting for new content to appear... maybe <i>i</i> need to get in the writing mood again, myself. and stop waiting around. perhaps that will bring out another old lurker who will comment or write something, and bring out another lurker, etc... hmm...</tt>',1,434,195,0,'130.219.8.253','en'),(22568,3996,'2006-10-25 20:22:35',195,'matt','yeah, i think that\\\'s probably the case - it\\\'s a cycle where it\\\'s gotten ever more quiet - nothing new to comment on so there are no new comments.<BR><BR>and i think people aren\\\'t lurking so much as they figure that things have gotten really slow, so they just check in every few weeks.  and that contributes to the cycle.<BR><BR>i\\\'ve noticed that a lot of people have kind of cooled to livejournal, too.  must mean they have a life outside the internet....',1,471,66,0,'24.26.7.38','en'),(22569,3996,'2006-10-25 23:12:29',66,'Peter','<br><tt>...or maybe its just you and me on here, who knows!</tt>',1,64,195,0,'24.45.8.18','en'),(22570,3996,'2006-10-25 23:13:30',66,'Peter','<br><tt>also... swinney, yer sister is hawt.</tt>',1,49,17,0,'24.45.8.18','en'),(22571,3996,'2006-10-26 22:54:35',93,'chiamattt','I check this site every morning as well, but I have devolved into pretty much only using the chat feature.',1,106,0,0,'211.202.17.229','en'),(22572,2757,'2006-11-13 04:31:02',195,'matt','that last comment is the only google-recognized occurence of <i>the night people are after the day people</i>, even though that is a wynton marsalis quote from the ken burns jazz documentary.<BR><BR>somehow, i have become a day person.  in the last three weeks.  i don\\\'t know why.  my eyes pop open as soon as the light hits the window.  i think it\\\'s something to do with getting the right thyroid treatment, finally.<BR><BR>and when i worked at the church, i set up chairs in the fellowship hall every friday for the old folks\\\' sunday school class.  i don\\\'t remember it ever being meditative, but i was stoned to the bone-own-own just about always, and that is probably why.<BR><BR>and once again i look at this thread and miss everybody who\\\'s gone.  come back, peoples, come back.',1,797,0,0,'24.26.7.38','en'),(22573,2757,'2006-11-19 03:47:29',17,'austin','Maybe in our golden years.',1,26,195,0,'69.17.112.129','en'),(22574,3996,'2006-11-19 06:03:49',155,'blue stocking','well, i\\\'m back.',0,18,195,0,'70.48.51.51','en'),(22575,2757,'2006-11-19 06:04:27',155,'blue stocking','hi le!!!!',0,9,65,0,'70.48.51.51','en'),(22576,4006,'2006-11-2