enr=301100375&Ref=AR\\\">what an amazing auntie! my hero!</a>',0,'66.108.188.37','en'),(27256,'2003-01-13 12:48:28',89,'sawks','\\\"\r\nA petite and determined lady with a twinkle in her eye\\\"  << all class',0,'144.132.117.109','en'),(27257,'2003-01-13 14:00:29',89,'sawks','\r\nTHE FLAT HOSE AND CALIFORNIA\\\'S \\\"PROPOSITION 65\\\" FAQ\r\n\r\n\r\nAll products sold in California, including the Flat hose, must comply with California\\\'s \\\"Safe Drinking Water and Toxic Enforcement Act of 1986,\\\" which is commonly referred to as \\\"Prop 65.\\\" Prop 65 requires manufacturers to put warnings on products sold in that state if they may expose consumers to any substance that is on a list of substances that have been identified by the State of California to cause cancer, birth defects or other reproductive harm. These substances may be naturally occurring or synthetic. Many products sold in California have this warning even though the warning does not appear on the same products sold in other states.\r\n\r\nBy putting a warning on the Flat Hose, we are informing the public that one or more of the substances on the Prop 65 list may be present in the hose. We provide this warning simply because one or more of the substances may be present, without undertaking an evaluation of potential exposure. The actual risk from exposure to these substances from drinking water from a hose could be below the Proposition 65 level of concern or even nonexistent.\r\n\r\nFor more information about Proposition 65 from The State of California, go to www.oehha.ca.gov/prop65/background/p65plain.html. For more information about Proposition 65 from The American Council on Science and Health, visit www.acsh.org/press/releases/prop65_120500.html.\r\n\r\nCAN I DRINK WATER FROM THE FLAT HOSE?\r\n\r\nYou should not drink water from the Flat Hose, or from any hose that does not expressly state that it is safe for drinking water use (and is maintained for that use).\r\n\r\nIn addition to possibly consuming substances that the hose itself is made out of, there are more obvious reasons for not drinking water from a garden hose. Garden hoses are exposed to dirt, insects, rodents, pet urine, rust, and yard chemicals. Obviously, the hose may have germs, bacteria and toxins from these and other sources, and if you drink water from the hose, these things can end up inside of you. It is especially important to instruct your children not to drink from a garden hose. You wouldn\\\'t let them drink from a glass of water that had been sitting outside for days! ',0,'144.132.117.109','en'),(27258,'2003-01-13 16:01:35',17,'austin','morning',0,'64.2.58.24','en'),(27259,'2003-01-13 16:46:41',175,'Paul G','http://monograph.org/taxi/pics/garage14.jpg',0,'67.195.79.219','en'),(27260,'2003-01-13 17:23:43',86,'egg','death dont have no mercy',0,'199.4.104.129','en'),(27261,'2003-01-13 18:41:56',66,'Peter','<img src=\\\"http://www.oricomtech.com/projects/dalek2.gif\\\">',0,'204.168.247.130','en'),(27262,'2003-01-13 19:38:45',195,'matt','exterminate!',0,'24.129.129.219','en'),(27263,'2003-01-13 20:10:48',17,'austin','I love my J-Pop.',0,'64.2.58.24','en'),(27264,'2003-01-13 20:20:10',129,'dr who','jellybaby, anyone?',0,'148.87.1.170','en'),(27265,'2003-01-13 21:02:29',234,'etienne','being back at work is weird',0,'210.54.120.200','en'),(27266,'2003-01-13 22:13:01',129,'moebius','work is weird, period',0,'148.87.1.170','en'),(27267,'2003-01-13 22:20:30',83,'adamajah','needs mastadon',0,'66.13.23.218','en'),(27268,'2003-01-13 22:30:39',17,'austin','i have oof\\\'s eyesight',0,'64.2.58.24','en'),(27269,'2003-01-13 22:33:14',122,'hool','<img src=\\\"http://inconduit.com/image/rand/bw212_400.jpg\\\" border=\\\"0\\\">',0,'66.185.85.80','en'),(27270,'2003-01-13 23:31:02',195,'matt','pictures of lily made my life so wonderful<BR>pictures of lily helped me sleep at night',0,'209.208.111.156','en'),(27271,'2003-01-14 00:52:42',66,'Peter','pictures help me compartmentalize my reality',0,'66.10