es and those more left-leaning? didn\\\'t bush win by creating a consensus on the right that gore abjectly failed to do with the left? (if we put aside the questionable legalese that was used to hijack the election in the end.) i\\\'m with sean on this one. nader-bashing, by your logic, ignores much larger, and frankly more frightening, problems inherent in the american democratic process. perhaps that postulation is what\\\'s behind the cheerful castigation of sean\\\'s arguments.',0,'24.192.68.235','en'),(32868,'2004-02-24 08:44:41',129,'moebius','interesting commentary from a kid who also believes in the existence of The Great Pumpkin and goes nowhere without his security blanket....',0,'63.203.70.163','en'),(32869,'2004-02-24 08:54:16',129,'moebius','also: i liked the part in today\\\'s White House press briefing where the reporters asked Scott McClellan \\\"so, just how loud was the cheering here when Nader announded his candidacy?\\\"',0,'63.203.70.163','en'),(32870,'2004-02-24 09:04:29',370,'the great pumpkin','ima get you suckers',0,'24.69.255.236','en'),(32871,'2004-02-24 09:30:53',370,'seanthecon','nader took a whopping three percent of the vote in the 2000 election. 25 percent of that came from republicans. 38 from democrats. \\\'special interest\\\' kerry won\\\'t change a damn thing in america. people are not voting on politics but personality. i don\\\'t think there is anything amusing about this at all. i\\\'m just shocked that america\\\'s gross flaws and faults have suddenly been shifted onto a skinney and boring consumer rights advocate that managed to strike a chord with three percent of half the registered voters in the US.',0,'24.69.255.236','en'),(32872,'2004-02-24 16:16:29',66,'Peter','gotta love coming here in the morning and finding american political pedagogy from the canadians.',0,'156.145.58.57','en'),(32873,'2004-02-24 16:50:04',129,'moebius','maybe. sometimes i think canadians know more about our political system than most US citizens d