d investments just like we do.  We	no longer live in a world of nations and ideologies, Mr. Beale.  The	world is a college of corporations, inexorably deter- mined by the immutable by-laws of business.  The world is a business, Mr. Beale!  It has been since man crawled out of the slime, and our children, Mr. Beale, will live to see that perfect world in which there is no war and famine, oppression and brutality -- one vast and ecumenical holding company, for whom all men will work to serve a common profit, in which	all men will hold a share of stock, all necessities provided, all anxieties tranquilized, all boredom amused.  And I have chosen you to preach this evangel, Mr. Beale.<BR><BR>HOWARD:  (humble whisper)  Why me?<BR><BR>JENSEN:  Because you\\\'re on television, dummy.  Sixty million people watch you every night of the week, Monday through Friday.',0,'207.239.93.170','en'),(33991,'2004-08-31 03:38:06',17,'austin','biotch.',0,'','en'),(33992,'2004-08-31 16:07:14',74,'jo','all in all, the total tally of august: my best friend and i stopped talking, my friend\\\'s cousin who was taking care of her dying grandmother died of a drug overdose, one of my oldest friends moved away and is miserable and i miss the shit out of her, another friend broke up with his boyfriend, an friend\\\'s  father lost the fight with cancer. for 3 weeks i wept once every day and got drunk every night and spent most days walking around with my hand over my heart, worried that it would just fall right out of my chest if i didn\\\'t. good fucking riddance, august. ',0,'216.142.229.132','en'),(33993,'2004-08-31 18:57:43',17,'austin','i tend to buy things on ebay.',0,'','en'),(33994,'2004-08-31 18:58:00',17,'austin','also, i poisoned myself with lysol Sunday night.',0,'','en'),(33995,'2004-08-31 22:48:26',17,'austin','fuck.',0,'','en'),(33996,'2004-09-01 03:24:03',57,'weeb','lysol\\\'s some cheap drinks, austie',0,'66.92.219.22','en'),(33997,'2004-09-01 17:43:31',67,'trouble','that\\\'s some 