-09 22:54:15',66,'Peter','austin: come visit nyc. its never boring here.',0,'141.155.152.166','en'),(34890,'2004-12-10 00:03:34',74,'jo','everything is the fault of texas.',0,'','en'),(34891,'2004-12-10 00:45:18',66,'Peter','and nyc is the solution to most things. imagine that.',0,'','en'),(34892,'2004-12-10 00:45:26',66,'Peter','drugs take care of the rest.',0,'','en'),(34893,'2004-12-10 03:56:42',195,'matt','well, they are effective, aren\\\'t they?  i have very vivid recollections of how effective they are.  recollections that wake me up at night, leave me speechless in the middle of conversations.  right now, i\\\'m wondering how long it might take my little auxilary boyfriend to lay his hands on some black tar.  i don\\\'t know if he\\\'s using regularly, but i\\\'m sure he knows where to get some.  here in the study.  they\\\'re out there, probably talking about me.  came over here for my protection, but you really can\\\'t protect yourself from yourself.  got so fucking angry at aftercare tonight about the ineffectivess of rehab, 12-step, god.  people falling away all around me.  i bet i could pop the screen out of the window and go right over the top of this desk.  how long before they would miss me?  i could get downtown by then.  hell, i could even run, bad as that would hurt.  find david, probably go to some mexican\\\'s apartment over towards the grocery store, talk to the guy about how he\\\'s going home for christmas.  david would pay for it.  back to mine, do it up and stare at the ceiling fan going around for four hours.  because it\\\'s every day.  and it\\\'s never going to stop until i\\\'m dead.  which is probably not that far off.  because i can take measures to keep all the demons in the world out of my apartment, but i can\\\'t do a damned thing about the one who lives there.  you can\\\'t cheat death.  because my time was up in january, and this is all the afterworld.  it isn\\\'t worth it.  i give up.',0,'','en'),(34894,'2004-12-10 04:08:08'