local likker store outta grey goose. time to switch to OE800 :',0,'68.28.123.108','en'),(35295,'2005-01-18 03:39:57',66,'Peter','hmm. a fellow musician tripped over sines cord, sending her violin tumbling. the neck of the violin broke off. super #1 suck. ouch!',0,'68.28.123.108','en'),(35296,'2005-01-18 03:40:42',66,'Peter','consult her lj',0,'68.28.123.108','en'),(35297,'2005-01-18 03:54:21',66,'Peter','the cult of the supreme being.',0,'68.28.123.108','en'),(35298,'2005-01-18 06:11:25',17,'austin','there is nothing on the lj',0,'','en'),(35299,'2005-01-18 15:17:18',74,'jo','matt, you\'re crazy, charlie kaufman OWNS',0,'216.142.229.132','en'),(35300,'2005-01-18 16:03:47',66,'Peter','my emplyer\'s HR website reads: <i>\"Provides profesional adminastrative and analitical support for the the Universities Compensation Program\"</i>. wow. someone must have written that in a real hurry.',0,'','en'),(35301,'2005-01-18 17:54:07',195,'matt','just because something\'s strange or clever, just because it may be critically acclaimed, just because there seems to be peer pressure to like it, doesn\'t mean it\'s good.  it didn\'t push my buttons, i didn\'t care about those characters, at all.  it was more an exercise than a movie.  (in that regard, <B><I>memento</B></I> sucks, too.)<BR><BR>i didn\'t laugh once.  or cry or wonder or become awed or tremble or have the electricity running down my back.  i\'m not really interested in art that doesn\'t make me feel something.<BR><BR>go watch it again.  there\'s nothing to it.  total emperor\'s new clothes.  the charlie kaufman character states quite plainly that there\'s no way a movie can be made out of the book.  and then he proceeds to write a screenplay about how he can\'t write a screenplay.  and then he makes it about drugs, exactly what he said he wouldn\'t do.  and ends it with a <I>deus ex machina</I>, just like he was cautioned against.  it was nothing but solipsism.<BR><BR>but i\'ll probably turn around and do something just like it someday.<BR><BR>maybe the other movies are different.  will i spend money to see them?  doubtful.  catch them on cable someday, maybe.<BR><BR>(the movie referenced deconstructionism, a philosophy unfamiliar to me.  i researched jacques derrida, and, although he did some good things socially, he was otherwise full of shit.  more clothing.<BR><BR>as a con man, i can appreciate it when other people get over, but that doesn\'t mean i don\'t resent it just as much as the next man when i get taken.',0,'24.92.185.89','en'),(35302,'2005-01-18 18:36:29',508,'ed','if we\'re talking about eternal sunshine... you\'re wrong. memento did suck, eternal sunshine did not. nevermind about buttons... kaufman goes beyond that, even if you do not like his movies, you cannot deny his art. really.',0,'193.11.88.235','en'),(35303,'2005-01-18 18:39:47',534,'griece','yes, if your opinions on a film do not conform to the status quo, it is not valid. conform! conform!',0,'','en'),(35304,'2005-01-18 19:16:51',508,'ed','yeah, totally. we just need to save some shit-ass hollywood rom-coms to have something left to devote all our hate on.',0,'193.11.88.235','en'),(35305,'2005-01-18 19:34:52',129,'moebius','<--just now clueing into \"<a href=\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/lj/user_lj.phtml?uid=129\">tripe from livejournal</a>\" reaction? \"cool!\"',0,'','en'),(35306,'2005-01-18 19:35:22',129,'moebius','hi everyone!',0,'','en'),(35307,'2005-01-18 20:23:42',66,'Peter','<a href=\"http://www.thebestlinks.com/Markovian_Parallax_Denigrate.html#\">http://www.thebestlinks.com/Markovian_Parallax_Denigrate.html#</a>',0,'','en'),(35308,'2005-01-18 20:49:20',508,'ed','concerning lj-tripe: should be linked with an icon instead of that \">> LJ\"',0,'193.11.88.235','en'),(35309,'2005-01-18 23:19:23',17,'austin','i dont think the livejournal tripe thing is working',0,'63.80.97.254','en'),(35310,'2005-01-19 05:00:05',74,'jo','oh i completely misunderstood. i ONLY like things if they\'re strange or clever or critically acclaimed or my friends liked it. i don\'t actually like kaufman because i have a mind of my own and i enjoy the shit out of his films. thank god you cleared that up, matt.',0,'216.142.229.132','en'),(35311,'2005-01-19 05:00:33',74,'jo','snarky jo &copy; 2001',0,'216.142.229.132','en'),(35312,'2005-01-19 05:24:48',82,'simon','heh',0,'24.215.233.23','en'),(35313,'2005-01-19 05:33:52',261,'sine','my violin is dead. so depressed right now.',0,'68.28.115.108','en'),(35314,'2005-01-19 07:51:51',177,'pony','<a href=\"http://images8.fotki.com/v145/photos/2/23376/93737/mordor-vi.gif\">ninja wizards!</a>',0,'24.7.71.79','en'),(35315,'2005-01-19 09:35:19',195,'matt','i\'m not attacking your taste.  i just said it was strange, it was clever, it was critically acclaimed, and just about everybody seemed to like it, but i couldn\'t see anything else there.  it puzzles me.  those things can be confused with quality, which i think happened in this case.  i\'m not accusing you of anything; i\'m not saying it isn\'t a great picture if you think it\'s great.  i\'m just stating my opinion.  try not to take it personally.<BR><BR>does anyone have a mind of their own?  i know i don\'t.  we\'re all influenced to some degree or another.  just about everyone is a member of one or more demographic groups and the target of aggressive marketing.  it\'s hard to see through the hype sometimes.  we\'d like things to be good.  we need good art, to be able to think, <I>i am delighted that this is going to be representative of my era.</I>  but there aren\'t many candidates for that.  just about all of it sucks, and hype is mistaken for quality.  there are only so many products (books, movies, cds) targeted towards our demographic at one time, and if you swallow the party line, they\'re all very excellent.  and people buy that.  they\'re pummelled with it in magazines, newspapers, tv, the internet.<BR><BR>and one can\'t help but be influenced by one\'s peer group.  the tyranny of cool.  everybody considers themselves a nonconformist these days, but the reality of it is that the lifestyle template is pretty dogmatic.  i would venture that, within a certain range, discounting racial, gender, sexual, background differences, your peer group is pretty homogenous.  same tastes, political views, dress, vernacular, etc.  <I>it was a mostly male audience of slender, peacoat-and-knit-cap-wearing smokers.</I>  that doesn\'t sound very appealing.  sounds pretty strictured.  not much room for dissent.<BR><BR>i paid five bucks for the dvd.  i wanted it to be good.  roger ebert gave it four stars.  i was disappointed.  but if people like it, more power to them.  it\'s great that we\'re all different people with different viewpoints, all of them valid.',0,'24.92.185.89','en'),(35316,'2005-01-19 14:38:10',74,'jo','okay matt, when you quoted me, you quoted me talking about an audience at an interpol show, not my peer group. sara and i were very much outside the classification of peacoatknitcapsmoking skinny boys. it was just interesting to me that they made up the majority of the crowd. and i didn\'t take it personally, i just think that the anti-populist argument is as tired as the populist argument. implying that those were the only reasons i might have liked adaptation since you didn\'t find it to be a good movie was a cheap shot. you got on and said you didn\'t like charlie kaufman. i got on and said, you\'re crazy, i think he owns. there was no need to turn that into a rant about the plight of media, matt. it\'s just taste.',0,'','en'),(35317,'2005-01-19 15:12:42',66,'Peter','holey schmoley! the ljtripe is completely fux3d.',0,'130.219.136.217','en'),(35318,'2005-01-19 15:13:20',66,'Peter','also: novella-sized thoughts. egads!',0,'130.219.136.217','en'),(35319,'2005-01-19 15:13:34',66,'Peter','three more and i can make it go away.',0,'130.219.136.217','en'),(35320,'2005-01-19 15:13:45',66,'Peter','two',0,'130.219.136.217','en'),(35321,'2005-01-19 15:13:47',66,'Peter','one',0,'130.219.136.217','en'),(35322,'2005-01-19 15:13:52',66,'Peter',':D',0,'130.219.136.217','en'),(35323,'2005-01-19 16:18:23',74,'jo','thanks, peter',0,'','en'),(35324,'2005-01-19 16:33:07',195,'matt','yes, you\'re right.  that <U>was</U> a cheap shot.i\'m sorry.  i\'m an asshole sometimes.  thanks for calling me on it.<BR><BR>friends?',0,'24.92.185.89','en'),(35325,'2005-01-19 19:08:02',496,'chemicalpilate','So does anyone else think the new Caribou record is really fantastic?',0,'','en'),(35326,'2005-01-19 19:10:16',534,'griece','what do you think this is, some sort of scenester discussion board?',0,'','en'),(35327,'2005-01-19 19:10:26',277,'moebius','so it\'s leaked, then? i was supposed to get a promo copy, but no dice. sigh.',0,'148.87.1.170','en'),(35328,'2005-01-19 19:11:09',277,'moebius','whoops! i only play a scenester on tv. sorry.',0,'148.87.1.170','en'),(35329,'2005-01-19 19:11:21',74,'jo','friends.',0,'216.142.229.132','en'),(35330,'2005-01-19 19:13:47',74,'jo','i can\'t be a scenester because i can never keep track if i like things for real or ironically. how do those kids KEEP IT STRAIGHT? i\'m all like, \"wait, do i like the strokes for real or do i roll my eyes when i\'m talking about their second album? wait, why do i think nebraska was springsteen\'s only good album? IS THE NEW WILCO GOOD OR BAD, GOOD OR BAD?\" it\'s exhausting. plus all that hair product!',0,'216.142.229.132','en'),(35331,'2005-01-19 19:14:19',74,'jo','all the springsteen albums are awesome.',0,'216.142.229.132','en'),(35332,'2005-01-19 19:14:30',496,'chemicalpilate','Love me?',0,'137.131.205.145','en'),(35333,'2005-01-19 19:14:53',534,'griece','i dont know any of these bands yer al ltalking about. cept for the boss. the boss rocks.',0,'','en'),(35334,'2005-01-19 19:16:09',496,'chemicalpilate','That handkerchief in the Boss\'s pocket, what color was it and what kind of action is he after???',0,'137.131.205.145','en'),(35335,'2005-01-19 19:16:50',277,'moebius','i\'m too old to really be a scenester. plus (confession) i rarely ever go out to live shows anymore. most of the folks i hang out with that are my age have absolutely no idea what i\'m on about 95% of the time, even if they were hipsters themselves, somewhen. \'s kinda lonely, being green. but i wouldn\'t have it any other way.',0,'148.87.1.170','en'),(35336,'2005-01-19 19:19:37',277,'moebius','thing is, i\'m fascinated by trends. all the weird crazy things people get into. i may not personally care for them myself, but i love following their ascendance/decline & seeing what\'s next. (apparently, it\'s reggaeton, but don\'t quote me on that)',0,'148.87.1.170','en'),(35337,'2005-01-19 19:22:47',277,'moebius','oh, and Caribou = Manitoba, if that clears anything up (ha). dude was forced to change his act\'s name fer legal reasons.',0,'148.87.1.170','en'),(35338,'2005-01-19 19:27:14',534,'griece','doesnt ring a bell. and what the hell is reggaeton?',0,'','en'),(35339,'2005-01-19 19:35:02',277,'moebius','<a href=\"http://www.stylusmagazine.com/feature.php?ID=1326\">reggaeton</a> is something you\'d be all over if you happened to have a penchant for latin pop. it\'s kinda like gangsta rap crossed with dancehall and various trad. latin dance music (salsa, merengue, etc.). started in central america, now hails mainly from Puerto Rico, the Dominican Republic, and, well, Miami. reggaeton artists like Daddy Freddy and <a href=\"http://www.mtv.com/bands/az/n_o_r_e_/artist.jhtml\">N.O.R.E.</a> are poised to crossover in a big way over the next couple yrs.',0,'148.87.1.170','en'),(35340,'2005-01-19 19:39:49',277,'moebius','whoa...Daddy Freddy is dancehall. i meant <a href=\"http://www.miaminewtimes.com/issues/2004-11-18/localheroes4.html\">Daddy Yankee</a> (lordy, i can\'t keep anything straight)',0,'148.87.1.170','en'),(35341,'2005-01-19 23:51:43',67,'trouble','i got N.O.R.E\'s \'Gods favorite\' disc a long time ago because i thought \'Nothin\' carried almost the same beat as Eric Se