of hours at night.  it was usually commandeered by four young guys - pat, jeremy, brandon, dean.  their viewing tastes ranged from mtv2 to bet.<BR><BR>this time last year, brian and i managed to wrangle it away from them to watch the state of the union address.  they were all like, <I>you suck</I>.<BR><BR>i liked when bush was enumerating the issues that had to be taken care of in the year ahead, and he said that the patriot act was going to expire in 2005, and all the democrats clapped.  he looked over at them and kind of smirked.  that was classic.',0,'24.92.186.239','en'),(35511,'2005-02-02 21:39:47',154,'ryan','it was his death stare',0,'206.228.191.196','en'),(35512,'2005-02-03 06:12:49',177,'pony','etienne....do you live in Auckland? ',0,'24.7.71.79','en'),(35513,'2005-02-03 06:14:43',177,'pony','i must needs chat with someone in that part of the world....',0,'24.7.71.79','en'),(35514,'2005-02-03 06:14:49',177,'pony','please?',0,'24.7.71.79','en'),(35515,'2005-02-03 06:34:57',195,'matt','i have not asked the refugees i\'ve come in contact with about their lives.  i would not presume.  in no way am i worthy to hear it, and it\'s none of my business.<BR><BR>i have, however, talked to the people who are trained to help them deal with the trauma inflicted upon them.<BR><BR>i used to think i was the survivor of a holocaust (of fate and my own making), but my history is nothing, absolutely nothing, in comparison to what these people have been through.  imagine being forced from your home, losing everything you own, losing track of everyone you ever knew, being imprisoned for years, suffering utter humiliation, undergoing torture, watching your children or other family members get killed in front of you.<BR><BR>i can\'t imagine that.  i can\'t imagine it happening to me.  i\'m spoiled.  consider yourself blessed.',0,'24.92.186.239','en'),(35516,'2005-02-03 19:09:35',154,'ryan','dong',0,'206.228.191.196','en'),(35517,'2005-02-03 19:20:46',66,'Peter','one two three fou