bout this family of sites that people write on (swinney / lj / citynoise / whatever ) is that it gives readers a more immersive experience.  they can read your fiction and frame it in the context of your journal and the journal of your girlfriend, and your friends.  and that is neat.',0,'','en'),(35885,'2005-03-12 06:43:47',17,'austin','kicking ass / taking nametags.',0,'','en'),(35886,'2005-03-12 20:09:34',604,'jdfalk','I\'ve recently been re-reading Asimov\'s Foundation series, and I was struck by the total lack of poetry in his writing.  Great stuff, but clearly written by a scientist.<br>I think a lot of \"hard\" science fiction is like that -- there\'s no poetry, no narrative.  Writing something self-contained is a goal of mine as well, but I don\'t want to lose the good parts of my narrative voice in the process.',0,'64.81.66.81','en'),(35887,'2005-03-12 20:51:37',66,'Peter','...then theres p. k. dick.',0,'','en'),(35888,'2005-03-13 17:24:06',587,'ackman','...Ellison, Bradbury, sometimes Benford',0,'','en'),(35896,'2005-03-14 06:44:48',17,'austin','cause i cancel yo shit!',0,'','en'),(35895,'2005-03-14 06:20:38',496,'chemicalpilate','Why not?',0,'','en'),(35894,'2005-03-13 22:43:39',17,'austin','why annoy me?',0,'','en'),(35897,'2005-03-14 07:37:28',17,'austin','i took a hot bath and now i feel to good to want sleep.',0,'','en'),(35898,'2005-03-14 17:44:56',240,'xep','woke up early.  lounged in a sunbeam for two hours.',0,'','en'),(35899,'2005-03-14 20:27:47',496,'chemicalpilate','It has now become a <a href=\"http://www.nytimes.com/2005/03/13/politics/13covert.html?oref=login\">literal parade</a> of bullshit.',0,'','en'),(35900,'2005-03-14 20:28:07',496,'chemicalpilate','oops: login/pass = iamaguest/iamaguest',0,'','en'),(35901,'2005-03-14 20:29:42',195,'matt','well, the man has won three hugo awards and three nebulas, so he\'s well-regarded among his peers, anyway.  i don\'t know how much poetry there is in his stuff.  genre fictioin doesn\'t always aim for style points.<BR><BR>it <U>would</U> be hard to publish anything of mine on here, for instance, the kristi and jamie stuff, exactly because of the context.  he was right about that.  there\'s too much backstory involved, and the readers know me in ways you wouldn\'t know somebody who\'s book you\'re reading.<BR><BR>then again, there\'s the hemingway iceberg theory that states that you only have to know a little about someone, and their history will be filled in by the reader, and their character will be dictated by their thoughts and their speech and their actions.',0,'','en'),(35902,'2005-03-14 21:44:27',587,'ackman','...Jeter. ',0,'67.117.130.91','en'),(35903,'2005-03-14 21:45:00',587,'ackman','A Song Called Youth',0,'67.117.130.91','en'),(35904,'2005-03-15 00:21:47',66,'Peter','<A href=\"http://saturn5.com/~peter/volvo/low240.jpg\">our car</a>.',0,'','en'),(35905,'2005-03-15 02:41:31',17,'austin','does it go up too?',0,'','en'),(35906,'2005-03-15 03:15:03',66,'Peter','hell yeah man, just like every volvo stationwagon should have. theres so much room for the hydros in the back.',0,'','en'),(35907,'2005-03-15 03:49:44',587,'ackman','let\'s try KW Jeter. the original cyber-punk ',0,'','en'),(35908,'2005-03-15 03:57:49',587,'ackman','Happy Loyalty Day, citizen',0,'','en'),(35909,'2005-03-15 07:28:25',17,'austin','i\'m talking like a cowboy',0,'','en'),(35910,'2005-03-15 08:06:14',496,'chemicalpilate','It is my sincere hope that tomorrow morning will include a) sunbeams and b) kombucha.',0,'','en'),(35911,'2005-03-15 17:53:53',82,'simon','i am not in the mood for today',0,'','en'),(35912,'2005-03-15 18:26:39',66,'Peter','today is overrated, yo.',0,'','en'),(35913,'2005-03-15 18:46:26',195,'matt','i tried to tell my doctor how the subtext (is that the word i\'m looking for?) of <B><I>julius caesar</B></I> is the story of jesus christ (judas, really), and that of <B><I>hamlet</B></I> is the story of martin luther.  he said i was full of shit.',0,'','en'),(35914,'2005-03