,(36211,'2005-05-23 19:07:49',195,'matt','<A HREF=\"http://achewood.com/index.php?date=05232005\">Why come manhole covers are round?</A>',0,'','en'),(36215,'2005-05-24 17:37:56',195,'matt','you know, i can remember the days when you could go away for six hours, and the thoughts box would be totally different.  \"slow-motion chat\" is how somebody described it.  what happened?  as recently as a couple of months ago, it was positively jumping around here in comparison to this.<BR><BR>i don\'t know - maybe people get bored or slowly drift away or get pissed or feel that they aren\'t welcome anymore.  look at the users screen and see how many people aren\'t around anymore (not much, if at all).  just recently, jo up and left with what seemed like pretty definite closure.<BR><BR>i thought it would be interesting if this could turn out to be a long-term thing.  i mean, if this is still going in ten years, i plan on being here.<BR><BR>maybe i\'m expecting too much out of this.  maybe i\'ve invested too much of myself in it.  but it\'s become something beyond a website to me.  and i know that it\'s played not insignificant roles in some of your lives, too.',0,'','en'),(36216,'2005-05-24 17:40:17',195,'matt','i have no idea what can be done about it, though.',0,'','en'),(36217,'2005-05-24 18:16:16',82,'simon','hey bro',0,'','en'),(36218,'2005-05-24 19:25:47',66,'Peter','thigns move in cycles, yo. no worries.',0,'','en'),(36219,'2005-05-24 19:27:27',66,'Peter','also: the best way to get thigns jumping is to write and submit. i have something in teh works. if you write osmething too, then well have two new pieces of content this week, heh.',0,'','en'),(36220,'2005-05-24 19:27:44',66,'Peter','geez, i swear i dont make many typos at all.',0,'','en'),(36221,'2005-05-24 20:52:59',17,'austin','i sense that in the near future OS X.4 users will have a swinney.org dashboard widget for updating thoughts.  that should increase traffic since it will save the login information such that y