re Good Photojournalism.  is that enough?  ',0,'70.24.130.3','en'),(38174,'2006-01-31 03:09:04',122,'hool','the only aspect of them that is Bad Photojournalism is the terrible exposure on the first group of photos.  so very bad, in all honesty.  i hang my head for those.',0,'70.24.130.3','en'),(38175,'2006-01-31 04:39:46',66,'Peter','<img src=\\\"http://saturn5.com/peter/ljphoto/duh/googly.jpg\\\">',0,'24.46.99.165','en'),(38176,'2006-01-31 05:38:50',17,'austin','when the shit hits the fan, hool, you have to be ready. FOCUS!  BE THE CAMERA!',0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(38177,'2006-01-31 05:45:52',17,'austin','seriously, i admire your dedication.',0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(38178,'2006-01-31 05:53:22',66,'Peter','if i were rich, id comission simon totake a portrait of hool, and hool to take a portrait of simz. then hang them on my wall.',0,'24.46.99.165','en'),(38179,'2006-01-31 06:01:17',17,'austin','i\\\'m sitting here drinking ginger tea.  trying to get off the sauce you know.',0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(38180,'2006-01-31 06:25:11',195,'matt','no, i don\\\'t mean \\\"sell\\\" as in get money for them.  and the fact that a \\\"major\\\" newspaper woud print them is a sad commentary in and of itself.  because they suck harder than linda lovelace.<BR><BR>which paper?',0,'71.99.163.87','en'),(38181,'2006-01-31 06:27:26',66,'Peter','who cares? its just the internet.',0,'24.46.99.165','en'),(38182,'2006-01-31 07:57:05',148,'jeeff','what about them sucks?  i don\\\'t get it',0,'70.24.130.3','en'),(38183,'2006-01-31 08:03:25',195,'matt','they suck because they look fake.<BR><BR>anything else i can help you with?',0,'71.99.163.87','en'),(38184,'2006-01-31 08:46:05',17,'austin','matt.... be nice.',0,'68.6.211.134','en'),(38185,'2006-01-31 10:41:23',400,'elaine','but how do they look fake? obviously hool coulda photoshopped the first ones \\\'up\\\' a bit, but being the kind of photographer he is, he wouldn\\\'t. however he is the kind of photographer who brazenly photographs people every day without being cramped up by shyness, and he also has a dead on eye for colour and composition, is this why they \\\'look\\\' fake to you? because they are good photos?',0,'62.56.23.250','en'),(38186,'2006-01-31 10:54:34',251,'jamie','<a href=\\\"http://www.google.co.uk/search?q=inurl%3A%22axis-cgi%2Fmjpg%22\\\">look look look</a>',0,'213.249.154.101','en'),(38187,'2006-01-31 11:03:23',93,'chiamattt','whoa, I think matt just made a chiam comment out of pure rage and emotion. ',0,'58.226.158.76','en'),(38188,'2006-01-31 11:26:29',195,'matt','they look fake for the same reason that this looks fake:<BR><BR><img src=\\\"http://inconduit.com/gal/streets/col791_18x12_print.jpg\\\"><BR><BR>and these:<BR><BR><img src=\\\"http://inconduit.com/gal/streets/col499_18x12_print.jpg\\\"><BR><img src=\\\"http://inconduit.com/gal/streets/col555_18x12_print.jpg\\\"><BR><img src=\\\"http://inconduit.com/gal/streets/col588_2_18x12_print.jpg\\\"><BR><BR>it looks like locations were scouted and models corralled into being costumed (in some instances) and posed.  if <i>Motorist vs. Courier</i> is fake, it\\\'s the first complex action sequence he\\\'s attempted, as far as i can tell, and it\\\'s a bit much for him.<BR><BR>if they are real, like i said, they should have been filtered out.',0,'71.99.163.87','en'),(38189,'2006-01-31 11:51:34',400,'elaine','i would put money on a trained eye. simple as. if you spend time really lookingat things, things jump out much more. it\\\'s like whatever you are accessing when you are tripping, except specialised. like a musician who hears melodies in the street. i have experienced something similar after painting for several days at a time, then going outside, and the colour sensitivity becomes blinding and beautiful',0,'62.56.23.250','en'),(38190,'2006-01-31 12:14:55',195,'matt','<i>Anyone here have an ACTRA Face-to-Face account? I do, and I can tell you right now that Mr. 905\\\'s gossamer-vested girlfriend is Liza Kruester, a struggling loca