6,'Peter','caller number 666, youre on the air...',0,'130.219.8.253','en'),(38905,'2006-04-25 20:47:10',741,'mute','boys go to jupiter to get more stupider.<BR>girls go to mars to eat candy bars.',0,'64.128.136.170','en'),(38906,'2006-04-25 21:33:46',175,'Paul G','Peter, what\\\'s up with the hostility towards me, on your site?  Why, when you\\\'ve deleted austin\\\'s comments, do you allow people to trash-talk me?  I don\\\'t care if it\\\'s an e-mail, or thought here, or whatever, but I\\\'d like you, or hool, or jamie, or jeff, to be straight with me.  Whether citynoise, or here, or anyplace, why contribute - only to be shit on?',0,'192.203.136.254','en'),(38907,'2006-04-25 21:35:21',175,'Paul G','This is so fucking tired.',0,'192.203.136.254','en'),(38908,'2006-04-25 21:35:47',175,'Paul G','GOD DAMMIT',0,'192.203.136.254','en'),(38909,'2006-04-25 23:44:49',17,'austin','is this some kind of inside joke?',0,'68.6.212.249','en'),(38910,'2006-04-26 00:56:15',66,'Peter','paulg- huh? what are you talking about?',0,'24.45.7.227','en'),(38911,'2006-04-26 00:59:23',66,'Peter','link me to any hostility and ill take care of it. but if youre worried, why not just email me the details instead of making vague rants about it publically? no offense, its just a tad confusing when you make allegations that dont make alot of sense.',0,'24.45.7.227','en'),(38912,'2006-04-26 01:00:44',66,'Peter','like, <a href=\\\"http://www.citynoise.org/article/3768\\\">this</a> looks fine to me. frankly, i dont see any problems on any of <A href=\\\"http://www.citynoise.org/author/Paul_G\\\">your entries</a>. so... whats the problem?',0,'24.45.7.227','en'),(38913,'2006-04-26 01:27:02',175,'Paul G','On the one hand, you call me \\\"friend.\\\"  On the other hand, you publish < href=\\\"http://www.citynoise.org/article/664/by/fuzzytank\\\">text only articles like this</a>.  So, people go from citynoise, to swinney, to my journal, website, etc.  Because I have tried to speak in my own name, about what I believe, I have exposed myself.  I want to live with honest people, who are open, and so it\\\'s incumbent upon me to act that way, myself.  Meanwhile, any person willing to employ an alias is free to vent their bile.',0,'64.107.88.242','en'),(38914,'2006-04-26 01:27:33',175,'Paul G','dammit....<a href=\\\"http://www.citynoise.org/article/664/by/fuzzytank\\\">here</a>.',0,'64.107.88.242','en'),(38915,'2006-04-26 01:33:31',175,'Paul G','I tried to \\\"make nice\\\" with you and submit an article along with two comments.  Why do I get <a href=\\\"http://www.citynoise.org/article/3778#29195\\\">this</a> sort of crap in response?  Should I argue with an alias, there?  My father became seriously ill during my teens, and died in my twenties.  I have done nothing but \\\"be the man\\\" for my mother and sisters, since.  I\\\'ve been through birth, death, marriage, divorce, illness, hospitalization, etc, with them.  I\\\'m going to play internet games with someone calling me a child, or boy?',0,'64.107.88.242','en'),(38916,'2006-04-26 01:33:51',66,'Peter','dude, thats from 16 months ago. didnt we cover that already? and no, i didnt publish that. fuzzytank did. im not sure why youre taking this up with me- seems like you should speak to him if it bothers you. if you want me to delete it, why dont you just say so? i will. relax. youre sort of freaking out for no reason, man, and i sort of resent you calling me out on something that ultimately doesnt involve me at all.',0,'24.45.7.227','en'),(38917,'2006-04-26 01:35:30',66,'Peter','make nice with me? wtf? do we have drama or something? youre sort of freaking me out at this point, dude, so im gonna just bow out of this conversation.',0,'24.45.7.227','en'),(38918,'2006-04-26 01:36:55',66,'Peter','cause its srota strange for you to reprimand me for shit strangers say to you on a high-traffic site. if you have a problem, take it up with them or ask me to remove it. but dont pick a fight with me for no reason.',0,'24.45.7.227','en'),(38919,'2006-04-26 01:48:26',175,'Paul G','It\\\'s a change in the internet, a change in your site, and a change in you.  I liked the hippies.  I liked the nice people.  I liked people exploring, sharing, and feeling sort of safe.  And then there was self-promotion, competition, and money-making.  Some people I don\\\'t know; other people I think of as friends - and I am confused.  Creating a new identity, or playing, has always been a part of this experience.  But, now it defines it.  I saw that fuzzytank article like...3 weeks ago - for the first time, by accident.  Old for you, new for me.  Not feeling good.  And I have wondered why people have been searching s.o. user 175.  Now I know.',0,'64.107.88.242','en'),(38920,'2006-04-26 01:54:44',175,'Paul G','Austin makes fun of my plaid pants, and sandals.  He calls me a hippie, and tells me to move to a commune.  I tell him it\\\'s time to move my foot to his butt.  That\\\'s it.  Out.  Over.  I see the stuff on citynoise, and I wonder why a friend would publish it.  Williamsboard too.  I just don\\\'t know.',0,'64.107.88.242','en'),(38921,'2006-04-26 02:04:32',66,'Peter','paul, are you feeling ok? firstly, you and i have discussed that fuzzytank article a number of times, both ehre and via email. you are going paranoid. try to relax. itll be ok. for real. you sort of seem to be freaking out for no reason.',0,'24.45.7.227','en'),(38922,'2006-04-26 02:59:16',17,'austin','paul, please take your wool socks off before putting your feet in my butt.',0,'68.6.212.249','en'),(38923,'2006-04-26 06:52:03',496,'chemicalpilate','Dudes, I am totally. fucking. confused.',0,'69.17.112.117','en'),(38924,'2006-04-26 07:43:04',17,'austin','chemlab, you are like a child who wanders in in the middle of a movie--',0,'68.6.212.249','en'),(38925,'2006-04-26 07:43:30',17,'DUDE','What\\\'s your point, Walter?',0,'68.6.212.249','en'),(38926,'2006-04-26 07:44:44',17,'austin','<a href=\\\"http://bednark.com/big.lebowski.script.html\\\"> There\\\'s no fucking reason--here\\\'s my point, Dude--there\\\'s no fucking reason-- </A>',0,'68.6.212.249','en'),(38927,'2006-04-26 07:45:11',17,'austin','NO FUCKING REASON!',0,'68.6.212.249','en'),(38928,'2006-04-26 07:46:56',17,'WALTER','Huh?  No!  What the fuck are you talking--I\\\'m not--we\\\'re talking about unchecked aggression here--',0,'68.6.212.249','en'),(38929,'2006-04-26 18:45:42',741,'mute','i think the woman at the bookstore was One of Them.  she had that look in her eye.  plus, she was cheap as the dickens, which is usually another good indicator.<BR><BR>remind me to tell you about my escapades sometime.  no, on second thought, scratch that.  seems like that would be good novel material.  you\\\'d have to change it enough to render it unrecognizable, though, or they\\\'d make your life a living hell.<BR><BR>i don\\\'t think it would make that much difference:  i\\\'ve started reading a book about the hare krishnas that i\\\'ve had for awhile, <i>Monkey on a Stick</i>.  it\\\'s kind of sloppily written, but it seems to confirm that the core experience would be pretty much the same for anything along those lines that you might happen to stumble into.',0,'64.128.136.170','en'),(38930,'2006-04-26 20:15:01',175,'Paul G','(1) text only article about me, on your website (2) article trashes me (3) article links to my personal details (4) no one tells me about said article (5) i stumble upon said article 2-3 weeks ago when it appears in your comments section (6) i wonder why someone who calls me a friend would maintain said article (you say) for 16 months (7) the first mention i made of this issue was here, in (chat) about a week ago (8) we have never written/spoken about it, before (9) i see a new, and unprovoked shitty comment, after trying to put things aside, and play nice (10) as i wonder about what you take down, and leave up, you play me off, here, like a dick.',0,'192.203.136.254','en'),(38931,'2006-04-26 20:33:39',175,'Paul G','the \\\"citynoise team\\\" is perfectly willing to edit and/or delete articles and comments - allegedly for violations of the theme: \\\"stories, narratives and often upload photos of their favourite cities, hometowns, travels, or current locations.\\\"  why, i must wonder, do personal attacks of which i am the target remain up, while other comments, including austin\\\'s, are made to disappear.  this isn\\\'t about an internet bill of rights, or lack of a venue for my own expression, this is about someone who has called me \\\"friend\\\" not acting friendly.  when you started that site you begged for submissions, and got them from me, amnda, and maybe one or two other people.  now that you\\\'ve got your \\\"high traffic\\\" i can go fuck myself?',0,'192.203.136.254','en'),(38932,'2006-04-26 22:18:24',66,'Peter','paul, youre nuts man. ill take the article down, but geez... youre waaay freaking out. its just the internet, man. relax.',0,'24.45.7.227','en'),(38933,'2006-04-26 22:20:13',66,'Peter','next time, email me privately if you have a problem, and ask me to fix it. dont go on some bizarre-o witch-hunt on swinchat, where you insult me, my site, and others involved in it. i mean, for real. you wanna talk about unfriendly behavior... yours takes the cake here.',0,'24.45.7.227','en'),(38934,'2006-04-26 22:23:56',66,'Peter','and speaking of <a href=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=2509\\\">creepy</a>...',0,'24.45.7.227','en'),(38935,'2006-04-26 22:25:25',66,'Peter','oh, and paul... if youd never heard of that article before last week, then why did you link to it and comment about it <a href=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/article.phtml?id=3734\\\">here</a> back in 2004? yup, youre nuts.',0,'24.45.7.227','en'),(38936,'2006-04-26 22:26:40',66,'Peter','er, or refer to it, as it were.',0,'24.45.7.227','en'),(38937,'2006-04-26 22:41:37',17,'austin','what the fuck is going on in here!',0,'68.6.212.249','en'),(38938,'2006-04-26 23:03:21',496,'WALTER','This is not Nam.  This is bowling.  There are rules.',0,'137.131.205.145','en'),(38939,'2006-04-26 23:12:17',66,'Peter','stupid internet drama stirred up by someone who\\\'s acting paranoid and antisocial.',0,'24.45.7.227','en'),(38940,'2006-04-27 00:45:04',66,'Peter','but anyway!',0,'24.45.7.227','en'),(38941,'2006-04-27 01:10:39',129,'moebius','Look upon me! I\\\'ll show <i>you</i> the life of the mind!',0,'70.132.43.21','en'),(38942,'2006-04-27 01:11:19',129,'moebius','oh, wait, wrong Coen Bros. flick. but at least it also features John Goodman....',0,'70.132.43.21','en'),(38943,'2006-04-27 01:24:00',66,'Peter','\\\"ill show you the life of the mind!\\\" is a fav quote of mine. i must say it at least twice a week.',0,'24.45.7.227','en'),(38944,'2006-04-27 01:46:13',129,'moebius','yea, me too. as long as the building you\\\'re in doesn\\\'t start to spontaneously combust when you say it, it figure it\\\'s ok.',0,'70.132.43.21','en'),(38945,'2006-04-27 01:46:51',129,'moebius','\\\"comdongt\\\"? huh. well you know what that translates to. (sigh)',0,'70.132.43.21','en'),(38946,'2006-04-27 02:52:29',17,'austin','Barton Fink was a great one.',0,'68.6.212.249','en'),(38947,'2006-04-27 02:52:57',17,'austin','i  like, \\\"WHERE IS MY HONEY!?\\\"',0,'68.6.212.249','en'),(38948,'2006-04-27 05:33:39',129,'moebius','\\\"I run this dump, and I don\\\'t know the technical mumbo-jumbo. Why do I run it? Cause I got horse sense goddamit, SHOWMANSHIP! And also I hope Lou told you this, I am bigger and meaner and louder than any other kike in this town. Did you tell him that Lou? And I don\\\'t mean my dick is bigger than yours, it\\\'s not a sexual thing. You\\\'re a writer, you know more about that. Coffee?\\\"',0,'70.132.43.21','en'),(38949,'2006-04-27 13:12:39',93,'chiamattt','it\\\'s like fatah vs hamas in here. puff puff pass everyone. chill winston.',0,'58.226.158.76','en'),(38950,'2006-04-27 13:16:02',93,'chiamattt','<img src=\\\"http://www.chiamattt.com/photo/osaka/osaka06.jpg\\\">',0,'58