clist magazine on-line issue to which I linked.',0,'76.210.13.176','en'),(39667,'2007-05-13 20:10:52',175,'Paul G','I had wondered how Beard was able to afford a seven-year course of college study, afford the bike/gear/fuel over several years on the road, purchase a substantial property and renovate it, all while living as a single parent.  Either there is money coming in from the outside, or she\\\'s very focused on herself - and willing to use people to get ahead.  She should be the one making *some* reference to Theresa Wallach, encouraging people to remember who came before her.  But Wallach is dead, and won\\\'t be doing any favors for anyone.  So, instead, it\\\'s \\\"ME-ME-ME!\\\"  And soon, I will bet, \\\"Buy my book.\\\"',0,'76.210.13.176','en'),(39668,'2007-05-13 22:06:43',93,'chiamattt','Will you buy her book?',0,'58.226.159.24','en'),(39669,'2007-05-14 06:15:34',175,'Paul G','Haha.  No.  And it gets weirder: Now, Motorcyclist features an article \\\"Long Way Down\\\" in which the \\\"Long Way Round\\\" guys (Ewan McGregor and Charley Boorman) are supposed to travel from Britain to South Africa.  <a href=\\\"http://www.motorcyclistonline.com/newsandupdates/122_0705_long_way-down/\\\">That\\\'s</a> Theresa Wallach\\\'s trip!  Not only no mention of Wallach, again, but they claim, \\\"when the team was in Africa that the idea for Long Way Down.\\\"  It\\\'s several bad recent trends coming together: distoring/neglecting the past; manipulating the reader - and content hungry outlets; self-promotion absent any original content for the sake of some questionable material gain; etc.  Too, moreso now than ever, we\\\'re comparing ourselves to these distorted images: tweaked jpegs, padded bios, careful ommissions of assisstance, etc.  Dave I need to learn to smoke, or something...',0,'76.210.13.176','en'),(39670,'2007-05-14 06:39:00',175,'Paul G','Oh yeahhhh!  <a href=\\\"http://www.longwaydown.com/\\\">OMGZBBQ</a>  Will they make it?!?  Bah-bah-cue!!!  Two total