re in france, a long way from <a href=\\\"http://m.assetbar.com/achewood/uua7F12Mj\\\">flokes county</a>.',0,'64.128.136.170','en'),(39715,'2007-06-06 06:45:51',175,'Paul G','<img src=\\\"http://www.davezilla.com/images/goodintentions_1.jpg\\\">',0,'76.210.13.225','en'),(39716,'2007-06-06 08:00:52',496,'chemicalpilate','That giant sucking sound is back.',0,'69.17.112.117','en'),(39717,'2007-06-06 18:45:29',175,'Paul G','hey chemicalpilate, how are you?  i looked at simon\\\'s flickr, and was reminded of something from my childhood: my friend\\\'s mother had a weird little pottery vase in the form of a man napping - with a cactus growing in place of a penis.  and i used google\\\'s image search with \\\"mexican penis pottery\\\" as the key phrase.  I found the clowns; but, sigh, no little men with sombreros.  My friend\\\'s mother was really weird.  And she sold Avon products.  I knew them in the 1970\\\'s, before everyone sucked.',0,'76.210.8.201','en'),(39718,'2007-06-06 23:25:27',496,'chemicalpilate','2007 has been kind of a shit year so far.  I\\\'ve got 6 months to turn it around.  When my family moved out of the city and into the country, we found two giant boxes of Avon perfume bottles in the attic.  They were totally worthless even on eBay, but at some point someone collected them, and it made me feel bad to think that we were just going to throw out something they had obviously put more than a little effort into.',0,'137.131.205.145','en'),(39719,'2007-06-07 00:05:50',175,'Paul G','Putting a positive spin on it: I ran out of money in 2006.  And I\\\'ve managed to \\\'fake it\\\' for the past 6 months.  I hit bottom and started selling my family\\\'s old junk.  And, yes, it was humiliating to be turned away from the second hand record/camera/etc shops - not even being allowed to leave it there for free!  <a href=\\\"http://denisonline.chez-alice.fr/clin/Mexique.jpg\\\">Mexican</a> penis guy.  <a href=\\\"http://denisonline.chez-alice.fr/clin/Mexique.jpg\\\">PNG</a> penis guys.  The Avon lady had twice as much skin as she needed, and her head looked like a folded accordian.  Her son had a huge penis and I think that he had sex with our music teacher when we were in junior high school.',0,'76.210.8.201','en'),(39720,'2007-06-07 01:14:52',66,'Peter','<br><img src=\\\"http://saturn5.com/peter/ljphoto/bounce1.jpg\\\"><br><br><img src=\\\"http://saturn5.com/peter/ljphoto/bounce2.jpg\\\">',0,'24.45.14.169','en'),(39721,'2007-06-07 02:45:49',496,'chemicalpilate','Peter you make me want to move to NYC.  When I was in junior high, I was asked to testify in a sexual assault case against the janitor.  The music teacher said he grabbed her ass.  I didn\\\'t see any of that I just saw him come out of her office while I was packing up my sheet music.',0,'69.17.112.117','en'),(39722,'2007-06-07 03:35:27',66,'Peter','come visit any time; lord knows ive got room now. when i was in junior high, i came this close to getting kicked out for cracking the class bully\\\'s forehead open with a lacrosse stick. remember \\\"sloth\\\" from goonies? he\\\'d taunt me and call me sloth. and after one too many <i>baby rooooth</i>s, he got his. and for anyone reading this, if you ever say \\\"baby rooooth!\\\" to me in person, ill fucking knock your lights out.',0,'24.45.14.169','en'),(39723,'2007-06-07 17:16:30',195,'matt','anybody have any <a href=\\\"http://brettderekwalsh.livejournal.com/204337.html?nc=1&style=mine\\\">thoughts</a>?',0,'64.128.136.170','en'),(39724,'2007-06-07 17:41:52',195,'matt','my grandma died at grady, too.  before my time.  mom said they all but lived in that lobby for a week.  my brother had just learned to run and was perpetually ready for a change of scene, something he never grew out of.<BR><BR>she told me about my grandmother\\\'s brother on the phone with his sister, holding his hand over the receiver, saying, <i>somebody come talk to bess ann.  she\\\'s done wore me out.</i>  about my uncle waking in the night on a vinyl-covered couch to find that some kind soul had come along and cut the side and bottom of his ass pocket and plucked out his wallet.  about my father\\\'s two youngest brothers in the cafeteria in line behind their cousin, a chunky boy named johnny cochran, now blind as a haint with the retinitis pigmentosa like his two older brothers.  when it was johnny\\\'s turn, he said, \\\"six hot dogs, please.\\\"  they couldn\\\'t get over that.',0,'64.128.136.170','en'),(39725,'2007-06-07 18:52:03',496,'chemicalpilate','\\\"On the other hand, you\\\'re really cute when you\\\'re totally absorbed in a book.\\\"',0,'137.131.205.145','en'),(39726,'2007-06-08 01:33:53',175,'Paul G','I think that the man with the answers to all of your questions is Chiamattt.',0,'76.209.239.224','en'),(39727,'2007-06-08 06:05:49',234,'etienne','i always come back here',0,'125.238.72.137','en'),(39728,'2007-06-08 13:33:36',92,'kini','me too.',0,'121.44.53.237','en'),(39729,'2007-06-08 16:00:55',66,'Peter','me three. multiple times a day. its a habit.',0,'130.219.8.253','en'),(39730,'2007-06-11 01:40:45',66,'Peter','speed seduction in a magazine<br>endless pleasure in a limousine<br>in the back shakes a tambourine<br>nicotine from a silver screen',0,'24.45.14.169','en'),(39731,'2007-06-11 03:35:32',66,'Peter','<a href=\\\"http://www.citynoise.org/article/6914\\\"><img src=\\\"http://www.citynoise.org/upload/21037.jpg\\\" border=\\\"0\\\"></a>',0,'24.45.14.169','en'),(39732,'2007-06-11 07:03:13',496,'chemicalpilate','The most I have to say isn\\\'t really that revealing at all.',0,'69.17.112.117','en'),(39733,'2007-06-11 17:02:11',195,'matt','<a href=\\\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wabi_sabi\\\">wabi-sabi</a>',0,'64.128.136.170','en'),(39734,'2007-06-11 20:41:40',66,'Peter','<A href=\\\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windows_Application_Binary_Interface\\\">WABI</a>',0,'130.219.8.253','en'),(39735,'2007-06-11 21:53:06',93,'chiamattt','why me?',0,'58.226.159.24','en'),(39736,'2007-06-12 01:12:15',496,'chemicalpilate','Because we love you.',0,'69.17.112.117','en'),(39737,'2007-06-12 02:36:55',66,'Peter','why ask why? try bud dry.',0,'24.45.14.169','en'),(39738,'2007-06-12 19:20:53',790,'cdr','Do elevators smell different to midgets?',0,'71.202.122.145','en'),(39739,'2007-06-12 19:45:11',66,'Peter','which reminds me of the time i began seeing in 4D after a particularly good evening of too many danziger dopplebiers with my friend, hans delbrück...',0,'130.219.8.253','en'),(39740,'2007-06-13 05:35:54',93,'chiamattt','I left the office for my usual smoking roost our back of the building and the sun bathed me in an intense white light. The light did not seem like the light I experienced during any other smoke breaks this day. It was somehow different and gave me the feeling that I was being watched. It did not burn like the sun usually does and I did not curse the heat like I usually do. My mind was preoccupied by the way it was illuminating my surroundings and as I stood there I found myself standing straight slowly looking up from the vividly green grass. I felt my body being engulfed by something I cannot describe and it calmed me. I was reminded of being young once. The safety of youth.',0,'211.253.15.130','en'),(39741,'2007-06-15 02:13:58',496,'chemicalpilate','I don\\\'t know what\\\'s worse: knowing that I will miss the feeling of youth or not being able to recognize the feeling of youth <i>now</i>.',0,'137.131.205.145','en'),(39742,'2007-06-15 02:36:55',66,'Peter','age aint nuthin but a numba',0,'24.45.14.169','en'),(39743,'2007-06-15 20:17:17',82,'simon','hey pals',0,'24.193.67.253','en'),(39744,'2007-06-16 04:06:58',66,'Peter','i pack heat like im da oven door',0,'24.45.14.169','en'),(39745,'2007-06-16 04:23:58',66,'Peter','check out those rims, simz.',0,'24.45.14.169','en'),(39746,'2007-06-16 07:21:21',496,'chemicalpilate','Holy balls, it was a good night.',0,'69.17.112.117','en'),(39747,'2007-06-16 07:44:24',175,'Paul G','I snipped sheet metal and drank coffee.  Then I looked at the net and drank wine.  <a href=\\\"http://www.printfetish.com\\\">printfetish.com</a> is awesome.  badatsports.com made my head hurt.  That is all.  G\\\'night.',0,'75.5.90.235','en'),(39748,'2007-06-16 17:11:47',66,'Peter','my favorite palindrome: \\\"a dog, a panic in a pagoda...\\\"',0,'24.45.14.169','en'),(39749,'2007-06-16 17:12:08',66,'Peter','also: \\\"im a lasagna, hang a salami\\\"',0,'24.45.14.169','en'),(39750,'2007-06-16 18:23:51',175,'Paul G','Morning brought the heat - waking wet to old Dylan, and the droning of the cicada brood.  Today my electric fan is a lover\\\'s tongue.',0,'76.210.12.233','en'),(39751,'2007-06-17 08:30:08',63,'olivia','it feels late, i\\\'m tired',0,'74.95.2.241','en'),(39752,'2007-06-17 08:49:42',65,'le','RENAISSANCE',0,'216.27.181.232','en'),(39753,'2007-06-17 15:41:33',496,'chemicalpilate','Is nothing sacred?',0,'69.17.112.117','en'),(39754,'2007-06-18 13:02:04',66,'Peter','nothing is as sacred as the chao.',0,'130.219.8.253','en'),(39755,'2007-06-18 17:31:29',496,'chemicalpilate','Hi swinsters.  If you could change anything about swinney.org, what would it be?',0,'137.131.205.145','en'),(39756,'2007-06-18 18:06:21',195,'matt','more pirate days.',0,'64.128.136.170','en'),(39757,'2007-06-18 23:41:33',66,'Peter','I don\\\'t have to tell you things are bad. Everybody knows things are bad. It\\\'s a depression. Everybody\\\'s out of work or scared of losing their job. The dollar buys a nickel\\\'s work, banks are going bust, shopkeepers keep a gun under the counter. Punks are running wild in the street and there\\\'s nobody anywhere who seems to know what to do, and there\\\'s no end to it. We know the air is unfit to breathe and our food is unfit to eat, and we sit watching our TV\\\'s while some local newscaster tells us that today we had fifteen homicides and sixty-three violent crimes, as if that\\\'s the way it\\\'s supposed to be. We know things are bad - worse than bad. They\\\'re crazy. It\\\'s like everything everywhere is going crazy, so we don\\\'t go out anymore. We sit in the house, and slowly the world we are living in is getting smaller, and all we say is, \\\'Please, at least leave us alone in our living rooms. Let me have my toaster and my TV and my steel-belted radials and I won\\\'t say anything. Just leave us alone.\\\' Well, I\\\'m not gonna leave you alone. I want you to get mad! I don\\\'t want you to protest. I don\\\'t want you to riot - I don\\\'t want you to write to your congressman because I wouldn\\\'t know what to tell you to write. I don\\\'t know what to do about the depression and the inflation and the Russians and the crime in the street. All I know is that first you\\\'ve got to get mad. I want you to get up right now, sit up, go to your windows, open them and stick your head out and yell - \\\'I\\\'m as mad as hell and I\\\'m not going to take this anymore!\\\' Things have got to change. But first, you\\\'ve gotta get mad!... You\\\'ve got to say, \\\'I\\\'m as mad as hell, and I\\\'m not going to take this anymore!\\\' Then we\\\'ll figure out what to do about the depression and the inflation and the oil crisis. But first get up out of your chairs, open the window, stick your head out, and yell, and say it: \\\"I\\\'M AS MAD AS HELL, AND I\\\'M NOT GOING TO TAKE THIS ANYMORE!\\\" ',0,'24.45.14.169','en'),(39758,'2007-06-18 23:45:13',66,'Peter','chempil: i miss the <a href=\\\"http://web.archive.org/web/20001206203000/http://swinney.org/\\\">old interface</a>.',0,'24.45.14.169','en'),(39759,'2007-06-20 16:58:44',17,'austin','i miss it too.',0,'68.107.35.12','en'),(39760,'2007-06-20 16:59:12',17,'austin','also we could use captchas.',0,'68.107.35.12','en'),(39761,'2007-06-20 18:51:40',496,'chemicalpilate','I say we go <a href=\\\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Copy_protection#Copy_protection_specific_to_old_games\\\">old school style</a> with the bot protection.',0,'137.131.205.145','en'),(39762,'2007-06-20 22:21:11',175,'Paul G','swinney.org is like an old motorcycle that austin keeps in a garage.  and it is cool because it is (1) old; (2) austin\\\'s; and (3) carries the marks of everyone who crashed while learning to ride.  austin\\\'s been free with the keys; and the saddle has many different butt prints in it.  and yeah, sure, he\\\'s talked about fixing it up and getting it to run \\\"right.\\\"  but then he opens a beer, slouches on the bean bag, and passes out.  the beer spills on his nuts; he wakes; elly\\\'s on the phone asking for help with something; austin says, \\\"hmmwell ok.\\\"  and by the grace of god, swinney.org remains un-restored.  i\\\'m opposed to yet another in-line 4 liter bike ridden by douche bags, i.e., myspace-i-fication.  old, austin\\\'s, free-with-the-keys, a few dents and sputters is good, i think.  better to have colorful people on a bland site - than bland people on a colorful site.  if it involves intense, creative personal stuff - then cool.  but it will always be the people and not the interface...',0,'76.210.10.167','en'),(39763,'2007-06-21 02:58:06',175,'Paul G','i hate loading the screen and seeing my thoughts.',0,'76.210.10.167','en'),(39764,'2007-06-21 02:58:35',175,'Paul G','and i hate loading the screen and seeing lengthy articles in the thoughts section.',0,'76.210.10.167','en'),(39765,'2007-06-21 02:59:38',175,'Paul G','when i load the scre and my own lengthy thoughts are displayed, i am tempted to enter many smaller thoughts - just to push the offending item off-screen.',0,'76.210.10.167','en'),(39766,'2007-06-21 03:00:53',175,'Paul G','inevitably, i\\\'ll misspell a word.  and then i\\\'ll be as self-conscious about the short thought as i was about the long thought.',0,'76.210.10.167','en'),(39767,'2007-06-21 03:09:42',175,'Paul G','my own life, my real thoughts, seem disconnected from this place - and the people here.  i don\\\'t sense that there is much [too long.]',0,'76.210.10.167','en'),(39768,'2007-06-21 05:39:29',93,'chiamattt','where are the colorful people?',0,'211.253.15.130','en'),(39769,'2007-06-21 15:37:14',496,'chemicalpilate','It is what you make it.',0,'69.17.112.117','en'),(39770,'2007-06-21 15:39:22',534,'griece','paulg, youre weird, man.',0,'24.45.14.169','en'),(39771,'2007-06-21 23:40:42',195,'matt','who <i>isn\\\'t</i> colorful?',0,'64.128.136.170','en'),(39772,'2007-06-22 22:29:20',63,'olivia','sausage party',0,'74.95.2.241','en'),(39773,'2007-06-23 21:29:03',175,'Paul G','<a href=\\\"http://germz.org/swinney/venus.html\\\">\\\"It is what you make it.\\\"</a>  Ref. \\\"sausage party, colorful,\\\" and, \\\"weird,\\\" me.',0,'76.209.243.54','en'),(39774,'2007-06-23 22:52:47',82,'simon','i love ballerinas and pickles',0,'24.193.67.253','en'),(39775,'2007-06-25 03:43:44',66,'Peter','i love pickled ballerinas.',0,'24.45.14.169','en'),(39776,'2007-06-26 04:58:11',175,'Paul G','Hi simon.  I loved PJ Harvey early-90\\\'s.  \\\"Rid of Me\\\" live is house-rocking, even more moving than B & B\\\'s \\\"100 Foot Weenie\\\" parody.',0,'76.209.54.134','en'),(39777,'2007-06-26 19:36:48',175,'Paul G',' ...so what happened before was that while the site presented itself as, \\\"an outlet of sorts to kindred spirits across this land...creative souls that feel the darkness,\\\" when someone took a chance and created something that was intended to be either sincere and/or humorous they received silence or mockery in reply. and that mockery was, frequently, off-site or under cover of an alias. hello griece.  hello ackman.  when more people critique than contribute, the thing collapses.  the temptation is to focus on yourself, saving anything worthwhile for your own site. read: advertising revenue, google rank, whatever. what\\\'s left is a model of infinite competition a la the global free market, as opposed to any sort of community. o.k. bye.',0,'75.5.89.231','en'),(39778,'2007-06-26 19:52:06',66,'Peter','i doubt that. bar none, my best writing is on this site, my lj, blog, or anything else nothwithstanding. im sure i can speak for many people in saying that. youre also the only person ive ever heard on here that complains, in an ongoing fashion, about criticism, anonymity, etc. its just the internet. take it easy.',0,'24.45.14.169','en'),(39779,'2007-06-26 19:53:39',66,'Peter','i guess its once again time for the annual \\\"state of swinney.org\\\" .o0Othoughts roundtable...',0,'24.45.14.169','en'),(39780,'2007-06-27 03:46:08',175,'Paul G','...so in response to chemicalpilate\\\'s question i make two observations: (1) the number of outlets for personal expression has multiplied greatly since swinney.org was founded, e.g., flickr, myspace, tribe, friendster, et al; and (2) with the growth of digital photography and template blogs expression is easier, i.e., requires less effort and skill than swinney.org submissions.  while there is very good writing here, one can\\\'t help but notice that it\\\'s, in the main, several years old.  even as my old history teachers suggested that the energy of the 1960\\\'s was akin to a \\\"sparkler\\\" shooting off in many directions, weakly, i suppose that \\\"internet energies\\\" are spread widely and weakly over many websites.  \\\"thoughts\\\" here is popular because of its ease of use, i think.  contemporary americans want instant results with zero effort and zero accountability, eh?  austin wrote in a comment, several years ago, that he noticed people had stopped writing - but hung around making douche bag remarks.  so the answer is to make everything as simple and graphic as possible, afford anonymity, and then promote, promote, promote.',0,'75.5.89.231','en'),(39781,'2007-06-27 04:54:14',66,'Peter','i, for one, am a fan of anonymity. i wasnt a big fan of requiring logins here back in 01, but definitely see the necessity. i think the ability to log in is important, but it <i>would</i> be nice to have the option to post \\\"anonymously\\\". its not like austin cant tell who it is anyway (not that he cares), but it sure would spark up more candid conversation round these parts, if not a little moderation now and then (but im always good for that).',0,'24.45.14.169','en'),(39782,'2007-06-27 20:49:24',606,'critic','i miss \\\"critic\\\"',0,'130.219.8.253','en'),(39783,'2007-06-27 23:55:18',17,'austin','algonquin round table',0,'68.107.35.12','en'),(39784,'2007-06-28 00:24:23',175,'Paul G','Now what sort of person would want to disassociate themselves from their words and actions?  Probably the same sort of person who would suggest that through deception truth would be revealed.  If only there were some place on the internet where one might remove words and pictures from their original context -- for the purpose of mocking their creator.  But I digress.  Here, now, the swinney.org \\\"home\\\" page is organized with 4 horizontal rows: (1) thoughts; (2) gifs; (3) articles; (4) credits.  Why not re-organize the \\\"home\\\" page with 3 vertical columns: (1) 180x600 vertical skyscraper ad; (2) a \\\"thoughts\\\" section 100 posts long -- containg images from cam-phones and anonymous slander; and (3) and article index.  The archives are maintained; ease of use promotes contribution; constant reloading = ad $$$ for austin.  Of course, the site loses its original purpose.  But hasn\\\'t America done the same thing?  I am serious about the 3 col-thing.  Ok, bye.',0,'76.209.226.5','en'),(39785,'2007-06-28 02:03:54',175,'Paul G','...so this is a sketch: <a href=\\\"http://germz.org/swinney/home.html\\\">swinney index</a> minus \\\"thoughts\\\" form.  someone with more time and talent would, of course, be able to greatly improve upon the design.  but, it illustrates the idea.  ok, bye.',0,'76.209.226.5','en'),(39786,'2007-06-28 08:39:23',93,'chiamattt','If the background colors were changed from Grays to Hot Pinks, the site would become popular again. But isn\\\'t it popular? I like to think we\\\'re so hip that all the other cats can\\\'t play with us anymore. ',0,'211.253.15.130','en'),(39787,'