ref=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/info_user.phtml?uid=538\\\">arcy</a> and a ton of poems by <A href=\\\"http://www.swinney.org/journals/info_user.phtml?uid=618\\\">skwooshi1</a>',0,'130.219.8.253','en'),(39814,'2007-07-13 01:04:29',66,'Peter','the last cat who tried to see me, now he gotta touch braille',0,'24.186.187.5','en'),(39815,'2007-07-13 02:32:23',66,'Peter','madhattan, queensbridge, bucktown, shaolin and the boogie down. know what im sayin?',0,'24.186.187.5','en'),(39816,'2007-07-13 02:52:54',66,'Peter','let me just post one more thought while im monopolizing the thoughts section...',0,'24.186.187.5','en'),(39817,'2007-07-13 05:02:01',496,'chemicalpilate','Anything you can feel, you can feel again.',0,'69.17.112.117','en'),(39818,'2007-07-13 05:05:59',496,'chemicalpilate','Holy fuck Kathy Foster is so hot.',0,'69.17.112.117','en'),(39819,'2007-07-13 12:53:42',66,'Peter','i saw a scantily-clad girl with a red-and-black mohawk speed past me on a classic merckx trackbike with fluorescent yellow aero rims radially laced with anodized blue aluminum spokes. that made my, um, nature rise...',0,'24.186.187.5','en'),(39820,'2007-07-13 12:54:35',66,'Peter','and honestly, it was more the bike than the girl that got me hot and bothered. funny, that.',0,'24.186.187.5','en'),(39821,'2007-07-13 21:46:28',82,'simon','hot bike!',0,'24.193.67.253','en'),(39822,'2007-07-14 05:34:25',66,'Peter','my shell, mechanical found ghost/but my ghetto is animal found toast',0,'24.186.187.5','en'),(39823,'2007-07-14 06:19:42',496,'chemicalpilate','From the ghetto to the medow/in the core you tore explore/experience what is real you feel',0,'69.17.112.117','en'),(39824,'2007-07-14 16:36:22',66,'Peter','yo it wasnt even like that/i wanted my cardiovascular to fight back/cupid had me runnin circles blindfolded/in the daytime with a flashlight looking for her',0,'24.186.187.5','en'),(39825,'2007-07-16 04:14:59',66,'Peter','hey man, i dont create the noise; i just feed it back into the system.',0,'24.186.187.5','en'),(39826,'2007-07-16 05:52:02',66,'Peter','you know, if all you motherfuckers would post more .o0Othoughts, i could post all my weird .o0Othoughts without it looking like i was monopolizing this shit. so get to cracking. more traffic on .o0Othoughts plz. (and down with the image ban ;)',0,'24.186.187.5','en'),(39827,'2007-07-16 06:08:57',66,'Peter','...cause ive gotta admit, ive been flirting with <a href=\\\"http://www.wikichan.org/index.php/B/\\\">/b/</a> lately...',0,'24.186.187.5','en'),(39828,'2007-07-16 07:32:28',496,'chemicalpilate','I\\\'ve been putting a lot of miles on my bike lately.  It\\\'s been really, really good.  In many ways.',0,'69.17.112.117','en'),(39829,'2007-07-16 15:56:17',82,'simon','DETROI',0,'24.193.67.253','en'),(39830,'2007-07-16 23:25:57',66,'Peter','i flow like detroit without tha t/yo i gottta pee from all the beers i drank/woulda drank more if they had more glasses to clank',0,'24.186.187.5','en'),(39831,'2007-07-17 04:27:14',66,'Peter','i got more .o0Othoughts than swinney .o0Othoughs can handle/mics i dandle/hittin up walls like a vandal/the brooklyn scandal in birkenstock sandals/lightin my blunt with a candle',0,'24.186.187.5','en'),(39832,'2007-07-17 16:54:26',195,'matt','when i first heard <a href=\\\"http://youtube.com/watch?v=UKHhqjx7FmY\\\">this song</a>, i thought the <a href=\\\"http://www.sing365.com/music/lyric.nsf/Phantom-Limb-lyrics-The-Shins/4C28DDB18AE962714825723400085086\\\">lyric</a> was \\\"family portrait, circa nine to five\\\".  i think i like that better.  dunno.  there cannot be a portrait circa 9 to 5 because everybody\\\'s at work or school; we grow up in a house full of strangers.  i can\\\'t decide which is more evocative, which more (relatively) timeless.  could be circa 1495, whatevs.',0,'64.128.136.170','en'),(39833,'2007-07-17 19:24:03',82,'simon','heh peter',0,'24.193.67.253','en'),(39834,'2007-07-17 23:20:53',496,'chemicalpilate','The doctor told a patient \\\"It\\\'s all in your imagination negro.\\\" Ahh, what do he know? About the buttery flow, he need to cut the ego.',0,'137.131.205.145','en'),(39835,'2007-07-18 03:53:24',66,'Peter','jesus saves so does the heimlich maneuver/yall be diggin my shit more than a pooper scooper',0,'24.186.187.5','en'),(39836,'2007-07-18 03:54:41',66,'Peter','no more quotes from hiphop tunes. were going straight up freestyle.',0,'24.186.187.5','en'),(39837,'2007-07-18 07:16:30',496,'chemicalpilate','i can\\\'t be hackin/this material be whackin\\\'/got my drunk on/gotta get my funk/playaz be hatin\\\'/what i be sprayin\\\'/working the crowd/lovin it loud/gotta drop a rhyme like newton/yall best gone get scootin\\\'',0,'69.17.112.117','en'),(39838,'2007-07-18 07:16:57',496,'chemicalpilate','<-- n00b',0,'69.17.112.117','en'),(39839,'2007-07-18 22:17:53',175,'Paul G','So you been to school for a year or two - And you know you\\\'ve seen it all - In daddy\\\'s car, thinkin\\\' you\\\'ll go far - Back east your type don\\\'t crawl - Play efficiency jazz to parade your snazz - On your five grand stereo - Braggin\\\' that you how the niggers feel the cold - And the slum\\\'s got so much soul - You\\\'re a star-belly sneech, you suck like a leech - You want everyone to act like you - Kiss ass while you bitch so you can get rich - While your boss gets richer of you...',0,'76.210.3.194','en'),(39840,'2007-07-18 22:29:20',175,'Paul G','I don\\\'t want to think - Don\\\'t make me care - I wanna melt in with the group...',0,'76.210.3.194','en'),(39841,'2007-07-18 22:37:11',175,'Paul G','Painless and mindless - Scraps from anywhere - Bunch of used parts - From garbage pails everywhere - Frankenstein became a monster - Just like you...',0,'76.210.3.194','en'),(39842,'2007-07-18 22:48:26',66,'Peter','<br>regardless, im emotionally bombarded<br>my breath smells like somebody farted<br>when the relationship started, I dropped my usually guarded<br>heart, and thats just the start<br>this story goes on for years, bringin up fears<br>makin ya ears bleed devour mics with internal angst<br>still waitin in line at Chase banks<br>i thought all these demons off i warded<br>departed, my connection with her<br>leaving me quartered, broken hearted<br>cadillac door open like someone ajared it<br>fuck this shit, im bushwick retarded...',0,'24.186.187.5','en'),(39843,'2007-07-18 22:50:55',66,'Peter','[edit: thats b-u-shwick retarded\\\". damned thoughts \\\"bus\\\" translator]',0,'24.186.187.5','en'),(39844,'2007-07-19 01:17:06',175,'Paul G','Funny Story: I leave home at 17 to get away from my father.  He smokes, drinks, yells and tries to kill me. I wind up at a crappy state school. While there, my gradfather - who acted like my real father - dies. Shortly thereafter, I sleep with my friend\\\'s ex, and he kills himself - after cutting off one of his fingers and leving a message for me/her on the wall.  I\\\'m kicked out of school, and go to work for some questionable Italian guys. It sucks, and I get into police work.  But I\\\'m stuck working in a jail.  Just when I\\\'ve got a career, my father dies after a long illness.  I go back to the crappy state school and finish the degree - but get screwed by a nut-job prof and lose the BA, leaving with a bullshit degree.  Nonetheless, I make it into grad school.  But after I finish the coursework, my grad prof won\\\'t read my thesis.  And it turns out that he - the grad prof - is pressuring female students for sex while he\\\'s going through a divorce - from a woman who\\\'s a former student.  And the department, school and dean won\\\'t hear my complaint.  I drive the taxi for 2 years - 80 hours a week - to pay the school debt.  But, surprise, my mother - now in her 70\\\'s - needs joint replacement surgery.  And I\\\'ve got to be there for 2 years of therapy to help her sit and stand - at the bed, shower, toilet, everywhere.  But when I get through all of that, and run away for a trip on the motorcycle, I find my pictures on williamsboard.com, and people choose me to mock on citynoise.org, and then I forget to laugh.',0,'76.210.3.194','en'),(39845,'2007-07-19 01:41:20',175,'Paul G','...I really should have set the scene with the image of my grandparents arriving penniless at Ellis Island, and then dying penniless in Chicago.  The grandfather\\\'s botched Union cataract surgery.  The father\\\'s first marriage, and the 1/2 brother in the mental institution.  The cousin with Down\\\'s Syndrome.  The one sister\\\'s child and the other sister\\\'s divorce.  The one relative still alive living in a trailer.  The fact that I\\\'ll be turning not 30, but 40, this year.  My ex.  Etc.  Etc.',0,'76.210.3.194','en'),(39846,'2007-07-19 02:34:18',66,'Peter','[non-freestyle notes: bus bus. thanks for the fix, austin. paulg, what youre posting should be posted as a proper entry. its far too interesting and important to just disappear into the nebulousness of .o0Othoughts, as they get bumped on down the line. for real. also email me from your current email address (mine is the same) because i want to talk to you about something, please] BACK TO DA FREESTEEZ, YO. id like to see simz next on the mic, plz...',0,'24.186.187.5','en'),(39847,'2007-07-19 02:37:36',66,'Peter','non-freestyle notes freestyle boasts/got me/runnin round spittin freestyle ghosts',0,'24.186.187.5','en'),(39848,'2007-07-19 16:52:58',496,'chemicalpilate','been runnin the scene/chasin a dream/got lost got tossed/out the club/in your mind/am i workin?/you\\\'re always smirkin/lead a man to believe/in shit he can\\\'t see',0,'137.131.205.145','en'),(39849,'2007-07-20 02:14:39',66,'Peter','<br>rhymes flow like sands through a sieve<br>you get it jacked if you be wearin ya heart on ya sleeve<br>theres two things in life: fact and fiction<br>with tact i listen<br>keep spittin rhymes until you start to believe',0,'24.186.187.5','en'),(39850,'2007-07-20 05:49:19',66,'Peter','<br>cipherpunks underground hiphop<b>a real chore for ear and brain-top<br>codeflow as knotted with riddles, chopped<br>imagery overripe as shitty bebop<br>and yo I don’t mean to boast<br>but ima keep droppin lyrics til somebody else posts...',0,'24.186.187.5','en'),(39851,'2007-07-20 17:06:54',175,'Paul G','paulgermanos@msn.com  two things in life: appearance and reality.  the people who \\\"succeed\\\" are not the ones who are good -- but rather the ones who learn to appear to be good.  story: i was a runner.  high school freshman numerals, sophmore letter, track and cross-country.  but i loved art and philosophy too.  so, even though i wasn\\\'t gay, a group of other runners would chase me and yell \\\"FAGGOT!\\\"  It went on for two years.  And all I needed to do to stop it was point the finger at someone else.  Learn about football.  Something.  One day I caught one of the taunters, alone.  And I threw him to the ground.  As I raised my hand to strike him -- the \\\"Coach\\\" caught my arm.  The taunter lept up, pointed his finger at me, and yelled: \\\"FAGGOT!FAGGOT!FAGGOT!\\\"  Time passed.  The taunters went to good schools, joined more teams, fraternities, and such.  And they\\\'ve all done very well in life.',0,'76.210.7.160','en'),(39852,'2007-07-20 19:37:54',195,'matt','you should put a tune to it.',0,'64.128.136.170','en'),(39853,'2007-07-21 00:44:32',175,'Paul G','Someone already published it -- and his name was J.R.R. Tolkien.  The ring had as its most notable property the power to render its wearer invisible to all but the most subtle eyes.  So that the ring stands in metaphor for the art of appearance, synonomous for the art of tyranny.  Tolkien found the ring in Plato\\\'s Republic.',0,'76.210.9.191','en'),(39854,'2007-07-21 00:49:01',175,'Paul G','time to shower',0,'76.210.9.191','en'),(39855,'2007-07-21 00:49:25',175,'Paul G','time to ride',0,'76.210.9.191','en'),(39856,'2007-07-21 00:49:36',175,'Paul G','time to look at art',0,'76.210.9.191','en'),(39857,'2007-07-21 00:50:03',175,'Paul G','time to drink',0,'76.210.9.191','en'),(39858,'2007-07-21 00:50:15',175,'Paul G','time to forget',0,'76.210.9.191','en'),(39859,'2007-07-21 01:25:37',66,'Peter','<br>flip the first cigarette to keep the wish real<br>flick the zippo, watchin the smoke touch steel<br>always the same wish, as my universe reverses<br>exhale love and inhale hexes and curses<br>spit for yesterday, today and all of my tomorrows<br>speaking the truth separates you from all your sorrows<br><br>who am i? who are you? whats the deal?<br>let your fingers do the walking but i still cant feel<br>so i pour it out in these syncopated verses<br>scopin undertakers cruising my block in platinum hearses<br>sample the beat, i dont bite, i just borrow<br>subwoofer eating my shit like osteoclasts on bone marrow',0,'24.186.187.5','en'),(39860,'2007-07-23 13:56:00',496,'chemicalpilate','Real steel reverses the curses of tomorrows sorrows/deal and feel/my verses or it\\\'s hearses/but just to borrow/I need \\\'em again on the \\\'morrow',0,'69.17.112.117','en'),(39861,'2007-07-24 04:40:20',66,'Peter','<br><br>got me a girl that looks like a boy<br>she says tell me the Drunken Hipster Bedtime Story',0,'24.186.187.5','en'),(39862,'2007-07-24 23:56:44',195,'matt','<a href=\\\"http://youtube.com/watch?v=Hk8bejZ16KU\\\"><i>pick it for me, james.</i></a>',0,'64.128.136.170','en'),(39863,'2007-07-25 19:02:02',66,'Peter','Go to the hill on the right hand side. On one side you can see a slope leading down from where the railing has broken, and a ramp leading up to the summit. Go up this ramp and the left the reach the sign, \\\"Penguin Heights.\\\" Pick up the tennis racquets from the left of the sign, the use the Christmas pudding where the railings have broken. This creates a huge snowball, bowling over the two polar bears blocking the bridge. Go down to the deep snow sign, the across the deep snow (making sure you have picked up the tennis racquets), to the bridge. Go across the bridge to the arch into the penguin village. The instant Spud enters th